{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017cv6esVxX8pGM5oEwxJCFA","type":"tool_result","content":"58:- **Agents**: `agents/autonomous-dev/*.md` are system-prompt files fed to the backend LLM per phase, each with a matching `<phase>.contract.json` defining expected I/O artifact schema. Phases communicate **only via file artifacts** under `artifacts/{phase}/{ticketId}/` — no in-process message passing.\n65:- Artifacts always at `artifacts/{phase}/{ticketId}/`, never nested inside phase path; check for existing artifacts before regenerating (resume support).\n89:Separately, `forge validate` and `forge init` aren't broken — they don't exist yet (not in `cli/index.js`'s `commands` map, no `cli/validate.js`/`cli/init.js`). Real migration work, already tracked below. `forge activate` and `forge jira`/`forge jira-sync` are implemented and were verified working (activate: regenerates `.mcp.json` + probes MCP servers correctly; jira commands: give correct, clear errors for missing ticket id / missing `JIRA_EMAIL`/`JIRA_API_TOKEN`/`JIRA_BASE_URL` — they just need real credentials, which aren't set in this environment).\n99:Newly ported `cli/`: `status, list, logs, watch, dashboard, validate, test-connection, api-setup, docs, config, red-team, security, agent-test, daemon, install, uninstall, doctor, fix, clean, reject, workspace, metrics(→metrics-dashboard.js), setup-observability, knowledge, diagnose, grooming-report, regression-build, session, task, workflow, bench, evaluate, plugin(→pdlc-plugin.js), mcp(→mcp-query.js)`. Newly ported `lib/` (see `docs/cli-migration-plans.md` for exact per-command dependency lists — several needed more transitive files than the plan estimated, e.g. `lib/bench/` pulled in 8 files not 4, `lib/security/` pulled in `scanners/`): `daemon/{auth-manager,task-queue}.js`, `setup/rtk-setup.js`, `cleanup/*`, `approval-manager.js` (now wired into the real approval-gate flow — see \"Approval gates\" below, supersedes the reject.js note that follows), `security/*`, `agent-tester/*`, `telemetry.js` (single-file, distinct from the `lib/telemetry/` dir), `teams-notifier.js` (didn't exist upstream, written fresh from setup-observability.js's usage contract), `knowledge/*` (11 files), `fingerprint.js`, `diagnostics/*`, `grooming/*`, `regression-builder.js` + its skill dir, `agor/*`, `workflow-dsl/*`, `git/azure-devops-client.js`, `prd-quality-scorer.js`, `jira/ticket-scorer.js`, `jira/jira-integration.js` (rewritten against this project's env-var auth model, old version was unportable), `utils/cli-flags.js`, `mcp-plugin-manager.js` (cli/).\n105:**`reject.js`/`approve.js` use `lib/approval-manager.js` directly** (2026-09-21, superseding an earlier note here that said this file was intentionally left unwired): both now call `approvalManager.approvePhase(phase, reason)`/`.rejectPhase(...)`, writing the real `artifacts/approvals/<phase>-approval.json` schema — the file the router's approval gate (below) actually polls. Flag interface stayed this project's simpler positional `<ticket> <phase> [--reason] [--workspace <path>]` (no `--workspace-id`/`WorkspaceManager` lookup — that's old-project-only machinery this project never ported and doesn't need, since `--workspace` is a literal path here, not a pooled workspace id). `lib/approval-manager.js`'s own hardcoded hint text (printed while a run is waiting) was fixed to print this project's real command shape instead of the old `--workspace-id` one.\n107:**Approval gates are now wired into `forge run`** (2026-09-21): the leaner workflow-v2 rewrite done early in this migration dropped the original's human-in-the-loop pause between phases entirely — `unified-workflow-router.js`'s phase loop just ran straight through regardless of `--autonomous`. Restored: after each phase in `approvalManager.approvalGates` (intake/architect/dev-planning/dev/qa/ui-verification), unless `--autonomous`, the router calls the real `ApprovalManager.requestApproval()` — an interactive inquirer prompt (approve/reject/explore/review/exit) on a real TTY, or file-based polling on `artifacts/approvals/<phase>-approval.json` (default 5 min timeout, `FORGE_APPROVAL_TIMEOUT_MS` to override) otherwise, unblocked by `forge approve`/`forge reject`. A rejection (or timeout) stops the run and `route()` throws — `summary.rejected = {phase, reason, pending}` is also set on the (otherwise-unreachable-on-throw) summary object for callers that want it without a try/catch. Constructor-injectable via `ApprovalManagerClass` for tests — `tests/unit/workflow-v2/unified-workflow-router.test.js`'s `makeRouter()` defaults to an auto-approving fake so the other ~16 phase-loop tests don't hang on a real prompt/poll; the approval-gate-specific tests override it. Verified end-to-end (real `ApprovalManager`, fake task engine, short `FORGE_APPROVAL_TIMEOUT_MS`) — a run genuinely pauses, `forge approve <ticket> <phase> --workspace <dir>` genuinely unblocks it, an un-approved phase genuinely times out and stops the run.\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1351e78-a61e-4705-9c3e-9d357cb70796","uuid":"2413550e-5837-4e01-ae3a-c38bc1f502d9","timestamp":"2026-10-16T16:34:21.790Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"58:- **Agents**: `agents/autonomous-dev/*.md` are system-prompt files fed to the backend LLM per phase, each with a matching `<phase>.contract.json` defining expected I/O artifact schema. Phases communicate **only via file artifacts** under `artifacts/{phase}/{ticketId}/` — no in-process message passing.\n65:- Artifacts always at `artifacts/{phase}/{ticketId}/`, never nested inside phase path; check for existing artifacts before regenerating (resume support).\n89:Separately, `forge validate` and `forge init` aren't broken — they don't exist yet (not in `cli/index.js`'s `commands` map, no `cli/validate.js`/`cli/init.js`). Real migration work, already tracked below. `forg