cised yet. Design doc should list these as stable exports later PRDs will import, not inline route logic. |\n| FR-23 | Permission Helpers | `src/server/auth/permissions.ts`: `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()`, `requireRole(...roles)`. No generic `can()` — explicit role checks is the sanctioned pattern, which the design doc should state plainly so later PRDs don't reintroduce a generic ACL layer. `requireUser`/`requireRole` are what FR-11's middleware perimeter is backed up by at the page/handler level. |\n| FR-24 | Audit Logging | `audit()` in `src/server/audit.ts` — single insert-only helper, captures IP from `x-forwarded-for`, never throws, never logs secrets. Every audit call site in this PRD (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19) goes through this one function; design doc should pin its signature once since it's the shared chokepoint. |\n| FR-25 | App Shell Integration | Top-bar user menu: real name/role badge/avatar initials, \"Sign out\" → `signOut()` → `/login`. Replaces PRD-00's placeholder menu slot (per `requirements-analysis-notes.md` history, FR-33 of abcd-1) — first real consumer of FR-9's session shape. |\n| FR-26 | App Shell Integration | `navigation.ts` role filtering switches from PRD-00's placeholder role to the real session role (FR-9). One-line dependency change, but the design doc should confirm `navigation.ts`'s existing filter signature already accepts a `Role` value so this is a wiring change, not a rewrite. |\n| FR-27 | Notifications Stub | `sendAuthEmail()` logs recipient/subject/link via `logger.info` instead of sending mail, pending PRD-04. Both FR-14 (invite... actually invite link is logged at seed time per FR-28) and FR-18 (reset email) call through this one stub — design doc should give it a stable signature now so PRD-04 can swap the implementation without touching call sites. |\n| FR-28 | Seed Data | Seed six ACTIVE users + one INVITED user (shared password `SchoolHub123!`), log the invited user's invite link. Depends on FR-1 (schema), FR-22 (`createUser`/`createInviteToken` — seed script should call the service functions, not duplicate their logic), and FR-27 (invite link logging path). |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Credentials Auth Core / Data Model | Hash-only token storage (no raw tokens persisted), constant-time comparison, HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Lax cookies, Auth.js-supplied CSRF. Cross-cutting constraint on FR-1 (`AuthToken` schema), FR-12/18 (token lookup must hash-then-compare, not store-then-compare), and the Auth.js config backing FR-9/10. |\n| NFR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | Dummy bcrypt compare on nonexistent-user path so timing doesn't leak user existence — a specific branch inside FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should call this out as a required no-op compare, not an optimization to skip. |\n| NFR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in p95 < 1s at bcrypt cost 12 — bounds how much extra work `authorize()` (FR-3) can do per attempt (e.g. rate-limit check, lockout read, dummy-compare branch all have to fit inside that budget). |\n| NFR-4 | Design System (MUI-only) | `aria-live=\"polite\"` error announcements + focus-to-first-invalid-field on submit — applies to every form in this PRD (FR-2 login, FR-13 invite-accept, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password`, FR-20 change-password). One shared form-error pattern, five call sites. |\n| NFR-5 | Lint/CI Gate | MUI-only constraint, enforced by the existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` rule from PRD-00 (abcd-1 FR-19) — no new lint rule needed here, just compliance; design doc should note this phase adds zero new UI libraries. |\n| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (password policy, token hash/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl guard) + Vitest integration against a test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) + Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed-login messaging, forgot-to-reset). Defines the testability bar for every pure function named above (FR-3, FR-6, FR-7, FR-15, FR-18) — they should be exported as standalone functions, not buried in route handlers, specifically so these tests can call them directly. |\n| NFR-7 | Service Layer / Permission Helpers | Brownfield discipline: reuse PRD-00's models/services/components/helpers, never re-scaffold, duplicate, or rename. Directly constrains FR-22/FR-23/FR-24's naming and location choices — they must slot into PRD-00's existing `src/server/` conventions rather than introduce a parallel structure. |\n| NFR-8 | Lint/CI Gate | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green, add only the tests this PRD lists, no scope creep into later-PRD behavior (e.g. don't build the generic `can()` helper FR-23 explicitly excludes, don't implement real email sending that FR-27 explicitly defers). |\n\n## Cross-cutting observations for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **Three shared chokepoints recur across almost every FR**: `authorize()` (FR-3) for sign-in, `audit()` (FR-24) for every audited action (FR-8/14/19), and the password-policy module (FR-15) for every password-setting path (FR-14/19/20). Design these three as named, independently-testable modules first — nearly everything else in this PRD calls into one of them.\n- **`AuthToken` has two producers with different rules**: invite tokens (FR-12, 7-day expiry) and reset tokens (FR-18, 60-min expiry, and uniquely \"invalidate older unused tokens for that user\" on each new issuance). Model both through the same table/enum (FR-1) but don't let the invalidate-on-reissue rule leak into the invite path — it's reset-specific per the PRD text.\n- **`passwordChangedAt` is the single mechanism tying together session invalidation (FR-10), change-password (FR-20), and reset-password (FR-19)** — one timestamp field, three write sites, one read site (the `jwt` callback). Worth a dedicated subsection in system-design.md's data-flow so the three writers don't drift.\n- **Rate limiting has two distinct key shapes on the same underlying module (FR-6)**: per-IP only (sign-in, FR-6) vs per-email-and-per-IP (forgot-password, FR-17). The module's exported API should accept a configurable key, not hardcode \"IP.\"\n- **No blockers were raised by intake** (`handoff-to-architect.json` blockers: none, 98% confidence) — nothing additional to surface in system-design.md's Overview beyond that confidence figure.\n- **This phase explicitly does not build**: a generic `can()`/ACL helper (FR-23 rules it out), real outbound email (FR-27 defers to PRD-04). Treat any such code found while implementing as scope creep per NFR-8.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":74,"newStart":1,"newLines":67,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-1","+# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-2"," "," Supporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 requirements, 100% confidence, no blockers).","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (36 requirements — 28 FR + 8 NFR,","+98% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`)."," ","-Architectural concern buckets used below: **Scaffold/Tooling**, **Data Model**,","-**Server Infra** (DB/env/logging), **API Layer**, **Design System /","-Component Library**, **App Shell / Layout**, **Routing / Pages**, **Auth","-Boundary (future)**, **Lint/CI Gate**, **Test Harness**.","+Architectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Credentials","+Auth Core**, **Rate Limiting**, **Session / Route Guard**, **Invite Flow**,","+**Password Policy**, **Password Reset Flow**, **Change Password**, **Service","+Layer**, **Permission Helpers**, **Audit Logging**, **App Shell Integration**,","+**Notifications Stub**, **Seed Data**, **Lint/CI Gate**, **Design System","+(MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**."," "," ## Functional Requirements"," "," | ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |"," |----|------------------------|-------|","-| FR-1 | Scaffold/Tooling | Next.js 14 App Router + React 18 + TS strict + ESLint/Prettier baseline. Drives every other decision's toolchain compatibility (e.g. MUI v9 + React 18 pairing). |","-| FR-2 | Scaffold/Tooling | npm script surface is a contract other phases (dev-planning, CI) will invoke by name — must exist verbatim. |","-| FR-3 | Scaffold/Tooling | `tsconfig.json` path alias; affects every import statement generated in later phases. |","-| FR-4 | Server Infra | `docker-compose.yml` Postgres 16 service — local dev dependency, no app code, but gates NFR-7 (5-minute fresh-clone bring-up). |","-| FR-5 | Server Infra | `.env.example` is the single source of truth for required env vars; must stay in sync with FR-6's Zod schema. |","-| FR-6 | Server Infra | `src/lib/env.ts` — startup validation boundary. Fail-fast module, imported by `src/server/db.ts` and any server entrypoint. |","-| FR-7 | Data Model | `prisma/schema.prisma`, singleton `SchoolSettings` model. First schema entity; later PRDs will add models but this phase only needs this one. |","-| FR-8 | Server Infra | `src/server/db.ts` — Prisma client singleton pattern (globalThis cache) to survive Next.js dev hot-reload. Shared by every API route. |","-| FR-9 | Data Model | `prisma/seed.ts` idempotent seed — upsert semantics on `SchoolSettings`, run by `db:seed` script from FR-2. |","-| FR-10 | API Layer | `ok()` helper — standard success envelope `{ data }` used by every GET/POST handler. |","-| FR-11 | API Layer | `paginated()` helper — list-response envelope; depends on FR-14's pagination parsing shape. |","-| FR-12 | API Layer | `apiError()` + status-code mapping table — standard error envelope, consumed by `withHandler` (FR-13) and by client-side error handling conventions later phases will rely on. |","-| FR-13 | API Layer | `withHandler(fn)` — centralized error-boundary wrapper for route handlers (Zod → VALIDATION_ERROR, AppError → mapped status, Prisma P2002/P2025 → CONFLICT/NOT_FOUND, else INTERNAL). This is the one chokepoint every API route must go through — key reuse surface for api-contracts phase. |","-| FR-14 | API Layer | `parsePagination()` — query-param parsing/clamping, shared by all list endpoints. |","-| FR-15 | API Layer | `parseBody()` / `parseQuery()` — Zod-backed request parsing, paired with `withHandler`'s ZodError branch. |","-| FR-16 | API Layer | `GET /api/health` — first concrete endpoint; exercises DB connectivity (`SELECT 1`) with a 2000ms timeout and the `ok`/error envelope from FR-10/12. This is the only endpoint `arch-api-contracts` has a hard requirement to define. |","-| FR-17 | Design System | MUI v9 package set + React 18 override (`react-is@18.3.1`) — dependency/version decision, belongs in tech-stack ADR, not design doc. |","-| FR-18 | Design System | `theme.ts` (cssVariables, light/dark colorSchemes) + root layout provider stack (`AppRouterCacheProvider` + `ThemeProvider` + `CssBaseline` + `LocalizationProvider`) + `InitColorSchemeScript` + `useColorScheme()` toggle. Cross-cutting: every page renders inside this provider tree. |","-| FR-19 | Lint/CI Gate | ESLint `no-restricted-imports` banning non-MUI UI libs; build-breaking rule, ties directly to NFR-1. No Tailwind config may exist. |","-| FR-20 | Design System | `PageHeader` shared component — used by `/dashboard` (FR-34) and every future page. |","-| FR-21 | Design System | `DataTable` (MUI X DataGrid wrapper) — server-side pagination/sort/search/URL-sync; the heaviest shared component, depends on API list-response shape (FR-11/14) for `rowCount`/`total`. |","-| FR-22 | Design System | `EmptyState` shared component — used by `/dashboard` (FR-34). |","-| FR-23 | Design System | `ConfirmDialog` shared component — async confirm + pending spinner, generic destructive-action pattern for later PRDs. |","-| FR-24 | Design System | `useToast()` + `ToastProvider` — single queued Snackbar/Alert; a global provider mounted once near the root layout. |","-| FR-25 | Design System | `FormField` helpers binding React Hook Form `Controller` to MUI inputs — shared form-binding layer every future CRUD form in later PRDs will use. |","-| FR-26 | Design System | `StatCard` shared component — card/label/value/delta/icon, dashboard-oriented. |","-| FR-27 | Design System | `UserAvatar` shared component — deterministic colour from user id; no auth dependency yet, just a pure function + Avatar. |","-| FR-28 | Design System | `DateDisplay` + `formatInSchoolTz()` util (`src/lib/dates.ts`) — school-timezone-aware date formatting, depends on `SchoolSettings` (FR-7) holding the timezone. |","-| FR-29 | Design System | `LoadingSkeleton` shared component — table/card/form variants. |","-| FR-30 | App Shell / Layout | `(app)/layout.tsx` — permanent/collapsible sidebar Drawer + AppBar/Toolbar top bar; collapse state persisted to localStorage. Root authenticated-app shell. |","-| FR-31 | App Shell / Layout | Responsive breakpoint (<1024px) swaps sidebar to temporary Drawer — same shell, behavior fork on viewport, ties to NFR-4. |","-| FR-32 | App Shell / Layout | `src/config/navigation.ts` — role-filtered nav item config, active-item highlighting by path prefix. Config-driven, not hardcoded — this is the extension point later PRDs add routes to. |","-| FR-33 | App Shell / Layout | Top bar: school branding (from `SchoolSettings`), theme toggle (FR-18), notification bell placeholder, user menu placeholder. Explicitly flags Profile/Sign-out as **future auth boundary** for PRD-01/03/04 — this phase builds the slot, not the wiring. |","-| FR-34 | Routing / Pages | `/dashboard` page — `PageHeader` + `EmptyState`, first concrete page in the `(app)` route group. |","-| FR-35 | Routing / Pages | `src/config/student-tabs.ts` — empty typed extension-point array for later PRDs to register into. Config-only, no UI yet. |","-| FR-36 | App Shell / Layout | `(public)/layout.tsx` — public header/footer, `SchoolSettings`-driven contact info. Separate layout tree from `(app)` — route-group boundary. |","-| FR-37 | Routing / Pages | `/` public landing page — hero + Sign-in CTA, lives under `(public)` layout. |","-| FR-38 | Routing / Pages | `not-found.tsx` / `error.tsx` (reset()) / `global-error.tsx` — Next.js App Router convention files, app-wide error boundaries. |","-| FR-39 | Routing / Pages | `/forbidden` page — 403 UI, reserved for later PRDs' auth-boundary redirects. |","-| FR-40 | Server Infra | `src/lib/logger.ts` — structured JSON logs in prod, readable in dev. Consumed by `withHandler`'s INTERNAL-error branch (FR-13) for stack logging. |","+| FR-1 | Data Model | `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` + `Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these three tables. Foundation entity; must land before any service/route work. |","+| FR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | `/login` page, MUI-only form (Card/TextField/Button/InputAdornment+IconButton/Alert). Pure UI surface over FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should keep this a thin client wrapper around `signIn('credentials')`. |","+| FR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | `authorize()` — the single chokepoint every sign-in attempt routes through (normalize email → status/lockout checks → bcrypt compare). Depends on FR-1's `User` fields; feeds FR-4 (messaging), FR-5 (lockout), FR-8 (audit), NFR-2 (timing). This is the one function `arch-design-system` should design as a named module, not inline route code. |","+| FR-4 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in failure messaging matrix (unknown/wrong-password vs locked vs disabled) — a branch inside/alongside `authorize()`'s result, consumed by FR-2's Alert. Must stay consistent with NFR-2 (same-message branches can't differ in timing either). |","+| FR-5 | Credentials Auth Core | Lockout counter (`failedLoginCount`/`lockedUntil`) — state mutation on `User` (FR-1) triggered from within `authorize()` (FR-3). Threshold/window (5 failures / 15 min) is a named constant the design doc should surface once, not re-literal. |","+| FR-6 | Rate Limiting | In-memory sliding-window limiter, `src/server/rate-limit.ts`, explicitly exported for reuse — `arch-design-system` should treat this as a shared utility other PRDs' rate limits (e.g. FR-17's forgot-password limits) can reuse rather than re-implement. |","+| FR-7 | Credentials Auth Core | Post-sign-in redirect with same-origin `callbackUrl` validation — a small pure function (open-redirect guard); shared by FR-11's middleware-generated `callbackUrl` and FR-12/14's invite-accept redirect-to-dashboard pattern. |","+| FR-8 | Audit Logging | `auth.login.success`/`auth.login.failure`/`auth.lockout` entries — first concrete caller of FR-24's `audit()` helper; fires from inside `authorize()` (FR-3), so the design doc should clarify whether `authorize()` calls `audit()` directly or returns a result the route layer audits. |","+| FR-9 | Session / Route Guard | JWT session strategy, 8h lifetime, `jwt`/`session` callbacks carry id/role/firstName/lastName/email — this is Auth.js config, not a new module; shapes what FR-23's `getCurrentUser()` can read without a DB round-trip. |","+| FR-10 | Session / Route Guard | `passwordChangedAt`-vs-token-issue-time invalidation, throttled to once per 5 minutes in the `jwt` callback — lives in the same Auth.js config object as FR-9; ties directly to FR-20 (change-password must bump `passwordChangedAt` to actually invalidate other sessions). |","+| FR-11 | Session / Route Guard | `middleware.ts` — redirect-to-login for `(app)` pages, 401 JSON for `/api/*` except an explicit allowlist (`/api/health`, `/api/auth/*`, `src/config/public-routes.ts`). This is the perimeter every protected route sits behind; MEDIUM confidence (allowlist file doesn't exist yet) — design doc should treat `public-routes.ts` as a new config file, not assume it. |","+| FR-12 | Invite Flow | `/invite/[token]` lookup by SHA-256 hash, type/used/expiry checks (7-day) — reads `AuthToken` (FR-1); the expired/invalid branch needs its own UI state distinct from FR-4's sign-in-failure messaging. |","+| FR-13 | Invite Flow | Accept-invitation form (read-only name/email + new/confirm password) — UI surface over FR-14's submit handler, same MUI-component constraint as FR-2. |","+| FR-14 | Invite Flow | Accept-invite submit: FR-15 password-policy validation → hash → `status=ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt=now` → mark token used → sign in → redirect `/dashboard` → audit `auth.invite.accepted`. Multi-step transaction; design doc should specify this as one service-layer function (likely alongside FR-22's `users.ts`) so the steps stay atomic rather than split across the route handler. |","+| FR-15 | Password Policy | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` — length/letter+digit/not-email/not-in-common-list rules. Pure validation module with no DB/session dependency; shared by FR-14 (invite accept), FR-19 (reset), FR-20 (change-password) — three call sites, one rule set. |","+| FR-16 | Password Policy | Live password-strength checklist UI — client-side mirror of FR-15's rules; design doc should flag the risk of the client-side rule list drifting from the server-side one and specify a single shared source (e.g. export rule predicates from `auth.ts` for both server validation and client display). |","+| FR-17 | Password Reset Flow | `/forgot-password` — constant response message regardless of account existence (anti-enumeration, pairs with NFR-2), plus its own rate limits (3/email/hour, 10/IP/hour) — second consumer of FR-6's rate-limit module, different window/key shape (per-email in addition to per-IP). |","+| FR-18 | Password Reset Flow | Reset-token issuance: 32 random bytes base64url, 60-min expiry, invalidate prior unused reset tokens for the user, `sendAuthEmail(..., 'password-reset', ...)`. Second `AuthToken` producer after FR-12's invite tokens — same table, different `AuthTokenType`; \"invalidate older unused tokens\" is a stateful rule the design doc should name explicitly (e.g. a `revokeUnusedTokens(userId, type)` helper shared with FR-14's token-used marking). |","+| FR-19 | Password Reset Flow | `/reset-password/[token]` — set new hash + `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout fields, mark token used, audit `auth.password.reset`, redirect to `/login`. Reuses FR-15 (policy), and clearing lockout fields here is a detail that must stay in sync with FR-5's lockout field set. |","+| FR-20 | Change Password | `/account/security` change-password form — current-password check (field error on mismatch) + FR-15 policy on new password; success bumps `passwordChangedAt` (which is what makes FR-10's other-session invalidation actually fire) and re-issues the current session's token so the acting user isn't logged out too. |","+| FR-21 | App Shell Integration | \"Account security\" user-menu entry → `/account/security`. Small nav-config addition, same user-menu surface as FR-25. |","+| FR-22 | Service Layer | `src/server/services/users.ts`: `createUser`/`createInviteToken`/`sendInvite`/`setUserStatus`/`unlockUser`. Explicitly \"for later PRDs\" — this phase defines the module's public surface/signatures even though only `createInviteToken`-adjacent logic (FR-14/28 seeding) is exercised yet. Design doc should list these as stable exports later PRDs will import, not inline route logic. |","+| FR-23 | Permission Helpers | `src/server/auth/permissions.ts`: `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()`, `requireRole(...roles)`. No generic `can()` — explicit role checks is the sanctioned pattern, which the design doc should state plainly so later PRDs don't reintroduce a generic ACL layer. `requireUser`/`requireRole` are what FR-11's middleware perimeter is backed up by at the page/handler level. |","+| FR-24 | Audit Logging | `audit()` in `src/server/audit.ts` — single insert-only helper, captures IP from `x-forwarded-for`, never throws, never logs secrets. Every audit call site in this PRD (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19) goes through this one function; design doc should pin its signature once since it's the shared chokepoint. |","+| FR-25 | App Shell Integration | Top-bar user menu: real name/role badge/avatar initials, \"Sign out\" → `signOut()` → `/login`. Replaces PRD-00's placeholder menu slot (per `requirements-analysis-notes.md` history, FR-33 of abcd-1) — first real consumer of FR-9's session shape. |","+| FR-26 | App Shell Integration | `navigation.ts` role filtering switches from PRD-00's placeholder role to the real session role (FR-9). One-line dependency change, but the design doc should confirm `navigation.ts`'s existing filter signature already accepts a `Role` value so this is a wiring change, not a rewrite. |","+| FR-27 | Notifications Stub | `sendAuthEmail()` logs recipient/subject/link via `logger.info` instead of sending mail, pending PRD-04. Both FR-14 (invite... actually invite link is logged at seed time per FR-28) and FR-18 (reset email) call through this one stub — design doc should give it a stable signature now so PRD-04 can swap the implementation without touching call sites. |","+| FR-28 | Seed Data | Seed six ACTIVE users + one INVITED user (shared password `SchoolHub123!`), log the invited user's invite link. Depends on FR-1 (schema), FR-22 (`createUser`/`createInviteToken` — seed script should call the service functions, not duplicate their logic), and FR-27 (invite link logging path). |"," "," ## Non-Functional Requirements"," "," | ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |"," |----|------------------------|-------|","-| NFR-1 | Lint/CI Gate | MUI-only UI library constraint, enforced by the FR-19 ESLint rule; also a process constraint (MUI MCP docs lookup before using any component) that doesn't map to code but should be called out in the design doc's Overview. |","-| NFR-2 | App Shell / Layout + Design System | LCP < 2.5s on `/dashboard` — constrains theme/provider setup (FR-18) and shared component weight (avoid heavy client-side work on first paint); informs server-vs-client component split. |","-| NFR-3 | Design System | WCAG 2.1 AA across shared components + axe-core Playwright checks on `/` and `/dashboard`. Cross-cutting acceptance criterion for every component in FR-20–29. |","-| NFR-4 | App Shell / Layout | 360px–1920px responsive range, no horizontal scroll — generalizes FR-31's breakpoint fork to the whole shell and all pages. |","-| NFR-5 | Server Infra | `next.config.js` security headers (nosniff, Referrer-Policy, X-Frame-Options, CSP) — app-wide config, not component-level. |","-| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest+Testing Library (unit/component) + Playwright (e2e) covering `withHandler`, `parsePagination`, `formatInSchoolTz`, `env.ts`, `DataTable`/`ConfirmDialog`/`useToast`, the ESLint rule, and axe scenarios. Defines the test-surface boundary `arch-design-system` should make testable (pure functions, isolated handlers). |","-| NFR-7 | Scaffold/Tooling | Fresh-clone bring-up in <5 min via `docker compose up -d && npm install && npm run db:migrate && npm run db:seed && npm run dev` — validates FR-2/4/9's script wiring end-to-end; no new design element, just an acceptance gate. |","-| NFR-8 | Lint/CI Gate | `lint`/`typecheck`/`test`/`test:e2e` must all pass on fresh clone — ties FR-2's scripts to NFR-6's test harness as the CI gate. |","+| NFR-1 | Credentials Auth Core / Data Model | Hash-only token storage (no raw tokens persisted), constant-time comparison, HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Lax cookies, Auth.js-supplied CSRF. Cross-cutting constraint on FR-1 (`AuthToken` schema), FR-12/18 (token lookup must hash-then-compare, not store-then-compare), and the Auth.js config backing FR-9/10. |","+| NFR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | Dummy bcrypt compare on nonexistent-user path so timing doesn't leak user existence — a specific branch inside FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should call this out as a required no-op compare, not an optimization to skip. |","+| NFR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in p95 < 1s at bcrypt cost 12 — bounds how much extra work `authorize()` (FR-3) can do per attempt (e.g. rate-limit check, lockout read, dummy-compare branch all have to fit inside that budget). |","+| NFR-4 | Design System (MUI-only) | `aria-live=\"polite\"` error announcements + focus-to-first-invalid-field on submit — applies to every form in this PRD (FR-2 login, FR-13 invite-accept, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password`, FR-20 change-password). One shared form-error pattern, five call sites. |","+| NFR-5 | Lint/CI Gate | MUI-only constraint, enforced by the existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` rule from PRD-00 (abcd-1 FR-19) — no new lint rule needed here, just compliance; design doc should note this phase adds zero new UI libraries. |","+| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (password policy, token hash/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl guard) + Vitest integration against a test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) + Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed-login messaging, forgot-to-reset). Defines the testability bar for every pure function named above (FR-3, FR-6, FR-7, FR-15, FR-18) — they should be exported as standalone functions, not buried in route handlers, specifically so these tests can call them directly. |","+| NFR-7 | Service Layer / Permission Helpers | Brownfield discipline: reuse PRD-00's models/services/components/helpers, never re-scaffold, duplicate, or rename. Directly constrains FR-22/FR-23/FR-24's naming and location choices — they must slot into PRD-00's existing `src/server/` conventions rather than introduce a parallel structure. |","+| NFR-8 | Lint/CI Gate | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green, add only the tests this PRD lists, no scope creep into later-PRD behavior (e.g. don't build the generic `can()` helper FR-23 explicitly excludes, don't implement real email sending that FR-27 explicitly defers). |"," "," ## Cross-cutting observations for `arch-design-system`"," ","-- **Auth is explicitly out of scope** for this phase (FR-33, FR-39 both say \"for later wiring by PRD-01/03/04\"). Design the user-menu/forbidden-page slots as placeholders only — do not invent an auth system to satisfy them.","-- **`SchoolSettings` is a shared read dependency** across FR-28 (timezone), FR-33/36 (branding, contact info) — single singleton row, likely fetched once per request/layout, not re-queried per component.","-- **`withHandler` + `ok`/`paginated`/`apiError` (FR-10–15) is the one mandatory API chokepoint** — `arch-api-contracts` should route every endpoint (including `/api/health`) through it.","-- **No blockers were raised by intake** (`handoff-to-architect.json` blockers: none) — nothing additional to surface in system-design.md's Overview beyond the 100% confidence figure.","+- **Three shared chokepoints recur across almost every FR**: `authorize()` (FR-3) for sign-in, `audit()` (FR-24) for every audited action (FR-8/14/19), and the password-policy module (FR-15) for every password-setting path (FR-14/19/20). Design these three as named, independently-testable modules first — nearly everything else in this PRD calls into one of them.","+- **`AuthToken` has two producers with different rules**: invite tokens (FR-12, 7-day expiry) and reset tokens (FR-18, 60-min expiry, and uniquely \"invalidate older unused tokens for that user\" on each new issuance). Model both through the same table/enum (FR-1) but don't let the invalidate-on-reissue rule leak into the invite path — it's reset-specific per the PRD text.","+- **`passwordChangedAt` is the single mechanism tying together session invalidation (FR-10), change-password (FR-20), and reset-password (FR-19)** — one timestamp field, three write sites, one read site (the `jwt` callback). Worth a dedicated subsection in system-design.md's data-flow so the three writers don't drift.","+- **Rate limiting has two distinct key shapes on the same underlying module (FR-6)**: per-IP only (sign-in, FR-6) vs per-email-and-per-IP (forgot-password, FR-17). The module's exported API should accept a configurable key, not hardcode \"IP.\"","+- **No blockers were raised by intake** (`handoff-to-architect.json` blockers: none, 98% confidence) — nothing additional to surface in system-design.md's Overview beyond that confidence figure.","+- **This phase explicitly does not build**: a generic `can()`/ACL helper (FR-23 rules it out), real outbound email (FR-27 defers to PRD-04). Treat any such code found while implementing as scope creep per NFR-8."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-1\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 requirements, 100% confidence, no blockers).\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Scaffold/Tooling**, **Data Model**,\n**Server Infra** (DB/env/logging), **API Layer**, **Design System /\nComponent Library**, **App Shell / Layout**, **Routing / Pages**, **Auth\nBoundary (future)**, **Lint/CI Gate**, **Test Harness**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Scaffold/Tooling | Next.js 14 App Router + React 18 + TS strict + ESLint/Prettier baseline. Drives every other decision's toolchain compatibility (e.g. MUI v9 + React 18 pairing). |\n| FR-2 | Scaffold/Tooling | npm script surface is a contract other phases (dev-planning, CI) will invoke by name — must exist verbatim. |\n| FR-3 | Scaffold/Tooling | `tsconfig.json` path alias; affects every import statement generated in later phases. |\n| FR-4 | Server Infra | `docker-compose.yml` Postgres 16 service — local dev dependency, no app code, but gates NFR-7 (5-minute fresh-clone bring-up). |\n| FR-5 | Server Infra | `.env.example` is the single source of truth for required env vars; must stay in sync with FR-6's Zod schema. |\n| FR-6 | Server Infra | `src/lib/env.ts` — startup validation boundary. Fail-fast module, imported by `src/server/db.ts` and any server entrypoint. |\n| FR-7 | Data Model | `prisma/schema.prisma`, singleton `SchoolSettings` model. First schema entity; later PRDs will add models but this phase only needs this one. |\n| FR-8 | Server Infra | `src/server/db.ts` — Prisma client singleton pattern (globalThis cache) to survive Next.js dev hot-reload. Shared by every API route. |\n| FR-9 | Data Model | `prisma/seed.ts` idempotent seed — upsert semantics on `SchoolSettings`, run by `db:seed` script from FR-2. |\n| FR-10 | API Layer | `ok()` helper — standard success envelope `{ data }` used by every GET/POST handler. |\n| FR-11 | API Layer | `paginated()` helper — list-response envelope; depends on FR-14's pagination parsing shape. |\n| FR-12 | API Layer | `apiError()` + status-code mapping table — standard error envelope, consumed by `withHandler` (FR-13) and by client-side error handling conventions later phases will rely on. |\n| FR-13 | API Layer | `withHandler(fn)` — centralized error-boundary wrapper for route handlers (Zod → VALIDATION_ERROR, AppError → mapped status, Prisma P2002/P2025 → CONFLICT/NOT_FOUND, else INTERNAL). This is the one chokepoint every API route must go through — key reuse surface for api-contracts phase. |\n| FR-14 | API Layer | `parsePagination()` — query-param parsing/clamping, shared by all list endpoints. |\n| FR-15 | API Layer | `parseBody()` / `parseQuery()` — Zod-backed request parsing, paired with `withHandler`'s ZodError branch. |\n| FR-16 | API Layer | `GET /api/health` — first concrete endpoint; exercises DB connectivity (`SELECT 1`) with a 2000ms timeout and the `ok`/error envelope from FR-10/12. This is the only endpoint `arch-api-contracts` has a hard requirement to define. |\n| FR-17 | Design System | MUI v9 package set + React 18 override (`react-is@18.3.1`) — dependency/version decision, belongs in tech-stack ADR, not design doc. |\n| FR-18 | Design System | `theme.ts` (cssVariables, light/dark colorSchemes) + root layout provider stack (`AppRouterCacheProvider` + `ThemeProvider` + `CssBaseline` + `LocalizationProvider`) + `InitColorSchemeScript` + `useColorScheme()` toggle. Cross-cutting: every page renders inside this provider tree. |\n| FR-19 | Lint/CI Gate | ESLint `no-restricted-imports` banning non-MUI UI libs; build-breaking rule, ties directly to NFR-1. No Tailwind config may exist. |\n| FR-20 | Design System | `PageHeader` shared component — used by `/dashboard` (FR-34) and every future page. |\n| FR-21 | Design System | `DataTable` (MUI X DataGrid wrapper) — server-side pagination/sort/search/URL-sync; the heaviest shared component, depends on API list-response shape (FR-11/14) for `rowCount`/`total`. |\n| FR-22 | Design System | `EmptyState` shared component — used by `/dashboard` (FR-34). |\n| FR-23 | Design System | `ConfirmDialog` shared component — async confirm + pending spinner, generic destructive-action pattern for later PRDs. |\n| FR-24 | Design System | `useToast()` + `ToastProvider` — single queued Snackbar/Alert; a global provider mounted once near the root layout. |\n| FR-25 | Design System | `FormField` helpers binding React Hook Form `Controller` to MUI inputs — shared form-binding layer every future CRUD form in later PRDs will use. |\n| FR-26 | Design System | `StatCard` shared component — card/label/value/delta/icon, dashboard-oriented. |\n| FR-27 | Design System | `UserAvatar` shared component — deterministic colour from user id; no auth dependency yet, just a pure function + Avatar. |\n| FR-28 | Design System | `DateDisplay` + `formatInSchoolTz()` util (`src/lib/dates.ts`) — school-timezone-aware date formatting, depends on `SchoolSettings` (FR-7) holding the timezone. |\n| FR-29 | Design System | `LoadingSkeleton` shared component — table/card/form variants. |\n| FR-30 | App Shell / Layout | `(app)/layout.tsx` — permanent/collapsible sidebar Drawer + AppBar/Toolbar top bar; collapse state persisted to localStorage. Root authenticated-app shell. |\n| FR-31 | App Shell / Layout | Responsive breakpoint (<1024px) swaps sidebar to temporary Drawer — same shell, behavior fork on viewport, ties to NFR-4. |\n| FR-32 | App Shell / Layout | `src/config/navigation.ts` — role-filtered nav item config, active-item highlighting by path prefix. Config-driven, not hardcoded — this is the extension point later PRDs add routes to. |\n| FR-33 | App Shell / Layout | Top bar: school branding (from `SchoolSettings`), theme toggle (FR-18), notification bell placeholder, user menu placeholder. Explicitly flags Profile/Sign-out as **future auth boundary** for PRD-01/03/04 — this phase builds the slot, not the wiring. |\n| FR-34 | Routing / Pages | `/dashboard` page — `PageHeader` + `EmptyState`, first concrete page in the `(app)` route group. |\n| FR-35 | Routing / Pages | `src/config/student-tabs.ts` — empty typed extension-point array for later PRDs to register into. Config-only, no UI yet. |\n| FR-36 | App Shell / Layout | `(public)/layout.tsx` — public header/footer, `SchoolSettings`-driven contact info. Separate layout tree from `(app)` — route-group boundary. |\n| FR-37 | Routing / Pages | `/` public landing page — hero + Sign-in CTA, lives under `(public)` layout. |\n| FR-38 | Routing / Pages | `not-found.tsx` / `error.tsx` (reset()) / `global-error.tsx` — Next.js App Router convention files, app-wide error boundaries. |\n| FR-39 | Routing / Pages | `/forbidden` page — 403 UI, reserved for later PRDs' auth-boundary redirects. |\n| FR-40 | Server Infra | `src/lib/logger.ts` — structured JSON logs in prod, readable in dev. Consumed by `withHandler`'s INTERNAL-error branch (FR-13) for stack logging. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Lint/CI Gate | MUI-only UI library constraint, enforced by the FR-19 ESLint rule; also a process constraint (MUI MCP docs lookup before using any component) that doesn't map to code but should be called out in the design doc's Overview. |\n| NFR-2 | App Shell / Layout + Design System | LCP < 2.5s on `/dashboard` — constrains theme/provider setup (FR-18) and shared component weight (avoid heavy client-side work on first paint); informs server-vs-client component split. |\n| NFR-3 | Design System | WCAG 2.1 AA across shared components + axe-core Playwright checks on `/` and `/dashboard`. Cross-cutting acceptance criterion for every component in FR-20–29. |\n| NFR-4 | App Shell / Layout | 360px–1920px responsive range, no horizontal scroll — generalizes FR-31's breakpoint fork to the whole shell and all pages. |\n| NFR-5 | Server Infra | `next.config.js` security headers (nosniff, Referrer-Policy, X-Frame-Options, CSP) — app-wide config, not component-level. |\n| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest+Testing Library (unit/component) + Playwright (e2e) covering `withHandler`, `parsePagination`, `formatInSchoolTz`, `env.ts`, `DataTable`/`ConfirmDialog`/`useToast`, the ESLint rule, and axe scenarios. Defines the test-surface boundary `arch-design-system` should make testable (pure functions, isolated handlers). |\n| NFR-7 | Scaffold/Tooling | Fresh-clone bring-up in <5 min via `docker compose up -d && npm install && npm run db:migrate && npm run db:seed && npm run dev` — validates FR-2/4/9's script wiring end-to-end; no new design element, just an acceptance gate. |\n| NFR-8 | Lint/CI Gate | `lint`/`typecheck`/`test`/`test:e2e` must all pass on fresh clone — ties FR-2's scripts to NFR-6's test harness as the CI gate. |\n\n## Cross-cutting observations for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **Auth is explicitly out of scope** for this phase (FR-33, FR-39 both say \"for later wiring by PRD-01/03/04\"). Design the user-menu/forbidden-page slots as placeholders only — do not invent an auth system to satisfy them.\n- **`SchoolSettings` is a shared read dependency** across FR-28 (timezone), FR-33/36 (branding, contact info) — single singleton row, likely fetched once per request/layout, not re-queried per component.\n- **`withHandler` + `ok`/`paginated`/`apiError` (FR-10–15) is the one mandatory API chokepoint** — `arch-api-contracts` should route every endpoint (including `/api/health`) through it.\n- **No blockers were raised by intake** (`handoff-to-architect.json` blockers: none) — nothing additional to surface in system-design.md's Overview beyond the 100% confidence figure.\n","userModified":false}}
