--------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Access Control Helper | `medicalNotes` must never reach STUDENT/PARENT — stripped in the service layer (not just the client) from `GET /api/students/:id`, and excluded from CSV exports (FR-5/FR-22 export paths). A field-level redaction rule the service layer and every export path must both honor. |\n| NFR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | Sub-300ms user-list page at 5,000 users, backed by a `(lastName, firstName, email)` index. Directly constrains FR-2/FR-3's query design — pushes toward server-side pagination/filtering, not client-side. |\n| NFR-3 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import batch is all-or-rollback — reinforces FR-20's \"one transaction per batch\" requirement; no partial-success state is ever persisted. |\n| NFR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | CSV export must neutralise formula injection (leading `=`,`+`,`-`,`@` → apostrophe-prefixed) — applies to FR-5's bulk export and FR-22's error-report CSV alike; best implemented as one shared CSV-serialization helper. |\n| NFR-5 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every surface in this PRD (list, stepper form, pickers, drawer, cards) must be MUI-only (`@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`, MUI X), checked via the MUI MCP server, enforced by ESLint `no-restricted-imports`. No non-MUI component library may be introduced. |\n| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit tests (CSV row validator, admission-number generator, formula-injection escaping, `getAccessibleStudentIds` per role); Vitest integration (import rollback, last-admin guard, primary-link uniqueness); Playwright e2e (create-student-with-parent, CSV import w/ error row, parent My-children → student page). Scopes exactly what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for — no more, no less. |\n| NFR-7 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Reuse PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components, helpers — never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model. Directly constrains FR-7 (reuse `sendInvite`), FR-12 (extend, don't duplicate, the PRD-01 session check), FR-24 (extend the existing tab registry), FR-29 (reuse the existing `AuditLog` table/write path), FR-31 (reuse PRD-01 lockout fields). |\n| NFR-8 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Keep lint/typecheck/test green, add only the tests NFR-6 lists, don't expand scope, don't touch behaviour owned by later PRDs (e.g. class/section membership is PRD-05's) — bounds `arch-design-system`'s scope the same way it bounds dev's. |\n\n## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **Three chokepoints to design as named modules, not inline code**: the\n  user list/filter service (FR-2/FR-3/NFR-2), the CSV import transaction\n  (FR-19–FR-23/NFR-3), and `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` (FR-17/NFR-1).\n  Every other FR in this PRD is a thin UI or read-view wrapper around one of\n  these three, or around the family-link service (FR-15/FR-16).\n- **Reuse, don't re-derive, from PRD-00/01/02** (NFR-7): session check\n  (FR-12), invite mechanism (FR-7), lockout fields (FR-31), `AuditLog` table\n  (FR-11/FR-29), student-tabs registry (FR-24). `arch-design-system` should\n  cite the existing modules by name/path if intake's tech-stack notes\n  identify them, rather than re-specifying their behaviour.\n- **FR-31 confidence is MEDIUM** (inferred from the API table, not an\n  explicit spec sentence) — worth a one-line flag in `system-design.md`'s\n  traceability table so `dev-planning` knows to verify the exact PRD-01\n  field names before implementation.\n- **Formula-injection escaping (NFR-4) and medicalNotes redaction (NFR-1)**\n  both cut across multiple export/read paths (FR-5, FR-11, FR-22, student\n  detail reads) — design each as one shared helper applied everywhere,\n  not per-endpoint logic, to avoid an endpoint missing the rule.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":67,"newStart":1,"newLines":85,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-2","+# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-03"," "," Supporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (36 requirements — 28 FR + 8 NFR,","-98% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`).","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (39 requirements — 31 FR + 8 NFR,","+97% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is","+PRD-03 (User Management): profiles, admin user CRUD/list, CSV import,","+student/parent detail surfaces, directory pickers, audit log viewer."," ","-Architectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Credentials","-Auth Core**, **Rate Limiting**, **Session / Route Guard**, **Invite Flow**,","-**Password Policy**, **Password Reset Flow**, **Change Password**, **Service","-Layer**, **Permission Helpers**, **Audit Logging**, **App Shell Integration**,","-**Notifications Stub**, **Seed Data**, **Lint/CI Gate**, **Design System","-(MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**.","+Architectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Admin List/Filter","+Service**, **User CRUD Form Flow**, **Session Invalidation**, **Status/","+Lifecycle Guard**, **Family Linking**, **Access Control Helper**, **CSV","+Import Pipeline**, **Student Surface**, **Parent Surface**, **Self-Service","+Profile**, **Directory Picker API**, **Audit Log Viewer**, **Navigation**,","+**Design System (MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**, **Brownfield/Delivery","+Discipline**."," "," ## Functional Requirements"," "," | ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |"," |----|------------------------|-------|","-| FR-1 | Data Model | `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` + `Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these three tables. Foundation entity; must land before any service/route work. |","-| FR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | `/login` page, MUI-only form (Card/TextField/Button/InputAdornment+IconButton/Alert). Pure UI surface over FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should keep this a thin client wrapper around `signIn('credentials')`. |","-| FR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | `authorize()` — the single chokepoint every sign-in attempt routes through (normalize email → status/lockout checks → bcrypt compare). Depends on FR-1's `User` fields; feeds FR-4 (messaging), FR-5 (lockout), FR-8 (audit), NFR-2 (timing). This is the one function `arch-design-system` should design as a named module, not inline route code. |","-| FR-4 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in failure messaging matrix (unknown/wrong-password vs locked vs disabled) — a branch inside/alongside `authorize()`'s result, consumed by FR-2's Alert. Must stay consistent with NFR-2 (same-message branches can't differ in timing either). |","-| FR-5 | Credentials Auth Core | Lockout counter (`failedLoginCount`/`lockedUntil`) — state mutation on `User` (FR-1) triggered from within `authorize()` (FR-3). Threshold/window (5 failures / 15 min) is a named constant the design doc should surface once, not re-literal. |","-| FR-6 | Rate Limiting | In-memory sliding-window limiter, `src/server/rate-limit.ts`, explicitly exported for reuse — `arch-design-system` should treat this as a shared utility other PRDs' rate limits (e.g. FR-17's forgot-password limits) can reuse rather than re-implement. |","-| FR-7 | Credentials Auth Core | Post-sign-in redirect with same-origin `callbackUrl` validation — a small pure function (open-redirect guard); shared by FR-11's middleware-generated `callbackUrl` and FR-12/14's invite-accept redirect-to-dashboard pattern. |","-| FR-8 | Audit Logging | `auth.login.success`/`auth.login.failure`/`auth.lockout` entries — first concrete caller of FR-24's `audit()` helper; fires from inside `authorize()` (FR-3), so the design doc should clarify whether `authorize()` calls `audit()` directly or returns a result the route layer audits. |","-| FR-9 | Session / Route Guard | JWT session strategy, 8h lifetime, `jwt`/`session` callbacks carry id/role/firstName/lastName/email — this is Auth.js config, not a new module; shapes what FR-23's `getCurrentUser()` can read without a DB round-trip. |","-| FR-10 | Session / Route Guard | `passwordChangedAt`-vs-token-issue-time invalidation, throttled to once per 5 minutes in the `jwt` callback — lives in the same Auth.js config object as FR-9; ties directly to FR-20 (change-password must bump `passwordChangedAt` to actually invalidate other sessions). |","-| FR-11 | Session / Route Guard | `middleware.ts` — redirect-to-login for `(app)` pages, 401 JSON for `/api/*` except an explicit allowlist (`/api/health`, `/api/auth/*`, `src/config/public-routes.ts`). This is the perimeter every protected route sits behind; MEDIUM confidence (allowlist file doesn't exist yet) — design doc should treat `public-routes.ts` as a new config file, not assume it. |","-| FR-12 | Invite Flow | `/invite/[token]` lookup by SHA-256 hash, type/used/expiry checks (7-day) — reads `AuthToken` (FR-1); the expired/invalid branch needs its own UI state distinct from FR-4's sign-in-failure messaging. |","-| FR-13 | Invite Flow | Accept-invitation form (read-only name/email + new/confirm password) — UI surface over FR-14's submit handler, same MUI-component constraint as FR-2. |","-| FR-14 | Invite Flow | Accept-invite submit: FR-15 password-policy validation → hash → `status=ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt=now` → mark token used → sign in → redirect `/dashboard` → audit `auth.invite.accepted`. Multi-step transaction; design doc should specify this as one service-layer function (likely alongside FR-22's `users.ts`) so the steps stay atomic rather than split across the route handler. |","-| FR-15 | Password Policy | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` — length/letter+digit/not-email/not-in-common-list rules. Pure validation module with no DB/session dependency; shared by FR-14 (invite accept), FR-19 (reset), FR-20 (change-password) — three call sites, one rule set. |","-| FR-16 | Password Policy | Live password-strength checklist UI — client-side mirror of FR-15's rules; design doc should flag the risk of the client-side rule list drifting from the server-side one and specify a single shared source (e.g. export rule predicates from `auth.ts` for both server validation and client display). |","-| FR-17 | Password Reset Flow | `/forgot-password` — constant response message regardless of account existence (anti-enumeration, pairs with NFR-2), plus its own rate limits (3/email/hour, 10/IP/hour) — second consumer of FR-6's rate-limit module, different window/key shape (per-email in addition to per-IP). |","-| FR-18 | Password Reset Flow | Reset-token issuance: 32 random bytes base64url, 60-min expiry, invalidate prior unused reset tokens for the user, `sendAuthEmail(..., 'password-reset', ...)`. Second `AuthToken` producer after FR-12's invite tokens — same table, different `AuthTokenType`; \"invalidate older unused tokens\" is a stateful rule the design doc should name explicitly (e.g. a `revokeUnusedTokens(userId, type)` helper shared with FR-14's token-used marking). |","-| FR-19 | Password Reset Flow | `/reset-password/[token]` — set new hash + `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout fields, mark token used, audit `auth.password.reset`, redirect to `/login`. Reuses FR-15 (policy), and clearing lockout fields here is a detail that must stay in sync with FR-5's lockout field set. |","-| FR-20 | Change Password | `/account/security` change-password form — current-password check (field error on mismatch) + FR-15 policy on new password; success bumps `passwordChangedAt` (which is what makes FR-10's other-session invalidation actually fire) and re-issues the current session's token so the acting user isn't logged out too. |","-| FR-21 | App Shell Integration | \"Account security\" user-menu entry → `/account/security`. Small nav-config addition, same user-menu surface as FR-25. |","-| FR-22 | Service Layer | `src/server/services/users.ts`: `createUser`/`createInviteToken`/`sendInvite`/`setUserStatus`/`unlockUser`. Explicitly \"for later PRDs\" — this phase defines the module's public surface/signatures even though only `createInviteToken`-adjacent logic (FR-14/28 seeding) is exercised yet. Design doc should list these as stable exports later PRDs will import, not inline route logic. |","-| FR-23 | Permission Helpers | `src/server/auth/permissions.ts`: `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()`, `requireRole(...roles)`. No generic `can()` — explicit role checks is the sanctioned pattern, which the design doc should state plainly so later PRDs don't reintroduce a generic ACL layer. `requireUser`/`requireRole` are what FR-11's middleware perimeter is backed up by at the page/handler level. |","-| FR-24 | Audit Logging | `audit()` in `src/server/audit.ts` — single insert-only helper, captures IP from `x-forwarded-for`, never throws, never logs secrets. Every audit call site in this PRD (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19) goes through this one function; design doc should pin its signature once since it's the shared chokepoint. |","-| FR-25 | App Shell Integration | Top-bar user menu: real name/role badge/avatar initials, \"Sign out\" → `signOut()` → `/login`. Replaces PRD-00's placeholder menu slot (per `requirements-analysis-notes.md` history, FR-33 of abcd-1) — first real consumer of FR-9's session shape. |","-| FR-26 | App Shell Integration | `navigation.ts` role filtering switches from PRD-00's placeholder role to the real session role (FR-9). One-line dependency change, but the design doc should confirm `navigation.ts`'s existing filter signature already accepts a `Role` value so this is a wiring change, not a rewrite. |","-| FR-27 | Notifications Stub | `sendAuthEmail()` logs recipient/subject/link via `logger.info` instead of sending mail, pending PRD-04. Both FR-14 (invite... actually invite link is logged at seed time per FR-28) and FR-18 (reset email) call through this one stub — design doc should give it a stable signature now so PRD-04 can swap the implementation without touching call sites. |","-| FR-28 | Seed Data | Seed six ACTIVE users + one INVITED user (shared password `SchoolHub123!`), log the invited user's invite link. Depends on FR-1 (schema), FR-22 (`createUser`/`createInviteToken` — seed script should call the service functions, not duplicate their logic), and FR-27 (invite link logging path). |","+| FR-1 | Data Model | `StudentProfile`/`TeacherProfile`/`ParentProfile`/`ParentStudentLink` + `Gender`/`GuardianRelationship` enums, relations from `User`. Foundation entity set — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these tables; must land before any service/route work. |","+| FR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | `/admin/users` DataTable (MUI X data-grid) columns incl. role/status chips. Read surface over the list service designed for FR-3/NFR-2. |","+| FR-3 | Admin List/Filter Service | Filters (role, status, grade level, search) + archived-hidden-by-default rule. Drives the query shape the list service and its index (NFR-2) must support. |","+| FR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | Row actions (View/Edit/Resend/Unlock/Disable-Enable/Archive-Restore) — thin UI dispatch onto FR-7/FR-12/FR-13/FR-31 service calls. |","+| FR-5 | Admin List/Filter Service | Bulk actions (resend/disable/export CSV) — same service calls as FR-4 applied to a selection; export path also triggers NFR-4 (formula-injection escaping). |","+| FR-6 | User CRUD Form Flow | MUI Stepper create/edit form with role-specific fields incl. inline family linking. Single form component the service layer (create/update user) must support for all four roles. |","+| FR-7 | User CRUD Form Flow | \"Send invitation email now\" checkbox → `sendInvite` on creation. Reuses the PRD-01 invite mechanism (NFR-7 brownfield reuse). |","+| FR-8 | User CRUD Form Flow | Email-change confirmation dialog + pending invite token invalidation — a guarded mutation path, not a plain field update. |","+| FR-9 | User CRUD Form Flow | Role immutable post-creation; edit form renders it read-only — a form/service-layer invariant, not just UI. |","+| FR-10 | User CRUD Form Flow | Field validation (DOB 3–21yo, phone regex) — shared validator used by both the form and FR-20's server-side re-validation. |","+| FR-11 | Admin List/Filter Service | User detail page: profile + status + last sign-in + linked family + 20 most recent audit entries. Composes the data model (FR-1), family links (FR-15), and audit log (FR-29) into one read view. |","+| FR-12 | Session Invalidation | Disable → `status=DISABLED` + PRD-01 session check extended so sessions die within 5 minutes. Touches the existing session-validation chokepoint from PRD-01 — must extend, not duplicate (NFR-7). |","+| FR-13 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Archive → `archivedAt` + `DISABLED`, excluded from pickers app-wide, history retained. Affects every picker/query that lists users (incl. FR-28's directory picker). |","+| FR-14 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Self-disable/self-archive block + \"last active admin\" invariant. A service-layer guard checked on every disable/archive mutation, not just the UI. |","+| FR-15 | Family Linking | Parent-student links manageable from student form, parent form, or student detail \"Family\" card — one link-management service, three entry points. |","+| FR-16 | Family Linking | Max 4 parents/student; exactly one `isPrimary` link (set-one-clears-others) — a data-integrity invariant enforced in the link service/transaction, not the UI. |","+| FR-17 | Access Control Helper | `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` + `assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId)` in `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`. Shared authorization chokepoint every student-scoped read (FR-11, FR-24, FR-25, FR-26) must route through; returns `[]` for TEACHER pending PRD-05. |","+| FR-18 | CSV Import Pipeline | Downloadable CSV templates (students/teachers) — static asset/route, defines the column contract FR-19/FR-20 parse against. |","+| FR-19 | CSV Import Pipeline | Client-side parse (papaparse) into a preview DataGrid with per-row/per-cell validation status — browser-only, no server round-trip yet. |","+| FR-20 | CSV Import Pipeline | `POST /api/users/import`, batches of 200, server re-validates, one transaction per batch, per-row results. The real import boundary — ties to NFR-3 (all-or-nothing batches) and reuses FR-10's validators server-side. |","+| FR-21 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import options (invite toggle, case-insensitive grade-level match, strict date format) — parsing/matching rules inside the FR-20 service. |","+| FR-22 | CSV Import Pipeline | Post-import summary + \"Download error report\" CSV — a response-shaping concern on top of FR-20's per-row results. |","+| FR-23 | CSV Import Pipeline | Idempotent re-import: existing emails reported \"Skipped — already exists\", no duplicates — an upsert/lookup rule inside the FR-20 transaction. |","+| FR-24 | Student Surface | `/students/[studentId]` header + \"Overview\" tab registered in `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (medical notes gated to ADMIN/TEACHER — ties to NFR-1). Extends an existing tab-registry pattern (NFR-7), not a new page framework. |","+| FR-25 | Student Surface | Page access gated through `assertCanViewStudent` (FR-17) — no separate auth logic here by design. |","+| FR-26 | Parent Surface | `/my-children` (PARENT only): card list of linked children with empty state — a thin read view over FR-15's links, scoped via FR-17. |","+| FR-27 | Self-Service Profile | `/account/profile`: self name/email/role read-only, phone (+occupation/address for parents) editable; adds a user-menu entry. Separate, narrower mutation path from the admin CRUD flow (FR-6) — must not reuse the admin-only form. |","+| FR-28 | Directory Picker API | `GET /api/users/search?role=&q=` (ADMIN/TEACHER only, excludes archived) + reusable `UserPicker` (MUI Autocomplete). A shared lookup endpoint/component other PRDs will likely reuse — keep it generic, not page-specific. |","+| FR-29 | Audit Log Viewer | `/admin/audit-log`: read-only table + filters + detail Drawer with pretty-printed JSON metadata. Pure read surface over the existing PRD-01 `AuditLog` table (NFR-7 reuse, no new write path). |","+| FR-30 | Navigation | New nav entries (Users, Import users, Audit log, My children, Profile) — a config/registration change in the existing nav structure, not a new shell. |","+| FR-31 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | `POST /api/users/:id/unlock` clears `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount` from PRD-01's lockout mechanism. Lower confidence (MEDIUM, inferred) — flag for `arch-design-system` to confirm the exact field names against the PRD-01 schema before finalizing the endpoint contract. |"," "," ## Non-Functional Requirements"," "," | ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |"," |----|------------------------|-------|","-| NFR-1 | Credentials Auth Core / Data Model | Hash-only token storage (no raw tokens persisted), constant-time comparison, HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Lax cookies, Auth.js-supplied CSRF. Cross-cutting constraint on FR-1 (`AuthToken` schema), FR-12/18 (token lookup must hash-then-compare, not store-then-compare), and the Auth.js config backing FR-9/10. |","-| NFR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | Dummy bcrypt compare on nonexistent-user path so timing doesn't leak user existence — a specific branch inside FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should call this out as a required no-op compare, not an optimization to skip. |","-| NFR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in p95 < 1s at bcrypt cost 12 — bounds how much extra work `authorize()` (FR-3) can do per attempt (e.g. rate-limit check, lockout read, dummy-compare branch all have to fit inside that budget). |","-| NFR-4 | Design System (MUI-only) | `aria-live=\"polite\"` error announcements + focus-to-first-invalid-field on submit — applies to every form in this PRD (FR-2 login, FR-13 invite-accept, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password`, FR-20 change-password). One shared form-error pattern, five call sites. |","-| NFR-5 | Lint/CI Gate | MUI-only constraint, enforced by the existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` rule from PRD-00 (abcd-1 FR-19) — no new lint rule needed here, just compliance; design doc should note this phase adds zero new UI libraries. |","-| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (password policy, token hash/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl guard) + Vitest integration against a test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) + Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed-login messaging, forgot-to-reset). Defines the testability bar for every pure function named above (FR-3, FR-6, FR-7, FR-15, FR-18) — they should be exported as standalone functions, not buried in route handlers, specifically so these tests can call them directly. |","-| NFR-7 | Service Layer / Permission Helpers | Brownfield discipline: reuse PRD-00's models/services/components/helpers, never re-scaffold, duplicate, or rename. Directly constrains FR-22/FR-23/FR-24's naming and location choices — they must slot into PRD-00's existing `src/server/` conventions rather than introduce a parallel structure. |","-| NFR-8 | Lint/CI Gate | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green, add only the tests this PRD lists, no scope creep into later-PRD behavior (e.g. don't build the generic `can()` helper FR-23 explicitly excludes, don't implement real email sending that FR-27 explicitly defers). |","+| NFR-1 | Access Control Helper | `medicalNotes` must never reach STUDENT/PARENT — stripped in the service layer (not just the client) from `GET /api/students/:id`, and excluded from CSV exports (FR-5/FR-22 export paths). A field-level redaction rule the service layer and every export path must both honor. |","+| NFR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | Sub-300ms user-list page at 5,000 users, backed by a `(lastName, firstName, email)` index. Directly constrains FR-2/FR-3's query design — pushes toward server-side pagination/filtering, not client-side. |","+| NFR-3 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import batch is all-or-rollback — reinforces FR-20's \"one transaction per batch\" requirement; no partial-success state is ever persisted. |","+| NFR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | CSV export must neutralise formula injection (leading `=`,`+`,`-`,`@` → apostrophe-prefixed) — applies to FR-5's bulk export and FR-22's error-report CSV alike; best implemented as one shared CSV-serialization helper. |","+| NFR-5 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every surface in this PRD (list, stepper form, pickers, drawer, cards) must be MUI-only (`@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`, MUI X), checked via the MUI MCP server, enforced by ESLint `no-restricted-imports`. No non-MUI component library may be introduced. |","+| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit tests (CSV row validator, admission-number generator, formula-injection escaping, `getAccessibleStudentIds` per role); Vitest integration (import rollback, last-admin guard, primary-link uniqueness); Playwright e2e (create-student-with-parent, CSV import w/ error row, parent My-children → student page). Scopes exactly what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for — no more, no less. |","+| NFR-7 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Reuse PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components, helpers — never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model. Directly constrains FR-7 (reuse `sendInvite`), FR-12 (extend, don't duplicate, the PRD-01 session check), FR-24 (extend the existing tab registry), FR-29 (reuse the existing `AuditLog` table/write path), FR-31 (reuse PRD-01 lockout fields). |","+| NFR-8 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Keep lint/typecheck/test green, add only the tests NFR-6 lists, don't expand scope, don't touch behaviour owned by later PRDs (e.g. class/section membership is PRD-05's) — bounds `arch-design-system`'s scope the same way it bounds dev's. |"," ","-## Cross-cutting observations for `arch-design-system`","+## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`"," ","-- **Three shared chokepoints recur across almost every FR**: `authorize()` (FR-3) for sign-in, `audit()` (FR-24) for every audited action (FR-8/14/19), and the password-policy module (FR-15) for every password-setting path (FR-14/19/20). Design these three as named, independently-testable modules first — nearly everything else in this PRD calls into one of them.","-- **`AuthToken` has two producers with different rules**: invite tokens (FR-12, 7-day expiry) and reset tokens (FR-18, 60-min expiry, and uniquely \"invalidate older unused tokens for that user\" on each new issuance). Model both through the same table/enum (FR-1) but don't let the invalidate-on-reissue rule leak into the invite path — it's reset-specific per the PRD text.","-- **`passwordChangedAt` is the single mechanism tying together session invalidation (FR-10), change-password (FR-20), and reset-password (FR-19)** — one timestamp field, three write sites, one read site (the `jwt` callback). Worth a dedicated subsection in system-design.md's data-flow so the three writers don't drift.","-- **Rate limiting has two distinct key shapes on the same underlying module (FR-6)**: per-IP only (sign-in, FR-6) vs per-email-and-per-IP (forgot-password, FR-17). The module's exported API should accept a configurable key, not hardcode \"IP.\"","-- **No blockers were raised by intake** (`handoff-to-architect.json` blockers: none, 98% confidence) — nothing additional to surface in system-design.md's Overview beyond that confidence figure.","-- **This phase explicitly does not build**: a generic `can()`/ACL helper (FR-23 rules it out), real outbound email (FR-27 defers to PRD-04). Treat any such code found while implementing as scope creep per NFR-8.","+- **Three chokepoints to design as named modules, not inline code**: the","+  user list/filter service (FR-2/FR-3/NFR-2), the CSV import transaction","+  (FR-19–FR-23/NFR-3), and `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` (FR-17/NFR-1).","+  Every other FR in this PRD is a thin UI or read-view wrapper around one of","+  these three, or around the family-link service (FR-15/FR-16).","+- **Reuse, don't re-derive, from PRD-00/01/02** (NFR-7): session check","+  (FR-12), invite mechanism (FR-7), lockout fields (FR-31), `AuditLog` table","+  (FR-11/FR-29), student-tabs registry (FR-24). `arch-design-system` should","+  cite the existing modules by name/path if intake's tech-stack notes","+  identify them, rather than re-specifying their behaviour.","+- **FR-31 confidence is MEDIUM** (inferred from the API table, not an","+  explicit spec sentence) — worth a one-line flag in `system-design.md`'s","+  traceability table so `dev-planning` knows to verify the exact PRD-01","+  field names before implementation.","+- **Formula-injection escaping (NFR-4) and medicalNotes redaction (NFR-1)**","+  both cut across multiple export/read paths (FR-5, FR-11, FR-22, student","+  detail reads) — design each as one shared helper applied everywhere,","+  not per-endpoint logic, to avoid an endpoint missing the rule."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-2\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (36 requirements — 28 FR + 8 NFR,\n98% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`).\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Credentials\nAuth Core**, **Rate Limiting**, **Session / Route Guard**, **Invite Flow**,\n**Password Policy**, **Password Reset Flow**, **Change Password**, **Service\nLayer**, **Permission Helpers**, **Audit Logging**, **App Shell Integration**,\n**Notifications Stub**, **Seed Data**, **Lint/CI Gate**, **Design System\n(MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` + `Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these three tables. Foundation entity; must land before any service/route work. |\n| FR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | `/login` page, MUI-only form (Card/TextField/Button/InputAdornment+IconButton/Alert). Pure UI surface over FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should keep this a thin client wrapper around `signIn('credentials')`. |\n| FR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | `authorize()` — the single chokepoint every sign-in attempt routes through (normalize email → status/lockout checks → bcrypt compare). Depends on FR-1's `User` fields; feeds FR-4 (messaging), FR-5 (lockout), FR-8 (audit), NFR-2 (timing). This is the one function `arch-design-system` should design as a named module, not inline route code. |\n| FR-4 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in failure messaging matrix (unknown/wrong-password vs locked vs disabled) — a branch inside/alongside `authorize()`'s result, consumed by FR-2's Alert. Must stay consistent with NFR-2 (same-message branches can't differ in timing either). |\n| FR-5 | Credentials Auth Core | Lockout counter (`failedLoginCount`/`lockedUntil`) — state mutation on `User` (FR-1) triggered from within `authorize()` (FR-3). Threshold/window (5 failures / 15 min) is a named constant the design doc should surface once, not re-literal. |\n| FR-6 | Rate Limiting | In-memory sliding-window limiter, `src/server/rate-limit.ts`, explicitly exported for reuse — `arch-design-system` should treat this as a shared utility other PRDs' rate limits (e.g. FR-17's forgot-password limits) can reuse rather than re-implement. |\n| FR-7 | Credentials Auth Core | Post-sign-in redirect with same-origin `callbackUrl` validation — a small pure function (open-redirect guard); shared by FR-11's middleware-generated `callbackUrl` and FR-12/14's invite-accept redirect-to-dashboard pattern. |\n| FR-8 | Audit Logging | `auth.login.success`/`auth.login.failure`/`auth.lockout` entries — first concrete caller of FR-24's `audit()` helper; fires from inside `authorize()` (FR-3), so the design doc should clarify whether `authorize()` calls `audit()` directly or returns a result the route layer audits. |\n| FR-9 | Session / Route Guard | JWT session strategy, 8h lifetime, `jwt`/`session` callbacks carry id/role/firstName/lastName/email — this is Auth.js config, not a new module; shapes what FR-23's `getCurrentUser()` can read without a DB round-trip. |\n| FR-10 | Session / Route Guard | `passwordChangedAt`-vs-token-issue-time invalidation, throttled to once per 5 minutes in the `jwt` callback — lives in the same Auth.js config object as FR-9; ties directly to FR-20 (change-password must bump `passwordChangedAt` to actually invalidate other sessions). |\n| FR-11 | Session / Route Guard | `middleware.ts` — redirect-to-login for `(app)` pages, 401 JSON for `/api/*` except an explicit allowlist (`/api/health`, `/api/auth/*`, `src/config/public-routes.ts`). This is the perimeter every protected route sits behind; MEDIUM confidence (allowlist file doesn't exist yet) — design doc should treat `public-routes.ts` as a new config file, not assume it. |\n| FR-12 | Invite Flow | `/invite/[token]` lookup by SHA-256 hash, type/used/expiry checks (7-day) — reads `AuthToken` (FR-1); the expired/invalid branch needs its own UI state distinct from FR-4's sign-in-failure messaging. |\n| FR-13 | Invite Flow | Accept-invitation form (read-only name/email + new/confirm password) — UI surface over FR-14's submit handler, same MUI-component constraint as FR-2. |\n| FR-14 | Invite Flow | Accept-invite submit: FR-15 password-policy validation → hash → `status=ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt=now` → mark token used → sign in → redirect `/dashboard` → audit `auth.invite.accepted`. Multi-step transaction; design doc should specify this as one service-layer function (likely alongside FR-22's `users.ts`) so the steps stay atomic rather than split across the route handler. |\n| FR-15 | Password Policy | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` — length/letter+digit/not-email/not-in-common-list rules. Pure validation module with no DB/session dependency; shared by FR-14 (invite accept), FR-19 (reset), FR-20 (change-password) — three call sites, one rule set. |\n| FR-16 | Password Policy | Live password-strength checklist UI — client-side mirror of FR-15's rules; design doc should flag the risk of the client-side rule list drifting from the server-side one and specify a single shared source (e.g. export rule predicates from `auth.ts` for both server validation and client display). |\n| FR-17 | Password Reset Flow | `/forgot-password` — constant response message regardless of account existence (anti-enumeration, pairs with NFR-2), plus its own rate limits (3/email/hour, 10/IP/hour) — second consumer of FR-6's rate-limit module, different window/key shape (per-email in addition to per-IP). |\n| FR-18 | Password Reset Flow | Reset-token issuance: 32 random bytes base64url, 60-min expiry, invalidate prior unused reset tokens for the user, `sendAuthEmail(..., 'password-reset', ...)`. Second `AuthToken` producer after FR-12's invite tokens — same table, different `AuthTokenType`; \"invalidate older unused tokens\" is a stateful rule the design doc should name explicitly (e.g. a `revokeUnusedTokens(userId, type)` helper shared with FR-14's token-used marking). |\n| FR-19 | Password Reset Flow | `/reset-password/[token]` — set new hash + `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout fields, mark token used, audit `auth.password.reset`, redirect to `/login`. Reuses FR-15 (policy), and clearing lockout fields here is a detail that must stay in sync with FR-5's lockout field set. |\n| FR-20 | Change Password | `/account/security` change-password form — current-password check (field error on mismatch) + FR-15 policy on new password; success bumps `passwordChangedAt` (which is what makes FR-10's other-session invalidation actually fire) and re-issues the current session's token so the acting user isn't logged out too. |\n| FR-21 | App Shell Integration | \"Account security\" user-menu entry → `/account/security`. Small nav-config addition, same user-menu surface as FR-25. |\n| FR-22 | Service Layer | `src/server/services/users.ts`: `createUser`/`createInviteToken`/`sendInvite`/`setUserStatus`/`unlockUser`. Explicitly \"for later PRDs\" — this phase defines the module's public surface/signatures even though only `createInviteToken`-adjacent logic (FR-14/28 seeding) is exercised yet. Design doc should list these as stable exports later PRDs will import, not inline route logic. |\n| FR-23 | Permission Helpers | `src/server/auth/permissions.ts`: `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()`, `requireRole(...roles)`. No generic `can()` — explicit role checks is the sanctioned pattern, which the design doc should state plainly so later PRDs don't reintroduce a generic ACL layer. `requireUser`/`requireRole` are what FR-11's middleware perimeter is backed up by at the page/handler level. |\n| FR-24 | Audit Logging | `audit()` in `src/server/audit.ts` — single insert-only helper, captures IP from `x-forwarded-for`, never throws, never logs secrets. Every audit call site in this PRD (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19) goes through this one function; design doc should pin its signature once since it's the shared chokepoint. |\n| FR-25 | App Shell Integration | Top-bar user menu: real name/role badge/avatar initials, \"Sign out\" → `signOut()` → `/login`. Replaces PRD-00's placeholder menu slot (per `requirements-analysis-notes.md` history, FR-33 of abcd-1) — first real consumer of FR-9's session shape. |\n| FR-26 | App Shell Integration | `navigation.ts` role filtering switches from PRD-00's placeholder role to the real session role (FR-9). One-line dependency change, but the design doc should confirm `navigation.ts`'s existing filter signature already accepts a `Role` value so this is a wiring change, not a rewrite. |\n| FR-27 | Notifications Stub | `sendAuthEmail()` logs recipient/subject/link via `logger.info` instead of sending mail, pending PRD-04. Both FR-14 (invite... actually invite link is logged at seed time per FR-28) and FR-18 (reset email) call through this one stub — design doc should give it a stable signature now so PRD-04 can swap the implementation without touching call sites. |\n| FR-28 | Seed Data | Seed six ACTIVE users + one INVITED user (shared password `SchoolHub123!`), log the invited user's invite link. Depends on FR-1 (schema), FR-22 (`createUser`/`createInviteToken` — seed script should call the service functions, not duplicate their logic), and FR-27 (invite link logging path). |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Credentials Auth Core / Data Model | Hash-only token storage (no raw tokens persisted), constant-time comparison, HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Lax cookies, Auth.js-supplied CSRF. Cross-cutting constraint on FR-1 (`AuthToken` schema), FR-12/18 (token lookup must hash-then-compare, not store-then-compare), and the Auth.js config backing FR-9/10. |\n| NFR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | Dummy bcrypt compare on nonexistent-user path so timing doesn't leak user existence — a specific branch inside FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should call this out as a required no-op compare, not an optimization to skip. |\n| NFR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in p95 < 1s at bcrypt cost 12 — bounds how much extra work `authorize()` (FR-3) can do per attempt (e.g. rate-limit check, lockout read, dummy-compare branch all have to fit inside that budget). |\n| NFR-4 | Design System (MUI-only) | `aria-live=\"polite\"` error announcements + focus-to-first-invalid-field on submit — applies to every form in this PRD (FR-2 login, FR-13 invite-accept, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password`, FR-20 change-password). One shared form-error pattern, five call sites. |\n| NFR-5 | Lint/CI Gate | MUI-only constraint, enforced by the existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` rule from PRD-00 (abcd-1 FR-19) — no new lint rule needed here, just compliance; design doc should note this phase adds zero new UI libraries. |\n| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (password policy, token hash/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl guard) + Vitest integration against a test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) + Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed-login messaging, forgot-to-reset). Defines the testability bar for every pure function named above (FR-3, FR-6, FR-7, FR-15, FR-18) — they should be exported as standalone functions, not buried in route handlers, specifically so these tests can call them directly. |\n| NFR-7 | Service Layer / Permission Helpers | Brownfield discipline: reuse PRD-00's models/services/components/helpers, never re-scaffold, duplicate, or rename. Directly constrains FR-22/FR-23/FR-24's naming and location choices — they must slot into PRD-00's existing `src/server/` conventions rather than introduce a parallel structure. |\n| NFR-8 | Lint/CI Gate | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green, add only the tests this PRD lists, no scope creep into later-PRD behavior (e.g. don't build the generic `can()` helper FR-23 explicitly excludes, don't implement real email sending that FR-27 explicitly defers). |\n\n## Cross-cutting observations for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **Three shared chokepoints recur across almost every FR**: `authorize()` (FR-3) for sign-in, `audit()` (FR-24) for every audited action (FR-8/14/19), and the password-policy module (FR-15) for every password-setting path (FR-14/19/20). Design these three as named, independently-testable modules first — nearly everything else in this PRD calls into one of them.\n- **`AuthToken` has two producers with different rules**: invite tokens (FR-12, 7-day expiry) and reset tokens (FR-18, 60-min expiry, and uniquely \"invalidate older unused tokens for that user\" on each new issuance). Model both through the same table/enum (FR-1) but don't let the invalidate-on-reissue rule leak into the invite path — it's reset-specific per the PRD text.\n- **`passwordChangedAt` is the single mechanism tying together session invalidation (FR-10), change-password (FR-20), and reset-password (FR-19)** — one timestamp field, three write sites, one read site (the `jwt` callback). Worth a dedicated subsection in system-design.md's data-flow so the three writers don't drift.\n- **Rate limiting has two distinct key shapes on the same underlying module (FR-6)**: per-IP only (sign-in, FR-6) vs per-email-and-per-IP (forgot-password, FR-17). The module's exported API should accept a configurable key, not hardcode \"IP.\"\n- **No blockers were raised by intake** (`handoff-to-architect.json` blockers: none, 98% confidence) — nothing additional to surface in system-design.md's Overview beyond that confidence figure.\n- **This phase explicitly does not build**: a generic `can()`/ACL helper (FR-23 rules it out), real outbound email (FR-27 defers to PRD-04). Treat any such code found while implementing as scope creep per NFR-8.\n","userModified":false}}
