{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015uUVgYxh845HVK4eZQ8fbh","type":"tool_result","content":"=== requirements-analysis-notes.md ===\n# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-03\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (39 requirements — 31 FR + 8 NFR,\n97% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is\nPRD-03 (User Management): profiles, admin user CRUD/list, CSV import,\nstudent/parent detail surfaces, directory pickers, audit log viewer.\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Admin List/Filter\nService**, **User CRUD Form Flow**, **Session Invalidation**, **Status/\nLifecycle Guard**, **Family Linking**, **Access Control Helper**, **CSV\nImport Pipeline**, **Student Surface**, **Parent Surface**, **Self-Service\nProfile**, **Directory Picker API**, **Audit Log Viewer**, **Navigation**,\n**Design System (MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**, **Brownfield/Delivery\nDiscipline**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `StudentProfile`/`TeacherProfile`/`ParentProfile`/`ParentStudentLink` + `Gender`/`GuardianRelationship` enums, relations from `User`. Foundation entity set — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these tables; must land before any service/route work. |\n| FR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | `/admin/users` DataTable (MUI X data-grid) columns incl. role/status chips. Read surface over the list service designed for FR-3/NFR-2. |\n| FR-3 | Admin List/Filter Service | Filters (role, status, grade level, search) + archived-hidden-by-default rule. Drives the query shape the list service and its index (NFR-2) must support. |\n| FR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | Row actions (View/Edit/Resend/Unlock/Disable-Enable/Archive-Restore) — thin UI dispatch onto FR-7/FR-12/FR-13/FR-31 service calls. |\n| FR-5 | Admin List/Filter Service | Bulk actions (resend/disable/export CSV) — same service calls as FR-4 applied to a selection; export path also triggers NFR-4 (formula-injection escaping). |\n| FR-6 | User CRUD Form Flow | MUI Stepper create/edit form with role-specific fields incl. inline family linking. Single form component the service layer (create/update user) must support for all four roles. |\n| FR-7 | User CRUD Form Flow | \"Send invitation email now\" checkbox → `sendInvite` on creation. Reuses the PRD-01 invite mechanism (NFR-7 brownfield reuse). |\n| FR-8 | User CRUD Form Flow | Email-change confirmation dialog + pending invite token invalidation — a guarded mutation path, not a plain field update. |\n| FR-9 | User CRUD Form Flow | Role immutable post-creation; edit form renders it read-only — a form/service-layer invariant, not just UI. |\n| FR-10 | User CRUD Form Flow | Field validation (DOB 3–21yo, phone regex) — shared validator used by both the form and FR-20's server-side re-validation. |\n| FR-11 | Admin List/Filter Service | User detail page: profile + status + last sign-in + linked family + 20 most recent audit entries. Composes the data model (FR-1), family links (FR-15), and audit log (FR-29) into one read view. |\n| FR-12 | Session Invalidation | Disable → `status=DISABLED` + PRD-01 session check extended so sessions die within 5 minutes. Touches the existing session-validation chokepoint from PRD-01 — must extend, not duplicate (NFR-7). |\n| FR-13 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Archive → `archivedAt` + `DISABLED`, excluded from pickers app-wide, history retained. Affects every picker/query that lists users (incl. FR-28's directory picker). |\n| FR-14 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Self-disable/self-archive block + \"last active admin\" invariant. A service-layer guard checked on every disable/archive mutation, not just the UI. |\n| FR-15 | Family Linking | Parent-student links manageable from student form, parent form, or student detail \"Family\" card — one link-management service, three entry points. |\n| FR-16 | Family Linking | Max 4 parents/student; exactly one `isPrimary` link (set-one-clears-others) — a data-integrity invariant enforced in the link service/transaction, not the UI. |\n| FR-17 | Access Control Helper | `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` + `assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId)` in `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`. Shared authorization chokepoint every student-scoped read (FR-11, FR-24, FR-25, FR-26) must route through; returns `[]` for TEACHER pending PRD-05. |\n| FR-18 | CSV Import Pipeline | Downloadable CSV templates (students/teachers) — static asset/route, defines the column contract FR-19/FR-20 parse against. |\n| FR-19 | CSV Import Pipeline | Client-side parse (papaparse) into a preview DataGrid with per-row/per-cell validation status — browser-only, no server round-trip yet. |\n| FR-20 | CSV Import Pipeline | `POST /api/users/import`, batches of 200, server re-validates, one transaction per batch, per-row results. The real import boundary — ties to NFR-3 (all-or-nothing batches) and reuses FR-10's validators server-side. |\n| FR-21 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import options (invite toggle, case-insensitive grade-level match, strict date format) — parsing/matching rules inside the FR-20 service. |\n| FR-22 | CSV Import Pipeline | Post-import summary + \"Download error report\" CSV — a response-shaping concern on top of FR-20's per-row results. |\n| FR-23 | CSV Import Pipeline | Idempotent re-import: existing emails reported \"Skipped — already exists\", no duplicates — an upsert/lookup rule inside the FR-20 transaction. |\n| FR-24 | Student Surface | `/students/[studentId]` header + \"Overview\" tab registered in `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (medical notes gated to ADMIN/TEACHER — ties to NFR-1). Extends an existing tab-registry pattern (NFR-7), not a new page framework. |\n| FR-25 | Student Surface | Page access gated through `assertCanViewStudent` (FR-17) — no separate auth logic here by design. |\n| FR-26 | Parent Surface | `/my-children` (PARENT only): card list of linked children with empty state — a thin read view over FR-15's links, scoped via FR-17. |\n| FR-27 | Self-Service Profile | `/account/profile`: self name/email/role read-only, phone (+occupation/address for parents) editable; adds a user-menu entry. Separate, narrower mutation path from the admin CRUD flow (FR-6) — must not reuse the admin-only form. |\n| FR-28 | Directory Picker API | `GET /api/users/search?role=&q=` (ADMIN/TEACHER only, excludes archived) + reusable `UserPicker` (MUI Autocomplete). A shared lookup endpoint/component other PRDs will likely reuse — keep it generic, not page-specific. |\n| FR-29 | Audit Log Viewer | `/admin/audit-log`: read-only table + filters + detail Drawer with pretty-printed JSON metadata. Pure read surface over the existing PRD-01 `AuditLog` table (NFR-7 reuse, no new write path). |\n| FR-30 | Navigation | New nav entries (Users, Import users, Audit log, My children, Profile) — a config/registration change in the existing nav structure, not a new shell. |\n| FR-31 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | `POST /api/users/:id/unlock` clears `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount` from PRD-01's lockout mechanism. Lower confidence (MEDIUM, inferred) — flag for `arch-design-system` to confirm the exact field names against the PRD-01 schema before finalizing the endpoint contract. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Access Control Helper | `medicalNotes` must never reach STUDENT/PARENT — stripped in the service layer (not just the client) from `GET /api/students/:id`, and excluded from CSV exports (FR-5/FR-22 export paths). A field-level redaction rule the service layer and every export path must both honor. |\n| NFR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | Sub-300ms user-list page at 5,000 users, backed by a `(lastName, firstName, email)` index. Directly constrains FR-2/FR-3's query design — pushes toward server-side pagination/filtering, not client-side. |\n| NFR-3 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import batch is all-or-rollback — reinforces FR-20's \"one transaction per batch\" requirement; no partial-success state is ever persisted. |\n| NFR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | CSV export must neutralise formula injection (leading `=`,`+`,`-`,`@` → apostrophe-prefixed) — applies to FR-5's bulk export and FR-22's error-report CSV alike; best implemented as one shared CSV-serialization helper. |\n| NFR-5 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every surface in this PRD (list, stepper form, pickers, drawer, cards) must be MUI-only (`@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`, MUI X), checked via the MUI MCP server, enforced by ESLint `no-restricted-imports`. No non-MUI component library may be introduced. |\n| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit tests (CSV row validator, admission-number generator, formula-injection escaping, `getAccessibleStudentIds` per role); Vitest integration (import rollback, last-admin guard, primary-link uniqueness); Playwright e2e (create-student-with-parent, CSV import w/ error row, parent My-children → student page). Scopes exactly what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for — no more, no less. |\n| NFR-7 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Reuse PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components, helpers — never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model. Directly constrains FR-7 (reuse `sendInvite`), FR-12 (extend, don't duplicate, the PRD-01 session check), FR-24 (extend the existing tab registry), FR-29 (reuse the existing `AuditLog` table/write path), FR-31 (reuse PRD-01 lockout fields). |\n| NFR-8 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Keep lint/typecheck/test green, add only the tests NFR-6 lists, don't expand scope, don't touch behaviour owned by later PRDs (e.g. class/section membership is PRD-05's) — bounds `arch-design-system`'s scope the same way it bounds dev's. |\n\n## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **Three chokepoints to design as named modules, not inline code**: the\n  user list/filter service (FR-2/FR-3/NFR-2), the CSV import transaction\n  (FR-19–FR-23/NFR-3), and `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` (FR-17/NFR-1).\n  Every other FR in this PRD is a thin UI or read-view wrapper around one of\n  these three, or around the family-link service (FR-15/FR-16).\n- **Reuse, don't re-derive, from PRD-00/01/02** (NFR-7): session check\n  (FR-12), invite mechanism (FR-7), lockout fields (FR-31), `AuditLog` table\n  (FR-11/FR-29), student-tabs registry (FR-24). `arch-design-system` should\n  cite the existing modules by name/path if intake's tech-stack notes\n  identify them, rather than re-specifying their behaviour.\n- **FR-31 confidence is MEDIUM** (inferred from the API table, not an\n  explicit spec sentence) — worth a one-line flag in `system-design.md`'s\n  traceability table so `dev-planning` knows to verify the exact PRD-01\n  field names before implementation.\n- **Formula-injection escaping (NFR-4) and medicalNotes redaction (NFR-1)**\n  both cut across multiple export/read paths (FR-5, FR-11, FR-22, student\n  detail reads) — design each as one shared helper applied everywhere,\n  not per-endpoint logic, to avoid an endpoint missing the rule.\n=== handoff-to-architect.json ===\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T15:06:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 34,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}\n=== ls -la architect ===\ntotal 136\ndrwxr-xr-x  8 ikramaansari  staff    256 Oct 19 14:16 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  7 ikramaansari  staff    224 Oct 16 20:20 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  13890 Oct 19 14:16 api-contracts.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   1435 Oct 19 14:16 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  11089 Oct 19 14:07 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  20957 Oct 19 14:13 system-design.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   6536 Oct 19 14:07 tech-stack-decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff    378 Oct 19 14:16 threat-model-notes.json","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ae16a67-54ad-4fde-954e-30bc9953e423","uuid":"3dc99312-aed0-4228-8e5f-64e44e078cd9","timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:05:40.146Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== requirements-analysis-notes.md ===\n# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-03\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (39 requirements — 31 FR + 8 NFR,\n97% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is\nPRD-03 (User Management): profiles, admin user CRUD/list, CSV import,\nstudent/parent detail surfaces, directory pickers, audit log viewer.\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Admin List/Filter\nService**, **User CRUD Form Flow**, **Session Invalidation**, **Status/\nLifecycle Guard**, **Family Linking**, **Access Control Helper**, **CSV\nImport Pipeline**, **Student Surface**, **Parent Surface**, **Self-Service\nProfile**, **Directory Picker API**, **Audit Log Viewer**, **Navigation**,\n**Design System (MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**, **Brownfield/Delivery\nDiscipline**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `StudentProfile`/`TeacherProfile`/`ParentProfile`/`ParentStudentLink` + `Gender`/`GuardianRelationship` enums, relations from `User`. Foundation entity set — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these tables; must land before any service/route work. |\n| FR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | `/admin/users` DataTable (MUI X data-grid) columns incl. role/status chips. Read surface over the list service designed for FR-3/NFR-2. |\n| FR-3 | Admin List/Filter Service | Filters (role, status, grade level, search) + archived-hidden-by-default rule. Drives the query shape the list service and its index (NFR-2) must support. |\n| FR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | Row actions (View/Edit/Resend/Unlock/Disable-Enable/Archive-Restore) — thin UI dispatch onto FR-7/FR-12/FR-13/FR-31 service calls. |\n| FR-5 | Admin List/Filter Service | Bulk actions (resend/disable/export CSV) — same service calls as FR-4 applied to a selection; export path also triggers NFR-4 (formula-injection escaping). |\n| FR-6 | User CRUD Form Flow | MUI Stepper create/edit form with role-specific fields incl. inline family linking. Single form component the service layer (create/update user) must support for all four roles. |\n| FR-7 | User CRUD Form Flow | \"Send invitation email now\" checkbox → `sendInvite` on creation. Reuses the PRD-01 invite mechanism (NFR-7 brownfield reuse). |\n| FR-8 | User CRUD Form Flow | Email-change confirmation dialog + pending invite token invalidation — a guarded mutation path, not a plain field update. |\n| FR-9 | User CRUD Form Flow | Role immutable post-creation; edit form renders it read-only — a form/service-layer invariant, not just UI. |\n| FR-10 | User CRUD Form Flow | Field validation (DOB 3–21yo, phone regex) — shared validator used by both the form and FR-20's server-side re-validation. |\n| FR-11 | Admin List/Filter Service | User detail page: profile + status + last sign-in + linked family + 20 most recent audit entries. Composes the data model (FR-1), family links (FR-15), and audit log (FR-29) into one read view. |\n| FR-12 | Session Invalidation | Disable → `status=DISABLED` + PRD-01 session check extended so sessions die within 5 minutes. Touches the existing session-validation chokepoint from PRD-01 — must extend, not duplicate (NFR-7). |\n| FR-13 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Archive → `archivedAt` + `DISABLED`, excluded from pickers app-wide, history retained. Affects every picker/query that lists users (incl. FR-28's directory picker). |\n| FR-14 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Self-disable/self-archive block + \"last active admin\" invariant. A service-layer guard checked on every disable/archive mutation, not just the UI. |\n| FR-15 | Family Linking | Parent-student links manageable from student form, parent form, or student detail \"Family\" card — one link-management service, three entry points. |\n| FR-16 | Family Linking | Max 4 parents/student; exactly one `isPrimary` link (set-one-clears-others) — a data-integrity invariant enforced in the link service/transaction, not the UI. |\n| FR-17 | Access Control Helper | `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` + `assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId)` in `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`. Shared authorization chokepoint every student-scoped read (FR-11, FR-24, FR-25, FR-26) must route through; returns `[]` for TEACHER pending PRD-05. |\n| FR-18 | CSV Import Pipeline | Downloadable CSV templates (students/teachers) — static asset/route, defines the column contract FR-19/FR-20 parse against. |\n| FR-19 | CSV Import Pipeline | Client-side parse (papaparse) into a preview DataGrid with per-row/per-cell validation status — browser-only, no server round-trip yet. |\n| FR-20 | CSV Import Pipeline | `POST /api/users/import`, batches of 200, server re-validates, one transaction per batch, per-row results. The real import boundary — ties to NFR-3 (all-or-nothing batches) and reuses FR-10's validators server-side. |\n| FR-21 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import options (invite toggle, case-insensitive grade-level match, strict date format) — parsing/matching rules inside the FR-20 service. |\n| FR-22 | CSV Import Pipeline | Post-import summary + \"Download error report\" CSV — a response-shaping concern on top of FR-20's per-row results. |\n| FR-23 | CSV Import Pipeline | Idempotent re-import: existing emails reported \"Skipped — already exists\", no duplicates — an upsert/lookup rule inside the FR-20 transaction. |\n| FR-24 | Student Surface | `/students/[studentId]` header + \"Overview\" tab registered in `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (medical notes gated to ADMIN/TEACHER — ties to NFR-1). Extends an existing tab-registry pattern (NFR-7), not a new page framework. |\n| FR-25 | Student Surface | Page access gated through `assertCanViewStudent` (FR-17) — no separate auth logic here by design. |\n| FR-26 | Parent Surface | `/my-children` (PARENT only): card list of linked children with empty state — a thin read view over FR-15's links, scoped via FR-17. |\n| FR-27 | Self-Service Profile | `/account/profile`: self name/email/role read-only, phone (+occupation/address for parents) editable; adds a user-menu entry. Separate, narrower mutation path from the admin CRUD flow (FR-6) — must not reuse the admin-only form. |\n| FR-28 | Directory Picker API | `GET /api/users/search?role=&q=` (ADMIN/TEACHER only, excludes archived) + reusable `UserPicker` (MUI Autocomplete). A shared lookup endpoint/component other PRDs will likely reuse — keep it generic, not page-specific. |\n| FR-29 | Audit Log Viewer | `/admin/audit-log`: read-only table + filters + detail Drawer with pretty-printed JSON metadata. Pure read surface over the existing PRD-01 `AuditLog` table (NFR-7 reuse, no new write path). |\n| FR-30 | Navigation | New nav entries (Users, Import users, Audit log, My children, Profile) — a config/registration change in the existing nav structure, not a new shell. |\n| FR-31 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | `POST /api/users/:id/unlock` clears `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount` from PRD-01's lockout mechanism. Lower confidence (MEDIUM, inferred) — flag for `arch-design-system` to confirm the exact field names against the PRD-01 schema before finalizing the endpoint contract. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Access Control Helper | `medicalNotes` must never reach STUDENT/PARENT — stripped in the service layer (not just the client) from `GET /api/students/:id`, and excluded from CSV exports (FR-5/FR-22 export paths). A field-level redaction rule the service layer and every export path must both honor. |\n| NFR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | Sub-300ms user-list page at 5,000 users, backed by a `(lastName, firstName, email)` index. Directly constrains FR-2/FR-3's query design — pushes toward server-side pagination/filtering, not client-side. |\n| NFR-3 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import batch is all-or-rollback — reinforces FR-20's \"one transaction per batch\" requirement; no partial-success state is ever persisted. |\n| NFR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | CSV export must neutralise formula injection (leading `=`,`+`,`-`,`@` → apostrophe-prefixed) — applies to FR-5's bulk export and FR-22's error-report CSV alike; best implemented as one shared CSV-serialization helper. |\n| NFR-5 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every surface in this PRD (list, stepper form, pickers, drawer, cards) must be MUI-only (`@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`, MUI X), checked via the MUI MCP server, enforced by ESLint `no-restricted-imports`. No non-MUI component library may be introduced. |\n| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit tests (CSV row validator, admission-number generator, formula-injection escaping, `getAccessibleStudentIds` per role); Vitest integration (import rollback, last-admin guard, primary-link uniqueness); Playwright e2e (create-student-with-parent, CSV import w/ error row, parent My-children → student page). Scopes exactly what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for — no more, no less. |\n| NFR-7 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Reuse PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components, helpers — never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model. Directly constrains FR-7 (reuse `sendInvite`), FR-12 (extend, don't duplicate, the PRD-01 session check), FR-24 (extend the existing tab registry), FR-29 (reuse the existing `AuditLog` table/write path), FR-31 (reuse PRD-01 lockout fields). |\n| NFR-8 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Keep lint/typecheck/test green, add only the tests NFR-6 lists, don't expand scope, don't touch behaviour owned by later PRDs (e.g. class/section membership is PRD-05's) — bounds `arch-design-system`'s scope the same way it bounds dev's. |\n\n## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **Three chokepoints to design as named modules, not inline code**: the\n  user list/filter service (FR-2/FR-3/NFR-2), the CSV import transaction\n  (FR-19–FR-23/NFR-3), and `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` (FR-17/NFR-1).\n  Every other FR in this PRD is a thin UI or read-view wrapper around one of\n  these three, or around the family-link service (FR-15/FR-16).\n- **Reuse, don't re-derive, from PRD-00/01/02** (NFR-7): session check\n  (FR-12), invite mechanism (FR-7), lockout fields (FR-31), `AuditLog` table\n  (FR-11/FR-29), student-tabs registry (FR-24). `arch-design-system` should\n  cite the existing modules by name/path if intake's tech-stack notes\n  identify them, rather than re-specifying their behaviour.\n- **FR-31 confidence is MEDIUM** (inferred from the API table, not an\n  explicit spec sentence) — worth a one-line flag in `system-design.md`'s\n  traceability table so `dev-planning` knows to verify the exact PRD-01\n  field names before implementation.\n- **Formula-injection escaping (NFR-4) and medicalNotes redaction (NFR-1)**\n  both cut across multiple export/read paths (FR-5, FR-11, FR-22, student\n  detail reads) — design each as one shared helper applied everywhere,\n  not per-endpoint logic, to avoid an endpoint missing the rule.\n=== handoff-to-architect.json ===\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T15:06:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 34,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}\n=== ls -la architect ===\ntotal 136\ndrwxr-xr-x  8 ikramaansari  staff    256 Oct 19 14:16 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  7 ikram