r-row read/unread toggle. Same list/read API surface as FR-15's popover — one list service backing both, not two. |\n| FR-17 | Retention Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` — delete notifications older than 180 days, invoked once/day from the dispatcher endpoint with in-memory last-run tracking (re-run after restart is acceptable). Piggybacks on FR-12's dispatch endpoint call site — not a separate cron/queue. |\n| FR-18 | Preferences UI | `/account/notifications`: MUI Table grouped by category, In-app/Email switches per visible type, mandatory in-app types shown disabled with tooltip. Pure read+toggle view over FR-2 (registry) + FR-1 (`NotificationPreference` rows). |\n| FR-19 | Preferences API | `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` saves immediately, optimistic UI + rollback on error — client-side concern (FR-18) paired with the server validation in FR-22. |\n| FR-20 | Admin Email Log | `/admin/email-log`: table (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/last-error), status filter, \"Retry now\" (resets attempts=0/status=PENDING/nextAttemptAt=now), \"Send test notification to me\" (calls `notify({ type: 'system.test', ... })`). Read/write surface directly over `EmailOutbox` (FR-1) and `notify()` (FR-4); \"Retry now\" must use the same reset semantics FR-11's backoff expects. |\n| FR-21 | REST API Surface | Full endpoint list (notifications CRUD-ish, preferences, dispatch, admin email-log, admin test) — to be finalized verbatim by `arch-api-contracts`, following PRD-00's envelope/pagination/error-code conventions. Every endpoint here must map 1:1 to a service already named in FR-4/FR-10/FR-16/FR-18/FR-20; no net-new business logic at the route layer. |\n| FR-22 | Preferences API | `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` must reject `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types — server-side enforcement mirroring FR-18's disabled-switch UI (defense in depth, UI alone is not sufficient). |\n| FR-23 | Navigation | Sidebar nav entries for notifications page (+ admin email-log) in `src/config/navigation.ts`, following the existing `NavItem` convention (currently only Dashboard). MEDIUM confidence on exact entries — flag for `arch-design-system` to confirm naming/grouping. |\n| FR-24 | Data Model (seed) | Seed 3 `system.test` `Notification` rows (1 read, 2 unread) for two existing seeded users. Pure seed-data task, depends on FR-1's schema and FR-2's registry key existing first. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every visible surface (bell, popover, notifications page, preferences table, admin log) MUI-only, checked via MUI MCP, no banned libraries; email templates explicitly exempt (use `@react-email/components` instead). A lint-enforced boundary (`no-restricted-imports`) `arch-design-system` should scope per-directory so the email-template exemption doesn't leak into app UI code. |\n| NFR-2 | Notification Service | `notify()` for 1,000 recipients < 2s — directly validates FR-5's ≤3-round-trip batching design; a perf budget the service implementation must be benchmarked against. |\n| NFR-3 | Notifications Page / Bell | `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` < 50ms, backed by a `(userId, readAt, createdAt)` index — constrains the `Notification` table's indexing (FR-1) and the query shape of FR-14/FR-21's unread-count endpoint. |\n| NFR-4 | Email Dispatcher | No double-send under concurrent dispatchers (`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`) + stuck-`SENDING`-for->10min recovery back to PENDING. A concurrency-safety invariant on FR-10's dispatch query — the stuck-row recovery is an extra step FR-10/FR-12 must schedule (e.g. at the top of each dispatch call), not an afterthought. |\n| NFR-5 | Security/Access Control | Notification `link` must be a validated relative path (`/`-prefixed, open-redirect prevention); email HTML must escape all user-provided text. Two related but distinct sanitization rules — one on `notify()`'s input (FR-4), one on the email template renderer (FR-7). |\n| NFR-6 | Email Templates | Every outbound email has HTML + plain-text parts + a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing at the preferences page. Extends FR-7's base layout contract and FR-10's send step (header must be set at send time, not template-render time). |\n| NFR-7 | Security/Access Control | Server-side `requireUser()`/`requireRole()` on every route: own-notifications-only for user routes, ADMIN-only for email-log routes, `CRON_SECRET` bearer for the internal dispatch route. A per-route authorization matrix `arch-api-contracts` must encode explicitly against FR-21's endpoint list — hiding UI (FR-20's admin page) is never sufficient. |\n| NFR-8 | Email Dispatcher | Dispatch without correct `CRON_SECRET` bearer → 401 via the standard error envelope. The negative-path companion to FR-12/NFR-7's auth check on that one route. |\n| NFR-9 | Test Harness | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green; add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements. Scopes exactly what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for. |\n| NFR-10 | Scope Discipline | No SMS/push, no websockets (bell polls only), no digest emails — bounds `arch-design-system`'s design the same way it bounds dev's; don't let FR-14's polling design grow into a push/websocket architecture. |\n\n## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **Two chokepoints to design as named, reusable modules, not inline\n  code**: `notify()` (FR-3/FR-4/FR-5/FR-6, in\n  `src/server/notifications/notify.ts`) and `dispatchEmails()` (FR-10/FR-11,\n  called identically by FR-12's HTTP route and worker loop). Nearly every\n  other FR is either a thin UI/read-view wrapper around these two, or a\n  template/config detail feeding them (FR-2 registry, FR-7/FR-8 templates,\n  FR-13 env config).\n- **One list/read service backs both the popover (FR-15) and the\n  `/notifications` page (FR-16)** — same pagination/filter/mark-read\n  surface, just different page sizes/UI chrome. Don't let `arch-design-system`\n  spec two separate query paths.\n- **Defense-in-depth pairs to call out explicitly in the traceability\n  table**: FR-18 (disabled switch) + FR-22 (server-side reject) for\n  mandatory in-app types; FR-9's brownfield stub swap must preserve\n  whatever call signature PRD-01's `sendInvite()` callers already use\n  (NFR-7-style reuse discipline, even though this PRD's NFRs don't\n  re-state it — see FR-9's own source note referencing\n  `src/server/services/users.ts:385-390`).\n- **NFR-4's stuck-`SENDING` recovery and FR-17's daily purge both need a\n  concrete trigger point** — likely \"run at the top of `dispatchEmails()`\n  calls, gated by in-memory last-run timestamps,\" per FR-17's own\n  acceptance of restart-driven re-runs. `arch-design-system` should pick\n  one scheduling mechanism for both rather than inventing two.\n- **FR-23's exact nav entries are MEDIUM confidence** (inferred from\n  layout conventions, not spelled out) — flag in `system-design.md`'s\n  traceability table so `dev-planning` knows the nav copy/grouping needs a\n  final decision, not just an endpoint contract.\n- **NFR-1's MUI-only rule needs a directory boundary, not a blanket rule**:\n  `src/server/email/templates/**` is explicitly exempt (React Email\n  components) while every app-UI path (bell, popover, `/notifications`,\n  `/account/notifications`, `/admin/email-log`) is MUI-only. Worth a single\n  sentence in `system-design.md`'s Overview so the ESLint config `dev`\n  writes doesn't over- or under-scope the `no-restricted-imports` exemption.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
