e()` stub (`src/server/services/users.ts:385-390`, currently log-only) with `sendAuthEmail()` that enqueues via `EmailOutbox`. A brownfield swap at an existing call site — must not change the stub's call signature/contract that PRD-01 callers depend on. |\n| FR-10 | Email Dispatcher | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` — `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` select of due PENDING rows, mark SENDING, send via Nodemailer, mark SENT or schedule retry. The other central chokepoint; must be designed as one module both the HTTP route (FR-12) and the worker loop (FR-12) call. |\n| FR-11 | Email Dispatcher | Retry backoff schedule (1/5/15/60/240 min across 5 attempts, FAILED after 5th) — state-machine detail inside FR-10's dispatch logic, also what FR-20's \"Retry now\" action resets. |\n| FR-12 | Email Dispatcher | Two callers of `dispatchEmails`: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (bearer `CRON_SECRET`, ties to NFR-8) and `npm run worker:email` (15s loop, local/simple deployments). Same underlying function, two thin entry points — do not fork the dispatch logic between them. |\n| FR-13 | Email Transport Config | Env vars (`SMTP_*`, `EMAIL_FROM`, `CRON_SECRET`, `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` smtp\\|console). Console transport is a dev-mode Nodemailer transport swap, not a separate code path through the dispatcher. |\n| FR-14 | Bell/Popover UI | Live unread-count bell (MUI IconButton + Badge) replacing the static badge at `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx:141`; polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30s, paused on `visibilitychange` hidden, \"9+\" cap. Read-only UI over FR-21's unread-count endpoint; polling pause/resume is a client-side concern only. |\n| FR-15 | Bell/Popover UI | Popover with 10 most recent notifications (unread styling, 2-line clamp, relative time), click marks-read + navigates; footer \"Mark all as read\" / \"View all\". Composes FR-21's list/read endpoints; no new server logic beyond what FR-16/FR-21 already define. |\n| FR-16 | Notifications Page | `/notifications`: pagin