 same pagination/filter/mark-read\n  surface, just different page sizes/UI chrome. Don't let `arch-design-system`\n  spec two separate query paths.\n- **Defense-in-depth pairs to call out explicitly in the traceability\n  table**: FR-18 (disabled switch) + FR-22 (server-side reject) for\n  mandatory in-app types; FR-9's brownfield stub swap must preserve\n  whatever call signature PRD-01's `sendInvite()` callers already use\n  (NFR-7-style reuse discipline, even though this PRD's NFRs don't\n  re-state it — see FR-9's own source note referencing\n  `src/server/services/users.ts:385-390`).\n- **NFR-4's stuck-`SENDING` recovery and FR-17's daily purge both need a\n  concrete trigger point** — likely \"run at the top of `dispatchEmails()`\n  calls, gated by in-memory last-run timestamps,\" per FR-17's own\n  acceptance of restart-driven re-runs. `arch-design-system` should pick\n  one scheduling mechanism for both rather than inventing two.\n- **FR-23's exact nav entries are MEDIUM confidence** (inferred from\n  layout conventions, not spelled out) — flag in `system-design.md`'s\n  traceability table so `dev-planning` knows the nav copy/grouping needs a\n  final decision, not just an endpoint contract.\n- **NFR-1's MUI-only rule needs a directory boundary, not a blanket rule**:\n  `src/server/email/templates/**` is explicitly exempt (React Email\n  components) while every app-UI path (bell, popover, `/notifications`,\n  `/account/notifications`, `/admin/email-log`) is MUI-only. Worth a single\n  sentence in `system-design.md`'s Overview so the ESLint config `dev`\n  writes doesn't over- or under-scope the `no-restricted-imports` exemption.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":85,"newStart":1,"newLines":96,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-03","+# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-04"," "," Supporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (39 requirements — 31 FR + 8 NFR,","-97% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is","-PRD-03 (User Management): profiles, admin user CRUD/list, CSV import,","-student/parent detail surfaces, directory pickers, audit log viewer.","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 requirements — 24 FR + 10","+NFR, 97% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is","+the Notifications & Email PRD: notification data model/registry, `notify()`","+service, email templates, an email outbox + dispatcher worker, bell/popover","+UI, the `/notifications` page, preferences UI, and the admin email log."," ","-Architectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Admin List/Filter","-Service**, **User CRUD Form Flow**, **Session Invalidation**, **Status/","-Lifecycle Guard**, **Family Linking**, **Access Control Helper**, **CSV","-Import Pipeline**, **Student Surface**, **Parent Surface**, **Self-Service","-Profile**, **Directory Picker API**, **Audit Log Viewer**, **Navigation**,","-**Design System (MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**, **Brownfield/Delivery","-Discipline**.","+Architectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Notification","+Type Registry**, **Notification Service**, **Family Fan-out Helper**, **Email","+Templates**, **Auth Email Integration**, **Email Dispatcher**, **Email","+Transport Config**, **Bell/Popover UI**, **Notifications Page**, **Retention","+Job**, **Preferences UI**, **Preferences API**, **Admin Email Log**, **REST","+API Surface**, **Navigation**, **Design System (MUI-only)**, **Security/","+Access Control**, **Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**."," "," ## Functional Requirements"," "," | ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |"," |----|------------------------|-------|","-| FR-1 | Data Model | `StudentProfile`/`TeacherProfile`/`ParentProfile`/`ParentStudentLink` + `Gender`/`GuardianRelationship` enums, relations from `User`. Foundation entity set — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these tables; must land before any service/route work. |","-| FR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | `/admin/users` DataTable (MUI X data-grid) columns incl. role/status chips. Read surface over the list service designed for FR-3/NFR-2. |","-| FR-3 | Admin List/Filter Service | Filters (role, status, grade level, search) + archived-hidden-by-default rule. Drives the query shape the list service and its index (NFR-2) must support. |","-| FR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | Row actions (View/Edit/Resend/Unlock/Disable-Enable/Archive-Restore) — thin UI dispatch onto FR-7/FR-12/FR-13/FR-31 service calls. |","-| FR-5 | Admin List/Filter Service | Bulk actions (resend/disable/export CSV) — same service calls as FR-4 applied to a selection; export path also triggers NFR-4 (formula-injection escaping). |","-| FR-6 | User CRUD Form Flow | MUI Stepper create/edit form with role-specific fields incl. inline family linking. Single form component the service layer (create/update user) must support for all four roles. |","-| FR-7 | User CRUD Form Flow | \"Send invitation email now\" checkbox → `sendInvite` on creation. Reuses the PRD-01 invite mechanism (NFR-7 brownfield reuse). |","-| FR-8 | User CRUD Form Flow | Email-change confirmation dialog + pending invite token invalidation — a guarded mutation path, not a plain field update. |","-| FR-9 | User CRUD Form Flow | Role immutable post-creation; edit form renders it read-only — a form/service-layer invariant, not just UI. |","-| FR-10 | User CRUD Form Flow | Field validation (DOB 3–21yo, phone regex) — shared validator used by both the form and FR-20's server-side re-validation. |","-| FR-11 | Admin List/Filter Service | User detail page: profile + status + last sign-in + linked family + 20 most recent audit entries. Composes the data model (FR-1), family links (FR-15), and audit log (FR-29) into one read view. |","-| FR-12 | Session Invalidation | Disable → `status=DISABLED` + PRD-01 session check extended so sessions die within 5 minutes. Touches the existing session-validation chokepoint from PRD-01 — must extend, not duplicate (NFR-7). |","-| FR-13 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Archive → `archivedAt` + `DISABLED`, excluded from pickers app-wide, history retained. Affects every picker/query that lists users (incl. FR-28's directory picker). |","-| FR-14 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Self-disable/self-archive block + \"last active admin\" invariant. A service-layer guard checked on every disable/archive mutation, not just the UI. |","-| FR-15 | Family Linking | Parent-student links manageable from student form, parent form, or student detail \"Family\" card — one link-management service, three entry points. |","-| FR-16 | Family Linking | Max 4 parents/student; exactly one `isPrimary` link (set-one-clears-others) — a data-integrity invariant enforced in the link service/transaction, not the UI. |","-| FR-17 | Access Control Helper | `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` + `assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId)` in `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`. Shared authorization chokepoint every student-scoped read (FR-11, FR-24, FR-25, FR-26) must route through; returns `[]` for TEACHER pending PRD-05. |","-| FR-18 | CSV Import Pipeline | Downloadable CSV templates (students/teachers) — static asset/route, defines the column contract FR-19/FR-20 parse against. |","-| FR-19 | CSV Import Pipeline | Client-side parse (papaparse) into a preview DataGrid with per-row/per-cell validation status — browser-only, no server round-trip yet. |","-| FR-20 | CSV Import Pipeline | `POST /api/users/import`, batches of 200, server re-validates, one transaction per batch, per-row results. The real import boundary — ties to NFR-3 (all-or-nothing batches) and reuses FR-10's validators server-side. |","-| FR-21 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import options (invite toggle, case-insensitive grade-level match, strict date format) — parsing/matching rules inside the FR-20 service. |","-| FR-22 | CSV Import Pipeline | Post-import summary + \"Download error report\" CSV — a response-shaping concern on top of FR-20's per-row results. |","-| FR-23 | CSV Import Pipeline | Idempotent re-import: existing emails reported \"Skipped — already exists\", no duplicates — an upsert/lookup rule inside the FR-20 transaction. |","-| FR-24 | Student Surface | `/students/[studentId]` header + \"Overview\" tab registered in `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (medical notes gated to ADMIN/TEACHER — ties to NFR-1). Extends an existing tab-registry pattern (NFR-7), not a new page framework. |","-| FR-25 | Student Surface | Page access gated through `assertCanViewStudent` (FR-17) — no separate auth logic here by design. |","-| FR-26 | Parent Surface | `/my-children` (PARENT only): card list of linked children with empty state — a thin read view over FR-15's links, scoped via FR-17. |","-| FR-27 | Self-Service Profile | `/account/profile`: self name/email/role read-only, phone (+occupation/address for parents) editable; adds a user-menu entry. Separate, narrower mutation path from the admin CRUD flow (FR-6) — must not reuse the admin-only form. |","-| FR-28 | Directory Picker API | `GET /api/users/search?role=&q=` (ADMIN/TEACHER only, excludes archived) + reusable `UserPicker` (MUI Autocomplete). A shared lookup endpoint/component other PRDs will likely reuse — keep it generic, not page-specific. |","-| FR-29 | Audit Log Viewer | `/admin/audit-log`: read-only table + filters + detail Drawer with pretty-printed JSON metadata. Pure read surface over the existing PRD-01 `AuditLog` table (NFR-7 reuse, no new write path). |","-| FR-30 | Navigation | New nav entries (Users, Import users, Audit log, My children, Profile) — a config/registration change in the existing nav structure, not a new shell. |","-| FR-31 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | `POST /api/users/:id/unlock` clears `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount` from PRD-01's lockout mechanism. Lower confidence (MEDIUM, inferred) — flag for `arch-design-system` to confirm the exact field names against the PRD-01 schema before finalizing the endpoint contract. |","+| FR-1 | Data Model | `Notification`, `NotificationPreference`, `EmailOutbox` + `EmailStatus` enum. Foundation tables — every other FR reads or writes one of these; must land before any service/route work. |","+| FR-2 | Notification Type Registry | Typed registry at `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles), seeded with `account.invite`, `account.password_reset`, `system.test`. Single source of truth the service layer (FR-4), preferences UI (FR-18), and compile-time typing (FR-3) all key off. |","+| FR-3 | Notification Service | `notify()` must reject unknown type keys at compile time (TS literal/union against the registry) — a typing constraint on FR-4's signature, not a runtime check. |","+| FR-4 | Notification Service | Core `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })` — skips archived/disabled users, resolves preferences (falling back to registry defaults), writes `Notification` rows and `EmailOutbox` rows as applicable. The central chokepoint everything else (FR-6, FR-9, FR-20, FR-24) calls into. |","+| FR-5 | Notification Service | Batching via `createMany` (≤3 round-trips per 1,000 users each for notifications/emails) + never-throw-to-caller (log failures) + \"call after your own transaction commits\" contract. Directly drives NFR-2's latency budget and the service's error-handling shape. |","+| FR-6 | Family Fan-out Helper | `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` — expands student → student + linked parents, deduped, for later PRDs to reuse. Thin wrapper over FR-4 plus whatever parent-link read path already exists (brownfield reuse, not a new link model). |","+| FR-7 | Email Templates | `@react-email/components` templates under `src/server/email/templates/`, rendered to HTML + plain text, sharing a base layout (header/content/footer, preferences link, disclosure sentence). One shared layout component — avoid three independently-styled templates. |","+| FR-8 | Email Templates | Concrete templates: invite, password-reset, generic-notification, each with their specified fields/CTA. Three thin wrappers over FR-7's base layout. |","+| FR-9 | Auth Email Integration | Replace the PRD-01 `sendInvite()` stub (`src/server/services/users.ts:385-390`, currently log-only) with `sendAuthEmail()` that enqueues via `EmailOutbox`. A brownfield swap at an existing call site — must not change the stub's call signature/contract that PRD-01 callers depend on. |","+| FR-10 | Email Dispatcher | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` — `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` select of due PENDING rows, mark SENDING, send via Nodemailer, mark SENT or schedule retry. The other central chokepoint; must be designed as one module both the HTTP route (FR-12) and the worker loop (FR-12) call. |","+| FR-11 | Email Dispatcher | Retry backoff schedule (1/5/15/60/240 min across 5 attempts, FAILED after 5th) — state-machine detail inside FR-10's dispatch logic, also what FR-20's \"Retry now\" action resets. |","+| FR-12 | Email Dispatcher | Two callers of `dispatchEmails`: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (bearer `CRON_SECRET`, ties to NFR-8) and `npm run worker:email` (15s loop, local/simple deployments). Same underlying function, two thin entry points — do not fork the dispatch logic between them. |","+| FR-13 | Email Transport Config | Env vars (`SMTP_*`, `EMAIL_FROM`, `CRON_SECRET`, `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` smtp\\|console). Console transport is a dev-mode Nodemailer transport swap, not a separate code path through the dispatcher. |","+| FR-14 | Bell/Popover UI | Live unread-count bell (MUI IconButton + Badge) replacing the static badge at `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx:141`; polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30s, paused on `visibilitychange` hidden, \"9+\" cap. Read-only UI over FR-21's unread-count endpoint; polling pause/resume is a client-side concern only. |","+| FR-15 | Bell/Popover UI | Popover with 10 most recent notifications (unread styling, 2-line clamp, relative time), click marks-read + navigates; footer \"Mark all as read\" / \"View all\". Composes FR-21's list/read endpoints; no new server logic beyond what FR-16/FR-21 already define. |","+| FR-16 | Notifications Page | `/notifications`: paginated (20/page), All/Unread tabs, category filter, bulk mark-all-read, per-row read/unread toggle. Same list/read API surface as FR-15's popover — one list service backing both, not two. |","+| FR-17 | Retention Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` — delete notifications older than 180 days, invoked once/day from the dispatcher endpoint with in-memory last-run tracking (re-run after restart is acceptable). Piggybacks on FR-12's dispatch endpoint call site — not a separate cron/queue. |","+| FR-18 | Preferences UI | `/account/notifications`: MUI Table grouped by category, In-app/Email switches per visible type, mandatory in-app types shown disabled with tooltip. Pure read+toggle view over FR-2 (registry) + FR-1 (`NotificationPreference` rows). |","+| FR-19 | Preferences API | `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` saves immediately, optimistic UI + rollback on error — client-side concern (FR-18) paired with the server validation in FR-22. |","+| FR-20 | Admin Email Log | `/admin/email-log`: table (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/last-error), status filter, \"Retry now\" (resets attempts=0/status=PENDING/nextAttemptAt=now), \"Send test notification to me\" (calls `notify({ type: 'system.test', ... })`). Read/write surface directly over `EmailOutbox` (FR-1) and `notify()` (FR-4); \"Retry now\" must use the same reset semantics FR-11's backoff expects. |","+| FR-21 | REST API Surface | Full endpoint list (notifications CRUD-ish, preferences, dispatch, admin email-log, admin test) — to be finalized verbatim by `arch-api-contracts`, following PRD-00's envelope/pagination/error-code conventions. Every endpoint here must map 1:1 to a service already named in FR-4/FR-10/FR-16/FR-18/FR-20; no net-new business logic at the route layer. |","+| FR-22 | Preferences API | `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` must reject `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types — server-side enforcement mirroring FR-18's disabled-switch UI (defense in depth, UI alone is not sufficient). |","+| FR-23 | Navigation | Sidebar nav entries for notifications page (+ admin email-log) in `src/config/navigation.ts`, following the existing `NavItem` convention (currently only Dashboard). MEDIUM confidence on exact entries — flag for `arch-design-system` to confirm naming/grouping. |","+| FR-24 | Data Model (seed) | Seed 3 `system.test` `Notification` rows (1 read, 2 unread) for two existing seeded users. Pure seed-data task, depends on FR-1's schema and FR-2's registry key existing first. |"," "," ## Non-Functional Requirements"," "," | ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |"," |----|------------------------|-------|","-| NFR-1 | Access Control Helper | `medicalNotes` must never reach STUDENT/PARENT — stripped in the service layer (not just the client) from `GET /api/students/:id`, and excluded from CSV exports (FR-5/FR-22 export paths). A field-level redaction rule the service layer and every export path must both honor. |","-| NFR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | Sub-300ms user-list page at 5,000 users, backed by a `(lastName, firstName, email)` index. Directly constrains FR-2/FR-3's query design — pushes toward server-side pagination/filtering, not client-side. |","-| NFR-3 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import batch is all-or-rollback — reinforces FR-20's \"one transaction per batch\" requirement; no partial-success state is ever persisted. |","-| NFR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | CSV export must neutralise formula injection (leading `=`,`+`,`-`,`@` → apostrophe-prefixed) — applies to FR-5's bulk export and FR-22's error-report CSV alike; best implemented as one shared CSV-serialization helper. |","-| NFR-5 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every surface in this PRD (list, stepper form, pickers, drawer, cards) must be MUI-only (`@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`, MUI X), checked via the MUI MCP server, enforced by ESLint `no-restricted-imports`. No non-MUI component library may be introduced. |","-| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit tests (CSV row validator, admission-number generator, formula-injection escaping, `getAccessibleStudentIds` per role); Vitest integration (import rollback, last-admin guard, primary-link uniqueness); Playwright e2e (create-student-with-parent, CSV import w/ error row, parent My-children → student page). Scopes exactly what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for — no more, no less. |","-| NFR-7 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Reuse PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components, helpers — never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model. Directly constrains FR-7 (reuse `sendInvite`), FR-12 (extend, don't duplicate, the PRD-01 session check), FR-24 (extend the existing tab registry), FR-29 (reuse the existing `AuditLog` table/write path), FR-31 (reuse PRD-01 lockout fields). |","-| NFR-8 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Keep lint/typecheck/test green, add only the tests NFR-6 lists, don't expand scope, don't touch behaviour owned by later PRDs (e.g. class/section membership is PRD-05's) — bounds `arch-design-system`'s scope the same way it bounds dev's. |","+| NFR-1 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every visible surface (bell, popover, notifications page, preferences table, admin log) MUI-only, checked via MUI MCP, no banned libraries; email templates explicitly exempt (use `@react-email/components` instead). A lint-enforced boundary (`no-restricted-imports`) `arch-design-system` should scope per-directory so the email-template exemption doesn't leak into app UI code. |","+| NFR-2 | Notification Service | `notify()` for 1,000 recipients < 2s — directly validates FR-5's ≤3-round-trip batching design; a perf budget the service implementation must be benchmarked against. |","+| NFR-3 | Notifications Page / Bell | `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` < 50ms, backed by a `(userId, readAt, createdAt)` index — constrains the `Notification` table's indexing (FR-1) and the query shape of FR-14/FR-21's unread-count endpoint. |","+| NFR-4 | Email Dispatcher | No double-send under concurrent dispatchers (`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`) + stuck-`SENDING`-for->10min recovery back to PENDING. A concurrency-safety invariant on FR-10's dispatch query — the stuck-row recovery is an extra step FR-10/FR-12 must schedule (e.g. at the top of each dispatch call), not an afterthought. |","+| NFR-5 | Security/Access Control | Notification `link` must be a validated relative path (`/`-prefixed, open-redirect prevention); email HTML must escape all user-provided text. Two related but distinct sanitization rules — one on `notify()`'s input (FR-4), one on the email template renderer (FR-7). |","+| NFR-6 | Email Templates | Every outbound email has HTML + plain-text parts + a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing at the preferences page. Extends FR-7's base layout contract and FR-10's send step (header must be set at send time, not template-render time). |","+| NFR-7 | Security/Access Control | Server-side `requireUser()`/`requireRole()` on every route: own-notifications-only for user routes, ADMIN-only for email-log routes, `CRON_SECRET` bearer for the internal dispatch route. A per-route authorization matrix `arch-api-contracts` must encode explicitly against FR-21's endpoint list — hiding UI (FR-20's admin page) is never sufficient. |","+| NFR-8 | Email Dispatcher | Dispatch without correct `CRON_SECRET` bearer → 401 via the standard error envelope. The negative-path companion to FR-12/NFR-7's auth check on that one route. |","+| NFR-9 | Test Harness | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green; add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements. Scopes exactly what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for. |","+| NFR-10 | Scope Discipline | No SMS/push, no websockets (bell polls only), no digest emails — bounds `arch-design-system`'s design the same way it bounds dev's; don't let FR-14's polling design grow into a push/websocket architecture. |"," "," ## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`"," ","-- **Three chokepoints to design as named modules, not inline code**: the","-  user list/filter service (FR-2/FR-3/NFR-2), the CSV import transaction","-  (FR-19–FR-23/NFR-3), and `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` (FR-17/NFR-1).","-  Every other FR in this PRD is a thin UI or read-view wrapper around one of","-  these three, or around the family-link service (FR-15/FR-16).","-- **Reuse, don't re-derive, from PRD-00/01/02** (NFR-7): session check","-  (FR-12), invite mechanism (FR-7), lockout fields (FR-31), `AuditLog` table","-  (FR-11/FR-29), student-tabs registry (FR-24). `arch-design-system` should","-  cite the existing modules by name/path if intake's tech-stack notes","-  identify them, rather than re-specifying their behaviour.","-- **FR-31 confidence is MEDIUM** (inferred from the API table, not an","-  explicit spec sentence) — worth a one-line flag in `system-design.md`'s","-  traceability table so `dev-planning` knows to verify the exact PRD-01","-  field names before implementation.","-- **Formula-injection escaping (NFR-4) and medicalNotes redaction (NFR-1)**","-  both cut across multiple export/read paths (FR-5, FR-11, FR-22, student","-  detail reads) — design each as one shared helper applied everywhere,","-  not per-endpoint logic, to avoid an endpoint missing the rule.","+- **Two chokepoints to design as named, reusable modules, not inline","+  code**: `notify()` (FR-3/FR-4/FR-5/FR-6, in","+  `src/server/notifications/notify.ts`) and `dispatchEmails()` (FR-10/FR-11,","+  called identically by FR-12's HTTP route and worker loop). Nearly every","+  other FR is either a thin UI/read-view wrapper around these two, or a","+  template/config detail feeding them (FR-2 registry, FR-7/FR-8 templates,","+  FR-13 env config).","+- **One list/read service backs both the popover (FR-15) and the","+  `/notifications` page (FR-16)** — same pagination/filter/mark-read","+  surface, just different page sizes/UI chrome. Don't let `arch-design-system`","+  spec two separate query paths.","+- **Defense-in-depth pairs to call out explicitly in the traceability","+  table**: FR-18 (disabled switch) + FR-22 (server-side reject) for","+  mandatory in-app types; FR-9's brownfield stub swap must preserve","+  whatever call signature PRD-01's `sendInvite()` callers already use","+  (NFR-7-style reuse discipline, even though this PRD's NFRs don't","+  re-state it — see FR-9's own source note referencing","+  `src/server/services/users.ts:385-390`).","+- **NFR-4's stuck-`SENDING` recovery and FR-17's daily purge both need a","+  concrete trigger point** — likely \"run at the top of `dispatchEmails()`","+  calls, gated by in-memory last-run timestamps,\" per FR-17's own","+  acceptance of restart-driven re-runs. `arch-design-system` should pick","+  one scheduling mechanism for both rather than inventing two.","+- **FR-23's exact nav entries are MEDIUM confidence** (inferred from","+  layout conventions, not spelled out) — flag in `system-design.md`'s","+  traceability table so `dev-planning` knows the nav copy/grouping needs a","+  final decision, not just an endpoint contract.","+- **NFR-1's MUI-only rule needs a directory boundary, not a blanket rule**:","+  `src/server/email/templates/**` is explicitly exempt (React Email","+  components) while every app-UI path (bell, popover, `/notifications`,","+  `/account/notifications`, `/admin/email-log`) is MUI-only. Worth a single","+  sentence in `system-design.md`'s Overview so the ESLint config `dev`","+  writes doesn't over- or under-scope the `no-restricted-imports` exemption."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-03\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (39 requirements — 31 FR + 8 NFR,\n97% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is\nPRD-03 (User Management): profiles, admin user CRUD/list, CSV import,\nstudent/parent detail surfaces, directory pickers, audit log viewer.\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Admin List/Filter\nService**, **User CRUD Form Flow**, **Session Invalidation**, **Status/\nLifecycle Guard**, **Family Linking**, **Access Control Helper**, **CSV\nImport Pipeline**, **Student Surface**, **Parent Surface**, **Self-Service\nProfile**, **Directory Picker API**, **Audit Log Viewer**, **Navigation**,\n**Design System (MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**, **Brownfield/Delivery\nDiscipline**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `StudentProfile`/`TeacherProfile`/`ParentProfile`/`ParentStudentLink` + `Gender`/`GuardianRelationship` enums, relations from `User`. Foundation entity set — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these tables; must land before any service/route work. |\n| FR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | `/admin/users` DataTable (MUI X data-grid) columns incl. role/status chips. Read surface over the list service designed for FR-3/NFR-2. |\n| FR-3 | Admin List/Filter Service | Filters (role, status, grade level, search) + archived-hidden-by-default rule. Drives the query shape the list service and its index (NFR-2) must support. |\n| FR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | Row actions (View/Edit/Resend/Unlock/Disable-Enable/Archive-Restore) — thin UI dispatch onto FR-7/FR-12/FR-13/FR-31 service calls. |\n| FR-5 | Admin List/Filter Service | Bulk actions (resend/disable/export CSV) — same service calls as FR-4 applied to a selection; export path also triggers NFR-4 (formula-injection escaping). |\n| FR-6 | User CRUD Form Flow | MUI Stepper create/edit form with role-specific fields incl. inline family linking. Single form component the service layer (create/update user) must support for all four roles. |\n| FR-7 | User CRUD Form Flow | \"Send invitation email now\" checkbox → `sendInvite` on creation. Reuses the PRD-01 invite mechanism (NFR-7 brownfield reuse). |\n| FR-8 | User CRUD Form Flow | Email-change confirmation dialog + pending invite token invalidation — a guarded mutation path, not a plain field update. |\n| FR-9 | User CRUD Form Flow | Role immutable post-creation; edit form renders it read-only — a form/service-layer invariant, not just UI. |\n| FR-10 | User CRUD Form Flow | Field validation (DOB 3–21yo, phone regex) — shared validator used by both the form and FR-20's server-side re-validation. |\n| FR-11 | Admin List/Filter Service | User detail page: profile + status + last sign-in + linked family + 20 most recent audit entries. Composes the data model (FR-1), family links (FR-15), and audit log (FR-29) into one read view. |\n| FR-12 | Session Invalidation | Disable → `status=DISABLED` + PRD-01 session check extended so sessions die within 5 minutes. Touches the existing session-validation chokepoint from PRD-01 — must extend, not duplicate (NFR-7). |\n| FR-13 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Archive → `archivedAt` + `DISABLED`, excluded from pickers app-wide, history retained. Affects every picker/query that lists users (incl. FR-28's directory picker). |\n| FR-14 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Self-disable/self-archive block + \"last active admin\" invariant. A service-layer guard checked on every disable/archive mutation, not just the UI. |\n| FR-15 | Family Linking | Parent-student links manageable from student form, parent form, or student detail \"Family\" card — one link-management service, three entry points. |\n| FR-16 | Family Linking | Max 4 parents/student; exactly one `isPrimary` link (set-one-clears-others) — a data-integrity invariant enforced in the link service/transaction, not the UI. |\n| FR-17 | Access Control Helper | `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` + `assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId)` in `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`. Shared authorization chokepoint every student-scoped read (FR-11, FR-24, FR-25, FR-26) must route through; returns `[]` for TEACHER pending PRD-05. |\n| FR-18 | CSV Import Pipeline | Downloadable CSV templates (students/teachers) — static asset/route, defines the column contract FR-19/FR-20 parse against. |\n| FR-19 | CSV Import Pipeline | Client-side parse (papaparse) into a preview DataGrid with per-row/per-cell validation status — browser-only, no server round-trip yet. |\n| FR-20 | CSV Import Pipeline | `POST /api/users/import`, batches of 200, server re-validates, one transaction per batch, per-row results. The real import boundary — ties to NFR-3 (all-or-nothing batches) and reuses FR-10's validators server-side. |\n| FR-21 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import options (invite toggle, case-insensitive grade-level match, strict date format) — parsing/matching rules inside the FR-20 service. |\n| FR-22 | CSV Import Pipeline | Post-import summary + \"Download error report\" CSV — a response-shaping concern on top of FR-20's per-row results. |\n| FR-23 | CSV Import Pipeline | Idempotent re-import: existing emails reported \"Skipped — already exists\", no duplicates — an upsert/lookup rule inside the FR-20 transaction. |\n| FR-24 | Student Surface | `/students/[studentId]` header + \"Overview\" tab registered in `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (medical notes gated to ADMIN/TEACHER — ties to NFR-1). Extends an existing tab-registry pattern (NFR-7), not a new page framework. |\n| FR-25 | Student Surface | Page access gated through `assertCanViewStudent` (FR-17) — no separate auth logic here by design. |\n| FR-26 | Parent Surface | `/my-children` (PARENT only): card list of linked children with empty state — a thin read view over FR-15's links, scoped via FR-17. |\n| FR-27 | Self-Service Profile | `/account/profile`: self name/email/role read-only, phone (+occupation/address for parents) editable; adds a user-menu entry. Separate, narrower mutation path from the admin CRUD flow (FR-6) — must not reuse the admin-only form. |\n| FR-28 | Directory Picker API | `GET /api/users/search?role=&q=` (ADMIN/TEACHER only, excludes archived) + reusable `UserPicker` (MUI Autocomplete). A shared lookup endpoint/component other PRDs will likely reuse — keep it generic, not page-specific. |\n| FR-29 | Audit Log Viewer | `/admin/audit-log`: read-only table + filters + detail Drawer with pretty-printed JSON metadata. Pure read surface over the existing PRD-01 `AuditLog` table (NFR-7 reuse, no new write path). |\n| FR-30 | Navigation | New nav entries (Users, Import users, Audit log, My children, Profile) — a config/registration change in the existing nav structure, not a new shell. |\n| FR-31 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | `POST /api/users/:id/unlock` clears `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount` from PRD-01's lockout mechanism. Lower confidence (MEDIUM, inferred) — flag for `arch-design-system` to confirm the exact field names against the PRD-01 schema before finalizing the endpoint contract. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Access Control Helper | `medicalNotes` must never reach STUDENT/PARENT — stripped in the service layer (not just the client) from `GET /api/students/:id`, and excluded from CSV exports (FR-5/FR-22 export paths). A field-level redaction rule the service layer and every export path must both honor. |\n| NFR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | Sub-300ms user-list page at 5,000 users, backed by a `(lastName, firstName, email)` index. Directly constrains FR-2/FR-3's query design — pushes toward server-side pagination/filtering, not client-side. |\n| NFR-3 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import batch is all-or-rollback — reinforces FR-20's \"one transaction per batch\" requirement; no partial-success state is ever persisted. |\n| NFR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | CSV export must neutralise formula injection (leading `=`,`+`,`-`,`@` → apostrophe-prefixed) — applies to FR-5's bulk export and FR-22's error-report CSV alike; best implemented as one shared CSV-serialization helper. |\n| NFR-5 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every surface in this PRD (list, stepper form, pickers, drawer, cards) must be MUI-only (`@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`, MUI X), checked via the MUI MCP server, enforced by ESLint `no-restricted-imports`. No non-MUI component library may be introduced. |\n| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit tests (CSV row validator, admission-number generator, formula-injection escaping, `getAccessibleStudentIds` per role); Vitest integration (import rollback, last-admin guard, primary-link uniqueness); Playwright e2e (create-student-with-parent, CSV import w/ error row, parent My-children → student page). Scopes exactly what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for — no more, no less. |\n| NFR-7 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Reuse PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components, helpers — never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model. Directly constrains FR-7 (reuse `sendInvite`), FR-12 (extend, don't duplicate, the PRD-01 session check), FR-24 (extend the existing tab registry), FR-29 (reuse the existing `AuditLog` table/write path), FR-31 (reuse PRD-01 lockout fields). |\n| NFR-8 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Keep lint/typecheck/test green, add only the tests NFR-6 lists, don't expand scope, don't touch behaviour owned by later PRDs (e.g. class/section membership is PRD-05's) — bounds `arch-design-system`'s scope the same way it bounds dev's. |\n\n## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **Three chokepoints to design as named modules, not inline code**: the\n  user list/filter service (FR-2/FR-3/NFR-2), the CSV import transaction\n  (FR-19–FR-23/NFR-3), and `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` (FR-17/NFR-1).\n  Every other FR in this PRD is a thin UI or read-view wrapper around one of\n  these three, or around the family-link service (FR-15/FR-16).\n- **Reuse, don't re-derive, from PRD-00/01/02** (NFR-7): session check\n  (FR-12), invite mechanism (FR-7), lockout fields (FR-31), `AuditLog` table\n  (FR-11/FR-29), student-tabs registry (FR-24). `arch-design-system` should\n  cite the existing modules by name/path if intake's tech-stack notes\n  identify them, rather than re-specifying their behaviour.\n- **FR-31 confidence is MEDIUM** (inferred from the API table, not an\n  explicit spec sentence) — worth a one-line flag in `system-design.md`'s\n  traceability table so `dev-planning` knows to verify the exact PRD-01\n  field names before implementation.\n- **Formula-injection escaping (NFR-4) and medicalNotes redaction (NFR-1)**\n  both cut across multiple export/read paths (FR-5, FR-11, FR-22, student\n  detail reads) — design each as one shared helper applied everywhere,\n  not per-endpoint logic, to avoid an endpoint missing the rule.\n","userModified":false}}
