{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012r99kTDgF6MegNzeXTkQRN","type":"tool_result","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-04\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 requirements — 24 FR + 10\nNFR, 97% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is\nthe Notifications & Email PRD: notification data model/registry, `notify()`\nservice, email templates, an email outbox + dispatcher worker, bell/popover\nUI, the `/notifications` page, preferences UI, and the admin email log.\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Notification\nType Registry**, **Notification Service**, **Family Fan-out Helper**, **Email\nTemplates**, **Auth Email Integration**, **Email Dispatcher**, **Email\nTransport Config**, **Bell/Popover UI**, **Notifications Page**, **Retention\nJob**, **Preferences UI**, **Preferences API**, **Admin Email Log**, **REST\nAPI Surface**, **Navigation**, **Design System (MUI-only)**, **Security/\nAccess Control**, **Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `Notification`, `NotificationPreference`, `EmailOutbox` + `EmailStatus` enum. Foundation tables — every other FR reads or writes one of these; must land before any service/route work. |\n| FR-2 | Notification Type Registry | Typed registry at `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles), seeded with `account.invite`, `account.password_reset`, `system.test`. Single source of truth the service layer (FR-4), preferences UI (FR-18), and compile-time typing (FR-3) all key off. |\n| FR-3 | Notification Service | `notify()` must reject unknown type keys at compile time (TS literal/union against the registry) — a typing constraint on FR-4's signature, not a runtime check. |\n| FR-4 | Notification Service | Core `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })` — skips archived/disabled users, resolves preferences (falling back to registry defaults), writes `Notification` rows and `EmailOutbox` rows as applicable. The central chokepoint everything else (FR-6, FR-9, FR-20, FR-24) calls into. |\n| FR-5 | Notification Service | Batching via `createMany` (≤3 round-trips per 1,000 users each for notifications/emails) + never-throw-to-caller (log failures) + \"call after your own transaction commits\" contract. Directly drives NFR-2's latency budget and the service's error-handling shape. |\n| FR-6 | Family Fan-out Helper | `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` — expands student → student + linked parents, deduped, for later PRDs to reuse. Thin wrapper over FR-4 plus whatever parent-link read path already exists (brownfield reuse, not a new link model). |\n| FR-7 | Email Templates | `@react-email/components` templates under `src/server/email/templates/`, rendered to HTML + plain text, sharing a base layout (header/content/footer, preferences link, disclosure sentence). One shared layout component — avoid three independently-styled templates. |\n| FR-8 | Email Templates | Concrete templates: invite, password-reset, generic-notification, each with their specified fields/CTA. Three thin wrappers over FR-7's base layout. |\n| FR-9 | Auth Email Integration | Replace the PRD-01 `sendInvite()` stub (`src/server/services/users.ts:385-390`, currently log-only) with `sendAuthEmail()` that enqueues via `EmailOutbox`. A brownfield swap at an existing call site — must not change the stub's call signature/contract that PRD-01 callers depend on. |\n| FR-10 | Email Dispatcher | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` — `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` select of due PENDING rows, mark SENDING, send via Nodemailer, mark SENT or schedule retry. The other central chokepoint; must be designed as one module both the HTTP route (FR-12) and the worker loop (FR-12) call. |\n| FR-11 | Email Dispatcher | Retry backoff schedule (1/5/15/60/240 min across 5 attempts, FAILED after 5th) — state-machine detail inside FR-10's dispatch logic, also what FR-20's \"Retry now\" action resets. |\n| FR-12 | Email Dispatcher | Two callers of `dispatchEmails`: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (bearer `CRON_SECRET`, ties to NFR-8) and `npm run worker:email` (15s loop, local/simple deployments). Same underlying function, two thin entry points — do not fork the dispatch logic between them. |\n| FR-13 | Email Transport Config | Env vars (`SMTP_*`, `EMAIL_FROM`, `CRON_SECRET`, `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` smtp\\|console). Console transport is a dev-mode Nodemailer transport swap, not a separate code path through the dispatcher. |\n| FR-14 | Bell/Popover UI | Live unread-count bell (MUI IconButton + Badge) replacing the static badge at `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx:141`; polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30s, paused on `visibilitychange` hidden, \"9+\" cap. Read-only UI over FR-21's unread-count endpoint; polling pause/resume is a client-side concern only. |\n| FR-15 | Bell/Popover UI | Popover with 10 most recent notifications (unread styling, 2-line clamp, relative time), click marks-read + navigates; footer \"Mark all as read\" / \"View all\". Composes FR-21's list/read endpoints; no new server logic beyond what FR-16/FR-21 already define. |\n| FR-16 | Notifications Page | `/notifications`: paginated (20/page), All/Unread tabs, category filter, bulk mark-all-read, per-row read/unread toggle. Same list/read API surface as FR-15's popover — one list service backing both, not two. |\n| FR-17 | Retention Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` — delete notifications older than 180 days, invoked once/day from the dispatcher endpoint with in-memory last-run tracking (re-run after restart is acceptable). Piggybacks on FR-12's dispatch endpoint call site — not a separate cron/queue. |\n| FR-18 | Preferences UI | `/account/notifications`: MUI Table grouped by category, In-app/Email switches per visible type, mandatory in-app types shown disabled with tooltip. Pure read+toggle view over FR-2 (registry) + FR-1 (`NotificationPreference` rows). |\n| FR-19 | Preferences API | `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` saves immediately, optimistic UI + rollback on error — client-side concern (FR-18) paired with the server validation in FR-22. |\n| FR-20 | Admin Email Log | `/admin/email-log`: table (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/last-error), status filter, \"Retry now\" (resets attempts=0/status=PENDING/nextAttemptAt=now), \"Send test notification to me\" (calls `notify({ type: 'system.test', ... })`). Read/write surface directly over `EmailOutbox` (FR-1) and `notify()` (FR-4); \"Retry now\" must use the same reset semantics FR-11's backoff expects. |\n| FR-21 | REST API Surface | Full endpoint list (notifications CRUD-ish, preferences, dispatch, admin email-log, admin test) — to be finalized verbatim by `arch-api-contracts`, following PRD-00's envelope/pagination/error-code conventions. Every endpoint here must map 1:1 to a service already named in FR-4/FR-10/FR-16/FR-18/FR-20; no net-new business logic at the route layer. |\n| FR-22 | Preferences API | `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` must reject `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types — server-side enforcement mirroring FR-18's disabled-switch UI (defense in depth, UI alone is not sufficient). |\n| FR-23 | Navigation | Sidebar nav entries for notifications page (+ admin email-log) in `src/config/navigation.ts`, following the existing `NavItem` convention (currently only Dashboard). MEDIUM confidence on exact entries — flag for `arch-design-system` to confirm naming/grouping. |\n| FR-24 | Data Model (seed) | Seed 3 `system.test` `Notification` rows (1 read, 2 unread) for two existing seeded users. Pure seed-data task, depends on FR-1's schema and FR-2's registry key existing first. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n===ticketcheck===\nartifacts/architect/api-contracts.json:  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",\nartifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json:  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",\nartifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json:  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ccabda5c-19a9-42ce-8599-287e66ed400c","uuid":"9224ebdd-1452-4520-981d-e345a51bc580","timestamp":"2026-10-20T05:58:07.575Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-04\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 requirements — 24 FR + 10\nNFR, 97% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is\nthe Notifications & Email PRD: notification data model/registry, `notify()`\nservice, email templates, an email outbox + dispatcher worker, bell/popover\nUI, the `/notifications` page, preferences UI, and the admin email log.\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Notification\nType Registry**, **Notification Service**, **Family Fan-out Helper**, **Email\nTemplates**, **Auth Email Integration**, **Email Dispatcher**, **Email\nTransport Config**, **Bell/Popover UI**, **Notifications Page**, **Retention\nJob**, **Preferences UI**, **Preferences API**, **Admin Email Log**, **REST\nAPI Surface**, **Navigation**, **Design System (MUI-only)**, **Security/\nAccess Control**, **Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `Notification`, `NotificationPreference`, `EmailOutbox` + `EmailStatus` enum. Foundation tables — every other FR reads or writes one of these; must land before any service/route work. |\n| FR-2 | Notification Type Registry | Typed registry at `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles), seeded with `account.invite`, `account.password_reset`, `system.test`. Single source of truth the service layer (FR-4), preferences UI (FR-18), and compile-time typing (FR-3) all key off. |\n| FR-3 | Notification Service | `notify()` must reject unknown type keys at compile time (TS literal/union against the registry) — a typing constraint on FR-4's signature, not a runtime check. |\n| FR-4 | Notification Service | Core `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })` — skips archived/disabled users, resolves preferences (falling back to registry defaults), writes `Notification` rows and `EmailOutbox` rows as applicable. The central chokepoint everything else (FR-6, FR-9, FR-20, FR-24) calls into. |\n| FR-5 | Notification Service | Batching via `createMany` (≤3 round-trips per 1,000 users each for notifications/emails) + never-throw-to-caller (log failures) + \"call after your own transaction commits\" contract. Directly drives NFR-2's latency budget and the service's error-handling shape. |\n| FR-6 | Family Fan-out Helper | `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` — expands student → student + linked parents, deduped, for later PRDs to reuse. Thin wrapper over FR-4 plus whatever parent-link read path already exists (brownfield reuse, not a new link model). |\n| FR-7 | Email Templates | `@react-email/components` templates under `src/server/email/templates/`, rendered to HTML + plain text, sharing a base layout (header/content/footer, preferences link, disclosure sentence). One shared layout component — avoid three independently-styled templates. |\n| FR-8 | Email Templates | Concrete templates: invite, password-reset, generic-notification, each with their specified fields/CTA. Three thin wrappers over FR-7's base layout. |\n| FR-9 | Auth Email Integration | Replace the PRD-01 `sendInvite()` stub (`src/server/services/users.ts:385-390`, currently log-only) with `sendAuthEmail()` that enqueues via `EmailOutbox`. A brownfield swap at an existing call site — must not change the stub's call signature/contract that PRD-01 callers depend on. |\n| FR-10 | Email Dispatcher | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` — `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` select of due PENDING rows, mark SENDING, send via Nodemailer, mark SENT or schedule retry. The other central chokepoint; must be designed as one module both the HTTP route (FR-12) and the worker loop (FR-12) call. |\n| FR-11 | Email Dispatcher | Retry backoff schedule (1/5/15/60/240 min across 5 attempts, FAILED after 5th) — state-machine detail inside FR-10's dispatch logic, also what FR-20's \"Retry now\" action resets. |\n| FR-12 | Email Dispatcher | Two callers of `dispatchEmails`: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (bearer `CRON_SECRET`, ties to NFR-8) and `npm run worker:email` (15s loop, local/simple deployments). Same underlying function, two thin entry points — do not fork the dispatch logic between them. |\n| FR-13 | Email Transport Config | Env vars (`SMTP_*`, `EMAIL_FROM`, `CRON_SECRET`, `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` smtp\\|console). Console transport is a dev-mode Nodemailer transport swap, not a separate code path through the dispatcher. |\n| FR-14 | Bell/Popover UI | Live unread-count bell (MUI IconButton + Badge) replacing the static badge at `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx:141`; polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30s, paused on `visibilitychange` hidden, \"9+\" cap. Read-only UI over FR-21's unread-count endpoint; polling pause/resume is a client-side concern only. |\n| FR-15 | Bell/Popover UI | Popover with 10 most recent notifications (unread styling, 2-line clamp, relative time), click marks-read + navigates; footer \"Mark all as read\" / \"View all\". Composes FR-21's list/read endpoints; no new server logic beyond what FR-16/FR-21 already define. |\n| FR-16 | Notifications Page | `/notifications`: paginated (20/page), All/Unread tabs, category filter, bulk mark-all-read, per-row read/unread toggle. Same list/read API surface as FR-15's popover — one list service backing both, not two. |\n| FR-17 | Retention Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` — delete notifications older than 180 days, invoked once/day from the dispatcher endpoint with in-memory last-run tracking (re-run after restart is acceptable). Piggybacks on FR-12's dispatch endpoint call site — not a separate cron/queue. |\n| FR-18 | Preferences UI | `/account/notifications`: MUI Table grouped by category, In-app/Email switches per visible type, mandatory in-app types shown disabled with tooltip. Pure read+toggle view over FR-2 (registry) + FR-1 (`NotificationPreference` rows). |\n| FR-19 | Preferences API | `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` saves immediately, optimistic UI + rollback on error — client-side concern (FR-18) paired with the server validation in FR-22. |\n| FR-20 | Admin Email Log | `/admin/email-log`: table (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/last-error), status filter, \"Retry now\" (resets attempts=0/status=PENDING/nextAttemptAt=now), \"Send test notification to me\" (calls `notify({ type: 'system.test', ... })`). Read/write surface directly over `EmailOutbox` (FR-1) and `notify()` (FR-4); \"Retry now\" must use the same reset semantics FR-11's backoff expects. |\n| FR-21 | REST API Surface | Full endpoint list (notifications CRUD-ish, preferences, dispatch, admin email-log, admin test) — to be finalized verbatim by `arch-api-contracts`, following PRD-00's envelope/pagination/error-code conventions. Every endpoint here must map 1:1 to a service already named in FR-4/FR-10/FR-16/FR-18/FR-20; no net-new business logic at the route layer. |\n| FR-22 | Preferences API | `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` must reject `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types — server-side enforcement mirroring FR-18's disabled-switch UI (defense in depth, UI alone is not sufficient). |\n| FR-23 | Navigation | Sidebar nav entries for notifications page (+ admin email-log) in `src/config/navigation.ts`, following the existing `NavItem` convention (currently only Dashboard). MEDIUM confidence on exact entries — flag for `arch-design-system` to confirm naming/grouping. |\n| FR-24 | Data Model (seed) | Seed 3 `system.test` `Notification` rows (1 read, 2 unread) for two existing seeded users. Pure seed-data task, depends on FR-1's schema and FR-2's registry key existing first. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n===ticketcheck===\nartifacts/architect/api-contracts.json:  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",\nartifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json:  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",\nartifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json:  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
