e full REST surface from the API table: sections CRUD + members + move-section + core-courses + copy-to-year; courses CRUD + roster + enrollments + enrollment status PATCH; GET /api/me/courses — each with the role gating shown in the table and the existing success/list/error response envelope and pagination/sort/search query conventions.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Every write (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*) records an AuditLog row via the existing audit() helper.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table footnote 'All writes audit (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*)'; verified audit() already exists and is exported from src/server/audit.ts\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element in the section/course/enrollment screens is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the MUI X packages (DataGrid via the existing shared DataTable, Autocomplete, Tabs, Dialog, Drawer, Snackbar+Alert via useToast()); every component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; no banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, react-select, etc.) in this PRD's code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD); Compliance Rule 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Integrity: the one-section-per-student-per-year rule is enforced by the database unique constraint (@@unique([studentId, academicYearId]) on SectionMember), not only in application code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: adding 30 students to a section with 8 core courses (240 resulting enrollments) completes in under 1 second.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Privacy: on the course Roster tab and GET /api/courses/:id/roster, students see classmates' names only — no emails, admission numbers or profile links in the response.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3; Acceptance Criteria #7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Scope containment: no timetable slots (PRD-06), no course content (PRD-08), no prerequisite or course-request workflows, and no automatic year-to-year student promotion — only the manual 'Copy sections to next year' shortcut.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization gap carried forward from PRD-01/PRD-04: the Platform Context describes src/server/auth/permissions.ts exposing requireUser()/requireRole(...roles), but only src/server/auth/requireRole.ts and student-access.ts exist today (no permissions.ts, no requireUser()). New route handlers in this PRD must use the existing requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)-style stand-in (as PRD-04's handoff also flagged) rather than invent a new auth helper, until PRD-01 lands.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement), cross-checked against the current contents of src/server/auth/ (only requireRole.ts and student-access.ts present)\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}}}
