{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015RaPn6HTMvfNoowur4c9DL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-04\n2\t\n3\tSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\n4\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 requirements — 24 FR + 10\n5\tNFR, 97% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is\n6\tthe Notifications & Email PRD: notification data model/registry, `notify()`\n7\tservice, email templates, an email outbox + dispatcher worker, bell/popover\n8\tUI, the `/notifications` page, preferences UI, and the admin email log.\n9\t\n10\tArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Notification\n11\tType Registry**, **Notification Service**, **Family Fan-out Helper**, **Email\n12\tTemplates**, **Auth Email Integration**, **Email Dispatcher**, **Email\n13\tTransport Config**, **Bell/Popover UI**, **Notifications Page**, **Retention\n14\tJob**, **Preferences UI**, **Preferences API**, **Admin Email Log**, **REST\n15\tAPI Surface**, **Navigation**, **Design System (MUI-only)**, **Security/\n16\tAccess Control**, **Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.\n17\t\n18\t## Functional Requirements\n19\t\n20\t| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n21\t|----|------------------------|-------|\n22\t| FR-1 | Data Model | `Notification`, `NotificationPreference`, `EmailOutbox` + `EmailStatus` enum. Foundation tables — every other FR reads or writes one of these; must land before any service/route work. |\n23\t| FR-2 | Notification Type Registry | Typed registry at `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles), seeded with `account.invite`, `account.password_reset`, `system.test`. Single source of truth the service layer (FR-4), preferences UI (FR-18), and compile-time typing (FR-3) all key off. |\n24\t| FR-3 | Notification Service | `notify()` must reject unknown type keys at compile time (TS literal/union against the registry) — a typing constraint on FR-4's signature, not a runtime check. |\n25\t| FR-4 | Notification Service | Core `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })` — skips archived/disabled users, resolves preferences (falling back to registry defaults), writes `Notification` rows and `EmailOutbox` rows as applicable. The central chokepoint everything else (FR-6, FR-9, FR-20, FR-24) calls into. |\n26\t| FR-5 | Notification Service | Batching via `createMany` (≤3 round-trips per 1,000 users each for notifications/emails) + never-throw-to-caller (log failures) + \"call after your own transaction commits\" contract. Directly drives NFR-2's latency budget and the service's error-handling shape. |\n27\t| FR-6 | Family Fan-out Helper | `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` — expands student → student + linked parents, deduped, for later PRDs to reuse. Thin wrapper over FR-4 plus whatever parent-link read path already exists (brownfield reuse, not a new link model). |\n28\t| FR-7 | Email Templates | `@react-email/components` templates under `src/server/email/templates/`, rendered to HTML + plain text, sharing a base layout (header/content/footer, preferences link, disclosure sentence). One shared layout component — avoid three independently-styled templates. |\n29\t| FR-8 | Email Templates | Concrete templates: invite, password-reset, generic-notification, each with their specified fields/CTA. Three thin wrappers over FR-7's base layout. |\n30\t| FR-9 | Auth Email Integration | Replace the PRD-01 `sendInvite()` stub (`src/server/services/users.ts:385-390`, currently log-only) with `sendAuthEmail()` that enqueues via `EmailOutbox`. A brownfield swap at an existing call site — must not change the stub's call signature/contract that PRD-01 callers depend on. |\n31\t| FR-10 | Email Dispatcher | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` — `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` select of due PENDING rows, mark SENDING, send via Nodemailer, mark SENT or schedule retry. The other central chokepoint; must be designed as one module both the HTTP route (FR-12) and the worker loop (FR-12) call. |\n32\t| FR-11 | Email Dispatcher | Retry backoff schedule (1/5/15/60/240 min across 5 attempts, FAILED after 5th) — state-machine detail inside FR-10's dispatch logic, also what FR-20's \"Retry now\" action resets. |\n33\t| FR-12 | Email Dispatcher | Two callers of `dispatchEmails`: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (bearer `CRON_SECRET`, ties to NFR-8) and `npm run worker:email` (15s loop, local/simple deployments). Same underlying function, two thin entry points — do not fork the dispatch logic between them. |\n34\t| FR-13 | Email Transport Config | Env vars (`SMTP_*`, `EMAIL_FROM`, `CRON_SECRET`, `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` smtp\\|console). Console transport is a dev-mode Nodemailer transport swap, not a separate code path through the dispatcher. |\n35\t| FR-14 | Bell/Popover UI | Live unread-count bell (MUI IconButton + Badge) replacing the static badge at `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx:141`; polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30s, paused on `visibilitychange` hidden, \"9+\" cap. Read-only UI over FR-21's unread-count endpoint; polling pause/resume is a client-side concern only. |\n36\t| FR-15 | Bell/Popover UI | Popover with 10 most recent notifications (unread styling, 2-line clamp, relative time), click marks-read + navigates; footer \"Mark all as read\" / \"View all\". Composes FR-21's list/read endpoints; no new server logic beyond what FR-16/FR-21 already define. |\n37\t| FR-16 | Notifications Page | `/notifications`: paginated (20/page), All/Unread tabs, category filter, bulk mark-all-read, per-row read/unread toggle. Same list/read API surface as FR-15's popover — one list service backing both, not two. |\n38\t| FR-17 | Retention Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` — delete notifications older than 180 days, invoked once/day from the dispatcher endpoint with in-memory last-run tracking (re-run after restart is acceptable). Piggybacks on FR-12's dispatch endpoint call site — not a separate cron/queue. |\n39\t| FR-18 | Preferences UI | `/account/notifications`: MUI Table grouped by category, In-app/Email switches per visible type, mandatory in-app types shown disabled with tooltip. Pure read+toggle view over FR-2 (registry) + FR-1 (`NotificationPreference` rows). |\n40\t| FR-19 | Preferences API | `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` saves immediately, optimistic UI + rollback on error — client-side concern (FR-18) paired with the server validation in FR-22. |\n41\t| FR-20 | Admin Email Log | `/admin/email-log`: table (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/last-error), status filter, \"Retry now\" (resets attempts=0/status=PENDING/nextAttemptAt=now), \"Send test notification to me\" (calls `notify({ type: 'system.test', ... })`). Read/write surface directly over `EmailOutbox` (FR-1) and `notify()` (FR-4); \"Retry now\" must use the same reset semantics FR-11's backoff expects. |\n42\t| FR-21 | REST API Surface | Full endpoint list (notifications CRUD-ish, preferences, dispatch, admin email-log, admin test) — to be finalized verbatim by `arch-api-contracts`, following PRD-00's envelope/pagination/error-code conventions. Every endpoint here must map 1:1 to a service already named in FR-4/FR-10/FR-16/FR-18/FR-20; no net-new business logic at the route layer. |\n43\t| FR-22 | Preferences API | `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` must reject `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types — server-side enforcement mirroring FR-18's disabled-switch UI (defense in depth, UI alone is not sufficient). |\n44\t| FR-23 | Navigation | Sidebar nav entries for notifications page (+ admin email-log) in `src/config/navigation.ts`, following the existing `NavItem` convention (currently only Dashboard). MEDIUM confidence on exact entries — flag for `arch-design-system` to confirm naming/grouping. |\n45\t| FR-24 | Data Model (seed) | Seed 3 `system.test` `Notification` rows (1 read, 2 unread) for two existing seeded users. Pure seed-data task, depends on FR-1's schema and FR-2's registry key existing first. |\n46\t\n47\t## Non-Functional Requirements\n48\t\n49\t| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n50\t|----|------------------------|-------|\n51\t| NFR-1 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every visible surface (bell, popover, notifications page, preferences table, admin log) MUI-only, checked via MUI MCP, no banned libraries; email templates explicitly exempt (use `@react-email/components` instead). A lint-enforced boundary (`no-restricted-imports`) `arch-design-system` should scope per-directory so the email-template exemption doesn't leak into app UI code. |\n52\t| NFR-2 | Notification Service | `notify()` for 1,000 recipients < 2s — directly validates FR-5's ≤3-round-trip batching design; a perf budget the service implementation must be benchmarked against. |\n53\t| NFR-3 | Notifications Page / Bell | `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` < 50ms, backed by a `(userId, readAt, createdAt)` index — constrains the `Notification` table's indexing (FR-1) and the query shape of FR-14/FR-21's unread-count endpoint. |\n54\t| NFR-4 | Email Dispatcher | No double-send under concurrent dispatchers (`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`) + stuck-`SENDING`-for->10min recovery back to PENDING. A concurrency-safety invariant on FR-10's dispatch query — the stuck-row recovery is an extra step FR-10/FR-12 must schedule (e.g. at the top of each dispatch call), not an afterthought. |\n55\t| NFR-5 | Security/Access Control | Notification `link` must be a validated relative path (`/`-prefixed, open-redirect prevention); email HTML must escape all user-provided text. Two related but distinct sanitization rules — one on `notify()`'s input (FR-4), one on the email template renderer (FR-7). |\n56\t| NFR-6 | Email Templates | Every outbound email has HTML + plain-text parts + a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing at the preferences page. Extends FR-7's base layout contract and FR-10's send step (header must be set at send time, not template-render time). |\n57\t| NFR-7 | Security/Access Control | Server-side `requireUser()`/`requireRole()` on every route: own-notifications-only for user routes, ADMIN-only for email-log routes, `CRON_SECRET` bearer for the internal dispatch route. A per-route authorization matrix `arch-api-contracts` must encode explicitly against FR-21's endpoint list — hiding UI (FR-20's admin page) is never sufficient. |\n58\t| NFR-8 | Email Dispatcher | Dispatch without correct `CRON_SECRET` bearer → 401 via the standard error envelope. The negative-path companion to FR-12/NFR-7's auth check on that one route. |\n59\t| NFR-9 | Test Harness | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green; add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements. Scopes exactly what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for. |\n60\t| NFR-10 | Scope Discipline | No SMS/push, no websockets (bell polls only), no digest emails — bounds `arch-design-system`'s design the same way it bounds dev's; don't let FR-14's polling design grow into a push/websocket architecture. |\n61\t\n62\t## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`\n63\t\n64\t- **Two chokepoints to design as named, reusable modules, not inline\n65\t  code**: `notify()` (FR-3/FR-4/FR-5/FR-6, in\n66\t  `src/server/notifications/notify.ts`) and `dispatchEmails()` (FR-10/FR-11,\n67\t  called identically by FR-12's HTTP route and worker loop). Nearly every\n68\t  other FR is either a thin UI/read-view wrapper around these two, or a\n69\t  template/config detail feeding them (FR-2 registry, FR-7/FR-8 templates,\n70\t  FR-13 env config).\n71\t- **One list/read service backs both the popover (FR-15) and the\n72\t  `/notifications` page (FR-16)** — same pagination/filter/mark-read\n73\t  surface, just different page sizes/UI chrome. Don't let `arch-design-system`\n74\t  spec two separate query paths.\n75\t- **Defense-in-depth pairs to call out explicitly in the traceability\n76\t  table**: FR-18 (disabled switch) + FR-22 (server-side reject) for\n77\t  mandatory in-app types; FR-9's brownfield stub swap must preserve\n78\t  whatever call signature PRD-01's `sendInvite()` callers already use\n79\t  (NFR-7-style reuse discipline, even though this PRD's NFRs don't\n80\t  re-state it — see FR-9's own source note referencing\n81\t  `src/server/services/users.ts:385-390`).\n82\t- **NFR-4's stuck-`SENDING` recovery and FR-17's daily purge both need a\n83\t  concrete trigger point** — likely \"run at the top of `dispatchEmails()`\n84\t  calls, gated by in-memory last-run timestamps,\" per FR-17's own\n85\t  acceptance of restart-driven re-runs. `arch-design-system` should pick\n86\t  one scheduling mechanism for both rather than inventing two.\n87\t- **FR-23's exact nav entries are MEDIUM confidence** (inferred from\n88\t  layout conventions, not spelled out) — flag in `system-design.md`'s\n89\t  traceability table so `dev-planning` knows the nav copy/grouping needs a\n90\t  final decision, not just an endpoint contract.\n91\t- **NFR-1's MUI-only rule needs a directory boundary, not a blanket rule**:\n92\t  `src/server/email/templates/**` is explicitly exempt (React Email\n93\t  components) while every app-UI path (bell, popover, `/notifications`,\n94\t  `/account/notifications`, `/admin/email-log`) is MUI-only. Worth a single\n95\t  sentence in `system-design.md`'s Overview so the ESLint config `dev`\n96\t  writes doesn't over- or under-scope the `no-restricted-imports` exemption.\n97\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8fc3ceb1-8385-4b37-8370-6806b83adbfd","uuid":"5e032880-c51d-4b3f-b13e-d0469632d09f","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:24:13.120Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-04\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 requirements — 24 FR + 10\nNFR, 97% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is\nthe Notifications & Email PRD: notification data model/registry, `notify()`\nservice, email templates, an email outbox + dispatcher worker, bell/popover\nUI, the `/notifications` page, preferences UI, and the admin email log.\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Notification\nType Registry**, **Notification Service**, **Family Fan-out Helper**, **Email\nTemplates**, **Auth Email Integration**, **Email Dispatcher**, **Email\nTransport Config**, **Bell/Popover UI**, **Notifications Page**, **Retention\nJob**, **Preferences UI**, **Preferences API**, **Admin Email Log**, **REST\nAPI Surface**, **Navigation**, **Design System (MUI-only)**, **Security/\nAccess Control**, **Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `Notification`, `NotificationPreference`, `EmailOutbox` + `EmailStatus` enum. Foundation tables — every other FR reads or writes one of these; must land before any service/route work. |\n| FR-2 | Notification Type Registry | Typed registry at `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles), seeded with `account.invite`, `account.password_reset`, `system.test`. Single source of truth the service layer (FR-4), preferences UI (FR-18), and compile-time typing (FR-3) all key off. |\n| FR-3 | Notification Service | `notify()` must reject unknown type keys at compile time (TS literal/union against the registry) — a typing constraint on FR-4's signature, not a runtime check. |\n| FR-4 | Notification Service | Core `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })` — skips archived/disabled users, resolves preferences (falling back to registry defaults), writes `Notification` rows and `EmailOutbox` rows as applicable. The central chokepoint everything else (FR-6, FR-9, FR-20, FR-24) calls into. |\n| FR-5 | Notification Service | Batching via `createMany` (≤3 round-trips per 1,000 users each for notifications/emails) + never-throw-to-caller (log failures) + \"call after your own transaction commits\" contract. Directly drives NFR-2's latency budget and the service's error-handling shape. |\n| FR-6 | Family Fan-out Helper | `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` — expands student → student + linked parents, deduped, for later PRDs to reuse. Thin wrapper over FR-4 plus whatever parent-link read path already exists (brownfield reuse, not a new link model). |\n| FR-7 | Email Templates | `@react-email/components` templates under `src/server/email/templates/`, rendered to HTML + plain text, sharing a base layout (header/content/footer, preferences link, disclosure sentence). One shared layout component — avoid three independently-styled templates. |\n| FR-8 | Email Templates | Concrete templates: invite, password-reset, generic-notification, each with their specified fields/CTA. Three thin wrappers over FR-7's base layout. |\n| FR-9 | Auth Email Integration | Replace the PRD-01 `sendInvite()` stub (`src/server/services/users.ts:385-390`, currently log-only) with `sendAuthEmail()` that enqueues via `EmailOutbox`. A brownfield swap at an existing call site — must not change the stub's call signature/contract that PRD-01 callers depend on. |\n| FR-10 | Email Dispatcher | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` — `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` select of due PENDING rows, mark SENDING, send via Nodemailer, mark SENT or schedule retry. The other central chokepoint; must be designed as one module both the HTTP route (FR-12) and the worker loop (FR-12) call. |\n| FR-11 | Email Dispatcher | Retry backoff schedule (1/5/15/60/240 min across 5 attempts, FAILED after 5th) — state-machine detail inside FR-10's dispatch logic, also what FR-20's \"Retry now\" action resets. |\n| FR-12 | Email Dispatcher | Two callers of `dispatchEmails`: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (bearer `CRON_SECRET`, ties to NFR-8) and `npm run worker:email` (15s loop, local/simple deployments). Same underlying function, two thin entry points — do not fork the dispatch logic between them. |\n| FR-13 | Email Transport Config | Env vars (`SMTP_*`, `EMAIL_FROM`, `CRON_SECRET`, `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` smtp\\|console). Console transport is a dev-mode Nodemailer transport swap, not a separate code path through the dispatcher. |\n| FR-14 | Bell/Popover UI | Live unread-count bell (MUI IconButton + Badge) replacing the static badge at `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx:141`; polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30s, paused on `visibilitychange` hidden, \"9+\" cap. Read-only UI over FR-21's unread-count endpoint; polling pause/resume is a client-side concern only. |\n| FR-15 | Bell/Popover UI | Popover with 10 most recent notifications (unread styling, 2-line clamp, relative time), click marks-read + navigates; footer \"Mark all as read\" / \"View all\". Composes FR-21's list/read endpoints; no new server logic beyond what FR-16/FR-21 already define. |\n| FR-16 | Notifications Page | `/notifications`: paginated (20/page), All/Unread tabs, category filter, bulk mark-all-read, per-row read/unread toggle. Same list/read API surface as FR-15's popover — one list service backing both, not two. |\n| FR-17 | Retention Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` — delete notifications older than 180 days, invoked once/day from the dispatcher endpoint with in-memory last-run tracking (re-run after restart is acceptable). Piggybacks on FR-12's dispatch endpoint call site — not a separate cron/queue. |\n| FR-18 | Preferences UI | `/account/notifications`: MUI Table grouped by category, In-app/Email switches per visible type, mandatory in-app types shown disabled with tooltip. Pure read+toggle view over FR-2 (registry) + FR-1 (`NotificationPreference` rows). |\n| FR-19 | Preferences API | `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` saves immediately, optimistic UI + rollback on error — client-side concern (FR-18) paired with the server validation in FR-22. |\n| FR-20 | Admin Email Log | `/admin/email-log`: table (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/last-error), status filter, \"Retry now\" (resets attempts=0/status=PENDING/nextAttemptAt=now), \"Send test notification to me\" (calls `notify({ type: 'system.test', ... })`). Read/write surface directly over `EmailOutbox` (FR-1) and `notify()` (FR-4); \"Retry now\" must use the same reset semantics FR-11's backoff expects. |\n| FR-21 | REST API Surface | Full endpoint list (notifications CRUD-ish, preferences, dispatch, admin email-log, admin test) — to be finalized verbatim by `arch-api-contracts`, following PRD-00's envelope/pagination/error-code conventions. Every endpoint here must map 1:1 to a service already named in FR-4/FR-10/FR-16/FR-18/FR-20; no net-new business logic at the route layer. |\n| FR-22 | Preferences API | `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` must reject `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types — server-side enforcement mirroring FR-18's disabled-switch UI (defense in depth, UI alone is not sufficient). |\n| FR-23 | Navigation | Sidebar nav entries for notifications page (+ admin email-log) in `src/config/navigation.ts`, following the existing `NavItem` convention (currently only Dashboard). MEDIUM confidence on exact entries — flag for `arch-design-system` to confirm naming/grouping. |\n| FR-24 | Data Model (seed) | Seed 3 `system.test` `Notification` rows (1 read, 2 unread) for two existing seeded users. Pure seed-data task, depends on FR-1's schema and FR-2's registry key existing first. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every visible surface (bell, popover, notifications page, preferences table, admin log) MUI-only, checked via MUI MCP, no banned libraries; email templates explicitly exempt (use `@react-email/components` instead). A lint-enforced boundary (`no-restricted-imports`) `arch-design-system` should scope per-directory so the email-template exemption doesn't leak into app UI code. |\n| NFR-2 | Notification Service | `notify()` for 1,000 recipients < 2s — directly validates FR-5's ≤3-round-trip batching design; a perf budget the service implementation must be benchmarked against. |\n| NFR-3 | Notifications Page / Bell | `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` < 50ms, backed by a `(userId, readAt, createdAt)` index — constrains the `Notification` table's indexing (FR-1) and the query shape of FR-14/FR-21's unread-count endpoint. |\n| NFR-4 | Email Dispatcher | No double-send under concurrent dispatchers (`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`) + stuck-`SENDING`-for->10min recovery back to PENDING. A concurrency-safety invariant on FR-10's dispatch query — the stuck-row recovery is an extra step FR-10/FR-12 must schedule (e.g. at the top of each dispatch call), not an afterthought. |\n| NFR-5 | Security/Access Control | Notification `link` must be a validated relative path (`/`-prefixed, open-redirect prevention); email HTML must escape all user-provided text. Two related but distinct sanitization rules — one on `notify()`'s input (FR-4), one on the email template renderer (FR-7). |\n| NFR-6 | Email Templates | Every outbound email has HTML + plain-text parts + a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing at the preferences page. Extends FR-7's base layout contract and FR-10's send step (header must be set at send time, not template-render time). |\n| NFR-7 | Security/Access Control | Server-side `requireUser()`/`requireRole()` on every route: own-notifications-only for user routes, ADMIN-only for email-log routes, `CRON_SECRET` bearer for the internal dispatch route. A per-route authorization matrix `arch-api-contracts` must encode explicitly against FR-21's endpoint list — hiding UI (FR-20's admin page) is never sufficient. |\n| NFR-8 | Email Dispatcher | Dispatch without correct `CRON_SECRET` bearer → 401 via the standard error envelope. The negative-path companion to FR-12/NFR-7's auth check on that one route. |\n| NFR-9 | Test Harness | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green; add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements. Scopes exactly what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for. |\n| NFR-10 | Scope Discipline | No SMS/push, no websockets (bell polls only), no digest emails — bounds `arch-design-system`'s design the same way it bounds dev's; don't let FR-14's polling design grow into a push/websocket architecture. |\n\n## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **Two chokepoints to design as named, reusable modules, not inline\n  code**: `notify()` (FR-3/FR-4/FR-5/FR-6, in\n  `src/server/notifications/notify.ts`) and `dispatchEmails()` (FR-10/FR-11,\n  called identically by FR-12's HTTP route and worker loop). Nearly every\n  other FR is either a thin UI/read-view wrapper around these two, or a\n  template/config detail feeding them (FR-2 registry, FR-7/FR-8 templates,\n  FR-13 env config).\n- **One list/read service backs both the popover (FR-15) and the\n  `/notifications` page (FR-16)** — same pagination/filter/mark-read\n  surface, just different page sizes/UI chrome. Don't let `arch-design-system`\n  spec two separate query paths.\n- **Defense-in-depth pairs to call out explicitly in the traceability\n  table**: FR-18 (disabled switch) + FR-22 (server-side reject) for\n  mandatory in-app types; FR-9's brownfield stub swap must preserve\n  whatever call signature PRD-01's `sendInvite()` callers already use\n  (NFR-7-style reuse discipline, even though this PRD's NFRs don't\n  re-state it — see FR-9's own source note referencing\n  `src/server/services/users.ts:385-390`).\n- **NFR-4's stuck-`SENDING` recovery and FR-17's daily purge both need a\n  concrete trigger point** — likely \"run at the top of `dispatchEmails()`\n  calls, gated by in-memory last-run timestamps,\" per FR-17's own\n  acceptance of restart-driven re-runs. `arch-design-system` should pick\n  one scheduling mechanism for both rather than inventing two.\n- **FR-23's exact nav entries are MEDIUM confidence** (inferred from\n  layout conventions, not spelled out) — flag in `system-design.md`'s\n  traceability table so `dev-planning` knows the nav copy/grouping needs a\n  final decision, not just an endpoint contract.\n- **NFR-1's MUI-only rule needs a directory boundary, not a blanket rule**:\n  `src/server/email/templates/**` is explicitly exempt (React Email\n  components) while every app-UI path (bell, popover, `/notifications`,\n  `/account/notifications`, `/admin/email-log`) is MUI-only. Worth a single\n  sentence in `system-design.md`'s Overview so the ESLint config `dev`\n  writes doesn't over- or under-scope the `no-restricted-imports` exemption.\n","numLines":97,"startLine":1,"totalLines":97}}}
