{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RVtT7hKB2XpVXmEotfg8u9","type":"tool_result","content":"architect\ndev\ndev-planning\nintake\ntelemetry\n\nartifacts/architect:\napi-contracts.json\nhandoff-to-dev-planning.json\nrequirements-analysis-notes.md\nsystem-design.md\ntech-stack-decisions.md\nthreat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/dev:\ndev-rerun-count.json\n\nartifacts/dev-planning:\nfile-ownership-matrix.json\nfile-structure.md\nimplementation-plan.json\nmodule-dependencies.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n\nartifacts/telemetry:\napi-retries.jsonl\ndaemon-handoff.json\nknowledge-log.jsonl\nmetering.jsonl\nphase-sessions.json\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma already contains Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog. Divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: UserStatus has an extra ARCHIVED value; AuditLog uses column `ip` (PRD says `ipAddress`) with indexes [actorId] and [action] (PRD says [entityType, entityId] and [actorId, createdAt]); AuthToken has an extra @@index([userId, type]); User has an extra @@index([lastName, firstName, email]) and many relations added by later PRDs. Platform rule 'never rename existing routes or models' applies, so these must be reconciled additively, not by renaming.\",\n    \"src/server/audit.ts already exists with audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata}); it never throws but has no `request` param and does not capture IP.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exists with PLACEHOLDER_USER (ADMIN) and only requireRole(); about 94 call sites across src use requireRole().\",\n    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has its own PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 42, 81, 171-176).\",\n    \"src/server/services/users.ts already exports createUser (PRD-03 shape: profile + links + sendInvite flag), setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status), unlockUser(userId) and a no-op sendInvite stub. createInviteToken does not exist.\",\n    \"Missing today: middleware.ts, src/server/auth/tokens.ts, src/server/rate-limit.ts, src/config/public-routes.ts, src/lib/validators/auth.ts, src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt, Auth.js config, and every (auth) page. next-auth ^5.0.0-beta.25 and bcrypt ^6 are already in package.json.\",\n    \"The EmailOutbox model exists in the schema, but no email or notification service code exists (no src/server/notifications). Per Out of Scope, sendAuthEmail() should log via logger.info.\",\n    \"prisma/seed.ts seeds only office@schoolhub.test; the 6 PRD seed users plus invited@schoolhub.test are missing.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Ensure the Prisma schema has Role, UserStatus (INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED), AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog per the PRD block; the models already exist, so reconcile only the missing fields and indexes additively (AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId]) and @@index([actorId, createdAt])) without renaming the existing `ip` column or dropping the ARCHIVED enum value.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 Data model; brownfield prisma/schema.prisma\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Store User.email lower-cased.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (User.email comment); §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Build the /login page from MUI Sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email and password fields; submit calls Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"The Credentials authorize function trims and lower-cases the email, rejects a missing user, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt set, or lockedUntil > now, and compares the password with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.' except locked ('This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.') and disabled ('This account is disabled. Contact the school office.').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3; AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Each wrong password increments failedLoginCount; at 5, set lockedUntil = now + 15 min and reset the count to 0. On success, reset the count and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.4; AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Rate-limit sign-in to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using an exported in-memory sliding window in src/server/rate-limit.ts. Over the limit, return RATE_LIMITED and show 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl only if it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.6; Test Requirements (callbackUrl unit test)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Write the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.7; AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Use JWT sessions with an 8-hour lifetime, refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"In the jwt callback, at most once every 5 minutes per token, invalidate the session if passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2; AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app) page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 UNAUTHENTICATED JSON for /api/* except /api/health, /api/auth/* and routes listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3; Goals 2; AC-8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/auth/tokens.ts as the single AuthToken module: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns a raw token (32 random bytes, base64url) and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns the token and user, or null if the token is missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.0; §FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] verifies an INVITE token (7-day expiry). If it is invalid, show 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1; AC-4, AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"The invite page shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Accepting an invite (POST /api/auth/accept-invite {token, password}) validates the policy, hashes the password, sets status ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3; Pages & Routes; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Define the password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled top-1,000 list at src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1; AC-10\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Show a live strength checklist under the password field, marking each policy rule as met or unmet.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password (POST /api/auth/forgot-password) always responds 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.', and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user only: create a PASSWORD_RESET token (60 min) through tokens.ts, invalidate older unused reset tokens and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] (POST /api/auth/reset-password {token, password}) sets the hash and passwordChangedAt, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, audits auth.password.reset and redirects to /login with a useToast success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.3; Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) logs recipient, subject and link via logger.info until PRD-04 replaces its body with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (email delivery)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"/account/security (POST /api/account/password {currentPassword, newPassword}) changes the password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1; Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the top-bar user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"users.ts: reuse the existing createUser (it already creates INVITED users; confirm a duplicate email maps to CONFLICT) instead of adding a second one, and reuse the existing setUserStatus/unlockUser signatures.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1, §FR-8.4; Platform Context 'never duplicate a helper'; brownfield users.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Add createInviteToken(userId) to users.ts. It calls createToken(userId, 'INVITE', {days: 7}), invalidates older unused invite tokens and returns the raw token.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Replace the no-op sendInvite stub with a real implementation that calls createInviteToken() then sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link), keeping its existing return shape for the current call sites.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.3; brownfield users.ts:388\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"In src/server/auth/requireRole.ts, delete PLACEHOLDER_USER and add getCurrentUser() (session user or null) and requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED, or redirects to /login in server pages). Do not create permissions.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1-9.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"requireRole(...roles) checks the real session role and throws FORBIDDEN (403), or redirects to /forbidden in server pages. Keep the signature compatible with the ~94 existing call sites. Do not add can().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.4-9.5; AC-9\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing audit() in src/server/audit.ts with an optional `request` param that captures the IP from x-forwarded-for into the existing `ip` column. It must still never throw.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.1; brownfield audit.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx so the shell reads the session user. The top-bar menu shows the real name, a role badge and avatar initials, and Sign out calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.1-11.2; AC-1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Filter the navigation.ts entries by the session role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Mount the Auth.js handlers at /api/auth/[...nextauth].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, teacher, teacher2, student, student2, parent @schoolhub.test, password SchoolHub123!) plus one INVITED invited@schoolhub.test whose invite link is logged during seeding. The existing office@schoolhub.test seed stays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; brownfield prisma/seed.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Add tests. Unit: password policy, token hashing and expiry, lockout logic, rate limiter, callbackUrl check. Integration: authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password. Playwright: sign-in/out, failed login message, forgot→reset.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"There is no public sign-up route; only invited users can activate an account.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Store only SHA-256 hashes of raw tokens and compare tokens in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; all auth forms use Auth.js CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Prevent timing-based user enumeration: run a dummy bcrypt compare when the user does not exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 s at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live='polite', and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: MUI only (@mui/material v9, icons, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, next-themes, lucide-react, notistack, sonner, etc.) and hand-styled raw HTML are not allowed. If the MCP is unreachable, report it as a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context 'UI component rule' items 1-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Every handler and server page enforces access server-side; hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Use the standard response and error envelopes ({data} / {error:{code,message,details}}) with codes UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403 and RATE_LIMITED 429. Route handlers stay thin: Zod parse → service → JSON.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models and helpers (audit.ts, users.ts, requireRole.ts, useToast, AppError); never rename routes or models; do not modify course-access.ts or student-access.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. No console.log outside the dev email transport; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Scope is fixed to this PRD: no admin user-management screens (PRD-03), no SSO/MFA/magic links, and no email infrastructure (PRD-04).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Store timestamps in UTC and display them in SchoolSettings.timezone (applies to the lockout 'N minutes' message and to lastLoginAt display).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps bullet)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-1: Should AuditLog.ip be renamed to ipAddress to match the PRD schema, or kept as `ip` under the 'never rename existing models' rule?\",\n        \"FR-1: Should UserStatus.ARCHIVED (added by an earlier PRD) be kept even though the PRD enum lists only INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED?\",\n        \"FR-25: The PRD's createUser({email, firstName, lastName, role, phone?}) differs from the existing PRD-03 createUser(CreateUserInput with profile/links/sendInvite). Reuse the existing one, or add an overload?\",\n        \"FR-25: The existing setUserStatus takes (actorId, userId, status) while the PRD says (userId, status). Keep the existing signature?\",\n        \"FR-28/29: Under middleware, should requireRole() keep returning {id, role} synchronously for its ~94 existing call sites, or become async (which would touch every caller)?\",\n        \"FR-12: How should /api/health and the existing public pages under src/app/(public) be represented in src/config/public-routes.ts?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"AuditLog.ip vs ipAddress. Default: keep `ip`, no rename; add the PRD's two indexes.\",\n        \"UserStatus.ARCHIVED. Default: keep it (removing it is a destructive migration).\",\n        \"createUser/setUserStatus signatures. Default: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures and do not duplicate them.\",\n        \"requireRole sync vs async. Auth.js auth() is async, so callers likely need `await`. The Architect must decide, and this may touch ~94 call sites.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T00:01:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 49,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"FR-1 (MEDIUM): The User, AuthToken and AuditLog models already exist with small divergences from the PRD (AuditLog.ip vs ipAddress, extra UserStatus.ARCHIVED, different AuditLog indexes). Default is to reconcile additively with no renames. Architect to confirm the migration.\",\n    \"FR-25 (MEDIUM): The existing createUser/setUserStatus signatures (PRD-03) differ from the PRD-01 FR-8 signatures. Default is to reuse the existing ones and not duplicate them.\",\n    \"FR-28/FR-29: requireRole() is currently synchronous with ~94 call sites. Reading the Auth.js session is async, so the Architect must choose between making callers await or another approach.\",\n    \"NFR-6: Dev must reach the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83d095ee-6e06-44f2-a07e-b304e1e0dcfe","uuid":"b72b9ed3-5f80-421b-a8e9-e241bff57ba9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:34:23.506Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"architect\ndev\ndev-planning\nintake\ntelemetry\n\nartifacts/architect:\napi-contracts.json\nhandoff-to-dev-planning.json\nrequirements-analysis-notes.md\nsystem-design.md\ntech-stack-decisions.md\nthreat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/dev:\ndev-rerun-count.json\n\nartifacts/dev-planning:\nfile-ownership-matrix.json\nfile-structure.md\nimplementation-plan.json\nmodule-dependencies.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n\nartifacts/telemetry:\napi-retries.jsonl\ndaemon-handoff.json\nknowledge-log.jsonl\nmetering.jsonl\nphase-sessions.json\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma already contains Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog. Divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: UserStatus has an extra ARCHIVED value; AuditLog uses column `ip` (PRD says `ipAddress`) with indexes [actorId] and [action] (PRD says [entityType, entityId] and [actorId, createdAt]); AuthToken has an extra @@index([userId, type]); User has an extra @@index([lastName, firstName, email]) and many relations added by later PRDs. Platform rule 'never rename existing routes or models' applies, so these must be reconciled additively, not by renaming.\",\n    \"src/server/audit.ts already exists with audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata}); it never throws but has no `request` param and does not capture IP.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exists with PLACEHOLDER_USER (ADMIN) and only requireRole(); about 94 call sites across src use requireRole().\",\n    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has its own PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 42, 81, 171-176).\",\n    \"src/server/services/users.ts already exports createUser (PRD-03 shape: profile + links + sendInvite flag), setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status), unlockUser(userId) and a no-op sendInvite stub. createInviteToken does not exist.\",\n    \"Missing today: middleware.ts, src/server/auth/tokens.ts, src/server/rate-limit.ts, src/config/public-routes.ts, src/lib/validators/auth.ts, src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt, Auth.js config, and every (auth) page. next-auth ^5.0.0-beta.25 and bcrypt ^6 are already in package.json.\",\n    \"The EmailOutbox model exists in the schema, but no email or notification service code exists (no src/server/notifications). Per Out of Scope, sendAuthEmail() should log via logger.info.\",\n    \"prisma/seed.ts seeds only office@schoolhub.test; the 6 PRD seed users plus invited@schoolhub.test are missing.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Ensure the Prisma schema has Role, UserStatus (INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED), AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog per the PRD block; the models already exist, so reconcile only the missing fields and indexes additively (AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId]) and @@index([actorId, createdAt])) without renaming the existing `ip` column or dropping the ARCHIVED enum value.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 Data model; brownfield prisma/schema.prisma\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Store User.email lower-cased.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (User.email comment); §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Build the /login page from MUI Sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email and password fields; submit calls Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"The Credentials authorize function trims and lower-cases the email, rejects a missing user, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt set, or lockedUntil > now, and compares the password with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.' except locked ('This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.') and disabled ('This account is disabled. Contact the school office.').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3; AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Each wrong password increments failedLoginCount; at 5, set lockedUntil = now + 15 min and reset the count to 0. On success, reset the count and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.4; AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Rate-limit sign-in to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using an exported in-memory sliding window in src/server/rate-limit.ts. Over the limit, return RATE_LIMITED and show 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl only if it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.6; Test Requirements (callbackUrl unit test)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Write the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.7; AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Use JWT sessions with an 8-hour lifetime, refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"In the jwt callback, at most once every 5 minutes per token, invalidate the session if passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2; AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app) page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 UNAUTHENTICATED JSON for /api/* except /api/health, /api/auth/* and routes listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3; Goals 2; AC-8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/auth/tokens.ts as the single AuthToken module: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns a raw token (32 random bytes, base64url) and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns the token and user, or null if the token is missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.0; §FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] verifies an INVITE token (7-day expiry). If it is invalid, show 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1; AC-4, AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"The invite page shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Accepting an invite (POST /api/auth/accept-invite {token, password}) validates the policy, hashes the password, sets status ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3; Pages & Routes; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Define the password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled top-1,000 list at src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1; AC-10\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Show a live strength checklist under the password field, marking each policy rule as met or unmet.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password (POST /api/auth/forgot-password) always responds 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.', and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user only: create a PASSWORD_RESET token (60 min) through tokens.ts, invalidate older unused reset tokens and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] (POST /api/auth/reset-password {token, password}) sets the hash and passwordChangedAt, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, audits auth.password.reset and redirects to /login with a useToast success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.3; Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) logs recipient, subject and link via logger.info until PRD-04 replaces its body with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (email delivery)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"/account/security (POST /api/account/password {currentPassword, newPassword}) changes the password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1; Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the top-bar user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"users.ts: reuse the existing createUser (it already creates INVITED users; confirm a duplicate email maps to CONFLICT) instead of adding a second one, and reuse the existing setUserStatus/unlockUser signatures.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1, §FR-8.4; Platform Context 'never duplicate a helper'; brownfield users.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Add createInviteToken(userId) to users.ts. It calls createToken(userId, 'INVITE', {days: 7}), invalidates older unused invite tokens and returns the raw token.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Replace the no-op sendInvite stub with a real implementation that calls createInviteToken() then sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link), keeping its existing return shape for the current call sites.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.3; brownfield users.ts:388\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"In src/server/auth/requireRole.ts, delete PLACEHOLDER_USER and add getCurrentUser() (session user or null) and requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED, or redirects to /login in server pages). Do not create permissions.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1-9.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"requireRole(...roles) checks the real session role and throws FORBIDDEN (403), or redirects to /forbidden in server pages. Keep the signature compatible with the ~94 existing call sites. Do not add can().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.4-9.5; AC-9\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing audit() in src/server/audit.ts with an optional `request` param that captures the IP from x-forwarded-for into the existing `ip` column. It must still never throw.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.1; brownfield audit.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx so the shell reads the session user. The top-bar menu shows the real name, a role badge and avatar initials, and Sign out calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.1-11.2; AC-1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Filter the navigation.ts entries by the session role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Mount the Auth.js handlers at /api/auth/[...nextauth].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, teacher, teacher2, student, student2, parent @schoolhub.test, password SchoolHub123!) plus one INVITED invited@schoolhub.test whose invite link is logged during seeding. The existing office@schoolhub.test seed stays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; brownfield prisma/seed.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Add tests. Unit: password policy, token hashing and expiry, lockout logic, rate limiter, callbackUrl check. Integration: authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password. Playwright: sign-in/out, failed login message, forgot→reset.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"There is no public sign-up route; only invited users can activate an account.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Store only SHA-256 hashes of raw tokens and compare tokens in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; all auth forms use Auth.js CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Prevent timing-based user enumeration: run a dummy bcrypt compare when the user does not exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 s at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live='polite', and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: MUI only (@mui/material v9, icons, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, next-themes, lucide-react, notistack, sonner, etc.) and hand-styled raw HTML are not allowed. If the MCP is unreachable, report it as a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context 'UI component rule' items 1-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Every handler and server page enforces access server-side; hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Use the standard response and error envelopes ({data} / {error:{code,message,details}}) with codes UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403 and RATE_LIMITED 429. Route handlers stay thin: Zod parse → service → JSON.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models and helpers (audit.ts, users.ts, requireRole.ts, useToast, AppError); never rename routes or models; do not modify course-access.ts or student-access.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. No console.log outside the dev email transport; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Scope is fixed to this PRD: no admin user-management screens (PRD-03), no SSO/MFA/magic links, and no email infrastructure (PRD-04).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Store timestamps in UTC and display them in SchoolSettings.timezone (applies to the lockout 'N minutes' message and to lastLoginAt display).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps bullet)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-1: Should AuditLog.ip be renamed to ipAddress to match the PRD schema, or kept as `ip` under the 'never rename existing models' rule?\",\n        \"FR-1: Should UserStatus.ARCHIVED (added by an earlier PRD) be kept even though the PRD enum lists only INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED?\",\n        \"FR-25: The PRD's createUser({email, firstName, lastName, role, phone?}) differs from the existing PRD-03 createUser(CreateUserInput with profile/links/sendInvite). Reuse the existing one, or add an overload?\",\n        \"FR-25: The existing setUserStatus takes (actorId, userId, status) while the PRD says (userId, status). Keep the existing signature?\",\n        \"FR-28/29: Under middleware, should requireRole() keep returning {id, role} synchronously for its ~94 existing call sites, or become async (which would touch every caller)?\",\n        \"FR-12: How should /api/health and the existing public pages under src/app/(public) be represented in src/config/public-routes.ts?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"AuditLog.ip vs ipAddress. Default: keep `ip`, no rename; add the PRD's two indexes.\",\n        \"UserStatus.ARCHIVED. Default: keep it (removing it is a destructive migration).\",\n        \"createUser/setUserStatus signatures. Default: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures and do not duplicate them.\",\n        \"requireRole sync vs async. Auth.js auth() is async, so callers likely need `await`. The Architect must decide, and this may touch ~94 call sites.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T00:01:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 49,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"FR-1 (MEDIUM): The User, AuthToken and AuditLog models already exist with small divergences from the PRD (AuditLog.ip vs ipAddress, extra UserStatus.ARCHIVED, different AuditLog indexes). Default is to reconcile additively with no renames. Architect to confirm the migration.\",\n    \"FR-25 (MEDIUM): The existing createUser/setUserStatus signatures (PRD-03) differ from the PRD-01 FR-8 signatures. Default is to reuse the existing ones and not duplicate them.\",\n    \"FR-28/FR-29: requireRole() is currently synchronous with ~94 call sites. Reading the Auth.js session is async, so the Architect must choose between making callers await or another approach.\",\n    \"NFR-6: Dev must reach the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RVtT7hKB2XpVXmEotfg8u9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
