al Verification / Auth UI | Auth.js v5 lets `authorize` throw a `CredentialsSignin` subclass with a `code` (`invalid`, `locked`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`). The UI maps code → message. Locked message needs remaining minutes from `lockedUntil` → the code must carry minutes (e.g. `locked:7`) or the UI calls back. Design must pick one. |\n| FR-6 | Lockout & Rate Limiting | Per-user counter on `User` row. Increment + lock must be one atomic update (`update ... failedLoginCount: { increment: 1 }` then conditional lock) to avoid races under parallel attempts. Pure helper `computeLockout(count, now)` for unit test. |\n| FR-7 | Lockout & Rate Limiting | `src/server/rate-limit.ts`: in-memory sliding window keyed by string (`login:ip:<ip>`). Single-process only — acceptable per PRD; note ceiling (multi-instance needs Redis). Reused by FR-19 with different keys/limits, so API is generic `check(key, limit, windowMs)`. Needs client IP → shared `getClientIp(request)` helper (also FR-30). |\n| FR-8 | Auth Core | Pure `safeCallbackUrl(url): string` — accept only paths starting with `/` and not `//` or `/\\`; else `/dashboard`. Used by login page and Auth.js `redirect` callback. Unit-tested (FR-36). |\n| FR-9 | Audit | Called from authorize branches. `auth.login.failure` metadata = `{ email, reason }` only (FR-31). `actorId` = user id when known, null for unknown email. |\n| FR-10 | Session/JWT | Auth.js `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8h, updateAge }`. `jwt`/`session` callbacks copy `id, role, firstName, lastName, email`. Module augmentation of `next-auth` types for typed `session.user`. |\n| FR-11 | Session/JWT | `jwt` callback stores `checkedAt` on the token; if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`, DB read of `passwordChangedAt`/`status`; return `null` to invalidate. This DB hit means the jwt callback must not run on edge → middleware must use an edge-safe config split (see FR-12). |\n| FR-12 | Edge Middleware | `middleware.ts` runs on edge: **cannot import Prisma or bcrypt**. Standard Auth.js v5 pattern: `auth.config.ts` (edge-safe, no providers' DB code) used by middleware; `auth.ts` (full, Node) for handlers. Middleware only checks token presence/validity; FR-11 revalidation happens in Node. Matcher excludes `_next`, static, `/api/auth/*`, `/api/health`, `(auth)` pages, `(public)` pages, plus `src/config/public-routes.ts` list. Pages → redirect `/login?callbackUrl=`; `/api/*` → 401 JSON envelope. |\n| FR-13 | Token Module | `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` — the only writer/reader of `AuthToken`. `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, store `sha256` hex. Lookup by hash (unique index) → constant-time compare after fetch (NFR-1). `consumeToken` should be conditional (`updateMany where usedAt null`) so double-submit can't consume twice. Add `invalidateUnused(userId, type)` used by FR-20/FR-26. |\n| FR-14 | Invite Flow | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` server component calls `verifyToken(raw, 'INVITE')`; invalid → error Alert. Token is in the URL path → ensure it isn't logged by request logging. |\n| FR-15 | Invite Flow / Auth UI | Read-only name/email from verified token's user; password + confirm fields reuse the FR-18 checklist component. |\n| FR-16 | Invite Flow / REST API | `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` — **note path sits under `/api/auth/*` alongside the `[...nextauth]` catch-all**; Next.js static segments win over catch-alls so this works, but design must confirm. Service in a transaction: verify → policy check → hash → `status=ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt=now` → consume. \"Signs the user in\": simplest is client calls `signIn('credentials')` with the just-set password after 200 OK (server-side session minting outside Auth.js is fragile). Audit `auth.invite.accepted`. |\n| FR-17 | Password Policy | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` — Zod schema shared client+server. Common-password list lives in `src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt` (server-only file read) → split: client checks length/letter/digit/≠email; server additionally checks common list. FR-18 checklist can't show the common-list rule live without shipping the list; either ship the list (~8 KB) to client or show that rule only on submit. Design decision. |\n| FR-18 | Password Policy / Auth UI | Shared `PasswordChecklist` component (MUI List + icons) used by invite, reset and change-password pages. |\n| FR-19 | Password Reset Flow / Lockout & Rate Limiting | `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` — identical response body and similar timing whether or not user exists (NFR-3 spirit). Two rate-limit keys: `forgot:email:<email>` (3/h), `forgot:ip:<ip>` (10/h). Over limit: still the generic message, or RATE_LIMITED 429? PRD says \"always responds\" → design must decide; 429 on IP limit is safe, email limit should stay silent to avoid enumeration. |\n| FR-20 | Password Reset Flow | Only ACTIVE users get a token; `invalidateUnused(userId,'PASSWORD_RESET')` then `createToken(…, 60 min)` then `sendAuthEmail`. Unknown email → no DB write. |\n| FR-21 | Password Reset Flow | `POST /api/auth/reset-password` transaction: verify → policy → hash → `passwordChangedAt=now`, `failedLoginCount=0`, `lockedUntil=null` → consume. Audit `auth.password.reset`. Success toast after redirect needs cross-navigation signal (`/login?reset=1` query param read on login page → `useToast`). |\n| FR-22 | Email Stub | `src/server/auth/email.ts` `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` → `logger.info`. Single seam PRD-04 swaps for EmailOutbox. Link base URL from env (`AUTH_URL`/`NEXTAUTH_URL`). |\n| FR-23 | Change Password | `/account/security` page inside `(app)` (authenticated). `POST /api/account/password` → `requireUser()` → bcrypt compare current → policy → hash → `passwordChangedAt=now`. \"Re-issue current session\": after `passwordChangedAt` bump, current JWT's `iat` < `passwordChangedAt` would be invalidated by FR-11 → must refresh current token (client `update()` from `useSession`, with jwt callback trigger `update` resetting `iat`/`checkedAt`). Key subtlety for design. Wrong current password → 400 with field-level `details` for the form. |\n| FR-24 | App Shell & Nav | Add menu item in `shell.tsx` user menu → `/account/security`. All roles. |\n| FR-25 | Users Service | No new `createUser`; confirm P2002 on email → CONFLICT via existing `http.ts` mapping. Keep `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)` and `unlockUser(userId)` (resolves blocker 2 per intake defaults). Ensure `createUser` lower-cases email (FR-2). |\n| FR-26 | Users Service / Token Module | `createInviteToken(userId)` in `users.ts` → `tokens.invalidateUnused` + `tokens.createToken(userId,'INVITE',{days:7})`. |\n| FR-27 | Users Service / Email Stub | `sendInvite` body: `createInviteToken` → `sendAuthEmail(user,'invite',link)`; keep return `{id, inviteSentAt}` for existing callers. |\n| FR-28 | Authorization Helpers | `requireRole.ts`: delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`; add `getCurrentUser()` (wraps `auth()`, memoised per request with React `cache()`), `requireUser()`. Server pages vs route handlers need different failure behaviour (redirect vs throw). Cleanest: separate fns or an option, since there's no reliable runtime way to detect context. Resolves blocker 3: **go async**; ~48 call sites add `await` (all already in async fns). No `permissions.ts`. |\n| FR-29 | Authorization Helpers | `requireRole(...roles)` → `Promise<SessionUser>` (superset of `{id, role}` so `course-access.ts` compiles unchanged). Throw `AppError('FORBIDDEN')` in handlers; pages redirect `/forbidden` (route exists). No `can()`. |\n| FR-30 | Audit | Add optional `request?: Request` to `AuditInput`; `ip = getClientIp(request)` (first value of `x-forwarded-for`, trimmed). Keep inside try/catch. Shared helper with FR-7. |\n| FR-31 | Audit / Security | Enforce by construction: audit callers pass explicit metadata objects; optionally a small denylist strip (`password`, `passwordHash`, `token`) in `audit()` as defence-in-depth. Covered by test. |\n| FR-32 | App Shell & Nav | `shell.tsx` reads session — either the `(app)/layout.tsx` server component passes `getCurrentUser()` as a prop, or `SessionProvider` + `useSession`. Prop-passing avoids a client fetch and flash. Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. Role badge + initials via MUI `Chip`/`Avatar`. |\n| FR-33 | App Shell & Nav | Filter `navigation.ts` entries by role (server-side, before passing to shell). UX only — NFR-7 still applies on every page. |\n| FR-34 | Auth Core / REST API | `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` exporting `{ GET, POST } = handlers` from `auth.ts`. |\n| FR-35 | Seed | Extend `prisma/seed.ts` idempotently (`upsert` by email): 6 ACTIVE users (bcrypt cost 12 of `SchoolHub123!`) + `invited@` INVITED with invite created via `createInviteToken` and link logged. Keep `office@`. Seeding goes through `tokens.ts` (FR-13 single-module rule). |\n| FR-36 | Test Harness | Unit (pure fns: policy, token hash/expiry, `computeLockout`, rate limiter, `safeCallbackUrl`) → design should keep these logic pieces as pure exported fns. Integration against DB for authorize/accept/reset/change. Playwright needs seeded users (FR-35) and the reset link from logs → e2e must read the token from DB or a test hook rather than email. |\n| FR-37 | Scope Discipline / Auth Core | No `/signup` route and no sign-up endpoint; the only path to ACTIVE is FR-16 (or admin `setUserStatus`). Middleware public list must not include any sign-up path. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Security / Token Module | SHA-256 at rest; `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on equal-length buffers. Unique index on `AuthToken.tokenHash` makes lookup O(1). |\n| NFR-2 | Security / Auth Core | Auth.js defaults already give HttpOnly, `__Secure-` prefix + Secure in prod, SameSite=Lax, CSRF on its own endpoints. **Custom POST routes (`accept-invite`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `account/password`) are outside Auth.js CSRF** — design must cover them (Origin/`Sec-Fetch-Site` same-origin check in route or middleware; SameSite=Lax alone doesn't protect unauthenticated endpoints). |\n| NFR-3 | Security / Credential Verification | Precompute a dummy bcrypt hash at module load; compare against it when the user is missing so timing matches. Same idea for forgot-password (no branch-visible timing difference). |\n| NFR-4 | Performance | bcrypt cost 12 ≈ 250 ms; budget fine. Keep authorize to 1 user query + 1 update + async audit; don't await non-critical writes serially beyond that. |\n| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Form `Alert` inside `aria-live=\"polite\"` region; on submit-with-errors focus first invalid `TextField` (`inputRef`). Shared form-error pattern across 5 auth forms. |\n| NFR-6 | Design System (MUI-only) | All auth pages, checklist, shell menu changes use MUI v9 only; dev must look up each component via mui-mcp. mui-mcp tools are visible in this environment (`useMuiDocs`, `fetchDocs`) — blocker 4 currently looks unblocked, dev must still confirm. |\n| NFR-7 | Authorization Helpers | Every new route handler and `(app)` page calls `requireUser()`/`requireRole()`; middleware is a first gate, not the only one. |\n| NFR-8 | REST API Surface | All custom auth routes: Zod parse → service → `{data}` / `{error:{code,message,details}}` using existing `http.ts` helpers. Auth.js catch-all is the sole exception (its own protocol). |\n| NFR-9 | Scope Discipline | Reuse `audit.ts`, `users.ts`, `requireRole.ts`, `useToast`, `AppError`; no renames; `course-access.ts` / `student-access.ts` untouched (constrains FR-29 return type). |\n| NFR-10 | Test Harness | Lint/typecheck/test green — the async `requireRole` change (FR-28/29) touches ~42 files, so typecheck is the safety net. `logger` only; `console.log` banned except the dev email transport. |\n| NFR-11 | Scope Discipline | No admin UI, SSO, MFA, magic links, or email infra. |\n| NFR-12 | Data Model / Auth UI | Timestamps UTC in DB. Lockout \"N minutes\" is a duration (timezone-independent); `lastLoginAt` display formatted in `SchoolSettings.timezone` (existing settings model). |\n\n## Cross-cutting items for `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **Edge/Node split** (FR-4, FR-11, FR-12): `auth.config.ts` edge-safe for middleware; `auth.ts` Node with Prisma/bcrypt.\n2. **requireRole goes async** (FR-28/29, blocker 3): ~48 sites, all already in async fns; return type superset of `{id, role}`.\n3. **Session re-issue after password change** (FR-11 vs FR-23): current session must survive its own `passwordChangedAt` bump.\n4. **CSRF for custom auth POSTs** (NFR-2): not covered by Auth.js.\n5. **Shared `getClientIp(request)`** (FR-7, FR-19, FR-30).\n6. **Shared password UI + Zod schema** (FR-15/17/18/21/23); decide whether the common-password list ships to the client.\n7. **Rate limiter is per-process** (FR-7/FR-19): fine for this PRD, Redis if multi-instance.\n8. **Additive migration only** (FR-1, blocker 1): two AuditLog indexes plus any missing User columns.\n\n## Blockers carried forward from intake\n\n- FR-1 schema divergences → resolved by additive migration (above).\n- FR-25 signature mismatch → keep the existing signatures.\n- FR-28/29 sync vs async → recommend async (call sites are fewer than intake reported and are all already async).\n- NFR-6 mui-mcp reachability → tools are registered in this environment; dev must still check before writing UI.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015nfX9eFUJKHAj3nAaRRboc","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83d095ee-6e06-44f2-a07e-b304e1e0dcfe","uuid":"40dab919-43a8-46ef-90fc-f2ca34b61776","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:35:43.868Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-1\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions\n& RBAC; 37 FR + 12 NFR = 49 requirements, 94% confidence, 4 blockers in\n`handoff-to-architect.json`). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\nArchitectural concern buckets: **Data Model**, **Auth Core (Auth.js)**,\n**Credential Verification**, **Lockout & Rate Limiting**, **Session/JWT**,\n**Edge Middleware**, **Token Module**, **Invite Flow**, **Password Policy**,\n**Password Reset Flow**, **Change Password**, **Email Stub**, **Users\nService**, **Authorization Helpers**, **Audit**, **App Shell & Nav**, **Auth\nUI Surface**, **REST API Surface**, **Seed**, **Test Harness**, **Security**,\n**Performance**, **Accessibility**, **Design System (MUI-only)**, **Scope\nDiscipline**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (correct intake where it differs)\n\n- `requireRole(` is called at **~48 sites in ~42 files**, not ~94 as intake\n  says. Every one of those files already contains `async`, i.e. the callers\n  are async route handlers / server components. **Making `requireRole()`\n  async (callers add `await`) is a mechanical change, not a redesign.**\n  `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` consumes requireRole's result but must\n  not be modified (NFR-9) — keep the returned shape a superset of\n  `{ id, role }`.\n- `src/server/http.ts` already defines `AppError` codes `UNAUTHENTICATED`\n  401, `FORBIDDEN` 403, `RATE_LIMITED` 429, `CONFLICT` 409, plus Prisma\n  P2002 → CONFLICT mapping. No new error infra needed.\n- `src/server/audit.ts` has `audit(input)` that swallows errors; no `request`\n  param, never writes `ip`. Nothing in `src` reads `x-forwarded-for` today.\n- `src/lib/logger.ts`, `src/components/Toast/useToast.ts`,\n  `src/config/navigation.ts` exist. `src/app/forbidden` exists (target for\n  FR-29 redirect). `src/app/(public)` has `layout.tsx` + `page.tsx` only.\n- `src/app/api/health` exists; `src/app/api/auth` does not.\n- `users.ts` exports `createUser`, `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)`,\n  `unlockUser(userId)`, `sendInvite(userId): Promise<{id, inviteSentAt}>`.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | Additive Prisma migration only: add `AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])`. Keep `ip` column, `ARCHIVED` enum value, and existing extra indexes (resolves blocker 1 per intake defaults). Verify `User` has `passwordHash`, `failedLoginCount`, `lockedUntil`, `lastLoginAt`, `passwordChangedAt`, `archivedAt`; add any missing as nullable/defaulted columns. |\n| FR-2 | Data Model / Credential Verification | Normalise `email.trim().toLowerCase()` in one place (Zod schema transform in `validators/auth.ts`) used by authorize, forgot-password and `createUser`. DB-level backstop optional (Postgres `citext` would be a type change — avoid; app-level is enough). |\n| FR-3 | Auth UI Surface | `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` — new `(auth)` route group with its own unauthenticated layout (no AppShell). Client component calling `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` so error codes can map to FR-5 messages. |\n| FR-4 | Credential Verification | Lives in Auth.js `Credentials.authorize`, but logic should be a plain service fn (`src/server/auth/credentials.ts` or inside the Auth.js config file) so integration tests (FR-36) can call it without HTTP. Order: rate-limit → lookup → status/archived/locked checks → bcrypt compare (cost 12). Runs on the **Node runtime** (bcrypt is native; not edge-safe). |\n| FR-5 | Credential Verification / Auth UI | Auth.js v5 lets `authorize` throw a `CredentialsSignin` subclass with a `code` (`invalid`, `locked`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`). The UI maps code → message. Locked message needs remaining minutes from `lockedUntil` → the code must carry minutes (e.g. `locked:7`) or the UI calls back. Design must pick one. |\n| FR-6 | Lockout & Rate Limiting | Per-user counter on `User` row. Increment + lock must be one atomic update (`update ... failedLoginCount: { increment: 1 }` then conditional lock) to avoid races under parallel attempts. Pure helper `computeLockout(count, now)` for unit test. |\n| FR-7 | Lockout & Rate Limiting | `src/server/rate-limit.ts`: in-memory sliding window keyed by string (`login:ip:<ip>`). Single-process only — acceptable per PRD; note ceiling (multi-instance needs Redis). Reused by FR-19 with different keys/limits, so API is generic `check(key, limit, windowMs)`. Needs client IP → shared `getClientIp(request)` helper (also FR-30). |\n| FR-8 | Auth Core | Pure `safeCallbackUrl(url): string` — accept only paths starting with `/` and not `//` or `/\\`; else `/dashboard`. Used by login page and Auth.js `redirect` callback. Unit-tested (FR-36). |\n| FR-9 | Audit | Called from authorize branches. `auth.login.failure` metadata = `{ email, reason }` only (FR-31). `actorId` = user id when known, null for unknown email. |\n| FR-10 | Session/JWT | Auth.js `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8h, updateAge }`. `jwt`/`session` callbacks copy `id, role, firstName, lastName, email`. Module augmentation of `next-auth` types for typed `session.user`. |\n| FR-11 | Session/JWT | `jwt` callback stores `checkedAt` on the token; if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`, DB read of `passwordChangedAt`/`status`; return `null` to invalidate. This DB hit means the jwt callback must not run on edge → middleware must use an edge-safe config split (see FR-12). |\n| FR-12 | Edge Middleware | `middleware.ts` runs on edge: **cannot import Prisma or bcrypt**. Standard Auth.js v5 pattern: `auth.config.ts` (edge-safe, no providers' DB code) used by middleware; `auth.ts` (full, Node) for handlers. Middleware only checks token presence/validity; FR-11 revalidation happens in Node. Matcher excludes `_next`, static, `/api/auth/*`, `/api/health`, `(auth)` pages, `(public)` pages, plus `src/config/public-routes.ts` list. Pages → redirect `/login?callbackUrl=`; `/api/*` → 401 JSON envelope. |\n| FR-13 | Token Module | `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` — the only writer/reader of `AuthToken`. `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, store `sha256` hex. Lookup by hash (unique index) → constant-time compare after fetch (NFR-1). `consumeToken` should be conditional (`updateMany where usedAt null`) so double-submit can't consume twice. Add `invalidateUnused(userId, type)` used by FR-20/FR-26. |\n| FR-14 | Invite Flow | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` server component calls `verifyToken(raw, 'INVITE')`; invalid → error Alert. Token is in the URL path → ensure it isn't logged by request logging. |\n| FR-15 | Invite Flow / Auth UI | Read-only name/email from verified token's user; password + confirm fields reuse the FR-18 checklist component. |\n| FR-16 | Invite Flow / REST API | `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` — **note path sits under `/api/auth/*` alongside the `[...nextauth]` catch-all**; Next.js static segments win over catch-alls so this works, but design must confirm. Service in a transaction: verify → policy check → hash → `status=ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt=now` → consume. \"Signs the user in\": simplest is client calls `signIn('credentials')` wit