sword` → `requireUser()` → bcrypt compare current → policy → hash → `passwordChangedAt=now`. \"Re-issue current session\": after `passwordChangedAt` bump, current JWT's `iat` < `passwordChangedAt` would be invalidated by FR-11 → must refresh current token (client `update()` from `useSession`, with jwt callback trigger `update` resetting `iat`/`checkedAt`). Key subtlety for design. Wrong current password → 400 with field-level `details` for the form. |\n| FR-24 | App Shell & Nav | Add menu item in `shell.tsx` user menu → `/account/security`. All roles. |\n| FR-25 | Users Service | No new `createUser`; confirm P2002 on email → CONFLICT via existing `http.ts` mapping. Keep `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)` and `unlockUser(userId)` (resolves blocker 2 per intake defaults). Ensure `createUser` lower-cases email (FR-2). |\n| FR-26 | Users Service / Token Module | `createInviteToken(userId)` in `users.ts` → `tokens.invalidateUnused` + `tokens.createToken(userId,'INVITE',{days:7})`. |\n| FR-27 | Users Service / Email Stub | `sendInvite` body: `createInviteToken` → `sendAuthEmail(user,'invite',link)`; keep return `{id, inviteSentAt}` for existing callers. |\n| FR-28 | Authorization Helpers | `requireRole.ts`: delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`; add `getCurrentUser()` (wraps `auth()`, memoised per request with React `cache()`), `requireUser()`. Server pages vs route handlers need different failure behaviour (redirect vs throw). Cleanest: separate fns or an option, since there's no reliable runtime way to detect context. Resolves blocker 3: **go async**; ~48 call sites add `await` (all already in async fns). No `permissions.ts`. |\n| FR-29 | Authorization Helpers | `requireRole(...roles)` → `Promise<SessionUser>` (superset of `{id, role}` so `course-access.ts` compiles unchanged). Throw `AppError('FORBIDDEN')` in handlers; pages redirect `/forbidden` (route exists). No `can()`. |\n| FR-30 | Audit | Add optional `request?: Request` to `AuditInput`; `ip = getClientIp(request)` (first value of `x-forwarded-for`, trimmed). Keep inside try/catch. Shared helper with FR-7. |\n| FR-31 | Audit / Security | Enforce by construction: audit callers pass explicit metadata objects; optionally a small denylist strip (`password`, `passwordHash`, `token`) in `audit()` as defence-in-depth. Covered by test. |\n| FR-32 | App Shell & Nav | `shell.tsx` reads session — either the `(app)/layout.tsx` server component passes `getCurrentUser()` as a prop, or `SessionProvider` + `useSession`. Prop-passing avoids a client fetch and flash. Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. Role badge + initials via MUI `Chip`/`Avatar`. |\n| FR-33 | App Shell & Nav | Filter `navigation.ts` entries by role (server-side, before passing to shell). UX only — NFR-7 still applies on every page. |\n| FR-34 | Auth Core / REST API | `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` exporting `{ GET, POST } = handlers` from `auth.ts`. |\n| FR-35 | Seed | Extend `prisma/seed.ts` idempotently (`upsert` by email): 6 ACTIVE users (bcrypt cost 12 of `SchoolHub123!`) + `invited@` INVITED with invite created via `createInviteToken` and link logged. Keep `office@`. Seeding goes through `tokens.ts` (FR-13 single-module rule). |\n| FR-36 | Test Harness | Unit (pure fns: policy, token hash/expiry, `computeLockout`, rate limiter, `safeCallbackUrl`) → design should keep these logic pieces as pure exported fns. Integration against DB for authorize/accept/reset/change. Playwright needs seeded users (FR-35) and the reset link from logs → e2e must read the token from DB or a test hook rather than email. |\n| FR-37 | Scope Discipline / Auth Core | No `/signup` route and no sign-up endpoint; the only path to ACTIVE is FR-16 (or admin `setUserStatus`). Middleware public list must not include any sign-up path. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Security / Token Module | SHA-256 at rest; `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on equal-length buffers. Unique index on `AuthToken.tokenHash` makes lookup O(1). |\n| NFR-2 | Security / Auth Core | Auth.js defaults already give HttpOnly, `__Secure-` prefix + Secure in prod, SameSite=Lax, CSRF on its own endpoints. **Custom POST routes (`accept-invite`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `account/password`) are outside Auth.js CSRF** — design must cover them (Origin/`Sec-Fetch-Site` same-origin check in route or middleware; SameSite=Lax alone doesn't protect unauthenticated endpoints). |\n| NFR-3 | Security / Credential Verification | Precompute a dummy bcrypt hash at module load; compare against it when the user is missing so timing matches. Same idea for forgot-password (no branch-visible timing difference). |\n| NFR-4 | Performance | bcrypt cost 12 ≈ 250 ms; budget fine. Keep authorize to 1 user query + 1 update + async audit; don't await non-critical writes serially beyond that. |\n| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Form `Alert` inside `aria-live=\"polite\"` region; on submit-with-errors focus first invalid `TextField` (`inputRef`). Shared form-error pattern across 5 auth forms. |\n| NFR-6 | Design System (MUI-only) | All auth pages, checklist, shell menu changes use MUI v9 only; dev must look up each component via mui-mcp. mui-mcp tools are visible in this environment (`useMuiDocs`, `fetchDocs`) — blocker 4 currently looks unblocked, dev must still confirm. |\n| NFR-7 | Authorization Helpers | Every new route handler and `(app)` page calls `requireUser()`/`requireRole()`; middleware is a first gate, not the only one. |\n| NFR-8 | REST API Surface | All custom auth routes: Zod parse → service → `{data}` / `{error:{code,message,details}}` using existing `http.ts` helpers. Auth.js catch-all is the sole exception (its own protocol). |\n| NFR-9 | Scope Discipline | Reuse `audit.ts`, `users.ts`, `requireRole.ts`, `useToast`, `AppError`; no renames; `course-access.ts` / `student-access.ts` untouched (constrains FR-29 return type). |\n| NFR-10 | Test Harness | Lint/typecheck/test green — the async `requireRole` change (FR-28/29) touches ~42 files, so typecheck is the safety net. `logger` only; `console.log` banned except the dev email transport. |\n| NFR-11 | Scope Discipline | No admin UI, SSO, MFA, magic links, or email infra. |\n| NFR-12 | Data Model / Auth UI | Timestamps UTC in DB. Lockout \"N minutes\" is a duration (timezone-independent); `lastLoginAt` display formatted in `SchoolSettings.timezone` (existing settings model). |\n\n## Cross-cutting items for `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **Edge/Node split** (FR-4, FR-11, FR-12): `auth.config.ts` edge-safe for middleware; `auth.ts` Node with Prisma/bcrypt.\n2. **requireRole goes async** (FR-28/29, blocker 3): ~48 sites, all already in async fns; return type superset of `{id, role}`.\n3. **Session re-issue after password change** (FR-11 vs FR-23): current session must survive its own `passwordChangedAt` bump.\n4. **CSRF for custom auth POSTs** (NFR-2): not covered by Auth.js.\n5. **Shared `getClientIp(request)`** (FR-7, FR-19, FR-30).\n6. **Shared password UI + Zod schema** (FR-15/17/18/21/23); decide whether the common-password list ships to the client.\n7. **Rate limiter is per-process** (FR-7/FR-19): fine for this PRD, Redis if multi-instance.\n8. **Additive migration only** (FR-1, blocker 1): two AuditLog indexes plus any missing User columns.\n\n## Blockers carried forward from intake\n\n- FR-1 schema divergences → resolved by additive migration (above).\n- FR-25 signature mismatch → keep the existing signatures.\n- FR-28/29 sync vs async → recommend async (call sites are fewer than intake reported and are all already async).\n- NFR-6 mui-mcp reachability → tools are registered in this environment; dev must still check before writing UI.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":96,"newStart":1,"newLines":113,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-05","+# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-1"," "," Supporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (31 requirements — 24 FR + 7","-NFR, 97% confidence, 2 MEDIUM-confidence blockers per","-`handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is the Sections/Courses/Enrollment PRD:","-Section/Course/Enrollment data model, admin Sections and Courses CRUD UIs,","-the roster auto-enroll/auto-drop engine, capacity enforcement, the public","-course surface (`/courses/[courseId]`, course tabs, `/my-courses`), course","-access control, student-side course tab, navigation, and the REST API","-surface.","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions","+& RBAC; 37 FR + 12 NFR = 49 requirements, 94% confidence, 4 blockers in","+`handoff-to-architect.json`). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`."," ","-Architectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Admin Sections","-UI**, **Section Detail & Membership**, **Core Courses Bootstrap**, **Roster","-Enrollment Engine**, **Year Rollover**, **Admin Courses UI**, **Course Public","-Surface**, **Auth/Access Control**, **My Courses Page**, **Navigation**,","-**Student Tab Integration**, **REST API Surface**, **Audit Logging**,","-**Design System (MUI-only)**, **Performance**, **Privacy/Roster Scrubbing**,","-**Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.","+Architectural concern buckets: **Data Model**, **Auth Core (Auth.js)**,","+**Credential Verification**, **Lockout & Rate Limiting**, **Session/JWT**,","+**Edge Middleware**, **Token Module**, **Invite Flow**, **Password Policy**,","+**Password Reset Flow**, **Change Password**, **Email Stub**, **Users","+Service**, **Authorization Helpers**, **Audit**, **App Shell & Nav**, **Auth","+UI Surface**, **REST API Surface**, **Seed**, **Test Harness**, **Security**,","+**Performance**, **Accessibility**, **Design System (MUI-only)**, **Scope","+Discipline**."," ","+## Brownfield facts verified on disk (correct intake where it differs)","+","+- `requireRole(` is called at **~48 sites in ~42 files**, not ~94 as intake","+  says. Every one of those files already contains `async`, i.e. the callers","+  are async route handlers / server components. **Making `requireRole()`","+  async (callers add `await`) is a mechanical change, not a redesign.**","+  `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` consumes requireRole's result but must","+  not be modified (NFR-9) — keep the returned shape a superset of","+  `{ id, role }`.","+- `src/server/http.ts` already defines `AppError` codes `UNAUTHENTICATED`","+  401, `FORBIDDEN` 403, `RATE_LIMITED` 429, `CONFLICT` 409, plus Prisma","+  P2002 → CONFLICT mapping. No new error infra needed.","+- `src/server/audit.ts` has `audit(input)` that swallows errors; no `request`","+  param, never writes `ip`. Nothing in `src` reads `x-forwarded-for` today.","+- `src/lib/logger.ts`, `src/components/Toast/useToast.ts`,","+  `src/config/navigation.ts` exist. `src/app/forbidden` exists (target for","+  FR-29 redirect). `src/app/(public)` has `layout.tsx` + `page.tsx` only.","+- `src/app/api/health` exists; `src/app/api/auth` does not.","+- `users.ts` exports `createUser`, `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)`,","+  `unlockUser(userId)`, `sendInvite(userId): Promise<{id, inviteSentAt}>`.","+"," ## Functional Requirements"," "," | ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |"," |----|------------------------|-------|","-| FR-1 | Data Model | `Section`, `SectionMember`, `Course`, `Enrollment` + `CourseKind`/`EnrollmentStatus` enums, with the specified unique constraints/index. Foundation tables — every other FR reads or writes one of these; must land before any service/route work. The `@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` on `SectionMember` is also NFR-2's integrity backstop, not just a schema detail. |","-| FR-2 | Admin Sections UI | `/admin/sections` list: filter by academic year (defaults to current, reuses `AcademicYear`), table with capacity warning colour at >=90%. Read-only view over FR-1's tables plus a capacity/course-count aggregate query. |","-| FR-3 | Admin Sections UI | Section create/edit dialog incl. `UserPicker` (role=TEACHER) reuse and the \"one homeroom teacher per section per year\" rule. That uniqueness rule is app-level validation (not a DB constraint per FR-1) — `arch-design-system` should decide where it's enforced (service layer) since two concurrent writes could race. |","-| FR-4 | Section Detail & Membership | `/admin/sections/[id]`: members table (add/remove), course list, \"Create core courses\" button. Add/remove here is the trigger point for FR-7/FR-8's enrollment side effects — this page is a thin UI over the Roster Enrollment Engine, not its own business logic. |","-| FR-5 | Core Courses Bootstrap | \"Create core courses\" dialog: one CORE course per checked subject, enrolls all current section members. Must call the same course-creation path as FR-10 (creating a CORE course always enrolls current members) — one code path, two entry points (bulk vs. single). |","-| FR-6 | Year Rollover | \"Copy sections to next year\": grade level advanced by `order`, no members/teacher. Independent of the enrollment engine — a structural copy only, gated on a future non-current academic year existing. |","-| FR-7 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Auto-enroll on section add: ACTIVE-enrolls into every non-archived CORE course of the section; reactivates DROPPED rather than duplicating. Central business rule — same reactivate-vs-duplicate semantics FR-9/FR-10 must share. |","-| FR-8 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Auto-drop on section removal: CORE enrollments → DROPPED + `droppedAt`; electives untouched. Mirror of FR-7; both must be designed as one named module (e.g. `enrollInSectionCoreCourses` / `dropSectionCoreCourses`), not inlined per call site. |","-| FR-9 | Roster Enrollment Engine | `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` — FR-7 enroll + FR-8 drop in one DB transaction. The only place FR-7+FR-8 compose; confirms both must be transaction-safe, composable functions rather than route-level logic. |","-| FR-10 | Core Courses Bootstrap | New CORE course on a section enrolls all current members (ACTIVE). Same enroll path as FR-7 — triggered from course-creation instead of membership-add. |","-| FR-11 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Capacity enforcement: CONFLICT error with exact message pattern, \"Override capacity\" escape hatch. A guard that must sit in front of every enroll path (FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, and the course-level \"Add students\" of FR-15) — one shared capacity-check function, not four. |","-| FR-12 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Dropped enrollments keep historical data visible to admin/teacher but vanish from active rosters and add-student pickers. A query-filtering concern (`status = ACTIVE` everywhere user-facing lists are built) layered on top of FR-8's state transition. |","-| FR-13 | Admin Courses UI | `/admin/courses` list: filters (year/grade/subject/teacher/kind/search), reuses `Subject.color`. Read-only view, same shape as FR-2 but for courses. |","-| FR-14 | Admin Courses UI | Course create/edit dialog: subject, section (required iff kind=CORE), teacher + up to 3 co-teachers, auto-filled uppercase code. Validation rule (\"section required iff CORE\") needs to live in one shared validator the dialog and the API route both call. |","-| FR-15 | Admin Courses UI | `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment`: roster table with drop/reactivate + add-students picker; CORE courses show an info note (membership managed via section). This page's \"Add students\" must still run through FR-11's capacity guard even though it bypasses the section-membership trigger. |","-| FR-16 | Course Public Surface | `/courses/[courseId]` header: subject colour band, teachers incl. co-teachers, section, room. Read-only composition of FR-1 data, gated by FR-18's `assertCanViewCourse`. |","-| FR-17 | Course Public Surface | New `src/config/course-tabs.ts` registry (mirrors `student-tabs.ts`, adds `roles`), registers Overview + Roster tabs with per-role visibility (student sees classmates' names only; parent tab hidden). Roster tab's student-facing truncation is also NFR-4's privacy rule — same tab, two render paths by role. |","-| FR-18 | Auth/Access Control | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`: `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse`. The authorization chokepoint every course route (FR-15, FR-16, FR-23) and the course-tabs registry (FR-17) must call — do not re-derive role logic per route. Built on top of NFR-7's existing `requireRole` stand-in, not a new auth primitive. |","-| FR-19 | My Courses Page | `/my-courses`: role-specific MUI Card grids (teacher/student/parent-by-child). Read view composing FR-18's access rules per role; parent grouping needs whatever parent-link read path already exists (brownfield reuse, same pattern as the prior PRD's family fan-out). |","-| FR-20 | Navigation | Sidebar entries: \"My courses\" (TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT) + \"Sections\"/\"Courses\" under an \"Administration\" group for ADMIN. **MEDIUM confidence / flagged blocker**: `NavItem` has no `group` field today and no other admin pages exist yet. `arch-design-system` must decide: add a lightweight `group` field now, or ship flat entries until a dedicated admin-nav PRD lands — this is an explicit architect decision point, not a detail to infer silently. |","-| FR-21 | Student Tab Integration | Register `student-tabs.ts` \"Courses\" tab: student's courses, section, homeroom teacher. Pure read view, no new service — reuses FR-1 data + FR-18-equivalent visibility (whoever can view the student). |","-| FR-22 | Auth/Access Control | Extend `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)`: TEACHER additionally sees students via taught/co-taught course enrollments and their homeroom section. A brownfield extension to an existing exported function — must preserve its existing signature/contract for current PRD-01/PRD-04 callers, only add to the TEACHER branch. |","-| FR-23 | REST API Surface | Full endpoint list (sections CRUD+members+move-section+core-courses+copy-to-year; courses CRUD+roster+enrollments+status PATCH; `GET /api/me/courses`) — to be finalized verbatim by `arch-api-contracts`, following the existing envelope/pagination/search conventions. Every endpoint must map 1:1 to a service already named above (FR-7/FR-8/FR-9/FR-11 enrollment engine, FR-18 access control) — no net-new business logic at the route layer. |","-| FR-24 | Audit Logging | Every `section.*`/`course.*`/`enrollment.*` write records an `AuditLog` row via the existing `audit()` helper. A cross-cutting call that belongs at the service layer (alongside FR-7/FR-8/FR-9/FR-11's shared functions), not duplicated per route handler. |","+| FR-1 | Data Model | Additive Prisma migration only: add `AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])`. Keep `ip` column, `ARCHIVED` enum value, and existing extra indexes (resolves blocker 1 per intake defaults). Verify `User` has `passwordHash`, `failedLoginCount`, `lockedUntil`, `lastLoginAt`, `passwordChangedAt`, `archivedAt`; add any missing as nullable/defaulted columns. |","+| FR-2 | Data Model / Credential Verification | Normalise `email.trim().toLowerCase()` in one place (Zod schema transform in `validators/auth.ts`) used by authorize, forgot-password and `createUser`. DB-level backstop optional (Postgres `citext` would be a type change — avoid; app-level is enough). |","+| FR-3 | Auth UI Surface | `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` — new `(auth)` route group with its own unauthenticated layout (no AppShell). Client component calling `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` so error codes can map to FR-5 messages. |","+| FR-4 | Credential Verification | Lives in Auth.js `Credentials.authorize`, but logic should be a plain service fn (`src/server/auth/credentials.ts` or inside the Auth.js config file) so integration tests (FR-36) can call it without HTTP. Order: rate-limit → lookup → status/archived/locked checks → bcrypt compare (cost 12). Runs on the **Node runtime** (bcrypt is native; not edge-safe). |","+| FR-5 | Credential Verification / Auth UI | Auth.js v5 lets `authorize` throw a `CredentialsSignin` subclass with a `code` (`invalid`, `locked`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`). The UI maps code → message. Locked message needs remaining minutes from `lockedUntil` → the code must carry minutes (e.g. `locked:7`) or the UI calls back. Design must pick one. |","+| FR-6 | Lockout & Rate Limiting | Per-user counter on `User` row. Increment + lock must be one atomic update (`update ... failedLoginCount: { increment: 1 }` then conditional lock) to avoid races under parallel attempts. Pure helper `computeLockout(count, now)` for unit test. |","+| FR-7 | Lockout & Rate Limiting | `src/server/rate-limit.ts`: in-memory sliding window keyed by string (`login:ip:<ip>`). Single-process only — acceptable per PRD; note ceiling (multi-instance needs Redis). Reused by FR-19 with different keys/limits, so API is generic `check(key, limit, windowMs)`. Needs client IP → shared `getClientIp(request)` helper (also FR-30). |","+| FR-8 | Auth Core | Pure `safeCallbackUrl(url): string` — accept only paths starting with `/` and not `//` or `/\\`; else `/dashboard`. Used by login page and Auth.js `redirect` callback. Unit-tested (FR-36). |","+| FR-9 | Audit | Called from authorize branches. `auth.login.failure` metadata = `{ email, reason }` only (FR-31). `actorId` = user id when known, null for unknown email. |","+| FR-10 | Session/JWT | Auth.js `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8h, updateAge }`. `jwt`/`session` callbacks copy `id, role, firstName, lastName, email`. Module augmentation of `next-auth` types for typed `session.user`. |","+| FR-11 | Session/JWT | `jwt` callback stores `checkedAt` on the token; if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`, DB read of `passwordChangedAt`/`status`; return `null` to invalidate. This DB hit means the jwt callback must not run on edge → middleware must use an edge-safe config split (see FR-12). |","+| FR-12 | Edge Middleware | `middleware.ts` runs on edge: **cannot import Prisma or bcrypt**. Standard Auth.js v5 pattern: `auth.config.ts` (edge-safe, no providers' DB code) used by middleware; `auth.ts` (full, Node) for handlers. Middleware only checks token presence/validity; FR-11 revalidation happens in Node. Matcher excludes `_next`, static, `/api/auth/*`, `/api/health`, `(auth)` pages, `(public)` pages, plus `src/config/public-routes.ts` list. Pages → redirect `/login?callbackUrl=`; `/api/*` → 401 JSON envelope. |","+| FR-13 | Token Module | `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` — the only writer/reader of `AuthToken`. `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, store `sha256` hex. Lookup by hash (unique index) → constant-time compare after fetch (NFR-1). `consumeToken` should be conditional (`updateMany where usedAt null`) so double-submit can't consume twice. Add `invalidateUnused(userId, type)` used by FR-20/FR-26. |","+| FR-14 | Invite Flow | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` server component calls `verifyToken(raw, 'INVITE')`; invalid → error Alert. Token is in the URL path → ensure it isn't logged by request logging. |","+| FR-15 | Invite Flow / Auth UI | Read-only name/email from verified token's user; password + confirm fields reuse the FR-18 checklist component. |","+| FR-16 | Invite Flow / REST API | `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` — **note path sits under `/api/auth/*` alongside the `[...nextauth]` catch-all**; Next.js static segments win over catch-alls so this works, but design must confirm. Service in a transaction: verify → policy check → hash → `status=ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt=now` → consume. \"Signs the user in\": simplest is client calls `signIn('credentials')` with the just-set password after 200 OK (server-side session minting outside Auth.js is fragile). Audit `auth.invite.accepted`. |","+| FR-17 | Password Policy | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` — Zod schema shared client+server. Common-password list lives in `src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt` (server-only file read) → split: client checks length/letter/digit/≠email; server additionally checks common list. FR-18 checklist can't show the common-list rule live without shipping the list; either ship the list (~8 KB) to client or show that rule only on submit. Design decision. |","+| FR-18 | Password Policy / Auth UI | Shared `PasswordChecklist` component (MUI List + icons) used by invite, reset and change-password pages. |","+| FR-19 | Password Reset Flow / Lockout & Rate Limiting | `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` — identical response body and similar timing whether or not user exists (NFR-3 spirit). Two rate-limit keys: `forgot:email:<email>` (3/h), `forgot:ip:<ip>` (10/h). Over limit: still the generic message, or RATE_LIMITED 429? PRD says \"always responds\" → design must decide; 429 on IP limit is safe, email limit should stay silent to avoid enumeration. |","+| FR-20 | Password Reset Flow | Only ACTIVE users get a token; `invalidateUnused(userId,'PASSWORD_RESET')` then `createToken(…, 60 min)` then `sendAuthEmail`. Unknown email → no DB write. |","+| FR-21 | Password Reset Flow | `POST /api/auth/reset-password` transaction: verify → policy → hash → `passwordChangedAt=now`, `failedLoginCount=0`, `lockedUntil=null` → consume. Audit `auth.password.reset`. Success toast after redirect needs cross-navigation signal (`/login?reset=1` query param read on login page → `useToast`). |","+| FR-22 | Email Stub | `src/server/auth/email.ts` `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` → `logger.info`. Single seam PRD-04 swaps for EmailOutbox. Link base URL from env (`AUTH_URL`/`NEXTAUTH_URL`). |","+| FR-23 | Change Password | `/account/security` page inside `(app)` (authenticated). `POST /api/account/password` → `requireUser()` → bcrypt compare current → policy → hash → `passwordChangedAt=now`. \"Re-issue current session\": after `passwordChangedAt` bump, current JWT's `iat` < `passwordChangedAt` would be invalidated by FR-11 → must refresh current token (client `update()` from `useSession`, with jwt callback trigger `update` resetting `iat`/`checkedAt`). Key subtlety for design. Wrong current password → 400 with field-level `details` for the form. |","+| FR-24 | App Shell & Nav | Add menu item in `shell.tsx` user menu → `/account/security`. All roles. |","+| FR-25 | Users Service | No new `createUser`; confirm P2002 on email → CONFLICT via existing `http.ts` mapping. Keep `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)` and `unlockUser(userId)` (resolves blocker 2 per intake defaults). Ensure `createUser` lower-cases email (FR-2). |","+| FR-26 | Users Service / Token Module | `createInviteToken(userId)` in `users.ts` → `tokens.invalidateUnused` + `tokens.createToken(userId,'INVITE',{days:7})`. |","+| FR-27 | Users Service / Email Stub | `sendInvite` body: `createInviteToken` → `sendAuthEmail(user,'invite',link)`; keep return `{id, inviteSentAt}` for existing callers. |","+| FR-28 | Authorization Helpers | `requireRole.ts`: delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`; add `getCurrentUser()` (wraps `auth()`, memoised per request with React `cache()`), `requireUser()`. Server pages vs route handlers need different failure behaviour (redirect vs throw). Cleanest: separate fns or an option, since there's no reliable runtime way to detect context. Resolves blocker 3: **go async**; ~48 call sites add `await` (all already in async fns). No `permissions.ts`. |","+| FR-29 | Authorization Helpers | `requireRole(...roles)` → `Promise<SessionUser>` (superset of `{id, role}` so `course-access.ts` compiles unchanged). Throw `AppError('FORBIDDEN')` in handlers; pages redirect `/forbidden` (route exists). No `can()`. |","+| FR-30 | Audit | Add optional `request?: Request` to `AuditInput`; `ip = getClientIp(request)` (first value of `x-forwarded-for`, trimmed). Keep inside try/catch. Shared helper with FR-7. |","+| FR-31 | Audit / Security | Enforce by construction: audit callers pass explicit metadata objects; optionally a small denylist strip (`password`, `passwordHash`, `token`) in `audit()` as defence-in-depth. Covered by test. |","+| FR-32 | App Shell & Nav | `shell.tsx` reads session — either the `(app)/layout.tsx` server component passes `getCurrentUser()` as a prop, or `SessionProvider` + `useSession`. Prop-passing avoids a client fetch and flash. Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. Role badge + initials via MUI `Chip`/`Avatar`. |","+| FR-33 | App Shell & Nav | Filter `navigation.ts` entries by role (server-side, before passing to shell). UX only — NFR-7 still applies on every page. |","+| FR-34 | Auth Core / REST API | `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` exporting `{ GET, POST } = handlers` from `auth.ts`. |","+| FR-35 | Seed | Extend `prisma/seed.ts` idempotently (`upsert` by email): 6 ACTIVE users (bcrypt cost 12 of `SchoolHub123!`) + `invited@` INVITED with invite created via `createInviteToken` and link logged. Keep `office@`. Seeding goes through `tokens.ts` (FR-13 single-module rule). |","+| FR-36 | Test Harness | Unit (pure fns: policy, token hash/expiry, `computeLockout`, rate limiter, `safeCallbackUrl`) → design should keep these logic pieces as pure exported fns. Integration against DB for authorize/accept/reset/change. Playwright needs seeded users (FR-35) and the reset link from logs → e2e must read the token from DB or a test hook rather than email. |","+| FR-37 | Scope Discipline / Auth Core | No `/signup` route and no sign-up endpoint; the only path to ACTIVE is FR-16 (or admin `setUserStatus`). Middleware public list must not include any sign-up path. |"," "," ## Non-Functional Requirements"," "," | ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |"," |----|------------------------|-------|","-| NFR-1 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every visible element across sections/courses/enrollment screens is MUI/MUI-X only (DataTable, Autocomplete, Tabs, Dialog, Drawer, `useToast()`), looked up via the MUI MCP server first; no Tailwind/shadcn/Radix/react-select. Applies uniformly — unlike the prior PRD, there's no template-rendering exemption needed here (no React Email in scope). |","-| NFR-2 | Data Model | One-section-per-student-per-year enforced by the DB unique constraint on `SectionMember`, not just app code — directly backs FR-1's schema and is the safety net under FR-3's app-level homeroom-teacher-uniqueness check (which has no DB constraint and must be designed knowing that). |","-| NFR-3 | Performance | 30 students × 8 core courses (240 enrollments) in under 1s — a batching requirement on FR-7's auto-enroll path specifically; `arch-design-system` should spec `createMany`/batched writes the same way the enrollment engine is designed, not per-row inserts. |","-| NFR-4 | Privacy/Roster Scrubbing | Students see classmates' names only on the Roster tab and `GET /api/courses/:id/roster` — no email/admission number/profile link. A response-shape rule on FR-17's Roster tab and FR-23's roster endpoint; must be enforced server-side at the API layer (FR-23), not just hidden in the FR-17 UI. |","-| NFR-5 | Test Harness | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green; add unit/integration/Playwright tests per Test Requirements. Scopes what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for; the roster engine (FR-7/FR-8/FR-9/FR-11) and capacity enforcement (FR-11) are the highest-value test targets given their reuse across routes. |","-| NFR-6 | Scope Discipline | No timetable slots, no course content, no prerequisites/course-request workflows, no automatic year-to-year promotion (only the manual FR-6 copy). Bounds `arch-design-system`'s design the same way it bounds dev's — don't let FR-6's \"copy\" grow into a promotion workflow. |","-| NFR-7 | Auth/Access Control | **Flagged blocker (MEDIUM confidence)**: `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` / `requireUser()` described in Platform Context do not exist yet — only `requireRole.ts` and `student-access.ts` are present (same gap PRD-04 flagged). New routes in this PRD (FR-23) must use the existing `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` stand-in rather than invent a new helper, until PRD-01 lands. This directly constrains FR-18's `course-access.ts` implementation — it should wrap `requireRole`, not assume `permissions.ts` exists. |","+| NFR-1 | Security / Token Module | SHA-256 at rest; `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on equal-length buffers. Unique index on `AuthToken.tokenHash` makes lookup O(1). |","+| NFR-2 | Security / Auth Core | Auth.js defaults already give HttpOnly, `__Secure-` prefix + Secure in prod, SameSite=Lax, CSRF on its own endpoints. **Custom POST routes (`accept-invite`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `account/password`) are outside Auth.js CSRF** — design must cover them (Origin/`Sec-Fetch-Site` same-origin check in route or middleware; SameSite=Lax alone doesn't protect unauthenticated endpoints). |","+| NFR-3 | Security / Credential Verification | Precompute a dummy bcrypt hash at module load; compare against it when the user is missing so timing matches. Same idea for forgot-password (no branch-visible timing difference). |","+| NFR-4 | Performance | bcrypt cost 12 ≈ 250 ms; budget fine. Keep authorize to 1 user query + 1 update + async audit; don't await non-critical writes serially beyond that. |","+| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Form `Alert` inside `aria-live=\"polite\"` region; on submit-with-errors focus first invalid `TextField` (`inputRef`). Shared form-error pattern across 5 auth forms. |","+| NFR-6 | Design System (MUI-only) | All auth pages, checklist, shell menu changes use MUI v9 only; dev must look up each component via mui-mcp. mui-mcp tools are visible in this environment (`useMuiDocs`, `fetchDocs`) — blocker 4 currently looks unblocked, dev must still confirm. |","+| NFR-7 | Authorization Helpers | Every new route handler and `(app)` page calls `requireUser()`/`requireRole()`; middleware is a first gate, not the only one. |","+| NFR-8 | REST API Surface | All custom auth routes: Zod parse → service → `{data}` / `{error:{code,message,details}}` using existing `http.ts` helpers. Auth.js catch-all is the sole exception (its own protocol). |","+| NFR-9 | Scope Discipline | Reuse `audit.ts`, `users.ts`, `requireRole.ts`, `useToast`, `AppError`; no renames; `course-access.ts` / `student-access.ts` untouched (constrains FR-29 return type). |","+| NFR-10 | Test Harness | Lint/typecheck/test green — the async `requireRole` change (FR-28/29) touches ~42 files, so typecheck is the safety net. `logger` only; `console.log` banned except the dev email transport. |","+| NFR-11 | Scope Discipline | No admin UI, SSO, MFA, magic links, or email infra. |","+| NFR-12 | Data Model / Auth UI | Timestamps UTC in DB. Lockout \"N minutes\" is a duration (timezone-independent); `lastLoginAt` display formatted in `SchoolSettings.timezone` (existing settings model). |"," ","-## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`","+## Cross-cutting items for `arch-design-system`"," ","-- **One enrollment engine, four callers**: FR-7 (add to section), FR-8","-  (remove from section), FR-9 (move-section transaction), and FR-10 (new","-  CORE course) all drive the same enroll/drop/reactivate semantics, and","-  FR-11's capacity guard plus FR-24's audit call must sit in front of/behind","-  all four. Design this as named, reusable service functions (e.g.","-  `enrollSectionCoreCourses`, `dropSectionCoreCourses`,","-  `checkCapacityOrThrow`), not duplicated per route — FR-9's single-transaction","-  requirement is the clearest signal these must already be composable,","-  transaction-safe units.","-- **FR-20's nav-grouping question is an explicit decision point**, not a","-  detail to quietly resolve — `handoff-to-architect.json` lists it as a","-  blocker. Record the chosen approach (add `group` to `NavItem` vs. flat","-  entries) in `system-design.md`'s Overview per Compliance Rule 5.","-- **NFR-7's auth-helper gap is also a carried-forward blocker** — FR-18's","-  `course-access.ts` must be designed against today's `requireRole.ts`","-  stand-in, not the not-yet-built `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()`. Surface","-  this explicitly in `system-design.md`'s Overview so `dev-planning` doesn't","-  schedule work against auth helpers that don't exist.","-- **Two independent app-level uniqueness rules have no DB backstop and need","-  an explicit concurrency decision**: FR-3's \"one homeroom teacher per","-  section per year\" and FR-14's \"section required iff kind=CORE\" are both","-  service-layer validations only (unlike NFR-2's DB-constrained rule) —","-  `arch-design-system` should say where each is checked and whether a race","-  (two concurrent section edits) is acceptable risk or needs a DB-level","-  constraint too.","-- **NFR-4's roster scrubbing must be enforced at the API layer (FR-23),","-  not just the FR-17 UI tab** — call this out explicitly in the","-  traceability table so the response-shape rule isn't treated as","-  presentation-only.","-- **FR-5 and FR-10 share one course-creation-enrolls-members code path** —","-  bulk (checked subjects) vs. single (one course) are two entry points into","-  the same underlying function, same pattern as the enrollment engine note","-  above.","+1. **Edge/Node split** (FR-4, FR-11, FR-12): `auth.config.ts` edge-safe for middleware; `auth.ts` Node with Prisma/bcrypt.","+2. **requireRole goes async** (FR-28/29, blocker 3): ~48 sites, all already in async fns; return type superset of `{id, role}`.","+3. **Session re-issue after password change** (FR-11 vs FR-23): current session must survive its own `passwordChangedAt` bump.","+4. **CSRF for custom auth POSTs** (NFR-2): not covered by Auth.js.","+5. **Shared `getClientIp(request)`** (FR-7, FR-19, FR-30).","+6. **Shared password UI + Zod schema** (FR-15/17/18/21/23); decide whether the common-password list ships to the client.","+7. **Rate limiter is per-process** (FR-7/FR-19): fine for this PRD, Redis if multi-instance.","+8. **Additive migration only** (FR-1, blocker 1): two AuditLog indexes plus any missing User columns.","+","+## Blockers carried forward from intake","+","+- FR-1 schema divergences → resolved by additive migration (above).","+- FR-25 signature mismatch → keep the existing signatures.","+- FR-28/29 sync vs async → recommend async (call sites are fewer than intake reported and are all already async).","+- NFR-6 mui-mcp reachability → tools are registered in this environment; dev must still check before writing UI."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-05\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (31 requirements — 24 FR + 7\nNFR, 97% confidence, 2 MEDIUM-confidence blockers per\n`handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is the Sections/Courses/Enrollment PRD:\nSection/Course/Enrollment data model, admin Sections and Courses CRUD UIs,\nthe roster auto-enroll/auto-drop engine, capacity enforcement, the public\ncourse surface (`/courses/[courseId]`, course tabs, `/my-courses`), course\naccess control, student-side course tab, navigation, and the REST API\nsurface.\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Admin Sections\nUI**, **Section Detail & Membership**, **Core Courses Bootstrap**, **Roster\nEnrollment Engine**, **Year Rollover**, **Admin Courses UI**, **Course Public\nSurface**, **Auth/Access Control**, **My Courses Page**, **Navigation**,\n**Student Tab Integration**, **REST API Surface**, **Audit Logging**,\n**Design System (MUI-only)**, **Performance**, **Privacy/Roster Scrubbing**,\n**Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `Section`, `SectionMember`, `Course`, `Enrollment` + `CourseKind`/`EnrollmentStatus` enums, with the specified unique constraints/index. Foundation tables — every other FR reads or writes one of these; must land before any service/route work. The `@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` on `SectionMember` is also NFR-2's integrity backstop, not just a schema detail. |\n| FR-2 | Admin Sections UI | `/admin/sections` list: filter by academic year (defaults to current, reuses `AcademicYear`), table with capacity warning colour at >=90%. Read-only view over FR-1's tables plus a capacity/course-count aggregate query. |\n| FR-3 | Admin Sections UI | Section create/edit dialog incl. `UserPicker` (role=TEACHER) reuse and the \"one homeroom teacher per section per year\" rule. That uniqueness rule is app-level validation (not a DB constraint per FR-1) — `arch-design-system` should decide where it's enforced (service layer) since two concurrent writes could race. |\n| FR-4 | Section Detail & Membership | `/admin/sections/[id]`: members table (add/remove), course list, \"Create core courses\" button. Add/remove here is the trigger point for FR-7/FR-8's enrollment side effects — this page is a thin UI over the Roster Enrollment Engine, not its own business logic. |\n| FR-5 | Core Courses Bootstrap | \"Create core courses\" dialog: one CORE course per checked subject, enrolls all current section members. Must call the same course-creation path as FR-10 (creating a CORE course always enrolls current members) — one code path, two entry points (bulk vs. single). |\n| FR-6 | Year Rollover | \"Copy sections to next year\": grade level advanced by `order`, no members/teacher. Independent of the enrollment engine — a structural copy only, gated on a future non-current academic year existing. |\n| FR-7 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Auto-enroll on section add: ACTIVE-enrolls into every non-archived CORE course of the section; reactivates DROPPED rather than duplicating. Central business rule — same reactivate-vs-duplicate semantics FR-9/FR-10 must share. |\n| FR-8 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Auto-drop on section removal: CORE enrollments → DROPPED + `droppedAt`; electives untouched. Mirror of FR-7; both must be designed as one named module (e.g. `enrollInSectionCoreCourses` / `dropSectionCoreCourses`), not inlined per call site. |\n| FR-9 | Roster Enrollment Engine | `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` — FR-7 enroll + FR-8 drop in one DB transaction. The only place FR-7+FR-8 compose; confirms both must be transaction-safe, composable functions rather than route-level logic. |\n| FR-10 | Core Courses Bootstrap | New CORE course on a section enrolls all current members (ACTIVE). Same enroll path as FR-7 — triggered from course-creation instead of membership-add. |\n| FR-11 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Capacity enforcement: CONFLICT error with exact message pattern, \"Override capacity\" escape hatch. A guard that must sit in front of every enroll path (FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, and the course-level \"Add students\" of FR-15) — one shared capacity-check function, not four. |\n| FR-12 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Dropped enrollments keep historical data visible to admin/teacher but vanish from active rosters and add-student pickers. A query-filtering concern (`status = ACTIVE` everywhere user-facing lists are built) layered on top of FR-8's state transition. |\n| FR-13 | Admin Courses UI | `/admin/courses` list: filters (year/grade/subject/teacher/kind/search), reuses `Subject.color`. Read-only view, same shape as FR-2 but for courses. |\n| FR-14 | Admin Courses UI | Course create/edit dialog: subject, section (required iff kind=CORE), teacher + up to 3 co-teachers, auto-filled uppercase code. Validation rule (\"section required iff CORE\") needs to live in one shared validator the dialog and the API route both call. |\n| FR-15 | Admin Courses UI | `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment`: roster table with drop/reactivate + add-students picker; CORE courses show an info note (membership managed via section). This page's \"Add students\" must still run through FR-11's capacity guard even though it bypasses the section-membership trigger. |\n| FR-16 | Course Public Surface | `/courses/[courseId]` header: subject colour band, teachers incl. co-teachers, section, room. Read-only composition of FR-1 data, gated by FR-18's `assertCanViewCourse`. |\n| FR-17 | Course Public Surface | New `src/config/course-tabs.ts` registry (mirrors `student-tabs.ts`, adds `roles`), registers Overview + Roster tabs with per-role visibility (student sees classmates' names only; parent tab hidden). Roster tab's student-facing truncation is also NFR-4's privacy rule — same tab, two render paths by role. |\n| FR-18 | Auth/Access Control | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`: `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse`. The authorization chokepoint every course route (FR-15, FR-16, FR-23) and the course-tabs registry (FR-17) must call — do not re-derive role logic per route. Built on top of NFR-7's existing `requireRole` stand-in, not a new auth primitive. |\n| FR-19 | My Courses Page | `/my-courses`: role-specific MUI Card grids (teacher/student/parent-by-child). Read view composing FR-18's access rules per role; parent grouping needs whatever parent-link read path already exists (brownfield reuse, same pattern as the prior PRD's family fan-out). |\n| FR-20 | Navigation | Sidebar entries: \"My courses\" (TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT) + \"Sections\"/\"Courses\" under an \"Administration\" group for ADMIN. **MEDIUM confidence / flagged blocker**: `NavItem` has no `group` field today and no other admin pages exist yet. `arch-design-system` must decide: add a lightweight `group` field now, or ship flat entries until a dedicated admin-nav PRD lands — this is an explicit architect decision point, not a detail to infer silently. |\n| FR-21 | Student Tab Integration | Register `student-tabs.ts` \"Courses\" tab: student's courses, section, homeroom teacher. Pure read view, no new service — reuses FR-1 data + FR-18-equivalent visibility (whoever can view the student). |\n| FR-22 | Auth/Access Control | Extend `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)`: TEACHER additionally sees students via taught/co-taught course enrollments and their homeroom section. A brownfield extension to an existing exported function — must preserve its existing signature/contract for current PRD-01/PRD-04 callers, only add to the TEACHER branch. |\n| FR-23 | REST API Surface | Full endpoint list (sections CRUD+members+move-section+core-courses+copy-to-year; courses CRUD+roster+enrollments+status PATCH; `GET /api/me/courses`) — to be finalized verbatim by `arch-api-contracts`, following the existing envelope/pagination/search conventions. Every endpoint must map 1:1 to a service already named above (FR-7/FR-8/FR-9/FR-11 enrollment engine, FR-18 access control) — no net-new business logic at the route layer. |\n| FR-24 | Audit Logging | Every `section.*`/`course.*`/`enrollment.*` write records an `AuditLog` row via the existing `audit()` helper. A cross-cutting call that belongs at the service layer (alongside FR-7/FR-8/FR-9/FR-11's shared functions), not duplicated per route handler. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every visible element across sections/courses/enrollment screens is MUI/MUI-X only (DataTable, Autocomplete, Tabs, Dialog, Drawer, `useToast()`), looked up via the MUI MCP server first; no Tailwind/shadcn/Radix/react-select. Applies uniformly — unlike the prior PRD, there's no template-rendering exemption needed here (no React Email in scope). |\n| NFR-2 | Data Model | One-section-per-student-per-year enforced by the DB unique constraint on `SectionMember`, not just app code — directly backs FR-1's schema and is the safety net under FR-3's app-level homeroom-teacher-uniqueness check (which has no DB constraint and must be designed knowing that). |\n| NFR-3 | Performance | 30 students × 8 core courses (240 enrollments) in under 1s — a batching requirement on FR-7's auto-enroll path specifically; `arch-design-system` should spec `createMany`/batched writes the same way the enrollment engine is designed, not per-row inserts. |\n| NFR-4 | Privacy/Roster Scrubbing | Students see classmates' names only on the Roster tab and `GET /api/courses/:id/roster` — no email/admission number/profile link. A response-shape rule on FR-17's Roster tab and FR-23's roster endpoint; must be enforced server-side at the API layer (FR-23), not just hidden in the FR-17 UI. |\n| NFR-5 | Test Harness | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green; add unit/integration/Playwright tests per Test Requirements. Scopes what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for; the roster engine (FR-7/FR-8/FR-9/FR-11) and capacity enforcement (FR-11) are the highest-value test targets given their reuse across routes. |\n| NFR-6 | Scope Discipline | No timetable slots, no course content, no prerequisites/course-request workflows, no automatic year-to-year promotion (only the manual FR-6 copy). Bounds `arch-design-system`'s design the same way it bounds dev's — don't let FR-6's \"copy\" grow into a promotion workflow. |\n| NFR-7 | Auth/Access Control | **Flagged blocker (MEDIUM confidence)**: `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` / `requireUser()` described in Platform Context do not exist yet — only `requireRole.ts` and `student-access.ts` are present (same gap PRD-04 flagged). New routes in this PRD (FR-23) must use the existing `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` stand-in rather than invent a new helper, until PRD-01 lands. This directly constrains FR-18's `course-access.ts` implementation — it should wrap `requireRole`, not assume `permissions.ts` exists. |\n\n## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **One enrollment engine, four callers**: FR-7 (add to section), FR-8\n  (remove from section), FR-9 (move-section transaction), and FR-10 (new\n  CORE course) all drive the same enroll/drop/reactivate semantics, and\n  FR-11's capacity guard plus FR-24's audit call must sit in front of/behind\n  all four. Design this as named, reusable service functions (e.g.\n  `enrollSectionCoreCourses`, `dropSectionCoreCourses`,\n  `checkCapacityOrThrow`), not duplicated per route — FR-9's single-transaction\n  requirement is the clearest signal these must already be composable,\n  transaction-safe units.\n- **FR-20's nav-grouping question is an explicit decision point**, not a\n  detail to quietly resolve — `handoff-to-architect.json` lists it as a\n  blocker. Record the chosen approach (add `group` to `NavItem` vs. flat\n  entries) in `system-design.md`'s Overview per Compliance Rule 5.\n- **NFR-7's auth-helper gap is also a carried-forward blocker** — FR-18's\n  `course-access.ts` must be designed against today's `requireRole.ts`\n  stand-in, not the not-yet-built `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()`. Surface\n  this explicitly in `system-design.md`'s Overview so `dev-planning` doesn't\n  schedule work against auth helpers that don't exist.\n- **Two independent app-level uniqueness rules have no DB backstop and need\n  an explicit concurrency decision**: FR-3's \"one homeroom teacher per\n  section per year\" and FR-14's \"section required iff kind=CORE\" are both\n  service-layer validations only (unlike NFR-2's DB-constrained rule) —\n  `arch-design-system` should say where each is checked and whether a race\n  (two concurrent section edits) is acceptable risk or needs a DB-level\n  constraint too.\n- **NFR-4's roster scrubbing must be enforced at the API layer (FR-23),\n  not just the FR-17 UI tab** — call this out explicitly in the\n  traceability table so the response-shape rule isn't treated as\n  presentation-only.\n- **FR-5 and FR-10 share one course-creation-enrolls-members code path** —\n  bulk (checked subjects) vs. single (one course) are two entry points into\n  the same underlying function, same pattern as the enrollment engine note\n  above.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015nfX9eFUJKHAj3nAaRRboc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
