{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghRZZv6NGv52Z8aMvu6o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've finished `arch-research-reqs` for ticket abcd-1 and written `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`. The table has one row for each of the 49 requirements (FR-1 to FR-37 and NFR-1 to NFR-12), and every id matches `requirements.json`.\n\nThe old file at that path was left over from a different ticket (abcd-05, the Sections/Courses PRD), so I overwrote it. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` come from that same earlier run. I left them alone because they belong to other sub-tasks, but the later sub-tasks will need to regenerate them.\n\nChecking the code on disk changed some of what intake reported:\n- **`requireRole()` call sites:** there are about 48 calls across 42 files, not about 94. Every one of those files already has async code, so making `requireRole()` async (blocker 3) only means adding `await` at each call. I recommended going async. The returned user must still include `{id, role}` so `course-access.ts` compiles without changes.\n- **Error codes:** `src/server/http.ts` already defines UNAUTHENTICATED, FORBIDDEN, RATE_LIMITED and CONFLICT, so no new error handling is needed.\n- **Pages:** `/forbidden` already exists, so `requireRole()` can redirect there from server pages.\n- **mui-mcp:** the mui-mcp tools are available in this environment, so blocker 4 looks resolved. Dev should still check before writing any UI.\n\nI flagged these design questions for `arch-design-system`:\n- **Middleware:** it runs on the edge, which can't load Prisma or bcrypt. The Auth.js settings need to be split into an edge-safe file for middleware and a full Node file for everything else.\n- **Changing your own password:** the change sets `passwordChangedAt`, which would log out the user's current session as well as their others. The current session needs to be re-issued.\n- **Cross-site request forgery:** Auth.js only protects its own endpoints. The four custom POST routes (accept-invite, forgot-password, reset-password, account/password) need their own protection.\n- **Small shared pieces:**\n  - one helper to read the client IP, used by both rate limiters and `audit()`\n  - whether the common-password list is sent to the browser for the live checklist\n  - whether forgot-password returns 429 or stays silent when the per-email limit is hit\n- **Rate limiter:** it's in-memory, so it only works with a single server process. That's fine for this PRD."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7491,"cache_read_input_tokens":39831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7491},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83d095ee-6e06-44f2-a07e-b304e1e0dcfe","uuid":"d1c147c4-27a3-4542-aea5-43a929ea2b60","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:35:53.135Z","request_id":"req_011CghRZZeir3sLtFW1H7qsC"}
