{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0191zFS6W259XkcwYT9Rm7Ar","type":"tool_result","content":"architect\ndev\ndev-planning\nintake\ntelemetry\n\nartifacts/architect:\napi-contracts.json\nhandoff-to-dev-planning.json\nrequirements-analysis-notes.md\nsystem-design.md\ntech-stack-decisions.md\nthreat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/dev:\ndev-rerun-count.json\n\nartifacts/dev-planning:\nfile-ownership-matrix.json\nfile-structure.md\nimplementation-plan.json\nmodule-dependencies.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n\nartifacts/telemetry:\napi-retries.jsonl\ndaemon-handoff.json\nknowledge-log.jsonl\nmetering.jsonl\nphase-sessions.json\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-04: Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma already declares enum EmailStatus and the models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox. None of the 4 existing migrations (init, user_management_profiles, classes_enrollment, auth_reconcile) creates them, so this ticket needs a new migration.\",\n    \"The schema has additive divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: Notification.updatedAt and EmailOutbox.updatedAt (the EmailOutbox one is used as the 'flipped to SENDING' timestamp for stuck-row recovery), plus a NotificationPreference.user relation with onDelete Cascade. Keep them. They are consistent with the platform rule that every model has createdAt and updatedAt.\",\n    \"The env vars are already declared in src/lib/env.ts and .env.example: EMAIL_TRANSPORT (default console), SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET and APP_URL. Do not redeclare them.\",\n    \"@react-email/components 0.0.25, @react-email/render 1.0.1, nodemailer ^6.9.14 and @types/nodemailer are already in package.json. No new dependencies are needed.\",\n    \"package.json already defines \\\"worker:email\\\": \\\"tsx scripts/worker-email.ts\\\". The scripts/ directory does not exist yet.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts already contains the 'Notifications' (/notifications, all roles) and 'Email log' (/admin/email-log, ADMIN) entries. Do not add them again.\",\n    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has the PRD-00 placeholder bell (an IconButton with NotificationsNoneIcon inside a Tooltip). FR-6 replaces it.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/email.ts sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) currently only logs the link. Its callers are src/server/services/users.ts:396 (invite) and src/server/services/auth.ts:54 (password-reset). Keep the signature and change only the body to enqueue to the outbox.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts already exports requireUser(), requireRole(), requirePageUser() and requirePageRole(). Reuse them.\",\n    \"UserStatus has ACTIVE, INVITED, DISABLED and ARCHIVED, and User also has archivedAt. For notify(), 'archived or disabled' means status in (DISABLED, ARCHIVED) or archivedAt set.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings already has name, shortName, logoUrl, addressLine1 and addressLine2, which the email base layout header and footer can use.\",\n    \"useToast() lives at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts, not under src/components/shared/. Reuse the existing hook and do not create a second one.\",\n    \"These directories do not exist yet: src/server/notifications/, src/server/email/, src/app/api/notifications/, src/app/api/internal/, src/app/api/admin/, src/app/(app)/notifications/, src/app/(app)/account/ and src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Persist the EmailStatus enum and the Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models (with indexes [userId, readAt, createdAt] and [status, nextAttemptAt]) through a new Prisma migration, keeping the existing additive updatedAt columns.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model; brownfield: no existing migration creates these tables\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES as a typed record: key → { label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Restrict notification categories to ACCOUNT, ACADEMIC, ATTENDANCE, COMMUNICATION, FINANCE and SYSTEM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Register the types account.invite and account.password_reset (email only, hidden from preferences) and system.test (admin test message).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Type notify()'s `type` parameter as keyof NOTIFICATION_TYPES so TypeScript rejects unknown keys, and let later PRDs extend the registry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1; Goals #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"For each recipient, notify() skips archived or disabled users and resolves preferences from NotificationPreference rows, falling back to registry defaults.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"notify() creates a Notification row when in-app is enabled or the type is mandatoryInApp.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"notify() enqueues an EmailOutbox row (rendered HTML and text) when email is enabled for the type and the user has an email address.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"notify() uses createMany so that 1,000 recipients take at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"notify() never throws to the caller. Failures are logged via logger, and callers invoke it after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }), which expands each student to the student plus all linked parents (via ParentStudentLink), deduplicated.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Build email templates in src/server/email/templates/ with @react-email/components, rendered to both HTML and plain text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Create a base email layout with a school logo and name header (from SchoolSettings), a content area, and a footer containing the school address, a 'Manage email preferences' link to /account/notifications, and the sentence 'You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Create templates invite (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), password-reset (link, 60-minute expiry notice) and generic-notification (title, body, CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Change the body of the existing sendAuthEmail() in src/server/auth/email.ts to enqueue the invite / password-reset template to EmailOutbox instead of only logging, keeping its signature and callers unchanged.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.4; §Summary; AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }). It selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, then marks them SENT (with sentAt) or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"On send failure, increment attempts, record lastError and back off 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes for attempts 1–5. Set FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2; AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, protected by 'Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}'. It returns { sent, failed, retried } and returns 401 when the token is missing or wrong.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3; §API; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Create scripts/worker-email.ts (already wired to `npm run worker:email`), a Node loop that calls dispatchEmails every 15 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Provide an email transport selected by EMAIL_TRANSPORT. 'smtp' uses Nodemailer with SMTP_* and EMAIL_FROM. 'console' (the dev default) logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell in shell.tsx with an MUI IconButton + Badge showing the unread count, displayed as '9+' above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"The bell polls GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30 seconds while the tab is visible and pauses when visibilitychange reports hidden.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; §Out of Scope (no websockets)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications. Unread items are bold with a dot, and each item shows its title, the body clamped to 2 lines, and a relative time such as '5 min ago'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Clicking a bell item marks it read and navigates to its link. The popover footer has 'Mark all as read' and 'View all' (/notifications).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: a paginated list (20 per page), All / Unread filter tabs, a category filter, bulk 'Mark all as read', and a per-row read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days. The dispatcher endpoint calls it at most about once per day, tracking the last run in memory (re-running after a restart is acceptable).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Build the /account/notifications preferences page: an MUI Table grouped by category, listing each type visible to the user's role with its label, description, an 'In app' Switch and an 'Email' Switch. Types marked email-only or hidden (account.*) are excluded.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"On the preferences page, mandatoryInApp types show a disabled 'In app' Switch with the tooltip 'Required by the school'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; Goals #3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately through PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI, and roll back with a toast on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Build the /admin/email-log page: a table of created, recipient, subject, status, attempts and last error, with a status filter.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Retry now' row action for FAILED email-log rows that resets attempts = 0, status = PENDING and nextAttemptAt = now.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1; §API POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Send test notification to me' admin button that calls notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [currentAdmin] }) via POST /api/admin/notifications/test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.2; §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications (?unread=true&category=&page=&pageSize=), returning only the caller's own notifications in the standard list shape.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications/unread-count, returning { data: { count } } for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /:id/unread, restricted to the owner (a non-owner gets 404 or 403), and POST /api/notifications/read-all for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/me/notification-preferences, which returns the caller's preferences merged with registry defaults and filtered to the caller's role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Expose PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with body { type, inApp, email }, validated by Zod. It upserts the row and refuses inApp=false for mandatoryInApp types with VALIDATION_ERROR.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/admin/email-log (paginated, ?status= filter) and POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, both ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 system.test notifications linking to /dashboard for each of student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test (one read, two unread), idempotently.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data (wording '3 sample notifications for student… and parent…' is read as 3 per user; idempotency inferred from existing seed.ts convention)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Zod validators for the notification and preference payloads live in src/lib/validators/notifications.ts and are shared by client and API.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (Validation row; validators/<feature>.ts)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Performance: notify() for 1,000 recipients completes in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the unread-count endpoint responds in under 50 ms, backed by the [userId, readAt, createdAt] index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Latency: no user request waits on SMTP. Emails are only enqueued in-request and are dispatched within 60 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals #2; §Background\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Reliability: an email is never sent twice by concurrent dispatchers, enforced with row locking (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Reliability: rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes (judged by updatedAt) are returned to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Security: notification link values must be relative paths starting with '/' and are validated to prevent open redirects. Protocol-relative '//' and backslash forms must be rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3 (the '//' rejection is MEDIUM, inferred from the open-redirect intent)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: email HTML escapes all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Security: every route enforces access server-side through requireUser/requireRole. Admin routes are ADMIN only, and the dispatch route checks CRON_SECRET (a missing CRON_SECRET env means always 401).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole); §API Role column; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Deliverability: every email has HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at APP_URL/account/notifications.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: all UI uses MUI only (@mui/material v9, @mui/icons-material, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs, then fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, notistack, sonner, etc.) must not be imported, and email templates are exempt via @react-email/components. QA must verify this. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §UI component rule (mandatory) items 1–6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Conventions: route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON) and use the standard response/error shapes and pagination (?page, ?pageSize default 20, max 100). New services go under src/server/notifications/ and src/server/email/. Use logger instead of console.log, except in the console email transport.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Timestamps are stored in UTC, and relative and absolute times are displayed in the SchoolSettings.timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps); applied to bell/list/email-log display\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: reuse existing models, helpers and navigation entries. Never rename existing routes or models, never re-scaffold, and keep `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"Tests (unit): preference resolution, retry backoff calculation, link validation, and notifyStudentAndParents expansion and dedupe.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Tests (integration, test DB): dispatcher locking with two concurrent calls, and stuck-SENDING recovery.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"Tests (Playwright): the bell count updates after a test notification, mark all as read works, and a preference toggle persists.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-17\", \"description\": \"Scope: SMS, mobile push, websockets and digest emails are out of scope and must not be built.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-18\", \"description\": \"Field limits: title is at most 140 characters, body at most 500 characters of plain text. notify() truncates or validates against these.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 schema comments (enforcement point inferred)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    { \"id\": \"AC-1\", \"text\": \"Default preferences + notify(system.test) → 1 Notification row + 1 EmailOutbox row; bell count +1 within 30 s.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-8\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-23\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-2\", \"text\": \"Parent turned email off for a type → only the in-app row is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-7\", \"FR-9\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-3\", \"text\": \"SMTP failure → attempts=1, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt ≈ now+1 min; after 5 failures FAILED and visible in the admin email log.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-18\", \"FR-31\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-4\", \"text\": \"Two concurrent dispatchers over 10 pending emails → each sent exactly once.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-17\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-15\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-5\", \"text\": \"Clicking a bell notification marks it read and navigates to its link.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-25\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-6\", \"text\": \"Dispatch without the correct bearer token → 401.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-19\", \"NFR-8\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-7\", \"text\": \"Admin resends an invite → an EmailOutbox row with the invite template is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-16\"] }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-40: Should the seed create 3 notifications per user (6 total) or 3 total across both users?\",\n        \"FR-28: The PRD calls the preferences view an MUI Table with 'ListSubheader-style' group rows. Is a full-width TableRow header per category acceptable?\",\n        \"FR-4: account.invite and account.password_reset are 'email only'. Should notify() skip in-app rows for them (sendAuthEmail enqueues directly rather than via notify())?\",\n        \"NFR-18: Should an over-length title/body be truncated silently or rejected? notify() must never throw.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-40: no interactive answer available. Defaulting to 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread each).\",\n        \"FR-28: defaulting to a full-width TableRow category header inside an MUI Table.\",\n        \"FR-4: defaulting to sendAuthEmail enqueuing the outbox directly with no Notification row (the types are registered with an email-only flag so preferences hide them).\",\n        \"NFR-18: defaulting to truncation with a logger.warn, since notify() must not throw.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:02:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 59,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"FR-1: The Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models exist in schema.prisma, but no migration creates them, so a new migration is required. Keep the additive updatedAt columns, because EmailOutbox.updatedAt backs the NFR-5 stuck-row recovery.\",\n    \"FR-4/FR-16: Default decision: sendAuthEmail() enqueues the outbox directly and creates no Notification row. The account.* types are registered as email-only and hidden from preferences. The Architect should confirm.\",\n    \"FR-40: The seed count is ambiguous. The default is 3 notifications per user (1 read, 2 unread each).\",\n    \"NFR-10: Dev must reach the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6976ca3f-645f-4a29-bf49-9d0601ccb133","uuid":"738ad75c-05c0-4e1f-b6e1-ce721e78374a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:59:12.859Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"architect\ndev\ndev-planning\nintake\ntelemetry\n\nartifacts/architect:\napi-contracts.json\nhandoff-to-dev-planning.json\nrequirements-analysis-notes.md\nsystem-design.md\ntech-stack-decisions.md\nthreat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/dev:\ndev-rerun-count.json\n\nartifacts/dev-planning:\nfile-ownership-matrix.json\nfile-structure.md\nimplementation-plan.json\nmodule-dependencies.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n\nartifacts/telemetry:\napi-retries.jsonl\ndaemon-handoff.json\nknowledge-log.jsonl\nmetering.jsonl\nphase-sessions.json\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-04: Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma already declares enum EmailStatus and the models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox. None of the 4 existing migrations (init, user_management_profiles, classes_enrollment, auth_reconcile) creates them, so this ticket needs a new migration.\",\n    \"The schema has additive divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: Notification.updatedAt and EmailOutbox.updatedAt (the EmailOutbox one is used as the 'flipped to SENDING' timestamp for stuck-row recovery), plus a NotificationPreference.user relation with onDelete Cascade. Keep them. They are consistent with the platform rule that every model has createdAt and updatedAt.\",\n    \"The env vars are already declared in src/lib/env.ts and .env.example: EMAIL_TRANSPORT (default console), SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET and APP_URL. Do not redeclare them.\",\n    \"@react-email/components 0.0.25, @react-email/render 1.0.1, nodemailer ^6.9.14 and @types/nodemailer are already in package.json. No new dependencies are needed.\",\n    \"package.json already defines \\\"worker:email\\\": \\\"tsx scripts/worker-email.ts\\\". The scripts/ directory does not exist yet.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts already contains the 'Notifications' (/notifications, all roles) and 'Email log' (/admin/email-log, ADMIN) entries. Do not add them again.\",\n    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has the PRD-00 placeholder bell (an IconButton with NotificationsNoneIcon inside a Tooltip). FR-6 replaces it.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/email.ts sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) currently only logs the link. Its callers are src/server/services/users.ts:396 (invite) and src/server/services/auth.ts:54 (password-reset). Keep the signature and change only the body to enqueue to the outbox.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts already exports requireUser(), requireRole(), requirePageUser() and requirePageRole(). Reuse them.\",\n    \"UserStatus has ACTIVE, INVITED, DISABLED and ARCHIVED, and User also has archivedAt. For notify(), 'archived or disabled' means status in (DISABLED, ARCHIVED) or archivedAt set.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings already has name, shortName, logoUrl, addressLine1 and addressLine2, which the email base layout header and footer can use.\",\n    \"useToast() lives at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts, not under src/components/shared/. Reuse the existing hook and do not create a second one.\",\n    \"These directories do not exist yet: src/server/notifications/, src/server/email/, src/app/api/notifications/, src/app/api/internal/, src/app/api/admin/, src/app/(app)/notifications/, src/app/(app)/account/ and src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Persist the EmailStatus enum and the Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models (with indexes [userId, readAt, createdAt] and [status, nextAttemptAt]) through a new Prisma migration, keeping the existing additive updatedAt columns.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model; brownfield: no existing migration creates these tables\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES as a typed record: key → { label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Restrict notification categories to ACCOUNT, ACADEMIC, ATTENDANCE, COMMUNICATION, FINANCE and SYSTEM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Register the types account.invite and account.password_reset (email only, hidden from preferences) and system.test (admin test message).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Type notify()'s `type` parameter as keyof NOTIFICATION_TYPES so TypeScript rejects unknown keys, and let later PRDs extend the registry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1; Goals #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"For each recipient, notify() skips archived or disabled users and resolves preferences from NotificationPreference rows, falling back to registry defaults.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"notify() creates a Notification row when in-app is enabled or the type is mandatoryInApp.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"notify() enqueues an EmailOutbox row (rendered HTML and text) when email is enabled for the type and the user has an email address.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"notify() uses createMany so that 1,000 recipients take at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"notify() never throws to the caller. Failures are logged via logger, and callers invoke it after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }), which expands each student to the student plus all linked parents (via ParentStudentLink), deduplicated.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Build email templates in src/server/email/templates/ with @react-email/components, rendered to both HTML and plain text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Create a base email layout with a school logo and name header (from SchoolSettings), a content area, and a footer containing the school address, a 'Manage email preferences' link to /account/notifications, and the sentence 'You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Create templates invite (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), password-reset (link, 60-minute expiry notice) and generic-notification (title, body, CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Change the body of the existing sendAuthEmail() in src/server/auth/email.ts to enqueue the invite / password-reset template to EmailOutbox instead of only logging, keeping its signature and callers unchanged.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.4; §Summary; AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }). It selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, then marks them SENT (with sentAt) or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"On send failure, increment attempts, record lastError and back off 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes for attempts 1–5. Set FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2; AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, protected by 'Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}'. It returns { sent, failed, retried } and returns 401 when the token is missing or wrong.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3; §API; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Create scripts/worker-email.ts (already wired to `npm run worker:email`), a Node loop that calls dispatchEmails every 15 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Provide an email transport selected by EMAIL_TRANSPORT. 'smtp' uses Nodemailer with SMTP_* and EMAIL_FROM. 'console' (the dev default) logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell in shell.tsx with an MUI IconButton + Badge showing the unread count, displayed as '9+' above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"The bell polls GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30 seconds while the tab is visible and pauses when visibilitychange reports hidden.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; §Out of Scope (no websockets)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications. Unread items are bold with a dot, and each item shows its title, the body clamped to 2 lines, and a relative time such as '5 min ago'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Clicking a bell item marks it read and navigates to its link. The popover footer has 'Mark all as read' and 'View all' (/notifications).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: a paginated list (20 per page), All / Unread filter tabs, a category filter, bulk 'Mark all as read', and a per-row read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days. The dispatcher endpoint calls it at most about once per day, tracking the last run in memory (re-running after a restart is acceptable).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Build the /account/notifications preferences page: an MUI Table grouped by category, listing each type visible to the user's role with its label, description, an 'In app' Switch and an 'Email' Switch. Types marked email-only or hidden (account.*) are excluded.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"On the preferences page, mandatoryInApp types show a disabled 'In app' Switch with the tooltip 'Required by the school'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; Goals #3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately through PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI, and roll back with a toast on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Build the /admin/email-log page: a table of created, recipient, subject, status, attempts and last error, with a status filter.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Retry now' row action for FAILED email-log rows that resets attempts = 0, status = PENDING and nextAttemptAt = now.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1; §API POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Send test notification to me' admin button that calls notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [currentAdmin] }) via POST /api/admin/notifications/test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.2; §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications (?unread=true&category=&page=&pageSize=), returning only the caller's own notifications in the standard list shape.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications/unread-count, returning { data: { count } } for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /:id/unread, restricted to the owner (a non-owner gets 404 or 403), and POST /api/notifications/read-all for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/me/notification-preferences, which returns the caller's preferences merged with registry defaults and filtered to the caller's role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Expose PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with body { type, inApp, email }, validated by Zod. It upserts the row and refuses inApp=false for mandatoryInApp types with VALIDATION_ERROR.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/admin/email-log (paginated, ?status= filter) and POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, both ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 system.test notifications linking to /dashboard for each of student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test (one read, two unread), idempotently.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data (wording '3 sample notifications for student… and parent…' is read as 3 per user; idempotency inferred from existing seed.ts convention)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Zod validators for the notification and preference payloads live in src/lib/validators/notifications.ts and are shared by client and API.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (Validation row; validators/<feature>.ts)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Performance: notify() for 1,000 recipients completes in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the unread-count endpoint responds in under 50 ms, backed by the [userId, readAt, createdAt] index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Latency: no user request waits on SMTP. Emails are only enqueued in-request and are dispatched within 60 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals #2; §Background\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Reliability: an email is never sent twice by concurrent dispatchers, enforced with row locking (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Reliability: rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes (judged by updatedAt) are returned to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Security: notification link values must be relative paths starting with '/' and are validated to prevent open redirects. Protocol-relative '//' and backslash forms must be rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3 (the '//' rejection is MEDIUM, inferred from the open-redirect intent)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: email HTML escapes all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Security: every route enforces access server-side through requireUser/requireRole. Admin routes are ADMIN only, and the dispatch route checks CRON_SECRET (a missing CRON_SECRET env means always 401).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole); §API Role column; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Deliverability: every email has HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at APP_URL/account/notifications.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: all UI uses MUI only (@mui/material v9, @mui/icons-material, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs, then fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, notistack, sonner, etc.) must not be imported, and email templates are exempt via @react-email/components. QA must verify this. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §UI component rule (mandatory) items 1–6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Conventions: route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON) and use the standard response/error shapes and pagination (?page, ?pageSize default 20, max 100). New services go under src/server/notifications/ and src/server/email/. Use logger instead of console.log, except in the console email transport.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Timestamps are stored in UTC, and relative and absolute times are displayed in the SchoolSettings.timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps); applied to bell/list/email-log display\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: reuse existing models, helpers and navigation entries. Never rename existing routes or models, never re-scaffold, and keep `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"Tests (unit): preference resolution, retry backoff calculation, link validation, and notifyStudentAndParents expansion and dedupe.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Tests (integration, test DB): dispatcher locking with two concurrent calls, and stuck-SENDING recovery.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"Tests (Playwright): the bell count updates after a test notification, mark all as read works, and a preference toggle persists.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-17\", \"description\": \"Scope: SMS, mobile push, websockets and digest emails are out of scope and must not be built.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-18\", \"description\": \"Field limits: title is at most 140 characters, body at most 500 characters of plain text. notify() truncates or validates against these.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 schema comments (enforcement point inferred)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    { \"id\": \"AC-1\", \"text\": \"Default preferences + notify(system.test) → 1 Notification row + 1 EmailOutbox row; bell count +1 within 30 s.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-8\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-23\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-2\", \"text\": \"Parent turned email off for a type → only the in-app row is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-7\", \"FR-9\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-3\", \"text\": \"SMTP failure → attempts=1, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt ≈ now+1 min; after 5 failures FAILED and visible in the admin email log.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-18\", \"FR-31\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-4\", \"text\": \"Two concurrent dispatchers over 10 pending emails → each sent exactly once.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-17\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-15\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-5\", \"text\": \"Clicking a bell notification marks it read and navigates to its link.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-25\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-6\", \"text\": \"Dispatch without the correct bearer token → 401.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-19\", \"NFR-8\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-7\", \"text\": \"Admin resends an invite → an EmailOutbox row with the invite template is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-16\"] }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-40: Should the seed create 3 notifications per user (6 total) or 3 total across both users?\",\n        \"FR-28: The PRD calls the preferences view an MUI Table with 'ListSubheader-style' group rows. Is a full-width TableRow header per category acceptable?\",\n        \"FR-4: account.invite and account.password_reset are 'email only'. Should notify() skip in-app rows for them (sendAuthEmail enqueues directly rather than via notify())?\",\n        \"NFR-18: Should an over-length title/body be truncated silently or rejected? notify() must never throw.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-40: no interactive answer available. Defaulting to 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread each).\",\n        \"FR-28: defaulting to a full-width TableRow category header inside an MUI Table.\",\n        \"FR-4: defaulting to sendAuthEmail enqueuing the outbox directly with no Notification row (the types are registered with an email-only flag so preferences hide them).\",\n        \"NFR-18: defaulting to truncation with a logger.warn, since notify() must not throw.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:02:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 59,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"FR-1: The Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models exist in schema.prisma, but no migration creates them, so a new migration is required. Keep the additive updatedAt columns, because EmailOutbox.updatedAt backs the NFR-5 stuck-row recovery.\",\n    \"FR-4/FR-16: Default decision: sendAuthEmail() enqueues the outbox directly and creates no Notification row. The account.* types are registered as email-only and hidden from preferences. The Architect should confirm.\",\n    \"FR-40: The seed count is ambiguous. The default is 3 notifications per user (1 read, 2 unread each).\",\n    \"NFR-10: Dev must reach the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0191zFS6W259XkcwYT9Rm7Ar","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
