{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTNzBH2qaKiSzW3RD3D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough to write the notes. Three brownfield corrections came up: the middleware would 401 the cron route, the seed has no student or parent users, and vitest doesn't include integration tests."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":302,"cache_read_input_tokens":46399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":302},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6976ca3f-645f-4a29-bf49-9d0601ccb133","uuid":"ec77f8f5-8ef8-412d-8fca-ebf606acddb6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:59:36.598Z","request_id":"req_011CghTNyyNHTTUv3cHc4cGh"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTNzBH2qaKiSzW3RD3D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CBZYa2oAVyftJa8ze5TzYj","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-4\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`. That file covers PRD-04 Notifications & Email\nInfrastructure (41 FR and 18 NFR, so 59 requirements) at 93% confidence, with 4 blockers in\n`handoff-to-architect.json`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\nConcern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Type Registry**, **Notify Service**,\n**Preference Resolution**, **Email Rendering**, **Auth Email Seam**, **Outbox Dispatcher**,\n**Transport**, **Background Job**, **Internal Endpoint**, **User API**, **Admin API**,\n**UI: Bell**, **UI: Notifications Page**, **UI: Preferences Page**, **UI: Admin Email Log**,\n**Validation**, **Seed**, **Security**, **Performance**, **Reliability**, **Conventions**,\n**Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these add to or correct intake)\n\n| # | Finding | Impact |\n|---|---------|--------|\n| B1 | `src/middleware.ts` returns **401 for any `/api/*` request without a session** unless `isPublicPath()` matches. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is only `['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`. | The cron call to `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` carries no session cookie, so it would be rejected by middleware before the handler runs. **`/api/internal/` must be added to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** (prefix match). The handler then becomes the only gate, so its CRON_SECRET check must be strict (NFR-8). The middleware's cross-origin guard does not block it, because cron calls send no `Origin` header. |\n| B2 | `prisma/seed.ts` (95 lines) seeds only SchoolSettings and academic reference data. **There are no `student@schoolhub.test` or `parent@schoolhub.test` users** anywhere in `prisma/` or `src/`. | FR-40 cannot simply attach notifications to existing users. Options: (a) look up those users by email and skip with a log line when they are missing, or (b) upsert minimal STUDENT/PARENT users. Recommend (a). It keeps the seed idempotent and avoids PRD-04 creating identity data that another PRD owns. Design should confirm. |\n| B3 | `vitest.config.ts` includes only `tests/unit/**` and uses `environment: 'jsdom'`. There is no `tests/integration/` folder and no test-DB setup. | NFR-15 needs a node environment plus a real Postgres to exercise `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`. This requires a separate vitest project or config (e.g. `vitest.integration.config.ts`, `environment: 'node'`, `include: tests/integration/**`) that is skipped when `DATABASE_URL_TEST` is absent, so that `npm run test` stays green (NFR-13). |\n| B4 | `EmailOutbox` has **no `userId` and no `type` column**. It stores only `toEmail`, `toName`, `subject`, `html`, `text`, `status`, `attempts`, `lastError`, `nextAttemptAt`, `sentAt`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. | The admin email log (FR-31) can only show recipient email and name, not a user link or type. That is sufficient for FR-31, so the schema should not change (NFR-13). `sendAuthEmail` (FR-16) fits naturally because it has no type. |\n| B5 | `NotificationPreference` uses a composite PK `@@id([userId, type])`. | FR-38's upsert keys on `userId_type`. FR-7's resolution reads with `findMany({ where: { userId: { in }, type } })`, which is a single query. |\n| B6 | `src/server/http.ts` already exports `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parsePagination` (default 20, max 100), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. `ApiErrorCode` already includes `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `NOT_FOUND`, `UNAUTHENTICATED` and `FORBIDDEN`. | All new route handlers reuse these (NFR-11). No new error codes are needed. |\n| B7 | `src/lib/dates.ts` exports `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, timezone)` (date-fns-tz). `SchoolSettings.timezone` defaults to `'UTC'`. `src/server/services/settings.ts` exists. | NFR-12 reuses these. Relative times (\"5 min ago\") are timezone-independent. Absolute times in the email log and the invite expiry date use `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| B8 | `src/server/rate-limit.ts` exports an in-memory `rateLimit()`. | It could optionally guard `POST /api/admin/notifications/test`, but no requirement asks for that. Skip it under compliance rule 1. |\n| B9 | `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx`, `Toast/useToast.ts`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader` and `DateDisplay` exist. | FR-26 and FR-31 reuse DataTable, PageHeader and EmptyState. FR-30 reuses `useToast`. Do not create duplicates. |\n| B10 | Prisma `$transaction` is used in `src/server/sections/`. No `$queryRaw` is used anywhere yet. | FR-17's `SKIP LOCKED` claim is the first raw SQL in the repo. Use tagged `$queryRaw` (parameterised) inside `$transaction`, or a single `UPDATE … WHERE id IN (SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *` statement, which claims rows atomically without holding a transaction across SMTP. |\n| B11 | All other intake brownfield findings were confirmed: there is no migration for the three models, the env vars and `worker:email` script are present, the navigation entries exist, `sendAuthEmail` has exactly 2 callers (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`), and the `requireRole` helpers exist. | — |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |\n|-----|----------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | One new migration `2026110400xxxx_notifications_email`. It creates `EmailStatus`, `Notification`, `NotificationPreference` and `EmailOutbox` exactly as `schema.prisma` declares them, including the additive `updatedAt` columns and both indexes. Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and do not edit `schema.prisma`. It must sort after `20261104000000_auth_reconcile`. |\n| FR-2 | Type Registry | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` exports `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` with `as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>`, which keeps literal keys for FR-5 while type-checking the shape. Add one field, `emailOnly?: true` (or `hidden`), to express FR-4. |\n| FR-3 | Type Registry | `NotificationCategory` is a string-literal union of the 6 values, not a Prisma enum, because the DB stores `type` as a free `String`. The UI groups by category (FR-26, FR-28). |\n| FR-4 | Type Registry, Auth Email Seam | `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are `emailOnly`, hidden from preferences and never passed to `notify()` (blocker default confirmed in \"Decisions for design\" below). `system.test` uses category SYSTEM, `defaultEmail: true` and all roles (AC-1 expects both rows). |\n| FR-5 | Type Registry | `type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. Later PRDs extend the registry by editing this one file, and no plugin mechanism is needed (YAGNI). |\n| FR-6 | Notify Service | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` is a pure server module. Its `email.template` param is a key into the template map (FR-13), and `data` is typed per template. |\n| FR-7 | Preference Resolution | Load users with `findMany({ id in userIds, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` and prefs with `findMany({ userId in, type })`. Then resolve each user with a pure function `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }`, which is unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| FR-8 | Notify Service | `inApp = row?.inApp ?? true`, with `mandatoryInApp` forcing true. Notifications are written with `createMany`. |\n| FR-9 | Notify Service, Email Rendering | `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` and requires `user.email`. Render once per recipient, because templates contain the name. Rendering cost dominates NFR-1, so `render()` calls should run with bounded `Promise.all` concurrency. Rows are written to `EmailOutbox` with `createMany`. |\n| FR-10 | Performance | 1,000 recipients means 3 round-trips: users, prefs and one `createMany`, per channel. Chunk `createMany` at about 500 rows only if the parameter limit bites (Postgres allows 65,535 params, and Notification has about 7 columns, so 1,000 rows fit in one call). |\n| FR-11 | Notify Service | Wrap the whole body in try/catch, call `logger.error`, and return `void` or a `{ notified, emailed }` summary. Callers invoke it after commit. Document that in JSDoc. |\n| FR-12 | Notify Service | `notifyStudentAndParents` makes one `ParentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call (indexed on `studentId`), merges into a `Set`, then calls `notify`. Expansion and dedupe are a pure function so they can be unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| FR-13 | Email Rendering | `src/server/email/templates/*.tsx` with `@react-email/components`. `src/server/email/render.ts` calls `render(el)` and `render(el, { plainText: true })` from `@react-email/render` 1.0.1, which is async. |\n| FR-14 | Email Rendering | `BaseLayout.tsx` takes `school: Pick<SchoolSettings, name, logoUrl, addressLine1, addressLine2>`. Fetch SchoolSettings once per `notify()` / `sendAuthEmail` call, not once per recipient. The footer link is `APP_URL/account/notifications`. |\n| FR-15 | Email Rendering | There are 3 templates. Invite needs an expiry date, which `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` does not receive. The template can derive it from the known invite TTL constant in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, so the signature stays unchanged. Password reset uses the hardcoded 60-minute notice. The generic CTA href is `APP_URL + link` (the link is already validated by NFR-6). |\n| FR-16 | Auth Email Seam | Only the body of `src/server/auth/email.ts` changes: render the template and call `prisma.emailOutbox.create`. Its 2 callers are untouched. Unlike `notify()`, failures here **should** surface, because the existing callers already handle errors and a silently lost invite is worse. Design should decide whether to keep the current awaited and throwable behaviour (recommended). |\n| FR-17 | Outbox Dispatcher | `src/server/email/dispatch.ts`. First, run stuck-row recovery (NFR-5). Next, claim rows with one atomic `UPDATE … SET status='SENDING', updatedAt=now() WHERE id IN (SELECT id … WHERE status='PENDING' AND nextAttemptAt<=now() ORDER BY nextAttemptAt LIMIT $n FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *`. Then send each row outside any transaction and update it individually. |\n| FR-18 | Outbox Dispatcher | A pure function `backoffMinutes(attempts) → [1,5,15,60,240][attempts-1]`, plus `attempts >= 5 → FAILED`. It is unit-tested (NFR-14). `lastError` is truncated to about 1,000 characters. |\n| FR-19 | Internal Endpoint | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`. Compare the bearer token against `env.CRON_SECRET` with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. A missing env value always returns 401. The response is `{ data: { sent, failed, retried } }` via `ok()`. **Requires B1** (the middleware allowlist). The route also triggers FR-27. |\n| FR-20 | Background Job | `scripts/worker-email.ts` imports `dispatchEmails` directly (tsx resolves the `@/` alias via tsconfig paths) and runs a `setTimeout` loop every 15 s with SIGINT/SIGTERM handling. It does not go over HTTP and does not call purge, because purge belongs to the endpoint only (FR-27). |\n| FR-21 | Transport | `src/server/email/transport.ts` exports `getTransport()` with 2 branches. `smtp` uses `nodemailer.createTransport` with SMTP_* settings and is memoised. `console` uses `console.log`, which NFR-11 explicitly allows. Each message includes `List-Unsubscribe` (NFR-9). Missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` under `smtp` should fail at transport creation, and the dispatcher must record that as a retryable `lastError`, not crash. |\n| FR-22 | UI: Bell | The `'use client'` component `NotificationBell.tsx` replaces the placeholder in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`. It uses MUI `Badge` with `max={9}`, which renders \"9+\" natively, so no custom formatting is needed. |\n| FR-23 | UI: Bell | A `setInterval` of 30 s gated on `document.visibilityState`, plus an immediate refetch on `visibilitychange → visible`. There is no SWR or react-query dependency, so plain `fetch` is enough. |\n| FR-24 | UI: Bell | `Popover` + `List` + `ListItemButton`. Unread items use bold `fontWeight` and a `Badge variant=\"dot\"` or small Box. The body is clamped with `sx={{ WebkitLineClamp: 2 }}`. Relative time uses `date-fns` `formatDistanceToNowStrict` (date-fns-tz is already installed, so date-fns is too). The popover fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10` on open. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Bell | On click, call `POST /:id/read`, then `router.push(link)`, then close. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" (`POST /read-all`) and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |\n| FR-26 | UI: Notifications Page | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` is a server shell using `requirePageUser()` and a client list. It has `Tabs` (All/Unread), a category `Select`, the pagination from DataTable or MUI `Pagination` with a page size of 20, and a per-row toggle calling `/:id/read` or `/:id/unread`. |\n| FR-27 | Background Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` (`deleteMany createdAt < now-180d`) lives in `src/server/notifications/`. A module-level `let lastPurgeAt` in the dispatch route allows at most one run per 24 h per process. It is best-effort, and its failure is logged and must not fail the dispatch response. |\n| FR-28 | UI: Preferences Page | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`. This is the first page under `/account/`, so the directory is new. It is an MUI `Table` with a full-width category header `TableRow` (the intake default is accepted) and data from `GET /api/me/notification-preferences`. |\n| FR-29 | UI: Preferences Page | `Tooltip` around a **span** wrapping the disabled `Switch`, because MUI Tooltip does not fire on disabled elements. |\n| FR-30 | UI: Preferences Page | Optimistic local state, `PUT`, and on error revert plus `useToast().error(...)`. |\n| FR-31 | UI: Admin Email Log | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` uses `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` with DataTable and a status `Select`. The recipient column shows `toName <toEmail>` (B4). |\n| FR-32 | Admin API, UI: Admin Email Log | The retry action is shown only when `status==='FAILED'`. The server guard uses `updateMany where { id, status: FAILED }`, and a count of 0 returns 409 CONFLICT or 404, so a double click is harmless. |\n| FR-33 | Admin API | `POST /api/admin/notifications/test` uses `requireRole('ADMIN')`, then `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title, body, link: '/dashboard' })`. The button sits on the email-log page because no separate admin page is needed. |\n| FR-34 | User API | `GET /api/notifications` uses `parseQuery` with Zod (`unread`, `category`), `parsePagination` and `paginated()`. **Category filter caveat:** Notification has no category column. Filter by the `type IN (keys of registry with that category)` derived from the registry at request time. This needs no schema change and remains index-compatible with `userId` leading. |\n| FR-35 | User API | `count({ where: { userId, readAt: null } })` is covered by the `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index (NFR-2). |\n| FR-36 | User API | Mark read or unread with `updateMany({ where: { id, userId: me.id } })`. A count of 0 returns 404, which hides existence from non-owners. `read-all` runs `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null })`. Route files: `[id]/read/route.ts`, `[id]/unread/route.ts` and `read-all/route.ts`. **Next.js routing note:** `read-all` and `unread-count` are static siblings of `[id]`, and static segments win, so they do not conflict. |\n| FR-37 | User API, Preference Resolution | `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` (GET and PUT in one file) is the first route under `/api/me/`. It filters the registry by `roles.includes(me.role)` and `!emailOnly`, merges the rows and returns `{ type, label, description, category, inApp, email, mandatoryInApp }[]`. |\n| FR-38 | User API, Validation | The Zod body is `{ type: z.enum(visibleTypeKeys), inApp: boolean, email: boolean }`. The service rejects `inApp=false` for mandatory types and role-invisible or `emailOnly` types with `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR')`, then calls `upsert` on `userId_type`. |\n| FR-39 | Admin API | `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` (GET) and `[id]/retry/route.ts` (POST), both protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The list is ordered by `createdAt desc` and **omits `html` and `text`** to keep the payload small. |\n| FR-40 | Seed | The seed appends to `prisma/seed.ts`. **See B2: the target users do not exist.** For idempotency, skip a user who already has any `system.test` notification (count > 0), giving 3 per user with 1 read and 2 unread, linking to `/dashboard`. |\n| FR-41 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` is a sibling of the existing `auth.ts`, `users.ts` and so on. It holds the list query schema, the preference PUT schema and `safeLink` (NFR-6). It must be client-safe: no server imports, so registry keys are passed in or the type is checked as a string and then against the registry in the service. |\n| NFR-1 | Performance | The budget of 2 s for 1,000 recipients is dominated by 1,000 react-email renders. Mitigate with SchoolSettings fetched once, bounded concurrency, and rendering only recipients with email enabled. If renders are too slow, render the generic template once with a name placeholder. Design should note this as the fallback. |\n| NFR-2 | Performance | Covered by the FR-1 index and FR-35 query shape. The bell must not call the list endpoint on every poll. |\n| NFR-3 | Reliability | No SMTP happens in the request path: `notify()` and `sendAuthEmail` only insert rows. The 15 s worker or the cron endpoint keeps delivery under 60 s. |\n| NFR-4 | Reliability | The FR-17 atomic claim with `SKIP LOCKED`. Each claimed row is owned by exactly one dispatcher. |\n| NFR-5 | Reliability | At the start of each dispatch: `updateMany({ status: SENDING, updatedAt < now-10m }, { status: PENDING })`. This relies on the additive `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`, which is why FR-1 keeps it. It does not increment attempts, because a crash mid-send was not proven to be a send failure. |\n| NFR-6 | Security | A shared `isSafeLink(s)` requires `s.startsWith('/')` and rejects `//`, `/\\`, any `\\` and control characters. It is applied in `notify()` (drop or nullify the link and warn instead of throwing, per FR-11) and in the Zod schema. Unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| NFR-7 | Security | React-email JSX escapes interpolated text by default. **Never** use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in templates. Body text is rendered as text with `white-space: pre-line`, not as HTML. |\n| NFR-8 | Security | Every new handler starts with `requireUser()` or `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The internal route uses a secret check only (B1). Pages use `requirePageUser()` or `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. |\n| NFR-9 | Security, Transport | Each `sendMail` call sets `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<APP_URL/account/notifications>' }` along with both `html` and `text`. Set it at send time rather than storing it in the outbox, because the outbox has no headers column (B4). |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions (UI) | All 4 UI surfaces (bell, notifications page, preferences page, email log) use MUI only. Dev must query mui-mcp before writing UI, and **this is an unresolved blocker carried forward**: if the server is unreachable, there is a hard stop. The existing `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned libs. Email templates are exempt. |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | Thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok`/`paginated`. Services live in `src/server/notifications/` and `src/server/email/`, and code uses `logger`, with `console` only in the console transport. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | UTC storage is the Prisma default. Display uses `formatInSchoolTz` (B7). The client components need the timezone, so pass it from the server page as a prop. |\n| NFR-13 | Conventions | Do not touch `schema.prisma`, navigation or env. Keep the `sendAuthEmail` signature. Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. This is the source of B1–B3 handling. |\n| NFR-14 | Test Harness | Pure units are `resolvePrefs`, `backoffMinutes`, `isSafeLink` and `expandStudentRecipients`. They go in `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`, run under the existing vitest config and need no DB. |\n| NFR-15 | Test Harness | **See B3.** A new `tests/integration/` folder with a node-env vitest config against a test DB. One test runs 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails` calls over 10 rows and asserts each row is sent once. A second test backdates a SENDING row's `updatedAt` by 11 minutes and asserts recovery. |\n| NFR-16 | Test Harness | Playwright tests go in `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`. They need a logged-in admin (the existing e2e harness pattern; check `dashboard.spec.ts` for auth setup). The flow is send test → bell count → mark all read → preference toggle persists after reload. |\n| NFR-17 | Scope Discipline | No SMS, push, websockets or digests. Polling only (FR-23), and do not add a `channel` abstraction for future SMS. |\n| NFR-18 | Notify Service | Silently truncate `title` to 140 characters and `body` to 500, with `logger.warn` (intake default accepted, since it is consistent with FR-11). There is no DB constraint, because the schema has plain `String`. |\n\n## Decisions for design (resolving intake blockers)\n\n1. **FR-1 migration**: Accepted. There is one new migration, `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `schema.prisma` is not changed.\n2. **FR-4/FR-16**: Accepted. `sendAuthEmail` enqueues directly and creates no Notification row. The `account.*` types are `emailOnly` and are filtered out of FR-28 and FR-37 and rejected by FR-38.\n3. **FR-40**: Use 3 per user, but the users are missing (B2). The recommendation is to look them up and skip if absent.\n4. **NFR-10**: Carried forward to dev as a precondition, because the architect cannot resolve it.\n5. **New**: Add `/api/internal/` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` (B1). Without it, AC-6 still passes (401), but real cron dispatch never works.\n\n## New/changed files implied (for arch-design-system to confirm)\n\n- **New**: `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/`, `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,purge}.ts`, `src/server/email/{transport,render,dispatch}.ts`, `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`, `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`, `src/app/api/notifications/{route,unread-count/route,read-all/route,[id]/read/route,[id]/unread/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/{route,[id]/retry/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `scripts/worker-email.ts`, plus tests under `tests/unit`, `tests/integration` and `tests/e2e`.\n- **Modified**: `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (bell), `src/config/public-routes.ts` (one entry), `prisma/seed.ts` (append), and possibly `package.json` (`test:integration` script only).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":302,"cache_read_input_tokens":46399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":302},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6976ca3f-645f-4a29-bf49-9d0601ccb133","uuid":"f4fc516b-6918-4a77-aa2b-334478f6a842","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:01:00.632Z","request_id":"req_011CghTNyyNHTTUv3cHc4cGh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CBZYa2oAVyftJa8ze5TzYj":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-4\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`. That file covers PRD-04 Notifications & Email\nInfrastructure (41 FR and 18 NFR, so 59 requirements) at 93% confidence, with 4 blockers in\n`handoff-to-architect.json`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\nConcern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Type Registry**, **Notify Service**,\n**Preference Resolution**, **Email Rendering**, **Auth Email Seam**, **Outbox Dispatcher**,\n**Transport**, **Background Job**, **Internal Endpoint**, **User API**, **Admin API**,\n**UI: Bell**, **UI: Notifications Page**, **UI: Preferences Page**, **UI: Admin Email Log**,\n**Validation**, **Seed**, **Security**, **Performance**, **Reliability**, **Conventions**,\n**Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these add to or correct intake)\n\n| # | Finding | Impact |\n|---|---------|--------|\n| B1 | `src/middleware.ts` returns **401 for any `/api/*` request without a session** unless `isPublicPath()` matches. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is only `['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`. | The cron call to `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` carries no session cookie, so it would be rejected by middleware before the handler runs. **`/api/internal/` must be added to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** (prefix match). The handler then becomes the only gate, so its CRON_SECRET check must be strict (NFR-8). The middleware's cross-origin guard does not block it, because cron calls send no `Origin` header. |\n| B2 | `prisma/seed.ts` (95 lines) seeds only SchoolSettings and academic reference data. **There are no `student@schoolhub.test` or `parent@schoolhub.test` users** anywhere in `prisma/` or `src/`. | FR-40 cannot simply attach notifications to existing users. Options: (a) look up those users by email and skip with a log line when they are missing, or (b) upsert minimal STUDENT/PARENT users. Recommend (a). It keeps the seed idempotent and avoids PRD-04 creating identity data that another PRD owns. Design should confirm. |\n| B3 | `vitest.config.ts` includes only `tests/unit/**` and uses `environment: 'jsdom'`. There is no `tests/integration/` folder and no test-DB setup. | NFR-15 needs a node environment plus a real Postgres to exercise `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`. This requires a separate vitest project or config (e.g. `vitest.integration.config.ts`, `environment: 'node'`, `include: tests/integration/**`) that is skipped when `DATABASE_URL_TEST` is absent, so that `npm run test` stays green (NFR-13). |\n| B4 | `EmailOutbox` has **no `userId` and no `type` column**. It stores only `toEmail`, `toName`, `subject`, `html`, `text`, `status`, `attempts`, `lastError`, `nextAttemptAt`, `sentAt`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. | The admin email log (FR-31) can only show recipient email and name, not a user link or type. That is sufficient for FR-31, so the schema should not change (NFR-13). `sendAuthEmail` (FR-16) fits naturally because it has no type. |\n| B5 | `NotificationPreference` uses a composite PK `@@id([userId, type])`. | FR-38's upsert keys on `userId_type`. FR-7's resolution reads with `findMany({ where: { userId: { in }, type } })`, which is a single query. |\n| B6 | `src/server/http.ts` already exports `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parsePagination` (default 20, max 100), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. `ApiErrorCode` already includes `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `NOT_FOUND`, `UNAUTHENTICATED` and `FORBIDDEN`. | All new route handlers reuse these (NFR-11). No new error codes are needed. |\n| B7 | `src/lib/dates.ts` exports `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, timezone)` (date-fns-tz). `SchoolSettings.timezone` defaults to `'UTC'`. `src/server/services/settings.ts` exists. | NFR-12 reuses these. Relative times (\"5 min ago\") are timezone-independent. Absolute times in the email log and the invite expiry date use `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| B8 | `src/server/rate-limit.ts` exports an in-memory `rateLimit()`. | It could optionally guard `POST /api/admin/notifications/test`, but no requirement asks for that. Skip it under compliance rule 1. |\n| B9 | `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx`, `Toast/useToast.ts`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader` and `DateDisplay` exist. | FR-26 and FR-31 reuse DataTable, PageHeader and EmptyState. FR-30 reuses `useToast`. Do not create duplicates. |\n| B10 | Prisma `$transaction` is used in `src/server/sections/`. No `$queryRaw` is used anywhere yet. | FR-17's `SKIP LOCKED` claim is the first raw SQL in the repo. Use tagged `$queryRaw` (parameterised) inside `$transaction`, or a single `UPDATE … WHERE id IN (SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *` statement, which claims rows atomically without holding a transaction across SMTP. |\n| B11 | All other intake brownfield findings were confirmed: there is no migration for the three models, the env vars and `worker:email` script are present, the navigation entries exist, `sendAuthEmail` has exactly 2 callers (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`), and the `requireRole` helpers exist. | — |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |\n|-----|----------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | One new migration `2026110400xxxx_notifications_email`. It creates `EmailStatus`, `Notification`, `NotificationPreference` and `EmailOutbox` exactly as `schema.prisma` declares them, including the additive `updatedAt` columns and both indexes. Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and do not edit `schema.prisma`. It must sort after `20261104000000_auth_reconcile`. |\n| FR-2 | Type Registry | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` exports `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` with `as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>`, which keeps literal keys for FR-5 while type-checking the shape. Add one field, `emailOnly?: true` (or `hidden`), to express FR-4. |\n| FR-3 | Type Registry | `NotificationCategory` is a string-literal union of the 6 values, not a Prisma enum, because the DB stores `type` as a free `String`. The UI groups by category (FR-26, FR-28). |\n| FR-4 | Type Registry, Auth Email Seam | `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are `emailOnly`, hidden from preferences and never passed to `notify()` (blocker default confirmed in \"Decisions for design\" below). `system.test` uses category SYSTEM, `defaultEmail: true` and all roles (AC-1 expects both rows). |\n| FR-5 | Type Registry | `type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. Later PRDs extend the registry by editing this one file, and no plugin mechanism is needed (YAGNI). |\n| FR-6 | Notify Service | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` is a pure server module. Its `email.template` param is a key into the template map (FR-13), and `data` is typed per template. |\n| FR-7 | Preference Resolution | Load users with `findMany({ id in userIds, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` and prefs with `findMany({ userId in, type })`. Then resolve each user with a pure function `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }`, which is unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| FR-8 | Notify Service | `inApp = row?.inApp ?? true`, with `mandatoryInApp` forcing true. Notifications are written with `createMany`. |\n| FR-9 | Notify Service, Email Rendering | `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` and requires `user.email`. Render once per recipient, because templates contain the name. Rendering cost dominates NFR-1, so `render()` calls should run with bounded `Promise.all` concurrency. Rows are written to `EmailOutbox` with `createMany`. |\n| FR-10 | Performance | 1,000 recipients means 3 round-trips: users, prefs and one `createMany`, per channel. Chunk `createMany` at about 500 rows only if the parameter limit bites (Postgres allows 65,535 params, and Notification has about 7 columns, so 1,000 rows fit in one call). |\n| FR-11 | Notify Service | Wrap the whole body in try/catch, call `logger.error`, and return `void` or a `{ notified, emailed }` summary. Callers invoke it after commit. Document that in JSDoc. |\n| FR-12 | Notify Service | `notifyStudentAndParents` makes one `ParentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call (indexed on `studentId`), merges into a `Set`, then calls `notify`. Expansion and dedupe are a pure function so they can be unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| FR-13 | Email Rendering | `src/server/email/templates/*.tsx` with `@react-email/components`. `src/server/email/render.ts` calls `render(el)` and `render(el, { plainText: true })` from `@react-email/render` 1.0.1, which is async. |\n| FR-14 | Email Rendering | `BaseLayout.tsx` takes `school: Pick<SchoolSettings, name, logoUrl, addressLine1, addressLine2>`. Fetch SchoolSettings once per `notify()` / `sendAuthEmail` call, not once per recipient. The footer link is `APP_URL/account/notifications`. |\n| FR-15 | Email Rendering | There are 3 templates. Invite needs an expiry date, which `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` does not receive. The template can derive it from the known invite TTL constant in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, so the signature stays unchanged. Password reset uses the hardcoded 60-minute notice. The generic CTA href is `APP_URL + link` (the link is already validated by NFR-6). |\n| FR-16 | Auth Email Seam | Only the body of `src/server/auth/email.ts` changes: render the template and call `prisma.emailOutbox.create`. Its 2 callers are untouched. Unlike `notify()`, failures here **should** surface, because the existing callers already handle errors and a silently lost invite is worse. Design should decide whether to keep the current awaited and throwable behaviour (recommended). |\n| FR-17 | Outbox Dispatcher | `src/server/email/dispatch.ts`. First, run stuck-row recovery (NFR-5). Next, claim rows with one atomic `UPDATE … SET status='SENDING', updatedAt=now() WHERE id IN (SELECT id … WHERE status='PENDING' AND nextAttemptAt<=now() ORDER BY nextAttemptAt LIMIT $n FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *`. Then send each row outside any transaction and update it individually. |\n| FR-18 | Outbox Dispatcher | A pure function `backoffMinutes(attempts) → [1,5,15,60,240][attempts-1]`, plus `attempts >= 5 → FAILED`. It is unit-tested (NFR-14). `lastError` is truncated to about 1,000 characters. |\n| FR-19 | Internal Endpoint | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`. Compare the bearer token against `env.CRON_SECRET` with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. A missing env value always returns 401. The response is `{ data: { sent, failed, retried } }` via `ok()`. **Requires B1** (the middleware allowlist). The route also triggers FR-27. |\n| FR-20 | Background Job | `scripts/worker-email.ts` imports `dispatchEmails` directly (tsx resolves the `@/` alias via tsconfig paths) and runs a `setTimeout` loop every 15 s with SIGINT/SIGTERM handling. It does not go over HTTP and does not call purge, because purge belongs to the endpoint only (FR-27). |\n| FR-21 | Transport | `src/server/email/transport.ts` exports `getTransport()` with 2 branches. `smtp` uses `nodemailer.createTransport` with SMTP_* settings and is memoised. `console` uses `console.log`, which NFR-11 explicitly allows. Each message includes `List-Unsubscribe` (NFR-9). Missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` under `smtp` should fail at transport creation, and the dispatcher must record that as a retryable `lastError`, not crash. |\n| FR-22 | UI: Bell | The `'use client'` component `NotificationBell.tsx` replaces the placeholder in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`. It uses MUI `Badge` with `max={9}`, which renders \"9+\" natively, so no custom formatting is needed. |\n| FR-23 | UI: Bell | A `setInterval` of 30 s gated on `document.visibilityState`, plus an immediate refetch on `visibilitychange → visible`. There is no SWR or react-query dependency, so plain `fetch` is enough. |\n| FR-24 | UI: Bell | `Popover` + `List` + `ListItemButton`. Unread items use bold `fontWeight` and a `Badge variant=\"dot\"` or small Box. The body is clamped with `sx={{ WebkitLineClamp: 2 }}`. Relative time uses `date-fns` `formatDistanceToNowStrict` (date-fns-tz is already installed, so date-fns is too). The popover fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10` on open. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Bell | On click, call `POST /:id/read`, then `router.push(link)`, then close. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" (`POST /read-all`) and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |\n| FR-26 | UI: Notifications Page | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` is a server shell using `requirePageUser()` and a client list. It has `Tabs` (All/Unread), a category `Select`, the pagination from DataTable or MUI `Pagination` with a page size of 20, and a per-row toggle calling `/:id/read` or `/:id/unread`. |\n| FR-27 | Background Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` (`deleteMany createdAt < now-180d`) lives in `src/server/notifications/`. A module-level `let lastPurgeAt` in the dispatch route allows at most one run per 24 h per process. It is best-effort, and its failure is logged and must not fail the dispatch response. |\n| FR-28 | UI: Preferences Page | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`. This is the first page under `/account/`, so the directory is new. It is an MUI `Table` with a full-width category header `TableRow` (the intake default is accepted) and data from `GET /api/me/notification-preferences`. |\n| FR-29 | UI: Preferences Page | `Tooltip` around a **span** wrapping the disabled `Switch`, because MUI Tooltip does not fire on disabled elements. |\n| FR-30 | UI: Preferences Page | Optimistic local state, `PUT`, and on error revert plus `useToast().error(...)`. |\n| FR-31 | UI: Admin Email Log | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` uses `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` with DataTable and a status `Select`. The recipient column shows `toName <toEmail>` (B4). |\n| FR-32 | Admin API, UI: Admin Email Log | The retry action is shown only when `status==='FAILED'`. The server guard uses `updateMany where { id, status: FAILED }`, and a count of 0 returns 409 CONFLICT or 404, so a double click is harmless. |\n| FR-33 | Admin API | `POST /api/admin/notifications/test` uses `requireRole('ADMIN')`, then `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title, body, link: '/dashboard' })`. The button sits on the email-log page because no separate admin page is needed. |\n| FR-34 | User API | `GET /api/notifications` uses `parseQuery` with Zod (`unread`, `category`), `parsePagination` and `paginated()`. **Category filter caveat:** Notification has no category column. Filter by the `type IN (keys of registry with that category)` derived from the registry at request time. This needs no schema change and remains index-compatible with `userId` leading. |\n| FR-35 | User API | `count({ where: { userId, readAt: null } })` is covered by the `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index (NFR-2). |\n| FR-36 | User API | Mark read or unread with `updateMany({ where: { id, userId: me.id } })`. A count of 0 returns 404, which hides existence from non-owners. `read-all` runs `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null })`. Route files: `[id]/read/route.ts`, `[id]/unread/route.ts` and `read-all/route.ts`. **Next.js routing note:** `read-all` and `unread-count` are static siblings of `[id]`, and static segments win, so they do not conflict. |\n| FR-37 | User API, Preference Resolution | `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` (GET and PUT in one file) is the first route under `/api/me/`. It filters the registry by `roles.includes(me.role)` and `!emailOnly`, merges the rows and returns `{ type, label, description, category, inApp, email, mandatoryInApp }[]`. |\n| FR-38 | User API, Validation | The Zod body is `{ type: z.enum(visibleTypeKeys), inApp: boolean, email: boolean }`. The service rejects `inApp=false` for mandatory types and role-invisible or `emailOnly` types with `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR')`, then calls `upsert` on `userId_type`. |\n| FR-39 | Admin API | `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` (GET) and `[id]/retry/route.ts` (POST), both protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The list is ordered by `createdAt desc` and **omits `html` and `text`** to keep the payload small. |\n| FR-40 | Seed | The seed appends to `prisma/seed.ts`. **See B2: the target users do not exist.** For idempotency, skip a user who already has any `system.test` notification (count > 0), giving 3 per user with 1 read and 2 unread, linking to `/dashboard`. |\n| FR-41 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` is a sibling of the existing `auth.ts`, `users.ts` and so on. It holds the list query schema, the preference PUT schema and `safeLink` (NFR-6). It must be client-safe: no server imports, so registry keys are passed in or the type is checked as a string and then against the registry in the service. |\n| NFR-1 | Performance | The budget of 2 s for 1,000 recipients is dominated by 1,000 react-email renders. Mitigate with SchoolSettings fetched once, bounded concurrency, and rendering only recipients with email enabled. If renders are too slow, render the generic template once with a name placeholder. Design should note this as the fallback. |\n| NFR-2 | Performance | Covered by the FR-1 index and FR-35 query shape. The bell must not call the list endpoint on every poll. |\n| NFR-3 | Reliability | No SMTP happens in the request path: `notify()` and `sendAuthEmail` only insert rows. The 15 s worker or the cron endpoint keeps delivery under 60 s. |\n| NFR-4 | Reliability | The FR-17 atomic claim with `SKIP LOCKED`. Each claimed row is owned by exactly one dispatcher. |\n| NFR-5 | Reliability | At the start of each dispatch: `updateMany({ status: SENDING, updatedAt < now-10m }, { status: PENDING })`. This relies on the additive `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`, which is why FR-1 keeps it. It does not increment attempts, because a crash mid-send was not proven to be a send failure. |\n| NFR-6 | Security | A shared `isSafeLink(s)` requires `s.startsWith('/')` and rejects `//`, `/\\`, any `\\` and control characters. It is applied in `notify()` (drop or nullify the link and warn instead of throwing, per FR-11) and in the Zod schema. Unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| NFR-7 | Security | React-email JSX escapes interpolated text by default. **Never** use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in templates. Body text is rendered as text with `white-space: pre-line`, not as HTML. |\n| NFR-8 | Security | Every new handler starts with `requireUser()` or `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The internal route uses a secret check only (B1). Pages use `requirePageUser()` or `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. |\n| NFR-9 | Security, Transport | Each `sendMail` call sets `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<APP_URL/account/notifications>' }` along with both `html` and `text`. Set it at send time rather than storing it in the outbox, because the outbox has no headers column (B4). |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions (UI) | All 4 UI surfaces (bell, notifications page, preferences page, email log) use MUI only. Dev must query mui-mcp before writing UI, and **this is an unresolved blocker carried forward**: if the server is unreachable, there is a hard stop. The existing `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned libs. Email templates are exempt. |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | Thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok`/`paginated`. Services live in `src/server/notifications/` and `src/server/email/`, and code uses `logger`, with `console` only in the console transport. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | UTC storage is the Prisma default. Display uses `formatInSchoolTz` (B7). The client components need the timezone, so pass it from the server page as a prop. |\n| NFR-13 | Conventions | Do not touch `schema.prisma`, navigation or env. Keep the `sendAuthEmail` signature. Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. This is the source of B1–B3 handling. |\n| NFR-14 | Test Harness | Pure units are `resolvePrefs`, `backoffMinutes`, `isSafeLink` and `expandStudentRecipients`. They go in `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`, run under the existing vitest config and need no DB. |\n| NFR-15 | Test Harness | **See B3.** A new `tests/integration/` folder with a node-env vitest config against a test DB. One test runs 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails` calls over 10 rows and asserts each row is sent once. A second test backdates a SENDING row's `updatedAt` by 11 minutes and asserts recovery. |\n| NFR-16 | Test Harness | Playwright tests go in `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`. They need a logged-in admin (the existing e2e harness pattern; check `dashboard.spec.ts` for auth setup). The flow is send test → bell count → mark all read → preference toggle persists after reload. |\n| NFR-17 | Scope Discipline | No SMS, push, websockets or digests. Polling only (FR-23), and do not add a `channel` abstraction for future SMS. |\n| NFR-18 | Notify Service | Silently truncate `title` to 140 characters and `body` to 500, with `logger.warn` (intake default accepted, since it is consistent with FR-11). There is no DB constraint, because the schema has plain `String`. |\n\n## Decisions for design (resolving intake blockers)\n\n1. **FR-1 migration**: Accepted. There is one new migration, `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `schema.prisma` is not changed.\n2. **FR-4/FR-16**: Accepted. `sendAuthEmail` enqueues directly and creates no Notification row. The `account.*` types are `emailOnly` and are filtered out of FR-28 and FR-37 and rejected by FR-38.\n3. **FR-40**: Use 3 per user, but the users are missing (B2). The recommendation is to look them up and skip if absent.\n4. **NFR-10**: Carried forward to dev as a precondition, because the architect cannot resolve it.\n5. **New**: Add `/api/internal/` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` (B1). Without it, AC-6 still passes (401), but real cron dispatch never works.\n\n## New/changed files implied (for arch-design-system to confirm)\n\n- **New**: `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/`, `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,purge}.ts`, `src/server/email/{transport,render,dispatch}.ts`, `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`, `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`, `src/app/api/notifications/{route,unread-count/route,read-all/route,[id]/read/route,[id]/unread/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/{route,[id]/retry/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `scripts/worker-email.ts`, plus tests under `tests/unit`, `tests/integration` and `tests/e2e`.\n- **Modified**: `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (bell), `src/config/public-routes.ts` (one entry), `prisma/seed.ts` (append), and possibly `package.json` (`test:integration` script only).\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CBZYa2oAVyftJa8ze5TzYj","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6976ca3f-645f-4a29-bf49-9d0601ccb133","uuid":"935cb984-cc43-437f-9b47-f324df8398ec","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:01:00.706Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-4\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`. That file covers PRD-04 Notifications & Email\nInfrastructure (41 FR and 18 NFR, so 59 requirements) at 93% confidence, with 4 blockers in\n`handoff-to-architect.json`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\nConcern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Type Registry**, **Notify Service**,\n**Preference Resolution**, **Email Rendering**, **Auth Email Seam**, **Outbox Dispatcher**,\n**Transport**, **Background Job**, **Internal Endpoint**, **User API**, **Admin API**,\n**UI: Bell**, **UI: Notifications Page**, **UI: Preferences Page**, **UI: Admin Email Log**,\n**Validation**, **Seed**, **Security**, **Performance**, **Reliability**, **Conventions**,\n**Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these add to or correct intake)\n\n| # | Finding | Impact |\n|---|---------|--------|\n| B1 | `src/middleware.ts` returns **401 for any `/api/*` request without a session** unless `isPublicPath()` matches. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is only `['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`. | The cron call to `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` carries no session cookie, so it would be rejected by middleware before the handler runs. **`/api/internal/` must be added to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** (prefix match). The handler then becomes the only gate, so its CRON_SECRET check must be strict (NFR-8). The middleware's cross-origin guard does not block it, because cron calls send no `Origin` header. |\n| B2 | `prisma/seed.ts` (95 lines) seeds only SchoolSettings and academic reference data. **There are no `student@schoolhub.test` or `parent@schoolhub.test` users** anywhere in `prisma/` or `src/`. | FR-40 cannot simply attach notifications to existing users. Options: (a) look up those users by email and skip with a log line when they are missing, or (b) upsert minimal STUDENT/PARENT users. Recommend (a). It keeps the seed idempotent and avoids PRD-04 creating identity data that another PRD owns. Design should confirm. |\n| B3 | `vitest.config.ts` includes only `tests/unit/**` and uses `environment: 'jsdom'`. There is no `tests/integration/` folder and no test-DB setup. | NFR-15 needs a node environment plus a real Postgres to exercise `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`. This requires a separate vitest project or config (e.g. `vitest.integration.config.ts`, `environment: 'node'`, `include: tests/integration/**`) that is skipped when `DATABASE_URL_TEST` is absent, so that `npm run test` stays green (NFR-13). |\n| B4 | `EmailOutbox` has **no `userId` and no `type` column**. It stores only `toEmail`, `toName`, `subject`, `html`, `text`, `status`, `attempts`, `lastError`, `nextAttemptAt`, `sentAt`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. | The admin email log (FR-31) can only show recipient email and name, not a user link or type. That is sufficient for FR-31, so the schema should not change (NFR-13). `sendAuthEmail` (FR-16) fits naturally because it has no type. |\n| B5 | `NotificationPreference` uses a composite PK `@@id([userId, type])`. | FR-38's upsert keys on `userId_type`. FR-7's resolution reads with `findMany({ where: { userId: { in }, type } })`, which is a single query. |\n| B6 | `src/server/http.ts` already exports `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parsePagination` (default 20, max 100), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. `ApiErrorCode` already includes `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `NOT_FOUND`, `UNAUTHENTICATED` and `FORBIDDEN`. | All new route handlers reuse these (NFR-11). No new error codes are needed. |\n| B7 | `src/lib/dates.ts` exports `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, timezone)` (date-fns-tz). `SchoolSettings.timezone` defaults to `'UTC'`. `src/server/services/settings.ts` exists. | NFR-12 reuses these. Relative times (\"5 min ago\") are timezone-independent. Absolute times in the email log and the invite expiry date use `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| B8 | `src/server/rate-limit.ts` exports an in-memory `rateLimit()`. | It could optionally guard `POST /api/admin/notifications/test`, but no requirement asks for that. Skip it under compliance rule 1. |\n| B9 | `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx`, `Toast/useToast.ts`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader` and `DateDisplay` exist. | FR-26 and FR-31 reuse DataTable, PageHeader and EmptyState. FR-30 reuses `useToast`. Do not create duplicates. |\n| B10 | Prisma `$transaction` is used in `src/server/sections/`. No `$queryRaw` is used anywhere yet. | FR-17's `SKIP LOCKED` claim is the first raw SQL in the repo. Use tagged `$queryRaw` (parameterised) inside `$transaction`, or a single `UPDATE … WHERE id IN (SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *` statement, which claims rows atomically without holding a transaction across SMTP. |\n| B11 | All other intake brownfield findings were confirmed: there is no migration for the three models, the env vars and `worker:email` script are present, the navigation entries exist, `sendAuthEmail` has exactly 2 callers (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`), and the `requireRole` helpers exist. | — |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |\n|-----|----------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | One new migration `2026110400xxxx_notifications_email`. It creates `EmailStatus`, `Notification`, `NotificationPreference` and `EmailOutbox` exactly as `schema.prisma` declares them, including the additive `updatedAt` columns and both indexes. Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and do not edit `schema.prisma`. It must sort after `20261104000000_auth_reconcile`. |\n| FR-2 | Type Registry | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` exports `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` with `as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>`, which keeps literal keys for FR-5 while type-checking the shape. Add one field, `emailOnly?: true` (or `hidden`), to express FR-4. |\n| FR-3 | Type Registry | `NotificationCategory` is a string-literal union of the 6 values, not a Prisma enum, because the DB stores `type` as a free `String`. The UI groups by category (FR-26, FR-28). |\n| FR-4 | Type Registry, Auth Email Seam | `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are `emailOnly`, hidden from preferences and never passed to `notify()` (blocker default confirmed in \"Decisions for design\" below). `system.test` uses category SYSTEM, `defaultEmail: true` and all roles (AC-1 expects both rows). |\n| FR-5 | Type Registry | `type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. Later PRDs extend the registry by editing this one file, and no plugin mechanism is needed (YAGNI). |\n| FR-6 | Notify Service | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` is a pure server module. Its `email.template` param is a key into the template map (FR-13), and `data` is typed per template. |\n| FR-7 | Preference Resolution | Load users with `findMany({ id in userIds, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` and prefs with `findMany({ userId in, type })`. Then resolve each user with a pure function `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }`, which is unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| FR-8 | Notify Service | `inApp = row?.inApp ?? true`, with `mandatoryInApp` forcing true. Notifications are written with `createMany`. |\n| FR-9 | Notify Service, Email Rendering | `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` and requires `user.email`. Render once per recipient, because templates contain the name. Rendering cost dominates NFR-1, so `render()` calls should run with bounded `Promise.all` concurrency. Rows are written to `EmailOutbox` with `createMany`. |\n| FR-10 | Performance | 1,000 recipients means 3 round-trips: users, prefs and one `createMany`, per channel. Chunk `createMany` at about 500 rows only if the parameter limit bites (Postgres allows 65,535 params, and Notification has about 7 columns, so 1,000 rows fit in one call). |\n| FR-11 | Notify Service | Wrap the whole body in try/catch, call `logger.error`, and return `void` or a `{ notified, emailed }` summary. Callers invoke it after commit. Document that in JSDoc. |\n| FR-12 | Notify Service | `notifyStudentAndParents` makes one `ParentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call (indexed on `studentId`), merges into a `Set`, then calls `notify`. Expansion and dedupe are a pure function so they can be unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| FR-13 | Email Rendering | `src/server/email/templates/*.tsx` with `@react-email/components`. `src/server/email/render.ts` calls `render(el)` and `render(el, { plainText: true })` from `@react-email/render` 1.0.1, which is async. |\n| FR-14 | Email Rendering | `BaseLayout.tsx` takes `school: Pick<SchoolSettings, name, logoUrl, addressLine1, addressLine2>`. Fetch SchoolSettings once per `notify()` / `sendAuthEmail` call, not once per recipient. The footer link is `APP_URL/account/notifications`. |\n| FR-15 | Email Rendering | There are 3 templates. Invite needs an expiry date, which `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` does not receive. The template can derive it from the known invite TTL constant in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, so the signature stays unchanged. Password reset uses the hardcoded 60-minute notice. The generic CTA href is `APP_URL + link` (the link is already validated by NFR-6). |\n| FR-16 | Auth Email Seam | Only the body of `src/server/auth/email.ts` changes: render the template and call `prisma.emailOutbox.create`. Its 2 callers are untouched. Unlike `notify()`, failures here **should** surface, because the existing callers already handle errors and a silently lost invite is worse. Design should decide whether to keep the current awaited and throwable behaviour (recommended). |\n| FR-17 | Outbox Dispatcher | `src/server/email/dispatch.ts`. First, run stuck-row recovery (NFR-5). Next, claim rows with one atomic `UPDATE … SET status='SENDING', updatedAt=now() WHERE id IN (SELECT id … WHERE status='PENDING' AND nextAttemptAt<=now() ORDER BY nextAttemptAt LIMIT $n FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *`. Then send each row outside any transaction and update it individually. |\n| FR-18 | Outbox Dispatcher | A pure function `backoffMinutes(attempts) → [1,5,15,60,240][attempts-1]`, plus `attempts >= 5 → FAILED`. It is unit-tested (NFR-14). `lastError` is truncated to about 1,000 characters. |\n| FR-19 | Internal Endpoint | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`. Compare the bearer token against `env.CRON_SECRET` with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. A missing env value always returns 401. The response is `{ data: { sent, failed, retried } }` via `ok()`. **Requires B1** (the middleware allowlist). The route also triggers FR-27. |\n| FR-20 | Background Job | `scripts/worker-email.ts` imports `dispatchEmails` directly (tsx resolves the `@/` alias via tsconfig paths) and runs a `setTimeout` loop every 15 s with SIGINT/SIGTERM handling. It does not go over HTTP and does not call purge, because purge belongs to the endpoint only (FR-27). |\n| FR-21 | Transport | `src/server/email/transport.ts` exports `getTransport()` with 2 branches. `smtp` uses `nodemailer.createTransport` with SMTP_* settings and is memoised. `console` uses `console.log`, which NFR-11 explicitly allows. Each message includes `List-Unsubscribe` (NFR-9). Missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` under `smtp` should fail at transport creation, and the dispatcher must record that as a retryable `lastError`, not crash. |\n| FR-22 | UI: Bell | The `'use client'` component `NotificationBell.tsx` replaces the placeholder in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`. It uses MUI `Badge` with `max={9}`, which renders \"9+\" natively, so no custom formatting is needed. |\n| FR-23 | UI: Bell | A `setInterval` of 30 s gated on `document.visibilityState`, plus an immediate refetch on `visibilitychange → visible`. There is no SWR or react-query dependency, so plain `fetch` is enough. |\n| FR-24 | UI: Bell | `Popover` + `List` + `ListItemButton`. Unread items use bold `fontWeight` and a `Badge variant=\"dot\"` or small Box. The body is clamped with `sx={{ WebkitLineClamp: 2 }}`. Relative time uses `date-fns` `formatDistanceToNowStrict` (date-fns-tz is already installed, so date-fns is too). The popover fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10` on open. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Bell | On click, call `POST /:id/read`, then `router.push(link)`, then close. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" (`POST /read-all`) and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |\n| FR-26 | UI: Notifications Page | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` is a server shell using `requirePageUser()` and a client list. It has `Tabs` (All/Unread), a category `Select`, the pagination from DataTable or MUI `Pagination` with a page size of 20, and a per-row toggle calling `/:id/read` or `/:id/unread`. |\n| FR-27 | Background Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` (`deleteMany createdAt < now-180d`) lives in `src/server/notifications/`. A module-level `let lastPurgeAt` in the dispatch route allows at most one run per 24 h per process. It is best-effort, and its failure is logged and must not fail the dispatch response. |\n| FR-28 | UI: Preferences Page | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`. This is the first page under `/account/`, so the directory is new. It is an MUI `Table` with a full-width category header `TableRow` (the intake default is accepted) and data from `GET /api/me/notification-preferences`. |\n| FR-29 | UI: Preferences Page | `Tooltip` around a **span** wrapping the disabled `Switch`, because MUI Tooltip does not fire on disabled elements. |\n| FR-30 | UI: Preferences Page | Optimistic local state, `PUT`, and on error revert plus `useToast().error(...)`. |\n| FR-31 | UI: Admin Email Log | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` uses `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` with DataTable and a status `Select`. The recipient column shows `toName <toEmail>` (B4). |\n| FR-32 | Admin API, UI: Admin Email Log | The retry action is shown only when `status==='FAILED'`. The server guard uses `updateMany where { id, status: FAILED }`, and a count of 0 returns 409 CONFLICT or 404, so a double click is harmless. |\n| FR-33 | Admin API | `POST /api/admin/notifications/test` uses `requireRole('ADMIN')`, then `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title, body, link: '/dashboard' })`. The button sits on the email-log page because no separate admin page is needed. |\n| FR-34 | User API | `GET /api/notifications` uses `parseQuery` with Zod (`unread`, `category`), `parsePagination` and `paginated()`. **Category filter caveat:** Notification has no category column. Filter by the `type IN (keys of registry with that category)` derived from the registry at request time. This needs no schema change and remains index-compatible with `userId` leading. |\n| FR-35 | User API | `count({ where: { userId, readAt: null } })` is covered by the `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index (NFR-2). |\n| FR-36 | User API | Mark read or unread with `updateMany({ where: { id, userId: me.id } })`. A count of 0 returns 404, which hides existence from non-owners. `read-all` runs `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null })`. Route files: `[id]/read/route.ts`, `[id]/unread/route.ts` and `read-all/route.ts`. **Next.js routing note:** `read-all` and `unread-count` are static siblings of `[id]`, and static segments win, so they do not conflict. |\n| FR-37 | User API, Preference Resolution | `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` (GET and PUT in one file) is the first route under `/api/me/`. It filters the registry by `roles.includes(me.role)` and `!emailOnly`, merges the rows and returns `{ type, label, description, category, inApp, email, mandatoryInApp }[]`. |\n| FR-38 | User API, Validation | The Zod body is `{ type: z.enum(visibleTypeKeys), inApp: boolean, email: boolean }`. The service rejects `inApp=false` for mandatory types and role-invisible or `emailOnly` types with `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR')`, then calls `upsert` on `userId_type`. |\n| FR-39 | Admin API | `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` (GET) and `[id]/retry/route.ts` (POST), both protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The list is ordered by `createdAt desc` and **omits `html` and `text`** to keep the payload small. |\n| FR-40 | Seed | The seed appends to `prisma/seed.ts`. **See B2: the target users do not exist.** For idempotency, skip a user who already has any `system.test` notification (count > 0), giving 3 per user with 1 read and 2 unread, linking to `/dashboard`. |\n| FR-41 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` is a sibling of the existing `auth.ts`, `users.ts` and so on. It holds the list query schema, the preference PUT schema and `safeLink` (NFR-6). It must be client-safe: no server imports, so registry keys are passed in or the type is checked as a string and then against the registry in the service. |\n| NFR-1 | Performance | The budget of 2 s for 1,000 recipients is dominated by 1,000 react-email renders. Mitigate with SchoolSettings fetched once, bounded concurrency, and rendering only recipients with email enabled. If renders are too slow, render the generic template once with a name placeholder. Design should note this as the fallback. |\n| NFR-2 | Performance | Covered by the FR-1 index and FR-35 query shape. The bell must not call the list endpoint on every poll. |\n| NFR-3 | Reliability | No SMTP happens in the request path: `notify()` and `sendAuthEmail` only insert rows. The 15 s worker or the cron endpoint keeps delivery under 60 s. |\n| NFR-4 | Reliability | The FR-17 atomic claim with `SKIP LOCKED`. Each claimed row is owned by exactly one dispatcher. |\n| NFR-5 | Reliability | At the start of each dispatch: `updateMany({ status: SENDING, updatedAt < now-10m }, { status: PENDING })`. This relies on the additive `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`, which is why FR-1 keeps it. It does not increment attempts, because a crash mid-send was not proven to be a send failure. |\n| NFR-6 | Security | A shared `isSafeLink(s)` requires `s.startsWith('/')` and rejects `//`, `/\\`, any `\\` and control characters. It is applied in `notify()` (drop or nullify the link and warn instead of throwing, per FR-11) and in the Zod schema. Unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| NFR-7 | Security | React-email JSX escapes interpolated text by default. **Never** use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in templates. Body text is rendered as text with `white-space: pre-line`, not as HTML. |\n| NFR-8 | Security | Every new handler starts with `requireUser()` or `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The internal route uses a secret check only (B1). Pages use `requirePageUser()` or `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. |\n| NFR-9 | Security, Transport | Each `sendMail` call sets `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<APP_URL/account/notifications>' }` along with both `html` and `text`. Set it at send time rather than storing it in the outbox, because the outbox has no headers column (B4). |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions (UI) | All 4 UI surfaces (bell, notifications page, preferences page, email log) use MUI only. Dev must query mui-mcp before writing UI, and **this is an unresolved blocker carried forward**: if the server is unreachable, there is a hard stop. The existing `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned libs. Email templates are exempt. |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | Thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok`/`paginated`. Services live in `src/server/notifications/` and `src/server/email/`, and code uses `logger`, with `console` only in the console transport. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | UTC storage is the Prisma default. Display uses `formatInSchoolTz` (B7). The client components need the timezone, so pass it from the server page as a prop. |\n| NFR-13 | Conventions | Do not touch `schema.prisma`, navigation or env. Keep the `sendAuthEmail` signature. Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. This is the source of B1–B3 handling. |\n| NFR-14 | Test Harness | Pure units are `resolvePrefs`, `backoffMinutes`, `isSafeLink` and `expandStudentRecipients`. They go in `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`, run under the existing vitest config and need no DB. |\n| NFR-15 | Test Harness | **See B3.** A new `tests/integration/` folder with a node-env vitest config against a test DB. One test runs 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails` calls over 10 rows and asserts each row is sent once. A second test backdates a SENDING row's `updatedAt` by 11 minutes and asserts recovery. |\n| NFR-16 | Test Harness | Playwright tests go in `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`. They need a logged-in admin (the existing e2e harness pattern; check `dashboard.spec.ts` for auth setup). The flow is send test → bell count → mark all read → preference toggle persists after reload. |\n| NFR-17 | Scope Discipline | No SMS, push, websockets or digests. Polling only (FR-23), and do not add a `channel` abstraction for future SMS. |\n| NFR-18 | Notify Service | Silently truncate `title` to 140 characters and `body` to 500, with `logger.warn` (intake default accepted, since it is consistent with FR-11). There is no DB constraint, because the schema has plain `String`. |\n\n## Decisions for design (resolving intake blockers)\n\n1. **FR-1 migration**: Accepted. There is one new migration, `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `schema.prisma` is not changed.\n2. **FR-4/FR-16**: Accepted. `sendAuthEmail` enqueues directly and creates no Notification row. The `account.*` types are `emailOnly` and are filtered out of FR-28 and FR-37 and rejected by FR-38.\n3. **FR-40**: Use 3 per user, but the users are missing (B2). The recommendation is to look them up and skip if absent.\n4. **NFR-10**: Carried forward to dev as a precondition, because the architect cannot resolve it.\n5. **New**: Add `/api/internal/` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` (B1). Without it, AC-6 still passes (401), but real cron dispatch never works.\n\n## New/changed files implied (for arch-design-system to confirm)\n\n- **New**: `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/`, `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,purge}.ts`, `src/server/email/{transport,render,dispatch}.ts`, `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`, `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`, `src/app/api/notifications/{route,unread-count/route,read-all/route,[id]/read/route,[id]/unread/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/{route,[id]/retry/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `scripts/worker-email.ts`, plus tests under `tests/unit`, `tests/integration` and `tests/e2e`.\n- **Modified**: `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (bell), `src/config/public-routes.ts` (one entry), `prisma/seed.ts` (append), and possibly `package.json` (`test:integration` script only).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":113,"newStart":1,"newLines":106,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-1","+# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-4"," ","-Supporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions","-& RBAC; 37 FR + 12 NFR = 49 requirements, 94% confidence, 4 blockers in","-`handoff-to-architect.json`). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.","+Supporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`. That file covers PRD-04 Notifications & Email","+Infrastructure (41 FR and 18 NFR, so 59 requirements) at 93% confidence, with 4 blockers in","+`handoff-to-architect.json`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`."," ","-Architectural concern buckets: **Data Model**, **Auth Core (Auth.js)**,","-**Credential Verification**, **Lockout & Rate Limiting**, **Session/JWT**,","-**Edge Middleware**, **Token Module**, **Invite Flow**, **Password Policy**,","-**Password Reset Flow**, **Change Password**, **Email Stub**, **Users","-Service**, **Authorization Helpers**, **Audit**, **App Shell & Nav**, **Auth","-UI Surface**, **REST API Surface**, **Seed**, **Test Harness**, **Security**,","-**Performance**, **Accessibility**, **Design System (MUI-only)**, **Scope","-Discipline**.","+Concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Type Registry**, **Notify Service**,","+**Preference Resolution**, **Email Rendering**, **Auth Email Seam**, **Outbox Dispatcher**,","+**Transport**, **Background Job**, **Internal Endpoint**, **User API**, **Admin API**,","+**UI: Bell**, **UI: Notifications Page**, **UI: Preferences Page**, **UI: Admin Email Log**,","+**Validation**, **Seed**, **Security**, **Performance**, **Reliability**, **Conventions**,","+**Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**."," ","-## Brownfield facts verified on disk (correct intake where it differs)","+## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these add to or correct intake)"," ","-- `requireRole(` is called at **~48 sites in ~42 files**, not ~94 as intake","-  says. Every one of those files already contains `async`, i.e. the callers","-  are async route handlers / server components. **Making `requireRole()`","-  async (callers add `await`) is a mechanical change, not a redesign.**","-  `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` consumes requireRole's result but must","-  not be modified (NFR-9) — keep the returned shape a superset of","-  `{ id, role }`.","-- `src/server/http.ts` already defines `AppError` codes `UNAUTHENTICATED`","-  401, `FORBIDDEN` 403, `RATE_LIMITED` 429, `CONFLICT` 409, plus Prisma","-  P2002 → CONFLICT mapping. No new error infra needed.","-- `src/server/audit.ts` has `audit(input)` that swallows errors; no `request`","-  param, never writes `ip`. Nothing in `src` reads `x-forwarded-for` today.","-- `src/lib/logger.ts`, `src/components/Toast/useToast.ts`,","-  `src/config/navigation.ts` exist. `src/app/forbidden` exists (target for","-  FR-29 redirect). `src/app/(public)` has `layout.tsx` + `page.tsx` only.","-- `src/app/api/health` exists; `src/app/api/auth` does not.","-- `users.ts` exports `createUser`, `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)`,","-  `unlockUser(userId)`, `sendInvite(userId): Promise<{id, inviteSentAt}>`.","+| # | Finding | Impact |","+|---|---------|--------|","+| B1 | `src/middleware.ts` returns **401 for any `/api/*` request without a session** unless `isPublicPath()` matches. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is only `['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`. | The cron call to `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` carries no session cookie, so it would be rejected by middleware before the handler runs. **`/api/internal/` must be added to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** (prefix match). The handler then becomes the only gate, so its CRON_SECRET check must be strict (NFR-8). The middleware's cross-origin guard does not block it, because cron calls send no `Origin` header. |","+| B2 | `prisma/seed.ts` (95 lines) seeds only SchoolSettings and academic reference data. **There are no `student@schoolhub.test` or `parent@schoolhub.test` users** anywhere in `prisma/` or `src/`. | FR-40 cannot simply attach notifications to existing users. Options: (a) look up those users by email and skip with a log line when they are missing, or (b) upsert minimal STUDENT/PARENT users. Recommend (a). It keeps the seed idempotent and avoids PRD-04 creating identity data that another PRD owns. Design should confirm. |","+| B3 | `vitest.config.ts` includes only `tests/unit/**` and uses `environment: 'jsdom'`. There is no `tests/integration/` folder and no test-DB setup. | NFR-15 needs a node environment plus a real Postgres to exercise `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`. This requires a separate vitest project or config (e.g. `vitest.integration.config.ts`, `environment: 'node'`, `include: tests/integration/**`) that is skipped when `DATABASE_URL_TEST` is absent, so that `npm run test` stays green (NFR-13). |","+| B4 | `EmailOutbox` has **no `userId` and no `type` column**. It stores only `toEmail`, `toName`, `subject`, `html`, `text`, `status`, `attempts`, `lastError`, `nextAttemptAt`, `sentAt`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. | The admin email log (FR-31) can only show recipient email and name, not a user link or type. That is sufficient for FR-31, so the schema should not change (NFR-13). `sendAuthEmail` (FR-16) fits naturally because it has no type. |","+| B5 | `NotificationPreference` uses a composite PK `@@id([userId, type])`. | FR-38's upsert keys on `userId_type`. FR-7's resolution reads with `findMany({ where: { userId: { in }, type } })`, which is a single query. |","+| B6 | `src/server/http.ts` already exports `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parsePagination` (default 20, max 100), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. `ApiErrorCode` already includes `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `NOT_FOUND`, `UNAUTHENTICATED` and `FORBIDDEN`. | All new route handlers reuse these (NFR-11). No new error codes are needed. |","+| B7 | `src/lib/dates.ts` exports `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, timezone)` (date-fns-tz). `SchoolSettings.timezone` defaults to `'UTC'`. `src/server/services/settings.ts` exists. | NFR-12 reuses these. Relative times (\"5 min ago\") are timezone-independent. Absolute times in the email log and the invite expiry date use `formatInSchoolTz`. |","+| B8 | `src/server/rate-limit.ts` exports an in-memory `rateLimit()`. | It could optionally guard `POST /api/admin/notifications/test`, but no requirement asks for that. Skip it under compliance rule 1. |","+| B9 | `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx`, `Toast/useToast.ts`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader` and `DateDisplay` exist. | FR-26 and FR-31 reuse DataTable, PageHeader and EmptyState. FR-30 reuses `useToast`. Do not create duplicates. |","+| B10 | Prisma `$transaction` is used in `src/server/sections/`. No `$queryRaw` is used anywhere yet. | FR-17's `SKIP LOCKED` claim is the first raw SQL in the repo. Use tagged `$queryRaw` (parameterised) inside `$transaction`, or a single `UPDATE … WHERE id IN (SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *` statement, which claims rows atomically without holding a transaction across SMTP. |","+| B11 | All other intake brownfield findings were confirmed: there is no migration for the three models, the env vars and `worker:email` script are present, the navigation entries exist, `sendAuthEmail` has exactly 2 callers (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`), and the `requireRole` helpers exist. | — |"," ","-## Functional Requirements","+## Requirement → architectural concern"," ","-| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |","-|----|------------------------|-------|","-| FR-1 | Data Model | Additive Prisma migration only: add `AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])`. Keep `ip` column, `ARCHIVED` enum value, and existing extra indexes (resolves blocker 1 per intake defaults). Verify `User` has `passwordHash`, `failedLoginCount`, `lockedUntil`, `lastLoginAt`, `passwordChangedAt`, `archivedAt`; add any missing as nullable/defaulted columns. |","-| FR-2 | Data Model / Credential Verification | Normalise `email.trim().toLowerCase()` in one place (Zod schema transform in `validators/auth.ts`) used by authorize, forgot-password and `createUser`. DB-level backstop optional (Postgres `citext` would be a type change — avoid; app-level is enough). |","-| FR-3 | Auth UI Surface | `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` — new `(auth)` route group with its own unauthenticated layout (no AppShell). Client component calling `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` so error codes can map to FR-5 messages. |","-| FR-4 | Credential Verification | Lives in Auth.js `Credentials.authorize`, but logic should be a plain service fn (`src/server/auth/credentials.ts` or inside the Auth.js config file) so integration tests (FR-36) can call it without HTTP. Order: rate-limit → lookup → status/archived/locked checks → bcrypt compare (cost 12). Runs on the **Node runtime** (bcrypt is native; not edge-safe). |","-| FR-5 | Credential Verification / Auth UI | Auth.js v5 lets `authorize` throw a `CredentialsSignin` subclass with a `code` (`invalid`, `locked`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`). The UI maps code → message. Locked message needs remaining minutes from `lockedUntil` → the code must carry minutes (e.g. `locked:7`) or the UI calls back. Design must pick one. |","-| FR-6 | Lockout & Rate Limiting | Per-user counter on `User` row. Increment + lock must be one atomic update (`update ... failedLoginCount: { increment: 1 }` then conditional lock) to avoid races under parallel attempts. Pure helper `computeLockout(count, now)` for unit test. |","-| FR-7 | Lockout & Rate Limiting | `src/server/rate-limit.ts`: in-memory sliding window keyed by string (`login:ip:<ip>`). Single-process only — acceptable per PRD; note ceiling (multi-instance needs Redis). Reused by FR-19 with different keys/limits, so API is generic `check(key, limit, windowMs)`. Needs client IP → shared `getClientIp(request)` helper (also FR-30). |","-| FR-8 | Auth Core | Pure `safeCallbackUrl(url): string` — accept only paths starting with `/` and not `//` or `/\\`; else `/dashboard`. Used by login page and Auth.js `redirect` callback. Unit-tested (FR-36). |","-| FR-9 | Audit | Called from authorize branches. `auth.login.failure` metadata = `{ email, reason }` only (FR-31). `actorId` = user id when known, null for unknown email. |","-| FR-10 | Session/JWT | Auth.js `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8h, updateAge }`. `jwt`/`session` callbacks copy `id, role, firstName, lastName, email`. Module augmentation of `next-auth` types for typed `session.user`. |","-| FR-11 | Session/JWT | `jwt` callback stores `checkedAt` on the token; if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`, DB read of `passwordChangedAt`/`status`; return `null` to invalidate. This DB hit means the jwt callback must not run on edge → middleware must use an edge-safe config split (see FR-12). |","-| FR-12 | Edge Middleware | `middleware.ts` runs on edge: **cannot import Prisma or bcrypt**. Standard Auth.js v5 pattern: `auth.config.ts` (edge-safe, no providers' DB code) used by middleware; `auth.ts` (full, Node) for handlers. Middleware only checks token presence/validity; FR-11 revalidation happens in Node. Matcher excludes `_next`, static, `/api/auth/*`, `/api/health`, `(auth)` pages, `(public)` pages, plus `src/config/public-routes.ts` list. Pages → redirect `/login?callbackUrl=`; `/api/*` → 401 JSON envelope. |","-| FR-13 | Token Module | `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` — the only writer/reader of `AuthToken`. `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, store `sha256` hex. Lookup by hash (unique index) → constant-time compare after fetch (NFR-1). `consumeToken` should be conditional (`updateMany where usedAt null`) so double-submit can't consume twice. Add `invalidateUnused(userId, type)` used by FR-20/FR-26. |","-| FR-14 | Invite Flow | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` server component calls `verifyToken(raw, 'INVITE')`; invalid → error Alert. Token is in the URL path → ensure it isn't logged by request logging. |","-| FR-15 | Invite Flow / Auth UI | Read-only name/email from verified token's user; password + confirm fields reuse the FR-18 checklist component. |","-| FR-16 | Invite Flow / REST API | `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` — **note path sits under `/api/auth/*` alongside the `[...nextauth]` catch-all**; Next.js static segments win over catch-alls so this works, but design must confirm. Service in a transaction: verify → policy check → hash → `status=ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt=now` → consume. \"Signs the user in\": simplest is client calls `signIn('credentials')` with the just-set password after 200 OK (server-side session minting outside Auth.js is fragile). Audit `auth.invite.accepted`. |","-| FR-17 | Password Policy | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` — Zod schema shared client+server. Common-password list lives in `src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt` (server-only file read) → split: client checks length/letter/digit/≠email; server additionally checks common list. FR-18 checklist can't show the common-list rule live without shipping the list; either ship the list (~8 KB) to client or show that rule only on submit. Design decision. |","-| FR-18 | Password Policy / Auth UI | Shared `PasswordChecklist` component (MUI List + icons) used by invite, reset and change-password pages. |","-| FR-19 | Password Reset Flow / Lockout & Rate Limiting | `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` — identical response body and similar timing whether or not user exists (NFR-3 spirit). Two rate-limit keys: `forgot:email:<email>` (3/h), `forgot:ip:<ip>` (10/h). Over limit: still the generic message, or RATE_LIMITED 429? PRD says \"always responds\" → design must decide; 429 on IP limit is safe, email limit should stay silent to avoid enumeration. |","-| FR-20 | Password Reset Flow | Only ACTIVE users get a token; `invalidateUnused(userId,'PASSWORD_RESET')` then `createToken(…, 60 min)` then `sendAuthEmail`. Unknown email → no DB write. |","-| FR-21 | Password Reset Flow | `POST /api/auth/reset-password` transaction: verify → policy → hash → `passwordChangedAt=now`, `failedLoginCount=0`, `lockedUntil=null` → consume. Audit `auth.password.reset`. Success toast after redirect needs cross-navigation signal (`/login?reset=1` query param read on login page → `useToast`). |","-| FR-22 | Email Stub | `src/server/auth/email.ts` `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` → `logger.info`. Single seam PRD-04 swaps for EmailOutbox. Link base URL from env (`AUTH_URL`/`NEXTAUTH_URL`). |","-| FR-23 | Change Password | `/account/security` page inside `(app)` (authenticated). `POST /api/account/password` → `requireUser()` → bcrypt compare current → policy → hash → `passwordChangedAt=now`. \"Re-issue current session\": after `passwordChangedAt` bump, current JWT's `iat` < `passwordChangedAt` would be invalidated by FR-11 → must refresh current token (client `update()` from `useSession`, with jwt callback trigger `update` resetting `iat`/`checkedAt`). Key subtlety for design. Wrong current password → 400 with field-level `details` for the form. |","-| FR-24 | App Shell & Nav | Add menu item in `shell.tsx` user menu → `/account/security`. All roles. |","-| FR-25 | Users Service | No new `createUser`; confirm P2002 on email → CONFLICT via existing `http.ts` mapping. Keep `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)` and `unlockUser(userId)` (resolves blocker 2 per intake defaults). Ensure `createUser` lower-cases email (FR-2). |","-| FR-26 | Users Service / Token Module | `createInviteToken(userId)` in `users.ts` → `tokens.invalidateUnused` + `tokens.createToken(userId,'INVITE',{days:7})`. |","-| FR-27 | Users Service / Email Stub | `sendInvite` body: `createInviteToken` → `sendAuthEmail(user,'invite',link)`; keep return `{id, inviteSentAt}` for existing callers. |","-| FR-28 | Authorization Helpers | `requireRole.ts`: delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`; add `getCurrentUser()` (wraps `auth()`, memoised per request with React `cache()`), `requireUser()`. Server pages vs route handlers need different failure behaviour (redirect vs throw). Cleanest: separate fns or an option, since there's no reliable runtime way to detect context. Resolves blocker 3: **go async**; ~48 call sites add `await` (all already in async fns). No `permissions.ts`. |","-| FR-29 | Authorization Helpers | `requireRole(...roles)` → `Promise<SessionUser>` (superset of `{id, role}` so `course-access.ts` compiles unchanged). Throw `AppError('FORBIDDEN')` in handlers; pages redirect `/forbidden` (route exists). No `can()`. |","-| FR-30 | Audit | Add optional `request?: Request` to `AuditInput`; `ip = getClientIp(request)` (first value of `x-forwarded-for`, trimmed). Keep inside try/catch. Shared helper with FR-7. |","-| FR-31 | Audit / Security | Enforce by construction: audit callers pass explicit metadata objects; optionally a small denylist strip (`password`, `passwordHash`, `token`) in `audit()` as defence-in-depth. Covered by test. |","-| FR-32 | App Shell & Nav | `shell.tsx` reads session — either the `(app)/layout.tsx` server component passes `getCurrentUser()` as a prop, or `SessionProvider` + `useSession`. Prop-passing avoids a client fetch and flash. Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. Role badge + initials via MUI `Chip`/`Avatar`. |","-| FR-33 | App Shell & Nav | Filter `navigation.ts` entries by role (server-side, before passing to shell). UX only — NFR-7 still applies on every page. |","-| FR-34 | Auth Core / REST API | `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` exporting `{ GET, POST } = handlers` from `auth.ts`. |","-| FR-35 | Seed | Extend `prisma/seed.ts` idempotently (`upsert` by email): 6 ACTIVE users (bcrypt cost 12 of `SchoolHub123!`) + `invited@` INVITED with invite created via `createInviteToken` and link logged. Keep `office@`. Seeding goes through `tokens.ts` (FR-13 single-module rule). |","-| FR-36 | Test Harness | Unit (pure fns: policy, token hash/expiry, `computeLockout`, rate limiter, `safeCallbackUrl`) → design should keep these logic pieces as pure exported fns. Integration against DB for authorize/accept/reset/change. Playwright needs seeded users (FR-35) and the reset link from logs → e2e must read the token from DB or a test hook rather than email. |","-| FR-37 | Scope Discipline / Auth Core | No `/signup` route and no sign-up endpoint; the only path to ACTIVE is FR-16 (or admin `setUserStatus`). Middleware public list must not include any sign-up path. |","+| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |","+|-----|----------------------|-------|","+| FR-1 | Data Model | One new migration `2026110400xxxx_notifications_email`. It creates `EmailStatus`, `Notification`, `NotificationPreference` and `EmailOutbox` exactly as `schema.prisma` declares them, including the additive `updatedAt` columns and both indexes. Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and do not edit `schema.prisma`. It must sort after `20261104000000_auth_reconcile`. |","+| FR-2 | Type Registry | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` exports `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` with `as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>`, which keeps literal keys for FR-5 while type-checking the shape. Add one field, `emailOnly?: true` (or `hidden`), to express FR-4. |","+| FR-3 | Type Registry | `NotificationCategory` is a string-literal union of the 6 values, not a Prisma enum, because the DB stores `type` as a free `String`. The UI groups by category (FR-26, FR-28). |","+| FR-4 | Type Registry, Auth Email Seam | `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are `emailOnly`, hidden from preferences and never passed to `notify()` (blocker default confirmed in \"Decisions for design\" below). `system.test` uses category SYSTEM, `defaultEmail: true` and all roles (AC-1 expects both rows). |","+| FR-5 | Type Registry | `type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. Later PRDs extend the registry by editing this one file, and no plugin mechanism is needed (YAGNI). |","+| FR-6 | Notify Service | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` is a pure server module. Its `email.template` param is a key into the template map (FR-13), and `data` is typed per template. |","+| FR-7 | Preference Resolution | Load users with `findMany({ id in userIds, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` and prefs with `findMany({ userId in, type })`. Then resolve each user with a pure function `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }`, which is unit-tested (NFR-14). |","+| FR-8 | Notify Service | `inApp = row?.inApp ?? true`, with `mandatoryInApp` forcing true. Notifications are written with `createMany`. |","+| FR-9 | Notify Service, Email Rendering | `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` and requires `user.email`. Render once per recipient, because templates contain the name. Rendering cost dominates NFR-1, so `render()` calls should run with bounded `Promise.all` concurrency. Rows are written to `EmailOutbox` with `createMany`. |","+| FR-10 | Performance | 1,000 recipients means 3 round-trips: users, prefs and one `createMany`, per channel. Chunk `createMany` at about 500 rows only if the parameter limit bites (Postgres allows 65,535 params, and Notification has about 7 columns, so 1,000 rows fit in one call). |","+| FR-11 | Notify Service | Wrap the whole body in try/catch, call `logger.error`, and return `void` or a `{ notified, emailed }` summary. Callers invoke it after commit. Document that in JSDoc. |","+| FR-12 | Notify Service | `notifyStudentAndParents` makes one `ParentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call (indexed on `studentId`), merges into a `Set`, then calls `notify`. Expansion and dedupe are a pure function so they can be unit-tested (NFR-14). |","+| FR-13 | Email Rendering | `src/server/email/templates/*.tsx` with `@react-email/components`. `src/server/email/render.ts` calls `render(el)` and `render(el, { plainText: true })` from `@react-email/render` 1.0.1, which is async. |","+| FR-14 | Email Rendering | `BaseLayout.tsx` takes `school: Pick<SchoolSettings, name, logoUrl, addressLine1, addressLine2>`. Fetch SchoolSettings once per `notify()` / `sendAuthEmail` call, not once per recipient. The footer link is `APP_URL/account/notifications`. |","+| FR-15 | Email Rendering | There are 3 templates. Invite needs an expiry date, which `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` does not receive. The template can derive it from the known invite TTL constant in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, so the signature stays unchanged. Password reset uses the hardcoded 60-minute notice. The generic CTA href is `APP_URL + link` (the link is already validated by NFR-6). |","+| FR-16 | Auth Email Seam | Only the body of `src/server/auth/email.ts` changes: render the template and call `prisma.emailOutbox.create`. Its 2 callers are untouched. Unlike `notify()`, failures here **should** surface, because the existing callers already handle errors and a silently lost invite is worse. Design should decide whether to keep the current awaited and throwable behaviour (recommended). |","+| FR-17 | Outbox Dispatcher | `src/server/email/dispatch.ts`. First, run stuck-row recovery (NFR-5). Next, claim rows with one atomic `UPDATE … SET status='SENDING', updatedAt=now() WHERE id IN (SELECT id … WHERE status='PENDING' AND nextAttemptAt<=now() ORDER BY nextAttemptAt LIMIT $n FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *`. Then send each row outside any transaction and update it individually. |","+| FR-18 | Outbox Dispatcher | A pure function `backoffMinutes(attempts) → [1,5,15,60,240][attempts-1]`, plus `attempts >= 5 → FAILED`. It is unit-tested (NFR-14). `lastError` is truncated to about 1,000 characters. |","+| FR-19 | Internal Endpoint | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`. Compare the bearer token against `env.CRON_SECRET` with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. A missing env value always returns 401. The response is `{ data: { sent, failed, retried } }` via `ok()`. **Requires B1** (the middleware allowlist). The route also triggers FR-27. |","+| FR-20 | Background Job | `scripts/worker-email.ts` imports `dispatchEmails` directly (tsx resolves the `@/` alias via tsconfig paths) and runs a `setTimeout` loop every 15 s with SIGINT/SIGTERM handling. It does not go over HTTP and does not call purge, because purge belongs to the endpoint only (FR-27). |","+| FR-21 | Transport | `src/server/email/transport.ts` exports `getTransport()` with 2 branches. `smtp` uses `nodemailer.createTransport` with SMTP_* settings and is memoised. `console` uses `console.log`, which NFR-11 explicitly allows. Each message includes `List-Unsubscribe` (NFR-9). Missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` under `smtp` should fail at transport creation, and the dispatcher must record that as a retryable `lastError`, not crash. |","+| FR-22 | UI: Bell | The `'use client'` component `NotificationBell.tsx` replaces the placeholder in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`. It uses MUI `Badge` with `max={9}`, which renders \"9+\" natively, so no custom formatting is needed. |","+| FR-23 | UI: Bell | A `setInterval` of 30 s gated on `document.visibilityState`, plus an immediate refetch on `visibilitychange → visible`. There is no SWR or react-query dependency, so plain `fetch` is enough. |","+| FR-24 | UI: Bell | `Popover` + `List` + `ListItemButton`. Unread items use bold `fontWeight` and a `Badge variant=\"dot\"` or small Box. The body is clamped with `sx={{ WebkitLineClamp: 2 }}`. Relative time uses `date-fns` `formatDistanceToNowStrict` (date-fns-tz is already installed, so date-fns is too). The popover fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10` on open. |","+| FR-25 | UI: Bell | On click, call `POST /:id/read`, then `router.push(link)`, then close. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" (`POST /read-all`) and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |","+| FR-26 | UI: Notifications Page | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` is a server shell using `requirePageUser()` and a client list. It has `Tabs` (All/Unread), a category `Select`, the pagination from DataTable or MUI `Pagination` with a page size of 20, and a per-row toggle calling `/:id/read` or `/:id/unread`. |","+| FR-27 | Background Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` (`deleteMany createdAt < now-180d`) lives in `src/server/notifications/`. A module-level `let lastPurgeAt` in the dispatch route allows at most one run per 24 h per process. It is best-effort, and its failure is logged and must not fail the dispatch response. |","+| FR-28 | UI: Preferences Page | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`. This is the first page under `/account/`, so the directory is new. It is an MUI `Table` with a full-width category header `TableRow` (the intake default is accepted) and data from `GET /api/me/notification-preferences`. |","+| FR-29 | UI: Preferences Page | `Tooltip` around a **span** wrapping the disabled `Switch`, because MUI Tooltip does not fire on disabled elements. |","+| FR-30 | UI: Preferences Page | Optimistic local state, `PUT`, and on error revert plus `useToast().error(...)`. |","+| FR-31 | UI: Admin Email Log | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` uses `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` with DataTable and a status `Select`. The recipient column shows `toName <toEmail>` (B4). |","+| FR-32 | Admin API, UI: Admin Email Log | The retry action is shown only when `status==='FAILED'`. The server guard uses `updateMany where { id, status: FAILED }`, and a count of 0 returns 409 CONFLICT or 404, so a double click is harmless. |","+| FR-33 | Admin API | `POST /api/admin/notifications/test` uses `requireRole('ADMIN')`, then `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title, body, link: '/dashboard' })`. The button sits on the email-log page because no separate admin page is needed. |","+| FR-34 | User API | `GET /api/notifications` uses `parseQuery` with Zod (`unread`, `category`), `parsePagination` and `paginated()`. **Category filter caveat:** Notification has no category column. Filter by the `type IN (keys of registry with that category)` derived from the registry at request time. This needs no schema change and remains index-compatible with `userId` leading. |","+| FR-35 | User API | `count({ where: { userId, readAt: null } })` is covered by the `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index (NFR-2). |","+| FR-36 | User API | Mark read or unread with `updateMany({ where: { id, userId: me.id } })`. A count of 0 returns 404, which hides existence from non-owners. `read-all` runs `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null })`. Route files: `[id]/read/route.ts`, `[id]/unread/route.ts` and `read-all/route.ts`. **Next.js routing note:** `read-all` and `unread-count` are static siblings of `[id]`, and static segments win, so they do not conflict. |","+| FR-37 | User API, Preference Resolution | `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` (GET and PUT in one file) is the first route under `/api/me/`. It filters the registry by `roles.includes(me.role)` and `!emailOnly`, merges the rows and returns `{ type, label, description, category, inApp, email, mandatoryInApp }[]`. |","+| FR-38 | User API, Validation | The Zod body is `{ type: z.enum(visibleTypeKeys), inApp: boolean, email: boolean }`. The service rejects `inApp=false` for mandatory types and role-invisible or `emailOnly` types with `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR')`, then calls `upsert` on `userId_type`. |","+| FR-39 | Admin API | `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` (GET) and `[id]/retry/route.ts` (POST), both protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The list is ordered by `createdAt desc` and **omits `html` and `text`** to keep the payload small. |","+| FR-40 | Seed | The seed appends to `prisma/seed.ts`. **See B2: the target users do not exist.** For idempotency, skip a user who already has any `system.test` notification (count > 0), giving 3 per user with 1 read and 2 unread, linking to `/dashboard`. |","+| FR-41 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` is a sibling of the existing `auth.ts`, `users.ts` and so on. It holds the list query schema, the preference PUT schema and `safeLink` (NFR-6). It must be client-safe: no server imports, so registry keys are passed in or the type is checked as a string and then against the registry in the service. |","+| NFR-1 | Performance | The budget of 2 s for 1,000 recipients is dominated by 1,000 react-email renders. Mitigate with SchoolSettings fetched once, bounded concurrency, and rendering only recipients with email enabled. If renders are too slow, render the generic template once with a name placeholder. Design should note this as the fallback. |","+| NFR-2 | Performance | Covered by the FR-1 index and FR-35 query shape. The bell must not call the list endpoint on every poll. |","+| NFR-3 | Reliability | No SMTP happens in the request path: `notify()` and `sendAuthEmail` only insert rows. The 15 s worker or the cron endpoint keeps delivery under 60 s. |","+| NFR-4 | Reliability | The FR-17 atomic claim with `SKIP LOCKED`. Each claimed row is owned by exactly one dispatcher. |","+| NFR-5 | Reliability | At the start of each dispatch: `updateMany({ status: SENDING, updatedAt < now-10m }, { status: PENDING })`. This relies on the additive `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`, which is why FR-1 keeps it. It does not increment attempts, because a crash mid-send was not proven to be a send failure. |","+| NFR-6 | Security | A shared `isSafeLink(s)` requires `s.startsWith('/')` and rejects `//`, `/\\`, any `\\` and control characters. It is applied in `notify()` (drop or nullify the link and warn instead of throwing, per FR-11) and in the Zod schema. Unit-tested (NFR-14). |","+| NFR-7 | Security | React-email JSX escapes interpolated text by default. **Never** use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in templates. Body text is rendered as text with `white-space: pre-line`, not as HTML. |","+| NFR-8 | Security | Every new handler starts with `requireUser()` or `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The internal route uses a secret check only (B1). Pages use `requirePageUser()` or `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. |","+| NFR-9 | Security, Transport | Each `sendMail` call sets `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<APP_URL/account/notifications>' }` along with both `html` and `text`. Set it at send time rather than storing it in the outbox, because the outbox has no headers column (B4). |","+| NFR-10 | Conventions (UI) | All 4 UI surfaces (bell, notifications page, preferences page, email log) use MUI only. Dev must query mui-mcp before writing UI, and **this is an unresolved blocker carried forward**: if the server is unreachable, there is a hard stop. The existing `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned libs. Email templates are exempt. |","+| NFR-11 | Conventions | Thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok`/`paginated`. Services live in `src/server/notifications/` and `src/server/email/`, and code uses `logger`, with `console` only in the console transport. |","+| NFR-12 | Conventions | UTC storage is the Prisma default. Display uses `formatInSchoolTz` (B7). The client components need the timezone, so pass it from the server page as a prop. |","+| NFR-13 | Conventions | Do not touch `schema.prisma`, navigation or env. Keep the `sendAuthEmail` signature. Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. This is the source of B1–B3 handling. |","+| NFR-14 | Test Harness | Pure units are `resolvePrefs`, `backoffMinutes`, `isSafeLink` and `expandStudentRecipients`. They go in `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`, run under the existing vitest config and need no DB. |","+| NFR-15 | Test Harness | **See B3.** A new `tests/integration/` folder with a node-env vitest config against a test DB. One test runs 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails` calls over 10 rows and asserts each row is sent once. A second test backdates a SENDING row's `updatedAt` by 11 minutes and asserts recovery. |","+| NFR-16 | Test Harness | Playwright tests go in `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`. They need a logged-in admin (the existing e2e harness pattern; check `dashboard.spec.ts` for auth setup). The flow is send test → bell count → mark all read → preference toggle persists after reload. |","+| NFR-17 | Scope Discipline | No SMS, push, websockets or digests. Polling only (FR-23), and do not add a `channel` abstraction for future SMS. |","+| NFR-18 | Notify Service | Silently truncate `title` to 140 characters and `body` to 500, with `logger.warn` (intake default accepted, since it is consistent with FR-11). There is no DB constraint, because the schema has plain `String`. |"," ","-## Non-Functional Requirements","+## Decisions for design (resolving intake blockers)"," ","-| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |","-|----|------------------------|-------|","-| NFR-1 | Security / Token Module | SHA-256 at rest; `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on equal-length buffers. Unique index on `AuthToken.tokenHash` makes lookup O(1). |","-| NFR-2 | Security / Auth Core | Auth.js defaults already give HttpOnly, `__Secure-` prefix + Secure in prod, SameSite=Lax, CSRF on its own endpoints. **Custom POST routes (`accept-invite`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `account/password`) are outside Auth.js CSRF** — design must cover them (Origin/`Sec-Fetch-Site` same-origin check in route or middleware; SameSite=Lax alone doesn't protect unauthenticated endpoints). |","-| NFR-3 | Security / Credential Verification | Precompute a dummy bcrypt hash at module load; compare against it when the user is missing so timing matches. Same idea for forgot-password (no branch-visible timing difference). |","-| NFR-4 | Performance | bcrypt cost 12 ≈ 250 ms; budget fine. Keep authorize to 1 user query + 1 update + async audit; don't await non-critical writes serially beyond that. |","-| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Form `Alert` inside `aria-live=\"polite\"` region; on submit-with-errors focus first invalid `TextField` (`inputRef`). Shared form-error pattern across 5 auth forms. |","-| NFR-6 | Design System (MUI-only) | All auth pages, checklist, shell menu changes use MUI v9 only; dev must look up each component via mui-mcp. mui-mcp tools are visible in this environment (`useMuiDocs`, `fetchDocs`) — blocker 4 currently looks unblocked, dev must still confirm. |","-| NFR-7 | Authorization Helpers | Every new route handler and `(app)` page calls `requireUser()`/`requireRole()`; middleware is a first gate, not the only one. |","-| NFR-8 | REST API Surface | All custom auth routes: Zod parse → service → `{data}` / `{error:{code,message,details}}` using existing `http.ts` helpers. Auth.js catch-all is the sole exception (its own protocol). |","-| NFR-9 | Scope Discipline | Reuse `audit.ts`, `users.ts`, `requireRole.ts`, `useToast`, `AppError`; no renames; `course-access.ts` / `student-access.ts` untouched (constrains FR-29 return type). |","-| NFR-10 | Test Harness | Lint/typecheck/test green — the async `requireRole` change (FR-28/29) touches ~42 files, so typecheck is the safety net. `logger` only; `console.log` banned except the dev email transport. |","-| NFR-11 | Scope Discipline | No admin UI, SSO, MFA, magic links, or email infra. |","-| NFR-12 | Data Model / Auth UI | Timestamps UTC in DB. Lockout \"N minutes\" is a duration (timezone-independent); `lastLoginAt` display formatted in `SchoolSettings.timezone` (existing settings model). |","+1. **FR-1 migration**: Accepted. There is one new migration, `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `schema.prisma` is not changed.","+2. **FR-4/FR-16**: Accepted. `sendAuthEmail` enqueues directly and creates no Notification row. The `account.*` types are `emailOnly` and are filtered out of FR-28 and FR-37 and rejected by FR-38.","+3. **FR-40**: Use 3 per user, but the users are missing (B2). The recommendation is to look them up and skip if absent.","+4. **NFR-10**: Carried forward to dev as a precondition, because the architect cannot resolve it.","+5. **New**: Add `/api/internal/` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` (B1). Without it, AC-6 still passes (401), but real cron dispatch never works."," ","-## Cross-cutting items for `arch-design-system`","+## New/changed files implied (for arch-design-system to confirm)"," ","-1. **Edge/Node split** (FR-4, FR-11, FR-12): `auth.config.ts` edge-safe for middleware; `auth.ts` Node with Prisma/bcrypt.","-2. **requireRole goes async** (FR-28/29, blocker 3): ~48 sites, all already in async fns; return type superset of `{id, role}`.","-3. **Session re-issue after password change** (FR-11 vs FR-23): current session must survive its own `passwordChangedAt` bump.","-4. **CSRF for custom auth POSTs** (NFR-2): not covered by Auth.js.","-5. **Shared `getClientIp(request)`** (FR-7, FR-19, FR-30).","-6. **Shared password UI + Zod schema** (FR-15/17/18/21/23); decide whether the common-password list ships to the client.","-7. **Rate limiter is per-process** (FR-7/FR-19): fine for this PRD, Redis if multi-instance.","-8. **Additive migration only** (FR-1, blocker 1): two AuditLog indexes plus any missing User columns.","-","-## Blockers carried forward from intake","-","-- FR-1 schema divergences → resolved by additive migration (above).","-- FR-25 signature mismatch → keep the existing signatures.","-- FR-28/29 sync vs async → recommend async (call sites are fewer than intake reported and are all already async).","-- NFR-6 mui-mcp reachability → tools are registered in this environment; dev must still check before writing UI.","+- **New**: `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/`, `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,purge}.ts`, `src/server/email/{transport,render,dispatch}.ts`, `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`, `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`, `src/app/api/notifications/{route,unread-count/route,read-all/route,[id]/read/route,[id]/unread/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/{route,[id]/retry/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `scripts/worker-email.ts`, plus tests under `tests/unit`, `tests/integration` and `tests/e2e`.","+- **Modified**: `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (bell), `src/config/public-routes.ts` (one entry), `prisma/seed.ts` (append), and possibly `package.json` (`test:integration` script only)."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-1\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions\n& RBAC; 37 FR + 12 NFR = 49 requirements, 94% confidence, 4 blockers in\n`handoff-to-architect.json`). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\nArchitectural concern buckets: **Data Model**, **Auth Core (Auth.js)**,\n**Credential Verification**, **Lockout & Rate Limiting**, **Session/JWT**,\n**Edge Middleware**, **Token Module**, **Invite Flow**, **Password Policy**,\n**Password Reset Flow**, **Change Password**, **Email Stub**, **Users\nService**, **Authorization Helpers**, **Audit**, **App Shell & Nav**, **Auth\nUI Surface**, **REST API Surface**, **Seed**, **Test Harness**, **Security**,\n**Performance**, **Accessibility**, **Design System (MUI-only)**, **Scope\nDiscipline**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (correct intake where it differs)\n\n- `requireRole(` is called at **~48 sites in ~42 files**, not ~94 as intake\n  says. Every one of those files already contains `async`, i.e. the callers\n  are async route handlers / server components. **Making `requireRole()`\n  async (callers add `await`) is a mechanical change, not a redesign.**\n  `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` consumes requireRole's result but must\n  not be modified (NFR-9) — keep the returned shape a superset of\n  `{ id, role }`.\n- `src/server/http.ts` already defines `AppError` codes `UNAUTHENTICATED`\n  401, `FORBIDDEN` 403, `RATE_LIMITED` 429, `CONFLICT` 409, plus Prisma\n  P2002 → CONFLICT mapping. No new error infra needed.\n- `src/server/audit.ts` has `audit(input)` that swallows errors; no `request`\n  param, never writes `ip`. Nothing in `src` reads `x-forwarded-for` today.\n- `src/lib/logger.ts`, `src/components/Toast/useToast.ts`,\n  `src/config/navigation.ts` exist. `src/app/forbidden` exists (target for\n  FR-29 redirect). `src/app/(public)` has `layout.tsx` + `page.tsx` only.\n- `src/app/api/health` exists; `src/app/api/auth` does not.\n- `users.ts` exports `createUser`, `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)`,\n  `unlockUser(userId)`, `sendInvite(userId): Promise<{id, inviteSentAt}>`.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | Additive Prisma migration only: add `AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])`. Keep `ip` column, `ARCHIVED` enum value, and existing extra indexes (resolves blocker 1 per intake defaults). Verify `User` has `passwordHash`, `failedLoginCount`, `lockedUntil`, `lastLoginAt`, `passwordChangedAt`, `archivedAt`; add any missing as nullable/defaulted columns. |\n| FR-2 | Data Model / Credential Verification | Normalise `email.trim().toLowerCase()` in one place (Zod schema transform in `validators/auth.ts`) used by authorize, forgot-password and `createUser`. DB-level backstop optional (Postgres `citext` would be a type change — avoid; app-level is enough). |\n| FR-3 | Auth UI Surface | `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` — new `(auth)` route group with its own unauthenticated layout (no AppShell). Client component calling `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` so error codes can map to FR-5 messages. |\n| FR-4 | Credential Verification | Lives in Auth.js `Credentials.authorize`, but logic should be a plain service fn (`src/server/auth/credentials.ts` or inside the Auth.js config file) so integration tests (FR-36) can call it without HTTP. Order: rate-limit → lookup → status/archived/locked checks → bcrypt compare (cost 12). Runs on the **Node runtime** (bcrypt is native; not edge-safe). |\n| FR-5 | Credential Verification / Auth UI | Auth.js v5 lets `authorize` throw a `CredentialsSignin` subclass with a `code` (`invalid`, `locked`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`). The UI maps code → message. Locked message needs remaining minutes from `lockedUntil` → the code must carry minutes (e.g. `locked:7`) or the UI calls back. Design must pick one. |\n| FR-6 | Lockout & Rate Limiting | Per-user counter on `User` row. Increment + lock must be one atomic update (`update ... failedLoginCount: { increment: 1 }` then conditional lock) to avoid races under parallel attempts. Pure helper `computeLockout(count, now)` for unit test. |\n| FR-7 | Lockout & Rate Limiting | `src/server/rate-limit.ts`: in-memory sliding window keyed by string (`login:ip:<ip>`). Single-process only — acceptable per PRD; note ceiling (multi-instance needs Redis). Reused by FR-19 with different keys/limits, so API is generic `check(key, limit, windowMs)`. Needs client IP → shared `getClientIp(request)` helper (also FR-30). |\n| FR-8 | Auth Core | Pure `safeCallbackUrl(url): string` — accept only paths starting with `/` and not `//` or `/\\`; else `/dashboard`. Used by login page and Auth.js `redirect` callback. Unit-tested (FR-36). |\n| FR-9 | Audit | Called from authorize branches. `auth.login.failure` metadata = `{ email, reason }` only (FR-31). `actorId` = user id when known, null for unknown email. |\n| FR-10 | Session/JWT | Auth.js `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8h, updateAge }`. `jwt`/`session` callbacks copy `id, role, firstName, lastName, email`. Module augmentation of `next-auth` types for typed `session.user`. |\n| FR-11 | Session/JWT | `jwt` callback stores `checkedAt` on the token; if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`, DB read of `passwordChangedAt`/`status`; return `null` to invalidate. This DB hit means the jwt callback must not run on edge → middleware must use an edge-safe config split (see FR-12). |\n| FR-12 | Edge Middleware | `middleware.ts` runs on edge: **cannot import Prisma or bcrypt**. Standard Auth.js v5 pattern: `auth.config.ts` (edge-safe, no providers' DB code) used by middleware; `auth.ts` (full, Node) for handlers. Middleware only checks token presence/validity; FR-11 revalidation happens in Node. Matcher excludes `_next`, static, `/api/auth/*`, `/api/health`, `(auth)` pages, `(public)` pages, plus `src/config/public-routes.ts` list. Pages → redirect `/login?callbackUrl=`; `/api/*` → 401 JSON envelope. |\n| FR-13 | Token Module | `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` — the only writer/reader of `AuthToken`. `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, store `sha256` hex. Lookup by hash (unique index) → constant-time compare after fetch (NFR-1). `consumeToken` should be conditional (`updateMany where usedAt null`) so double-submit can't consume twice. Add `invalidateUnused(userId, type)` used by FR-20/FR-26. |\n| FR-14 | Invite Flow | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` server component calls `verifyToken(raw, 'INVITE')`; invalid → error Alert. Token is in the URL path → ensure it isn't logged by request logging. |\n| FR-15 | Invite Flow / Auth UI | Read-only name/email from verified token's user; password + confirm fields reuse the FR-18 checklist component. |\n| FR-16 | Invite Flow / REST API | `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` — **note path sits under `/api/auth/*` alongside the `[...nextauth]` catch-all**; Next.js static segments win over catch-alls so this works, but design must confirm. Service in a transaction: verify → policy check → hash → `status=ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt=now` → consume. \"Signs the user in\": simplest is client calls `signIn('credentials')` with the just-set password after 200 OK (server-side session minting outside Auth.js is fragile). Audit `auth.invite.accepted`. |\n| FR-17 | Password Policy | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` — Zod schema shared client+server. Common-password list lives in `src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt` (server-only file read) → split: client checks length/letter/digit/≠email; server additionally checks common list. FR-18 checklist can't show the common-list rule live without shipping the list; either ship the list (~8 KB) to client or show that rule only on submit. Design decision. |\n| FR-18 | Password Policy / Auth UI | Shared `PasswordChecklist` component (MUI List + icons) used by invite, reset and change-password pages. |\n| FR-19 | Password Reset Flow / Lockout & Rate Limiting | `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` — identical response body and similar timing whether or not user exists (NFR-3 spirit). Two rate-limit keys: `forgot:email:<email>` (3/h), `forgot:ip:<ip>` (10/h). Over limit: still the generic message, or RATE_LIMITED 429? PRD says \"always responds\" → design must decide; 429 on IP limit is safe, email limit should stay silent to avoid enumeration. |\n| FR-20 | Password Reset Flow | Only ACTIVE users get a token; `invalidateUnused(userId,'PASSWORD_RESET')` then `createToken(…, 60 min)` then `sendAuthEmail`. Unknown email → no DB write. |\n| FR-21 | Password Reset Flow | `POST /api/auth/reset-password` transaction: verify → policy → hash → `passwordChangedAt=now`, `failedLoginCount=0`, `lockedUntil=null` → consume. Audit `auth.password.reset`. Success toast after redirect needs cross-navigation signal (`/login?reset=1` query param read on login page → `useToast`). |\n| FR-22 | Email Stub | `src/server/auth/email.ts` `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` → `logger.info`. Single seam PRD-04 swaps for EmailOutbox. Link base URL from env (`AUTH_URL`/`NEXTAUTH_URL`). |\n| FR-23 | Change Password | `/account/security` page inside `(app)` (authenticated). `POST /api/account/password` → `requireUser()` → bcrypt compare current → policy → hash → `passwordChangedAt=now`. \"Re-issue current session\": after `passwordChangedAt` bump, current JWT's `iat` < `passwordChangedAt` would be invalidated by FR-11 → must refresh current token (client `update()` from `useSession`, with jwt callback trigger `update` resetting `iat`/`checkedAt`). Key subtlety for design. Wrong current password → 400 with field-level `details` for the form. |\n| FR-24 | App Shell & Nav | Add menu item in `shell.tsx` user menu → `/account/security`. All roles. |\n| FR-25 | Users Service | No new `createUser`; confirm P2002 on email → CONFLICT via existing `http.ts` mapping. Keep `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)` and `unlockUser(userId)` (resolves blocker 2 per intake defaults). Ensure `createUser` lower-cases email (FR-2). |\n| FR-26 | Users Service / Token Module | `createInviteToken(userId)` in `users.ts` → `tokens.invalidateUnused` + `tokens.createToken(userId,'INVITE',{days:7})`. |\n| FR-27 | Users Service / Email Stub | `sendInvite` body: `createInviteToken` → `sendAuthEmail(user,'invite',link)`; keep return `{id, inviteSentAt}` for existing callers. |\n| FR-28 | Authorization Helpers | `requireRole.ts`: delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`; add `getCurrentUser()` (wraps `auth()`, memoised per request with React `cache()`), `requireUser()`. Server pages vs route handlers need different failure behaviour (redirect vs throw). Cleanest: separate fns or an option, since there's no reliable runtime way to detect context. Resolves blocker 3: **go async**; ~48 call sites add `await` (all already in async fns). No `permissions.ts`. |\n| FR-29 | Authorization Helpers | `requireRole(...roles)` → `Promise<SessionUser>` (superset of `{id, role}` so `course-access.ts` compiles unchanged). Throw `AppError('FORBIDDEN')` in handlers; pages redirect `/forbidden` (route exists). No `can()`. |\n| FR-30 | Audit | Add optional `request?: Request` to `AuditInput`; `ip = getClientIp(request)` (first value of `x-forwarded-for`, trimmed). Keep inside try/catch. Shared helper with FR-7. |\n| FR-31 | Audit / Security | Enforce by construction: audit callers pass explicit metadata objects; optionally a small denylist strip (`password`, `passwordHash`, `token`) in `audit()` as defence-in-depth. Covered by test. |\n| FR-32 | App Shell & Nav | `shell.tsx` reads session — either the `(app)/layout.tsx` server component passes `getCurrentUser()` as a prop, or `SessionProvider` + `useSession`. Prop-passing avoids a client fetch and flash. Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. Role badge + initials via MUI `Chip`/`Avatar`. |\n| FR-33 | App Shell & Nav | Filter `navigation.ts` entries by role (server-side, before passing to shell). UX only — NFR-7 still applies on every page. |\n| FR-34 | Auth Core / REST API | `src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` exporting `{ GET, POST } = handlers` from `auth.ts`. |\n| FR-35 | Seed | Extend `prisma/seed.ts` idempotently (`upsert` by email): 6 ACTIVE users (bcrypt cost 12 of `SchoolHub123!`) + `invited@` INVITED with invite created via `createInviteToken` and link logged. Keep `office@`. Seeding goes through `tokens.ts` (FR-13 single-module rule). |\n| FR-36 | Test Harness | Unit (pure fns: policy, token hash/expiry, `computeLockout`, rate limiter, `safeCallbackUrl`) → design should keep these logic pieces as pure exported fns. Integration against DB for authorize/accept/reset/change. Playwright needs seeded users (FR-35) and the reset link from logs → e2e must read the token from DB or a test hook rather than email. |\n| FR-37 | Scope Discipline / Auth Core | No `/signup` route and no sign-up endpoint; the only path to ACTIVE is FR-16 (or admin `setUserStatus`). Middleware public list must not include any sign-up path. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Security / Token Module | SHA-256 at rest; `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on equal-length buffers. Unique index on `AuthToken.tokenHash` makes lookup O(1). |\n| NFR-2 | Security / Auth Core | Auth.js defaults already give HttpOnly, `__Secure-` prefix + Secure in prod, SameSite=Lax, CSRF on its own endpoints. **Custom POST routes (`accept-invite`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `account/password`) are outside Auth.js CSRF** — design must cover them (Origin/`Sec-Fetch-Site` same-origin check in route or middleware; SameSite=Lax alone doesn't protect unauthenticated endpoints). |\n| NFR-3 | Security / Credential Verification | Precompute a dummy bcrypt hash at module load; compare against it when the user is missing so timing matches. Same idea for forgot-password (no branch-visible timing difference). |\n| NFR-4 | Performance | bcrypt cost 12 ≈ 250 ms; budget fine. Keep authorize to 1 user query + 1 update + async audit; don't await non-critical writes serially beyond that. |\n| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Form `Alert` inside `aria-live=\"polite\"` region; on submit-with-errors focus first invalid `TextField` (`inputRef`). Shared form-error pattern across 5 auth forms. |\n| NFR-6 | Design System (MUI-only) | All auth pages, checklist, shell menu changes use MUI v9 only; dev must look up each component via mui-mcp. mui-mcp tools are visible in this environment (`useMuiDocs`, `fetchDocs`) — blocker 4 currently looks unblocked, dev must still confirm. |\n| NFR-7 | Authorization Helpers | Every new route handler and `(app)` page calls `requireUser()`/`requireRole()`; middleware is a first gate, not the only one. |\n| NFR-8 | REST API Surface | All custom auth routes: Zod parse → service → `{data}` / `{error:{code,message,details}}` using existing `http.ts` helpers. Auth.js catch-all is the sole exception (its own protocol). |\n| NFR-9 | Scope Discipline | Reuse `audit.ts`, `users.ts`, `requireRole.ts`, `useToast`, `AppError`; no renames; `course-access.ts` / `student-access.ts` untouched (constrains FR-29 return type). |\n| NFR-10 | Test Harness | Lint/typecheck/test green — the async `requireRole` change (FR-28/29) touches ~42 files, so typecheck is the safety net. `logger` only; `console.log` banned except the dev email transport. |\n| NFR-11 | Scope Discipline | No admin UI, SSO, MFA, magic links, or email infra. |\n| NFR-12 | Data Model / Auth UI | Timestamps UTC in DB. Lockout \"N minutes\" is a duration (timezone-independent); `lastLoginAt` display formatted in `SchoolSettings.timezone` (existing settings model). |\n\n## Cross-cutting items for `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **Edge/Node split** (FR-4, FR-11, FR-12): `auth.config.ts` edge-safe for middleware; `auth.ts` Node with Prisma/bcrypt.\n2. **requireRole goes async** (FR-28/29, blocker 3): ~48 sites, all already in async fns; return type superset of `{id, role}`.\n3. **Session re-issue after password change** (FR-11 vs FR-23): current session must survive its own `passwordChangedAt` bump.\n4. **CSRF for custom auth POSTs** (NFR-2): not covered by Auth.js.\n5. **Shared `getClientIp(request)`** (FR-7, FR-19, FR-30).\n6. **Shared password UI + Zod schema** (FR-15/17/18/21/23); decide whether the common-password list ships to the client.\n7. **Rate limiter is per-process** (FR-7/FR-19): fine for this PRD, Redis if multi-instance.\n8. **Additive migration only** (FR-1, blocker 1): two AuditLog indexes plus any missing User columns.\n\n## Blockers carried forward from intake\n\n- FR-1 schema divergences → resolved by additive migration (above).\n- FR-25 signature mismatch → keep the existing signatures.\n- FR-28/29 sync vs async → recommend async (call sites are fewer than intake reported and are all already async).\n- NFR-6 mui-mcp reachability → tools are registered in this environment; dev must still check before writing UI.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CBZYa2oAVyftJa8ze5TzYj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
