{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTVcQHUegxxz1vvbD9Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the requirements analysis notes for SH-4 (task `arch-research-reqs`) to `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`. A script check confirmed that all 59 requirements (FR-1–41 and NFR-1–18) have a row in the table and that every id I cite exists in `requirements.json`.\n\nThe file was already there, but from a different ticket (`abcd-1`), so I replaced it. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are also left over from `abcd-1`. They belong to the other architect tasks, so I didn't touch them; those tasks will overwrite them when they run.\n\nChecking the intake's codebase notes against the actual code turned up three problems the design task needs to handle:\n\n- **The cron email route would always be rejected.** The middleware returns 401 for any API request that isn't signed in, unless the path is on a short public list. `/api/internal/email/dispatch` isn't on that list. The test that a wrong token gets a 401 would still pass, but the real scheduled email send could never run. The fix is to add `/api/internal/` to the public list in `src/config/public-routes.ts` and let the route's own `CRON_SECRET` check be the only gate.\n- **The seed users don't exist.** `prisma/seed.ts` doesn't create `student@schoolhub.test` or `parent@schoolhub.test`, so FR-40 has no one to attach the sample notifications to. I recommend looking those users up and skipping them if they're missing, rather than creating user accounts in this ticket.\n- **There's no setup for database tests.** The test config only runs unit tests in a simulated browser. The locking and stuck-email tests (NFR-15) need a real Postgres, so they need a separate test config. It should skip itself when no test database is set, so `npm run test` stays green.\n\nOther points the design task should know:\n\n- The email outbox table has no user or type column, so the admin email log can only show the recipient's name and address. That's enough for FR-31, and no schema change is needed.\n- Notifications don't store a category, so the category filter on the list endpoint has to work out the matching types from the type registry.\n- On the intake's open questions:\n  - I accepted its defaults for the migration, the email-only account types, and the seed count of 3 per user.\n  - The mui-mcp lookup requirement (NFR-10) stays a blocker for the dev phase, because only dev can resolve it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":325,"cache_read_input_tokens":56574,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":325},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6976ca3f-645f-4a29-bf49-9d0601ccb133","uuid":"76804759-3073-4a35-86b3-c50bc4907de3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:01:12.545Z","request_id":"req_011CghTVc5vv7gC5VeZn3et8"}
