{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A59oqp6wmK336M741ieweQ","type":"tool_result","content":"architect\ndev\ndev-planning\nintake\ntelemetry\n\nartifacts/architect:\napi-contracts.json\nhandoff-to-dev-planning.json\nrequirements-analysis-notes.md\nsystem-design.md\ntech-stack-decisions.md\nthreat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/dev:\ndev-log.md\ndev-rerun-count.json\ntask-completion-markers.json\n\nartifacts/dev-planning:\nfile-ownership-matrix.json\nfile-structure.md\nimplementation-plan.json\nmodule-dependencies.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n\nartifacts/telemetry:\napi-retries.jsonl\ndaemon-handoff.json\nknowledge-log.jsonl\nmetering.jsonl\nphase-sessions.json\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-6\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T05:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-06: Bell Schedule & Timetable (SCH-006)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind yet. 5 migrations exist (latest 20261104120000_notifications_email), so this ticket needs a new additive migration.\",\n    \"Prisma requires back-relations for the FR-1 relations: Course.timetableSlots, Period.slots and Room.timetableSlots. They are additive and rename nothing.\",\n    \"Course has teacherId, coTeacherIds String[] (query with `has`), sectionId (null for cross-section electives), kind CORE|ELECTIVE, archivedAt and academicYearId. Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED with @@index([studentId, status]). Section has roomId (the homeroom room) and homeroomTeacherId.\",\n    \"Room has name @unique and archivedAt. Seeded rooms: Room 101, Room 102, Science Lab A, Gymnasium, Art Studio.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings.timezone exists (default 'UTC'). date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and @mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0 (TimeField) are installed. @dnd-kit/core is NOT installed and must be added.\",\n    \"prisma/seed.ts only seeds settings, academic year 2026-2027, terms, grade levels, subjects (MATH, ELA, SCI, SOC, PE, ART), and rooms. It seeds no users, sections, courses or enrollments. The PRD seed (7A/7B week, Robotics Club) and the acceptance-criteria personas (Tom, Sam, Pat) have nothing to attach to yet.\",\n    \"The seeded subject codes are ELA and SOC, not the ENG and HIST the PRD seed section names.\",\n    \"The shared UI components live in src/components/<Name>/ (ConfirmDialog, DataTable, PageHeader, EmptyState, UserPicker, Toast/useToast...), not in src/components/shared/. useToast() is at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts and exposes showToast({ message, severity }).\",\n    \"Feature services follow the PRD-05 subdirectory precedent (src/server/sections/sections-service.ts, src/server/courses/courses-service.ts). The PRD mandates src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts.\",\n    \"These access helpers exist: requireUser/requireRole/requirePageUser/requirePageRole (src/server/auth/requireRole.ts), assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse (course-access.ts), and getAccessibleStudentIds/assertCanViewStudent (student-access.ts). The HTTP helpers in src/server/http.ts are ok, paginated, apiError, AppError, withHandler, parseBody and parseQuery. audit() is in src/server/audit.ts.\",\n    \"The student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]). student-tabs.ts currently has 'courses'. course-tabs.ts exists with 'overview' and 'roster', and the Course 'Schedule' tab goes there.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts entries support an optional `group: 'Administration'`. There is no Timetable entry yet.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY } and model Period (name, startTime/endTime 'HH:MM' strings in school timezone, kind default CLASS, order Int @unique, createdAt/updatedAt) exactly as specified.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add model SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id (ISO 1=Mon…7=Sun), isTeaching Boolean @default(true) }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add model TimetableSlot (academicYearId, courseId → Course onDelete Cascade, dayOfWeek 1–7, periodId → Period, roomId? → Room, timestamps) with @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId]) and @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId]).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Create one new additive Prisma migration for FR-1–FR-3, including the back-relation fields Prisma requires on Course, Period and Room. Do not rename or alter any existing model.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 + Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'; inferred from Prisma relation rules\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Bell schedule page /admin/timetable/periods (ADMIN): an ordered MUI Table of periods (name, start, end, kind) with add / edit / delete / reorder. Times are edited with MUI X TimeField.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Period validation (shared Zod + service): times are 'HH:MM' 24-hour, endTime is after startTime, and periods must not overlap any other period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Teaching days editor: seven MUI ToggleButtons (Mon–Sun). Turning off a day that has slots shows a confirmation with the number of slots to be removed, and confirming deletes those slots and marks the day non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Deleting a period that still has slots is refused with 409 CONFLICT, and the message/details give the count of affected slots.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: teacher. Reject when any other slot in the same academic year at (day, period) belongs to a course whose teacher or any co-teacher equals the new course's teacher or any co-teacher. Message: 'Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: room. When roomId is set, reject if another slot at (day, period) in the same academic year uses the same room. Message: 'Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: section. Reject if another slot at (day, period) belongs to a course with the same non-null sectionId. Message: 'Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: student overlap. Reject if any student has ACTIVE enrollment in both the new course and a course in another slot at (day, period). The message includes the student count: 'Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4; Acceptance Criteria 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Reject slots on a non-CLASS period ('Period '<name>' is not a class period.') or on a non-teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5; FR-1 TimetableSlot.dayOfWeek comment; Acceptance Criteria 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"validateSlot(input) in src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts returns ALL clashes (not just the first). When moving a slot (PATCH), the slot itself is excluded from comparison.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3 (closing sentence); FR-4.3 move\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Timetable editor /admin/timetable: a view selector (Section default, Teacher, Room), an entity picker (Autocomplete) and an academic year selector.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Editor grid: columns are teaching days and rows are periods in order. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and non-droppable. A filled cell shows the subject colour, course code, teacher surname and room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Section view sidebar lists the section's courses, each with a 'placed N' counter. Dropping a course on a cell calls POST /api/timetable/slots with the section's homeroom room (Section.roomId) as the default roomId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Dragging an existing slot to another cell moves it (PATCH). Dragging a slot out of the grid, or pressing Delete on a focused slot, removes it after a confirmation Dialog.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"While dragging, cells that would clash are tinted red and also show an icon and a Tooltip with the messages. These come from a clash map preloaded via GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId=.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.4; NFR-3 Accessibility\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"If the server rejects a drop or move, the card snaps back and an error toast (useToast) lists every clash returned in details.clashes[].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Clicking a slot opens an MUI Popover with an Autocomplete to change the room. The picker lists only rooms free at that day/period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Keyboard alternative: every grid cell is focusable, and Enter on an empty cell opens a 'Place course' Dialog listing the section's courses.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Drag behaviour uses @dnd-kit/core only. The grid is an MUI Table or CSS-grid Box, and every course card and cell is an MUI Paper/Card with Chips and Tooltips.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.8; UI component rule 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Personal timetable page /timetable for TEACHER (own courses incl. co-teaching), STUDENT (ACTIVE enrollments) and PARENT. It uses the same grid read-only and highlights the current period when today is a teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"A PARENT with more than one linked child sees a child selector on /timetable, and switching it changes the grid.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criteria 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"A 'Week' / 'Today' toggle. The Today view is a vertical list of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus 'Now' (in progress) and 'Next' badges.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2; Acceptance Criteria 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Timetable' student tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts that reuses the read-only grid for that student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Add a course 'Schedule' tab (registered in the existing src/config/course-tabs.ts) that lists the course's weekly meeting times (day, period, times, room).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.4; registry file inferred from the brownfield course-tabs.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"A 'Print' button on any grid view gives a print-friendly layout (@media print, A4 landscape, no sidebar). The printed page contains only the grid, the entity name and the academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.5; Acceptance Criteria 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Export getScheduleForDate(userOrSection, date), which returns an ordered list of { period, course, room } for that date and returns empty on non-teaching days. Holidays are deferred to PRD-14.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Goals 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Export getCurrentSlot(user, now), which returns the slot in progress (period start ≤ now < end in the school timezone) or null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Navigation: add 'Timetable' (/timetable) for TEACHER, STUDENT and PARENT. Add 'Timetable editor' (/admin/timetable) and 'Bell schedule' (/admin/timetable/periods) for ADMIN in the Administration group.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Periods API: GET /api/periods (any role, ordered). POST /api/periods, PATCH and DELETE /api/periods/:id, and POST /api/periods/reorder { periodIds } are ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"School days API: GET /api/school-days (any role) and PUT /api/school-days (ADMIN).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable?view=section|teacher|room&id=&academicYearId= returns slots with course, teacher and room. ADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use only their own teacher view and sections they are homeroom teacher of; anything else is 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId= (ADMIN) returns { '<day>-<periodId>': [clash messages] } for that course's academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; FR-4.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Slots API (ADMIN): POST /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId? }, PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id and DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id. A clash returns 409 CONFLICT with details.clashes[] and saves nothing. academicYearId is derived from the course server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"GET /api/me/timetable?studentId= (any role) returns the caller's own timetable. studentId is required for a PARENT with multiple children and must be a linked child; otherwise 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Zod schemas for periods, school days, slots and timetable queries live in src/lib/validators/timetable.ts, shared by the forms and the handlers.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Fixed technology decisions (Validation) and §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Write AuditLog rows via audit() for slot create/move/delete, period create/update/delete/reorder, and teaching-day changes (including the cascade-deleted slot count).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout ('Mutations that change records owned by someone else write an AuditLog row'). Whether school-wide admin config counts as 'owned by someone else' is assumed.\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Seed the periods: Period 1 08:00–08:45, Period 2 08:50–09:35, Break 09:35–09:55 (BREAK), Period 3 09:55–10:40, Period 4 10:45–11:30, Lunch 11:30–12:15 (LUNCH), Period 5 12:15–13:00, Period 6 13:05–13:50. The seed is idempotent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"Seed SchoolDay rows 1–7 with Monday–Friday teaching and Saturday–Sunday non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; FR-1 SchoolDay comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-43\", \"description\": \"Seed a complete clash-free week for 7A and 7B: MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2 and ART 2 (21 of 30 class slots each), plus Robotics Club on Wednesday Period 6 with 7A and 7B free then.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data. The prerequisite sections, courses and subjects are not in the brownfield seed (see FR-44).\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-44\", \"description\": \"Seed the minimal prerequisite fixtures the timetable seed and acceptance criteria rely on: teacher Tom (teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B), student Sam (7A, enrolled in Robotics Club and ART-7A), parent Pat linked to two children, sections 7A/7B with homeroom rooms, their courses, and the Robotics Club elective (sectionId null). Reuse the existing ELA/SOC subjects for ENG/HIST.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Inferred from PRD §Seed Data and Acceptance Criteria 1, 2, 4, 5. The brownfield prisma/seed.ts has no users, sections or courses.\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-45\", \"description\": \"All 'now' calculations (current period highlight, Now/Next badges, getCurrentSlot, today's day-of-week) use SchoolSettings.timezone, not the server or browser timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Period.startTime comment; Test Requirements ('across timezones'); Platform Context timestamps rule\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Integrity: clash validation and the slot insert/update run in one SERIALIZABLE Prisma transaction (retry on serialization failure), so two concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1; Test Requirements (integration)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the editor loads a section week (up to 7 days × 12 periods) in under 400 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: the availability map for one course returns in under 300 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: drag-and-drop has a keyboard alternative (FR-22), and colour is never the only signal (clashing cells also show an icon and a tooltip; 'Now'/'Next' are text badges).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, and every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker; never guess props.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 1, 2, 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"No banned UI/styling libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, FullCalendar, react-datepicker, notistack, etc.; enforced by ESLint no-restricted-imports). The only new dependency allowed is the non-visual @dnd-kit/core (pinned), plus @dnd-kit/sortable only if needed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 3, 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: every handler and server page enforces role and per-entity access server-side via requireUser/requireRole and the existing access helpers. Hiding UI is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout (requireRole) and §Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"API conventions: thin handlers (Zod → service → JSON), the { data } / { error: { code, message, details } } shape, and the standard error codes (409 CONFLICT for clashes and for period delete-with-slots).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield reuse: never re-scaffold. Reuse the existing helpers (http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, the access helpers). New service at src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts. Do not rename existing routes or models.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context intro; FR-3 service path\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test all keep passing with TypeScript strict.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: every clash rule (including co-teacher and student overlap), the non-class period/day rule, period overlap validation, and current/next slot calculation across timezones.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Integration test: concurrent conflicting slot inserts, where only one succeeds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Playwright e2e: drag a course into a cell, see a clash error snackbar on a conflicting drop, and the student Today view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Scope guard: no automatic timetable solver, no A/B multi-week cycles, no substitute-teacher management, and no holiday handling (PRD-14). A single repeating week only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; FR-6.1; Constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"English-only UI, single school, and support for the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari (including print output).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,\n  \"confidenceMethod\": \"Weighted mean over 61 requirements (HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40): 54 HIGH, 5 MEDIUM, 2 LOW.\",\n\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-44: The brownfield seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments. May intake assume the timetable seed also creates minimal fixtures (Tom, Sam, Pat + 2 children, 7A/7B, the courses, Robotics Club)?\",\n        \"FR-43: The seed subjects are ELA and SOC, but the PRD says ENG and HIST. Should courses reuse ELA/SOC (with course codes ENG-7A/HIST-7A), or should new subjects be added?\",\n        \"FR-21: No API listed returns free rooms for a day/period. Should we add a small ADMIN endpoint (e.g. GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek=&periodId=&academicYearId=) or extend the availability response?\",\n        \"FR-7: How does the client learn the slot count before confirming a teaching-day switch-off? Option A: GET /api/school-days returns slotCount per day. Option B: PUT without confirm returns 409 with details.slotCount.\",\n        \"FR-5/FR-33: Must Period.order match chronological startTime order, or is reorder purely presentational? Also, Period.order @unique means the reorder needs a two-phase update in one transaction.\",\n        \"FR-40: Should timetable and bell-schedule mutations be audited, given they are school-wide admin configuration?\",\n        \"FR-35: Does 'own sections' for TEACHER mean homeroom sections only, or also sections whose courses they teach?\",\n        \"Archived courses and rooms (archivedAt set): exclude them from the editor sidebar, the room picker and the clash checks?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-44 default: seed minimal idempotent fixtures needed by the PRD seed and acceptance criteria.\",\n        \"FR-43 default: reuse the existing ELA and SOC subjects. Course codes follow the PRD names (MATH-7A, ENG-7A, SCI-7A, HIST-7A, PE-7A, ART-7A, likewise for 7B, and ROBOTICS).\",\n        \"FR-21 default: Architect decides. The recommendation is one ADMIN-only GET /api/timetable/free-rooms endpoint, the smallest addition.\",\n        \"FR-7 default: GET /api/school-days includes slotCount per day for the current academic year. PUT deletes the slots of switched-off days in one transaction.\",\n        \"FR-5 default: order is the display order and is not forced to be chronological. Reorder uses up/down buttons (no @dnd-kit/sortable) and a two-phase update in a transaction.\",\n        \"FR-40 default: audit slot, period and school-day mutations (LOW, Architect to confirm).\",\n        \"FR-35 default: TEACHER can view their own teacher view, sections they are homeroom teacher of (per the §Roles wording), and sections of courses they teach.\",\n        \"Archived default: archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-6\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T05:31:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 61,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"FR-44: The brownfield seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments. Default: the seed adds minimal idempotent fixtures (Tom, Sam, Pat + 2 children, 7A/7B, the courses, Robotics Club) so that the PRD seed and the acceptance criteria work.\",\n    \"FR-43: The PRD's ENG and HIST subjects do not exist (the seed has ELA and SOC). Default: reuse ELA/SOC, with course codes ENG-7A/HIST-7A.\",\n    \"FR-21: No listed API returns free rooms for a day/period. The Architect should pick the smallest option (recommended: ADMIN-only GET /api/timetable/free-rooms).\",\n    \"FR-7: The confirmation slot count is not covered by the API. Default: GET /api/school-days includes slotCount per day.\",\n    \"FR-4/NFR-6: A new additive migration is needed, with back-relations on Course, Period and Room. @dnd-kit/core must be added as a pinned dependency.\",\n    \"NFR-5: Dev must reach the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24f05be5-3d50-40f4-9d3a-c65b90598d64","uuid":"fc1090e1-bcf4-40a5-8adc-79ab3d928be3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:14:01.455Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"architect\ndev\ndev-planning\nintake\ntelemetry\n\nartifacts/architect:\napi-contracts.json\nhandoff-to-dev-planning.json\nrequirements-analysis-notes.md\nsystem-design.md\ntech-stack-decisions.md\nthreat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/dev:\ndev-log.md\ndev-rerun-count.json\ntask-completion-markers.json\n\nartifacts/dev-planning:\nfile-ownership-matrix.json\nfile-structure.md\nimplementation-plan.json\nmodule-dependencies.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n\nartifacts/telemetry:\napi-retries.jsonl\ndaemon-handoff.json\nknowledge-log.jsonl\nmetering.jsonl\nphase-sessions.json\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-6\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T05:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-06: Bell Schedule & Timetable (SCH-006)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind yet. 5 migrations exist (latest 20261104120000_notifications_email), so this ticket needs a new additive migration.\",\n    \"Prisma requires back-relations for the FR-1 relations: Course.timetableSlots, Period.slots and Room.timetableSlots. They are additive and rename nothing.\",\n    \"Course has teacherId, coTeacherIds String[] (query with `has`), sectionId (null for cross-section electives), kind CORE|ELECTIVE, archivedAt and academicYearId. Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED with @@index([studentId, status]). Section has roomId (the homeroom room) and homeroomTeacherId.\",\n    \"Room has name @unique and archivedAt. Seeded rooms: Room 101, Room 102, Science Lab A, Gymnasium, Art Studio.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings.timezone exists (default 'UTC'). date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and @mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0 (TimeField) are installed. @dnd-kit/core is NOT installed and must be added.\",\n    \"prisma/seed.ts only seeds settings, academic year 2026-2027, terms, grade levels, subjects (MATH, ELA, SCI, SOC, PE, ART), and rooms. It seeds no users, sections, courses or enrollments. The PRD seed (7A/7B week, Robotics Club) and the acceptance-criteria personas (Tom, Sam, Pat) have nothing to attach to yet.\",\n    \"The seeded subject codes are ELA and SOC, not the ENG and HIST the PRD seed section names.\",\n    \"The shared UI components live in src/components/<Name>/ (ConfirmDialog, DataTable, PageHeader, EmptyState, UserPicker, Toast/useToast...), not in src/components/shared/. useToast() is at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts and exposes showToast({ message, severity }).\",\n    \"Feature services follow the PRD-05 subdirectory precedent (src/server/sections/sections-service.ts, src/server/courses/courses-service.ts). The PRD mandates src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts.\",\n    \"These access helpers exist: requireUser/requireRole/requirePageUser/requirePageRole (src/server/auth/requireRole.ts), assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse (course-access.ts), and getAccessibleStudentIds/assertCanViewStudent (student-access.ts). The HTTP helpers in src/server/http.ts are ok, paginated, apiError, AppError, withHandler, parseBody and parseQuery. audit() is in src/server/audit.ts.\",\n    \"The student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]). student-tabs.ts currently has 'courses'. course-tabs.ts exists with 'overview' and 'roster', and the Course 'Schedule' tab goes there.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts entries support an optional `group: 'Administration'`. There is no Timetable entry yet.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY } and model Period (name, startTime/endTime 'HH:MM' strings in school timezone, kind default CLASS, order Int @unique, createdAt/updatedAt) exactly as specified.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add model SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id (ISO 1=Mon…7=Sun), isTeaching Boolean @default(true) }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add model TimetableSlot (academicYearId, courseId → Course onDelete Cascade, dayOfWeek 1–7, periodId → Period, roomId? → Room, timestamps) with @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId]) and @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId]).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Create one new additive Prisma migration for FR-1–FR-3, including the back-relation fields Prisma requires on Course, Period and Room. Do not rename or alter any existing model.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 + Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'; inferred from Prisma relation rules\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Bell schedule page /admin/timetable/periods (ADMIN): an ordered MUI Table of periods (name, start, end, kind) with add / edit / delete / reorder. Times are edited with MUI X TimeField.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Period validation (shared Zod + service): times are 'HH:MM' 24-hour, endTime is after startTime, and periods must not overlap any other period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Teaching days editor: seven MUI ToggleButtons (Mon–Sun). Turning off a day that has slots shows a confirmation with the number of slots to be removed, and confirming deletes those slots and marks the day non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Deleting a period that still has slots is refused with 409 CONFLICT, and the message/details give the count of affected slots.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: teacher. Reject when any other slot in the same academic year at (day, period) belongs to a course whose teacher or any co-teacher equals the new course's teacher or any co-teacher. Message: 'Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: room. When roomId is set, reject if another slot at (day, period) in the same academic year uses the same room. Message: 'Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: section. Reject if another slot at (day, period) belongs to a course with the same non-null sectionId. Message: 'Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: student overlap. Reject if any student has ACTIVE enrollment in both the new course and a course in another slot at (day, period). The message includes the student count: 'Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4; Acceptance Criteria 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Reject slots on a non-CLASS period ('Period '<name>' is not a class period.') or on a non-teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5; FR-1 TimetableSlot.dayOfWeek comment; Acceptance Criteria 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"validateSlot(input) in src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts returns ALL clashes (not just the first). When moving a slot (PATCH), the slot itself is excluded from comparison.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3 (closing sentence); FR-4.3 move\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Timetable editor /admin/timetable: a view selector (Section default, Teacher, Room), an entity picker (Autocomplete) and an academic year selector.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Editor grid: columns are teaching days and rows are periods in order. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and non-droppable. A filled cell shows the subject colour, course code, teacher surname and room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Section view sidebar lists the section's courses, each with a 'placed N' counter. Dropping a course on a cell calls POST /api/timetable/slots with the section's homeroom room (Section.roomId) as the default roomId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Dragging an existing slot to another cell moves it (PATCH). Dragging a slot out of the grid, or pressing Delete on a focused slot, removes it after a confirmation Dialog.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"While dragging, cells that would clash are tinted red and also show an icon and a Tooltip with the messages. These come from a clash map preloaded via GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId=.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.4; NFR-3 Accessibility\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"If the server rejects a drop or move, the card snaps back and an error toast (useToast) lists every clash returned in details.clashes[].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Clicking a slot opens an MUI Popover with an Autocomplete to change the room. The picker lists only rooms free at that day/period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Keyboard alternative: every grid cell is focusable, and Enter on an empty cell opens a 'Place course' Dialog listing the section's courses.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Drag behaviour uses @dnd-kit/core only. The grid is an MUI Table or CSS-grid Box, and every course card and cell is an MUI Paper/Card with Chips and Tooltips.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.8; UI component rule 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Personal timetable page /timetable for TEACHER (own courses incl. co-teaching), STUDENT (ACTIVE enrollments) and PARENT. It uses the same grid read-only and highlights the current period when today is a teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"A PARENT with more than one linked child sees a child selector on /timetable, and switching it changes the grid.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criteria 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"A 'Week' / 'Today' toggle. The Today view is a vertical list of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus 'Now' (in progress) and 'Next' badges.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2; Acceptance Criteria 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Timetable' student tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts that reuses the read-only grid for that student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Add a course 'Schedule' tab (registered in the existing src/config/course-tabs.ts) that lists the course's weekly meeting times (day, period, times, room).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.4; registry file inferred from the brownfield course-tabs.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"A 'Print' button on any grid view gives a print-friendly layout (@media print, A4 landscape, no sidebar). The printed page contains only the grid, the entity name and the academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.5; Acceptance Criteria 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Export getScheduleForDate(userOrSection, date), which returns an ordered list of { period, course, room } for that date and returns empty on non-teaching days. Holidays are deferred to PRD-14.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Goals 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Export getCurrentSlot(user, now), which returns the slot in progress (period start ≤ now < end in the school timezone) or null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Navigation: add 'Timetable' (/timetable) for TEACHER, STUDENT and PARENT. Add 'Timetable editor' (/admin/timetable) and 'Bell schedule' (/admin/timetable/periods) for ADMIN in the Administration group.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Periods API: GET /api/periods (any role, ordered). POST /api/periods, PATCH and DELETE /api/periods/:id, and POST /api/periods/reorder { periodIds } are ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"School days API: GET /api/school-days (any role) and PUT /api/school-days (ADMIN).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable?view=section|teacher|room&id=&academicYearId= returns slots with course, teacher and room. ADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use only their own teacher view and sections they are homeroom teacher of; anything else is 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId= (ADMIN) returns { '<day>-<periodId>': [clash messages] } for that course's academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; FR-4.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Slots API (ADMIN): POST /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId? }, PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id and DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id. A clash returns 409 CONFLICT with details.clashes[] and saves nothing. academicYearId is derived from the course server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"GET /api/me/timetable?studentId= (any role) returns the caller's own timetable. studentId is required for a PARENT with multiple children and must be a linked child; otherwise 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Zod schemas for periods, school days, slots and timetable queries live in src/lib/validators/timetable.ts, shared by the forms and the handlers.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Fixed technology decisions (Validation) and §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Write AuditLog rows via audit() for slot create/move/delete, period create/update/delete/reorder, and teaching-day changes (including the cascade-deleted slot count).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout ('Mutations that change records owned by someone else write an AuditLog row'). Whether school-wide admin config counts as 'owned by someone else' is assumed.\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Seed the periods: Period 1 08:00–08:45, Period 2 08:50–09:35, Break 09:35–09:55 (BREAK), Period 3 09:55–10:40, Period 4 10:45–11:30, Lunch 11:30–12:15 (LUNCH), Period 5 12:15–13:00, Period 6 13:05–13:50. The seed is idempotent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"Seed SchoolDay rows 1–7 with Monday–Friday teaching and Saturday–Sunday non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; FR-1 SchoolDay comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-43\", \"description\": \"Seed a complete clash-free week for 7A and 7B: MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2 and ART 2 (21 of 30 class slots each), plus Robotics Club on Wednesday Period 6 with 7A and 7B free then.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data. The prerequisite sections, courses and subjects are not in the brownfield seed (see FR-44).\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-44\", \"description\": \"Seed the minimal prerequisite fixtures the timetable seed and acceptance criteria rely on: teacher Tom (teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B), student Sam (7A, enrolled in Robotics Club and ART-7A), parent Pat linked to two children, sections 7A/7B with homeroom rooms, their courses, and the Robotics Club elective (sectionId null). Reuse the existing ELA/SOC subjects for ENG/HIST.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Inferred from PRD §Seed Data and Acceptance Criteria 1, 2, 4, 5. The brownfield prisma/seed.ts has no users, sections or courses.\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-45\", \"description\": \"All 'now' calculations (current period highlight, Now/Next badges, getCurrentSlot, today's day-of-week) use SchoolSettings.timezone, not the server or browser timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Period.startTime comment; Test Requirements ('across timezones'); Platform Context timestamps rule\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Integrity: clash validation and the slot insert/update run in one SERIALIZABLE Prisma transaction (retry on serialization failure), so two concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1; Test Requirements (integration)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the editor loads a section week (up to 7 days × 12 periods) in under 400 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: the availability map for one course returns in under 300 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: drag-and-drop has a keyboard alternative (FR-22), and colour is never the only signal (clashing cells also show an icon and a tooltip; 'Now'/'Next' are text badges).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, and every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker; never guess props.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 1, 2, 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"No banned UI/styling libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, FullCalendar, react-datepicker, notistack, etc.; enforced by ESLint no-restricted-imports). The only new dependency allowed is the non-visual @dnd-kit/core (pinned), plus @dnd-kit/sortable only if needed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 3, 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: every handler and server page enforces role and per-entity access server-side via requireUser/requireRole and the existing access helpers. Hiding UI is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout (requireRole) and §Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"API conventions: thin handlers (Zod → service → JSON), the { data } / { error: { code, message, details } } shape, and the standard error codes (409 CONFLICT for clashes and for period delete-with-slots).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield reuse: never re-scaffold. Reuse the existing helpers (http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, the access helpers). New service at src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts. Do not rename existing routes or models.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context intro; FR-3 service path\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test all keep passing with TypeScript strict.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: every clash rule (including co-teacher and student overlap), the non-class period/day rule, period overlap validation, and current/next slot calculation across timezones.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Integration test: concurrent conflicting slot inserts, where only one succeeds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Playwright e2e: drag a course into a cell, see a clash error snackbar on a conflicting drop, and the student Today view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Scope guard: no automatic timetable solver, no A/B multi-week cycles, no substitute-teacher management, and no holiday handling (PRD-14). A single repeating week only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; FR-6.1; Constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"English-only UI, single school, and support for the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari (including print output).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,\n  \"confidenceMethod\": \"Weighted mean over 61 requirements (HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40): 54 HIGH, 5 MEDIUM, 2 LOW.\",\n\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-44: The brownfield seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments. May intake assume the timetable seed also creates minimal fixtures (Tom, Sam, Pat + 2 children, 7A/7B, the courses, Robotics Club)?\",\n        \"FR-43: The seed subjects are ELA and SOC, but the PRD says ENG and HIST. Should courses reuse ELA/SOC (with course codes ENG-7A/HIST-7A), or should new subjects be added?\",\n        \"FR-21: No API listed returns free rooms for a day/period. Should we add a small ADMIN endpoint (e.g. GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek=&periodId=&academicYearId=) or extend the availability response?\",\n        \"FR-7: How does the client learn the slot count before confirming a teaching-day switch-off? Option A: GET /api/school-days returns slotCount per day. Option B: PUT without confirm returns 409 with details.slotCount.\",\n        \"FR-5/FR-33: Must Period.order match chronological startTime order, or is reorder purely presentational? Also, Period.order @unique means the reorder needs a two-phase update in one transaction.\",\n        \"FR-40: Should timetable and bell-schedule mutations be audited, given they are school-wide admin configuration?\",\n        \"FR-35: Does 'own sections' for TEACHER mean homeroom sections only, or also sections whose courses they teach?\",\n        \"Archived courses and rooms (archivedAt set): exclude them from the editor sidebar, the room picker and the clash checks?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-44 default: seed minimal idempotent fixtures needed by the PRD seed and acceptance criteria.\",\n        \"FR-43 default: reuse the existing ELA and SOC subjects. Course codes follow the PRD names (MATH-7A, ENG-7A, SCI-7A, HIST-7A, PE-7A, ART-7A, likewise for 7B, and ROBOTICS).\",\n        \"FR-21 default: Architect decides. The recommendation is one ADMIN-only GET /api/timetable/free-rooms endpoint, the smallest addition.\",\n        \"FR-7 default: GET /api/school-days includes slotCount per day for the current academic year. PUT deletes the slots of switched-off days in one transaction.\",\n        \"FR-5 default: order is the display order and is not forced to be chronological. Reorder uses up/down buttons (no @dnd-kit/sortable) and a two-phase update in a transaction.\",\n        \"FR-40 default: audit slot, period and school-day mutations (LOW, Architect to confirm).\",\n        \"FR-35 default: TEACHER can view their own teacher view, sections they are homeroom teacher of (per the §Roles wording), and sections of courses they teach.\",\n        \"Archived default: archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-6\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T05:31:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 61,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"FR-44: The brownfield seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments. Default: the seed adds minimal idempotent fixtures (Tom, Sam, Pat + 2 children, 7A/7B, the courses, Robotics Club) so that the PRD seed and the acceptance criteria work.\",\n    \"FR-43: The PRD's ENG and HIST subjects do not exist (the seed has ELA and SOC). Default: reuse ELA/SOC, with course codes ENG-7A/HIST-7A.\",\n    \"FR-21: No listed API returns free rooms for a day/period. The Architect should pick the smallest option (recommended: ADMIN-only GET /api/timetable/free-rooms).\",\n    \"FR-7: The confirmation slot count is not covered by the API. Default: GET /api/school-days includes slotCount per day.\",\n    \"FR-4/NFR-6: A new additive migration is needed, with back-relations on Course, Period and Room. @dnd-kit/core must be added as a pinned dependency.\",\n    \"NFR-5: Dev must reach the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01A59oqp6wmK336M741ieweQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
