{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013GaneQDXFMijKbtVFRKcWz","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24f05be5-3d50-40f4-9d3a-c65b90598d64","uuid":"1332231c-0846-4e09-a54b-d55ffb1c4cdb","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:15:45.742Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-6\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`, which covers PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable\n(45 FR and 16 NFR, 61 requirements) at 96% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (`api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`,\n> `system-design.md`, `tech-stack-decisions.md`, `threat-model-notes.json`) are **stale SH-4 outputs**.\n> The other sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-6 input, except for\n> `tech-stack-decisions.md` once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-6.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Validation**, **Clash Engine**, **Service**,\n**Admin API**, **Read API**, **Access Control**, **UI: Bell Schedule**, **UI: Editor**,\n**UI: Personal Timetable**, **UI: Tabs/Nav**, **Print**, **Time/TZ**, **Audit**, **Seed**,\n**Concurrency**, **Performance**, **Accessibility**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these confirm or add to intake)\n\n| # | Fact | Design implication |\n|---|------|--------------------|\n| B1 | `prisma/schema.prisma` has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind. The latest migration is `20261104120000_notifications_email`. | The new migration needs a later timestamp (for example `20261105000000_timetable`). |\n| B2 | `Room` already has a back-relation `sections Section[]`. `Course` has `enrollments` but no slots relation. | Add `Room.timetableSlots`, `Course.timetableSlots` and `Period.slots`. All are additive. |\n| B3 | `Course.coTeacherIds String[]`, nullable `sectionId`, `archivedAt`, `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. `Enrollment @@index([studentId, status])`, `onDelete: Cascade` from Course. | The teacher clash check needs `teacherId IN set OR coTeacherIds hasSome set`. The student-overlap check joins Enrollment on both courses. |\n| B4 | `Section.roomId?` (homeroom room) and `Section.homeroomTeacherId?`. `@@unique([academicYearId, name])`. | FR-17 uses `Section.roomId` as the default room. FR-35 checks TEACHER access through `homeroomTeacherId`. |\n| B5 | `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` with `@@index([studentId])`. `/api/me/children` already exists. | FR-25 and FR-38 can reuse `/api/me/children` for the child selector, so no new endpoint is needed. Parent access goes through `assertCanViewStudent`. |\n| B6 | `SchoolSettings.timezone` (default `'UTC'`) is read by the cached `getSchoolSettings()` in `src/server/services/settings.ts`. `src/lib/dates.ts` has `formatInSchoolTz` (date-fns-tz `formatInTimeZone`). | All \"now\" maths (FR-31, FR-45) uses `formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')` and ISO day `'i'`. Plain `HH:MM` string comparison then works. |\n| B7 | SERIALIZABLE precedent: `academicYears.ts` and `terms.ts` use `prisma.$transaction(fn, { isolationLevel: Serializable })` but **do not retry**. There is no P2034 handling in `src/`. | NFR-1 needs a small retry wrapper for P2034 (serialization failure). It is new code, so keep it local to timetable-service unless the design wants to reuse it. |\n| B8 | `http.ts` has `ApiErrorCode` with CONFLICT=409 and FORBIDDEN=403, plus `AppError`, `withHandler` (maps P2002 → CONFLICT, P2025 → NOT_FOUND), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. | Clashes are thrown as `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })`. The handler shape is already standard. |\n| B9 | `audit({ actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request })` never throws. By convention `action` is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|delete`. | FR-40 actions: `timetableSlot.create\\|update\\|delete`, `period.create\\|update\\|delete\\|reorder`, `schoolDay.update` (metadata includes `deletedSlotCount`). |\n| B10 | Validators live in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts` (courses, sections, ...). Feature services live in `src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts`. Tabs live in `src/config/course-tabs.ts` and `student-tabs.ts` (`{ key, label, href, roles }`). | FR-39: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`. FR-27 and FR-28 each register one entry. |\n| B11 | API route dirs exist: `rooms`, `sections`, `courses`, `me/*`, `admin/*`. There are no `periods`, `school-days` or `timetable` routes. App admin pages: `admin/courses`, `admin/sections`, `admin/email-log`. | Everything here is new. Nothing gets renamed. |\n| B12 | `package.json` pins `@mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0`, `date-fns 3.6.0`, `date-fns-tz 3.2.0` and `@prisma/client 5.20.0`. `@dnd-kit/*` is absent. | FR-23 and NFR-6 add exactly one pinned dependency, `@dnd-kit/core`. Reorder (FR-5) uses up/down buttons, so `@dnd-kit/sortable` is not needed. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n### Data model and migration\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `enum PeriodKind` and `model Period`. Store `startTime`/`endTime` as `String` `HH:MM`. `order Int @unique` affects reorder (see FR-5). |\n| FR-2 | Data Model | `SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id, isTeaching Boolean }` is a 7-row lookup with no relations. Do not add a FK from TimetableSlot to it (the PRD defines `dayOfWeek Int`). |\n| FR-3 | Data Model | Index `@@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` covers every clash query (all are scoped to year + day + period). `academicYearId` is denormalised from Course. It is set server-side only (FR-37). `periodId` has no cascade, so deletion is guarded by FR-8 in the service. `roomId?` with `onDelete: SetNull` is the safe default, and rooms are archived rather than deleted. |\n| FR-4 | Migration | One additive migration plus the B2 back-relations. `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then review the SQL. It should only contain CREATE TYPE, CREATE TABLE and CREATE INDEX statements. |\n\n### Validation and the clash engine (core domain)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-6 | Validation + Service | Zod handles the `^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$` format and `end > start`. These are plain string comparisons, so no Date parsing is needed. The overlap check against other periods is in the service, because it needs the DB: `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self on update. |\n| FR-9 | Clash Engine | Teacher set T = {teacherId} ∪ coTeacherIds of the new course. Other slots at (year, day, period) whose course has teacherId ∈ T or coTeacherIds overlapping T. The message needs the teacher's display name, so join User. |\n| FR-10 | Clash Engine | Only when roomId ≠ null: same year, day, period and roomId. |\n| FR-11 | Clash Engine | Only when the course's sectionId ≠ null: another slot whose course.sectionId equals it. A cross-section elective (sectionId null) is skipped by this rule but still caught by FR-12. |\n| FR-12 | Clash Engine | One grouped query: count distinct studentIds where Enrollment(ACTIVE) is in the new course and also in course X, for each X in a slot at (year, day, period). Produce one clash per conflicting course with its count N. Use raw SQL or `groupBy`, because this is the costliest rule (NFR-3). |\n| FR-13 | Clash Engine | Precondition rules: Period.kind ≠ CLASS → `Period '<name>' is not a class period.`, and SchoolDay.isTeaching false → non-teaching day. These go into the same clashes[] list. |\n| FR-14 | Clash Engine / Service | `validateSlot({ courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId?, excludeSlotId? })` returns `Clash[]`, collecting **all** clashes. It is a pure-ish function that takes a `tx`, so the transaction (NFR-1) and the availability map (FR-36) can share it. Clash shape: `{ rule: 'TEACHER'\\|'ROOM'\\|'SECTION'\\|'STUDENT'\\|'PERIOD_KIND'\\|'NON_TEACHING_DAY', message }`. |\n| FR-36 | Clash Engine (batch) | Availability for one course covers ≤7 days × ≤12 periods = 84 cells. Do **not** call validateSlot 84 times. Run each rule once as a year-wide query over all slots, then bucket by `day-periodId`. Room rule: the course has no fixed room, so availability uses the default room (the section homeroom) or skips the room rule. **Design decision needed.** Recommendation: skip the room rule in availability, because the room is checked on drop. |\n| NFR-1 | Concurrency | `$transaction(async tx => { clashes = validateSlot(tx,…); if any throw CONFLICT; insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable })`. Retry on P2034 up to 3 times. `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` is a second guard (P2002 → 409 through withHandler). |\n| NFR-11 | Tests | Unit tests for every rule. This argues for keeping message building and the rule predicates pure (input rows → Clash[]), with Prisma calls kept thin so tests can use small fixtures. Testing the timezone current/next calculation needs an injectable `now` and `tz`. |\n| NFR-12 | Tests | Integration test against a real Postgres (docker-compose). Run `Promise.all` with two conflicting POSTs and assert exactly one succeeds. |\n\n### Service functions (exports used by later PRDs)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-30 | Service | `getScheduleForDate(target: { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }, date)`: get the ISO day in the school timezone, return `[]` if the day is not teaching, else that day's slots for the target, ordered by Period.order. Note for PRD-07 (attendance) and PRD-16 (dashboards): holidays are left out (NFR-15). |\n| FR-31 | Service + Time/TZ | `getCurrentSlot(user, now)`: `hhmm = formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')`, then return the slot where `start ≤ hhmm < end`. It reuses the FR-30 query for \"today\". |\n| FR-45 | Time/TZ | Use one helper (`schoolNow(tz, now)` → `{ isoDay, hhmm }`) everywhere: server pages, the service, and the client Today view (pass tz and the server time in props, never the browser timezone). |\n\n### APIs and access control\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-33 | Admin API | Periods CRUD and reorder. GET is open to any authenticated user. |\n| FR-5 (reorder) | Admin API / Data Model | Because `order` is `@unique`, the update must happen in two phases in one transaction: set all to negative temporary values, then to 1..n. The request lists all period ids, so the service validates that the set equals the existing set. |\n| FR-8 | Admin API | DELETE counts slots on the period. If more than 0, return 409 `{ details: { slotCount } }`. |\n| FR-34 + FR-7 | Admin API | GET returns 7 rows plus `slotCount` for each day (for the current academic year), which resolves the intake blocker. PUT `{ days: [{ dayOfWeek, isTeaching }] }`: in one transaction, delete the slots of days being switched off, update the rows, and audit with the deleted count. **Design decision:** should slotCount and the delete be scoped to the current year or to all years? Recommendation: delete across all years, because a non-teaching day makes every slot invalid. Show the count across all years too, so the confirm number matches what gets deleted. |\n| FR-35 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/timetable?view&id&academicYearId`. Run one query with `include` course → subject, teacher, section, and room, then filter by view. The TEACHER rule is: own id for the teacher view; for the section view, homeroom sections (`Section.homeroomTeacherId`) or sections of courses they teach (intake default). Room view is ADMIN only. Anything else is 403. |\n| FR-37 | Admin API | POST/PATCH run NFR-1. PATCH may change day, period and roomId, and validation excludes the slot itself (FR-14). DELETE is a plain delete plus audit. academicYearId comes from Course. Reject archived courses on POST. |\n| FR-21 | Admin API (new) | The intake blocker: no endpoint lists free rooms. Recommendation: **ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId`** returns non-archived rooms that have no slot at that cell. This is one query. The alternative of putting rooms into the availability map adds weight to every drag preload. |\n| FR-38 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId`. TEACHER: courses where teacherId = me or coTeacherIds has me. STUDENT: courses with an ACTIVE enrollment. PARENT: studentId must be a linked child (`assertCanViewStudent`). It is optional when there is exactly one child. Other roles (ADMIN) get an empty result or a 400 (design decision). |\n| FR-27 | Read API reuse | The student tab needs another student's timetable. It reuses the FR-38 service by studentId, with access checked by `assertCanViewStudent` on the server page. No new route is needed. |\n| FR-28 | Read API reuse | The course Schedule tab is a server page. It reads `prisma.timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` with Period and Room after `assertCanViewCourse`. No new route is needed. |\n| NFR-7 | Access Control | `requireRole('ADMIN')` on every mutation, availability and free-rooms. `requireUser` plus a per-entity check on reads. Pages use `requirePageRole` / `requirePageUser`. |\n| NFR-8 | Conventions | Thin handlers: `withHandler` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` (FR-39 schemas) → service → `ok()`. A clash is `{ error: { code: 'CONFLICT', message: <first clash or summary>, details: { clashes } } }`. |\n| FR-39 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`: `periodSchema`, `periodReorderSchema`, `schoolDaysSchema`, `slotCreateSchema`, `slotUpdateSchema`, `timetableQuerySchema`, `availabilityQuerySchema`, `freeRoomsQuerySchema`, `meTimetableQuerySchema`. The `dayOfWeek` type is `int 1..7`. |\n| FR-40 | Audit | Confirming the intake default: audit all slot, period and school-day mutations (see B9). It is cheap, and audit() never throws. |\n\n### UI\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-5 | UI: Bell Schedule | `/admin/timetable/periods`: PageHeader + MUI Table + an add/edit Dialog with TimeField (`@mui/x-date-pickers`, needs a LocalizationProvider with the date-fns adapter; check whether the app already provides one) + up/down reorder IconButtons + ConfirmDialog for delete. Show a 409 slotCount error through useToast. |\n| FR-7 | UI: Bell Schedule | Seven ToggleButtons (multi-select) on the same page. Switching off a day with slotCount > 0 opens a ConfirmDialog with the count before the PUT. |\n| FR-15 | UI: Editor | `/admin/timetable`: view ToggleButtonGroup, entity Autocomplete (sections, teachers via UserPicker or Autocomplete, rooms) and an academic year Select. The selection state goes in URL search params so the view survives a refresh. |\n| FR-16 | UI: Editor | A shared `TimetableGrid` component with editable and read-only modes. It is reused by FR-24, FR-27 and FR-29. Columns are teaching days. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and not droppable. The cell is a Paper with the subject colour. **Gap:** `Subject` may have no colour field. Check the schema. If it has none, derive a stable colour from the subject code hash and do not change the model. |\n| FR-17 | UI: Editor | Section view only: a sidebar with the section's non-archived courses and a \"placed N\" Chip. On drop, POST with `roomId = section.roomId`. The teacher and room views are read-only grids with no sidebar. |\n| FR-18 | UI: Editor | Drag a slot to a cell to PATCH it. Drop outside the grid or press Delete to open a ConfirmDialog, then DELETE. |\n| FR-19 | UI: Editor + Accessibility | On drag start, fetch or reuse the cached availability map for the course. Clashing cells get a red tint, an ErrorOutline icon and a Tooltip listing the messages (NFR-4). For a slot being moved, ignore its own cell's clashes. |\n| FR-20 | UI: Editor | Optimistic placement is optional. Simplest approach: render from server state only, so there is nothing to snap back. Show a toast with `details.clashes.map(c => c.message)`. |\n| FR-21 | UI: Editor | Clicking a slot opens a Popover with an Autocomplete fed by free-rooms, then PATCH `{ roomId }`. |\n| FR-22 | UI: Editor + Accessibility | Grid cells get `tabIndex=0`. Enter on an empty cell opens a \"Place course\" Dialog (List of section courses) and the same POST as a drop. Delete on a focused slot opens the FR-18 confirm. |\n| FR-23 | UI: Editor | `@dnd-kit/core` only (DndContext, useDraggable, useDroppable). Use MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip for visuals. Do not use a sortable or calendar library. |\n| FR-24 | UI: Personal Timetable | `/timetable` server page, `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')`. Loads the FR-38 data, settings.tz and server \"now\", and renders the read-only grid with the current-period highlight. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Personal Timetable | The child selector (Select from `/api/me/children` or a server query) updates `?studentId=` in the URL. |\n| FR-26 | UI: Personal Timetable | Week/Today ToggleButtonGroup. The Today view is a List with \"Now\" and \"Next\" Chips (text, NFR-4). It is computed with the B6 helper from server-supplied tz. A client tick (every minute) only advances the server-supplied now. |\n| FR-27 | UI: Tabs/Nav | `studentTabs` adds `{ key: 'timetable', href: /students/[id]/timetable }` and a page that reuses the read-only grid. |\n| FR-28 | UI: Tabs/Nav | `courseTabs` adds `{ key: 'schedule', href: /courses/[id]/schedule }` and a page with a simple Table (day, period, times, room). |\n| FR-32 | UI: Tabs/Nav | Add 3 entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: Timetable, plus Timetable editor and Bell schedule with `group: 'Administration'`. |\n| FR-29 | Print | A Print Button calls `window.print()`. `@media print` (via MUI `GlobalStyles` or `sx`, not a CSS library) hides the nav, sidebar and controls, and sets `@page { size: A4 landscape }`. A print-only header shows the entity name and academic year. NFR-16 requires checking Safari print. |\n| NFR-4 | Accessibility | Covered by FR-19, FR-22 and FR-26. Also give each cell an `aria-label` (\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Room 101\"). |\n| NFR-5 | Conventions (UI) | Dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI/MUI X component used (Table, ToggleButton, Autocomplete, Popover, Dialog, Tooltip, Chip, Paper, TimeField, LocalizationProvider, GlobalStyles). If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a hard blocker. This is a dev-phase gate, not a design element. |\n| NFR-6 | Conventions (deps) | Only `@dnd-kit/core` (pinned exact) is added. The existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` must stay green. |\n\n### Seed\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-41 | Seed | Upsert periods by `order` (1..8). Idempotent. |\n| FR-42 | Seed | Upsert SchoolDay 1..7 (1–5 teaching). |\n| FR-44 | Seed (fixtures) | Intake blocker, using the default. Add minimal idempotent fixtures upserted by email or code: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and a sibling (STUDENT), Pat (PARENT linked to both), sections 7A and 7B (homeroom rooms Room 101 and Room 102), courses `MATH-7A`… (subjects ELA for ENG and SOC for HIST), Robotics Club (ELECTIVE, sectionId null), and enrollments. **Check first:** PRD-03 and PRD-05 seed helpers or users may already exist in another seed file. Reuse them before adding new ones. |\n| FR-43 | Seed | A fixed, hand-written clash-free week (21 class slots per section; 30 = 5 days × 6 class periods). Robotics on Wed P6 with both sections free then. To avoid hidden clashes, the seed should insert through `validateSlot`, or a unit test should assert the seed has zero clashes. Tom teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B, so those courses must never share a cell. |\n\n### Performance, quality and scope\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| NFR-2 | Performance | Section week load (≤84 cells): one indexed query with includes, plus the periods and school days (cached or small). Easily under 400 ms. Avoid N+1 queries for teacher names. |\n| NFR-3 | Performance | Availability under 300 ms means the batch evaluation in FR-36 makes about 4 queries total, not one per cell. The student-overlap rule is a single SQL statement grouped by `(dayOfWeek, periodId, otherCourseId)`. |\n| NFR-9 | Conventions | Reuse http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader and the access helpers. The new service path is `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Do not create a parallel helpers folder. |\n| NFR-10 | Tests | lint, typecheck and test gate. |\n| NFR-13 | Tests | Playwright: drag works through mouse events with dnd-kit's PointerSensor (step-wise `mouse.move`). The keyboard path (FR-22) is a more reliable e2e fallback for placement. |\n| NFR-14 | Conventions | Use `logger` (for example, to log P2034 retries). |\n| NFR-15 | Scope | No solver, no A/B weeks, no substitutes, no holidays. `getScheduleForDate` is the single place PRD-14 will hook holidays later. |\n| NFR-16 | Scope | English only and a single school. Print must be tested across the 4 browsers. |\n\n## Open design decisions handed to `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **Free rooms (FR-21):** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` (recommended), or fold rooms into the availability response.\n2. **Availability room rule (FR-36):** skip it (recommended; it is checked on drop), or evaluate against the section homeroom.\n3. **School-day slotCount and cascade scope (FR-7/FR-34):** all years (recommended) or the current year only.\n4. **Archived entities:** exclude archived courses and rooms from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks (intake default, agreed).\n5. **Subject colour (FR-16):** check `Subject` for a colour field. If there is none, use a deterministic hash-to-palette approach and make no schema change.\n6. **ADMIN on `/api/me/timetable` (FR-38):** return an empty list (recommended) or a 400.\n7. **Serialization retry helper (NFR-1):** a new small `withSerializableRetry` with no existing precedent (B7). Keep it in timetable-service.\n\n## Intake blockers and how this analysis covers them\n\n| Blocker | Covered by |\n|---------|-----------|\n| FR-44 seed fixtures | Seed rows above. Reuse any existing PRD-03/05 fixtures first. |\n| FR-43 ENG/HIST subjects | Reuse ELA/SOC with PRD course codes. |\n| FR-21 free rooms | Decision 1. |\n| FR-7 slot count | GET /api/school-days `slotCount` (FR-34 row), decision 3. |\n| FR-4/NFR-6 migration + dnd-kit | B1, B2, B12. |\n| NFR-5 mui-mcp | Dev-phase hard gate (NFR-5 row). The mui-mcp server is configured in this environment. |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":106,"newStart":1,"newLines":156,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-4","+# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-6"," "," Supporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`. That file covers PRD-04 Notifications & Email","-Infrastructure (41 FR and 18 NFR, so 59 requirements) at 93% confidence, with 4 blockers in","-`handoff-to-architect.json`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`, which covers PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable","+(45 FR and 16 NFR, 61 requirements) at 96% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.","+Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`."," ","-Concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Type Registry**, **Notify Service**,","-**Preference Resolution**, **Email Rendering**, **Auth Email Seam**, **Outbox Dispatcher**,","-**Transport**, **Background Job**, **Internal Endpoint**, **User API**, **Admin API**,","-**UI: Bell**, **UI: Notifications Page**, **UI: Preferences Page**, **UI: Admin Email Log**,","-**Validation**, **Seed**, **Security**, **Performance**, **Reliability**, **Conventions**,","-**Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.","+> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (`api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`,","+> `system-design.md`, `tech-stack-decisions.md`, `threat-model-notes.json`) are **stale SH-4 outputs**.","+> The other sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-6 input, except for","+> `tech-stack-decisions.md` once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-6."," ","-## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these add to or correct intake)","+Concern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Validation**, **Clash Engine**, **Service**,","+**Admin API**, **Read API**, **Access Control**, **UI: Bell Schedule**, **UI: Editor**,","+**UI: Personal Timetable**, **UI: Tabs/Nav**, **Print**, **Time/TZ**, **Audit**, **Seed**,","+**Concurrency**, **Performance**, **Accessibility**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**."," ","-| # | Finding | Impact |","-|---|---------|--------|","-| B1 | `src/middleware.ts` returns **401 for any `/api/*` request without a session** unless `isPublicPath()` matches. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is only `['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`. | The cron call to `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` carries no session cookie, so it would be rejected by middleware before the handler runs. **`/api/internal/` must be added to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** (prefix match). The handler then becomes the only gate, so its CRON_SECRET check must be strict (NFR-8). The middleware's cross-origin guard does not block it, because cron calls send no `Origin` header. |","-| B2 | `prisma/seed.ts` (95 lines) seeds only SchoolSettings and academic reference data. **There are no `student@schoolhub.test` or `parent@schoolhub.test` users** anywhere in `prisma/` or `src/`. | FR-40 cannot simply attach notifications to existing users. Options: (a) look up those users by email and skip with a log line when they are missing, or (b) upsert minimal STUDENT/PARENT users. Recommend (a). It keeps the seed idempotent and avoids PRD-04 creating identity data that another PRD owns. Design should confirm. |","-| B3 | `vitest.config.ts` includes only `tests/unit/**` and uses `environment: 'jsdom'`. There is no `tests/integration/` folder and no test-DB setup. | NFR-15 needs a node environment plus a real Postgres to exercise `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`. This requires a separate vitest project or config (e.g. `vitest.integration.config.ts`, `environment: 'node'`, `include: tests/integration/**`) that is skipped when `DATABASE_URL_TEST` is absent, so that `npm run test` stays green (NFR-13). |","-| B4 | `EmailOutbox` has **no `userId` and no `type` column**. It stores only `toEmail`, `toName`, `subject`, `html`, `text`, `status`, `attempts`, `lastError`, `nextAttemptAt`, `sentAt`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. | The admin email log (FR-31) can only show recipient email and name, not a user link or type. That is sufficient for FR-31, so the schema should not change (NFR-13). `sendAuthEmail` (FR-16) fits naturally because it has no type. |","-| B5 | `NotificationPreference` uses a composite PK `@@id([userId, type])`. | FR-38's upsert keys on `userId_type`. FR-7's resolution reads with `findMany({ where: { userId: { in }, type } })`, which is a single query. |","-| B6 | `src/server/http.ts` already exports `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parsePagination` (default 20, max 100), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. `ApiErrorCode` already includes `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `NOT_FOUND`, `UNAUTHENTICATED` and `FORBIDDEN`. | All new route handlers reuse these (NFR-11). No new error codes are needed. |","-| B7 | `src/lib/dates.ts` exports `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, timezone)` (date-fns-tz). `SchoolSettings.timezone` defaults to `'UTC'`. `src/server/services/settings.ts` exists. | NFR-12 reuses these. Relative times (\"5 min ago\") are timezone-independent. Absolute times in the email log and the invite expiry date use `formatInSchoolTz`. |","-| B8 | `src/server/rate-limit.ts` exports an in-memory `rateLimit()`. | It could optionally guard `POST /api/admin/notifications/test`, but no requirement asks for that. Skip it under compliance rule 1. |","-| B9 | `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx`, `Toast/useToast.ts`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader` and `DateDisplay` exist. | FR-26 and FR-31 reuse DataTable, PageHeader and EmptyState. FR-30 reuses `useToast`. Do not create duplicates. |","-| B10 | Prisma `$transaction` is used in `src/server/sections/`. No `$queryRaw` is used anywhere yet. | FR-17's `SKIP LOCKED` claim is the first raw SQL in the repo. Use tagged `$queryRaw` (parameterised) inside `$transaction`, or a single `UPDATE … WHERE id IN (SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *` statement, which claims rows atomically without holding a transaction across SMTP. |","-| B11 | All other intake brownfield findings were confirmed: there is no migration for the three models, the env vars and `worker:email` script are present, the navigation entries exist, `sendAuthEmail` has exactly 2 callers (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`), and the `requireRole` helpers exist. | — |","+## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these confirm or add to intake)"," ","+| # | Fact | Design implication |","+|---|------|--------------------|","+| B1 | `prisma/schema.prisma` has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind. The latest migration is `20261104120000_notifications_email`. | The new migration needs a later timestamp (for example `20261105000000_timetable`). |","+| B2 | `Room` already has a back-relation `sections Section[]`. `Course` has `enrollments` but no slots relation. | Add `Room.timetableSlots`, `Course.timetableSlots` and `Period.slots`. All are additive. |","+| B3 | `Course.coTeacherIds String[]`, nullable `sectionId`, `archivedAt`, `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. `Enrollment @@index([studentId, status])`, `onDelete: Cascade` from Course. | The teacher clash check needs `teacherId IN set OR coTeacherIds hasSome set`. The student-overlap check joins Enrollment on both courses. |","+| B4 | `Section.roomId?` (homeroom room) and `Section.homeroomTeacherId?`. `@@unique([academicYearId, name])`. | FR-17 uses `Section.roomId` as the default room. FR-35 checks TEACHER access through `homeroomTeacherId`. |","+| B5 | `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` with `@@index([studentId])`. `/api/me/children` already exists. | FR-25 and FR-38 can reuse `/api/me/children` for the child selector, so no new endpoint is needed. Parent access goes through `assertCanViewStudent`. |","+| B6 | `SchoolSettings.timezone` (default `'UTC'`) is read by the cached `getSchoolSettings()` in `src/server/services/settings.ts`. `src/lib/dates.ts` has `formatInSchoolTz` (date-fns-tz `formatInTimeZone`). | All \"now\" maths (FR-31, FR-45) uses `formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')` and ISO day `'i'`. Plain `HH:MM` string comparison then works. |","+| B7 | SERIALIZABLE precedent: `academicYears.ts` and `terms.ts` use `prisma.$transaction(fn, { isolationLevel: Serializable })` but **do not retry**. There is no P2034 handling in `src/`. | NFR-1 needs a small retry wrapper for P2034 (serialization failure). It is new code, so keep it local to timetable-service unless the design wants to reuse it. |","+| B8 | `http.ts` has `ApiErrorCode` with CONFLICT=409 and FORBIDDEN=403, plus `AppError`, `withHandler` (maps P2002 → CONFLICT, P2025 → NOT_FOUND), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. | Clashes are thrown as `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })`. The handler shape is already standard. |","+| B9 | `audit({ actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request })` never throws. By convention `action` is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|delete`. | FR-40 actions: `timetableSlot.create\\|update\\|delete`, `period.create\\|update\\|delete\\|reorder`, `schoolDay.update` (metadata includes `deletedSlotCount`). |","+| B10 | Validators live in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts` (courses, sections, ...). Feature services live in `src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts`. Tabs live in `src/config/course-tabs.ts` and `student-tabs.ts` (`{ key, label, href, roles }`). | FR-39: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`. FR-27 and FR-28 each register one entry. |","+| B11 | API route dirs exist: `rooms`, `sections`, `courses`, `me/*`, `admin/*`. There are no `periods`, `school-days` or `timetable` routes. App admin pages: `admin/courses`, `admin/sections`, `admin/email-log`. | Everything here is new. Nothing gets renamed. |","+| B12 | `package.json` pins `@mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0`, `date-fns 3.6.0`, `date-fns-tz 3.2.0` and `@prisma/client 5.20.0`. `@dnd-kit/*` is absent. | FR-23 and NFR-6 add exactly one pinned dependency, `@dnd-kit/core`. Reorder (FR-5) uses up/down buttons, so `@dnd-kit/sortable` is not needed. |","+"," ## Requirement → architectural concern"," ","-| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |","-|-----|----------------------|-------|","-| FR-1 | Data Model | One new migration `2026110400xxxx_notifications_email`. It creates `EmailStatus`, `Notification`, `NotificationPreference` and `EmailOutbox` exactly as `schema.prisma` declares them, including the additive `updatedAt` columns and both indexes. Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and do not edit `schema.prisma`. It must sort after `20261104000000_auth_reconcile`. |","-| FR-2 | Type Registry | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` exports `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` with `as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>`, which keeps literal keys for FR-5 while type-checking the shape. Add one field, `emailOnly?: true` (or `hidden`), to express FR-4. |","-| FR-3 | Type Registry | `NotificationCategory` is a string-literal union of the 6 values, not a Prisma enum, because the DB stores `type` as a free `String`. The UI groups by category (FR-26, FR-28). |","-| FR-4 | Type Registry, Auth Email Seam | `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are `emailOnly`, hidden from preferences and never passed to `notify()` (blocker default confirmed in \"Decisions for design\" below). `system.test` uses category SYSTEM, `defaultEmail: true` and all roles (AC-1 expects both rows). |","-| FR-5 | Type Registry | `type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. Later PRDs extend the registry by editing this one file, and no plugin mechanism is needed (YAGNI). |","-| FR-6 | Notify Service | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` is a pure server module. Its `email.template` param is a key into the template map (FR-13), and `data` is typed per template. |","-| FR-7 | Preference Resolution | Load users with `findMany({ id in userIds, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` and prefs with `findMany({ userId in, type })`. Then resolve each user with a pure function `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }`, which is unit-tested (NFR-14). |","-| FR-8 | Notify Service | `inApp = row?.inApp ?? true`, with `mandatoryInApp` forcing true. Notifications are written with `createMany`. |","-| FR-9 | Notify Service, Email Rendering | `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` and requires `user.email`. Render once per recipient, because templates contain the name. Rendering cost dominates NFR-1, so `render()` calls should run with bounded `Promise.all` concurrency. Rows are written to `EmailOutbox` with `createMany`. |","-| FR-10 | Performance | 1,000 recipients means 3 round-trips: users, prefs and one `createMany`, per channel. Chunk `createMany` at about 500 rows only if the parameter limit bites (Postgres allows 65,535 params, and Notification has about 7 columns, so 1,000 rows fit in one call). |","-| FR-11 | Notify Service | Wrap the whole body in try/catch, call `logger.error`, and return `void` or a `{ notified, emailed }` summary. Callers invoke it after commit. Document that in JSDoc. |","-| FR-12 | Notify Service | `notifyStudentAndParents` makes one `ParentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call (indexed on `studentId`), merges into a `Set`, then calls `notify`. Expansion and dedupe are a pure function so they can be unit-tested (NFR-14). |","-| FR-13 | Email Rendering | `src/server/email/templates/*.tsx` with `@react-email/components`. `src/server/email/render.ts` calls `render(el)` and `render(el, { plainText: true })` from `@react-email/render` 1.0.1, which is async. |","-| FR-14 | Email Rendering | `BaseLayout.tsx` takes `school: Pick<SchoolSettings, name, logoUrl, addressLine1, addressLine2>`. Fetch SchoolSettings once per `notify()` / `sendAuthEmail` call, not once per recipient. The footer link is `APP_URL/account/notifications`. |","-| FR-15 | Email Rendering | There are 3 templates. Invite needs an expiry date, which `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` does not receive. The template can derive it from the known invite TTL constant in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, so the signature stays unchanged. Password reset uses the hardcoded 60-minute notice. The generic CTA href is `APP_URL + link` (the link is already validated by NFR-6). |","-| FR-16 | Auth Email Seam | Only the body of `src/server/auth/email.ts` changes: render the template and call `prisma.emailOutbox.create`. Its 2 callers are untouched. Unlike `notify()`, failures here **should** surface, because the existing callers already handle errors and a silently lost invite is worse. Design should decide whether to keep the current awaited and throwable behaviour (recommended). |","-| FR-17 | Outbox Dispatcher | `src/server/email/dispatch.ts`. First, run stuck-row recovery (NFR-5). Next, claim rows with one atomic `UPDATE … SET status='SENDING', updatedAt=now() WHERE id IN (SELECT id … WHERE status='PENDING' AND nextAttemptAt<=now() ORDER BY nextAttemptAt LIMIT $n FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *`. Then send each row outside any transaction and update it individually. |","-| FR-18 | Outbox Dispatcher | A pure function `backoffMinutes(attempts) → [1,5,15,60,240][attempts-1]`, plus `attempts >= 5 → FAILED`. It is unit-tested (NFR-14). `lastError` is truncated to about 1,000 characters. |","-| FR-19 | Internal Endpoint | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`. Compare the bearer token against `env.CRON_SECRET` with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. A missing env value always returns 401. The response is `{ data: { sent, failed, retried } }` via `ok()`. **Requires B1** (the middleware allowlist). The route also triggers FR-27. |","-| FR-20 | Background Job | `scripts/worker-email.ts` imports `dispatchEmails` directly (tsx resolves the `@/` alias via tsconfig paths) and runs a `setTimeout` loop every 15 s with SIGINT/SIGTERM handling. It does not go over HTTP and does not call purge, because purge belongs to the endpoint only (FR-27). |","-| FR-21 | Transport | `src/server/email/transport.ts` exports `getTransport()` with 2 branches. `smtp` uses `nodemailer.createTransport` with SMTP_* settings and is memoised. `console` uses `console.log`, which NFR-11 explicitly allows. Each message includes `List-Unsubscribe` (NFR-9). Missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` under `smtp` should fail at transport creation, and the dispatcher must record that as a retryable `lastError`, not crash. |","-| FR-22 | UI: Bell | The `'use client'` component `NotificationBell.tsx` replaces the placeholder in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`. It uses MUI `Badge` with `max={9}`, which renders \"9+\" natively, so no custom formatting is needed. |","-| FR-23 | UI: Bell | A `setInterval` of 30 s gated on `document.visibilityState`, plus an immediate refetch on `visibilitychange → visible`. There is no SWR or react-query dependency, so plain `fetch` is enough. |","-| FR-24 | UI: Bell | `Popover` + `List` + `ListItemButton`. Unread items use bold `fontWeight` and a `Badge variant=\"dot\"` or small Box. The body is clamped with `sx={{ WebkitLineClamp: 2 }}`. Relative time uses `date-fns` `formatDistanceToNowStrict` (date-fns-tz is already installed, so date-fns is too). The popover fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10` on open. |","-| FR-25 | UI: Bell | On click, call `POST /:id/read`, then `router.push(link)`, then close. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" (`POST /read-all`) and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |","-| FR-26 | UI: Notifications Page | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` is a server shell using `requirePageUser()` and a client list. It has `Tabs` (All/Unread), a category `Select`, the pagination from DataTable or MUI `Pagination` with a page size of 20, and a per-row toggle calling `/:id/read` or `/:id/unread`. |","-| FR-27 | Background Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` (`deleteMany createdAt < now-180d`) lives in `src/server/notifications/`. A module-level `let lastPurgeAt` in the dispatch route allows at most one run per 24 h per process. It is best-effort, and its failure is logged and must not fail the dispatch response. |","-| FR-28 | UI: Preferences Page | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`. This is the first page under `/account/`, so the directory is new. It is an MUI `Table` with a full-width category header `TableRow` (the intake default is accepted) and data from `GET /api/me/notification-preferences`. |","-| FR-29 | UI: Preferences Page | `Tooltip` around a **span** wrapping the disabled `Switch`, because MUI Tooltip does not fire on disabled elements. |","-| FR-30 | UI: Preferences Page | Optimistic local state, `PUT`, and on error revert plus `useToast().error(...)`. |","-| FR-31 | UI: Admin Email Log | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` uses `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` with DataTable and a status `Select`. The recipient column shows `toName <toEmail>` (B4). |","-| FR-32 | Admin API, UI: Admin Email Log | The retry action is shown only when `status==='FAILED'`. The server guard uses `updateMany where { id, status: FAILED }`, and a count of 0 returns 409 CONFLICT or 404, so a double click is harmless. |","-| FR-33 | Admin API | `POST /api/admin/notifications/test` uses `requireRole('ADMIN')`, then `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title, body, link: '/dashboard' })`. The button sits on the email-log page because no separate admin page is needed. |","-| FR-34 | User API | `GET /api/notifications` uses `parseQuery` with Zod (`unread`, `category`), `parsePagination` and `paginated()`. **Category filter caveat:** Notification has no category column. Filter by the `type IN (keys of registry with that category)` derived from the registry at request time. This needs no schema change and remains index-compatible with `userId` leading. |","-| FR-35 | User API | `count({ where: { userId, readAt: null } })` is covered by the `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index (NFR-2). |","-| FR-36 | User API | Mark read or unread with `updateMany({ where: { id, userId: me.id } })`. A count of 0 returns 404, which hides existence from non-owners. `read-all` runs `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null })`. Route files: `[id]/read/route.ts`, `[id]/unread/route.ts` and `read-all/route.ts`. **Next.js routing note:** `read-all` and `unread-count` are static siblings of `[id]`, and static segments win, so they do not conflict. |","-| FR-37 | User API, Preference Resolution | `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` (GET and PUT in one file) is the first route under `/api/me/`. It filters the registry by `roles.includes(me.role)` and `!emailOnly`, merges the rows and returns `{ type, label, description, category, inApp, email, mandatoryInApp }[]`. |","-| FR-38 | User API, Validation | The Zod body is `{ type: z.enum(visibleTypeKeys), inApp: boolean, email: boolean }`. The service rejects `inApp=false` for mandatory types and role-invisible or `emailOnly` types with `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR')`, then calls `upsert` on `userId_type`. |","-| FR-39 | Admin API | `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` (GET) and `[id]/retry/route.ts` (POST), both protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The list is ordered by `createdAt desc` and **omits `html` and `text`** to keep the payload small. |","-| FR-40 | Seed | The seed appends to `prisma/seed.ts`. **See B2: the target users do not exist.** For idempotency, skip a user who already has any `system.test` notification (count > 0), giving 3 per user with 1 read and 2 unread, linking to `/dashboard`. |","-| FR-41 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` is a sibling of the existing `auth.ts`, `users.ts` and so on. It holds the list query schema, the preference PUT schema and `safeLink` (NFR-6). It must be client-safe: no server imports, so registry keys are passed in or the type is checked as a string and then against the registry in the service. |","-| NFR-1 | Performance | The budget of 2 s for 1,000 recipients is dominated by 1,000 react-email renders. Mitigate with SchoolSettings fetched once, bounded concurrency, and rendering only recipients with email enabled. If renders are too slow, render the generic template once with a name placeholder. Design should note this as the fallback. |","-| NFR-2 | Performance | Covered by the FR-1 index and FR-35 query shape. The bell must not call the list endpoint on every poll. |","-| NFR-3 | Reliability | No SMTP happens in the request path: `notify()` and `sendAuthEmail` only insert rows. The 15 s worker or the cron endpoint keeps delivery under 60 s. |","-| NFR-4 | Reliability | The FR-17 atomic claim with `SKIP LOCKED`. Each claimed row is owned by exactly one dispatcher. |","-| NFR-5 | Reliability | At the start of each dispatch: `updateMany({ status: SENDING, updatedAt < now-10m }, { status: PENDING })`. This relies on the additive `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`, which is why FR-1 keeps it. It does not increment attempts, because a crash mid-send was not proven to be a send failure. |","-| NFR-6 | Security | A shared `isSafeLink(s)` requires `s.startsWith('/')` and rejects `//`, `/\\`, any `\\` and control characters. It is applied in `notify()` (drop or nullify the link and warn instead of throwing, per FR-11) and in the Zod schema. Unit-tested (NFR-14). |","-| NFR-7 | Security | React-email JSX escapes interpolated text by default. **Never** use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in templates. Body text is rendered as text with `white-space: pre-line`, not as HTML. |","-| NFR-8 | Security | Every new handler starts with `requireUser()` or `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The internal route uses a secret check only (B1). Pages use `requirePageUser()` or `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. |","-| NFR-9 | Security, Transport | Each `sendMail` call sets `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<APP_URL/account/notifications>' }` along with both `html` and `text`. Set it at send time rather than storing it in the outbox, because the outbox has no headers column (B4). |","-| NFR-10 | Conventions (UI) | All 4 UI surfaces (bell, notifications page, preferences page, email log) use MUI only. Dev must query mui-mcp before writing UI, and **this is an unresolved blocker carried forward**: if the server is unreachable, there is a hard stop. The existing `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned libs. Email templates are exempt. |","-| NFR-11 | Conventions | Thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok`/`paginated`. Services live in `src/server/notifications/` and `src/server/email/`, and code uses `logger`, with `console` only in the console transport. |","-| NFR-12 | Conventions | UTC storage is the Prisma default. Display uses `formatInSchoolTz` (B7). The client components need the timezone, so pass it from the server page as a prop. |","-| NFR-13 | Conventions | Do not touch `schema.prisma`, navigation or env. Keep the `sendAuthEmail` signature. Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. This is the source of B1–B3 handling. |","-| NFR-14 | Test Harness | Pure units are `resolvePrefs`, `backoffMinutes`, `isSafeLink` and `expandStudentRecipients`. They go in `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`, run under the existing vitest config and need no DB. |","-| NFR-15 | Test Harness | **See B3.** A new `tests/integration/` folder with a node-env vitest config against a test DB. One test runs 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails` calls over 10 rows and asserts each row is sent once. A second test backdates a SENDING row's `updatedAt` by 11 minutes and asserts recovery. |","-| NFR-16 | Test Harness | Playwright tests go in `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`. They need a logged-in admin (the existing e2e harness pattern; check `dashboard.spec.ts` for auth setup). The flow is send test → bell count → mark all read → preference toggle persists after reload. |","-| NFR-17 | Scope Discipline | No SMS, push, websockets or digests. Polling only (FR-23), and do not add a `channel` abstraction for future SMS. |","-| NFR-18 | Notify Service | Silently truncate `title` to 140 characters and `body` to 500, with `logger.warn` (intake default accepted, since it is consistent with FR-11). There is no DB constraint, because the schema has plain `String`. |","+### Data model and migration"," ","-## Decisions for design (resolving intake blockers)","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|-----|---------|-------|","+| FR-1 | Data Model | `enum PeriodKind` and `model Period`. Store `startTime`/`endTime` as `String` `HH:MM`. `order Int @unique` affects reorder (see FR-5). |","+| FR-2 | Data Model | `SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id, isTeaching Boolean }` is a 7-row lookup with no relations. Do not add a FK from TimetableSlot to it (the PRD defines `dayOfWeek Int`). |","+| FR-3 | Data Model | Index `@@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` covers every clash query (all are scoped to year + day + period). `academicYearId` is denormalised from Course. It is set server-side only (FR-37). `periodId` has no cascade, so deletion is guarded by FR-8 in the service. `roomId?` with `onDelete: SetNull` is the safe default, and rooms are archived rather than deleted. |","+| FR-4 | Migration | One additive migration plus the B2 back-relations. `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then review the SQL. It should only contain CREATE TYPE, CREATE TABLE and CREATE INDEX statements. |"," ","-1. **FR-1 migration**: Accepted. There is one new migration, `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `schema.prisma` is not changed.","-2. **FR-4/FR-16**: Accepted. `sendAuthEmail` enqueues directly and creates no Notification row. The `account.*` types are `emailOnly` and are filtered out of FR-28 and FR-37 and rejected by FR-38.","-3. **FR-40**: Use 3 per user, but the users are missing (B2). The recommendation is to look them up and skip if absent.","-4. **NFR-10**: Carried forward to dev as a precondition, because the architect cannot resolve it.","-5. **New**: Add `/api/internal/` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` (B1). Without it, AC-6 still passes (401), but real cron dispatch never works.","+### Validation and the clash engine (core domain)"," ","-## New/changed files implied (for arch-design-system to confirm)","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|-----|---------|-------|","+| FR-6 | Validation + Service | Zod handles the `^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$` format and `end > start`. These are plain string comparisons, so no Date parsing is needed. The overlap check against other periods is in the service, because it needs the DB: `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self on update. |","+| FR-9 | Clash Engine | Teacher set T = {teacherId} ∪ coTeacherIds of the new course. Other slots at (year, day, period) whose course has teacherId ∈ T or coTeacherIds overlapping T. The message needs the teacher's display name, so join User. |","+| FR-10 | Clash Engine | Only when roomId ≠ null: same year, day, period and roomId. |","+| FR-11 | Clash Engine | Only when the course's sectionId ≠ null: another slot whose course.sectionId equals it. A cross-section elective (sectionId null) is skipped by this rule but still caught by FR-12. |","+| FR-12 | Clash Engine | One grouped query: count distinct studentIds where Enrollment(ACTIVE) is in the new course and also in course X, for each X in a slot at (year, day, period). Produce one clash per conflicting course with its count N. Use raw SQL or `groupBy`, because this is the costliest rule (NFR-3). |","+| FR-13 | Clash Engine | Precondition rules: Period.kind ≠ CLASS → `Period '<name>' is not a class period.`, and SchoolDay.isTeaching false → non-teaching day. These go into the same clashes[] list. |","+| FR-14 | Clash Engine / Service | `validateSlot({ courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId?, excludeSlotId? })` returns `Clash[]`, collecting **all** clashes. It is a pure-ish function that takes a `tx`, so the transaction (NFR-1) and the availability map (FR-36) can share it. Clash shape: `{ rule: 'TEACHER'\\|'ROOM'\\|'SECTION'\\|'STUDENT'\\|'PERIOD_KIND'\\|'NON_TEACHING_DAY', message }`. |","+| FR-36 | Clash Engine (batch) | Availability for one course covers ≤7 days × ≤12 periods = 84 cells. Do **not** call validateSlot 84 times. Run each rule once as a year-wide query over all slots, then bucket by `day-periodId`. Room rule: the course has no fixed room, so availability uses the default room (the section homeroom) or skips the room rule. **Design decision needed.** Recommendation: skip the room rule in availability, because the room is checked on drop. |","+| NFR-1 | Concurrency | `$transaction(async tx => { clashes = validateSlot(tx,…); if any throw CONFLICT; insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable })`. Retry on P2034 up to 3 times. `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` is a second guard (P2002 → 409 through withHandler). |","+| NFR-11 | Tests | Unit tests for every rule. This argues for keeping message building and the rule predicates pure (input rows → Clash[]), with Prisma calls kept thin so tests can use small fixtures. Testing the timezone current/next calculation needs an injectable `now` and `tz`. |","+| NFR-12 | Tests | Integration test against a real Postgres (docker-compose). Run `Promise.all` with two conflicting POSTs and assert exactly one succeeds. |"," ","-- **New**: `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/`, `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,purge}.ts`, `src/server/email/{transport,render,dispatch}.ts`, `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`, `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`, `src/app/api/notifications/{route,unread-count/route,read-all/route,[id]/read/route,[id]/unread/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/{route,[id]/retry/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `scripts/worker-email.ts`, plus tests under `tests/unit`, `tests/integration` and `tests/e2e`.","-- **Modified**: `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (bell), `src/config/public-routes.ts` (one entry), `prisma/seed.ts` (append), and possibly `package.json` (`test:integration` script only).","+### Service functions (exports used by later PRDs)","+","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|-----|---------|-------|","+| FR-30 | Service | `getScheduleForDate(target: { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }, date)`: get the ISO day in the school timezone, return `[]` if the day is not teaching, else that day's slots for the target, ordered by Period.order. Note for PRD-07 (attendance) and PRD-16 (dashboards): holidays are left out (NFR-15). |","+| FR-31 | Service + Time/TZ | `getCurrentSlot(user, now)`: `hhmm = formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')`, then return the slot where `start ≤ hhmm < end`. It reuses the FR-30 query for \"today\". |","+| FR-45 | Time/TZ | Use one helper (`schoolNow(tz, now)` → `{ isoDay, hhmm }`) everywhere: server pages, the service, and the client Today view (pass tz and the server time in props, never the browser timezone). |","+","+### APIs and access control","+","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|-----|---------|-------|","+| FR-33 | Admin API | Periods CRUD and reorder. GET is open to any authenticated user. |","+| FR-5 (reorder) | Admin API / Data Model | Because `order` is `@unique`, the update must happen in two phases in one transaction: set all to negative temporary values, then to 1..n. The request lists all period ids, so the service validates that the set equals the existing set. |","+| FR-8 | Admin API | DELETE counts slots on the period. If more than 0, return 409 `{ details: { slotCount } }`. |","+| FR-34 + FR-7 | Admin API | GET returns 7 rows plus `slotCount` for each day (for the current academic year), which resolves the intake blocker. PUT `{ days: [{ dayOfWeek, isTeaching }] }`: in one transaction, delete the slots of days being switched off, update the rows, and audit with the deleted count. **Design decision:** should slotCount and the delete be scoped to the current year or to all years? Recommendation: delete across all years, because a non-teaching day makes every slot invalid. Show the count across all years too, so the confirm number matches what gets deleted. |","+| FR-35 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/timetable?view&id&academicYearId`. Run one query with `include` course → subject, teacher, section, and room, then filter by view. The TEACHER rule is: own id for the teacher view; for the section view, homeroom sections (`Section.homeroomTeacherId`) or sections of courses they teach (intake default). Room view is ADMIN only. Anything else is 403. |","+| FR-37 | Admin API | POST/PATCH run NFR-1. PATCH may change day, period and roomId, and validation excludes the slot itself (FR-14). DELETE is a plain delete plus audit. academicYearId comes from Course. Reject archived courses on POST. |","+| FR-21 | Admin API (new) | The intake blocker: no endpoint lists free rooms. Recommendation: **ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId`** returns non-archived rooms that have no slot at that cell. This is one query. The alternative of putting rooms into the availability map adds weight to every drag preload. |","+| FR-38 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId`. TEACHER: courses where teacherId = me or coTeacherIds has me. STUDENT: courses with an ACTIVE enrollment. PARENT: studentId must be a linked child (`assertCanViewStudent`). It is optional when there is exactly one child. Other roles (ADMIN) get an empty result or a 400 (design decision). |","+| FR-27 | Read API reuse | The student tab needs another student's timetable. It reuses the FR-38 service by studentId, with access checked by `assertCanViewStudent` on the server page. No new route is needed. |","+| FR-28 | Read API reuse | The course Schedule tab is a server page. It reads `prisma.timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` with Period and Room after `assertCanViewCourse`. No new route is needed. |","+| NFR-7 | Access Control | `requireRole('ADMIN')` on every mutation, availability and free-rooms. `requireUser` plus a per-entity check on reads. Pages use `requirePageRole` / `requirePageUser`. |","+| NFR-8 | Conventions | Thin handlers: `withHandler` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` (FR-39 schemas) → service → `ok()`. A clash is `{ error: { code: 'CONFLICT', message: <first clash or summary>, details: { clashes } } }`. |","+| FR-39 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`: `periodSchema`, `periodReorderSchema`, `schoolDaysSchema`, `slotCreateSchema`, `slotUpdateSchema`, `timetableQuerySchema`, `availabilityQuerySchema`, `freeRoomsQuerySchema`, `meTimetableQuerySchema`. The `dayOfWeek` type is `int 1..7`. |","+| FR-40 | Audit | Confirming the intake default: audit all slot, period and school-day mutations (see B9). It is cheap, and audit() never throws. |","+","+### UI","+","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|-----|---------|-------|","+| FR-5 | UI: Bell Schedule | `/admin/timetable/periods`: PageHeader + MUI Table + an add/edit Dialog with TimeField (`@mui/x-date-pickers`, needs a LocalizationProvider with the date-fns adapter; check whether the app already provides one) + up/down reorder IconButtons + ConfirmDialog for delete. Show a 409 slotCount error through useToast. |","+| FR-7 | UI: Bell Schedule | Seven ToggleButtons (multi-select) on the same page. Switching off a day with slotCount > 0 opens a ConfirmDialog with the count before the PUT. |","+| FR-15 | UI: Editor | `/admin/timetable`: view ToggleButtonGroup, entity Autocomplete (sections, teachers via UserPicker or Autocomplete, rooms) and an academic year Select. The selection state goes in URL search params so the view survives a refresh. |","+| FR-16 | UI: Editor | A shared `TimetableGrid` component with editable and read-only modes. It is reused by FR-24, FR-27 and FR-29. Columns are teaching days. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and not droppable. The cell is a Paper with the subject colour. **Gap:** `Subject` may have no colour field. Check the schema. If it has none, derive a stable colour from the subject code hash and do not change the model. |","+| FR-17 | UI: Editor | Section view only: a sidebar with the section's non-archived courses and a \"placed N\" Chip. On drop, POST with `roomId = section.roomId`. The teacher and room views are read-only grids with no sidebar. |","+| FR-18 | UI: Editor | Drag a slot to a cell to PATCH it. Drop outside the grid or press Delete to open a ConfirmDialog, then DELETE. |","+| FR-19 | UI: Editor + Accessibility | On drag start, fetch or reuse the cached availability map for the course. Clashing cells get a red tint, an ErrorOutline icon and a Tooltip listing the messages (NFR-4). For a slot being moved, ignore its own cell's clashes. |","+| FR-20 | UI: Editor | Optimistic placement is optional. Simplest approach: render from server state only, so there is nothing to snap back. Show a toast with `details.clashes.map(c => c.message)`. |","+| FR-21 | UI: Editor | Clicking a slot opens a Popover with an Autocomplete fed by free-rooms, then PATCH `{ roomId }`. |","+| FR-22 | UI: Editor + Accessibility | Grid cells get `tabIndex=0`. Enter on an empty cell opens a \"Place course\" Dialog (List of section courses) and the same POST as a drop. Delete on a focused slot opens the FR-18 confirm. |","+| FR-23 | UI: Editor | `@dnd-kit/core` only (DndContext, useDraggable, useDroppable). Use MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip for visuals. Do not use a sortable or calendar library. |","+| FR-24 | UI: Personal Timetable | `/timetable` server page, `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')`. Loads the FR-38 data, settings.tz and server \"now\", and renders the read-only grid with the current-period highlight. |","+| FR-25 | UI: Personal Timetable | The child selector (Select from `/api/me/children` or a server query) updates `?studentId=` in the URL. |","+| FR-26 | UI: Personal Timetable | Week/Today ToggleButtonGroup. The Today view is a List with \"Now\" and \"Next\" Chips (text, NFR-4). It is computed with the B6 helper from server-supplied tz. A client tick (every minute) only advances the server-supplied now. |","+| FR-27 | UI: Tabs/Nav | `studentTabs` adds `{ key: 'timetable', href: /students/[id]/timetable }` and a page that reuses the read-only grid. |","+| FR-28 | UI: Tabs/Nav | `courseTabs` adds `{ key: 'schedule', href: /courses/[id]/schedule }` and a page with a simple Table (day, period, times, room). |","+| FR-32 | UI: Tabs/Nav | Add 3 entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: Timetable, plus Timetable editor and Bell schedule with `group: 'Administration'`. |","+| FR-29 | Print | A Print Button calls `window.print()`. `@media print` (via MUI `GlobalStyles` or `sx`, not a CSS library) hides the nav, sidebar and controls, and sets `@page { size: A4 landscape }`. A print-only header shows the entity name and academic year. NFR-16 requires checking Safari print. |","+| NFR-4 | Accessibility | Covered by FR-19, FR-22 and FR-26. Also give each cell an `aria-label` (\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Room 101\"). |","+| NFR-5 | Conventions (UI) | Dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI/MUI X component used (Table, ToggleButton, Autocomplete, Popover, Dialog, Tooltip, Chip, Paper, TimeField, LocalizationProvider, GlobalStyles). If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a hard blocker. This is a dev-phase gate, not a design element. |","+| NFR-6 | Conventions (deps) | Only `@dnd-kit/core` (pinned exact) is added. The existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` must stay green. |","+","+### Seed","+","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|-----|---------|-------|","+| FR-41 | Seed | Upsert periods by `order` (1..8). Idempotent. |","+| FR-42 | Seed | Upsert SchoolDay 1..7 (1–5 teaching). |","+| FR-44 | Seed (fixtures) | Intake blocker, using the default. Add minimal idempotent fixtures upserted by email or code: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and a sibling (STUDENT), Pat (PARENT linked to both), sections 7A and 7B (homeroom rooms Room 101 and Room 102), courses `MATH-7A`… (subjects ELA for ENG and SOC for HIST), Robotics Club (ELECTIVE, sectionId null), and enrollments. **Check first:** PRD-03 and PRD-05 seed helpers or users may already exist in another seed file. Reuse them before adding new ones. |","+| FR-43 | Seed | A fixed, hand-written clash-free week (21 class slots per section; 30 = 5 days × 6 class periods). Robotics on Wed P6 with both sections free then. To avoid hidden clashes, the seed should insert through `validateSlot`, or a unit test should assert the seed has zero clashes. Tom teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B, so those courses must never share a cell. |","+","+### Performance, quality and scope","+","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|-----|---------|-------|","+| NFR-2 | Performance | Section week load (≤84 cells): one indexed query with includes, plus the periods and school days (cached or small). Easily under 400 ms. Avoid N+1 queries for teacher names. |","+| NFR-3 | Performance | Availability under 300 ms means the batch evaluation in FR-36 makes about 4 queries total, not one per cell. The student-overlap rule is a single SQL statement grouped by `(dayOfWeek, periodId, otherCourseId)`. |","+| NFR-9 | Conventions | Reuse http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader and the access helpers. The new service path is `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Do not create a parallel helpers folder. |","+| NFR-10 | Tests | lint, typecheck and test gate. |","+| NFR-13 | Tests | Playwright: drag works through mouse events with dnd-kit's PointerSensor (step-wise `mouse.move`). The keyboard path (FR-22) is a more reliable e2e fallback for placement. |","+| NFR-14 | Conventions | Use `logger` (for example, to log P2034 retries). |","+| NFR-15 | Scope | No solver, no A/B weeks, no substitutes, no holidays. `getScheduleForDate` is the single place PRD-14 will hook holidays later. |","+| NFR-16 | Scope | English only and a single school. Print must be tested across the 4 browsers. |","+","+## Open design decisions handed to `arch-design-system`","+","+1. **Free rooms (FR-21):** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` (recommended), or fold rooms into the availability response.","+2. **Availability room rule (FR-36):** skip it (recommended; it is checked on drop), or evaluate against the section homeroom.","+3. **School-day slotCount and cascade scope (FR-7/FR-34):** all years (recommended) or the current year only.","+4. **Archived entities:** exclude archived courses and rooms from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks (intake default, agreed).","+5. **Subject colour (FR-16):** check `Subject` for a colour field. If there is none, use a deterministic hash-to-palette approach and make no schema change.","+6. **ADMIN on `/api/me/timetable` (FR-38):** return an empty list (recommended) or a 400.","+7. **Serialization retry helper (NFR-1):** a new small `withSerializableRetry` with no existing precedent (B7). Keep it in timetable-service.","+","+## Intake blockers and how this analysis covers them","+","+| Blocker | Covered by |","+|---------|-----------|","+| FR-44 seed fixtures | Seed rows above. Reuse any existing PRD-03/05 fixtures first. |","+| FR-43 ENG/HIST subjects | Reuse ELA/SOC with PRD course codes. |","+| FR-21 free rooms | Decision 1. |","+| FR-7 slot count | GET /api/school-days `slotCount` (FR-34 row), decision 3. |","+| FR-4/NFR-6 migration + dnd-kit | B1, B2, B12. |","+| NFR-5 mui-mcp | Dev-phase hard gate (NFR-5 row). The mui-mcp server is configured in this environment. |"]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-4\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`. That file covers PRD-04 Notifications & Email\nInfrastructure (41 FR and 18 NFR, so 59 requirements) at 93% confidence, with 4 blockers in\n`handoff-to-architect.json`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\nConcern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Type Registry**, **Notify Service**,\n**Preference Resolution**, **Email Rendering**, **Auth Email Seam**, **Outbox Dispatcher**,\n**Transport**, **Background Job**, **Internal Endpoint**, **User API**, **Admin API**,\n**UI: Bell**, **UI: Notifications Page**, **UI: Preferences Page**, **UI: Admin Email Log**,\n**Validation**, **Seed**, **Security**, **Performance**, **Reliability**, **Conventions**,\n**Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these add to or correct intake)\n\n| # | Finding | Impact |\n|---|---------|--------|\n| B1 | `src/middleware.ts` returns **401 for any `/api/*` request without a session** unless `isPublicPath()` matches. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is only `['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`. | The cron call to `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` carries no session cookie, so it would be rejected by middleware before the handler runs. **`/api/internal/` must be added to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** (prefix match). The handler then becomes the only gate, so its CRON_SECRET check must be strict (NFR-8). The middleware's cross-origin guard does not block it, because cron calls send no `Origin` header. |\n| B2 | `prisma/seed.ts` (95 lines) seeds only SchoolSettings and academic reference data. **There are no `student@schoolhub.test` or `parent@schoolhub.test` users** anywhere in `prisma/` or `src/`. | FR-40 cannot simply attach notifications to existing users. Options: (a) look up those users by email and skip with a log line when they are missing, or (b) upsert minimal STUDENT/PARENT users. Recommend (a). It keeps the seed idempotent and avoids PRD-04 creating identity data that another PRD owns. Design should confirm. |\n| B3 | `vitest.config.ts` includes only `tests/unit/**` and uses `environment: 'jsdom'`. There is no `tests/integration/` folder and no test-DB setup. | NFR-15 needs a node environment plus a real Postgres to exercise `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`. This requires a separate vitest project or config (e.g. `vitest.integration.config.ts`, `environment: 'node'`, `include: tests/integration/**`) that is skipped when `DATABASE_URL_TEST` is absent, so that `npm run test` stays green (NFR-13). |\n| B4 | `EmailOutbox` has **no `userId` and no `type` column**. It stores only `toEmail`, `toName`, `subject`, `html`, `text`, `status`, `attempts`, `lastError`, `nextAttemptAt`, `sentAt`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. | The admin email log (FR-31) can only show recipient email and name, not a user link or type. That is sufficient for FR-31, so the schema should not change (NFR-13). `sendAuthEmail` (FR-16) fits naturally because it has no type. |\n| B5 | `NotificationPreference` uses a composite PK `@@id([userId, type])`. | FR-38's upsert keys on `userId_type`. FR-7's resolution reads with `findMany({ where: { userId: { in }, type } })`, which is a single query. |\n| B6 | `src/server/http.ts` already exports `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parsePagination` (default 20, max 100), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. `ApiErrorCode` already includes `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `NOT_FOUND`, `UNAUTHENTICATED` and `FORBIDDEN`. | All new route handlers reuse these (NFR-11). No new error codes are needed. |\n| B7 | `src/lib/dates.ts` exports `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, timezone)` (date-fns-tz). `SchoolSettings.timezone` defaults to `'UTC'`. `src/server/services/settings.ts` exists. | NFR-12 reuses these. Relative times (\"5 min ago\") are timezone-independent. Absolute times in the email log and the invite expiry date use `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| B8 | `src/server/rate-limit.ts` exports an in-memory `rateLimit()`. | It could optionally guard `POST /api/admin/notifications/test`, but no requirement asks for that. Skip it under compliance rule 1. |\n| B9 | `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx`, `Toast/useToast.ts`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader` and `DateDisplay` exist. | FR-26 and FR-31 reuse DataTable, PageHeader and EmptyState. FR-30 reuses `useToast`. Do not create duplicates. |\n| B10 | Prisma `$transaction` is used in `src/server/sections/`. No `$queryRaw` is used anywhere yet. | FR-17's `SKIP LOCKED` claim is the first raw SQL in the repo. Use tagged `$queryRaw` (parameterised) inside `$transaction`, or a single `UPDATE … WHERE id IN (SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *` statement, which claims rows atomically without holding a transaction across SMTP. |\n| B11 | All other intake brownfield findings were confirmed: there is no migration for the three models, the env vars and `worker:email` script are present, the navigation entries exist, `sendAuthEmail` has exactly 2 callers (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`), and the `requireRole` helpers exist. | — |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |\n|-----|----------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | One new migration `2026110400xxxx_notifications_email`. It creates `EmailStatus`, `Notification`, `NotificationPreference` and `EmailOutbox` exactly as `schema.prisma` declares them, including the additive `updatedAt` columns and both indexes. Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and do not edit `schema.prisma`. It must sort after `20261104000000_auth_reconcile`. |\n| FR-2 | Type Registry | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` exports `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` with `as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>`, which keeps literal keys for FR-5 while type-checking the shape. Add one field, `emailOnly?: true` (or `hidden`), to express FR-4. |\n| FR-3 | Type Registry | `NotificationCategory` is a string-literal union of the 6 values, not a Prisma enum, because the DB stores `type` as a free `String`. The UI groups by category (FR-26, FR-28). |\n| FR-4 | Type Registry, Auth Email Seam | `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are `emailOnly`, hidden from preferences and never passed to `notify()` (blocker default confirmed in \"Decisions for design\" below). `system.test` uses category SYSTEM, `defaultEmail: true` and all roles (AC-1 expects both rows). |\n| FR-5 | Type Registry | `type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. Later PRDs extend the registry by editing this one file, and no plugin mechanism is needed (YAGNI). |\n| FR-6 | Notify Service | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` is a pure server module. Its `email.template` param is a key into the template map (FR-13), and `data` is typed per template. |\n| FR-7 | Preference Resolution | Load users with `findMany({ id in userIds, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` and prefs with `findMany({ userId in, type })`. Then resolve each user with a pure function `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }`, which is unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| FR-8 | Notify Service | `inApp = row?.inApp ?? true`, with `mandatoryInApp` forcing true. Notifications are written with `createMany`. |\n| FR-9 | Notify Service, Email Rendering | `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` and requires `user.email`. Render once per recipient, because templates contain the name. Rendering cost dominates NFR-1, so `render()` calls should run with bounded `Promise.all` concurrency. Rows are written to `EmailOutbox` with `createMany`. |\n| FR-10 | Performance | 1,000 recipients means 3 round-trips: users, prefs and one `createMany`, per channel. Chunk `createMany` at about 500 rows only if the parameter limit bites (Postgres allows 65,535 params, and Notification has about 7 columns, so 1,000 rows fit in one call). |\n| FR-11 | Notify Service | Wrap the whole body in try/catch, call `logger.error`, and return `void` or a `{ notified, emailed }` summary. Callers invoke it after commit. Document that in JSDoc. |\n| FR-12 | Notify Service | `notifyStudentAndParents` makes one `ParentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call (indexed on `studentId`), merges into a `Set`, then calls `notify`. Expansion and dedupe are a pure function so they can be unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| FR-13 | Email Rendering | `src/server/email/templates/*.tsx` with `@react-email/components`. `src/server/email/render.ts` calls `render(el)` and `render(el, { plainText: true })` from `@react-email/render` 1.0.1, which is async. |\n| FR-14 | Email Rendering | `BaseLayout.tsx` takes `school: Pick<SchoolSettings, name, logoUrl, addressLine1, addressLine2>`. Fetch SchoolSettings once per `notify()` / `sendAuthEmail` call, not once per recipient. The footer link is `APP_URL/account/notifications`. |\n| FR-15 | Email Rendering | There are 3 templates. Invite needs an expiry date, which `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` does not receive. The template can derive it from the known invite TTL constant in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, so the signature stays unchanged. Password reset uses the hardcoded 60-minute notice. The generic CTA href is `APP_URL + link` (the link is already validated by NFR-6). |\n| FR-16 | Auth Email Seam | Only the body of `src/server/auth/email.ts` changes: render the template and call `prisma.emailOutbox.create`. Its 2 callers are untouched. Unlike `notify()`, failures here **should** surface, because the existing callers already handle errors and a silently lost invite is worse. Design should decide whether to keep the current awaited and throwable behaviour (recommended). |\n| FR-17 | Outbox Dispatcher | `src/server/email/dispatch.ts`. First, run stuck-row recovery (NFR-5). Next, claim rows with one atomic `UPDATE … SET status='SENDING', updatedAt=now() WHERE id IN (SELECT id … WHERE status='PENDING' AND nextAttemptAt<=now() ORDER BY nextAttemptAt LIMIT $n FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *`. Then send each row outside any transaction and update it individually. |\n| FR-18 | Outbox Dispatcher | A pure function `backoffMinutes(attempts) → [1,5,15,60,240][attempts-1]`, plus `attempts >= 5 → FAILED`. It is unit-tested (NFR-14). `lastError` is truncated to about 1,000 characters. |\n| FR-19 | Internal Endpoint | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`. Compare the bearer token against `env.CRON_SECRET` with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. A missing env value always returns 401. The response is `{ data: { sent, failed, retried } }` via `ok()`. **Requires B1** (the middleware allowlist). The route also triggers FR-27. |\n| FR-20 | Background Job | `scripts/worker-email.ts` imports `dispatchEmails` directly (tsx resolves the `@/` alias via tsconfig paths) and runs a `setTimeout` loop every 15 s with SIGINT/SIGTERM handling. It does not go over HTTP and does not call purge, because purge belongs to the endpoint only (FR-27). |\n| FR-21 | Transport | `src/server/email/transport.ts` exports `getTransport()` with 2 branches. `smtp` uses `nodemailer.createTransport` with SMTP_* settings and is memoised. `console` uses `console.log`, which NFR-11 explicitly allows. Each message includes `List-Unsubscribe` (NFR-9). Missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` under `smtp` should fail at transport creation, and the dispatcher must record that as a retryable `lastError`, not crash. |\n| FR-22 | UI: Bell | The `'use client'` component `NotificationBell.tsx` replaces the placeholder in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`. It uses MUI `Badge` with `max={9}`, which renders \"9+\" natively, so no custom formatting is needed. |\n| FR-23 | UI: Bell | A `setInterval` of 30 s gated on `document.visibilityState`, plus an immediate refetch on `visibilitychange → visible`. There is no SWR or react-query dependency, so plain `fetch` is enough. |\n| FR-24 | UI: Bell | `Popover` + `List` + `ListItemButton`. Unread items use bold `fontWeight` and a `Badge variant=\"dot\"` or small Box. The body is clamped with `sx={{ WebkitLineClamp: 2 }}`. Relative time uses `date-fns` `formatDistanceToNowStrict` (date-fns-tz is already installed, so date-fns is too). The popover fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10` on open. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Bell | On click, call `POST /:id/read`, then `router.push(link)`, then close. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" (`POST /read-all`) and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |\n| FR-26 | UI: Notifications Page | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` is a server shell using `requirePageUser()` and a client list. It has `Tabs` (All/Unread), a category `Select`, the pagination from DataTable or MUI `Pagination` with a page size of 20, and a per-row toggle calling `/:id/read` or `/:id/unread`. |\n| FR-27 | Background Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` (`deleteMany createdAt < now-180d`) lives in `src/server/notifications/`. A module-level `let lastPurgeAt` in the dispatch route allows at most one run per 24 h per process. It is best-effort, and its failure is logged and must not fail the dispatch response. |\n| FR-28 | UI: Preferences Page | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`. This is the first page under `/account/`, so the directory is new. It is an MUI `Table` with a full-width category header `TableRow` (the intake default is accepted) and data from `GET /api/me/notification-preferences`. |\n| FR-29 | UI: Preferences Page | `Tooltip` around a **span** wrapping the disabled `Switch`, because MUI Tooltip does not fire on disabled elements. |\n| FR-30 | UI: Preferences Page | Optimistic local state, `PUT`, and on error revert plus `useToast().error(...)`. |\n| FR-31 | UI: Admin Email Log | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` uses `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` with DataTable and a status `Select`. The recipient column shows `toName <toEmail>` (B4). |\n| FR-32 | Admin API, UI: Admin Email Log | The retry action is shown only when `status==='FAILED'`. The server guard uses `updateMany where { id, status: FAILED }`, and a count of 0 returns 409 CONFLICT or 404, so a double click is harmless. |\n| FR-33 | Admin API | `POST /api/admin/notifications/test` uses `requireRole('ADMIN')`, then `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title, body, link: '/dashboard' })`. The button sits on the email-log page because no separate admin page is needed. |\n| FR-34 | User API | `GET /api/notifications` uses `parseQuery` with Zod (`unread`, `category`), `parsePagination` and `paginated()`. **Category filter caveat:** Notification has no category column. Filter by the `type IN (keys of registry with that category)` derived from the registry at request time. This needs no schema change and remains index-compatible with `userId` leading. |\n| FR-35 | User API | `count({ where: { userId, readAt: null } })` is covered by the `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index (NFR-2). |\n| FR-36 | User API | Mark read or unread with `updateMany({ where: { id, userId: me.id } })`. A count of 0 returns 404, which hides existence from non-owners. `read-all` runs `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null })`. Route files: `[id]/read/route.ts`, `[id]/unread/route.ts` and `read-all/route.ts`. **Next.js routing note:** `read-all` and `unread-count` are static siblings of `[id]`, and static segments win, so they do not conflict. |\n| FR-37 | User API, Preference Resolution | `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` (GET and PUT in one file) is the first route under `/api/me/`. It filters the registry by `roles.includes(me.role)` and `!emailOnly`, merges the rows and returns `{ type, label, description, category, inApp, email, mandatoryInApp }[]`. |\n| FR-38 | User API, Validation | The Zod body is `{ type: z.enum(visibleTypeKeys), inApp: boolean, email: boolean }`. The service rejects `inApp=false` for mandatory types and role-invisible or `emailOnly` types with `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR')`, then calls `upsert` on `userId_type`. |\n| FR-39 | Admin API | `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` (GET) and `[id]/retry/route.ts` (POST), both protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The list is ordered by `createdAt desc` and **omits `html` and `text`** to keep the payload small. |\n| FR-40 | Seed | The seed appends to `prisma/seed.ts`. **See B2: the target users do not exist.** For idempotency, skip a user who already has any `system.test` notification (count > 0), giving 3 per user with 1 read and 2 unread, linking to `/dashboard`. |\n| FR-41 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` is a sibling of the existing `auth.ts`, `users.ts` and so on. It holds the list query schema, the preference PUT schema and `safeLink` (NFR-6). It must be client-safe: no server imports, so registry keys are passed in or the type is checked as a string and then against the registry in the service. |\n| NFR-1 | Performance | The budget of 2 s for 1,000 recipients is dominated by 1,000 react-email renders. Mitigate with SchoolSettings fetched once, bounded concurrency, and rendering only recipients with email enabled. If renders are too slow, render the generic template once with a name placeholder. Design should note this as the fallback. |\n| NFR-2 | Performance | Covered by the FR-1 index and FR-35 query shape. The bell must not call the list endpoint on every poll. |\n| NFR-3 | Reliability | No SMTP happens in the request path: `notify()` and `sendAuthEmail` only insert rows. The 15 s worker or the cron endpoint keeps delivery under 60 s. |\n| NFR-4 | Reliability | The FR-17 atomic claim with `SKIP LOCKED`. Each claimed row is owned by exactly one dispatcher. |\n| NFR-5 | Reliability | At the start of each dispatch: `updateMany({ status: SENDING, updatedAt < now-10m }, { status: PENDING })`. This relies on the additive `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`, which is why FR-1 keeps it. It does not increment attempts, because a crash mid-send was not proven to be a send failure. |\n| NFR-6 | Security | A shared `isSafeLink(s)` requires `s.startsWith('/')` and rejects `//`, `/\\`, any `\\` and control characters. It is applied in `notify()` (drop or nullify the link and warn instead of throwing, per FR-11) and in the Zod schema. Unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| NFR-7 | Security | React-email JSX escapes interpolated text by default. **Never** use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in templates. Body text is rendered as text with `white-space: pre-line`, not as HTML. |\n| NFR-8 | Security | Every new handler starts with `requireUser()` or `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The internal route uses a secret check only (B1). Pages use `requirePageUser()` or `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. |\n| NFR-9 | Security, Transport | Each `sendMail` call sets `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<APP_URL/account/notifications>' }` along with both `html` and `text`. Set it at send time rather than storing it in the outbox, because the outbox has no headers column (B4). |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions (UI) | All 4 UI surfaces (bell, notifications page, preferences page, email log) use MUI only. Dev must query mui-mcp before writing UI, and **this is an unresolved blocker carried forward**: if the server is unreachable, there is a hard stop. The existing `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned libs. Email templates are exempt. |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | Thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok`/`paginated`. Services live in `src/server/notifications/` and `src/server/email/`, and code uses `logger`, with `console` only in the console transport. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | UTC storage is the Prisma default. Display uses `formatInSchoolTz` (B7). The client components need the timezone, so pass it from the server page as a prop. |\n| NFR-13 | Conventions | Do not touch `schema.prisma`, navigation or env. Keep the `sendAuthEmail` signature. Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. This is the source of B1–B3 handling. |\n| NFR-14 | Test Harness | Pure units are `resolvePrefs`, `backoffMinutes`, `isSafeLink` and `expandStudentRecipients`. They go in `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`, run under the existing vitest config and need no DB. |\n| NFR-15 | Test Harness | **See B3.** A new `tests/integration/` folder with a node-env vitest config against a test DB. One test runs 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails` calls over 10 rows and asserts each row is sent once. A second test backdates a SENDING row's `updatedAt` by 11 minutes and asserts recovery. |\n| NFR-16 | Test Harness | Playwright tests go in `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`. They need a logged-in admin (the existing e2e harness pattern; check `dashboard.spec.ts` for auth setup). The flow is send test → bell count → mark all read → preference toggle persists after reload. |\n| NFR-17 | Scope Discipline | No SMS, push, websockets or digests. Polling only (FR-23), and do not add a `channel` abstraction for future SMS. |\n| NFR-18 | Notify Service | Silently truncate `title` to 140 characters and `body` to 500, with `logger.warn` (intake default accepted, since it is consistent with FR-11). There is no DB constraint, because the schema has plain `String`. |\n\n## Decisions for design (resolving intake blockers)\n\n1. **FR-1 migration**: Accepted. There is one new migration, `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `schema.prisma` is not changed.\n2. **FR-4/FR-16**: Accepted. `sendAuthEmail` enqueues directly and creates no Notification row. The `account.*` types are `emailOnly` and are filtered out of FR-28 and FR-37 and rejected by FR-38.\n3. **FR-40**: Use 3 per user, but the users are missing (B2). The recommendation is to look them up and skip if absent.\n4. **NFR-10**: Carried forward to dev as a precondition, because the architect cannot resolve it.\n5. **New**: Add `/api/internal/` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` (B1). Without it, AC-6 still passes (401), but real cron dispatch never works.\n\n## New/changed files implied (for arch-design-system to confirm)\n\n- **New**: `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/`, `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,purge}.ts`, `src/server/email/{transport,render,dispatch}.ts`, `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`, `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`, `src/app/api/notifications/{route,unread-count/route,read-all/route,[id]/read/route,[id]/unread/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/{route,[id]/retry/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `scripts/worker-email.ts`, plus tests under `tests/unit`, `tests/integration` and `tests/e2e`.\n- **Modified**: `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (bell), `src/config/public-routes.ts` (one entry), `prisma/seed.ts` (append), and possibly `package.json` (`test:integration` script only).\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013GaneQDXFMijKbtVFRKcWz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
