InputSlot`. Do not write a second checklist or fetch helper. |\n| B3 | `credentials.ts` throws `AuthError(code)` (a `CredentialsSignin` subclass). Codes: `invalid`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `locked:<N>`. | `/login` calls `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react` and maps `result.code` to the FR-4 and FR-6 copy. That mapping is a pure function and should get one unit test. |\n| B4 | `auth.ts` exports `signIn`, `signOut` and `unstable_update`. The `jwt` callback handles `trigger==='update' && session.reauth`. `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({reauth:true})`. | FR-20 \"re-issue current session\" is **already done server-side**. The page only POSTs and shows a toast. |\n| B5 | `app/providers.tsx` has **no `SessionProvider`**. | Client `signIn`/`signOut` from `next-auth/react` work without it. The shell gets the user as a **prop from the server layout**, so no provider and no `useSession` are needed. |\n| B6 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders the client `AppShell({ schoolShortName })`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user` (`id`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `role`) to `AppShell`. This removes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (FR-25/26/27) and gives one source of the current user. |\n| B7 | `shell.tsx` already imports `LogoutIcon`, `PersonOutlineIcon`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `Chip` and `UserAvatar`. | FR-21/FR-26 only change menu items. Add the `Account security` link and an `onClick={() => signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })}` handler. |\n| B8 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** sign the user in. Its error copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | FR-14: after a successful POST, the client calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` and then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. The FR-13 copy is rendered by the **page** when the server-side `verifyToken()` fails, and is reused when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. |\n| B9 | `tokens.ts` exports `verifyToken(raw, type)`, which is read-only and does not consume the token. | `/invite/[token]/page.tsx` is a server component that calls `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')` to show the name and email (FR-13). `/reset-password/[token]` can do the same up front. Neither needs a new endpoint. |\n| B10 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN', …)` is a code **outside** the NFR-10 code list. | This is existing behaviour; keep it (NFR-13). The UI must handle the `INVALID_TOKEN` code. Flag it for `arch-api-contracts` to document. |\n| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | FR-11 and NFR-14 are satisfied. Middleware needs no change. |\n| B12 | `prisma/seed.ts` already looks up `student@` and `parent@` to attach PRD-04 notifications, and **skips them if missing**. It uses `console.log`. | FR-28 user upserts must run **before** the notifications block. New seed code uses `logger` (NFR-12). The existing `console.log` lines are out of scope (NFR-13). |\n| B13 | Existing tests: unit `tokens`, `lockout`, `rate-limit`, `password-policy`, `auth-validators`. Integration has no auth tests. E2E has no auth specs. | FR-34 adds 4 integration files and 1–2 Playwright specs. Unit tests are already done. |\n| B14 | The existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) hit `(app)` pages. Once a real session is required, they redirect to `/login`. | **Regression risk (NFR-13):** the e2e suite needs a shared sign-in helper or `storageState` using the seed users. Check whether these specs currently pass without auth. |\n| B15 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. | `/forgot-password` displays the API's `data.message`, or imports this constant, rather than retyping the string. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | Already present; no change. |\n| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, a thin server wrapper that reads `callbackUrl` plus a client `LoginForm`. It uses RHF + `signInSchema`, `TextField`, a show-password `InputAdornment`/`IconButton` (reuse `passwordInputSlot`) and an `Alert`. It links to `/forgot-password`. |\n| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`; verify only. |\n| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Pure `loginErrorMessage(code)` maps `invalid`, `disabled` and `locked:N` to the PRD copy. The locked message reads \"Try again in N minutes.\" |\n| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`); covered by the integration test. |\n| FR-6 | UI: Auth Pages | Limiter present. Map `rate_limited` to \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |\n| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` after `signIn` succeeds. Reuse the validator. |\n| FR-8 | Audit | Already emitted by `authorizeCredentials`; integration test asserts the rows. |\n| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present; no change. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`). The `reauth` path keeps the changing session alive. |\n| FR-11 | Access Control | Present in `middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` (B11). |\n| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. UI pages call `verifyToken` server-side (B9) and never hash anything themselves. |\n| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name and email. Invalid: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. Uses `verifyToken`, not consume. |\n| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client POSTs `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials')`, then `/dashboard` (B8). Service and audit already present. |\n| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is server-only and surfaces through `fieldErrors.password`. |\n| FR-16 | UI: Auth Pages / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` on invite, reset and change forms (B2). |\n| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`. RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password')`. Always shows the success `Alert` and handles `RATE_LIMITED`. API, limiter and service are present. |\n| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` + `sendAuthEmail`); integration test only. |\n| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`. Uses `SetPasswordForm`, then `/login?reset=1`, where `LoginForm` fires `useToast` once on mount. The query param is the lazy channel; there is no shared state. |\n| FR-20 | UI: Account | New `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form (current/new/confirm, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`). On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show the field error. On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form. Session re-issue is already server-side (B4). |\n| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` \"Account security\" item to the user menu. |\n| FR-22 | Service | Present; verify only. |\n| FR-23 | Access Control | Present; `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole` are used by the new pages. |\n| FR-24 | Audit | Present. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`; `AppShell` takes a `user` prop (B6). |\n| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name = `firstName lastName`, role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |\n| FR-27 | UI: Shell | `navigationForRole(user.role)`. |\n| FR-28 | Seed | `prisma.user.upsert` × 6 by email, `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)`, status ACTIVE and `passwordChangedAt` set. Idempotent with `update: {}`. Place before the notifications block (B12). |\n| FR-29 | Seed | Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` (INVITED, no `passwordHash`). |\n| FR-30 | Seed | `createInviteToken(user.id)` (which invalidates older invites on rerun) and `logger.info(authLink('invite', raw))`. Do not use `sendAuthEmail`. |\n| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `email.ts`. |\n| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip`; no rename (default per intake). |\n| FR-33 | Migration | Add a new additive migration with `@@index([role, status])` on `User` (default per intake). |\n| FR-34 | Tests | Integration files `auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`) run against the test DB. The e2e `auth.spec.ts` covers sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus a unit test for `loginErrorMessage`. |\n| NFR-1 | Security | Present in `tokens.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` fetches the CSRF token automatically. JSON POST routes are same-origin and SameSite=Lax. |\n| NFR-3 | Security | Present (`DUMMY_HASH`). |\n| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt is about 250 ms, so this is met. Nothing new to design. |\n| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every form has an `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`, and RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default) focuses the first invalid field. `applyFieldErrors` already focuses the first server-reported field. |\n| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate:** dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev blocks and does not guess. |\n| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |\n| NFR-8 | Audit | Existing metadata is `{ email, reason }`, which is safe. New code adds no audit calls. |\n| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers already conform (B10 notes the one extra code). |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | All forms use RHF + `zodResolver` with the shared `auth.ts` schemas. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger` (seed included). |\n| NFR-13 | Scope | No edits to `course-access.ts`/`student-access.ts` or any existing auth module. Watch B14 so e2e does not regress. |\n| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page; `/login` has no \"create account\" link. |\n| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI, English copy. Nothing to design. |\n\n## New files (expected) vs modified files\n\n**New:** `(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`,\n`(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`, `(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + client form, one additive migration, 4 integration tests, 1 e2e spec\n(+ e2e sign-in helper if B14 bites).\n\n**Modified:** `(app)/layout.tsx` (session user → prop), `(app)/shell.tsx` (drop placeholder, menu items),\n`prisma/schema.prisma` (index), `prisma/seed.ts` (users + invite).\n\n**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts` and `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`.\n\n## Open items carried from intake\n\n1. FR-32: keep `ip`.\n2. FR-33: add the index.\n3. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`.\n4. Ticket id is SH-1.\n5. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a dev-phase hard gate.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B9p88ynzm9UBNpJc1z1ZX9","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"608f2610-ae4e-4b2e-af6e-d46d1dae17cd","uuid":"0dcab7ce-fb63-487f-a51b-cf802f1a19b3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:38:50.595Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-1\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` for PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001).\nIt has 34 FRs and 15 NFRs (49 requirements) at 97% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are **stale outputs from an earlier ticket**, and the other\n> sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-1 input, with one exception: `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n> once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-1.\n\n**Headline:** this is a **UI + seed + tests** ticket. Every backend module and API route already exists.\nThe design must add pages and wire them to existing code, not add services or endpoints.\n**No new API endpoint is needed.** `arch-api-contracts` should document the 5 existing routes as-is.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Auth Core**, **Service**, **API (existing)**,\n**UI: Auth Pages**, **UI: Account**, **UI: Shell**, **Access Control**, **Security**, **Audit**,\n**Seed**, **Accessibility**, **UI Rules**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these confirm or add to intake)\n\n| # | Fact | Design implication |\n|---|------|--------------------|\n| B1 | `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` already renders the centred `Card` shell (SchoolHub logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"`). | Auth pages render **only the card body**, with no Card or Container of their own. |\n| B2 | `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure`. Nothing imports them yet. | FR-16 checklist and the invite/reset forms **reuse `SetPasswordForm`**. `/account/security` and `/login` reuse `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`. Do not write a second checklist or fetch helper. |\n| B3 | `credentials.ts` throws `AuthError(code)` (a `CredentialsSignin` subclass). Codes: `invalid`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `locked:<N>`. | `/login` calls `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react` and maps `result.code` to the FR-4 and FR-6 copy. That mapping is a pure function and should get one unit test. |\n| B4 | `auth.ts` exports `signIn`, `signOut` and `unstable_update`. The `jwt` callback handles `trigger==='update' && session.reauth`. `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({reauth:true})`. | FR-20 \"re-issue current session\" is **already done server-side**. The page only POSTs and shows a toast. |\n| B5 | `app/providers.tsx` has **no `SessionProvider`**. | Client `signIn`/`signOut` from `next-auth/react` work without it. The shell gets the user as a **prop from the server layout**, so no provider and no `useSession` are needed. |\n| B6 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders the client `AppShell({ schoolShortName })`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user` (`id`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `role`) to `AppShell`. This removes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (FR-25/26/27) and gives one source of the current user. |\n| B7 | `shell.tsx` already imports `LogoutIcon`, `PersonOutlineIcon`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `Chip` and `UserAvatar`. | FR-21/FR-26 only change menu items. Add the `Account security` link and an `onClick={() => signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })}` handler. |\n| B8 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** sign the user in. Its error copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | FR-14: after a successful POST, the client calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` and then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. The FR-13 copy is rendered by the **page** when the server-side `verifyToken()` fails, and is reused when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. |\n| B9 | `tokens.ts` exports `verifyToken(raw, type)`, which is read-only and does not consume the token. | `/invite/[token]/page.tsx` is a server component that calls `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')` to show the name and email (FR-13). `/reset-password/[token]` can do the same up front. Neither needs a new endpoint. |\n| B10 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN', …)` is a code **outside** the NFR-10 code list. | This is existing behaviour; keep it (NFR-13). The UI must handle the `INVALID_TOKEN` code. Flag it for `arch-api-contracts` to document. |\n| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | FR-11 and NFR-14 are satisfied. Middleware needs no change. |\n| B12 | `prisma/seed.ts` already looks up `student@` and `parent@` to attach PRD-04 notifications, and **skips them if missing**. It uses `console.log`. | FR-28 user upserts must run **before** the notifications block. New seed code uses `logger` (NFR-12). The existing `console.log` lines are out of scope (NFR-13). |\n| B13 | Existing tests: unit `tokens`, `lockout`, `rate-limit`, `password-policy`, `auth-validators`. Integration has no auth tests. E2E has no auth specs. | FR-34 adds 4 integration files and 1–2 Playwright specs. Unit tests are already done. |\n| B14 | The existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) hit `(app)` pages. Once a real session is required, they redirect to `/login`. | **Regression risk (NFR-13):** the e2e suite needs a shared sign-in helper or `storageState` using the seed users. Check whether these specs currently pass without auth. |\n| B15 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. | `/forgot-password` displays the API's `data.message`, or imports this constant, rather than retyping the string. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | Already present; no change. |\n| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, a thin server wrapper that reads `callbackUrl` plus a client `LoginForm`. It uses RHF + `signInSchema`, `TextField`, a show-password `InputAdornment`/`IconButton` (reuse `passwordInputSlot`) and an `Alert`. It links to `/forgot-password`. |\n| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`; verify only. |\n| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Pure `loginErrorMessage(code)` maps `invalid`, `disabled` and `locked:N` to the PRD copy. The locked message reads \"Try again in N minutes.\" |\n| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`); covered by the integration test. |\n| FR-6 | UI: Auth Pages | Limiter present. Map `rate_limited` to \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |\n| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` after `signIn` succeeds. Reuse the validator. |\n| FR-8 | Audit | Already emitted by `authorizeCredentials`; integration test asserts the rows. |\n| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present; no change. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`). The `reauth` path keeps the changing session alive. |\n| FR-11 | Access Control | Present in `middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` (B11). |\n| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. UI pages call `verifyToken` server-side (B9) and never hash anything themselves. |\n| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name and email. Invalid: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. Uses `verifyToken`, not consume. |\n| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client POSTs `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials')`, then `/dashboard` (B8). Service and audit already present. |\n| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is server-only and surfaces through `fieldErrors.password`. |\n| FR-16 | UI: Auth Pages / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` on invite, reset and change forms (B2). |\n| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`. RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password')`. Always shows the success `Alert` and handles `RATE_LIMITED`. API, limiter and service are present. |\n| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` + `sendAuthEmail`); integration test only. |\n| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`. Uses `SetPasswordForm`, then `/login?reset=1`, where `LoginForm` fires `useToast` once on mount. The query param is the lazy channel; there is no shared state. |\n| FR-20 | UI: Account | New `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form (current/new/confirm, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`). On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show the field error. On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form. Session re-issue is already server-side (B4). |\n| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` \"Account security\" item to the user menu. |\n| FR-22 | Service | Present; verify only. |\n| FR-23 | Access Control | Present; `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole` are used by the new pages. |\n| FR-24 | Audit | Present. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`; `AppShell` takes a `user` prop (B6). |\n| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name = `firstName lastName`, role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |\n| FR-27 | UI: Shell | `navigationForRole(user.role)`. |\n| FR-28 | Seed | `prisma.user.upsert` × 6 by email, `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)`, status ACTIVE and `passwordChangedAt` set. Idempotent with `update: {}`. Place before the notifications block (B12). |\n| FR-29 | Seed | Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` (INVITED, no `passwordHash`). |\n| FR-30 | Seed | `createInviteToken(user.id)` (which invalidates older invites on rerun) and `logger.info(authLink('invite', raw))`. Do not use `sendAuthEmail`. |\n| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `email.ts`. |\n| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip`; no rename (default per intake). |\n| FR-33 | Migration | Add a new additive migration with `@@index([role, status])` on `User` (default per intake). |\n| FR-34 | Tests | Integration files `auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`) run against the test DB. The e2e `auth.spec.ts` covers sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus a unit test for `loginErrorMessage`. |\n| NFR-1 | Security | Present in `tokens.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` fetches the CSRF token automatically. JSON POST routes are same-origin and SameSite=Lax. |\n| NFR-3 | Security | Present (`DUMMY_HASH`). |\n| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt is about 250 ms, so this is met. Nothing new to design. |\n| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every form has an `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`, and RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default) focuses the first invalid field. `applyFieldErrors` already focuses the first server-reported field. |\n| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate:** dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev blocks and does not guess. |\n| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |\n| NFR-8 | Audit | Existing metadata is `{ email, reason }`, which is safe. New code adds no audit calls. |\n| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers already conform (B10 notes the one extra code). |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | All forms use RHF + `zodResolver` with the shared `auth.ts` schemas. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger` (seed included). |\n| NFR-13 | Scope | No edits to `course-access.ts`/`student-access.ts` or any existing auth module. Watch B14 so e2e does not regress. |\n| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page; `/login` has no \"create account\" link. |\n| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI, English copy. Nothing to design. |\n\n## New files (expected) vs modified files\n\n**New:** `(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`,\n`(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`, `(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + client form, one additive migration, 4 integration tests, 1 e2e spec\n(+ e2e sign-in helper if B14 bites).\n\n**Modified:** `(app)/layout.tsx` (session user → prop), `(app)/shell.tsx` (drop placeholder, menu items),\n`prisma/schema.prisma` (index), `prisma/seed.ts` (users + invite).\n\n**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts` and `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`.\n\n## Open items carried from intake\n\n1. FR-32: keep `ip`.\n2. FR-33: add the index.\n3. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`.\n4. Ticket id is SH-1.\n5. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a dev-phase hard gate.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":156,"newStart":1,"newLines":112,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-6","+# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-1"," "," Supporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`, which covers PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable","-(45 FR and 16 NFR, 61 requirements) at 96% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` for PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001).","+It has 34 FRs and 15 NFRs (49 requirements) at 97% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers."," Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`."," ","-> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (`api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`,","-> `system-design.md`, `tech-stack-decisions.md`, `threat-model-notes.json`) are **stale SH-4 outputs**.","-> The other sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-6 input, except for","-> `tech-stack-decisions.md` once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-6.","+> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are **stale outputs from an earlier ticket**, and the other","+> sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-1 input, with one exception: `tech-stack-decisions.md`","+> once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-1."," ","-Concern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Validation**, **Clash Engine**, **Service**,","-**Admin API**, **Read API**, **Access Control**, **UI: Bell Schedule**, **UI: Editor**,","-**UI: Personal Timetable**, **UI: Tabs/Nav**, **Print**, **Time/TZ**, **Audit**, **Seed**,","-**Concurrency**, **Performance**, **Accessibility**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.","+**Headline:** this is a **UI + seed + tests** ticket. Every backend module and API route already exists.","+The design must add pages and wire them to existing code, not add services or endpoints.","+**No new API endpoint is needed.** `arch-api-contracts` should document the 5 existing routes as-is."," ","+Concern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Auth Core**, **Service**, **API (existing)**,","+**UI: Auth Pages**, **UI: Account**, **UI: Shell**, **Access Control**, **Security**, **Audit**,","+**Seed**, **Accessibility**, **UI Rules**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.","+"," ## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these confirm or add to intake)"," "," | # | Fact | Design implication |"," |---|------|--------------------|","-| B1 | `prisma/schema.prisma` has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind. The latest migration is `20261104120000_notifications_email`. | The new migration needs a later timestamp (for example `20261105000000_timetable`). |","-| B2 | `Room` already has a back-relation `sections Section[]`. `Course` has `enrollments` but no slots relation. | Add `Room.timetableSlots`, `Course.timetableSlots` and `Period.slots`. All are additive. |","-| B3 | `Course.coTeacherIds String[]`, nullable `sectionId`, `archivedAt`, `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. `Enrollment @@index([studentId, status])`, `onDelete: Cascade` from Course. | The teacher clash check needs `teacherId IN set OR coTeacherIds hasSome set`. The student-overlap check joins Enrollment on both courses. |","-| B4 | `Section.roomId?` (homeroom room) and `Section.homeroomTeacherId?`. `@@unique([academicYearId, name])`. | FR-17 uses `Section.roomId` as the default room. FR-35 checks TEACHER access through `homeroomTeacherId`. |","-| B5 | `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` with `@@index([studentId])`. `/api/me/children` already exists. | FR-25 and FR-38 can reuse `/api/me/children` for the child selector, so no new endpoint is needed. Parent access goes through `assertCanViewStudent`. |","-| B6 | `SchoolSettings.timezone` (default `'UTC'`) is read by the cached `getSchoolSettings()` in `src/server/services/settings.ts`. `src/lib/dates.ts` has `formatInSchoolTz` (date-fns-tz `formatInTimeZone`). | All \"now\" maths (FR-31, FR-45) uses `formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')` and ISO day `'i'`. Plain `HH:MM` string comparison then works. |","-| B7 | SERIALIZABLE precedent: `academicYears.ts` and `terms.ts` use `prisma.$transaction(fn, { isolationLevel: Serializable })` but **do not retry**. There is no P2034 handling in `src/`. | NFR-1 needs a small retry wrapper for P2034 (serialization failure). It is new code, so keep it local to timetable-service unless the design wants to reuse it. |","-| B8 | `http.ts` has `ApiErrorCode` with CONFLICT=409 and FORBIDDEN=403, plus `AppError`, `withHandler` (maps P2002 → CONFLICT, P2025 → NOT_FOUND), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. | Clashes are thrown as `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })`. The handler shape is already standard. |","-| B9 | `audit({ actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request })` never throws. By convention `action` is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|delete`. | FR-40 actions: `timetableSlot.create\\|update\\|delete`, `period.create\\|update\\|delete\\|reorder`, `schoolDay.update` (metadata includes `deletedSlotCount`). |","-| B10 | Validators live in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts` (courses, sections, ...). Feature services live in `src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts`. Tabs live in `src/config/course-tabs.ts` and `student-tabs.ts` (`{ key, label, href, roles }`). | FR-39: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`. FR-27 and FR-28 each register one entry. |","-| B11 | API route dirs exist: `rooms`, `sections`, `courses`, `me/*`, `admin/*`. There are no `periods`, `school-days` or `timetable` routes. App admin pages: `admin/courses`, `admin/sections`, `admin/email-log`. | Everything here is new. Nothing gets renamed. |","-| B12 | `package.json` pins `@mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0`, `date-fns 3.6.0`, `date-fns-tz 3.2.0` and `@prisma/client 5.20.0`. `@dnd-kit/*` is absent. | FR-23 and NFR-6 add exactly one pinned dependency, `@dnd-kit/core`. Reorder (FR-5) uses up/down buttons, so `@dnd-kit/sortable` is not needed. |","+| B1 | `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` already renders the centred `Card` shell (SchoolHub logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"`). | Auth pages render **only the card body**, with no Card or Container of their own. |","+| B2 | `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure`. Nothing imports them yet. | FR-16 checklist and the invite/reset forms **reuse `SetPasswordForm`**. `/account/security` and `/login` reuse `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`. Do not write a second checklist or fetch helper. |","+| B3 | `credentials.ts` throws `AuthError(code)` (a `CredentialsSignin` subclass). Codes: `invalid`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `locked:<N>`. | `/login` calls `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react` and maps `result.code` to the FR-4 and FR-6 copy. That mapping is a pure function and should get one unit test. |","+| B4 | `auth.ts` exports `signIn`, `signOut` and `unstable_update`. The `jwt` callback handles `trigger==='update' && session.reauth`. `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({reauth:true})`. | FR-20 \"re-issue current session\" is **already done server-side**. The page only POSTs and shows a toast. |","+| B5 | `app/providers.tsx` has **no `SessionProvider`**. | Client `signIn`/`signOut` from `next-auth/react` work without it. The shell gets the user as a **prop from the server layout**, so no provider and no `useSession` are needed. |","+| B6 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders the client `AppShell({ schoolShortName })`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user` (`id`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `role`) to `AppShell`. This removes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (FR-25/26/27) and gives one source of the current user. |","+| B7 | `shell.tsx` already imports `LogoutIcon`, `PersonOutlineIcon`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `Chip` and `UserAvatar`. | FR-21/FR-26 only change menu items. Add the `Account security` link and an `onClick={() => signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })}` handler. |","+| B8 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** sign the user in. Its error copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | FR-14: after a successful POST, the client calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` and then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. The FR-13 copy is rendered by the **page** when the server-side `verifyToken()` fails, and is reused when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. |","+| B9 | `tokens.ts` exports `verifyToken(raw, type)`, which is read-only and does not consume the token. | `/invite/[token]/page.tsx` is a server component that calls `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')` to show the name and email (FR-13). `/reset-password/[token]` can do the same up front. Neither needs a new endpoint. |","+| B10 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN', …)` is a code **outside** the NFR-10 code list. | This is existing behaviour; keep it (NFR-13). The UI must handle the `INVALID_TOKEN` code. Flag it for `arch-api-contracts` to document. |","+| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | FR-11 and NFR-14 are satisfied. Middleware needs no change. |","+| B12 | `prisma/seed.ts` already looks up `student@` and `parent@` to attach PRD-04 notifications, and **skips them if missing**. It uses `console.log`. | FR-28 user upserts must run **before** the notifications block. New seed code uses `logger` (NFR-12). The existing `console.log` lines are out of scope (NFR-13). |","+| B13 | Existing tests: unit `tokens`, `lockout`, `rate-limit`, `password-policy`, `auth-validators`. Integration has no auth tests. E2E has no auth specs. | FR-34 adds 4 integration files and 1–2 Playwright specs. Unit tests are already done. |","+| B14 | The existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) hit `(app)` pages. Once a real session is required, they redirect to `/login`. | **Regression risk (NFR-13):** the e2e suite needs a shared sign-in helper or `storageState` using the seed users. Check whether these specs currently pass without auth. |","+| B15 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. | `/forgot-password` displays the API's `data.message`, or imports this constant, rather than retyping the string. |"," "," ## Requirement → architectural concern"," ","-### Data model and migration","-"," | Req | Concern | Notes |"," |-----|---------|-------|","-| FR-1 | Data Model | `enum PeriodKind` and `model Period`. Store `startTime`/`endTime` as `String` `HH:MM`. `order Int @unique` affects reorder (see FR-5). |","-| FR-2 | Data Model | `SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id, isTeaching Boolean }` is a 7-row lookup with no relations. Do not add a FK from TimetableSlot to it (the PRD defines `dayOfWeek Int`). |","-| FR-3 | Data Model | Index `@@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` covers every clash query (all are scoped to year + day + period). `academicYearId` is denormalised from Course. It is set server-side only (FR-37). `periodId` has no cascade, so deletion is guarded by FR-8 in the service. `roomId?` with `onDelete: SetNull` is the safe default, and rooms are archived rather than deleted. |","-| FR-4 | Migration | One additive migration plus the B2 back-relations. `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then review the SQL. It should only contain CREATE TYPE, CREATE TABLE and CREATE INDEX statements. |","+| FR-1 | Data Model | Already present; no change. |","+| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, a thin server wrapper that reads `callbackUrl` plus a client `LoginForm`. It uses RHF + `signInSchema`, `TextField`, a show-password `InputAdornment`/`IconButton` (reuse `passwordInputSlot`) and an `Alert`. It links to `/forgot-password`. |","+| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`; verify only. |","+| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Pure `loginErrorMessage(code)` maps `invalid`, `disabled` and `locked:N` to the PRD copy. The locked message reads \"Try again in N minutes.\" |","+| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`); covered by the integration test. |","+| FR-6 | UI: Auth Pages | Limiter present. Map `rate_limited` to \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |","+| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` after `signIn` succeeds. Reuse the validator. |","+| FR-8 | Audit | Already emitted by `authorizeCredentials`; integration test asserts the rows. |","+| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present; no change. |","+| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`). The `reauth` path keeps the changing session alive. |","+| FR-11 | Access Control | Present in `middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` (B11). |","+| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. UI pages call `verifyToken` server-side (B9) and never hash anything themselves. |","+| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name and email. Invalid: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. Uses `verifyToken`, not consume. |","+| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client POSTs `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials')`, then `/dashboard` (B8). Service and audit already present. |","+| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is server-only and surfaces through `fieldErrors.password`. |","+| FR-16 | UI: Auth Pages / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` on invite, reset and change forms (B2). |","+| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`. RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password')`. Always shows the success `Alert` and handles `RATE_LIMITED`. API, limiter and service are present. |","+| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` + `sendAuthEmail`); integration test only. |","+| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`. Uses `SetPasswordForm`, then `/login?reset=1`, where `LoginForm` fires `useToast` once on mount. The query param is the lazy channel; there is no shared state. |","+| FR-20 | UI: Account | New `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form (current/new/confirm, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`). On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show the field error. On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form. Session re-issue is already server-side (B4). |","+| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` \"Account security\" item to the user menu. |","+| FR-22 | Service | Present; verify only. |","+| FR-23 | Access Control | Present; `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole` are used by the new pages. |","+| FR-24 | Audit | Present. |","+| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`; `AppShell` takes a `user` prop (B6). |","+| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name = `firstName lastName`, role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |","+| FR-27 | UI: Shell | `navigationForRole(user.role)`. |","+| FR-28 | Seed | `prisma.user.upsert` × 6 by email, `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)`, status ACTIVE and `passwordChangedAt` set. Idempotent with `update: {}`. Place before the notifications block (B12). |","+| FR-29 | Seed | Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` (INVITED, no `passwordHash`). |","+| FR-30 | Seed | `createInviteToken(user.id)` (which invalidates older invites on rerun) and `logger.info(authLink('invite', raw))`. Do not use `sendAuthEmail`. |","+| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `email.ts`. |","+| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip`; no rename (default per intake). |","+| FR-33 | Migration | Add a new additive migration with `@@index([role, status])` on `User` (default per intake). |","+| FR-34 | Tests | Integration files `auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`) run against the test DB. The e2e `auth.spec.ts` covers sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus a unit test for `loginErrorMessage`. |","+| NFR-1 | Security | Present in `tokens.ts`. |","+| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` fetches the CSRF token automatically. JSON POST routes are same-origin and SameSite=Lax. |","+| NFR-3 | Security | Present (`DUMMY_HASH`). |","+| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt is about 250 ms, so this is met. Nothing new to design. |","+| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every form has an `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`, and RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default) focuses the first invalid field. `applyFieldErrors` already focuses the first server-reported field. |","+| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate:** dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev blocks and does not guess. |","+| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |","+| NFR-8 | Audit | Existing metadata is `{ email, reason }`, which is safe. New code adds no audit calls. |","+| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |","+| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers already conform (B10 notes the one extra code). |","+| NFR-11 | Conventions | All forms use RHF + `zodResolver` with the shared `auth.ts` schemas. |","+| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger` (seed included). |","+| NFR-13 | Scope | No edits to `course-access.ts`/`student-access.ts` or any existing auth module. Watch B14 so e2e does not regress. |","+| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page; `/login` has no \"create account\" link. |","+| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI, English copy. Nothing to design. |"," ","-### Validation and the clash engine (core domain)","+## New files (expected) vs modified files"," ","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|-----|---------|-------|","-| FR-6 | Validation + Service | Zod handles the `^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$` format and `end > start`. These are plain string comparisons, so no Date parsing is needed. The overlap check against other periods is in the service, because it needs the DB: `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self on update. |","-| FR-9 | Clash Engine | Teacher set T = {teacherId} ∪ coTeacherIds of the new course. Other slots at (year, day, period) whose course has teacherId ∈ T or coTeacherIds overlapping T. The message needs the teacher's display name, so join User. |","-| FR-10 | Clash Engine | Only when roomId ≠ null: same year, day, period and roomId. |","-| FR-11 | Clash Engine | Only when the course's sectionId ≠ null: another slot whose course.sectionId equals it. A cross-section elective (sectionId null) is skipped by this rule but still caught by FR-12. |","-| FR-12 | Clash Engine | One grouped query: count distinct studentIds where Enrollment(ACTIVE) is in the new course and also in course X, for each X in a slot at (year, day, period). Produce one clash per conflicting course with its count N. Use raw SQL or `groupBy`, because this is the costliest rule (NFR-3). |","-| FR-13 | Clash Engine | Precondition rules: Period.kind ≠ CLASS → `Period '<name>' is not a class period.`, and SchoolDay.isTeaching false → non-teaching day. These go into the same clashes[] list. |","-| FR-14 | Clash Engine / Service | `validateSlot({ courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId?, excludeSlotId? })` returns `Clash[]`, collecting **all** clashes. It is a pure-ish function that takes a `tx`, so the transaction (NFR-1) and the availability map (FR-36) can share it. Clash shape: `{ rule: 'TEACHER'\\|'ROOM'\\|'SECTION'\\|'STUDENT'\\|'PERIOD_KIND'\\|'NON_TEACHING_DAY', message }`. |","-| FR-36 | Clash Engine (batch) | Availability for one course covers ≤7 days × ≤12 periods = 84 cells. Do **not** call validateSlot 84 times. Run each rule once as a year-wide query over all slots, then bucket by `day-periodId`. Room rule: the course has no fixed room, so availability uses the default room (the section homeroom) or skips the room rule. **Design decision needed.** Recommendation: skip the room rule in availability, because the room is checked on drop. |","-| NFR-1 | Concurrency | `$transaction(async tx => { clashes = validateSlot(tx,…); if any throw CONFLICT; insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable })`. Retry on P2034 up to 3 times. `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` is a second guard (P2002 → 409 through withHandler). |","-| NFR-11 | Tests | Unit tests for every rule. This argues for keeping message building and the rule predicates pure (input rows → Clash[]), with Prisma calls kept thin so tests can use small fixtures. Testing the timezone current/next calculation needs an injectable `now` and `tz`. |","-| NFR-12 | Tests | Integration test against a real Postgres (docker-compose). Run `Promise.all` with two conflicting POSTs and assert exactly one succeeds. |","+**New:** `(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`,","+`(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`, `(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`,","+`(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + client form, one additive migration, 4 integration tests, 1 e2e spec","+(+ e2e sign-in helper if B14 bites)."," ","-### Service functions (exports used by later PRDs)","+**Modified:** `(app)/layout.tsx` (session user → prop), `(app)/shell.tsx` (drop placeholder, menu items),","+`prisma/schema.prisma` (index), `prisma/seed.ts` (users + invite)."," ","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|-----|---------|-------|","-| FR-30 | Service | `getScheduleForDate(target: { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }, date)`: get the ISO day in the school timezone, return `[]` if the day is not teaching, else that day's slots for the target, ordered by Period.order. Note for PRD-07 (attendance) and PRD-16 (dashboards): holidays are left out (NFR-15). |","-| FR-31 | Service + Time/TZ | `getCurrentSlot(user, now)`: `hhmm = formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')`, then return the slot where `start ≤ hhmm < end`. It reuses the FR-30 query for \"today\". |","-| FR-45 | Time/TZ | Use one helper (`schoolNow(tz, now)` → `{ isoDay, hhmm }`) everywhere: server pages, the service, and the client Today view (pass tz and the server time in props, never the browser timezone). |","+**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts` and `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`."," ","-### APIs and access control","+## Open items carried from intake"," ","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|-----|---------|-------|","-| FR-33 | Admin API | Periods CRUD and reorder. GET is open to any authenticated user. |","-| FR-5 (reorder) | Admin API / Data Model | Because `order` is `@unique`, the update must happen in two phases in one transaction: set all to negative temporary values, then to 1..n. The request lists all period ids, so the service validates that the set equals the existing set. |","-| FR-8 | Admin API | DELETE counts slots on the period. If more than 0, return 409 `{ details: { slotCount } }`. |","-| FR-34 + FR-7 | Admin API | GET returns 7 rows plus `slotCount` for each day (for the current academic year), which resolves the intake blocker. PUT `{ days: [{ dayOfWeek, isTeaching }] }`: in one transaction, delete the slots of days being switched off, update the rows, and audit with the deleted count. **Design decision:** should slotCount and the delete be scoped to the current year or to all years? Recommendation: delete across all years, because a non-teaching day makes every slot invalid. Show the count across all years too, so the confirm number matches what gets deleted. |","-| FR-35 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/timetable?view&id&academicYearId`. Run one query with `include` course → subject, teacher, section, and room, then filter by view. The TEACHER rule is: own id for the teacher view; for the section view, homeroom sections (`Section.homeroomTeacherId`) or sections of courses they teach (intake default). Room view is ADMIN only. Anything else is 403. |","-| FR-37 | Admin API | POST/PATCH run NFR-1. PATCH may change day, period and roomId, and validation excludes the slot itself (FR-14). DELETE is a plain delete plus audit. academicYearId comes from Course. Reject archived courses on POST. |","-| FR-21 | Admin API (new) | The intake blocker: no endpoint lists free rooms. Recommendation: **ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId`** returns non-archived rooms that have no slot at that cell. This is one query. The alternative of putting rooms into the availability map adds weight to every drag preload. |","-| FR-38 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId`. TEACHER: courses where teacherId = me or coTeacherIds has me. STUDENT: courses with an ACTIVE enrollment. PARENT: studentId must be a linked child (`assertCanViewStudent`). It is optional when there is exactly one child. Other roles (ADMIN) get an empty result or a 400 (design decision). |","-| FR-27 | Read API reuse | The student tab needs another student's timetable. It reuses the FR-38 service by studentId, with access checked by `assertCanViewStudent` on the server page. No new route is needed. |","-| FR-28 | Read API reuse | The course Schedule tab is a server page. It reads `prisma.timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` with Period and Room after `assertCanViewCourse`. No new route is needed. |","-| NFR-7 | Access Control | `requireRole('ADMIN')` on every mutation, availability and free-rooms. `requireUser` plus a per-entity check on reads. Pages use `requirePageRole` / `requirePageUser`. |","-| NFR-8 | Conventions | Thin handlers: `withHandler` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` (FR-39 schemas) → service → `ok()`. A clash is `{ error: { code: 'CONFLICT', message: <first clash or summary>, details: { clashes } } }`. |","-| FR-39 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`: `periodSchema`, `periodReorderSchema`, `schoolDaysSchema`, `slotCreateSchema`, `slotUpdateSchema`, `timetableQuerySchema`, `availabilityQuerySchema`, `freeRoomsQuerySchema`, `meTimetableQuerySchema`. The `dayOfWeek` type is `int 1..7`. |","-| FR-40 | Audit | Confirming the intake default: audit all slot, period and school-day mutations (see B9). It is cheap, and audit() never throws. |","-","-### UI","-","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|-----|---------|-------|","-| FR-5 | UI: Bell Schedule | `/admin/timetable/periods`: PageHeader + MUI Table + an add/edit Dialog with TimeField (`@mui/x-date-pickers`, needs a LocalizationProvider with the date-fns adapter; check whether the app already provides one) + up/down reorder IconButtons + ConfirmDialog for delete. Show a 409 slotCount error through useToast. |","-| FR-7 | UI: Bell Schedule | Seven ToggleButtons (multi-select) on the same page. Switching off a day with slotCount > 0 opens a ConfirmDialog with the count before the PUT. |","-| FR-15 | UI: Editor | `/admin/timetable`: view ToggleButtonGroup, entity Autocomplete (sections, teachers via UserPicker or Autocomplete, rooms) and an academic year Select. The selection state goes in URL search params so the view survives a refresh. |","-| FR-16 | UI: Editor | A shared `TimetableGrid` component with editable and read-only modes. It is reused by FR-24, FR-27 and FR-29. Columns are teaching days. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and not droppable. The cell is a Paper with the subject colour, which comes from the existing `Subject.color String @default(\"#4F46E5\")`. Choose the text colour for contrast (`theme.palette.getContrastText`). |","-| FR-17 | UI: Editor | Section view only: a sidebar with the section's non-archived courses and a \"placed N\" Chip. On drop, POST with `roomId = section.roomId`. The teacher and room views are read-only grids with no sidebar. |","-| FR-18 | UI: Editor | Drag a slot to a cell to PATCH it. Drop outside the grid or press Delete to open a ConfirmDialog, then DELETE. |","-| FR-19 | UI: Editor + Accessibility | On drag start, fetch or reuse the cached availability map for the course. Clashing cells get a red tint, an ErrorOutline icon and a Tooltip listing the messages (NFR-4). For a slot being moved, ignore its own cell's clashes. |","-| FR-20 | UI: Editor | Optimistic placement is optional. Simplest approach: render from server state only, so there is nothing to snap back. Show a toast with `details.clashes.map(c => c.message)`. |","-| FR-21 | UI: Editor | Clicking a slot opens a Popover with an Autocomplete fed by free-rooms, then PATCH `{ roomId }`. |","-| FR-22 | UI: Editor + Accessibility | Grid cells get `tabIndex=0`. Enter on an empty cell opens a \"Place course\" Dialog (List of section courses) and the same POST as a drop. Delete on a focused slot opens the FR-18 confirm. |","-| FR-23 | UI: Editor | `@dnd-kit/core` only (DndContext, useDraggable, useDroppable). Use MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip for visuals. Do not use a sortable or calendar library. |","-| FR-24 | UI: Personal Timetable | `/timetable` server page, `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')`. Loads the FR-38 data, settings.tz and server \"now\", and renders the read-only grid with the current-period highlight. |","-| FR-25 | UI: Personal Timetable | The child selector (Select from `/api/me/children` or a server query) updates `?studentId=` in the URL. |","-| FR-26 | UI: Personal Timetable | Week/Today ToggleButtonGroup. The Today view is a List with \"Now\" and \"Next\" Chips (text, NFR-4). It is computed with the B6 helper from server-supplied tz. A client tick (every minute) only advances the server-supplied now. |","-| FR-27 | UI: Tabs/Nav | `studentTabs` adds `{ key: 'timetable', href: /students/[id]/timetable }` and a page that reuses the read-only grid. |","-| FR-28 | UI: Tabs/Nav | `courseTabs` adds `{ key: 'schedule', href: /courses/[id]/schedule }` and a page with a simple Table (day, period, times, room). |","-| FR-32 | UI: Tabs/Nav | Add 3 entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: Timetable, plus Timetable editor and Bell schedule with `group: 'Administration'`. |","-| FR-29 | Print | A Print Button calls `window.print()`. `@media print` (via MUI `GlobalStyles` or `sx`, not a CSS library) hides the nav, sidebar and controls, and sets `@page { size: A4 landscape }`. A print-only header shows the entity name and academic year. NFR-16 requires checking Safari print. |","-| NFR-4 | Accessibility | Covered by FR-19, FR-22 and FR-26. Also give each cell an `aria-label` (\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Room 101\"). |","-| NFR-5 | Conventions (UI) | Dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI/MUI X component used (Table, ToggleButton, Autocomplete, Popover, Dialog, Tooltip, Chip, Paper, TimeField, LocalizationProvider, GlobalStyles). If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a hard blocker. This is a dev-phase gate, not a design element. |","-| NFR-6 | Conventions (deps) | Only `@dnd-kit/core` (pinned exact) is added. The existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` must stay green. |","-","-### Seed","-","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|-----|---------|-------|","-| FR-41 | Seed | Upsert periods by `order` (1..8). Idempotent. |","-| FR-42 | Seed | Upsert SchoolDay 1..7 (1–5 teaching). |","-| FR-44 | Seed (fixtures) | Intake blocker, using the default. Add minimal idempotent fixtures upserted by email or code: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and a sibling (STUDENT), Pat (PARENT linked to both), sections 7A and 7B (homeroom rooms Room 101 and Room 102), courses `MATH-7A`… (subjects ELA for ENG and SOC for HIST), Robotics Club (ELECTIVE, sectionId null), and enrollments. **Check first:** PRD-03 and PRD-05 seed helpers or users may already exist in another seed file. Reuse them before adding new ones. |","-| FR-43 | Seed | A fixed, hand-written clash-free week (21 class slots per section; 30 = 5 days × 6 class periods). Robotics on Wed P6 with both sections free then. To avoid hidden clashes, the seed should insert through `validateSlot`, or a unit test should assert the seed has zero clashes. Tom teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B, so those courses must never share a cell. |","-","-### Performance, quality and scope","-","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|-----|---------|-------|","-| NFR-2 | Performance | Section week load (≤84 cells): one indexed query with includes, plus the periods and school days (cached or small). Easily under 400 ms. Avoid N+1 queries for teacher names. |","-| NFR-3 | Performance | Availability under 300 ms means the batch evaluation in FR-36 makes about 4 queries total, not one per cell. The student-overlap rule is a single SQL statement grouped by `(dayOfWeek, periodId, otherCourseId)`. |","-| NFR-9 | Conventions | Reuse http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader and the access helpers. The new service path is `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Do not create a parallel helpers folder. |","-| NFR-10 | Tests | lint, typecheck and test gate. |","-| NFR-13 | Tests | Playwright: drag works through mouse events with dnd-kit's PointerSensor (step-wise `mouse.move`). The keyboard path (FR-22) is a more reliable e2e fallback for placement. |","-| NFR-14 | Conventions | Use `logger` (for example, to log P2034 retries). |","-| NFR-15 | Scope | No solver, no A/B weeks, no substitutes, no holidays. `getScheduleForDate` is the single place PRD-14 will hook holidays later. |","-| NFR-16 | Scope | English only and a single school. Print must be tested across the 4 browsers. |","-","-## Open design decisions handed to `arch-design-system`","-","-1. **Free rooms (FR-21):** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` (recommended), or fold rooms into the availability response.","-2. **Availability room rule (FR-36):** skip it (recommended; it is checked on drop), or evaluate against the section homeroom.","-3. **School-day slotCount and cascade scope (FR-7/FR-34):** all years (recommended) or the current year only.","-4. **Archived entities:** exclude archived courses and rooms from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks (intake default, agreed).","-5. ~~Subject colour (FR-16)~~ Resolved: `Subject.color` already exists in the schema.","-6. **ADMIN on `/api/me/timetable` (FR-38):** return an empty list (recommended) or a 400.","-7. **Serialization retry helper (NFR-1):** a new small `withSerializableRetry` with no existing precedent (B7). Keep it in timetable-service.","-","-## Intake blockers and how this analysis covers them","-","-| Blocker | Covered by |","-|---------|-----------|","-| FR-44 seed fixtures | Seed rows above. Reuse any existing PRD-03/05 fixtures first. |","-| FR-43 ENG/HIST subjects | Reuse ELA/SOC with PRD course codes. |","-| FR-21 free rooms | Decision 1. |","-| FR-7 slot count | GET /api/school-days `slotCount` (FR-34 row), decision 3. |","-| FR-4/NFR-6 migration + dnd-kit | B1, B2, B12. |","-| NFR-5 mui-mcp | Dev-phase hard gate (NFR-5 row). The mui-mcp server is configured in this environment. |","+1. FR-32: keep `ip`.","+2. FR-33: add the index.","+3. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`.","+4. Ticket id is SH-1.","+5. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a dev-phase hard gate."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-6\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`, which covers PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable\n(45 FR and 16 NFR, 61 requirements) at 96% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (`api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`,\n> `system-design.md`, `tech-stack-decisions.md`, `threat-model-notes.json`) are **stale SH-4 outputs**.\n> The other sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-6 input, except for\n> `tech-stack-decisions.md` once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-6.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Validation**, **Clash Engine**, **Service**,\n**Admin API**, **Read API**, **Access Control**, **UI: Bell Schedule**, **UI: Editor**,\n**UI: Personal Timetable**, **UI: Tabs/Nav**, **Print**, **Time/TZ**, **Audit**, **Seed**,\n**Concurrency**, **Performance**, **Accessibility**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these confirm or add to intake)\n\n| # | Fact | Design implication |\n|---|------|--------------------|\n| B1 | `prisma/schema.prisma` has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind. The latest migration is `20261104120000_notifications_email`. | The new migration needs a later timestamp (for example `20261105000000_timetable`). |\n| B2 | `Room` already has a back-relation `sections Section[]`. `Course` has `enrollments` but no slots relation. | Add `Room.timetableSlots`, `Course.timetableSlots` and `Period.slots`. All are additive. |\n| B3 | `Course.coTeacherIds String[]`, nullable `sectionId`, `archivedAt`, `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. `Enrollment @@index([studentId, status])`, `onDelete: Cascade` from Course. | The teacher clash check needs `teacherId IN set OR coTeacherIds hasSome set`. The student-overlap check joins Enrollment on both courses. |\n| B4 | `Section.roomId?` (homeroom room) and `Section.homeroomTeacherId?`. `@@unique([academicYearId, name])`. | FR-17 uses `Section.roomId` as the default room. FR-35 checks TEACHER access through `homeroomTeacherId`. |\n| B5 | `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` with `@@index([studentId])`. `/api/me/children` already exists. | FR-25 and FR-38 can reuse `/api/me/children` for the child selector, so no new endpoint is needed. Parent access goes through `assertCanViewStudent`. |\n| B6 | `SchoolSettings.timezone` (default `'UTC'`) is read by the cached `getSchoolSettings()` in `src/server/services/settings.ts`. `src/lib/dates.ts` has `formatInSchoolTz` (date-fns-tz `formatInTimeZone`). | All \"now\" maths (FR-31, FR-45) uses `formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')` and ISO day `'i'`. Plain `HH:MM` string comparison then works. |\n| B7 | SERIALIZABLE precedent: `academicYears.ts` and `terms.ts` use `prisma.$transaction(fn, { isolationLevel: Serializable })` but **do not retry**. There is no P2034 handling in `src/`. | NFR-1 needs a small retry wrapper for P2034 (serialization failure). It is new code, so keep it local to timetable-service unless the design wants to reuse it. |\n| B8 | `http.ts` has `ApiErrorCode` with CONFLICT=409 and FORBIDDEN=403, plus `AppError`, `withHandler` (maps P2002 → CONFLICT, P2025 → NOT_FOUND), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. | Clashes are thrown as `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })`. The handler shape is already standard. |\n| B9 | `audit({ actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request })` never throws. By convention `action` is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|delete`. | FR-40 actions: `timetableSlot.create\\|update\\|delete`, `period.create\\|update\\|delete\\|reorder`, `schoolDay.update` (metadata includes `deletedSlotCount`). |\n| B10 | Validators live in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts` (courses, sections, ...). Feature services live in `src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts`. Tabs live in `src/config/course-tabs.ts` and `student-tabs.ts` (`{ key, label, href, roles }`). | FR-39: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`. FR-27 and FR-28 each register one entry. |\n| B11 | API route dirs exist: `rooms`, `sections`, `courses`, `me/*`, `admin/*`. There are no `periods`, `school-days` or `timetable` routes. App admin pages: `admin/courses`, `admin/sections`, `admin/email-log`. | Everything here is new. Nothing gets renamed. |\n| B12 | `package.json` pins `@mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0`, `date-fns 3.6.0`, `date-fns-tz 3.2.0` and `@prisma/client 5.20.0`. `@dnd-kit/*` is absent. | FR-23 and NFR-6 add exactly one pinned dependency, `@dnd-kit/core`. Reorder (FR-5) uses up/down buttons, so `@dnd-kit/sortable` is not needed. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n### Data model and migration\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `enum PeriodKind` and `model Period`. Store `startTime`/`endTime` as `String` `HH:MM`. `order Int @unique` affects reorder (see FR-5). |\n| FR-2 | Data Model | `SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id, isTeaching Boolean }` is a 7-row lookup with no relations. Do not add a FK from TimetableSlot to it (the PRD defines `dayOfWeek Int`). |\n| FR-3 | Data Model | Index `@@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` covers every clash query (all are scoped to year + day + period). `academicYearId` is denormalised from Course. It is set server-side only (FR-37). `periodId` has no cascade, so deletion is guarded by FR-8 in the service. `roomId?` with `onDelete: SetNull` is the safe default, and rooms are archived rather than deleted. |\n| FR-4 | Migration | One additive migration plus the B2 back-relations. `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then review the SQL. It should only contain CREATE TYPE, CREATE TABLE and CREATE INDEX statements. |\n\n### Validation and the clash engine (core domain)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-6 | Validation + Service | Zod handles the `^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$` format and `end > start`. These are plain string comparisons, so no Date parsing is needed. The overlap check against other periods is in the service, because it needs the DB: `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self on update. |\n| FR-9 | Clash Engine | Teacher set T = {teacherId} ∪ coTeacherIds of the new course. Other slots at (year, day, period) whose course has teacherId ∈ T or coTeacherIds overlapping T. The message needs the teacher's display name, so join User. |\n| FR-10 | Clash Engine | Only when roomId ≠ null: same year, day, period and roomId. |\n| FR-11 | Clash Engine | Only when the course's sectionId ≠ null: another slot whose course.sectionId equals it. A cross-section elective (sectionId null) is skipped by this rule but still caught by FR-12. |\n| FR-12 | Clash Engine | One grouped query: count distinct studentIds where Enrollment(ACTIVE) is in the new course and also in course X, for each X in a slot at (year, day, period). Produce one clash per conflicting course with its count N. Use raw SQL or `groupBy`, because this is the costliest rule (NFR-3). |\n| FR-13 | Clash Engine | Precondition rules: Period.kind ≠ CLASS → `Period '<name>' is not a class period.`, and SchoolDay.isTeaching false → non-teaching day. These go into the same clashes[] list. |\n| FR-14 | Clash Engine / Service | `validateSlot({ courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId?, excludeSlotId? })` returns `Clash[]`, collecting **all** clashes. It is a pure-ish function that takes a `tx`, so the transaction (NFR-1) and the availability map (FR-36) can share it. Clash shape: `{ rule: 'TEACHER'\\|'ROOM'\\|'SECTION'\\|'STUDENT'\\|'PERIOD_KIND'\\|'NON_TEACHING_DAY', message }`. |\n| FR-36 | Clash Engine (batch) | Availability for one course covers ≤7 days × ≤12 periods = 84 cells. Do **not** call validateSlot 84 times. Run each rule once as a year-wide query over all slots, then bucket by `day-periodId`. Room rule: the course has no fixed room, so availability uses the default room (the section homeroom) or skips the room rule. **Design decision needed.** Recommendation: skip the room rule in availability, because the room is checked on drop. |\n| NFR-1 | Concurrency | `$transaction(async tx => { clashes = validateSlot(tx,…); if any throw CONFLICT; insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable })`. Retry on P2034 up to 3 times. `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` is a second guard (P2002 → 409 through withHandler). |\n| NFR-11 | Tests | Unit tests for every rule. This argues for keeping message building and the rule predicates pure (input rows → Clash[]), with Prisma calls kept thin so tests can use small fixtures. Testing the timezone current/next calculation needs an injectable `now` and `tz`. |\n| NFR-12 | Tests | Integration test against a real Postgres (docker-compose). Run `Promise.all` with two conflicting POSTs and assert exactly one succeeds. |\n\n### Service functions (exports used by later PRDs)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-30 | Service | `getScheduleForDate(target: { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }, date)`: get the ISO day in the school timezone, return `[]` if the day is not teaching, else that day's slots for the target, ordered by Period.order. Note for PRD-07 (attendance) and PRD-16 (dashboards): holidays are left out (NFR-15). |\n| FR-31 | Service + Time/TZ | `getCurrentSlot(user, now)`: `hhmm = formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')`, then return the slot where `start ≤ hhmm < end`. It reuses the FR-30 query for \"today\". |\n| FR-45 | Time/TZ | Use one helper (`schoolNow(tz, now)` → `{ isoDay, hhmm }`) everywhere: server pages, the service, and the client Today view (pass tz and the server time in props, never the browser timezone). |\n\n### APIs and access control\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-33 | Admin API | Periods CRUD and reorder. GET is open to any authenticated user. |\n| FR-5 (reorder) | Admin API / Data Model | Because `order` is `@unique`, the update must happen in two phases in one transaction: set all to negative temporary values, then to 1..n. The request lists all period ids, so the service validates that the set equals the existing set. |\n| FR-8 | Admin API | DELETE counts slots on the period. If more than 0, return 409 `{ details: { slotCount } }`. |\n| FR-34 + FR-7 | Admin API | GET returns 7 rows plus `slotCount` for each day (for the current academic year), which resolves the intake blocker. PUT `{ days: [{ dayOfWeek, isTeaching }] }`: in one transaction, delete the slots of days being switched off, update the rows, and audit with the deleted count. **Design decision:** should slotCount and the delete be scoped to the current year or to all years? Recommendation: delete across all years, because a non-teaching day makes every slot invalid. Show the count across all years too, so the confirm number matches what gets deleted. |\n| FR-35 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/timetable?view&id&academicYearId`. Run one query with `include` course → subject, teacher, section, and room, then filter by view. The TEACHER rule is: own id for the teacher view; for the section view, homeroom sections (`Section.homeroomTeacherId`) or sections of courses they teach (intake default). Room view is ADMIN only. Anything else is 403. |\n| FR-37 | Admin API | POST/PATCH run NFR-1. PATCH may change day, period and roomId, and validation excludes the slot itself (FR-14). DELETE is a plain delete plus audit. academicYearId comes from Course. Reject archived courses on POST. |\n| FR-21 | Admin API (new) | The intake blocker: no endpoint lists free rooms. Recommendation: **ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId`** returns non-archived rooms that have no slot at that cell. This is one query. The alternative of putting rooms into the availability map adds weight to every drag preload. |\n| FR-38 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId`. TEACHER: courses where teacherId = me or coTeacherIds has me. STUDENT: courses with an ACTIVE enrollment. PARENT: studentId must be a linked child (`assertCanViewStudent`). It is optional when there is exactly one child. Other roles (ADMIN) get an empty result or a 400 (design decision). |\n| FR-27 | Read API reuse | The student tab needs another student's timetable. It reuses the FR-38 service by studentId, with access checked by `assertCanViewStudent` on the server page. No new route is needed. |\n| FR-28 | Read API reuse | The course Schedule tab is a server page. It reads `prisma.timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` with Period and Room after `assertCanViewCourse`. No new route is needed. |\n| NFR-7 | Access Control | `requireRole('ADMIN')` on every mutation, availability and free-rooms. `requireUser` plus a per-entity check on reads. Pages use `requirePageRole` / `requirePageUser`. |\n| NFR-8 | Conventions | Thin handlers: `withHandler` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` (FR-39 schemas) → service → `ok()`. A clash is `{ error: { code: 'CONFLICT', message: <first clash or summary>, details: { clashes } } }`. |\n| FR-39 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`: `periodSchema`, `periodReorderSchema`, `schoolDaysSchema`, `slotCreateSchema`, `slotUpdateSchema`, `timetableQuerySchema`, `availabilityQuerySchema`, `freeRoomsQuerySchema`, `meTimetableQuerySchema`. The `dayOfWeek` type is `int 1..7`. |\n| FR-40 | Audit | Confirming the intake default: audit all slot, period and school-day mutations (see B9). It is cheap, and audit() never throws. |\n\n### UI\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-5 | UI: Bell Schedule | `/admin/timetable/periods`: PageHeader + MUI Table + an add/edit Dialog with TimeField (`@mui/x-date-pickers`, needs a LocalizationProvider with the date-fns adapter; check whether the app already provides one) + up/down reorder IconButtons + ConfirmDialog for delete. Show a 409 slotCount error through useToast. |\n| FR-7 | UI: Bell Schedule | Seven ToggleButtons (multi-select) on the same page. Switching off a day with slotCount > 0 opens a ConfirmDialog with the count before the PUT. |\n| FR-15 | UI: Editor | `/admin/timetable`: view ToggleButtonGroup, entity Autocomplete (sections, teachers via UserPicker or Autocomplete, rooms) and an academic year Select. The selection state goes in URL search params so the view survives a refresh. |\n| FR-16 | UI: Editor | A shared `TimetableGrid` component with editable and read-only modes. It is reused by FR-24, FR-27 and FR-29. Columns are teaching days. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and not droppable. The cell is a Paper with the subject colour, which comes from the existing `Subject.color String @default(\"#4F46E5\")`. Choose the text colour for contrast (`theme.palette.getContrastText`). |\n| FR-17 | UI: Editor | Section view only: a sidebar with the section's non-archived courses and a \"placed N\" Chip. On drop, POST with `roomId = section.roomId`. The teacher and room views are read-only grids with no sidebar. |\n| FR-18 | UI: Editor | Drag a slot to a cell to PATCH it. Drop outside the grid or press Delete to open a ConfirmDialog, then DELETE. |\n| FR-19 | UI: Editor + Accessibility | On drag start, fetch or reuse the cached availability map for the course. Clashing cells get a red tint, an ErrorOutline icon and a Tooltip listing the messages (NFR-4). For a slot being moved, ignore its own cell's clashes. |\n| FR-20 | UI: Editor | Optimistic placement is optional. Simplest approach: render from server state only, so there is nothing to snap back. Show a toast with `details.clashes.map(c => c.message)`. |\n| FR-21 | UI: Editor | Clicking a slot opens a Popover with an Autocomplete fed by free-rooms, then PATCH `{ roomId }`. |\n| FR-22 | UI: Editor + Accessibility | Grid cells get `tabIndex=0`. Enter on an empty cell opens a \"Place course\" Dialog (List of section courses) and the same POST as a drop. Delete on a focused slot opens the FR-18 confirm. |\n| FR-23 | UI: Editor | `@dnd-kit/core` only (DndContext, useDraggable, useDroppable). Use MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip for visuals. Do not use a sortable or calendar library. |\n| FR-24 | UI: Personal Timetable | `/timetable` server page, `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')`. Loads the FR-38 data, settings.tz and server \"now\", and renders the read-only grid with the current-period highlight. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Personal Timetable | The child selector (Select from `/api/me/children` or a server query) updates `?studentId=` in the URL. |\n| FR-26 | UI: Personal Timetable | Week/Today ToggleButtonGroup. The Today view is a List with \"Now\" and \"Next\" Chips (text, NFR-4). It is computed with the B6 helper from server-supplied tz. A client tick (every minute) only advances the server-supplied now. |\n| FR-27 | UI: Tabs/Nav | `studentTabs` adds `{ key: 'timetable', href: /students/[id]/timetable }` and a page that reuses the read-only grid. |\n| FR-28 | UI: Tabs/Nav | `courseTabs` adds `{ key: 'schedule', href: /courses/[id]/schedule }` and a page with a simple Table (day, period, times, room). |\n| FR-32 | UI: Tabs/Nav | Add 3 entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: Timetable, plus Timetable editor and Bell schedule with `group: 'Administration'`. |\n| FR-29 | Print | A Print Button calls `window.print()`. `@media print` (via MUI `GlobalStyles` or `sx`, not a CSS library) hides the nav, sidebar and controls, and sets `@page { size: A4 landscape }`. A print-only header shows the entity name and academic year. NFR-16 requires checking Safari print. |\n| NFR-4 | Accessibility | Covered by FR-19, FR-22 and FR-26. Also give each cell an `aria-label` (\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Room 101\"). |\n| NFR-5 | Conventions (UI) | Dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI/MUI X component used (Table, ToggleButton, Autocomplete, Popover, Dialog, Tooltip, Chip, Paper, TimeField, LocalizationProvider, GlobalStyles). If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a hard blocker. This is a dev-phase gate, not a design element. |\n| NFR-6 | Conventions (deps) | Only `@dnd-kit/core` (pinned exact) is added. The existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` must stay green. |\n\n### Seed\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-41 | Seed | Upsert periods by `order` (1..8). Idempotent. |\n| FR-42 | Seed | Upsert SchoolDay 1..7 (1–5 teaching). |\n| FR-44 | Seed (fixtures) | Intake blocker, using the default. Add minimal idempotent fixtures upserted by email or code: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and a sibling (STUDENT), Pat (PARENT linked to both), sections 7A and 7B (homeroom rooms Room 101 and Room 102), courses `MATH-7A`… (subjects ELA for ENG and SOC for HIST), Robotics Club (ELECTIVE, sectionId null), and enrollments. **Check first:** PRD-03 and PRD-05 seed helpers or users may already exist in another seed file. Reuse them before adding new ones. |\n| FR-43 | Seed | A fixed, hand-written clash-free week (21 class slots per section; 30 = 5 days × 6 class periods). Robotics on Wed P6 with both sections free then. To avoid hidden clashes, the seed should insert through `validateSlot`, or a unit test should assert the seed has zero clashes. Tom teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B, so those courses must never share a cell. |\n\n### Performance, quality and scope\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| NFR-2 | Performance | Section week load (≤84 cells): one indexed query with includes, plus the periods and school days (cached or small). Easily under 400 ms. Avoid N+1 queries for teacher names. |\n| NFR-3 | Performance | Availability under 300 ms means the batch evaluation in FR-36 makes about 4 queries total, not one per cell. The student-overlap rule is a single SQL statement grouped by `(dayOfWeek, periodId, otherCourseId)`. |\n| NFR-9 | Conventions | Reuse http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader and the access helpers. The new service path is `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Do not create a parallel helpers folder. |\n| NFR-10 | Tests | lint, typecheck and test gate. |\n| NFR-13 | Tests | Playwright: drag works through mouse events with dnd-kit's PointerSensor (step-wise `mouse.move`). The keyboard path (FR-22) is a more reliable e2e fallback for placement. |\n| NFR-14 | Conventions | Use `logger` (for example, to log P2034 retries). |\n| NFR-15 | Scope | No solver, no A/B weeks, no substitutes, no holidays. `getScheduleForDate` is the single place PRD-14 will hook holidays later. |\n| NFR-16 | Scope | English only and a single school. Print must be tested across the 4 browsers. |\n\n## Open design decisions handed to `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **Free rooms (FR-21):** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` (recommended), or fold rooms into the availability response.\n2. **Availability room rule (FR-36):** skip it (recommended; it is checked on drop), or evaluate against the section homeroom.\n3. **School-day slotCount and cascade scope (FR-7/FR-34):** all years (recommended) or the current year only.\n4. **Archived entities:** exclude archived courses and rooms from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks (intake default, agreed).\n5. ~~Subject colour (FR-16)~~ Resolved: `Subject.color` already exists in the schema.\n6. **ADMIN on `/api/me/timetable` (FR-38):** return an empty list (recommended) or a 400.\n7. **Serialization retry helper (NFR-1):** a new small `withSerializableRetry` with no existing precedent (B7). Keep it in timetable-service.\n\n## Intake blockers and how this analysis covers them\n\n| Blocker | Covered by |\n|---------|-----------|\n| FR-44 seed fixtures | Seed rows above. Reuse any existing PRD-03/05 fixtures first. |\n| FR-43 ENG/HIST subjects | Reuse ELA/SOC with PRD course codes. |\n| FR-21 free rooms | Decision 1. |\n| FR-7 slot count | GET /api/school-days `slotCount` (FR-34 row), decision 3. |\n| FR-4/NFR-6 migration + dnd-kit | B1, B2, B12. |\n| NFR-5 mui-mcp | Dev-phase hard gate (NFR-5 row). The mui-mcp server is configured in this environment. |\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01B9p88ynzm9UBNpJc1z1ZX9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
