{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjKcFzUox851HAXWmaNQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've finished `arch-research-reqs` for SH-1 and written `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`. The old copy of that file was left over from SH-6, so I replaced it. All 49 requirements are mapped to an architectural concern, and every ID cited exists in `requirements.json`.\n\nWhat I found when checking the code against intake:\n- **Only the UI, seed and tests are missing.** No new API endpoint or service is needed; the 5 existing routes cover everything.\n- **Some of the UI already exists and isn't used yet.** The password checklist and password-setting form components are already written, so the invite, reset and change-password pages should reuse them.\n- **Two pieces are already handled server-side:**\n  - The change-password endpoint already refreshes the current session after a change, so that page only needs to submit and show a toast.\n  - Sign-in already returns error codes the `/login` page can turn into the PRD messages.\n- **Sign-in after accepting an invite has to happen in the browser.** Accepting an invite doesn't sign the user in, so the page signs them in itself afterwards.\n- **The shell's user should come from the server layout.** The app has no client-side session provider, so the layout should pass the signed-in user into the shell as a prop. That removes `PLACEHOLDER_USER`.\n- **Seed order matters.** The new users must be created before the existing notifications block, which silently skips users it can't find.\n- **One error code isn't in the PRD's list.** Invalid invite and reset links return `INVALID_TOKEN`; the pages must handle it and the API contracts should document it.\n\nThe main risk is that the existing end-to-end tests (`dashboard`, `notifications`) will probably start being redirected to `/login` once a real session is required. They will likely need a shared sign-in step using the seed users.\n\nThe open items from intake keep their defaults: keep the `ip` column name, add the user role/status index, and have the seed log the invite link. The MUI docs server must be reachable before any UI is written, or the dev phase is blocked.\n\nI didn't touch any other sub-task's files. `arch-design-system` can start once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten the stack decisions for SH-1."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5938,"cache_read_input_tokens":51391,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5938},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"608f2610-ae4e-4b2e-af6e-d46d1dae17cd","uuid":"e28c4688-9718-4ac6-a142-0c38d386433f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:38:58.547Z","request_id":"req_011CgjKcFh7h2Q7u2CBKqiNa"}
