{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AeHtdP7j1528Dz3o5WXRc5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-1\n2\t\n3\tSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\n4\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` for PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001).\n5\tIt has 34 FRs and 15 NFRs (49 requirements) at 97% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\n6\tRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n7\t\n8\t> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are **stale outputs from an earlier ticket**, and the other\n9\t> sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-1 input, with one exception: `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n10\t> once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-1.\n11\t\n12\t**Headline:** this is a **UI + seed + tests** ticket. Every backend module and API route already exists.\n13\tThe design must add pages and wire them to existing code, not add services or endpoints.\n14\t**No new API endpoint is needed.** `arch-api-contracts` should document the 5 existing routes as-is.\n15\t\n16\tConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Auth Core**, **Service**, **API (existing)**,\n17\t**UI: Auth Pages**, **UI: Account**, **UI: Shell**, **Access Control**, **Security**, **Audit**,\n18\t**Seed**, **Accessibility**, **UI Rules**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n19\t\n20\t## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these confirm or add to intake)\n21\t\n22\t| # | Fact | Design implication |\n23\t|---|------|--------------------|\n24\t| B1 | `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` already renders the centred `Card` shell (SchoolHub logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"`). | Auth pages render **only the card body**, with no Card or Container of their own. |\n25\t| B2 | `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure`. Nothing imports them yet. | FR-16 checklist and the invite/reset forms **reuse `SetPasswordForm`**. `/account/security` and `/login` reuse `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`. Do not write a second checklist or fetch helper. |\n26\t| B3 | `credentials.ts` throws `AuthError(code)` (a `CredentialsSignin` subclass). Codes: `invalid`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `locked:<N>`. | `/login` calls `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react` and maps `result.code` to the FR-4 and FR-6 copy. That mapping is a pure function and should get one unit test. |\n27\t| B4 | `auth.ts` exports `signIn`, `signOut` and `unstable_update`. The `jwt` callback handles `trigger==='update' && session.reauth`. `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({reauth:true})`. | FR-20 \"re-issue current session\" is **already done server-side**. The page only POSTs and shows a toast. |\n28\t| B5 | `app/providers.tsx` has **no `SessionProvider`**. | Client `signIn`/`signOut` from `next-auth/react` work without it. The shell gets the user as a **prop from the server layout**, so no provider and no `useSession` are needed. |\n29\t| B6 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders the client `AppShell({ schoolShortName })`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user` (`id`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `role`) to `AppShell`. This removes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (FR-25/26/27) and gives one source of the current user. |\n30\t| B7 | `shell.tsx` already imports `LogoutIcon`, `PersonOutlineIcon`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `Chip` and `UserAvatar`. | FR-21/FR-26 only change menu items. Add the `Account security` link and an `onClick={() => signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })}` handler. |\n31\t| B8 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** sign the user in. Its error copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | FR-14: after a successful POST, the client calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` and then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. The FR-13 copy is rendered by the **page** when the server-side `verifyToken()` fails, and is reused when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. |\n32\t| B9 | `tokens.ts` exports `verifyToken(raw, type)`, which is read-only and does not consume the token. | `/invite/[token]/page.tsx` is a server component that calls `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')` to show the name and email (FR-13). `/reset-password/[token]` can do the same up front. Neither needs a new endpoint. |\n33\t| B10 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN', …)` is a code **outside** the NFR-10 code list. | This is existing behaviour; keep it (NFR-13). The UI must handle the `INVALID_TOKEN` code. Flag it for `arch-api-contracts` to document. |\n34\t| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | FR-11 and NFR-14 are satisfied. Middleware needs no change. |\n35\t| B12 | `prisma/seed.ts` already looks up `student@` and `parent@` to attach PRD-04 notifications, and **skips them if missing**. It uses `console.log`. | FR-28 user upserts must run **before** the notifications block. New seed code uses `logger` (NFR-12). The existing `console.log` lines are out of scope (NFR-13). |\n36\t| B13 | Existing tests: unit `tokens`, `lockout`, `rate-limit`, `password-policy`, `auth-validators`. Integration has no auth tests. E2E has no auth specs. | FR-34 adds 4 integration files and 1–2 Playwright specs. Unit tests are already done. |\n37\t| B14 | The existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) hit `(app)` pages. Once a real session is required, they redirect to `/login`. | **Regression risk (NFR-13):** the e2e suite needs a shared sign-in helper or `storageState` using the seed users. Check whether these specs currently pass without auth. |\n38\t| B15 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. | `/forgot-password` displays the API's `data.message`, or imports this constant, rather than retyping the string. |\n39\t\n40\t## Requirement → architectural concern\n41\t\n42\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n43\t|-----|---------|-------|\n44\t| FR-1 | Data Model | Already present; no change. |\n45\t| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, a thin server wrapper that reads `callbackUrl` plus a client `LoginForm`. It uses RHF + `signInSchema`, `TextField`, a show-password `InputAdornment`/`IconButton` (reuse `passwordInputSlot`) and an `Alert`. It links to `/forgot-password`. |\n46\t| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`; verify only. |\n47\t| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Pure `loginErrorMessage(code)` maps `invalid`, `disabled` and `locked:N` to the PRD copy. The locked message reads \"Try again in N minutes.\" |\n48\t| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`); covered by the integration test. |\n49\t| FR-6 | UI: Auth Pages | Limiter present. Map `rate_limited` to \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |\n50\t| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` after `signIn` succeeds. Reuse the validator. |\n51\t| FR-8 | Audit | Already emitted by `authorizeCredentials`; integration test asserts the rows. |\n52\t| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present; no change. |\n53\t| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`). The `reauth` path keeps the changing session alive. |\n54\t| FR-11 | Access Control | Present in `middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` (B11). |\n55\t| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. UI pages call `verifyToken` server-side (B9) and never hash anything themselves. |\n56\t| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name and email. Invalid: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. Uses `verifyToken`, not consume. |\n57\t| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client POSTs `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials')`, then `/dashboard` (B8). Service and audit already present. |\n58\t| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is server-only and surfaces through `fieldErrors.password`. |\n59\t| FR-16 | UI: Auth Pages / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` on invite, reset and change forms (B2). |\n60\t| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`. RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password')`. Always shows the success `Alert` and handles `RATE_LIMITED`. API, limiter and service are present. |\n61\t| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` + `sendAuthEmail`); integration test only. |\n62\t| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`. Uses `SetPasswordForm`, then `/login?reset=1`, where `LoginForm` fires `useToast` once on mount. The query param is the lazy channel; there is no shared state. |\n63\t| FR-20 | UI: Account | New `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form (current/new/confirm, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`). On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show the field error. On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form. Session re-issue is already server-side (B4). |\n64\t| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` \"Account security\" item to the user menu. |\n65\t| FR-22 | Service | Present; verify only. |\n66\t| FR-23 | Access Control | Present; `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole` are used by the new pages. |\n67\t| FR-24 | Audit | Present. |\n68\t| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`; `AppShell` takes a `user` prop (B6). |\n69\t| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name = `firstName lastName`, role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |\n70\t| FR-27 | UI: Shell | `navigationForRole(user.role)`. |\n71\t| FR-28 | Seed | `prisma.user.upsert` × 6 by email, `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)`, status ACTIVE and `passwordChangedAt` set. Idempotent with `update: {}`. Place before the notifications block (B12). |\n72\t| FR-29 | Seed | Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` (INVITED, no `passwordHash`). |\n73\t| FR-30 | Seed | `createInviteToken(user.id)` (which invalidates older invites on rerun) and `logger.info(authLink('invite', raw))`. Do not use `sendAuthEmail`. |\n74\t| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `email.ts`. |\n75\t| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip`; no rename (default per intake). |\n76\t| FR-33 | Migration | Add a new additive migration with `@@index([role, status])` on `User` (default per intake). |\n77\t| FR-34 | Tests | Integration files `auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`) run against the test DB. The e2e `auth.spec.ts` covers sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus a unit test for `loginErrorMessage`. |\n78\t| NFR-1 | Security | Present in `tokens.ts`. |\n79\t| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` fetches the CSRF token automatically. JSON POST routes are same-origin and SameSite=Lax. |\n80\t| NFR-3 | Security | Present (`DUMMY_HASH`). |\n81\t| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt is about 250 ms, so this is met. Nothing new to design. |\n82\t| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every form has an `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`, and RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default) focuses the first invalid field. `applyFieldErrors` already focuses the first server-reported field. |\n83\t| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate:** dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev blocks and does not guess. |\n84\t| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |\n85\t| NFR-8 | Audit | Existing metadata is `{ email, reason }`, which is safe. New code adds no audit calls. |\n86\t| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |\n87\t| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers already conform (B10 notes the one extra code). |\n88\t| NFR-11 | Conventions | All forms use RHF + `zodResolver` with the shared `auth.ts` schemas. |\n89\t| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger` (seed included). |\n90\t| NFR-13 | Scope | No edits to `course-access.ts`/`student-access.ts` or any existing auth module. Watch B14 so e2e does not regress. |\n91\t| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page; `/login` has no \"create account\" link. |\n92\t| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI, English copy. Nothing to design. |\n93\t\n94\t## New files (expected) vs modified files\n95\t\n96\t**New:** `(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`,\n97\t`(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`, `(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`,\n98\t`(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + client form, one additive migration, 4 integration tests, 1 e2e spec\n99\t(+ e2e sign-in helper if B14 bites).\n100\t\n101\t**Modified:** `(app)/layout.tsx` (session user → prop), `(app)/shell.tsx` (drop placeholder, menu items),\n102\t`prisma/schema.prisma` (index), `prisma/seed.ts` (users + invite).\n103\t\n104\t**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts` and `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`.\n105\t\n106\t## Open items carried from intake\n107\t\n108\t1. FR-32: keep `ip`.\n109\t2. FR-33: add the index.\n110\t3. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`.\n111\t4. Ticket id is SH-1.\n112\t5. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a dev-phase hard gate.\n113\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f674949-015a-48f5-8729-2f49c8704d06","uuid":"155f847d-ad62-48f6-ba68-929b6ab357d8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:27:14.550Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-1\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` for PRD-01 Authenticati