{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RatAiB7zJy2J1VoLjGqpjG","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f674949-015a-48f5-8729-2f49c8704d06","uuid":"0eb45715-1e0d-4ed2-bbba-96120765f5c3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:28:15.243Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-1\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z) for PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001).\nIt has 34 FRs and 15 NFRs (49 requirements) at 97% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 5 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces an earlier SH-1 notes file. That version listed `/login`, the seed users and the role/status\n> migration as new work. All three are now **present** on disk.\n\n**Headline:** this is a **UI-gap + tests** ticket. The backend, every API route, `/login`, the seed and the\nmigration already exist. The design adds **4 pages**, rewires the **shell**, and adds **tests**.\n**No new endpoint, service, model or migration is needed.** `arch-api-contracts` documents the 5 existing routes as they are.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Auth Core**, **Service**, **API (existing)**, **UI: Auth Pages**,\n**UI: Account**, **UI: Shell**, **Access Control**, **Security**, **Audit**, **Seed**, **Accessibility**,\n**UI Rules**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Design implication |\n|---|------|--------------------|\n| B1 | `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` already renders the centred Card shell. | New auth pages render only the card body. |\n| B2 | `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure`. Today only `LoginForm` imports any of them. | Invite and reset pages **reuse `SetPasswordForm`**. `/account/security` reuses `PasswordChecklist`, `passwordInputSlot`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors`. Do not add a second fetch or checklist helper. |\n| B3 | `SetPasswordForm` **requires `email`**, because the policy rejects a password equal to the email. | `/reset-password/[token]` must also call `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` server-side, to get the email and to show the invalid-link state before the form renders. |\n| B4 | `tokens.ts` `verifyToken(raw, type)` is read-only. `consumeToken` throws `INVALID_TOKEN` on a double submit. | The token pages are **server components** that call `verifyToken`. They show user data or the invalid-link `Alert`. No new endpoint. |\n| B5 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` maps to **410**, a code outside the NFR-10 list. The service copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | Keep this (NFR-13). The UI handles 410 `INVALID_TOKEN` by switching to the page's invalid-link copy. `arch-api-contracts` should document the 410. |\n| B6 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** create a session. | FR-14 flow on the client: POST `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. |\n| B7 | `/login` already exists. `LoginForm({ callbackUrl, reset })` fires a `useToast` once when `reset` is set, and exports `loginErrorMessage` (unit-tested). | FR-19 redirects to `/login?reset=1`. **Do not touch `/login`.** FR-2, FR-4, FR-6 and FR-7 only need verification. Intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date: `loginErrorMessage` covers `rate_limited`. Dev should verify this. |\n| B8 | `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`. The `jwt` callback keeps the current session alive on `reauth`. | FR-20 \"re-issue the current session\" is done server-side. The page only POSTs, then shows a toast and resets the form. |\n| B9 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders `<AppShell schoolShortName>` and does no auth. `providers.tsx` has no `SessionProvider`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user: SessionUser` (`id`, `role`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `email`) to `AppShell`. **Prop, not `useSession`**, so no provider is needed. This is the one source of the current user (FR-25). |\n| B10 | `shell.tsx` uses `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167). Its menu has 2 `MenuItem`s that only close the menu, and there is no `signOut`. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26 and FR-27 are all in this one file plus the layout. Sign out is `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`. |\n| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | Middleware needs no change (FR-11, NFR-14). |\n| B12 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. `requestPasswordReset` throws `RATE_LIMITED`. | `/forgot-password` shows `data.message` from the API rather than retyping the string, and shows an error `Alert` on 429. |\n| B13 | `src/app/forbidden/page.tsx` exists. | `requirePageRole` → `/forbidden` is already wired (FR-23). |\n| B14 | Existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) call `page.goto('/dashboard')` with no sign-in. The middleware already requires a session. | **Regression risk (NFR-13).** These specs are probably already failing, or will once the layout calls `requirePageUser`. Add one shared e2e sign-in helper using the seed users and reuse it in the existing specs. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | Present. No change. |\n| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | `/login` is present (B7). Verify only. |\n| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`. Verify via the integration test. |\n| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Present (`loginErrorMessage`). Verify only. |\n| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`). Covered by the authorize integration test. |\n| FR-6 | Auth Core / UI | Limiter and message are both present (B7). Verify only. |\n| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | Present (`safeCallbackUrl` in `LoginForm`). Verify only. |\n| FR-8 | Audit | Emitted by `authorize`. The integration test asserts the AuditLog rows. |\n| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present. No change. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`, `reauth`). The change-password integration test covers `passwordChangedAt`. |\n| FR-11 | Access Control | Present (B11). No change. |\n| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. Pages call `verifyToken` only and never hash anything (B4). |\n| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: read-only name and email + `SetPasswordForm`. Invalid, used or expired: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. |\n| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client flow from B6. A 410 response switches to the invalid-link copy. Service and audit are present. |\n| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is enforced server-side and comes back through `fieldErrors.password` → `applyFieldErrors`. |\n| FR-16 | UI: Auth / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` (inside `SetPasswordForm`) on the invite, reset and security pages (B2). |\n| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + a client form (RHF + the shared forgot-password schema, `postJson`). Always shows the success `Alert`. Handles 429. API and limiter are present. |\n| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` → `sendAuthEmail`). Integration test only. |\n| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server, `verifyToken` for the email, B3) + `SetPasswordForm` → POST `/api/auth/reset-password` → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')` (B7 toast). |\n| FR-20 | UI: Account | **New** `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form with current, new and confirm fields, the shared change-password schema, `PasswordChecklist` and `passwordInputSlot`. On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show \"Current password is incorrect.\" On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form (B8). |\n| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` item labelled \"Account security\" (B10). |\n| FR-22 | Service | Present. Verify only. |\n| FR-23 | Access Control | Present (B13). New pages use `requirePageUser`. |\n| FR-24 | Audit | Present. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. The layout passes `user` to `AppShell` (B9). |\n| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name is `firstName lastName`, with a role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), and Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |\n| FR-27 | UI: Shell | `navigationForRole(user.role)`. |\n| FR-28 | Seed | Present. No change. |\n| FR-29 | Seed | Present. No change. |\n| FR-30 | Seed | Present (`createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))`). No change. |\n| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `src/server/auth/email.ts`. |\n| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip` (intake default). No rename. |\n| FR-33 | Migration | Present (`20261106000000_user_role_status_index`). No change. |\n| FR-34 | Tests | **New** integration files `tests/integration/auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`), run against the test DB. **New** `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`: sign-in/out, the failed-login message, and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus the shared e2e sign-in helper (B14). The unit tests already exist. |\n| NFR-1 | Security | Present in `tokens.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` handles CSRF. The JSON routes are same-origin with SameSite=Lax. |\n| NFR-3 | Security | Present (`DUMMY_HASH`). |\n| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt, so this is met. Nothing to design. |\n| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every new form has an error `Alert` in an `aria-live=\"polite\"` region, and RHF `shouldFocusError` is on. `SetPasswordForm` and `applyFieldErrors` already do this. The security form must match. |\n| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate for dev:** call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev is blocked. |\n| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. The existing banned-import lint test guards this. |\n| NFR-8 | Audit | The new UI code adds no audit calls. Existing metadata is safe. |\n| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`, and the `(app)` layout now does too. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers conform, apart from the B5 `INVALID_TOKEN` 410. |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`. Add no new schemas unless one is missing. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger`. The existing seed `console.log` (line 148) is out of scope. |\n| NFR-13 | Scope | Leave `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `middleware.ts`, `/login`, the seed and the schema alone. Watch B14. |\n| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page. |\n| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI and English copy. Nothing to design. |\n\n## Change footprint\n\n**New (6 source files + tests):** `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (+ a client form), `(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (+ a client form), 4 integration tests,\n`tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` and the e2e sign-in helper.\n\n**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (`requirePageUser`, then the `user` prop), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (drop the placeholder, real\nuser, sign out, Account security item), and the existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) to use the sign-in helper.\n\n**Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,\n`src/lib/validators/auth.ts` (unless a form schema is genuinely missing).\n\n## Open items carried from intake\n\n1. FR-32: keep `ip` (LOW confidence, default applied).\n2. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`. `sendAuthEmail` is unchanged.\n3. The ticket id is SH-1.\n4. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a hard gate for the dev phase.\n5. New: intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" looks out of date (B7). Verify, don't build.\n6. New: existing e2e specs may already be failing without auth (B14).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":112,"newStart":1,"newLines":111,"lines":[" # Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-1"," ","-Supporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` for PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001).","-It has 34 FRs and 15 NFRs (49 requirements) at 97% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.","+Written by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z) for PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001).","+It has 34 FRs and 15 NFRs (49 requirements) at 97% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 5 blockers."," Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`."," ","-> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are **stale outputs from an earlier ticket**, and the other","-> sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-1 input, with one exception: `tech-stack-decisions.md`","-> once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-1.","+> This file replaces an earlier SH-1 notes file. That version listed `/login`, the seed users and the role/status","+> migration as new work. All three are now **present** on disk."," ","-**Headline:** this is a **UI + seed + tests** ticket. Every backend module and API route already exists.","-The design must add pages and wire them to existing code, not add services or endpoints.","-**No new API endpoint is needed.** `arch-api-contracts` should document the 5 existing routes as-is.","+**Headline:** this is a **UI-gap + tests** ticket. The backend, every API route, `/login`, the seed and the","+migration already exist. The design adds **4 pages**, rewires the **shell**, and adds **tests**.","+**No new endpoint, service, model or migration is needed.** `arch-api-contracts` documents the 5 existing routes as they are."," ","-Concern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Auth Core**, **Service**, **API (existing)**,","-**UI: Auth Pages**, **UI: Account**, **UI: Shell**, **Access Control**, **Security**, **Audit**,","-**Seed**, **Accessibility**, **UI Rules**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.","+Concern buckets: **Data Model**, **Auth Core**, **Service**, **API (existing)**, **UI: Auth Pages**,","+**UI: Account**, **UI: Shell**, **Access Control**, **Security**, **Audit**, **Seed**, **Accessibility**,","+**UI Rules**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**."," ","-## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these confirm or add to intake)","+## Brownfield facts verified on disk"," "," | # | Fact | Design implication |"," |---|------|--------------------|","-| B1 | `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` already renders the centred `Card` shell (SchoolHub logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"`). | Auth pages render **only the card body**, with no Card or Container of their own. |","-| B2 | `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure`. Nothing imports them yet. | FR-16 checklist and the invite/reset forms **reuse `SetPasswordForm`**. `/account/security` and `/login` reuse `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`. Do not write a second checklist or fetch helper. |","-| B3 | `credentials.ts` throws `AuthError(code)` (a `CredentialsSignin` subclass). Codes: `invalid`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `locked:<N>`. | `/login` calls `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react` and maps `result.code` to the FR-4 and FR-6 copy. That mapping is a pure function and should get one unit test. |","-| B4 | `auth.ts` exports `signIn`, `signOut` and `unstable_update`. The `jwt` callback handles `trigger==='update' && session.reauth`. `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({reauth:true})`. | FR-20 \"re-issue current session\" is **already done server-side**. The page only POSTs and shows a toast. |","-| B5 | `app/providers.tsx` has **no `SessionProvider`**. | Client `signIn`/`signOut` from `next-auth/react` work without it. The shell gets the user as a **prop from the server layout**, so no provider and no `useSession` are needed. |","-| B6 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders the client `AppShell({ schoolShortName })`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user` (`id`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `role`) to `AppShell`. This removes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (FR-25/26/27) and gives one source of the current user. |","-| B7 | `shell.tsx` already imports `LogoutIcon`, `PersonOutlineIcon`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `Chip` and `UserAvatar`. | FR-21/FR-26 only change menu items. Add the `Account security` link and an `onClick={() => signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })}` handler. |","-| B8 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** sign the user in. Its error copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | FR-14: after a successful POST, the client calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` and then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. The FR-13 copy is rendered by the **page** when the server-side `verifyToken()` fails, and is reused when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. |","-| B9 | `tokens.ts` exports `verifyToken(raw, type)`, which is read-only and does not consume the token. | `/invite/[token]/page.tsx` is a server component that calls `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')` to show the name and email (FR-13). `/reset-password/[token]` can do the same up front. Neither needs a new endpoint. |","-| B10 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN', …)` is a code **outside** the NFR-10 code list. | This is existing behaviour; keep it (NFR-13). The UI must handle the `INVALID_TOKEN` code. Flag it for `arch-api-contracts` to document. |","-| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | FR-11 and NFR-14 are satisfied. Middleware needs no change. |","-| B12 | `prisma/seed.ts` already looks up `student@` and `parent@` to attach PRD-04 notifications, and **skips them if missing**. It uses `console.log`. | FR-28 user upserts must run **before** the notifications block. New seed code uses `logger` (NFR-12). The existing `console.log` lines are out of scope (NFR-13). |","-| B13 | Existing tests: unit `tokens`, `lockout`, `rate-limit`, `password-policy`, `auth-validators`. Integration has no auth tests. E2E has no auth specs. | FR-34 adds 4 integration files and 1–2 Playwright specs. Unit tests are already done. |","-| B14 | The existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) hit `(app)` pages. Once a real session is required, they redirect to `/login`. | **Regression risk (NFR-13):** the e2e suite needs a shared sign-in helper or `storageState` using the seed users. Check whether these specs currently pass without auth. |","-| B15 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. | `/forgot-password` displays the API's `data.message`, or imports this constant, rather than retyping the string. |","+| B1 | `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` already renders the centred Card shell. | New auth pages render only the card body. |","+| B2 | `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure`. Today only `LoginForm` imports any of them. | Invite and reset pages **reuse `SetPasswordForm`**. `/account/security` reuses `PasswordChecklist`, `passwordInputSlot`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors`. Do not add a second fetch or checklist helper. |","+| B3 | `SetPasswordForm` **requires `email`**, because the policy rejects a password equal to the email. | `/reset-password/[token]` must also call `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` server-side, to get the email and to show the invalid-link state before the form renders. |","+| B4 | `tokens.ts` `verifyToken(raw, type)` is read-only. `consumeToken` throws `INVALID_TOKEN` on a double submit. | The token pages are **server components** that call `verifyToken`. They show user data or the invalid-link `Alert`. No new endpoint. |","+| B5 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` maps to **410**, a code outside the NFR-10 list. The service copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | Keep this (NFR-13). The UI handles 410 `INVALID_TOKEN` by switching to the page's invalid-link copy. `arch-api-contracts` should document the 410. |","+| B6 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** create a session. | FR-14 flow on the client: POST `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. |","+| B7 | `/login` already exists. `LoginForm({ callbackUrl, reset })` fires a `useToast` once when `reset` is set, and exports `loginErrorMessage` (unit-tested). | FR-19 redirects to `/login?reset=1`. **Do not touch `/login`.** FR-2, FR-4, FR-6 and FR-7 only need verification. Intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date: `loginErrorMessage` covers `rate_limited`. Dev should verify this. |","+| B8 | `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`. The `jwt` callback keeps the current session alive on `reauth`. | FR-20 \"re-issue the current session\" is done server-side. The page only POSTs, then shows a toast and resets the form. |","+| B9 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders `<AppShell schoolShortName>` and does no auth. `providers.tsx` has no `SessionProvider`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user: SessionUser` (`id`, `role`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `email`) to `AppShell`. **Prop, not `useSession`**, so no provider is needed. This is the one source of the current user (FR-25). |","+| B10 | `shell.tsx` uses `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167). Its menu has 2 `MenuItem`s that only close the menu, and there is no `signOut`. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26 and FR-27 are all in this one file plus the layout. Sign out is `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`. |","+| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | Middleware needs no change (FR-11, NFR-14). |","+| B12 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. `requestPasswordReset` throws `RATE_LIMITED`. | `/forgot-password` shows `data.message` from the API rather than retyping the string, and shows an error `Alert` on 429. |","+| B13 | `src/app/forbidden/page.tsx` exists. | `requirePageRole` → `/forbidden` is already wired (FR-23). |","+| B14 | Existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) call `page.goto('/dashboard')` with no sign-in. The middleware already requires a session. | **Regression risk (NFR-13).** These specs are probably already failing, or will once the layout calls `requirePageUser`. Add one shared e2e sign-in helper using the seed users and reuse it in the existing specs. |"," "," ## Requirement → architectural concern"," "," | Req | Concern | Notes |"," |-----|---------|-------|","-| FR-1 | Data Model | Already present; no change. |","-| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, a thin server wrapper that reads `callbackUrl` plus a client `LoginForm`. It uses RHF + `signInSchema`, `TextField`, a show-password `InputAdornment`/`IconButton` (reuse `passwordInputSlot`) and an `Alert`. It links to `/forgot-password`. |","-| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`; verify only. |","-| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Pure `loginErrorMessage(code)` maps `invalid`, `disabled` and `locked:N` to the PRD copy. The locked message reads \"Try again in N minutes.\" |","-| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`); covered by the integration test. |","-| FR-6 | UI: Auth Pages | Limiter present. Map `rate_limited` to \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |","-| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` after `signIn` succeeds. Reuse the validator. |","-| FR-8 | Audit | Already emitted by `authorizeCredentials`; integration test asserts the rows. |","-| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present; no change. |","-| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`). The `reauth` path keeps the changing session alive. |","-| FR-11 | Access Control | Present in `middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` (B11). |","-| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. UI pages call `verifyToken` server-side (B9) and never hash anything themselves. |","-| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name and email. Invalid: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. Uses `verifyToken`, not consume. |","-| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client POSTs `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials')`, then `/dashboard` (B8). Service and audit already present. |","-| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is server-only and surfaces through `fieldErrors.password`. |","-| FR-16 | UI: Auth Pages / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` on invite, reset and change forms (B2). |","-| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`. RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password')`. Always shows the success `Alert` and handles `RATE_LIMITED`. API, limiter and service are present. |","-| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` + `sendAuthEmail`); integration test only. |","-| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`. Uses `SetPasswordForm`, then `/login?reset=1`, where `LoginForm` fires `useToast` once on mount. The query param is the lazy channel; there is no shared state. |","-| FR-20 | UI: Account | New `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form (current/new/confirm, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`). On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show the field error. On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form. Session re-issue is already server-side (B4). |","-| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` \"Account security\" item to the user menu. |","-| FR-22 | Service | Present; verify only. |","-| FR-23 | Access Control | Present; `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole` are used by the new pages. |","+| FR-1 | Data Model | Present. No change. |","+| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | `/login` is present (B7). Verify only. |","+| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`. Verify via the integration test. |","+| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Present (`loginErrorMessage`). Verify only. |","+| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`). Covered by the authorize integration test. |","+| FR-6 | Auth Core / UI | Limiter and message are both present (B7). Verify only. |","+| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | Present (`safeCallbackUrl` in `LoginForm`). Verify only. |","+| FR-8 | Audit | Emitted by `authorize`. The integration test asserts the AuditLog rows. |","+| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present. No change. |","+| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`, `reauth`). The change-password integration test covers `passwordChangedAt`. |","+| FR-11 | Access Control | Present (B11). No change. |","+| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. Pages call `verifyToken` only and never hash anything (B4). |","+| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: read-only name and email + `SetPasswordForm`. Invalid, used or expired: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. |","+| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client flow from B6. A 410 response switches to the invalid-link copy. Service and audit are present. |","+| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is enforced server-side and comes back through `fieldErrors.password` → `applyFieldErrors`. |","+| FR-16 | UI: Auth / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` (inside `SetPasswordForm`) on the invite, reset and security pages (B2). |","+| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + a client form (RHF + the shared forgot-password schema, `postJson`). Always shows the success `Alert`. Handles 429. API and limiter are present. |","+| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` → `sendAuthEmail`). Integration test only. |","+| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server, `verifyToken` for the email, B3) + `SetPasswordForm` → POST `/api/auth/reset-password` → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')` (B7 toast). |","+| FR-20 | UI: Account | **New** `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form with current, new and confirm fields, the shared change-password schema, `PasswordChecklist` and `passwordInputSlot`. On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show \"Current password is incorrect.\" On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form (B8). |","+| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` item labelled \"Account security\" (B10). |","+| FR-22 | Service | Present. Verify only. |","+| FR-23 | Access Control | Present (B13). New pages use `requirePageUser`. |"," | FR-24 | Audit | Present. |","-| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`; `AppShell` takes a `user` prop (B6). |","-| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name = `firstName lastName`, role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |","+| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. The layout passes `user` to `AppShell` (B9). |","+| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name is `firstName lastName`, with a role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), and Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |"," | FR-27 | UI: Shell | `navigationForRole(user.role)`. |","-| FR-28 | Seed | `prisma.user.upsert` × 6 by email, `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)`, status ACTIVE and `passwordChangedAt` set. Idempotent with `update: {}`. Place before the notifications block (B12). |","-| FR-29 | Seed | Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` (INVITED, no `passwordHash`). |","-| FR-30 | Seed | `createInviteToken(user.id)` (which invalidates older invites on rerun) and `logger.info(authLink('invite', raw))`. Do not use `sendAuthEmail`. |","-| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `email.ts`. |","-| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip`; no rename (default per intake). |","-| FR-33 | Migration | Add a new additive migration with `@@index([role, status])` on `User` (default per intake). |","-| FR-34 | Tests | Integration files `auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`) run against the test DB. The e2e `auth.spec.ts` covers sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus a unit test for `loginErrorMessage`. |","+| FR-28 | Seed | Present. No change. |","+| FR-29 | Seed | Present. No change. |","+| FR-30 | Seed | Present (`createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))`). No change. |","+| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `src/server/auth/email.ts`. |","+| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip` (intake default). No rename. |","+| FR-33 | Migration | Present (`20261106000000_user_role_status_index`). No change. |","+| FR-34 | Tests | **New** integration files `tests/integration/auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`), run against the test DB. **New** `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`: sign-in/out, the failed-login message, and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus the shared e2e sign-in helper (B14). The unit tests already exist. |"," | NFR-1 | Security | Present in `tokens.ts`. |","-| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` fetches the CSRF token automatically. JSON POST routes are same-origin and SameSite=Lax. |","+| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` handles CSRF. The JSON routes are same-origin with SameSite=Lax. |"," | NFR-3 | Security | Present (`DUMMY_HASH`). |","-| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt is about 250 ms, so this is met. Nothing new to design. |","-| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every form has an `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`, and RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default) focuses the first invalid field. `applyFieldErrors` already focuses the first server-reported field. |","-| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate:** dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev blocks and does not guess. |","-| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |","-| NFR-8 | Audit | Existing metadata is `{ email, reason }`, which is safe. New code adds no audit calls. |","-| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |","-| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers already conform (B10 notes the one extra code). |","-| NFR-11 | Conventions | All forms use RHF + `zodResolver` with the shared `auth.ts` schemas. |","-| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger` (seed included). |","-| NFR-13 | Scope | No edits to `course-access.ts`/`student-access.ts` or any existing auth module. Watch B14 so e2e does not regress. |","-| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page; `/login` has no \"create account\" link. |","-| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI, English copy. Nothing to design. |","+| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt, so this is met. Nothing to design. |","+| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every new form has an error `Alert` in an `aria-live=\"polite\"` region, and RHF `shouldFocusError` is on. `SetPasswordForm` and `applyFieldErrors` already do this. The security form must match. |","+| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate for dev:** call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev is blocked. |","+| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. The existing banned-import lint test guards this. |","+| NFR-8 | Audit | The new UI code adds no audit calls. Existing metadata is safe. |","+| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`, and the `(app)` layout now does too. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |","+| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers conform, apart from the B5 `INVALID_TOKEN` 410. |","+| NFR-11 | Conventions | RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`. Add no new schemas unless one is missing. |","+| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger`. The existing seed `console.log` (line 148) is out of scope. |","+| NFR-13 | Scope | Leave `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `middleware.ts`, `/login`, the seed and the schema alone. Watch B14. |","+| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page. |","+| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI and English copy. Nothing to design. |"," ","-## New files (expected) vs modified files","+## Change footprint"," ","-**New:** `(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`,","-`(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`, `(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`,","-`(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + client form, one additive migration, 4 integration tests, 1 e2e spec","-(+ e2e sign-in helper if B14 bites).","+**New (6 source files + tests):** `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (+ a client form), `(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,","+`(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (+ a client form), 4 integration tests,","+`tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` and the e2e sign-in helper."," ","-**Modified:** `(app)/layout.tsx` (session user → prop), `(app)/shell.tsx` (drop placeholder, menu items),","-`prisma/schema.prisma` (index), `prisma/seed.ts` (users + invite).","+**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (`requirePageUser`, then the `user` prop), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (drop the placeholder, real","+user, sign out, Account security item), and the existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) to use the sign-in helper."," ","-**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts` and `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`.","+**Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,","+`src/lib/validators/auth.ts` (unless a form schema is genuinely missing)."," "," ## Open items carried from intake"," ","-1. FR-32: keep `ip`.","-2. FR-33: add the index.","-3. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`.","-4. Ticket id is SH-1.","-5. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a dev-phase hard gate.","+1. FR-32: keep `ip` (LOW confidence, default applied).","+2. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`. `sendAuthEmail` is unchanged.","+3. The ticket id is SH-1.","+4. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a hard gate for the dev phase.","+5. New: intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" looks out of date (B7). Verify, don't build.","+6. New: existing e2e specs may already be failing without auth (B14)."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-1\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` for PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001).\nIt has 34 FRs and 15 NFRs (49 requirements) at 97% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are **stale outputs from an earlier ticket**, and the other\n> sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-1 input, with one exception: `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n> once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-1.\n\n**Headline:** this is a **UI + seed + tests** ticket. Every backend module and API route already exists.\nThe design must add pages and wire them to existing code, not add services or endpoints.\n**No new API endpoint is needed.** `arch-api-contracts` should document the 5 existing routes as-is.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Auth Core**, **Service**, **API (existing)**,\n**UI: Auth Pages**, **UI: Account**, **UI: Shell**, **Access Control**, **Security**, **Audit**,\n**Seed**, **Accessibility**, **UI Rules**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these confirm or add to intake)\n\n| # | Fact | Design implication |\n|---|------|--------------------|\n| B1 | `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` already renders the centred `Card` shell (SchoolHub logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"`). | Auth pages render **only the card body**, with no Card or Container of their own. |\n| B2 | `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure`. Nothing imports them yet. | FR-16 checklist and the invite/reset forms **reuse `SetPasswordForm`**. `/account/security` and `/login` reuse `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`. Do not write a second checklist or fetch helper. |\n| B3 | `credentials.ts` throws `AuthError(code)` (a `CredentialsSignin` subclass). Codes: `invalid`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `locked:<N>`. | `/login` calls `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react` and maps `result.code` to the FR-4 and FR-6 copy. That mapping is a pure function and should get one unit test. |\n| B4 | `auth.ts` exports `signIn`, `signOut` and `unstable_update`. The `jwt` callback handles `trigger==='update' && session.reauth`. `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({reauth:true})`. | FR-20 \"re-issue current session\" is **already done server-side**. The page only POSTs and shows a toast. |\n| B5 | `app/providers.tsx` has **no `SessionProvider`**. | Client `signIn`/`signOut` from `next-auth/react` work without it. The shell gets the user as a **prop from the server layout**, so no provider and no `useSession` are needed. |\n| B6 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders the client `AppShell({ schoolShortName })`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user` (`id`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `role`) to `AppShell`. This removes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (FR-25/26/27) and gives one source of the current user. |\n| B7 | `shell.tsx` already imports `LogoutIcon`, `PersonOutlineIcon`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `Chip` and `UserAvatar`. | FR-21/FR-26 only change menu items. Add the `Account security` link and an `onClick={() => signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })}` handler. |\n| B8 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** sign the user in. Its error copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | FR-14: after a successful POST, the client calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` and then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. The FR-13 copy is rendered by the **page** when the server-side `verifyToken()` fails, and is reused when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. |\n| B9 | `tokens.ts` exports `verifyToken(raw, type)`, which is read-only and does not consume the token. | `/invite/[token]/page.tsx` is a server component that calls `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')` to show the name and email (FR-13). `/reset-password/[token]` can do the same up front. Neither needs a new endpoint. |\n| B10 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN', …)` is a code **outside** the NFR-10 code list. | This is existing behaviour; keep it (NFR-13). The UI must handle the `INVALID_TOKEN` code. Flag it for `arch-api-contracts` to document. |\n| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | FR-11 and NFR-14 are satisfied. Middleware needs no change. |\n| B12 | `prisma/seed.ts` already looks up `student@` and `parent@` to attach PRD-04 notifications, and **skips them if missing**. It uses `console.log`. | FR-28 user upserts must run **before** the notifications block. New seed code uses `logger` (NFR-12). The existing `console.log` lines are out of scope (NFR-13). |\n| B13 | Existing tests: unit `tokens`, `lockout`, `rate-limit`, `password-policy`, `auth-validators`. Integration has no auth tests. E2E has no auth specs. | FR-34 adds 4 integration files and 1–2 Playwright specs. Unit tests are already done. |\n| B14 | The existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) hit `(app)` pages. Once a real session is required, they redirect to `/login`. | **Regression risk (NFR-13):** the e2e suite needs a shared sign-in helper or `storageState` using the seed users. Check whether these specs currently pass without auth. |\n| B15 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. | `/forgot-password` displays the API's `data.message`, or imports this constant, rather than retyping the string. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | Already present; no change. |\n| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, a thin server wrapper that reads `callbackUrl` plus a client `LoginForm`. It uses RHF + `signInSchema`, `TextField`, a show-password `InputAdornment`/`IconButton` (reuse `passwordInputSlot`) and an `Alert`. It links to `/forgot-password`. |\n| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`; verify only. |\n| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Pure `loginErrorMessage(code)` maps `invalid`, `disabled` and `locked:N` to the PRD copy. The locked message reads \"Try again in N minutes.\" |\n| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`); covered by the integration test. |\n| FR-6 | UI: Auth Pages | Limiter present. Map `rate_limited` to \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |\n| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` after `signIn` succeeds. Reuse the validator. |\n| FR-8 | Audit | Already emitted by `authorizeCredentials`; integration test asserts the rows. |\n| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present; no change. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`). The `reauth` path keeps the changing session alive. |\n| FR-11 | Access Control | Present in `middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` (B11). |\n| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. UI pages call `verifyToken` server-side (B9) and never hash anything themselves. |\n| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name and email. Invalid: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. Uses `verifyToken`, not consume. |\n| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client POSTs `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials')`, then `/dashboard` (B8). Service and audit already present. |\n| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is server-only and surfaces through `fieldErrors.password`. |\n| FR-16 | UI: Auth Pages / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` on invite, reset and change forms (B2). |\n| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`. RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password')`. Always shows the success `Alert` and handles `RATE_LIMITED`. API, limiter and service are present. |\n| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` + `sendAuthEmail`); integration test only. |\n| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`. Uses `SetPasswordForm`, then `/login?reset=1`, where `LoginForm` fires `useToast` once on mount. The query param is the lazy channel; there is no shared state. |\n| FR-20 | UI: Account | New `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form (current/new/confirm, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`). On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show the field error. On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form. Session re-issue is already server-side (B4). |\n| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` \"Account security\" item to the user menu. |\n| FR-22 | Service | Present; verify only. |\n| FR-23 | Access Control | Present; `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole` are used by the new pages. |\n| FR-24 | Audit | Present. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`; `AppShell` takes a `user` prop (B6). |\n| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name = `firstName lastName`, role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |\n| FR-27 | UI: Shell | `navigationForRole(user.role)`. |\n| FR-28 | Seed | `prisma.user.upsert` × 6 by email, `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)`, status ACTIVE and `passwordChangedAt` set. Idempotent with `update: {}`. Place before the notifications block (B12). |\n| FR-29 | Seed | Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` (INVITED, no `passwordHash`). |\n| FR-30 | Seed | `createInviteToken(user.id)` (which invalidates older invites on rerun) and `logger.info(authLink('invite', raw))`. Do not use `sendAuthEmail`. |\n| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `email.ts`. |\n| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip`; no rename (default per intake). |\n| FR-33 | Migration | Add a new additive migration with `@@index([role, status])` on `User` (default per intake). |\n| FR-34 | Tests | Integration files `auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`) run against the test DB. The e2e `auth.spec.ts` covers sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus a unit test for `loginErrorMessage`. |\n| NFR-1 | Security | Present in `tokens.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` fetches the CSRF token automatically. JSON POST routes are same-origin and SameSite=Lax. |\n| NFR-3 | Security | Present (`DUMMY_HASH`). |\n| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt is about 250 ms, so this is met. Nothing new to design. |\n| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every form has an `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`, and RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default) focuses the first invalid field. `applyFieldErrors` already focuses the first server-reported field. |\n| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate:** dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev blocks and does not guess. |\n| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |\n| NFR-8 | Audit | Existing metadata is `{ email, reason }`, which is safe. New code adds no audit calls. |\n| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers already conform (B10 notes the one extra code). |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | All forms use RHF + `zodResolver` with the shared `auth.ts` schemas. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger` (seed included). |\n| NFR-13 | Scope | No edits to `course-access.ts`/`student-access.ts` or any existing auth module. Watch B14 so e2e does not regress. |\n| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page; `/login` has no \"create account\" link. |\n| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI, English copy. Nothing to design. |\n\n## New files (expected) vs modified files\n\n**New:** `(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`,\n`(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`, `(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + client form, one additive migration, 4 integration tests, 1 e2e spec\n(+ e2e sign-in helper if B14 bites).\n\n**Modified:** `(app)/layout.tsx` (session user → prop), `(app)/shell.tsx` (drop placeholder, menu items),\n`prisma/schema.prisma` (index), `prisma/seed.ts` (users + invite).\n\n**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts` and `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`.\n\n## Open items carried from intake\n\n1. FR-32: keep `ip`.\n2. FR-33: add the index.\n3. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`.\n4. Ticket id is SH-1.\n5. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a dev-phase hard gate.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RatAiB7zJy2J1VoLjGqpjG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
