{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgk6Z8Xf9UFuQuAyUUePY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've rewritten `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` for SH-1. It maps every requirement (FR-1–34, NFR-1–15) to its design concern, and every ID it cites exists in `requirements.json`.\n\nThe notes file already on disk was from an earlier run. It listed `/login`, the seed users and the role/status migration as work to do, but all three now exist. I checked the code again and replaced it.\n\n**Result:** this ticket needs only UI pages, shell changes and tests. No new endpoint, service, model or migration is needed.\n\n**New work:**\n- Four pages: `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]` and `/account/security`.\n- Shell rewiring: the `(app)` layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes the signed-in user to the shell as a prop. That deletes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and adds the role badge, sign-out and an \"Account security\" menu item.\n- Tests: four integration tests (sign-in checks, accept invite, reset password, change password), one Playwright auth spec, and a shared e2e sign-in helper.\n\n**Things I found that intake didn't say:**\n- **Reset page:** it must look up the token on the server first. The shared password form needs the user's email, because the policy rejects a password equal to the email.\n- **Invite sign-in:** accepting an invite doesn't sign the user in. The page has to call `signIn` itself after the POST succeeds.\n- **Error code:** the API returns 410 `INVALID_TOKEN` for a bad link. That code isn't in the standard error list, so `arch-api-contracts` should document it.\n- **FR-6:** intake says the rate-limit message is missing from the UI, but the login form already handles it. Dev should check it, not build it.\n- **Existing e2e tests:** the `dashboard` and `notifications` specs open `/dashboard` without signing in, while the middleware already requires a session. They are likely failing already, or will be once the layout requires a user. The shared sign-in helper should fix them.\n\nI didn't write any other sub-task's file. `system-design.md`, `api-contracts.json` and the rest in that folder are still the earlier run's versions until those sub-tasks rewrite them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5545,"cache_read_input_tokens":52155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5545},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f674949-015a-48f5-8729-2f49c8704d06","uuid":"b6d794a2-97cc-4247-9048-a41082dd34cd","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:28:23.995Z","request_id":"req_011Cgk6Z8JGcUC2Ei3e8FDdU"}
