{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0113xGKPdQDudwsXJpqWrCba","type":"tool_result","content":"approvals\narchitect\ndev\ndev-planning\nintake\nqa\nrun-summary.json\ntelemetry\nui-verification\n\nartifacts/approvals:\narchitect-approval.json\ndev-planning-approval.json\nintake-approval.json\n\nartifacts/architect:\napi-contracts.json\nhandoff-to-dev-planning.json\nrequirements-analysis-notes.md\nsystem-design.md\ntech-stack-decisions.md\nthreat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/dev:\ndev-log.md\ndev-rerun-count.json\nsecurity-scan-report.json\ntask-completion-markers.json\n\nartifacts/dev-planning:\nfile-ownership-matrix.json\nfile-structure.md\nimplementation-plan.json\nmodule-dependencies.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n\nartifacts/qa:\ncoverage-report.md\nqa-report.md\n\nartifacts/telemetry:\napi-retries.jsonl\ndaemon-handoff.json\nknowledge-log.jsonl\nmetering.jsonl\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T05:29:02Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-07: Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-7 and the PRD header says SCH-007. All artifacts use SH-7. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-1 and are overwritten.\",\n    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no attendance code yet. There are no AttendanceSession/AttendanceRecord models, no AttendanceStatus enum, no attendance routes, pages, services, validators or tests, and no attendance.* notification types. The only mentions are the ATTENDANCE notification category in src/server/notifications/types.ts and a comment in timetable-service.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE (already exported): getScheduleForDate(target, date) and the ScheduleTarget/ScheduleEntry types from src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts (PRD-06 FR-30/31). It returns [] on non-teaching days and has a PRD-14 holiday hook comment.\",\n    \"REUSE: notifyStudentAndParents() and notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts. Both never throw. Register new type keys in the NOTIFICATION_TYPES map in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: assertCanManageCourse()/assertCanViewCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts and assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts. requireUser()/requireRole() come from src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: audit() from src/server/audit.ts, toCsv()/escapeCsvCell() from src/server/csv.ts, the HTTP response helpers in src/server/http.ts, and getSchoolSettings()/updateSchoolSettings() from src/server/services/settings.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE UI: shared components live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast). They are NOT in src/components/shared/ as the PRD says. Reuse them where they are and do not move or duplicate them.\",\n    \"EXTENSION POINTS: src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently only 'courses'), src/config/course-tabs.ts (overview and roster) and src/config/navigation.ts.\",\n    \"DATA MODEL FACTS: Section has homeroomTeacherId and members (SectionMember with studentId, sectionId, academicYearId and joinedAt, unique on [studentId, academicYearId]). Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED plus enrolledAt and droppedAt, and DROPPED rows are kept. Period has startTime/endTime as strings and an order field. Term has startDate/endDate per academicYear. SchoolSettings is a singleton with a timezone field and no attendanceMode or attendanceAlertThreshold yet.\",\n    \"GAP: there is no school settings page under src/app/(app)/admin, and src/app/api/settings/school/ is an empty directory, although the service has updateSchoolSettings(). FR-2 assumes an existing 'school settings page'. See FR-5 below (MEDIUM).\",\n    \"The latest migration is 20261106000000_user_role_status_index. The new attendance migration must come after it and must include the raw SQL CHECK and the two partial unique indexes.\",\n    \"Installed packages already cover this PRD. @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts, @mui/material and @mui/icons-material are all 9.5.0, along with date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and papaparse. No new dependencies are needed.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the AttendanceStatus enum (PRESENT, ABSENT, LATE, EXCUSED) and the AttendanceSession and AttendanceRecord Prisma models exactly as specified, with @@unique([sessionId, studentId]) and @@index([studentId, createdAt]) on records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Exactly one of AttendanceSession.courseId or sectionId must be set. Enforce this in the service layer and with a raw SQL CHECK constraint in the migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add two partial unique indexes in migration SQL: (courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL, and (sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Add attendanceMode (PER_PERIOD default | DAILY_HOMEROOM | BOTH) and attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90) to SchoolSettings.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1, FR-8.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Admins can edit attendanceMode (and attendanceAlertThreshold) on the school settings page. No such page or API route exists today, so the Architect must choose the smallest admin UI and API that satisfies this.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1 ('Admin edits it on the school settings page'), FR-8.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"/attendance/take shows the teacher's schedule for today (via getScheduleForDate), with each meeting's status ('Not taken' / 'Taken HH:mm by <name>'), and highlights the current period's meeting with a primary 'Take attendance' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"When attendanceMode includes daily registers, homeroom teachers also see a 'Daily register – <section>' entry on the landing page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"A date picker lets teachers open a register for any date in the past 14 days for their own courses, and admins for any date. Future dates are refused on both client and server.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"The register page /attendance/take/[courseId]?date=&periodId= lists ACTIVE enrolled students sorted by last name, with an avatar, the name and an exclusive MUI ToggleButtonGroup (P/A/L/E). Buttons are coloured via the theme palette and have screen-reader labels. Nothing is selected by default for a new register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"The EXCUSED option is available only to ADMIN in this PRD. It is hidden or disabled for teachers and rejected server-side for non-admins.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, Out of Scope (PRD-15 EXCUSED workflow)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"A 'Mark all present' button sets every unselected student to PRESENT without overwriting existing selections.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Selecting L reveals a minutes-late input (default 5, valid range 1–240, required when LATE). Each row has an optional note (max 500 characters) behind a note icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5, FR-1 field comments\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"The header shows live counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked). Save stays disabled while any student is unmarked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.6, AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Save creates or updates the session and all records in one DB transaction. Editing an existing register shows who last changed it and when.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"A daily homeroom register (sectionId + date, no period) can be read and saved by the section's homeroom teacher and by admins. Its roster is the section members.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table (register ?sectionId=), FR-3.1, NFR-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"The daily register page route and UI. The PRD names only the course register route, so the daily register is assumed to reuse the same register component at a section-scoped route (e.g. /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1 ('Daily register – 7A'), API table — route not specified\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Mobile layout: works one-handed at 360 px width, rows at least 48 px tall, toggle buttons at least 44×44 px, and a sticky save bar (MUI Paper, position: sticky) at the bottom.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Every status change to an existing record writes an audit() entry 'attendance.record.update' with the old status, the new status, the actor and the note.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Edit window: teachers can edit their own course records until 14 days after the register date. After that only admins can edit, and others see the register read-only with an explanation. This is enforced server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2, AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register notification types 'attendance.absent' (category ATTENDANCE, default email true, mandatoryInApp true, roles PARENT and STUDENT) and 'attendance.late' (default email false) in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"After the save transaction commits, call notifyStudentAndParents once for each student whose status changed to ABSENT or LATE compared with the previously saved value. Use title 'X was marked absent' / 'X was marked late (N min)', body '<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <Weekday d MMM yyyy>' and link /students/<id>/attendance.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2, AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"When a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT on the same day, send 'attendance.corrected' (title 'Attendance corrected: X was present') to the same recipients. At most one absence notification per student per session, so re-saving never sends a duplicate.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Register the 'attendance.corrected' and 'attendance.register_missing' notification type keys. The PRD does not give their category, email default or roles, so these are assumed: corrected = ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false; register_missing = ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, FR-8.1 — type metadata unspecified\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts at /students/[studentId]/attendance, visible to every role that can view the student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"The student Attendance tab shows summary cards for the current term and the year (attendance rate %, absent count, late count, excused count).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The tab shows a read-only month calendar built with MUI X DateCalendar and a custom 'day' slot coloured success (all present), warning (any late), error (any absent) or default (no data), with a Tooltip summary and month navigation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"The tab has a filterable table of records (date, period, course, status, minutes late, note). Notes are visible only to ADMIN and TEACHER and are stripped from the API response for STUDENT and PARENT.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, API table, AC-8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Attendance rate = (PRESENT + LATE + EXCUSED) / total marked records × 100, rounded to one decimal place. Records from DROPPED enrollments still count. Per-period records are used when the mode is PER_PERIOD or BOTH, and daily records when it is DAILY_HOMEROOM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2, FR-2.1, AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts (TEACHER and ADMIN) showing a DataGrid matrix: students as rows, the last 20 session dates as horizontally scrollable columns, coloured P/A/L/E cells and a per-student rate column. Clicking a column header opens that register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"/admin/attendance Today overview shows sessions expected vs taken today and the school-wide rate today.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"It lists 'Missing registers' (meetings with no register 15 minutes after period start, in the school timezone), each with a 'Remind teacher' button that POSTs to /api/admin/attendance/remind and sends 'attendance.register_missing' to the teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1, API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"The report builder filters by date range (max 366 days), grade level, section, course and status, and shows a per-student summary (records, present, absent, late, excused, rate). CSV export with the same columns comes from ?format=csv.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.2, Goal 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"The 'Below threshold' view lists students whose year-to-date rate is below SchoolSettings.attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90), sorted ascending, each linked to the student page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.3, AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Add navigation entries: 'Attendance' for TEACHER (to /attendance/take) and 'Attendance' for ADMIN in the main group (to /admin/attendance). Students and parents use the student-page tab.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"API routes: GET /api/attendance/today; GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (course or section variant); GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=; GET /api/courses/:id/attendance; GET /api/admin/attendance/overview?date=; GET /api/admin/attendance/report (?format=csv); GET /api/admin/attendance/below-threshold; POST /api/admin/attendance/remind. Each route uses the role or access check listed in the API table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Zod validators live in src/lib/validators/attendance.ts and are shared by the register form and the API handlers (PUT body, query params, report filters).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Fixed technology decisions (Validation), Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"The attendance service lives at src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts, following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions (services path)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Seed: attendance sessions for 7A and 7B covering the 15 teaching days before the seed run date. Use a fixed RNG seed and roughly 94% present, 3% late and 3% absent, with two Grade 7 students deliberately below 85%.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: rate calculation, the edit-window rule, and change detection for notifications (no duplicate on re-save).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Integration tests: the register save transaction, enrollment validation, and the partial unique indexes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Playwright tests: the take-attendance flow on a mobile viewport (375 px), and a parent seeing the notification and the absence on the attendance calendar.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Saving a 35-student register completes in under 500 ms. A student's yearly attendance tab loads in under 400 ms with 1,200 records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"If saving fails because of a network error, unsaved marks persist in localStorage keyed by course or section, date and period, and the next open offers 'Restore unsaved attendance'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Reliability)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Records may only be saved for students with an ACTIVE enrollment on that date (or section members for daily registers). Others are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR (400).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 3 (Integrity)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"A teacher can take attendance for a 30-student class in under 30 seconds on a phone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Parents receive absence notifications within 5 minutes. In-app notifications are immediate, and the email is queued in EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 2, AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: build only with MUI (@mui/material, icons and the MUI X packages), looking up every component via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for 9.5.0) before use. No banned libraries are allowed. An unreachable MCP server is a hard blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › UI component rule (items 1–6)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page. Parents see only linked students, students see only themselves, teachers see their courses and homeroom sections, and admins see everything.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout (requireRole), Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Follow the platform conventions: response shapes and error codes, pagination (pageSize max 100), cuid IDs, @db.Date for date-only values, UTC storage with display in SchoolSettings.timezone, the logger instead of console.log, and audit() for mutations to records owned by others.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: toggle buttons have screen-reader labels, and touch targets are at least 44×44 px.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, FR-3.8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Brownfield safety: reuse existing helpers, components and models, never rename routes or models, keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test green, and do not implement scope owned by PRD-14 (holidays) or PRD-15 (absence notes and the EXCUSED workflow).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Assumptions and constraints, Out of Scope\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-5: Should a minimal /admin/settings page (or an attendance section on it) be built, given that no school settings page or API route exists? Default: add a small 'Attendance settings' card editing attendanceMode and attendanceAlertThreshold, plus PATCH /api/settings/school built on updateSchoolSettings().\",\n        \"FR-16: Which route should the daily homeroom register use? Default: /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=, reusing the course register component.\",\n        \"FR-23: What metadata should attendance.corrected and attendance.register_missing have? Default: category ATTENDANCE, email false; corrected goes to PARENT+STUDENT, register_missing to TEACHER.\",\n        \"FR-21: The PRD's sample body is 'Mathematics – 7A, Period 1, ...'. For daily registers (no course or period), is '<Section> daily register, <date>' acceptable? Default: yes.\",\n        \"FR-28: Does 'current term' mean the Term whose startDate–endDate contains today in the current AcademicYear? Default: yes. If today falls between terms, use the most recent ended term.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-5 school settings page does not exist; proceeding with the default above (MEDIUM).\",\n        \"FR-16 daily register route not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\",\n        \"FR-23 notification metadata for attendance.corrected / attendance.register_missing not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c9af49-395f-43b5-8c02-c9a3647dc0ab","uuid":"31aa5ad2-fb33-49ef-b4bc-32ba2cf1b5e9","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:30:55.394Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"approvals\narchitect\ndev\ndev-planning\nintake\nqa\nrun-summary.json\ntelemetry\nui-verification\n\nartifacts/approvals:\narchitect-approval.json\ndev-planning-approval.json\nintake-approval.json\n\nartifacts/architect:\napi-contracts.json\nhandoff-to-dev-planning.json\nrequirements-analysis-notes.md\nsystem-design.md\ntech-stack-decisions.md\nthreat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/dev:\ndev-log.md\ndev-rerun-count.json\nsecurity-scan-report.json\ntask-completion-markers.json\n\nartifacts/dev-planning:\nfile-ownership-matrix.json\nfile-structure.md\nimplementation-plan.json\nmodule-dependencies.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n\nartifacts/qa:\ncoverage-report.md\nqa-report.md\n\nartifacts/telemetry:\napi-retries.jsonl\ndaemon-handoff.json\nknowledge-log.jsonl\nmetering.jsonl\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T05:29:02Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-07: Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-7 and the PRD header says SCH-007. All artifacts use SH-7. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-1 and are overwritten.\",\n    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no attendance code yet. There are no AttendanceSession/AttendanceRecord models, no AttendanceStatus enum, no attendance routes, pages, services, validators or tests, and no attendance.* notification types. The only mentions are the ATTENDANCE notification category in src/server/notifications/types.ts and a comment in timetable-service.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE (already exported): getScheduleForDate(target, date) and the ScheduleTarget/ScheduleEntry types from src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts (PRD-06 FR-30/31). It returns [] on non-teaching days and has a PRD-14 holiday hook comment.\",\n    \"REUSE: notifyStudentAndParents() and notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts. Both never throw. Register new type keys in the NOTIFICATION_TYPES map in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: assertCanManageCourse()/assertCanViewCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts and assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts. requireUser()/requireRole() come from src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: audit() from src/server/audit.ts, toCsv()/escapeCsvCell() from src/server/csv.ts, the HTTP response helpers in src/server/http.ts, and getSchoolSettings()/updateSchoolSettings() from src/server/services/settings.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE UI: shared components live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast). They are NOT in src/components/shared/ as the PRD says. Reuse them where they are and do not move or duplicate them.\",\n    \"EXTENSION POINTS: src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently only 'courses'), src/config/course-tabs.ts (overview and roster) and src/config/navigation.ts.\",\n    \"DATA MODEL FACTS: Section has homeroomTeacherId and members (SectionMember with studentId, sectionId, academicYearId and joinedAt, unique on [studentId, academicYearId]). Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED plus enrolledAt and droppedAt, and DROPPED rows are kept. Period has startTime/endTime as strings and an order field. Term has startDate/endDate per academicYear. SchoolSettings is a singleton with a timezone field and no attendanceMode or attendanceAlertThreshold yet.\",\n    \"GAP: there is no school settings page under src/app/(app)/admin, and src/app/api/settings/school/ is an empty directory, although the service has updateSchoolSettings(). FR-2 assumes an existing 'school settings page'. See FR-5 below (MEDIUM).\",\n    \"The latest migration is 20261106000000_user_role_status_index. The new attendance migration must come after it and must include the raw SQL CHECK and the two partial unique indexes.\",\n    \"Installed packages already cover this PRD. @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts, @mui/material and @mui/icons-material are all 9.5.0, along with date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and papaparse. No new dependencies are needed.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the AttendanceStatus enum (PRESENT, ABSENT, LATE, EXCUSED) and the AttendanceSession and AttendanceRecord Prisma models exactly as specified, with @@unique([sessionId, studentId]) and @@index([studentId, createdAt]) on records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Exactly one of AttendanceSession.courseId or sectionId must be set. Enforce this in the service layer and with a raw SQL CHECK constraint in the migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add two partial unique indexes in migration SQL: (courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL, and (sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Add attendanceMode (PER_PERIOD default | DAILY_HOMEROOM | BOTH) and attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90) to SchoolSettings.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1, FR-8.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Admins can edit attendanceMode (and attendanceAlertThreshold) on the school settings page. No such page or API route exists today, so the Architect must choose the smallest admin UI and API that satisfies this.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1 ('Admin edits it on the school settings page'), FR-8.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"/attendance/take shows the teacher's schedule for today (via getScheduleForDate), with each meeting's status ('Not taken' / 'Taken HH:mm by <name>'), and highlights the current period's meeting with a primary 'Take attendance' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"When attendanceMode includes daily registers, homeroom teachers also see a 'Daily register – <section>' entry on the landing page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"A date picker lets teachers open a register for any date in the past 14 days for their own courses, and admins for any date. Future dates are refused on both client and server.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"The register page /attendance/take/[courseId]?date=&periodId= lists ACTIVE enrolled students sorted by last name, with an avatar, the name and an exclusive MUI ToggleButtonGroup (P/A/L/E). Buttons are coloured via the theme palette and have screen-reader labels. Nothing is selected by default for a new register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"The EXCUSED option is available only to ADMIN in this PRD. It is hidden or disabled for teachers and rejected server-side for non-admins.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, Out of Scope (PRD-15 EXCUSED workflow)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"A 'Mark all present' button sets every unselected student to PRESENT without overwriting existing selections.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Selecting L reveals a minutes-late input (default 5, valid range 1–240, required when LATE). Each row has an optional note (max 500 characters) behind a note icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5, FR-1 field comments\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"The header shows live counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked). Save stays disabled while any student is unmarked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.6, AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Save creates or updates the session and all records in one DB transaction. Editing an existing register shows who last changed it and when.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"A daily homeroom register (sectionId + date, no period) can be read and saved by the section's homeroom teacher and by admins. Its roster is the section members.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table (register ?sectionId=), FR-3.1, NFR-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"The daily register page route and UI. The PRD names only the course register route, so the daily register is assumed to reuse the same register component at a section-scoped route (e.g. /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1 ('Daily register – 7A'), API table — route not specified\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Mobile layout: works one-handed at 360 px width, rows at least 48 px tall, toggle buttons at least 44×44 px, and a sticky save bar (MUI Paper, position: sticky) at the bottom.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Every status change to an existing record writes an audit() entry 'attendance.record.update' with the old status, the new status, the actor and the note.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Edit window: teachers can edit their own course records until 14 days after the register date. After that only admins can edit, and others see the register read-only with an explanation. This is enforced server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2, AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register notification types 'attendance.absent' (category ATTENDANCE, default email true, mandatoryInApp true, roles PARENT and STUDENT) and 'attendance.late' (default email false) in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"After the save transaction commits, call notifyStudentAndParents once for each student whose status changed to ABSENT or LATE compared with the previously saved value. Use title 'X was marked absent' / 'X was marked late (N min)', body '<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <Weekday d MMM yyyy>' and link /students/<id>/attendance.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2, AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"When a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT on the same day, send 'attendance.corrected' (title 'Attendance corrected: X was present') to the same recipients. At most one absence notification per student per session, so re-saving never sends a duplicate.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Register the 'attendance.corrected' and 'attendance.register_missing' notification type keys. The PRD does not give their category, email default or roles, so these are assumed: corrected = ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false; register_missing = ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, FR-8.1 — type metadata unspecified\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts at /students/[studentId]/attendance, visible to every role that can view the student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"The student Attendance tab shows summary cards for the current term and the year (attendance rate %, absent count, late count, excused count).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The tab shows a read-only month calendar built with MUI X DateCalendar and a custom 'day' slot coloured success (all present), warning (any late), error (any absent) or default (no data), with a Tooltip summary and month navigation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"The tab has a filterable table of records (date, period, course, status, minutes late, note). Notes are visible only to ADMIN and TEACHER and are stripped from the API response for STUDENT and PARENT.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, API table, AC-8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Attendance rate = (PRESENT + LATE + EXCUSED) / total marked records × 100, rounded to one decimal place. Records from DROPPED enrollments still count. Per-period records are used when the mode is PER_PERIOD or BOTH, and daily records when it is DAILY_HOMEROOM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2, FR-2.1, AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts (TEACHER and ADMIN) showing a DataGrid matrix: students as rows, the last 20 session dates as horizontally scrollable columns, coloured P/A/L/E cells and a per-student rate column. Clicking a column header opens that register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"/admin/attendance Today overview shows sessions expected vs taken today and the school-wide rate today.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"It lists 'Missing registers' (meetings with no register 15 minutes after period start, in the school timezone), each with a 'Remind teacher' button that POSTs to /api/admin/attendance/remind and sends 'attendance.register_missing' to the teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1, API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"The report builder filters by date range (max 366 days), grade level, section, course and status, and shows a per-student summary (records, present, absent, late, excused, rate). CSV export with the same columns comes from ?format=csv.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.2, Goal 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"The 'Below threshold' view lists students whose year-to-date rate is below SchoolSettings.attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90), sorted ascending, each linked to the student page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.3, AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Add navigation entries: 'Attendance' for TEACHER (to /attendance/take) and 'Attendance' for ADMIN in the main group (to /admin/attendance). Students and parents use the student-page tab.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"API routes: GET /api/attendance/today; GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (course or section variant); GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=; GET /api/courses/:id/attendance; GET /api/admin/attendance/overview?date=; GET /api/admin/attendance/report (?format=csv); GET /api/admin/attendance/below-threshold; POST /api/admin/attendance/remind. Each route uses the role or access check listed in the API table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Zod validators live in src/lib/validators/attendance.ts and are shared by the register form and the API handlers (PUT body, query params, report filters).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Fixed technology decisions (Validation), Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"The attendance service lives at src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts, following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions (services path)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Seed: attendance sessions for 7A and 7B covering the 15 teaching days before the seed run date. Use a fixed RNG seed and roughly 94% present, 3% late and 3% absent, with two Grade 7 students deliberately below 85%.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: rate calculation, the edit-window rule, and change detection for notifications (no duplicate on re-save).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Integration tests: the register save transaction, enrollment validation, and the partial unique indexes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Playwright tests: the take-attendance flow on a mobile viewport (375 px), and a parent seeing the notification and the absence on the attendance calendar.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Saving a 35-student register completes in under 500 ms. A student's yearly attendance tab loads in under 400 ms with 1,200 records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"If saving fails because of a network error, unsaved marks persist in localStorage keyed by course or section, date and period, and the next open offers 'Restore unsaved attendance'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Reliability)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Records may only be saved for students with an ACTIVE enrollment on that date (or section members for daily registers). Others are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR (400).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 3 (Integrity)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"A teacher can take attendance for a 30-student class in under 30 seconds on a phone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Parents receive absence notifications within 5 minutes. In-app notifications are immediate, and the email is queued in EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 2, AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: build only with MUI (@mui/material, icons and the MUI X packages), looking up every component via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for 9.5.0) before use. No banned libraries are allowed. An unreachable MCP server is a hard blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › UI component rule (items 1–6)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page. Parents see only linked students, students see only themselves, teachers see their courses and homeroom sections, and admins see everything.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout (requireRole), Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Follow the platform conventions: response shapes and error codes, pagination (pageSize max 100), cuid IDs, @db.Date for date-only values, UTC storage with display in SchoolSettings.timezone, the logger instead of console.log, and audit() for mutations to records owned by others.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: toggle buttons have screen-reader labels, and touch targets are at least 44×44 px.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, FR-3.8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Brownfield safety: reuse existing helpers, components and models, never rename routes or models, keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test green, and do not implement scope owned by PRD-14 (holidays) or PRD-15 (absence notes and the EXCUSED workflow).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Assumptions and constraints, Out of Scope\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-5: Should a minimal /admin/settings page (or an attendance section on it) be built, given that no school settings page or API route exists? Default: add a small 'Attendance settings' card editing attendanceMode and attendanceAlertThreshold, plus PATCH /api/settings/school built on updateSchoolSettings().\",\n        \"FR-16: Which route should the daily homeroom register use? Default: /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=, reusing the course register component.\",\n        \"FR-23: What metadata should attendance.corrected and attendance.register_missing have? Default: category ATTENDANCE, email false; corrected goes to PARENT+STUDENT, register_missing to TEACHER.\",\n        \"FR-21: The PRD's sample body is 'Mathematics – 7A, Period 1, ...'. For daily registers (no course or period), is '<Section> daily register, <date>' acceptable? Default: yes.\",\n        \"FR-28: Does 'current term' mean the Term whose startDate–endDate contains today in the current AcademicYear? Default: yes. If today falls between terms, use the most recent ended term.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-5 school settings page does not exist; proceeding with the default above (MEDIUM).\",\n        \"FR-16 daily register route not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\",\n        \"FR-23 notification metadata for attendance.corrected / attendance.register_missing not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0113xGKPdQDudwsXJpqWrCba","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
