{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm8Fco1nUNUwBRSFH42Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough context. Writing the notes file now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2149,"cache_read_input_tokens":40446,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2149},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c9af49-395f-43b5-8c02-c9a3647dc0ab","uuid":"71a982b8-7adc-4046-b76c-9bce2caa74b0","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:31:09.968Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm8FcarqTKcNFG2axPW6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm8Fco1nUNUwBRSFH42Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LsABFhPVaRxcbx7kSizRML","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-7\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T05:29:02Z), PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007).\nIt has 41 FRs and 10 NFRs (51 requirements) at 94% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-1 notes that were here before.\n\n**Headline:** this is a **greenfield feature inside a brownfield app**. Everything attendance-related is new: the\nmodels, migration, service, validators, 10 API routes (9 from FR-35 plus PATCH settings from FR-5), 4 page areas,\n2 tabs, nav entries, seed data and tests. It builds on these existing exports. I checked each one on disk:\n\n| Reuse | Location | Verified signature / note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Schedule | `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts:542` | `getScheduleForDate(target: {userId, role} \\| {sectionId}, date)` → `{period, course, room}[]`. Returns `[]` for ADMIN/PARENT and on non-teaching days. Has the PRD-14 holiday hook comment. `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` at :565 already finds the running period, so use it for the FR-6 highlight. |\n| Notify | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts:98` | `notifyStudentAndParents({...NotifyInput minus userIds, studentIds})` never throws. Title and body are per student, so call it **once per student** (FR-21). |\n| Notif types | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` map + `NotificationTypeDef {label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. The `ATTENDANCE` category already exists. |\n| Access | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | `assertCanManageCourse`, `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanViewStudent`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`'ALL' \\| string[]`). |\n| Settings | `src/server/services/settings.ts` | `getSchoolSettings()` (singleton upsert, `cache`d) and `updateSchoolSettings(input)`. **`UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` must gain** `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?`. |\n| Misc | `src/server/audit.ts`, `src/server/csv.ts`, `src/server/http.ts` | `audit(input)`, `toCsv(columns, rows)`, response helpers. |\n| UI | `src/components/<Name>/` | DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast. They are **not** in `components/shared/`. |\n| Extension points | `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | Arrays of `{key, label, href(id), roles}`. Append entries to them. |\n\nGaps confirmed on disk: `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty and `src/app/(app)/admin/` has only `courses`,\n`email-log` and `sections`, with no settings page. The latest migration is `20261106000000_user_role_status_index`.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Service**, **Validation**, **API**, **Auth Boundary**, **Notifications**,\n**UI: Register**, **UI: Tabs**, **UI: Admin**, **Config/Nav**, **Seed**, **Tests**, **Cross-cutting**.\n\n## Requirement → Concern table\n\n| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | New `AttendanceStatus` enum and `AttendanceSession` / `AttendanceRecord` models. Records use `@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` and `@@index([studentId, createdAt])`. `date` is `@db.Date` (NFR-8). The session needs a `takenById`/`updatedById` + `updatedAt` for FR-6/FR-14. Records need `minutesLate Int?` and `note String?` (FR-12). |\n| FR-2 | Data Model + Service | XOR courseId/sectionId: raw SQL `CHECK ((courseId IS NULL) <> (sectionId IS NULL))` in the migration, and a guard in the service before insert. |\n| FR-3 | Data Model (migration SQL) | Two partial unique indexes: `(courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL` and `(sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL`. Prisma can't express these, so they go in hand-written SQL in the migration after `20261106000000`. **Consequence:** `upsert` cannot target them. The service must use `findFirst` + create/update inside the transaction, and catch P2002 on a race. |\n| FR-4 | Data Model | `SchoolSettings.attendanceMode` (new enum `AttendanceMode`, default `PER_PERIOD`) and `attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)`. Same migration. |\n| FR-5 | API + UI: Admin (MEDIUM) | No settings page exists. Smallest fix: `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN, Zod-validated, calls the extended `updateSchoolSettings`) and an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance`. That avoids a new page. |\n| FR-6 | Service + UI: Register | `GET /api/attendance/today` → `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` joined with today's sessions to show \"Taken HH:mm by name\". Highlight comes from `getCurrentSlot`. Times are shown in the school tz. |\n| FR-7 | Service + UI | If mode ∈ {DAILY_HOMEROOM, BOTH}, add entries for `Section.homeroomTeacherId = user` to `/today`. |\n| FR-8 | Validation + Auth Boundary | Shared date rule in the validators: no future date (school tz). Teachers can go back 14 days, admins any date. The same rule runs on the client and the server. |\n| FR-9 | Service + UI: Register | Course roster = `Enrollment` where status ACTIVE on the date, sorted by last name. Use the MUI `ToggleButtonGroup` (exclusive). Initial state is null for a new register. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Boundary + Validation | The server rejects `EXCUSED` from non-ADMIN with 403/VALIDATION_ERROR. The UI disables it for teachers. |\n| FR-11 | UI: Register | Client-only: fill nulls with PRESENT. |\n| FR-12 | Validation + UI | `minutesLate` 1–240 is required iff LATE (Zod `superRefine`) and defaults to 5 in the UI. `note` max 500. |\n| FR-13 | UI: Register | Derived counters. Save is disabled while any row is unmarked. The server also requires a full roster (or at least one valid record per student sent). |\n| FR-14 | Service | One `prisma.$transaction`: find/create the session, then upsert the records (`@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` works for `upsert`). Set `updatedById` on the session. The GET returns last-changed-by/at. |\n| FR-15 | Service + Auth Boundary | Section variant: roster = `SectionMember` for the current academic year. Access = `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` or ADMIN. No existing `assertCanManageSection` helper, so add a small one in the attendance service (or `auth/`). |\n| FR-16 | UI: Register (LOW) | Route `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` component with a section-scoped GET/PUT. |\n| FR-17 | UI: Register | Mobile: rows ≥ 48 px, toggles ≥ 44×44, sticky `Paper` save bar. Use theme `sx` only. |\n| FR-18 | Service + Audit | Inside the save, diff old vs new per student. For changed existing records call `audit({action:'attendance.record.update', before, after, actor, note})`. |\n| FR-19 | Service + Auth Boundary | Pure function `canEdit(user, sessionDate, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today - date ≤ 14 days`. The GET returns `readOnly` + `readOnlyReason`. The PUT returns 403. Unit-tested (FR-39). |\n| FR-20 | Notifications | Add `attendance.absent` (ATTENDANCE, email true, mandatoryInApp true, PARENT+STUDENT) and `attendance.late` (email false). |\n| FR-21 | Notifications + Service | After commit (outside the tx), call `notifyStudentAndParents` per changed student. Daily-register body: `<Section> daily register, <date>` (intake default). Link `/students/<id>/attendance`. |\n| FR-22 | Notifications + Service | Pure `diffForNotifications(prev, next)` → `{absent[], late[], corrected[]}`. Only a transition *into* ABSENT/LATE sends a notice, so re-saving with the same status sends nothing. ABSENT→PRESENT sends `attendance.corrected`. Unit-tested (FR-39). |\n| FR-23 | Notifications (LOW) | `attendance.corrected` (ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false), `attendance.register_missing` (ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false). |\n| FR-24 | Config | Append `{key:'attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}` to `studentTabs`. |\n| FR-25 | Service + UI: Tabs | Term = the Term containing today, else the most recent ended term (intake default). Use `StatCard` ×4 for term and year. |\n| FR-26 | UI: Tabs | MUI X `DateCalendar` read-only with a custom `day` slot coloured from per-day aggregates and a `Tooltip`. Month change refetches or filters `?from=&to=`. |\n| FR-27 | API + Auth Boundary | `GET /api/students/:id/attendance` → `assertCanViewStudent`. **Strip `note`** for STUDENT/PARENT on the server (AC-8). The table uses `DataTable`. |\n| FR-28 | Service (pure) | `attendanceRate(records)` = (P+L+E)/total×100, rounded to 1 dp; empty → null. Include DROPPED enrollments (filter on student, not enrollment). Mode chooses the source: course sessions (PER_PERIOD/BOTH) or section sessions (DAILY_HOMEROOM). Unit-tested. |\n| FR-29 | API + UI: Tabs + Config | `GET /api/courses/:id/attendance` (`assertCanManageCourse`) → last 20 sessions × enrolled students. Use MUI X DataGrid with dynamic columns. The header click links to the register. Course tab roles: ADMIN, TEACHER. |\n| FR-30 | Service + UI: Admin | Overview: expected = all timetable slots for today (all teachers) + sections if the mode includes daily; taken = sessions today; rate today. ADMIN gets `[]` from `getScheduleForDate`, so it **needs a school-wide slot query** (a direct `timetableSlot.findMany` by `dayOfWeek`, or a new helper next to `getScheduleForDate`). |\n| FR-31 | Service + API + Notifications | Missing = expected meetings with no session and `now ≥ period.startTime + 15 min` (school tz). `POST /api/admin/attendance/remind` → `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[teacherId]})`. |\n| FR-32 | Service + API + Validation | Report filters (range ≤ 366 days, grade, section, course, status) go into a per-student aggregate (use a SQL `groupBy` for performance). `?format=csv` → `toCsv` with the same columns. |\n| FR-33 | Service + API | YTD rate per student < threshold, sorted ascending. Reuses the same aggregate as FR-32 with the year's date range. |\n| FR-34 | Config/Nav | `navigation.ts`: TEACHER → `/attendance/take`, ADMIN → `/admin/attendance`. |\n| FR-35 | API | The 9 listed routes, plus PATCH settings from FR-5. Every handler starts with `requireUser`/`requireRole` and then the resource assert. They use the `http.ts` helpers. |\n| FR-36 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts`: `registerQuery`, `registerPutBody`, `studentAttendanceQuery`, `reportFilters`, `remindBody`, `attendanceSettingsPatch`. The register form imports them too. |\n| FR-37 | Service | `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts`. Keep the pure helpers (`attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`) in the same file or a sibling `attendance-rules.ts` so the tests need no DB. |\n| FR-38 | Seed | Extend the existing seed. Use a seeded RNG, 15 teaching days before the run date, 7A and 7B, a 94/3/3 split, and two Grade 7 students forced below 85%. Respect the existing school-day config. |\n| FR-39 | Tests (unit) | `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`. |\n| FR-40 | Tests (integration) | The save transaction, non-enrolled rejection (NFR-3), and the partial unique indexes (a duplicate insert raises). |\n| FR-41 | Tests (e2e) | Playwright: the 375 px take flow, and a parent seeing the notification plus the calendar absence. |\n| NFR-1 | Performance | Save: one tx with batched upserts (≈35). Avoid N+1 by loading existing records in one query. Student tab: one indexed query on `[studentId, createdAt]` (consider filtering on `session.date` and adding an index if needed). Aggregate in memory (1,200 rows is fine). |\n| NFR-2 | UI: Register (client) | localStorage key `attendance:<course\\|section>:<id>:<date>:<periodId\\|daily>`. Write it on a network failure, clear it on success, and offer a restore banner when it is present. |\n| NFR-3 | Service (integrity) | Validate every `studentId` against the ACTIVE enrollment on the date (`enrolledAt ≤ date` and not dropped before it) or the section membership. Any miss → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR and the whole save is rejected. |\n| NFR-4 | UI: Register | Satisfied by FR-11 + FR-17 (mark all present, then fix the exceptions). |\n| NFR-5 | Notifications | `notify()` writes in-app notifications immediately and queues EmailOutbox. Call it post-commit without blocking the response on email. |\n| NFR-6 | Cross-cutting (UI) | MUI only. Dev must use mui-mcp docs for 9.5.0 (ToggleButtonGroup, DateCalendar day slot, DataGrid, Paper sticky). **Hard blocker if unreachable.** |\n| NFR-7 | Auth Boundary | Server-side checks on every handler and server page. Per-role scope is listed above. Teachers also get their homeroom sections. |\n| NFR-8 | Cross-cutting | `@db.Date`, cuid IDs, UTC storage with display in school tz (`date-fns-tz`, already installed), the logger, `audit()` for edits to records owned by others, and pageSize ≤ 100 on the report and student records. |\n| NFR-9 | UI accessibility | `aria-label` on each toggle (\"Mark <name> present\"), 44 px targets. |\n| NFR-10 | Cross-cutting | Reuse the helpers above, add no new deps, rename nothing. Holidays (PRD-14) and the EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) are out of scope beyond the admin-only option. |\n\n## Open points for `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **Intake blockers (for the Overview):** FR-5 (MEDIUM), FR-16 (LOW), FR-23 (LOW) and the NFR-6 mui-mcp hard dependency. The defaults are listed above.\n2. **Partial unique indexes vs Prisma upsert (FR-3/FR-14):** sessions can't be `upsert`ed via Prisma. Use find + create in the tx and catch P2002 → retry as an update.\n3. **Admin school-wide schedule (FR-30/31):** `getScheduleForDate` returns `[]` for ADMIN. It needs a school-wide slot query. Prefer a small exported helper in `timetable-service.ts` over duplicating `slotInclude` logic.\n4. **Section access helper (FR-15):** none exists today. Add one small function and don't generalise it.\n5. **\"ACTIVE on date\" (NFR-3):** `Enrollment` has `enrolledAt`/`droppedAt`. Define the rule as `enrolledAt ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt > date)`. For back-dated registers, the roster should use the same rule.\n6. **Rate source by mode (FR-28):** in BOTH mode, rates use the per-period records only. Daily records are stored but not counted.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2149,"cache_read_input_tokens":40446,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2149},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c9af49-395f-43b5-8c02-c9a3647dc0ab","uuid":"717ce502-6f4f-4436-8084-475ca5d4e188","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:32:03.156Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm8FcarqTKcNFG2axPW6","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LsABFhPVaRxcbx7kSizRML":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-7\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T05:29:02Z), PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007).\nIt has 41 FRs and 10 NFRs (51 requirements) at 94% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-1 notes that were here before.\n\n**Headline:** this is a **greenfield feature inside a brownfield app**. Everything attendance-related is new: the\nmodels, migration, service, validators, 10 API routes (9 from FR-35 plus PATCH settings from FR-5), 4 page areas,\n2 tabs, nav entries, seed data and tests. It builds on these existing exports. I checked each one on disk:\n\n| Reuse | Location | Verified signature / note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Schedule | `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts:542` | `getScheduleForDate(target: {userId, role} \\| {sectionId}, date)` → `{period, course, room}[]`. Returns `[]` for ADMIN/PARENT and on non-teaching days. Has the PRD-14 holiday hook comment. `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` at :565 already finds the running period, so use it for the FR-6 highlight. |\n| Notify | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts:98` | `notifyStudentAndParents({...NotifyInput minus userIds, studentIds})` never throws. Title and body are per student, so call it **once per student** (FR-21). |\n| Notif types | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` map + `NotificationTypeDef {label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. The `ATTENDANCE` category already exists. |\n| Access | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | `assertCanManageCourse`, `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanViewStudent`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`'ALL' \\| string[]`). |\n| Settings | `src/server/services/settings.ts` | `getSchoolSettings()` (singleton upsert, `cache`d) and `updateSchoolSettings(input)`. **`UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` must gain** `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?`. |\n| Misc | `src/server/audit.ts`, `src/server/csv.ts`, `src/server/http.ts` | `audit(input)`, `toCsv(columns, rows)`, response helpers. |\n| UI | `src/components/<Name>/` | DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast. They are **not** in `components/shared/`. |\n| Extension points | `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | Arrays of `{key, label, href(id), roles}`. Append entries to them. |\n\nGaps confirmed on disk: `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty and `src/app/(app)/admin/` has only `courses`,\n`email-log` and `sections`, with no settings page. The latest migration is `20261106000000_user_role_status_index`.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Service**, **Validation**, **API**, **Auth Boundary**, **Notifications**,\n**UI: Register**, **UI: Tabs**, **UI: Admin**, **Config/Nav**, **Seed**, **Tests**, **Cross-cutting**.\n\n## Requirement → Concern table\n\n| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | New `AttendanceStatus` enum and `AttendanceSession` / `AttendanceRecord` models. Records use `@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` and `@@index([studentId, createdAt])`. `date` is `@db.Date` (NFR-8). The session needs a `takenById`/`updatedById` + `updatedAt` for FR-6/FR-14. Records need `minutesLate Int?` and `note String?` (FR-12). |\n| FR-2 | Data Model + Service | XOR courseId/sectionId: raw SQL `CHECK ((courseId IS NULL) <> (sectionId IS NULL))` in the migration, and a guard in the service before insert. |\n| FR-3 | Data Model (migration SQL) | Two partial unique indexes: `(courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL` and `(sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL`. Prisma can't express these, so they go in hand-written SQL in the migration after `20261106000000`. **Consequence:** `upsert` cannot target them. The service must use `findFirst` + create/update inside the transaction, and catch P2002 on a race. |\n| FR-4 | Data Model | `SchoolSettings.attendanceMode` (new enum `AttendanceMode`, default `PER_PERIOD`) and `attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)`. Same migration. |\n| FR-5 | API + UI: Admin (MEDIUM) | No settings page exists. Smallest fix: `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN, Zod-validated, calls the extended `updateSchoolSettings`) and an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance`. That avoids a new page. |\n| FR-6 | Service + UI: Register | `GET /api/attendance/today` → `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` joined with today's sessions to show \"Taken HH:mm by name\". Highlight comes from `getCurrentSlot`. Times are shown in the school tz. |\n| FR-7 | Service + UI | If mode ∈ {DAILY_HOMEROOM, BOTH}, add entries for `Section.homeroomTeacherId = user` to `/today`. |\n| FR-8 | Validation + Auth Boundary | Shared date rule in the validators: no future date (school tz). Teachers can go back 14 days, admins any date. The same rule runs on the client and the server. |\n| FR-9 | Service + UI: Register | Course roster = `Enrollment` where status ACTIVE on the date, sorted by last name. Use the MUI `ToggleButtonGroup` (exclusive). Initial state is null for a new register. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Boundary + Validation | The server rejects `EXCUSED` from non-ADMIN with 403/VALIDATION_ERROR. The UI disables it for teachers. |\n| FR-11 | UI: Register | Client-only: fill nulls with PRESENT. |\n| FR-12 | Validation + UI | `minutesLate` 1–240 is required iff LATE (Zod `superRefine`) and defaults to 5 in the UI. `note` max 500. |\n| FR-13 | UI: Register | Derived counters. Save is disabled while any row is unmarked. The server also requires a full roster (or at least one valid record per student sent). |\n| FR-14 | Service | One `prisma.$transaction`: find/create the session, then upsert the records (`@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` works for `upsert`). Set `updatedById` on the session. The GET returns last-changed-by/at. |\n| FR-15 | Service + Auth Boundary | Section variant: roster = `SectionMember` for the current academic year. Access = `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` or ADMIN. No existing `assertCanManageSection` helper, so add a small one in the attendance service (or `auth/`). |\n| FR-16 | UI: Register (LOW) | Route `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` component with a section-scoped GET/PUT. |\n| FR-17 | UI: Register | Mobile: rows ≥ 48 px, toggles ≥ 44×44, sticky `Paper` save bar. Use theme `sx` only. |\n| FR-18 | Service + Audit | Inside the save, diff old vs new per student. For changed existing records call `audit({action:'attendance.record.update', before, after, actor, note})`. |\n| FR-19 | Service + Auth Boundary | Pure function `canEdit(user, sessionDate, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today - date ≤ 14 days`. The GET returns `readOnly` + `readOnlyReason`. The PUT returns 403. Unit-tested (FR-39). |\n| FR-20 | Notifications | Add `attendance.absent` (ATTENDANCE, email true, mandatoryInApp true, PARENT+STUDENT) and `attendance.late` (email false). |\n| FR-21 | Notifications + Service | After commit (outside the tx), call `notifyStudentAndParents` per changed student. Daily-register body: `<Section> daily register, <date>` (intake default). Link `/students/<id>/attendance`. |\n| FR-22 | Notifications + Service | Pure `diffForNotifications(prev, next)` → `{absent[], late[], corrected[]}`. Only a transition *into* ABSENT/LATE sends a notice, so re-saving with the same status sends nothing. ABSENT→PRESENT sends `attendance.corrected`. Unit-tested (FR-39). |\n| FR-23 | Notifications (LOW) | `attendance.corrected` (ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false), `attendance.register_missing` (ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false). |\n| FR-24 | Config | Append `{key:'attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}` to `studentTabs`. |\n| FR-25 | Service + UI: Tabs | Term = the Term containing today, else the most recent ended term (intake default). Use `StatCard` ×4 for term and year. |\n| FR-26 | UI: Tabs | MUI X `DateCalendar` read-only with a custom `day` slot coloured from per-day aggregates and a `Tooltip`. Month change refetches or filters `?from=&to=`. |\n| FR-27 | API + Auth Boundary | `GET /api/students/:id/attendance` → `assertCanViewStudent`. **Strip `note`** for STUDENT/PARENT on the server (AC-8). The table uses `DataTable`. |\n| FR-28 | Service (pure) | `attendanceRate(records)` = (P+L+E)/total×100, rounded to 1 dp; empty → null. Include DROPPED enrollments (filter on student, not enrollment). Mode chooses the source: course sessions (PER_PERIOD/BOTH) or section sessions (DAILY_HOMEROOM). Unit-tested. |\n| FR-29 | API + UI: Tabs + Config | `GET /api/courses/:id/attendance` (`assertCanManageCourse`) → last 20 sessions × enrolled students. Use MUI X DataGrid with dynamic columns. The header click links to the register. Course tab roles: ADMIN, TEACHER. |\n| FR-30 | Service + UI: Admin | Overview: expected = all timetable slots for today (all teachers) + sections if the mode includes daily; taken = sessions today; rate today. ADMIN gets `[]` from `getScheduleForDate`, so it **needs a school-wide slot query** (a direct `timetableSlot.findMany` by `dayOfWeek`, or a new helper next to `getScheduleForDate`). |\n| FR-31 | Service + API + Notifications | Missing = expected meetings with no session and `now ≥ period.startTime + 15 min` (school tz). `POST /api/admin/attendance/remind` → `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[teacherId]})`. |\n| FR-32 | Service + API + Validation | Report filters (range ≤ 366 days, grade, section, course, status) go into a per-student aggregate (use a SQL `groupBy` for performance). `?format=csv` → `toCsv` with the same columns. |\n| FR-33 | Service + API | YTD rate per student < threshold, sorted ascending. Reuses the same aggregate as FR-32 with the year's date range. |\n| FR-34 | Config/Nav | `navigation.ts`: TEACHER → `/attendance/take`, ADMIN → `/admin/attendance`. |\n| FR-35 | API | The 9 listed routes, plus PATCH settings from FR-5. Every handler starts with `requireUser`/`requireRole` and then the resource assert. They use the `http.ts` helpers. |\n| FR-36 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts`: `registerQuery`, `registerPutBody`, `studentAttendanceQuery`, `reportFilters`, `remindBody`, `attendanceSettingsPatch`. The register form imports them too. |\n| FR-37 | Service | `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts`. Keep the pure helpers (`attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`) in the same file or a sibling `attendance-rules.ts` so the tests need no DB. |\n| FR-38 | Seed | Extend the existing seed. Use a seeded RNG, 15 teaching days before the run date, 7A and 7B, a 94/3/3 split, and two Grade 7 students forced below 85%. Respect the existing school-day config. |\n| FR-39 | Tests (unit) | `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`. |\n| FR-40 | Tests (integration) | The save transaction, non-enrolled rejection (NFR-3), and the partial unique indexes (a duplicate insert raises). |\n| FR-41 | Tests (e2e) | Playwright: the 375 px take flow, and a parent seeing the notification plus the calendar absence. |\n| NFR-1 | Performance | Save: one tx with batched upserts (≈35). Avoid N+1 by loading existing records in one query. Student tab: one indexed query on `[studentId, createdAt]` (consider filtering on `session.date` and adding an index if needed). Aggregate in memory (1,200 rows is fine). |\n| NFR-2 | UI: Register (client) | localStorage key `attendance:<course\\|section>:<id>:<date>:<periodId\\|daily>`. Write it on a network failure, clear it on success, and offer a restore banner when it is present. |\n| NFR-3 | Service (integrity) | Validate every `studentId` against the ACTIVE enrollment on the date (`enrolledAt ≤ date` and not dropped before it) or the section membership. Any miss → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR and the whole save is rejected. |\n| NFR-4 | UI: Register | Satisfied by FR-11 + FR-17 (mark all present, then fix the exceptions). |\n| NFR-5 | Notifications | `notify()` writes in-app notifications immediately and queues EmailOutbox. Call it post-commit without blocking the response on email. |\n| NFR-6 | Cross-cutting (UI) | MUI only. Dev must use mui-mcp docs for 9.5.0 (ToggleButtonGroup, DateCalendar day slot, DataGrid, Paper sticky). **Hard blocker if unreachable.** |\n| NFR-7 | Auth Boundary | Server-side checks on every handler and server page. Per-role scope is listed above. Teachers also get their homeroom sections. |\n| NFR-8 | Cross-cutting | `@db.Date`, cuid IDs, UTC storage with display in school tz (`date-fns-tz`, already installed), the logger, `audit()` for edits to records owned by others, and pageSize ≤ 100 on the report and student records. |\n| NFR-9 | UI accessibility | `aria-label` on each toggle (\"Mark <name> present\"), 44 px targets. |\n| NFR-10 | Cross-cutting | Reuse the helpers above, add no new deps, rename nothing. Holidays (PRD-14) and the EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) are out of scope beyond the admin-only option. |\n\n## Open points for `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **Intake blockers (for the Overview):** FR-5 (MEDIUM), FR-16 (LOW), FR-23 (LOW) and the NFR-6 mui-mcp hard dependency. The defaults are listed above.\n2. **Partial unique indexes vs Prisma upsert (FR-3/FR-14):** sessions can't be `upsert`ed via Prisma. Use find + create in the tx and catch P2002 → retry as an update.\n3. **Admin school-wide schedule (FR-30/31):** `getScheduleForDate` returns `[]` for ADMIN. It needs a school-wide slot query. Prefer a small exported helper in `timetable-service.ts` over duplicating `slotInclude` logic.\n4. **Section access helper (FR-15):** none exists today. Add one small function and don't generalise it.\n5. **\"ACTIVE on date\" (NFR-3):** `Enrollment` has `enrolledAt`/`droppedAt`. Define the rule as `enrolledAt ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt > date)`. For back-dated registers, the roster should use the same rule.\n6. **Rate source by mode (FR-28):** in BOTH mode, rates use the per-period records only. Daily records are stored but not counted.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LsABFhPVaRxcbx7kSizRML","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69c9af49-395f-43b5-8c02-c9a3647dc0ab","uuid":"63824041-de98-427a-bac8-d22b0e0025ce","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:32:03.552Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-7\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T05:29:02Z), PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007).\nIt has 41 FRs and 10 NFRs (51 requirements) at 94% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-1 notes that were here before.\n\n**Headline:** this is a **greenfield feature inside a brownfield app**. Everything attendance-related is new: the\nmodels, migration, service, validators, 10 API routes (9 from FR-35 plus PATCH settings from FR-5), 4 page areas,\n2 tabs, nav entries, seed data and tests. It builds on these existing exports. I checked each one on disk:\n\n| Reuse | Location | Verified signature / note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Schedule | `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts:542` | `getScheduleForDate(target: {userId, role} \\| {sectionId}, date)` → `{period, course, room}[]`. Returns `[]` for ADMIN/PARENT and on non-teaching days. Has the PRD-14 holiday hook comment. `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` at :565 already finds the running period, so use it for the FR-6 highlight. |\n| Notify | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts:98` | `notifyStudentAndParents({...NotifyInput minus userIds, studentIds})` never throws. Title and body are per student, so call it **once per student** (FR-21). |\n| Notif types | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` map + `NotificationTypeDef {label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. The `ATTENDANCE` category already exists. |\n| Access | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | `assertCanManageCourse`, `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanViewStudent`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`'ALL' \\| string[]`). |\n| Settings | `src/server/services/settings.ts` | `getSchoolSettings()` (singleton upsert, `cache`d) and `updateSchoolSettings(input)`. **`UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` must gain** `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?`. |\n| Misc | `src/server/audit.ts`, `src/server/csv.ts`, `src/server/http.ts` | `audit(input)`, `toCsv(columns, rows)`, response helpers. |\n| UI | `src/components/<Name>/` | DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast. They are **not** in `components/shared/`. |\n| Extension points | `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | Arrays of `{key, label, href(id), roles}`. Append entries to them. |\n\nGaps confirmed on disk: `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty and `src/app/(app)/admin/` has only `courses`,\n`email-log` and `sections`, with no settings page. The latest migration is `20261106000000_user_role_status_index`.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Service**, **Validation**, **API**, **Auth Boundary**, **Notifications**,\n**UI: Register**, **UI: Tabs**, **UI: Admin**, **Config/Nav**, **Seed**, **Tests**, **Cross-cutting**.\n\n## Requirement → Concern table\n\n| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | New `AttendanceStatus` enum and `AttendanceSession` / `AttendanceRecord` models. Records use `@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` and `@@index([studentId, createdAt])`. `date` is `@db.Date` (NFR-8). The session needs a `takenById`/`updatedById` + `updatedAt` for FR-6/FR-14. Records need `minutesLate Int?` and `note String?` (FR-12). |\n| FR-2 | Data Model + Service | XOR courseId/sectionId: raw SQL `CHECK ((courseId IS NULL) <> (sectionId IS NULL))` in the migration, and a guard in the service before insert. |\n| FR-3 | Data Model (migration SQL) | Two partial unique indexes: `(courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL` and `(sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL`. Prisma can't express these, so they go in hand-written SQL in the migration after `20261106000000`. **Consequence:** `upsert` cannot target them. The service must use `findFirst` + create/update inside the transaction, and catch P2002 on a race. |\n| FR-4 | Data Model | `SchoolSettings.attendanceMode` (new enum `AttendanceMode`, default `PER_PERIOD`) and `attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)`. Same migration. |\n| FR-5 | API + UI: Admin (MEDIUM) | No settings page exists. Smallest fix: `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN, Zod-validated, calls the extended `updateSchoolSettings`) and an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance`. That avoids a new page. |\n| FR-6 | Service + UI: Register | `GET /api/attendance/today` → `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` joined with today's sessions to show \"Taken HH:mm by name\". Highlight comes from `getCurrentSlot`. Times are shown in the school tz. |\n| FR-7 | Service + UI | If mode ∈ {DAILY_HOMEROOM, BOTH}, add entries for `Section.homeroomTeacherId = user` to `/today`. |\n| FR-8 | Validation + Auth Boundary | Shared date rule in the validators: no future date (school tz). Teachers can go back 14 days, admins any date. The same rule runs on the client and the server. |\n| FR-9 | Service + UI: Register | Course roster = `Enrollment` where status ACTIVE on the date, sorted by last name. Use the MUI `ToggleButtonGroup` (exclusive). Initial state is null for a new register. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Boundary + Validation | The server rejects `EXCUSED` from non-ADMIN with 403/VALIDATION_ERROR. The UI disables it for teachers. |\n| FR-11 | UI: Register | Client-only: fill nulls with PRESENT. |\n| FR-12 | Validation + UI | `minutesLate` 1–240 is required iff LATE (Zod `superRefine`) and defaults to 5 in the UI. `note` max 500. |\n| FR-13 | UI: Register | Derived counters. Save is disabled while any row is unmarked. The server also requires a full roster (or at least one valid record per student sent). |\n| FR-14 | Service | One `prisma.$transaction`: find/create the session, then upsert the records (`@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` works for `upsert`). Set `updatedById` on the session. The GET returns last-changed-by/at. |\n| FR-15 | Service + Auth Boundary | Section variant: roster = `SectionMember` for the current academic year. Access = `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` or ADMIN. No existing `assertCanManageSection` helper, so add a small one in the attendance service (or `auth/`). |\n| FR-16 | UI: Register (LOW) | Route `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` component with a section-scoped GET/PUT. |\n| FR-17 | UI: Register | Mobile: rows ≥ 48 px, toggles ≥ 44×44, sticky `Paper` save bar. Use theme `sx` only. |\n| FR-18 | Service + Audit | Inside the save, diff old vs new per student. For changed existing records call `audit({action:'attendance.record.update', before, after, actor, note})`. |\n| FR-19 | Service + Auth Boundary | Pure function `canEdit(user, sessionDate, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today - date ≤ 14 days`. The GET returns `readOnly` + `readOnlyReason`. The PUT returns 403. Unit-tested (FR-39). |\n| FR-20 | Notifications | Add `attendance.absent` (ATTENDANCE, email true, mandatoryInApp true, PARENT+STUDENT) and `attendance.late` (email false). |\n| FR-21 | Notifications + Service | After commit (outside the tx), call `notifyStudentAndParents` per changed student. Daily-register body: `<Section> daily register, <date>` (intake default). Link `/students/<id>/attendance`. |\n| FR-22 | Notifications + Service | Pure `diffForNotifications(prev, next)` → `{absent[], late[], corrected[]}`. Only a transition *into* ABSENT/LATE sends a notice, so re-saving with the same status sends nothing. ABSENT→PRESENT sends `attendance.corrected`. Unit-tested (FR-39). |\n| FR-23 | Notifications (LOW) | `attendance.corrected` (ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false), `attendance.register_missing` (ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false). |\n| FR-24 | Config | Append `{key:'attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}` to `studentTabs`. |\n| FR-25 | Service + UI: Tabs | Term = the Term containing today, else the most recent ended term (intake default). Use `StatCard` ×4 for term and year. |\n| FR-26 | UI: Tabs | MUI X `DateCalendar` read-only with a custom `day` slot coloured from per-day aggregates and a `Tooltip`. Month change refetches or filters `?from=&to=`. |\n| FR-27 | API + Auth Boundary | `GET /api/students/:id/attendance` → `assertCanViewStudent`. **Strip `note`** for STUDENT/PARENT on the server (AC-8). The table uses `DataTable`. |\n| FR-28 | Service (pure) | `attendanceRate(records)` = (P+L+E)/total×100, rounded to 1 dp; empty → null. Include DROPPED enrollments (filter on student, not enrollment). Mode chooses the source: course sessions (PER_PERIOD/BOTH) or section sessions (DAILY_HOMEROOM). Unit-tested. |\n| FR-29 | API + UI: Tabs + Config | `GET /api/courses/:id/attendance` (`assertCanManageCourse`) → last 20 sessions × enrolled students. Use MUI X DataGrid with dynamic columns. The header click links to the register. Course tab roles: ADMIN, TEACHER. |\n| FR-30 | Service + UI: Admin | Overview: expected = all timetable slots for today (all teachers) + sections if the mode includes daily; taken = sessions today; rate today. ADMIN gets `[]` from `getScheduleForDate`, so it **needs a school-wide slot query** (a direct `timetableSlot.findMany` by `dayOfWeek`, or a new helper next to `getScheduleForDate`). |\n| FR-31 | Service + API + Notifications | Missing = expected meetings with no session and `now ≥ period.startTime + 15 min` (school tz). `POST /api/admin/attendance/remind` → `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[teacherId]})`. |\n| FR-32 | Service + API + Validation | Report filters (range ≤ 366 days, grade, section, course, status) go into a per-student aggregate (use a SQL `groupBy` for performance). `?format=csv` → `toCsv` with the same columns. |\n| FR-33 | Service + API | YTD rate per student < threshold, sorted ascending. Reuses the same aggregate as FR-32 with the year's date range. |\n| FR-34 | Config/Nav | `navigation.ts`: TEACHER → `/attendance/take`, ADMIN → `/admin/attendance`. |\n| FR-35 | API | The 9 listed routes, plus PATCH settings from FR-5. Every handler starts with `requireUser`/`requireRole` and then the resource assert. They use the `http.ts` helpers. |\n| FR-36 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts`: `registerQuery`, `registerPutBody`, `studentAttendanceQuery`, `reportFilters`, `remindBody`, `attendanceSettingsPatch`. The register form imports them too. |\n| FR-37 | Service | `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts`. Keep the pure helpers (`attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`) in the same file or a sibling `attendance-rules.ts` so the tests need no DB. |\n| FR-38 | Seed | Extend the existing seed. Use a seeded RNG, 15 teaching days before the run date, 7A and 7B, a 94/3/3 split, and two Grade 7 students forced below 85%. Respect the existing school-day config. |\n| FR-39 | Tests (unit) | `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`. |\n| FR-40 | Tests (integration) | The save transaction, non-enrolled rejection (NFR-3), and the partial unique indexes (a duplicate insert raises). |\n| FR-41 | Tests (e2e) | Playwright: the 375 px take flow, and a parent seeing the notification plus the calendar absence. |\n| NFR-1 | Performance | Save: one tx with batched upserts (≈35). Avoid N+1 by loading existing records in one query. Student tab: one indexed query on `[studentId, createdAt]` (consider filtering on `session.date` and adding an index if needed). Aggregate in memory (1,200 rows is fine). |\n| NFR-2 | UI: Register (client) | localStorage key `attendance:<course\\|section>:<id>:<date>:<periodId\\|daily>`. Write it on a network failure, clear it on success, and offer a restore banner when it is present. |\n| NFR-3 | Service (integrity) | Validate every `studentId` against the ACTIVE enrollment on the date (`enrolledAt ≤ date` and not dropped before it) or the section membership. Any miss → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR and the whole save is rejected. |\n| NFR-4 | UI: Register | Satisfied by FR-11 + FR-17 (mark all present, then fix the exceptions). |\n| NFR-5 | Notifications | `notify()` writes in-app notifications immediately and queues EmailOutbox. Call it post-commit without blocking the response on email. |\n| NFR-6 | Cross-cutting (UI) | MUI only. Dev must use mui-mcp docs for 9.5.0 (ToggleButtonGroup, DateCalendar day slot, DataGrid, Paper sticky). **Hard blocker if unreachable.** |\n| NFR-7 | Auth Boundary | Server-side checks on every handler and server page. Per-role scope is listed above. Teachers also get their homeroom sections. |\n| NFR-8 | Cross-cutting | `@db.Date`, cuid IDs, UTC storage with display in school tz (`date-fns-tz`, already installed), the logger, `audit()` for edits to records owned by others, and pageSize ≤ 100 on the report and student records. |\n| NFR-9 | UI accessibility | `aria-label` on each toggle (\"Mark <name> present\"), 44 px targets. |\n| NFR-10 | Cross-cutting | Reuse the helpers above, add no new deps, rename nothing. Holidays (PRD-14) and the EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) are out of scope beyond the admin-only option. |\n\n## Open points for `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **Intake blockers (for the Overview):** FR-5 (MEDIUM), FR-16 (LOW), FR-23 (LOW) and the NFR-6 mui-mcp hard dependency. The defaults are listed above.\n2. **Partial unique indexes vs Prisma upsert (FR-3/FR-14):** sessions can't be `upsert`ed via Prisma. Use find + create in the tx and catch P2002 → retry as an update.\n3. **Admin school-wide schedule (FR-30/31):** `getScheduleForDate` returns `[]` for ADMIN. It needs a school-wide slot query. Prefer a small exported helper in `timetable-service.ts` over duplicating `slotInclude` logic.\n4. **Section access helper (FR-15):** none exists today. Add one small function and don't generalise it.\n5. **\"ACTIVE on date\" (NFR-3):** `Enrollment` has `enrolledAt`/`droppedAt`. Define the rule as `enrolledAt ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt > date)`. For back-dated registers, the roster should use the same rule.\n6. **Rate source by mode (FR-28):** in BOTH mode, rates use the per-period records only. Daily records are stored but not counted.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":111,"newStart":1,"newLines":94,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-1","+# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-7"," "," Written by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z) for PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001).","-It has 34 FRs and 15 NFRs (49 requirements) at 97% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 5 blockers.","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T05:29:02Z), PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007).","+It has 41 FRs and 10 NFRs (51 requirements) at 94% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers."," Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`."," ","-> This file replaces an earlier SH-1 notes file. That version listed `/login`, the seed users and the role/status","-> migration as new work. All three are now **present** on disk.","+> This file replaces the stale SH-1 notes that were here before."," ","-**Headline:** this is a **UI-gap + tests** ticket. The backend, every API route, `/login`, the seed and the","-migration already exist. The design adds **4 pages**, rewires the **shell**, and adds **tests**.","-**No new endpoint, service, model or migration is needed.** `arch-api-contracts` documents the 5 existing routes as they are.","+**Headline:** this is a **greenfield feature inside a brownfield app**. Everything attendance-related is new: the","+models, migration, service, validators, 10 API routes (9 from FR-35 plus PATCH settings from FR-5), 4 page areas,","+2 tabs, nav entries, seed data and tests. It builds on these existing exports. I checked each one on disk:"," ","-Concern buckets: **Data Model**, **Auth Core**, **Service**, **API (existing)**, **UI: Auth Pages**,","-**UI: Account**, **UI: Shell**, **Access Control**, **Security**, **Audit**, **Seed**, **Accessibility**,","-**UI Rules**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.","+| Reuse | Location | Verified signature / note |","+|---|---|---|","+| Schedule | `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts:542` | `getScheduleForDate(target: {userId, role} \\| {sectionId}, date)` → `{period, course, room}[]`. Returns `[]` for ADMIN/PARENT and on non-teaching days. Has the PRD-14 holiday hook comment. `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` at :565 already finds the running period, so use it for the FR-6 highlight. |","+| Notify | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts:98` | `notifyStudentAndParents({...NotifyInput minus userIds, studentIds})` never throws. Title and body are per student, so call it **once per student** (FR-21). |","+| Notif types | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` map + `NotificationTypeDef {label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. The `ATTENDANCE` category already exists. |","+| Access | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | `assertCanManageCourse`, `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanViewStudent`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`'ALL' \\| string[]`). |","+| Settings | `src/server/services/settings.ts` | `getSchoolSettings()` (singleton upsert, `cache`d) and `updateSchoolSettings(input)`. **`UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` must gain** `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?`. |","+| Misc | `src/server/audit.ts`, `src/server/csv.ts`, `src/server/http.ts` | `audit(input)`, `toCsv(columns, rows)`, response helpers. |","+| UI | `src/components/<Name>/` | DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast. They are **not** in `components/shared/`. |","+| Extension points | `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | Arrays of `{key, label, href(id), roles}`. Append entries to them. |"," ","-## Brownfield facts verified on disk","+Gaps confirmed on disk: `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty and `src/app/(app)/admin/` has only `courses`,","+`email-log` and `sections`, with no settings page. The latest migration is `20261106000000_user_role_status_index`."," ","-| # | Fact | Design implication |","-|---|------|--------------------|","-| B1 | `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` already renders the centred Card shell. | New auth pages render only the card body. |","-| B2 | `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure`. Today only `LoginForm` imports any of them. | Invite and reset pages **reuse `SetPasswordForm`**. `/account/security` reuses `PasswordChecklist`, `passwordInputSlot`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors`. Do not add a second fetch or checklist helper. |","-| B3 | `SetPasswordForm` **requires `email`**, because the policy rejects a password equal to the email. | `/reset-password/[token]` must also call `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` server-side, to get the email and to show the invalid-link state before the form renders. |","-| B4 | `tokens.ts` `verifyToken(raw, type)` is read-only. `consumeToken` throws `INVALID_TOKEN` on a double submit. | The token pages are **server components** that call `verifyToken`. They show user data or the invalid-link `Alert`. No new endpoint. |","-| B5 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` maps to **410**, a code outside the NFR-10 list. The service copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | Keep this (NFR-13). The UI handles 410 `INVALID_TOKEN` by switching to the page's invalid-link copy. `arch-api-contracts` should document the 410. |","-| B6 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** create a session. | FR-14 flow on the client: POST `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. |","-| B7 | `/login` already exists. `LoginForm({ callbackUrl, reset })` fires a `useToast` once when `reset` is set, and exports `loginErrorMessage` (unit-tested). | FR-19 redirects to `/login?reset=1`. **Do not touch `/login`.** FR-2, FR-4, FR-6 and FR-7 only need verification. Intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date: `loginErrorMessage` covers `rate_limited`. Dev should verify this. |","-| B8 | `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`. The `jwt` callback keeps the current session alive on `reauth`. | FR-20 \"re-issue the current session\" is done server-side. The page only POSTs, then shows a toast and resets the form. |","-| B9 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders `<AppShell schoolShortName>` and does no auth. `providers.tsx` has no `SessionProvider`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user: SessionUser` (`id`, `role`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `email`) to `AppShell`. **Prop, not `useSession`**, so no provider is needed. This is the one source of the current user (FR-25). |","-| B10 | `shell.tsx` uses `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167). Its menu has 2 `MenuItem`s that only close the menu, and there is no `signOut`. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26 and FR-27 are all in this one file plus the layout. Sign out is `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`. |","-| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | Middleware needs no change (FR-11, NFR-14). |","-| B12 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. `requestPasswordReset` throws `RATE_LIMITED`. | `/forgot-password` shows `data.message` from the API rather than retyping the string, and shows an error `Alert` on 429. |","-| B13 | `src/app/forbidden/page.tsx` exists. | `requirePageRole` → `/forbidden` is already wired (FR-23). |","-| B14 | Existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) call `page.goto('/dashboard')` with no sign-in. The middleware already requires a session. | **Regression risk (NFR-13).** These specs are probably already failing, or will once the layout calls `requirePageUser`. Add one shared e2e sign-in helper using the seed users and reuse it in the existing specs. |","+Concern buckets: **Data Model**, **Service**, **Validation**, **API**, **Auth Boundary**, **Notifications**,","+**UI: Register**, **UI: Tabs**, **UI: Admin**, **Config/Nav**, **Seed**, **Tests**, **Cross-cutting**."," ","-## Requirement → architectural concern","+## Requirement → Concern table"," ","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|-----|---------|-------|","-| FR-1 | Data Model | Present. No change. |","-| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | `/login` is present (B7). Verify only. |","-| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`. Verify via the integration test. |","-| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Present (`loginErrorMessage`). Verify only. |","-| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`). Covered by the authorize integration test. |","-| FR-6 | Auth Core / UI | Limiter and message are both present (B7). Verify only. |","-| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | Present (`safeCallbackUrl` in `LoginForm`). Verify only. |","-| FR-8 | Audit | Emitted by `authorize`. The integration test asserts the AuditLog rows. |","-| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present. No change. |","-| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`, `reauth`). The change-password integration test covers `passwordChangedAt`. |","-| FR-11 | Access Control | Present (B11). No change. |","-| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. Pages call `verifyToken` only and never hash anything (B4). |","-| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: read-only name and email + `SetPasswordForm`. Invalid, used or expired: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. |","-| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client flow from B6. A 410 response switches to the invalid-link copy. Service and audit are present. |","-| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is enforced server-side and comes back through `fieldErrors.password` → `applyFieldErrors`. |","-| FR-16 | UI: Auth / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` (inside `SetPasswordForm`) on the invite, reset and security pages (B2). |","-| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + a client form (RHF + the shared forgot-password schema, `postJson`). Always shows the success `Alert`. Handles 429. API and limiter are present. |","-| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` → `sendAuthEmail`). Integration test only. |","-| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server, `verifyToken` for the email, B3) + `SetPasswordForm` → POST `/api/auth/reset-password` → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')` (B7 toast). |","-| FR-20 | UI: Account | **New** `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form with current, new and confirm fields, the shared change-password schema, `PasswordChecklist` and `passwordInputSlot`. On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show \"Current password is incorrect.\" On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form (B8). |","-| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` item labelled \"Account security\" (B10). |","-| FR-22 | Service | Present. Verify only. |","-| FR-23 | Access Control | Present (B13). New pages use `requirePageUser`. |","-| FR-24 | Audit | Present. |","-| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. The layout passes `user` to `AppShell` (B9). |","-| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name is `firstName lastName`, with a role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), and Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |","-| FR-27 | UI: Shell | `navigationForRole(user.role)`. |","-| FR-28 | Seed | Present. No change. |","-| FR-29 | Seed | Present. No change. |","-| FR-30 | Seed | Present (`createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))`). No change. |","-| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `src/server/auth/email.ts`. |","-| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip` (intake default). No rename. |","-| FR-33 | Migration | Present (`20261106000000_user_role_status_index`). No change. |","-| FR-34 | Tests | **New** integration files `tests/integration/auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`), run against the test DB. **New** `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`: sign-in/out, the failed-login message, and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus the shared e2e sign-in helper (B14). The unit tests already exist. |","-| NFR-1 | Security | Present in `tokens.ts`. |","-| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` handles CSRF. The JSON routes are same-origin with SameSite=Lax. |","-| NFR-3 | Security | Present (`DUMMY_HASH`). |","-| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt, so this is met. Nothing to design. |","-| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every new form has an error `Alert` in an `aria-live=\"polite\"` region, and RHF `shouldFocusError` is on. `SetPasswordForm` and `applyFieldErrors` already do this. The security form must match. |","-| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate for dev:** call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev is blocked. |","-| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. The existing banned-import lint test guards this. |","-| NFR-8 | Audit | The new UI code adds no audit calls. Existing metadata is safe. |","-| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`, and the `(app)` layout now does too. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |","-| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers conform, apart from the B5 `INVALID_TOKEN` 410. |","-| NFR-11 | Conventions | RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`. Add no new schemas unless one is missing. |","-| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger`. The existing seed `console.log` (line 148) is out of scope. |","-| NFR-13 | Scope | Leave `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `middleware.ts`, `/login`, the seed and the schema alone. Watch B14. |","-| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page. |","-| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI and English copy. Nothing to design. |","+| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |","+|---|---|---|","+| FR-1 | Data Model | New `AttendanceStatus` enum and `AttendanceSession` / `AttendanceRecord` models. Records use `@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` and `@@index([studentId, createdAt])`. `date` is `@db.Date` (NFR-8). The session needs a `takenById`/`updatedById` + `updatedAt` for FR-6/FR-14. Records need `minutesLate Int?` and `note String?` (FR-12). |","+| FR-2 | Data Model + Service | XOR courseId/sectionId: raw SQL `CHECK ((courseId IS NULL) <> (sectionId IS NULL))` in the migration, and a guard in the service before insert. |","+| FR-3 | Data Model (migration SQL) | Two partial unique indexes: `(courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL` and `(sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL`. Prisma can't express these, so they go in hand-written SQL in the migration after `20261106000000`. **Consequence:** `upsert` cannot target them. The service must use `findFirst` + create/update inside the transaction, and catch P2002 on a race. |","+| FR-4 | Data Model | `SchoolSettings.attendanceMode` (new enum `AttendanceMode`, default `PER_PERIOD`) and `attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)`. Same migration. |","+| FR-5 | API + UI: Admin (MEDIUM) | No settings page exists. Smallest fix: `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN, Zod-validated, calls the extended `updateSchoolSettings`) and an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance`. That avoids a new page. |","+| FR-6 | Service + UI: Register | `GET /api/attendance/today` → `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` joined with today's sessions to show \"Taken HH:mm by name\". Highlight comes from `getCurrentSlot`. Times are shown in the school tz. |","+| FR-7 | Service + UI | If mode ∈ {DAILY_HOMEROOM, BOTH}, add entries for `Section.homeroomTeacherId = user` to `/today`. |","+| FR-8 | Validation + Auth Boundary | Shared date rule in the validators: no future date (school tz). Teachers can go back 14 days, admins any date. The same rule runs on the client and the server. |","+| FR-9 | Service + UI: Register | Course roster = `Enrollment` where status ACTIVE on the date, sorted by last name. Use the MUI `ToggleButtonGroup` (exclusive). Initial state is null for a new register. |","+| FR-10 | Auth Boundary + Validation | The server rejects `EXCUSED` from non-ADMIN with 403/VALIDATION_ERROR. The UI disables it for teachers. |","+| FR-11 | UI: Register | Client-only: fill nulls with PRESENT. |","+| FR-12 | Validation + UI | `minutesLate` 1–240 is required iff LATE (Zod `superRefine`) and defaults to 5 in the UI. `note` max 500. |","+| FR-13 | UI: Register | Derived counters. Save is disabled while any row is unmarked. The server also requires a full roster (or at least one valid record per student sent). |","+| FR-14 | Service | One `prisma.$transaction`: find/create the session, then upsert the records (`@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` works for `upsert`). Set `updatedById` on the session. The GET returns last-changed-by/at. |","+| FR-15 | Service + Auth Boundary | Section variant: roster = `SectionMember` for the current academic year. Access = `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` or ADMIN. No existing `assertCanManageSection` helper, so add a small one in the attendance service (or `auth/`). |","+| FR-16 | UI: Register (LOW) | Route `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` component with a section-scoped GET/PUT. |","+| FR-17 | UI: Register | Mobile: rows ≥ 48 px, toggles ≥ 44×44, sticky `Paper` save bar. Use theme `sx` only. |","+| FR-18 | Service + Audit | Inside the save, diff old vs new per student. For changed existing records call `audit({action:'attendance.record.update', before, after, actor, note})`. |","+| FR-19 | Service + Auth Boundary | Pure function `canEdit(user, sessionDate, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today - date ≤ 14 days`. The GET returns `readOnly` + `readOnlyReason`. The PUT returns 403. Unit-tested (FR-39). |","+| FR-20 | Notifications | Add `attendance.absent` (ATTENDANCE, email true, mandatoryInApp true, PARENT+STUDENT) and `attendance.late` (email false). |","+| FR-21 | Notifications + Service | After commit (outside the tx), call `notifyStudentAndParents` per changed student. Daily-register body: `<Section> daily register, <date>` (intake default). Link `/students/<id>/attendance`. |","+| FR-22 | Notifications + Service | Pure `diffForNotifications(prev, next)` → `{absent[], late[], corrected[]}`. Only a transition *into* ABSENT/LATE sends a notice, so re-saving with the same status sends nothing. ABSENT→PRESENT sends `attendance.corrected`. Unit-tested (FR-39). |","+| FR-23 | Notifications (LOW) | `attendance.corrected` (ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false), `attendance.register_missing` (ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false). |","+| FR-24 | Config | Append `{key:'attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}` to `studentTabs`. |","+| FR-25 | Service + UI: Tabs | Term = the Term containing today, else the most recent ended term (intake default). Use `StatCard` ×4 for term and year. |","+| FR-26 | UI: Tabs | MUI X `DateCalendar` read-only with a custom `day` slot coloured from per-day aggregates and a `Tooltip`. Month change refetches or filters `?from=&to=`. |","+| FR-27 | API + Auth Boundary | `GET /api/students/:id/attendance` → `assertCanViewStudent`. **Strip `note`** for STUDENT/PARENT on the server (AC-8). The table uses `DataTable`. |","+| FR-28 | Service (pure) | `attendanceRate(records)` = (P+L+E)/total×100, rounded to 1 dp; empty → null. Include DROPPED enrollments (filter on student, not enrollment). Mode chooses the source: course sessions (PER_PERIOD/BOTH) or section sessions (DAILY_HOMEROOM). Unit-tested. |","+| FR-29 | API + UI: Tabs + Config | `GET /api/courses/:id/attendance` (`assertCanManageCourse`) → last 20 sessions × enrolled students. Use MUI X DataGrid with dynamic columns. The header click links to the register. Course tab roles: ADMIN, TEACHER. |","+| FR-30 | Service + UI: Admin | Overview: expected = all timetable slots for today (all teachers) + sections if the mode includes daily; taken = sessions today; rate today. ADMIN gets `[]` from `getScheduleForDate`, so it **needs a school-wide slot query** (a direct `timetableSlot.findMany` by `dayOfWeek`, or a new helper next to `getScheduleForDate`). |","+| FR-31 | Service + API + Notifications | Missing = expected meetings with no session and `now ≥ period.startTime + 15 min` (school tz). `POST /api/admin/attendance/remind` → `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[teacherId]})`. |","+| FR-32 | Service + API + Validation | Report filters (range ≤ 366 days, grade, section, course, status) go into a per-student aggregate (use a SQL `groupBy` for performance). `?format=csv` → `toCsv` with the same columns. |","+| FR-33 | Service + API | YTD rate per student < threshold, sorted ascending. Reuses the same aggregate as FR-32 with the year's date range. |","+| FR-34 | Config/Nav | `navigation.ts`: TEACHER → `/attendance/take`, ADMIN → `/admin/attendance`. |","+| FR-35 | API | The 9 listed routes, plus PATCH settings from FR-5. Every handler starts with `requireUser`/`requireRole` and then the resource assert. They use the `http.ts` helpers. |","+| FR-36 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts`: `registerQuery`, `registerPutBody`, `studentAttendanceQuery`, `reportFilters`, `remindBody`, `attendanceSettingsPatch`. The register form imports them too. |","+| FR-37 | Service | `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts`. Keep the pure helpers (`attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`) in the same file or a sibling `attendance-rules.ts` so the tests need no DB. |","+| FR-38 | Seed | Extend the existing seed. Use a seeded RNG, 15 teaching days before the run date, 7A and 7B, a 94/3/3 split, and two Grade 7 students forced below 85%. Respect the existing school-day config. |","+| FR-39 | Tests (unit) | `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`. |","+| FR-40 | Tests (integration) | The save transaction, non-enrolled rejection (NFR-3), and the partial unique indexes (a duplicate insert raises). |","+| FR-41 | Tests (e2e) | Playwright: the 375 px take flow, and a parent seeing the notification plus the calendar absence. |","+| NFR-1 | Performance | Save: one tx with batched upserts (≈35). Avoid N+1 by loading existing records in one query. Student tab: one indexed query on `[studentId, createdAt]` (consider filtering on `session.date` and adding an index if needed). Aggregate in memory (1,200 rows is fine). |","+| NFR-2 | UI: Register (client) | localStorage key `attendance:<course\\|section>:<id>:<date>:<periodId\\|daily>`. Write it on a network failure, clear it on success, and offer a restore banner when it is present. |","+| NFR-3 | Service (integrity) | Validate every `studentId` against the ACTIVE enrollment on the date (`enrolledAt ≤ date` and not dropped before it) or the section membership. Any miss → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR and the whole save is rejected. |","+| NFR-4 | UI: Register | Satisfied by FR-11 + FR-17 (mark all present, then fix the exceptions). |","+| NFR-5 | Notifications | `notify()` writes in-app notifications immediately and queues EmailOutbox. Call it post-commit without blocking the response on email. |","+| NFR-6 | Cross-cutting (UI) | MUI only. Dev must use mui-mcp docs for 9.5.0 (ToggleButtonGroup, DateCalendar day slot, DataGrid, Paper sticky). **Hard blocker if unreachable.** |","+| NFR-7 | Auth Boundary | Server-side checks on every handler and server page. Per-role scope is listed above. Teachers also get their homeroom sections. |","+| NFR-8 | Cross-cutting | `@db.Date`, cuid IDs, UTC storage with display in school tz (`date-fns-tz`, already installed), the logger, `audit()` for edits to records owned by others, and pageSize ≤ 100 on the report and student records. |","+| NFR-9 | UI accessibility | `aria-label` on each toggle (\"Mark <name> present\"), 44 px targets. |","+| NFR-10 | Cross-cutting | Reuse the helpers above, add no new deps, rename nothing. Holidays (PRD-14) and the EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) are out of scope beyond the admin-only option. |"," ","-## Change footprint","+## Open points for `arch-design-system`"," ","-**New (6 source files + tests):** `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (+ a client form), `(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,","-`(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (+ a client form), 4 integration tests,","-`tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` and the e2e sign-in helper.","-","-**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (`requirePageUser`, then the `user` prop), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (drop the placeholder, real","-user, sign out, Account security item), and the existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) to use the sign-in helper.","-","-**Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,","-`src/lib/validators/auth.ts` (unless a form schema is genuinely missing).","-","-## Open items carried from intake","-","-1. FR-32: keep `ip` (LOW confidence, default applied).","-2. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`. `sendAuthEmail` is unchanged.","-3. The ticket id is SH-1.","-4. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a hard gate for the dev phase.","-5. New: intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" looks out of date (B7). Verify, don't build.","-6. New: existing e2e specs may already be failing without auth (B14).","+1. **Intake blockers (for the Overview):** FR-5 (MEDIUM), FR-16 (LOW), FR-23 (LOW) and the NFR-6 mui-mcp hard dependency. The defaults are listed above.","+2. **Partial unique indexes vs Prisma upsert (FR-3/FR-14):** sessions can't be `upsert`ed via Prisma. Use find + create in the tx and catch P2002 → retry as an update.","+3. **Admin school-wide schedule (FR-30/31):** `getScheduleForDate` returns `[]` for ADMIN. It needs a school-wide slot query. Prefer a small exported helper in `timetable-service.ts` over duplicating `slotInclude` logic.","+4. **Section access helper (FR-15):** none exists today. Add one small function and don't generalise it.","+5. **\"ACTIVE on date\" (NFR-3):** `Enrollment` has `enrolledAt`/`droppedAt`. Define the rule as `enrolledAt ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt > date)`. For back-dated registers, the roster should use the same rule.","+6. **Rate source by mode (FR-28):** in BOTH mode, rates use the per-period records only. Daily records are stored but not counted."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-1\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z) for PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001).\nIt has 34 FRs and 15 NFRs (49 requirements) at 97% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 5 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces an earlier SH-1 notes file. That version listed `/login`, the seed users and the role/status\n> migration as new work. All three are now **present** on disk.\n\n**Headline:** this is a **UI-gap + tests** ticket. The backend, every API route, `/login`, the seed and the\nmigration already exist. The design adds **4 pages**, rewires the **shell**, and adds **tests**.\n**No new endpoint, service, model or migration is needed.** `arch-api-contracts` documents the 5 existing routes as they are.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Auth Core**, **Service**, **API (existing)**, **UI: Auth Pages**,\n**UI: Account**, **UI: Shell**, **Access Control**, **Security**, **Audit**, **Seed**, **Accessibility**,\n**UI Rules**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Design implication |\n|---|------|--------------------|\n| B1 | `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` already renders the centred Card shell. | New auth pages render only the card body. |\n| B2 | `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure`. Today only `LoginForm` imports any of them. | Invite and reset pages **reuse `SetPasswordForm`**. `/account/security` reuses `PasswordChecklist`, `passwordInputSlot`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors`. Do not add a second fetch or checklist helper. |\n| B3 | `SetPasswordForm` **requires `email`**, because the policy rejects a password equal to the email. | `/reset-password/[token]` must also call `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` server-side, to get the email and to show the invalid-link state before the form renders. |\n| B4 | `tokens.ts` `verifyToken(raw, type)` is read-only. `consumeToken` throws `INVALID_TOKEN` on a double submit. | The token pages are **server components** that call `verifyToken`. They show user data or the invalid-link `Alert`. No new endpoint. |\n| B5 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` maps to **410**, a code outside the NFR-10 list. The service copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | Keep this (NFR-13). The UI handles 410 `INVALID_TOKEN` by switching to the page's invalid-link copy. `arch-api-contracts` should document the 410. |\n| B6 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** create a session. | FR-14 flow on the client: POST `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. |\n| B7 | `/login` already exists. `LoginForm({ callbackUrl, reset })` fires a `useToast` once when `reset` is set, and exports `loginErrorMessage` (unit-tested). | FR-19 redirects to `/login?reset=1`. **Do not touch `/login`.** FR-2, FR-4, FR-6 and FR-7 only need verification. Intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date: `loginErrorMessage` covers `rate_limited`. Dev should verify this. |\n| B8 | `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`. The `jwt` callback keeps the current session alive on `reauth`. | FR-20 \"re-issue the current session\" is done server-side. The page only POSTs, then shows a toast and resets the form. |\n| B9 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders `<AppShell schoolShortName>` and does no auth. `providers.tsx` has no `SessionProvider`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user: SessionUser` (`id`, `role`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `email`) to `AppShell`. **Prop, not `useSession`**, so no provider is needed. This is the one source of the current user (FR-25). |\n| B10 | `shell.tsx` uses `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167). Its menu has 2 `MenuItem`s that only close the menu, and there is no `signOut`. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26 and FR-27 are all in this one file plus the layout. Sign out is `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`. |\n| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | Middleware needs no change (FR-11, NFR-14). |\n| B12 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. `requestPasswordReset` throws `RATE_LIMITED`. | `/forgot-password` shows `data.message` from the API rather than retyping the string, and shows an error `Alert` on 429. |\n| B13 | `src/app/forbidden/page.tsx` exists. | `requirePageRole` → `/forbidden` is already wired (FR-23). |\n| B14 | Existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) call `page.goto('/dashboard')` with no sign-in. The middleware already requires a session. | **Regression risk (NFR-13).** These specs are probably already failing, or will once the layout calls `requirePageUser`. Add one shared e2e sign-in helper using the seed users and reuse it in the existing specs. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | Present. No change. |\n| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | `/login` is present (B7). Verify only. |\n| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`. Verify via the integration test. |\n| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Present (`loginErrorMessage`). Verify only. |\n| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`). Covered by the authorize integration test. |\n| FR-6 | Auth Core / UI | Limiter and message are both present (B7). Verify only. |\n| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | Present (`safeCallbackUrl` in `LoginForm`). Verify only. |\n| FR-8 | Audit | Emitted by `authorize`. The integration test asserts the AuditLog rows. |\n| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present. No change. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`, `reauth`). The change-password integration test covers `passwordChangedAt`. |\n| FR-11 | Access Control | Present (B11). No change. |\n| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. Pages call `verifyToken` only and never hash anything (B4). |\n| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: read-only name and email + `SetPasswordForm`. Invalid, used or expired: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. |\n| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client flow from B6. A 410 response switches to the invalid-link copy. Service and audit are present. |\n| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is enforced server-side and comes back through `fieldErrors.password` → `applyFieldErrors`. |\n| FR-16 | UI: Auth / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` (inside `SetPasswordForm`) on the invite, reset and security pages (B2). |\n| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + a client form (RHF + the shared forgot-password schema, `postJson`). Always shows the success `Alert`. Handles 429. API and limiter are present. |\n| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` → `sendAuthEmail`). Integration test only. |\n| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server, `verifyToken` for the email, B3) + `SetPasswordForm` → POST `/api/auth/reset-password` → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')` (B7 toast). |\n| FR-20 | UI: Account | **New** `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form with current, new and confirm fields, the shared change-password schema, `PasswordChecklist` and `passwordInputSlot`. On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show \"Current password is incorrect.\" On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form (B8). |\n| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` item labelled \"Account security\" (B10). |\n| FR-22 | Service | Present. Verify only. |\n| FR-23 | Access Control | Present (B13). New pages use `requirePageUser`. |\n| FR-24 | Audit | Present. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. The layout passes `user` to `AppShell` (B9). |\n| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name is `firstName lastName`, with a role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), and Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |\n| FR-27 | UI: Shell | `navigationForRole(user.role)`. |\n| FR-28 | Seed | Present. No change. |\n| FR-29 | Seed | Present. No change. |\n| FR-30 | Seed | Present (`createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))`). No change. |\n| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `src/server/auth/email.ts`. |\n| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip` (intake default). No rename. |\n| FR-33 | Migration | Present (`20261106000000_user_role_status_index`). No change. |\n| FR-34 | Tests | **New** integration files `tests/integration/auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`), run against the test DB. **New** `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`: sign-in/out, the failed-login message, and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus the shared e2e sign-in helper (B14). The unit tests already exist. |\n| NFR-1 | Security | Present in `tokens.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` handles CSRF. The JSON routes are same-origin with SameSite=Lax. |\n| NFR-3 | Security | Present (`DUMMY_HASH`). |\n| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt, so this is met. Nothing to design. |\n| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every new form has an error `Alert` in an `aria-live=\"polite\"` region, and RHF `shouldFocusError` is on. `SetPasswordForm` and `applyFieldErrors` already do this. The security form must match. |\n| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate for dev:** call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev is blocked. |\n| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. The existing banned-import lint test guards this. |\n| NFR-8 | Audit | The new UI code adds no audit calls. Existing metadata is safe. |\n| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`, and the `(app)` layout now does too. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers conform, apart from the B5 `INVALID_TOKEN` 410. |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`. Add no new schemas unless one is missing. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger`. The existing seed `console.log` (line 148) is out of scope. |\n| NFR-13 | Scope | Leave `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `middleware.ts`, `/login`, the seed and the schema alone. Watch B14. |\n| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page. |\n| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI and English copy. Nothing to design. |\n\n## Change footprint\n\n**New (6 source files + tests):** `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (+ a client form), `(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (+ a client form), 4 integration tests,\n`tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` and the e2e sign-in helper.\n\n**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (`requirePageUser`, then the `user` prop), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (drop the placeholder, real\nuser, sign out, Account security item), and the existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) to use the sign-in helper.\n\n**Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,\n`src/lib/validators/auth.ts` (unless a form schema is genuinely missing).\n\n## Open items carried from intake\n\n1. FR-32: keep `ip` (LOW confidence, default applied).\n2. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`. `sendAuthEmail` is unchanged.\n3. The ticket id is SH-1.\n4. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a hard gate for the dev phase.\n5. New: intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" looks out of date (B7). Verify, don't build.\n6. New: existing e2e specs may already be failing without auth (B14).\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LsABFhPVaRxcbx7kSizRML","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
