arts:\n- **Reusable code:** a table of the existing functions and components the feature can build on. I checked each one's actual signature in the code.\n- **Requirements table:** each requirement → the kind of change it needs → notes.\n- **Open points:** six issues for `arch-design-system` to decide.\n\nThings found in the code that the design needs to handle:\n- **Saving a register:** the two partial unique indexes on sessions can't be used by Prisma's `upsert`. My suggestion is to look up the session and create or update it inside the transaction, and treat a duplicate-key error (P2002) as an update.\n- **Admin overview:** `getScheduleForDate` returns nothing for ADMIN, so the \"Today\" overview and \"Missing registers\" list (FR-30/31) need a separate query for the whole school's timetable.\n- **Notifications:** `notifyStudentAndParents` gets called once per student, because each student's title and message are different.\n- **Settings:** `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` needs the two new attendance fields added. There is no settings page to put them on, so I suggest an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance` plus a `PATCH /api/settings/school` route.\n- **Daily registers:** no access check exists for a homeroom teacher's section, so a small new one is needed.\n\nTwo of the open points are my own suggestions, not from intake. One is the rule for \"ACTIVE enrollment on that date\": `enrolledAt ≤ date` and the student either still ACTIVE or dropped after that date. The other is the duplicate-key fallback above. The intake blockers (FR-5, FR-16, FR-23 and the mui-mcp dependency) are listed so they get carried into the Overview of `system-design.md`.\n\nThe other files in `artifacts/architect/` are still from SH-1. I left them alone because the other sub-tasks own them and will overwrite them.","ttft_ms":3124,"type":"result","duration_ms":90744,"uuid":"4b9bceb3-60ea-4f3b-80cb-42af199dc797","ttft_stream_ms":2029,"time_to_request_ms":180,"first_content_frame_m