{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnB4cs2J8r8ngwrxxt2i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WAAodb1piB4j2mGmiS9EVi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-8\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T06:00:00Z), PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008).\nIt has 48 FRs and 12 NFRs (60 requirements) at 93% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers, and they must be surfaced in `system-design.md` Overview.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are still **SH-7** leftovers at the time of writing. Downstream sub-tasks own them and must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-8 input.\n\n## Brownfield findings verified on disk (arch-research-reqs)\n\n| # | Finding | Evidence | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | **Middleware blocks unauthenticated `/api/files/:id`.** `src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for any `/api/*` not matched by `isPublicPath()`. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is `['/api/health','/api/auth/','/api/internal/']`. | middleware.ts L36-40, public-routes.ts L7 | FR-10's public `logo` context cannot work (login page, emails) unless `/api/files/` is made public. **Recommended:** add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. Then the GET handler resolves the session itself (optional user → access registry), and POST/DELETE **must** call `requireUser()` explicitly, because middleware no longer guards them. This is a security-critical design point (NFR-1, NFR-8). |\n| B2 | Daily hook exists: `lastPurgeAt` + `purgeOldNotifications()` in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` L11-31. | grep | FR-12 adds a second call in the same `if` block. No new scheduler. |\n| B3 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) → {ok, retryAfterMs}` is a per-process sliding window. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-3: `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)`. |\n| B4 | `logoUrl` consumers: `BaseLayout.tsx` L28 uses `<Img src={school.logoUrl}>` raw, and `render.ts` already passes `appUrl`. | grep | FR-40 stores a relative `/api/files/<id>`, so BaseLayout must prefix `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. Combined with B1, that makes the logo fetchable from mail clients. |\n| B5 | No `.gitignore` at the repo root. | `ls` | Create one with `uploads/` (plus `node_modules`, `.next`, `.env` if missing). |\n| B6 | No `src/server/files/` and no content code. | ls | Confirms greenfield. |\n| B7 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are arrays of `CourseTab`/`StudentTab` in `src/config/`. | grep | FR-20 / FR-35 append one entry each. |\n| B8 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object in `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, and `ACADEMIC` is a valid category. | grep | FR-38 adds one key. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = server service/module · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = background/maintenance · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = config/env/registry · **TEST**\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | `FileObject` + `@@index([context, contextId])`, unique `storageKey`. `context` is a plain String (registry keys), not an enum, so new contexts need no migration. One migration together with FR-15. |\n| FR-2 | SVC, CFG | `src/server/storage.ts`: `saveFile`/`readFile`/`deleteFile`. Resolve paths with `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR, key)` and assert they stay under UPLOAD_DIR (traversal guard). Add env `UPLOAD_DIR` to the env schema. Single local-disk impl, no interface (NFR-11). |\n| FR-3 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/files` multipart. Use `request.formData()`? It buffers, which conflicts with NFR-5. Use `busboy`-free streaming via `req.body` + the Web `Request` multipart parser? **Design must pick.** Next.js route handlers expose `request.body` (a ReadableStream), but a multipart parser isn't in the allowed deps. Practical option: `formData()` is acceptable only if the size cap is pre-checked via `Content-Length` (≤ MAX_UPLOAD_MB + overhead) before parsing, then `File.stream()` → disk with sha256. Flag as a NFR-5 trade-off for design. |\n| FR-4 | VAL, CFG | `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` env (default 25). Enforce with a byte counter in the write stream (abort and unlink the partial file), plus an early `Content-Length` reject. Logo override: 2 MB (FR-40). Make the limit per-context: `{ logo: 2 }`, default env. |\n| FR-5 | VAL | Extension allowlist + `fileTypeFromBuffer` on the first ~4100 bytes (peek before or while writing). New dep `file-type` (ESM-only, so check the Next server bundling). |\n| FR-6 | VAL | Rule table: txt/csv → sniff must be `undefined`. docx/xlsx/pptx → sniff ∈ {zip, matching OOXML mime}. zip → zip. Others → sniff ext must match the declared ext (jpg≡jpeg). Pure function, unit-testable (FR-48). |\n| FR-7 | VAL | `sanitizeFilename()`: strip `/ \\ ` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trim, and cap at 150 while preserving the extension. Pure function and unit test. |\n| FR-8 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/files/:id`: registry check **before** `readFile`. Headers: stored mime, `nosniff`, `attachment; filename*=UTF-8''…`, and `inline` only if `?inline=1` and mime is image/* or application/pdf. Stream via `Readable.toWeb(fs.createReadStream)`. |\n| FR-9 | SVC, AUTH, CFG | `src/server/files/access.ts`: a `Map<string, resolver>`. Default: owner or ADMIN. Return **404** for denied (don't leak existence) and 401 for unauthenticated non-public. Contexts are registered via side-effect import, so the GET handler must import the module that registers `lesson`/`logo` (avoid a lazy-registration bug). |\n| FR-10 | AUTH | `lesson` resolver: load lesson+module+course, then `assertCanViewCourse` + visibility rule (FR-18) for STUDENT/PARENT, while managers see drafts. `logo`: `() => true` incl. `user=null`. Depends on B1. Unattached files (contextId null) fall to the owner/ADMIN check even within the 'lesson' context, which lets editor previews work before attach. |\n| FR-11 | EP, AUTH | `DELETE /api/files/:id`: owner/ADMIN, `contextId === null`, else CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR. Delete the row, then the bytes (log on bytes failure, since orphan bytes are harmless). Audit when ADMIN deletes another user's file (FR-46). |\n| FR-12 | JOB | `purgeOrphanFiles()` in `src/server/files/purge.ts`, hooked at B2. Batch `findMany` where contextId null and createdAt < now-24h, delete bytes then rows. **Caveat:** the logo is \"attached\" how? FR-40 stores a URL in logoUrl but contextId stays null, so the logo gets purged after 24h. **Design must set `contextId` for logo** (e.g. the SchoolSettings id/`'school'`) when settings are saved. |\n| FR-13 | UI | `src/components/FileUpload/`. XHR (not fetch) for `upload.onprogress`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`/`onChange` (FileObject summaries), and optional reorder (FR-27). MUI only (NFR-7). |\n| FR-14 | UI | `src/components/FileList/`: read-only list, links `/api/files/:id`. |\n| FR-15 | DM | `ContentStatus` enum, Module(courseId, title, position, status, publishAt), Lesson(moduleId, title, position, status, publishAt, contentMarkdown, estimatedMinutes, videoUrl, createdById?), LessonAttachment(lessonId, fileId, position), LessonLink(lessonId, title, url, position), and LessonProgress PK [lessonId, studentId]. Cascades: Course→Module→Lesson→Attachment/Link/Progress. Add back-relations on Course/User/StudentProfile. Index `[courseId, position]`, `[moduleId, position]`. Follow the PRD's exact field list. |\n| FR-16 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/content.ts` (Zod), shared by client and server. URL refinements reuse the FR-30 parser for videoUrl. |\n| FR-17 | SVC, AUTH | Inside the PATCH lesson transaction: verify each fileId is (owner==caller or ADMIN) and (contextId null or already == this lessonId), then `updateMany` context/contextId. Removed attachments should be detached (contextId → null), which leaves them purgeable in 24h. Decide explicitly. |\n| FR-18 | SVC | Pure `isVisible(entity, now)` + Prisma `where` fragment `visibleWhere(now)` = `OR[{status:PUBLISHED},{status:SCHEDULED, publishAt:{lte:now}}]` applied to both module and lesson. One source of truth used by list, get, prev/next, files, progress and learning. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Status Chip (grey/blue+date/green). Manager view = no visibility filter. |\n| FR-20 | UI, CFG | `courseTabs` entry `content`, all roles. A server component loads via content-service (not via HTTP). |\n| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Progress is computed over **visible** lessons only. \"Continue\" = first visible lesson in (module.position, lesson.position) order without completedAt. |\n| FR-22 | UI, EP | Menu actions map to PATCH /api/modules/:id (status/publishAt/title), DELETE, and reorder (move up/down reuses the reorder endpoint). |\n| FR-23 | EP, SVC, UI | `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder` with the full tree. Server validates that the set of module ids == the course's modules and the set of lesson ids == all the course's lessons (no foreign ids, no omissions), then rewrites positions + moduleId in one transaction. New dep `@dnd-kit/sortable`. |\n| FR-24 | UI | Type-to-confirm Dialog. Can ConfirmDialog be extended or does it need a local Dialog? Server DELETE cascades regardless. |\n| FR-25 | UI | Page `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` (manage). Client editor with Tabs Write/Preview (Preview = MarkdownView). Toolbar inserts text at the selection. |\n| FR-26 | UI | Image insert → FileUpload context `lesson` → `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. The file must then be attached (FR-17) or it gets purged. **Design:** on save, parse `/api/files/<id>` refs in markdown and attach them as context=lesson (not as LessonAttachment rows), or require explicit attach. |\n| FR-27 | EP, UI | PATCH /api/lessons/:id with `attachments: [{fileId}]` (order = position) and `links: [{title,url}]`. Replace-all semantics in a transaction. |\n| FR-28 | UI, VAL | Schedule: MUI X DateTimePicker (check the MUI X pickers package is installed and allowed, NFR-7). Convert school-tz → UTC on the client or server (NFR-10). Server rejects `publishAt <= now`. |\n| FR-29 | UI | Client timer + dirty flag, `beforeunload` + in-app navigation guard. PATCH with `status` untouched. |\n| FR-30 | SVC | `src/lib/video.ts` `parseVideoUrl(url) → {provider,id}|null`, shared by validator and renderer. Pure, unit test. |\n| FR-31 | UI | `src/components/MarkdownView/`. rehype-sanitize schema: default + `img.src` restricted to `/`-relative (same origin). New deps react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize. Client or server component is fine (react-markdown works in RSC). |\n| FR-32 | UI, SVC | Viewer page. Prev/next computed over the ordered visible-lesson list of the course (service helper reusing FR-18). |\n| FR-33 | EP, SVC, AUTH | First view: an upsert in the viewer page's server load for STUDENT with ACTIVE enrollment (set `firstViewedAt` only on create). `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress {completed}` sets/clears completedAt. Reject PARENT/TEACHER with FORBIDDEN, and a non-visible lesson → NOT_FOUND. |\n| FR-34 | EP, UI | `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` (assertCanManageCourse): ACTIVE enrollments left-joined with progress. 2 queries. |\n| FR-35 | EP, UI, CFG | `studentTabs` entry `learning`, `GET /api/students/:id/learning` (assertCanViewStudent). Per course of ACTIVE enrollments: visible lesson count, completed count, max(updatedAt/completedAt). Avoid per-course N+1 (group queries). |\n| FR-36 | UI, AUTH | Parent read-only: hide the button **and** the server rejects (FR-33). |\n| FR-37 | AUTH | Reuse `assertCanViewCourse` unchanged. |\n| FR-38 | CFG, SVC | `content.lesson_published` in NOTIFICATION_TYPES. Fire only on the transition to visible via \"Publish now\" (lesson PUBLISHED **and** module currently visible). Recipients = ACTIVE enrolled students, using notify() with a batch/loop. |\n| FR-39 | UI | Tooltip only. No job (consistent with FR-18). |\n| FR-40 | UI, SVC | Logo FileUpload, context `logo`, size cap 2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg. On settings save, set FileObject.contextId (see FR-12 caveat) and logoUrl = `/api/files/<id>`. Fix the BaseLayout absolute URL (B4). |\n| FR-41 | VAL, EP | Allowlist is context-aware: `svg` is only in `logo`. file-type can't sniff SVG (it's text), so validate that it's text and contains `<svg`. On GET, add `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` when mime is image/svg+xml. |\n| FR-42 | UI | New `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` (requireRole ADMIN) + a nav entry. LOW confidence, accepted default. |\n| FR-43 | EP | 15 endpoints total (files ×3, modules ×4 incl. POST lessons, lessons ×3, reorder, progress ×2, learning). Use the existing response/error envelope and `{error:{code,message}}`. |\n| FR-44 | EP, AUTH | STUDENT/PARENT get NOT_FOUND (not FORBIDDEN) for hidden lessons. Same rule for files under FR-10. |\n| FR-45 | SVC | Layout: `src/server/content/content-service.ts`, `src/server/files/{access,service,purge,validate}.ts`, `src/server/storage.ts`. Thin routes. |\n| FR-46 | SVC | `audit()` when actor ≠ lesson/module creator. Needs a `createdById` on Module/Lesson, or always audit ADMIN mutations. Check whether FR-15's exact schema includes a creator field. If not, audit when the actor is ADMIN. |\n| FR-47 | DM (seed) | Extend `prisma/seed.ts`. Add `prisma/seed-assets/*.pdf` copied into UPLOAD_DIR by the seed via `saveFile`. Sam = the existing seeded student. |\n| FR-48 | TEST | Unit: sanitizer, video parser, visibility, registry dispatch, sniff rules (FR-6). Integration: upload→attach→download + purge (a temp UPLOAD_DIR). One Playwright e2e. |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH | No files under `public/`, and every read goes through FR-9. Watch B1: making `/api/files/` public must not skip the registry. |\n| NFR-2 | UI | rehype-sanitize strips `javascript:`. Also apply link `href` protocol check in the `a` mapper (defence in depth). Unit/e2e with `[x](javascript:alert(1))`. |\n| NFR-3 | EP | B3. Return 429 RATE_LIMITED with `Retry-After`. Note the ceiling: per-process. |\n| NFR-4 | SVC | Content tab: ≤4 queries (modules with lessons ordered + `_count.attachments` + caller progress `where lessonId in`). Add DB indexes (FR-15). |\n| NFR-5 | SVC | Stream → hash → disk, with the byte cap during the stream. See the FR-3 multipart trade-off. Write to a temp name, then rename on success (no partial files under the final key). |\n| NFR-6 | UI | iframe `title`, alt-text warning, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | Dev must use mui-mcp docs before UI work. Blocker if unreachable. Includes the DateTimePicker (FR-28) package choice. |\n| NFR-8 | AUTH | Every route/page calls the assert helpers. Especially relevant for POST/DELETE /api/files if B1 is applied. |\n| NFR-9 | CFG | 5 new deps only. No renames. lint/typecheck/test green. |\n| NFR-10 | UI, SVC | UTC in the DB. Display via SchoolSettings.timezone (reuse the existing tz formatting helper if present). |\n| NFR-11 | — | No storage interface/S3 abstraction. No content copy. |\n| NFR-12 | CFG | Use the logger instead of console.log. Add `UPLOAD_DIR`, `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` to `.env.example` and the env schema. |\n\n## Open design decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **B1 public files path**: either add `/api/files/` to PUBLIC_API_PATHS with explicit `requireUser()` on POST/DELETE (recommended), or special-case GET in middleware.\n2. **Logo orphan purge (FR-12 × FR-40)**: give logo files a non-null `contextId` on save, or they get deleted after 24h.\n3. **Inline markdown images (FR-26 × FR-12)**: attach images referenced in `contentMarkdown` on save, or they get purged.\n4. **Multipart vs streaming (FR-3 × NFR-5)**: `formData()` + a Content-Length pre-check, or a hand-rolled stream parser. No multipart dep is allowed.\n5. **Detach semantics (FR-17/FR-27)**: removing an attachment either nulls contextId (purged later) or deletes immediately.\n6. **Audit trigger (FR-46)**: either add a creator field or audit all ADMIN mutations on content.\n7. **SVG validation (FR-41)**: text sniff for `<svg`, logo context only, CSP header on serve.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":422,"cache_read_input_tokens":43181,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":422},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"602dd78b-ddb5-4a5b-87b4-9966477239d5","uuid":"b9ebaa91-b0f4-44be-8022-0e73cfc37a09","timestamp":"2026-11-06T18:49:41.527Z","request_id":"req_011CgnB4cdtYk2Qn9bFFBexB","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WAAodb1piB4j2mGmiS9EVi":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-8\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T06:00:00Z), PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008).\nIt has 48 FRs and 12 NFRs (60 requirements) at 93% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers, and they must be surfaced in `system-design.md` Overview.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are still **SH-7** leftovers at the time of writing. Downstream sub-tasks own them and must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-8 input.\n\n## Brownfield findings verified on disk (arch-research-reqs)\n\n| # | Finding | Evidence | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | **Middleware blocks unauthenticated `/api/files/:id`.** `src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for any `/api/*` not matched by `isPublicPath()`. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is `['/api/health','/api/auth/','/api/internal/']`. | middleware.ts L36-40, public-routes.ts L7 | FR-10's public `logo` context cannot work (login page, emails) unless `/api/files/` is made public. **Recommended:** add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. Then the GET handler resolves the session itself (optional user → access registry), and POST/DELETE **must** call `requireUser()` explicitly, because middleware no longer guards them. This is a security-critical design point (NFR-1, NFR-8). |\n| B2 | Daily hook exists: `lastPurgeAt` + `purgeOldNotifications()` in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` L11-31. | grep | FR-12 adds a second call in the same `if` block. No new scheduler. |\n| B3 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) → {ok, retryAfterMs}` is a per-process sliding window. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-3: `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)`. |\n| B4 | `logoUrl` consumers: `BaseLayout.tsx` L28 uses `<Img src={school.logoUrl}>` raw, and `render.ts` already passes `appUrl`. | grep | FR-40 stores a relative `/api/files/<id>`, so BaseLayout must prefix `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. Combined with B1, that makes the logo fetchable from mail clients. |\n| B5 | No `.gitignore` at the repo root. | `ls` | Create one with `uploads/` (plus `node_modules`, `.next`, `.env` if missing). |\n| B6 | No `src/server/files/` and no content code. | ls | Confirms greenfield. |\n| B7 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are arrays of `CourseTab`/`StudentTab` in `src/config/`. | grep | FR-20 / FR-35 append one entry each. |\n| B8 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object in `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, and `ACADEMIC` is a valid category. | grep | FR-38 adds one key. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = server service/module · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = background/maintenance · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = config/env/registry · **TEST**\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | `FileObject` + `@@index([context, contextId])`, unique `storageKey`. `context` is a plain String (registry keys), not an enum, so new contexts need no migration. One migration together with FR-15. |\n| FR-2 | SVC, CFG | `src/server/storage.ts`: `saveFile`/`readFile`/`deleteFile`. Resolve paths with `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR, key)` and assert they stay under UPLOAD_DIR (traversal guard). Add env `UPLOAD_DIR` to the env schema. Single local-disk impl, no interface (NFR-11). |\n| FR-3 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/files` multipart. Use `request.formData()`? It buffers, which conflicts with NFR-5. Use `busboy`-free streaming via `req.body` + the Web `Request` multipart parser? **Design must pick.** Next.js route handlers expose `request.body` (a ReadableStream), but a multipart parser isn't in the allowed deps. Practical option: `formData()` is acceptable only if the size cap is pre-checked via `Content-Length` (≤ MAX_UPLOAD_MB + overhead) before parsing, then `File.stream()` → disk with sha256. Flag as a NFR-5 trade-off for design. |\n| FR-4 | VAL, CFG | `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` env (default 25). Enforce with a byte counter in the write stream (abort and unlink the partial file), plus an early `Content-Length` reject. Logo override: 2 MB (FR-40). Make the limit per-context: `{ logo: 2 }`, default env. |\n| FR-5 | VAL | Extension allowlist + `fileTypeFromBuffer` on the first ~4100 bytes (peek before or while writing). New dep `file-type` (ESM-only, so check the Next server bundling). |\n| FR-6 | VAL | Rule table: txt/csv → sniff must be `undefined`. docx/xlsx/pptx → sniff ∈ {zip, matching OOXML mime}. zip → zip. Others → sniff ext must match the declared ext (jpg≡jpeg). Pure function, unit-testable (FR-48). |\n| FR-7 | VAL | `sanitizeFilename()`: strip `/ \\ ` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trim, and cap at 150 while preserving the extension. Pure function and unit test. |\n| FR-8 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/files/:id`: registry check **before** `readFile`. Headers: stored mime, `nosniff`, `attachment; filename*=UTF-8''…`, and `inline` only if `?inline=1` and mime is image/* or application/pdf. Stream via `Readable.toWeb(fs.createReadStream)`. |\n| FR-9 | SVC, AUTH, CFG | `src/server/files/access.ts`: a `Map<string, resolver>`. Default: owner or ADMIN. Return **404** for denied (don't leak existence) and 401 for unauthenticated non-public. Contexts are registered via side-effect import, so the GET handler must import the module that registers `lesson`/`logo` (avoid a lazy-registration bug). |\n| FR-10 | AUTH | `lesson` resolver: load lesson+module+course, then `assertCanViewCourse` + visibility rule (FR-18) for STUDENT/PARENT, while managers see drafts. `logo`: `() => true` incl. `user=null`. Depends on B1. Unattached files (contextId null) fall to the owner/ADMIN check even within the 'lesson' context, which lets editor previews work before attach. |\n| FR-11 | EP, AUTH | `DELETE /api/files/:id`: owner/ADMIN, `contextId === null`, else CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR. Delete the row, then the bytes (log on bytes failure, since orphan bytes are harmless). Audit when ADMIN deletes another user's file (FR-46). |\n| FR-12 | JOB | `purgeOrphanFiles()` in `src/server/files/purge.ts`, hooked at B2. Batch `findMany` where contextId null and createdAt < now-24h, delete bytes then rows. **Caveat:** the logo is \"attached\" how? FR-40 stores a URL in logoUrl but contextId stays null, so the logo gets purged after 24h. **Design must set `contextId` for logo** (e.g. the SchoolSettings id/`'school'`) when settings are saved. |\n| FR-13 | UI | `src/components/FileUpload/`. XHR (not fetch) for `upload.onprogress`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`/`onChange` (FileObject summaries), and optional reorder (FR-27). MUI only (NFR-7). |\n| FR-14 | UI | `src/components/FileList/`: read-only list, links `/api/files/:id`. |\n| FR-15 | DM | `ContentStatus` enum, Module(courseId, title, position, status, publishAt), Lesson(moduleId, title, position, status, publishAt, contentMarkdown, estimatedMinutes, videoUrl, createdById?), LessonAttachment(lessonId, fileId, position), LessonLink(lessonId, title, url, position), and LessonProgress PK [lessonId, studentId]. Cascades: Course→Module→Lesson→Attachment/Link/Progress. Add back-relations on Course/User/StudentProfile. Index `[courseId, position]`, `[moduleId, position]`. Follow the PRD's exact field list. |\n| FR-16 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/content.ts` (Zod), shared by client and server. URL refinements reuse the FR-30 parser for videoUrl. |\n| FR-17 | SVC, AUTH | Inside the PATCH lesson transaction: verify each fileId is (owner==caller or ADMIN) and (contextId null or already == this lessonId), then `updateMany` context/contextId. Removed attachments should be detached (contextId → null), which leaves them purgeable in 24h. Decide explicitly. |\n| FR-18 | SVC | Pure `isVisible(entity, now)` + Prisma `where` fragment `visibleWhere(now)` = `OR[{status:PUBLISHED},{status:SCHEDULED, publishAt:{lte:now}}]` applied to both module and lesson. One source of truth used by list, get, prev/next, files, progress and learning. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Status Chip (grey/blue+date/green). Manager view = no visibility filter. |\n| FR-20 | UI, CFG | `courseTabs` entry `content`, all roles. A server component loads via content-service (not via HTTP). |\n| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Progress is computed over **visible** lessons only. \"Continue\" = first visible lesson in (module.position, lesson.position) order without completedAt. |\n| FR-22 | UI, EP | Menu actions map to PATCH /api/modules/:id (status/publishAt/title), DELETE, and reorder (move up/down reuses the reorder endpoint). |\n| FR-23 | EP, SVC, UI | `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder` with the full tree. Server validates that the set of module ids == the course's modules and the set of lesson ids == all the course's lessons (no foreign ids, no omissions), then rewrites positions + moduleId in one transaction. New dep `@dnd-kit/sortable`. |\n| FR-24 | UI | Type-to-confirm Dialog. Can ConfirmDialog be extended or does it need a local Dialog? Server DELETE cascades regardless. |\n| FR-25 | UI | Page `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` (manage). Client editor with Tabs Write/Preview (Preview = MarkdownView). Toolbar inserts text at the selection. |\n| FR-26 | UI | Image insert → FileUpload context `lesson` → `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. The file must then be attached (FR-17) or it gets purged. **Design:** on save, parse `/api/files/<id>` refs in markdown and attach them as context=lesson (not as LessonAttachment rows), or require explicit attach. |\n| FR-27 | EP, UI | PATCH /api/lessons/:id with `attachments: [{fileId}]` (order = position) and `links: [{title,url}]`. Replace-all semantics in a transaction. |\n| FR-28 | UI, VAL | Schedule: MUI X DateTimePicker (check the MUI X pickers package is installed and allowed, NFR-7). Convert school-tz → UTC on the client or server (NFR-10). Server rejects `publishAt <= now`. |\n| FR-29 | UI | Client timer + dirty flag, `beforeunload` + in-app navigation guard. PATCH with `status` untouched. |\n| FR-30 | SVC | `src/lib/video.ts` `parseVideoUrl(url) → {provider,id}|null`, shared by validator and renderer. Pure, unit test. |\n| FR-31 | UI | `src/components/MarkdownView/`. rehype-sanitize schema: default + `img.src` restricted to `/`-relative (same origin). New deps react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize. Client or server component is fine (react-markdown works in RSC). |\n| FR-32 | UI, SVC | Viewer page. Prev/next computed over the ordered visible-lesson list of the course (service helper reusing FR-18). |\n| FR-33 | EP, SVC, AUTH | First view: an upsert in the viewer page's server load for STUDENT with ACTIVE enrollment (set `firstViewedAt` only on create). `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress {completed}` sets/clears completedAt. Reject PARENT/TEACHER with FORBIDDEN, and a non-visible lesson → NOT_FOUND. |\n| FR-34 | EP, UI | `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` (assertCanManageCourse): ACTIVE enrollments left-joined with progress. 2 queries. |\n| FR-35 | EP, UI, CFG | `studentTabs` entry `learning`, `GET /api/students/:id/learning` (assertCanViewStudent). Per course of ACTIVE enrollments: visible lesson count, completed count, max(updatedAt/completedAt). Avoid per-course N+1 (group queries). |\n| FR-36 | UI, AUTH | Parent read-only: hide the button **and** the server rejects (FR-33). |\n| FR-37 | AUTH | Reuse `assertCanViewCourse` unchanged. |\n| FR-38 | CFG, SVC | `content.lesson_published` in NOTIFICATION_TYPES. Fire only on the transition to visible via \"Publish now\" (lesson PUBLISHED **and** module currently visible). Recipients = ACTIVE enrolled students, using notify() with a batch/loop. |\n| FR-39 | UI | Tooltip only. No job (consistent with FR-18). |\n| FR-40 | UI, SVC | Logo FileUpload, context `logo`, size cap 2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg. On settings save, set FileObject.contextId (see FR-12 caveat) and logoUrl = `/api/files/<id>`. Fix the BaseLayout absolute URL (B4). |\n| FR-41 | VAL, EP | Allowlist is context-aware: `svg` is only in `logo`. file-type can't sniff SVG (it's text), so validate that it's text and contains `<svg`. On GET, add `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` when mime is image/svg+xml. |\n| FR-42 | UI | New `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` (requireRole ADMIN) + a nav entry. LOW confidence, accepted default. |\n| FR-43 | EP | 15 endpoints total (files ×3, modules ×4 incl. POST lessons, lessons ×3, reorder, progress ×2, learning). Use the existing response/error envelope and `{error:{code,message}}`. |\n| FR-44 | EP, AUTH | STUDENT/PARENT get NOT_FOUND (not FORBIDDEN) for hidden lessons. Same rule for files under FR-10. |\n| FR-45 | SVC | Layout: `src/server/content/content-service.ts`, `src/server/files/{access,service,purge,validate}.ts`, `src/server/storage.ts`. Thin routes. |\n| FR-46 | SVC | `audit()` when actor ≠ lesson/module creator. Needs a `createdById` on Module/Lesson, or always audit ADMIN mutations. Check whether FR-15's exact schema includes a creator field. If not, audit when the actor is ADMIN. |\n| FR-47 | DM (seed) | Extend `prisma/seed.ts`. Add `prisma/seed-assets/*.pdf` copied into UPLOAD_DIR by the seed via `saveFile`. Sam = the existing seeded student. |\n| FR-48 | TEST | Unit: sanitizer, video parser, visibility, registry dispatch, sniff rules (FR-6). Integration: upload→attach→download + purge (a temp UPLOAD_DIR). One Playwright e2e. |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH | No files under `public/`, and every read goes through FR-9. Watch B1: making `/api/files/` public must not skip the registry. |\n| NFR-2 | UI | rehype-sanitize strips `javascript:`. Also apply link `href` protocol check in the `a` mapper (defence in depth). Unit/e2e with `[x](javascript:alert(1))`. |\n| NFR-3 | EP | B3. Return 429 RATE_LIMITED with `Retry-After`. Note the ceiling: per-process. |\n| NFR-4 | SVC | Content tab: ≤4 queries (modules with lessons ordered + `_count.attachments` + caller progress `where lessonId in`). Add DB indexes (FR-15). |\n| NFR-5 | SVC | Stream → hash → disk, with the byte cap during the stream. See the FR-3 multipart trade-off. Write to a temp name, then rename on success (no partial files under the final key). |\n| NFR-6 | UI | iframe `title`, alt-text warning, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | Dev must use mui-mcp docs before UI work. Blocker if unreachable. Includes the DateTimePicker (FR-28) package choice. |\n| NFR-8 | AUTH | Every route/page calls the assert helpers. Especially relevant for POST/DELETE /api/files if B1 is applied. |\n| NFR-9 | CFG | 5 new deps only. No renames. lint/typecheck/test green. |\n| NFR-10 | UI, SVC | UTC in the DB. Display via SchoolSettings.timezone (reuse the existing tz formatting helper if present). |\n| NFR-11 | — | No storage interface/S3 abstraction. No content copy. |\n| NFR-12 | CFG | Use the logger instead of console.log. Add `UPLOAD_DIR`, `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` to `.env.example` and the env schema. |\n\n## Open design decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **B1 public files path**: either add `/api/files/` to PUBLIC_API_PATHS with explicit `requireUser()` on POST/DELETE (recommended), or special-case GET in middleware.\n2. **Logo orphan purge (FR-12 × FR-40)**: give logo files a non-null `contextId` on save, or they get deleted after 24h.\n3. **Inline markdown images (FR-26 × FR-12)**: attach images referenced in `contentMarkdown` on save, or they get purged.\n4. **Multipart vs streaming (FR-3 × NFR-5)**: `formData()` + a Content-Length pre-check, or a hand-rolled stream parser. No multipart dep is allowed.\n5. **Detach semantics (FR-17/FR-27)**: removing an attachment either nulls contextId (purged later) or deletes immediately.\n6. **Audit trigger (FR-46)**: either add a creator field or audit all ADMIN mutations on content.\n7. **SVG validation (FR-41)**: text sniff for `<svg`, logo context only, CSP header on serve.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WAAodb1piB4j2mGmiS9EVi","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"602dd78b-ddb5-4a5b-87b4-9966477239d5","uuid":"47dfb0dc-eeef-4daf-9709-e83d0e871602","timestamp":"2026-11-06T18:49:41.638Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-8\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T06:00:00Z), PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008).\nIt has 48 FRs and 12 NFRs (60 requirements) at 93% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers, and they must be surfaced in `system-design.md` Overview.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are still **SH-7** leftovers at the time of writing. Downstream sub-tasks own them and must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-8 input.\n\n## Brownfield findings verified on disk (arch-research-reqs)\n\n| # | Finding | Evidence | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | **Middleware blocks unauthenticated `/api/files/:id`.** `src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for any `/api/*` not matched by `isPublicPath()`. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is `['/api/health','/api/auth/','/api/internal/']`. | middleware.ts L36-40, public-routes.ts L7 | FR-10's public `logo` context cannot work (login page, emails) unless `/api/files/` is made public. **Recommended:** add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. Then the GET handler resolves the session itself (optional user → access registry), and POST/DELETE **must** call `requireUser()` explicitly, because middleware no longer guards them. This is a security-critical design point (NFR-1, NFR-8). |\n| B2 | Daily hook exists: `lastPurgeAt` + `purgeOldNotifications()` in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` L11-31. | grep | FR-12 adds a second call in the same `if` block. No new scheduler. |\n| B3 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) → {ok, retryAfterMs}` is a per-process sliding window. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-3: `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)`. |\n| B4 | `logoUrl` consumers: `BaseLayout.tsx` L28 uses `<Img src={school.logoUrl}>` raw, and `render.ts` already passes `appUrl`. | grep | FR-40 stores a relative `/api/files/<id>`, so BaseLayout must prefix `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. Combined with B1, that makes the logo fetchable from mail clients. |\n| B5 | No `.gitignore` at the repo root. | `ls` | Create one with `uploads/` (plus `node_modules`, `.next`, `.env` if missing). |\n| B6 | No `src/server/files/` and no content code. | ls | Confirms greenfield. |\n| B7 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are arrays of `CourseTab`/`StudentTab` in `src/config/`. | grep | FR-20 / FR-35 append one entry each. |\n| B8 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object in `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, and `ACADEMIC` is a valid category. | grep | FR-38 adds one key. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = server service/module · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = background/maintenance · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = config/env/registry · **TEST**\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | `FileObject` + `@@index([context, contextId])`, unique `storageKey`. `context` is a plain String (registry keys), not an enum, so new contexts need no migration. One migration together with FR-15. |\n| FR-2 | SVC, CFG | `src/server/storage.ts`: `saveFile`/`readFile`/`deleteFile`. Resolve paths with `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR, key)` and assert they stay under UPLOAD_DIR (traversal guard). Add env `UPLOAD_DIR` to the env schema. Single local-disk impl, no interface (NFR-11). |\n| FR-3 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/files` multipart. Use `request.formData()`? It buffers, which conflicts with NFR-5. Use `busboy`-free streaming via `req.body` + the Web `Request` multipart parser? **Design must pick.** Next.js route handlers expose `request.body` (a ReadableStream), but a multipart parser isn't in the allowed deps. Practical option: `formData()` is acceptable only if the size cap is pre-checked via `Content-Length` (≤ MAX_UPLOAD_MB + overhead) before parsing, then `File.stream()` → disk with sha256. Flag as a NFR-5 trade-off for design. |\n| FR-4 | VAL, CFG | `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` env (default 25). Enforce with a byte counter in the write stream (abort and unlink the partial file), plus an early `Content-Length` reject. Logo override: 2 MB (FR-40). Make the limit per-context: `{ logo: 2 }`, default env. |\n| FR-5 | VAL | Extension allowlist + `fileTypeFromBuffer` on the first ~4100 bytes (peek before or while writing). New dep `file-type` (ESM-only, so check the Next server bundling). |\n| FR-6 | VAL | Rule table: txt/csv → sniff must be `undefined`. docx/xlsx/pptx → sniff ∈ {zip, matching OOXML mime}. zip → zip. Others → sniff ext must match the declared ext (jpg≡jpeg). Pure function, unit-testable (FR-48). |\n| FR-7 | VAL | `sanitizeFilename()`: strip `/ \\ ` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trim, and cap at 150 while preserving the extension. Pure function and unit test. |\n| FR-8 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/files/:id`: registry check **before** `readFile`. Headers: stored mime, `nosniff`, `attachment; filename*=UTF-8''…`, and `inline` only if `?inline=1` and mime is image/* or application/pdf. Stream via `Readable.toWeb(fs.createReadStream)`. |\n| FR-9 | SVC, AUTH, CFG | `src/server/files/access.ts`: a `Map<string, resolver>`. Default: owner or ADMIN. Return **404** for denied (don't leak existence) and 401 for unauthenticated non-public. Contexts are registered via side-effect import, so the GET handler must import the module that registers `lesson`/`logo` (avoid a lazy-registration bug). |\n| FR-10 | AUTH | `lesson` resolver: load lesson+module+course, then `assertCanViewCourse` + visibility rule (FR-18) for STUDENT/PARENT, while managers see drafts. `logo`: `() => true` incl. `user=null`. Depends on B1. Unattached files (contextId null) fall to the owner/ADMIN check even within the 'lesson' context, which lets editor previews work before attach. |\n| FR-11 | EP, AUTH | `DELETE /api/files/:id`: owner/ADMIN, `contextId === null`, else CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR. Delete the row, then the bytes (log on bytes failure, since orphan bytes are harmless). Audit when ADMIN deletes another user's file (FR-46). |\n| FR-12 | JOB | `purgeOrphanFiles()` in `src/server/files/purge.ts`, hooked at B2. Batch `findMany` where contextId null and createdAt < now-24h, delete bytes then rows. **Caveat:** the logo is \"attached\" how? FR-40 stores a URL in logoUrl but contextId stays null, so the logo gets purged after 24h. **Design must set `contextId` for logo** (e.g. the SchoolSettings id/`'school'`) when settings are saved. |\n| FR-13 | UI | `src/components/FileUpload/`. XHR (not fetch) for `upload.onprogress`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`/`onChange` (FileObject summaries), and optional reorder (FR-27). MUI only (NFR-7). |\n| FR-14 | UI | `src/components/FileList/`: read-only list, links `/api/files/:id`. |\n| FR-15 | DM | `ContentStatus` enum, Module(courseId, title, position, status, publishAt), Lesson(moduleId, title, position, status, publishAt, contentMarkdown, estimatedMinutes, videoUrl, createdById?), LessonAttachment(lessonId, fileId, position), LessonLink(lessonId, title, url, position), and LessonProgress PK [lessonId, studentId]. Cascades: Course→Module→Lesson→Attachment/Link/Progress. Add back-relations on Course/User/StudentProfile. Index `[courseId, position]`, `[moduleId, position]`. Follow the PRD's exact field list. |\n| FR-16 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/content.ts` (Zod), shared by client and server. URL refinements reuse the FR-30 parser for videoUrl. |\n| FR-17 | SVC, AUTH | Inside the PATCH lesson transaction: verify each fileId is (owner==caller or ADMIN) and (contextId null or already == this lessonId), then `updateMany` context/contextId. Removed attachments should be detached (contextId → null), which leaves them purgeable in 24h. Decide explicitly. |\n| FR-18 | SVC | Pure `isVisible(entity, now)` + Prisma `where` fragment `visibleWhere(now)` = `OR[{status:PUBLISHED},{status:SCHEDULED, publishAt:{lte:now}}]` applied to both module and lesson. One source of truth used by list, get, prev/next, files, progress and learning. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Status Chip (grey/blue+date/green). Manager view = no visibility filter. |\n| FR-20 | UI, CFG | `courseTabs` entry `content`, all roles. A server component loads via content-service (not via HTTP). |\n| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Progress is computed over **visible** lessons only. \"Continue\" = first visible lesson in (module.position, lesson.position) order without completedAt. |\n| FR-22 | UI, EP | Menu actions map to PATCH /api/modules/:id (status/publishAt/title), DELETE, and reorder (move up/down reuses the reorder endpoint). |\n| FR-23 | EP, SVC, UI | `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder` with the full tree. Server validates that the set of module ids == the course's modules and the set of lesson ids == all the course's lessons (no foreign ids, no omissions), then rewrites positions + moduleId in one transaction. New dep `@dnd-kit/sortable`. |\n| FR-24 | UI | Type-to-confirm Dialog. Can ConfirmDialog be extended or does it need a local Dialog? Server DELETE cascades regardless. |\n| FR-25 | UI | Page `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` (manage). Client editor with Tabs Write/Preview (Preview = MarkdownView). Toolbar inserts text at the selection. |\n| FR-26 | UI | Image insert → FileUpload context `lesson` → `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. The file must then be attached (FR-17) or it gets purged. **Design:** on save, parse `/api/files/<id>` refs in markdown and attach them as context=lesson (not as LessonAttachment rows), or require explicit attach. |\n| FR-27 | EP, UI | PATCH /api/lessons/:id with `attachments: [{fileId}]` (order = position) and `links: [{title,url}]`. Replace-all semantics in a transaction. |\n| FR-28 | UI, VAL | Schedule: MUI X DateTimePicker (check the MUI X pickers package is installed and allowed, NFR-7). Convert school-tz → UTC on the client or server (NFR-10). Server rejects `publishAt <= now`. |\n| FR-29 | UI | Client timer + dirty flag, `beforeunload` + in-app navigation guard. PATCH with `status` untouched. |\n| FR-30 | SVC | `src/lib/video.ts` `parseVideoUrl(url) → {provider,id}|null`, shared by validator and renderer. Pure, unit test. |\n| FR-31 | UI | `src/components/MarkdownView/`. rehype-sanitize schema: default + `img.src` restricted to `/`-relative (same origin). New deps react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize. Client or server component is fine (react-markdown works in RSC). |\n| FR-32 | UI, SVC | Viewer page. Prev/next computed over the ordered visible-lesson list of the course (service helper reusing FR-18). |\n| FR-33 | EP, SVC, AUTH | First view: an upsert in the viewer page's server load for STUDENT with ACTIVE enrollment (set `firstViewedAt` only on create). `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress {completed}` sets/clears completedAt. Reject PARENT/TEACHER with FORBIDDEN, and a non-visible lesson → NOT_FOUND. |\n| FR-34 | EP, UI | `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` (assertCanManageCourse): ACTIVE enrollments left-joined with progress. 2 queries. |\n| FR-35 | EP, UI, CFG | `studentTabs` entry `learning`, `GET /api/students/:id/learning` (assertCanViewStudent). Per course of ACTIVE enrollments: visible lesson count, completed count, max(updatedAt/completedAt). Avoid per-course N+1 (group queries). |\n| FR-36 | UI, AUTH | Parent read-only: hide the button **and** the server rejects (FR-33). |\n| FR-37 | AUTH | Reuse `assertCanViewCourse` unchanged. |\n| FR-38 | CFG, SVC | `content.lesson_published` in NOTIFICATION_TYPES. Fire only on the transition to visible via \"Publish now\" (lesson PUBLISHED **and** module currently visible). Recipients = ACTIVE enrolled students, using notify() with a batch/loop. |\n| FR-39 | UI | Tooltip only. No job (consistent with FR-18). |\n| FR-40 | UI, SVC | Logo FileUpload, context `logo`, size cap 2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg. On settings save, set FileObject.contextId (see FR-12 caveat) and logoUrl = `/api/files/<id>`. Fix the BaseLayout absolute URL (B4). |\n| FR-41 | VAL, EP | Allowlist is context-aware: `svg` is only in `logo`. file-type can't sniff SVG (it's text), so validate that it's text and contains `<svg`. On GET, add `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` when mime is image/svg+xml. |\n| FR-42 | UI | New `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` (requireRole ADMIN) + a nav entry. LOW confidence, accepted default. |\n| FR-43 | EP | 15 endpoints total (files ×3, modules ×4 incl. POST lessons, lessons ×3, reorder, progress ×2, learning). Use the existing response/error envelope and `{error:{code,message}}`. |\n| FR-44 | EP, AUTH | STUDENT/PARENT get NOT_FOUND (not FORBIDDEN) for hidden lessons. Same rule for files under FR-10. |\n| FR-45 | SVC | Layout: `src/server/content/content-service.ts`, `src/server/files/{access,service,purge,validate}.ts`, `src/server/storage.ts`. Thin routes. |\n| FR-46 | SVC | `audit()` when actor ≠ lesson/module creator. Needs a `createdById` on Module/Lesson, or always audit ADMIN mutations. Check whether FR-15's exact schema includes a creator field. If not, audit when the actor is ADMIN. |\n| FR-47 | DM (seed) | Extend `prisma/seed.ts`. Add `prisma/seed-assets/*.pdf` copied into UPLOAD_DIR by the seed via `saveFile`. Sam = the existing seeded student. |\n| FR-48 | TEST | Unit: sanitizer, video parser, visibility, registry dispatch, sniff rules (FR-6). Integration: upload→attach→download + purge (a temp UPLOAD_DIR). One Playwright e2e. |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH | No files under `public/`, and every read goes through FR-9. Watch B1: making `/api/files/` public must not skip the registry. |\n| NFR-2 | UI | rehype-sanitize strips `javascript:`. Also apply link `href` protocol check in the `a` mapper (defence in depth). Unit/e2e with `[x](javascript:alert(1))`. |\n| NFR-3 | EP | B3. Return 429 RATE_LIMITED with `Retry-After`. Note the ceiling: per-process. |\n| NFR-4 | SVC | Content tab: ≤4 queries (modules with lessons ordered + `_count.attachments` + caller progress `where lessonId in`). Add DB indexes (FR-15). |\n| NFR-5 | SVC | Stream → hash → disk, with the byte cap during the stream. See the FR-3 multipart trade-off. Write to a temp name, then rename on success (no partial files under the final key). |\n| NFR-6 | UI | iframe `title`, alt-text warning, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | Dev must use mui-mcp docs before UI work. Blocker if unreachable. Includes the DateTimePicker (FR-28) package choice. |\n| NFR-8 | AUTH | Every route/page calls the assert helpers. Especially relevant for POST/DELETE /api/files if B1 is applied. |\n| NFR-9 | CFG | 5 new deps only. No renames. lint/typecheck/test green. |\n| NFR-10 | UI, SVC | UTC in the DB. Display via SchoolSettings.timezone (reuse the existing tz formatting helper if present). |\n| NFR-11 | — | No storage interface/S3 abstraction. No content copy. |\n| NFR-12 | CFG | Use the logger instead of console.log. Add `UPLOAD_DIR`, `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` to `.env.example` and the env schema. |\n\n## Open design decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **B1 public files path**: either add `/api/files/` to PUBLIC_API_PATHS with explicit `requireUser()` on POST/DELETE (recommended), or special-case GET in middleware.\n2. **Logo orphan purge (FR-12 × FR-40)**: give logo files a non-null `contextId` on save, or they get deleted after 24h.\n3. **Inline markdown images (FR-26 × FR-12)**: attach images referenced in `contentMarkdown` on save, or they get purged.\n4. **Multipart vs streaming (FR-3 × NFR-5)**: `formData()` + a Content-Length pre-check, or a hand-rolled stream parser. No multipart dep is allowed.\n5. **Detach semantics (FR-17/FR-27)**: removing an attachment either nulls contextId (purged later) or deletes immediately.\n6. **Audit trigger (FR-46)**: either add a creator field or audit all ADMIN mutations on content.\n7. **SVG validation (FR-41)**: text sniff for `<svg`, logo context only, CSP header on serve.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":94,"newStart":1,"newLines":97,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-7","+# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-8"," "," Written by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T05:29:02Z), PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007).","-It has 41 FRs and 10 NFRs (51 requirements) at 94% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.","-Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T06:00:00Z), PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008).","+It has 48 FRs and 12 NFRs (60 requirements) at 93% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers, and they must be surfaced in `system-design.md` Overview."," ","-> This file replaces the stale SH-1 notes that were here before.","+> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are still **SH-7** leftovers at the time of writing. Downstream sub-tasks own them and must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-8 input."," ","-**Headline:** this is a **greenfield feature inside a brownfield app**. Everything attendance-related is new: the","-models, migration, service, validators, 10 API routes (9 from FR-35 plus PATCH settings from FR-5), 4 page areas,","-2 tabs, nav entries, seed data and tests. It builds on these existing exports. I checked each one on disk:","+## Brownfield findings verified on disk (arch-research-reqs)"," ","-| Reuse | Location | Verified signature / note |","-|---|---|---|","-| Schedule | `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts:542` | `getScheduleForDate(target: {userId, role} \\| {sectionId}, date)` → `{period, course, room}[]`. Returns `[]` for ADMIN/PARENT and on non-teaching days. Has the PRD-14 holiday hook comment. `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` at :565 already finds the running period, so use it for the FR-6 highlight. |","-| Notify | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts:98` | `notifyStudentAndParents({...NotifyInput minus userIds, studentIds})` never throws. Title and body are per student, so call it **once per student** (FR-21). |","-| Notif types | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` map + `NotificationTypeDef {label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. The `ATTENDANCE` category already exists. |","-| Access | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | `assertCanManageCourse`, `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanViewStudent`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`'ALL' \\| string[]`). |","-| Settings | `src/server/services/settings.ts` | `getSchoolSettings()` (singleton upsert, `cache`d) and `updateSchoolSettings(input)`. **`UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` must gain** `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?`. |","-| Misc | `src/server/audit.ts`, `src/server/csv.ts`, `src/server/http.ts` | `audit(input)`, `toCsv(columns, rows)`, response helpers. |","-| UI | `src/components/<Name>/` | DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast. They are **not** in `components/shared/`. |","-| Extension points | `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | Arrays of `{key, label, href(id), roles}`. Append entries to them. |","+| # | Finding | Evidence | Impact |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| B1 | **Middleware blocks unauthenticated `/api/files/:id`.** `src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for any `/api/*` not matched by `isPublicPath()`. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is `['/api/health','/api/auth/','/api/internal/']`. | middleware.ts L36-40, public-routes.ts L7 | FR-10's public `logo` context cannot work (login page, emails) unless `/api/files/` is made public. **Recommended:** add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. Then the GET handler resolves the session itself (optional user → access registry), and POST/DELETE **must** call `requireUser()` explicitly, because middleware no longer guards them. This is a security-critical design point (NFR-1, NFR-8). |","+| B2 | Daily hook exists: `lastPurgeAt` + `purgeOldNotifications()` in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` L11-31. | grep | FR-12 adds a second call in the same `if` block. No new scheduler. |","+| B3 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) → {ok, retryAfterMs}` is a per-process sliding window. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-3: `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)`. |","+| B4 | `logoUrl` consumers: `BaseLayout.tsx` L28 uses `<Img src={school.logoUrl}>` raw, and `render.ts` already passes `appUrl`. | grep | FR-40 stores a relative `/api/files/<id>`, so BaseLayout must prefix `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. Combined with B1, that makes the logo fetchable from mail clients. |","+| B5 | No `.gitignore` at the repo root. | `ls` | Create one with `uploads/` (plus `node_modules`, `.next`, `.env` if missing). |","+| B6 | No `src/server/files/` and no content code. | ls | Confirms greenfield. |","+| B7 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are arrays of `CourseTab`/`StudentTab` in `src/config/`. | grep | FR-20 / FR-35 append one entry each. |","+| B8 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object in `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, and `ACADEMIC` is a valid category. | grep | FR-38 adds one key. |"," ","-Gaps confirmed on disk: `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty and `src/app/(app)/admin/` has only `courses`,","-`email-log` and `sections`, with no settings page. The latest migration is `20261106000000_user_role_status_index`.","+## Requirement → architectural concern"," ","-Concern buckets: **Data Model**, **Service**, **Validation**, **API**, **Auth Boundary**, **Notifications**,","-**UI: Register**, **UI: Tabs**, **UI: Admin**, **Config/Nav**, **Seed**, **Tests**, **Cross-cutting**.","+Concern legend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = server service/module · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = background/maintenance · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = config/env/registry · **TEST**"," ","-## Requirement → Concern table","-","-| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |","+| Req | Concern | Notes |"," |---|---|---|","-| FR-1 | Data Model | New `AttendanceStatus` enum and `AttendanceSession` / `AttendanceRecord` models. Records use `@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` and `@@index([studentId, createdAt])`. `date` is `@db.Date` (NFR-8). The session needs a `takenById`/`updatedById` + `updatedAt` for FR-6/FR-14. Records need `minutesLate Int?` and `note String?` (FR-12). |","-| FR-2 | Data Model + Service | XOR courseId/sectionId: raw SQL `CHECK ((courseId IS NULL) <> (sectionId IS NULL))` in the migration, and a guard in the service before insert. |","-| FR-3 | Data Model (migration SQL) | Two partial unique indexes: `(courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL` and `(sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL`. Prisma can't express these, so they go in hand-written SQL in the migration after `20261106000000`. **Consequence:** `upsert` cannot target them. The service must use `findFirst` + create/update inside the transaction, and catch P2002 on a race. |","-| FR-4 | Data Model | `SchoolSettings.attendanceMode` (new enum `AttendanceMode`, default `PER_PERIOD`) and `attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)`. Same migration. |","-| FR-5 | API + UI: Admin (MEDIUM) | No settings page exists. Smallest fix: `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN, Zod-validated, calls the extended `updateSchoolSettings`) and an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance`. That avoids a new page. |","-| FR-6 | Service + UI: Register | `GET /api/attendance/today` → `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` joined with today's sessions to show \"Taken HH:mm by name\". Highlight comes from `getCurrentSlot`. Times are shown in the school tz. |","-| FR-7 | Service + UI | If mode ∈ {DAILY_HOMEROOM, BOTH}, add entries for `Section.homeroomTeacherId = user` to `/today`. |","-| FR-8 | Validation + Auth Boundary | Shared date rule in the validators: no future date (school tz). Teachers can go back 14 days, admins any date. The same rule runs on the client and the server. |","-| FR-9 | Service + UI: Register | Course roster = `Enrollment` where status ACTIVE on the date, sorted by last name. Use the MUI `ToggleButtonGroup` (exclusive). Initial state is null for a new register. |","-| FR-10 | Auth Boundary + Validation | The server rejects `EXCUSED` from non-ADMIN with 403/VALIDATION_ERROR. The UI disables it for teachers. |","-| FR-11 | UI: Register | Client-only: fill nulls with PRESENT. |","-| FR-12 | Validation + UI | `minutesLate` 1–240 is required iff LATE (Zod `superRefine`) and defaults to 5 in the UI. `note` max 500. |","-| FR-13 | UI: Register | Derived counters. Save is disabled while any row is unmarked. The server also requires a full roster (or at least one valid record per student sent). |","-| FR-14 | Service | One `prisma.$transaction`: find/create the session, then upsert the records (`@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` works for `upsert`). Set `updatedById` on the session. The GET returns last-changed-by/at. |","-| FR-15 | Service + Auth Boundary | Section variant: roster = `SectionMember` for the current academic year. Access = `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` or ADMIN. No existing `assertCanManageSection` helper, so add a small one in the attendance service (or `auth/`). |","-| FR-16 | UI: Register (LOW) | Route `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` component with a section-scoped GET/PUT. |","-| FR-17 | UI: Register | Mobile: rows ≥ 48 px, toggles ≥ 44×44, sticky `Paper` save bar. Use theme `sx` only. |","-| FR-18 | Service + Audit | Inside the save, diff old vs new per student. For changed existing records call `audit({action:'attendance.record.update', before, after, actor, note})`. |","-| FR-19 | Service + Auth Boundary | Pure function `canEdit(user, sessionDate, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today - date ≤ 14 days`. The GET returns `readOnly` + `readOnlyReason`. The PUT returns 403. Unit-tested (FR-39). |","-| FR-20 | Notifications | Add `attendance.absent` (ATTENDANCE, email true, mandatoryInApp true, PARENT+STUDENT) and `attendance.late` (email false). |","-| FR-21 | Notifications + Service | After commit (outside the tx), call `notifyStudentAndParents` per changed student. Daily-register body: `<Section> daily register, <date>` (intake default). Link `/students/<id>/attendance`. |","-| FR-22 | Notifications + Service | Pure `diffForNotifications(prev, next)` → `{absent[], late[], corrected[]}`. Only a transition *into* ABSENT/LATE sends a notice, so re-saving with the same status sends nothing. ABSENT→PRESENT sends `attendance.corrected`. Unit-tested (FR-39). |","-| FR-23 | Notifications (LOW) | `attendance.corrected` (ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false), `attendance.register_missing` (ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false). |","-| FR-24 | Config | Append `{key:'attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}` to `studentTabs`. |","-| FR-25 | Service + UI: Tabs | Term = the Term containing today, else the most recent ended term (intake default). Use `StatCard` ×4 for term and year. |","-| FR-26 | UI: Tabs | MUI X `DateCalendar` read-only with a custom `day` slot coloured from per-day aggregates and a `Tooltip`. Month change refetches or filters `?from=&to=`. |","-| FR-27 | API + Auth Boundary | `GET /api/students/:id/attendance` → `assertCanViewStudent`. **Strip `note`** for STUDENT/PARENT on the server (AC-8). The table uses `DataTable`. |","-| FR-28 | Service (pure) | `attendanceRate(records)` = (P+L+E)/total×100, rounded to 1 dp; empty → null. Include DROPPED enrollments (filter on student, not enrollment). Mode chooses the source: course sessions (PER_PERIOD/BOTH) or section sessions (DAILY_HOMEROOM). Unit-tested. |","-| FR-29 | API + UI: Tabs + Config | `GET /api/courses/:id/attendance` (`assertCanManageCourse`) → last 20 sessions × enrolled students. Use MUI X DataGrid with dynamic columns. The header click links to the register. Course tab roles: ADMIN, TEACHER. |","-| FR-30 | Service + UI: Admin | Overview: expected = all timetable slots for today (all teachers) + sections if the mode includes daily; taken = sessions today; rate today. ADMIN gets `[]` from `getScheduleForDate`, so it **needs a school-wide slot query** (a direct `timetableSlot.findMany` by `dayOfWeek`, or a new helper next to `getScheduleForDate`). |","-| FR-31 | Service + API + Notifications | Missing = expected meetings with no session and `now ≥ period.startTime + 15 min` (school tz). `POST /api/admin/attendance/remind` → `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[teacherId]})`. |","-| FR-32 | Service + API + Validation | Report filters (range ≤ 366 days, grade, section, course, status) go into a per-student aggregate (use a SQL `groupBy` for performance). `?format=csv` → `toCsv` with the same columns. |","-| FR-33 | Service + API | YTD rate per student < threshold, sorted ascending. Reuses the same aggregate as FR-32 with the year's date range. |","-| FR-34 | Config/Nav | `navigation.ts`: TEACHER → `/attendance/take`, ADMIN → `/admin/attendance`. |","-| FR-35 | API | The 9 listed routes, plus PATCH settings from FR-5. Every handler starts with `requireUser`/`requireRole` and then the resource assert. They use the `http.ts` helpers. |","-| FR-36 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts`: `registerQuery`, `registerPutBody`, `studentAttendanceQuery`, `reportFilters`, `remindBody`, `attendanceSettingsPatch`. The register form imports them too. |","-| FR-37 | Service | `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts`. Keep the pure helpers (`attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`) in the same file or a sibling `attendance-rules.ts` so the tests need no DB. |","-| FR-38 | Seed | Extend the existing seed. Use a seeded RNG, 15 teaching days before the run date, 7A and 7B, a 94/3/3 split, and two Grade 7 students forced below 85%. Respect the existing school-day config. |","-| FR-39 | Tests (unit) | `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`. |","-| FR-40 | Tests (integration) | The save transaction, non-enrolled rejection (NFR-3), and the partial unique indexes (a duplicate insert raises). |","-| FR-41 | Tests (e2e) | Playwright: the 375 px take flow, and a parent seeing the notification plus the calendar absence. |","-| NFR-1 | Performance | Save: one tx with batched upserts (≈35). Avoid N+1 by loading existing records in one query. Student tab: one indexed query on `[studentId, createdAt]` (consider filtering on `session.date` and adding an index if needed). Aggregate in memory (1,200 rows is fine). |","-| NFR-2 | UI: Register (client) | localStorage key `attendance:<course\\|section>:<id>:<date>:<periodId\\|daily>`. Write it on a network failure, clear it on success, and offer a restore banner when it is present. |","-| NFR-3 | Service (integrity) | Validate every `studentId` against the ACTIVE enrollment on the date (`enrolledAt ≤ date` and not dropped before it) or the section membership. Any miss → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR and the whole save is rejected. |","-| NFR-4 | UI: Register | Satisfied by FR-11 + FR-17 (mark all present, then fix the exceptions). |","-| NFR-5 | Notifications | `notify()` writes in-app notifications immediately and queues EmailOutbox. Call it post-commit without blocking the response on email. |","-| NFR-6 | Cross-cutting (UI) | MUI only. Dev must use mui-mcp docs for 9.5.0 (ToggleButtonGroup, DateCalendar day slot, DataGrid, Paper sticky). **Hard blocker if unreachable.** |","-| NFR-7 | Auth Boundary | Server-side checks on every handler and server page. Per-role scope is listed above. Teachers also get their homeroom sections. |","-| NFR-8 | Cross-cutting | `@db.Date`, cuid IDs, UTC storage with display in school tz (`date-fns-tz`, already installed), the logger, `audit()` for edits to records owned by others, and pageSize ≤ 100 on the report and student records. |","-| NFR-9 | UI accessibility | `aria-label` on each toggle (\"Mark <name> present\"), 44 px targets. |","-| NFR-10 | Cross-cutting | Reuse the helpers above, add no new deps, rename nothing. Holidays (PRD-14) and the EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) are out of scope beyond the admin-only option. |","+| FR-1 | DM | `FileObject` + `@@index([context, contextId])`, unique `storageKey`. `context` is a plain String (registry keys), not an enum, so new contexts need no migration. One migration together with FR-15. |","+| FR-2 | SVC, CFG | `src/server/storage.ts`: `saveFile`/`readFile`/`deleteFile`. Resolve paths with `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR, key)` and assert they stay under UPLOAD_DIR (traversal guard). Add env `UPLOAD_DIR` to the env schema. Single local-disk impl, no interface (NFR-11). |","+| FR-3 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/files` multipart. Use `request.formData()`? It buffers, which conflicts with NFR-5. Use `busboy`-free streaming via `req.body` + the Web `Request` multipart parser? **Design must pick.** Next.js route handlers expose `request.body` (a ReadableStream), but a multipart parser isn't in the allowed deps. Practical option: `formData()` is acceptable only if the size cap is pre-checked via `Content-Length` (≤ MAX_UPLOAD_MB + overhead) before parsing, then `File.stream()` → disk with sha256. Flag as a NFR-5 trade-off for design. |","+| FR-4 | VAL, CFG | `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` env (default 25). Enforce with a byte counter in the write stream (abort and unlink the partial file), plus an early `Content-Length` reject. Logo override: 2 MB (FR-40). Make the limit per-context: `{ logo: 2 }`, default env. |","+| FR-5 | VAL | Extension allowlist + `fileTypeFromBuffer` on the first ~4100 bytes (peek before or while writing). New dep `file-type` (ESM-only, so check the Next server bundling). |","+| FR-6 | VAL | Rule table: txt/csv → sniff must be `undefined`. docx/xlsx/pptx → sniff ∈ {zip, matching OOXML mime}. zip → zip. Others → sniff ext must match the declared ext (jpg≡jpeg). Pure function, unit-testable (FR-48). |","+| FR-7 | VAL | `sanitizeFilename()`: strip `/ \\ ` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trim, and cap at 150 while preserving the extension. Pure function and unit test. |","+| FR-8 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/files/:id`: registry check **before** `readFile`. Headers: stored mime, `nosniff`, `attachment; filename*=UTF-8''…`, and `inline` only if `?inline=1` and mime is image/* or application/pdf. Stream via `Readable.toWeb(fs.createReadStream)`. |","+| FR-9 | SVC, AUTH, CFG | `src/server/files/access.ts`: a `Map<string, resolver>`. Default: owner or ADMIN. Return **404** for denied (don't leak existence) and 401 for unauthenticated non-public. Contexts are registered via side-effect import, so the GET handler must import the module that registers `lesson`/`logo` (avoid a lazy-registration bug). |","+| FR-10 | AUTH | `lesson` resolver: load lesson+module+course, then `assertCanViewCourse` + visibility rule (FR-18) for STUDENT/PARENT, while managers see drafts. `logo`: `() => true` incl. `user=null`. Depends on B1. Unattached files (contextId null) fall to the owner/ADMIN check even within the 'lesson' context, which lets editor previews work before attach. |","+| FR-11 | EP, AUTH | `DELETE /api/files/:id`: owner/ADMIN, `contextId === null`, else CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR. Delete the row, then the bytes (log on bytes failure, since orphan bytes are harmless). Audit when ADMIN deletes another user's file (FR-46). |","+| FR-12 | JOB | `purgeOrphanFiles()` in `src/server/files/purge.ts`, hooked at B2. Batch `findMany` where contextId null and createdAt < now-24h, delete bytes then rows. **Caveat:** the logo is \"attached\" how? FR-40 stores a URL in logoUrl but contextId stays null, so the logo gets purged after 24h. **Design must set `contextId` for logo** (e.g. the SchoolSettings id/`'school'`) when settings are saved. |","+| FR-13 | UI | `src/components/FileUpload/`. XHR (not fetch) for `upload.onprogress`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`/`onChange` (FileObject summaries), and optional reorder (FR-27). MUI only (NFR-7). |","+| FR-14 | UI | `src/components/FileList/`: read-only list, links `/api/files/:id`. |","+| FR-15 | DM | `ContentStatus` enum, Module(courseId, title, position, status, publishAt), Lesson(moduleId, title, position, status, publishAt, contentMarkdown, estimatedMinutes, videoUrl, createdById?), LessonAttachment(lessonId, fileId, position), LessonLink(lessonId, title, url, position), and LessonProgress PK [lessonId, studentId]. Cascades: Course→Module→Lesson→Attachment/Link/Progress. Add back-relations on Course/User/StudentProfile. Index `[courseId, position]`, `[moduleId, position]`. Follow the PRD's exact field list. |","+| FR-16 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/content.ts` (Zod), shared by client and server. URL refinements reuse the FR-30 parser for videoUrl. |","+| FR-17 | SVC, AUTH | Inside the PATCH lesson transaction: verify each fileId is (owner==caller or ADMIN) and (contextId null or already == this lessonId), then `updateMany` context/contextId. Removed attachments should be detached (contextId → null), which leaves them purgeable in 24h. Decide explicitly. |","+| FR-18 | SVC | Pure `isVisible(entity, now)` + Prisma `where` fragment `visibleWhere(now)` = `OR[{status:PUBLISHED},{status:SCHEDULED, publishAt:{lte:now}}]` applied to both module and lesson. One source of truth used by list, get, prev/next, files, progress and learning. |","+| FR-19 | UI | Status Chip (grey/blue+date/green). Manager view = no visibility filter. |","+| FR-20 | UI, CFG | `courseTabs` entry `content`, all roles. A server component loads via content-service (not via HTTP). |","+| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Progress is computed over **visible** lessons only. \"Continue\" = first visible lesson in (module.position, lesson.position) order without completedAt. |","+| FR-22 | UI, EP | Menu actions map to PATCH /api/modules/:id (status/publishAt/title), DELETE, and reorder (move up/down reuses the reorder endpoint). |","+| FR-23 | EP, SVC, UI | `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder` with the full tree. Server validates that the set of module ids == the course's modules and the set of lesson ids == all the course's lessons (no foreign ids, no omissions), then rewrites positions + moduleId in one transaction. New dep `@dnd-kit/sortable`. |","+| FR-24 | UI | Type-to-confirm Dialog. Can ConfirmDialog be extended or does it need a local Dialog? Server DELETE cascades regardless. |","+| FR-25 | UI | Page `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` (manage). Client editor with Tabs Write/Preview (Preview = MarkdownView). Toolbar inserts text at the selection. |","+| FR-26 | UI | Image insert → FileUpload context `lesson` → `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. The file must then be attached (FR-17) or it gets purged. **Design:** on save, parse `/api/files/<id>` refs in markdown and attach them as context=lesson (not as LessonAttachment rows), or require explicit attach. |","+| FR-27 | EP, UI | PATCH /api/lessons/:id with `attachments: [{fileId}]` (order = position) and `links: [{title,url}]`. Replace-all semantics in a transaction. |","+| FR-28 | UI, VAL | Schedule: MUI X DateTimePicker (check the MUI X pickers package is installed and allowed, NFR-7). Convert school-tz → UTC on the client or server (NFR-10). Server rejects `publishAt <= now`. |","+| FR-29 | UI | Client timer + dirty flag, `beforeunload` + in-app navigation guard. PATCH with `status` untouched. |","+| FR-30 | SVC | `src/lib/video.ts` `parseVideoUrl(url) → {provider,id}|null`, shared by validator and renderer. Pure, unit test. |","+| FR-31 | UI | `src/components/MarkdownView/`. rehype-sanitize schema: default + `img.src` restricted to `/`-relative (same origin). New deps react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize. Client or server component is fine (react-markdown works in RSC). |","+| FR-32 | UI, SVC | Viewer page. Prev/next computed over the ordered visible-lesson list of the course (service helper reusing FR-18). |","+| FR-33 | EP, SVC, AUTH | First view: an upsert in the viewer page's server load for STUDENT with ACTIVE enrollment (set `firstViewedAt` only on create). `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress {completed}` sets/clears completedAt. Reject PARENT/TEACHER with FORBIDDEN, and a non-visible lesson → NOT_FOUND. |","+| FR-34 | EP, UI | `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` (assertCanManageCourse): ACTIVE enrollments left-joined with progress. 2 queries. |","+| FR-35 | EP, UI, CFG | `studentTabs` entry `learning`, `GET /api/students/:id/learning` (assertCanViewStudent). Per course of ACTIVE enrollments: visible lesson count, completed count, max(updatedAt/completedAt). Avoid per-course N+1 (group queries). |","+| FR-36 | UI, AUTH | Parent read-only: hide the button **and** the server rejects (FR-33). |","+| FR-37 | AUTH | Reuse `assertCanViewCourse` unchanged. |","+| FR-38 | CFG, SVC | `content.lesson_published` in NOTIFICATION_TYPES. Fire only on the transition to visible via \"Publish now\" (lesson PUBLISHED **and** module currently visible). Recipients = ACTIVE enrolled students, using notify() with a batch/loop. |","+| FR-39 | UI | Tooltip only. No job (consistent with FR-18). |","+| FR-40 | UI, SVC | Logo FileUpload, context `logo`, size cap 2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg. On settings save, set FileObject.contextId (see FR-12 caveat) and logoUrl = `/api/files/<id>`. Fix the BaseLayout absolute URL (B4). |","+| FR-41 | VAL, EP | Allowlist is context-aware: `svg` is only in `logo`. file-type can't sniff SVG (it's text), so validate that it's text and contains `<svg`. On GET, add `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` when mime is image/svg+xml. |","+| FR-42 | UI | New `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` (requireRole ADMIN) + a nav entry. LOW confidence, accepted default. |","+| FR-43 | EP | 15 endpoints total (files ×3, modules ×4 incl. POST lessons, lessons ×3, reorder, progress ×2, learning). Use the existing response/error envelope and `{error:{code,message}}`. |","+| FR-44 | EP, AUTH | STUDENT/PARENT get NOT_FOUND (not FORBIDDEN) for hidden lessons. Same rule for files under FR-10. |","+| FR-45 | SVC | Layout: `src/server/content/content-service.ts`, `src/server/files/{access,service,purge,validate}.ts`, `src/server/storage.ts`. Thin routes. |","+| FR-46 | SVC | `audit()` when actor ≠ lesson/module creator. Needs a `createdById` on Module/Lesson, or always audit ADMIN mutations. Check whether FR-15's exact schema includes a creator field. If not, audit when the actor is ADMIN. |","+| FR-47 | DM (seed) | Extend `prisma/seed.ts`. Add `prisma/seed-assets/*.pdf` copied into UPLOAD_DIR by the seed via `saveFile`. Sam = the existing seeded student. |","+| FR-48 | TEST | Unit: sanitizer, video parser, visibility, registry dispatch, sniff rules (FR-6). Integration: upload→attach→download + purge (a temp UPLOAD_DIR). One Playwright e2e. |","+| NFR-1 | AUTH | No files under `public/`, and every read goes through FR-9. Watch B1: making `/api/files/` public must not skip the registry. |","+| NFR-2 | UI | rehype-sanitize strips `javascript:`. Also apply link `href` protocol check in the `a` mapper (defence in depth). Unit/e2e with `[x](javascript:alert(1))`. |","+| NFR-3 | EP | B3. Return 429 RATE_LIMITED with `Retry-After`. Note the ceiling: per-process. |","+| NFR-4 | SVC | Content tab: ≤4 queries (modules with lessons ordered + `_count.attachments` + caller progress `where lessonId in`). Add DB indexes (FR-15). |","+| NFR-5 | SVC | Stream → hash → disk, with the byte cap during the stream. See the FR-3 multipart trade-off. Write to a temp name, then rename on success (no partial files under the final key). |","+| NFR-6 | UI | iframe `title`, alt-text warning, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels. |","+| NFR-7 | UI | Dev must use mui-mcp docs before UI work. Blocker if unreachable. Includes the DateTimePicker (FR-28) package choice. |","+| NFR-8 | AUTH | Every route/page calls the assert helpers. Especially relevant for POST/DELETE /api/files if B1 is applied. |","+| NFR-9 | CFG | 5 new deps only. No renames. lint/typecheck/test green. |","+| NFR-10 | UI, SVC | UTC in the DB. Display via SchoolSettings.timezone (reuse the existing tz formatting helper if present). |","+| NFR-11 | — | No storage interface/S3 abstraction. No content copy. |","+| NFR-12 | CFG | Use the logger instead of console.log. Add `UPLOAD_DIR`, `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` to `.env.example` and the env schema. |"," ","-## Open points for `arch-design-system`","+## Open design decisions for `arch-design-system`"," ","-1. **Intake blockers (for the Overview):** FR-5 (MEDIUM), FR-16 (LOW), FR-23 (LOW) and the NFR-6 mui-mcp hard dependency. The defaults are listed above.","-2. **Partial unique indexes vs Prisma upsert (FR-3/FR-14):** sessions can't be `upsert`ed via Prisma. Use find + create in the tx and catch P2002 → retry as an update.","-3. **Admin school-wide schedule (FR-30/31):** `getScheduleForDate` returns `[]` for ADMIN. It needs a school-wide slot query. Prefer a small exported helper in `timetable-service.ts` over duplicating `slotInclude` logic.","-4. **Section access helper (FR-15):** none exists today. Add one small function and don't generalise it.","-5. **\"ACTIVE on date\" (NFR-3):** `Enrollment` has `enrolledAt`/`droppedAt`. Define the rule as `enrolledAt ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt > date)`. For back-dated registers, the roster should use the same rule.","-6. **Rate source by mode (FR-28):** in BOTH mode, rates use the per-period records only. Daily records are stored but not counted.","+1. **B1 public files path**: either add `/api/files/` to PUBLIC_API_PATHS with explicit `requireUser()` on POST/DELETE (recommended), or special-case GET in middleware.","+2. **Logo orphan purge (FR-12 × FR-40)**: give logo files a non-null `contextId` on save, or they get deleted after 24h.","+3. **Inline markdown images (FR-26 × FR-12)**: attach images referenced in `contentMarkdown` on save, or they get purged.","+4. **Multipart vs streaming (FR-3 × NFR-5)**: `formData()` + a Content-Length pre-check, or a hand-rolled stream parser. No multipart dep is allowed.","+5. **Detach semantics (FR-17/FR-27)**: removing an attachment either nulls contextId (purged later) or deletes immediately.","+6. **Audit trigger (FR-46)**: either add a creator field or audit all ADMIN mutations on content.","+7. **SVG validation (FR-41)**: text sniff for `<svg`, logo context only, CSP header on serve."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-7\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T05:29:02Z), PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007).\nIt has 41 FRs and 10 NFRs (51 requirements) at 94% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-1 notes that were here before.\n\n**Headline:** this is a **greenfield feature inside a brownfield app**. Everything attendance-related is new: the\nmodels, migration, service, validators, 10 API routes (9 from FR-35 plus PATCH settings from FR-5), 4 page areas,\n2 tabs, nav entries, seed data and tests. It builds on these existing exports. I checked each one on disk:\n\n| Reuse | Location | Verified signature / note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Schedule | `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts:542` | `getScheduleForDate(target: {userId, role} \\| {sectionId}, date)` → `{period, course, room}[]`. Returns `[]` for ADMIN/PARENT and on non-teaching days. Has the PRD-14 holiday hook comment. `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` at :565 already finds the running period, so use it for the FR-6 highlight. |\n| Notify | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts:98` | `notifyStudentAndParents({...NotifyInput minus userIds, studentIds})` never throws. Title and body are per student, so call it **once per student** (FR-21). |\n| Notif types | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` map + `NotificationTypeDef {label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. The `ATTENDANCE` category already exists. |\n| Access | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | `assertCanManageCourse`, `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanViewStudent`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`'ALL' \\| string[]`). |\n| Settings | `src/server/services/settings.ts` | `getSchoolSettings()` (singleton upsert, `cache`d) and `updateSchoolSettings(input)`. **`UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` must gain** `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?`. |\n| Misc | `src/server/audit.ts`, `src/server/csv.ts`, `src/server/http.ts` | `audit(input)`, `toCsv(columns, rows)`, response helpers. |\n| UI | `src/components/<Name>/` | DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast. They are **not** in `components/shared/`. |\n| Extension points | `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | Arrays of `{key, label, href(id), roles}`. Append entries to them. |\n\nGaps confirmed on disk: `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty and `src/app/(app)/admin/` has only `courses`,\n`email-log` and `sections`, with no settings page. The latest migration is `20261106000000_user_role_status_index`.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Service**, **Validation**, **API**, **Auth Boundary**, **Notifications**,\n**UI: Register**, **UI: Tabs**, **UI: Admin**, **Config/Nav**, **Seed**, **Tests**, **Cross-cutting**.\n\n## Requirement → Concern table\n\n| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | New `AttendanceStatus` enum and `AttendanceSession` / `AttendanceRecord` models. Records use `@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` and `@@index([studentId, createdAt])`. `date` is `@db.Date` (NFR-8). The session needs a `takenById`/`updatedById` + `updatedAt` for FR-6/FR-14. Records need `minutesLate Int?` and `note String?` (FR-12). |\n| FR-2 | Data Model + Service | XOR courseId/sectionId: raw SQL `CHECK ((courseId IS NULL) <> (sectionId IS NULL))` in the migration, and a guard in the service before insert. |\n| FR-3 | Data Model (migration SQL) | Two partial unique indexes: `(courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL` and `(sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL`. Prisma can't express these, so they go in hand-written SQL in the migration after `20261106000000`. **Consequence:** `upsert` cannot target them. The service must use `findFirst` + create/update inside the transaction, and catch P2002 on a race. |\n| FR-4 | Data Model | `SchoolSettings.attendanceMode` (new enum `AttendanceMode`, default `PER_PERIOD`) and `attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)`. Same migration. |\n| FR-5 | API + UI: Admin (MEDIUM) | No settings page exists. Smallest fix: `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN, Zod-validated, calls the extended `updateSchoolSettings`) and an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance`. That avoids a new page. |\n| FR-6 | Service + UI: Register | `GET /api/attendance/today` → `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` joined with today's sessions to show \"Taken HH:mm by name\". Highlight comes from `getCurrentSlot`. Times are shown in the school tz. |\n| FR-7 | Service + UI | If mode ∈ {DAILY_HOMEROOM, BOTH}, add entries for `Section.homeroomTeacherId = user` to `/today`. |\n| FR-8 | Validation + Auth Boundary | Shared date rule in the validators: no future date (school tz). Teachers can go back 14 days, admins any date. The same rule runs on the client and the server. |\n| FR-9 | Service + UI: Register | Course roster = `Enrollment` where status ACTIVE on the date, sorted by last name. Use the MUI `ToggleButtonGroup` (exclusive). Initial state is null for a new register. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Boundary + Validation | The server rejects `EXCUSED` from non-ADMIN with 403/VALIDATION_ERROR. The UI disables it for teachers. |\n| FR-11 | UI: Register | Client-only: fill nulls with PRESENT. |\n| FR-12 | Validation + UI | `minutesLate` 1–240 is required iff LATE (Zod `superRefine`) and defaults to 5 in the UI. `note` max 500. |\n| FR-13 | UI: Register | Derived counters. Save is disabled while any row is unmarked. The server also requires a full roster (or at least one valid record per student sent). |\n| FR-14 | Service | One `prisma.$transaction`: find/create the session, then upsert the records (`@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` works for `upsert`). Set `updatedById` on the session. The GET returns last-changed-by/at. |\n| FR-15 | Service + Auth Boundary | Section variant: roster = `SectionMember` for the current academic year. Access = `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` or ADMIN. No existing `assertCanManageSection` helper, so add a small one in the attendance service (or `auth/`). |\n| FR-16 | UI: Register (LOW) | Route `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` component with a section-scoped GET/PUT. |\n| FR-17 | UI: Register | Mobile: rows ≥ 48 px, toggles ≥ 44×44, sticky `Paper` save bar. Use theme `sx` only. |\n| FR-18 | Service + Audit | Inside the save, diff old vs new per student. For changed existing records call `audit({action:'attendance.record.update', before, after, actor, note})`. |\n| FR-19 | Service + Auth Boundary | Pure function `canEdit(user, sessionDate, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today - date ≤ 14 days`. The GET returns `readOnly` + `readOnlyReason`. The PUT returns 403. Unit-tested (FR-39). |\n| FR-20 | Notifications | Add `attendance.absent` (ATTENDANCE, email true, mandatoryInApp true, PARENT+STUDENT) and `attendance.late` (email false). |\n| FR-21 | Notifications + Service | After commit (outside the tx), call `notifyStudentAndParents` per changed student. Daily-register body: `<Section> daily register, <date>` (intake default). Link `/students/<id>/attendance`. |\n| FR-22 | Notifications + Service | Pure `diffForNotifications(prev, next)` → `{absent[], late[], corrected[]}`. Only a transition *into* ABSENT/LATE sends a notice, so re-saving with the same status sends nothing. ABSENT→PRESENT sends `attendance.corrected`. Unit-tested (FR-39). |\n| FR-23 | Notifications (LOW) | `attendance.corrected` (ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false), `attendance.register_missing` (ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false). |\n| FR-24 | Config | Append `{key:'attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}` to `studentTabs`. |\n| FR-25 | Service + UI: Tabs | Term = the Term containing today, else the most recent ended term (intake default). Use `StatCard` ×4 for term and year. |\n| FR-26 | UI: Tabs | MUI X `DateCalendar` read-only with a custom `day` slot coloured from per-day aggregates and a `Tooltip`. Month change refetches or filters `?from=&to=`. |\n| FR-27 | API + Auth Boundary | `GET /api/students/:id/attendance` → `assertCanViewStudent`. **Strip `note`** for STUDENT/PARENT on the server (AC-8). The table uses `DataTable`. |\n| FR-28 | Service (pure) | `attendanceRate(records)` = (P+L+E)/total×100, rounded to 1 dp; empty → null. Include DROPPED enrollments (filter on student, not enrollment). Mode chooses the source: course sessions (PER_PERIOD/BOTH) or section sessions (DAILY_HOMEROOM). Unit-tested. |\n| FR-29 | API + UI: Tabs + Config | `GET /api/courses/:id/attendance` (`assertCanManageCourse`) → last 20 sessions × enrolled students. Use MUI X DataGrid with dynamic columns. The header click links to the register. Course tab roles: ADMIN, TEACHER. |\n| FR-30 | Service + UI: Admin | Overview: expected = all timetable slots for today (all teachers) + sections if the mode includes daily; taken = sessions today; rate today. ADMIN gets `[]` from `getScheduleForDate`, so it **needs a school-wide slot query** (a direct `timetableSlot.findMany` by `dayOfWeek`, or a new helper next to `getScheduleForDate`). |\n| FR-31 | Service + API + Notifications | Missing = expected meetings with no session and `now ≥ period.startTime + 15 min` (school tz). `POST /api/admin/attendance/remind` → `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[teacherId]})`. |\n| FR-32 | Service + API + Validation | Report filters (range ≤ 366 days, grade, section, course, status) go into a per-student aggregate (use a SQL `groupBy` for performance). `?format=csv` → `toCsv` with the same columns. |\n| FR-33 | Service + API | YTD rate per student < threshold, sorted ascending. Reuses the same aggregate as FR-32 with the year's date range. |\n| FR-34 | Config/Nav | `navigation.ts`: TEACHER → `/attendance/take`, ADMIN → `/admin/attendance`. |\n| FR-35 | API | The 9 listed routes, plus PATCH settings from FR-5. Every handler starts with `requireUser`/`requireRole` and then the resource assert. They use the `http.ts` helpers. |\n| FR-36 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts`: `registerQuery`, `registerPutBody`, `studentAttendanceQuery`, `reportFilters`, `remindBody`, `attendanceSettingsPatch`. The register form imports them too. |\n| FR-37 | Service | `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts`. Keep the pure helpers (`attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`) in the same file or a sibling `attendance-rules.ts` so the tests need no DB. |\n| FR-38 | Seed | Extend the existing seed. Use a seeded RNG, 15 teaching days before the run date, 7A and 7B, a 94/3/3 split, and two Grade 7 students forced below 85%. Respect the existing school-day config. |\n| FR-39 | Tests (unit) | `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`. |\n| FR-40 | Tests (integration) | The save transaction, non-enrolled rejection (NFR-3), and the partial unique indexes (a duplicate insert raises). |\n| FR-41 | Tests (e2e) | Playwright: the 375 px take flow, and a parent seeing the notification plus the calendar absence. |\n| NFR-1 | Performance | Save: one tx with batched upserts (≈35). Avoid N+1 by loading existing records in one query. Student tab: one indexed query on `[studentId, createdAt]` (consider filtering on `session.date` and adding an index if needed). Aggregate in memory (1,200 rows is fine). |\n| NFR-2 | UI: Register (client) | localStorage key `attendance:<course\\|section>:<id>:<date>:<periodId\\|daily>`. Write it on a network failure, clear it on success, and offer a restore banner when it is present. |\n| NFR-3 | Service (integrity) | Validate every `studentId` against the ACTIVE enrollment on the date (`enrolledAt ≤ date` and not dropped before it) or the section membership. Any miss → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR and the whole save is rejected. |\n| NFR-4 | UI: Register | Satisfied by FR-11 + FR-17 (mark all present, then fix the exceptions). |\n| NFR-5 | Notifications | `notify()` writes in-app notifications immediately and queues EmailOutbox. Call it post-commit without blocking the response on email. |\n| NFR-6 | Cross-cutting (UI) | MUI only. Dev must use mui-mcp docs for 9.5.0 (ToggleButtonGroup, DateCalendar day slot, DataGrid, Paper sticky). **Hard blocker if unreachable.** |\n| NFR-7 | Auth Boundary | Server-side checks on every handler and server page. Per-role scope is listed above. Teachers also get their homeroom sections. |\n| NFR-8 | Cross-cutting | `@db.Date`, cuid IDs, UTC storage with display in school tz (`date-fns-tz`, already installed), the logger, `audit()` for edits to records owned by others, and pageSize ≤ 100 on the report and student records. |\n| NFR-9 | UI accessibility | `aria-label` on each toggle (\"Mark <name> present\"), 44 px targets. |\n| NFR-10 | Cross-cutting | Reuse the helpers above, add no new deps, rename nothing. Holidays (PRD-14) and the EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) are out of scope beyond the admin-only option. |\n\n## Open points for `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **Intake blockers (for the Overview):** FR-5 (MEDIUM), FR-16 (LOW), FR-23 (LOW) and the NFR-6 mui-mcp hard dependency. The defaults are listed above.\n2. **Partial unique indexes vs Prisma upsert (FR-3/FR-14):** sessions can't be `upsert`ed via Prisma. Use find + create in the tx and catch P2002 → retry as an update.\n3. **Admin school-wide schedule (FR-30/31):** `getScheduleForDate` returns `[]` for ADMIN. It needs a school-wide slot query. Prefer a small exported helper in `timetable-service.ts` over duplicating `slotInclude` logic.\n4. **Section access helper (FR-15):** none exists today. Add one small function and don't generalise it.\n5. **\"ACTIVE on date\" (NFR-3):** `Enrollment` has `enrolledAt`/`droppedAt`. Define the rule as `enrolledAt ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt > date)`. For back-dated registers, the roster should use the same rule.\n6. **Rate source by mode (FR-28):** in BOTH mode, rates use the per-period records only. Daily records are stored but not counted.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WAAodb1piB4j2mGmiS9EVi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
