{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgroAQ6SdvLXbjBmGHYoh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013N8tgmiCMZemFpxPGT82Wm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-9\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T09:00:00Z), PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions (SCH-009). It has 61 FRs and 17 NFRs (78 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers. They must be surfaced in the `system-design.md` Overview (compliance rule 5). Decisions D1–D4 below answer them.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-8 leftovers** as of this writing. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-9 input.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-9 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` sets `context` and `contextId` on unattached files owned by the caller (any file for ADMIN). It does **not** check the file's upload context. `detachFiles` sets `contextId = null`, and `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes those files after 24 h. | src/server/files/files-service.ts L215-245, purge.ts | FR-53 requires uploads with context `'submission'`. The service must check `context === 'submission'` before calling attachFiles. On resubmission, **never detach the previous attempt's files**: `SubmissionHistory.fileIds` points at them, and detaching would let the purge delete history bytes. Keep them attached to the same submission id. |\n| B2 | `FileObject.storageKey` is `@unique`, and a FileObject holds a single `(context, contextId)`. `storage.ts` exports `saveFile(stream)`, `readFile(key)` and `deleteFile`. | schema L564-578, storage.ts | FR-15 duplicate **cannot share** attachment rows. For each target course, copy the bytes (`readFile` → `saveFile`), create a new FileObject (context `'assignment'`), then attach it. |\n| B3 | `FileObject` has a back-relation `lessonAttachments LessonAttachment[]`. | schema L577 | FR-3/FR-4 add back-relations `assignmentAttachments` and `submissionFiles` to FileObject. This is an additive edit to an existing model, so NFR-11 allows it. |\n| B4 | `canAccessFile` order: unattached → owner/ADMIN; registered resolver; unknown context → owner/ADMIN. Resolver errors deny. `registerBuiltInContexts` currently registers `lesson` and `logo`. | access.ts L35-50, contexts.ts L36-39 | FR-47 adds `assignmentResolver` (contextId = assignmentId) and `submissionResolver` (contextId = submissionId) in contexts.ts. Before submit, a student's own upload is unattached, so it is already readable by owner/ADMIN only. |\n| B5 | `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` is a pure read-time check: PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt ≤ now. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` covers ADMIN, teacher and co-teacher. | visibility.ts | FR-13 can reuse both by mapping `availableFrom → publishAt`. Widen the `Publishable.status` type to accept `AssignmentStatus`, which has the same string values, rather than writing a second helper (NFR-11). |\n| B6 | `assertCanViewCourse` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child (`studentLinks`). `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Errors are `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These already provide all of NFR-5's course checks. A parent who views a course still needs to be scoped to *which* child (FR-18, FR-38). |\n| B7 | `ParentStudentLink {parentId, studentId}`. `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds, ...})` never throws. | notify.ts L98-117 | FR-44 uses it as-is. For FR-45 (parents only), call `notify()` with the parent ids from `parentStudentLink`. |\n| B8 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` **on every call**. Purges run in a once-per-day `if` (`lastPurgeAt`, in memory). | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-43/FR-45: call `sendDueReminders(now)` on **every** call, outside the daily block (due_soon has a 24 h window, so daily would miss it). Wrap it in its own try/catch + logger, like the purges. |\n| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object with `{label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. `content.lesson_published` is the closest precedent. | types.ts L33, L90-100 | FR-46: add four keys. Roles: `published` [STUDENT]; `due_soon` [STUDENT]; `returned` [STUDENT, PARENT]; `missing` [PARENT], with defaultEmail true. |\n| B10 | `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, tz)` and `schoolNow(now, tz)` live in `src/lib/dates.ts`, using date-fns-tz, which is already installed. | dates.ts | FR-10 next-teaching-day 23:59 and FR-25 receipt formatting. Convert wall time to UTC with date-fns-tz `fromZonedTime` (NFR-9 DST). |\n| B11 | `SchoolDay {dayOfWeek 1-7, isTeaching}` is seeded with all 7 rows. | schema L477-480 | FR-10 loops forward at most 7 days. If no day is teaching, fall back to tomorrow. |\n| B12 | `courseTabs` = overview, roster, attendance (there is **no content tab**: PRD-08 UI is missing). It is rendered by `CourseTabs.tsx`. `src/app/(app)/students/[id]/` has `attendance/` and `courses/` but no tab bar. | course-tabs.ts, ls | FR-16: append one entry with ALL_ROLES. FR-41: register the entry plus the page `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx`. It stays unreachable through tabs (blocker 5), but direct URLs work. |\n| B13 | `navigation.ts` entries are `{label, href, icon, roles, group?}`. | navigation.ts L31-38 | FR-40: one entry with roles [STUDENT, PARENT, TEACHER]. Default ADMIN to the \"To grade\" view through the API (clarification). Add ADMIN to the nav only if design adopts that default. |\n| B14 | `src/server/assignments/` and `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` do not exist. Validator precedent: `src/lib/validators/content.ts`. HTTP helpers: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` and `AppError` in `src/server/http.ts`. | ls, grep | Greenfield feature folder (NFR-8). Route handlers follow NFR-7 using the existing helpers. |\n| B15 | Existing components: ConfirmDialog, DataTable, DateDisplay, EmptyState, FormField, LoadingSkeleton, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker. **There is no** FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView or MarkdownEditor. | ls src/components | Blocker 1, see D1. |\n| B16 | Tests live in `tests/{unit,integration,e2e}`. | ls | NFR-14 placement. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = service logic · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = maintenance pass · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = registry/config · **NOTIF** = notification · **TEST** = test · **SEED** = seed data\n\n### Data model (one migration: FR-1…FR-6)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | New enums `SubmissionType`, `AssignmentStatus`, `SubmissionStatus`. Do not reuse `ContentStatus`, because the PRD names a new enum (the values happen to match, and B5 relies on that). |\n| FR-2 | DM | `Assignment` with `allowExtraCredit`, `notifiedAt?`, `archivedAt?`, `rubricId String? @unique`, Course relation with Cascade, and `@@index([courseId, dueAt])`. Add the back-relation `assignments Assignment[]` on Course. |\n| FR-3 | DM | `AssignmentAttachment` (join to FileObject, back-relation per B3), `Rubric`, `RubricCriterion` (`maxPoints Decimal(6,2)`, `order Int`, `levels Json`). A 1:1 Rubric↔Assignment via `rubricId @unique` means a rubric is never shared, so delete it together with the assignment. |\n| FR-4 | DM | `Submission @@unique([assignmentId, studentId])`, which means one row per student. Attempts live in `SubmissionHistory`. The Decimal fields are `rawScore`, `penaltyPercent` and `finalScore`. `rubricScores Json`. `SubmissionFile` join, back-relation per B3. `SubmissionHistory.fileIds String[]` has no FK, so the files must not be purged (B1). |\n| FR-5 | DM | `GradeExemption @@id([assignmentId, studentId])`. Cascade on assignment delete. |\n| FR-6 | DM | `AssignmentReminder @@unique([assignmentId, studentId, kind])`. `kind` is a String ('due_soon' / 'missing'). Insert with `createMany({skipDuplicates:true})`, or catch P2002, and send only for the rows actually inserted (idempotent under concurrent dispatchers). |\n| FR-7 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`, shared by client forms and route handlers. Cross-field rules (`lateCutoffAt > dueAt`, rubric sum) use `.superRefine`. Decimal inputs come in as number/string and the service converts them to `Prisma.Decimal` (NFR-1). |\n| FR-8 | SVC, DM | Offline marker: `attemptNumber = 0`, `text = null`, no files, `submittedAt = gradedAt`. **Edge case for design:** a student may later submit online against an offline-graded row (`status = SUBMITTED`, unique row). Recommend allowing it and treating it as a resubmission (move the attempt-0 grade into history and clear the grade), unless it is already RETURNED. |\n\n### Assignment authoring (teacher)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-9 | UI | `/courses/[courseId]/assignments/new` and an edit route (`[assignmentId]/edit`). MUI DateTimePicker (MUI X pickers, same version-alignment risk as D2) in the school timezone. It depends on D1 (FileUpload, MarkdownEditor). |\n| FR-10 | SVC | `nextTeachingDayDueAt(now, tz)`: a pure helper next to `schoolNow` in `src/lib/dates.ts`. Computed server-side and passed as a default prop (NFR-2). |\n| FR-11 | UI, VAL | The rubric builder uses `@dnd-kit/sortable`, which is already installed, for reorder. The rubric-sum check is in the Zod schema (shared), using Decimal sum, so the server rejects with VALIDATION_ERROR. The exact message string is required. |\n| FR-12 | UI, VAL | The status comes from the button. SCHEDULED requires `availableFrom > serverNow`, checked in the service, not only in Zod (Zod has no server clock guarantee). |\n| FR-13 | SVC | `isAssignmentVisible(a, now) = !archivedAt && isVisible({status, publishAt: availableFrom}, now)`. Use it in **every** student/parent read path, the file resolver, submission rules and reminders. It is the single source of truth. |\n| FR-14 | UI | Show the warning when the assignment is published and `submissionCount > 0`, and the dueAt or maxPoints changes. No recalculation happens on the server. Keep a `maxPointsChangedAt` banner? Simplest is a client-side banner on save success. **Design should pick one, and not add a column unless needed.** |\n| FR-15 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/duplicate {courseIds}`. Check `assertCanManageCourse` for **each** target. Make it one transaction per target. Copy the rubric and criteria as new rows (1:1), and copy the attachment bytes per B2. Status DRAFT, `notifiedAt` null. LOW confidence default: identical dueAt plus the availableFrom/lateCutoffAt offsets. |\n\n### Lists and navigation\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-16 | CFG | Append `{key:'assignments', href:/courses/:id/assignments, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. |\n| FR-17 | UI, EP | The teacher table depends on D2 (DataTable compile break). The counts come from FR-48's manager shape using `groupBy` aggregates, not N+1 queries. |\n| FR-18 | UI, AUTH | Student groups: Upcoming / Past due (missing) / Submitted / Returned. A parent viewing a course needs a child context: use `?studentId=`, validated against `ParentStudentLink` **and** active enrollment in this course. Default to the only linked child enrolled. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Assignment page: sanitised Markdown (D1 MarkdownView), late-policy summary, rubric, and a countdown under 48 h. Compute the countdown client-side from a server-provided `serverNow` offset, so a skewed client clock doesn't show a wrong countdown. It is display-only (NFR-2). |\n| FR-20 | UI | The panel switches on submissionType. Draft autosave to `localStorage` keyed by `assignmentId:userId`. Clear it after a successful submit. |\n| FR-21 | UI | Reuse `ConfirmDialog`. |\n| FR-25 | UI | Receipt formatted with `formatInSchoolTz(submittedAt, \"EEE d MMM yyyy, HH:mm\", tz)` plus the attempt number. |\n| FR-26 | UI, AUTH | Grading fields appear only when `status = RETURNED` (FR-27). |\n| FR-27 | AUTH, SVC | **Response-shaping boundary.** One serializer `toStudentSubmission(sub)` removes `rawScore/penaltyPercent/finalScore/feedback/rubricScores/gradedAt/gradedById` unless the status is RETURNED. Every student/parent path uses it: FR-48, FR-50, FR-55, FR-57, FR-58 when the viewer is the student or parent. This covers NFR-4. |\n| FR-37 | UI, EP | `/assignments` STUDENT: 4 tabs plus a course filter, across ACTIVE enrollments. Missing = visible, not archived, `dueAt < now`, no submission, not exempt, `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (FR-60). Define one Prisma `where` builder `missingFilter(now)` and share it with the reminders (FR-43/45) and the counts. |\n| FR-38 | UI, AUTH | PARENT: a child selector using linked students only. The server validates `studentId` against `ParentStudentLink`. The view is read-only, so the submit panel is not rendered **and** the API rejects it (FR-53 is STUDENT-only). |\n| FR-39 | UI, EP | TEACHER \"To grade\": `status = SUBMITTED AND gradedAt IS NULL` in courses where `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`, ordered by `submittedAt asc`. ADMIN gets the same list across all courses (clarification default). |\n| FR-40 | CFG | One nav entry (B13). |\n| FR-41 | CFG, UI | studentTabs entry plus a page. It is invisible until a tab bar exists (blocker 5). Out of scope to build one here: do not add a tab-bar renderer just for this (NFR-15 scope / YAGNI), and surface it as a known gap. |\n\n### Submission (student)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-22 | SVC, AUTH | Rule order: (1) the assignment is visible and not archived; (2) `role = STUDENT` and ACTIVE-enrolled; (3) not exempt; (4) `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (implied); (5) deadline: `now ≤ dueAt`, or `allowLate && (!lateCutoffAt || now ≤ lateCutoffAt)`. The exact error string is required. `now = new Date()` on the server only (NFR-2). |\n| FR-23 | SVC, TEST | Pure `lateDays(submittedAt, dueAt) = ceil((s − d) / 86_400_000)` for `s > d`, else 0. Use UTC milliseconds, so DST cannot affect it (NFR-9: a 24 h wall day across DST is 23/25 h of real time, and the PRD defines late days in 24 h units). Exactly 24 h gives 1. This is unit-test territory (NFR-14). |\n| FR-24 | SVC, DM | In one transaction: if a row exists, require `status = SUBMITTED` (RETURNED gives a VALIDATION/CONFLICT error), insert `SubmissionHistory` from the current row, `attemptNumber++`, clear the grade fields, replace the `SubmissionFile` rows, and attach the new files. Do not detach the old files (B1). Concurrency: two concurrent first submits hit the unique key. Catch P2002 and retry as a resubmit, or `upsert`. |\n| FR-53 | EP, VAL, AUTH | `POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions {text?, fileIds[]}`. Validation: `fileIds.length ≤ maxFileCount`; the content matches submissionType (text required for ONLINE_TEXT, files for FILE_UPLOAD, at least one for TEXT_AND_FILE); each file is `ownerId = me`, `context = 'submission'` and unattached, or already on this submission (B1). |\n\n### Grading (teacher)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-28 | UI, EP | The left panel is fed by FR-54. Status chip derivation is a pure function: Exempt > Returned > Graded > Late > Submitted > Not submitted. Shared by the server (FR-54) and tests. |\n| FR-29 | UI | `<img>`/`<iframe src=\"/api/files/:id?inline=1\">`. **CSP check for design:** confirm that `next.config.js` `frame-src`/`img-src` allow `'self'`. The CSP `script-src` issue is blocker 4. The history dropdown reads FR-55 (manager-only history). |\n| FR-30 | UI, SVC | Rubric ToggleButtonGroup with an auto-sum. Penalty prefill `min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)`. The live final score uses decimal.js on the client too, so the preview and server values agree (NFR-1). The prefill is display-only. The server stores what is submitted, after FR-36 validation. |\n| FR-31 | SVC, TEST | `finalScore = raw × (1 − p/100)`, computed with `Decimal`, `toDecimalPlaces(2, ROUND_HALF_UP)`. One pure function in the service, unit-tested (18 at 20 % = 14.40). |\n| FR-32 | EP, SVC, NOTIF | \"Save\" = `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade`. \"Save & return\" = the same call with `{return:true}`, or grade followed by return. **Design should pick a single round trip.** The bulk route is `POST /api/assignments/:id/return {submissionIds?}`, with the default `gradedAt not null AND status ≠ RETURNED`. Each return sets RETURNED and returnedAt, fires FR-44, and writes an audit (FR-59). |\n| FR-33 | UI | A keydown listener on the grading page. Ignore J/K when `event.target` is an input, textarea or contenteditable. Ctrl/Cmd+Enter always works. Accessibility: show the shortcuts in a help hint (NFR-17). |\n| FR-34 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}`. The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Reject it if a submission already exists (grade that one instead). Creates the FR-8 row with the grade fields set, penalty 0, and an audit row. |\n| FR-35 | EP, SVC | `PUT/DELETE /api/assignments/:id/exemptions/:studentId`. Idempotent (`upsert` / `deleteMany`). Writes an audit row. Its effects come through `missingFilter` and the FR-22 rule. A PRD-11 exclusion flag = the GradeExemption row itself, so no extra column. |\n| FR-36 | VAL, SVC | Server-side, Decimal-based: `0 ≤ raw ≤ maxPoints` (×1.2 if allowExtraCredit). Each rubric score `0 ≤ points ≤ criterion.maxPoints` (extra credit is raw-only, per the clarification), and each `criterionId` belongs to this rubric. `0 ≤ penalty ≤ 100`. With a rubric, should raw equal the sum of the rubric points? The PRD says it auto-sums but stays overridable only via the penalty. **Recommend the server enforces raw = Σ rubric points when rubricScores are given.** |\n| FR-54 | EP | `GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions` (manage). LEFT JOIN of ACTIVE enrollments × submissions × exemptions. Paginate per NFR-7, but grading needs all students for J/K: allow `pageSize` up to 100 and document the limit. |\n| FR-55 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/submissions/:id`: the submitter, linked parents or course managers. History only for managers. Grade fields go through the FR-27 serializer for the student and parent. Also needed by NFR-3 prefetch. |\n| FR-56 | EP, SVC | Sets `gradedById`, `gradedAt` and the computed `finalScore`. Does not change status (it stays SUBMITTED until return). Writes an audit row. |\n| FR-59 | SVC | `audit()` on grade, return (one row per submission, or one bulk row with the ids; **design should pick**), exempt/unexempt and offline grade. |\n\n### Assignment API\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-48 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/courses/:id/assignments`. Two response shapes depending on `canSeeDrafts`. Students and parents get FR-13-visible, non-archived assignments plus their own submission state (via the FR-27 serializer). |\n| FR-49 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/courses/:id/assignments`. One transaction: rubric and criteria, assignment, attachments (`attachFiles` with `'assignment'`, contextId = assignment.id), and on PUBLISHED the FR-42 notify after commit. |\n| FR-50 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/assignments/:id`. A non-manager on an invisible/archived assignment gets NOT_FOUND, not FORBIDDEN, so existence is not leaked. Includes `serverNow` for FR-19. |\n| FR-51 | EP, SVC | PATCH: re-validate the rubric sum against maxPoints. Diff the attachments (detach the removed ones, which are then purged after 24 h per B1; that is fine for assignment attachments). DRAFT→PUBLISHED triggers FR-42. DELETE: hard delete if there are 0 submissions (cascade; the attachment files are detached first so the purge reclaims them), else set `archivedAt`. |\n| FR-52 | AUTH, SVC | Covered by `isAssignmentVisible` (FR-13), which includes `!archivedAt`. One check, applied everywhere. LOW confidence default. |\n| FR-57 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab=`. Role switch: STUDENT gets its own data; PARENT requires a linked `studentId`; TEACHER/ADMIN get To grade. `tab ∈ upcoming/missing/submitted/returned`. |\n| FR-58 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/students/:id/assignments` → `assertCanViewStudent`, then the same query as the FR-57 student view, built with a shared service function. A student or parent viewer gets the FR-27 serializer. Teachers and admins see grades? The PRD says \"same per-student data\", so **recommend the same serializer for all non-managers and full fields for the student's course managers.** Design should confirm. |\n\n### Notifications and maintenance\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-42 | NOTIF, SVC | Exactly once: `UPDATE assignment SET notifiedAt = now WHERE id = ? AND notifiedAt IS NULL` (`updateMany`, count = 1 → send). Triggered on publish (FR-49/51), and for SCHEDULED assignments in the student list read path (FR-48/57) when visible and `notifiedAt` is null. **A side effect on GET:** keep it fire-and-forget after the response data is built, and never fail the read. Design may also add it to `sendDueReminders` as a safety net, but must not do both without the atomic guard (the guard makes both safe). |\n| FR-43 | JOB, NOTIF | `sendDueReminders(now)` in `src/server/assignments/reminders.ts`, called on every dispatcher call (B8). The window is `dueAt − 24h ≤ now < dueAt`. Targets: ACTIVE-enrolled, no submission, not exempt, visible, not archived, not NO_SUBMISSION. Idempotent via FR-6. Bound the query (only assignments with `dueAt` in [now, now+24h]). |\n| FR-44 | NOTIF | On return: `notifyStudentAndParents` with a body like `\"{course}: {title} — {finalScore}/{maxPoints}\"`. Bulk return sends one notify per student. |\n| FR-45 | JOB, NOTIF | In the same pass: `now ≥ dueAt + 24h`, with the `missingFilter` targets. Parents only (`notify` to the linked parent ids). FR-6 kind 'missing'. Bound the query to avoid scanning all history, e.g. `dueAt` in [now − 8 d, now − 24 h], with a `ponytail:` note on that window. |\n| FR-46 | CFG | Four keys (B9). |\n| FR-47 | AUTH | `assignmentResolver`: load the assignment and course, then `assertCanViewCourse`, then `canSeeDrafts \\|\\| isAssignmentVisible`. `submissionResolver`: load the submission; allow the submitting student, a linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`) or `canSeeDrafts(course)` (managers/ADMIN). Deny everyone else, including other students (NFR-4, AC-10). Integration test needed. |\n\n### Seed\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-60 | SVC | Exclude NO_SUBMISSION in `missingFilter` and the reminder targets. The submission panel is hidden and FR-53 rejects. LOW confidence default. |\n| FR-61 | SEED | Idempotent: look up the courses by code and skip if they are missing. Upsert the assignments by `(courseId, title)`. Seed Decimal scores via strings. Seeded attachments/files are not required, so skip byte storage. |\n\n### Non-functional\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| NFR-1 | SVC, VAL | Decimal end to end: Prisma `Decimal(6,2)` columns, `Prisma.Decimal` in the service, decimal.js in the client preview. Serialize Decimals in API responses as **strings**, to avoid float loss in JSON. Design must state this convention for api-contracts. |\n| NFR-2 | SVC | Every deadline, visibility or reminder check uses `new Date()` on the server. There is no client timestamp field in any request schema. |\n| NFR-3 | UI, EP | Prefetch the next and previous `GET /api/submissions/:id` into a client cache keyed by id (a plain `Map` in the grading page; no data-fetching library added). The <300 ms target is a client switch from cache. |\n| NFR-4 | AUTH | Enforced at three boundaries: the FR-27 serializer, the FR-47 file resolvers, and query scoping (a student only ever queries `studentId = me`). |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every route: `requireUser`/`requireRole`, then assertCan*. Every page: `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`. |\n| NFR-6 | UI | MUI 9.5.0 + MUI X only, with mui-mcp lookups before use. Components needed: List, Chip, ToggleButtonGroup, Dialog, Tabs, DataGrid (D2), DateTimePicker, Autocomplete, Snackbar. Hard blocker if mui-mcp is unreachable (blocker 8). |\n| NFR-7 | EP | Thin handlers. `{data}` / paginated / `{error}` envelopes via the http.ts helpers. |\n| NFR-8 | CFG | `src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts`, plus `reminders.ts` and pure `scoring.ts` (lateDays, penalty, finalScore, chip status) for unit tests. Validators in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`. |\n| NFR-9 | SVC, TEST | Store UTC. Display via formatInSchoolTz. Late days in UTC ms (FR-23). The FR-10 default uses `fromZonedTime`. |\n| NFR-10 | UI | react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize are installed, with MUI component mapping (D1). |\n| NFR-11 | — | Reuse list: B1–B10, B15. |\n| NFR-12 | — | Use the logger, never console.log. |\n| NFR-13 | TEST, CFG | Blocker 3: fix the `vitest.config.ts` import to `'vitest/config'` (a one-line fix, in scope because NFR-13 requires a working `npm test`). |\n| NFR-14 | TEST | Unit: scoring.ts. Integration: resubmit history, return, reminder idempotency, exemption vs missing, and the file resolvers (AC-10). E2E: the full flow plus the parent missing list (needs bypassCSP, blocker 4). |\n| NFR-15 | — | No gradebook, peer review, group work or annotation. FR-35 stores the exemption only, and PRD-11 consumes it. |\n| NFR-16 | UI | Two-minute publish: sensible defaults (FR-10 due date, max points 100?, submissionType FILE_UPLOAD?). **Design should set the form defaults.** 30-submission keyboard grading via FR-33 + NFR-3. |\n| NFR-17 | UI | Labelled inputs and keyboard-operable controls: the ToggleButtonGroup and the J/K help hint. |\n\n## Decisions arch-design-system must make (answers to the intake blockers)\n\n| # | Blocker / gap | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | Blocker 1: PRD-08 UI components are missing. | Build the **minimum** shared components in this ticket: `src/components/MarkdownView` (react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, mapped to MUI), `src/components/MarkdownEditor` (MUI TextField multiline + a Write/Preview Tabs toggle using MarkdownView; no new editor dependency), `src/components/FileUpload` (input type=file → `POST /api/files` with the context field, list with remove, `maxFiles` prop) and `FileList` (links to `/api/files/:id`). Shape them so PRD-08 can adopt them later. Do not build PRD-08's remaining scope. |\n| D2 | Blocker 2: the MUI X DataGrid compile break. | Preferred: align `@mui/x-*` versions in package.json/lockfile (it also unblocks the DateTimePicker from `@mui/x-date-pickers`, if that package shares the internals). Fallback for FR-17: an MUI `Table`, which needs no DataGrid. **Check whether `@mui/x-date-pickers` is installed and affected**, because FR-9 needs it. |\n| D3 | Blockers 3/4: vitest import and CSP. | vitest: one-line import fix. CSP: keep `bypassCSP` in Playwright as before. A CSP fix is outside the PRD scope (NFR-15). Note the FR-29 iframe/img `'self'` dependency. |\n| D4 | Blocker 5: the studentTabs renderer. | Register the tab and build the page. Do not build a tab bar. Report it as a known gap. |\n| D5 | Decimal JSON serialization | Decimal fields are strings in API responses (NFR-1). |\n| D6 | The \"Save & return\" round trip | `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade` with an optional `return: true` gives one transaction. |\n| D7 | Rubric raw score | When rubricScores are present, the server sets or enforces `rawScore = Σ points`. |\n| D8 | Teacher/admin view of FR-58 grade fields | Course managers get full fields. Other viewers get the FR-27 serializer. |\n| D9 | Offline-graded row followed by an online submit | Treat it as a resubmission while it is not RETURNED. |\n| D10 | Missing-reminder query window | Bound it (e.g. dueAt within the last 8 days), marked with a `ponytail:` note. |\n\n## Shared pure functions (single source of truth; unit-test targets)\n\n`isAssignmentVisible`, `missingFilter(now)` (Prisma where), `lateDays`, `defaultPenalty`, `computeFinalScore`, `rubricTotal`, `submissionChipStatus`, `nextTeachingDayDueAt`, `toStudentSubmission` (serializer). Each of these is used by two or more call sites listed above. Keeping one copy of each prevents the drift that leads to privacy and correctness bugs (NFR-1, NFR-4).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2812,"cache_read_input_tokens":57740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2812},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91d7b1a5-c851-4385-b1f3-145425ca0827","uuid":"aa6edbd6-a4b2-4b27-95c9-96b5c314fe01","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:26:15.218Z","request_id":"req_011CgroAPoLbLjjRvT5ayMKT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013N8tgmiCMZemFpxPGT82Wm":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-9\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T09:00:00Z), PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions (SCH-009). It has 61 FRs and 17 NFRs (78 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers. They must be surfaced in the `system-design.md` Overview (compliance rule 5). Decisions D1–D4 below answer them.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-8 leftovers** as of this writing. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-9 input.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-9 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` sets `context` and `contextId` on unattached files owned by the caller (any file for ADMIN). It does **not** check the file's upload context. `detachFiles` sets `contextId = null`, and `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes those files after 24 h. | src/server/files/files-service.ts L215-245, purge.ts | FR-53 requires uploads with context `'submission'`. The service must check `context === 'submission'` before calling attachFiles. On resubmission, **never detach the previous attempt's files**: `SubmissionHistory.fileIds` points at them, and detaching would let the purge delete history bytes. Keep them attached to the same submission id. |\n| B2 | `FileObject.storageKey` is `@unique`, and a FileObject holds a single `(context, contextId)`. `storage.ts` exports `saveFile(stream)`, `readFile(key)` and `deleteFile`. | schema L564-578, storage.ts | FR-15 duplicate **cannot share** attachment rows. For each target course, copy the bytes (`readFile` → `saveFile`), create a new FileObject (context `'assignment'`), then attach it. |\n| B3 | `FileObject` has a back-relation `lessonAttachments LessonAttachment[]`. | schema L577 | FR-3/FR-4 add back-relations `assignmentAttachments` and `submissionFiles` to FileObject. This is an additive edit to an existing model, so NFR-11 allows it. |\n| B4 | `canAccessFile` order: unattached → owner/ADMIN; registered resolver; unknown context → owner/ADMIN. Resolver errors deny. `registerBuiltInContexts` currently registers `lesson` and `logo`. | access.ts L35-50, contexts.ts L36-39 | FR-47 adds `assignmentResolver` (contextId = assignmentId) and `submissionResolver` (contextId = submissionId) in contexts.ts. Before submit, a student's own upload is unattached, so it is already readable by owner/ADMIN only. |\n| B5 | `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` is a pure read-time check: PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt ≤ now. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` covers ADMIN, teacher and co-teacher. | visibility.ts | FR-13 can reuse both by mapping `availableFrom → publishAt`. Widen the `Publishable.status` type to accept `AssignmentStatus`, which has the same string values, rather than writing a second helper (NFR-11). |\n| B6 | `assertCanViewCourse` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child (`studentLinks`). `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Errors are `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These already provide all of NFR-5's course checks. A parent who views a course still needs to be scoped to *which* child (FR-18, FR-38). |\n| B7 | `ParentStudentLink {parentId, studentId}`. `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds, ...})` never throws. | notify.ts L98-117 | FR-44 uses it as-is. For FR-45 (parents only), call `notify()` with the parent ids from `parentStudentLink`. |\n| B8 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` **on every call**. Purges run in a once-per-day `if` (`lastPurgeAt`, in memory). | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-43/FR-45: call `sendDueReminders(now)` on **every** call, outside the daily block (due_soon has a 24 h window, so daily would miss it). Wrap it in its own try/catch + logger, like the purges. |\n| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object with `{label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. `content.lesson_published` is the closest precedent. | types.ts L33, L90-100 | FR-46: add four keys. Roles: `published` [STUDENT]; `due_soon` [STUDENT]; `returned` [STUDENT, PARENT]; `missing` [PARENT], with defaultEmail true. |\n| B10 | `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, tz)` and `schoolNow(now, tz)` live in `src/lib/dates.ts`, using date-fns-tz, which is already installed. | dates.ts | FR-10 next-teaching-day 23:59 and FR-25 receipt formatting. Convert wall time to UTC with date-fns-tz `fromZonedTime` (NFR-9 DST). |\n| B11 | `SchoolDay {dayOfWeek 1-7, isTeaching}` is seeded with all 7 rows. | schema L477-480 | FR-10 loops forward at most 7 days. If no day is teaching, fall back to tomorrow. |\n| B12 | `courseTabs` = overview, roster, attendance (there is **no content tab**: PRD-08 UI is missing). It is rendered by `CourseTabs.tsx`. `src/app/(app)/students/[id]/` has `attendance/` and `courses/` but no tab bar. | course-tabs.ts, ls | FR-16: append one entry with ALL_ROLES. FR-41: register the entry plus the page `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx`. It stays unreachable through tabs (blocker 5), but direct URLs work. |\n| B13 | `navigation.ts` entries are `{label, href, icon, roles, group?}`. | navigation.ts L31-38 | FR-40: one entry with roles [STUDENT, PARENT, TEACHER]. Default ADMIN to the \"To grade\" view through the API (clarification). Add ADMIN to the nav only if design adopts that default. |\n| B14 | `src/server/assignments/` and `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` do not exist. Validator precedent: `src/lib/validators/content.ts`. HTTP helpers: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` and `AppError` in `src/server/http.ts`. | ls, grep | Greenfield feature folder (NFR-8). Route handlers follow NFR-7 using the existing helpers. |\n| B15 | Existing components: ConfirmDialog, DataTable, DateDisplay, EmptyState, FormField, LoadingSkeleton, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker. **There is no** FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView or MarkdownEditor. | ls src/components | Blocker 1, see D1. |\n| B16 | Tests live in `tests/{unit,integration,e2e}`. | ls | NFR-14 placement. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = service logic · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = maintenance pass · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = registry/config · **NOTIF** = notification · **TEST** = test · **SEED** = seed data\n\n### Data model (one migration: FR-1…FR-6)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | New enums `SubmissionType`, `AssignmentStatus`, `SubmissionStatus`. Do not reuse `ContentStatus`, because the PRD names a new enum (the values happen to match, and B5 relies on that). |\n| FR-2 | DM | `Assignment` with `allowExtraCredit`, `notifiedAt?`, `archivedAt?`, `rubricId String? @unique`, Course relation with Cascade, and `@@index([courseId, dueAt])`. Add the back-relation `assignments Assignment[]` on Course. |\n| FR-3 | DM | `AssignmentAttachment` (join to FileObject, back-relation per B3), `Rubric`, `RubricCriterion` (`maxPoints Decimal(6,2)`, `order Int`, `levels Json`). A 1:1 Rubric↔Assignment via `rubricId @unique` means a rubric is never shared, so delete it together with the assignment. |\n| FR-4 | DM | `Submission @@unique([assignmentId, studentId])`, which means one row per student. Attempts live in `SubmissionHistory`. The Decimal fields are `rawScore`, `penaltyPercent` and `finalScore`. `rubricScores Json`. `SubmissionFile` join, back-relation per B3. `SubmissionHistory.fileIds String[]` has no FK, so the files must not be purged (B1). |\n| FR-5 | DM | `GradeExemption @@id([assignmentId, studentId])`. Cascade on assignment delete. |\n| FR-6 | DM | `AssignmentReminder @@unique([assignmentId, studentId, kind])`. `kind` is a String ('due_soon' / 'missing'). Insert with `createMany({skipDuplicates:true})`, or catch P2002, and send only for the rows actually inserted (idempotent under concurrent dispatchers). |\n| FR-7 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`, shared by client forms and route handlers. Cross-field rules (`lateCutoffAt > dueAt`, rubric sum) use `.superRefine`. Decimal inputs come in as number/string and the service converts them to `Prisma.Decimal` (NFR-1). |\n| FR-8 | SVC, DM | Offline marker: `attemptNumber = 0`, `text = null`, no files, `submittedAt = gradedAt`. **Edge case for design:** a student may later submit online against an offline-graded row (`status = SUBMITTED`, unique row). Recommend allowing it and treating it as a resubmission (move the attempt-0 grade into history and clear the grade), unless it is already RETURNED. |\n\n### Assignment authoring (teacher)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-9 | UI | `/courses/[courseId]/assignments/new` and an edit route (`[assignmentId]/edit`). MUI DateTimePicker (MUI X pickers, same version-alignment risk as D2) in the school timezone. It depends on D1 (FileUpload, MarkdownEditor). |\n| FR-10 | SVC | `nextTeachingDayDueAt(now, tz)`: a pure helper next to `schoolNow` in `src/lib/dates.ts`. Computed server-side and passed as a default prop (NFR-2). |\n| FR-11 | UI, VAL | The rubric builder uses `@dnd-kit/sortable`, which is already installed, for reorder. The rubric-sum check is in the Zod schema (shared), using Decimal sum, so the server rejects with VALIDATION_ERROR. The exact message string is required. |\n| FR-12 | UI, VAL | The status comes from the button. SCHEDULED requires `availableFrom > serverNow`, checked in the service, not only in Zod (Zod has no server clock guarantee). |\n| FR-13 | SVC | `isAssignmentVisible(a, now) = !archivedAt && isVisible({status, publishAt: availableFrom}, now)`. Use it in **every** student/parent read path, the file resolver, submission rules and reminders. It is the single source of truth. |\n| FR-14 | UI | Show the warning when the assignment is published and `submissionCount > 0`, and the dueAt or maxPoints changes. No recalculation happens on the server. Keep a `maxPointsChangedAt` banner? Simplest is a client-side banner on save success. **Design should pick one, and not add a column unless needed.** |\n| FR-15 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/duplicate {courseIds}`. Check `assertCanManageCourse` for **each** target. Make it one transaction per target. Copy the rubric and criteria as new rows (1:1), and copy the attachment bytes per B2. Status DRAFT, `notifiedAt` null. LOW confidence default: identical dueAt plus the availableFrom/lateCutoffAt offsets. |\n\n### Lists and navigation\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-16 | CFG | Append `{key:'assignments', href:/courses/:id/assignments, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. |\n| FR-17 | UI, EP | The teacher table depends on D2 (DataTable compile break). The counts come from FR-48's manager shape using `groupBy` aggregates, not N+1 queries. |\n| FR-18 | UI, AUTH | Student groups: Upcoming / Past due (missing) / Submitted / Returned. A parent viewing a course needs a child context: use `?studentId=`, validated against `ParentStudentLink` **and** active enrollment in this course. Default to the only linked child enrolled. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Assignment page: sanitised Markdown (D1 MarkdownView), late-policy summary, rubric, and a countdown under 48 h. Compute the countdown client-side from a server-provided `serverNow` offset, so a skewed client clock doesn't show a wrong countdown. It is display-only (NFR-2). |\n| FR-20 | UI | The panel switches on submissionType. Draft autosave to `localStorage` keyed by `assignmentId:userId`. Clear it after a successful submit. |\n| FR-21 | UI | Reuse `ConfirmDialog`. |\n| FR-25 | UI | Receipt formatted with `formatInSchoolTz(submittedAt, \"EEE d MMM yyyy, HH:mm\", tz)` plus the attempt number. |\n| FR-26 | UI, AUTH | Grading fields appear only when `status = RETURNED` (FR-27). |\n| FR-27 | AUTH, SVC | **Response-shaping boundary.** One serializer `toStudentSubmission(sub)` removes `rawScore/penaltyPercent/finalScore/feedback/rubricScores/gradedAt/gradedById` unless the status is RETURNED. Every student/parent path uses it: FR-48, FR-50, FR-55, FR-57, FR-58 when the viewer is the student or parent. This covers NFR-4. |\n| FR-37 | UI, EP | `/assignments` STUDENT: 4 tabs plus a course filter, across ACTIVE enrollments. Missing = visible, not archived, `dueAt < now`, no submission, not exempt, `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (FR-60). Define one Prisma `where` builder `missingFilter(now)` and share it with the reminders (FR-43/45) and the counts. |\n| FR-38 | UI, AUTH | PARENT: a child selector using linked students only. The server validates `studentId` against `ParentStudentLink`. The view is read-only, so the submit panel is not rendered **and** the API rejects it (FR-53 is STUDENT-only). |\n| FR-39 | UI, EP | TEACHER \"To grade\": `status = SUBMITTED AND gradedAt IS NULL` in courses where `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`, ordered by `submittedAt asc`. ADMIN gets the same list across all courses (clarification default). |\n| FR-40 | CFG | One nav entry (B13). |\n| FR-41 | CFG, UI | studentTabs entry plus a page. It is invisible until a tab bar exists (blocker 5). Out of scope to build one here: do not add a tab-bar renderer just for this (NFR-15 scope / YAGNI), and surface it as a known gap. |\n\n### Submission (student)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-22 | SVC, AUTH | Rule order: (1) the assignment is visible and not archived; (2) `role = STUDENT` and ACTIVE-enrolled; (3) not exempt; (4) `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (implied); (5) deadline: `now ≤ dueAt`, or `allowLate && (!lateCutoffAt || now ≤ lateCutoffAt)`. The exact error string is required. `now = new Date()` on the server only (NFR-2). |\n| FR-23 | SVC, TEST | Pure `lateDays(submittedAt, dueAt) = ceil((s − d) / 86_400_000)` for `s > d`, else 0. Use UTC milliseconds, so DST cannot affect it (NFR-9: a 24 h wall day across DST is 23/25 h of real time, and the PRD defines late days in 24 h units). Exactly 24 h gives 1. This is unit-test territory (NFR-14). |\n| FR-24 | SVC, DM | In one transaction: if a row exists, require `status = SUBMITTED` (RETURNED gives a VALIDATION/CONFLICT error), insert `SubmissionHistory` from the current row, `attemptNumber++`, clear the grade fields, replace the `SubmissionFile` rows, and attach the new files. Do not detach the old files (B1). Concurrency: two concurrent first submits hit the unique key. Catch P2002 and retry as a resubmit, or `upsert`. |\n| FR-53 | EP, VAL, AUTH | `POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions {text?, fileIds[]}`. Validation: `fileIds.length ≤ maxFileCount`; the content matches submissionType (text required for ONLINE_TEXT, files for FILE_UPLOAD, at least one for TEXT_AND_FILE); each file is `ownerId = me`, `context = 'submission'` and unattached, or already on this submission (B1). |\n\n### Grading (teacher)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-28 | UI, EP | The left panel is fed by FR-54. Status chip derivation is a pure function: Exempt > Returned > Graded > Late > Submitted > Not submitted. Shared by the server (FR-54) and tests. |\n| FR-29 | UI | `<img>`/`<iframe src=\"/api/files/:id?inline=1\">`. **CSP check for design:** confirm that `next.config.js` `frame-src`/`img-src` allow `'self'`. The CSP `script-src` issue is blocker 4. The history dropdown reads FR-55 (manager-only history). |\n| FR-30 | UI, SVC | Rubric ToggleButtonGroup with an auto-sum. Penalty prefill `min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)`. The live final score uses decimal.js on the client too, so the preview and server values agree (NFR-1). The prefill is display-only. The server stores what is submitted, after FR-36 validation. |\n| FR-31 | SVC, TEST | `finalScore = raw × (1 − p/100)`, computed with `Decimal`, `toDecimalPlaces(2, ROUND_HALF_UP)`. One pure function in the service, unit-tested (18 at 20 % = 14.40). |\n| FR-32 | EP, SVC, NOTIF | \"Save\" = `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade`. \"Save & return\" = the same call with `{return:true}`, or grade followed by return. **Design should pick a single round trip.** The bulk route is `POST /api/assignments/:id/return {submissionIds?}`, with the default `gradedAt not null AND status ≠ RETURNED`. Each return sets RETURNED and returnedAt, fires FR-44, and writes an audit (FR-59). |\n| FR-33 | UI | A keydown listener on the grading page. Ignore J/K when `event.target` is an input, textarea or contenteditable. Ctrl/Cmd+Enter always works. Accessibility: show the shortcuts in a help hint (NFR-17). |\n| FR-34 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}`. The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Reject it if a submission already exists (grade that one instead). Creates the FR-8 row with the grade fields set, penalty 0, and an audit row. |\n| FR-35 | EP, SVC | `PUT/DELETE /api/assignments/:id/exemptions/:studentId`. Idempotent (`upsert` / `deleteMany`). Writes an audit row. Its effects come through `missingFilter` and the FR-22 rule. A PRD-11 exclusion flag = the GradeExemption row itself, so no extra column. |\n| FR-36 | VAL, SVC | Server-side, Decimal-based: `0 ≤ raw ≤ maxPoints` (×1.2 if allowExtraCredit). Each rubric score `0 ≤ points ≤ criterion.maxPoints` (extra credit is raw-only, per the clarification), and each `criterionId` belongs to this rubric. `0 ≤ penalty ≤ 100`. With a rubric, should raw equal the sum of the rubric points? The PRD says it auto-sums but stays overridable only via the penalty. **Recommend the server enforces raw = Σ rubric points when rubricScores are given.** |\n| FR-54 | EP | `GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions` (manage). LEFT JOIN of ACTIVE enrollments × submissions × exemptions. Paginate per NFR-7, but grading needs all students for J/K: allow `pageSize` up to 100 and document the limit. |\n| FR-55 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/submissions/:id`: the submitter, linked parents or course managers. History only for managers. Grade fields go through the FR-27 serializer for the student and parent. Also needed by NFR-3 prefetch. |\n| FR-56 | EP, SVC | Sets `gradedById`, `gradedAt` and the computed `finalScore`. Does not change status (it stays SUBMITTED until return). Writes an audit row. |\n| FR-59 | SVC | `audit()` on grade, return (one row per submission, or one bulk row with the ids; **design should pick**), exempt/unexempt and offline grade. |\n\n### Assignment API\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-48 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/courses/:id/assignments`. Two response shapes depending on `canSeeDrafts`. Students and parents get FR-13-visible, non-archived assignments plus their own submission state (via the FR-27 serializer). |\n| FR-49 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/courses/:id/assignments`. One transaction: rubric and criteria, assignment, attachments (`attachFiles` with `'assignment'`, contextId = assignment.id), and on PUBLISHED the FR-42 notify after commit. |\n| FR-50 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/assignments/:id`. A non-manager on an invisible/archived assignment gets NOT_FOUND, not FORBIDDEN, so existence is not leaked. Includes `serverNow` for FR-19. |\n| FR-51 | EP, SVC | PATCH: re-validate the rubric sum against maxPoints. Diff the attachments (detach the removed ones, which are then purged after 24 h per B1; that is fine for assignment attachments). DRAFT→PUBLISHED triggers FR-42. DELETE: hard delete if there are 0 submissions (cascade; the attachment files are detached first so the purge reclaims them), else set `archivedAt`. |\n| FR-52 | AUTH, SVC | Covered by `isAssignmentVisible` (FR-13), which includes `!archivedAt`. One check, applied everywhere. LOW confidence default. |\n| FR-57 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab=`. Role switch: STUDENT gets its own data; PARENT requires a linked `studentId`; TEACHER/ADMIN get To grade. `tab ∈ upcoming/missing/submitted/returned`. |\n| FR-58 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/students/:id/assignments` → `assertCanViewStudent`, then the same query as the FR-57 student view, built with a shared service function. A student or parent viewer gets the FR-27 serializer. Teachers and admins see grades? The PRD says \"same per-student data\", so **recommend the same serializer for all non-managers and full fields for the student's course managers.** Design should confirm. |\n\n### Notifications and maintenance\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-42 | NOTIF, SVC | Exactly once: `UPDATE assignment SET notifiedAt = now WHERE id = ? AND notifiedAt IS NULL` (`updateMany`, count = 1 → send). Triggered on publish (FR-49/51), and for SCHEDULED assignments in the student list read path (FR-48/57) when visible and `notifiedAt` is null. **A side effect on GET:** keep it fire-and-forget after the response data is built, and never fail the read. Design may also add it to `sendDueReminders` as a safety net, but must not do both without the atomic guard (the guard makes both safe). |\n| FR-43 | JOB, NOTIF | `sendDueReminders(now)` in `src/server/assignments/reminders.ts`, called on every dispatcher call (B8). The window is `dueAt − 24h ≤ now < dueAt`. Targets: ACTIVE-enrolled, no submission, not exempt, visible, not archived, not NO_SUBMISSION. Idempotent via FR-6. Bound the query (only assignments with `dueAt` in [now, now+24h]). |\n| FR-44 | NOTIF | On return: `notifyStudentAndParents` with a body like `\"{course}: {title} — {finalScore}/{maxPoints}\"`. Bulk return sends one notify per student. |\n| FR-45 | JOB, NOTIF | In the same pass: `now ≥ dueAt + 24h`, with the `missingFilter` targets. Parents only (`notify` to the linked parent ids). FR-6 kind 'missing'. Bound the query to avoid scanning all history, e.g. `dueAt` in [now − 8 d, now − 24 h], with a `ponytail:` note on that window. |\n| FR-46 | CFG | Four keys (B9). |\n| FR-47 | AUTH | `assignmentResolver`: load the assignment and course, then `assertCanViewCourse`, then `canSeeDrafts \\|\\| isAssignmentVisible`. `submissionResolver`: load the submission; allow the submitting student, a linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`) or `canSeeDrafts(course)` (managers/ADMIN). Deny everyone else, including other students (NFR-4, AC-10). Integration test needed. |\n\n### Seed\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-60 | SVC | Exclude NO_SUBMISSION in `missingFilter` and the reminder targets. The submission panel is hidden and FR-53 rejects. LOW confidence default. |\n| FR-61 | SEED | Idempotent: look up the courses by code and skip if they are missing. Upsert the assignments by `(courseId, title)`. Seed Decimal scores via strings. Seeded attachments/files are not required, so skip byte storage. |\n\n### Non-functional\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| NFR-1 | SVC, VAL | Decimal end to end: Prisma `Decimal(6,2)` columns, `Prisma.Decimal` in the service, decimal.js in the client preview. Serialize Decimals in API responses as **strings**, to avoid float loss in JSON. Design must state this convention for api-contracts. |\n| NFR-2 | SVC | Every deadline, visibility or reminder check uses `new Date()` on the server. There is no client timestamp field in any request schema. |\n| NFR-3 | UI, EP | Prefetch the next and previous `GET /api/submissions/:id` into a client cache keyed by id (a plain `Map` in the grading page; no data-fetching library added). The <300 ms target is a client switch from cache. |\n| NFR-4 | AUTH | Enforced at three boundaries: the FR-27 serializer, the FR-47 file resolvers, and query scoping (a student only ever queries `studentId = me`). |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every route: `requireUser`/`requireRole`, then assertCan*. Every page: `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`. |\n| NFR-6 | UI | MUI 9.5.0 + MUI X only, with mui-mcp lookups before use. Components needed: List, Chip, ToggleButtonGroup, Dialog, Tabs, DataGrid (D2), DateTimePicker, Autocomplete, Snackbar. Hard blocker if mui-mcp is unreachable (blocker 8). |\n| NFR-7 | EP | Thin handlers. `{data}` / paginated / `{error}` envelopes via the http.ts helpers. |\n| NFR-8 | CFG | `src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts`, plus `reminders.ts` and pure `scoring.ts` (lateDays, penalty, finalScore, chip status) for unit tests. Validators in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`. |\n| NFR-9 | SVC, TEST | Store UTC. Display via formatInSchoolTz. Late days in UTC ms (FR-23). The FR-10 default uses `fromZonedTime`. |\n| NFR-10 | UI | react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize are installed, with MUI component mapping (D1). |\n| NFR-11 | — | Reuse list: B1–B10, B15. |\n| NFR-12 | — | Use the logger, never console.log. |\n| NFR-13 | TEST, CFG | Blocker 3: fix the `vitest.config.ts` import to `'vitest/config'` (a one-line fix, in scope because NFR-13 requires a working `npm test`). |\n| NFR-14 | TEST | Unit: scoring.ts. Integration: resubmit history, return, reminder idempotency, exemption vs missing, and the file resolvers (AC-10). E2E: the full flow plus the parent missing list (needs bypassCSP, blocker 4). |\n| NFR-15 | — | No gradebook, peer review, group work or annotation. FR-35 stores the exemption only, and PRD-11 consumes it. |\n| NFR-16 | UI | Two-minute publish: sensible defaults (FR-10 due date, max points 100?, submissionType FILE_UPLOAD?). **Design should set the form defaults.** 30-submission keyboard grading via FR-33 + NFR-3. |\n| NFR-17 | UI | Labelled inputs and keyboard-operable controls: the ToggleButtonGroup and the J/K help hint. |\n\n## Decisions arch-design-system must make (answers to the intake blockers)\n\n| # | Blocker / gap | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | Blocker 1: PRD-08 UI components are missing. | Build the **minimum** shared components in this ticket: `src/components/MarkdownView` (react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, mapped to MUI), `src/components/MarkdownEditor` (MUI TextField multiline + a Write/Preview Tabs toggle using MarkdownView; no new editor dependency), `src/components/FileUpload` (input type=file → `POST /api/files` with the context field, list with remove, `maxFiles` prop) and `FileList` (links to `/api/files/:id`). Shape them so PRD-08 can adopt them later. Do not build PRD-08's remaining scope. |\n| D2 | Blocker 2: the MUI X DataGrid compile break. | Preferred: align `@mui/x-*` versions in package.json/lockfile (it also unblocks the DateTimePicker from `@mui/x-date-pickers`, if that package shares the internals). Fallback for FR-17: an MUI `Table`, which needs no DataGrid. **Check whether `@mui/x-date-pickers` is installed and affected**, because FR-9 needs it. |\n| D3 | Blockers 3/4: vitest import and CSP. | vitest: one-line import fix. CSP: keep `bypassCSP` in Playwright as before. A CSP fix is outside the PRD scope (NFR-15). Note the FR-29 iframe/img `'self'` dependency. |\n| D4 | Blocker 5: the studentTabs renderer. | Register the tab and build the page. Do not build a tab bar. Report it as a known gap. |\n| D5 | Decimal JSON serialization | Decimal fields are strings in API responses (NFR-1). |\n| D6 | The \"Save & return\" round trip | `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade` with an optional `return: true` gives one transaction. |\n| D7 | Rubric raw score | When rubricScores are present, the server sets or enforces `rawScore = Σ points`. |\n| D8 | Teacher/admin view of FR-58 grade fields | Course managers get full fields. Other viewers get the FR-27 serializer. |\n| D9 | Offline-graded row followed by an online submit | Treat it as a resubmission while it is not RETURNED. |\n| D10 | Missing-reminder query window | Bound it (e.g. dueAt within the last 8 days), marked with a `ponytail:` note. |\n\n## Shared pure functions (single source of truth; unit-test targets)\n\n`isAssignmentVisible`, `missingFilter(now)` (Prisma where), `lateDays`, `defaultPenalty`, `computeFinalScore`, `rubricTotal`, `submissionChipStatus`, `nextTeachingDayDueAt`, `toStudentSubmission` (serializer). Each of these is used by two or more call sites listed above. Keeping one copy of each prevents the drift that leads to privacy and correctness bugs (NFR-1, NFR-4).\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013N8tgmiCMZemFpxPGT82Wm","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91d7b1a5-c851-4385-b1f3-145425ca0827","uuid":"6be48968-359b-4b7d-83b9-2d05c1a6b9a1","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:26:15.380Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-9\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T09:00:00Z), PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions (SCH-009). It has 61 FRs and 17 NFRs (78 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers. They must be surfaced in the `system-design.md` Overview (compliance rule 5). Decisions D1–D4 below answer them.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-8 leftovers** as of this writing. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-9 input.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-9 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` sets `context` and `contextId` on unattached files owned by the caller (any file for ADMIN). It does **not** check the file's upload context. `detachFiles` sets `contextId = null`, and `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes those files after 24 h. | src/server/files/files-service.ts L215-245, purge.ts | FR-53 requires uploads with context `'submission'`. The service must check `context === 'submission'` before calling attachFiles. On resubmission, **never detach the previous attempt's files**: `SubmissionHistory.fileIds` points at them, and detaching would let the purge delete history bytes. Keep them attached to the same submission id. |\n| B2 | `FileObject.storageKey` is `@unique`, and a FileObject holds a single `(context, contextId)`. `storage.ts` exports `saveFile(stream)`, `readFile(key)` and `deleteFile`. | schema L564-578, storage.ts | FR-15 duplicate **cannot share** attachment rows. For each target course, copy the bytes (`readFile` → `saveFile`), create a new FileObject (context `'assignment'`), then attach it. |\n| B3 | `FileObject` has a back-relation `lessonAttachments LessonAttachment[]`. | schema L577 | FR-3/FR-4 add back-relations `assignmentAttachments` and `submissionFiles` to FileObject. This is an additive edit to an existing model, so NFR-11 allows it. |\n| B4 | `canAccessFile` order: unattached → owner/ADMIN; registered resolver; unknown context → owner/ADMIN. Resolver errors deny. `registerBuiltInContexts` currently registers `lesson` and `logo`. | access.ts L35-50, contexts.ts L36-39 | FR-47 adds `assignmentResolver` (contextId = assignmentId) and `submissionResolver` (contextId = submissionId) in contexts.ts. Before submit, a student's own upload is unattached, so it is already readable by owner/ADMIN only. |\n| B5 | `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` is a pure read-time check: PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt ≤ now. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` covers ADMIN, teacher and co-teacher. | visibility.ts | FR-13 can reuse both by mapping `availableFrom → publishAt`. Widen the `Publishable.status` type to accept `AssignmentStatus`, which has the same string values, rather than writing a second helper (NFR-11). |\n| B6 | `assertCanViewCourse` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child (`studentLinks`). `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Errors are `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These already provide all of NFR-5's course checks. A parent who views a course still needs to be scoped to *which* child (FR-18, FR-38). |\n| B7 | `ParentStudentLink {parentId, studentId}`. `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds, ...})` never throws. | notify.ts L98-117 | FR-44 uses it as-is. For FR-45 (parents only), call `notify()` with the parent ids from `parentStudentLink`. |\n| B8 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` **on every call**. Purges run in a once-per-day `if` (`lastPurgeAt`, in memory). | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-43/FR-45: call `sendDueReminders(now)` on **every** call, outside the daily block (due_soon has a 24 h window, so daily would miss it). Wrap it in its own try/catch + logger, like the purges. |\n| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object with `{label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. `content.lesson_published` is the closest precedent. | types.ts L33, L90-100 | FR-46: add four keys. Roles: `published` [STUDENT]; `due_soon` [STUDENT]; `returned` [STUDENT, PARENT]; `missing` [PARENT], with defaultEmail true. |\n| B10 | `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, tz)` and `schoolNow(now, tz)` live in `src/lib/dates.ts`, using date-fns-tz, which is already installed. | dates.ts | FR-10 next-teaching-day 23:59 and FR-25 receipt formatting. Convert wall time to UTC with date-fns-tz `fromZonedTime` (NFR-9 DST). |\n| B11 | `SchoolDay {dayOfWeek 1-7, isTeaching}` is seeded with all 7 rows. | schema L477-480 | FR-10 loops forward at most 7 days. If no day is teaching, fall back to tomorrow. |\n| B12 | `courseTabs` = overview, roster, attendance (there is **no content tab**: PRD-08 UI is missing). It is rendered by `CourseTabs.tsx`. `src/app/(app)/students/[id]/` has `attendance/` and `courses/` but no tab bar. | course-tabs.ts, ls | FR-16: append one entry with ALL_ROLES. FR-41: register the entry plus the page `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx`. It stays unreachable through tabs (blocker 5), but direct URLs work. |\n| B13 | `navigation.ts` entries are `{label, href, icon, roles, group?}`. | navigation.ts L31-38 | FR-40: one entry with roles [STUDENT, PARENT, TEACHER]. Default ADMIN to the \"To grade\" view through the API (clarification). Add ADMIN to the nav only if design adopts that default. |\n| B14 | `src/server/assignments/` and `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` do not exist. Validator precedent: `src/lib/validators/content.ts`. HTTP helpers: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` and `AppError` in `src/server/http.ts`. | ls, grep | Greenfield feature folder (NFR-8). Route handlers follow NFR-7 using the existing helpers. |\n| B15 | Existing components: ConfirmDialog, DataTable, DateDisplay, EmptyState, FormField, LoadingSkeleton, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker. **There is no** FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView or MarkdownEditor. | ls src/components | Blocker 1, see D1. |\n| B16 | Tests live in `tests/{unit,integration,e2e}`. | ls | NFR-14 placement. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = service logic · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = maintenance pass · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = registry/config · **NOTIF** = notification · **TEST** = test · **SEED** = seed data\n\n### Data model (one migration: FR-1…FR-6)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | New enums `SubmissionType`, `AssignmentStatus`, `SubmissionStatus`. Do not reuse `ContentStatus`, because the PRD names a new enum (the values happen to match, and B5 relies on that). |\n| FR-2 | DM | `Assignment` with `allowExtraCredit`, `notifiedAt?`, `archivedAt?`, `rubricId String? @unique`, Course relation with Cascade, and `@@index([courseId, dueAt])`. Add the back-relation `assignments Assignment[]` on Course. |\n| FR-3 | DM | `AssignmentAttachment` (join to FileObject, back-relation per B3), `Rubric`, `RubricCriterion` (`maxPoints Decimal(6,2)`, `order Int`, `levels Json`). A 1:1 Rubric↔Assignment via `rubricId @unique` means a rubric is never shared, so delete it together with the assignment. |\n| FR-4 | DM | `Submission @@unique([assignmentId, studentId])`, which means one row per student. Attempts live in `SubmissionHistory`. The Decimal fields are `rawScore`, `penaltyPercent` and `finalScore`. `rubricScores Json`. `SubmissionFile` join, back-relation per B3. `SubmissionHistory.fileIds String[]` has no FK, so the files must not be purged (B1). |\n| FR-5 | DM | `GradeExemption @@id([assignmentId, studentId])`. Cascade on assignment delete. |\n| FR-6 | DM | `AssignmentReminder @@unique([assignmentId, studentId, kind])`. `kind` is a String ('due_soon' / 'missing'). Insert with `createMany({skipDuplicates:true})`, or catch P2002, and send only for the rows actually inserted (idempotent under concurrent dispatchers). |\n| FR-7 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`, shared by client forms and route handlers. Cross-field rules (`lateCutoffAt > dueAt`, rubric sum) use `.superRefine`. Decimal inputs come in as number/string and the service converts them to `Prisma.Decimal` (NFR-1). |\n| FR-8 | SVC, DM | Offline marker: `attemptNumber = 0`, `text = null`, no files, `submittedAt = gradedAt`. **Edge case for design:** a student may later submit online against an offline-graded row (`status = SUBMITTED`, unique row). Recommend allowing it and treating it as a resubmission (move the attempt-0 grade into history and clear the grade), unless it is already RETURNED. |\n\n### Assignment authoring (teacher)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-9 | UI | `/courses/[courseId]/assignments/new` and an edit route (`[assignmentId]/edit`). MUI DateTimePicker (MUI X pickers, same version-alignment risk as D2) in the school timezone. It depends on D1 (FileUpload, MarkdownEditor). |\n| FR-10 | SVC | `nextTeachingDayDueAt(now, tz)`: a pure helper next to `schoolNow` in `src/lib/dates.ts`. Computed server-side and passed as a default prop (NFR-2). |\n| FR-11 | UI, VAL | The rubric builder uses `@dnd-kit/sortable`, which is already installed, for reorder. The rubric-sum check is in the Zod schema (shared), using Decimal sum, so the server rejects with VALIDATION_ERROR. The exact message string is required. |\n| FR-12 | UI, VAL | The status comes from the button. SCHEDULED requires `availableFrom > serverNow`, checked in the service, not only in Zod (Zod has no server clock guarantee). |\n| FR-13 | SVC | `isAssignmentVisible(a, now) = !archivedAt && isVisible({status, publishAt: availableFrom}, now)`. Use it in **every** student/parent read path, the file resolver, submission rules and reminders. It is the single source of truth. |\n| FR-14 | UI | Show the warning when the assignment is published and `submissionCount > 0`, and the dueAt or maxPoints changes. No recalculation happens on the server. Keep a `maxPointsChangedAt` banner? Simplest is a client-side banner on save success. **Design should pick one, and not add a column unless needed.** |\n| FR-15 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/duplicate {courseIds}`. Check `assertCanManageCourse` for **each** target. Make it one transaction per target. Copy the rubric and criteria as new rows (1:1), and copy the attachment bytes per B2. Status DRAFT, `notifiedAt` null. LOW confidence default: identical dueAt plus the availableFrom/lateCutoffAt offsets. |\n\n### Lists and navigation\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-16 | CFG | Append `{key:'assignments', href:/courses/:id/assignments, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. |\n| FR-17 | UI, EP | The teacher table depends on D2 (DataTable compile break). The counts come from FR-48's manager shape using `groupBy` aggregates, not N+1 queries. |\n| FR-18 | UI, AUTH | Student groups: Upcoming / Past due (missing) / Submitted / Returned. A parent viewing a course needs a child context: use `?studentId=`, validated against `ParentStudentLink` **and** active enrollment in this course. Default to the only linked child enrolled. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Assignment page: sanitised Markdown (D1 MarkdownView), late-policy summary, rubric, and a countdown under 48 h. Compute the countdown client-side from a server-provided `serverNow` offset, so a skewed client clock doesn't show a wrong countdown. It is display-only (NFR-2). |\n| FR-20 | UI | The panel switches on submissionType. Draft autosave to `localStorage` keyed by `assignmentId:userId`. Clear it after a successful submit. |\n| FR-21 | UI | Reuse `ConfirmDialog`. |\n| FR-25 | UI | Receipt formatted with `formatInSchoolTz(submittedAt, \"EEE d MMM yyyy, HH:mm\", tz)` plus the attempt number. |\n| FR-26 | UI, AUTH | Grading fields appear only when `status = RETURNED` (FR-27). |\n| FR-27 | AUTH, SVC | **Response-shaping boundary.** One serializer `toStudentSubmission(sub)` removes `rawScore/penaltyPercent/finalScore/feedback/rubricScores/gradedAt/gradedById` unless the status is RETURNED. Every student/parent path uses it: FR-48, FR-50, FR-55, FR-57, FR-58 when the viewer is the student or parent. This covers NFR-4. |\n| FR-37 | UI, EP | `/assignments` STUDENT: 4 tabs plus a course filter, across ACTIVE enrollments. Missing = visible, not archived, `dueAt < now`, no submission, not exempt, `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (FR-60). Define one Prisma `where` builder `missingFilter(now)` and share it with the reminders (FR-43/45) and the counts. |\n| FR-38 | UI, AUTH | PARENT: a child selector using linked students only. The server validates `studentId` against `ParentStudentLink`. The view is read-only, so the submit panel is not rendered **and** the API rejects it (FR-53 is STUDENT-only). |\n| FR-39 | UI, EP | TEACHER \"To grade\": `status = SUBMITTED AND gradedAt IS NULL` in courses where `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`, ordered by `submittedAt asc`. ADMIN gets the same list across all courses (clarification default). |\n| FR-40 | CFG | One nav entry (B13). |\n| FR-41 | CFG, UI | studentTabs entry plus a page. It is invisible until a tab bar exists (blocker 5). Out of scope to build one here: do not add a tab-bar renderer just for this (NFR-15 scope / YAGNI), and surface it as a known gap. |\n\n### Submission (student)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-22 | SVC, AUTH | Rule order: (1) the assignment is visible and not archived; (2) `role = STUDENT` and ACTIVE-enrolled; (3) not exempt; (4) `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (implied); (5) deadline: `now ≤ dueAt`, or `allowLate && (!lateCutoffAt || now ≤ lateCutoffAt)`. The exact error string is required. `now = new Date()` on the server only (NFR-2). |\n| FR-23 | SVC, TEST | Pure `lateDays(submittedAt, dueAt) = ceil((s − d) / 86_400_000)` for `s > d`, else 0. Use UTC milliseconds, so DST cannot affect it (NFR-9: a 24 h wall day across DST is 23/25 h of real time, and the PRD defines late days in 24 h units). Exactly 24 h gives 1. This is unit-test territory (NFR-14). |\n| FR-24 | SVC, DM | In one transaction: if a row exists, require `status = SUBMITTED` (RETURNED gives a VALIDATION/CONFLICT error), insert `SubmissionHistory` from the current row, `attemptNumber++`, clear the grade fields, replace the `SubmissionFile` rows, and attach the new files. Do not detach the old files (B1). Concurrency: two concurrent first submits hit the unique key. Catch P2002 and retry as a resubmit, or `upsert`. |\n| FR-53 | EP, VAL, AUTH | `POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions {text?, fileIds[]}`. Validation: `fileIds.length ≤ maxFileCount`; the content matches submissionType (text required for ONLINE_TEXT, files for FILE_UPLOAD, at least one for TEXT_AND_FILE); each file is `ownerId = me`, `context = 'submission'` and unattached, or already on this submission (B1). |\n\n### Grading (teacher)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-28 | UI, EP | The left panel is fed by FR-54. Status chip derivation is a pure function: Exempt > Returned > Graded > Late > Submitted > Not submitted. Shared by the server (FR-54) and tests. |\n| FR-29 | UI | `<img>`/`<iframe src=\"/api/files/:id?inline=1\">`. **CSP check for design:** confirm that `next.config.js` `frame-src`/`img-src` allow `'self'`. The CSP `script-src` issue is blocker 4. The history dropdown reads FR-55 (manager-only history). |\n| FR-30 | UI, SVC | Rubric ToggleButtonGroup with an auto-sum. Penalty prefill `min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)`. The live final score uses decimal.js on the client too, so the preview and server values agree (NFR-1). The prefill is display-only. The server stores what is submitted, after FR-36 validation. |\n| FR-31 | SVC, TEST | `finalScore = raw × (1 − p/100)`, computed with `Decimal`, `toDecimalPlaces(2, ROUND_HALF_UP)`. One pure function in the service, unit-tested (18 at 20 % = 14.40). |\n| FR-32 | EP, SVC, NOTIF | \"Save\" = `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade`. \"Save & return\" = the same call with `{return:true}`, or grade followed by return. **Design should pick a single round trip.** The bulk route is `POST /api/assignments/:id/return {submissionIds?}`, with the default `gradedAt not null AND status ≠ RETURNED`. Each return sets RETURNED and returnedAt, fires FR-44, and writes an audit (FR-59). |\n| FR-33 | UI | A keydown listener on the grading page. Ignore J/K when `event.target` is an input, textarea or contenteditable. Ctrl/Cmd+Enter always works. Accessibility: show the shortcuts in a help hint (NFR-17). |\n| FR-34 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}`. The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Reject it if a submission already exists (grade that one instead). Creates the FR-8 row with the grade fields set, penalty 0, and an audit row. |\n| FR-35 | EP, SVC | `PUT/DELETE /api/assignments/:id/exemptions/:studentId`. Idempotent (`upsert` / `deleteMany`). Writes an audit row. Its effects come through `missingFilter` and the FR-22 rule. A PRD-11 exclusion flag = the GradeExemption row itself, so no extra column. |\n| FR-36 | VAL, SVC | Server-side, Decimal-based: `0 ≤ raw ≤ maxPoints` (×1.2 if allowExtraCredit). Each rubric score `0 ≤ points ≤ criterion.maxPoints` (extra credit is raw-only, per the clarification), and each `criterionId` belongs to this rubric. `0 ≤ penalty ≤ 100`. With a rubric, should raw equal the sum of the rubric points? The PRD says it auto-sums but stays overridable only via the penalty. **Recommend the server enforces raw = Σ rubric points when rubricScores are given.** |\n| FR-54 | EP | `GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions` (manage). LEFT JOIN of ACTIVE enrollments × submissions × exemptions. Paginate per NFR-7, but grading needs all students for J/K: allow `pageSize` up to 100 and document the limit. |\n| FR-55 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/submissions/:id`: the submitter, linked parents or course managers. History only for managers. Grade fields go through the FR-27 serializer for the student and parent. Also needed by NFR-3 prefetch. |\n| FR-56 | EP, SVC | Sets `gradedById`, `gradedAt` and the computed `finalScore`. Does not change status (it stays SUBMITTED until return). Writes an audit row. |\n| FR-59 | SVC | `audit()` on grade, return (one row per submission, or one bulk row with the ids; **design should pick**), exempt/unexempt and offline grade. |\n\n### Assignment API\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-48 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/courses/:id/assignments`. Two response shapes depending on `canSeeDrafts`. Students and parents get FR-13-visible, non-archived assignments plus their own submission state (via the FR-27 serializer). |\n| FR-49 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/courses/:id/assignments`. One transaction: rubric and criteria, assignment, attachments (`attachFiles` with `'assignment'`, contextId = assignment.id), and on PUBLISHED the FR-42 notify after commit. |\n| FR-50 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/assignments/:id`. A non-manager on an invisible/archived assignment gets NOT_FOUND, not FORBIDDEN, so existence is not leaked. Includes `serverNow` for FR-19. |\n| FR-51 | EP, SVC | PATCH: re-validate the rubric sum against maxPoints. Diff the attachments (detach the removed ones, which are then purged after 24 h per B1; that is fine for assignment attachments). DRAFT→PUBLISHED triggers FR-42. DELETE: hard delete if there are 0 submissions (cascade; the attachment files are detached first so the purge reclaims them), else set `archivedAt`. |\n| FR-52 | AUTH, SVC | Covered by `isAssignmentVisible` (FR-13), which includes `!archivedAt`. One check, applied everywhere. LOW confidence default. |\n| FR-57 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab=`. Role switch: STUDENT gets its own data; PARENT requires a linked `studentId`; TEACHER/ADMIN get To grade. `tab ∈ upcoming/missing/submitted/returned`. |\n| FR-58 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/students/:id/assignments` → `assertCanViewStudent`, then the same query as the FR-57 student view, built with a shared service function. A student or parent viewer gets the FR-27 serializer. Teachers and admins see grades? The PRD says \"same per-student data\", so **recommend the same serializer for all non-managers and full fields for the student's course managers.** Design should confirm. |\n\n### Notifications and maintenance\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-42 | NOTIF, SVC | Exactly once: `UPDATE assignment SET notifiedAt = now WHERE id = ? AND notifiedAt IS NULL` (`updateMany`, count = 1 → send). Triggered on publish (FR-49/51), and for SCHEDULED assignments in the student list read path (FR-48/57) when visible and `notifiedAt` is null. **A side effect on GET:** keep it fire-and-forget after the response data is built, and never fail the read. Design may also add it to `sendDueReminders` as a safety net, but must not do both without the atomic guard (the guard makes both safe). |\n| FR-43 | JOB, NOTIF | `sendDueReminders(now)` in `src/server/assignments/reminders.ts`, called on every dispatcher call (B8). The window is `dueAt − 24h ≤ now < dueAt`. Targets: ACTIVE-enrolled, no submission, not exempt, visible, not archived, not NO_SUBMISSION. Idempotent via FR-6. Bound the query (only assignments with `dueAt` in [now, now+24h]). |\n| FR-44 | NOTIF | On return: `notifyStudentAndParents` with a body like `\"{course}: {title} — {finalScore}/{maxPoints}\"`. Bulk return sends one notify per student. |\n| FR-45 | JOB, NOTIF | In the same pass: `now ≥ dueAt + 24h`, with the `missingFilter` targets. Parents only (`notify` to the linked parent ids). FR-6 kind 'missing'. Bound the query to avoid scanning all history, e.g. `dueAt` in [now − 8 d, now − 24 h], with a `ponytail:` note on that window. |\n| FR-46 | CFG | Four keys (B9). |\n| FR-47 | AUTH | `assignmentResolver`: load the assignment and course, then `assertCanViewCourse`, then `canSeeDrafts \\|\\| isAssignmentVisible`. `submissionResolver`: load the submission; allow the submitting student, a linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`) or `canSeeDrafts(course)` (managers/ADMIN). Deny everyone else, including other students (NFR-4, AC-10). Integration test needed. |\n\n### Seed\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-60 | SVC | Exclude NO_SUBMISSION in `missingFilter` and the reminder targets. The submission panel is hidden and FR-53 rejects. LOW confidence default. |\n| FR-61 | SEED | Idempotent: look up the courses by code and skip if they are missing. Upsert the assignments by `(courseId, title)`. Seed Decimal scores via strings. Seeded attachments/files are not required, so skip byte storage. |\n\n### Non-functional\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| NFR-1 | SVC, VAL | Decimal end to end: Prisma `Decimal(6,2)` columns, `Prisma.Decimal` in the service, decimal.js in the client preview. Serialize Decimals in API responses as **strings**, to avoid float loss in JSON. Design must state this convention for api-contracts. |\n| NFR-2 | SVC | Every deadline, visibility or reminder check uses `new Date()` on the server. There is no client timestamp field in any request schema. |\n| NFR-3 | UI, EP | Prefetch the next and previous `GET /api/submissions/:id` into a client cache keyed by id (a plain `Map` in the grading page; no data-fetching library added). The <300 ms target is a client switch from cache. |\n| NFR-4 | AUTH | Enforced at three boundaries: the FR-27 serializer, the FR-47 file resolvers, and query scoping (a student only ever queries `studentId = me`). |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every route: `requireUser`/`requireRole`, then assertCan*. Every page: `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`. |\n| NFR-6 | UI | MUI 9.5.0 + MUI X only, with mui-mcp lookups before use. Components needed: List, Chip, ToggleButtonGroup, Dialog, Tabs, DataGrid (D2), DateTimePicker, Autocomplete, Snackbar. Hard blocker if mui-mcp is unreachable (blocker 8). |\n| NFR-7 | EP | Thin handlers. `{data}` / paginated / `{error}` envelopes via the http.ts helpers. |\n| NFR-8 | CFG | `src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts`, plus `reminders.ts` and pure `scoring.ts` (lateDays, penalty, finalScore, chip status) for unit tests. Validators in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`. |\n| NFR-9 | SVC, TEST | Store UTC. Display via formatInSchoolTz. Late days in UTC ms (FR-23). The FR-10 default uses `fromZonedTime`. |\n| NFR-10 | UI | react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize are installed, with MUI component mapping (D1). |\n| NFR-11 | — | Reuse list: B1–B10, B15. |\n| NFR-12 | — | Use the logger, never console.log. |\n| NFR-13 | TEST, CFG | Blocker 3: fix the `vitest.config.ts` import to `'vitest/config'` (a one-line fix, in scope because NFR-13 requires a working `npm test`). |\n| NFR-14 | TEST | Unit: scoring.ts. Integration: resubmit history, return, reminder idempotency, exemption vs missing, and the file resolvers (AC-10). E2E: the full flow plus the parent missing list (needs bypassCSP, blocker 4). |\n| NFR-15 | — | No gradebook, peer review, group work or annotation. FR-35 stores the exemption only, and PRD-11 consumes it. |\n| NFR-16 | UI | Two-minute publish: sensible defaults (FR-10 due date, max points 100?, submissionType FILE_UPLOAD?). **Design should set the form defaults.** 30-submission keyboard grading via FR-33 + NFR-3. |\n| NFR-17 | UI | Labelled inputs and keyboard-operable controls: the ToggleButtonGroup and the J/K help hint. |\n\n## Decisions arch-design-system must make (answers to the intake blockers)\n\n| # | Blocker / gap | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | Blocker 1: PRD-08 UI components are missing. | Build the **minimum** shared components in this ticket: `src/components/MarkdownView` (react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, mapped to MUI), `src/components/MarkdownEditor` (MUI TextField multiline + a Write/Preview Tabs toggle using MarkdownView; no new editor dependency), `src/components/FileUpload` (input type=file → `POST /api/files` with the context field, list with remove, `maxFiles` prop) and `FileList` (links to `/api/files/:id`). Shape them so PRD-08 can adopt them later. Do not build PRD-08's remaining scope. |\n| D2 | Blocker 2: the MUI X DataGrid compile break. | Preferred: align `@mui/x-*` versions in package.json/lockfile (it also unblocks the DateTimePicker from `@mui/x-date-pickers`, if that package shares the internals). Fallback for FR-17: an MUI `Table`, which needs no DataGrid. **Check whether `@mui/x-date-pickers` is installed and affected**, because FR-9 needs it. |\n| D3 | Blockers 3/4: vitest import and CSP. | vitest: one-line import fix. CSP: keep `bypassCSP` in Playwright as before. A CSP fix is outside the PRD scope (NFR-15). Note the FR-29 iframe/img `'self'` dependency. |\n| D4 | Blocker 5: the studentTabs renderer. | Register the tab and build the page. Do not build a tab bar. Report it as a known gap. |\n| D5 | Decimal JSON serialization | Decimal fields are strings in API responses (NFR-1). |\n| D6 | The \"Save & return\" round trip | `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade` with an optional `return: true` gives one transaction. |\n| D7 | Rubric raw score | When rubricScores are present, the server sets or enforces `rawScore = Σ points`. |\n| D8 | Teacher/admin view of FR-58 grade fields | Course managers get full fields. Other viewers get the FR-27 serializer. |\n| D9 | Offline-graded row followed by an online submit | Treat it as a resubmission while it is not RETURNED. |\n| D10 | Missing-reminder query window | Bound it (e.g. dueAt within the last 8 days), marked with a `ponytail:` note. |\n\n## Shared pure functions (single source of truth; unit-test targets)\n\n`isAssignmentVisible`, `missingFilter(now)` (Prisma where), `lateDays`, `defaultPenalty`, `computeFinalScore`, `rubricTotal`, `submissionChipStatus`, `nextTeachingDayDueAt`, `toStudentSubmission` (serializer). Each of these is used by two or more call sites listed above. Keeping one copy of each prevents the drift that leads to privacy and correctness bugs (NFR-1, NFR-4).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":97,"newStart":1,"newLines":174,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-8","+# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-9"," "," Written by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T06:00:00Z), PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008).","-It has 48 FRs and 12 NFRs (60 requirements) at 93% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers, and they must be surfaced in `system-design.md` Overview.","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T09:00:00Z), PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions (SCH-009). It has 61 FRs and 17 NFRs (78 requirements) at 95% confidence.","+`handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers. They must be surfaced in the `system-design.md` Overview (compliance rule 5). Decisions D1–D4 below answer them."," ","-> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are still **SH-7** leftovers at the time of writing. Downstream sub-tasks own them and must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-8 input.","+> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-8 leftovers** as of this writing. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-9 input."," ","-## Brownfield findings verified on disk (arch-research-reqs)","+## Brownfield facts verified on disk"," ","-| # | Finding | Evidence | Impact |","+| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-9 |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| B1 | **Middleware blocks unauthenticated `/api/files/:id`.** `src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for any `/api/*` not matched by `isPublicPath()`. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is `['/api/health','/api/auth/','/api/internal/']`. | middleware.ts L36-40, public-routes.ts L7 | FR-10's public `logo` context cannot work (login page, emails) unless `/api/files/` is made public. **Recommended:** add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. Then the GET handler resolves the session itself (optional user → access registry), and POST/DELETE **must** call `requireUser()` explicitly, because middleware no longer guards them. This is a security-critical design point (NFR-1, NFR-8). |","-| B2 | Daily hook exists: `lastPurgeAt` + `purgeOldNotifications()` in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` L11-31. | grep | FR-12 adds a second call in the same `if` block. No new scheduler. |","-| B3 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) → {ok, retryAfterMs}` is a per-process sliding window. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-3: `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)`. |","-| B4 | `logoUrl` consumers: `BaseLayout.tsx` L28 uses `<Img src={school.logoUrl}>` raw, and `render.ts` already passes `appUrl`. | grep | FR-40 stores a relative `/api/files/<id>`, so BaseLayout must prefix `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. Combined with B1, that makes the logo fetchable from mail clients. |","-| B5 | No `.gitignore` at the repo root. | `ls` | Create one with `uploads/` (plus `node_modules`, `.next`, `.env` if missing). |","-| B6 | No `src/server/files/` and no content code. | ls | Confirms greenfield. |","-| B7 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are arrays of `CourseTab`/`StudentTab` in `src/config/`. | grep | FR-20 / FR-35 append one entry each. |","-| B8 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object in `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, and `ACADEMIC` is a valid category. | grep | FR-38 adds one key. |","+| B1 | `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` sets `context` and `contextId` on unattached files owned by the caller (any file for ADMIN). It does **not** check the file's upload context. `detachFiles` sets `contextId = null`, and `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes those files after 24 h. | src/server/files/files-service.ts L215-245, purge.ts | FR-53 requires uploads with context `'submission'`. The service must check `context === 'submission'` before calling attachFiles. On resubmission, **never detach the previous attempt's files**: `SubmissionHistory.fileIds` points at them, and detaching would let the purge delete history bytes. Keep them attached to the same submission id. |","+| B2 | `FileObject.storageKey` is `@unique`, and a FileObject holds a single `(context, contextId)`. `storage.ts` exports `saveFile(stream)`, `readFile(key)` and `deleteFile`. | schema L564-578, storage.ts | FR-15 duplicate **cannot share** attachment rows. For each target course, copy the bytes (`readFile` → `saveFile`), create a new FileObject (context `'assignment'`), then attach it. |","+| B3 | `FileObject` has a back-relation `lessonAttachments LessonAttachment[]`. | schema L577 | FR-3/FR-4 add back-relations `assignmentAttachments` and `submissionFiles` to FileObject. This is an additive edit to an existing model, so NFR-11 allows it. |","+| B4 | `canAccessFile` order: unattached → owner/ADMIN; registered resolver; unknown context → owner/ADMIN. Resolver errors deny. `registerBuiltInContexts` currently registers `lesson` and `logo`. | access.ts L35-50, contexts.ts L36-39 | FR-47 adds `assignmentResolver` (contextId = assignmentId) and `submissionResolver` (contextId = submissionId) in contexts.ts. Before submit, a student's own upload is unattached, so it is already readable by owner/ADMIN only. |","+| B5 | `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` is a pure read-time check: PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt ≤ now. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` covers ADMIN, teacher and co-teacher. | visibility.ts | FR-13 can reuse both by mapping `availableFrom → publishAt`. Widen the `Publishable.status` type to accept `AssignmentStatus`, which has the same string values, rather than writing a second helper (NFR-11). |","+| B6 | `assertCanViewCourse` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child (`studentLinks`). `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Errors are `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These already provide all of NFR-5's course checks. A parent who views a course still needs to be scoped to *which* child (FR-18, FR-38). |","+| B7 | `ParentStudentLink {parentId, studentId}`. `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds, ...})` never throws. | notify.ts L98-117 | FR-44 uses it as-is. For FR-45 (parents only), call `notify()` with the parent ids from `parentStudentLink`. |","+| B8 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` **on every call**. Purges run in a once-per-day `if` (`lastPurgeAt`, in memory). | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-43/FR-45: call `sendDueReminders(now)` on **every** call, outside the daily block (due_soon has a 24 h window, so daily would miss it). Wrap it in its own try/catch + logger, like the purges. |","+| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object with `{label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. `content.lesson_published` is the closest precedent. | types.ts L33, L90-100 | FR-46: add four keys. Roles: `published` [STUDENT]; `due_soon` [STUDENT]; `returned` [STUDENT, PARENT]; `missing` [PARENT], with defaultEmail true. |","+| B10 | `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, tz)` and `schoolNow(now, tz)` live in `src/lib/dates.ts`, using date-fns-tz, which is already installed. | dates.ts | FR-10 next-teaching-day 23:59 and FR-25 receipt formatting. Convert wall time to UTC with date-fns-tz `fromZonedTime` (NFR-9 DST). |","+| B11 | `SchoolDay {dayOfWeek 1-7, isTeaching}` is seeded with all 7 rows. | schema L477-480 | FR-10 loops forward at most 7 days. If no day is teaching, fall back to tomorrow. |","+| B12 | `courseTabs` = overview, roster, attendance (there is **no content tab**: PRD-08 UI is missing). It is rendered by `CourseTabs.tsx`. `src/app/(app)/students/[id]/` has `attendance/` and `courses/` but no tab bar. | course-tabs.ts, ls | FR-16: append one entry with ALL_ROLES. FR-41: register the entry plus the page `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx`. It stays unreachable through tabs (blocker 5), but direct URLs work. |","+| B13 | `navigation.ts` entries are `{label, href, icon, roles, group?}`. | navigation.ts L31-38 | FR-40: one entry with roles [STUDENT, PARENT, TEACHER]. Default ADMIN to the \"To grade\" view through the API (clarification). Add ADMIN to the nav only if design adopts that default. |","+| B14 | `src/server/assignments/` and `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` do not exist. Validator precedent: `src/lib/validators/content.ts`. HTTP helpers: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` and `AppError` in `src/server/http.ts`. | ls, grep | Greenfield feature folder (NFR-8). Route handlers follow NFR-7 using the existing helpers. |","+| B15 | Existing components: ConfirmDialog, DataTable, DateDisplay, EmptyState, FormField, LoadingSkeleton, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker. **There is no** FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView or MarkdownEditor. | ls src/components | Blocker 1, see D1. |","+| B16 | Tests live in `tests/{unit,integration,e2e}`. | ls | NFR-14 placement. |"," "," ## Requirement → architectural concern"," ","-Concern legend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = server service/module · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = background/maintenance · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = config/env/registry · **TEST**","+Legend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = service logic · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = maintenance pass · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = registry/config · **NOTIF** = notification · **TEST** = test · **SEED** = seed data"," ","+### Data model (one migration: FR-1…FR-6)","+"," | Req | Concern | Notes |"," |---|---|---|","-| FR-1 | DM | `FileObject` + `@@index([context, contextId])`, unique `storageKey`. `context` is a plain String (registry keys), not an enum, so new contexts need no migration. One migration together with FR-15. |","-| FR-2 | SVC, CFG | `src/server/storage.ts`: `saveFile`/`readFile`/`deleteFile`. Resolve paths with `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR, key)` and assert they stay under UPLOAD_DIR (traversal guard). Add env `UPLOAD_DIR` to the env schema. Single local-disk impl, no interface (NFR-11). |","-| FR-3 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/files` multipart. Use `request.formData()`? It buffers, which conflicts with NFR-5. Use `busboy`-free streaming via `req.body` + the Web `Request` multipart parser? **Design must pick.** Next.js route handlers expose `request.body` (a ReadableStream), but a multipart parser isn't in the allowed deps. Practical option: `formData()` is acceptable only if the size cap is pre-checked via `Content-Length` (≤ MAX_UPLOAD_MB + overhead) before parsing, then `File.stream()` → disk with sha256. Flag as a NFR-5 trade-off for design. |","-| FR-4 | VAL, CFG | `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` env (default 25). Enforce with a byte counter in the write stream (abort and unlink the partial file), plus an early `Content-Length` reject. Logo override: 2 MB (FR-40). Make the limit per-context: `{ logo: 2 }`, default env. |","-| FR-5 | VAL | Extension allowlist + `fileTypeFromBuffer` on the first ~4100 bytes (peek before or while writing). New dep `file-type` (ESM-only, so check the Next server bundling). |","-| FR-6 | VAL | Rule table: txt/csv → sniff must be `undefined`. docx/xlsx/pptx → sniff ∈ {zip, matching OOXML mime}. zip → zip. Others → sniff ext must match the declared ext (jpg≡jpeg). Pure function, unit-testable (FR-48). |","-| FR-7 | VAL | `sanitizeFilename()`: strip `/ \\ ` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trim, and cap at 150 while preserving the extension. Pure function and unit test. |","-| FR-8 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/files/:id`: registry check **before** `readFile`. Headers: stored mime, `nosniff`, `attachment; filename*=UTF-8''…`, and `inline` only if `?inline=1` and mime is image/* or application/pdf. Stream via `Readable.toWeb(fs.createReadStream)`. |","-| FR-9 | SVC, AUTH, CFG | `src/server/files/access.ts`: a `Map<string, resolver>`. Default: owner or ADMIN. Return **404** for denied (don't leak existence) and 401 for unauthenticated non-public. Contexts are registered via side-effect import, so the GET handler must import the module that registers `lesson`/`logo` (avoid a lazy-registration bug). |","-| FR-10 | AUTH | `lesson` resolver: load lesson+module+course, then `assertCanViewCourse` + visibility rule (FR-18) for STUDENT/PARENT, while managers see drafts. `logo`: `() => true` incl. `user=null`. Depends on B1. Unattached files (contextId null) fall to the owner/ADMIN check even within the 'lesson' context, which lets editor previews work before attach. |","-| FR-11 | EP, AUTH | `DELETE /api/files/:id`: owner/ADMIN, `contextId === null`, else CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR. Delete the row, then the bytes (log on bytes failure, since orphan bytes are harmless). Audit when ADMIN deletes another user's file (FR-46). |","-| FR-12 | JOB | `purgeOrphanFiles()` in `src/server/files/purge.ts`, hooked at B2. Batch `findMany` where contextId null and createdAt < now-24h, delete bytes then rows. **Caveat:** the logo is \"attached\" how? FR-40 stores a URL in logoUrl but contextId stays null, so the logo gets purged after 24h. **Design must set `contextId` for logo** (e.g. the SchoolSettings id/`'school'`) when settings are saved. |","-| FR-13 | UI | `src/components/FileUpload/`. XHR (not fetch) for `upload.onprogress`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`/`onChange` (FileObject summaries), and optional reorder (FR-27). MUI only (NFR-7). |","-| FR-14 | UI | `src/components/FileList/`: read-only list, links `/api/files/:id`. |","-| FR-15 | DM | `ContentStatus` enum, Module(courseId, title, position, status, publishAt), Lesson(moduleId, title, position, status, publishAt, contentMarkdown, estimatedMinutes, videoUrl, createdById?), LessonAttachment(lessonId, fileId, position), LessonLink(lessonId, title, url, position), and LessonProgress PK [lessonId, studentId]. Cascades: Course→Module→Lesson→Attachment/Link/Progress. Add back-relations on Course/User/StudentProfile. Index `[courseId, position]`, `[moduleId, position]`. Follow the PRD's exact field list. |","-| FR-16 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/content.ts` (Zod), shared by client and server. URL refinements reuse the FR-30 parser for videoUrl. |","-| FR-17 | SVC, AUTH | Inside the PATCH lesson transaction: verify each fileId is (owner==caller or ADMIN) and (contextId null or already == this lessonId), then `updateMany` context/contextId. Removed attachments should be detached (contextId → null), which leaves them purgeable in 24h. Decide explicitly. |","-| FR-18 | SVC | Pure `isVisible(entity, now)` + Prisma `where` fragment `visibleWhere(now)` = `OR[{status:PUBLISHED},{status:SCHEDULED, publishAt:{lte:now}}]` applied to both module and lesson. One source of truth used by list, get, prev/next, files, progress and learning. |","-| FR-19 | UI | Status Chip (grey/blue+date/green). Manager view = no visibility filter. |","-| FR-20 | UI, CFG | `courseTabs` entry `content`, all roles. A server component loads via content-service (not via HTTP). |","-| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Progress is computed over **visible** lessons only. \"Continue\" = first visible lesson in (module.position, lesson.position) order without completedAt. |","-| FR-22 | UI, EP | Menu actions map to PATCH /api/modules/:id (status/publishAt/title), DELETE, and reorder (move up/down reuses the reorder endpoint). |","-| FR-23 | EP, SVC, UI | `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder` with the full tree. Server validates that the set of module ids == the course's modules and the set of lesson ids == all the course's lessons (no foreign ids, no omissions), then rewrites positions + moduleId in one transaction. New dep `@dnd-kit/sortable`. |","-| FR-24 | UI | Type-to-confirm Dialog. Can ConfirmDialog be extended or does it need a local Dialog? Server DELETE cascades regardless. |","-| FR-25 | UI | Page `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` (manage). Client editor with Tabs Write/Preview (Preview = MarkdownView). Toolbar inserts text at the selection. |","-| FR-26 | UI | Image insert → FileUpload context `lesson` → `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. The file must then be attached (FR-17) or it gets purged. **Design:** on save, parse `/api/files/<id>` refs in markdown and attach them as context=lesson (not as LessonAttachment rows), or require explicit attach. |","-| FR-27 | EP, UI | PATCH /api/lessons/:id with `attachments: [{fileId}]` (order = position) and `links: [{title,url}]`. Replace-all semantics in a transaction. |","-| FR-28 | UI, VAL | Schedule: MUI X DateTimePicker (check the MUI X pickers package is installed and allowed, NFR-7). Convert school-tz → UTC on the client or server (NFR-10). Server rejects `publishAt <= now`. |","-| FR-29 | UI | Client timer + dirty flag, `beforeunload` + in-app navigation guard. PATCH with `status` untouched. |","-| FR-30 | SVC | `src/lib/video.ts` `parseVideoUrl(url) → {provider,id}|null`, shared by validator and renderer. Pure, unit test. |","-| FR-31 | UI | `src/components/MarkdownView/`. rehype-sanitize schema: default + `img.src` restricted to `/`-relative (same origin). New deps react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize. Client or server component is fine (react-markdown works in RSC). |","-| FR-32 | UI, SVC | Viewer page. Prev/next computed over the ordered visible-lesson list of the course (service helper reusing FR-18). |","-| FR-33 | EP, SVC, AUTH | First view: an upsert in the viewer page's server load for STUDENT with ACTIVE enrollment (set `firstViewedAt` only on create). `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress {completed}` sets/clears completedAt. Reject PARENT/TEACHER with FORBIDDEN, and a non-visible lesson → NOT_FOUND. |","-| FR-34 | EP, UI | `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` (assertCanManageCourse): ACTIVE enrollments left-joined with progress. 2 queries. |","-| FR-35 | EP, UI, CFG | `studentTabs` entry `learning`, `GET /api/students/:id/learning` (assertCanViewStudent). Per course of ACTIVE enrollments: visible lesson count, completed count, max(updatedAt/completedAt). Avoid per-course N+1 (group queries). |","-| FR-36 | UI, AUTH | Parent read-only: hide the button **and** the server rejects (FR-33). |","-| FR-37 | AUTH | Reuse `assertCanViewCourse` unchanged. |","-| FR-38 | CFG, SVC | `content.lesson_published` in NOTIFICATION_TYPES. Fire only on the transition to visible via \"Publish now\" (lesson PUBLISHED **and** module currently visible). Recipients = ACTIVE enrolled students, using notify() with a batch/loop. |","-| FR-39 | UI | Tooltip only. No job (consistent with FR-18). |","-| FR-40 | UI, SVC | Logo FileUpload, context `logo`, size cap 2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg. On settings save, set FileObject.contextId (see FR-12 caveat) and logoUrl = `/api/files/<id>`. Fix the BaseLayout absolute URL (B4). |","-| FR-41 | VAL, EP | Allowlist is context-aware: `svg` is only in `logo`. file-type can't sniff SVG (it's text), so validate that it's text and contains `<svg`. On GET, add `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` when mime is image/svg+xml. |","-| FR-42 | UI | New `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` (requireRole ADMIN) + a nav entry. LOW confidence, accepted default. |","-| FR-43 | EP | 15 endpoints total (files ×3, modules ×4 incl. POST lessons, lessons ×3, reorder, progress ×2, learning). Use the existing response/error envelope and `{error:{code,message}}`. |","-| FR-44 | EP, AUTH | STUDENT/PARENT get NOT_FOUND (not FORBIDDEN) for hidden lessons. Same rule for files under FR-10. |","-| FR-45 | SVC | Layout: `src/server/content/content-service.ts`, `src/server/files/{access,service,purge,validate}.ts`, `src/server/storage.ts`. Thin routes. |","-| FR-46 | SVC | `audit()` when actor ≠ lesson/module creator. Needs a `createdById` on Module/Lesson, or always audit ADMIN mutations. Check whether FR-15's exact schema includes a creator field. If not, audit when the actor is ADMIN. |","-| FR-47 | DM (seed) | Extend `prisma/seed.ts`. Add `prisma/seed-assets/*.pdf` copied into UPLOAD_DIR by the seed via `saveFile`. Sam = the existing seeded student. |","-| FR-48 | TEST | Unit: sanitizer, video parser, visibility, registry dispatch, sniff rules (FR-6). Integration: upload→attach→download + purge (a temp UPLOAD_DIR). One Playwright e2e. |","-| NFR-1 | AUTH | No files under `public/`, and every read goes through FR-9. Watch B1: making `/api/files/` public must not skip the registry. |","-| NFR-2 | UI | rehype-sanitize strips `javascript:`. Also apply link `href` protocol check in the `a` mapper (defence in depth). Unit/e2e with `[x](javascript:alert(1))`. |","-| NFR-3 | EP | B3. Return 429 RATE_LIMITED with `Retry-After`. Note the ceiling: per-process. |","-| NFR-4 | SVC | Content tab: ≤4 queries (modules with lessons ordered + `_count.attachments` + caller progress `where lessonId in`). Add DB indexes (FR-15). |","-| NFR-5 | SVC | Stream → hash → disk, with the byte cap during the stream. See the FR-3 multipart trade-off. Write to a temp name, then rename on success (no partial files under the final key). |","-| NFR-6 | UI | iframe `title`, alt-text warning, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels. |","-| NFR-7 | UI | Dev must use mui-mcp docs before UI work. Blocker if unreachable. Includes the DateTimePicker (FR-28) package choice. |","-| NFR-8 | AUTH | Every route/page calls the assert helpers. Especially relevant for POST/DELETE /api/files if B1 is applied. |","-| NFR-9 | CFG | 5 new deps only. No renames. lint/typecheck/test green. |","-| NFR-10 | UI, SVC | UTC in the DB. Display via SchoolSettings.timezone (reuse the existing tz formatting helper if present). |","-| NFR-11 | — | No storage interface/S3 abstraction. No content copy. |","-| NFR-12 | CFG | Use the logger instead of console.log. Add `UPLOAD_DIR`, `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` to `.env.example` and the env schema. |","+| FR-1 | DM | New enums `SubmissionType`, `AssignmentStatus`, `SubmissionStatus`. Do not reuse `ContentStatus`, because the PRD names a new enum (the values happen to match, and B5 relies on that). |","+| FR-2 | DM | `Assignment` with `allowExtraCredit`, `notifiedAt?`, `archivedAt?`, `rubricId String? @unique`, Course relation with Cascade, and `@@index([courseId, dueAt])`. Add the back-relation `assignments Assignment[]` on Course. |","+| FR-3 | DM | `AssignmentAttachment` (join to FileObject, back-relation per B3), `Rubric`, `RubricCriterion` (`maxPoints Decimal(6,2)`, `order Int`, `levels Json`). A 1:1 Rubric↔Assignment via `rubricId @unique` means a rubric is never shared, so delete it together with the assignment. |","+| FR-4 | DM | `Submission @@unique([assignmentId, studentId])`, which means one row per student. Attempts live in `SubmissionHistory`. The Decimal fields are `rawScore`, `penaltyPercent` and `finalScore`. `rubricScores Json`. `SubmissionFile` join, back-relation per B3. `SubmissionHistory.fileIds String[]` has no FK, so the files must not be purged (B1). |","+| FR-5 | DM | `GradeExemption @@id([assignmentId, studentId])`. Cascade on assignment delete. |","+| FR-6 | DM | `AssignmentReminder @@unique([assignmentId, studentId, kind])`. `kind` is a String ('due_soon' / 'missing'). Insert with `createMany({skipDuplicates:true})`, or catch P2002, and send only for the rows actually inserted (idempotent under concurrent dispatchers). |","+| FR-7 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`, shared by client forms and route handlers. Cross-field rules (`lateCutoffAt > dueAt`, rubric sum) use `.superRefine`. Decimal inputs come in as number/string and the service converts them to `Prisma.Decimal` (NFR-1). |","+| FR-8 | SVC, DM | Offline marker: `attemptNumber = 0`, `text = null`, no files, `submittedAt = gradedAt`. **Edge case for design:** a student may later submit online against an offline-graded row (`status = SUBMITTED`, unique row). Recommend allowing it and treating it as a resubmission (move the attempt-0 grade into history and clear the grade), unless it is already RETURNED. |"," ","-## Open design decisions for `arch-design-system`","+### Assignment authoring (teacher)"," ","-1. **B1 public files path**: either add `/api/files/` to PUBLIC_API_PATHS with explicit `requireUser()` on POST/DELETE (recommended), or special-case GET in middleware.","-2. **Logo orphan purge (FR-12 × FR-40)**: give logo files a non-null `contextId` on save, or they get deleted after 24h.","-3. **Inline markdown images (FR-26 × FR-12)**: attach images referenced in `contentMarkdown` on save, or they get purged.","-4. **Multipart vs streaming (FR-3 × NFR-5)**: `formData()` + a Content-Length pre-check, or a hand-rolled stream parser. No multipart dep is allowed.","-5. **Detach semantics (FR-17/FR-27)**: removing an attachment either nulls contextId (purged later) or deletes immediately.","-6. **Audit trigger (FR-46)**: either add a creator field or audit all ADMIN mutations on content.","-7. **SVG validation (FR-41)**: text sniff for `<svg`, logo context only, CSP header on serve.","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|---|---|---|","+| FR-9 | UI | `/courses/[courseId]/assignments/new` and an edit route (`[assignmentId]/edit`). MUI DateTimePicker (MUI X pickers, same version-alignment risk as D2) in the school timezone. It depends on D1 (FileUpload, MarkdownEditor). |","+| FR-10 | SVC | `nextTeachingDayDueAt(now, tz)`: a pure helper next to `schoolNow` in `src/lib/dates.ts`. Computed server-side and passed as a default prop (NFR-2). |","+| FR-11 | UI, VAL | The rubric builder uses `@dnd-kit/sortable`, which is already installed, for reorder. The rubric-sum check is in the Zod schema (shared), using Decimal sum, so the server rejects with VALIDATION_ERROR. The exact message string is required. |","+| FR-12 | UI, VAL | The status comes from the button. SCHEDULED requires `availableFrom > serverNow`, checked in the service, not only in Zod (Zod has no server clock guarantee). |","+| FR-13 | SVC | `isAssignmentVisible(a, now) = !archivedAt && isVisible({status, publishAt: availableFrom}, now)`. Use it in **every** student/parent read path, the file resolver, submission rules and reminders. It is the single source of truth. |","+| FR-14 | UI | Show the warning when the assignment is published and `submissionCount > 0`, and the dueAt or maxPoints changes. No recalculation happens on the server. Keep a `maxPointsChangedAt` banner? Simplest is a client-side banner on save success. **Design should pick one, and not add a column unless needed.** |","+| FR-15 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/duplicate {courseIds}`. Check `assertCanManageCourse` for **each** target. Make it one transaction per target. Copy the rubric and criteria as new rows (1:1), and copy the attachment bytes per B2. Status DRAFT, `notifiedAt` null. LOW confidence default: identical dueAt plus the availableFrom/lateCutoffAt offsets. |","+","+### Lists and navigation","+","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|---|---|---|","+| FR-16 | CFG | Append `{key:'assignments', href:/courses/:id/assignments, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. |","+| FR-17 | UI, EP | The teacher table depends on D2 (DataTable compile break). The counts come from FR-48's manager shape using `groupBy` aggregates, not N+1 queries. |","+| FR-18 | UI, AUTH | Student groups: Upcoming / Past due (missing) / Submitted / Returned. A parent viewing a course needs a child context: use `?studentId=`, validated against `ParentStudentLink` **and** active enrollment in this course. Default to the only linked child enrolled. |","+| FR-19 | UI | Assignment page: sanitised Markdown (D1 MarkdownView), late-policy summary, rubric, and a countdown under 48 h. Compute the countdown client-side from a server-provided `serverNow` offset, so a skewed client clock doesn't show a wrong countdown. It is display-only (NFR-2). |","+| FR-20 | UI | The panel switches on submissionType. Draft autosave to `localStorage` keyed by `assignmentId:userId`. Clear it after a successful submit. |","+| FR-21 | UI | Reuse `ConfirmDialog`. |","+| FR-25 | UI | Receipt formatted with `formatInSchoolTz(submittedAt, \"EEE d MMM yyyy, HH:mm\", tz)` plus the attempt number. |","+| FR-26 | UI, AUTH | Grading fields appear only when `status = RETURNED` (FR-27). |","+| FR-27 | AUTH, SVC | **Response-shaping boundary.** One serializer `toStudentSubmission(sub)` removes `rawScore/penaltyPercent/finalScore/feedback/rubricScores/gradedAt/gradedById` unless the status is RETURNED. Every student/parent path uses it: FR-48, FR-50, FR-55, FR-57, FR-58 when the viewer is the student or parent. This covers NFR-4. |","+| FR-37 | UI, EP | `/assignments` STUDENT: 4 tabs plus a course filter, across ACTIVE enrollments. Missing = visible, not archived, `dueAt < now`, no submission, not exempt, `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (FR-60). Define one Prisma `where` builder `missingFilter(now)` and share it with the reminders (FR-43/45) and the counts. |","+| FR-38 | UI, AUTH | PARENT: a child selector using linked students only. The server validates `studentId` against `ParentStudentLink`. The view is read-only, so the submit panel is not rendered **and** the API rejects it (FR-53 is STUDENT-only). |","+| FR-39 | UI, EP | TEACHER \"To grade\": `status = SUBMITTED AND gradedAt IS NULL` in courses where `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`, ordered by `submittedAt asc`. ADMIN gets the same list across all courses (clarification default). |","+| FR-40 | CFG | One nav entry (B13). |","+| FR-41 | CFG, UI | studentTabs entry plus a page. It is invisible until a tab bar exists (blocker 5). Out of scope to build one here: do not add a tab-bar renderer just for this (NFR-15 scope / YAGNI), and surface it as a known gap. |","+","+### Submission (student)","+","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|---|---|---|","+| FR-22 | SVC, AUTH | Rule order: (1) the assignment is visible and not archived; (2) `role = STUDENT` and ACTIVE-enrolled; (3) not exempt; (4) `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (implied); (5) deadline: `now ≤ dueAt`, or `allowLate && (!lateCutoffAt || now ≤ lateCutoffAt)`. The exact error string is required. `now = new Date()` on the server only (NFR-2). |","+| FR-23 | SVC, TEST | Pure `lateDays(submittedAt, dueAt) = ceil((s − d) / 86_400_000)` for `s > d`, else 0. Use UTC milliseconds, so DST cannot affect it (NFR-9: a 24 h wall day across DST is 23/25 h of real time, and the PRD defines late days in 24 h units). Exactly 24 h gives 1. This is unit-test territory (NFR-14). |","+| FR-24 | SVC, DM | In one transaction: if a row exists, require `status = SUBMITTED` (RETURNED gives a VALIDATION/CONFLICT error), insert `SubmissionHistory` from the current row, `attemptNumber++`, clear the grade fields, replace the `SubmissionFile` rows, and attach the new files. Do not detach the old files (B1). Concurrency: two concurrent first submits hit the unique key. Catch P2002 and retry as a resubmit, or `upsert`. |","+| FR-53 | EP, VAL, AUTH | `POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions {text?, fileIds[]}`. Validation: `fileIds.length ≤ maxFileCount`; the content matches submissionType (text required for ONLINE_TEXT, files for FILE_UPLOAD, at least one for TEXT_AND_FILE); each file is `ownerId = me`, `context = 'submission'` and unattached, or already on this submission (B1). |","+","+### Grading (teacher)","+","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|---|---|---|","+| FR-28 | UI, EP | The left panel is fed by FR-54. Status chip derivation is a pure function: Exempt > Returned > Graded > Late > Submitted > Not submitted. Shared by the server (FR-54) and tests. |","+| FR-29 | UI | `<img>`/`<iframe src=\"/api/files/:id?inline=1\">`. **CSP check for design:** confirm that `next.config.js` `frame-src`/`img-src` allow `'self'`. The CSP `script-src` issue is blocker 4. The history dropdown reads FR-55 (manager-only history). |","+| FR-30 | UI, SVC | Rubric ToggleButtonGroup with an auto-sum. Penalty prefill `min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)`. The live final score uses decimal.js on the client too, so the preview and server values agree (NFR-1). The prefill is display-only. The server stores what is submitted, after FR-36 validation. |","+| FR-31 | SVC, TEST | `finalScore = raw × (1 − p/100)`, computed with `Decimal`, `toDecimalPlaces(2, ROUND_HALF_UP)`. One pure function in the service, unit-tested (18 at 20 % = 14.40). |","+| FR-32 | EP, SVC, NOTIF | \"Save\" = `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade`. \"Save & return\" = the same call with `{return:true}`, or grade followed by return. **Design should pick a single round trip.** The bulk route is `POST /api/assignments/:id/return {submissionIds?}`, with the default `gradedAt not null AND status ≠ RETURNED`. Each return sets RETURNED and returnedAt, fires FR-44, and writes an audit (FR-59). |","+| FR-33 | UI | A keydown listener on the grading page. Ignore J/K when `event.target` is an input, textarea or contenteditable. Ctrl/Cmd+Enter always works. Accessibility: show the shortcuts in a help hint (NFR-17). |","+| FR-34 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}`. The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Reject it if a submission already exists (grade that one instead). Creates the FR-8 row with the grade fields set, penalty 0, and an audit row. |","+| FR-35 | EP, SVC | `PUT/DELETE /api/assignments/:id/exemptions/:studentId`. Idempotent (`upsert` / `deleteMany`). Writes an audit row. Its effects come through `missingFilter` and the FR-22 rule. A PRD-11 exclusion flag = the GradeExemption row itself, so no extra column. |","+| FR-36 | VAL, SVC | Server-side, Decimal-based: `0 ≤ raw ≤ maxPoints` (×1.2 if allowExtraCredit). Each rubric score `0 ≤ points ≤ criterion.maxPoints` (extra credit is raw-only, per the clarification), and each `criterionId` belongs to this rubric. `0 ≤ penalty ≤ 100`. With a rubric, should raw equal the sum of the rubric points? The PRD says it auto-sums but stays overridable only via the penalty. **Recommend the server enforces raw = Σ rubric points when rubricScores are given.** |","+| FR-54 | EP | `GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions` (manage). LEFT JOIN of ACTIVE enrollments × submissions × exemptions. Paginate per NFR-7, but grading needs all students for J/K: allow `pageSize` up to 100 and document the limit. |","+| FR-55 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/submissions/:id`: the submitter, linked parents or course managers. History only for managers. Grade fields go through the FR-27 serializer for the student and parent. Also needed by NFR-3 prefetch. |","+| FR-56 | EP, SVC | Sets `gradedById`, `gradedAt` and the computed `finalScore`. Does not change status (it stays SUBMITTED until return). Writes an audit row. |","+| FR-59 | SVC | `audit()` on grade, return (one row per submission, or one bulk row with the ids; **design should pick**), exempt/unexempt and offline grade. |","+","+### Assignment API","+","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|---|---|---|","+| FR-48 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/courses/:id/assignments`. Two response shapes depending on `canSeeDrafts`. Students and parents get FR-13-visible, non-archived assignments plus their own submission state (via the FR-27 serializer). |","+| FR-49 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/courses/:id/assignments`. One transaction: rubric and criteria, assignment, attachments (`attachFiles` with `'assignment'`, contextId = assignment.id), and on PUBLISHED the FR-42 notify after commit. |","+| FR-50 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/assignments/:id`. A non-manager on an invisible/archived assignment gets NOT_FOUND, not FORBIDDEN, so existence is not leaked. Includes `serverNow` for FR-19. |","+| FR-51 | EP, SVC | PATCH: re-validate the rubric sum against maxPoints. Diff the attachments (detach the removed ones, which are then purged after 24 h per B1; that is fine for assignment attachments). DRAFT→PUBLISHED triggers FR-42. DELETE: hard delete if there are 0 submissions (cascade; the attachment files are detached first so the purge reclaims them), else set `archivedAt`. |","+| FR-52 | AUTH, SVC | Covered by `isAssignmentVisible` (FR-13), which includes `!archivedAt`. One check, applied everywhere. LOW confidence default. |","+| FR-57 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab=`. Role switch: STUDENT gets its own data; PARENT requires a linked `studentId`; TEACHER/ADMIN get To grade. `tab ∈ upcoming/missing/submitted/returned`. |","+| FR-58 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/students/:id/assignments` → `assertCanViewStudent`, then the same query as the FR-57 student view, built with a shared service function. A student or parent viewer gets the FR-27 serializer. Teachers and admins see grades? The PRD says \"same per-student data\", so **recommend the same serializer for all non-managers and full fields for the student's course managers.** Design should confirm. |","+","+### Notifications and maintenance","+","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|---|---|---|","+| FR-42 | NOTIF, SVC | Exactly once: `UPDATE assignment SET notifiedAt = now WHERE id = ? AND notifiedAt IS NULL` (`updateMany`, count = 1 → send). Triggered on publish (FR-49/51), and for SCHEDULED assignments in the student list read path (FR-48/57) when visible and `notifiedAt` is null. **A side effect on GET:** keep it fire-and-forget after the response data is built, and never fail the read. Design may also add it to `sendDueReminders` as a safety net, but must not do both without the atomic guard (the guard makes both safe). |","+| FR-43 | JOB, NOTIF | `sendDueReminders(now)` in `src/server/assignments/reminders.ts`, called on every dispatcher call (B8). The window is `dueAt − 24h ≤ now < dueAt`. Targets: ACTIVE-enrolled, no submission, not exempt, visible, not archived, not NO_SUBMISSION. Idempotent via FR-6. Bound the query (only assignments with `dueAt` in [now, now+24h]). |","+| FR-44 | NOTIF | On return: `notifyStudentAndParents` with a body like `\"{course}: {title} — {finalScore}/{maxPoints}\"`. Bulk return sends one notify per student. |","+| FR-45 | JOB, NOTIF | In the same pass: `now ≥ dueAt + 24h`, with the `missingFilter` targets. Parents only (`notify` to the linked parent ids). FR-6 kind 'missing'. Bound the query to avoid scanning all history, e.g. `dueAt` in [now − 8 d, now − 24 h], with a `ponytail:` note on that window. |","+| FR-46 | CFG | Four keys (B9). |","+| FR-47 | AUTH | `assignmentResolver`: load the assignment and course, then `assertCanViewCourse`, then `canSeeDrafts \\|\\| isAssignmentVisible`. `submissionResolver`: load the submission; allow the submitting student, a linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`) or `canSeeDrafts(course)` (managers/ADMIN). Deny everyone else, including other students (NFR-4, AC-10). Integration test needed. |","+","+### Seed","+","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|---|---|---|","+| FR-60 | SVC | Exclude NO_SUBMISSION in `missingFilter` and the reminder targets. The submission panel is hidden and FR-53 rejects. LOW confidence default. |","+| FR-61 | SEED | Idempotent: look up the courses by code and skip if they are missing. Upsert the assignments by `(courseId, title)`. Seed Decimal scores via strings. Seeded attachments/files are not required, so skip byte storage. |","+","+### Non-functional","+","+| Req | Concern | Notes |","+|---|---|---|","+| NFR-1 | SVC, VAL | Decimal end to end: Prisma `Decimal(6,2)` columns, `Prisma.Decimal` in the service, decimal.js in the client preview. Serialize Decimals in API responses as **strings**, to avoid float loss in JSON. Design must state this convention for api-contracts. |","+| NFR-2 | SVC | Every deadline, visibility or reminder check uses `new Date()` on the server. There is no client timestamp field in any request schema. |","+| NFR-3 | UI, EP | Prefetch the next and previous `GET /api/submissions/:id` into a client cache keyed by id (a plain `Map` in the grading page; no data-fetching library added). The <300 ms target is a client switch from cache. |","+| NFR-4 | AUTH | Enforced at three boundaries: the FR-27 serializer, the FR-47 file resolvers, and query scoping (a student only ever queries `studentId = me`). |","+| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every route: `requireUser`/`requireRole`, then assertCan*. Every page: `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`. |","+| NFR-6 | UI | MUI 9.5.0 + MUI X only, with mui-mcp lookups before use. Components needed: List, Chip, ToggleButtonGroup, Dialog, Tabs, DataGrid (D2), DateTimePicker, Autocomplete, Snackbar. Hard blocker if mui-mcp is unreachable (blocker 8). |","+| NFR-7 | EP | Thin handlers. `{data}` / paginated / `{error}` envelopes via the http.ts helpers. |","+| NFR-8 | CFG | `src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts`, plus `reminders.ts` and pure `scoring.ts` (lateDays, penalty, finalScore, chip status) for unit tests. Validators in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`. |","+| NFR-9 | SVC, TEST | Store UTC. Display via formatInSchoolTz. Late days in UTC ms (FR-23). The FR-10 default uses `fromZonedTime`. |","+| NFR-10 | UI | react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize are installed, with MUI component mapping (D1). |","+| NFR-11 | — | Reuse list: B1–B10, B15. |","+| NFR-12 | — | Use the logger, never console.log. |","+| NFR-13 | TEST, CFG | Blocker 3: fix the `vitest.config.ts` import to `'vitest/config'` (a one-line fix, in scope because NFR-13 requires a working `npm test`). |","+| NFR-14 | TEST | Unit: scoring.ts. Integration: resubmit history, return, reminder idempotency, exemption vs missing, and the file resolvers (AC-10). E2E: the full flow plus the parent missing list (needs bypassCSP, blocker 4). |","+| NFR-15 | — | No gradebook, peer review, group work or annotation. FR-35 stores the exemption only, and PRD-11 consumes it. |","+| NFR-16 | UI | Two-minute publish: sensible defaults (FR-10 due date, max points 100?, submissionType FILE_UPLOAD?). **Design should set the form defaults.** 30-submission keyboard grading via FR-33 + NFR-3. |","+| NFR-17 | UI | Labelled inputs and keyboard-operable controls: the ToggleButtonGroup and the J/K help hint. |","+","+## Decisions arch-design-system must make (answers to the intake blockers)","+","+| # | Blocker / gap | Recommendation |","+|---|---|---|","+| D1 | Blocker 1: PRD-08 UI components are missing. | Build the **minimum** shared components in this ticket: `src/components/MarkdownView` (react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, mapped to MUI), `src/components/MarkdownEditor` (MUI TextField multiline + a Write/Preview Tabs toggle using MarkdownView; no new editor dependency), `src/components/FileUpload` (input type=file → `POST /api/files` with the context field, list with remove, `maxFiles` prop) and `FileList` (links to `/api/files/:id`). Shape them so PRD-08 can adopt them later. Do not build PRD-08's remaining scope. |","+| D2 | Blocker 2: the MUI X DataGrid compile break. | Preferred: align `@mui/x-*` versions in package.json/lockfile (it also unblocks the DateTimePicker from `@mui/x-date-pickers`, if that package shares the internals). Fallback for FR-17: an MUI `Table`, which needs no DataGrid. **Check whether `@mui/x-date-pickers` is installed and affected**, because FR-9 needs it. |","+| D3 | Blockers 3/4: vitest import and CSP. | vitest: one-line import fix. CSP: keep `bypassCSP` in Playwright as before. A CSP fix is outside the PRD scope (NFR-15). Note the FR-29 iframe/img `'self'` dependency. |","+| D4 | Blocker 5: the studentTabs renderer. | Register the tab and build the page. Do not build a tab bar. Report it as a known gap. |","+| D5 | Decimal JSON serialization | Decimal fields are strings in API responses (NFR-1). |","+| D6 | The \"Save & return\" round trip | `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade` with an optional `return: true` gives one transaction. |","+| D7 | Rubric raw score | When rubricScores are present, the server sets or enforces `rawScore = Σ points`. |","+| D8 | Teacher/admin view of FR-58 grade fields | Course managers get full fields. Other viewers get the FR-27 serializer. |","+| D9 | Offline-graded row followed by an online submit | Treat it as a resubmission while it is not RETURNED. |","+| D10 | Missing-reminder query window | Bound it (e.g. dueAt within the last 8 days), marked with a `ponytail:` note. |","+","+## Shared pure functions (single source of truth; unit-test targets)","+","+`isAssignmentVisible`, `missingFilter(now)` (Prisma where), `lateDays`, `defaultPenalty`, `computeFinalScore`, `rubricTotal`, `submissionChipStatus`, `nextTeachingDayDueAt`, `toStudentSubmission` (serializer). Each of these is used by two or more call sites listed above. Keeping one copy of each prevents the drift that leads to privacy and correctness bugs (NFR-1, NFR-4)."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-8\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T06:00:00Z), PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008).\nIt has 48 FRs and 12 NFRs (60 requirements) at 93% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers, and they must be surfaced in `system-design.md` Overview.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are still **SH-7** leftovers at the time of writing. Downstream sub-tasks own them and must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-8 input.\n\n## Brownfield findings verified on disk (arch-research-reqs)\n\n| # | Finding | Evidence | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | **Middleware blocks unauthenticated `/api/files/:id`.** `src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for any `/api/*` not matched by `isPublicPath()`. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is `['/api/health','/api/auth/','/api/internal/']`. | middleware.ts L36-40, public-routes.ts L7 | FR-10's public `logo` context cannot work (login page, emails) unless `/api/files/` is made public. **Recommended:** add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. Then the GET handler resolves the session itself (optional user → access registry), and POST/DELETE **must** call `requireUser()` explicitly, because middleware no longer guards them. This is a security-critical design point (NFR-1, NFR-8). |\n| B2 | Daily hook exists: `lastPurgeAt` + `purgeOldNotifications()` in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` L11-31. | grep | FR-12 adds a second call in the same `if` block. No new scheduler. |\n| B3 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) → {ok, retryAfterMs}` is a per-process sliding window. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-3: `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)`. |\n| B4 | `logoUrl` consumers: `BaseLayout.tsx` L28 uses `<Img src={school.logoUrl}>` raw, and `render.ts` already passes `appUrl`. | grep | FR-40 stores a relative `/api/files/<id>`, so BaseLayout must prefix `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. Combined with B1, that makes the logo fetchable from mail clients. |\n| B5 | No `.gitignore` at the repo root. | `ls` | Create one with `uploads/` (plus `node_modules`, `.next`, `.env` if missing). |\n| B6 | No `src/server/files/` and no content code. | ls | Confirms greenfield. |\n| B7 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are arrays of `CourseTab`/`StudentTab` in `src/config/`. | grep | FR-20 / FR-35 append one entry each. |\n| B8 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object in `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, and `ACADEMIC` is a valid category. | grep | FR-38 adds one key. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = server service/module · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = background/maintenance · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = config/env/registry · **TEST**\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | `FileObject` + `@@index([context, contextId])`, unique `storageKey`. `context` is a plain String (registry keys), not an enum, so new contexts need no migration. One migration together with FR-15. |\n| FR-2 | SVC, CFG | `src/server/storage.ts`: `saveFile`/`readFile`/`deleteFile`. Resolve paths with `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR, key)` and assert they stay under UPLOAD_DIR (traversal guard). Add env `UPLOAD_DIR` to the env schema. Single local-disk impl, no interface (NFR-11). |\n| FR-3 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/files` multipart. Use `request.formData()`? It buffers, which conflicts with NFR-5. Use `busboy`-free streaming via `req.body` + the Web `Request` multipart parser? **Design must pick.** Next.js route handlers expose `request.body` (a ReadableStream), but a multipart parser isn't in the allowed deps. Practical option: `formData()` is acceptable only if the size cap is pre-checked via `Content-Length` (≤ MAX_UPLOAD_MB + overhead) before parsing, then `File.stream()` → disk with sha256. Flag as a NFR-5 trade-off for design. |\n| FR-4 | VAL, CFG | `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` env (default 25). Enforce with a byte counter in the write stream (abort and unlink the partial file), plus an early `Content-Length` reject. Logo override: 2 MB (FR-40). Make the limit per-context: `{ logo: 2 }`, default env. |\n| FR-5 | VAL | Extension allowlist + `fileTypeFromBuffer` on the first ~4100 bytes (peek before or while writing). New dep `file-type` (ESM-only, so check the Next server bundling). |\n| FR-6 | VAL | Rule table: txt/csv → sniff must be `undefined`. docx/xlsx/pptx → sniff ∈ {zip, matching OOXML mime}. zip → zip. Others → sniff ext must match the declared ext (jpg≡jpeg). Pure function, unit-testable (FR-48). |\n| FR-7 | VAL | `sanitizeFilename()`: strip `/ \\ ` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trim, and cap at 150 while preserving the extension. Pure function and unit test. |\n| FR-8 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/files/:id`: registry check **before** `readFile`. Headers: stored mime, `nosniff`, `attachment; filename*=UTF-8''…`, and `inline` only if `?inline=1` and mime is image/* or application/pdf. Stream via `Readable.toWeb(fs.createReadStream)`. |\n| FR-9 | SVC, AUTH, CFG | `src/server/files/access.ts`: a `Map<string, resolver>`. Default: owner or ADMIN. Return **404** for denied (don't leak existence) and 401 for unauthenticated non-public. Contexts are registered via side-effect import, so the GET handler must import the module that registers `lesson`/`logo` (avoid a lazy-registration bug). |\n| FR-10 | AUTH | `lesson` resolver: load lesson+module+course, then `assertCanViewCourse` + visibility rule (FR-18) for STUDENT/PARENT, while managers see drafts. `logo`: `() => true` incl. `user=null`. Depends on B1. Unattached files (contextId null) fall to the owner/ADMIN check even within the 'lesson' context, which lets editor previews work before attach. |\n| FR-11 | EP, AUTH | `DELETE /api/files/:id`: owner/ADMIN, `contextId === null`, else CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR. Delete the row, then the bytes (log on bytes failure, since orphan bytes are harmless). Audit when ADMIN deletes another user's file (FR-46). |\n| FR-12 | JOB | `purgeOrphanFiles()` in `src/server/files/purge.ts`, hooked at B2. Batch `findMany` where contextId null and createdAt < now-24h, delete bytes then rows. **Caveat:** the logo is \"attached\" how? FR-40 stores a URL in logoUrl but contextId stays null, so the logo gets purged after 24h. **Design must set `contextId` for logo** (e.g. the SchoolSettings id/`'school'`) when settings are saved. |\n| FR-13 | UI | `src/components/FileUpload/`. XHR (not fetch) for `upload.onprogress`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`/`onChange` (FileObject summaries), and optional reorder (FR-27). MUI only (NFR-7). |\n| FR-14 | UI | `src/components/FileList/`: read-only list, links `/api/files/:id`. |\n| FR-15 | DM | `ContentStatus` enum, Module(courseId, title, position, status, publishAt), Lesson(moduleId, title, position, status, publishAt, contentMarkdown, estimatedMinutes, videoUrl, createdById?), LessonAttachment(lessonId, fileId, position), LessonLink(lessonId, title, url, position), and LessonProgress PK [lessonId, studentId]. Cascades: Course→Module→Lesson→Attachment/Link/Progress. Add back-relations on Course/User/StudentProfile. Index `[courseId, position]`, `[moduleId, position]`. Follow the PRD's exact field list. |\n| FR-16 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/content.ts` (Zod), shared by client and server. URL refinements reuse the FR-30 parser for videoUrl. |\n| FR-17 | SVC, AUTH | Inside the PATCH lesson transaction: verify each fileId is (owner==caller or ADMIN) and (contextId null or already == this lessonId), then `updateMany` context/contextId. Removed attachments should be detached (contextId → null), which leaves them purgeable in 24h. Decide explicitly. |\n| FR-18 | SVC | Pure `isVisible(entity, now)` + Prisma `where` fragment `visibleWhere(now)` = `OR[{status:PUBLISHED},{status:SCHEDULED, publishAt:{lte:now}}]` applied to both module and lesson. One source of truth used by list, get, prev/next, files, progress and learning. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Status Chip (grey/blue+date/green). Manager view = no visibility filter. |\n| FR-20 | UI, CFG | `courseTabs` entry `content`, all roles. A server component loads via content-service (not via HTTP). |\n| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Progress is computed over **visible** lessons only. \"Continue\" = first visible lesson in (module.position, lesson.position) order without completedAt. |\n| FR-22 | UI, EP | Menu actions map to PATCH /api/modules/:id (status/publishAt/title), DELETE, and reorder (move up/down reuses the reorder endpoint). |\n| FR-23 | EP, SVC, UI | `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder` with the full tree. Server validates that the set of module ids == the course's modules and the set of lesson ids == all the course's lessons (no foreign ids, no omissions), then rewrites positions + moduleId in one transaction. New dep `@dnd-kit/sortable`. |\n| FR-24 | UI | Type-to-confirm Dialog. Can ConfirmDialog be extended or does it need a local Dialog? Server DELETE cascades regardless. |\n| FR-25 | UI | Page `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` (manage). Client editor with Tabs Write/Preview (Preview = MarkdownView). Toolbar inserts text at the selection. |\n| FR-26 | UI | Image insert → FileUpload context `lesson` → `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. The file must then be attached (FR-17) or it gets purged. **Design:** on save, parse `/api/files/<id>` refs in markdown and attach them as context=lesson (not as LessonAttachment rows), or require explicit attach. |\n| FR-27 | EP, UI | PATCH /api/lessons/:id with `attachments: [{fileId}]` (order = position) and `links: [{title,url}]`. Replace-all semantics in a transaction. |\n| FR-28 | UI, VAL | Schedule: MUI X DateTimePicker (check the MUI X pickers package is installed and allowed, NFR-7). Convert school-tz → UTC on the client or server (NFR-10). Server rejects `publishAt <= now`. |\n| FR-29 | UI | Client timer + dirty flag, `beforeunload` + in-app navigation guard. PATCH with `status` untouched. |\n| FR-30 | SVC | `src/lib/video.ts` `parseVideoUrl(url) → {provider,id}|null`, shared by validator and renderer. Pure, unit test. |\n| FR-31 | UI | `src/components/MarkdownView/`. rehype-sanitize schema: default + `img.src` restricted to `/`-relative (same origin). New deps react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize. Client or server component is fine (react-markdown works in RSC). |\n| FR-32 | UI, SVC | Viewer page. Prev/next computed over the ordered visible-lesson list of the course (service helper reusing FR-18). |\n| FR-33 | EP, SVC, AUTH | First view: an upsert in the viewer page's server load for STUDENT with ACTIVE enrollment (set `firstViewedAt` only on create). `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress {completed}` sets/clears completedAt. Reject PARENT/TEACHER with FORBIDDEN, and a non-visible lesson → NOT_FOUND. |\n| FR-34 | EP, UI | `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` (assertCanManageCourse): ACTIVE enrollments left-joined with progress. 2 queries. |\n| FR-35 | EP, UI, CFG | `studentTabs` entry `learning`, `GET /api/students/:id/learning` (assertCanViewStudent). Per course of ACTIVE enrollments: visible lesson count, completed count, max(updatedAt/completedAt). Avoid per-course N+1 (group queries). |\n| FR-36 | UI, AUTH | Parent read-only: hide the button **and** the server rejects (FR-33). |\n| FR-37 | AUTH | Reuse `assertCanViewCourse` unchanged. |\n| FR-38 | CFG, SVC | `content.lesson_published` in NOTIFICATION_TYPES. Fire only on the transition to visible via \"Publish now\" (lesson PUBLISHED **and** module currently visible). Recipients = ACTIVE enrolled students, using notify() with a batch/loop. |\n| FR-39 | UI | Tooltip only. No job (consistent with FR-18). |\n| FR-40 | UI, SVC | Logo FileUpload, context `logo`, size cap 2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg. On settings save, set FileObject.contextId (see FR-12 caveat) and logoUrl = `/api/files/<id>`. Fix the BaseLayout absolute URL (B4). |\n| FR-41 | VAL, EP | Allowlist is context-aware: `svg` is only in `logo`. file-type can't sniff SVG (it's text), so validate that it's text and contains `<svg`. On GET, add `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` when mime is image/svg+xml. |\n| FR-42 | UI | New `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` (requireRole ADMIN) + a nav entry. LOW confidence, accepted default. |\n| FR-43 | EP | 15 endpoints total (files ×3, modules ×4 incl. POST lessons, lessons ×3, reorder, progress ×2, learning). Use the existing response/error envelope and `{error:{code,message}}`. |\n| FR-44 | EP, AUTH | STUDENT/PARENT get NOT_FOUND (not FORBIDDEN) for hidden lessons. Same rule for files under FR-10. |\n| FR-45 | SVC | Layout: `src/server/content/content-service.ts`, `src/server/files/{access,service,purge,validate}.ts`, `src/server/storage.ts`. Thin routes. |\n| FR-46 | SVC | `audit()` when actor ≠ lesson/module creator. Needs a `createdById` on Module/Lesson, or always audit ADMIN mutations. Check whether FR-15's exact schema includes a creator field. If not, audit when the actor is ADMIN. |\n| FR-47 | DM (seed) | Extend `prisma/seed.ts`. Add `prisma/seed-assets/*.pdf` copied into UPLOAD_DIR by the seed via `saveFile`. Sam = the existing seeded student. |\n| FR-48 | TEST | Unit: sanitizer, video parser, visibility, registry dispatch, sniff rules (FR-6). Integration: upload→attach→download + purge (a temp UPLOAD_DIR). One Playwright e2e. |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH | No files under `public/`, and every read goes through FR-9. Watch B1: making `/api/files/` public must not skip the registry. |\n| NFR-2 | UI | rehype-sanitize strips `javascript:`. Also apply link `href` protocol check in the `a` mapper (defence in depth). Unit/e2e with `[x](javascript:alert(1))`. |\n| NFR-3 | EP | B3. Return 429 RATE_LIMITED with `Retry-After`. Note the ceiling: per-process. |\n| NFR-4 | SVC | Content tab: ≤4 queries (modules with lessons ordered + `_count.attachments` + caller progress `where lessonId in`). Add DB indexes (FR-15). |\n| NFR-5 | SVC | Stream → hash → disk, with the byte cap during the stream. See the FR-3 multipart trade-off. Write to a temp name, then rename on success (no partial files under the final key). |\n| NFR-6 | UI | iframe `title`, alt-text warning, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | Dev must use mui-mcp docs before UI work. Blocker if unreachable. Includes the DateTimePicker (FR-28) package choice. |\n| NFR-8 | AUTH | Every route/page calls the assert helpers. Especially relevant for POST/DELETE /api/files if B1 is applied. |\n| NFR-9 | CFG | 5 new deps only. No renames. lint/typecheck/test green. |\n| NFR-10 | UI, SVC | UTC in the DB. Display via SchoolSettings.timezone (reuse the existing tz formatting helper if present). |\n| NFR-11 | — | No storage interface/S3 abstraction. No content copy. |\n| NFR-12 | CFG | Use the logger instead of console.log. Add `UPLOAD_DIR`, `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` to `.env.example` and the env schema. |\n\n## Open design decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **B1 public files path**: either add `/api/files/` to PUBLIC_API_PATHS with explicit `requireUser()` on POST/DELETE (recommended), or special-case GET in middleware.\n2. **Logo orphan purge (FR-12 × FR-40)**: give logo files a non-null `contextId` on save, or they get deleted after 24h.\n3. **Inline markdown images (FR-26 × FR-12)**: attach images referenced in `contentMarkdown` on save, or they get purged.\n4. **Multipart vs streaming (FR-3 × NFR-5)**: `formData()` + a Content-Length pre-check, or a hand-rolled stream parser. No multipart dep is allowed.\n5. **Detach semantics (FR-17/FR-27)**: removing an attachment either nulls contextId (purged later) or deletes immediately.\n6. **Audit trigger (FR-46)**: either add a creator field or audit all ADMIN mutations on content.\n7. **SVG validation (FR-41)**: text sniff for `<svg`, logo context only, CSP header on serve.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013N8tgmiCMZemFpxPGT82Wm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
