{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrvbgesXWUnWdYP7mvmv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1989,"cache_read_input_tokens":51852,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1989,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73285dce-b12a-41d8-b326-53463f575912","uuid":"72097f32-5e6b-4744-b354-b71604cce072","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:01:54.284Z","request_id":"req_011CgrvbgSDwFD6qob5frCCG","thinking_duration_ms":806,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrvbgesXWUnWdYP7mvmv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P3vy6Dj6UomMigkMBT1BtY","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-10\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams (SCH-010). It has 39 FRs and 10 NFRs (49 requirements) at 96% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It flags assumptions on FR-33/34/35/37/38/39. Those are restated in §3 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-9 leftovers** as of this writing (`ticketId: \"SH-9\"`). Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-10 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-10 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child. `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Both throw `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These cover FR-34 and the course part of NFR-5. Attempt-level checks are still new: owner, linked parent, or manager. |\n| B2 | `courseTabs` is a static array of `{key, label, href, roles}`. | src/config/course-tabs.ts | FR-11: add one entry, `{ key: 'quizzes', href: id => /courses/${id}/quizzes, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. |\n| B3 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` and then `sendDueReminders(now)` on every request, each wrapped in its own try/catch + logger. Purges run in a once-per-day block. | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-18/FR-30/FR-35: add `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` and `sendQuizResultsReleased(now)` **on every call**, next to sendDueReminders, each with its own try/catch. |\n| B4 | `sendDueReminders` is idempotent through a unique-key claim row (`AssignmentReminder`, P2002 → skip). | src/server/assignments/reminders.ts | FR-30 AFTER_CLOSE needs a \"sent once\" marker. The simplest option is a nullable `Quiz.resultsNotifiedAt`, claimed with `updateMany({ where: { id, resultsNotifiedAt: null } })` and a count check. That needs no new table. If FR-1's model list must stay exact, a claim table is the alternative. |\n| B5 | `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds})` never throw. Call them after commit. | src/server/notifications/notify.ts | FR-29 → `notify()` to enrolled students. FR-30 → `notifyStudentAndParents`. |\n| B6 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object. New keys need `label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles`. | src/server/notifications/types.ts | FR-29: `quiz.published` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, roles STUDENT). `quiz.results_released` (ACADEMIC, roles STUDENT+PARENT). The PRD doesn't give a default email setting for results_released. Default it to true to match assignment.graded, and flag that choice. |\n| B7 | `audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request})` never throws. | src/server/audit.ts | FR-38 actions: `quizAnswer.grade`, `quiz.regrade`, `quiz.release_results`, `quizAccommodation.update`. |\n| B8 | `grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic. It exports `dec`, `fixed2` and `Decimal` from the Prisma browser runtime. `assignments-service.ts` exports `serializeDecimal` and `getSchoolTimezone`. | src/server/assignments/* | FR-3/FR-22/FR-25 reuse dec/fixed2 (NFR-7). Importing from `@/server/assignments/grading-math` is fine. Only lift it to a shared module if dev-planning wants that. Do not copy it. |\n| B9 | `http.ts` provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `AppError`. The codes include CONFLICT (409). Zod errors become VALIDATION_ERROR. Prisma P2002 becomes CONFLICT. | src/server/http.ts | NFR-6. FR-16's 409 is `AppError('CONFLICT', ...)`. |\n| B10 | The DB is PostgreSQL. The project already uses raw-SQL partial unique indexes in migrations. | prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/migration.sql L77-78 | FR-19 race-safety: `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE status = 'IN_PROGRESS'`, hand-added to the FR-1 migration. Add `@@unique([quizId, studentId, attemptNumber])` too. On P2002 during start, re-read and resume. |\n| B11 | File contexts are registered in `registerBuiltInContexts` (lesson, logo, assignment, submission). `attachFiles` sets context/contextId. | src/server/files/contexts.ts, files-service.ts | FR-39: question images need a `'quiz'` context (contextId = quizId) with a resolver: manager, or a viewer with an IN_PROGRESS or visible attempt. The prompt Markdown references the file URL. |\n| B12 | Courses MATH-7A and ENG-7A are looked up in seed.ts with `findCourse([...])`. The seed already uses `console.log` for skips. | prisma/seed.ts L302, L340 | FR-36 follows that pattern (the seed is exempt from the no-console.log rule in practice). |\n| B13 | Installed: @mui/* 9.5.0 (incl. x-charts, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers), @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + sortable 10.0.0, zod 3.23.8, prisma 5.20, vitest, Playwright + axe. | package.json | FR-7, FR-26 and NFR-8 need **no new dependencies** (NFR-7). |\n| B14 | Shared components are DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast, MarkdownEditor, MarkdownView, FileUpload, StatCard, EmptyState, PageHeader, DateDisplay. | src/components/ | FR-7/12/17/24/26/39 reuse them. |\n| B15 | `toStudentSubmission(dto)` is the precedent for a student-shaped serializer. | assignments-service.ts L199 | NFR-1: add `toStudentQuiz` / `toStudentAttempt` in `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts`, with a unit test asserting the `correct` key is absent. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **VAL** validator · **PURE** pure domain logic · **SVC** service (src/server/quiz/) · **API** route handler · **UI** page/component · **JOB** maintenance pass · **AUTH** access boundary · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **SEED** seed · **CFG** config registry · **TEST**\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | One migration, `add_quizzes`. 5 enums, 5 models. Back-relations on Course (`quizzes`) and User (attempts, accommodations, graded answers). QuizAnswer PK `(attemptId, questionId)` (NFR-2). QuizAccommodation unique `(quizId, studentId)`. Include the partial unique index from B10 in the SQL. Money-like fields (points, scores) are `Decimal(6,2)`, per the assignments precedent. |\n| FR-2 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`, client-safe, shared by the builder UI and the handlers. Use per-type question schemas as a discriminated union on `type`. `availableUntil > availableFrom` and the time-limit cross-field checks use `.superRefine`. |\n| FR-3 | PURE | `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. No Prisma import, so the builder preview and tests can use it. `gradeAnswer(question, response) → { points, flagged }`. Partial-credit formula from FR-3. Use Decimal and round with fixed2. |\n| FR-4 | PURE | Same module. `normalize = s.trim().replace(/\\s+/g,' ')`, with case-folding unless `caseSensitive` is set. A non-match returns `flagged: true` and 0 points. |\n| FR-5 | PURE | ESSAY → `{ points: null, flagged: true }`. `correct` holds the guidance text and is server-only (NFR-1). |\n| FR-6 | UI, AUTH | Server page `/courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit`, protected by assertCanManageCourse. The settings panel uses MUI x-date-pickers. The time-limit vs window check reuses the FR-2 validator on the client. |\n| FR-7 | UI | Sortable question list (@dnd-kit/sortable wrapping MUI items). Per-type editor components. Reorder calls `POST /questions/reorder`. |\n| FR-8 | UI | The points total is derived client-side. Preview mode reuses the player component with a `preview` prop. It gets data from the manager GET (with `correct`) and grades locally with the pure grading.ts. It **never calls the attempt endpoints**, so nothing is recorded. |\n| FR-9 | SVC, PURE | `canPublish(quiz, questions) → string[]` (pure, so it can be shared with the UI). The PATCH status→PUBLISHED transition enforces it server-side. Publishing triggers FR-29. |\n| FR-10 | SVC, API, AUD | A lock check runs when `attemptCount > 0` (`_count.attempts`). It whitelists `prompt/explanation/correct (SHORT_ANSWER only)` and returns CONFLICT with an explanation otherwise. `POST /api/quizzes/:id/regrade` re-runs gradeAnswer on non-manually-graded answers in one transaction, then recomputes attempt scores (FR-25 logic). It must not override teacher-graded answers (manual grade wins). |\n| FR-11 | CFG, UI, SVC | The course tab entry (B2). `GET /api/courses/:id/quizzes` is role-shaped. Teachers get aggregates (count, avg, needsGrading via groupBy). Students get bucketed rows (Upcoming / Available / Completed / **Missed = closed with zero attempts**, assumed). Parents get completed results only, scoped to the linked child. |\n| FR-12 | UI | Server page `/quizzes/[quizId]/take`. It resolves the course from the quiz and calls assertCanViewCourse (STUDENT). Attempts used/allowed uses FR-23. ConfirmDialog guards Start. |\n| FR-13 | SVC, PURE | Inside the start transaction: freeze `questionOrder: String[]`. Option order is a deterministic seeded shuffle (seed = attempt id). Use a pure `seededShuffle(items, seed)` (a small string hash + mulberry32) in grading.ts or a sibling. `deadlineAt = min(startedAt + (limit + extra) min, availableUntil)`. With no time limit, it is `availableUntil` (handoff risk 4). Pure `computeDeadline()`, unit-tested (NFR-8). |\n| FR-14 | UI | Player client component (MUI RadioGroup/FormGroup/TextField/LinearProgress, a navigator grid of Buttons). The sticky header timer is display-only (FR-16). The server returns `deadlineAt` and the client counts down from it. |\n| FR-15 | UI, API | `useAutosave` hook: 800 ms debounce per question, a localStorage queue keyed `quiz-attempt:<id>`, a 5 s retry interval, and `navigator.onLine`. Three-state pill. The server upsert is idempotent, so replays are safe. |\n| FR-16 | SVC, API | The answer PUT reads only the attempt row `{studentId, status, deadlineAt}` (NFR-2). Past `deadlineAt + 30 s` it calls submitAttempt(auto) and then throws CONFLICT. The client then routes to the submitted view. |\n| FR-17 | SVC, UI | `submitAttempt(attemptId, { auto })`, in one transaction. Grade every answer, create zero-score rows for unanswered questions, and set `score`, `submittedAt` and status (NEEDS_GRADING if anything is flagged, else GRADED). Guard with `updateMany where status = IN_PROGRESS` so double submits are no-ops (this also makes FR-18 idempotent). |\n| FR-18 | SVC, JOB | A lazy check on `GET /api/attempts/:id`, on `POST /attempts` (start/resume), and on the teacher list/grade loads: `if IN_PROGRESS && now > deadlineAt → submitAttempt({auto:true})`. `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` does a batch find + submitAttempt each (B3). |\n| FR-19 | DM, SVC | Start or resume: find the IN_PROGRESS attempt and return it. Otherwise create one. Rely on the partial unique index (B10), and on P2002 re-read. Two tabs end up on the same attempt id. |\n| FR-20 | PURE, SVC, API, AUD | `resultsVisible(quiz, now)`: IMMEDIATELY → true after submit, AFTER_CLOSE → `now ≥ availableUntil`, MANUAL → `resultsReleasedAt != null`. `POST /release-results` (manager) sets resultsReleasedAt, then audit + FR-30. This one predicate drives the NFR-1 serializer. |\n| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Result view. The serializer includes `correct` and explanation only when `resultsVisible && showCorrectAnswers`. Score and per-question points only when `resultsVisible`. |\n| FR-22 | SVC | `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId) → { score, maxScore, isPractice, attemptsCounted } \\| null`. HIGHEST/LATEST/AVERAGE over GRADED attempts (Decimal average, fixed2). An exported service function. No endpoint. |\n| FR-23 | SVC, PURE | `attemptLimit = maxAttempts + (accommodation?.extraAttempts ?? 0)`. Start throws CONFLICT when `count(attempts) ≥ limit` and there's no IN_PROGRESS attempt to resume. Pure helper, unit-tested. |\n| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH, AUD | Grade page with two modes (DataTable by student, or by question). `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId/grade` (manager): points 0..question.points step 0.5, plus feedback. Sets `gradedById/manuallyGraded`, then audit, then FR-25. |\n| FR-25 | SVC | After each grade: if no answer in the attempt is still ungraded, set status GRADED and recompute the score as Σ points. Recompute the score on every grade regardless, so overrides on GRADED attempts update it. |\n| FR-26 | SVC, API, UI | `GET /api/quizzes/:id/analytics` (manager). Aggregates are computed in TS over submitted attempts. The class sizes are small, so compute in memory. Median computed in code. Histogram with 10 buckets (100% goes in the last bucket). MUI X BarChart + StatCard. |\n| FR-27 | SVC, API | Per-question stats come from the same pass. The option distribution counts option ids in responses. `?format=csv` reuses `src/server/csv.ts` and returns text/csv with one row per attempt. |\n| FR-28 | API, DM, AUD | `PUT /api/quizzes/:id/accommodations/:studentId` upserts QuizAccommodation (manager). The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Changes apply only to attempts started later (deadlineAt is frozen at start). Note this for the UI copy. |\n| FR-29 | NOTIF | Fires on the first transition to PUBLISHED only (track `publishedAt` or check the previous status). Link `/quizzes/:id/take`. Recipients are ACTIVE enrollees. Skip if the quiz is practice? No: the PRD doesn't say, so send. |\n| FR-30 | NOTIF, JOB | MANUAL → on release (once, guarded by `resultsReleasedAt` going null→set). AFTER_CLOSE → the maintenance pass picks closed quizzes with `resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` (B4) and notifies students who submitted, plus their parents. IMMEDIATELY → never. |\n| FR-31 | API, AUTH | Routes under `src/app/api/{courses/[id]/quizzes, quizzes/[id], quizzes/[id]/questions, quizzes/[id]/questions/reorder, questions/[id]}`. DELETE quiz → CONFLICT if any attempt exists. Reorder accepts the full id list and rejects ids that don't match the quiz's set exactly. |\n| FR-32 | API, AUTH | `POST /api/quizzes/:id/attempts` (STUDENT, course view, quiz PUBLISHED and within its window). `GET /api/attempts/:id` (owner, linked parent once results are released, or manager). The answers PUT and the submit POST are owner-only. |\n| FR-33 | DM, SVC | `isPractice` is returned in FR-22's result. It counts for attempts and analytics like a graded quiz (intake assumption). |\n| FR-34 | AUTH | B1, reused unchanged. Add one helper, `assertCanAccessAttempt(user, attempt)`, in src/server/quiz/: owner, manager via assertCanManageCourse, or a PARENT linked to the student. Parent access is read-only and only when results are visible. |\n| FR-35 | JOB | B3. Both functions must be idempotent: FR-17's status guard and FR-30's claim column. |\n| FR-36 | SEED | Extend prisma/seed.ts. 'Fractions Check' (8 objective questions, closed, every MATH-7A student has a GRADED attempt; scores via grading.ts so the seed data is consistent). 'Unit 1 Test' (12 questions incl. 2 ESSAY, AFTER_CLOSE, window now → +3 days, no attempts). 'Parts of Speech' (ENG-7A, practice, maxAttempts 3, HIGHEST). The seed must be idempotent like the existing one (upsert by title + course). |\n| FR-37 | — | **No work** (LOW, assumed). No sidebar entry. The course tab covers it. Design should drop it explicitly. |\n| FR-38 | AUD | B7. Write after commit, inside the service functions, not in the handlers. |\n| FR-39 | UI, AUTH | MarkdownEditor/MarkdownView for prompts, FileUpload with a `'quiz'` context, and a resolver (B11). |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH, SVC, TEST | **Highest-risk item.** All student-facing reads (quiz GET, attempt GET, course list, answer-PUT response) go through `serializers.ts`. Prisma selects for student paths never select `correct`/`explanation` at all (defence in depth). The unit test asserts `'correct' in obj === false` recursively. |\n| NFR-2 | DM, SVC | The answer PUT does exactly one attempt read plus one upsert. Don't load the Question row: the questionId is validated against `attempt.questionOrder` (already on the attempt row). The response validator for the answer shape is type-agnostic (`string[] \\| string`). It is type-checked at grade time. |\n| NFR-3 | UI | Native inputs via MUI Radio/Checkbox. An `aria-live=\"assertive\"` region announces only at the 5:00 and 1:00 thresholds, not every tick. Keyboard nav for the navigator grid. The axe check is part of the e2e. |\n| NFR-4 | UI | MUI only. Look up each component through mui-mcp before use. This is a dev-phase obligation, so carry it into the plan. |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every handler starts with requireUser/requireRole and then a course or attempt check. The server pages use requirePageRole. |\n| NFR-6 | API | withHandler + Zod parse. `{data}` / `paginated` envelopes. The course quiz list is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100). cuid ids, UTC timestamps. The UI formats dates with DateDisplay / formatInSchoolTz. |\n| NFR-7 | — | Constraint on all of the above: `src/server/quiz/` only, reuse B5–B9 and B14, no new deps, no console.log in app code. |\n| NFR-8 | TEST | Unit: grading.ts (partial credit incl. the FR-3 example, short-answer normalisation), computeDeadline + accommodations, scoring policies, serializer. Integration: autosave 409 after deadline+grace, auto-submit on GET, regrade. E2E: a single Playwright spec. |\n| NFR-9 | UI | Builder ergonomics: default type MULTIPLE/SINGLE_CHOICE, Enter adds an option row, and Duplicate. No architectural change. |\n| NFR-10 | — | Out of scope. Design must not add question banks, proctoring or LaTeX. |\n\n## 3. Cross-cutting decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **D1 Module layout (NFR-7):**\n  - `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (pure: gradeAnswer, seededShuffle, computeDeadline, attemptLimit, resultsVisible, canPublish, applyScoringPolicy)\n  - `quiz-service.ts` (CRUD, publish, lock, regrade, release, accommodations)\n  - `attempt-service.ts` (start/resume, saveAnswer, submit, lazy auto-submit, grade, getStudentQuizScore)\n  - `analytics.ts`\n  - `serializers.ts`\n  - `maintenance.ts` (autoSubmitExpiredAttempts, sendQuizResultsReleased)\n  - `access.ts` (assertCanAccessAttempt)\n\n  Keep the pure helpers together in one file unless it grows past what one file reads comfortably.\n- **D2 Single submit path:** manual submit, deadline-PUT rejection, lazy load and the maintenance pass all call one `submitAttempt`. The `status = IN_PROGRESS` conditional update makes it idempotent and race-safe.\n- **D3 Visibility predicate:** one `resultsVisible()` drives the serializer, the parent access and the FR-11 \"score if visible\" display.\n- **D4 Frozen-at-start:** questionOrder, option order (via seed) and deadlineAt are fixed at start. Later accommodation or settings edits don't move in-flight attempts. FR-10 locks prevent structural changes anyway.\n- **D5 Manual grade precedence:** regrade (FR-10) only recomputes answers where `manuallyGraded = false`. If FR-1's QuizAnswer field list doesn't include such a flag, use `gradedById IS NULL` as the marker.\n\n## 4. Assumptions and open points to surface in the system-design Overview\n\n1. FR-37: no sidebar entry (LOW).\n2. Missed = closed with zero attempts by that student.\n3. Regrade runs only on the explicit action. Editing accepted answers doesn't auto-regrade.\n4. Practice quizzes count toward attempts and analytics. They are excluded only from the gradebook (FR-22's caller filters on isPractice).\n5. `quiz.results_released` defaultEmail = true. The PRD doesn't specify it.\n6. FR-30's AFTER_CLOSE \"sent once\" needs a marker. B4 proposes `Quiz.resultsNotifiedAt`, which is an addition to FR-1's \"exactly as listed\" model. If that isn't acceptable, use a claim table.\n7. Accommodation changes affect only attempts started after the change.\n8. Intake handoff blockers: **none**.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1989,"cache_read_input_tokens":51852,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1989,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73285dce-b12a-41d8-b326-53463f575912","uuid":"1b1e1cb7-345e-494c-b46b-d91d3f8fd1c7","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:03:11.010Z","request_id":"req_011CgrvbgSDwFD6qob5frCCG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01P3vy6Dj6UomMigkMBT1BtY":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-10\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams (SCH-010). It has 39 FRs and 10 NFRs (49 requirements) at 96% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It flags assumptions on FR-33/34/35/37/38/39. Those are restated in §3 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-9 leftovers** as of this writing (`ticketId: \"SH-9\"`). Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-10 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-10 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child. `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Both throw `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These cover FR-34 and the course part of NFR-5. Attempt-level checks are still new: owner, linked parent, or manager. |\n| B2 | `courseTabs` is a static array of `{key, label, href, roles}`. | src/config/course-tabs.ts | FR-11: add one entry, `{ key: 'quizzes', href: id => /courses/${id}/quizzes, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. |\n| B3 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` and then `sendDueReminders(now)` on every request, each wrapped in its own try/catch + logger. Purges run in a once-per-day block. | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-18/FR-30/FR-35: add `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` and `sendQuizResultsReleased(now)` **on every call**, next to sendDueReminders, each with its own try/catch. |\n| B4 | `sendDueReminders` is idempotent through a unique-key claim row (`AssignmentReminder`, P2002 → skip). | src/server/assignments/reminders.ts | FR-30 AFTER_CLOSE needs a \"sent once\" marker. The simplest option is a nullable `Quiz.resultsNotifiedAt`, claimed with `updateMany({ where: { id, resultsNotifiedAt: null } })` and a count check. That needs no new table. If FR-1's model list must stay exact, a claim table is the alternative. |\n| B5 | `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds})` never throw. Call them after commit. | src/server/notifications/notify.ts | FR-29 → `notify()` to enrolled students. FR-30 → `notifyStudentAndParents`. |\n| B6 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object. New keys need `label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles`. | src/server/notifications/types.ts | FR-29: `quiz.published` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, roles STUDENT). `quiz.results_released` (ACADEMIC, roles STUDENT+PARENT). The PRD doesn't give a default email setting for results_released. Default it to true to match assignment.graded, and flag that choice. |\n| B7 | `audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request})` never throws. | src/server/audit.ts | FR-38 actions: `quizAnswer.grade`, `quiz.regrade`, `quiz.release_results`, `quizAccommodation.update`. |\n| B8 | `grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic. It exports `dec`, `fixed2` and `Decimal` from the Prisma browser runtime. `assignments-service.ts` exports `serializeDecimal` and `getSchoolTimezone`. | src/server/assignments/* | FR-3/FR-22/FR-25 reuse dec/fixed2 (NFR-7). Importing from `@/server/assignments/grading-math` is fine. Only lift it to a shared module if dev-planning wants that. Do not copy it. |\n| B9 | `http.ts` provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `AppError`. The codes include CONFLICT (409). Zod errors become VALIDATION_ERROR. Prisma P2002 becomes CONFLICT. | src/server/http.ts | NFR-6. FR-16's 409 is `AppError('CONFLICT', ...)`. |\n| B10 | The DB is PostgreSQL. The project already uses raw-SQL partial unique indexes in migrations. | prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/migration.sql L77-78 | FR-19 race-safety: `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE status = 'IN_PROGRESS'`, hand-added to the FR-1 migration. Add `@@unique([quizId, studentId, attemptNumber])` too. On P2002 during start, re-read and resume. |\n| B11 | File contexts are registered in `registerBuiltInContexts` (lesson, logo, assignment, submission). `attachFiles` sets context/contextId. | src/server/files/contexts.ts, files-service.ts | FR-39: question images need a `'quiz'` context (contextId = quizId) with a resolver: manager, or a viewer with an IN_PROGRESS or visible attempt. The prompt Markdown references the file URL. |\n| B12 | Courses MATH-7A and ENG-7A are looked up in seed.ts with `findCourse([...])`. The seed already uses `console.log` for skips. | prisma/seed.ts L302, L340 | FR-36 follows that pattern (the seed is exempt from the no-console.log rule in practice). |\n| B13 | Installed: @mui/* 9.5.0 (incl. x-charts, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers), @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + sortable 10.0.0, zod 3.23.8, prisma 5.20, vitest, Playwright + axe. | package.json | FR-7, FR-26 and NFR-8 need **no new dependencies** (NFR-7). |\n| B14 | Shared components are DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast, MarkdownEditor, MarkdownView, FileUpload, StatCard, EmptyState, PageHeader, DateDisplay. | src/components/ | FR-7/12/17/24/26/39 reuse them. |\n| B15 | `toStudentSubmission(dto)` is the precedent for a student-shaped serializer. | assignments-service.ts L199 | NFR-1: add `toStudentQuiz` / `toStudentAttempt` in `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts`, with a unit test asserting the `correct` key is absent. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **VAL** validator · **PURE** pure domain logic · **SVC** service (src/server/quiz/) · **API** route handler · **UI** page/component · **JOB** maintenance pass · **AUTH** access boundary · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **SEED** seed · **CFG** config registry · **TEST**\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | One migration, `add_quizzes`. 5 enums, 5 models. Back-relations on Course (`quizzes`) and User (attempts, accommodations, graded answers). QuizAnswer PK `(attemptId, questionId)` (NFR-2). QuizAccommodation unique `(quizId, studentId)`. Include the partial unique index from B10 in the SQL. Money-like fields (points, scores) are `Decimal(6,2)`, per the assignments precedent. |\n| FR-2 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`, client-safe, shared by the builder UI and the handlers. Use per-type question schemas as a discriminated union on `type`. `availableUntil > availableFrom` and the time-limit cross-field checks use `.superRefine`. |\n| FR-3 | PURE | `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. No Prisma import, so the builder preview and tests can use it. `gradeAnswer(question, response) → { points, flagged }`. Partial-credit formula from FR-3. Use Decimal and round with fixed2. |\n| FR-4 | PURE | Same module. `normalize = s.trim().replace(/\\s+/g,' ')`, with case-folding unless `caseSensitive` is set. A non-match returns `flagged: true` and 0 points. |\n| FR-5 | PURE | ESSAY → `{ points: null, flagged: true }`. `correct` holds the guidance text and is server-only (NFR-1). |\n| FR-6 | UI, AUTH | Server page `/courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit`, protected by assertCanManageCourse. The settings panel uses MUI x-date-pickers. The time-limit vs window check reuses the FR-2 validator on the client. |\n| FR-7 | UI | Sortable question list (@dnd-kit/sortable wrapping MUI items). Per-type editor components. Reorder calls `POST /questions/reorder`. |\n| FR-8 | UI | The points total is derived client-side. Preview mode reuses the player component with a `preview` prop. It gets data from the manager GET (with `correct`) and grades locally with the pure grading.ts. It **never calls the attempt endpoints**, so nothing is recorded. |\n| FR-9 | SVC, PURE | `canPublish(quiz, questions) → string[]` (pure, so it can be shared with the UI). The PATCH status→PUBLISHED transition enforces it server-side. Publishing triggers FR-29. |\n| FR-10 | SVC, API, AUD | A lock check runs when `attemptCount > 0` (`_count.attempts`). It whitelists `prompt/explanation/correct (SHORT_ANSWER only)` and returns CONFLICT with an explanation otherwise. `POST /api/quizzes/:id/regrade` re-runs gradeAnswer on non-manually-graded answers in one transaction, then recomputes attempt scores (FR-25 logic). It must not override teacher-graded answers (manual grade wins). |\n| FR-11 | CFG, UI, SVC | The course tab entry (B2). `GET /api/courses/:id/quizzes` is role-shaped. Teachers get aggregates (count, avg, needsGrading via groupBy). Students get bucketed rows (Upcoming / Available / Completed / **Missed = closed with zero attempts**, assumed). Parents get completed results only, scoped to the linked child. |\n| FR-12 | UI | Server page `/quizzes/[quizId]/take`. It resolves the course from the quiz and calls assertCanViewCourse (STUDENT). Attempts used/allowed uses FR-23. ConfirmDialog guards Start. |\n| FR-13 | SVC, PURE | Inside the start transaction: freeze `questionOrder: String[]`. Option order is a deterministic seeded shuffle (seed = attempt id). Use a pure `seededShuffle(items, seed)` (a small string hash + mulberry32) in grading.ts or a sibling. `deadlineAt = min(startedAt + (limit + extra) min, availableUntil)`. With no time limit, it is `availableUntil` (handoff risk 4). Pure `computeDeadline()`, unit-tested (NFR-8). |\n| FR-14 | UI | Player client component (MUI RadioGroup/FormGroup/TextField/LinearProgress, a navigator grid of Buttons). The sticky header timer is display-only (FR-16). The server returns `deadlineAt` and the client counts down from it. |\n| FR-15 | UI, API | `useAutosave` hook: 800 ms debounce per question, a localStorage queue keyed `quiz-attempt:<id>`, a 5 s retry interval, and `navigator.onLine`. Three-state pill. The server upsert is idempotent, so replays are safe. |\n| FR-16 | SVC, API | The answer PUT reads only the attempt row `{studentId, status, deadlineAt}` (NFR-2). Past `deadlineAt + 30 s` it calls submitAttempt(auto) and then throws CONFLICT. The client then routes to the submitted view. |\n| FR-17 | SVC, UI | `submitAttempt(attemptId, { auto })`, in one transaction. Grade every answer, create zero-score rows for unanswered questions, and set `score`, `submittedAt` and status (NEEDS_GRADING if anything is flagged, else GRADED). Guard with `updateMany where status = IN_PROGRESS` so double submits are no-ops (this also makes FR-18 idempotent). |\n| FR-18 | SVC, JOB | A lazy check on `GET /api/attempts/:id`, on `POST /attempts` (start/resume), and on the teacher list/grade loads: `if IN_PROGRESS && now > deadlineAt → submitAttempt({auto:true})`. `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` does a batch find + submitAttempt each (B3). |\n| FR-19 | DM, SVC | Start or resume: find the IN_PROGRESS attempt and return it. Otherwise create one. Rely on the partial unique index (B10), and on P2002 re-read. Two tabs end up on the same attempt id. |\n| FR-20 | PURE, SVC, API, AUD | `resultsVisible(quiz, now)`: IMMEDIATELY → true after submit, AFTER_CLOSE → `now ≥ availableUntil`, MANUAL → `resultsReleasedAt != null`. `POST /release-results` (manager) sets resultsReleasedAt, then audit + FR-30. This one predicate drives the NFR-1 serializer. |\n| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Result view. The serializer includes `correct` and explanation only when `resultsVisible && showCorrectAnswers`. Score and per-question points only when `resultsVisible`. |\n| FR-22 | SVC | `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId) → { score, maxScore, isPractice, attemptsCounted } \\| null`. HIGHEST/LATEST/AVERAGE over GRADED attempts (Decimal average, fixed2). An exported service function. No endpoint. |\n| FR-23 | SVC, PURE | `attemptLimit = maxAttempts + (accommodation?.extraAttempts ?? 0)`. Start throws CONFLICT when `count(attempts) ≥ limit` and there's no IN_PROGRESS attempt to resume. Pure helper, unit-tested. |\n| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH, AUD | Grade page with two modes (DataTable by student, or by question). `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId/grade` (manager): points 0..question.points step 0.5, plus feedback. Sets `gradedById/manuallyGraded`, then audit, then FR-25. |\n| FR-25 | SVC | After each grade: if no answer in the attempt is still ungraded, set status GRADED and recompute the score as Σ points. Recompute the score on every grade regardless, so overrides on GRADED attempts update it. |\n| FR-26 | SVC, API, UI | `GET /api/quizzes/:id/analytics` (manager). Aggregates are computed in TS over submitted attempts. The class sizes are small, so compute in memory. Median computed in code. Histogram with 10 buckets (100% goes in the last bucket). MUI X BarChart + StatCard. |\n| FR-27 | SVC, API | Per-question stats come from the same pass. The option distribution counts option ids in responses. `?format=csv` reuses `src/server/csv.ts` and returns text/csv with one row per attempt. |\n| FR-28 | API, DM, AUD | `PUT /api/quizzes/:id/accommodations/:studentId` upserts QuizAccommodation (manager). The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Changes apply only to attempts started later (deadlineAt is frozen at start). Note this for the UI copy. |\n| FR-29 | NOTIF | Fires on the first transition to PUBLISHED only (track `publishedAt` or check the previous status). Link `/quizzes/:id/take`. Recipients are ACTIVE enrollees. Skip if the quiz is practice? No: the PRD doesn't say, so send. |\n| FR-30 | NOTIF, JOB | MANUAL → on release (once, guarded by `resultsReleasedAt` going null→set). AFTER_CLOSE → the maintenance pass picks closed quizzes with `resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` (B4) and notifies students who submitted, plus their parents. IMMEDIATELY → never. |\n| FR-31 | API, AUTH | Routes under `src/app/api/{courses/[id]/quizzes, quizzes/[id], quizzes/[id]/questions, quizzes/[id]/questions/reorder, questions/[id]}`. DELETE quiz → CONFLICT if any attempt exists. Reorder accepts the full id list and rejects ids that don't match the quiz's set exactly. |\n| FR-32 | API, AUTH | `POST /api/quizzes/:id/attempts` (STUDENT, course view, quiz PUBLISHED and within its window). `GET /api/attempts/:id` (owner, linked parent once results are released, or manager). The answers PUT and the submit POST are owner-only. |\n| FR-33 | DM, SVC | `isPractice` is returned in FR-22's result. It counts for attempts and analytics like a graded quiz (intake assumption). |\n| FR-34 | AUTH | B1, reused unchanged. Add one helper, `assertCanAccessAttempt(user, attempt)`, in src/server/quiz/: owner, manager via assertCanManageCourse, or a PARENT linked to the student. Parent access is read-only and only when results are visible. |\n| FR-35 | JOB | B3. Both functions must be idempotent: FR-17's status guard and FR-30's claim column. |\n| FR-36 | SEED | Extend prisma/seed.ts. 'Fractions Check' (8 objective questions, closed, every MATH-7A student has a GRADED attempt; scores via grading.ts so the seed data is consistent). 'Unit 1 Test' (12 questions incl. 2 ESSAY, AFTER_CLOSE, window now → +3 days, no attempts). 'Parts of Speech' (ENG-7A, practice, maxAttempts 3, HIGHEST). The seed must be idempotent like the existing one (upsert by title + course). |\n| FR-37 | — | **No work** (LOW, assumed). No sidebar entry. The course tab covers it. Design should drop it explicitly. |\n| FR-38 | AUD | B7. Write after commit, inside the service functions, not in the handlers. |\n| FR-39 | UI, AUTH | MarkdownEditor/MarkdownView for prompts, FileUpload with a `'quiz'` context, and a resolver (B11). |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH, SVC, TEST | **Highest-risk item.** All student-facing reads (quiz GET, attempt GET, course list, answer-PUT response) go through `serializers.ts`. Prisma selects for student paths never select `correct`/`explanation` at all (defence in depth). The unit test asserts `'correct' in obj === false` recursively. |\n| NFR-2 | DM, SVC | The answer PUT does exactly one attempt read plus one upsert. Don't load the Question row: the questionId is validated against `attempt.questionOrder` (already on the attempt row). The response validator for the answer shape is type-agnostic (`string[] \\| string`). It is type-checked at grade time. |\n| NFR-3 | UI | Native inputs via MUI Radio/Checkbox. An `aria-live=\"assertive\"` region announces only at the 5:00 and 1:00 thresholds, not every tick. Keyboard nav for the navigator grid. The axe check is part of the e2e. |\n| NFR-4 | UI | MUI only. Look up each component through mui-mcp before use. This is a dev-phase obligation, so carry it into the plan. |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every handler starts with requireUser/requireRole and then a course or attempt check. The server pages use requirePageRole. |\n| NFR-6 | API | withHandler + Zod parse. `{data}` / `paginated` envelopes. The course quiz list is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100). cuid ids, UTC timestamps. The UI formats dates with DateDisplay / formatInSchoolTz. |\n| NFR-7 | — | Constraint on all of the above: `src/server/quiz/` only, reuse B5–B9 and B14, no new deps, no console.log in app code. |\n| NFR-8 | TEST | Unit: grading.ts (partial credit incl. the FR-3 example, short-answer normalisation), computeDeadline + accommodations, scoring policies, serializer. Integration: autosave 409 after deadline+grace, auto-submit on GET, regrade. E2E: a single Playwright spec. |\n| NFR-9 | UI | Builder ergonomics: default type MULTIPLE/SINGLE_CHOICE, Enter adds an option row, and Duplicate. No architectural change. |\n| NFR-10 | — | Out of scope. Design must not add question banks, proctoring or LaTeX. |\n\n## 3. Cross-cutting decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **D1 Module layout (NFR-7):**\n  - `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (pure: gradeAnswer, seededShuffle, computeDeadline, attemptLimit, resultsVisible, canPublish, applyScoringPolicy)\n  - `quiz-service.ts` (CRUD, publish, lock, regrade, release, accommodations)\n  - `attempt-service.ts` (start/resume, saveAnswer, submit, lazy auto-submit, grade, getStudentQuizScore)\n  - `analytics.ts`\n  - `serializers.ts`\n  - `maintenance.ts` (autoSubmitExpiredAttempts, sendQuizResultsReleased)\n  - `access.ts` (assertCanAccessAttempt)\n\n  Keep the pure helpers together in one file unless it grows past what one file reads comfortably.\n- **D2 Single submit path:** manual submit, deadline-PUT rejection, lazy load and the maintenance pass all call one `submitAttempt`. The `status = IN_PROGRESS` conditional update makes it idempotent and race-safe.\n- **D3 Visibility predicate:** one `resultsVisible()` drives the serializer, the parent access and the FR-11 \"score if visible\" display.\n- **D4 Frozen-at-start:** questionOrder, option order (via seed) and deadlineAt are fixed at start. Later accommodation or settings edits don't move in-flight attempts. FR-10 locks prevent structural changes anyway.\n- **D5 Manual grade precedence:** regrade (FR-10) only recomputes answers where `manuallyGraded = false`. If FR-1's QuizAnswer field list doesn't include such a flag, use `gradedById IS NULL` as the marker.\n\n## 4. Assumptions and open points to surface in the system-design Overview\n\n1. FR-37: no sidebar entry (LOW).\n2. Missed = closed with zero attempts by that student.\n3. Regrade runs only on the explicit action. Editing accepted answers doesn't auto-regrade.\n4. Practice quizzes count toward attempts and analytics. They are excluded only from the gradebook (FR-22's caller filters on isPractice).\n5. `quiz.results_released` defaultEmail = true. The PRD doesn't specify it.\n6. FR-30's AFTER_CLOSE \"sent once\" needs a marker. B4 proposes `Quiz.resultsNotifiedAt`, which is an addition to FR-1's \"exactly as listed\" model. If that isn't acceptable, use a claim table.\n7. Accommodation changes affect only attempts started after the change.\n8. Intake handoff blockers: **none**.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P3vy6Dj6UomMigkMBT1BtY","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73285dce-b12a-41d8-b326-53463f575912","uuid":"e8e3c2a1-17a4-4fa5-8abd-29383f31d704","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:03:11.111Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-10\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams (SCH-010). It has 39 FRs and 10 NFRs (49 requirements) at 96% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It flags assumptions on FR-33/34/35/37/38/39. Those are restated in §3 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-9 leftovers** as of this writing (`ticketId: \"SH-9\"`). Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-10 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-10 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child. `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Both throw `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These cover FR-34 and the course part of NFR-5. Attempt-level checks are still new: owner, linked parent, or manager. |\n| B2 | `courseTabs` is a static array of `{key, label, href, roles}`. | src/config/course-tabs.ts | FR-11: add one entry, `{ key: 'quizzes', href: id => /courses/${id}/quizzes, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. |\n| B3 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` and then `sendDueReminders(now)` on every request, each wrapped in its own try/catch + logger. Purges run in a once-per-day block. | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-18/FR-30/FR-35: add `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` and `sendQuizResultsReleased(now)` **on every call**, next to sendDueReminders, each with its own try/catch. |\n| B4 | `sendDueReminders` is idempotent through a unique-key claim row (`AssignmentReminder`, P2002 → skip). | src/server/assignments/reminders.ts | FR-30 AFTER_CLOSE needs a \"sent once\" marker. The simplest option is a nullable `Quiz.resultsNotifiedAt`, claimed with `updateMany({ where: { id, resultsNotifiedAt: null } })` and a count check. That needs no new table. If FR-1's model list must stay exact, a claim table is the alternative. |\n| B5 | `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds})` never throw. Call them after commit. | src/server/notifications/notify.ts | FR-29 → `notify()` to enrolled students. FR-30 → `notifyStudentAndParents`. |\n| B6 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object. New keys need `label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles`. | src/server/notifications/types.ts | FR-29: `quiz.published` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, roles STUDENT). `quiz.results_released` (ACADEMIC, roles STUDENT+PARENT). The PRD doesn't give a default email setting for results_released. Default it to true to match assignment.graded, and flag that choice. |\n| B7 | `audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request})` never throws. | src/server/audit.ts | FR-38 actions: `quizAnswer.grade`, `quiz.regrade`, `quiz.release_results`, `quizAccommodation.update`. |\n| B8 | `grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic. It exports `dec`, `fixed2` and `Decimal` from the Prisma browser runtime. `assignments-service.ts` exports `serializeDecimal` and `getSchoolTimezone`. | src/server/assignments/* | FR-3/FR-22/FR-25 reuse dec/fixed2 (NFR-7). Importing from `@/server/assignments/grading-math` is fine. Only lift it to a shared module if dev-planning wants that. Do not copy it. |\n| B9 | `http.ts` provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `AppError`. The codes include CONFLICT (409). Zod errors become VALIDATION_ERROR. Prisma P2002 becomes CONFLICT. | src/server/http.ts | NFR-6. FR-16's 409 is `AppError('CONFLICT', ...)`. |\n| B10 | The DB is PostgreSQL. The project already uses raw-SQL partial unique indexes in migrations. | prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/migration.sql L77-78 | FR-19 race-safety: `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE status = 'IN_PROGRESS'`, hand-added to the FR-1 migration. Add `@@unique([quizId, studentId, attemptNumber])` too. On P2002 during start, re-read and resume. |\n| B11 | File contexts are registered in `registerBuiltInContexts` (lesson, logo, assignment, submission). `attachFiles` sets context/contextId. | src/server/files/contexts.ts, files-service.ts | FR-39: question images need a `'quiz'` context (contextId = quizId) with a resolver: manager, or a viewer with an IN_PROGRESS or visible attempt. The prompt Markdown references the file URL. |\n| B12 | Courses MATH-7A and ENG-7A are looked up in seed.ts with `findCourse([...])`. The seed already uses `console.log` for skips. | prisma/seed.ts L302, L340 | FR-36 follows that pattern (the seed is exempt from the no-console.log rule in practice). |\n| B13 | Installed: @mui/* 9.5.0 (incl. x-charts, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers), @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + sortable 10.0.0, zod 3.23.8, prisma 5.20, vitest, Playwright + axe. | package.json | FR-7, FR-26 and NFR-8 need **no new dependencies** (NFR-7). |\n| B14 | Shared components are DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast, MarkdownEditor, MarkdownView, FileUpload, StatCard, EmptyState, PageHeader, DateDisplay. | src/components/ | FR-7/12/17/24/26/39 reuse them. |\n| B15 | `toStudentSubmission(dto)` is the precedent for a student-shaped serializer. | assignments-service.ts L199 | NFR-1: add `toStudentQuiz` / `toStudentAttempt` in `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts`, with a unit test asserting the `correct` key is absent. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **VAL** validator · **PURE** pure domain logic · **SVC** service (src/server/quiz/) · **API** route handler · **UI** page/component · **JOB** maintenance pass · **AUTH** access boundary · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **SEED** seed · **CFG** config registry · **TEST**\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | One migration, `add_quizzes`. 5 enums, 5 models. Back-relations on Course (`quizzes`) and User (attempts, accommodations, graded answers). QuizAnswer PK `(attemptId, questionId)` (NFR-2). QuizAccommodation unique `(quizId, studentId)`. Include the partial unique index from B10 in the SQL. Money-like fields (points, scores) are `Decimal(6,2)`, per the assignments precedent. |\n| FR-2 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`, client-safe, shared by the builder UI and the handlers. Use per-type question schemas as a discriminated union on `type`. `availableUntil > availableFrom` and the time-limit cross-field checks use `.superRefine`. |\n| FR-3 | PURE | `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. No Prisma import, so the builder preview and tests can use it. `gradeAnswer(question, response) → { points, flagged }`. Partial-credit formula from FR-3. Use Decimal and round with fixed2. |\n| FR-4 | PURE | Same module. `normalize = s.trim().replace(/\\s+/g,' ')`, with case-folding unless `caseSensitive` is set. A non-match returns `flagged: true` and 0 points. |\n| FR-5 | PURE | ESSAY → `{ points: null, flagged: true }`. `correct` holds the guidance text and is server-only (NFR-1). |\n| FR-6 | UI, AUTH | Server page `/courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit`, protected by assertCanManageCourse. The settings panel uses MUI x-date-pickers. The time-limit vs window check reuses the FR-2 validator on the client. |\n| FR-7 | UI | Sortable question list (@dnd-kit/sortable wrapping MUI items). Per-type editor components. Reorder calls `POST /questions/reorder`. |\n| FR-8 | UI | The points total is derived client-side. Preview mode reuses the player component with a `preview` prop. It gets data from the manager GET (with `correct`) and grades locally with the pure grading.ts. It **never calls the attempt endpoints**, so nothing is recorded. |\n| FR-9 | SVC, PURE | `canPublish(quiz, questions) → string[]` (pure, so it can be shared with the UI). The PATCH status→PUBLISHED transition enforces it server-side. Publishing triggers FR-29. |\n| FR-10 | SVC, API, AUD | A lock check runs when `attemptCount > 0` (`_count.attempts`). It whitelists `prompt/explanation/correct (SHORT_ANSWER only)` and returns CONFLICT with an explanation otherwise. `POST /api/quizzes/:id/regrade` re-runs gradeAnswer on non-manually-graded answers in one transaction, then recomputes attempt scores (FR-25 logic). It must not override teacher-graded answers (manual grade wins). |\n| FR-11 | CFG, UI, SVC | The course tab entry (B2). `GET /api/courses/:id/quizzes` is role-shaped. Teachers get aggregates (count, avg, needsGrading via groupBy). Students get bucketed rows (Upcoming / Available / Completed / **Missed = closed with zero attempts**, assumed). Parents get completed results only, scoped to the linked child. |\n| FR-12 | UI | Server page `/quizzes/[quizId]/take`. It resolves the course from the quiz and calls assertCanViewCourse (STUDENT). Attempts used/allowed uses FR-23. ConfirmDialog guards Start. |\n| FR-13 | SVC, PURE | Inside the start transaction: freeze `questionOrder: String[]`. Option order is a deterministic seeded shuffle (seed = attempt id). Use a pure `seededShuffle(items, seed)` (a small string hash + mulberry32) in grading.ts or a sibling. `deadlineAt = min(startedAt + (limit + extra) min, availableUntil)`. With no time limit, it is `availableUntil` (handoff risk 4). Pure `computeDeadline()`, unit-tested (NFR-8). |\n| FR-14 | UI | Player client component (MUI RadioGroup/FormGroup/TextField/LinearProgress, a navigator grid of Buttons). The sticky header timer is display-only (FR-16). The server returns `deadlineAt` and the client counts down from it. |\n| FR-15 | UI, API | `useAutosave` hook: 800 ms debounce per question, a localStorage queue keyed `quiz-attempt:<id>`, a 5 s retry interval, and `navigator.onLine`. Three-state pill. The server upsert is idempotent, so replays are safe. |\n| FR-16 | SVC, API | The answer PUT reads only the attempt row `{studentId, status, deadlineAt}` (NFR-2). Past `deadlineAt + 30 s` it calls submitAttempt(auto) and then throws CONFLICT. The client then routes to the submitted view. |\n| FR-17 | SVC, UI | `submitAttempt(attemptId, { auto })`, in one transaction. Grade every answer, create zero-score rows for unanswered questions, and set `score`, `submittedAt` and status (NEEDS_GRADING if anything is flagged, else GRADED). Guard with `updateMany where status = IN_PROGRESS` so double submits are no-ops (this also makes FR-18 idempotent). |\n| FR-18 | SVC, JOB | A lazy check on `GET /api/attempts/:id`, on `POST /attempts` (start/resume), and on the teacher list/grade loads: `if IN_PROGRESS && now > deadlineAt → submitAttempt({auto:true})`. `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` does a batch find + submitAttempt each (B3). |\n| FR-19 | DM, SVC | Start or resume: find the IN_PROGRESS attempt and return it. Otherwise create one. Rely on the partial unique index (B10), and on P2002 re-read. Two tabs end up on the same attempt id. |\n| FR-20 | PURE, SVC, API, AUD | `resultsVisible(quiz, now)`: IMMEDIATELY → true after submit, AFTER_CLOSE → `now ≥ availableUntil`, MANUAL → `resultsReleasedAt != null`. `POST /release-results` (manager) sets resultsReleasedAt, then audit + FR-30. This one predicate drives the NFR-1 serializer. |\n| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Result view. The serializer includes `correct` and explanation only when `resultsVisible && showCorrectAnswers`. Score and per-question points only when `resultsVisible`. |\n| FR-22 | SVC | `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId) → { score, maxScore, isPractice, attemptsCounted } \\| null`. HIGHEST/LATEST/AVERAGE over GRADED attempts (Decimal average, fixed2). An exported service function. No endpoint. |\n| FR-23 | SVC, PURE | `attemptLimit = maxAttempts + (accommodation?.extraAttempts ?? 0)`. Start throws CONFLICT when `count(attempts) ≥ limit` and there's no IN_PROGRESS attempt to resume. Pure helper, unit-tested. |\n| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH, AUD | Grade page with two modes (DataTable by student, or by question). `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId/grade` (manager): points 0..question.points step 0.5, plus feedback. Sets `gradedById/manuallyGraded`, then audit, then FR-25. |\n| FR-25 | SVC | After each grade: if no answer in the attempt is still ungraded, set status GRADED and recompute the score as Σ points. Recompute the score on every grade regardless, so overrides on GRADED attempts update it. |\n| FR-26 | SVC, API, UI | `GET /api/quizzes/:id/analytics` (manager). Aggregates are computed in TS over submitted attempts. The class sizes are small, so compute in memory. Median computed in code. Histogram with 10 buckets (100% goes in the last bucket). MUI X BarChart + StatCard. |\n| FR-27 | SVC, API | Per-question stats come from the same pass. The option distribution counts option ids in responses. `?format=csv` reuses `src/server/csv.ts` and returns text/csv with one row per attempt. |\n| FR-28 | API, DM, AUD | `PUT /api/quizzes/:id/accommodations/:studentId` upserts QuizAccommodation (manager). The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Changes apply only to attempts started later (deadlineAt is frozen at start). Note this for the UI copy. |\n| FR-29 | NOTIF | Fires on the first transition to PUBLISHED only (track `publishedAt` or check the previous status). Link `/quizzes/:id/take`. Recipients are ACTIVE enrollees. Skip if the quiz is practice? No: the PRD doesn't say, so send. |\n| FR-30 | NOTIF, JOB | MANUAL → on release (once, guarded by `resultsReleasedAt` going null→set). AFTER_CLOSE → the maintenance pass picks closed quizzes with `resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` (B4) and notifies students who submitted, plus their parents. IMMEDIATELY → never. |\n| FR-31 | API, AUTH | Routes under `src/app/api/{courses/[id]/quizzes, quizzes/[id], quizzes/[id]/questions, quizzes/[id]/questions/reorder, questions/[id]}`. DELETE quiz → CONFLICT if any attempt exists. Reorder accepts the full id list and rejects ids that don't match the quiz's set exactly. |\n| FR-32 | API, AUTH | `POST /api/quizzes/:id/attempts` (STUDENT, course view, quiz PUBLISHED and within its window). `GET /api/attempts/:id` (owner, linked parent once results are released, or manager). The answers PUT and the submit POST are owner-only. |\n| FR-33 | DM, SVC | `isPractice` is returned in FR-22's result. It counts for attempts and analytics like a graded quiz (intake assumption). |\n| FR-34 | AUTH | B1, reused unchanged. Add one helper, `assertCanAccessAttempt(user, attempt)`, in src/server/quiz/: owner, manager via assertCanManageCourse, or a PARENT linked to the student. Parent access is read-only and only when results are visible. |\n| FR-35 | JOB | B3. Both functions must be idempotent: FR-17's status guard and FR-30's claim column. |\n| FR-36 | SEED | Extend prisma/seed.ts. 'Fractions Check' (8 objective questions, closed, every MATH-7A student has a GRADED attempt; scores via grading.ts so the seed data is consistent). 'Unit 1 Test' (12 questions incl. 2 ESSAY, AFTER_CLOSE, window now → +3 days, no attempts). 'Parts of Speech' (ENG-7A, practice, maxAttempts 3, HIGHEST). The seed must be idempotent like the existing one (upsert by title + course). |\n| FR-37 | — | **No work** (LOW, assumed). No sidebar entry. The course tab covers it. Design should drop it explicitly. |\n| FR-38 | AUD | B7. Write after commit, inside the service functions, not in the handlers. |\n| FR-39 | UI, AUTH | MarkdownEditor/MarkdownView for prompts, FileUpload with a `'quiz'` context, and a resolver (B11). |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH, SVC, TEST | **Highest-risk item.** All student-facing reads (quiz GET, attempt GET, course list, answer-PUT response) go through `serializers.ts`. Prisma selects for student paths never select `correct`/`explanation` at all (defence in depth). The unit test asserts `'correct' in obj === false` recursively. |\n| NFR-2 | DM, SVC | The answer PUT does exactly one attempt read plus one upsert. Don't load the Question row: the questionId is validated against `attempt.questionOrder` (already on the attempt row). The response validator for the answer shape is type-agnostic (`string[] \\| string`). It is type-checked at grade time. |\n| NFR-3 | UI | Native inputs via MUI Radio/Checkbox. An `aria-live=\"assertive\"` region announces only at the 5:00 and 1:00 thresholds, not every tick. Keyboard nav for the navigator grid. The axe check is part of the e2e. |\n| NFR-4 | UI | MUI only. Look up each component through mui-mcp before use. This is a dev-phase obligation, so carry it into the plan. |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every handler starts with requireUser/requireRole and then a course or attempt check. The server pages use requirePageRole. |\n| NFR-6 | API | withHandler + Zod parse. `{data}` / `paginated` envelopes. The course quiz list is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100). cuid ids, UTC timestamps. The UI formats dates with DateDisplay / formatInSchoolTz. |\n| NFR-7 | — | Constraint on all of the above: `src/server/quiz/` only, reuse B5–B9 and B14, no new deps, no console.log in app code. |\n| NFR-8 | TEST | Unit: grading.ts (partial credit incl. the FR-3 example, short-answer normalisation), computeDeadline + accommodations, scoring policies, serializer. Integration: autosave 409 after deadline+grace, auto-submit on GET, regrade. E2E: a single Playwright spec. |\n| NFR-9 | UI | Builder ergonomics: default type MULTIPLE/SINGLE_CHOICE, Enter adds an option row, and Duplicate. No architectural change. |\n| NFR-10 | — | Out of scope. Design must not add question banks, proctoring or LaTeX. |\n\n## 3. Cross-cutting decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **D1 Module layout (NFR-7):**\n  - `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (pure: gradeAnswer, seededShuffle, computeDeadline, attemptLimit, resultsVisible, canPublish, applyScoringPolicy)\n  - `quiz-service.ts` (CRUD, publish, lock, regrade, release, accommodations)\n  - `attempt-service.ts` (start/resume, saveAnswer, submit, lazy auto-submit, grade, getStudentQuizScore)\n  - `analytics.ts`\n  - `serializers.ts`\n  - `maintenance.ts` (autoSubmitExpiredAttempts, sendQuizResultsReleased)\n  - `access.ts` (assertCanAccessAttempt)\n\n  Keep the pure helpers together in one file unless it grows past what one file reads comfortably.\n- **D2 Single submit path:** manual submit, deadline-PUT rejection, lazy load and the maintenance pass all call one `submitAttempt`. The `status = IN_PROGRESS` conditional update makes it idempotent and race-safe.\n- **D3 Visibility predicate:** one `resultsVisible()` drives the serializer, the parent access and the FR-11 \"score if visible\" display.\n- **D4 Frozen-at-start:** questionOrder, option order (via seed) and deadlineAt are fixed at start. Later accommodation or settings edits don't move in-flight attempts. FR-10 locks prevent structural changes anyway.\n- **D5 Manual grade precedence:** regrade (FR-10) only recomputes answers where `manuallyGraded = false`. If FR-1's QuizAnswer field list doesn't include such a flag, use `gradedById IS NULL` as the marker.\n\n## 4. Assumptions and open points to surface in the system-design Overview\n\n1. FR-37: no sidebar entry (LOW).\n2. Missed = closed with zero attempts by that student.\n3. Regrade runs only on the explicit action. Editing accepted answers doesn't auto-regrade.\n4. Practice quizzes count toward attempts and analytics. They are excluded only from the gradebook (FR-22's caller filters on isPractice).\n5. `quiz.results_released` defaultEmail = true. The PRD doesn't specify it.\n6. FR-30's AFTER_CLOSE \"sent once\" needs a marker. B4 proposes `Quiz.resultsNotifiedAt`, which is an addition to FR-1's \"exactly as listed\" model. If that isn't acceptable, use a claim table.\n7. Accommodation changes affect only attempts started after the change.\n8. Intake handoff blockers: **none**.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":174,"newStart":1,"newLines":111,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-9","+# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-10"," "," Written by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T09:00:00Z), PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions (SCH-009). It has 61 FRs and 17 NFRs (78 requirements) at 95% confidence.","-`handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers. They must be surfaced in the `system-design.md` Overview (compliance rule 5). Decisions D1–D4 below answer them.","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams (SCH-010). It has 39 FRs and 10 NFRs (49 requirements) at 96% confidence.","+`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It flags assumptions on FR-33/34/35/37/38/39. Those are restated in §3 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward."," ","-> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-8 leftovers** as of this writing. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-9 input.","+> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-9 leftovers** as of this writing (`ticketId: \"SH-9\"`). Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-10 input."," ","-## Brownfield facts verified on disk","+## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk"," ","-| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-9 |","+| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-10 |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| B1 | `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` sets `context` and `contextId` on unattached files owned by the caller (any file for ADMIN). It does **not** check the file's upload context. `detachFiles` sets `contextId = null`, and `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes those files after 24 h. | src/server/files/files-service.ts L215-245, purge.ts | FR-53 requires uploads with context `'submission'`. The service must check `context === 'submission'` before calling attachFiles. On resubmission, **never detach the previous attempt's files**: `SubmissionHistory.fileIds` points at them, and detaching would let the purge delete history bytes. Keep them attached to the same submission id. |","-| B2 | `FileObject.storageKey` is `@unique`, and a FileObject holds a single `(context, contextId)`. `storage.ts` exports `saveFile(stream)`, `readFile(key)` and `deleteFile`. | schema L564-578, storage.ts | FR-15 duplicate **cannot share** attachment rows. For each target course, copy the bytes (`readFile` → `saveFile`), create a new FileObject (context `'assignment'`), then attach it. |","-| B3 | `FileObject` has a back-relation `lessonAttachments LessonAttachment[]`. | schema L577 | FR-3/FR-4 add back-relations `assignmentAttachments` and `submissionFiles` to FileObject. This is an additive edit to an existing model, so NFR-11 allows it. |","-| B4 | `canAccessFile` order: unattached → owner/ADMIN; registered resolver; unknown context → owner/ADMIN. Resolver errors deny. `registerBuiltInContexts` currently registers `lesson` and `logo`. | access.ts L35-50, contexts.ts L36-39 | FR-47 adds `assignmentResolver` (contextId = assignmentId) and `submissionResolver` (contextId = submissionId) in contexts.ts. Before submit, a student's own upload is unattached, so it is already readable by owner/ADMIN only. |","-| B5 | `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` is a pure read-time check: PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt ≤ now. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` covers ADMIN, teacher and co-teacher. | visibility.ts | FR-13 can reuse both by mapping `availableFrom → publishAt`. Widen the `Publishable.status` type to accept `AssignmentStatus`, which has the same string values, rather than writing a second helper (NFR-11). |","-| B6 | `assertCanViewCourse` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child (`studentLinks`). `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Errors are `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These already provide all of NFR-5's course checks. A parent who views a course still needs to be scoped to *which* child (FR-18, FR-38). |","-| B7 | `ParentStudentLink {parentId, studentId}`. `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds, ...})` never throws. | notify.ts L98-117 | FR-44 uses it as-is. For FR-45 (parents only), call `notify()` with the parent ids from `parentStudentLink`. |","-| B8 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` **on every call**. Purges run in a once-per-day `if` (`lastPurgeAt`, in memory). | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-43/FR-45: call `sendDueReminders(now)` on **every** call, outside the daily block (due_soon has a 24 h window, so daily would miss it). Wrap it in its own try/catch + logger, like the purges. |","-| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object with `{label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. `content.lesson_published` is the closest precedent. | types.ts L33, L90-100 | FR-46: add four keys. Roles: `published` [STUDENT]; `due_soon` [STUDENT]; `returned` [STUDENT, PARENT]; `missing` [PARENT], with defaultEmail true. |","-| B10 | `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, tz)` and `schoolNow(now, tz)` live in `src/lib/dates.ts`, using date-fns-tz, which is already installed. | dates.ts | FR-10 next-teaching-day 23:59 and FR-25 receipt formatting. Convert wall time to UTC with date-fns-tz `fromZonedTime` (NFR-9 DST). |","-| B11 | `SchoolDay {dayOfWeek 1-7, isTeaching}` is seeded with all 7 rows. | schema L477-480 | FR-10 loops forward at most 7 days. If no day is teaching, fall back to tomorrow. |","-| B12 | `courseTabs` = overview, roster, attendance (there is **no content tab**: PRD-08 UI is missing). It is rendered by `CourseTabs.tsx`. `src/app/(app)/students/[id]/` has `attendance/` and `courses/` but no tab bar. | course-tabs.ts, ls | FR-16: append one entry with ALL_ROLES. FR-41: register the entry plus the page `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx`. It stays unreachable through tabs (blocker 5), but direct URLs work. |","-| B13 | `navigation.ts` entries are `{label, href, icon, roles, group?}`. | navigation.ts L31-38 | FR-40: one entry with roles [STUDENT, PARENT, TEACHER]. Default ADMIN to the \"To grade\" view through the API (clarification). Add ADMIN to the nav only if design adopts that default. |","-| B14 | `src/server/assignments/` and `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` do not exist. Validator precedent: `src/lib/validators/content.ts`. HTTP helpers: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` and `AppError` in `src/server/http.ts`. | ls, grep | Greenfield feature folder (NFR-8). Route handlers follow NFR-7 using the existing helpers. |","-| B15 | Existing components: ConfirmDialog, DataTable, DateDisplay, EmptyState, FormField, LoadingSkeleton, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker. **There is no** FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView or MarkdownEditor. | ls src/components | Blocker 1, see D1. |","-| B16 | Tests live in `tests/{unit,integration,e2e}`. | ls | NFR-14 placement. |","+| B1 | `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child. `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Both throw `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These cover FR-34 and the course part of NFR-5. Attempt-level checks are still new: owner, linked parent, or manager. |","+| B2 | `courseTabs` is a static array of `{key, label, href, roles}`. | src/config/course-tabs.ts | FR-11: add one entry, `{ key: 'quizzes', href: id => /courses/${id}/quizzes, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. |","+| B3 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` and then `sendDueReminders(now)` on every request, each wrapped in its own try/catch + logger. Purges run in a once-per-day block. | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-18/FR-30/FR-35: add `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` and `sendQuizResultsReleased(now)` **on every call**, next to sendDueReminders, each with its own try/catch. |","+| B4 | `sendDueReminders` is idempotent through a unique-key claim row (`AssignmentReminder`, P2002 → skip). | src/server/assignments/reminders.ts | FR-30 AFTER_CLOSE needs a \"sent once\" marker. The simplest option is a nullable `Quiz.resultsNotifiedAt`, claimed with `updateMany({ where: { id, resultsNotifiedAt: null } })` and a count check. That needs no new table. If FR-1's model list must stay exact, a claim table is the alternative. |","+| B5 | `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds})` never throw. Call them after commit. | src/server/notifications/notify.ts | FR-29 → `notify()` to enrolled students. FR-30 → `notifyStudentAndParents`. |","+| B6 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object. New keys need `label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles`. | src/server/notifications/types.ts | FR-29: `quiz.published` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, roles STUDENT). `quiz.results_released` (ACADEMIC, roles STUDENT+PARENT). The PRD doesn't give a default email setting for results_released. Default it to true to match assignment.graded, and flag that choice. |","+| B7 | `audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request})` never throws. | src/server/audit.ts | FR-38 actions: `quizAnswer.grade`, `quiz.regrade`, `quiz.release_results`, `quizAccommodation.update`. |","+| B8 | `grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic. It exports `dec`, `fixed2` and `Decimal` from the Prisma browser runtime. `assignments-service.ts` exports `serializeDecimal` and `getSchoolTimezone`. | src/server/assignments/* | FR-3/FR-22/FR-25 reuse dec/fixed2 (NFR-7). Importing from `@/server/assignments/grading-math` is fine. Only lift it to a shared module if dev-planning wants that. Do not copy it. |","+| B9 | `http.ts` provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `AppError`. The codes include CONFLICT (409). Zod errors become VALIDATION_ERROR. Prisma P2002 becomes CONFLICT. | src/server/http.ts | NFR-6. FR-16's 409 is `AppError('CONFLICT', ...)`. |","+| B10 | The DB is PostgreSQL. The project already uses raw-SQL partial unique indexes in migrations. | prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/migration.sql L77-78 | FR-19 race-safety: `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE status = 'IN_PROGRESS'`, hand-added to the FR-1 migration. Add `@@unique([quizId, studentId, attemptNumber])` too. On P2002 during start, re-read and resume. |","+| B11 | File contexts are registered in `registerBuiltInContexts` (lesson, logo, assignment, submission). `attachFiles` sets context/contextId. | src/server/files/contexts.ts, files-service.ts | FR-39: question images need a `'quiz'` context (contextId = quizId) with a resolver: manager, or a viewer with an IN_PROGRESS or visible attempt. The prompt Markdown references the file URL. |","+| B12 | Courses MATH-7A and ENG-7A are looked up in seed.ts with `findCourse([...])`. The seed already uses `console.log` for skips. | prisma/seed.ts L302, L340 | FR-36 follows that pattern (the seed is exempt from the no-console.log rule in practice). |","+| B13 | Installed: @mui/* 9.5.0 (incl. x-charts, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers), @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + sortable 10.0.0, zod 3.23.8, prisma 5.20, vitest, Playwright + axe. | package.json | FR-7, FR-26 and NFR-8 need **no new dependencies** (NFR-7). |","+| B14 | Shared components are DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast, MarkdownEditor, MarkdownView, FileUpload, StatCard, EmptyState, PageHeader, DateDisplay. | src/components/ | FR-7/12/17/24/26/39 reuse them. |","+| B15 | `toStudentSubmission(dto)` is the precedent for a student-shaped serializer. | assignments-service.ts L199 | NFR-1: add `toStudentQuiz` / `toStudentAttempt` in `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts`, with a unit test asserting the `correct` key is absent. |"," ","-## Requirement → architectural concern","+## 2. Requirement → architectural concern"," ","-Legend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = service logic · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = maintenance pass · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = registry/config · **NOTIF** = notification · **TEST** = test · **SEED** = seed data","+Concern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **VAL** validator · **PURE** pure domain logic · **SVC** service (src/server/quiz/) · **API** route handler · **UI** page/component · **JOB** maintenance pass · **AUTH** access boundary · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **SEED** seed · **CFG** config registry · **TEST**"," ","-### Data model (one migration: FR-1…FR-6)","-"," | Req | Concern | Notes |"," |---|---|---|","-| FR-1 | DM | New enums `SubmissionType`, `AssignmentStatus`, `SubmissionStatus`. Do not reuse `ContentStatus`, because the PRD names a new enum (the values happen to match, and B5 relies on that). |","-| FR-2 | DM | `Assignment` with `allowExtraCredit`, `notifiedAt?`, `archivedAt?`, `rubricId String? @unique`, Course relation with Cascade, and `@@index([courseId, dueAt])`. Add the back-relation `assignments Assignment[]` on Course. |","-| FR-3 | DM | `AssignmentAttachment` (join to FileObject, back-relation per B3), `Rubric`, `RubricCriterion` (`maxPoints Decimal(6,2)`, `order Int`, `levels Json`). A 1:1 Rubric↔Assignment via `rubricId @unique` means a rubric is never shared, so delete it together with the assignment. |","-| FR-4 | DM | `Submission @@unique([assignmentId, studentId])`, which means one row per student. Attempts live in `SubmissionHistory`. The Decimal fields are `rawScore`, `penaltyPercent` and `finalScore`. `rubricScores Json`. `SubmissionFile` join, back-relation per B3. `SubmissionHistory.fileIds String[]` has no FK, so the files must not be purged (B1). |","-| FR-5 | DM | `GradeExemption @@id([assignmentId, studentId])`. Cascade on assignment delete. |","-| FR-6 | DM | `AssignmentReminder @@unique([assignmentId, studentId, kind])`. `kind` is a String ('due_soon' / 'missing'). Insert with `createMany({skipDuplicates:true})`, or catch P2002, and send only for the rows actually inserted (idempotent under concurrent dispatchers). |","-| FR-7 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`, shared by client forms and route handlers. Cross-field rules (`lateCutoffAt > dueAt`, rubric sum) use `.superRefine`. Decimal inputs come in as number/string and the service converts them to `Prisma.Decimal` (NFR-1). |","-| FR-8 | SVC, DM | Offline marker: `attemptNumber = 0`, `text = null`, no files, `submittedAt = gradedAt`. **Edge case for design:** a student may later submit online against an offline-graded row (`status = SUBMITTED`, unique row). Recommend allowing it and treating it as a resubmission (move the attempt-0 grade into history and clear the grade), unless it is already RETURNED. |","+| FR-1 | DM | One migration, `add_quizzes`. 5 enums, 5 models. Back-relations on Course (`quizzes`) and User (attempts, accommodations, graded answers). QuizAnswer PK `(attemptId, questionId)` (NFR-2). QuizAccommodation unique `(quizId, studentId)`. Include the partial unique index from B10 in the SQL. Money-like fields (points, scores) are `Decimal(6,2)`, per the assignments precedent. |","+| FR-2 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`, client-safe, shared by the builder UI and the handlers. Use per-type question schemas as a discriminated union on `type`. `availableUntil > availableFrom` and the time-limit cross-field checks use `.superRefine`. |","+| FR-3 | PURE | `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. No Prisma import, so the builder preview and tests can use it. `gradeAnswer(question, response) → { points, flagged }`. Partial-credit formula from FR-3. Use Decimal and round with fixed2. |","+| FR-4 | PURE | Same module. `normalize = s.trim().replace(/\\s+/g,' ')`, with case-folding unless `caseSensitive` is set. A non-match returns `flagged: true` and 0 points. |","+| FR-5 | PURE | ESSAY → `{ points: null, flagged: true }`. `correct` holds the guidance text and is server-only (NFR-1). |","+| FR-6 | UI, AUTH | Server page `/courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit`, protected by assertCanManageCourse. The settings panel uses MUI x-date-pickers. The time-limit vs window check reuses the FR-2 validator on the client. |","+| FR-7 | UI | Sortable question list (@dnd-kit/sortable wrapping MUI items). Per-type editor components. Reorder calls `POST /questions/reorder`. |","+| FR-8 | UI | The points total is derived client-side. Preview mode reuses the player component with a `preview` prop. It gets data from the manager GET (with `correct`) and grades locally with the pure grading.ts. It **never calls the attempt endpoints**, so nothing is recorded. |","+| FR-9 | SVC, PURE | `canPublish(quiz, questions) → string[]` (pure, so it can be shared with the UI). The PATCH status→PUBLISHED transition enforces it server-side. Publishing triggers FR-29. |","+| FR-10 | SVC, API, AUD | A lock check runs when `attemptCount > 0` (`_count.attempts`). It whitelists `prompt/explanation/correct (SHORT_ANSWER only)` and returns CONFLICT with an explanation otherwise. `POST /api/quizzes/:id/regrade` re-runs gradeAnswer on non-manually-graded answers in one transaction, then recomputes attempt scores (FR-25 logic). It must not override teacher-graded answers (manual grade wins). |","+| FR-11 | CFG, UI, SVC | The course tab entry (B2). `GET /api/courses/:id/quizzes` is role-shaped. Teachers get aggregates (count, avg, needsGrading via groupBy). Students get bucketed rows (Upcoming / Available / Completed / **Missed = closed with zero attempts**, assumed). Parents get completed results only, scoped to the linked child. |","+| FR-12 | UI | Server page `/quizzes/[quizId]/take`. It resolves the course from the quiz and calls assertCanViewCourse (STUDENT). Attempts used/allowed uses FR-23. ConfirmDialog guards Start. |","+| FR-13 | SVC, PURE | Inside the start transaction: freeze `questionOrder: String[]`. Option order is a deterministic seeded shuffle (seed = attempt id). Use a pure `seededShuffle(items, seed)` (a small string hash + mulberry32) in grading.ts or a sibling. `deadlineAt = min(startedAt + (limit + extra) min, availableUntil)`. With no time limit, it is `availableUntil` (handoff risk 4). Pure `computeDeadline()`, unit-tested (NFR-8). |","+| FR-14 | UI | Player client component (MUI RadioGroup/FormGroup/TextField/LinearProgress, a navigator grid of Buttons). The sticky header timer is display-only (FR-16). The server returns `deadlineAt` and the client counts down from it. |","+| FR-15 | UI, API | `useAutosave` hook: 800 ms debounce per question, a localStorage queue keyed `quiz-attempt:<id>`, a 5 s retry interval, and `navigator.onLine`. Three-state pill. The server upsert is idempotent, so replays are safe. |","+| FR-16 | SVC, API | The answer PUT reads only the attempt row `{studentId, status, deadlineAt}` (NFR-2). Past `deadlineAt + 30 s` it calls submitAttempt(auto) and then throws CONFLICT. The client then routes to the submitted view. |","+| FR-17 | SVC, UI | `submitAttempt(attemptId, { auto })`, in one transaction. Grade every answer, create zero-score rows for unanswered questions, and set `score`, `submittedAt` and status (NEEDS_GRADING if anything is flagged, else GRADED). Guard with `updateMany where status = IN_PROGRESS` so double submits are no-ops (this also makes FR-18 idempotent). |","+| FR-18 | SVC, JOB | A lazy check on `GET /api/attempts/:id`, on `POST /attempts` (start/resume), and on the teacher list/grade loads: `if IN_PROGRESS && now > deadlineAt → submitAttempt({auto:true})`. `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` does a batch find + submitAttempt each (B3). |","+| FR-19 | DM, SVC | Start or resume: find the IN_PROGRESS attempt and return it. Otherwise create one. Rely on the partial unique index (B10), and on P2002 re-read. Two tabs end up on the same attempt id. |","+| FR-20 | PURE, SVC, API, AUD | `resultsVisible(quiz, now)`: IMMEDIATELY → true after submit, AFTER_CLOSE → `now ≥ availableUntil`, MANUAL → `resultsReleasedAt != null`. `POST /release-results` (manager) sets resultsReleasedAt, then audit + FR-30. This one predicate drives the NFR-1 serializer. |","+| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Result view. The serializer includes `correct` and explanation only when `resultsVisible && showCorrectAnswers`. Score and per-question points only when `resultsVisible`. |","+| FR-22 | SVC | `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId) → { score, maxScore, isPractice, attemptsCounted } \\| null`. HIGHEST/LATEST/AVERAGE over GRADED attempts (Decimal average, fixed2). An exported service function. No endpoint. |","+| FR-23 | SVC, PURE | `attemptLimit = maxAttempts + (accommodation?.extraAttempts ?? 0)`. Start throws CONFLICT when `count(attempts) ≥ limit` and there's no IN_PROGRESS attempt to resume. Pure helper, unit-tested. |","+| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH, AUD | Grade page with two modes (DataTable by student, or by question). `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId/grade` (manager): points 0..question.points step 0.5, plus feedback. Sets `gradedById/manuallyGraded`, then audit, then FR-25. |","+| FR-25 | SVC | After each grade: if no answer in the attempt is still ungraded, set status GRADED and recompute the score as Σ points. Recompute the score on every grade regardless, so overrides on GRADED attempts update it. |","+| FR-26 | SVC, API, UI | `GET /api/quizzes/:id/analytics` (manager). Aggregates are computed in TS over submitted attempts. The class sizes are small, so compute in memory. Median computed in code. Histogram with 10 buckets (100% goes in the last bucket). MUI X BarChart + StatCard. |","+| FR-27 | SVC, API | Per-question stats come from the same pass. The option distribution counts option ids in responses. `?format=csv` reuses `src/server/csv.ts` and returns text/csv with one row per attempt. |","+| FR-28 | API, DM, AUD | `PUT /api/quizzes/:id/accommodations/:studentId` upserts QuizAccommodation (manager). The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Changes apply only to attempts started later (deadlineAt is frozen at start). Note this for the UI copy. |","+| FR-29 | NOTIF | Fires on the first transition to PUBLISHED only (track `publishedAt` or check the previous status). Link `/quizzes/:id/take`. Recipients are ACTIVE enrollees. Skip if the quiz is practice? No: the PRD doesn't say, so send. |","+| FR-30 | NOTIF, JOB | MANUAL → on release (once, guarded by `resultsReleasedAt` going null→set). AFTER_CLOSE → the maintenance pass picks closed quizzes with `resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` (B4) and notifies students who submitted, plus their parents. IMMEDIATELY → never. |","+| FR-31 | API, AUTH | Routes under `src/app/api/{courses/[id]/quizzes, quizzes/[id], quizzes/[id]/questions, quizzes/[id]/questions/reorder, questions/[id]}`. DELETE quiz → CONFLICT if any attempt exists. Reorder accepts the full id list and rejects ids that don't match the quiz's set exactly. |","+| FR-32 | API, AUTH | `POST /api/quizzes/:id/attempts` (STUDENT, course view, quiz PUBLISHED and within its window). `GET /api/attempts/:id` (owner, linked parent once results are released, or manager). The answers PUT and the submit POST are owner-only. |","+| FR-33 | DM, SVC | `isPractice` is returned in FR-22's result. It counts for attempts and analytics like a graded quiz (intake assumption). |","+| FR-34 | AUTH | B1, reused unchanged. Add one helper, `assertCanAccessAttempt(user, attempt)`, in src/server/quiz/: owner, manager via assertCanManageCourse, or a PARENT linked to the student. Parent access is read-only and only when results are visible. |","+| FR-35 | JOB | B3. Both functions must be idempotent: FR-17's status guard and FR-30's claim column. |","+| FR-36 | SEED | Extend prisma/seed.ts. 'Fractions Check' (8 objective questions, closed, every MATH-7A student has a GRADED attempt; scores via grading.ts so the seed data is consistent). 'Unit 1 Test' (12 questions incl. 2 ESSAY, AFTER_CLOSE, window now → +3 days, no attempts). 'Parts of Speech' (ENG-7A, practice, maxAttempts 3, HIGHEST). The seed must be idempotent like the existing one (upsert by title + course). |","+| FR-37 | — | **No work** (LOW, assumed). No sidebar entry. The course tab covers it. Design should drop it explicitly. |","+| FR-38 | AUD | B7. Write after commit, inside the service functions, not in the handlers. |","+| FR-39 | UI, AUTH | MarkdownEditor/MarkdownView for prompts, FileUpload with a `'quiz'` context, and a resolver (B11). |","+| NFR-1 | AUTH, SVC, TEST | **Highest-risk item.** All student-facing reads (quiz GET, attempt GET, course list, answer-PUT response) go through `serializers.ts`. Prisma selects for student paths never select `correct`/`explanation` at all (defence in depth). The unit test asserts `'correct' in obj === false` recursively. |","+| NFR-2 | DM, SVC | The answer PUT does exactly one attempt read plus one upsert. Don't load the Question row: the questionId is validated against `attempt.questionOrder` (already on the attempt row). The response validator for the answer shape is type-agnostic (`string[] \\| string`). It is type-checked at grade time. |","+| NFR-3 | UI | Native inputs via MUI Radio/Checkbox. An `aria-live=\"assertive\"` region announces only at the 5:00 and 1:00 thresholds, not every tick. Keyboard nav for the navigator grid. The axe check is part of the e2e. |","+| NFR-4 | UI | MUI only. Look up each component through mui-mcp before use. This is a dev-phase obligation, so carry it into the plan. |","+| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every handler starts with requireUser/requireRole and then a course or attempt check. The server pages use requirePageRole. |","+| NFR-6 | API | withHandler + Zod parse. `{data}` / `paginated` envelopes. The course quiz list is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100). cuid ids, UTC timestamps. The UI formats dates with DateDisplay / formatInSchoolTz. |","+| NFR-7 | — | Constraint on all of the above: `src/server/quiz/` only, reuse B5–B9 and B14, no new deps, no console.log in app code. |","+| NFR-8 | TEST | Unit: grading.ts (partial credit incl. the FR-3 example, short-answer normalisation), computeDeadline + accommodations, scoring policies, serializer. Integration: autosave 409 after deadline+grace, auto-submit on GET, regrade. E2E: a single Playwright spec. |","+| NFR-9 | UI | Builder ergonomics: default type MULTIPLE/SINGLE_CHOICE, Enter adds an option row, and Duplicate. No architectural change. |","+| NFR-10 | — | Out of scope. Design must not add question banks, proctoring or LaTeX. |"," ","-### Assignment authoring (teacher)","+## 3. Cross-cutting decisions for `arch-design-system`"," ","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|---|---|---|","-| FR-9 | UI | `/courses/[courseId]/assignments/new` and an edit route (`[assignmentId]/edit`). MUI DateTimePicker (MUI X pickers, same version-alignment risk as D2) in the school timezone. It depends on D1 (FileUpload, MarkdownEditor). |","-| FR-10 | SVC | `nextTeachingDayDueAt(now, tz)`: a pure helper next to `schoolNow` in `src/lib/dates.ts`. Computed server-side and passed as a default prop (NFR-2). |","-| FR-11 | UI, VAL | The rubric builder uses `@dnd-kit/sortable`, which is already installed, for reorder. The rubric-sum check is in the Zod schema (shared), using Decimal sum, so the server rejects with VALIDATION_ERROR. The exact message string is required. |","-| FR-12 | UI, VAL | The status comes from the button. SCHEDULED requires `availableFrom > serverNow`, checked in the service, not only in Zod (Zod has no server clock guarantee). |","-| FR-13 | SVC | `isAssignmentVisible(a, now) = !archivedAt && isVisible({status, publishAt: availableFrom}, now)`. Use it in **every** student/parent read path, the file resolver, submission rules and reminders. It is the single source of truth. |","-| FR-14 | UI | Show the warning when the assignment is published and `submissionCount > 0`, and the dueAt or maxPoints changes. No recalculation happens on the server. Keep a `maxPointsChangedAt` banner? Simplest is a client-side banner on save success. **Design should pick one, and not add a column unless needed.** |","-| FR-15 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/duplicate {courseIds}`. Check `assertCanManageCourse` for **each** target. Make it one transaction per target. Copy the rubric and criteria as new rows (1:1), and copy the attachment bytes per B2. Status DRAFT, `notifiedAt` null. LOW confidence default: identical dueAt plus the availableFrom/lateCutoffAt offsets. |","+- **D1 Module layout (NFR-7):**","+  - `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (pure: gradeAnswer, seededShuffle, computeDeadline, attemptLimit, resultsVisible, canPublish, applyScoringPolicy)","+  - `quiz-service.ts` (CRUD, publish, lock, regrade, release, accommodations)","+  - `attempt-service.ts` (start/resume, saveAnswer, submit, lazy auto-submit, grade, getStudentQuizScore)","+  - `analytics.ts`","+  - `serializers.ts`","+  - `maintenance.ts` (autoSubmitExpiredAttempts, sendQuizResultsReleased)","+  - `access.ts` (assertCanAccessAttempt)"," ","-### Lists and navigation","+  Keep the pure helpers together in one file unless it grows past what one file reads comfortably.","+- **D2 Single submit path:** manual submit, deadline-PUT rejection, lazy load and the maintenance pass all call one `submitAttempt`. The `status = IN_PROGRESS` conditional update makes it idempotent and race-safe.","+- **D3 Visibility predicate:** one `resultsVisible()` drives the serializer, the parent access and the FR-11 \"score if visible\" display.","+- **D4 Frozen-at-start:** questionOrder, option order (via seed) and deadlineAt are fixed at start. Later accommodation or settings edits don't move in-flight attempts. FR-10 locks prevent structural changes anyway.","+- **D5 Manual grade precedence:** regrade (FR-10) only recomputes answers where `manuallyGraded = false`. If FR-1's QuizAnswer field list doesn't include such a flag, use `gradedById IS NULL` as the marker."," ","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|---|---|---|","-| FR-16 | CFG | Append `{key:'assignments', href:/courses/:id/assignments, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. |","-| FR-17 | UI, EP | The teacher table depends on D2 (DataTable compile break). The counts come from FR-48's manager shape using `groupBy` aggregates, not N+1 queries. |","-| FR-18 | UI, AUTH | Student groups: Upcoming / Past due (missing) / Submitted / Returned. A parent viewing a course needs a child context: use `?studentId=`, validated against `ParentStudentLink` **and** active enrollment in this course. Default to the only linked child enrolled. |","-| FR-19 | UI | Assignment page: sanitised Markdown (D1 MarkdownView), late-policy summary, rubric, and a countdown under 48 h. Compute the countdown client-side from a server-provided `serverNow` offset, so a skewed client clock doesn't show a wrong countdown. It is display-only (NFR-2). |","-| FR-20 | UI | The panel switches on submissionType. Draft autosave to `localStorage` keyed by `assignmentId:userId`. Clear it after a successful submit. |","-| FR-21 | UI | Reuse `ConfirmDialog`. |","-| FR-25 | UI | Receipt formatted with `formatInSchoolTz(submittedAt, \"EEE d MMM yyyy, HH:mm\", tz)` plus the attempt number. |","-| FR-26 | UI, AUTH | Grading fields appear only when `status = RETURNED` (FR-27). |","-| FR-27 | AUTH, SVC | **Response-shaping boundary.** One serializer `toStudentSubmission(sub)` removes `rawScore/penaltyPercent/finalScore/feedback/rubricScores/gradedAt/gradedById` unless the status is RETURNED. Every student/parent path uses it: FR-48, FR-50, FR-55, FR-57, FR-58 when the viewer is the student or parent. This covers NFR-4. |","-| FR-37 | UI, EP | `/assignments` STUDENT: 4 tabs plus a course filter, across ACTIVE enrollments. Missing = visible, not archived, `dueAt < now`, no submission, not exempt, `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (FR-60). Define one Prisma `where` builder `missingFilter(now)` and share it with the reminders (FR-43/45) and the counts. |","-| FR-38 | UI, AUTH | PARENT: a child selector using linked students only. The server validates `studentId` against `ParentStudentLink`. The view is read-only, so the submit panel is not rendered **and** the API rejects it (FR-53 is STUDENT-only). |","-| FR-39 | UI, EP | TEACHER \"To grade\": `status = SUBMITTED AND gradedAt IS NULL` in courses where `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`, ordered by `submittedAt asc`. ADMIN gets the same list across all courses (clarification default). |","-| FR-40 | CFG | One nav entry (B13). |","-| FR-41 | CFG, UI | studentTabs entry plus a page. It is invisible until a tab bar exists (blocker 5). Out of scope to build one here: do not add a tab-bar renderer just for this (NFR-15 scope / YAGNI), and surface it as a known gap. |","+## 4. Assumptions and open points to surface in the system-design Overview"," ","-### Submission (student)","-","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|---|---|---|","-| FR-22 | SVC, AUTH | Rule order: (1) the assignment is visible and not archived; (2) `role = STUDENT` and ACTIVE-enrolled; (3) not exempt; (4) `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (implied); (5) deadline: `now ≤ dueAt`, or `allowLate && (!lateCutoffAt || now ≤ lateCutoffAt)`. The exact error string is required. `now = new Date()` on the server only (NFR-2). |","-| FR-23 | SVC, TEST | Pure `lateDays(submittedAt, dueAt) = ceil((s − d) / 86_400_000)` for `s > d`, else 0. Use UTC milliseconds, so DST cannot affect it (NFR-9: a 24 h wall day across DST is 23/25 h of real time, and the PRD defines late days in 24 h units). Exactly 24 h gives 1. This is unit-test territory (NFR-14). |","-| FR-24 | SVC, DM | In one transaction: if a row exists, require `status = SUBMITTED` (RETURNED gives a VALIDATION/CONFLICT error), insert `SubmissionHistory` from the current row, `attemptNumber++`, clear the grade fields, replace the `SubmissionFile` rows, and attach the new files. Do not detach the old files (B1). Concurrency: two concurrent first submits hit the unique key. Catch P2002 and retry as a resubmit, or `upsert`. |","-| FR-53 | EP, VAL, AUTH | `POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions {text?, fileIds[]}`. Validation: `fileIds.length ≤ maxFileCount`; the content matches submissionType (text required for ONLINE_TEXT, files for FILE_UPLOAD, at least one for TEXT_AND_FILE); each file is `ownerId = me`, `context = 'submission'` and unattached, or already on this submission (B1). |","-","-### Grading (teacher)","-","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|---|---|---|","-| FR-28 | UI, EP | The left panel is fed by FR-54. Status chip derivation is a pure function: Exempt > Returned > Graded > Late > Submitted > Not submitted. Shared by the server (FR-54) and tests. |","-| FR-29 | UI | `<img>`/`<iframe src=\"/api/files/:id?inline=1\">`. **CSP check for design:** confirm that `next.config.js` `frame-src`/`img-src` allow `'self'`. The CSP `script-src` issue is blocker 4. The history dropdown reads FR-55 (manager-only history). |","-| FR-30 | UI, SVC | Rubric ToggleButtonGroup with an auto-sum. Penalty prefill `min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)`. The live final score uses decimal.js on the client too, so the preview and server values agree (NFR-1). The prefill is display-only. The server stores what is submitted, after FR-36 validation. |","-| FR-31 | SVC, TEST | `finalScore = raw × (1 − p/100)`, computed with `Decimal`, `toDecimalPlaces(2, ROUND_HALF_UP)`. One pure function in the service, unit-tested (18 at 20 % = 14.40). |","-| FR-32 | EP, SVC, NOTIF | \"Save\" = `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade`. \"Save & return\" = the same call with `{return:true}`, or grade followed by return. **Design should pick a single round trip.** The bulk route is `POST /api/assignments/:id/return {submissionIds?}`, with the default `gradedAt not null AND status ≠ RETURNED`. Each return sets RETURNED and returnedAt, fires FR-44, and writes an audit (FR-59). |","-| FR-33 | UI | A keydown listener on the grading page. Ignore J/K when `event.target` is an input, textarea or contenteditable. Ctrl/Cmd+Enter always works. Accessibility: show the shortcuts in a help hint (NFR-17). |","-| FR-34 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}`. The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Reject it if a submission already exists (grade that one instead). Creates the FR-8 row with the grade fields set, penalty 0, and an audit row. |","-| FR-35 | EP, SVC | `PUT/DELETE /api/assignments/:id/exemptions/:studentId`. Idempotent (`upsert` / `deleteMany`). Writes an audit row. Its effects come through `missingFilter` and the FR-22 rule. A PRD-11 exclusion flag = the GradeExemption row itself, so no extra column. |","-| FR-36 | VAL, SVC | Server-side, Decimal-based: `0 ≤ raw ≤ maxPoints` (×1.2 if allowExtraCredit). Each rubric score `0 ≤ points ≤ criterion.maxPoints` (extra credit is raw-only, per the clarification), and each `criterionId` belongs to this rubric. `0 ≤ penalty ≤ 100`. With a rubric, should raw equal the sum of the rubric points? The PRD says it auto-sums but stays overridable only via the penalty. **Recommend the server enforces raw = Σ rubric points when rubricScores are given.** |","-| FR-54 | EP | `GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions` (manage). LEFT JOIN of ACTIVE enrollments × submissions × exemptions. Paginate per NFR-7, but grading needs all students for J/K: allow `pageSize` up to 100 and document the limit. |","-| FR-55 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/submissions/:id`: the submitter, linked parents or course managers. History only for managers. Grade fields go through the FR-27 serializer for the student and parent. Also needed by NFR-3 prefetch. |","-| FR-56 | EP, SVC | Sets `gradedById`, `gradedAt` and the computed `finalScore`. Does not change status (it stays SUBMITTED until return). Writes an audit row. |","-| FR-59 | SVC | `audit()` on grade, return (one row per submission, or one bulk row with the ids; **design should pick**), exempt/unexempt and offline grade. |","-","-### Assignment API","-","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|---|---|---|","-| FR-48 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/courses/:id/assignments`. Two response shapes depending on `canSeeDrafts`. Students and parents get FR-13-visible, non-archived assignments plus their own submission state (via the FR-27 serializer). |","-| FR-49 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/courses/:id/assignments`. One transaction: rubric and criteria, assignment, attachments (`attachFiles` with `'assignment'`, contextId = assignment.id), and on PUBLISHED the FR-42 notify after commit. |","-| FR-50 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/assignments/:id`. A non-manager on an invisible/archived assignment gets NOT_FOUND, not FORBIDDEN, so existence is not leaked. Includes `serverNow` for FR-19. |","-| FR-51 | EP, SVC | PATCH: re-validate the rubric sum against maxPoints. Diff the attachments (detach the removed ones, which are then purged after 24 h per B1; that is fine for assignment attachments). DRAFT→PUBLISHED triggers FR-42. DELETE: hard delete if there are 0 submissions (cascade; the attachment files are detached first so the purge reclaims them), else set `archivedAt`. |","-| FR-52 | AUTH, SVC | Covered by `isAssignmentVisible` (FR-13), which includes `!archivedAt`. One check, applied everywhere. LOW confidence default. |","-| FR-57 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab=`. Role switch: STUDENT gets its own data; PARENT requires a linked `studentId`; TEACHER/ADMIN get To grade. `tab ∈ upcoming/missing/submitted/returned`. |","-| FR-58 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/students/:id/assignments` → `assertCanViewStudent`, then the same query as the FR-57 student view, built with a shared service function. A student or parent viewer gets the FR-27 serializer. Teachers and admins see grades? The PRD says \"same per-student data\", so **recommend the same serializer for all non-managers and full fields for the student's course managers.** Design should confirm. |","-","-### Notifications and maintenance","-","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|---|---|---|","-| FR-42 | NOTIF, SVC | Exactly once: `UPDATE assignment SET notifiedAt = now WHERE id = ? AND notifiedAt IS NULL` (`updateMany`, count = 1 → send). Triggered on publish (FR-49/51), and for SCHEDULED assignments in the student list read path (FR-48/57) when visible and `notifiedAt` is null. **A side effect on GET:** keep it fire-and-forget after the response data is built, and never fail the read. Design may also add it to `sendDueReminders` as a safety net, but must not do both without the atomic guard (the guard makes both safe). |","-| FR-43 | JOB, NOTIF | `sendDueReminders(now)` in `src/server/assignments/reminders.ts`, called on every dispatcher call (B8). The window is `dueAt − 24h ≤ now < dueAt`. Targets: ACTIVE-enrolled, no submission, not exempt, visible, not archived, not NO_SUBMISSION. Idempotent via FR-6. Bound the query (only assignments with `dueAt` in [now, now+24h]). |","-| FR-44 | NOTIF | On return: `notifyStudentAndParents` with a body like `\"{course}: {title} — {finalScore}/{maxPoints}\"`. Bulk return sends one notify per student. |","-| FR-45 | JOB, NOTIF | In the same pass: `now ≥ dueAt + 24h`, with the `missingFilter` targets. Parents only (`notify` to the linked parent ids). FR-6 kind 'missing'. Bound the query to avoid scanning all history, e.g. `dueAt` in [now − 8 d, now − 24 h], with a `ponytail:` note on that window. |","-| FR-46 | CFG | Four keys (B9). |","-| FR-47 | AUTH | `assignmentResolver`: load the assignment and course, then `assertCanViewCourse`, then `canSeeDrafts \\|\\| isAssignmentVisible`. `submissionResolver`: load the submission; allow the submitting student, a linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`) or `canSeeDrafts(course)` (managers/ADMIN). Deny everyone else, including other students (NFR-4, AC-10). Integration test needed. |","-","-### Seed","-","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|---|---|---|","-| FR-60 | SVC | Exclude NO_SUBMISSION in `missingFilter` and the reminder targets. The submission panel is hidden and FR-53 rejects. LOW confidence default. |","-| FR-61 | SEED | Idempotent: look up the courses by code and skip if they are missing. Upsert the assignments by `(courseId, title)`. Seed Decimal scores via strings. Seeded attachments/files are not required, so skip byte storage. |","-","-### Non-functional","-","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","-|---|---|---|","-| NFR-1 | SVC, VAL | Decimal end to end: Prisma `Decimal(6,2)` columns, `Prisma.Decimal` in the service, decimal.js in the client preview. Serialize Decimals in API responses as **strings**, to avoid float loss in JSON. Design must state this convention for api-contracts. |","-| NFR-2 | SVC | Every deadline, visibility or reminder check uses `new Date()` on the server. There is no client timestamp field in any request schema. |","-| NFR-3 | UI, EP | Prefetch the next and previous `GET /api/submissions/:id` into a client cache keyed by id (a plain `Map` in the grading page; no data-fetching library added). The <300 ms target is a client switch from cache. |","-| NFR-4 | AUTH | Enforced at three boundaries: the FR-27 serializer, the FR-47 file resolvers, and query scoping (a student only ever queries `studentId = me`). |","-| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every route: `requireUser`/`requireRole`, then assertCan*. Every page: `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`. |","-| NFR-6 | UI | MUI 9.5.0 + MUI X only, with mui-mcp lookups before use. Components needed: List, Chip, ToggleButtonGroup, Dialog, Tabs, DataGrid (D2), DateTimePicker, Autocomplete, Snackbar. Hard blocker if mui-mcp is unreachable (blocker 8). |","-| NFR-7 | EP | Thin handlers. `{data}` / paginated / `{error}` envelopes via the http.ts helpers. |","-| NFR-8 | CFG | `src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts`, plus `reminders.ts` and pure `scoring.ts` (lateDays, penalty, finalScore, chip status) for unit tests. Validators in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`. |","-| NFR-9 | SVC, TEST | Store UTC. Display via formatInSchoolTz. Late days in UTC ms (FR-23). The FR-10 default uses `fromZonedTime`. |","-| NFR-10 | UI | react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize are installed, with MUI component mapping (D1). |","-| NFR-11 | — | Reuse list: B1–B10, B15. |","-| NFR-12 | — | Use the logger, never console.log. |","-| NFR-13 | TEST, CFG | Blocker 3: fix the `vitest.config.ts` import to `'vitest/config'` (a one-line fix, in scope because NFR-13 requires a working `npm test`). |","-| NFR-14 | TEST | Unit: scoring.ts. Integration: resubmit history, return, reminder idempotency, exemption vs missing, and the file resolvers (AC-10). E2E: the full flow plus the parent missing list (needs bypassCSP, blocker 4). |","-| NFR-15 | — | No gradebook, peer review, group work or annotation. FR-35 stores the exemption only, and PRD-11 consumes it. |","-| NFR-16 | UI | Two-minute publish: sensible defaults (FR-10 due date, max points 100?, submissionType FILE_UPLOAD?). **Design should set the form defaults.** 30-submission keyboard grading via FR-33 + NFR-3. |","-| NFR-17 | UI | Labelled inputs and keyboard-operable controls: the ToggleButtonGroup and the J/K help hint. |","-","-## Decisions arch-design-system must make (answers to the intake blockers)","-","-| # | Blocker / gap | Recommendation |","-|---|---|---|","-| D1 | Blocker 1: PRD-08 UI components are missing. | Build the **minimum** shared components in this ticket: `src/components/MarkdownView` (react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, mapped to MUI), `src/components/MarkdownEditor` (MUI TextField multiline + a Write/Preview Tabs toggle using MarkdownView; no new editor dependency), `src/components/FileUpload` (input type=file → `POST /api/files` with the context field, list with remove, `maxFiles` prop) and `FileList` (links to `/api/files/:id`). Shape them so PRD-08 can adopt them later. Do not build PRD-08's remaining scope. |","-| D2 | Blocker 2: the MUI X DataGrid compile break. | Preferred: align `@mui/x-*` versions in package.json/lockfile (it also unblocks the DateTimePicker from `@mui/x-date-pickers`, if that package shares the internals). Fallback for FR-17: an MUI `Table`, which needs no DataGrid. `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0 **is installed** (package.json L34). It very likely has the same `@mui/x-internals` 9.15.0 mismatch, so FR-9's DateTimePicker is also at risk. That makes aligning the versions the real fix, rather than a Table workaround. |","-| D3 | Blockers 3/4: vitest import and CSP. | vitest: one-line import fix. CSP: keep `bypassCSP` in Playwright as before. A CSP fix is outside the PRD scope (NFR-15). Note the FR-29 iframe/img `'self'` dependency. |","-| D4 | Blocker 5: the studentTabs renderer. | Register the tab and build the page. Do not build a tab bar. Report it as a known gap. |","-| D5 | Decimal JSON serialization | Decimal fields are strings in API responses (NFR-1). |","-| D6 | The \"Save & return\" round trip | `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade` with an optional `return: true` gives one transaction. |","-| D7 | Rubric raw score | When rubricScores are present, the server sets or enforces `rawScore = Σ points`. |","-| D8 | Teacher/admin view of FR-58 grade fields | Course managers get full fields. Other viewers get the FR-27 serializer. |","-| D9 | Offline-graded row followed by an online submit | Treat it as a resubmission while it is not RETURNED. |","-| D10 | Missing-reminder query window | Bound it (e.g. dueAt within the last 8 days), marked with a `ponytail:` note. |","-","-## Shared pure functions (single source of truth; unit-test targets)","-","-`isAssignmentVisible`, `missingFilter(now)` (Prisma where), `lateDays`, `defaultPenalty`, `computeFinalScore`, `rubricTotal`, `submissionChipStatus`, `nextTeachingDayDueAt`, `toStudentSubmission` (serializer). Each of these is used by two or more call sites listed above. Keeping one copy of each prevents the drift that leads to privacy and correctness bugs (NFR-1, NFR-4).","+1. FR-37: no sidebar entry (LOW).","+2. Missed = closed with zero attempts by that student.","+3. Regrade runs only on the explicit action. Editing accepted answers doesn't auto-regrade.","+4. Practice quizzes count toward attempts and analytics. They are excluded only from the gradebook (FR-22's caller filters on isPractice).","+5. `quiz.results_released` defaultEmail = true. The PRD doesn't specify it.","+6. FR-30's AFTER_CLOSE \"sent once\" needs a marker. B4 proposes `Quiz.resultsNotifiedAt`, which is an addition to FR-1's \"exactly as listed\" model. If that isn't acceptable, use a claim table.","+7. Accommodation changes affect only attempts started after the change.","+8. Intake handoff blockers: **none**."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-9\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T09:00:00Z), PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions (SCH-009). It has 61 FRs and 17 NFRs (78 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers. They must be surfaced in the `system-design.md` Overview (compliance rule 5). Decisions D1–D4 below answer them.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-8 leftovers** as of this writing. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-9 input.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-9 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` sets `context` and `contextId` on unattached files owned by the caller (any file for ADMIN). It does **not** check the file's upload context. `detachFiles` sets `contextId = null`, and `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes those files after 24 h. | src/server/files/files-service.ts L215-245, purge.ts | FR-53 requires uploads with context `'submission'`. The service must check `context === 'submission'` before calling attachFiles. On resubmission, **never detach the previous attempt's files**: `SubmissionHistory.fileIds` points at them, and detaching would let the purge delete history bytes. Keep them attached to the same submission id. |\n| B2 | `FileObject.storageKey` is `@unique`, and a FileObject holds a single `(context, contextId)`. `storage.ts` exports `saveFile(stream)`, `readFile(key)` and `deleteFile`. | schema L564-578, storage.ts | FR-15 duplicate **cannot share** attachment rows. For each target course, copy the bytes (`readFile` → `saveFile`), create a new FileObject (context `'assignment'`), then attach it. |\n| B3 | `FileObject` has a back-relation `lessonAttachments LessonAttachment[]`. | schema L577 | FR-3/FR-4 add back-relations `assignmentAttachments` and `submissionFiles` to FileObject. This is an additive edit to an existing model, so NFR-11 allows it. |\n| B4 | `canAccessFile` order: unattached → owner/ADMIN; registered resolver; unknown context → owner/ADMIN. Resolver errors deny. `registerBuiltInContexts` currently registers `lesson` and `logo`. | access.ts L35-50, contexts.ts L36-39 | FR-47 adds `assignmentResolver` (contextId = assignmentId) and `submissionResolver` (contextId = submissionId) in contexts.ts. Before submit, a student's own upload is unattached, so it is already readable by owner/ADMIN only. |\n| B5 | `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` is a pure read-time check: PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt ≤ now. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` covers ADMIN, teacher and co-teacher. | visibility.ts | FR-13 can reuse both by mapping `availableFrom → publishAt`. Widen the `Publishable.status` type to accept `AssignmentStatus`, which has the same string values, rather than writing a second helper (NFR-11). |\n| B6 | `assertCanViewCourse` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child (`studentLinks`). `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Errors are `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These already provide all of NFR-5's course checks. A parent who views a course still needs to be scoped to *which* child (FR-18, FR-38). |\n| B7 | `ParentStudentLink {parentId, studentId}`. `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds, ...})` never throws. | notify.ts L98-117 | FR-44 uses it as-is. For FR-45 (parents only), call `notify()` with the parent ids from `parentStudentLink`. |\n| B8 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` **on every call**. Purges run in a once-per-day `if` (`lastPurgeAt`, in memory). | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-43/FR-45: call `sendDueReminders(now)` on **every** call, outside the daily block (due_soon has a 24 h window, so daily would miss it). Wrap it in its own try/catch + logger, like the purges. |\n| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object with `{label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. `content.lesson_published` is the closest precedent. | types.ts L33, L90-100 | FR-46: add four keys. Roles: `published` [STUDENT]; `due_soon` [STUDENT]; `returned` [STUDENT, PARENT]; `missing` [PARENT], with defaultEmail true. |\n| B10 | `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, tz)` and `schoolNow(now, tz)` live in `src/lib/dates.ts`, using date-fns-tz, which is already installed. | dates.ts | FR-10 next-teaching-day 23:59 and FR-25 receipt formatting. Convert wall time to UTC with date-fns-tz `fromZonedTime` (NFR-9 DST). |\n| B11 | `SchoolDay {dayOfWeek 1-7, isTeaching}` is seeded with all 7 rows. | schema L477-480 | FR-10 loops forward at most 7 days. If no day is teaching, fall back to tomorrow. |\n| B12 | `courseTabs` = overview, roster, attendance (there is **no content tab**: PRD-08 UI is missing). It is rendered by `CourseTabs.tsx`. `src/app/(app)/students/[id]/` has `attendance/` and `courses/` but no tab bar. | course-tabs.ts, ls | FR-16: append one entry with ALL_ROLES. FR-41: register the entry plus the page `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx`. It stays unreachable through tabs (blocker 5), but direct URLs work. |\n| B13 | `navigation.ts` entries are `{label, href, icon, roles, group?}`. | navigation.ts L31-38 | FR-40: one entry with roles [STUDENT, PARENT, TEACHER]. Default ADMIN to the \"To grade\" view through the API (clarification). Add ADMIN to the nav only if design adopts that default. |\n| B14 | `src/server/assignments/` and `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` do not exist. Validator precedent: `src/lib/validators/content.ts`. HTTP helpers: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` and `AppError` in `src/server/http.ts`. | ls, grep | Greenfield feature folder (NFR-8). Route handlers follow NFR-7 using the existing helpers. |\n| B15 | Existing components: ConfirmDialog, DataTable, DateDisplay, EmptyState, FormField, LoadingSkeleton, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker. **There is no** FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView or MarkdownEditor. | ls src/components | Blocker 1, see D1. |\n| B16 | Tests live in `tests/{unit,integration,e2e}`. | ls | NFR-14 placement. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = service logic · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = maintenance pass · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = registry/config · **NOTIF** = notification · **TEST** = test · **SEED** = seed data\n\n### Data model (one migration: FR-1…FR-6)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | New enums `SubmissionType`, `AssignmentStatus`, `SubmissionStatus`. Do not reuse `ContentStatus`, because the PRD names a new enum (the values happen to match, and B5 relies on that). |\n| FR-2 | DM | `Assignment` with `allowExtraCredit`, `notifiedAt?`, `archivedAt?`, `rubricId String? @unique`, Course relation with Cascade, and `@@index([courseId, dueAt])`. Add the back-relation `assignments Assignment[]` on Course. |\n| FR-3 | DM | `AssignmentAttachment` (join to FileObject, back-relation per B3), `Rubric`, `RubricCriterion` (`maxPoints Decimal(6,2)`, `order Int`, `levels Json`). A 1:1 Rubric↔Assignment via `rubricId @unique` means a rubric is never shared, so delete it together with the assignment. |\n| FR-4 | DM | `Submission @@unique([assignmentId, studentId])`, which means one row per student. Attempts live in `SubmissionHistory`. The Decimal fields are `rawScore`, `penaltyPercent` and `finalScore`. `rubricScores Json`. `SubmissionFile` join, back-relation per B3. `SubmissionHistory.fileIds String[]` has no FK, so the files must not be purged (B1). |\n| FR-5 | DM | `GradeExemption @@id([assignmentId, studentId])`. Cascade on assignment delete. |\n| FR-6 | DM | `AssignmentReminder @@unique([assignmentId, studentId, kind])`. `kind` is a String ('due_soon' / 'missing'). Insert with `createMany({skipDuplicates:true})`, or catch P2002, and send only for the rows actually inserted (idempotent under concurrent dispatchers). |\n| FR-7 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`, shared by client forms and route handlers. Cross-field rules (`lateCutoffAt > dueAt`, rubric sum) use `.superRefine`. Decimal inputs come in as number/string and the service converts them to `Prisma.Decimal` (NFR-1). |\n| FR-8 | SVC, DM | Offline marker: `attemptNumber = 0`, `text = null`, no files, `submittedAt = gradedAt`. **Edge case for design:** a student may later submit online against an offline-graded row (`status = SUBMITTED`, unique row). Recommend allowing it and treating it as a resubmission (move the attempt-0 grade into history and clear the grade), unless it is already RETURNED. |\n\n### Assignment authoring (teacher)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-9 | UI | `/courses/[courseId]/assignments/new` and an edit route (`[assignmentId]/edit`). MUI DateTimePicker (MUI X pickers, same version-alignment risk as D2) in the school timezone. It depends on D1 (FileUpload, MarkdownEditor). |\n| FR-10 | SVC | `nextTeachingDayDueAt(now, tz)`: a pure helper next to `schoolNow` in `src/lib/dates.ts`. Computed server-side and passed as a default prop (NFR-2). |\n| FR-11 | UI, VAL | The rubric builder uses `@dnd-kit/sortable`, which is already installed, for reorder. The rubric-sum check is in the Zod schema (shared), using Decimal sum, so the server rejects with VALIDATION_ERROR. The exact message string is required. |\n| FR-12 | UI, VAL | The status comes from the button. SCHEDULED requires `availableFrom > serverNow`, checked in the service, not only in Zod (Zod has no server clock guarantee). |\n| FR-13 | SVC | `isAssignmentVisible(a, now) = !archivedAt && isVisible({status, publishAt: availableFrom}, now)`. Use it in **every** student/parent read path, the file resolver, submission rules and reminders. It is the single source of truth. |\n| FR-14 | UI | Show the warning when the assignment is published and `submissionCount > 0`, and the dueAt or maxPoints changes. No recalculation happens on the server. Keep a `maxPointsChangedAt` banner? Simplest is a client-side banner on save success. **Design should pick one, and not add a column unless needed.** |\n| FR-15 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/duplicate {courseIds}`. Check `assertCanManageCourse` for **each** target. Make it one transaction per target. Copy the rubric and criteria as new rows (1:1), and copy the attachment bytes per B2. Status DRAFT, `notifiedAt` null. LOW confidence default: identical dueAt plus the availableFrom/lateCutoffAt offsets. |\n\n### Lists and navigation\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-16 | CFG | Append `{key:'assignments', href:/courses/:id/assignments, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. |\n| FR-17 | UI, EP | The teacher table depends on D2 (DataTable compile break). The counts come from FR-48's manager shape using `groupBy` aggregates, not N+1 queries. |\n| FR-18 | UI, AUTH | Student groups: Upcoming / Past due (missing) / Submitted / Returned. A parent viewing a course needs a child context: use `?studentId=`, validated against `ParentStudentLink` **and** active enrollment in this course. Default to the only linked child enrolled. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Assignment page: sanitised Markdown (D1 MarkdownView), late-policy summary, rubric, and a countdown under 48 h. Compute the countdown client-side from a server-provided `serverNow` offset, so a skewed client clock doesn't show a wrong countdown. It is display-only (NFR-2). |\n| FR-20 | UI | The panel switches on submissionType. Draft autosave to `localStorage` keyed by `assignmentId:userId`. Clear it after a successful submit. |\n| FR-21 | UI | Reuse `ConfirmDialog`. |\n| FR-25 | UI | Receipt formatted with `formatInSchoolTz(submittedAt, \"EEE d MMM yyyy, HH:mm\", tz)` plus the attempt number. |\n| FR-26 | UI, AUTH | Grading fields appear only when `status = RETURNED` (FR-27). |\n| FR-27 | AUTH, SVC | **Response-shaping boundary.** One serializer `toStudentSubmission(sub)` removes `rawScore/penaltyPercent/finalScore/feedback/rubricScores/gradedAt/gradedById` unless the status is RETURNED. Every student/parent path uses it: FR-48, FR-50, FR-55, FR-57, FR-58 when the viewer is the student or parent. This covers NFR-4. |\n| FR-37 | UI, EP | `/assignments` STUDENT: 4 tabs plus a course filter, across ACTIVE enrollments. Missing = visible, not archived, `dueAt < now`, no submission, not exempt, `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (FR-60). Define one Prisma `where` builder `missingFilter(now)` and share it with the reminders (FR-43/45) and the counts. |\n| FR-38 | UI, AUTH | PARENT: a child selector using linked students only. The server validates `studentId` against `ParentStudentLink`. The view is read-only, so the submit panel is not rendered **and** the API rejects it (FR-53 is STUDENT-only). |\n| FR-39 | UI, EP | TEACHER \"To grade\": `status = SUBMITTED AND gradedAt IS NULL` in courses where `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`, ordered by `submittedAt asc`. ADMIN gets the same list across all courses (clarification default). |\n| FR-40 | CFG | One nav entry (B13). |\n| FR-41 | CFG, UI | studentTabs entry plus a page. It is invisible until a tab bar exists (blocker 5). Out of scope to build one here: do not add a tab-bar renderer just for this (NFR-15 scope / YAGNI), and surface it as a known gap. |\n\n### Submission (student)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-22 | SVC, AUTH | Rule order: (1) the assignment is visible and not archived; (2) `role = STUDENT` and ACTIVE-enrolled; (3) not exempt; (4) `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (implied); (5) deadline: `now ≤ dueAt`, or `allowLate && (!lateCutoffAt || now ≤ lateCutoffAt)`. The exact error string is required. `now = new Date()` on the server only (NFR-2). |\n| FR-23 | SVC, TEST | Pure `lateDays(submittedAt, dueAt) = ceil((s − d) / 86_400_000)` for `s > d`, else 0. Use UTC milliseconds, so DST cannot affect it (NFR-9: a 24 h wall day across DST is 23/25 h of real time, and the PRD defines late days in 24 h units). Exactly 24 h gives 1. This is unit-test territory (NFR-14). |\n| FR-24 | SVC, DM | In one transaction: if a row exists, require `status = SUBMITTED` (RETURNED gives a VALIDATION/CONFLICT error), insert `SubmissionHistory` from the current row, `attemptNumber++`, clear the grade fields, replace the `SubmissionFile` rows, and attach the new files. Do not detach the old files (B1). Concurrency: two concurrent first submits hit the unique key. Catch P2002 and retry as a resubmit, or `upsert`. |\n| FR-53 | EP, VAL, AUTH | `POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions {text?, fileIds[]}`. Validation: `fileIds.length ≤ maxFileCount`; the content matches submissionType (text required for ONLINE_TEXT, files for FILE_UPLOAD, at least one for TEXT_AND_FILE); each file is `ownerId = me`, `context = 'submission'` and unattached, or already on this submission (B1). |\n\n### Grading (teacher)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-28 | UI, EP | The left panel is fed by FR-54. Status chip derivation is a pure function: Exempt > Returned > Graded > Late > Submitted > Not submitted. Shared by the server (FR-54) and tests. |\n| FR-29 | UI | `<img>`/`<iframe src=\"/api/files/:id?inline=1\">`. **CSP check for design:** confirm that `next.config.js` `frame-src`/`img-src` allow `'self'`. The CSP `script-src` issue is blocker 4. The history dropdown reads FR-55 (manager-only history). |\n| FR-30 | UI, SVC | Rubric ToggleButtonGroup with an auto-sum. Penalty prefill `min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)`. The live final score uses decimal.js on the client too, so the preview and server values agree (NFR-1). The prefill is display-only. The server stores what is submitted, after FR-36 validation. |\n| FR-31 | SVC, TEST | `finalScore = raw × (1 − p/100)`, computed with `Decimal`, `toDecimalPlaces(2, ROUND_HALF_UP)`. One pure function in the service, unit-tested (18 at 20 % = 14.40). |\n| FR-32 | EP, SVC, NOTIF | \"Save\" = `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade`. \"Save & return\" = the same call with `{return:true}`, or grade followed by return. **Design should pick a single round trip.** The bulk route is `POST /api/assignments/:id/return {submissionIds?}`, with the default `gradedAt not null AND status ≠ RETURNED`. Each return sets RETURNED and returnedAt, fires FR-44, and writes an audit (FR-59). |\n| FR-33 | UI | A keydown listener on the grading page. Ignore J/K when `event.target` is an input, textarea or contenteditable. Ctrl/Cmd+Enter always works. Accessibility: show the shortcuts in a help hint (NFR-17). |\n| FR-34 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}`. The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Reject it if a submission already exists (grade that one instead). Creates the FR-8 row with the grade fields set, penalty 0, and an audit row. |\n| FR-35 | EP, SVC | `PUT/DELETE /api/assignments/:id/exemptions/:studentId`. Idempotent (`upsert` / `deleteMany`). Writes an audit row. Its effects come through `missingFilter` and the FR-22 rule. A PRD-11 exclusion flag = the GradeExemption row itself, so no extra column. |\n| FR-36 | VAL, SVC | Server-side, Decimal-based: `0 ≤ raw ≤ maxPoints` (×1.2 if allowExtraCredit). Each rubric score `0 ≤ points ≤ criterion.maxPoints` (extra credit is raw-only, per the clarification), and each `criterionId` belongs to this rubric. `0 ≤ penalty ≤ 100`. With a rubric, should raw equal the sum of the rubric points? The PRD says it auto-sums but stays overridable only via the penalty. **Recommend the server enforces raw = Σ rubric points when rubricScores are given.** |\n| FR-54 | EP | `GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions` (manage). LEFT JOIN of ACTIVE enrollments × submissions × exemptions. Paginate per NFR-7, but grading needs all students for J/K: allow `pageSize` up to 100 and document the limit. |\n| FR-55 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/submissions/:id`: the submitter, linked parents or course managers. History only for managers. Grade fields go through the FR-27 serializer for the student and parent. Also needed by NFR-3 prefetch. |\n| FR-56 | EP, SVC | Sets `gradedById`, `gradedAt` and the computed `finalScore`. Does not change status (it stays SUBMITTED until return). Writes an audit row. |\n| FR-59 | SVC | `audit()` on grade, return (one row per submission, or one bulk row with the ids; **design should pick**), exempt/unexempt and offline grade. |\n\n### Assignment API\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-48 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/courses/:id/assignments`. Two response shapes depending on `canSeeDrafts`. Students and parents get FR-13-visible, non-archived assignments plus their own submission state (via the FR-27 serializer). |\n| FR-49 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/courses/:id/assignments`. One transaction: rubric and criteria, assignment, attachments (`attachFiles` with `'assignment'`, contextId = assignment.id), and on PUBLISHED the FR-42 notify after commit. |\n| FR-50 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/assignments/:id`. A non-manager on an invisible/archived assignment gets NOT_FOUND, not FORBIDDEN, so existence is not leaked. Includes `serverNow` for FR-19. |\n| FR-51 | EP, SVC | PATCH: re-validate the rubric sum against maxPoints. Diff the attachments (detach the removed ones, which are then purged after 24 h per B1; that is fine for assignment attachments). DRAFT→PUBLISHED triggers FR-42. DELETE: hard delete if there are 0 submissions (cascade; the attachment files are detached first so the purge reclaims them), else set `archivedAt`. |\n| FR-52 | AUTH, SVC | Covered by `isAssignmentVisible` (FR-13), which includes `!archivedAt`. One check, applied everywhere. LOW confidence default. |\n| FR-57 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab=`. Role switch: STUDENT gets its own data; PARENT requires a linked `studentId`; TEACHER/ADMIN get To grade. `tab ∈ upcoming/missing/submitted/returned`. |\n| FR-58 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/students/:id/assignments` → `assertCanViewStudent`, then the same query as the FR-57 student view, built with a shared service function. A student or parent viewer gets the FR-27 serializer. Teachers and admins see grades? The PRD says \"same per-student data\", so **recommend the same serializer for all non-managers and full fields for the student's course managers.** Design should confirm. |\n\n### Notifications and maintenance\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-42 | NOTIF, SVC | Exactly once: `UPDATE assignment SET notifiedAt = now WHERE id = ? AND notifiedAt IS NULL` (`updateMany`, count = 1 → send). Triggered on publish (FR-49/51), and for SCHEDULED assignments in the student list read path (FR-48/57) when visible and `notifiedAt` is null. **A side effect on GET:** keep it fire-and-forget after the response data is built, and never fail the read. Design may also add it to `sendDueReminders` as a safety net, but must not do both without the atomic guard (the guard makes both safe). |\n| FR-43 | JOB, NOTIF | `sendDueReminders(now)` in `src/server/assignments/reminders.ts`, called on every dispatcher call (B8). The window is `dueAt − 24h ≤ now < dueAt`. Targets: ACTIVE-enrolled, no submission, not exempt, visible, not archived, not NO_SUBMISSION. Idempotent via FR-6. Bound the query (only assignments with `dueAt` in [now, now+24h]). |\n| FR-44 | NOTIF | On return: `notifyStudentAndParents` with a body like `\"{course}: {title} — {finalScore}/{maxPoints}\"`. Bulk return sends one notify per student. |\n| FR-45 | JOB, NOTIF | In the same pass: `now ≥ dueAt + 24h`, with the `missingFilter` targets. Parents only (`notify` to the linked parent ids). FR-6 kind 'missing'. Bound the query to avoid scanning all history, e.g. `dueAt` in [now − 8 d, now − 24 h], with a `ponytail:` note on that window. |\n| FR-46 | CFG | Four keys (B9). |\n| FR-47 | AUTH | `assignmentResolver`: load the assignment and course, then `assertCanViewCourse`, then `canSeeDrafts \\|\\| isAssignmentVisible`. `submissionResolver`: load the submission; allow the submitting student, a linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`) or `canSeeDrafts(course)` (managers/ADMIN). Deny everyone else, including other students (NFR-4, AC-10). Integration test needed. |\n\n### Seed\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-60 | SVC | Exclude NO_SUBMISSION in `missingFilter` and the reminder targets. The submission panel is hidden and FR-53 rejects. LOW confidence default. |\n| FR-61 | SEED | Idempotent: look up the courses by code and skip if they are missing. Upsert the assignments by `(courseId, title)`. Seed Decimal scores via strings. Seeded attachments/files are not required, so skip byte storage. |\n\n### Non-functional\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| NFR-1 | SVC, VAL | Decimal end to end: Prisma `Decimal(6,2)` columns, `Prisma.Decimal` in the service, decimal.js in the client preview. Serialize Decimals in API responses as **strings**, to avoid float loss in JSON. Design must state this convention for api-contracts. |\n| NFR-2 | SVC | Every deadline, visibility or reminder check uses `new Date()` on the server. There is no client timestamp field in any request schema. |\n| NFR-3 | UI, EP | Prefetch the next and previous `GET /api/submissions/:id` into a client cache keyed by id (a plain `Map` in the grading page; no data-fetching library added). The <300 ms target is a client switch from cache. |\n| NFR-4 | AUTH | Enforced at three boundaries: the FR-27 serializer, the FR-47 file resolvers, and query scoping (a student only ever queries `studentId = me`). |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every route: `requireUser`/`requireRole`, then assertCan*. Every page: `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`. |\n| NFR-6 | UI | MUI 9.5.0 + MUI X only, with mui-mcp lookups before use. Components needed: List, Chip, ToggleButtonGroup, Dialog, Tabs, DataGrid (D2), DateTimePicker, Autocomplete, Snackbar. Hard blocker if mui-mcp is unreachable (blocker 8). |\n| NFR-7 | EP | Thin handlers. `{data}` / paginated / `{error}` envelopes via the http.ts helpers. |\n| NFR-8 | CFG | `src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts`, plus `reminders.ts` and pure `scoring.ts` (lateDays, penalty, finalScore, chip status) for unit tests. Validators in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`. |\n| NFR-9 | SVC, TEST | Store UTC. Display via formatInSchoolTz. Late days in UTC ms (FR-23). The FR-10 default uses `fromZonedTime`. |\n| NFR-10 | UI | react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize are installed, with MUI component mapping (D1). |\n| NFR-11 | — | Reuse list: B1–B10, B15. |\n| NFR-12 | — | Use the logger, never console.log. |\n| NFR-13 | TEST, CFG | Blocker 3: fix the `vitest.config.ts` import to `'vitest/config'` (a one-line fix, in scope because NFR-13 requires a working `npm test`). |\n| NFR-14 | TEST | Unit: scoring.ts. Integration: resubmit history, return, reminder idempotency, exemption vs missing, and the file resolvers (AC-10). E2E: the full flow plus the parent missing list (needs bypassCSP, blocker 4). |\n| NFR-15 | — | No gradebook, peer review, group work or annotation. FR-35 stores the exemption only, and PRD-11 consumes it. |\n| NFR-16 | UI | Two-minute publish: sensible defaults (FR-10 due date, max points 100?, submissionType FILE_UPLOAD?). **Design should set the form defaults.** 30-submission keyboard grading via FR-33 + NFR-3. |\n| NFR-17 | UI | Labelled inputs and keyboard-operable controls: the ToggleButtonGroup and the J/K help hint. |\n\n## Decisions arch-design-system must make (answers to the intake blockers)\n\n| # | Blocker / gap | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | Blocker 1: PRD-08 UI components are missing. | Build the **minimum** shared components in this ticket: `src/components/MarkdownView` (react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, mapped to MUI), `src/components/MarkdownEditor` (MUI TextField multiline + a Write/Preview Tabs toggle using MarkdownView; no new editor dependency), `src/components/FileUpload` (input type=file → `POST /api/files` with the context field, list with remove, `maxFiles` prop) and `FileList` (links to `/api/files/:id`). Shape them so PRD-08 can adopt them later. Do not build PRD-08's remaining scope. |\n| D2 | Blocker 2: the MUI X DataGrid compile break. | Preferred: align `@mui/x-*` versions in package.json/lockfile (it also unblocks the DateTimePicker from `@mui/x-date-pickers`, if that package shares the internals). Fallback for FR-17: an MUI `Table`, which needs no DataGrid. `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0 **is installed** (package.json L34). It very likely has the same `@mui/x-internals` 9.15.0 mismatch, so FR-9's DateTimePicker is also at risk. That makes aligning the versions the real fix, rather than a Table workaround. |\n| D3 | Blockers 3/4: vitest import and CSP. | vitest: one-line import fix. CSP: keep `bypassCSP` in Playwright as before. A CSP fix is outside the PRD scope (NFR-15). Note the FR-29 iframe/img `'self'` dependency. |\n| D4 | Blocker 5: the studentTabs renderer. | Register the tab and build the page. Do not build a tab bar. Report it as a known gap. |\n| D5 | Decimal JSON serialization | Decimal fields are strings in API responses (NFR-1). |\n| D6 | The \"Save & return\" round trip | `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade` with an optional `return: true` gives one transaction. |\n| D7 | Rubric raw score | When rubricScores are present, the server sets or enforces `rawScore = Σ points`. |\n| D8 | Teacher/admin view of FR-58 grade fields | Course managers get full fields. Other viewers get the FR-27 serializer. |\n| D9 | Offline-graded row followed by an online submit | Treat it as a resubmission while it is not RETURNED. |\n| D10 | Missing-reminder query window | Bound it (e.g. dueAt within the last 8 days), marked with a `ponytail:` note. |\n\n## Shared pure functions (single source of truth; unit-test targets)\n\n`isAssignmentVisible`, `missingFilter(now)` (Prisma where), `lateDays`, `defaultPenalty`, `computeFinalScore`, `rubricTotal`, `submissionChipStatus`, `nextTeachingDayDueAt`, `toStudentSubmission` (serializer). Each of these is used by two or more call sites listed above. Keeping one copy of each prevents the drift that leads to privacy and correctness bugs (NFR-1, NFR-4).\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P3vy6Dj6UomMigkMBT1BtY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
