 course access checks, the maintenance route, `notify()` and `audit()`, the Decimal grading helpers, Postgres partial unique indexes (already used in the attendance migration), file contexts, the seed data, and the installed packages. Nothing new needs to be installed.\n- **Requirements table:** all 49 requirements (FR-1–39, NFR-1–10), each with the kind of work it needs and implementation notes. FR-37 (sidebar entry) and NFR-10 (out of scope) are marked as no work.\n- **Decisions D1–D5:** how the `src/server/quiz/` folder is split into files, one submit function used by every submit path, one rule that decides when results are visible, what gets fixed when an attempt starts, and regrade never overwriting a teacher's grade.\n- **8 assumptions/open points** for the system-design Overview to carry forward.\n\nTwo of those points need a decision from `arch-design-system`:\n- **Sending \"results released\" once:** for AFTER_CLOSE quizzes, FR-30 needs a record that the notification went out. I suggest adding a `Quiz.resultsNotifiedAt` field. FR-1 says the models must be \"exactly as listed\", so if a new field isn't acceptable, a separate claim table works instead.\n- **Email default:** the PRD doesn't say whether `quiz.results_released` sends email by default. I assumed it does, matching the existing `assignment.graded` notification.\n\nThe other files in `artifacts/architect/` still have `ticketId: \"SH-9\"`. They are old SH-9 output, not SH-10 input. The note says so, and the sub-tasks that own them will overwrite them.","ttft_ms":8471,"type":"result","duration_ms":125911,"uuid":"d06d7bd9-114c-4982-986e-970c08823ed8","ttft_stream_ms":7095,"time_to_request_ms":305,"first_content_frame_ms":7095,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":11248,"cacheReadInputTokens":310414,"cacheCreationInputTokens":52695,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6016208000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTok