{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsKcy2pLKEvq2oM6Jvuz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012RW7s6dVESemUsNtsFo6WW","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-11\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards (SCH-011). It has 42 FRs and 13 NFRs (55 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions (FR-6, FR-7, FR-13, FR-27/33, NFR-10, FR-3 no-term) are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> As of this writing the other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **leftovers from earlier tickets**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-11 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-11 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | **`getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` already exists.** It is labelled \"PRD-11 export\". It loads GRADED attempts, applies `applyScoringPolicy(quiz.scoringPolicy, …)`, and returns `{score, maxScore, percent, attemptsCounted, isPractice}` (fixed2 strings) or null. | src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts L355-372 | **This corrects intake** (B-finding 5 and the FR-7 assumption). FR-7 calls it directly, with no new helper. It does **not** check `resultsVisible`, so the sync caller must gate on that (NFR-5). The batch path (FR-8 backfill, NFR-3) should run `applyScoringPolicy` in memory over attempts it has already loaded, rather than calling this per student. |\n| B2 | `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` covers IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE (`now >= availableUntil`) / MANUAL (`resultsReleasedAt != null`). | src/server/quiz/grading.ts L94 | FR-7 / NFR-5 gate. AFTER_CLOSE depends on time, so a GRADED attempt is not syncable until close. See B4. |\n| B3 | Every quiz attempt status change goes through `recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)`. It is called from `submitAttempt` (L123, which includes auto-submit), `gradeAnswerManually` (L338) and `regradeQuiz` (quiz-service L435). | attempt-service.ts L73-81 | FR-7 hook. After each caller commits, call `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`, which no-ops unless GRADED + visible + !isPractice. Making this one function the only quiz sync entry point covers all three callers. |\n| B4 | Results become visible through `releaseResults` (MANUAL, quiz-service L464) and `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased` (AFTER_CLOSE). The latter claims `resultsReleasedAt` with `updateMany` on each maintenance tick. | quiz-service.ts L464; quiz/maintenance.ts L27-40 | FR-7 also needs a **bulk** `syncQuizGrades(quizId)` in both places. Otherwise AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL quizzes never reach the gradebook. The maintenance claim is already idempotent, so put the sync after `count === 1`. |\n| B5 | Quiz lifecycle: `createQuiz`, `updateQuiz` (DRAFT→PUBLISHED and PUBLISHED→CLOSED via guarded `updateMany`, L304-305), `deleteQuiz` (hard delete, L317). Quizzes have **no archive**. | quiz-service.ts L259-317 | FR-3: upsert the item on →PUBLISHED. FR-4: delete the item on deleteQuiz. CLOSED is **not** unpublish, so the item stays visible. Settings edits to a published quiz (title, availableUntil, categoryId, max) re-upsert the item. |\n| B6 | Assignment lifecycle: `createAssignment` / `updateAssignment` (status DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED); `publishOnce` (cron, makes SCHEDULED visible once `availableFrom` passes); `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` (hard delete in a tx, or sets `archivedAt` when submissions exist, L479-492). `isAssignmentVisible` = !archivedAt && published-or-scheduled-reached. | assignments-service.ts L67-74, L292-330, L437-492 | FR-3/FR-4: compute GradeItem.isVisible from `isAssignmentVisible`. Upsert on create/update/publishOnce, set isVisible=false on archive, delete inside the delete tx. **FR-24's teacher hide toggle conflicts with this** (see §3 R2). |\n| B7 | Return paths: `gradeSubmission` (`returning = input.return && status !== 'RETURNED'`; it also re-grades an already-RETURNED submission), `bulkReturn`, and `gradeOffline` (`input.return`). | assignments-service.ts ~L696-800 | FR-5: sync when the submission **is RETURNED after the write**, not only on the transition. Re-grading a returned submission must update Grade.score, and grade-without-return must not sync (AC-3). Use one `syncSubmissionGrade(submissionId)` from all three. |\n| B8 | `setExemption(…, exempt)` upserts or deletes `GradeExemption` (L818/L824) and audits `assignment.exempt` / `assignment.unexempt`. | assignments-service.ts L815-838 | FR-6: call `syncSubmissionGrade` (or a by-(assignment, student) variant) after both branches. Unexempt re-derives the score from a RETURNED submission, else null. |\n| B9 | GradeItem has a polymorphic `source + sourceId` with **no FK**. Assignment and Quiz deletes will not cascade. | FR-1 model spec | FR-4: delete the GradeItem explicitly inside the same transaction as the source delete (and in `deleteQuiz`, which today runs outside a tx). Grade → GradeItem should be `onDelete: Cascade`. |\n| B10 | `Term` has no `isCurrent`. It has `academicYearId`, `startDate`/`endDate` as `@db.Date`, `order`. `AcademicYear.isCurrent` exists. `Course.academicYearId` exists. | schema.prisma L240-252, Course ~L415 | FR-3 term placement: pick the term of **the course's academic year** whose `[startDate, endDate]` contains dueAt, comparing dates in the school timezone (NFR-10). The fallback \"current term\" is the term of that year containing today (tz), else skip + `logger.warn`. Put this in one pure helper `termFor(date, terms, tz)`. |\n| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from assignments-service. `dec` / `fixed2` / `Decimal` come from grading-math (isomorphic). `percentOf` (1 dp half-up) is in quiz/grading.ts. | assignments-service.ts L57; grading-math.ts L7-15; grading.ts L133 | NFR-1/NFR-10/FR-13 reuse these. `percentOf` rounds to 1 dp on a single value. grade-calc must keep full-precision Decimal until the **final** rounding (FR-13), so it must not round category percents early. |\n| B12 | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` exist. `getAccessibleStudentIds` / `assertCanViewStudent` cover own student, linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`), teacher and admin, with homeroom handled there too. `src/server/quiz/access.ts` has `canManageCourse`. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts, student-access.ts | FR-39 \"manage\"/\"view\" and FR-42 reuse these. FR-37 report-card access is new: ADMIN; teachers of any course on the card or the homeroom teacher; the student or a linked parent only when PUBLISHED. Return NOT_FOUND to everyone else (AC-7). |\n| B13 | Attendance aggregation already exists: `getReport(filters)` → `StudentSummaryRow` (StatusCounts per student) using a single `groupBy(studentId, status)`. It filters by date range, grade level, section and course. | attendance-service.ts L528-582 | FR-30 attendance summary and NFR-3 batching: call `getReport({from: term.start, to: term.end, sectionId/gradeLevelId})` **once** per generate request. Do not loop per student. Rate formula: reuse whatever StatusCounts consumers use. Do not invent a new one. |\n| B14 | `SchoolSettings` singleton: name, shortName, logoUrl, timezone, address fields. Student profile: `admissionNumber`, `gradeLevel`. `Section.homeroomTeacherId`. | schema.prisma L109-113, L198-215 | FR-30 snapshot fields all come from existing models. No schema change beyond FR-1. |\n| B15 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const already contains assignment.* and quiz.* entries. `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents()` never throw. `audit()` never throws. | notifications/types.ts, notify.ts L28/L98, audit.ts L26 | FR-38: add `grade.posted` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, STUDENT+PARENT) and `report_card.published` (defaultEmail true, STUDENT+PARENT). Call them after commit. NFR-4 audit actions: `grade.update`, `termOverride.upsert`, `reportCard.unpublish` (plus `reportCard.publish` and `gradingScale.*` as nice-to-haves). |\n| B16 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are static arrays. `studentTabs` notes \"No tab bar renders studentTabs yet\". `navigation` is a flat array with `roles` and an optional `group: 'Administration'`. | src/config/*.ts | FR-18/28: add course tabs `gradebook` (TEACHER, ADMIN) and `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT). FR-26/36: add student tabs `grades` and `report-cards`. These are reachable by URL only, the same as `assignments`. FR-27/33 + admin pages: nav entries `/grades`, `/report-cards`, `/admin/grading-scales`, `/admin/report-cards`. |\n| B17 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` are in src/server/csv.ts. Shared components: DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast (useToast), PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, DateDisplay, UserPicker, FormField, LoadingSkeleton. **No existing `@mui/x-data-grid` usage in src.** | src/server/csv.ts; src/components/ | FR-25: export on the server with `toCsv`, building the same columns as the grid. FR-18 is the first DataGrid in the codebase, so its MIT-tier API (columnGroupingModel, processRowUpdate, virtualisation, no pinning) must be looked up via mui-mcp for 9.5.0 (NFR-7/8). FR-29 table → DataTable. |\n| B18 | Scripts: `db:seed` = `tsx prisma/seed.ts`. There is no `gradebook:backfill`. The seed looks up courses by code with `findCourse([...])`. | package.json; prisma/seed.ts | FR-8: add `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`, a thin wrapper over an exported `backfillGradebook()` in src/server/gradebook/ that the seed also calls before the FR-41 data. |\n| B19 | Postgres. Migrations already hand-add raw SQL partial indexes. Prisma 5.20. | prisma/migrations/* | FR-1: one migration. It needs `@@unique([source, sourceId])` on GradeItem (sync and backfill idempotency), `@@unique([gradeItemId, studentId])` on Grade, `@@unique([courseId, termId, studentId])` on TermGradeOverride, and `@@unique([studentId, termId])` on ReportCard. These make the upserts race-safe. A one-default-scale rule can be a partial unique index `WHERE \"isDefault\"` (FR-16). |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **SYNC** source→gradebook sync hook · **CALC** pure calculation · **API** REST endpoint · **UI** page/component · **AUTH** access boundary · **JOB** script/batch · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **CFG** config registry.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | New enums + 6 models in one `prisma migrate` migration. Use the unique keys from B19. Grade: `score Decimal?`, `excused`, `missing`, `comment`, `gradedById`, `gradedAt`. ReportCard: `status`, `snapshot Json`, `homeroomComment`, `principalComment`, `publishedAt`, `publishedById`. |\n| FR-2 | DM, UI | Nullable `Course.gradingScaleId`, `Assignment.categoryId` and `Quiz.categoryId` with `onDelete: SetNull`. Category deletion via FR-40 must not delete sources. Add one `Select` to the existing assignment and quiz editors, plus the validator fields in assignments.ts / quiz.ts (optional and nullable). Don't change existing behaviour. |\n| FR-3 | SYNC | `upsertGradeItemFromAssignment(id)` / `…FromQuiz(id)` keyed on (source, sourceId). Skip practice quizzes. Term placement via `termFor` (B10). Callers per B5/B6. Keep the GradeItem's term stable after first creation unless the date changes, so grades don't jump terms on unrelated edits. |\n| FR-4 | SYNC | Archive sets isVisible=false. Delete removes the GradeItem in the same tx (B9). Quiz has no archive or unpublish. A practice-toggle after publish should delete or hide the item. |\n| FR-5 | SYNC | `syncSubmissionGrade` from 3 return paths (B7). It writes only when RETURNED. Score = `finalScore`. |\n| FR-6 | SYNC | From `setExemption` (B8). Exemption wins over the score: excused=true and the score is kept. |\n| FR-7 | SYNC | Per-attempt `syncQuizGrade` after `recomputeAttempt` callers (B3). Bulk `syncQuizGrades` on release and AFTER_CLOSE (B4). Score scaled: `score/maxScore × GradeItem.maxPoints`, Decimal. |\n| FR-8 | JOB | `backfillGradebook()`: batch load per course, reuse the same upsert builders as live sync (one code path), idempotent through the unique keys. npm script + seed call (B18). |\n| FR-9 | API, AUTH | The service rejects score/excused/missing edits on non-MANUAL items (`AppError('FORBIDDEN'/'VALIDATION_ERROR')`). Comment stays editable. The grid marks those columns non-editable. |\n| FR-10 | CALC | `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts`: pure, Decimal-only, no Prisma client import (types only). Input: items, grades, categories, scale, override, `now`. Counted = visible ∧ ¬excused ∧ (score≠null ∨ (missing ∧ now>dueAt)). |\n| FR-11 | CALC | Drop lowest by item **percentage**, keeping ≥1. Ties are dropped deterministically (by dueAt, then id). |\n| FR-12 | CALC | Implicit \"Uncategorised\" bucket. What weight does it get? The PRD is silent, so see §3 R3. No categories gives a points total. |\n| FR-13 | CALC | `toDecimalPlaces(1, ROUND_HALF_UP)` only at the end. Bands are sorted descending, first `percent >= minPercent`. |\n| FR-14 | CALC | The override is applied after computing. A letter-only override keeps the computed percent. A percent-only override probably re-derives the letter from the scale (unstated, so flag it). |\n| FR-15 | CALC, UI | Golden unit test (78.0 C+). The gradebook and student Grades **must call the same function**, with no client-side recomputation. |\n| FR-16 | API, UI, DM | `/admin/grading-scales` (ADMIN). Band validation lives in a Zod refinement shared by client and server. \"Exactly one default\" uses a tx that clears others + a partial unique index. Deleting a scale in use is either blocked or falls back to the default; decide this. |\n| FR-17 | UI, API | Course settings page. The live weight sum is client-side, with the 100 check repeated server-side in FR-40. Decimal weights: compare with `dec(sum).eq(100)`, not floats. |\n| FR-18 | UI, API, CALC | First DataGrid. The server returns one denormalised payload `{students, items, categories, grades, computed}` for (course, term) in a fixed number of queries (NFR-2). Columns are built client-side from it. Sort by last name on the server. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Pure cell renderer. \"Late\" needs `Submission.isLate`, so the gradebook payload must carry the source submission's isLate. |\n| FR-20 | UI, API | `processRowUpdate` → PATCH a single grade. E/M/Delete need a custom edit cell / `onCellKeyDown` (check mui-mcp). Optimistic update with per-cell error. Audited (NFR-4). Triggers `grade.posted` (FR-38). |\n| FR-21 | UI | The cell click opens a link to the submission grading page or the quiz attempt. The payload needs `submissionId` / `attemptId` per synced grade. |\n| FR-22 | API, UI | POST manual item. Validate that the term belongs to the course's academic year and the category belongs to the course. |\n| FR-23 | API, UI, AUD | PUT override (upsert). Comment ≤1000 chars. Audit with old/new values. |\n| FR-24 | API, UI | Toggle visibility (see R2). Bulk-missing allowed only if `now > dueAt` and only for ungraded rows. Stats come from the computed payload, client-side, over counted scores. |\n| FR-25 | API | Server CSV via `toCsv`, using the same row builder as the grid. \"As displayed\" means EX/M/— markers and the term letter. |\n| FR-26 | UI, API, CFG | Student tab → `GET /api/students/:id/grades?termId`. The colour thresholds come from a single helper reused by FR-27/28. |\n| FR-27 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/grades` reuses the FR-26 component. Parent child selector from `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Nav entry. |\n| FR-28 | UI, CFG | Course tab `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT): same endpoint filtered by courseId. |\n| FR-29 | UI, API | `/admin/report-cards`: list query joins students (grade level, section filters) with ReportCard status for the term. Missing-data warnings are computed in batch (ungraded counted-eligible items, missing TermGradeOverride.comment per course). |\n| FR-30 | JOB, API | `generate`: batch load (NFR-3), compute in memory, write the snapshot JSON (versioned shape, e.g. `snapshot.v = 1`). Teacher comment = `TermGradeOverride.comment`. Attendance via B13. |\n| FR-31 | JOB, DM | `upsert` with `where status = DRAFT` semantics: createMany for new cards, `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})` for existing ones, never touching PUBLISHED. Grade-edit services never import report-cards code. |\n| FR-32 | API, UI, AUTH | PATCH: field-level role check (homeroomComment: homeroom teacher of the student's section or ADMIN; principalComment: ADMIN). Edits are allowed only while DRAFT (implied, so flag it). |\n| FR-33 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/report-cards` (TEACHER): drafts for sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Nav entry. |\n| FR-34 | API, NOTIF, AUD | Publish (one or bulk) with a guarded `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})`, then notify after commit. Unpublish: ADMIN, reason required, audit, back to DRAFT. |\n| FR-35 | UI | `/report-cards/[id]/print` renders from the **snapshot only**. `@media print` via MUI `GlobalStyles`, hiding the sidebar. Bulk print: one page renders N cards with `break-after: page`. |\n| FR-36 | UI, CFG, API | Student tab \"Report cards\". The list endpoint filters to PUBLISHED for student/parent (NFR-5). |\n| FR-37 | AUTH | New `assertCanViewReportCard`. Non-entitled users get NOT_FOUND, so existence isn't leaked. |\n| FR-38 | NOTIF | Register 2 types (B15). `grade.posted`: only for MANUAL items, only when a score is first entered or changed (one per student per item, so an idempotency marker such as `Grade.notifiedAt` is needed; flag it). |\n| FR-39 | API, AUTH | Thin route handlers using `withHandler`, Zod in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, and services in `src/server/gradebook/` + `src/server/report-cards/`. |\n| FR-40 | API | Replace-all in a tx: delete missing ids (sources → SetNull), upsert the rest. Weights total 100 (Decimal). |\n| FR-41 | JOB | Seed: scale, 7A categories, 'Oral presentation' + grades, draft S1 cards for 7A with MATH/ENG override comments. Run after `backfillGradebook()`. |\n| FR-42 | API, AUTH | Student serializer: visible items only. Grade rows only exist for released scores (sync gating), so the risk is mainly hidden items and MANUAL items with isVisible=false. Still filter explicitly. |\n| NFR-1 | CALC | Decimal throughout. Unit matrix in `grade-calc.test.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | API | Gradebook: ~5 queries (enrollments, items, grades, categories, scale + override), all indexed by (courseId, termId). The grid virtualises. |\n| NFR-3 | JOB | Generation: per term, `findMany` items/grades/overrides/categories for all courses in scope with `in` filters, then group in memory. One attendance `groupBy`. Chunk the writes. |\n| NFR-4 | AUD | Old/new values in metadata for grade.update, termOverride.upsert and reportCard.unpublish. |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Enforced in 3 layers: sync gating (B2/B7), student serializer (FR-42), report-card guard (FR-37). Integration tests for each. |\n| NFR-6 | AUTH | Every route uses requireUser/requireRole + an entity check (B12). Server pages check too, not just the API. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | MUI only, with mui-mcp lookup. Toast via useToast, confirm via Dialog/ConfirmDialog. |\n| NFR-8 | UI | DataGrid MIT: no `pinnedColumns` and no `@mui/x-data-grid-pro`. Sticky header is the default. |\n| NFR-9 | all | New code only in src/server/gradebook/ and src/server/report-cards/. Hooks into existing services are one-line calls. Use `logger`, no console.log. |\n| NFR-10 | CALC, SYNC | Past-due uses an instant comparison (`now > dueAt`). Term containment uses a tz date comparison (B10). |\n| NFR-11 | UI | A4 portrait `@page` rule. Long course lists may need a 2nd page, with table rows set to `break-inside: avoid`. |\n| NFR-12 | all | Tests per the intake list. Integration tests hit the real sync hooks (B3/B4/B7). |\n| NFR-13 | — | Scope guard: store `gpa`, never compute it. No rank or transcript. |\n\n## 3. Risks / decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **R1 (FR-7 timing):** AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL visibility arrive later than GRADED. Without the B4 bulk hooks, those quizzes never sync. Syncing early would break NFR-5.\n- **R2 (FR-4 vs FR-24):** the teacher's hide toggle and the source-driven `isVisible` share one column. Re-saving an assignment would silently re-show a teacher-hidden item. Options: (a) source sync writes isVisible only on publish/archive *transitions*; (b) add a separate `hiddenByTeacher` flag and make visible = sourceVisible ∧ ¬hiddenByTeacher. (b) is clearer but adds a column beyond FR-1's \"exactly as specified\". Pick one and state it.\n- **R3 (FR-12 Uncategorised weight):** the PRD doesn't say what weight the implicit bucket carries when real categories exist. A sensible default is weight 0, so it's shown but excluded from the weighted mean, unless it's the only bucket. This affects the FR-15 golden test only if it has uncategorised items (it doesn't). Flag it.\n- **R4 (FR-38 dedupe):** \"one notification per student per item\" needs a marker. A nullable `Grade.notifiedAt` claimed via `updateMany` follows the existing claim pattern.\n- **R5 (FR-3 term drift):** re-deriving the term on every edit can move existing grades between terms. Only recompute it when dueAt/availableUntil changes.\n- **R6 (FR-16 delete):** deleting a scale referenced by courses or by DRAFT snapshots (PUBLISHED ones embed the legend, so they're safe). Recommend blocking the delete with CONFLICT while courses reference the scale.\n- **R7 (first DataGrid):** there is no in-repo precedent. Keyboard E/M/Delete handling within the MIT tier is the main implementation risk (intake keyRisk). The design should keep the grid behind one client component.\n\n## 4. Carried-forward assumptions (from intake, adjusted)\n\n1. FR-6: unexempting clears excused and re-syncs the score from the source.\n2. FR-7: **use the existing `getStudentQuizScore`** (B1) plus a caller-side `resultsVisible` gate. This replaces intake's \"build a new helper\".\n3. FR-13: 89.95 → 90.0 → **A−** under the seed scale. The test asserts 90.0 and the 90-band letter.\n4. FR-27/FR-33: add nav entries per the convention.\n5. NFR-10: past due = `now > dueAt` (exact instant). Term containment is evaluated in the school timezone.\n6. FR-3: no containing term and no current term → skip the item + `logger.warn`.\n7. New and unstated (needs sign-off): FR-14 percent-only override re-derives the letter; FR-32 comments are editable only while DRAFT; FR-34 unpublish returns to DRAFT.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2202,"cache_read_input_tokens":56683,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2202},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8dcae7d9-b717-4417-9584-7ef748d2b9e4","uuid":"d081b2eb-ec87-44fa-9a8f-0c98c1efe880","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:05:18.859Z","request_id":"req_011CgsKcxmCDsXU3oqmYJjrg","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012RW7s6dVESemUsNtsFo6WW":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-11\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards (SCH-011). It has 42 FRs and 13 NFRs (55 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions (FR-6, FR-7, FR-13, FR-27/33, NFR-10, FR-3 no-term) are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> As of this writing the other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **leftovers from earlier tickets**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-11 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-11 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | **`getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` already exists.** It is labelled \"PRD-11 export\". It loads GRADED attempts, applies `applyScoringPolicy(quiz.scoringPolicy, …)`, and returns `{score, maxScore, percent, attemptsCounted, isPractice}` (fixed2 strings) or null. | src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts L355-372 | **This corrects intake** (B-finding 5 and the FR-7 assumption). FR-7 calls it directly, with no new helper. It does **not** check `resultsVisible`, so the sync caller must gate on that (NFR-5). The batch path (FR-8 backfill, NFR-3) should run `applyScoringPolicy` in memory over attempts it has already loaded, rather than calling this per student. |\n| B2 | `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` covers IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE (`now >= availableUntil`) / MANUAL (`resultsReleasedAt != null`). | src/server/quiz/grading.ts L94 | FR-7 / NFR-5 gate. AFTER_CLOSE depends on time, so a GRADED attempt is not syncable until close. See B4. |\n| B3 | Every quiz attempt status change goes through `recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)`. It is called from `submitAttempt` (L123, which includes auto-submit), `gradeAnswerManually` (L338) and `regradeQuiz` (quiz-service L435). | attempt-service.ts L73-81 | FR-7 hook. After each caller commits, call `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`, which no-ops unless GRADED + visible + !isPractice. Making this one function the only quiz sync entry point covers all three callers. |\n| B4 | Results become visible through `releaseResults` (MANUAL, quiz-service L464) and `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased` (AFTER_CLOSE). The latter claims `resultsReleasedAt` with `updateMany` on each maintenance tick. | quiz-service.ts L464; quiz/maintenance.ts L27-40 | FR-7 also needs a **bulk** `syncQuizGrades(quizId)` in both places. Otherwise AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL quizzes never reach the gradebook. The maintenance claim is already idempotent, so put the sync after `count === 1`. |\n| B5 | Quiz lifecycle: `createQuiz`, `updateQuiz` (DRAFT→PUBLISHED and PUBLISHED→CLOSED via guarded `updateMany`, L304-305), `deleteQuiz` (hard delete, L317). Quizzes have **no archive**. | quiz-service.ts L259-317 | FR-3: upsert the item on →PUBLISHED. FR-4: delete the item on deleteQuiz. CLOSED is **not** unpublish, so the item stays visible. Settings edits to a published quiz (title, availableUntil, categoryId, max) re-upsert the item. |\n| B6 | Assignment lifecycle: `createAssignment` / `updateAssignment` (status DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED); `publishOnce` (cron, makes SCHEDULED visible once `availableFrom` passes); `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` (hard delete in a tx, or sets `archivedAt` when submissions exist, L479-492). `isAssignmentVisible` = !archivedAt && published-or-scheduled-reached. | assignments-service.ts L67-74, L292-330, L437-492 | FR-3/FR-4: compute GradeItem.isVisible from `isAssignmentVisible`. Upsert on create/update/publishOnce, set isVisible=false on archive, delete inside the delete tx. **FR-24's teacher hide toggle conflicts with this** (see §3 R2). |\n| B7 | Return paths: `gradeSubmission` (`returning = input.return && status !== 'RETURNED'`; it also re-grades an already-RETURNED submission), `bulkReturn`, and `gradeOffline` (`input.return`). | assignments-service.ts ~L696-800 | FR-5: sync when the submission **is RETURNED after the write**, not only on the transition. Re-grading a returned submission must update Grade.score, and grade-without-return must not sync (AC-3). Use one `syncSubmissionGrade(submissionId)` from all three. |\n| B8 | `setExemption(…, exempt)` upserts or deletes `GradeExemption` (L818/L824) and audits `assignment.exempt` / `assignment.unexempt`. | assignments-service.ts L815-838 | FR-6: call `syncSubmissionGrade` (or a by-(assignment, student) variant) after both branches. Unexempt re-derives the score from a RETURNED submission, else null. |\n| B9 | GradeItem has a polymorphic `source + sourceId` with **no FK**. Assignment and Quiz deletes will not cascade. | FR-1 model spec | FR-4: delete the GradeItem explicitly inside the same transaction as the source delete (and in `deleteQuiz`, which today runs outside a tx). Grade → GradeItem should be `onDelete: Cascade`. |\n| B10 | `Term` has no `isCurrent`. It has `academicYearId`, `startDate`/`endDate` as `@db.Date`, `order`. `AcademicYear.isCurrent` exists. `Course.academicYearId` exists. | schema.prisma L240-252, Course ~L415 | FR-3 term placement: pick the term of **the course's academic year** whose `[startDate, endDate]` contains dueAt, comparing dates in the school timezone (NFR-10). The fallback \"current term\" is the term of that year containing today (tz), else skip + `logger.warn`. Put this in one pure helper `termFor(date, terms, tz)`. |\n| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from assignments-service. `dec` / `fixed2` / `Decimal` come from grading-math (isomorphic). `percentOf` (1 dp half-up) is in quiz/grading.ts. | assignments-service.ts L57; grading-math.ts L7-15; grading.ts L133 | NFR-1/NFR-10/FR-13 reuse these. `percentOf` rounds to 1 dp on a single value. grade-calc must keep full-precision Decimal until the **final** rounding (FR-13), so it must not round category percents early. |\n| B12 | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` exist. `getAccessibleStudentIds` / `assertCanViewStudent` cover own student, linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`), teacher and admin, with homeroom handled there too. `src/server/quiz/access.ts` has `canManageCourse`. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts, student-access.ts | FR-39 \"manage\"/\"view\" and FR-42 reuse these. FR-37 report-card access is new: ADMIN; teachers of any course on the card or the homeroom teacher; the student or a linked parent only when PUBLISHED. Return NOT_FOUND to everyone else (AC-7). |\n| B13 | Attendance aggregation already exists: `getReport(filters)` → `StudentSummaryRow` (StatusCounts per student) using a single `groupBy(studentId, status)`. It filters by date range, grade level, section and course. | attendance-service.ts L528-582 | FR-30 attendance summary and NFR-3 batching: call `getReport({from: term.start, to: term.end, sectionId/gradeLevelId})` **once** per generate request. Do not loop per student. Rate formula: reuse whatever StatusCounts consumers use. Do not invent a new one. |\n| B14 | `SchoolSettings` singleton: name, shortName, logoUrl, timezone, address fields. Student profile: `admissionNumber`, `gradeLevel`. `Section.homeroomTeacherId`. | schema.prisma L109-113, L198-215 | FR-30 snapshot fields all come from existing models. No schema change beyond FR-1. |\n| B15 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const already contains assignment.* and quiz.* entries. `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents()` never throw. `audit()` never throws. | notifications/types.ts, notify.ts L28/L98, audit.ts L26 | FR-38: add `grade.posted` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, STUDENT+PARENT) and `report_card.published` (defaultEmail true, STUDENT+PARENT). Call them after commit. NFR-4 audit actions: `grade.update`, `termOverride.upsert`, `reportCard.unpublish` (plus `reportCard.publish` and `gradingScale.*` as nice-to-haves). |\n| B16 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are static arrays. `studentTabs` notes \"No tab bar renders studentTabs yet\". `navigation` is a flat array with `roles` and an optional `group: 'Administration'`. | src/config/*.ts | FR-18/28: add course tabs `gradebook` (TEACHER, ADMIN) and `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT). FR-26/36: add student tabs `grades` and `report-cards`. These are reachable by URL only, the same as `assignments`. FR-27/33 + admin pages: nav entries `/grades`, `/report-cards`, `/admin/grading-scales`, `/admin/report-cards`. |\n| B17 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` are in src/server/csv.ts. Shared components: DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast (useToast), PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, DateDisplay, UserPicker, FormField, LoadingSkeleton. **No existing `@mui/x-data-grid` usage in src.** | src/server/csv.ts; src/components/ | FR-25: export on the server with `toCsv`, building the same columns as the grid. FR-18 is the first DataGrid in the codebase, so its MIT-tier API (columnGroupingModel, processRowUpdate, virtualisation, no pinning) must be looked up via mui-mcp for 9.5.0 (NFR-7/8). FR-29 table → DataTable. |\n| B18 | Scripts: `db:seed` = `tsx prisma/seed.ts`. There is no `gradebook:backfill`. The seed looks up courses by code with `findCourse([...])`. | package.json; prisma/seed.ts | FR-8: add `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`, a thin wrapper over an exported `backfillGradebook()` in src/server/gradebook/ that the seed also calls before the FR-41 data. |\n| B19 | Postgres. Migrations already hand-add raw SQL partial indexes. Prisma 5.20. | prisma/migrations/* | FR-1: one migration. It needs `@@unique([source, sourceId])` on GradeItem (sync and backfill idempotency), `@@unique([gradeItemId, studentId])` on Grade, `@@unique([courseId, termId, studentId])` on TermGradeOverride, and `@@unique([studentId, termId])` on ReportCard. These make the upserts race-safe. A one-default-scale rule can be a partial unique index `WHERE \"isDefault\"` (FR-16). |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **SYNC** source→gradebook sync hook · **CALC** pure calculation · **API** REST endpoint · **UI** page/component · **AUTH** access boundary · **JOB** script/batch · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **CFG** config registry.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | New enums + 6 models in one `prisma migrate` migration. Use the unique keys from B19. Grade: `score Decimal?`, `excused`, `missing`, `comment`, `gradedById`, `gradedAt`. ReportCard: `status`, `snapshot Json`, `homeroomComment`, `principalComment`, `publishedAt`, `publishedById`. |\n| FR-2 | DM, UI | Nullable `Course.gradingScaleId`, `Assignment.categoryId` and `Quiz.categoryId` with `onDelete: SetNull`. Category deletion via FR-40 must not delete sources. Add one `Select` to the existing assignment and quiz editors, plus the validator fields in assignments.ts / quiz.ts (optional and nullable). Don't change existing behaviour. |\n| FR-3 | SYNC | `upsertGradeItemFromAssignment(id)` / `…FromQuiz(id)` keyed on (source, sourceId). Skip practice quizzes. Term placement via `termFor` (B10). Callers per B5/B6. Keep the GradeItem's term stable after first creation unless the date changes, so grades don't jump terms on unrelated edits. |\n| FR-4 | SYNC | Archive sets isVisible=false. Delete removes the GradeItem in the same tx (B9). Quiz has no archive or unpublish. A practice-toggle after publish should delete or hide the item. |\n| FR-5 | SYNC | `syncSubmissionGrade` from 3 return paths (B7). It writes only when RETURNED. Score = `finalScore`. |\n| FR-6 | SYNC | From `setExemption` (B8). Exemption wins over the score: excused=true and the score is kept. |\n| FR-7 | SYNC | Per-attempt `syncQuizGrade` after `recomputeAttempt` callers (B3). Bulk `syncQuizGrades` on release and AFTER_CLOSE (B4). Score scaled: `score/maxScore × GradeItem.maxPoints`, Decimal. |\n| FR-8 | JOB | `backfillGradebook()`: batch load per course, reuse the same upsert builders as live sync (one code path), idempotent through the unique keys. npm script + seed call (B18). |\n| FR-9 | API, AUTH | The service rejects score/excused/missing edits on non-MANUAL items (`AppError('FORBIDDEN'/'VALIDATION_ERROR')`). Comment stays editable. The grid marks those columns non-editable. |\n| FR-10 | CALC | `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts`: pure, Decimal-only, no Prisma client import (types only). Input: items, grades, categories, scale, override, `now`. Counted = visible ∧ ¬excused ∧ (score≠null ∨ (missing ∧ now>dueAt)). |\n| FR-11 | CALC | Drop lowest by item **percentage**, keeping ≥1. Ties are dropped deterministically (by dueAt, then id). |\n| FR-12 | CALC | Implicit \"Uncategorised\" bucket. What weight does it get? The PRD is silent, so see §3 R3. No categories gives a points total. |\n| FR-13 | CALC | `toDecimalPlaces(1, ROUND_HALF_UP)` only at the end. Bands are sorted descending, first `percent >= minPercent`. |\n| FR-14 | CALC | The override is applied after computing. A letter-only override keeps the computed percent. A percent-only override probably re-derives the letter from the scale (unstated, so flag it). |\n| FR-15 | CALC, UI | Golden unit test (78.0 C+). The gradebook and student Grades **must call the same function**, with no client-side recomputation. |\n| FR-16 | API, UI, DM | `/admin/grading-scales` (ADMIN). Band validation lives in a Zod refinement shared by client and server. \"Exactly one default\" uses a tx that clears others + a partial unique index. Deleting a scale in use is either blocked or falls back to the default; decide this. |\n| FR-17 | UI, API | Course settings page. The live weight sum is client-side, with the 100 check repeated server-side in FR-40. Decimal weights: compare with `dec(sum).eq(100)`, not floats. |\n| FR-18 | UI, API, CALC | First DataGrid. The server returns one denormalised payload `{students, items, categories, grades, computed}` for (course, term) in a fixed number of queries (NFR-2). Columns are built client-side from it. Sort by last name on the server. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Pure cell renderer. \"Late\" needs `Submission.isLate`, so the gradebook payload must carry the source submission's isLate. |\n| FR-20 | UI, API | `processRowUpdate` → PATCH a single grade. E/M/Delete need a custom edit cell / `onCellKeyDown` (check mui-mcp). Optimistic update with per-cell error. Audited (NFR-4). Triggers `grade.posted` (FR-38). |\n| FR-21 | UI | The cell click opens a link to the submission grading page or the quiz attempt. The payload needs `submissionId` / `attemptId` per synced grade. |\n| FR-22 | API, UI | POST manual item. Validate that the term belongs to the course's academic year and the category belongs to the course. |\n| FR-23 | API, UI, AUD | PUT override (upsert). Comment ≤1000 chars. Audit with old/new values. |\n| FR-24 | API, UI | Toggle visibility (see R2). Bulk-missing allowed only if `now > dueAt` and only for ungraded rows. Stats come from the computed payload, client-side, over counted scores. |\n| FR-25 | API | Server CSV via `toCsv`, using the same row builder as the grid. \"As displayed\" means EX/M/— markers and the term letter. |\n| FR-26 | UI, API, CFG | Student tab → `GET /api/students/:id/grades?termId`. The colour thresholds come from a single helper reused by FR-27/28. |\n| FR-27 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/grades` reuses the FR-26 component. Parent child selector from `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Nav entry. |\n| FR-28 | UI, CFG | Course tab `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT): same endpoint filtered by courseId. |\n| FR-29 | UI, API | `/admin/report-cards`: list query joins students (grade level, section filters) with ReportCard status for the term. Missing-data warnings are computed in batch (ungraded counted-eligible items, missing TermGradeOverride.comment per course). |\n| FR-30 | JOB, API | `generate`: batch load (NFR-3), compute in memory, write the snapshot JSON (versioned shape, e.g. `snapshot.v = 1`). Teacher comment = `TermGradeOverride.comment`. Attendance via B13. |\n| FR-31 | JOB, DM | `upsert` with `where status = DRAFT` semantics: createMany for new cards, `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})` for existing ones, never touching PUBLISHED. Grade-edit services never import report-cards code. |\n| FR-32 | API, UI, AUTH | PATCH: field-level role check (homeroomComment: homeroom teacher of the student's section or ADMIN; principalComment: ADMIN). Edits are allowed only while DRAFT (implied, so flag it). |\n| FR-33 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/report-cards` (TEACHER): drafts for sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Nav entry. |\n| FR-34 | API, NOTIF, AUD | Publish (one or bulk) with a guarded `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})`, then notify after commit. Unpublish: ADMIN, reason required, audit, back to DRAFT. |\n| FR-35 | UI | `/report-cards/[id]/print` renders from the **snapshot only**. `@media print` via MUI `GlobalStyles`, hiding the sidebar. Bulk print: one page renders N cards with `break-after: page`. |\n| FR-36 | UI, CFG, API | Student tab \"Report cards\". The list endpoint filters to PUBLISHED for student/parent (NFR-5). |\n| FR-37 | AUTH | New `assertCanViewReportCard`. Non-entitled users get NOT_FOUND, so existence isn't leaked. |\n| FR-38 | NOTIF | Register 2 types (B15). `grade.posted`: only for MANUAL items, only when a score is first entered or changed (one per student per item, so an idempotency marker such as `Grade.notifiedAt` is needed; flag it). |\n| FR-39 | API, AUTH | Thin route handlers using `withHandler`, Zod in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, and services in `src/server/gradebook/` + `src/server/report-cards/`. |\n| FR-40 | API | Replace-all in a tx: delete missing ids (sources → SetNull), upsert the rest. Weights total 100 (Decimal). |\n| FR-41 | JOB | Seed: scale, 7A categories, 'Oral presentation' + grades, draft S1 cards for 7A with MATH/ENG override comments. Run after `backfillGradebook()`. |\n| FR-42 | API, AUTH | Student serializer: visible items only. Grade rows only exist for released scores (sync gating), so the risk is mainly hidden items and MANUAL items with isVisible=false. Still filter explicitly. |\n| NFR-1 | CALC | Decimal throughout. Unit matrix in `grade-calc.test.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | API | Gradebook: ~5 queries (enrollments, items, grades, categories, scale + override), all indexed by (courseId, termId). The grid virtualises. |\n| NFR-3 | JOB | Generation: per term, `findMany` items/grades/overrides/categories for all courses in scope with `in` filters, then group in memory. One attendance `groupBy`. Chunk the writes. |\n| NFR-4 | AUD | Old/new values in metadata for grade.update, termOverride.upsert and reportCard.unpublish. |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Enforced in 3 layers: sync gating (B2/B7), student serializer (FR-42), report-card guard (FR-37). Integration tests for each. |\n| NFR-6 | AUTH | Every route uses requireUser/requireRole + an entity check (B12). Server pages check too, not just the API. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | MUI only, with mui-mcp lookup. Toast via useToast, confirm via Dialog/ConfirmDialog. |\n| NFR-8 | UI | DataGrid MIT: no `pinnedColumns` and no `@mui/x-data-grid-pro`. Sticky header is the default. |\n| NFR-9 | all | New code only in src/server/gradebook/ and src/server/report-cards/. Hooks into existing services are one-line calls. Use `logger`, no console.log. |\n| NFR-10 | CALC, SYNC | Past-due uses an instant comparison (`now > dueAt`). Term containment uses a tz date comparison (B10). |\n| NFR-11 | UI | A4 portrait `@page` rule. Long course lists may need a 2nd page, with table rows set to `break-inside: avoid`. |\n| NFR-12 | all | Tests per the intake list. Integration tests hit the real sync hooks (B3/B4/B7). |\n| NFR-13 | — | Scope guard: store `gpa`, never compute it. No rank or transcript. |\n\n## 3. Risks / decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **R1 (FR-7 timing):** AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL visibility arrive later than GRADED. Without the B4 bulk hooks, those quizzes never sync. Syncing early would break NFR-5.\n- **R2 (FR-4 vs FR-24):** the teacher's hide toggle and the source-driven `isVisible` share one column. Re-saving an assignment would silently re-show a teacher-hidden item. Options: (a) source sync writes isVisible only on publish/archive *transitions*; (b) add a separate `hiddenByTeacher` flag and make visible = sourceVisible ∧ ¬hiddenByTeacher. (b) is clearer but adds a column beyond FR-1's \"exactly as specified\". Pick one and state it.\n- **R3 (FR-12 Uncategorised weight):** the PRD doesn't say what weight the implicit bucket carries when real categories exist. A sensible default is weight 0, so it's shown but excluded from the weighted mean, unless it's the only bucket. This affects the FR-15 golden test only if it has uncategorised items (it doesn't). Flag it.\n- **R4 (FR-38 dedupe):** \"one notification per student per item\" needs a marker. A nullable `Grade.notifiedAt` claimed via `updateMany` follows the existing claim pattern.\n- **R5 (FR-3 term drift):** re-deriving the term on every edit can move existing grades between terms. Only recompute it when dueAt/availableUntil changes.\n- **R6 (FR-16 delete):** deleting a scale referenced by courses or by DRAFT snapshots (PUBLISHED ones embed the legend, so they're safe). Recommend blocking the delete with CONFLICT while courses reference the scale.\n- **R7 (first DataGrid):** there is no in-repo precedent. Keyboard E/M/Delete handling within the MIT tier is the main implementation risk (intake keyRisk). The design should keep the grid behind one client component.\n\n## 4. Carried-forward assumptions (from intake, adjusted)\n\n1. FR-6: unexempting clears excused and re-syncs the score from the source.\n2. FR-7: **use the existing `getStudentQuizScore`** (B1) plus a caller-side `resultsVisible` gate. This replaces intake's \"build a new helper\".\n3. FR-13: 89.95 → 90.0 → **A−** under the seed scale. The test asserts 90.0 and the 90-band letter.\n4. FR-27/FR-33: add nav entries per the convention.\n5. NFR-10: past due = `now > dueAt` (exact instant). Term containment is evaluated in the school timezone.\n6. FR-3: no containing term and no current term → skip the item + `logger.warn`.\n7. New and unstated (needs sign-off): FR-14 percent-only override re-derives the letter; FR-32 comments are editable only while DRAFT; FR-34 unpublish returns to DRAFT.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012RW7s6dVESemUsNtsFo6WW","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8dcae7d9-b717-4417-9584-7ef748d2b9e4","uuid":"8106fc67-8207-4da3-ac9c-aecf81d0b06e","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:05:19.153Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-11\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards (SCH-011). It has 42 FRs and 13 NFRs (55 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions (FR-6, FR-7, FR-13, FR-27/33, NFR-10, FR-3 no-term) are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> As of this writing the other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **leftovers from earlier tickets**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-11 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-11 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | **`getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` already exists.** It is labelled \"PRD-11 export\". It loads GRADED attempts, applies `applyScoringPolicy(quiz.scoringPolicy, …)`, and returns `{score, maxScore, percent, attemptsCounted, isPractice}` (fixed2 strings) or null. | src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts L355-372 | **This corrects intake** (B-finding 5 and the FR-7 assumption). FR-7 calls it directly, with no new helper. It does **not** check `resultsVisible`, so the sync caller must gate on that (NFR-5). The batch path (FR-8 backfill, NFR-3) should run `applyScoringPolicy` in memory over attempts it has already loaded, rather than calling this per student. |\n| B2 | `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` covers IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE (`now >= availableUntil`) / MANUAL (`resultsReleasedAt != null`). | src/server/quiz/grading.ts L94 | FR-7 / NFR-5 gate. AFTER_CLOSE depends on time, so a GRADED attempt is not syncable until close. See B4. |\n| B3 | Every quiz attempt status change goes through `recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)`. It is called from `submitAttempt` (L123, which includes auto-submit), `gradeAnswerManually` (L338) and `regradeQuiz` (quiz-service L435). | attempt-service.ts L73-81 | FR-7 hook. After each caller commits, call `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`, which no-ops unless GRADED + visible + !isPractice. Making this one function the only quiz sync entry point covers all three callers. |\n| B4 | Results become visible through `releaseResults` (MANUAL, quiz-service L464) and `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased` (AFTER_CLOSE). The latter claims `resultsReleasedAt` with `updateMany` on each maintenance tick. | quiz-service.ts L464; quiz/maintenance.ts L27-40 | FR-7 also needs a **bulk** `syncQuizGrades(quizId)` in both places. Otherwise AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL quizzes never reach the gradebook. The maintenance claim is already idempotent, so put the sync after `count === 1`. |\n| B5 | Quiz lifecycle: `createQuiz`, `updateQuiz` (DRAFT→PUBLISHED and PUBLISHED→CLOSED via guarded `updateMany`, L304-305), `deleteQuiz` (hard delete, L317). Quizzes have **no archive**. | quiz-service.ts L259-317 | FR-3: upsert the item on →PUBLISHED. FR-4: delete the item on deleteQuiz. CLOSED is **not** unpublish, so the item stays visible. Settings edits to a published quiz (title, availableUntil, categoryId, max) re-upsert the item. |\n| B6 | Assignment lifecycle: `createAssignment` / `updateAssignment` (status DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED); `publishOnce` (cron, makes SCHEDULED visible once `availableFrom` passes); `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` (hard delete in a tx, or sets `archivedAt` when submissions exist, L479-492). `isAssignmentVisible` = !archivedAt && published-or-scheduled-reached. | assignments-service.ts L67-74, L292-330, L437-492 | FR-3/FR-4: compute GradeItem.isVisible from `isAssignmentVisible`. Upsert on create/update/publishOnce, set isVisible=false on archive, delete inside the delete tx. **FR-24's teacher hide toggle conflicts with this** (see §3 R2). |\n| B7 | Return paths: `gradeSubmission` (`returning = input.return && status !== 'RETURNED'`; it also re-grades an already-RETURNED submission), `bulkReturn`, and `gradeOffline` (`input.return`). | assignments-service.ts ~L696-800 | FR-5: sync when the submission **is RETURNED after the write**, not only on the transition. Re-grading a returned submission must update Grade.score, and grade-without-return must not sync (AC-3). Use one `syncSubmissionGrade(submissionId)` from all three. |\n| B8 | `setExemption(…, exempt)` upserts or deletes `GradeExemption` (L818/L824) and audits `assignment.exempt` / `assignment.unexempt`. | assignments-service.ts L815-838 | FR-6: call `syncSubmissionGrade` (or a by-(assignment, student) variant) after both branches. Unexempt re-derives the score from a RETURNED submission, else null. |\n| B9 | GradeItem has a polymorphic `source + sourceId` with **no FK**. Assignment and Quiz deletes will not cascade. | FR-1 model spec | FR-4: delete the GradeItem explicitly inside the same transaction as the source delete (and in `deleteQuiz`, which today runs outside a tx). Grade → GradeItem should be `onDelete: Cascade`. |\n| B10 | `Term` has no `isCurrent`. It has `academicYearId`, `startDate`/`endDate` as `@db.Date`, `order`. `AcademicYear.isCurrent` exists. `Course.academicYearId` exists. | schema.prisma L240-252, Course ~L415 | FR-3 term placement: pick the term of **the course's academic year** whose `[startDate, endDate]` contains dueAt, comparing dates in the school timezone (NFR-10). The fallback \"current term\" is the term of that year containing today (tz), else skip + `logger.warn`. Put this in one pure helper `termFor(date, terms, tz)`. |\n| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from assignments-service. `dec` / `fixed2` / `Decimal` come from grading-math (isomorphic). `percentOf` (1 dp half-up) is in quiz/grading.ts. | assignments-service.ts L57; grading-math.ts L7-15; grading.ts L133 | NFR-1/NFR-10/FR-13 reuse these. `percentOf` rounds to 1 dp on a single value. grade-calc must keep full-precision Decimal until the **final** rounding (FR-13), so it must not round category percents early. |\n| B12 | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` exist. `getAccessibleStudentIds` / `assertCanViewStudent` cover own student, linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`), teacher and admin, with homeroom handled there too. `src/server/quiz/access.ts` has `canManageCourse`. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts, student-access.ts | FR-39 \"manage\"/\"view\" and FR-42 reuse these. FR-37 report-card access is new: ADMIN; teachers of any course on the card or the homeroom teacher; the student or a linked parent only when PUBLISHED. Return NOT_FOUND to everyone else (AC-7). |\n| B13 | Attendance aggregation already exists: `getReport(filters)` → `StudentSummaryRow` (StatusCounts per student) using a single `groupBy(studentId, status)`. It filters by date range, grade level, section and course. | attendance-service.ts L528-582 | FR-30 attendance summary and NFR-3 batching: call `getReport({from: term.start, to: term.end, sectionId/gradeLevelId})` **once** per generate request. Do not loop per student. Rate formula: reuse whatever StatusCounts consumers use. Do not invent a new one. |\n| B14 | `SchoolSettings` singleton: name, shortName, logoUrl, timezone, address fields. Student profile: `admissionNumber`, `gradeLevel`. `Section.homeroomTeacherId`. | schema.prisma L109-113, L198-215 | FR-30 snapshot fields all come from existing models. No schema change beyond FR-1. |\n| B15 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const already contains assignment.* and quiz.* entries. `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents()` never throw. `audit()` never throws. | notifications/types.ts, notify.ts L28/L98, audit.ts L26 | FR-38: add `grade.posted` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, STUDENT+PARENT) and `report_card.published` (defaultEmail true, STUDENT+PARENT). Call them after commit. NFR-4 audit actions: `grade.update`, `termOverride.upsert`, `reportCard.unpublish` (plus `reportCard.publish` and `gradingScale.*` as nice-to-haves). |\n| B16 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are static arrays. `studentTabs` notes \"No tab bar renders studentTabs yet\". `navigation` is a flat array with `roles` and an optional `group: 'Administration'`. | src/config/*.ts | FR-18/28: add course tabs `gradebook` (TEACHER, ADMIN) and `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT). FR-26/36: add student tabs `grades` and `report-cards`. These are reachable by URL only, the same as `assignments`. FR-27/33 + admin pages: nav entries `/grades`, `/report-cards`, `/admin/grading-scales`, `/admin/report-cards`. |\n| B17 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` are in src/server/csv.ts. Shared components: DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast (useToast), PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, DateDisplay, UserPicker, FormField, LoadingSkeleton. **No existing `@mui/x-data-grid` usage in src.** | src/server/csv.ts; src/components/ | FR-25: export on the server with `toCsv`, building the same columns as the grid. FR-18 is the first DataGrid in the codebase, so its MIT-tier API (columnGroupingModel, processRowUpdate, virtualisation, no pinning) must be looked up via mui-mcp for 9.5.0 (NFR-7/8). FR-29 table → DataTable. |\n| B18 | Scripts: `db:seed` = `tsx prisma/seed.ts`. There is no `gradebook:backfill`. The seed looks up courses by code with `findCourse([...])`. | package.json; prisma/seed.ts | FR-8: add `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`, a thin wrapper over an exported `backfillGradebook()` in src/server/gradebook/ that the seed also calls before the FR-41 data. |\n| B19 | Postgres. Migrations already hand-add raw SQL partial indexes. Prisma 5.20. | prisma/migrations/* | FR-1: one migration. It needs `@@unique([source, sourceId])` on GradeItem (sync and backfill idempotency), `@@unique([gradeItemId, studentId])` on Grade, `@@unique([courseId, termId, studentId])` on TermGradeOverride, and `@@unique([studentId, termId])` on ReportCard. These make the upserts race-safe. A one-default-scale rule can be a partial unique index `WHERE \"isDefault\"` (FR-16). |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **SYNC** source→gradebook sync hook · **CALC** pure calculation · **API** REST endpoint · **UI** page/component · **AUTH** access boundary · **JOB** script/batch · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **CFG** config registry.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | New enums + 6 models in one `prisma migrate` migration. Use the unique keys from B19. Grade: `score Decimal?`, `excused`, `missing`, `comment`, `gradedById`, `gradedAt`. ReportCard: `status`, `snapshot Json`, `homeroomComment`, `principalComment`, `publishedAt`, `publishedById`. |\n| FR-2 | DM, UI | Nullable `Course.gradingScaleId`, `Assignment.categoryId` and `Quiz.categoryId` with `onDelete: SetNull`. Category deletion via FR-40 must not delete sources. Add one `Select` to the existing assignment and quiz editors, plus the validator fields in assignments.ts / quiz.ts (optional and nullable). Don't change existing behaviour. |\n| FR-3 | SYNC | `upsertGradeItemFromAssignment(id)` / `…FromQuiz(id)` keyed on (source, sourceId). Skip practice quizzes. Term placement via `termFor` (B10). Callers per B5/B6. Keep the GradeItem's term stable after first creation unless the date changes, so grades don't jump terms on unrelated edits. |\n| FR-4 | SYNC | Archive sets isVisible=false. Delete removes the GradeItem in the same tx (B9). Quiz has no archive or unpublish. A practice-toggle after publish should delete or hide the item. |\n| FR-5 | SYNC | `syncSubmissionGrade` from 3 return paths (B7). It writes only when RETURNED. Score = `finalScore`. |\n| FR-6 | SYNC | From `setExemption` (B8). Exemption wins over the score: excused=true and the score is kept. |\n| FR-7 | SYNC | Per-attempt `syncQuizGrade` after `recomputeAttempt` callers (B3). Bulk `syncQuizGrades` on release and AFTER_CLOSE (B4). Score scaled: `score/maxScore × GradeItem.maxPoints`, Decimal. |\n| FR-8 | JOB | `backfillGradebook()`: batch load per course, reuse the same upsert builders as live sync (one code path), idempotent through the unique keys. npm script + seed call (B18). |\n| FR-9 | API, AUTH | The service rejects score/excused/missing edits on non-MANUAL items (`AppError('FORBIDDEN'/'VALIDATION_ERROR')`). Comment stays editable. The grid marks those columns non-editable. |\n| FR-10 | CALC | `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts`: pure, Decimal-only, no Prisma client import (types only). Input: items, grades, categories, scale, override, `now`. Counted = visible ∧ ¬excused ∧ (score≠null ∨ (missing ∧ now>dueAt)). |\n| FR-11 | CALC | Drop lowest by item **percentage**, keeping ≥1. Ties are dropped deterministically (by dueAt, then id). |\n| FR-12 | CALC | Implicit \"Uncategorised\" bucket. What weight does it get? The PRD is silent, so see §3 R3. No categories gives a points total. |\n| FR-13 | CALC | `toDecimalPlaces(1, ROUND_HALF_UP)` only at the end. Bands are sorted descending, first `percent >= minPercent`. |\n| FR-14 | CALC | The override is applied after computing. A letter-only override keeps the computed percent. A percent-only override probably re-derives the letter from the scale (unstated, so flag it). |\n| FR-15 | CALC, UI | Golden unit test (78.0 C+). The gradebook and student Grades **must call the same function**, with no client-side recomputation. |\n| FR-16 | API, UI, DM | `/admin/grading-scales` (ADMIN). Band validation lives in a Zod refinement shared by client and server. \"Exactly one default\" uses a tx that clears others + a partial unique index. Deleting a scale in use is either blocked or falls back to the default; decide this. |\n| FR-17 | UI, API | Course settings page. The live weight sum is client-side, with the 100 check repeated server-side in FR-40. Decimal weights: compare with `dec(sum).eq(100)`, not floats. |\n| FR-18 | UI, API, CALC | First DataGrid. The server returns one denormalised payload `{students, items, categories, grades, computed}` for (course, term) in a fixed number of queries (NFR-2). Columns are built client-side from it. Sort by last name on the server. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Pure cell renderer. \"Late\" needs `Submission.isLate`, so the gradebook payload must carry the source submission's isLate. |\n| FR-20 | UI, API | `processRowUpdate` → PATCH a single grade. E/M/Delete need a custom edit cell / `onCellKeyDown` (check mui-mcp). Optimistic update with per-cell error. Audited (NFR-4). Triggers `grade.posted` (FR-38). |\n| FR-21 | UI | The cell click opens a link to the submission grading page or the quiz attempt. The payload needs `submissionId` / `attemptId` per synced grade. |\n| FR-22 | API, UI | POST manual item. Validate that the term belongs to the course's academic year and the category belongs to the course. |\n| FR-23 | API, UI, AUD | PUT override (upsert). Comment ≤1000 chars. Audit with old/new values. |\n| FR-24 | API, UI | Toggle visibility (see R2). Bulk-missing allowed only if `now > dueAt` and only for ungraded rows. Stats come from the computed payload, client-side, over counted scores. |\n| FR-25 | API | Server CSV via `toCsv`, using the same row builder as the grid. \"As displayed\" means EX/M/— markers and the term letter. |\n| FR-26 | UI, API, CFG | Student tab → `GET /api/students/:id/grades?termId`. The colour thresholds come from a single helper reused by FR-27/28. |\n| FR-27 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/grades` reuses the FR-26 component. Parent child selector from `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Nav entry. |\n| FR-28 | UI, CFG | Course tab `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT): same endpoint filtered by courseId. |\n| FR-29 | UI, API | `/admin/report-cards`: list query joins students (grade level, section filters) with ReportCard status for the term. Missing-data warnings are computed in batch (ungraded counted-eligible items, missing TermGradeOverride.comment per course). |\n| FR-30 | JOB, API | `generate`: batch load (NFR-3), compute in memory, write the snapshot JSON (versioned shape, e.g. `snapshot.v = 1`). Teacher comment = `TermGradeOverride.comment`. Attendance via B13. |\n| FR-31 | JOB, DM | `upsert` with `where status = DRAFT` semantics: createMany for new cards, `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})` for existing ones, never touching PUBLISHED. Grade-edit services never import report-cards code. |\n| FR-32 | API, UI, AUTH | PATCH: field-level role check (homeroomComment: homeroom teacher of the student's section or ADMIN; principalComment: ADMIN). Edits are allowed only while DRAFT (implied, so flag it). |\n| FR-33 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/report-cards` (TEACHER): drafts for sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Nav entry. |\n| FR-34 | API, NOTIF, AUD | Publish (one or bulk) with a guarded `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})`, then notify after commit. Unpublish: ADMIN, reason required, audit, back to DRAFT. |\n| FR-35 | UI | `/report-cards/[id]/print` renders from the **snapshot only**. `@media print` via MUI `GlobalStyles`, hiding the sidebar. Bulk print: one page renders N cards with `break-after: page`. |\n| FR-36 | UI, CFG, API | Student tab \"Report cards\". The list endpoint filters to PUBLISHED for student/parent (NFR-5). |\n| FR-37 | AUTH | New `assertCanViewReportCard`. Non-entitled users get NOT_FOUND, so existence isn't leaked. |\n| FR-38 | NOTIF | Register 2 types (B15). `grade.posted`: only for MANUAL items, only when a score is first entered or changed (one per student per item, so an idempotency marker such as `Grade.notifiedAt` is needed; flag it). |\n| FR-39 | API, AUTH | Thin route handlers using `withHandler`, Zod in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, and services in `src/server/gradebook/` + `src/server/report-cards/`. |\n| FR-40 | API | Replace-all in a tx: delete missing ids (sources → SetNull), upsert the rest. Weights total 100 (Decimal). |\n| FR-41 | JOB | Seed: scale, 7A categories, 'Oral presentation' + grades, draft S1 cards for 7A with MATH/ENG override comments. Run after `backfillGradebook()`. |\n| FR-42 | API, AUTH | Student serializer: visible items only. Grade rows only exist for released scores (sync gating), so the risk is mainly hidden items and MANUAL items with isVisible=false. Still filter explicitly. |\n| NFR-1 | CALC | Decimal throughout. Unit matrix in `grade-calc.test.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | API | Gradebook: ~5 queries (enrollments, items, grades, categories, scale + override), all indexed by (courseId, termId). The grid virtualises. |\n| NFR-3 | JOB | Generation: per term, `findMany` items/grades/overrides/categories for all courses in scope with `in` filters, then group in memory. One attendance `groupBy`. Chunk the writes. |\n| NFR-4 | AUD | Old/new values in metadata for grade.update, termOverride.upsert and reportCard.unpublish. |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Enforced in 3 layers: sync gating (B2/B7), student serializer (FR-42), report-card guard (FR-37). Integration tests for each. |\n| NFR-6 | AUTH | Every route uses requireUser/requireRole + an entity check (B12). Server pages check too, not just the API. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | MUI only, with mui-mcp lookup. Toast via useToast, confirm via Dialog/ConfirmDialog. |\n| NFR-8 | UI | DataGrid MIT: no `pinnedColumns` and no `@mui/x-data-grid-pro`. Sticky header is the default. |\n| NFR-9 | all | New code only in src/server/gradebook/ and src/server/report-cards/. Hooks into existing services are one-line calls. Use `logger`, no console.log. |\n| NFR-10 | CALC, SYNC | Past-due uses an instant comparison (`now > dueAt`). Term containment uses a tz date comparison (B10). |\n| NFR-11 | UI | A4 portrait `@page` rule. Long course lists may need a 2nd page, with table rows set to `break-inside: avoid`. |\n| NFR-12 | all | Tests per the intake list. Integration tests hit the real sync hooks (B3/B4/B7). |\n| NFR-13 | — | Scope guard: store `gpa`, never compute it. No rank or transcript. |\n\n## 3. Risks / decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **R1 (FR-7 timing):** AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL visibility arrive later than GRADED. Without the B4 bulk hooks, those quizzes never sync. Syncing early would break NFR-5.\n- **R2 (FR-4 vs FR-24):** the teacher's hide toggle and the source-driven `isVisible` share one column. Re-saving an assignment would silently re-show a teacher-hidden item. Options: (a) source sync writes isVisible only on publish/archive *transitions*; (b) add a separate `hiddenByTeacher` flag and make visible = sourceVisible ∧ ¬hiddenByTeacher. (b) is clearer but adds a column beyond FR-1's \"exactly as specified\". Pick one and state it.\n- **R3 (FR-12 Uncategorised weight):** the PRD doesn't say what weight the implicit bucket carries when real categories exist. A sensible default is weight 0, so it's shown but excluded from the weighted mean, unless it's the only bucket. This affects the FR-15 golden test only if it has uncategorised items (it doesn't). Flag it.\n- **R4 (FR-38 dedupe):** \"one notification per student per item\" needs a marker. A nullable `Grade.notifiedAt` claimed via `updateMany` follows the existing claim pattern.\n- **R5 (FR-3 term drift):** re-deriving the term on every edit can move existing grades between terms. Only recompute it when dueAt/availableUntil changes.\n- **R6 (FR-16 delete):** deleting a scale referenced by courses or by DRAFT snapshots (PUBLISHED ones embed the legend, so they're safe). Recommend blocking the delete with CONFLICT while courses reference the scale.\n- **R7 (first DataGrid):** there is no in-repo precedent. Keyboard E/M/Delete handling within the MIT tier is the main implementation risk (intake keyRisk). The design should keep the grid behind one client component.\n\n## 4. Carried-forward assumptions (from intake, adjusted)\n\n1. FR-6: unexempting clears excused and re-syncs the score from the source.\n2. FR-7: **use the existing `getStudentQuizScore`** (B1) plus a caller-side `resultsVisible` gate. This replaces intake's \"build a new helper\".\n3. FR-13: 89.95 → 90.0 → **A−** under the seed scale. The test asserts 90.0 and the 90-band letter.\n4. FR-27/FR-33: add nav entries per the convention.\n5. NFR-10: past due = `now > dueAt` (exact instant). Term containment is evaluated in the school timezone.\n6. FR-3: no containing term and no current term → skip the item + `logger.warn`.\n7. New and unstated (needs sign-off): FR-14 percent-only override re-derives the letter; FR-32 comments are editable only while DRAFT; FR-34 unpublish returns to DRAFT.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":111,"newStart":1,"newLines":113,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-10","+# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-11"," "," Written by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams (SCH-010). It has 39 FRs and 10 NFRs (49 requirements) at 96% confidence.","-`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It flags assumptions on FR-33/34/35/37/38/39. Those are restated in §3 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards (SCH-011). It has 42 FRs and 13 NFRs (55 requirements) at 95% confidence.","+`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions (FR-6, FR-7, FR-13, FR-27/33, NFR-10, FR-3 no-term) are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward."," ","-> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-9 leftovers** as of this writing (`ticketId: \"SH-9\"`). Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-10 input.","+> As of this writing the other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **leftovers from earlier tickets**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-11 input."," "," ## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk"," ","-| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-10 |","+| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-11 |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| B1 | `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child. `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Both throw `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These cover FR-34 and the course part of NFR-5. Attempt-level checks are still new: owner, linked parent, or manager. |","-| B2 | `courseTabs` is a static array of `{key, label, href, roles}`. | src/config/course-tabs.ts | FR-11: add one entry, `{ key: 'quizzes', href: id => /courses/${id}/quizzes, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. |","-| B3 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` and then `sendDueReminders(now)` on every request, each wrapped in its own try/catch + logger. Purges run in a once-per-day block. | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-18/FR-30/FR-35: add `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` and `sendQuizResultsReleased(now)` **on every call**, next to sendDueReminders, each with its own try/catch. |","-| B4 | `sendDueReminders` is idempotent through a unique-key claim row (`AssignmentReminder`, P2002 → skip). | src/server/assignments/reminders.ts | FR-30 AFTER_CLOSE needs a \"sent once\" marker. The simplest option is a nullable `Quiz.resultsNotifiedAt`, claimed with `updateMany({ where: { id, resultsNotifiedAt: null } })` and a count check. That needs no new table. If FR-1's model list must stay exact, a claim table is the alternative. |","-| B5 | `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds})` never throw. Call them after commit. | src/server/notifications/notify.ts | FR-29 → `notify()` to enrolled students. FR-30 → `notifyStudentAndParents`. |","-| B6 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object. New keys need `label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles`. | src/server/notifications/types.ts | FR-29: `quiz.published` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, roles STUDENT). `quiz.results_released` (ACADEMIC, roles STUDENT+PARENT). The PRD doesn't give a default email setting for results_released. Default it to true to match assignment.graded, and flag that choice. |","-| B7 | `audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request})` never throws. | src/server/audit.ts | FR-38 actions: `quizAnswer.grade`, `quiz.regrade`, `quiz.release_results`, `quizAccommodation.update`. |","-| B8 | `grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic. It exports `dec`, `fixed2` and `Decimal` from the Prisma browser runtime. `assignments-service.ts` exports `serializeDecimal` and `getSchoolTimezone`. | src/server/assignments/* | FR-3/FR-22/FR-25 reuse dec/fixed2 (NFR-7). Importing from `@/server/assignments/grading-math` is fine. Only lift it to a shared module if dev-planning wants that. Do not copy it. |","-| B9 | `http.ts` provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `AppError`. The codes include CONFLICT (409). Zod errors become VALIDATION_ERROR. Prisma P2002 becomes CONFLICT. | src/server/http.ts | NFR-6. FR-16's 409 is `AppError('CONFLICT', ...)`. |","-| B10 | The DB is PostgreSQL. The project already uses raw-SQL partial unique indexes in migrations. | prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/migration.sql L77-78 | FR-19 race-safety: `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE status = 'IN_PROGRESS'`, hand-added to the FR-1 migration. Add `@@unique([quizId, studentId, attemptNumber])` too. On P2002 during start, re-read and resume. |","-| B11 | File contexts are registered in `registerBuiltInContexts` (lesson, logo, assignment, submission). `attachFiles` sets context/contextId. | src/server/files/contexts.ts, files-service.ts | FR-39: question images need a `'quiz'` context (contextId = quizId) with a resolver: manager, or a viewer with an IN_PROGRESS or visible attempt. The prompt Markdown references the file URL. |","-| B12 | Courses MATH-7A and ENG-7A are looked up in seed.ts with `findCourse([...])`. The seed already uses `console.log` for skips. | prisma/seed.ts L302, L340 | FR-36 follows that pattern (the seed is exempt from the no-console.log rule in practice). |","-| B13 | Installed: @mui/* 9.5.0 (incl. x-charts, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers), @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + sortable 10.0.0, zod 3.23.8, prisma 5.20, vitest, Playwright + axe. | package.json | FR-7, FR-26 and NFR-8 need **no new dependencies** (NFR-7). |","-| B14 | Shared components are DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast, MarkdownEditor, MarkdownView, FileUpload, StatCard, EmptyState, PageHeader, DateDisplay. | src/components/ | FR-7/12/17/24/26/39 reuse them. |","-| B15 | `toStudentSubmission(dto)` is the precedent for a student-shaped serializer. | assignments-service.ts L199 | NFR-1: add `toStudentQuiz` / `toStudentAttempt` in `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts`, with a unit test asserting the `correct` key is absent. |","+| B1 | **`getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` already exists.** It is labelled \"PRD-11 export\". It loads GRADED attempts, applies `applyScoringPolicy(quiz.scoringPolicy, …)`, and returns `{score, maxScore, percent, attemptsCounted, isPractice}` (fixed2 strings) or null. | src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts L355-372 | **This corrects intake** (B-finding 5 and the FR-7 assumption). FR-7 calls it directly, with no new helper. It does **not** check `resultsVisible`, so the sync caller must gate on that (NFR-5). The batch path (FR-8 backfill, NFR-3) should run `applyScoringPolicy` in memory over attempts it has already loaded, rather than calling this per student. |","+| B2 | `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` covers IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE (`now >= availableUntil`) / MANUAL (`resultsReleasedAt != null`). | src/server/quiz/grading.ts L94 | FR-7 / NFR-5 gate. AFTER_CLOSE depends on time, so a GRADED attempt is not syncable until close. See B4. |","+| B3 | Every quiz attempt status change goes through `recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)`. It is called from `submitAttempt` (L123, which includes auto-submit), `gradeAnswerManually` (L338) and `regradeQuiz` (quiz-service L435). | attempt-service.ts L73-81 | FR-7 hook. After each caller commits, call `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`, which no-ops unless GRADED + visible + !isPractice. Making this one function the only quiz sync entry point covers all three callers. |","+| B4 | Results become visible through `releaseResults` (MANUAL, quiz-service L464) and `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased` (AFTER_CLOSE). The latter claims `resultsReleasedAt` with `updateMany` on each maintenance tick. | quiz-service.ts L464; quiz/maintenance.ts L27-40 | FR-7 also needs a **bulk** `syncQuizGrades(quizId)` in both places. Otherwise AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL quizzes never reach the gradebook. The maintenance claim is already idempotent, so put the sync after `count === 1`. |","+| B5 | Quiz lifecycle: `createQuiz`, `updateQuiz` (DRAFT→PUBLISHED and PUBLISHED→CLOSED via guarded `updateMany`, L304-305), `deleteQuiz` (hard delete, L317). Quizzes have **no archive**. | quiz-service.ts L259-317 | FR-3: upsert the item on →PUBLISHED. FR-4: delete the item on deleteQuiz. CLOSED is **not** unpublish, so the item stays visible. Settings edits to a published quiz (title, availableUntil, categoryId, max) re-upsert the item. |","+| B6 | Assignment lifecycle: `createAssignment` / `updateAssignment` (status DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED); `publishOnce` (cron, makes SCHEDULED visible once `availableFrom` passes); `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` (hard delete in a tx, or sets `archivedAt` when submissions exist, L479-492). `isAssignmentVisible` = !archivedAt && published-or-scheduled-reached. | assignments-service.ts L67-74, L292-330, L437-492 | FR-3/FR-4: compute GradeItem.isVisible from `isAssignmentVisible`. Upsert on create/update/publishOnce, set isVisible=false on archive, delete inside the delete tx. **FR-24's teacher hide toggle conflicts with this** (see §3 R2). |","+| B7 | Return paths: `gradeSubmission` (`returning = input.return && status !== 'RETURNED'`; it also re-grades an already-RETURNED submission), `bulkReturn`, and `gradeOffline` (`input.return`). | assignments-service.ts ~L696-800 | FR-5: sync when the submission **is RETURNED after the write**, not only on the transition. Re-grading a returned submission must update Grade.score, and grade-without-return must not sync (AC-3). Use one `syncSubmissionGrade(submissionId)` from all three. |","+| B8 | `setExemption(…, exempt)` upserts or deletes `GradeExemption` (L818/L824) and audits `assignment.exempt` / `assignment.unexempt`. | assignments-service.ts L815-838 | FR-6: call `syncSubmissionGrade` (or a by-(assignment, student) variant) after both branches. Unexempt re-derives the score from a RETURNED submission, else null. |","+| B9 | GradeItem has a polymorphic `source + sourceId` with **no FK**. Assignment and Quiz deletes will not cascade. | FR-1 model spec | FR-4: delete the GradeItem explicitly inside the same transaction as the source delete (and in `deleteQuiz`, which today runs outside a tx). Grade → GradeItem should be `onDelete: Cascade`. |","+| B10 | `Term` has no `isCurrent`. It has `academicYearId`, `startDate`/`endDate` as `@db.Date`, `order`. `AcademicYear.isCurrent` exists. `Course.academicYearId` exists. | schema.prisma L240-252, Course ~L415 | FR-3 term placement: pick the term of **the course's academic year** whose `[startDate, endDate]` contains dueAt, comparing dates in the school timezone (NFR-10). The fallback \"current term\" is the term of that year containing today (tz), else skip + `logger.warn`. Put this in one pure helper `termFor(date, terms, tz)`. |","+| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from assignments-service. `dec` / `fixed2` / `Decimal` come from grading-math (isomorphic). `percentOf` (1 dp half-up) is in quiz/grading.ts. | assignments-service.ts L57; grading-math.ts L7-15; grading.ts L133 | NFR-1/NFR-10/FR-13 reuse these. `percentOf` rounds to 1 dp on a single value. grade-calc must keep full-precision Decimal until the **final** rounding (FR-13), so it must not round category percents early. |","+| B12 | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` exist. `getAccessibleStudentIds` / `assertCanViewStudent` cover own student, linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`), teacher and admin, with homeroom handled there too. `src/server/quiz/access.ts` has `canManageCourse`. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts, student-access.ts | FR-39 \"manage\"/\"view\" and FR-42 reuse these. FR-37 report-card access is new: ADMIN; teachers of any course on the card or the homeroom teacher; the student or a linked parent only when PUBLISHED. Return NOT_FOUND to everyone else (AC-7). |","+| B13 | Attendance aggregation already exists: `getReport(filters)` → `StudentSummaryRow` (StatusCounts per student) using a single `groupBy(studentId, status)`. It filters by date range, grade level, section and course. | attendance-service.ts L528-582 | FR-30 attendance summary and NFR-3 batching: call `getReport({from: term.start, to: term.end, sectionId/gradeLevelId})` **once** per generate request. Do not loop per student. Rate formula: reuse whatever StatusCounts consumers use. Do not invent a new one. |","+| B14 | `SchoolSettings` singleton: name, shortName, logoUrl, timezone, address fields. Student profile: `admissionNumber`, `gradeLevel`. `Section.homeroomTeacherId`. | schema.prisma L109-113, L198-215 | FR-30 snapshot fields all come from existing models. No schema change beyond FR-1. |","+| B15 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const already contains assignment.* and quiz.* entries. `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents()` never throw. `audit()` never throws. | notifications/types.ts, notify.ts L28/L98, audit.ts L26 | FR-38: add `grade.posted` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, STUDENT+PARENT) and `report_card.published` (defaultEmail true, STUDENT+PARENT). Call them after commit. NFR-4 audit actions: `grade.update`, `termOverride.upsert`, `reportCard.unpublish` (plus `reportCard.publish` and `gradingScale.*` as nice-to-haves). |","+| B16 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are static arrays. `studentTabs` notes \"No tab bar renders studentTabs yet\". `navigation` is a flat array with `roles` and an optional `group: 'Administration'`. | src/config/*.ts | FR-18/28: add course tabs `gradebook` (TEACHER, ADMIN) and `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT). FR-26/36: add student tabs `grades` and `report-cards`. These are reachable by URL only, the same as `assignments`. FR-27/33 + admin pages: nav entries `/grades`, `/report-cards`, `/admin/grading-scales`, `/admin/report-cards`. |","+| B17 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` are in src/server/csv.ts. Shared components: DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast (useToast), PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, DateDisplay, UserPicker, FormField, LoadingSkeleton. **No existing `@mui/x-data-grid` usage in src.** | src/server/csv.ts; src/components/ | FR-25: export on the server with `toCsv`, building the same columns as the grid. FR-18 is the first DataGrid in the codebase, so its MIT-tier API (columnGroupingModel, processRowUpdate, virtualisation, no pinning) must be looked up via mui-mcp for 9.5.0 (NFR-7/8). FR-29 table → DataTable. |","+| B18 | Scripts: `db:seed` = `tsx prisma/seed.ts`. There is no `gradebook:backfill`. The seed looks up courses by code with `findCourse([...])`. | package.json; prisma/seed.ts | FR-8: add `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`, a thin wrapper over an exported `backfillGradebook()` in src/server/gradebook/ that the seed also calls before the FR-41 data. |","+| B19 | Postgres. Migrations already hand-add raw SQL partial indexes. Prisma 5.20. | prisma/migrations/* | FR-1: one migration. It needs `@@unique([source, sourceId])` on GradeItem (sync and backfill idempotency), `@@unique([gradeItemId, studentId])` on Grade, `@@unique([courseId, termId, studentId])` on TermGradeOverride, and `@@unique([studentId, termId])` on ReportCard. These make the upserts race-safe. A one-default-scale rule can be a partial unique index `WHERE \"isDefault\"` (FR-16). |"," "," ## 2. Requirement → architectural concern"," ","-Concern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **VAL** validator · **PURE** pure domain logic · **SVC** service (src/server/quiz/) · **API** route handler · **UI** page/component · **JOB** maintenance pass · **AUTH** access boundary · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **SEED** seed · **CFG** config registry · **TEST**","+Concern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **SYNC** source→gradebook sync hook · **CALC** pure calculation · **API** REST endpoint · **UI** page/component · **AUTH** access boundary · **JOB** script/batch · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **CFG** config registry."," "," | Req | Concern | Notes |"," |---|---|---|","-| FR-1 | DM | One migration, `add_quizzes`. 5 enums, 5 models. Back-relations on Course (`quizzes`) and User (attempts, accommodations, graded answers). QuizAnswer PK `(attemptId, questionId)` (NFR-2). QuizAccommodation unique `(quizId, studentId)`. Include the partial unique index from B10 in the SQL. Money-like fields (points, scores) are `Decimal(6,2)`, per the assignments precedent. |","-| FR-2 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`, client-safe, shared by the builder UI and the handlers. Use per-type question schemas as a discriminated union on `type`. `availableUntil > availableFrom` and the time-limit cross-field checks use `.superRefine`. |","-| FR-3 | PURE | `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. No Prisma import, so the builder preview and tests can use it. `gradeAnswer(question, response) → { points, flagged }`. Partial-credit formula from FR-3. Use Decimal and round with fixed2. |","-| FR-4 | PURE | Same module. `normalize = s.trim().replace(/\\s+/g,' ')`, with case-folding unless `caseSensitive` is set. A non-match returns `flagged: true` and 0 points. |","-| FR-5 | PURE | ESSAY → `{ points: null, flagged: true }`. `correct` holds the guidance text and is server-only (NFR-1). |","-| FR-6 | UI, AUTH | Server page `/courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit`, protected by assertCanManageCourse. The settings panel uses MUI x-date-pickers. The time-limit vs window check reuses the FR-2 validator on the client. |","-| FR-7 | UI | Sortable question list (@dnd-kit/sortable wrapping MUI items). Per-type editor components. Reorder calls `POST /questions/reorder`. |","-| FR-8 | UI | The points total is derived client-side. Preview mode reuses the player component with a `preview` prop. It gets data from the manager GET (with `correct`) and grades locally with the pure grading.ts. It **never calls the attempt endpoints**, so nothing is recorded. |","-| FR-9 | SVC, PURE | `canPublish(quiz, questions) → string[]` (pure, so it can be shared with the UI). The PATCH status→PUBLISHED transition enforces it server-side. Publishing triggers FR-29. |","-| FR-10 | SVC, API, AUD | A lock check runs when `attemptCount > 0` (`_count.attempts`). It whitelists `prompt/explanation/correct (SHORT_ANSWER only)` and returns CONFLICT with an explanation otherwise. `POST /api/quizzes/:id/regrade` re-runs gradeAnswer on non-manually-graded answers in one transaction, then recomputes attempt scores (FR-25 logic). It must not override teacher-graded answers (manual grade wins). |","-| FR-11 | CFG, UI, SVC | The course tab entry (B2). `GET /api/courses/:id/quizzes` is role-shaped. Teachers get aggregates (count, avg, needsGrading via groupBy). Students get bucketed rows (Upcoming / Available / Completed / **Missed = closed with zero attempts**, assumed). Parents get completed results only, scoped to the linked child. |","-| FR-12 | UI | Server page `/quizzes/[quizId]/take`. It resolves the course from the quiz and calls assertCanViewCourse (STUDENT). Attempts used/allowed uses FR-23. ConfirmDialog guards Start. |","-| FR-13 | SVC, PURE | Inside the start transaction: freeze `questionOrder: String[]`. Option order is a deterministic seeded shuffle (seed = attempt id). Use a pure `seededShuffle(items, seed)` (a small string hash + mulberry32) in grading.ts or a sibling. `deadlineAt = min(startedAt + (limit + extra) min, availableUntil)`. With no time limit, it is `availableUntil` (handoff risk 4). Pure `computeDeadline()`, unit-tested (NFR-8). |","-| FR-14 | UI | Player client component (MUI RadioGroup/FormGroup/TextField/LinearProgress, a navigator grid of Buttons). The sticky header timer is display-only (FR-16). The server returns `deadlineAt` and the client counts down from it. |","-| FR-15 | UI, API | `useAutosave` hook: 800 ms debounce per question, a localStorage queue keyed `quiz-attempt:<id>`, a 5 s retry interval, and `navigator.onLine`. Three-state pill. The server upsert is idempotent, so replays are safe. |","-| FR-16 | SVC, API | The answer PUT reads only the attempt row `{studentId, status, deadlineAt}` (NFR-2). Past `deadlineAt + 30 s` it calls submitAttempt(auto) and then throws CONFLICT. The client then routes to the submitted view. |","-| FR-17 | SVC, UI | `submitAttempt(attemptId, { auto })`, in one transaction. Grade every answer, create zero-score rows for unanswered questions, and set `score`, `submittedAt` and status (NEEDS_GRADING if anything is flagged, else GRADED). Guard with `updateMany where status = IN_PROGRESS` so double submits are no-ops (this also makes FR-18 idempotent). |","-| FR-18 | SVC, JOB | A lazy check on `GET /api/attempts/:id`, on `POST /attempts` (start/resume), and on the teacher list/grade loads: `if IN_PROGRESS && now > deadlineAt → submitAttempt({auto:true})`. `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` does a batch find + submitAttempt each (B3). |","-| FR-19 | DM, SVC | Start or resume: find the IN_PROGRESS attempt and return it. Otherwise create one. Rely on the partial unique index (B10), and on P2002 re-read. Two tabs end up on the same attempt id. |","-| FR-20 | PURE, SVC, API, AUD | `resultsVisible(quiz, now)`: IMMEDIATELY → true after submit, AFTER_CLOSE → `now ≥ availableUntil`, MANUAL → `resultsReleasedAt != null`. `POST /release-results` (manager) sets resultsReleasedAt, then audit + FR-30. This one predicate drives the NFR-1 serializer. |","-| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Result view. The serializer includes `correct` and explanation only when `resultsVisible && showCorrectAnswers`. Score and per-question points only when `resultsVisible`. |","-| FR-22 | SVC | `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId) → { score, maxScore, isPractice, attemptsCounted } \\| null`. HIGHEST/LATEST/AVERAGE over GRADED attempts (Decimal average, fixed2). An exported service function. No endpoint. |","-| FR-23 | SVC, PURE | `attemptLimit = maxAttempts + (accommodation?.extraAttempts ?? 0)`. Start throws CONFLICT when `count(attempts) ≥ limit` and there's no IN_PROGRESS attempt to resume. Pure helper, unit-tested. |","-| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH, AUD | Grade page with two modes (DataTable by student, or by question). `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId/grade` (manager): points 0..question.points step 0.5, plus feedback. Sets `gradedById/manuallyGraded`, then audit, then FR-25. |","-| FR-25 | SVC | After each grade: if no answer in the attempt is still ungraded, set status GRADED and recompute the score as Σ points. Recompute the score on every grade regardless, so overrides on GRADED attempts update it. |","-| FR-26 | SVC, API, UI | `GET /api/quizzes/:id/analytics` (manager). Aggregates are computed in TS over submitted attempts. The class sizes are small, so compute in memory. Median computed in code. Histogram with 10 buckets (100% goes in the last bucket). MUI X BarChart + StatCard. |","-| FR-27 | SVC, API | Per-question stats come from the same pass. The option distribution counts option ids in responses. `?format=csv` reuses `src/server/csv.ts` and returns text/csv with one row per attempt. |","-| FR-28 | API, DM, AUD | `PUT /api/quizzes/:id/accommodations/:studentId` upserts QuizAccommodation (manager). The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Changes apply only to attempts started later (deadlineAt is frozen at start). Note this for the UI copy. |","-| FR-29 | NOTIF | Fires on the first transition to PUBLISHED only (track `publishedAt` or check the previous status). Link `/quizzes/:id/take`. Recipients are ACTIVE enrollees. Skip if the quiz is practice? No: the PRD doesn't say, so send. |","-| FR-30 | NOTIF, JOB | MANUAL → on release (once, guarded by `resultsReleasedAt` going null→set). AFTER_CLOSE → the maintenance pass picks closed quizzes with `resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` (B4) and notifies students who submitted, plus their parents. IMMEDIATELY → never. |","-| FR-31 | API, AUTH | Routes under `src/app/api/{courses/[id]/quizzes, quizzes/[id], quizzes/[id]/questions, quizzes/[id]/questions/reorder, questions/[id]}`. DELETE quiz → CONFLICT if any attempt exists. Reorder accepts the full id list and rejects ids that don't match the quiz's set exactly. |","-| FR-32 | API, AUTH | `POST /api/quizzes/:id/attempts` (STUDENT, course view, quiz PUBLISHED and within its window). `GET /api/attempts/:id` (owner, linked parent once results are released, or manager). The answers PUT and the submit POST are owner-only. |","-| FR-33 | DM, SVC | `isPractice` is returned in FR-22's result. It counts for attempts and analytics like a graded quiz (intake assumption). |","-| FR-34 | AUTH | B1, reused unchanged. Add one helper, `assertCanAccessAttempt(user, attempt)`, in src/server/quiz/: owner, manager via assertCanManageCourse, or a PARENT linked to the student. Parent access is read-only and only when results are visible. |","-| FR-35 | JOB | B3. Both functions must be idempotent: FR-17's status guard and FR-30's claim column. |","-| FR-36 | SEED | Extend prisma/seed.ts. 'Fractions Check' (8 objective questions, closed, every MATH-7A student has a GRADED attempt; scores via grading.ts so the seed data is consistent). 'Unit 1 Test' (12 questions incl. 2 ESSAY, AFTER_CLOSE, window now → +3 days, no attempts). 'Parts of Speech' (ENG-7A, practice, maxAttempts 3, HIGHEST). The seed must be idempotent like the existing one (upsert by title + course). |","-| FR-37 | — | **No work** (LOW, assumed). No sidebar entry. The course tab covers it. Design should drop it explicitly. |","-| FR-38 | AUD | B7. Write after commit, inside the service functions, not in the handlers. |","-| FR-39 | UI, AUTH | MarkdownEditor/MarkdownView for prompts, FileUpload with a `'quiz'` context, and a resolver (B11). |","-| NFR-1 | AUTH, SVC, TEST | **Highest-risk item.** All student-facing reads (quiz GET, attempt GET, course list, answer-PUT response) go through `serializers.ts`. Prisma selects for student paths never select `correct`/`explanation` at all (defence in depth). The unit test asserts `'correct' in obj === false` recursively. |","-| NFR-2 | DM, SVC | The answer PUT does exactly one attempt read plus one upsert. Don't load the Question row: the questionId is validated against `attempt.questionOrder` (already on the attempt row). The response validator for the answer shape is type-agnostic (`string[] \\| string`). It is type-checked at grade time. |","-| NFR-3 | UI | Native inputs via MUI Radio/Checkbox. An `aria-live=\"assertive\"` region announces only at the 5:00 and 1:00 thresholds, not every tick. Keyboard nav for the navigator grid. The axe check is part of the e2e. |","-| NFR-4 | UI | MUI only. Look up each component through mui-mcp before use. This is a dev-phase obligation, so carry it into the plan. |","-| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every handler starts with requireUser/requireRole and then a course or attempt check. The server pages use requirePageRole. |","-| NFR-6 | API | withHandler + Zod parse. `{data}` / `paginated` envelopes. The course quiz list is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100). cuid ids, UTC timestamps. The UI formats dates with DateDisplay / formatInSchoolTz. |","-| NFR-7 | — | Constraint on all of the above: `src/server/quiz/` only, reuse B5–B9 and B14, no new deps, no console.log in app code. |","-| NFR-8 | TEST | Unit: grading.ts (partial credit incl. the FR-3 example, short-answer normalisation), computeDeadline + accommodations, scoring policies, serializer. Integration: autosave 409 after deadline+grace, auto-submit on GET, regrade. E2E: a single Playwright spec. |","-| NFR-9 | UI | Builder ergonomics: default type MULTIPLE/SINGLE_CHOICE, Enter adds an option row, and Duplicate. No architectural change. |","-| NFR-10 | — | Out of scope. Design must not add question banks, proctoring or LaTeX. |","+| FR-1 | DM | New enums + 6 models in one `prisma migrate` migration. Use the unique keys from B19. Grade: `score Decimal?`, `excused`, `missing`, `comment`, `gradedById`, `gradedAt`. ReportCard: `status`, `snapshot Json`, `homeroomComment`, `principalComment`, `publishedAt`, `publishedById`. |","+| FR-2 | DM, UI | Nullable `Course.gradingScaleId`, `Assignment.categoryId` and `Quiz.categoryId` with `onDelete: SetNull`. Category deletion via FR-40 must not delete sources. Add one `Select` to the existing assignment and quiz editors, plus the validator fields in assignments.ts / quiz.ts (optional and nullable). Don't change existing behaviour. |","+| FR-3 | SYNC | `upsertGradeItemFromAssignment(id)` / `…FromQuiz(id)` keyed on (source, sourceId). Skip practice quizzes. Term placement via `termFor` (B10). Callers per B5/B6. Keep the GradeItem's term stable after first creation unless the date changes, so grades don't jump terms on unrelated edits. |","+| FR-4 | SYNC | Archive sets isVisible=false. Delete removes the GradeItem in the same tx (B9). Quiz has no archive or unpublish. A practice-toggle after publish should delete or hide the item. |","+| FR-5 | SYNC | `syncSubmissionGrade` from 3 return paths (B7). It writes only when RETURNED. Score = `finalScore`. |","+| FR-6 | SYNC | From `setExemption` (B8). Exemption wins over the score: excused=true and the score is kept. |","+| FR-7 | SYNC | Per-attempt `syncQuizGrade` after `recomputeAttempt` callers (B3). Bulk `syncQuizGrades` on release and AFTER_CLOSE (B4). Score scaled: `score/maxScore × GradeItem.maxPoints`, Decimal. |","+| FR-8 | JOB | `backfillGradebook()`: batch load per course, reuse the same upsert builders as live sync (one code path), idempotent through the unique keys. npm script + seed call (B18). |","+| FR-9 | API, AUTH | The service rejects score/excused/missing edits on non-MANUAL items (`AppError('FORBIDDEN'/'VALIDATION_ERROR')`). Comment stays editable. The grid marks those columns non-editable. |","+| FR-10 | CALC | `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts`: pure, Decimal-only, no Prisma client import (types only). Input: items, grades, categories, scale, override, `now`. Counted = visible ∧ ¬excused ∧ (score≠null ∨ (missing ∧ now>dueAt)). |","+| FR-11 | CALC | Drop lowest by item **percentage**, keeping ≥1. Ties are dropped deterministically (by dueAt, then id). |","+| FR-12 | CALC | Implicit \"Uncategorised\" bucket. What weight does it get? The PRD is silent, so see §3 R3. No categories gives a points total. |","+| FR-13 | CALC | `toDecimalPlaces(1, ROUND_HALF_UP)` only at the end. Bands are sorted descending, first `percent >= minPercent`. |","+| FR-14 | CALC | The override is applied after computing. A letter-only override keeps the computed percent. A percent-only override probably re-derives the letter from the scale (unstated, so flag it). |","+| FR-15 | CALC, UI | Golden unit test (78.0 C+). The gradebook and student Grades **must call the same function**, with no client-side recomputation. |","+| FR-16 | API, UI, DM | `/admin/grading-scales` (ADMIN). Band validation lives in a Zod refinement shared by client and server. \"Exactly one default\" uses a tx that clears others + a partial unique index. Deleting a scale in use is either blocked or falls back to the default; decide this. |","+| FR-17 | UI, API | Course settings page. The live weight sum is client-side, with the 100 check repeated server-side in FR-40. Decimal weights: compare with `dec(sum).eq(100)`, not floats. |","+| FR-18 | UI, API, CALC | First DataGrid. The server returns one denormalised payload `{students, items, categories, grades, computed}` for (course, term) in a fixed number of queries (NFR-2). Columns are built client-side from it. Sort by last name on the server. |","+| FR-19 | UI | Pure cell renderer. \"Late\" needs `Submission.isLate`, so the gradebook payload must carry the source submission's isLate. |","+| FR-20 | UI, API | `processRowUpdate` → PATCH a single grade. E/M/Delete need a custom edit cell / `onCellKeyDown` (check mui-mcp). Optimistic update with per-cell error. Audited (NFR-4). Triggers `grade.posted` (FR-38). |","+| FR-21 | UI | The cell click opens a link to the submission grading page or the quiz attempt. The payload needs `submissionId` / `attemptId` per synced grade. |","+| FR-22 | API, UI | POST manual item. Validate that the term belongs to the course's academic year and the category belongs to the course. |","+| FR-23 | API, UI, AUD | PUT override (upsert). Comment ≤1000 chars. Audit with old/new values. |","+| FR-24 | API, UI | Toggle visibility (see R2). Bulk-missing allowed only if `now > dueAt` and only for ungraded rows. Stats come from the computed payload, client-side, over counted scores. |","+| FR-25 | API | Server CSV via `toCsv`, using the same row builder as the grid. \"As displayed\" means EX/M/— markers and the term letter. |","+| FR-26 | UI, API, CFG | Student tab → `GET /api/students/:id/grades?termId`. The colour thresholds come from a single helper reused by FR-27/28. |","+| FR-27 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/grades` reuses the FR-26 component. Parent child selector from `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Nav entry. |","+| FR-28 | UI, CFG | Course tab `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT): same endpoint filtered by courseId. |","+| FR-29 | UI, API | `/admin/report-cards`: list query joins students (grade level, section filters) with ReportCard status for the term. Missing-data warnings are computed in batch (ungraded counted-eligible items, missing TermGradeOverride.comment per course). |","+| FR-30 | JOB, API | `generate`: batch load (NFR-3), compute in memory, write the snapshot JSON (versioned shape, e.g. `snapshot.v = 1`). Teacher comment = `TermGradeOverride.comment`. Attendance via B13. |","+| FR-31 | JOB, DM | `upsert` with `where status = DRAFT` semantics: createMany for new cards, `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})` for existing ones, never touching PUBLISHED. Grade-edit services never import report-cards code. |","+| FR-32 | API, UI, AUTH | PATCH: field-level role check (homeroomComment: homeroom teacher of the student's section or ADMIN; principalComment: ADMIN). Edits are allowed only while DRAFT (implied, so flag it). |","+| FR-33 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/report-cards` (TEACHER): drafts for sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Nav entry. |","+| FR-34 | API, NOTIF, AUD | Publish (one or bulk) with a guarded `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})`, then notify after commit. Unpublish: ADMIN, reason required, audit, back to DRAFT. |","+| FR-35 | UI | `/report-cards/[id]/print` renders from the **snapshot only**. `@media print` via MUI `GlobalStyles`, hiding the sidebar. Bulk print: one page renders N cards with `break-after: page`. |","+| FR-36 | UI, CFG, API | Student tab \"Report cards\". The list endpoint filters to PUBLISHED for student/parent (NFR-5). |","+| FR-37 | AUTH | New `assertCanViewReportCard`. Non-entitled users get NOT_FOUND, so existence isn't leaked. |","+| FR-38 | NOTIF | Register 2 types (B15). `grade.posted`: only for MANUAL items, only when a score is first entered or changed (one per student per item, so an idempotency marker such as `Grade.notifiedAt` is needed; flag it). |","+| FR-39 | API, AUTH | Thin route handlers using `withHandler`, Zod in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, and services in `src/server/gradebook/` + `src/server/report-cards/`. |","+| FR-40 | API | Replace-all in a tx: delete missing ids (sources → SetNull), upsert the rest. Weights total 100 (Decimal). |","+| FR-41 | JOB | Seed: scale, 7A categories, 'Oral presentation' + grades, draft S1 cards for 7A with MATH/ENG override comments. Run after `backfillGradebook()`. |","+| FR-42 | API, AUTH | Student serializer: visible items only. Grade rows only exist for released scores (sync gating), so the risk is mainly hidden items and MANUAL items with isVisible=false. Still filter explicitly. |","+| NFR-1 | CALC | Decimal throughout. Unit matrix in `grade-calc.test.ts`. |","+| NFR-2 | API | Gradebook: ~5 queries (enrollments, items, grades, categories, scale + override), all indexed by (courseId, termId). The grid virtualises. |","+| NFR-3 | JOB | Generation: per term, `findMany` items/grades/overrides/categories for all courses in scope with `in` filters, then group in memory. One attendance `groupBy`. Chunk the writes. |","+| NFR-4 | AUD | Old/new values in metadata for grade.update, termOverride.upsert and reportCard.unpublish. |","+| NFR-5 | AUTH | Enforced in 3 layers: sync gating (B2/B7), student serializer (FR-42), report-card guard (FR-37). Integration tests for each. |","+| NFR-6 | AUTH | Every route uses requireUser/requireRole + an entity check (B12). Server pages check too, not just the API. |","+| NFR-7 | UI | MUI only, with mui-mcp lookup. Toast via useToast, confirm via Dialog/ConfirmDialog. |","+| NFR-8 | UI | DataGrid MIT: no `pinnedColumns` and no `@mui/x-data-grid-pro`. Sticky header is the default. |","+| NFR-9 | all | New code only in src/server/gradebook/ and src/server/report-cards/. Hooks into existing services are one-line calls. Use `logger`, no console.log. |","+| NFR-10 | CALC, SYNC | Past-due uses an instant comparison (`now > dueAt`). Term containment uses a tz date comparison (B10). |","+| NFR-11 | UI | A4 portrait `@page` rule. Long course lists may need a 2nd page, with table rows set to `break-inside: avoid`. |","+| NFR-12 | all | Tests per the intake list. Integration tests hit the real sync hooks (B3/B4/B7). |","+| NFR-13 | — | Scope guard: store `gpa`, never compute it. No rank or transcript. |"," ","-## 3. Cross-cutting decisions for `arch-design-system`","+## 3. Risks / decisions for `arch-design-system`"," ","-- **D1 Module layout (NFR-7):**","-  - `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (pure: gradeAnswer, seededShuffle, computeDeadline, attemptLimit, resultsVisible, canPublish, applyScoringPolicy)","-  - `quiz-service.ts` (CRUD, publish, lock, regrade, release, accommodations)","-  - `attempt-service.ts` (start/resume, saveAnswer, submit, lazy auto-submit, grade, getStudentQuizScore)","-  - `analytics.ts`","-  - `serializers.ts`","-  - `maintenance.ts` (autoSubmitExpiredAttempts, sendQuizResultsReleased)","-  - `access.ts` (assertCanAccessAttempt)","+- **R1 (FR-7 timing):** AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL visibility arrive later than GRADED. Without the B4 bulk hooks, those quizzes never sync. Syncing early would break NFR-5.","+- **R2 (FR-4 vs FR-24):** the teacher's hide toggle and the source-driven `isVisible` share one column. Re-saving an assignment would silently re-show a teacher-hidden item. Options: (a) source sync writes isVisible only on publish/archive *transitions*; (b) add a separate `hiddenByTeacher` flag and make visible = sourceVisible ∧ ¬hiddenByTeacher. (b) is clearer but adds a column beyond FR-1's \"exactly as specified\". Pick one and state it.","+- **R3 (FR-12 Uncategorised weight):** the PRD doesn't say what weight the implicit bucket carries when real categories exist. A sensible default is weight 0, so it's shown but excluded from the weighted mean, unless it's the only bucket. This affects the FR-15 golden test only if it has uncategorised items (it doesn't). Flag it.","+- **R4 (FR-38 dedupe):** \"one notification per student per item\" needs a marker. A nullable `Grade.notifiedAt` claimed via `updateMany` follows the existing claim pattern.","+- **R5 (FR-3 term drift):** re-deriving the term on every edit can move existing grades between terms. Only recompute it when dueAt/availableUntil changes.","+- **R6 (FR-16 delete):** deleting a scale referenced by courses or by DRAFT snapshots (PUBLISHED ones embed the legend, so they're safe). Recommend blocking the delete with CONFLICT while courses reference the scale.","+- **R7 (first DataGrid):** there is no in-repo precedent. Keyboard E/M/Delete handling within the MIT tier is the main implementation risk (intake keyRisk). The design should keep the grid behind one client component."," ","-  Keep the pure helpers together in one file unless it grows past what one file reads comfortably.","-- **D2 Single submit path:** manual submit, deadline-PUT rejection, lazy load and the maintenance pass all call one `submitAttempt`. The `status = IN_PROGRESS` conditional update makes it idempotent and race-safe.","-- **D3 Visibility predicate:** one `resultsVisible()` drives the serializer, the parent access and the FR-11 \"score if visible\" display.","-- **D4 Frozen-at-start:** questionOrder, option order (via seed) and deadlineAt are fixed at start. Later accommodation or settings edits don't move in-flight attempts. FR-10 locks prevent structural changes anyway.","-- **D5 Manual grade precedence:** regrade (FR-10) only recomputes answers where `manuallyGraded = false`. If FR-1's QuizAnswer field list doesn't include such a flag, use `gradedById IS NULL` as the marker.","+## 4. Carried-forward assumptions (from intake, adjusted)"," ","-## 4. Assumptions and open points to surface in the system-design Overview","-","-1. FR-37: no sidebar entry (LOW).","-2. Missed = closed with zero attempts by that student.","-3. Regrade runs only on the explicit action. Editing accepted answers doesn't auto-regrade.","-4. Practice quizzes count toward attempts and analytics. They are excluded only from the gradebook (FR-22's caller filters on isPractice).","-5. `quiz.results_released` defaultEmail = true. The PRD doesn't specify it.","-6. FR-30's AFTER_CLOSE \"sent once\" needs a marker. B4 proposes `Quiz.resultsNotifiedAt`, which is an addition to FR-1's \"exactly as listed\" model. If that isn't acceptable, use a claim table.","-7. Accommodation changes affect only attempts started after the change.","-8. Intake handoff blockers: **none**.","+1. FR-6: unexempting clears excused and re-syncs the score from the source.","+2. FR-7: **use the existing `getStudentQuizScore`** (B1) plus a caller-side `resultsVisible` gate. This replaces intake's \"build a new helper\".","+3. FR-13: 89.95 → 90.0 → **A−** under the seed scale. The test asserts 90.0 and the 90-band letter.","+4. FR-27/FR-33: add nav entries per the convention.","+5. NFR-10: past due = `now > dueAt` (exact instant). Term containment is evaluated in the school timezone.","+6. FR-3: no containing term and no current term → skip the item + `logger.warn`.","+7. New and unstated (needs sign-off): FR-14 percent-only override re-derives the letter; FR-32 comments are editable only while DRAFT; FR-34 unpublish returns to DRAFT."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-10\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams (SCH-010). It has 39 FRs and 10 NFRs (49 requirements) at 96% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It flags assumptions on FR-33/34/35/37/38/39. Those are restated in §3 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-9 leftovers** as of this writing (`ticketId: \"SH-9\"`). Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-10 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-10 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child. `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Both throw `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These cover FR-34 and the course part of NFR-5. Attempt-level checks are still new: owner, linked parent, or manager. |\n| B2 | `courseTabs` is a static array of `{key, label, href, roles}`. | src/config/course-tabs.ts | FR-11: add one entry, `{ key: 'quizzes', href: id => /courses/${id}/quizzes, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. |\n| B3 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` and then `sendDueReminders(now)` on every request, each wrapped in its own try/catch + logger. Purges run in a once-per-day block. | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-18/FR-30/FR-35: add `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` and `sendQuizResultsReleased(now)` **on every call**, next to sendDueReminders, each with its own try/catch. |\n| B4 | `sendDueReminders` is idempotent through a unique-key claim row (`AssignmentReminder`, P2002 → skip). | src/server/assignments/reminders.ts | FR-30 AFTER_CLOSE needs a \"sent once\" marker. The simplest option is a nullable `Quiz.resultsNotifiedAt`, claimed with `updateMany({ where: { id, resultsNotifiedAt: null } })` and a count check. That needs no new table. If FR-1's model list must stay exact, a claim table is the alternative. |\n| B5 | `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds})` never throw. Call them after commit. | src/server/notifications/notify.ts | FR-29 → `notify()` to enrolled students. FR-30 → `notifyStudentAndParents`. |\n| B6 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object. New keys need `label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles`. | src/server/notifications/types.ts | FR-29: `quiz.published` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, roles STUDENT). `quiz.results_released` (ACADEMIC, roles STUDENT+PARENT). The PRD doesn't give a default email setting for results_released. Default it to true to match assignment.graded, and flag that choice. |\n| B7 | `audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request})` never throws. | src/server/audit.ts | FR-38 actions: `quizAnswer.grade`, `quiz.regrade`, `quiz.release_results`, `quizAccommodation.update`. |\n| B8 | `grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic. It exports `dec`, `fixed2` and `Decimal` from the Prisma browser runtime. `assignments-service.ts` exports `serializeDecimal` and `getSchoolTimezone`. | src/server/assignments/* | FR-3/FR-22/FR-25 reuse dec/fixed2 (NFR-7). Importing from `@/server/assignments/grading-math` is fine. Only lift it to a shared module if dev-planning wants that. Do not copy it. |\n| B9 | `http.ts` provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `AppError`. The codes include CONFLICT (409). Zod errors become VALIDATION_ERROR. Prisma P2002 becomes CONFLICT. | src/server/http.ts | NFR-6. FR-16's 409 is `AppError('CONFLICT', ...)`. |\n| B10 | The DB is PostgreSQL. The project already uses raw-SQL partial unique indexes in migrations. | prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/migration.sql L77-78 | FR-19 race-safety: `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE status = 'IN_PROGRESS'`, hand-added to the FR-1 migration. Add `@@unique([quizId, studentId, attemptNumber])` too. On P2002 during start, re-read and resume. |\n| B11 | File contexts are registered in `registerBuiltInContexts` (lesson, logo, assignment, submission). `attachFiles` sets context/contextId. | src/server/files/contexts.ts, files-service.ts | FR-39: question images need a `'quiz'` context (contextId = quizId) with a resolver: manager, or a viewer with an IN_PROGRESS or visible attempt. The prompt Markdown references the file URL. |\n| B12 | Courses MATH-7A and ENG-7A are looked up in seed.ts with `findCourse([...])`. The seed already uses `console.log` for skips. | prisma/seed.ts L302, L340 | FR-36 follows that pattern (the seed is exempt from the no-console.log rule in practice). |\n| B13 | Installed: @mui/* 9.5.0 (incl. x-charts, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers), @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + sortable 10.0.0, zod 3.23.8, prisma 5.20, vitest, Playwright + axe. | package.json | FR-7, FR-26 and NFR-8 need **no new dependencies** (NFR-7). |\n| B14 | Shared components are DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast, MarkdownEditor, MarkdownView, FileUpload, StatCard, EmptyState, PageHeader, DateDisplay. | src/components/ | FR-7/12/17/24/26/39 reuse them. |\n| B15 | `toStudentSubmission(dto)` is the precedent for a student-shaped serializer. | assignments-service.ts L199 | NFR-1: add `toStudentQuiz` / `toStudentAttempt` in `src/server/quiz/serializers.ts`, with a unit test asserting the `correct` key is absent. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **VAL** validator · **PURE** pure domain logic · **SVC** service (src/server/quiz/) · **API** route handler · **UI** page/component · **JOB** maintenance pass · **AUTH** access boundary · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **SEED** seed · **CFG** config registry · **TEST**\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | One migration, `add_quizzes`. 5 enums, 5 models. Back-relations on Course (`quizzes`) and User (attempts, accommodations, graded answers). QuizAnswer PK `(attemptId, questionId)` (NFR-2). QuizAccommodation unique `(quizId, studentId)`. Include the partial unique index from B10 in the SQL. Money-like fields (points, scores) are `Decimal(6,2)`, per the assignments precedent. |\n| FR-2 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`, client-safe, shared by the builder UI and the handlers. Use per-type question schemas as a discriminated union on `type`. `availableUntil > availableFrom` and the time-limit cross-field checks use `.superRefine`. |\n| FR-3 | PURE | `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. No Prisma import, so the builder preview and tests can use it. `gradeAnswer(question, response) → { points, flagged }`. Partial-credit formula from FR-3. Use Decimal and round with fixed2. |\n| FR-4 | PURE | Same module. `normalize = s.trim().replace(/\\s+/g,' ')`, with case-folding unless `caseSensitive` is set. A non-match returns `flagged: true` and 0 points. |\n| FR-5 | PURE | ESSAY → `{ points: null, flagged: true }`. `correct` holds the guidance text and is server-only (NFR-1). |\n| FR-6 | UI, AUTH | Server page `/courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit`, protected by assertCanManageCourse. The settings panel uses MUI x-date-pickers. The time-limit vs window check reuses the FR-2 validator on the client. |\n| FR-7 | UI | Sortable question list (@dnd-kit/sortable wrapping MUI items). Per-type editor components. Reorder calls `POST /questions/reorder`. |\n| FR-8 | UI | The points total is derived client-side. Preview mode reuses the player component with a `preview` prop. It gets data from the manager GET (with `correct`) and grades locally with the pure grading.ts. It **never calls the attempt endpoints**, so nothing is recorded. |\n| FR-9 | SVC, PURE | `canPublish(quiz, questions) → string[]` (pure, so it can be shared with the UI). The PATCH status→PUBLISHED transition enforces it server-side. Publishing triggers FR-29. |\n| FR-10 | SVC, API, AUD | A lock check runs when `attemptCount > 0` (`_count.attempts`). It whitelists `prompt/explanation/correct (SHORT_ANSWER only)` and returns CONFLICT with an explanation otherwise. `POST /api/quizzes/:id/regrade` re-runs gradeAnswer on non-manually-graded answers in one transaction, then recomputes attempt scores (FR-25 logic). It must not override teacher-graded answers (manual grade wins). |\n| FR-11 | CFG, UI, SVC | The course tab entry (B2). `GET /api/courses/:id/quizzes` is role-shaped. Teachers get aggregates (count, avg, needsGrading via groupBy). Students get bucketed rows (Upcoming / Available / Completed / **Missed = closed with zero attempts**, assumed). Parents get completed results only, scoped to the linked child. |\n| FR-12 | UI | Server page `/quizzes/[quizId]/take`. It resolves the course from the quiz and calls assertCanViewCourse (STUDENT). Attempts used/allowed uses FR-23. ConfirmDialog guards Start. |\n| FR-13 | SVC, PURE | Inside the start transaction: freeze `questionOrder: String[]`. Option order is a deterministic seeded shuffle (seed = attempt id). Use a pure `seededShuffle(items, seed)` (a small string hash + mulberry32) in grading.ts or a sibling. `deadlineAt = min(startedAt + (limit + extra) min, availableUntil)`. With no time limit, it is `availableUntil` (handoff risk 4). Pure `computeDeadline()`, unit-tested (NFR-8). |\n| FR-14 | UI | Player client component (MUI RadioGroup/FormGroup/TextField/LinearProgress, a navigator grid of Buttons). The sticky header timer is display-only (FR-16). The server returns `deadlineAt` and the client counts down from it. |\n| FR-15 | UI, API | `useAutosave` hook: 800 ms debounce per question, a localStorage queue keyed `quiz-attempt:<id>`, a 5 s retry interval, and `navigator.onLine`. Three-state pill. The server upsert is idempotent, so replays are safe. |\n| FR-16 | SVC, API | The answer PUT reads only the attempt row `{studentId, status, deadlineAt}` (NFR-2). Past `deadlineAt + 30 s` it calls submitAttempt(auto) and then throws CONFLICT. The client then routes to the submitted view. |\n| FR-17 | SVC, UI | `submitAttempt(attemptId, { auto })`, in one transaction. Grade every answer, create zero-score rows for unanswered questions, and set `score`, `submittedAt` and status (NEEDS_GRADING if anything is flagged, else GRADED). Guard with `updateMany where status = IN_PROGRESS` so double submits are no-ops (this also makes FR-18 idempotent). |\n| FR-18 | SVC, JOB | A lazy check on `GET /api/attempts/:id`, on `POST /attempts` (start/resume), and on the teacher list/grade loads: `if IN_PROGRESS && now > deadlineAt → submitAttempt({auto:true})`. `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` does a batch find + submitAttempt each (B3). |\n| FR-19 | DM, SVC | Start or resume: find the IN_PROGRESS attempt and return it. Otherwise create one. Rely on the partial unique index (B10), and on P2002 re-read. Two tabs end up on the same attempt id. |\n| FR-20 | PURE, SVC, API, AUD | `resultsVisible(quiz, now)`: IMMEDIATELY → true after submit, AFTER_CLOSE → `now ≥ availableUntil`, MANUAL → `resultsReleasedAt != null`. `POST /release-results` (manager) sets resultsReleasedAt, then audit + FR-30. This one predicate drives the NFR-1 serializer. |\n| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Result view. The serializer includes `correct` and explanation only when `resultsVisible && showCorrectAnswers`. Score and per-question points only when `resultsVisible`. |\n| FR-22 | SVC | `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId) → { score, maxScore, isPractice, attemptsCounted } \\| null`. HIGHEST/LATEST/AVERAGE over GRADED attempts (Decimal average, fixed2). An exported service function. No endpoint. |\n| FR-23 | SVC, PURE | `attemptLimit = maxAttempts + (accommodation?.extraAttempts ?? 0)`. Start throws CONFLICT when `count(attempts) ≥ limit` and there's no IN_PROGRESS attempt to resume. Pure helper, unit-tested. |\n| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH, AUD | Grade page with two modes (DataTable by student, or by question). `PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId/grade` (manager): points 0..question.points step 0.5, plus feedback. Sets `gradedById/manuallyGraded`, then audit, then FR-25. |\n| FR-25 | SVC | After each grade: if no answer in the attempt is still ungraded, set status GRADED and recompute the score as Σ points. Recompute the score on every grade regardless, so overrides on GRADED attempts update it. |\n| FR-26 | SVC, API, UI | `GET /api/quizzes/:id/analytics` (manager). Aggregates are computed in TS over submitted attempts. The class sizes are small, so compute in memory. Median computed in code. Histogram with 10 buckets (100% goes in the last bucket). MUI X BarChart + StatCard. |\n| FR-27 | SVC, API | Per-question stats come from the same pass. The option distribution counts option ids in responses. `?format=csv` reuses `src/server/csv.ts` and returns text/csv with one row per attempt. |\n| FR-28 | API, DM, AUD | `PUT /api/quizzes/:id/accommodations/:studentId` upserts QuizAccommodation (manager). The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Changes apply only to attempts started later (deadlineAt is frozen at start). Note this for the UI copy. |\n| FR-29 | NOTIF | Fires on the first transition to PUBLISHED only (track `publishedAt` or check the previous status). Link `/quizzes/:id/take`. Recipients are ACTIVE enrollees. Skip if the quiz is practice? No: the PRD doesn't say, so send. |\n| FR-30 | NOTIF, JOB | MANUAL → on release (once, guarded by `resultsReleasedAt` going null→set). AFTER_CLOSE → the maintenance pass picks closed quizzes with `resultsNotifiedAt IS NULL` (B4) and notifies students who submitted, plus their parents. IMMEDIATELY → never. |\n| FR-31 | API, AUTH | Routes under `src/app/api/{courses/[id]/quizzes, quizzes/[id], quizzes/[id]/questions, quizzes/[id]/questions/reorder, questions/[id]}`. DELETE quiz → CONFLICT if any attempt exists. Reorder accepts the full id list and rejects ids that don't match the quiz's set exactly. |\n| FR-32 | API, AUTH | `POST /api/quizzes/:id/attempts` (STUDENT, course view, quiz PUBLISHED and within its window). `GET /api/attempts/:id` (owner, linked parent once results are released, or manager). The answers PUT and the submit POST are owner-only. |\n| FR-33 | DM, SVC | `isPractice` is returned in FR-22's result. It counts for attempts and analytics like a graded quiz (intake assumption). |\n| FR-34 | AUTH | B1, reused unchanged. Add one helper, `assertCanAccessAttempt(user, attempt)`, in src/server/quiz/: owner, manager via assertCanManageCourse, or a PARENT linked to the student. Parent access is read-only and only when results are visible. |\n| FR-35 | JOB | B3. Both functions must be idempotent: FR-17's status guard and FR-30's claim column. |\n| FR-36 | SEED | Extend prisma/seed.ts. 'Fractions Check' (8 objective questions, closed, every MATH-7A student has a GRADED attempt; scores via grading.ts so the seed data is consistent). 'Unit 1 Test' (12 questions incl. 2 ESSAY, AFTER_CLOSE, window now → +3 days, no attempts). 'Parts of Speech' (ENG-7A, practice, maxAttempts 3, HIGHEST). The seed must be idempotent like the existing one (upsert by title + course). |\n| FR-37 | — | **No work** (LOW, assumed). No sidebar entry. The course tab covers it. Design should drop it explicitly. |\n| FR-38 | AUD | B7. Write after commit, inside the service functions, not in the handlers. |\n| FR-39 | UI, AUTH | MarkdownEditor/MarkdownView for prompts, FileUpload with a `'quiz'` context, and a resolver (B11). |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH, SVC, TEST | **Highest-risk item.** All student-facing reads (quiz GET, attempt GET, course list, answer-PUT response) go through `serializers.ts`. Prisma selects for student paths never select `correct`/`explanation` at all (defence in depth). The unit test asserts `'correct' in obj === false` recursively. |\n| NFR-2 | DM, SVC | The answer PUT does exactly one attempt read plus one upsert. Don't load the Question row: the questionId is validated against `attempt.questionOrder` (already on the attempt row). The response validator for the answer shape is type-agnostic (`string[] \\| string`). It is type-checked at grade time. |\n| NFR-3 | UI | Native inputs via MUI Radio/Checkbox. An `aria-live=\"assertive\"` region announces only at the 5:00 and 1:00 thresholds, not every tick. Keyboard nav for the navigator grid. The axe check is part of the e2e. |\n| NFR-4 | UI | MUI only. Look up each component through mui-mcp before use. This is a dev-phase obligation, so carry it into the plan. |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every handler starts with requireUser/requireRole and then a course or attempt check. The server pages use requirePageRole. |\n| NFR-6 | API | withHandler + Zod parse. `{data}` / `paginated` envelopes. The course quiz list is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100). cuid ids, UTC timestamps. The UI formats dates with DateDisplay / formatInSchoolTz. |\n| NFR-7 | — | Constraint on all of the above: `src/server/quiz/` only, reuse B5–B9 and B14, no new deps, no console.log in app code. |\n| NFR-8 | TEST | Unit: grading.ts (partial credit incl. the FR-3 example, short-answer normalisation), computeDeadline + accommodations, scoring policies, serializer. Integration: autosave 409 after deadline+grace, auto-submit on GET, regrade. E2E: a single Playwright spec. |\n| NFR-9 | UI | Builder ergonomics: default type MULTIPLE/SINGLE_CHOICE, Enter adds an option row, and Duplicate. No architectural change. |\n| NFR-10 | — | Out of scope. Design must not add question banks, proctoring or LaTeX. |\n\n## 3. Cross-cutting decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **D1 Module layout (NFR-7):**\n  - `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (pure: gradeAnswer, seededShuffle, computeDeadline, attemptLimit, resultsVisible, canPublish, applyScoringPolicy)\n  - `quiz-service.ts` (CRUD, publish, lock, regrade, release, accommodations)\n  - `attempt-service.ts` (start/resume, saveAnswer, submit, lazy auto-submit, grade, getStudentQuizScore)\n  - `analytics.ts`\n  - `serializers.ts`\n  - `maintenance.ts` (autoSubmitExpiredAttempts, sendQuizResultsReleased)\n  - `access.ts` (assertCanAccessAttempt)\n\n  Keep the pure helpers together in one file unless it grows past what one file reads comfortably.\n- **D2 Single submit path:** manual submit, deadline-PUT rejection, lazy load and the maintenance pass all call one `submitAttempt`. The `status = IN_PROGRESS` conditional update makes it idempotent and race-safe.\n- **D3 Visibility predicate:** one `resultsVisible()` drives the serializer, the parent access and the FR-11 \"score if visible\" display.\n- **D4 Frozen-at-start:** questionOrder, option order (via seed) and deadlineAt are fixed at start. Later accommodation or settings edits don't move in-flight attempts. FR-10 locks prevent structural changes anyway.\n- **D5 Manual grade precedence:** regrade (FR-10) only recomputes answers where `manuallyGraded = false`. If FR-1's QuizAnswer field list doesn't include such a flag, use `gradedById IS NULL` as the marker.\n\n## 4. Assumptions and open points to surface in the system-design Overview\n\n1. FR-37: no sidebar entry (LOW).\n2. Missed = closed with zero attempts by that student.\n3. Regrade runs only on the explicit action. Editing accepted answers doesn't auto-regrade.\n4. Practice quizzes count toward attempts and analytics. They are excluded only from the gradebook (FR-22's caller filters on isPractice).\n5. `quiz.results_released` defaultEmail = true. The PRD doesn't specify it.\n6. FR-30's AFTER_CLOSE \"sent once\" needs a marker. B4 proposes `Quiz.resultsNotifiedAt`, which is an addition to FR-1's \"exactly as listed\" model. If that isn't acceptable, use a claim table.\n7. Accommodation changes affect only attempts started after the change.\n8. Intake handoff blockers: **none**.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012RW7s6dVESemUsNtsFo6WW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
