{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsKkG4wDTjgM16JBvhg5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've rewritten `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` for SH-11. The old file was left over from SH-10. A script check confirmed that all 55 requirements (FR-1 to FR-42, NFR-1 to NFR-13) appear in the table and that every requirement id cited is real.\n\n**Intake got two things wrong:**\n- **`getStudentQuizScore` already exists.** It's at `src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts:359`, labelled as an export for PRD-11. FR-7 should call it rather than build a new one. It doesn't check whether quiz results are visible yet, so the code that copies quiz scores into the gradebook has to check that first.\n- **Copying a quiz score when the attempt is graded isn't enough.** Quizzes whose results show after close or on manual release only become visible later. Those quizzes also need a bulk update when results are released (`releaseResults`) and when the quiz closes (`sendAfterCloseResultsReleased`). Without it they never reach the gradebook.\n\n**Other findings for `arch-design-system`:**\n- **Assignment returns:** there are three code paths that return a submission. The gradebook has to update whenever the submission ends up returned, including when an already-returned submission is re-graded.\n- **Deletes:** a gradebook item points at its assignment or quiz without a database foreign key, so deleting the source won't remove the item. It has to be deleted explicitly in the same transaction.\n- **Terms:** terms have no \"current\" flag. An item's term has to be worked out from the course's academic year using the school timezone.\n- **Batching:** the attendance summary for report cards can come from the existing `getReport` in one query per generation run, not one query per student.\n\n**Design decisions needed** (section 3 of the notes):\n- The teacher's hide/show toggle (FR-24) and the visibility set from the assignment or quiz (FR-4) share one field. Re-saving an assignment would quietly un-hide an item the teacher hid.\n- The PRD doesn't say what weight the implicit \"Uncategorised\" category gets when real categories exist. I suggest 0.\n- Sending only one `grade.posted` notification per student per item needs a way to record that it was sent.\n\nI also added three new assumptions that need sign-off:\n- An override with only a percent re-derives the letter from the scale.\n- Report card comments can only be edited while the card is a draft.\n- Unpublishing a report card returns it to draft.\n\nI didn't touch any other sub-task's files. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are still from earlier tickets until their sub-tasks overwrite them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":362,"cache_read_input_tokens":69089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":362},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8dcae7d9-b717-4417-9584-7ef748d2b9e4","uuid":"5550ca24-586b-4d7d-a956-18458d9056ac","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:05:35.633Z","request_id":"req_011CgsKkFpofp6WAwaTzUBbH"}
