{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgsftcu8SnuyC4ejSLCNT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wc56sNEhDxTioi1zj5AFmM","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-12\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T18:00:00Z), PRD-12 Announcements & News. It has 36 FRs and 11 NFRs (47 requirements) at 94% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> All other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **SH-11 leftovers**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-12 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-12 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no Announcement* models or enums. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1: add a new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_announcements`). Add back-relations on `User` (authored, reads) and `FileObject` (attachments, and the cover image if it is an FK). |\n| B2 | `User.status` is `ACTIVE/INVITED/DISABLED/ARCHIVED` and `archivedAt` is a separate column. `notify()` filters `status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED]`, so it **includes INVITED**. | schema L17, L59; notify.ts L43 | FR-3 is stricter: audience = `status: ACTIVE, archivedAt: null`. Pass the resolved ids to `notify()`, which then filters on its own. Don't rely on notify's filter. |\n| B3 | `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId` (required). `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` has `@@index([studentId])` and a `@@unique([parentId, studentId])`. | schema L106, L144 | FR-4/5/6 parent expansion: join through the link. Parent → children is covered by the unique index's leading `parentId`. |\n| B4 | `Section(academicYearId, gradeLevelId, homeroomTeacherId?)`. `SectionMember(studentId, academicYearId)` is unique on `(studentId, academicYearId)`, and its academicYearId is denormalised. **There is no index on `sectionId`.** | schema L377-411 | FR-5: \"members\" = SectionMember rows where `academicYearId` = the section's year (that is already true per row, so filtering by `sectionId` is enough). A section belongs to one year, so the \"current year\" question reduces to \"is the section in the current year\". See §4 A1. |\n| B5 | `Course(academicYearId, sectionId?, teacherId, coTeacherIds String[], archivedAt?)`. `coTeacherIds` is queried with `has`. `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. | schema L414-447 | FR-4/5/6/10 teacher branches. `has` isn't indexable without a GIN index. The rows involved are small (only a user's own courses), so this is fine for NFR-2. Decide whether archived courses' teachers count (§4 A6). |\n| B6 | `Enrollment.status` ACTIVE/DROPPED, with `@@index([studentId, status])` and `@@unique([courseId, studentId])`. | schema L371, L450 | FR-6 student branch. Both directions are indexed. |\n| B7 | `FileObject(context, contextId)` is indexed. Uploads are created with `contextId: null`. `attachFiles(tx, context, contextId, ids)` / detach live in files-service. **`purgeOrphanFiles` deletes `contextId: null` files after 24 h.** | files-service.ts L212-244; files/purge.ts | FR-13/FR-30: attach the cover image and attachments with `context='announcement'`, `contextId=announcement.id` inside the create/update tx. A cover that is uploaded but never attached (e.g. an abandoned draft) is purged, which is correct. **A draft must still attach its files**, or they vanish after 24 h. |\n| B8 | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)`. Resolvers receive `null` for anonymous callers. Built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (contexts.ts). Resolver errors deny. `/api/files/` is already in PUBLIC_API_PATHS. | files/access.ts; contexts.ts; public-routes.ts | FR-30: add `register('announcement', announcementResolver)` to `registerBuiltInContexts` so it is guaranteed loaded, rather than as a side-effect import. Anonymous downloads already route through, so no public-route change is needed for files. |\n| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). `COMMUNICATION` exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a **static boolean per type**. | notifications/types.ts | **FR-26 conflict**: \"mandatoryInApp true when requiresAck\" can't be expressed per instance. Options: (a) two types, `announcement.published` (mandatoryInApp false) and `announcement.published_ack` (true); or (b) one type with `mandatoryInApp: true`. Recommend (a) as the smallest faithful mapping. **arch-design-system decides.** |\n| B10 | `notify({type, userIds, title, body, link, email:{template:'generic-notification', data}})` dedupes, never throws, and is called after commit. It truncates body to BODY_MAX and drops non-relative links. | notify.ts L8-60 | FR-27/28: call it after the notifiedAt claim commits. `link: /announcements/${id}`. Large audiences (a SCHOOL announcement can be thousands of users) go through one `findMany` + `createMany`. That's acceptable, but chunk the userIds if notify's `in` lists get large. |\n| B11 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` runs each pass in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take: BATCH)` → `updateMany({where:{id, claimCol: null}})` → act only if `count === 1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts L28-43 | FR-27: `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` copies this pattern exactly: `where status SCHEDULED, publishAt <= now, notifiedAt null`, claim `notifiedAt`. Publish-now uses the same claim helper, so one code path sends. |\n| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes both `RATE_LIMITED` (429) and `CONFLICT` (409). `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` exist. | src/server/http.ts | FR-34 handler conventions. FR-25: recommend **429 RATE_LIMITED** with `details.retryAfter` (ISO). It is semantically a time-based throttle, and intake suggested the same. |\n| B13 | `audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request})` never throws. The action convention is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|archive\\|delete`. | src/server/audit.ts | FR-12: `announcement.update` / `announcement.archive` when an admin acts on another author's row. Also audit the author's own archive (cheap; optional). |\n| B14 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` (formula-injection safe). | src/server/csv.ts | FR-24 `?format=csv`. |\n| B15 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from **assignments-service.ts**, not a shared module. `formatInSchoolTz` is in src/lib/dates.ts. | assignments-service.ts L64; src/lib/dates.ts L7 | NFR-7: reuse both. Importing `getSchoolTimezone` from assignments-service is the existing precedent (contexts.ts already imports from it). Don't duplicate it. |\n| B16 | `MarkdownView` = react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema) rendering to MUI components. **There is no Markdown→plain-text helper** in the codebase. | src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx | FR-18 (200-char excerpt) and FR-28 (300-char email body) need a new small pure `markdownToPlainText(md)` (e.g. in `src/lib/markdown-text.ts`). Plain text rendered by React/the email template is escaped, so NFR-4 is met as long as the excerpt is never rendered as HTML/Markdown. Prefer a regex strip over a new dependency (remark is already installed transitively if an AST approach is preferred). |\n| B17 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `navigation` is a static array. `NotificationBell` polls `/api/notifications/unread-count` every 30 s, gated by visibility, and shows an MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L42-62 | FR-32: add an optional `badge?: 'announcements-unread'` key (or a badge endpoint string) to NavItem. The sidebar renders a polled Badge for items that have one. Reuse the bell's polling hook shape. |\n| B18 | `courseTabs` is a static array with `roles`. | src/config/course-tabs.ts | FR-21: `{ key: 'announcements', label: 'Announcements', href: id => /courses/${id}/announcements, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. |\n| B19 | `assertCanViewCourse` covers ADMIN, TEACHER (teacher or co-teacher only, **not homeroom**), STUDENT (enrollment) and PARENT (child enrolled). `canSeeDrafts` checks the course-manager test. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts L25+ | FR-21 gate: `assertCanViewCourse` and then the normal audience filter. FR-10 \"courses they manage\" = the same `teacherId \\|\\| coTeacherIds.includes` test, so reuse it rather than re-deriving. |\n| B20 | Seed: Tom/Sam/Pat by email. Courses are looked up with `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` and skipped if missing. The Grade 7 GradeLevel row **is** seeded. No 7A/7B/6A sections and no `ParentStudentLink` rows are created by the seed (they come from other scripts/fixtures, if at all). | prisma/seed.ts L18-22, L109-115, L275-305 | FR-35: grade/course/section-targeted seeds skip when their target is missing, using the same `logger.info`/`console.log` style. School-wide, staff and public seeds always run. Idempotency: upsert by a stable title + author, or check for existence first. |\n| B21 | Test layout: `tests/unit`, `tests/integration/<feature>/`, `tests/e2e/*.spec.ts` + `helpers/`. | tests/ | NFR-10: `tests/unit/announcements/*`, `tests/integration/announcements/*`, `tests/e2e/announcements.spec.ts`. |\n| B22 | `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0 is installed (`@mui/x-data-grid` too). | package.json | FR-13 publishAt/expiresAt: DateTimePicker. FR-23/24 tables: the existing `DataTable` component. Look up via mui-mcp per NFR-1. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend for **Concern**: DM = data model / migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance/cron, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | 2 enums, 4 models, 1 migration. AnnouncementRead has a composite PK `(announcementId, userId)`. **Needed beyond the PRD's model** (flag as deliberate additions): `Announcement.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` (FR-25), `notifiedAt DateTime?` (FR-27, likely already in the spec since FR-27 names it), and indexes `AnnouncementAudience @@index([type, refId])` and `Announcement @@index([status, publishAt])` (NFR-2). AnnouncementAudience columns implied by FR-2.1: `type`, `refId?` (null for SCHOOL/STAFF), `includeStudents/Parents/Teachers` booleans. Cascade deletes from Announcement to its children. |\n| FR-2 | XC / validation | `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts`, isomorphic Zod schema, shared by the composer and the handlers. Also validate: `expiresAt > publishAt` when both are set; ROLE refId ∈ Role enum; refId required unless SCHOOL/STAFF; at least one include flag true for GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION/COURSE. |\n| FR-3 | SVC | `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`. `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` returns a set union over the rows, all filtered to `ACTIVE && archivedAt null`. SCHOOL = all, STAFF = role ∈ {ADMIN, TEACHER}, ROLE = role = refId. Do the active filter **once** at the end, including on parents. |\n| FR-4 | SVC | GRADE_LEVEL: students via `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`; parents via ParentStudentLink of **those students** (before the active filter on the students? see §4 A3); teachers = `teacherId` ∪ `coTeacherIds` of courses where `section.gradeLevelId = refId AND academicYear.isCurrent`. |\n| FR-5 | SVC | SECTION: SectionMember(sectionId) students, their parents, `homeroomTeacherId` plus the teachers/co-teachers of `Course.sectionId = refId`. \"Current year\" is implicit (§4 A1). |\n| FR-6 | SVC | COURSE: `Enrollment(courseId, status ACTIVE)` students, their parents, teacher plus coTeachers. |\n| FR-7 | SVC / perf | `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`. **Key design point**: compute a per-user *membership key set* once (≤ ~4 small queries): role; own/children's gradeLevelIds; own/children's sectionIds (current year); own/children's ACTIVE courseIds; for teachers, managed courseIds + their sectionIds/gradeLevelIds + homeroom sectionIds. Then audience matching is a pure function over `(audience, keys)`. The same key set also becomes a Prisma `where` (an OR of `{type, refId in keys[type], include<Flag>: true}`) for the feed (FR-17/NFR-2). This puts the rules in one place (intake key risk), and `resolveAudienceUserIds` is the inverse expansion. The agreement test (NFR-10) checks both. For a parent the flag is `includeParents`, and the keys come from the children. |\n| FR-8 | SVC / XC | audience.ts must not import Announcement types. Its input is `{type, refId, includeStudents, includeParents, includeTeachers}[]`, so PRD-14 can reuse it. Export the `AudienceType` enum from Prisma. |\n| FR-9 | AUTH | ADMIN: any type, `isPublic` allowed. |\n| FR-10 | AUTH | `assertCanTarget(user, audiences, isPublic)` in the service, called by **both** create and update (PATCH can change the audience). TEACHER: COURSE where they manage the course (B19); SECTION where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Everything else, and `isPublic=true`, → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')` 403. On PATCH by a teacher, also re-check when `isPublic` is omitted but already true (it can't be, since only admins set it). |\n| FR-11 | AUTH | `requireRole('ADMIN','TEACHER')` on POST, PATCH, archive, preview-audience, manage, stats and remind. |\n| FR-12 | AUTH / audit | Edit: `authorId === user.id \\|\\| ADMIN`. Archive: same. Archive sets ARCHIVED (terminal for authors, §4 A7). Admin-on-others → `audit()`. A teacher who is no longer allowed to target the existing audience (e.g. lost co-teacher status) → PATCH fails on re-validation. That's acceptable. |\n| FR-13 | UI | Pages `/announcements/new` and `/announcements/[id]/edit` (server page + client form). Reuse MarkdownEditor, FileUpload (context 'announcement'), FileList, Autocomplete pickers per audience type (grade levels, sections, courses, roles). Teachers only see their own courses/homeroom in the pickers (UX; the server still enforces). Public toggle hidden for non-admins. Show and accept dates in the school tz (NFR-7). |\n| FR-14 | API / SVC | `POST /api/announcements/preview-audience`, body = audiences[] (same Zod schema). Run `assertCanTarget` first so the preview can't enumerate other audiences' sizes. Returns `{total, byRole:{STUDENT,PARENT,TEACHER,ADMIN}}`. Debounce in the UI. Uses `resolveAudienceUserIds` + `groupBy role` (or one count query). |\n| FR-15 | SVC | On transition to PUBLISHED/SCHEDULED (create or PATCH), resolve the count and if it is 0, `VALIDATION_ERROR`. Drafts are exempt (§4 A2). Scheduled ones are validated at schedule time, not again at publishAt; an emptied audience just notifies nobody. |\n| FR-16 | SVC / XC | **Visibility predicate in one place**: `visibleWhere(now) = { OR: [{status: PUBLISHED}, {status: SCHEDULED, publishAt: {lte: now}}], AND: [{OR: [{expiresAt: null}, {expiresAt: {gt: now}}]}] }`. Use it in the feed, detail, ack, files, public news and unread-count. Precedent: `isAssignmentVisible`/`isLessonVisible`. The status column stays SCHEDULED after publishAt (unless the maintenance run also flips it to PUBLISHED; recommend it does, in the same claim, for clean manage-view status). |\n| FR-17 | API / SVC / perf | `GET /api/announcements`: `visibleWhere(now) AND audiences: { some: audienceWhereForKeys(keys) }`. Plus `?filter=unread` (`reads: {none: {userId}}` or `readAt null`) and `?filter=ack` (`requiresAck AND no acknowledgedAt`). Ordering: up to 3 pinned first (separate `take:3` query on page 1, exclude those ids from the main list), then newest by **effective publish time** (`publishAt ?? createdAt` → store a `publishedAt`, or order by `publishAt` and set it on publish-now). Overflow pins fall into the newest list (§4 A4). Include the per-user read row via a `reads: {where:{userId}}` include. |\n| FR-18 | API / UI | The card DTO = cover fileId, title, author name + role, date, audience chips (labels need names for grade/section/course refIds, so batch-load by refId), `excerpt` (B16, 200 chars, computed server-side), attachment count (`_count`). |\n| FR-19 | API / AUTH | `GET /api/announcements/:id`: access if ADMIN, the author, or (visible AND isUserInAudience). Otherwise **404** (don't leak existence, NFR-6). Upsert AnnouncementRead `{readAt: now}` only for audience members (not for admins/authors outside the audience, since that would distort stats). Client renders the body with MarkdownView. |\n| FR-20 | API / AUTH | `POST /:id/ack`: visible AND requiresAck AND audience member → upsert `{readAt ?? now, acknowledgedAt ?? now}` (idempotent; keep the first ack time). Non-member → 404. `requiresAck=false` → 409 or VALIDATION_ERROR. Display with `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| FR-21 | API / CFG / UI | `GET /api/announcements?courseId=` → `assertCanViewCourse` then the feed query additionally filtered to `audiences some {type: COURSE, refId: courseId}`. The user must still be in the audience (a parent-only course announcement isn't shown to the course's students). Course tab page `/courses/[id]/announcements`. |\n| FR-22 | SVC / UI | Parent feed only: for each item, find matching audience rows and map them back to the children whose keys matched → `forChildren: [{id, firstName}]`. This falls out of the key-set design if keys are tracked per child (`Map<refKey, childIds>`). |\n| FR-23 | API / UI | `GET /api/announcements/manage`: no visibility filter. TEACHER `authorId = me`, ADMIN all. Reach = resolved recipient count (**expensive per row**: compute for the current page only; or snapshot `recipientCount` at publish and recompute live only on stats). Read % = `count(reads readAt not null) / reach`; ack % similar. Recommendation: resolve audiences per page row (≤ pageSize calls); keep it simple, a ponytail note for a snapshot later. |\n| FR-24 | API / UI | `GET /:id/stats`: author or ADMIN, else 404. Recipients = `resolveAudienceUserIds` (live) LEFT JOIN reads. Filters `?filter=unread\\|unacked`. `?format=csv` → `toCsv`, `Content-Disposition` attachment. Percentages over the live recipient set (AC-5: 30/50 = 60%). Readers who later left the audience are not counted. |\n| FR-25 | API / NOTIF / DM | `POST /:id/remind`: author or ADMIN. requiresAck must be true and the announcement visible. Atomic claim: `updateMany({where:{id, OR:[{lastRemindedAt:null},{lastRemindedAt:{lte: now-24h}}]}, data:{lastRemindedAt: now}})`. `count 0` → **429 RATE_LIMITED** (decision, B12). Then notify `announcement.reminder` to recipients − acknowledged. Returns `{notified: n}` (AC-5: 20). |\n| FR-26 | CFG / NOTIF | Add the types to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` (B9 conflict). roles: ALL. reminder: COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true (an ack is being chased). |\n| FR-27 | JOB / NOTIF | One `claimAndNotifyPublished(id, now)` helper: `updateMany({where:{id, notifiedAt:null, <visible>}, data:{notifiedAt: now, status: PUBLISHED}})`. If count = 1 → resolve recipients → notify. Called by publish-now (after the tx commits) and by `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` (batch 200, B11). Hook it into the dispatch route in its own try/catch. |\n| FR-28 | NOTIF | Email data: `{title, body: markdownToPlainText(body).slice(0,300), ctaLabel:'Read announcement', ctaUrl}`. Check GenericNotificationData's field names when designing. |\n| FR-29 | SVC | Follows from the notifiedAt claim: PATCH never clears notifiedAt. Also a draft → PATCH publish of an already-notified row (an archived-then-edited one) must not resend. |\n| FR-30 | FILE / AUTH | `announcementResolver(user, file)`: load the announcement by `file.contextId`. If `isPublic && visible` → true (including null user). If `!user` → false. If ADMIN or author → true. If visible && isUserInAudience → true. Else false. Register it in `registerBuiltInContexts` (B8). |\n| FR-31 | API / CFG | `getPublicNews({page})` in announcements-service: `isPublic && visibleWhere(now)`, a minimal DTO (no author email, no audience). Route `src/app/api/public/news/route.ts`. Add `'/api/public/news'` (exact match) to PUBLIC_API_PATHS. Consider `rateLimit` by IP since it is unauthenticated (cheap; the helper exists). |\n| FR-32 | CFG / UI / API | Nav entry for ALL_ROLES + the badge (B17). `GET /api/announcements/unread-count` = `count(visibleWhere ∧ audience keys ∧ no read row)`. It is polled every 30 s by every user, so it must be the same indexed query as the feed (NFR-2). |\n| FR-33 | UI | Conditional button on the feed page by role. |\n| FR-34 | API | Routes under `src/app/api/announcements/` (+`[id]/`, `[id]/archive`, `[id]/ack`, `[id]/stats`, `[id]/remind`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`, `manage`) + `src/app/api/public/news`. Note that static segments (`manage`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`) coexist with `[id]`; Next resolves static first, so that is fine. All use `withHandler` + Zod `parseBody`/`parseQuery`. |\n| FR-35 | SEED | 6 announcements, idempotent, with skip-if-missing for Grade 7 (exists), MATH-7A and the parent link (B20). The scheduled one is `publishAt = now + 2 days`, so `notifiedAt` stays null and the first real cron after that sends it. The welcome and staff-meeting seeds are already published: set `notifiedAt = now` so the seed never triggers a notification storm. The expired one has `expiresAt` in the past. |\n| FR-36 | XC | `src/server/announcements/{announcements-service.ts, audience.ts}` + (from FR-27) a `maintenance.ts` following the quiz precedent, or the function lives in the service. |\n| NFR-1 | UI / XC | MUI only. Confirm archive/remind with ConfirmDialog; toasts via useToast; pickers via Autocomplete; DateTimePicker for publishAt/expiresAt; the badge via MUI Badge; the \"Unread\" dot as a Badge/Box with visually hidden text. Every component looked up through mui-mcp (the mui-mcp server is listed in this session). `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |\n| NFR-2 | perf / DM | Feed = key-set OR join on `AnnouncementAudience(type, refId)` + `Announcement(status, publishAt)` indexes. Never `resolveAudienceUserIds` on the read path. Parent with 3 children: keys come from about 3 queries over 3 children. Verify with a seeded 2,000-row integration timing test (optional; mark as non-gating if CI is noisy). |\n| NFR-3 | AUTH | `requireUser`/`requireRole` in every handler and server page; FR-10 checks in the service (not only the route). AC-3 is an integration test. |\n| NFR-4 | XC | The body is rendered only via MarkdownView. Excerpt/email text = plain text (B16), never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Titles are plain strings. |\n| NFR-5 | UI | The unread dot has a visually-hidden \"Unread\" label (MUI `visuallyHidden` from `@mui/utils`, which ships with MUI). |\n| NFR-6 | AUTH | 404 for non-members on detail/ack/stats (not 403, to avoid existence leaks; stats → 404 for non-author non-admin). Files → the resolver denies (the files route maps that). Scheduled/expired → hidden from feeds and from non-author, non-admin detail. |\n| NFR-7 | XC | DB columns are UTC `DateTime`. The composer converts school-tz local → UTC on the server (or the client sends ISO with the tz applied). Displays use `formatInSchoolTz(getSchoolTimezone())`. |\n| NFR-8 | XC | Reuse list: notify, audit, registerFileAccess/attachFiles, toCsv, MarkdownEditor/View, FileUpload/FileList, DataTable, UserPicker (likely unused: pickers are entity pickers, not users), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, getSchoolTimezone, formatInSchoolTz, withHandler/parse*, assertCanViewCourse. |\n| NFR-9 | scope | No comments, reactions, i18n or SMS, and no public website pages. Just the service + the `/api/public/news` route. |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | Unit: audience matching per type × flag (pure key-set matcher, so no DB is needed), `assertCanTarget` rules, markdownToPlainText. Integration: an agreement property test over every seed user × every seed announcement audience; publishDueAnnouncements run twice / concurrently → one notification set; AC-3 403; AC-5 reminder 20 + 429. E2E: admin composes with ack → parent reads + acks → admin stats. The fixture creates the 6A child + Pat link (§4 A5). |\n| NFR-11 | XC | `logger` in all new server code, including the maintenance hook. |\n\n## 3. Risks and conflicts for arch-design-system\n\n| # | Risk / conflict | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1 | **Two audience code paths must agree** (FR-7, NFR-10). | Single source of rules: the `UserAudienceKeys` builder + a pure `matchesAudience(audience, keys)` + `audienceWhere(keys)`. `resolveAudienceUserIds` is written separately (set expansion) but tested against the matcher for every seed user. |\n| R2 | **FR-26 per-instance `mandatoryInApp`** isn't expressible in the static registry (B9). | Two type keys (`announcement.published`, `announcement.published_ack`), or accept a static `true`. Design picks one and records it as an ADR. |\n| R3 | **FR-1 \"exactly as specified\" vs. the needed additions** (`lastRemindedAt`, indexes, possibly `publishedAt`). | Add them as explicitly flagged additions; intake already pre-approved `lastRemindedAt`. |\n| R4 | **Feed ordering by \"newest\"** when publishAt is null for publish-now. | Set `publishAt = now` on publish-now so one column orders everything. |\n| R5 | **Status column vs. read-time visibility** (FR-16). | Visibility is computed from `publishAt`. The maintenance claim also flips SCHEDULED→PUBLISHED for the manage view. The UI should derive the display status with the same predicate, so it is correct between cron ticks. |\n| R6 | **Manage-view reach** (FR-23) means resolving N audiences per page. | Per-page live resolve (pageSize ≤ 50); `ponytail:` note for a `recipientCount` snapshot later. |\n| R7 | **Notification fan-out** on SCHOOL announcements (thousands of userIds in one notify). | Chunk userIds (e.g. 1,000) when calling notify. The notifiedAt claim happens before the send, so a crash mid-send loses the remainder rather than double-sending. That matches the existing quiz-release semantics; note it. |\n| R8 | **Teacher PATCH re-validation** (FR-10 on PATCH). | Run `assertCanTarget` on the *resulting* audience set whenever audiences or isPublic are present in the PATCH. |\n| R9 | **Orphan purge vs. drafts** (B7). | Attach files on every save, including drafts. |\n| R10 | **Public endpoint abuse** (FR-31). | Paginate with the max pageSize clamp from `parsePagination`, and optionally use `rateLimit` by IP. |\n| R11 | **Stats for audience changes after publish** (FR-29). | Stats use the live audience. Reads by users no longer in the audience are excluded from the percentages. Document this. |\n\n## 4. Assumptions carried from intake (must surface in system-design.md Overview)\n\n| # | Assumption | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| A1 | FR-5 section members = current academic-year SectionMember rows. | Members of the section row itself (a section belongs to one year). Teachers may only target current-year sections via the pickers. |\n| A2 | FR-15 drafts may have zero recipients. | Refused only on publish/schedule. |\n| A3 | Parent expansion uses linked parents of matching students; the ACTIVE filter applies to each final user. | A parent of an archived student is **not** reached through that student. Recommendation: only ACTIVE students expand to parents, and the matcher does the same. |\n| A4 | FR-17: overflow pins (>3) fall into newest-first. | Yes. |\n| A5 | AC-8: the test fixture creates Pat's 6A child + link if the seed lacks them. | Yes; the seed itself stays skip-if-missing. |\n| A6 | Archived courses (`Course.archivedAt`) in audience resolution. | Exclude archived courses from the teacher branches of GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION. Not stated in the PRD; flag it. |\n| A7 | FR-12: archive is terminal for authors; admins may still edit. | Yes. |\n| A8 | FR-25: 429 RATE_LIMITED + `lastRemindedAt` column. | Decided here (architect owns it per intake). |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1642,"cache_read_input_tokens":64976,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1642,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"612c4910-0bea-4d59-adbf-fcf9d39f8b8d","uuid":"65f57d4b-ddef-4475-9858-6f9b5e99c949","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:31:25.927Z","request_id":"req_011CgsftcfzLb4N8WJu2r7Hk","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Wc56sNEhDxTioi1zj5AFmM":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-12\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T18:00:00Z), PRD-12 Announcements & News. It has 36 FRs and 11 NFRs (47 requirements) at 94% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> All other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **SH-11 leftovers**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-12 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-12 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no Announcement* models or enums. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1: add a new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_announcements`). Add back-relations on `User` (authored, reads) and `FileObject` (attachments, and the cover image if it is an FK). |\n| B2 | `User.status` is `ACTIVE/INVITED/DISABLED/ARCHIVED` and `archivedAt` is a separate column. `notify()` filters `status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED]`, so it **includes INVITED**. | schema L17, L59; notify.ts L43 | FR-3 is stricter: audience = `status: ACTIVE, archivedAt: null`. Pass the resolved ids to `notify()`, which then filters on its own. Don't rely on notify's filter. |\n| B3 | `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId` (required). `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` has `@@index([studentId])` and a `@@unique([parentId, studentId])`. | schema L106, L144 | FR-4/5/6 parent expansion: join through the link. Parent → children is covered by the unique index's leading `parentId`. |\n| B4 | `Section(academicYearId, gradeLevelId, homeroomTeacherId?)`. `SectionMember(studentId, academicYearId)` is unique on `(studentId, academicYearId)`, and its academicYearId is denormalised. **There is no index on `sectionId`.** | schema L377-411 | FR-5: \"members\" = SectionMember rows where `academicYearId` = the section's year (that is already true per row, so filtering by `sectionId` is enough). A section belongs to one year, so the \"current year\" question reduces to \"is the section in the current year\". See §4 A1. |\n| B5 | `Course(academicYearId, sectionId?, teacherId, coTeacherIds String[], archivedAt?)`. `coTeacherIds` is queried with `has`. `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. | schema L414-447 | FR-4/5/6/10 teacher branches. `has` isn't indexable without a GIN index. The rows involved are small (only a user's own courses), so this is fine for NFR-2. Decide whether archived courses' teachers count (§4 A6). |\n| B6 | `Enrollment.status` ACTIVE/DROPPED, with `@@index([studentId, status])` and `@@unique([courseId, studentId])`. | schema L371, L450 | FR-6 student branch. Both directions are indexed. |\n| B7 | `FileObject(context, contextId)` is indexed. Uploads are created with `contextId: null`. `attachFiles(tx, context, contextId, ids)` / detach live in files-service. **`purgeOrphanFiles` deletes `contextId: null` files after 24 h.** | files-service.ts L212-244; files/purge.ts | FR-13/FR-30: attach the cover image and attachments with `context='announcement'`, `contextId=announcement.id` inside the create/update tx. A cover that is uploaded but never attached (e.g. an abandoned draft) is purged, which is correct. **A draft must still attach its files**, or they vanish after 24 h. |\n| B8 | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)`. Resolvers receive `null` for anonymous callers. Built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (contexts.ts). Resolver errors deny. `/api/files/` is already in PUBLIC_API_PATHS. | files/access.ts; contexts.ts; public-routes.ts | FR-30: add `register('announcement', announcementResolver)` to `registerBuiltInContexts` so it is guaranteed loaded, rather than as a side-effect import. Anonymous downloads already route through, so no public-route change is needed for files. |\n| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). `COMMUNICATION` exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a **static boolean per type**. | notifications/types.ts | **FR-26 conflict**: \"mandatoryInApp true when requiresAck\" can't be expressed per instance. Options: (a) two types, `announcement.published` (mandatoryInApp false) and `announcement.published_ack` (true); or (b) one type with `mandatoryInApp: true`. Recommend (a) as the smallest faithful mapping. **arch-design-system decides.** |\n| B10 | `notify({type, userIds, title, body, link, email:{template:'generic-notification', data}})` dedupes, never throws, and is called after commit. It truncates body to BODY_MAX and drops non-relative links. | notify.ts L8-60 | FR-27/28: call it after the notifiedAt claim commits. `link: /announcements/${id}`. Large audiences (a SCHOOL announcement can be thousands of users) go through one `findMany` + `createMany`. That's acceptable, but chunk the userIds if notify's `in` lists get large. |\n| B11 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` runs each pass in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take: BATCH)` → `updateMany({where:{id, claimCol: null}})` → act only if `count === 1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts L28-43 | FR-27: `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` copies this pattern exactly: `where status SCHEDULED, publishAt <= now, notifiedAt null`, claim `notifiedAt`. Publish-now uses the same claim helper, so one code path sends. |\n| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes both `RATE_LIMITED` (429) and `CONFLICT` (409). `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` exist. | src/server/http.ts | FR-34 handler conventions. FR-25: recommend **429 RATE_LIMITED** with `details.retryAfter` (ISO). It is semantically a time-based throttle, and intake suggested the same. |\n| B13 | `audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request})` never throws. The action convention is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|archive\\|delete`. | src/server/audit.ts | FR-12: `announcement.update` / `announcement.archive` when an admin acts on another author's row. Also audit the author's own archive (cheap; optional). |\n| B14 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` (formula-injection safe). | src/server/csv.ts | FR-24 `?format=csv`. |\n| B15 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from **assignments-service.ts**, not a shared module. `formatInSchoolTz` is in src/lib/dates.ts. | assignments-service.ts L64; src/lib/dates.ts L7 | NFR-7: reuse both. Importing `getSchoolTimezone` from assignments-service is the existing precedent (contexts.ts already imports from it). Don't duplicate it. |\n| B16 | `MarkdownView` = react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema) rendering to MUI components. **There is no Markdown→plain-text helper** in the codebase. | src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx | FR-18 (200-char excerpt) and FR-28 (300-char email body) need a new small pure `markdownToPlainText(md)` (e.g. in `src/lib/markdown-text.ts`). Plain text rendered by React/the email template is escaped, so NFR-4 is met as long as the excerpt is never rendered as HTML/Markdown. Prefer a regex strip over a new dependency (remark is already installed transitively if an AST approach is preferred). |\n| B17 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `navigation` is a static array. `NotificationBell` polls `/api/notifications/unread-count` every 30 s, gated by visibility, and shows an MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L42-62 | FR-32: add an optional `badge?: 'announcements-unread'` key (or a badge endpoint string) to NavItem. The sidebar renders a polled Badge for items that have one. Reuse the bell's polling hook shape. |\n| B18 | `courseTabs` is a static array with `roles`. | src/config/course-tabs.ts | FR-21: `{ key: 'announcements', label: 'Announcements', href: id => /courses/${id}/announcements, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. |\n| B19 | `assertCanViewCourse` covers ADMIN, TEACHER (teacher or co-teacher only, **not homeroom**), STUDENT (enrollment) and PARENT (child enrolled). `canSeeDrafts` checks the course-manager test. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts L25+ | FR-21 gate: `assertCanViewCourse` and then the normal audience filter. FR-10 \"courses they manage\" = the same `teacherId \\|\\| coTeacherIds.includes` test, so reuse it rather than re-deriving. |\n| B20 | Seed: Tom/Sam/Pat by email. Courses are looked up with `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` and skipped if missing. The Grade 7 GradeLevel row **is** seeded. No 7A/7B/6A sections and no `ParentStudentLink` rows are created by the seed (they come from other scripts/fixtures, if at all). | prisma/seed.ts L18-22, L109-115, L275-305 | FR-35: grade/course/section-targeted seeds skip when their target is missing, using the same `logger.info`/`console.log` style. School-wide, staff and public seeds always run. Idempotency: upsert by a stable title + author, or check for existence first. |\n| B21 | Test layout: `tests/unit`, `tests/integration/<feature>/`, `tests/e2e/*.spec.ts` + `helpers/`. | tests/ | NFR-10: `tests/unit/announcements/*`, `tests/integration/announcements/*`, `tests/e2e/announcements.spec.ts`. |\n| B22 | `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0 is installed (`@mui/x-data-grid` too). | package.json | FR-13 publishAt/expiresAt: DateTimePicker. FR-23/24 tables: the existing `DataTable` component. Look up via mui-mcp per NFR-1. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend for **Concern**: DM = data model / migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance/cron, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | 2 enums, 4 models, 1 migration. AnnouncementRead has a composite PK `(announcementId, userId)`. **Needed beyond the PRD's model** (flag as deliberate additions): `Announcement.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` (FR-25), `notifiedAt DateTime?` (FR-27, likely already in the spec since FR-27 names it), and indexes `AnnouncementAudience @@index([type, refId])` and `Announcement @@index([status, publishAt])` (NFR-2). AnnouncementAudience columns implied by FR-2.1: `type`, `refId?` (null for SCHOOL/STAFF), `includeStudents/Parents/Teachers` booleans. Cascade deletes from Announcement to its children. |\n| FR-2 | XC / validation | `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts`, isomorphic Zod schema, shared by the composer and the handlers. Also validate: `expiresAt > publishAt` when both are set; ROLE refId ∈ Role enum; refId required unless SCHOOL/STAFF; at least one include flag true for GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION/COURSE. |\n| FR-3 | SVC | `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`. `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` returns a set union over the rows, all filtered to `ACTIVE && archivedAt null`. SCHOOL = all, STAFF = role ∈ {ADMIN, TEACHER}, ROLE = role = refId. Do the active filter **once** at the end, including on parents. |\n| FR-4 | SVC | GRADE_LEVEL: students via `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`; parents via ParentStudentLink of **those students** (before the active filter on the students? see §4 A3); teachers = `teacherId` ∪ `coTeacherIds` of courses where `section.gradeLevelId = refId AND academicYear.isCurrent`. |\n| FR-5 | SVC | SECTION: SectionMember(sectionId) students, their parents, `homeroomTeacherId` plus the teachers/co-teachers of `Course.sectionId = refId`. \"Current year\" is implicit (§4 A1). |\n| FR-6 | SVC | COURSE: `Enrollment(courseId, status ACTIVE)` students, their parents, teacher plus coTeachers. |\n| FR-7 | SVC / perf | `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`. **Key design point**: compute a per-user *membership key set* once (≤ ~4 small queries): role; own/children's gradeLevelIds; own/children's sectionIds (current year); own/children's ACTIVE courseIds; for teachers, managed courseIds + their sectionIds/gradeLevelIds + homeroom sectionIds. Then audience matching is a pure function over `(audience, keys)`. The same key set also becomes a Prisma `where` (an OR of `{type, refId in keys[type], include<Flag>: true}`) for the feed (FR-17/NFR-2). This puts the rules in one place (intake key risk), and `resolveAudienceUserIds` is the inverse expansion. The agreement test (NFR-10) checks both. For a parent the flag is `includeParents`, and the keys come from the children. |\n| FR-8 | SVC / XC | audience.ts must not import Announcement types. Its input is `{type, refId, includeStudents, includeParents, includeTeachers}[]`, so PRD-14 can reuse it. Export the `AudienceType` enum from Prisma. |\n| FR-9 | AUTH | ADMIN: any type, `isPublic` allowed. |\n| FR-10 | AUTH | `assertCanTarget(user, audiences, isPublic)` in the service, called by **both** create and update (PATCH can change the audience). TEACHER: COURSE where they manage the course (B19); SECTION where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Everything else, and `isPublic=true`, → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')` 403. On PATCH by a teacher, also re-check when `isPublic` is omitted but already true (it can't be, since only admins set it). |\n| FR-11 | AUTH | `requireRole('ADMIN','TEACHER')` on POST, PATCH, archive, preview-audience, manage, stats and remind. |\n| FR-12 | AUTH / audit | Edit: `authorId === user.id \\|\\| ADMIN`. Archive: same. Archive sets ARCHIVED (terminal for authors, §4 A7). Admin-on-others → `audit()`. A teacher who is no longer allowed to target the existing audience (e.g. lost co-teacher status) → PATCH fails on re-validation. That's acceptable. |\n| FR-13 | UI | Pages `/announcements/new` and `/announcements/[id]/edit` (server page + client form). Reuse MarkdownEditor, FileUpload (context 'announcement'), FileList, Autocomplete pickers per audience type (grade levels, sections, courses, roles). Teachers only see their own courses/homeroom in the pickers (UX; the server still enforces). Public toggle hidden for non-admins. Show and accept dates in the school tz (NFR-7). |\n| FR-14 | API / SVC | `POST /api/announcements/preview-audience`, body = audiences[] (same Zod schema). Run `assertCanTarget` first so the preview can't enumerate other audiences' sizes. Returns `{total, byRole:{STUDENT,PARENT,TEACHER,ADMIN}}`. Debounce in the UI. Uses `resolveAudienceUserIds` + `groupBy role` (or one count query). |\n| FR-15 | SVC | On transition to PUBLISHED/SCHEDULED (create or PATCH), resolve the count and if it is 0, `VALIDATION_ERROR`. Drafts are exempt (§4 A2). Scheduled ones are validated at schedule time, not again at publishAt; an emptied audience just notifies nobody. |\n| FR-16 | SVC / XC | **Visibility predicate in one place**: `visibleWhere(now) = { OR: [{status: PUBLISHED}, {status: SCHEDULED, publishAt: {lte: now}}], AND: [{OR: [{expiresAt: null}, {expiresAt: {gt: now}}]}] }`. Use it in the feed, detail, ack, files, public news and unread-count. Precedent: `isAssignmentVisible`/`isLessonVisible`. The status column stays SCHEDULED after publishAt (unless the maintenance run also flips it to PUBLISHED; recommend it does, in the same claim, for clean manage-view status). |\n| FR-17 | API / SVC / perf | `GET /api/announcements`: `visibleWhere(now) AND audiences: { some: audienceWhereForKeys(keys) }`. Plus `?filter=unread` (`reads: {none: {userId}}` or `readAt null`) and `?filter=ack` (`requiresAck AND no acknowledgedAt`). Ordering: up to 3 pinned first (separate `take:3` query on page 1, exclude those ids from the main list), then newest by **effective publish time** (`publishAt ?? createdAt` → store a `publishedAt`, or order by `publishAt` and set it on publish-now). Overflow pins fall into the newest list (§4 A4). Include the per-user read row via a `reads: {where:{userId}}` include. |\n| FR-18 | API / UI | The card DTO = cover fileId, title, author name + role, date, audience chips (labels need names for grade/section/course refIds, so batch-load by refId), `excerpt` (B16, 200 chars, computed server-side), attachment count (`_count`). |\n| FR-19 | API / AUTH | `GET /api/announcements/:id`: access if ADMIN, the author, or (visible AND isUserInAudience). Otherwise **404** (don't leak existence, NFR-6). Upsert AnnouncementRead `{readAt: now}` only for audience members (not for admins/authors outside the audience, since that would distort stats). Client renders the body with MarkdownView. |\n| FR-20 | API / AUTH | `POST /:id/ack`: visible AND requiresAck AND audience member → upsert `{readAt ?? now, acknowledgedAt ?? now}` (idempotent; keep the first ack time). Non-member → 404. `requiresAck=false` → 409 or VALIDATION_ERROR. Display with `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| FR-21 | API / CFG / UI | `GET /api/announcements?courseId=` → `assertCanViewCourse` then the feed query additionally filtered to `audiences some {type: COURSE, refId: courseId}`. The user must still be in the audience (a parent-only course announcement isn't shown to the course's students). Course tab page `/courses/[id]/announcements`. |\n| FR-22 | SVC / UI | Parent feed only: for each item, find matching audience rows and map them back to the children whose keys matched → `forChildren: [{id, firstName}]`. This falls out of the key-set design if keys are tracked per child (`Map<refKey, childIds>`). |\n| FR-23 | API / UI | `GET /api/announcements/manage`: no visibility filter. TEACHER `authorId = me`, ADMIN all. Reach = resolved recipient count (**expensive per row**: compute for the current page only; or snapshot `recipientCount` at publish and recompute live only on stats). Read % = `count(reads readAt not null) / reach`; ack % similar. Recommendation: resolve audiences per page row (≤ pageSize calls); keep it simple, a ponytail note for a snapshot later. |\n| FR-24 | API / UI | `GET /:id/stats`: author or ADMIN, else 404. Recipients = `resolveAudienceUserIds` (live) LEFT JOIN reads. Filters `?filter=unread\\|unacked`. `?format=csv` → `toCsv`, `Content-Disposition` attachment. Percentages over the live recipient set (AC-5: 30/50 = 60%). Readers who later left the audience are not counted. |\n| FR-25 | API / NOTIF / DM | `POST /:id/remind`: author or ADMIN. requiresAck must be true and the announcement visible. Atomic claim: `updateMany({where:{id, OR:[{lastRemindedAt:null},{lastRemindedAt:{lte: now-24h}}]}, data:{lastRemindedAt: now}})`. `count 0` → **429 RATE_LIMITED** (decision, B12). Then notify `announcement.reminder` to recipients − acknowledged. Returns `{notified: n}` (AC-5: 20). |\n| FR-26 | CFG / NOTIF | Add the types to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` (B9 conflict). roles: ALL. reminder: COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true (an ack is being chased). |\n| FR-27 | JOB / NOTIF | One `claimAndNotifyPublished(id, now)` helper: `updateMany({where:{id, notifiedAt:null, <visible>}, data:{notifiedAt: now, status: PUBLISHED}})`. If count = 1 → resolve recipients → notify. Called by publish-now (after the tx commits) and by `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` (batch 200, B11). Hook it into the dispatch route in its own try/catch. |\n| FR-28 | NOTIF | Email data: `{title, body: markdownToPlainText(body).slice(0,300), ctaLabel:'Read announcement', ctaUrl}`. Check GenericNotificationData's field names when designing. |\n| FR-29 | SVC | Follows from the notifiedAt claim: PATCH never clears notifiedAt. Also a draft → PATCH publish of an already-notified row (an archived-then-edited one) must not resend. |\n| FR-30 | FILE / AUTH | `announcementResolver(user, file)`: load the announcement by `file.contextId`. If `isPublic && visible` → true (including null user). If `!user` → false. If ADMIN or author → true. If visible && isUserInAudience → true. Else false. Register it in `registerBuiltInContexts` (B8). |\n| FR-31 | API / CFG | `getPublicNews({page})` in announcements-service: `isPublic && visibleWhere(now)`, a minimal DTO (no author email, no audience). Route `src/app/api/public/news/route.ts`. Add `'/api/public/news'` (exact match) to PUBLIC_API_PATHS. Consider `rateLimit` by IP since it is unauthenticated (cheap; the helper exists). |\n| FR-32 | CFG / UI / API | Nav entry for ALL_ROLES + the badge (B17). `GET /api/announcements/unread-count` = `count(visibleWhere ∧ audience keys ∧ no read row)`. It is polled every 30 s by every user, so it must be the same indexed query as the feed (NFR-2). |\n| FR-33 | UI | Conditional button on the feed page by role. |\n| FR-34 | API | Routes under `src/app/api/announcements/` (+`[id]/`, `[id]/archive`, `[id]/ack`, `[id]/stats`, `[id]/remind`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`, `manage`) + `src/app/api/public/news`. Note that static segments (`manage`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`) coexist with `[id]`; Next resolves static first, so that is fine. All use `withHandler` + Zod `parseBody`/`parseQuery`. |\n| FR-35 | SEED | 6 announcements, idempotent, with skip-if-missing for Grade 7 (exists), MATH-7A and the parent link (B20). The scheduled one is `publishAt = now + 2 days`, so `notifiedAt` stays null and the first real cron after that sends it. The welcome and staff-meeting seeds are already published: set `notifiedAt = now` so the seed never triggers a notification storm. The expired one has `expiresAt` in the past. |\n| FR-36 | XC | `src/server/announcements/{announcements-service.ts, audience.ts}` + (from FR-27) a `maintenance.ts` following the quiz precedent, or the function lives in the service. |\n| NFR-1 | UI / XC | MUI only. Confirm archive/remind with ConfirmDialog; toasts via useToast; pickers via Autocomplete; DateTimePicker for publishAt/expiresAt; the badge via MUI Badge; the \"Unread\" dot as a Badge/Box with visually hidden text. Every component looked up through mui-mcp (the mui-mcp server is listed in this session). `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |\n| NFR-2 | perf / DM | Feed = key-set OR join on `AnnouncementAudience(type, refId)` + `Announcement(status, publishAt)` indexes. Never `resolveAudienceUserIds` on the read path. Parent with 3 children: keys come from about 3 queries over 3 children. Verify with a seeded 2,000-row integration timing test (optional; mark as non-gating if CI is noisy). |\n| NFR-3 | AUTH | `requireUser`/`requireRole` in every handler and server page; FR-10 checks in the service (not only the route). AC-3 is an integration test. |\n| NFR-4 | XC | The body is rendered only via MarkdownView. Excerpt/email text = plain text (B16), never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Titles are plain strings. |\n| NFR-5 | UI | The unread dot has a visually-hidden \"Unread\" label (MUI `visuallyHidden` from `@mui/utils`, which ships with MUI). |\n| NFR-6 | AUTH | 404 for non-members on detail/ack/stats (not 403, to avoid existence leaks; stats → 404 for non-author non-admin). Files → the resolver denies (the files route maps that). Scheduled/expired → hidden from feeds and from non-author, non-admin detail. |\n| NFR-7 | XC | DB columns are UTC `DateTime`. The composer converts school-tz local → UTC on the server (or the client sends ISO with the tz applied). Displays use `formatInSchoolTz(getSchoolTimezone())`. |\n| NFR-8 | XC | Reuse list: notify, audit, registerFileAccess/attachFiles, toCsv, MarkdownEditor/View, FileUpload/FileList, DataTable, UserPicker (likely unused: pickers are entity pickers, not users), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, getSchoolTimezone, formatInSchoolTz, withHandler/parse*, assertCanViewCourse. |\n| NFR-9 | scope | No comments, reactions, i18n or SMS, and no public website pages. Just the service + the `/api/public/news` route. |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | Unit: audience matching per type × flag (pure key-set matcher, so no DB is needed), `assertCanTarget` rules, markdownToPlainText. Integration: an agreement property test over every seed user × every seed announcement audience; publishDueAnnouncements run twice / concurrently → one notification set; AC-3 403; AC-5 reminder 20 + 429. E2E: admin composes with ack → parent reads + acks → admin stats. The fixture creates the 6A child + Pat link (§4 A5). |\n| NFR-11 | XC | `logger` in all new server code, including the maintenance hook. |\n\n## 3. Risks and conflicts for arch-design-system\n\n| # | Risk / conflict | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1 | **Two audience code paths must agree** (FR-7, NFR-10). | Single source of rules: the `UserAudienceKeys` builder + a pure `matchesAudience(audience, keys)` + `audienceWhere(keys)`. `resolveAudienceUserIds` is written separately (set expansion) but tested against the matcher for every seed user. |\n| R2 | **FR-26 per-instance `mandatoryInApp`** isn't expressible in the static registry (B9). | Two type keys (`announcement.published`, `announcement.published_ack`), or accept a static `true`. Design picks one and records it as an ADR. |\n| R3 | **FR-1 \"exactly as specified\" vs. the needed additions** (`lastRemindedAt`, indexes, possibly `publishedAt`). | Add them as explicitly flagged additions; intake already pre-approved `lastRemindedAt`. |\n| R4 | **Feed ordering by \"newest\"** when publishAt is null for publish-now. | Set `publishAt = now` on publish-now so one column orders everything. |\n| R5 | **Status column vs. read-time visibility** (FR-16). | Visibility is computed from `publishAt`. The maintenance claim also flips SCHEDULED→PUBLISHED for the manage view. The UI should derive the display status with the same predicate, so it is correct between cron ticks. |\n| R6 | **Manage-view reach** (FR-23) means resolving N audiences per page. | Per-page live resolve (pageSize ≤ 50); `ponytail:` note for a `recipientCount` snapshot later. |\n| R7 | **Notification fan-out** on SCHOOL announcements (thousands of userIds in one notify). | Chunk userIds (e.g. 1,000) when calling notify. The notifiedAt claim happens before the send, so a crash mid-send loses the remainder rather than double-sending. That matches the existing quiz-release semantics; note it. |\n| R8 | **Teacher PATCH re-validation** (FR-10 on PATCH). | Run `assertCanTarget` on the *resulting* audience set whenever audiences or isPublic are present in the PATCH. |\n| R9 | **Orphan purge vs. drafts** (B7). | Attach files on every save, including drafts. |\n| R10 | **Public endpoint abuse** (FR-31). | Paginate with the max pageSize clamp from `parsePagination`, and optionally use `rateLimit` by IP. |\n| R11 | **Stats for audience changes after publish** (FR-29). | Stats use the live audience. Reads by users no longer in the audience are excluded from the percentages. Document this. |\n\n## 4. Assumptions carried from intake (must surface in system-design.md Overview)\n\n| # | Assumption | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| A1 | FR-5 section members = current academic-year SectionMember rows. | Members of the section row itself (a section belongs to one year). Teachers may only target current-year sections via the pickers. |\n| A2 | FR-15 drafts may have zero recipients. | Refused only on publish/schedule. |\n| A3 | Parent expansion uses linked parents of matching students; the ACTIVE filter applies to each final user. | A parent of an archived student is **not** reached through that student. Recommendation: only ACTIVE students expand to parents, and the matcher does the same. |\n| A4 | FR-17: overflow pins (>3) fall into newest-first. | Yes. |\n| A5 | AC-8: the test fixture creates Pat's 6A child + link if the seed lacks them. | Yes; the seed itself stays skip-if-missing. |\n| A6 | Archived courses (`Course.archivedAt`) in audience resolution. | Exclude archived courses from the teacher branches of GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION. Not stated in the PRD; flag it. |\n| A7 | FR-12: archive is terminal for authors; admins may still edit. | Yes. |\n| A8 | FR-25: 429 RATE_LIMITED + `lastRemindedAt` column. | Decided here (architect owns it per intake). |\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wc56sNEhDxTioi1zj5AFmM","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"612c4910-0bea-4d59-adbf-fcf9d39f8b8d","uuid":"ecb17301-7e97-4a64-9e47-0f3cb3e1c932","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:31:26.041Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-12\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T18:00:00Z), PRD-12 Announcements & News. It has 36 FRs and 11 NFRs (47 requirements) at 94% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> All other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **SH-11 leftovers**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-12 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-12 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no Announcement* models or enums. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1: add a new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_announcements`). Add back-relations on `User` (authored, reads) and `FileObject` (attachments, and the cover image if it is an FK). |\n| B2 | `User.status` is `ACTIVE/INVITED/DISABLED/ARCHIVED` and `archivedAt` is a separate column. `notify()` filters `status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED]`, so it **includes INVITED**. | schema L17, L59; notify.ts L43 | FR-3 is stricter: audience = `status: ACTIVE, archivedAt: null`. Pass the resolved ids to `notify()`, which then filters on its own. Don't rely on notify's filter. |\n| B3 | `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId` (required). `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` has `@@index([studentId])` and a `@@unique([parentId, studentId])`. | schema L106, L144 | FR-4/5/6 parent expansion: join through the link. Parent → children is covered by the unique index's leading `parentId`. |\n| B4 | `Section(academicYearId, gradeLevelId, homeroomTeacherId?)`. `SectionMember(studentId, academicYearId)` is unique on `(studentId, academicYearId)`, and its academicYearId is denormalised. **There is no index on `sectionId`.** | schema L377-411 | FR-5: \"members\" = SectionMember rows where `academicYearId` = the section's year (that is already true per row, so filtering by `sectionId` is enough). A section belongs to one year, so the \"current year\" question reduces to \"is the section in the current year\". See §4 A1. |\n| B5 | `Course(academicYearId, sectionId?, teacherId, coTeacherIds String[], archivedAt?)`. `coTeacherIds` is queried with `has`. `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. | schema L414-447 | FR-4/5/6/10 teacher branches. `has` isn't indexable without a GIN index. The rows involved are small (only a user's own courses), so this is fine for NFR-2. Decide whether archived courses' teachers count (§4 A6). |\n| B6 | `Enrollment.status` ACTIVE/DROPPED, with `@@index([studentId, status])` and `@@unique([courseId, studentId])`. | schema L371, L450 | FR-6 student branch. Both directions are indexed. |\n| B7 | `FileObject(context, contextId)` is indexed. Uploads are created with `contextId: null`. `attachFiles(tx, context, contextId, ids)` / detach live in files-service. **`purgeOrphanFiles` deletes `contextId: null` files after 24 h.** | files-service.ts L212-244; files/purge.ts | FR-13/FR-30: attach the cover image and attachments with `context='announcement'`, `contextId=announcement.id` inside the create/update tx. A cover that is uploaded but never attached (e.g. an abandoned draft) is purged, which is correct. **A draft must still attach its files**, or they vanish after 24 h. |\n| B8 | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)`. Resolvers receive `null` for anonymous callers. Built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (contexts.ts). Resolver errors deny. `/api/files/` is already in PUBLIC_API_PATHS. | files/access.ts; contexts.ts; public-routes.ts | FR-30: add `register('announcement', announcementResolver)` to `registerBuiltInContexts` so it is guaranteed loaded, rather than as a side-effect import. Anonymous downloads already route through, so no public-route change is needed for files. |\n| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). `COMMUNICATION` exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a **static boolean per type**. | notifications/types.ts | **FR-26 conflict**: \"mandatoryInApp true when requiresAck\" can't be expressed per instance. Options: (a) two types, `announcement.published` (mandatoryInApp false) and `announcement.published_ack` (true); or (b) one type with `mandatoryInApp: true`. Recommend (a) as the smallest faithful mapping. **arch-design-system decides.** |\n| B10 | `notify({type, userIds, title, body, link, email:{template:'generic-notification', data}})` dedupes, never throws, and is called after commit. It truncates body to BODY_MAX and drops non-relative links. | notify.ts L8-60 | FR-27/28: call it after the notifiedAt claim commits. `link: /announcements/${id}`. Large audiences (a SCHOOL announcement can be thousands of users) go through one `findMany` + `createMany`. That's acceptable, but chunk the userIds if notify's `in` lists get large. |\n| B11 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` runs each pass in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take: BATCH)` → `updateMany({where:{id, claimCol: null}})` → act only if `count === 1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts L28-43 | FR-27: `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` copies this pattern exactly: `where status SCHEDULED, publishAt <= now, notifiedAt null`, claim `notifiedAt`. Publish-now uses the same claim helper, so one code path sends. |\n| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes both `RATE_LIMITED` (429) and `CONFLICT` (409). `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` exist. | src/server/http.ts | FR-34 handler conventions. FR-25: recommend **429 RATE_LIMITED** with `details.retryAfter` (ISO). It is semantically a time-based throttle, and intake suggested the same. |\n| B13 | `audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request})` never throws. The action convention is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|archive\\|delete`. | src/server/audit.ts | FR-12: `announcement.update` / `announcement.archive` when an admin acts on another author's row. Also audit the author's own archive (cheap; optional). |\n| B14 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` (formula-injection safe). | src/server/csv.ts | FR-24 `?format=csv`. |\n| B15 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from **assignments-service.ts**, not a shared module. `formatInSchoolTz` is in src/lib/dates.ts. | assignments-service.ts L64; src/lib/dates.ts L7 | NFR-7: reuse both. Importing `getSchoolTimezone` from assignments-service is the existing precedent (contexts.ts already imports from it). Don't duplicate it. |\n| B16 | `MarkdownView` = react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema) rendering to MUI components. **There is no Markdown→plain-text helper** in the codebase. | src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx | FR-18 (200-char excerpt) and FR-28 (300-char email body) need a new small pure `markdownToPlainText(md)` (e.g. in `src/lib/markdown-text.ts`). Plain text rendered by React/the email template is escaped, so NFR-4 is met as long as the excerpt is never rendered as HTML/Markdown. Prefer a regex strip over a new dependency (remark is already installed transitively if an AST approach is preferred). |\n| B17 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `navigation` is a static array. `NotificationBell` polls `/api/notifications/unread-count` every 30 s, gated by visibility, and shows an MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L42-62 | FR-32: add an optional `badge?: 'announcements-unread'` key (or a badge endpoint string) to NavItem. The sidebar renders a polled Badge for items that have one. Reuse the bell's polling hook shape. |\n| B18 | `courseTabs` is a static array with `roles`. | src/config/course-tabs.ts | FR-21: `{ key: 'announcements', label: 'Announcements', href: id => /courses/${id}/announcements, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. |\n| B19 | `assertCanViewCourse` covers ADMIN, TEACHER (teacher or co-teacher only, **not homeroom**), STUDENT (enrollment) and PARENT (child enrolled). `canSeeDrafts` checks the course-manager test. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts L25+ | FR-21 gate: `assertCanViewCourse` and then the normal audience filter. FR-10 \"courses they manage\" = the same `teacherId \\|\\| coTeacherIds.includes` test, so reuse it rather than re-deriving. |\n| B20 | Seed: Tom/Sam/Pat by email. Courses are looked up with `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` and skipped if missing. The Grade 7 GradeLevel row **is** seeded. No 7A/7B/6A sections and no `ParentStudentLink` rows are created by the seed (they come from other scripts/fixtures, if at all). | prisma/seed.ts L18-22, L109-115, L275-305 | FR-35: grade/course/section-targeted seeds skip when their target is missing, using the same `logger.info`/`console.log` style. School-wide, staff and public seeds always run. Idempotency: upsert by a stable title + author, or check for existence first. |\n| B21 | Test layout: `tests/unit`, `tests/integration/<feature>/`, `tests/e2e/*.spec.ts` + `helpers/`. | tests/ | NFR-10: `tests/unit/announcements/*`, `tests/integration/announcements/*`, `tests/e2e/announcements.spec.ts`. |\n| B22 | `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0 is installed (`@mui/x-data-grid` too). | package.json | FR-13 publishAt/expiresAt: DateTimePicker. FR-23/24 tables: the existing `DataTable` component. Look up via mui-mcp per NFR-1. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend for **Concern**: DM = data model / migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance/cron, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | 2 enums, 4 models, 1 migration. AnnouncementRead has a composite PK `(announcementId, userId)`. **Needed beyond the PRD's model** (flag as deliberate additions): `Announcement.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` (FR-25), `notifiedAt DateTime?` (FR-27, likely already in the spec since FR-27 names it), and indexes `AnnouncementAudience @@index([type, refId])` and `Announcement @@index([status, publishAt])` (NFR-2). AnnouncementAudience columns implied by FR-2.1: `type`, `refId?` (null for SCHOOL/STAFF), `includeStudents/Parents/Teachers` booleans. Cascade deletes from Announcement to its children. |\n| FR-2 | XC / validation | `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts`, isomorphic Zod schema, shared by the composer and the handlers. Also validate: `expiresAt > publishAt` when both are set; ROLE refId ∈ Role enum; refId required unless SCHOOL/STAFF; at least one include flag true for GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION/COURSE. |\n| FR-3 | SVC | `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`. `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` returns a set union over the rows, all filtered to `ACTIVE && archivedAt null`. SCHOOL = all, STAFF = role ∈ {ADMIN, TEACHER}, ROLE = role = refId. Do the active filter **once** at the end, including on parents. |\n| FR-4 | SVC | GRADE_LEVEL: students via `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`; parents via ParentStudentLink of **those students** (before the active filter on the students? see §4 A3); teachers = `teacherId` ∪ `coTeacherIds` of courses where `section.gradeLevelId = refId AND academicYear.isCurrent`. |\n| FR-5 | SVC | SECTION: SectionMember(sectionId) students, their parents, `homeroomTeacherId` plus the teachers/co-teachers of `Course.sectionId = refId`. \"Current year\" is implicit (§4 A1). |\n| FR-6 | SVC | COURSE: `Enrollment(courseId, status ACTIVE)` students, their parents, teacher plus coTeachers. |\n| FR-7 | SVC / perf | `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`. **Key design point**: compute a per-user *membership key set* once (≤ ~4 small queries): role; own/children's gradeLevelIds; own/children's sectionIds (current year); own/children's ACTIVE courseIds; for teachers, managed courseIds + their sectionIds/gradeLevelIds + homeroom sectionIds. Then audience matching is a pure function over `(audience, keys)`. The same key set also becomes a Prisma `where` (an OR of `{type, refId in keys[type], include<Flag>: true}`) for the feed (FR-17/NFR-2). This puts the rules in one place (intake key risk), and `resolveAudienceUserIds` is the inverse expansion. The agreement test (NFR-10) checks both. For a parent the flag is `includeParents`, and the keys come from the children. |\n| FR-8 | SVC / XC | audience.ts must not import Announcement types. Its input is `{type, refId, includeStudents, includeParents, includeTeachers}[]`, so PRD-14 can reuse it. Export the `AudienceType` enum from Prisma. |\n| FR-9 | AUTH | ADMIN: any type, `isPublic` allowed. |\n| FR-10 | AUTH | `assertCanTarget(user, audiences, isPublic)` in the service, called by **both** create and update (PATCH can change the audience). TEACHER: COURSE where they manage the course (B19); SECTION where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Everything else, and `isPublic=true`, → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')` 403. On PATCH by a teacher, also re-check when `isPublic` is omitted but already true (it can't be, since only admins set it). |\n| FR-11 | AUTH | `requireRole('ADMIN','TEACHER')` on POST, PATCH, archive, preview-audience, manage, stats and remind. |\n| FR-12 | AUTH / audit | Edit: `authorId === user.id \\|\\| ADMIN`. Archive: same. Archive sets ARCHIVED (terminal for authors, §4 A7). Admin-on-others → `audit()`. A teacher who is no longer allowed to target the existing audience (e.g. lost co-teacher status) → PATCH fails on re-validation. That's acceptable. |\n| FR-13 | UI | Pages `/announcements/new` and `/announcements/[id]/edit` (server page + client form). Reuse MarkdownEditor, FileUpload (context 'announcement'), FileList, Autocomplete pickers per audience type (grade levels, sections, courses, roles). Teachers only see their own courses/homeroom in the pickers (UX; the server still enforces). Public toggle hidden for non-admins. Show and accept dates in the school tz (NFR-7). |\n| FR-14 | API / SVC | `POST /api/announcements/preview-audience`, body = audiences[] (same Zod schema). Run `assertCanTarget` first so the preview can't enumerate other audiences' sizes. Returns `{total, byRole:{STUDENT,PARENT,TEACHER,ADMIN}}`. Debounce in the UI. Uses `resolveAudienceUserIds` + `groupBy role` (or one count query). |\n| FR-15 | SVC | On transition to PUBLISHED/SCHEDULED (create or PATCH), resolve the count and if it is 0, `VALIDATION_ERROR`. Drafts are exempt (§4 A2). Scheduled ones are validated at schedule time, not again at publishAt; an emptied audience just notifies nobody. |\n| FR-16 | SVC / XC | **Visibility predicate in one place**: `visibleWhere(now) = { OR: [{status: PUBLISHED}, {status: SCHEDULED, publishAt: {lte: now}}], AND: [{OR: [{expiresAt: null}, {expiresAt: {gt: now}}]}] }`. Use it in the feed, detail, ack, files, public news and unread-count. Precedent: `isAssignmentVisible`/`isLessonVisible`. The status column stays SCHEDULED after publishAt (unless the maintenance run also flips it to PUBLISHED; recommend it does, in the same claim, for clean manage-view status). |\n| FR-17 | API / SVC / perf | `GET /api/announcements`: `visibleWhere(now) AND audiences: { some: audienceWhereForKeys(keys) }`. Plus `?filter=unread` (`reads: {none: {userId}}` or `readAt null`) and `?filter=ack` (`requiresAck AND no acknowledgedAt`). Ordering: up to 3 pinned first (separate `take:3` query on page 1, exclude those ids from the main list), then newest by **effective publish time** (`publishAt ?? createdAt` → store a `publishedAt`, or order by `publishAt` and set it on publish-now). Overflow pins fall into the newest list (§4 A4). Include the per-user read row via a `reads: {where:{userId}}` include. |\n| FR-18 | API / UI | The card DTO = cover fileId, title, author name + role, date, audience chips (labels need names for grade/section/course refIds, so batch-load by refId), `excerpt` (B16, 200 chars, computed server-side), attachment count (`_count`). |\n| FR-19 | API / AUTH | `GET /api/announcements/:id`: access if ADMIN, the author, or (visible AND isUserInAudience). Otherwise **404** (don't leak existence, NFR-6). Upsert AnnouncementRead `{readAt: now}` only for audience members (not for admins/authors outside the audience, since that would distort stats). Client renders the body with MarkdownView. |\n| FR-20 | API / AUTH | `POST /:id/ack`: visible AND requiresAck AND audience member → upsert `{readAt ?? now, acknowledgedAt ?? now}` (idempotent; keep the first ack time). Non-member → 404. `requiresAck=false` → 409 or VALIDATION_ERROR. Display with `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| FR-21 | API / CFG / UI | `GET /api/announcements?courseId=` → `assertCanViewCourse` then the feed query additionally filtered to `audiences some {type: COURSE, refId: courseId}`. The user must still be in the audience (a parent-only course announcement isn't shown to the course's students). Course tab page `/courses/[id]/announcements`. |\n| FR-22 | SVC / UI | Parent feed only: for each item, find matching audience rows and map them back to the children whose keys matched → `forChildren: [{id, firstName}]`. This falls out of the key-set design if keys are tracked per child (`Map<refKey, childIds>`). |\n| FR-23 | API / UI | `GET /api/announcements/manage`: no visibility filter. TEACHER `authorId = me`, ADMIN all. Reach = resolved recipient count (**expensive per row**: compute for the current page only; or snapshot `recipientCount` at publish and recompute live only on stats). Read % = `count(reads readAt not null) / reach`; ack % similar. Recommendation: resolve audiences per page row (≤ pageSize calls); keep it simple, a ponytail note for a snapshot later. |\n| FR-24 | API / UI | `GET /:id/stats`: author or ADMIN, else 404. Recipients = `resolveAudienceUserIds` (live) LEFT JOIN reads. Filters `?filter=unread\\|unacked`. `?format=csv` → `toCsv`, `Content-Disposition` attachment. Percentages over the live recipient set (AC-5: 30/50 = 60%). Readers who later left the audience are not counted. |\n| FR-25 | API / NOTIF / DM | `POST /:id/remind`: author or ADMIN. requiresAck must be true and the announcement visible. Atomic claim: `updateMany({where:{id, OR:[{lastRemindedAt:null},{lastRemindedAt:{lte: now-24h}}]}, data:{lastRemindedAt: now}})`. `count 0` → **429 RATE_LIMITED** (decision, B12). Then notify `announcement.reminder` to recipients − acknowledged. Returns `{notified: n}` (AC-5: 20). |\n| FR-26 | CFG / NOTIF | Add the types to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` (B9 conflict). roles: ALL. reminder: COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true (an ack is being chased). |\n| FR-27 | JOB / NOTIF | One `claimAndNotifyPublished(id, now)` helper: `updateMany({where:{id, notifiedAt:null, <visible>}, data:{notifiedAt: now, status: PUBLISHED}})`. If count = 1 → resolve recipients → notify. Called by publish-now (after the tx commits) and by `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` (batch 200, B11). Hook it into the dispatch route in its own try/catch. |\n| FR-28 | NOTIF | Email data: `{title, body: markdownToPlainText(body).slice(0,300), ctaLabel:'Read announcement', ctaUrl}`. Check GenericNotificationData's field names when designing. |\n| FR-29 | SVC | Follows from the notifiedAt claim: PATCH never clears notifiedAt. Also a draft → PATCH publish of an already-notified row (an archived-then-edited one) must not resend. |\n| FR-30 | FILE / AUTH | `announcementResolver(user, file)`: load the announcement by `file.contextId`. If `isPublic && visible` → true (including null user). If `!user` → false. If ADMIN or author → true. If visible && isUserInAudience → true. Else false. Register it in `registerBuiltInContexts` (B8). |\n| FR-31 | API / CFG | `getPublicNews({page})` in announcements-service: `isPublic && visibleWhere(now)`, a minimal DTO (no author email, no audience). Route `src/app/api/public/news/route.ts`. Add `'/api/public/news'` (exact match) to PUBLIC_API_PATHS. Consider `rateLimit` by IP since it is unauthenticated (cheap; the helper exists). |\n| FR-32 | CFG / UI / API | Nav entry for ALL_ROLES + the badge (B17). `GET /api/announcements/unread-count` = `count(visibleWhere ∧ audience keys ∧ no read row)`. It is polled every 30 s by every user, so it must be the same indexed query as the feed (NFR-2). |\n| FR-33 | UI | Conditional button on the feed page by role. |\n| FR-34 | API | Routes under `src/app/api/announcements/` (+`[id]/`, `[id]/archive`, `[id]/ack`, `[id]/stats`, `[id]/remind`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`, `manage`) + `src/app/api/public/news`. Note that static segments (`manage`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`) coexist with `[id]`; Next resolves static first, so that is fine. All use `withHandler` + Zod `parseBody`/`parseQuery`. |\n| FR-35 | SEED | 6 announcements, idempotent, with skip-if-missing for Grade 7 (exists), MATH-7A and the parent link (B20). The scheduled one is `publishAt = now + 2 days`, so `notifiedAt` stays null and the first real cron after that sends it. The welcome and staff-meeting seeds are already published: set `notifiedAt = now` so the seed never triggers a notification storm. The expired one has `expiresAt` in the past. |\n| FR-36 | XC | `src/server/announcements/{announcements-service.ts, audience.ts}` + (from FR-27) a `maintenance.ts` following the quiz precedent, or the function lives in the service. |\n| NFR-1 | UI / XC | MUI only. Confirm archive/remind with ConfirmDialog; toasts via useToast; pickers via Autocomplete; DateTimePicker for publishAt/expiresAt; the badge via MUI Badge; the \"Unread\" dot as a Badge/Box with visually hidden text. Every component looked up through mui-mcp (the mui-mcp server is listed in this session). `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |\n| NFR-2 | perf / DM | Feed = key-set OR join on `AnnouncementAudience(type, refId)` + `Announcement(status, publishAt)` indexes. Never `resolveAudienceUserIds` on the read path. Parent with 3 children: keys come from about 3 queries over 3 children. Verify with a seeded 2,000-row integration timing test (optional; mark as non-gating if CI is noisy). |\n| NFR-3 | AUTH | `requireUser`/`requireRole` in every handler and server page; FR-10 checks in the service (not only the route). AC-3 is an integration test. |\n| NFR-4 | XC | The body is rendered only via MarkdownView. Excerpt/email text = plain text (B16), never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Titles are plain strings. |\n| NFR-5 | UI | The unread dot has a visually-hidden \"Unread\" label (MUI `visuallyHidden` from `@mui/utils`, which ships with MUI). |\n| NFR-6 | AUTH | 404 for non-members on detail/ack/stats (not 403, to avoid existence leaks; stats → 404 for non-author non-admin). Files → the resolver denies (the files route maps that). Scheduled/expired → hidden from feeds and from non-author, non-admin detail. |\n| NFR-7 | XC | DB columns are UTC `DateTime`. The composer converts school-tz local → UTC on the server (or the client sends ISO with the tz applied). Displays use `formatInSchoolTz(getSchoolTimezone())`. |\n| NFR-8 | XC | Reuse list: notify, audit, registerFileAccess/attachFiles, toCsv, MarkdownEditor/View, FileUpload/FileList, DataTable, UserPicker (likely unused: pickers are entity pickers, not users), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, getSchoolTimezone, formatInSchoolTz, withHandler/parse*, assertCanViewCourse. |\n| NFR-9 | scope | No comments, reactions, i18n or SMS, and no public website pages. Just the service + the `/api/public/news` route. |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | Unit: audience matching per type × flag (pure key-set matcher, so no DB is needed), `assertCanTarget` rules, markdownToPlainText. Integration: an agreement property test over every seed user × every seed announcement audience; publishDueAnnouncements run twice / concurrently → one notification set; AC-3 403; AC-5 reminder 20 + 429. E2E: admin composes with ack → parent reads + acks → admin stats. The fixture creates the 6A child + Pat link (§4 A5). |\n| NFR-11 | XC | `logger` in all new server code, including the maintenance hook. |\n\n## 3. Risks and conflicts for arch-design-system\n\n| # | Risk / conflict | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1 | **Two audience code paths must agree** (FR-7, NFR-10). | Single source of rules: the `UserAudienceKeys` builder + a pure `matchesAudience(audience, keys)` + `audienceWhere(keys)`. `resolveAudienceUserIds` is written separately (set expansion) but tested against the matcher for every seed user. |\n| R2 | **FR-26 per-instance `mandatoryInApp`** isn't expressible in the static registry (B9). | Two type keys (`announcement.published`, `announcement.published_ack`), or accept a static `true`. Design picks one and records it as an ADR. |\n| R3 | **FR-1 \"exactly as specified\" vs. the needed additions** (`lastRemindedAt`, indexes, possibly `publishedAt`). | Add them as explicitly flagged additions; intake already pre-approved `lastRemindedAt`. |\n| R4 | **Feed ordering by \"newest\"** when publishAt is null for publish-now. | Set `publishAt = now` on publish-now so one column orders everything. |\n| R5 | **Status column vs. read-time visibility** (FR-16). | Visibility is computed from `publishAt`. The maintenance claim also flips SCHEDULED→PUBLISHED for the manage view. The UI should derive the display status with the same predicate, so it is correct between cron ticks. |\n| R6 | **Manage-view reach** (FR-23) means resolving N audiences per page. | Per-page live resolve (pageSize ≤ 50); `ponytail:` note for a `recipientCount` snapshot later. |\n| R7 | **Notification fan-out** on SCHOOL announcements (thousands of userIds in one notify). | Chunk userIds (e.g. 1,000) when calling notify. The notifiedAt claim happens before the send, so a crash mid-send loses the remainder rather than double-sending. That matches the existing quiz-release semantics; note it. |\n| R8 | **Teacher PATCH re-validation** (FR-10 on PATCH). | Run `assertCanTarget` on the *resulting* audience set whenever audiences or isPublic are present in the PATCH. |\n| R9 | **Orphan purge vs. drafts** (B7). | Attach files on every save, including drafts. |\n| R10 | **Public endpoint abuse** (FR-31). | Paginate with the max pageSize clamp from `parsePagination`, and optionally use `rateLimit` by IP. |\n| R11 | **Stats for audience changes after publish** (FR-29). | Stats use the live audience. Reads by users no longer in the audience are excluded from the percentages. Document this. |\n\n## 4. Assumptions carried from intake (must surface in system-design.md Overview)\n\n| # | Assumption | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| A1 | FR-5 section members = current academic-year SectionMember rows. | Members of the section row itself (a section belongs to one year). Teachers may only target current-year sections via the pickers. |\n| A2 | FR-15 drafts may have zero recipients. | Refused only on publish/schedule. |\n| A3 | Parent expansion uses linked parents of matching students; the ACTIVE filter applies to each final user. | A parent of an archived student is **not** reached through that student. Recommendation: only ACTIVE students expand to parents, and the matcher does the same. |\n| A4 | FR-17: overflow pins (>3) fall into newest-first. | Yes. |\n| A5 | AC-8: the test fixture creates Pat's 6A child + link if the seed lacks them. | Yes; the seed itself stays skip-if-missing. |\n| A6 | Archived courses (`Course.archivedAt`) in audience resolution. | Exclude archived courses from the teacher branches of GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION. Not stated in the PRD; flag it. |\n| A7 | FR-12: archive is terminal for authors; admins may still edit. | Yes. |\n| A8 | FR-25: 429 RATE_LIMITED + `lastRemindedAt` column. | Decided here (architect owns it per intake). |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":113,"newStart":1,"newLines":117,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-11","+# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-12"," "," Written by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards (SCH-011). It has 42 FRs and 13 NFRs (55 requirements) at 95% confidence.","-`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions (FR-6, FR-7, FR-13, FR-27/33, NFR-10, FR-3 no-term) are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T18:00:00Z), PRD-12 Announcements & News. It has 36 FRs and 11 NFRs (47 requirements) at 94% confidence.","+`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward."," ","-> As of this writing the other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **leftovers from earlier tickets**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-11 input.","+> All other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **SH-11 leftovers**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-12 input."," "," ## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk"," ","-| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-11 |","+| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-12 |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| B1 | **`getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` already exists.** It is labelled \"PRD-11 export\". It loads GRADED attempts, applies `applyScoringPolicy(quiz.scoringPolicy, …)`, and returns `{score, maxScore, percent, attemptsCounted, isPractice}` (fixed2 strings) or null. | src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts L355-372 | **This corrects intake** (B-finding 5 and the FR-7 assumption). FR-7 calls it directly, with no new helper. It does **not** check `resultsVisible`, so the sync caller must gate on that (NFR-5). The batch path (FR-8 backfill, NFR-3) should run `applyScoringPolicy` in memory over attempts it has already loaded, rather than calling this per student. |","-| B2 | `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` covers IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE (`now >= availableUntil`) / MANUAL (`resultsReleasedAt != null`). | src/server/quiz/grading.ts L94 | FR-7 / NFR-5 gate. AFTER_CLOSE depends on time, so a GRADED attempt is not syncable until close. See B4. |","-| B3 | Every quiz attempt status change goes through `recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)`. It is called from `submitAttempt` (L123, which includes auto-submit), `gradeAnswerManually` (L338) and `regradeQuiz` (quiz-service L435). | attempt-service.ts L73-81 | FR-7 hook. After each caller commits, call `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`, which no-ops unless GRADED + visible + !isPractice. Making this one function the only quiz sync entry point covers all three callers. |","-| B4 | Results become visible through `releaseResults` (MANUAL, quiz-service L464) and `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased` (AFTER_CLOSE). The latter claims `resultsReleasedAt` with `updateMany` on each maintenance tick. | quiz-service.ts L464; quiz/maintenance.ts L27-40 | FR-7 also needs a **bulk** `syncQuizGrades(quizId)` in both places. Otherwise AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL quizzes never reach the gradebook. The maintenance claim is already idempotent, so put the sync after `count === 1`. |","-| B5 | Quiz lifecycle: `createQuiz`, `updateQuiz` (DRAFT→PUBLISHED and PUBLISHED→CLOSED via guarded `updateMany`, L304-305), `deleteQuiz` (hard delete, L317). Quizzes have **no archive**. | quiz-service.ts L259-317 | FR-3: upsert the item on →PUBLISHED. FR-4: delete the item on deleteQuiz. CLOSED is **not** unpublish, so the item stays visible. Settings edits to a published quiz (title, availableUntil, categoryId, max) re-upsert the item. |","-| B6 | Assignment lifecycle: `createAssignment` / `updateAssignment` (status DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED); `publishOnce` (cron, makes SCHEDULED visible once `availableFrom` passes); `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` (hard delete in a tx, or sets `archivedAt` when submissions exist, L479-492). `isAssignmentVisible` = !archivedAt && published-or-scheduled-reached. | assignments-service.ts L67-74, L292-330, L437-492 | FR-3/FR-4: compute GradeItem.isVisible from `isAssignmentVisible`. Upsert on create/update/publishOnce, set isVisible=false on archive, delete inside the delete tx. **FR-24's teacher hide toggle conflicts with this** (see §3 R2). |","-| B7 | Return paths: `gradeSubmission` (`returning = input.return && status !== 'RETURNED'`; it also re-grades an already-RETURNED submission), `bulkReturn`, and `gradeOffline` (`input.return`). | assignments-service.ts ~L696-800 | FR-5: sync when the submission **is RETURNED after the write**, not only on the transition. Re-grading a returned submission must update Grade.score, and grade-without-return must not sync (AC-3). Use one `syncSubmissionGrade(submissionId)` from all three. |","-| B8 | `setExemption(…, exempt)` upserts or deletes `GradeExemption` (L818/L824) and audits `assignment.exempt` / `assignment.unexempt`. | assignments-service.ts L815-838 | FR-6: call `syncSubmissionGrade` (or a by-(assignment, student) variant) after both branches. Unexempt re-derives the score from a RETURNED submission, else null. |","-| B9 | GradeItem has a polymorphic `source + sourceId` with **no FK**. Assignment and Quiz deletes will not cascade. | FR-1 model spec | FR-4: delete the GradeItem explicitly inside the same transaction as the source delete (and in `deleteQuiz`, which today runs outside a tx). Grade → GradeItem should be `onDelete: Cascade`. |","-| B10 | `Term` has no `isCurrent`. It has `academicYearId`, `startDate`/`endDate` as `@db.Date`, `order`. `AcademicYear.isCurrent` exists. `Course.academicYearId` exists. | schema.prisma L240-252, Course ~L415 | FR-3 term placement: pick the term of **the course's academic year** whose `[startDate, endDate]` contains dueAt, comparing dates in the school timezone (NFR-10). The fallback \"current term\" is the term of that year containing today (tz), else skip + `logger.warn`. Put this in one pure helper `termFor(date, terms, tz)`. |","-| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from assignments-service. `dec` / `fixed2` / `Decimal` come from grading-math (isomorphic). `percentOf` (1 dp half-up) is in quiz/grading.ts. | assignments-service.ts L57; grading-math.ts L7-15; grading.ts L133 | NFR-1/NFR-10/FR-13 reuse these. `percentOf` rounds to 1 dp on a single value. grade-calc must keep full-precision Decimal until the **final** rounding (FR-13), so it must not round category percents early. |","-| B12 | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` exist. `getAccessibleStudentIds` / `assertCanViewStudent` cover own student, linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`), teacher and admin, with homeroom handled there too. `src/server/quiz/access.ts` has `canManageCourse`. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts, student-access.ts | FR-39 \"manage\"/\"view\" and FR-42 reuse these. FR-37 report-card access is new: ADMIN; teachers of any course on the card or the homeroom teacher; the student or a linked parent only when PUBLISHED. Return NOT_FOUND to everyone else (AC-7). |","-| B13 | Attendance aggregation already exists: `getReport(filters)` → `StudentSummaryRow` (StatusCounts per student) using a single `groupBy(studentId, status)`. It filters by date range, grade level, section and course. | attendance-service.ts L528-582 | FR-30 attendance summary and NFR-3 batching: call `getReport({from: term.start, to: term.end, sectionId/gradeLevelId})` **once** per generate request. Do not loop per student. Rate formula: reuse whatever StatusCounts consumers use. Do not invent a new one. |","-| B14 | `SchoolSettings` singleton: name, shortName, logoUrl, timezone, address fields. Student profile: `admissionNumber`, `gradeLevel`. `Section.homeroomTeacherId`. | schema.prisma L109-113, L198-215 | FR-30 snapshot fields all come from existing models. No schema change beyond FR-1. |","-| B15 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const already contains assignment.* and quiz.* entries. `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents()` never throw. `audit()` never throws. | notifications/types.ts, notify.ts L28/L98, audit.ts L26 | FR-38: add `grade.posted` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, STUDENT+PARENT) and `report_card.published` (defaultEmail true, STUDENT+PARENT). Call them after commit. NFR-4 audit actions: `grade.update`, `termOverride.upsert`, `reportCard.unpublish` (plus `reportCard.publish` and `gradingScale.*` as nice-to-haves). |","-| B16 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are static arrays. `studentTabs` notes \"No tab bar renders studentTabs yet\". `navigation` is a flat array with `roles` and an optional `group: 'Administration'`. | src/config/*.ts | FR-18/28: add course tabs `gradebook` (TEACHER, ADMIN) and `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT). FR-26/36: add student tabs `grades` and `report-cards`. These are reachable by URL only, the same as `assignments`. FR-27/33 + admin pages: nav entries `/grades`, `/report-cards`, `/admin/grading-scales`, `/admin/report-cards`. |","-| B17 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` are in src/server/csv.ts. Shared components: DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast (useToast), PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, DateDisplay, UserPicker, FormField, LoadingSkeleton. **No existing `@mui/x-data-grid` usage in src.** | src/server/csv.ts; src/components/ | FR-25: export on the server with `toCsv`, building the same columns as the grid. FR-18 is the first DataGrid in the codebase, so its MIT-tier API (columnGroupingModel, processRowUpdate, virtualisation, no pinning) must be looked up via mui-mcp for 9.5.0 (NFR-7/8). FR-29 table → DataTable. |","-| B18 | Scripts: `db:seed` = `tsx prisma/seed.ts`. There is no `gradebook:backfill`. The seed looks up courses by code with `findCourse([...])`. | package.json; prisma/seed.ts | FR-8: add `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`, a thin wrapper over an exported `backfillGradebook()` in src/server/gradebook/ that the seed also calls before the FR-41 data. |","-| B19 | Postgres. Migrations already hand-add raw SQL partial indexes. Prisma 5.20. | prisma/migrations/* | FR-1: one migration. It needs `@@unique([source, sourceId])` on GradeItem (sync and backfill idempotency), `@@unique([gradeItemId, studentId])` on Grade, `@@unique([courseId, termId, studentId])` on TermGradeOverride, and `@@unique([studentId, termId])` on ReportCard. These make the upserts race-safe. A one-default-scale rule can be a partial unique index `WHERE \"isDefault\"` (FR-16). |","+| B1 | The schema has no Announcement* models or enums. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1: add a new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_announcements`). Add back-relations on `User` (authored, reads) and `FileObject` (attachments, and the cover image if it is an FK). |","+| B2 | `User.status` is `ACTIVE/INVITED/DISABLED/ARCHIVED` and `archivedAt` is a separate column. `notify()` filters `status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED]`, so it **includes INVITED**. | schema L17, L59; notify.ts L43 | FR-3 is stricter: audience = `status: ACTIVE, archivedAt: null`. Pass the resolved ids to `notify()`, which then filters on its own. Don't rely on notify's filter. |","+| B3 | `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId` (required). `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` has `@@index([studentId])` and a `@@unique([parentId, studentId])`. | schema L106, L144 | FR-4/5/6 parent expansion: join through the link. Parent → children is covered by the unique index's leading `parentId`. |","+| B4 | `Section(academicYearId, gradeLevelId, homeroomTeacherId?)`. `SectionMember(studentId, academicYearId)` is unique on `(studentId, academicYearId)`, and its academicYearId is denormalised. **There is no index on `sectionId`.** | schema L377-411 | FR-5: \"members\" = SectionMember rows where `academicYearId` = the section's year (that is already true per row, so filtering by `sectionId` is enough). A section belongs to one year, so the \"current year\" question reduces to \"is the section in the current year\". See §4 A1. |","+| B5 | `Course(academicYearId, sectionId?, teacherId, coTeacherIds String[], archivedAt?)`. `coTeacherIds` is queried with `has`. `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. | schema L414-447 | FR-4/5/6/10 teacher branches. `has` isn't indexable without a GIN index. The rows involved are small (only a user's own courses), so this is fine for NFR-2. Decide whether archived courses' teachers count (§4 A6). |","+| B6 | `Enrollment.status` ACTIVE/DROPPED, with `@@index([studentId, status])` and `@@unique([courseId, studentId])`. | schema L371, L450 | FR-6 student branch. Both directions are indexed. |","+| B7 | `FileObject(context, contextId)` is indexed. Uploads are created with `contextId: null`. `attachFiles(tx, context, contextId, ids)` / detach live in files-service. **`purgeOrphanFiles` deletes `contextId: null` files after 24 h.** | files-service.ts L212-244; files/purge.ts | FR-13/FR-30: attach the cover image and attachments with `context='announcement'`, `contextId=announcement.id` inside the create/update tx. A cover that is uploaded but never attached (e.g. an abandoned draft) is purged, which is correct. **A draft must still attach its files**, or they vanish after 24 h. |","+| B8 | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)`. Resolvers receive `null` for anonymous callers. Built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (contexts.ts). Resolver errors deny. `/api/files/` is already in PUBLIC_API_PATHS. | files/access.ts; contexts.ts; public-routes.ts | FR-30: add `register('announcement', announcementResolver)` to `registerBuiltInContexts` so it is guaranteed loaded, rather than as a side-effect import. Anonymous downloads already route through, so no public-route change is needed for files. |","+| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). `COMMUNICATION` exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a **static boolean per type**. | notifications/types.ts | **FR-26 conflict**: \"mandatoryInApp true when requiresAck\" can't be expressed per instance. Options: (a) two types, `announcement.published` (mandatoryInApp false) and `announcement.published_ack` (true); or (b) one type with `mandatoryInApp: true`. Recommend (a) as the smallest faithful mapping. **arch-design-system decides.** |","+| B10 | `notify({type, userIds, title, body, link, email:{template:'generic-notification', data}})` dedupes, never throws, and is called after commit. It truncates body to BODY_MAX and drops non-relative links. | notify.ts L8-60 | FR-27/28: call it after the notifiedAt claim commits. `link: /announcements/${id}`. Large audiences (a SCHOOL announcement can be thousands of users) go through one `findMany` + `createMany`. That's acceptable, but chunk the userIds if notify's `in` lists get large. |","+| B11 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` runs each pass in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take: BATCH)` → `updateMany({where:{id, claimCol: null}})` → act only if `count === 1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts L28-43 | FR-27: `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` copies this pattern exactly: `where status SCHEDULED, publishAt <= now, notifiedAt null`, claim `notifiedAt`. Publish-now uses the same claim helper, so one code path sends. |","+| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes both `RATE_LIMITED` (429) and `CONFLICT` (409). `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` exist. | src/server/http.ts | FR-34 handler conventions. FR-25: recommend **429 RATE_LIMITED** with `details.retryAfter` (ISO). It is semantically a time-based throttle, and intake suggested the same. |","+| B13 | `audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request})` never throws. The action convention is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|archive\\|delete`. | src/server/audit.ts | FR-12: `announcement.update` / `announcement.archive` when an admin acts on another author's row. Also audit the author's own archive (cheap; optional). |","+| B14 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` (formula-injection safe). | src/server/csv.ts | FR-24 `?format=csv`. |","+| B15 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from **assignments-service.ts**, not a shared module. `formatInSchoolTz` is in src/lib/dates.ts. | assignments-service.ts L64; src/lib/dates.ts L7 | NFR-7: reuse both. Importing `getSchoolTimezone` from assignments-service is the existing precedent (contexts.ts already imports from it). Don't duplicate it. |","+| B16 | `MarkdownView` = react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema) rendering to MUI components. **There is no Markdown→plain-text helper** in the codebase. | src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx | FR-18 (200-char excerpt) and FR-28 (300-char email body) need a new small pure `markdownToPlainText(md)` (e.g. in `src/lib/markdown-text.ts`). Plain text rendered by React/the email template is escaped, so NFR-4 is met as long as the excerpt is never rendered as HTML/Markdown. Prefer a regex strip over a new dependency (remark is already installed transitively if an AST approach is preferred). |","+| B17 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `navigation` is a static array. `NotificationBell` polls `/api/notifications/unread-count` every 30 s, gated by visibility, and shows an MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L42-62 | FR-32: add an optional `badge?: 'announcements-unread'` key (or a badge endpoint string) to NavItem. The sidebar renders a polled Badge for items that have one. Reuse the bell's polling hook shape. |","+| B18 | `courseTabs` is a static array with `roles`. | src/config/course-tabs.ts | FR-21: `{ key: 'announcements', label: 'Announcements', href: id => /courses/${id}/announcements, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. |","+| B19 | `assertCanViewCourse` covers ADMIN, TEACHER (teacher or co-teacher only, **not homeroom**), STUDENT (enrollment) and PARENT (child enrolled). `canSeeDrafts` checks the course-manager test. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts L25+ | FR-21 gate: `assertCanViewCourse` and then the normal audience filter. FR-10 \"courses they manage\" = the same `teacherId \\|\\| coTeacherIds.includes` test, so reuse it rather than re-deriving. |","+| B20 | Seed: Tom/Sam/Pat by email. Courses are looked up with `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` and skipped if missing. The Grade 7 GradeLevel row **is** seeded. No 7A/7B/6A sections and no `ParentStudentLink` rows are created by the seed (they come from other scripts/fixtures, if at all). | prisma/seed.ts L18-22, L109-115, L275-305 | FR-35: grade/course/section-targeted seeds skip when their target is missing, using the same `logger.info`/`console.log` style. School-wide, staff and public seeds always run. Idempotency: upsert by a stable title + author, or check for existence first. |","+| B21 | Test layout: `tests/unit`, `tests/integration/<feature>/`, `tests/e2e/*.spec.ts` + `helpers/`. | tests/ | NFR-10: `tests/unit/announcements/*`, `tests/integration/announcements/*`, `tests/e2e/announcements.spec.ts`. |","+| B22 | `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0 is installed (`@mui/x-data-grid` too). | package.json | FR-13 publishAt/expiresAt: DateTimePicker. FR-23/24 tables: the existing `DataTable` component. Look up via mui-mcp per NFR-1. |"," "," ## 2. Requirement → architectural concern"," ","-Concern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **SYNC** source→gradebook sync hook · **CALC** pure calculation · **API** REST endpoint · **UI** page/component · **AUTH** access boundary · **JOB** script/batch · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **CFG** config registry.","+Legend for **Concern**: DM = data model / migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance/cron, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule."," "," | Req | Concern | Notes |"," |---|---|---|","-| FR-1 | DM | New enums + 6 models in one `prisma migrate` migration. Use the unique keys from B19. Grade: `score Decimal?`, `excused`, `missing`, `comment`, `gradedById`, `gradedAt`. ReportCard: `status`, `snapshot Json`, `homeroomComment`, `principalComment`, `publishedAt`, `publishedById`. |","-| FR-2 | DM, UI | Nullable `Course.gradingScaleId`, `Assignment.categoryId` and `Quiz.categoryId` with `onDelete: SetNull`. Category deletion via FR-40 must not delete sources. Add one `Select` to the existing assignment and quiz editors, plus the validator fields in assignments.ts / quiz.ts (optional and nullable). Don't change existing behaviour. |","-| FR-3 | SYNC | `upsertGradeItemFromAssignment(id)` / `…FromQuiz(id)` keyed on (source, sourceId). Skip practice quizzes. Term placement via `termFor` (B10). Callers per B5/B6. Keep the GradeItem's term stable after first creation unless the date changes, so grades don't jump terms on unrelated edits. |","-| FR-4 | SYNC | Archive sets isVisible=false. Delete removes the GradeItem in the same tx (B9). Quiz has no archive or unpublish. A practice-toggle after publish should delete or hide the item. |","-| FR-5 | SYNC | `syncSubmissionGrade` from 3 return paths (B7). It writes only when RETURNED. Score = `finalScore`. |","-| FR-6 | SYNC | From `setExemption` (B8). Exemption wins over the score: excused=true and the score is kept. |","-| FR-7 | SYNC | Per-attempt `syncQuizGrade` after `recomputeAttempt` callers (B3). Bulk `syncQuizGrades` on release and AFTER_CLOSE (B4). Score scaled: `score/maxScore × GradeItem.maxPoints`, Decimal. |","-| FR-8 | JOB | `backfillGradebook()`: batch load per course, reuse the same upsert builders as live sync (one code path), idempotent through the unique keys. npm script + seed call (B18). |","-| FR-9 | API, AUTH | The service rejects score/excused/missing edits on non-MANUAL items (`AppError('FORBIDDEN'/'VALIDATION_ERROR')`). Comment stays editable. The grid marks those columns non-editable. |","-| FR-10 | CALC | `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts`: pure, Decimal-only, no Prisma client import (types only). Input: items, grades, categories, scale, override, `now`. Counted = visible ∧ ¬excused ∧ (score≠null ∨ (missing ∧ now>dueAt)). |","-| FR-11 | CALC | Drop lowest by item **percentage**, keeping ≥1. Ties are dropped deterministically (by dueAt, then id). |","-| FR-12 | CALC | Implicit \"Uncategorised\" bucket. What weight does it get? The PRD is silent, so see §3 R3. No categories gives a points total. |","-| FR-13 | CALC | `toDecimalPlaces(1, ROUND_HALF_UP)` only at the end. Bands are sorted descending, first `percent >= minPercent`. |","-| FR-14 | CALC | The override is applied after computing. A letter-only override keeps the computed percent. A percent-only override probably re-derives the letter from the scale (unstated, so flag it). |","-| FR-15 | CALC, UI | Golden unit test (78.0 C+). The gradebook and student Grades **must call the same function**, with no client-side recomputation. |","-| FR-16 | API, UI, DM | `/admin/grading-scales` (ADMIN). Band validation lives in a Zod refinement shared by client and server. \"Exactly one default\" uses a tx that clears others + a partial unique index. Deleting a scale in use is either blocked or falls back to the default; decide this. |","-| FR-17 | UI, API | Course settings page. The live weight sum is client-side, with the 100 check repeated server-side in FR-40. Decimal weights: compare with `dec(sum).eq(100)`, not floats. |","-| FR-18 | UI, API, CALC | First DataGrid. The server returns one denormalised payload `{students, items, categories, grades, computed}` for (course, term) in a fixed number of queries (NFR-2). Columns are built client-side from it. Sort by last name on the server. |","-| FR-19 | UI | Pure cell renderer. \"Late\" needs `Submission.isLate`, so the gradebook payload must carry the source submission's isLate. |","-| FR-20 | UI, API | `processRowUpdate` → PATCH a single grade. E/M/Delete need a custom edit cell / `onCellKeyDown` (check mui-mcp). Optimistic update with per-cell error. Audited (NFR-4). Triggers `grade.posted` (FR-38). |","-| FR-21 | UI | The cell click opens a link to the submission grading page or the quiz attempt. The payload needs `submissionId` / `attemptId` per synced grade. |","-| FR-22 | API, UI | POST manual item. Validate that the term belongs to the course's academic year and the category belongs to the course. |","-| FR-23 | API, UI, AUD | PUT override (upsert). Comment ≤1000 chars. Audit with old/new values. |","-| FR-24 | API, UI | Toggle visibility (see R2). Bulk-missing allowed only if `now > dueAt` and only for ungraded rows. Stats come from the computed payload, client-side, over counted scores. |","-| FR-25 | API | Server CSV via `toCsv`, using the same row builder as the grid. \"As displayed\" means EX/M/— markers and the term letter. |","-| FR-26 | UI, API, CFG | Student tab → `GET /api/students/:id/grades?termId`. The colour thresholds come from a single helper reused by FR-27/28. |","-| FR-27 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/grades` reuses the FR-26 component. Parent child selector from `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Nav entry. |","-| FR-28 | UI, CFG | Course tab `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT): same endpoint filtered by courseId. |","-| FR-29 | UI, API | `/admin/report-cards`: list query joins students (grade level, section filters) with ReportCard status for the term. Missing-data warnings are computed in batch (ungraded counted-eligible items, missing TermGradeOverride.comment per course). |","-| FR-30 | JOB, API | `generate`: batch load (NFR-3), compute in memory, write the snapshot JSON (versioned shape, e.g. `snapshot.v = 1`). Teacher comment = `TermGradeOverride.comment`. Attendance via B13. |","-| FR-31 | JOB, DM | `upsert` with `where status = DRAFT` semantics: createMany for new cards, `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})` for existing ones, never touching PUBLISHED. Grade-edit services never import report-cards code. |","-| FR-32 | API, UI, AUTH | PATCH: field-level role check (homeroomComment: homeroom teacher of the student's section or ADMIN; principalComment: ADMIN). Edits are allowed only while DRAFT (implied, so flag it). |","-| FR-33 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/report-cards` (TEACHER): drafts for sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Nav entry. |","-| FR-34 | API, NOTIF, AUD | Publish (one or bulk) with a guarded `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})`, then notify after commit. Unpublish: ADMIN, reason required, audit, back to DRAFT. |","-| FR-35 | UI | `/report-cards/[id]/print` renders from the **snapshot only**. `@media print` via MUI `GlobalStyles`, hiding the sidebar. Bulk print: one page renders N cards with `break-after: page`. |","-| FR-36 | UI, CFG, API | Student tab \"Report cards\". The list endpoint filters to PUBLISHED for student/parent (NFR-5). |","-| FR-37 | AUTH | New `assertCanViewReportCard`. Non-entitled users get NOT_FOUND, so existence isn't leaked. |","-| FR-38 | NOTIF | Register 2 types (B15). `grade.posted`: only for MANUAL items, only when a score is first entered or changed (one per student per item, so an idempotency marker such as `Grade.notifiedAt` is needed; flag it). |","-| FR-39 | API, AUTH | Thin route handlers using `withHandler`, Zod in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, and services in `src/server/gradebook/` + `src/server/report-cards/`. |","-| FR-40 | API | Replace-all in a tx: delete missing ids (sources → SetNull), upsert the rest. Weights total 100 (Decimal). |","-| FR-41 | JOB | Seed: scale, 7A categories, 'Oral presentation' + grades, draft S1 cards for 7A with MATH/ENG override comments. Run after `backfillGradebook()`. |","-| FR-42 | API, AUTH | Student serializer: visible items only. Grade rows only exist for released scores (sync gating), so the risk is mainly hidden items and MANUAL items with isVisible=false. Still filter explicitly. |","-| NFR-1 | CALC | Decimal throughout. Unit matrix in `grade-calc.test.ts`. |","-| NFR-2 | API | Gradebook: ~5 queries (enrollments, items, grades, categories, scale + override), all indexed by (courseId, termId). The grid virtualises. |","-| NFR-3 | JOB | Generation: per term, `findMany` items/grades/overrides/categories for all courses in scope with `in` filters, then group in memory. One attendance `groupBy`. Chunk the writes. |","-| NFR-4 | AUD | Old/new values in metadata for grade.update, termOverride.upsert and reportCard.unpublish. |","-| NFR-5 | AUTH | Enforced in 3 layers: sync gating (B2/B7), student serializer (FR-42), report-card guard (FR-37). Integration tests for each. |","-| NFR-6 | AUTH | Every route uses requireUser/requireRole + an entity check (B12). Server pages check too, not just the API. |","-| NFR-7 | UI | MUI only, with mui-mcp lookup. Toast via useToast, confirm via Dialog/ConfirmDialog. |","-| NFR-8 | UI | DataGrid MIT: no `pinnedColumns` and no `@mui/x-data-grid-pro`. Sticky header is the default. |","-| NFR-9 | all | New code only in src/server/gradebook/ and src/server/report-cards/. Hooks into existing services are one-line calls. Use `logger`, no console.log. |","-| NFR-10 | CALC, SYNC | Past-due uses an instant comparison (`now > dueAt`). Term containment uses a tz date comparison (B10). |","-| NFR-11 | UI | A4 portrait `@page` rule. Long course lists may need a 2nd page, with table rows set to `break-inside: avoid`. |","-| NFR-12 | all | Tests per the intake list. Integration tests hit the real sync hooks (B3/B4/B7). |","-| NFR-13 | — | Scope guard: store `gpa`, never compute it. No rank or transcript. |","+| FR-1 | DM | 2 enums, 4 models, 1 migration. AnnouncementRead has a composite PK `(announcementId, userId)`. **Needed beyond the PRD's model** (flag as deliberate additions): `Announcement.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` (FR-25), `notifiedAt DateTime?` (FR-27, likely already in the spec since FR-27 names it), and indexes `AnnouncementAudience @@index([type, refId])` and `Announcement @@index([status, publishAt])` (NFR-2). AnnouncementAudience columns implied by FR-2.1: `type`, `refId?` (null for SCHOOL/STAFF), `includeStudents/Parents/Teachers` booleans. Cascade deletes from Announcement to its children. |","+| FR-2 | XC / validation | `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts`, isomorphic Zod schema, shared by the composer and the handlers. Also validate: `expiresAt > publishAt` when both are set; ROLE refId ∈ Role enum; refId required unless SCHOOL/STAFF; at least one include flag true for GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION/COURSE. |","+| FR-3 | SVC | `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`. `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` returns a set union over the rows, all filtered to `ACTIVE && archivedAt null`. SCHOOL = all, STAFF = role ∈ {ADMIN, TEACHER}, ROLE = role = refId. Do the active filter **once** at the end, including on parents. |","+| FR-4 | SVC | GRADE_LEVEL: students via `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`; parents via ParentStudentLink of **those students** (before the active filter on the students? see §4 A3); teachers = `teacherId` ∪ `coTeacherIds` of courses where `section.gradeLevelId = refId AND academicYear.isCurrent`. |","+| FR-5 | SVC | SECTION: SectionMember(sectionId) students, their parents, `homeroomTeacherId` plus the teachers/co-teachers of `Course.sectionId = refId`. \"Current year\" is implicit (§4 A1). |","+| FR-6 | SVC | COURSE: `Enrollment(courseId, status ACTIVE)` students, their parents, teacher plus coTeachers. |","+| FR-7 | SVC / perf | `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`. **Key design point**: compute a per-user *membership key set* once (≤ ~4 small queries): role; own/children's gradeLevelIds; own/children's sectionIds (current year); own/children's ACTIVE courseIds; for teachers, managed courseIds + their sectionIds/gradeLevelIds + homeroom sectionIds. Then audience matching is a pure function over `(audience, keys)`. The same key set also becomes a Prisma `where` (an OR of `{type, refId in keys[type], include<Flag>: true}`) for the feed (FR-17/NFR-2). This puts the rules in one place (intake key risk), and `resolveAudienceUserIds` is the inverse expansion. The agreement test (NFR-10) checks both. For a parent the flag is `includeParents`, and the keys come from the children. |","+| FR-8 | SVC / XC | audience.ts must not import Announcement types. Its input is `{type, refId, includeStudents, includeParents, includeTeachers}[]`, so PRD-14 can reuse it. Export the `AudienceType` enum from Prisma. |","+| FR-9 | AUTH | ADMIN: any type, `isPublic` allowed. |","+| FR-10 | AUTH | `assertCanTarget(user, audiences, isPublic)` in the service, called by **both** create and update (PATCH can change the audience). TEACHER: COURSE where they manage the course (B19); SECTION where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Everything else, and `isPublic=true`, → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')` 403. On PATCH by a teacher, also re-check when `isPublic` is omitted but already true (it can't be, since only admins set it). |","+| FR-11 | AUTH | `requireRole('ADMIN','TEACHER')` on POST, PATCH, archive, preview-audience, manage, stats and remind. |","+| FR-12 | AUTH / audit | Edit: `authorId === user.id \\|\\| ADMIN`. Archive: same. Archive sets ARCHIVED (terminal for authors, §4 A7). Admin-on-others → `audit()`. A teacher who is no longer allowed to target the existing audience (e.g. lost co-teacher status) → PATCH fails on re-validation. That's acceptable. |","+| FR-13 | UI | Pages `/announcements/new` and `/announcements/[id]/edit` (server page + client form). Reuse MarkdownEditor, FileUpload (context 'announcement'), FileList, Autocomplete pickers per audience type (grade levels, sections, courses, roles). Teachers only see their own courses/homeroom in the pickers (UX; the server still enforces). Public toggle hidden for non-admins. Show and accept dates in the school tz (NFR-7). |","+| FR-14 | API / SVC | `POST /api/announcements/preview-audience`, body = audiences[] (same Zod schema). Run `assertCanTarget` first so the preview can't enumerate other audiences' sizes. Returns `{total, byRole:{STUDENT,PARENT,TEACHER,ADMIN}}`. Debounce in the UI. Uses `resolveAudienceUserIds` + `groupBy role` (or one count query). |","+| FR-15 | SVC | On transition to PUBLISHED/SCHEDULED (create or PATCH), resolve the count and if it is 0, `VALIDATION_ERROR`. Drafts are exempt (§4 A2). Scheduled ones are validated at schedule time, not again at publishAt; an emptied audience just notifies nobody. |","+| FR-16 | SVC / XC | **Visibility predicate in one place**: `visibleWhere(now) = { OR: [{status: PUBLISHED}, {status: SCHEDULED, publishAt: {lte: now}}], AND: [{OR: [{expiresAt: null}, {expiresAt: {gt: now}}]}] }`. Use it in the feed, detail, ack, files, public news and unread-count. Precedent: `isAssignmentVisible`/`isLessonVisible`. The status column stays SCHEDULED after publishAt (unless the maintenance run also flips it to PUBLISHED; recommend it does, in the same claim, for clean manage-view status). |","+| FR-17 | API / SVC / perf | `GET /api/announcements`: `visibleWhere(now) AND audiences: { some: audienceWhereForKeys(keys) }`. Plus `?filter=unread` (`reads: {none: {userId}}` or `readAt null`) and `?filter=ack` (`requiresAck AND no acknowledgedAt`). Ordering: up to 3 pinned first (separate `take:3` query on page 1, exclude those ids from the main list), then newest by **effective publish time** (`publishAt ?? createdAt` → store a `publishedAt`, or order by `publishAt` and set it on publish-now). Overflow pins fall into the newest list (§4 A4). Include the per-user read row via a `reads: {where:{userId}}` include. |","+| FR-18 | API / UI | The card DTO = cover fileId, title, author name + role, date, audience chips (labels need names for grade/section/course refIds, so batch-load by refId), `excerpt` (B16, 200 chars, computed server-side), attachment count (`_count`). |","+| FR-19 | API / AUTH | `GET /api/announcements/:id`: access if ADMIN, the author, or (visible AND isUserInAudience). Otherwise **404** (don't leak existence, NFR-6). Upsert AnnouncementRead `{readAt: now}` only for audience members (not for admins/authors outside the audience, since that would distort stats). Client renders the body with MarkdownView. |","+| FR-20 | API / AUTH | `POST /:id/ack`: visible AND requiresAck AND audience member → upsert `{readAt ?? now, acknowledgedAt ?? now}` (idempotent; keep the first ack time). Non-member → 404. `requiresAck=false` → 409 or VALIDATION_ERROR. Display with `formatInSchoolTz`. |","+| FR-21 | API / CFG / UI | `GET /api/announcements?courseId=` → `assertCanViewCourse` then the feed query additionally filtered to `audiences some {type: COURSE, refId: courseId}`. The user must still be in the audience (a parent-only course announcement isn't shown to the course's students). Course tab page `/courses/[id]/announcements`. |","+| FR-22 | SVC / UI | Parent feed only: for each item, find matching audience rows and map them back to the children whose keys matched → `forChildren: [{id, firstName}]`. This falls out of the key-set design if keys are tracked per child (`Map<refKey, childIds>`). |","+| FR-23 | API / UI | `GET /api/announcements/manage`: no visibility filter. TEACHER `authorId = me`, ADMIN all. Reach = resolved recipient count (**expensive per row**: compute for the current page only; or snapshot `recipientCount` at publish and recompute live only on stats). Read % = `count(reads readAt not null) / reach`; ack % similar. Recommendation: resolve audiences per page row (≤ pageSize calls); keep it simple, a ponytail note for a snapshot later. |","+| FR-24 | API / UI | `GET /:id/stats`: author or ADMIN, else 404. Recipients = `resolveAudienceUserIds` (live) LEFT JOIN reads. Filters `?filter=unread\\|unacked`. `?format=csv` → `toCsv`, `Content-Disposition` attachment. Percentages over the live recipient set (AC-5: 30/50 = 60%). Readers who later left the audience are not counted. |","+| FR-25 | API / NOTIF / DM | `POST /:id/remind`: author or ADMIN. requiresAck must be true and the announcement visible. Atomic claim: `updateMany({where:{id, OR:[{lastRemindedAt:null},{lastRemindedAt:{lte: now-24h}}]}, data:{lastRemindedAt: now}})`. `count 0` → **429 RATE_LIMITED** (decision, B12). Then notify `announcement.reminder` to recipients − acknowledged. Returns `{notified: n}` (AC-5: 20). |","+| FR-26 | CFG / NOTIF | Add the types to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` (B9 conflict). roles: ALL. reminder: COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true (an ack is being chased). |","+| FR-27 | JOB / NOTIF | One `claimAndNotifyPublished(id, now)` helper: `updateMany({where:{id, notifiedAt:null, <visible>}, data:{notifiedAt: now, status: PUBLISHED}})`. If count = 1 → resolve recipients → notify. Called by publish-now (after the tx commits) and by `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` (batch 200, B11). Hook it into the dispatch route in its own try/catch. |","+| FR-28 | NOTIF | Email data: `{title, body: markdownToPlainText(body).slice(0,300), ctaLabel:'Read announcement', ctaUrl}`. Check GenericNotificationData's field names when designing. |","+| FR-29 | SVC | Follows from the notifiedAt claim: PATCH never clears notifiedAt. Also a draft → PATCH publish of an already-notified row (an archived-then-edited one) must not resend. |","+| FR-30 | FILE / AUTH | `announcementResolver(user, file)`: load the announcement by `file.contextId`. If `isPublic && visible` → true (including null user). If `!user` → false. If ADMIN or author → true. If visible && isUserInAudience → true. Else false. Register it in `registerBuiltInContexts` (B8). |","+| FR-31 | API / CFG | `getPublicNews({page})` in announcements-service: `isPublic && visibleWhere(now)`, a minimal DTO (no author email, no audience). Route `src/app/api/public/news/route.ts`. Add `'/api/public/news'` (exact match) to PUBLIC_API_PATHS. Consider `rateLimit` by IP since it is unauthenticated (cheap; the helper exists). |","+| FR-32 | CFG / UI / API | Nav entry for ALL_ROLES + the badge (B17). `GET /api/announcements/unread-count` = `count(visibleWhere ∧ audience keys ∧ no read row)`. It is polled every 30 s by every user, so it must be the same indexed query as the feed (NFR-2). |","+| FR-33 | UI | Conditional button on the feed page by role. |","+| FR-34 | API | Routes under `src/app/api/announcements/` (+`[id]/`, `[id]/archive`, `[id]/ack`, `[id]/stats`, `[id]/remind`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`, `manage`) + `src/app/api/public/news`. Note that static segments (`manage`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`) coexist with `[id]`; Next resolves static first, so that is fine. All use `withHandler` + Zod `parseBody`/`parseQuery`. |","+| FR-35 | SEED | 6 announcements, idempotent, with skip-if-missing for Grade 7 (exists), MATH-7A and the parent link (B20). The scheduled one is `publishAt = now + 2 days`, so `notifiedAt` stays null and the first real cron after that sends it. The welcome and staff-meeting seeds are already published: set `notifiedAt = now` so the seed never triggers a notification storm. The expired one has `expiresAt` in the past. |","+| FR-36 | XC | `src/server/announcements/{announcements-service.ts, audience.ts}` + (from FR-27) a `maintenance.ts` following the quiz precedent, or the function lives in the service. |","+| NFR-1 | UI / XC | MUI only. Confirm archive/remind with ConfirmDialog; toasts via useToast; pickers via Autocomplete; DateTimePicker for publishAt/expiresAt; the badge via MUI Badge; the \"Unread\" dot as a Badge/Box with visually hidden text. Every component looked up through mui-mcp (the mui-mcp server is listed in this session). `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |","+| NFR-2 | perf / DM | Feed = key-set OR join on `AnnouncementAudience(type, refId)` + `Announcement(status, publishAt)` indexes. Never `resolveAudienceUserIds` on the read path. Parent with 3 children: keys come from about 3 queries over 3 children. Verify with a seeded 2,000-row integration timing test (optional; mark as non-gating if CI is noisy). |","+| NFR-3 | AUTH | `requireUser`/`requireRole` in every handler and server page; FR-10 checks in the service (not only the route). AC-3 is an integration test. |","+| NFR-4 | XC | The body is rendered only via MarkdownView. Excerpt/email text = plain text (B16), never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Titles are plain strings. |","+| NFR-5 | UI | The unread dot has a visually-hidden \"Unread\" label (MUI `visuallyHidden` from `@mui/utils`, which ships with MUI). |","+| NFR-6 | AUTH | 404 for non-members on detail/ack/stats (not 403, to avoid existence leaks; stats → 404 for non-author non-admin). Files → the resolver denies (the files route maps that). Scheduled/expired → hidden from feeds and from non-author, non-admin detail. |","+| NFR-7 | XC | DB columns are UTC `DateTime`. The composer converts school-tz local → UTC on the server (or the client sends ISO with the tz applied). Displays use `formatInSchoolTz(getSchoolTimezone())`. |","+| NFR-8 | XC | Reuse list: notify, audit, registerFileAccess/attachFiles, toCsv, MarkdownEditor/View, FileUpload/FileList, DataTable, UserPicker (likely unused: pickers are entity pickers, not users), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, getSchoolTimezone, formatInSchoolTz, withHandler/parse*, assertCanViewCourse. |","+| NFR-9 | scope | No comments, reactions, i18n or SMS, and no public website pages. Just the service + the `/api/public/news` route. |","+| NFR-10 | TEST | Unit: audience matching per type × flag (pure key-set matcher, so no DB is needed), `assertCanTarget` rules, markdownToPlainText. Integration: an agreement property test over every seed user × every seed announcement audience; publishDueAnnouncements run twice / concurrently → one notification set; AC-3 403; AC-5 reminder 20 + 429. E2E: admin composes with ack → parent reads + acks → admin stats. The fixture creates the 6A child + Pat link (§4 A5). |","+| NFR-11 | XC | `logger` in all new server code, including the maintenance hook. |"," ","-## 3. Risks / decisions for `arch-design-system`","+## 3. Risks and conflicts for arch-design-system"," ","-- **R1 (FR-7 timing):** AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL visibility arrive later than GRADED. Without the B4 bulk hooks, those quizzes never sync. Syncing early would break NFR-5.","-- **R2 (FR-4 vs FR-24):** the teacher's hide toggle and the source-driven `isVisible` share one column. Re-saving an assignment would silently re-show a teacher-hidden item. Options: (a) source sync writes isVisible only on publish/archive *transitions*; (b) add a separate `hiddenByTeacher` flag and make visible = sourceVisible ∧ ¬hiddenByTeacher. (b) is clearer but adds a column beyond FR-1's \"exactly as specified\". Pick one and state it.","-- **R3 (FR-12 Uncategorised weight):** the PRD doesn't say what weight the implicit bucket carries when real categories exist. A sensible default is weight 0, so it's shown but excluded from the weighted mean, unless it's the only bucket. This affects the FR-15 golden test only if it has uncategorised items (it doesn't). Flag it.","-- **R4 (FR-38 dedupe):** \"one notification per student per item\" needs a marker. A nullable `Grade.notifiedAt` claimed via `updateMany` follows the existing claim pattern.","-- **R5 (FR-3 term drift):** re-deriving the term on every edit can move existing grades between terms. Only recompute it when dueAt/availableUntil changes.","-- **R6 (FR-16 delete):** deleting a scale referenced by courses or by DRAFT snapshots (PUBLISHED ones embed the legend, so they're safe). Recommend blocking the delete with CONFLICT while courses reference the scale.","-- **R7 (first DataGrid):** there is no in-repo precedent. Keyboard E/M/Delete handling within the MIT tier is the main implementation risk (intake keyRisk). The design should keep the grid behind one client component.","+| # | Risk / conflict | Recommendation |","+|---|---|---|","+| R1 | **Two audience code paths must agree** (FR-7, NFR-10). | Single source of rules: the `UserAudienceKeys` builder + a pure `matchesAudience(audience, keys)` + `audienceWhere(keys)`. `resolveAudienceUserIds` is written separately (set expansion) but tested against the matcher for every seed user. |","+| R2 | **FR-26 per-instance `mandatoryInApp`** isn't expressible in the static registry (B9). | Two type keys (`announcement.published`, `announcement.published_ack`), or accept a static `true`. Design picks one and records it as an ADR. |","+| R3 | **FR-1 \"exactly as specified\" vs. the needed additions** (`lastRemindedAt`, indexes, possibly `publishedAt`). | Add them as explicitly flagged additions; intake already pre-approved `lastRemindedAt`. |","+| R4 | **Feed ordering by \"newest\"** when publishAt is null for publish-now. | Set `publishAt = now` on publish-now so one column orders everything. |","+| R5 | **Status column vs. read-time visibility** (FR-16). | Visibility is computed from `publishAt`. The maintenance claim also flips SCHEDULED→PUBLISHED for the manage view. The UI should derive the display status with the same predicate, so it is correct between cron ticks. |","+| R6 | **Manage-view reach** (FR-23) means resolving N audiences per page. | Per-page live resolve (pageSize ≤ 50); `ponytail:` note for a `recipientCount` snapshot later. |","+| R7 | **Notification fan-out** on SCHOOL announcements (thousands of userIds in one notify). | Chunk userIds (e.g. 1,000) when calling notify. The notifiedAt claim happens before the send, so a crash mid-send loses the remainder rather than double-sending. That matches the existing quiz-release semantics; note it. |","+| R8 | **Teacher PATCH re-validation** (FR-10 on PATCH). | Run `assertCanTarget` on the *resulting* audience set whenever audiences or isPublic are present in the PATCH. |","+| R9 | **Orphan purge vs. drafts** (B7). | Attach files on every save, including drafts. |","+| R10 | **Public endpoint abuse** (FR-31). | Paginate with the max pageSize clamp from `parsePagination`, and optionally use `rateLimit` by IP. |","+| R11 | **Stats for audience changes after publish** (FR-29). | Stats use the live audience. Reads by users no longer in the audience are excluded from the percentages. Document this. |"," ","-## 4. Carried-forward assumptions (from intake, adjusted)","+## 4. Assumptions carried from intake (must surface in system-design.md Overview)"," ","-1. FR-6: unexempting clears excused and re-syncs the score from the source.","-2. FR-7: **use the existing `getStudentQuizScore`** (B1) plus a caller-side `resultsVisible` gate. This replaces intake's \"build a new helper\".","-3. FR-13: 89.95 → 90.0 → **A−** under the seed scale. The test asserts 90.0 and the 90-band letter.","-4. FR-27/FR-33: add nav entries per the convention.","-5. NFR-10: past due = `now > dueAt` (exact instant). Term containment is evaluated in the school timezone.","-6. FR-3: no containing term and no current term → skip the item + `logger.warn`.","-7. New and unstated (needs sign-off): FR-14 percent-only override re-derives the letter; FR-32 comments are editable only while DRAFT; FR-34 unpublish returns to DRAFT.","+| # | Assumption | Default |","+|---|---|---|","+| A1 | FR-5 section members = current academic-year SectionMember rows. | Members of the section row itself (a section belongs to one year). Teachers may only target current-year sections via the pickers. |","+| A2 | FR-15 drafts may have zero recipients. | Refused only on publish/schedule. |","+| A3 | Parent expansion uses linked parents of matching students; the ACTIVE filter applies to each final user. | A parent of an archived student is **not** reached through that student. Recommendation: only ACTIVE students expand to parents, and the matcher does the same. |","+| A4 | FR-17: overflow pins (>3) fall into newest-first. | Yes. |","+| A5 | AC-8: the test fixture creates Pat's 6A child + link if the seed lacks them. | Yes; the seed itself stays skip-if-missing. |","+| A6 | Archived courses (`Course.archivedAt`) in audience resolution. | Exclude archived courses from the teacher branches of GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION. Not stated in the PRD; flag it. |","+| A7 | FR-12: archive is terminal for authors; admins may still edit. | Yes. |","+| A8 | FR-25: 429 RATE_LIMITED + `lastRemindedAt` column. | Decided here (architect owns it per intake). |"]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-11\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards (SCH-011). It has 42 FRs and 13 NFRs (55 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions (FR-6, FR-7, FR-13, FR-27/33, NFR-10, FR-3 no-term) are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> As of this writing the other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **leftovers from earlier tickets**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-11 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-11 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | **`getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` already exists.** It is labelled \"PRD-11 export\". It loads GRADED attempts, applies `applyScoringPolicy(quiz.scoringPolicy, …)`, and returns `{score, maxScore, percent, attemptsCounted, isPractice}` (fixed2 strings) or null. | src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts L355-372 | **This corrects intake** (B-finding 5 and the FR-7 assumption). FR-7 calls it directly, with no new helper. It does **not** check `resultsVisible`, so the sync caller must gate on that (NFR-5). The batch path (FR-8 backfill, NFR-3) should run `applyScoringPolicy` in memory over attempts it has already loaded, rather than calling this per student. |\n| B2 | `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` covers IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE (`now >= availableUntil`) / MANUAL (`resultsReleasedAt != null`). | src/server/quiz/grading.ts L94 | FR-7 / NFR-5 gate. AFTER_CLOSE depends on time, so a GRADED attempt is not syncable until close. See B4. |\n| B3 | Every quiz attempt status change goes through `recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)`. It is called from `submitAttempt` (L123, which includes auto-submit), `gradeAnswerManually` (L338) and `regradeQuiz` (quiz-service L435). | attempt-service.ts L73-81 | FR-7 hook. After each caller commits, call `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`, which no-ops unless GRADED + visible + !isPractice. Making this one function the only quiz sync entry point covers all three callers. |\n| B4 | Results become visible through `releaseResults` (MANUAL, quiz-service L464) and `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased` (AFTER_CLOSE). The latter claims `resultsReleasedAt` with `updateMany` on each maintenance tick. | quiz-service.ts L464; quiz/maintenance.ts L27-40 | FR-7 also needs a **bulk** `syncQuizGrades(quizId)` in both places. Otherwise AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL quizzes never reach the gradebook. The maintenance claim is already idempotent, so put the sync after `count === 1`. |\n| B5 | Quiz lifecycle: `createQuiz`, `updateQuiz` (DRAFT→PUBLISHED and PUBLISHED→CLOSED via guarded `updateMany`, L304-305), `deleteQuiz` (hard delete, L317). Quizzes have **no archive**. | quiz-service.ts L259-317 | FR-3: upsert the item on →PUBLISHED. FR-4: delete the item on deleteQuiz. CLOSED is **not** unpublish, so the item stays visible. Settings edits to a published quiz (title, availableUntil, categoryId, max) re-upsert the item. |\n| B6 | Assignment lifecycle: `createAssignment` / `updateAssignment` (status DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED); `publishOnce` (cron, makes SCHEDULED visible once `availableFrom` passes); `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` (hard delete in a tx, or sets `archivedAt` when submissions exist, L479-492). `isAssignmentVisible` = !archivedAt && published-or-scheduled-reached. | assignments-service.ts L67-74, L292-330, L437-492 | FR-3/FR-4: compute GradeItem.isVisible from `isAssignmentVisible`. Upsert on create/update/publishOnce, set isVisible=false on archive, delete inside the delete tx. **FR-24's teacher hide toggle conflicts with this** (see §3 R2). |\n| B7 | Return paths: `gradeSubmission` (`returning = input.return && status !== 'RETURNED'`; it also re-grades an already-RETURNED submission), `bulkReturn`, and `gradeOffline` (`input.return`). | assignments-service.ts ~L696-800 | FR-5: sync when the submission **is RETURNED after the write**, not only on the transition. Re-grading a returned submission must update Grade.score, and grade-without-return must not sync (AC-3). Use one `syncSubmissionGrade(submissionId)` from all three. |\n| B8 | `setExemption(…, exempt)` upserts or deletes `GradeExemption` (L818/L824) and audits `assignment.exempt` / `assignment.unexempt`. | assignments-service.ts L815-838 | FR-6: call `syncSubmissionGrade` (or a by-(assignment, student) variant) after both branches. Unexempt re-derives the score from a RETURNED submission, else null. |\n| B9 | GradeItem has a polymorphic `source + sourceId` with **no FK**. Assignment and Quiz deletes will not cascade. | FR-1 model spec | FR-4: delete the GradeItem explicitly inside the same transaction as the source delete (and in `deleteQuiz`, which today runs outside a tx). Grade → GradeItem should be `onDelete: Cascade`. |\n| B10 | `Term` has no `isCurrent`. It has `academicYearId`, `startDate`/`endDate` as `@db.Date`, `order`. `AcademicYear.isCurrent` exists. `Course.academicYearId` exists. | schema.prisma L240-252, Course ~L415 | FR-3 term placement: pick the term of **the course's academic year** whose `[startDate, endDate]` contains dueAt, comparing dates in the school timezone (NFR-10). The fallback \"current term\" is the term of that year containing today (tz), else skip + `logger.warn`. Put this in one pure helper `termFor(date, terms, tz)`. |\n| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from assignments-service. `dec` / `fixed2` / `Decimal` come from grading-math (isomorphic). `percentOf` (1 dp half-up) is in quiz/grading.ts. | assignments-service.ts L57; grading-math.ts L7-15; grading.ts L133 | NFR-1/NFR-10/FR-13 reuse these. `percentOf` rounds to 1 dp on a single value. grade-calc must keep full-precision Decimal until the **final** rounding (FR-13), so it must not round category percents early. |\n| B12 | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` exist. `getAccessibleStudentIds` / `assertCanViewStudent` cover own student, linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`), teacher and admin, with homeroom handled there too. `src/server/quiz/access.ts` has `canManageCourse`. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts, student-access.ts | FR-39 \"manage\"/\"view\" and FR-42 reuse these. FR-37 report-card access is new: ADMIN; teachers of any course on the card or the homeroom teacher; the student or a linked parent only when PUBLISHED. Return NOT_FOUND to everyone else (AC-7). |\n| B13 | Attendance aggregation already exists: `getReport(filters)` → `StudentSummaryRow` (StatusCounts per student) using a single `groupBy(studentId, status)`. It filters by date range, grade level, section and course. | attendance-service.ts L528-582 | FR-30 attendance summary and NFR-3 batching: call `getReport({from: term.start, to: term.end, sectionId/gradeLevelId})` **once** per generate request. Do not loop per student. Rate formula: reuse whatever StatusCounts consumers use. Do not invent a new one. |\n| B14 | `SchoolSettings` singleton: name, shortName, logoUrl, timezone, address fields. Student profile: `admissionNumber`, `gradeLevel`. `Section.homeroomTeacherId`. | schema.prisma L109-113, L198-215 | FR-30 snapshot fields all come from existing models. No schema change beyond FR-1. |\n| B15 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const already contains assignment.* and quiz.* entries. `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents()` never throw. `audit()` never throws. | notifications/types.ts, notify.ts L28/L98, audit.ts L26 | FR-38: add `grade.posted` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, STUDENT+PARENT) and `report_card.published` (defaultEmail true, STUDENT+PARENT). Call them after commit. NFR-4 audit actions: `grade.update`, `termOverride.upsert`, `reportCard.unpublish` (plus `reportCard.publish` and `gradingScale.*` as nice-to-haves). |\n| B16 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are static arrays. `studentTabs` notes \"No tab bar renders studentTabs yet\". `navigation` is a flat array with `roles` and an optional `group: 'Administration'`. | src/config/*.ts | FR-18/28: add course tabs `gradebook` (TEACHER, ADMIN) and `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT). FR-26/36: add student tabs `grades` and `report-cards`. These are reachable by URL only, the same as `assignments`. FR-27/33 + admin pages: nav entries `/grades`, `/report-cards`, `/admin/grading-scales`, `/admin/report-cards`. |\n| B17 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` are in src/server/csv.ts. Shared components: DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast (useToast), PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, DateDisplay, UserPicker, FormField, LoadingSkeleton. **No existing `@mui/x-data-grid` usage in src.** | src/server/csv.ts; src/components/ | FR-25: export on the server with `toCsv`, building the same columns as the grid. FR-18 is the first DataGrid in the codebase, so its MIT-tier API (columnGroupingModel, processRowUpdate, virtualisation, no pinning) must be looked up via mui-mcp for 9.5.0 (NFR-7/8). FR-29 table → DataTable. |\n| B18 | Scripts: `db:seed` = `tsx prisma/seed.ts`. There is no `gradebook:backfill`. The seed looks up courses by code with `findCourse([...])`. | package.json; prisma/seed.ts | FR-8: add `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`, a thin wrapper over an exported `backfillGradebook()` in src/server/gradebook/ that the seed also calls before the FR-41 data. |\n| B19 | Postgres. Migrations already hand-add raw SQL partial indexes. Prisma 5.20. | prisma/migrations/* | FR-1: one migration. It needs `@@unique([source, sourceId])` on GradeItem (sync and backfill idempotency), `@@unique([gradeItemId, studentId])` on Grade, `@@unique([courseId, termId, studentId])` on TermGradeOverride, and `@@unique([studentId, termId])` on ReportCard. These make the upserts race-safe. A one-default-scale rule can be a partial unique index `WHERE \"isDefault\"` (FR-16). |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **SYNC** source→gradebook sync hook · **CALC** pure calculation · **API** REST endpoint · **UI** page/component · **AUTH** access boundary · **JOB** script/batch · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **CFG** config registry.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | New enums + 6 models in one `prisma migrate` migration. Use the unique keys from B19. Grade: `score Decimal?`, `excused`, `missing`, `comment`, `gradedById`, `gradedAt`. ReportCard: `status`, `snapshot Json`, `homeroomComment`, `principalComment`, `publishedAt`, `publishedById`. |\n| FR-2 | DM, UI | Nullable `Course.gradingScaleId`, `Assignment.categoryId` and `Quiz.categoryId` with `onDelete: SetNull`. Category deletion via FR-40 must not delete sources. Add one `Select` to the existing assignment and quiz editors, plus the validator fields in assignments.ts / quiz.ts (optional and nullable). Don't change existing behaviour. |\n| FR-3 | SYNC | `upsertGradeItemFromAssignment(id)` / `…FromQuiz(id)` keyed on (source, sourceId). Skip practice quizzes. Term placement via `termFor` (B10). Callers per B5/B6. Keep the GradeItem's term stable after first creation unless the date changes, so grades don't jump terms on unrelated edits. |\n| FR-4 | SYNC | Archive sets isVisible=false. Delete removes the GradeItem in the same tx (B9). Quiz has no archive or unpublish. A practice-toggle after publish should delete or hide the item. |\n| FR-5 | SYNC | `syncSubmissionGrade` from 3 return paths (B7). It writes only when RETURNED. Score = `finalScore`. |\n| FR-6 | SYNC | From `setExemption` (B8). Exemption wins over the score: excused=true and the score is kept. |\n| FR-7 | SYNC | Per-attempt `syncQuizGrade` after `recomputeAttempt` callers (B3). Bulk `syncQuizGrades` on release and AFTER_CLOSE (B4). Score scaled: `score/maxScore × GradeItem.maxPoints`, Decimal. |\n| FR-8 | JOB | `backfillGradebook()`: batch load per course, reuse the same upsert builders as live sync (one code path), idempotent through the unique keys. npm script + seed call (B18). |\n| FR-9 | API, AUTH | The service rejects score/excused/missing edits on non-MANUAL items (`AppError('FORBIDDEN'/'VALIDATION_ERROR')`). Comment stays editable. The grid marks those columns non-editable. |\n| FR-10 | CALC | `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts`: pure, Decimal-only, no Prisma client import (types only). Input: items, grades, categories, scale, override, `now`. Counted = visible ∧ ¬excused ∧ (score≠null ∨ (missing ∧ now>dueAt)). |\n| FR-11 | CALC | Drop lowest by item **percentage**, keeping ≥1. Ties are dropped deterministically (by dueAt, then id). |\n| FR-12 | CALC | Implicit \"Uncategorised\" bucket. What weight does it get? The PRD is silent, so see §3 R3. No categories gives a points total. |\n| FR-13 | CALC | `toDecimalPlaces(1, ROUND_HALF_UP)` only at the end. Bands are sorted descending, first `percent >= minPercent`. |\n| FR-14 | CALC | The override is applied after computing. A letter-only override keeps the computed percent. A percent-only override probably re-derives the letter from the scale (unstated, so flag it). |\n| FR-15 | CALC, UI | Golden unit test (78.0 C+). The gradebook and student Grades **must call the same function**, with no client-side recomputation. |\n| FR-16 | API, UI, DM | `/admin/grading-scales` (ADMIN). Band validation lives in a Zod refinement shared by client and server. \"Exactly one default\" uses a tx that clears others + a partial unique index. Deleting a scale in use is either blocked or falls back to the default; decide this. |\n| FR-17 | UI, API | Course settings page. The live weight sum is client-side, with the 100 check repeated server-side in FR-40. Decimal weights: compare with `dec(sum).eq(100)`, not floats. |\n| FR-18 | UI, API, CALC | First DataGrid. The server returns one denormalised payload `{students, items, categories, grades, computed}` for (course, term) in a fixed number of queries (NFR-2). Columns are built client-side from it. Sort by last name on the server. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Pure cell renderer. \"Late\" needs `Submission.isLate`, so the gradebook payload must carry the source submission's isLate. |\n| FR-20 | UI, API | `processRowUpdate` → PATCH a single grade. E/M/Delete need a custom edit cell / `onCellKeyDown` (check mui-mcp). Optimistic update with per-cell error. Audited (NFR-4). Triggers `grade.posted` (FR-38). |\n| FR-21 | UI | The cell click opens a link to the submission grading page or the quiz attempt. The payload needs `submissionId` / `attemptId` per synced grade. |\n| FR-22 | API, UI | POST manual item. Validate that the term belongs to the course's academic year and the category belongs to the course. |\n| FR-23 | API, UI, AUD | PUT override (upsert). Comment ≤1000 chars. Audit with old/new values. |\n| FR-24 | API, UI | Toggle visibility (see R2). Bulk-missing allowed only if `now > dueAt` and only for ungraded rows. Stats come from the computed payload, client-side, over counted scores. |\n| FR-25 | API | Server CSV via `toCsv`, using the same row builder as the grid. \"As displayed\" means EX/M/— markers and the term letter. |\n| FR-26 | UI, API, CFG | Student tab → `GET /api/students/:id/grades?termId`. The colour thresholds come from a single helper reused by FR-27/28. |\n| FR-27 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/grades` reuses the FR-26 component. Parent child selector from `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Nav entry. |\n| FR-28 | UI, CFG | Course tab `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT): same endpoint filtered by courseId. |\n| FR-29 | UI, API | `/admin/report-cards`: list query joins students (grade level, section filters) with ReportCard status for the term. Missing-data warnings are computed in batch (ungraded counted-eligible items, missing TermGradeOverride.comment per course). |\n| FR-30 | JOB, API | `generate`: batch load (NFR-3), compute in memory, write the snapshot JSON (versioned shape, e.g. `snapshot.v = 1`). Teacher comment = `TermGradeOverride.comment`. Attendance via B13. |\n| FR-31 | JOB, DM | `upsert` with `where status = DRAFT` semantics: createMany for new cards, `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})` for existing ones, never touching PUBLISHED. Grade-edit services never import report-cards code. |\n| FR-32 | API, UI, AUTH | PATCH: field-level role check (homeroomComment: homeroom teacher of the student's section or ADMIN; principalComment: ADMIN). Edits are allowed only while DRAFT (implied, so flag it). |\n| FR-33 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/report-cards` (TEACHER): drafts for sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Nav entry. |\n| FR-34 | API, NOTIF, AUD | Publish (one or bulk) with a guarded `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})`, then notify after commit. Unpublish: ADMIN, reason required, audit, back to DRAFT. |\n| FR-35 | UI | `/report-cards/[id]/print` renders from the **snapshot only**. `@media print` via MUI `GlobalStyles`, hiding the sidebar. Bulk print: one page renders N cards with `break-after: page`. |\n| FR-36 | UI, CFG, API | Student tab \"Report cards\". The list endpoint filters to PUBLISHED for student/parent (NFR-5). |\n| FR-37 | AUTH | New `assertCanViewReportCard`. Non-entitled users get NOT_FOUND, so existence isn't leaked. |\n| FR-38 | NOTIF | Register 2 types (B15). `grade.posted`: only for MANUAL items, only when a score is first entered or changed (one per student per item, so an idempotency marker such as `Grade.notifiedAt` is needed; flag it). |\n| FR-39 | API, AUTH | Thin route handlers using `withHandler`, Zod in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, and services in `src/server/gradebook/` + `src/server/report-cards/`. |\n| FR-40 | API | Replace-all in a tx: delete missing ids (sources → SetNull), upsert the rest. Weights total 100 (Decimal). |\n| FR-41 | JOB | Seed: scale, 7A categories, 'Oral presentation' + grades, draft S1 cards for 7A with MATH/ENG override comments. Run after `backfillGradebook()`. |\n| FR-42 | API, AUTH | Student serializer: visible items only. Grade rows only exist for released scores (sync gating), so the risk is mainly hidden items and MANUAL items with isVisible=false. Still filter explicitly. |\n| NFR-1 | CALC | Decimal throughout. Unit matrix in `grade-calc.test.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | API | Gradebook: ~5 queries (enrollments, items, grades, categories, scale + override), all indexed by (courseId, termId). The grid virtualises. |\n| NFR-3 | JOB | Generation: per term, `findMany` items/grades/overrides/categories for all courses in scope with `in` filters, then group in memory. One attendance `groupBy`. Chunk the writes. |\n| NFR-4 | AUD | Old/new values in metadata for grade.update, termOverride.upsert and reportCard.unpublish. |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Enforced in 3 layers: sync gating (B2/B7), student serializer (FR-42), report-card guard (FR-37). Integration tests for each. |\n| NFR-6 | AUTH | Every route uses requireUser/requireRole + an entity check (B12). Server pages check too, not just the API. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | MUI only, with mui-mcp lookup. Toast via useToast, confirm via Dialog/ConfirmDialog. |\n| NFR-8 | UI | DataGrid MIT: no `pinnedColumns` and no `@mui/x-data-grid-pro`. Sticky header is the default. |\n| NFR-9 | all | New code only in src/server/gradebook/ and src/server/report-cards/. Hooks into existing services are one-line calls. Use `logger`, no console.log. |\n| NFR-10 | CALC, SYNC | Past-due uses an instant comparison (`now > dueAt`). Term containment uses a tz date comparison (B10). |\n| NFR-11 | UI | A4 portrait `@page` rule. Long course lists may need a 2nd page, with table rows set to `break-inside: avoid`. |\n| NFR-12 | all | Tests per the intake list. Integration tests hit the real sync hooks (B3/B4/B7). |\n| NFR-13 | — | Scope guard: store `gpa`, never compute it. No rank or transcript. |\n\n## 3. Risks / decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **R1 (FR-7 timing):** AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL visibility arrive later than GRADED. Without the B4 bulk hooks, those quizzes never sync. Syncing early would break NFR-5.\n- **R2 (FR-4 vs FR-24):** the teacher's hide toggle and the source-driven `isVisible` share one column. Re-saving an assignment would silently re-show a teacher-hidden item. Options: (a) source sync writes isVisible only on publish/archive *transitions*; (b) add a separate `hiddenByTeacher` flag and make visible = sourceVisible ∧ ¬hiddenByTeacher. (b) is clearer but adds a column beyond FR-1's \"exactly as specified\". Pick one and state it.\n- **R3 (FR-12 Uncategorised weight):** the PRD doesn't say what weight the implicit bucket carries when real categories exist. A sensible default is weight 0, so it's shown but excluded from the weighted mean, unless it's the only bucket. This affects the FR-15 golden test only if it has uncategorised items (it doesn't). Flag it.\n- **R4 (FR-38 dedupe):** \"one notification per student per item\" needs a marker. A nullable `Grade.notifiedAt` claimed via `updateMany` follows the existing claim pattern.\n- **R5 (FR-3 term drift):** re-deriving the term on every edit can move existing grades between terms. Only recompute it when dueAt/availableUntil changes.\n- **R6 (FR-16 delete):** deleting a scale referenced by courses or by DRAFT snapshots (PUBLISHED ones embed the legend, so they're safe). Recommend blocking the delete with CONFLICT while courses reference the scale.\n- **R7 (first DataGrid):** there is no in-repo precedent. Keyboard E/M/Delete handling within the MIT tier is the main implementation risk (intake keyRisk). The design should keep the grid behind one client component.\n\n## 4. Carried-forward assumptions (from intake, adjusted)\n\n1. FR-6: unexempting clears excused and re-syncs the score from the source.\n2. FR-7: **use the existing `getStudentQuizScore`** (B1) plus a caller-side `resultsVisible` gate. This replaces intake's \"build a new helper\".\n3. FR-13: 89.95 → 90.0 → **A−** under the seed scale. The test asserts 90.0 and the 90-band letter.\n4. FR-27/FR-33: add nav entries per the convention.\n5. NFR-10: past due = `now > dueAt` (exact instant). Term containment is evaluated in the school timezone.\n6. FR-3: no containing term and no current term → skip the item + `logger.warn`.\n7. New and unstated (needs sign-off): FR-14 percent-only override re-derives the letter; FR-32 comments are editable only while DRAFT; FR-34 unpublish returns to DRAFT.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Wc56sNEhDxTioi1zj5AFmM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
