{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HjSXBeg1uXyCQKao33kZeE","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"612c4910-0bea-4d59-adbf-fcf9d39f8b8d","uuid":"0a677202-654a-4329-b6f4-2b0a9e4fa609","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:31:29.867Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","oldString":"columns implied by FR-2.1:","newString":"columns implied by FR-3..FR-6:","originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-12\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T18:00:00Z), PRD-12 Announcements & News. It has 36 FRs and 11 NFRs (47 requirements) at 94% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> All other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **SH-11 leftovers**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-12 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-12 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no Announcement* models or enums. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1: add a new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_announcements`). Add back-relations on `User` (authored, reads) and `FileObject` (attachments, and the cover image if it is an FK). |\n| B2 | `User.status` is `ACTIVE/INVITED/DISABLED/ARCHIVED` and `archivedAt` is a separate column. `notify()` filters `status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED]`, so it **includes INVITED**. | schema L17, L59; notify.ts L43 | FR-3 is stricter: audience = `status: ACTIVE, archivedAt: null`. Pass the resolved ids to `notify()`, which then filters on its own. Don't rely on notify's filter. |\n| B3 | `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId` (required). `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` has `@@index([studentId])` and a `@@unique([parentId, studentId])`. | schema L106, L144 | FR-4/5/6 parent expansion: join through the link. Parent → children is covered by the unique index's leading `parentId`. |\n| B4 | `Section(academicYearId, gradeLevelId, homeroomTeacherId?)`. `SectionMember(studentId, academicYearId)` is unique on `(studentId, academicYearId)`, and its academicYearId is denormalised. **There is no index on `sectionId`.** | schema L377-411 | FR-5: \"members\" = SectionMember rows where `academicYearId` = the section's year (that is already true per row, so filtering by `sectionId` is enough). A section belongs to one year, so the \"current year\" question reduces to \"is the section in the current year\". See §4 A1. |\n| B5 | `Course(academicYearId, sectionId?, teacherId, coTeacherIds String[], archivedAt?)`. `coTeacherIds` is queried with `has`. `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. | schema L414-447 | FR-4/5/6/10 teacher branches. `has` isn't indexable without a GIN index. The rows involved are small (only a user's own courses), so this is fine for NFR-2. Decide whether archived courses' teachers count (§4 A6). |\n| B6 | `Enrollment.status` ACTIVE/DROPPED, with `@@index([studentId, status])` and `@@unique([courseId, studentId])`. | schema L371, L450 | FR-6 student branch. Both directions are indexed. |\n| B7 | `FileObject(context, contextId)` is indexed. Uploads are created with `contextId: null`. `attachFiles(tx, context, contextId, ids)` / detach live in files-service. **`purgeOrphanFiles` deletes `contextId: null` files after 24 h.** | files-service.ts L212-244; files/purge.ts | FR-13/FR-30: attach the cover image and attachments with `context='announcement'`, `contextId=announcement.id` inside the create/update tx. A cover that is uploaded but never attached (e.g. an abandoned draft) is purged, which is correct. **A draft must still attach its files**, or they vanish after 24 h. |\n| B8 | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)`. Resolvers receive `null` for anonymous callers. Built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (contexts.ts). Resolver errors deny. `/api/files/` is already in PUBLIC_API_PATHS. | files/access.ts; contexts.ts; public-routes.ts | FR-30: add `register('announcement', announcementResolver)` to `registerBuiltInContexts` so it is guaranteed loaded, rather than as a side-effect import. Anonymous downloads already route through, so no public-route change is needed for files. |\n| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). `COMMUNICATION` exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a **static boolean per type**. | notifications/types.ts | **FR-26 conflict**: \"mandatoryInApp true when requiresAck\" can't be expressed per instance. Options: (a) two types, `announcement.published` (mandatoryInApp false) and `announcement.published_ack` (true); or (b) one type with `mandatoryInApp: true`. Recommend (a) as the smallest faithful mapping. **arch-design-system decides.** |\n| B10 | `notify({type, userIds, title, body, link, email:{template:'generic-notification', data}})` dedupes, never throws, and is called after commit. It truncates body to BODY_MAX and drops non-relative links. | notify.ts L8-60 | FR-27/28: call it after the notifiedAt claim commits. `link: /announcements/${id}`. Large audiences (a SCHOOL announcement can be thousands of users) go through one `findMany` + `createMany`. That's acceptable, but chunk the userIds if notify's `in` lists get large. |\n| B11 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` runs each pass in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take: BATCH)` → `updateMany({where:{id, claimCol: null}})` → act only if `count === 1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts L28-43 | FR-27: `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` copies this pattern exactly: `where status SCHEDULED, publishAt <= now, notifiedAt null`, claim `notifiedAt`. Publish-now uses the same claim helper, so one code path sends. |\n| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes both `RATE_LIMITED` (429) and `CONFLICT` (409). `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` exist. | src/server/http.ts | FR-34 handler conventions. FR-25: recommend **429 RATE_LIMITED** with `details.retryAfter` (ISO). It is semantically a time-based throttle, and intake suggested the same. |\n| B13 | `audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request})` never throws. The action convention is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|archive\\|delete`. | src/server/audit.ts | FR-12: `announcement.update` / `announcement.archive` when an admin acts on another author's row. Also audit the author's own archive (cheap; optional). |\n| B14 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` (formula-injection safe). | src/server/csv.ts | FR-24 `?format=csv`. |\n| B15 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from **assignments-service.ts**, not a shared module. `formatInSchoolTz` is in src/lib/dates.ts. | assignments-service.ts L64; src/lib/dates.ts L7 | NFR-7: reuse both. Importing `getSchoolTimezone` from assignments-service is the existing precedent (contexts.ts already imports from it). Don't duplicate it. |\n| B16 | `MarkdownView` = react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema) rendering to MUI components. **There is no Markdown→plain-text helper** in the codebase. | src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx | FR-18 (200-char excerpt) and FR-28 (300-char email body) need a new small pure `markdownToPlainText(md)` (e.g. in `src/lib/markdown-text.ts`). Plain text rendered by React/the email template is escaped, so NFR-4 is met as long as the excerpt is never rendered as HTML/Markdown. Prefer a regex strip over a new dependency (remark is already installed transitively if an AST approach is preferred). |\n| B17 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `navigation` is a static array. `NotificationBell` polls `/api/notifications/unread-count` every 30 s, gated by visibility, and shows an MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L42-62 | FR-32: add an optional `badge?: 'announcements-unread'` key (or a badge endpoint string) to NavItem. The sidebar renders a polled Badge for items that have one. Reuse the bell's polling hook shape. |\n| B18 | `courseTabs` is a static array with `roles`. | src/config/course-tabs.ts | FR-21: `{ key: 'announcements', label: 'Announcements', href: id => /courses/${id}/announcements, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. |\n| B19 | `assertCanViewCourse` covers ADMIN, TEACHER (teacher or co-teacher only, **not homeroom**), STUDENT (enrollment) and PARENT (child enrolled). `canSeeDrafts` checks the course-manager test. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts L25+ | FR-21 gate: `assertCanViewCourse` and then the normal audience filter. FR-10 \"courses they manage\" = the same `teacherId \\|\\| coTeacherIds.includes` test, so reuse it rather than re-deriving. |\n| B20 | Seed: Tom/Sam/Pat by email. Courses are looked up with `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` and skipped if missing. The Grade 7 GradeLevel row **is** seeded. No 7A/7B/6A sections and no `ParentStudentLink` rows are created by the seed (they come from other scripts/fixtures, if at all). | prisma/seed.ts L18-22, L109-115, L275-305 | FR-35: grade/course/section-targeted seeds skip when their target is missing, using the same `logger.info`/`console.log` style. School-wide, staff and public seeds always run. Idempotency: upsert by a stable title + author, or check for existence first. |\n| B21 | Test layout: `tests/unit`, `tests/integration/<feature>/`, `tests/e2e/*.spec.ts` + `helpers/`. | tests/ | NFR-10: `tests/unit/announcements/*`, `tests/integration/announcements/*`, `tests/e2e/announcements.spec.ts`. |\n| B22 | `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0 is installed (`@mui/x-data-grid` too). | package.json | FR-13 publishAt/expiresAt: DateTimePicker. FR-23/24 tables: the existing `DataTable` component. Look up via mui-mcp per NFR-1. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend for **Concern**: DM = data model / migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance/cron, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | 2 enums, 4 models, 1 migration. AnnouncementRead has a composite PK `(announcementId, userId)`. **Needed beyond the PRD's model** (flag as deliberate additions): `Announcement.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` (FR-25), `notifiedAt DateTime?` (FR-27, likely already in the spec since FR-27 names it), and indexes `AnnouncementAudience @@index([type, refId])` and `Announcement @@index([status, publishAt])` (NFR-2). AnnouncementAudience columns implied by FR-2.1: `type`, `refId?` (null for SCHOOL/STAFF), `includeStudents/Parents/Teachers` booleans. Cascade deletes from Announcement to its children. |\n| FR-2 | XC / validation | `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts`, isomorphic Zod schema, shared by the composer and the handlers. Also validate: `expiresAt > publishAt` when both are set; ROLE refId ∈ Role enum; refId required unless SCHOOL/STAFF; at least one include flag true for GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION/COURSE. |\n| FR-3 | SVC | `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`. `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` returns a set union over the rows, all filtered to `ACTIVE && archivedAt null`. SCHOOL = all, STAFF = role ∈ {ADMIN, TEACHER}, ROLE = role = refId. Do the active filter **once** at the end, including on parents. |\n| FR-4 | SVC | GRADE_LEVEL: students via `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`; parents via ParentStudentLink of **those students** (before the active filter on the students? see §4 A3); teachers = `teacherId` ∪ `coTeacherIds` of courses where `section.gradeLevelId = refId AND academicYear.isCurrent`. |\n| FR-5 | SVC | SECTION: SectionMember(sectionId) students, their parents, `homeroomTeacherId` plus the teachers/co-teachers of `Course.sectionId = refId`. \"Current year\" is implicit (§4 A1). |\n| FR-6 | SVC | COURSE: `Enrollment(courseId, status ACTIVE)` students, their parents, teacher plus coTeachers. |\n| FR-7 | SVC / perf | `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`. **Key design point**: compute a per-user *membership key set* once (≤ ~4 small queries): role; own/children's gradeLevelIds; own/children's sectionIds (current year); own/children's ACTIVE courseIds; for teachers, managed courseIds + their sectionIds/gradeLevelIds + homeroom sectionIds. Then audience matching is a pure function over `(audience, keys)`. The same key set also becomes a Prisma `where` (an OR of `{type, refId in keys[type], include<Flag>: true}`) for the feed (FR-17/NFR-2). This puts the rules in one place (intake key risk), and `resolveAudienceUserIds` is the inverse expansion. The agreement test (NFR-10) checks both. For a parent the flag is `includeParents`, and the keys come from the children. |\n| FR-8 | SVC / XC | audience.ts must not import Announcement types. Its input is `{type, refId, includeStudents, includeParents, includeTeachers}[]`, so PRD-14 can reuse it. Export the `AudienceType` enum from Prisma. |\n| FR-9 | AUTH | ADMIN: any type, `isPublic` allowed. |\n| FR-10 | AUTH | `assertCanTarget(user, audiences, isPublic)` in the service, called by **both** create and update (PATCH can change the audience). TEACHER: COURSE where they manage the course (B19); SECTION where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Everything else, and `isPublic=true`, → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')` 403. On PATCH by a teacher, also re-check when `isPublic` is omitted but already true (it can't be, since only admins set it). |\n| FR-11 | AUTH | `requireRole('ADMIN','TEACHER')` on POST, PATCH, archive, preview-audience, manage, stats and remind. |\n| FR-12 | AUTH / audit | Edit: `authorId === user.id \\|\\| ADMIN`. Archive: same. Archive sets ARCHIVED (terminal for authors, §4 A7). Admin-on-others → `audit()`. A teacher who is no longer allowed to target the existing audience (e.g. lost co-teacher status) → PATCH fails on re-validation. That's acceptable. |\n| FR-13 | UI | Pages `/announcements/new` and `/announcements/[id]/edit` (server page + client form). Reuse MarkdownEditor, FileUpload (context 'announcement'), FileList, Autocomplete pickers per audience type (grade levels, sections, courses, roles). Teachers only see their own courses/homeroom in the pickers (UX; the server still enforces). Public toggle hidden for non-admins. Show and accept dates in the school tz (NFR-7). |\n| FR-14 | API / SVC | `POST /api/announcements/preview-audience`, body = audiences[] (same Zod schema). Run `assertCanTarget` first so the preview can't enumerate other audiences' sizes. Returns `{total, byRole:{STUDENT,PARENT,TEACHER,ADMIN}}`. Debounce in the UI. Uses `resolveAudienceUserIds` + `groupBy role` (or one count query). |\n| FR-15 | SVC | On transition to PUBLISHED/SCHEDULED (create or PATCH), resolve the count and if it is 0, `VALIDATION_ERROR`. Drafts are exempt (§4 A2). Scheduled ones are validated at schedule time, not again at publishAt; an emptied audience just notifies nobody. |\n| FR-16 | SVC / XC | **Visibility predicate in one place**: `visibleWhere(now) = { OR: [{status: PUBLISHED}, {status: SCHEDULED, publishAt: {lte: now}}], AND: [{OR: [{expiresAt: null}, {expiresAt: {gt: now}}]}] }`. Use it in the feed, detail, ack, files, public news and unread-count. Precedent: `isAssignmentVisible`/`isLessonVisible`. The status column stays SCHEDULED after publishAt (unless the maintenance run also flips it to PUBLISHED; recommend it does, in the same claim, for clean manage-view status). |\n| FR-17 | API / SVC / perf | `GET /api/announcements`: `visibleWhere(now) AND audiences: { some: audienceWhereForKeys(keys) }`. Plus `?filter=unread` (`reads: {none: {userId}}` or `readAt null`) and `?filter=ack` (`requiresAck AND no acknowledgedAt`). Ordering: up to 3 pinned first (separate `take:3` query on page 1, exclude those ids from the main list), then newest by **effective publish time** (`publishAt ?? createdAt` → store a `publishedAt`, or order by `publishAt` and set it on publish-now). Overflow pins fall into the newest list (§4 A4). Include the per-user read row via a `reads: {where:{userId}}` include. |\n| FR-18 | API / UI | The card DTO = cover fileId, title, author name + role, date, audience chips (labels need names for grade/section/course refIds, so batch-load by refId), `excerpt` (B16, 200 chars, computed server-side), attachment count (`_count`). |\n| FR-19 | API / AUTH | `GET /api/announcements/:id`: access if ADMIN, the author, or (visible AND isUserInAudience). Otherwise **404** (don't leak existence, NFR-6). Upsert AnnouncementRead `{readAt: now}` only for audience members (not for admins/authors outside the audience, since that would distort stats). Client renders the body with MarkdownView. |\n| FR-20 | API / AUTH | `POST /:id/ack`: visible AND requiresAck AND audience member → upsert `{readAt ?? now, acknowledgedAt ?? now}` (idempotent; keep the first ack time). Non-member → 404. `requiresAck=false` → 409 or VALIDATION_ERROR. Display with `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| FR-21 | API / CFG / UI | `GET /api/announcements?courseId=` → `assertCanViewCourse` then the feed query additionally filtered to `audiences some {type: COURSE, refId: courseId}`. The user must still be in the audience (a parent-only course announcement isn't shown to the course's students). Course tab page `/courses/[id]/announcements`. |\n| FR-22 | SVC / UI | Parent feed only: for each item, find matching audience rows and map them back to the children whose keys matched → `forChildren: [{id, firstName}]`. This falls out of the key-set design if keys are tracked per child (`Map<refKey, childIds>`). |\n| FR-23 | API / UI | `GET /api/announcements/manage`: no visibility filter. TEACHER `authorId = me`, ADMIN all. Reach = resolved recipient count (**expensive per row**: compute for the current page only; or snapshot `recipientCount` at publish and recompute live only on stats). Read % = `count(reads readAt not null) / reach`; ack % similar. Recommendation: resolve audiences per page row (≤ pageSize calls); keep it simple, a ponytail note for a snapshot later. |\n| FR-24 | API / UI | `GET /:id/stats`: author or ADMIN, else 404. Recipients = `resolveAudienceUserIds` (live) LEFT JOIN reads. Filters `?filter=unread\\|unacked`. `?format=csv` → `toCsv`, `Content-Disposition` attachment. Percentages over the live recipient set (AC-5: 30/50 = 60%). Readers who later left the audience are not counted. |\n| FR-25 | API / NOTIF / DM | `POST /:id/remind`: author or ADMIN. requiresAck must be true and the announcement visible. Atomic claim: `updateMany({where:{id, OR:[{lastRemindedAt:null},{lastRemindedAt:{lte: now-24h}}]}, data:{lastRemindedAt: now}})`. `count 0` → **429 RATE_LIMITED** (decision, B12). Then notify `announcement.reminder` to recipients − acknowledged. Returns `{notified: n}` (AC-5: 20). |\n| FR-26 | CFG / NOTIF | Add the types to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` (B9 conflict). roles: ALL. reminder: COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true (an ack is being chased). |\n| FR-27 | JOB / NOTIF | One `claimAndNotifyPublished(id, now)` helper: `updateMany({where:{id, notifiedAt:null, <visible>}, data:{notifiedAt: now, status: PUBLISHED}})`. If count = 1 → resolve recipients → notify. Called by publish-now (after the tx commits) and by `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` (batch 200, B11). Hook it into the dispatch route in its own try/catch. |\n| FR-28 | NOTIF | Email data: `{title, body: markdownToPlainText(body).slice(0,300), ctaLabel:'Read announcement', ctaUrl}`. Check GenericNotificationData's field names when designing. |\n| FR-29 | SVC | Follows from the notifiedAt claim: PATCH never clears notifiedAt. Also a draft → PATCH publish of an already-notified row (an archived-then-edited one) must not resend. |\n| FR-30 | FILE / AUTH | `announcementResolver(user, file)`: load the announcement by `file.contextId`. If `isPublic && visible` → true (including null user). If `!user` → false. If ADMIN or author → true. If visible && isUserInAudience → true. Else false. Register it in `registerBuiltInContexts` (B8). |\n| FR-31 | API / CFG | `getPublicNews({page})` in announcements-service: `isPublic && visibleWhere(now)`, a minimal DTO (no author email, no audience). Route `src/app/api/public/news/route.ts`. Add `'/api/public/news'` (exact match) to PUBLIC_API_PATHS. Consider `rateLimit` by IP since it is unauthenticated (cheap; the helper exists). |\n| FR-32 | CFG / UI / API | Nav entry for ALL_ROLES + the badge (B17). `GET /api/announcements/unread-count` = `count(visibleWhere ∧ audience keys ∧ no read row)`. It is polled every 30 s by every user, so it must be the same indexed query as the feed (NFR-2). |\n| FR-33 | UI | Conditional button on the feed page by role. |\n| FR-34 | API | Routes under `src/app/api/announcements/` (+`[id]/`, `[id]/archive`, `[id]/ack`, `[id]/stats`, `[id]/remind`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`, `manage`) + `src/app/api/public/news`. Note that static segments (`manage`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`) coexist with `[id]`; Next resolves static first, so that is fine. All use `withHandler` + Zod `parseBody`/`parseQuery`. |\n| FR-35 | SEED | 6 announcements, idempotent, with skip-if-missing for Grade 7 (exists), MATH-7A and the parent link (B20). The scheduled one is `publishAt = now + 2 days`, so `notifiedAt` stays null and the first real cron after that sends it. The welcome and staff-meeting seeds are already published: set `notifiedAt = now` so the seed never triggers a notification storm. The expired one has `expiresAt` in the past. |\n| FR-36 | XC | `src/server/announcements/{announcements-service.ts, audience.ts}` + (from FR-27) a `maintenance.ts` following the quiz precedent, or the function lives in the service. |\n| NFR-1 | UI / XC | MUI only. Confirm archive/remind with ConfirmDialog; toasts via useToast; pickers via Autocomplete; DateTimePicker for publishAt/expiresAt; the badge via MUI Badge; the \"Unread\" dot as a Badge/Box with visually hidden text. Every component looked up through mui-mcp (the mui-mcp server is listed in this session). `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |\n| NFR-2 | perf / DM | Feed = key-set OR join on `AnnouncementAudience(type, refId)` + `Announcement(status, publishAt)` indexes. Never `resolveAudienceUserIds` on the read path. Parent with 3 children: keys come from about 3 queries over 3 children. Verify with a seeded 2,000-row integration timing test (optional; mark as non-gating if CI is noisy). |\n| NFR-3 | AUTH | `requireUser`/`requireRole` in every handler and server page; FR-10 checks in the service (not only the route). AC-3 is an integration test. |\n| NFR-4 | XC | The body is rendered only via MarkdownView. Excerpt/email text = plain text (B16), never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Titles are plain strings. |\n| NFR-5 | UI | The unread dot has a visually-hidden \"Unread\" label (MUI `visuallyHidden` from `@mui/utils`, which ships with MUI). |\n| NFR-6 | AUTH | 404 for non-members on detail/ack/stats (not 403, to avoid existence leaks; stats → 404 for non-author non-admin). Files → the resolver denies (the files route maps that). Scheduled/expired → hidden from feeds and from non-author, non-admin detail. |\n| NFR-7 | XC | DB columns are UTC `DateTime`. The composer converts school-tz local → UTC on the server (or the client sends ISO with the tz applied). Displays use `formatInSchoolTz(getSchoolTimezone())`. |\n| NFR-8 | XC | Reuse list: notify, audit, registerFileAccess/attachFiles, toCsv, MarkdownEditor/View, FileUpload/FileList, DataTable, UserPicker (likely unused: pickers are entity pickers, not users), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, getSchoolTimezone, formatInSchoolTz, withHandler/parse*, assertCanViewCourse. |\n| NFR-9 | scope | No comments, reactions, i18n or SMS, and no public website pages. Just the service + the `/api/public/news` route. |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | Unit: audience matching per type × flag (pure key-set matcher, so no DB is needed), `assertCanTarget` rules, markdownToPlainText. Integration: an agreement property test over every seed user × every seed announcement audience; publishDueAnnouncements run twice / concurrently → one notification set; AC-3 403; AC-5 reminder 20 + 429. E2E: admin composes with ack → parent reads + acks → admin stats. The fixture creates the 6A child + Pat link (§4 A5). |\n| NFR-11 | XC | `logger` in all new server code, including the maintenance hook. |\n\n## 3. Risks and conflicts for arch-design-system\n\n| # | Risk / conflict | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1 | **Two audience code paths must agree** (FR-7, NFR-10). | Single source of rules: the `UserAudienceKeys` builder + a pure `matchesAudience(audience, keys)` + `audienceWhere(keys)`. `resolveAudienceUserIds` is written separately (set expansion) but tested against the matcher for every seed user. |\n| R2 | **FR-26 per-instance `mandatoryInApp`** isn't expressible in the static registry (B9). | Two type keys (`announcement.published`, `announcement.published_ack`), or accept a static `true`. Design picks one and records it as an ADR. |\n| R3 | **FR-1 \"exactly as specified\" vs. the needed additions** (`lastRemindedAt`, indexes, possibly `publishedAt`). | Add them as explicitly flagged additions; intake already pre-approved `lastRemindedAt`. |\n| R4 | **Feed ordering by \"newest\"** when publishAt is null for publish-now. | Set `publishAt = now` on publish-now so one column orders everything. |\n| R5 | **Status column vs. read-time visibility** (FR-16). | Visibility is computed from `publishAt`. The maintenance claim also flips SCHEDULED→PUBLISHED for the manage view. The UI should derive the display status with the same predicate, so it is correct between cron ticks. |\n| R6 | **Manage-view reach** (FR-23) means resolving N audiences per page. | Per-page live resolve (pageSize ≤ 50); `ponytail:` note for a `recipientCount` snapshot later. |\n| R7 | **Notification fan-out** on SCHOOL announcements (thousands of userIds in one notify). | Chunk userIds (e.g. 1,000) when calling notify. The notifiedAt claim happens before the send, so a crash mid-send loses the remainder rather than double-sending. That matches the existing quiz-release semantics; note it. |\n| R8 | **Teacher PATCH re-validation** (FR-10 on PATCH). | Run `assertCanTarget` on the *resulting* audience set whenever audiences or isPublic are present in the PATCH. |\n| R9 | **Orphan purge vs. drafts** (B7). | Attach files on every save, including drafts. |\n| R10 | **Public endpoint abuse** (FR-31). | Paginate with the max pageSize clamp from `parsePagination`, and optionally use `rateLimit` by IP. |\n| R11 | **Stats for audience changes after publish** (FR-29). | Stats use the live audience. Reads by users no longer in the audience are excluded from the percentages. Document this. |\n\n## 4. Assumptions carried from intake (must surface in system-design.md Overview)\n\n| # | Assumption | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| A1 | FR-5 section members = current academic-year SectionMember rows. | Members of the section row itself (a section belongs to one year). Teachers may only target current-year sections via the pickers. |\n| A2 | FR-15 drafts may have zero recipients. | Refused only on publish/schedule. |\n| A3 | Parent expansion uses linked parents of matching students; the ACTIVE filter applies to each final user. | A parent of an archived student is **not** reached through that student. Recommendation: only ACTIVE students expand to parents, and the matcher does the same. |\n| A4 | FR-17: overflow pins (>3) fall into newest-first. | Yes. |\n| A5 | AC-8: the test fixture creates Pat's 6A child + link if the seed lacks them. | Yes; the seed itself stays skip-if-missing. |\n| A6 | Archived courses (`Course.archivedAt`) in audience resolution. | Exclude archived courses from the teacher branches of GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION. Not stated in the PRD; flag it. |\n| A7 | FR-12: archive is terminal for authors; admins may still edit. | Yes. |\n| A8 | FR-25: 429 RATE_LIMITED + `lastRemindedAt` column. | Decided here (architect owns it per intake). |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":39,"oldLines":7,"newStart":39,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," | Req | Concern | Notes |"," |---|---|---|","-| FR-1 | DM | 2 enums, 4 models, 1 migration. AnnouncementRead has a composite PK `(announcementId, userId)`. **Needed beyond the PRD's model** (flag as deliberate additions): `Announcement.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` (FR-25), `notifiedAt DateTime?` (FR-27, likely already in the spec since FR-27 names it), and indexes `AnnouncementAudience @@index([type, refId])` and `Announcement @@index([status, publishAt])` (NFR-2). AnnouncementAudience columns implied by FR-2.1: `type`, `refId?` (null for SCHOOL/STAFF), `includeStudents/Parents/Teachers` booleans. Cascade deletes from Announcement to its children. |","+| FR-1 | DM | 2 enums, 4 models, 1 migration. AnnouncementRead has a composite PK `(announcementId, userId)`. **Needed beyond the PRD's model** (flag as deliberate additions): `Announcement.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` (FR-25), `notifiedAt DateTime?` (FR-27, likely already in the spec since FR-27 names it), and indexes `AnnouncementAudience @@index([type, refId])` and `Announcement @@index([status, publishAt])` (NFR-2). AnnouncementAudience columns implied by FR-3..FR-6: `type`, `refId?` (null for SCHOOL/STAFF), `includeStudents/Parents/Teachers` booleans. Cascade deletes from Announcement to its children. |"," | FR-2 | XC / validation | `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts`, isomorphic Zod schema, shared by the composer and the handlers. Also validate: `expiresAt > publishAt` when both are set; ROLE refId ∈ Role enum; refId required unless SCHOOL/STAFF; at least one include flag true for GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION/COURSE. |"," | FR-3 | SVC | `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`. `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` returns a set union over the rows, all filtered to `ACTIVE && archivedAt null`. SCHOOL = all, STAFF = role ∈ {ADMIN, TEACHER}, ROLE = role = refId. Do the active filter **once** at the end, including on parents. |"," | FR-4 | SVC | GRADE_LEVEL: students via `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`; parents via ParentStudentLink of **those students** (before the active filter on the students? see §4 A3); teachers = `teacherId` ∪ `coTeacherIds` of courses where `section.gradeLevelId = refId AND academicYear.isCurrent`. |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HjSXBeg1uXyCQKao33kZeE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
