hat's already in the code:** 22 facts about the existing code that affect this ticket, each with the file and line it comes from.\n- **Per-requirement concerns:** a table mapping all 47 requirements (FR-1 to FR-36, NFR-1 to NFR-11) to what each one needs architecturally.\n- **Risks:** 11 conflicts and risks for `arch-design-system` to resolve.\n- **Assumptions:** 8 assumptions carried over from intake, which belong in the Overview section of `system-design.md`.\n\nWhat `arch-design-system` most needs to know:\n- **Audience matching:** two code paths have to agree on who is in an audience. I recommend building one set of membership keys per user. That set drives a single-user check, the feed query and the unread count, so the rules live in one place. The function that expands an audience into a full user list is tested against it.\n- **Notification setting conflict:** FR-26 wants announcement notifications to be forced in-app only when acknowledgement is required. The notification type registry is a fixed list, so that setting can't change per announcement. I suggest two types, `announcement.published` and `announcement.published_ack`; the design sub-task should make the final call.\n- **Reminder limit (decided here):** a second reminder within 24 hours returns 429 RATE_LIMITED. The time of the last reminder is stored in a new nullable `lastRemindedAt` column and claimed atomically.\n- **Files on drafts:** uploaded files with no owner record are deleted after 24 hours. Drafts must therefore link their cover image and attachments on every save, or the files disappear.\n- **Additions to the specified data model:** `lastRemindedAt`, plus two database indexes needed to meet the 200 ms feed target. These go beyond FR-1's \"exactly as specified\", so they are flagged as deliberate.\n- **No plain-text helper exists:** the 200-character card excerpt and 300-character email body need a new small Markdown-to-plain-text function.\n\nThere are no blockers. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are still SH-11 leftovers, and the other sub-tasks need to overwrite them.","ttft_ms":2171,"type":"result","duration_ms":166169,"uuid":"bd6d709e-219f-46ab-9bc5-b3a61760dae5","ttft_stream_ms":1101,"time_to_request_ms":207,"first_content_frame_ms":1101,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":20,"outputTokens":16986,"cacheReadInputTokens":486068,"cacheCreationInputTokens":69335,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8315836,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1287,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":53370,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":15965,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
