{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsjiSo75Mr8LqX1Erm3u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AnCxdcDNTxEHjA3Dia73yx","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-13\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:00:00Z), PRD-13 Direct Messaging. It has 32 FRs and 11 NFRs (43 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. The open decisions intake handed to the architect are in §4.\n\n> Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is left over from an earlier ticket (SH-12/SH-11). Its owning sub-task must overwrite it. None of those files is an SH-13 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-13 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no messaging models. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. `User` has `role`, `status` (default INVITED) and `archivedAt`, with `@@index([role, status])`. `FileObject` back-relations are explicit per attachment table. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1..4: one new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_messaging`). Add back-relations on `User` (participants, sent messages, reports filed/reviewed, settings, pending emails) and on `FileObject` (`messageAttachments`). |\n| B2 | `Notification` has **no entity/context column**: only `userId, type, title, body, link, readAt`, indexed on `(userId, readAt, createdAt)`. | schema L304-317 | FR-19 collapsing: \"replace older unread message.received rows for that conversation\" can only key on `link = /messages/<conversationId>` (plus `type` and `readAt: null`). Recommend `deleteMany({ userId in, type:'message.received', readAt:null, link })` before `notify()`. This is fine for performance because the leading `userId` index column applies. No schema change to Notification is needed. |\n| B3 | `notify()` writes the in-app rows **and enqueues email immediately** (EmailOutbox) when `input.email` is passed. It never throws and dedupes userIds. It filters DISABLED/ARCHIVED users. Preferences come from `resolvePrefs(def, pref)` in `notifications/preferences.ts`. | notify.ts L8-80 | FR-19/20 conflict: message email must be **deferred**. Call `notify()` for `message.received` **without** `email`, so only the in-app row is written. Upsert a `PendingMessageEmail` per recipient whose resolved `prefs.email` is true. The maintenance pass then re-checks `lastReadAt`/quiet hours and enqueues to EmailOutbox using the same `renderEmail('generic-notification')`. **arch-design-system** should define a small exported helper (e.g. `enqueueEmail(userIds, …)` or reuse of `resolvePrefs`) rather than duplicating notify's internals. |\n| B4 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). The `COMMUNICATION` category exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a static boolean per type and `roles` is a per-type role list. | notifications/types.ts | FR-19: `message.received` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp false, roles ALL}. FR-26: `message.reported` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true, roles ['ADMIN']}. |\n| B5 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` is a per-process sliding window that returns `{ ok, retryAfterMs }`. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-4: `rateLimit('msg:'+userId, 30, 60_000)`. On failure, throw `AppError('RATE_LIMITED')` (429) with `details.retryAfterMs`. The limiter is per-process. This is accepted (existing ponytail note). |\n| B6 | `registerFileAccess`: built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (files/contexts.ts). Unattached files (`contextId null`) are owner/ADMIN only. Resolver errors deny. Orphan files are purged after 24 h. | files/access.ts; files/contexts.ts | FR-27: add `register('message', messageResolver)` in `registerBuiltInContexts`. The resolver loads the Message by `file.contextId` (contextId = **messageId**, so a soft-deleted message can still be resolved), then allows a participant (`leftAt` irrelevant? see A7) or `isSafeguardingLead`. Attach files in the send transaction, or they are purged. Note: `FileAccessUser` is `{id, role}` only, so the resolver must query `isSafeguardingLead` itself. |\n| B7 | `SessionUser` = `{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}`. It has **no `isSafeguardingLead`**. | requireRole.ts L14-26 | NFR-1/FR-23..25: add a `requireSafeguardingLead()` helper (in `src/server/messaging/` or auth) that does `requireRole('ADMIN')` plus a DB read of the flag. Do not put the flag in the JWT: a revoked flag must take effect immediately. The page variant redirects to /forbidden (FR-23 says \"others get 403\"). |\n| B8 | Teacher→student reachability already exists: `getAccessibleStudentIds(TEACHER)` = ACTIVE enrollment in courses where `teacherId` or `coTeacherIds has` the teacher, **plus** SectionMember of sections they homeroom. The homeroom branch has **no academic-year filter**. `teaches(user, course)` is in course-access.ts. | student-access.ts L20-55; course-access.ts | FR-5/FR-32: reuse the same predicates (ideally share the Prisma `where` fragments) so contact rules and student-record access never disagree. Decide on the current-year filter for homeroom (A5). The PARENT branch is ParentStudentLink. |\n| B9 | `Enrollment @@unique([courseId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId, status])`. `ParentStudentLink @@unique([parentId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId])`. `SectionMember @@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` (no `sectionId` index). | schema | FR-5/FR-8 queries are index-backed from the student side. `coTeacherIds has` is not indexable, but a single user's course set is small. |\n| B10 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (CRON_SECRET) runs each job in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take)` → conditional `updateMany` claim → act if `count===1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts | FR-20: add `sendDueMessageEmails(now)`, isolated in its own try/catch. Process `PendingMessageEmail where dueAt <= now`. If the participant's `lastReadAt >= message time`, drop the row. If now is inside quiet hours, push `dueAt` to the end of quiet hours. Otherwise enqueue and delete the row (delete = claim; `deleteMany` count===1). |\n| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` lives in `assignments-service.ts` (precedent: other modules import it). `schoolNow(now, tz)` returns `{isoDay, hhmm}`. `formatInSchoolTz`, and `fromZonedTime` from date-fns-tz, are available. | src/lib/dates.ts; assignments-service.ts L64 | FR-20/21 quiet hours: a pure `isInQuietHours(hhmm, start, end)` with midnight wrap (`start > end`) and `quietHoursEnd(now, tz, end)` → UTC instant. Unit-test both (NFR-10). FR-10 day grouping uses `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes `RATE_LIMITED`, `FORBIDDEN`, `NOT_FOUND`, `CONFLICT`, `VALIDATION`. `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `audit()` exist. | src/server/http.ts; src/server/audit.ts | FR-28/NFR-6 handler conventions. Recommend returning 404 (not 403) for a non-participant on `GET /api/conversations/:id`, so cuids reveal nothing (NFR-1). FR-6 explicitly mandates 403 for **create** violations. |\n| B13 | **No admin user-edit UI exists.** `src/app/(app)/admin` has only attendance, courses, email-log, grading-scales, report-cards and sections. Users are edited only via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (ADMIN, `updateUserSchema`, audited). | src/app/api/users/[id]/route.ts; src/lib/validators/users.ts L103 | FR-2 resolution (intake's open question): add `isSafeguardingLead: z.boolean().optional()` to `updateUserSchema`. Reject or ignore it when the target role ≠ ADMIN. Audit the change (`user.update` metadata). **No form to extend.** Building a user-admin page is out of scope. |\n| B14 | **`/students/[id]` has no page.tsx or layout.tsx.** There are only sub-pages (attendance, assignments, courses, grades, report-cards), so there is no shared \"student page header\" today. | find src/app/(app)/students | FR-16: arch-design-system must pick the surface. Options: (a) add `students/[id]/layout.tsx` with a PageHeader + actions (affects all sub-pages, minimal per-page edits), or (b) put actions on each sub-page header. Recommend (a), keeping the `[id]` segment (no rename, per the PRD). The actions are client components that call `POST /api/conversations`. |\n| B15 | The course roster page is a **server component** rendering an MUI Table with no selection. PARENT gets notFound and STUDENT sees a name list. | courses/[courseId]/roster/page.tsx | FR-17: extract the TEACHER/ADMIN table into a client component with Checkbox selection and a toolbar button \"Message selected students\". It opens the FR-12 dialog prefilled. Rows carry `enrollmentId`, so the student id needs to be included in `RosterEntry` if it is not already there. |\n| B16 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `NotificationBell` implements a visibility-gated 30 s poll + MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L23-73 | FR-18: add `{label:'Messages', href:'/messages', roles: ALL_ROLES}` and an optional `badge?: 'messages'` key. The shell renders a polled Badge from `/api/messaging/unread-count`. Extract the bell's poll loop into a small `usePolling(fn, ms)` hook and reuse it for FR-13's 5 s/30 s polls. |\n| B17 | `/account/notifications` = page.tsx + `PreferencesTable.tsx`. `/api/me/*` routes exist (notification-preferences, profile, …). | src/app/(app)/account/notifications | FR-21: add a `QuietHoursSection` client component under that page, plus `src/app/api/me/messaging-settings/route.ts` (GET/PUT, any role). |\n| B18 | Seed users: Alice Admin, Tom Teacher, Tina Tutor, Sam Student, Sara Scholar and Pat Parent (by email). The seed creates **no ParentStudentLink** and no enrollments. Courses come from elsewhere and `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` skips when missing. | prisma/seed.ts L16-22, L304 | FR-29: set `isSafeguardingLead=true` on Alice. The Pat↔Tom thread \"about Sam's homework\" needs a Pat↔Sam link to satisfy contact rules at runtime. Recommend the seed upsert that link (or skip the thread with a log, like other seeds). The MATH-7A group uses the first 4 ACTIVE enrollments and skips if there are fewer or the course is missing. Seeds write via Prisma directly (bypassing canMessage) but must leave data valid under canMessage. Make it idempotent by checking for existing seeded conversations (subject/participants). |\n| B19 | Shared components: FileUpload, FileList, UserAvatar, UserPicker, ConfirmDialog, Toast, EmptyState, PageHeader, DataTable (in `src/components/<Name>/`). `@mui/x-date-pickers` is installed. | src/components | FR-10/11/12/23/24: reuse FileList/FileUpload (context 'message'), UserAvatar, ConfirmDialog (delete/leave), Toast (report confirmation), DataTable (safeguarding lists). FR-12 recipient picker: UserPicker is a candidate only if it accepts a custom options source (grouped contacts). Otherwise use MUI Autocomplete with `groupBy`. FR-21 time inputs: x-date-pickers TimePicker. |\n| B20 | The mui-mcp server failed to connect in this session (CONNECT_TIMEOUT). | session | NFR-5 requires mui-mcp lookups during dev. The dev phase must retry it. This is not a blocker for architecture. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend: DM = data model/migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance job, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | Conversation, ConversationParticipant (`@@unique([conversationId,userId])`, `@@index([userId])`, per-user `lastReadAt`, `mutedAt`/`archivedAt`, `leftAt`), Message (`@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, which NFR-2 depends on; `editedAt`, `deletedAt`), MessageAttachment (messageId, fileId; cascade on message), MessageReport + `ReportStatus`, MessagingSettings (userId unique, quietStart/End `String? HH:mm`). Add `updatedAt` per convention (A2). |\n| FR-2 | DM, API, AUTH | `User.isSafeguardingLead`. It can only be edited via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (B13) and is meaningful only for ADMIN. |\n| FR-3 | DM, SVC | `MessageRevision(messageId, body, createdAt)`, `@@index([messageId])`. Written in the same tx as the edit (original body before overwrite). Cascade with Message (messages are never hard-deleted anyway, NFR-3). |\n| FR-4 | DM, JOB | `PendingMessageEmail(userId, conversationId, dueAt)`, `@@unique([userId, conversationId])` so repeated sends upsert one row (the first unread message sets dueAt = now+10 min; later sends keep the earliest dueAt). `@@index([dueAt])`. |\n| FR-5 | SVC, AUTH | `canMessage(sender, recipient)` is a pure decision over pre-loaded relationship facts. Expose a batch form `messageableIds(sender, candidateIds)` to avoid N+1 queries for groups (≤25) and contacts (FR-8). Matrix: ADMIN→any, any→ADMIN, TEACHER↔TEACHER, TEACHER→STUDENT (managed course or homeroom, B8), TEACHER→PARENT (via the linked child under the same rule), STUDENT→own teachers, PARENT→linked child's teachers, all others false. Symmetry: student→teacher uses the same relation as teacher→student. Disabled/archived recipients → false. |\n| FR-6 | SVC, AUTH | Create conversation in one tx: participants = creator ∪ recipients (dedupe, exclude self from count rules), 2..25 total. Check `canMessage(creator, each)`. If any STUDENT is present, require ≥1 TEACHER/ADMIN. Any violation → 403 with nothing created. \"Students may reply in staff groups but cannot start student-student\" follows from canMessage(student, student)=false at create, plus the send-time rule (FR-7) being evaluated per-sender against **staff** participants only (A4). |\n| FR-7 | SVC, AUTH, UI | Send-time re-check. Non-staff sender: allowed iff canMessage(sender, p) holds for at least one remaining staff participant (A4). Otherwise 403 with code/reason `RELATIONSHIP_ENDED`. Staff always pass. `GET /api/conversations/:id` returns `canSend: boolean` so the composer shows the disabled message without a failed POST. |\n| FR-8 | SVC, API | `GET /api/messaging/contacts?q=`: role-specific grouped queries (PARENT: per child, \"My child's teachers (<child>)\"; STUDENT: \"My teachers\"; TEACHER: \"Students in <course>\", \"Parents of students in <course>\", homeroom, staff; all: \"School office\" = ADMINs). Status ACTIVE only. `q` filters on name. Cap each group (e.g. 50). |\n| FR-9 | UI, API | `/messages` layout with a two-pane `useMediaQuery(theme.breakpoints.down('md'))`, single pane + back below 768 px (theme `md`=900, so use a custom `down(768)` or confirm breakpoint, A8). List from `GET /api/conversations?archived=&q=` sorted `lastMessageAt desc`, with preview and `unreadCount` per row. Route: `/messages` and `/messages/[conversationId]`. |\n| FR-10 | UI, API | `GET /api/conversations/:id/messages?before=<id>&limit=30` (keyset on `(createdAt,id)`). Deleted messages are returned with `body: null, deleted: true` and attachments stripped for normal users (NFR-3: content is never exposed to non-safeguarding users). Day grouping in the school timezone (B11). |\n| FR-11 | UI, XC | Composer validation shared by the client and `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts` (body trim 1..5000, ≤5 fileIds). Enter=send / Shift+Enter=newline. Counter shows at >4500. |\n| FR-12 | UI | New-conversation dialog: Autocomplete multi-select grouped by contacts label, subject ≤120, first message. It posts `POST /api/conversations` with `{participantIds, subject?, body, fileIds?}`, creating the conversation + first message atomically. Also opened prefilled from FR-16/FR-17. |\n| FR-13 | UI, API, XC | 5 s poll of `?after=<lastId>` on the visible thread. 30 s poll on the list + nav badge. Gate on `document.visibilityState` (B16). The `after` query must also surface **edits/deletes** of already-loaded messages, or edits only appear on reload (A9). |\n| FR-14 | API, SVC, UI | `POST /api/conversations/:id/read` (sets lastReadAt=now and marks this conversation's unread `message.received` notifications read; deletes the PendingMessageEmail row), `/mute`, `/archive` (toggle body `{archived}`), `/leave`. Leave: set `leftAt`, which blocks further reads/sends for that user. Refuse (409/403) for the creator when `involvesStudent` is true. Group-only: DMs with 2 participants cannot be left (A10). Sending auto-unarchives for other participants? (A11). |\n| FR-15 | SVC, API | `PATCH /api/messages/:id` / `DELETE` (soft: `deletedAt`). Sender only, `now - createdAt ≤ 15 min`, not already deleted. Edit writes a MessageRevision + `editedAt` in one tx. No hard-delete path exists anywhere. |\n| FR-16 | UI | Student page actions (surface per B14). TEACHER/ADMIN \"Message parents\": participants = linked parents (+ creator). Hide the action if there are none or canMessage fails. PARENT \"Message teacher\": picker of the child's teachers (subset of contacts) → dialog. |\n| FR-17 | UI | Roster selection + action (B15). TEACHER only (ADMIN may also be offered, harmless). |\n| FR-18 | CFG, API, UI | Nav entry + badge (B16). `GET /api/messaging/unread-count` = count of the user's non-left participations where `lastMessageAt > coalesce(lastReadAt, epoch)` (count conversations, not messages: cheap, index-friendly). Archived conversations excluded? (A11). |\n| FR-19 | NOTIF, SVC | After the send tx commits: for each other participant not muted and not left, delete older unread `message.received` rows with the same link (B2), then `notify()` in-app only (B3). Title \"New message from <sender>\", body = 200-char plain preview, link `/messages/<id>`. |\n| FR-20 | JOB, DM, NOTIF | Upsert a PendingMessageEmail (dueAt=now+10 min) for recipients whose email pref is on (B3). Job per B10. Quiet hours read from MessagingSettings, evaluated in the school timezone (B11). |\n| FR-21 | UI, API, DM | MessagingSettings GET (defaults: no quiet hours) / PUT, Zod `HH:mm` regex. Both-or-neither validation. start == end is rejected. Applies to all roles (A3). |\n| FR-22 | API, SVC, NOTIF | `POST /api/messages/:id/report {reason ≤1000}`. Participant only. Allowed on own/others' messages (or other people's only? A12). One OPEN report per (message, reporter) to avoid spam (unique or check). Then FR-26 notify. |\n| FR-23 | UI, API, AUTH, XC | `/admin/safeguarding` (tabs Reports / Conversations), gated by `requireSafeguardingLead` (B7). `GET /api/safeguarding/reports?status=` with OPEN first, then createdAt desc. Detail includes the message, ±5 messages (including deleted and with revisions) and participants. `PATCH /api/safeguarding/reports/:id {action: review\\|dismiss, note?}` sets status, reviewedById, reviewedAt and note, then calls `audit()` (NFR-11). The nav entry is shown only to leads (the nav filter is role-based, so either show it to ADMIN and 403 non-leads, or extend NavItem with a predicate, A13). |\n| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH | `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations?participantId=&from=&to=` with `involvesStudent: true`, paginated. `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations/:id` = read-only full thread with deleted bodies and `revisions[]`. Same lead gate. |\n| FR-25 | XC, AUTH | `audit({action:'safeguarding.conversation.view', entityType:'Conversation', entityId})` on every safeguarding conversation view **and** on report detail views, since they expose conversation context. Done in the service, so both the API and the server page paths are covered. |\n| FR-26 | NOTIF | Notify `User where role=ADMIN, isSafeguardingLead, status ACTIVE` with `message.reported` (email allowed via notify's normal path: no deferral). Link `/admin/safeguarding?report=<id>`. The body must not include the message text (keep emails minimal). |\n| FR-27 | FILE, AUTH | B6. Send validates that each fileId is owned by the sender, unattached, and context 'message', then attaches in the tx (contextId = messageId). |\n| FR-28 | API, XC | All routes under `src/app/api/{conversations,messages,messaging,safeguarding,me/messaging-settings}`. Thin handlers + Zod + services in `src/server/messaging/`. Standard ok/paginated/error shapes. |\n| FR-29 | SEED | B18. |\n| FR-30 | SVC, DM | `involvesStudent` is computed in the create tx and is immutable afterwards (no participant-add API exists, so it stays correct). |\n| FR-31 | SVC | Update `lastMessageAt` in the send tx. `@@index` on ConversationParticipant `(userId)` + Conversation `lastMessageAt` serves the list ordering. Edits/deletes do **not** bump it. |\n| FR-32 | AUTH | B8: `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`. Resolved as yes (intake default, matches the existing `teaches()`). |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH, XC | Every service entry takes the SessionUser and loads `ConversationParticipant(conversationId, userId, leftAt null)` first. Non-participant → 404. Safeguarding → `requireSafeguardingLead`. File resolver per B6. Contacts never leak non-messageable users. |\n| NFR-2 | DM, API | `after` poll = participant check (unique-index lookup) + `Message where conversationId, (createdAt,id) > cursor` on `@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, `take 100`. Return `[]` fast. The 30 s list/unread polls use the participant index. Avoid count-per-message aggregation for unread (FR-18). |\n| NFR-3 | DM, SVC, AUTH | No DELETE that removes rows. FK cascades exist only for actual tree cleanup. Deleted/edited originals are exposed only through safeguarding services. |\n| NFR-4 | API, XC | B5. Applies to `POST /api/conversations/:id/messages`. Recommend counting `POST /api/conversations` (it also sends) against the same key. |\n| NFR-5 | UI, XC | MUI only; B19/B20. Badge, Drawer/List, Autocomplete, TimePicker, Tabs, Menu, Chip, TextField. |\n| NFR-6 | XC | `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts`, `src/server/messaging/{contact-rules,conversations,messages,notifications,quiet-hours,safeguarding,maintenance}.ts`, logger, cuid, UTC storage. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | See FR-9 (breakpoint, A8). |\n| NFR-8 | XC | A 5 s poll guarantees ≤ ~5 s + request latency < 6 s. No websockets/SSE. |\n| NFR-9 | XC | There is no reactions, typing or broadcast endpoint. Do not touch announcements (PRD-12 is absent). |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | `tests/unit/messaging/contact-rules.test.ts` (matrix incl. co-teacher, homeroom, DROPPED enrollment, group student-needs-staff, 26 participants), `quiet-hours.test.ts` (wrap midnight). `tests/integration/messaging/` (notification collapse, quiet-hours deferral via maintenance job, revision capture, 15-min window, rate limit, non-participant 404, safeguarding 403 + audit). `tests/e2e/messaging.spec.ts` (two browser contexts parent→teacher < 6 s; student→student blocked in the picker and on POST 403). |\n| NFR-11 | XC | Audit report review/dismiss and `isSafeguardingLead` changes. Users' own edits/deletes of their messages are not \"someone else's\" records, so no audit is needed. |\n\n## 3. New surface summary (for traceability)\n\n- **Models:** Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageAttachment, MessageRevision, MessageReport (+ReportStatus), MessagingSettings, PendingMessageEmail. Plus User.isSafeguardingLead. (FR-1..4, FR-30, FR-31)\n- **Services (`src/server/messaging/`):** contact-rules, contacts, conversations, messages, read-state, notifications/pending-email, quiet-hours, safeguarding, maintenance (`sendDueMessageEmails`). (FR-5..8, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19..27)\n- **Routes:** conversations (list/create/get/read/mute/archive/leave), conversation messages (list before/after, send), messages/:id (patch/delete/report), messaging/unread-count, messaging/contacts, me/messaging-settings, safeguarding reports + conversations, and a hook into the internal dispatch route. (FR-28, FR-20)\n- **Pages:** `/messages`, `/messages/[conversationId]`, `/admin/safeguarding`, plus a Quiet hours section on `/account/notifications`, student layout actions and roster selection. (FR-9..18, FR-21, FR-23, FR-24)\n- **Registries:** 2 notification types, 1 file context, 1 nav item (+badge). (FR-18, FR-19, FR-26, FR-27)\n\n## 4. Open decisions for arch-design-system\n\n| # | Question | Recommendation | Drives |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A1 | Co-teachers count as \"managing\" a course? | **Yes**: matches `teaches()`/`getAccessibleStudentIds`. | FR-32, FR-5 |\n| A2 | `updatedAt` on new models (the PRD block omits it)? | Add `updatedAt @updatedAt` to Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageReport and MessagingSettings (platform convention). Leave it off append-only MessageRevision, MessageAttachment and PendingMessageEmail. Treat the PRD block as the minimum field set. | FR-1, NFR-6 |\n| A3 | Quiet hours for all roles? | **All roles** (the settings endpoint is open to any role). | FR-21, FR-20 |\n| A4 | Send-time rule in groups: what does \"relationship ended\" mean when there are many participants? | Non-staff sender may send iff canMessage(sender, s) for ≥1 staff participant still present. If no staff remain (all left), they are refused. Note that staff can never leave a student group they created (FR-14). | FR-7, FR-6 |\n| A5 | Homeroom teacher reachability: current academic year only? | Filter `section.academicYear.isCurrent = true` for messaging (otherwise last year's homeroom stays reachable). Keep student-access.ts unchanged (do not modify other PRDs' behaviour). | FR-5 |\n| A6 | Where is isSafeguardingLead edited? | API/validator only (no form exists, B13). Document that the flag is set via the seed or the API. | FR-2 |\n| A7 | Does a participant who **left** keep read access to the old thread and attachments? | No: `leftAt` set → treat as non-participant (list hides it, 404 on get). Safeguarding still sees everything. | FR-14, FR-27, NFR-1 |\n| A8 | The 768 px breakpoint does not match MUI default `md` (900). | Use `theme.breakpoints.down(768)` locally, not a theme change. | FR-9, NFR-7 |\n| A9 | How do polling clients learn about edits/deletes? | `after` responses also return `changed[]` = messages in the loaded window with `updatedAt > since` (pass `since` ISO alongside `after`). Alternatively accept staleness until reload. Recommend the former (cheap; same index plus `updatedAt`). | FR-13, FR-15 |\n| A10 | Can a participant leave a 1:1 conversation? | No: \"leave group\" only applies when there are >2 participants. Archive covers 1:1. | FR-14 |\n| A11 | Does a new message unarchive the conversation for recipients, and does the unread badge count archived conversations? | Yes, unarchive for recipients on new message (standard inbox behaviour). Unread count then needs no archive filter. | FR-9, FR-14, FR-18 |\n| A12 | Can a user report their own message, or report the same message twice? | Others' messages only. One OPEN report per (message, reporter): return 409 CONFLICT otherwise. | FR-22 |\n| A13 | Nav visibility for `/admin/safeguarding` (role-only nav filter)? | Show the item to ADMIN only via a new optional `NavItem.requires?: 'safeguardingLead'` evaluated in the shell with the flag loaded server-side. The page still enforces 403. Otherwise leave it out of nav and link from the `message.reported` notification. | FR-23 |\n| A14 | Seed Pat↔Sam link missing (B18). | The seed upserts `ParentStudentLink(Pat, Sam)` if absent before creating the Pat↔Tom thread, and skips the thread if Tom does not teach Sam. | FR-29 |\n\n## 5. Risks\n\n- **Notification collapse via `link` match** (B2) is coupled to the link format. Keep link building in a single helper used by both send and read paths.\n- **Per-process rate limiter and in-memory state** (B5) are not shared across instances. This is accepted per the existing ponytail note.\n- **Email-preference bypass**: deferring email outside `notify()` (B3) must still honour `NotificationPreference` and DISABLED/ARCHIVED filtering. Reuse `resolvePrefs`, and cover it in integration tests.\n- **mui-mcp unavailable** in this session (B20). The dev phase must retry it before writing UI.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1309,"cache_read_input_tokens":56604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1309},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"56451f7d-c784-4a25-a233-3bc873207cca","uuid":"301f8646-fcb5-422b-aa87-4ddad722e34b","timestamp":"2026-11-09T17:21:33.119Z","request_id":"req_011CgsjiSLp9rDNDCKaxSpMS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AnCxdcDNTxEHjA3Dia73yx":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-13\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:00:00Z), PRD-13 Direct Messaging. It has 32 FRs and 11 NFRs (43 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. The open decisions intake handed to the architect are in §4.\n\n> Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is left over from an earlier ticket (SH-12/SH-11). Its owning sub-task must overwrite it. None of those files is an SH-13 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-13 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no messaging models. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. `User` has `role`, `status` (default INVITED) and `archivedAt`, with `@@index([role, status])`. `FileObject` back-relations are explicit per attachment table. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1..4: one new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_messaging`). Add back-relations on `User` (participants, sent messages, reports filed/reviewed, settings, pending emails) and on `FileObject` (`messageAttachments`). |\n| B2 | `Notification` has **no entity/context column**: only `userId, type, title, body, link, readAt`, indexed on `(userId, readAt, createdAt)`. | schema L304-317 | FR-19 collapsing: \"replace older unread message.received rows for that conversation\" can only key on `link = /messages/<conversationId>` (plus `type` and `readAt: null`). Recommend `deleteMany({ userId in, type:'message.received', readAt:null, link })` before `notify()`. This is fine for performance because the leading `userId` index column applies. No schema change to Notification is needed. |\n| B3 | `notify()` writes the in-app rows **and enqueues email immediately** (EmailOutbox) when `input.email` is passed. It never throws and dedupes userIds. It filters DISABLED/ARCHIVED users. Preferences come from `resolvePrefs(def, pref)` in `notifications/preferences.ts`. | notify.ts L8-80 | FR-19/20 conflict: message email must be **deferred**. Call `notify()` for `message.received` **without** `email`, so only the in-app row is written. Upsert a `PendingMessageEmail` per recipient whose resolved `prefs.email` is true. The maintenance pass then re-checks `lastReadAt`/quiet hours and enqueues to EmailOutbox using the same `renderEmail('generic-notification')`. **arch-design-system** should define a small exported helper (e.g. `enqueueEmail(userIds, …)` or reuse of `resolvePrefs`) rather than duplicating notify's internals. |\n| B4 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). The `COMMUNICATION` category exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a static boolean per type and `roles` is a per-type role list. | notifications/types.ts | FR-19: `message.received` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp false, roles ALL}. FR-26: `message.reported` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true, roles ['ADMIN']}. |\n| B5 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` is a per-process sliding window that returns `{ ok, retryAfterMs }`. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-4: `rateLimit('msg:'+userId, 30, 60_000)`. On failure, throw `AppError('RATE_LIMITED')` (429) with `details.retryAfterMs`. The limiter is per-process. This is accepted (existing ponytail note). |\n| B6 | `registerFileAccess`: built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (files/contexts.ts). Unattached files (`contextId null`) are owner/ADMIN only. Resolver errors deny. Orphan files are purged after 24 h. | files/access.ts; files/contexts.ts | FR-27: add `register('message', messageResolver)` in `registerBuiltInContexts`. The resolver loads the Message by `file.contextId` (contextId = **messageId**, so a soft-deleted message can still be resolved), then allows a participant (`leftAt` irrelevant? see A7) or `isSafeguardingLead`. Attach files in the send transaction, or they are purged. Note: `FileAccessUser` is `{id, role}` only, so the resolver must query `isSafeguardingLead` itself. |\n| B7 | `SessionUser` = `{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}`. It has **no `isSafeguardingLead`**. | requireRole.ts L14-26 | NFR-1/FR-23..25: add a `requireSafeguardingLead()` helper (in `src/server/messaging/` or auth) that does `requireRole('ADMIN')` plus a DB read of the flag. Do not put the flag in the JWT: a revoked flag must take effect immediately. The page variant redirects to /forbidden (FR-23 says \"others get 403\"). |\n| B8 | Teacher→student reachability already exists: `getAccessibleStudentIds(TEACHER)` = ACTIVE enrollment in courses where `teacherId` or `coTeacherIds has` the teacher, **plus** SectionMember of sections they homeroom. The homeroom branch has **no academic-year filter**. `teaches(user, course)` is in course-access.ts. | student-access.ts L20-55; course-access.ts | FR-5/FR-32: reuse the same predicates (ideally share the Prisma `where` fragments) so contact rules and student-record access never disagree. Decide on the current-year filter for homeroom (A5). The PARENT branch is ParentStudentLink. |\n| B9 | `Enrollment @@unique([courseId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId, status])`. `ParentStudentLink @@unique([parentId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId])`. `SectionMember @@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` (no `sectionId` index). | schema | FR-5/FR-8 queries are index-backed from the student side. `coTeacherIds has` is not indexable, but a single user's course set is small. |\n| B10 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (CRON_SECRET) runs each job in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take)` → conditional `updateMany` claim → act if `count===1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts | FR-20: add `sendDueMessageEmails(now)`, isolated in its own try/catch. Process `PendingMessageEmail where dueAt <= now`. If the participant's `lastReadAt >= message time`, drop the row. If now is inside quiet hours, push `dueAt` to the end of quiet hours. Otherwise enqueue and delete the row (delete = claim; `deleteMany` count===1). |\n| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` lives in `assignments-service.ts` (precedent: other modules import it). `schoolNow(now, tz)` returns `{isoDay, hhmm}`. `formatInSchoolTz`, and `fromZonedTime` from date-fns-tz, are available. | src/lib/dates.ts; assignments-service.ts L64 | FR-20/21 quiet hours: a pure `isInQuietHours(hhmm, start, end)` with midnight wrap (`start > end`) and `quietHoursEnd(now, tz, end)` → UTC instant. Unit-test both (NFR-10). FR-10 day grouping uses `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes `RATE_LIMITED`, `FORBIDDEN`, `NOT_FOUND`, `CONFLICT`, `VALIDATION`. `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `audit()` exist. | src/server/http.ts; src/server/audit.ts | FR-28/NFR-6 handler conventions. Recommend returning 404 (not 403) for a non-participant on `GET /api/conversations/:id`, so cuids reveal nothing (NFR-1). FR-6 explicitly mandates 403 for **create** violations. |\n| B13 | **No admin user-edit UI exists.** `src/app/(app)/admin` has only attendance, courses, email-log, grading-scales, report-cards and sections. Users are edited only via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (ADMIN, `updateUserSchema`, audited). | src/app/api/users/[id]/route.ts; src/lib/validators/users.ts L103 | FR-2 resolution (intake's open question): add `isSafeguardingLead: z.boolean().optional()` to `updateUserSchema`. Reject or ignore it when the target role ≠ ADMIN. Audit the change (`user.update` metadata). **No form to extend.** Building a user-admin page is out of scope. |\n| B14 | **`/students/[id]` has no page.tsx or layout.tsx.** There are only sub-pages (attendance, assignments, courses, grades, report-cards), so there is no shared \"student page header\" today. | find src/app/(app)/students | FR-16: arch-design-system must pick the surface. Options: (a) add `students/[id]/layout.tsx` with a PageHeader + actions (affects all sub-pages, minimal per-page edits), or (b) put actions on each sub-page header. Recommend (a), keeping the `[id]` segment (no rename, per the PRD). The actions are client components that call `POST /api/conversations`. |\n| B15 | The course roster page is a **server component** rendering an MUI Table with no selection. PARENT gets notFound and STUDENT sees a name list. | courses/[courseId]/roster/page.tsx | FR-17: extract the TEACHER/ADMIN table into a client component with Checkbox selection and a toolbar button \"Message selected students\". It opens the FR-12 dialog prefilled. Rows carry `enrollmentId`, so the student id needs to be included in `RosterEntry` if it is not already there. |\n| B16 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `NotificationBell` implements a visibility-gated 30 s poll + MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L23-73 | FR-18: add `{label:'Messages', href:'/messages', roles: ALL_ROLES}` and an optional `badge?: 'messages'` key. The shell renders a polled Badge from `/api/messaging/unread-count`. Extract the bell's poll loop into a small `usePolling(fn, ms)` hook and reuse it for FR-13's 5 s/30 s polls. |\n| B17 | `/account/notifications` = page.tsx + `PreferencesTable.tsx`. `/api/me/*` routes exist (notification-preferences, profile, …). | src/app/(app)/account/notifications | FR-21: add a `QuietHoursSection` client component under that page, plus `src/app/api/me/messaging-settings/route.ts` (GET/PUT, any role). |\n| B18 | Seed users: Alice Admin, Tom Teacher, Tina Tutor, Sam Student, Sara Scholar and Pat Parent (by email). The seed creates **no ParentStudentLink** and no enrollments. Courses come from elsewhere and `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` skips when missing. | prisma/seed.ts L16-22, L304 | FR-29: set `isSafeguardingLead=true` on Alice. The Pat↔Tom thread \"about Sam's homework\" needs a Pat↔Sam link to satisfy contact rules at runtime. Recommend the seed upsert that link (or skip the thread with a log, like other seeds). The MATH-7A group uses the first 4 ACTIVE enrollments and skips if there are fewer or the course is missing. Seeds write via Prisma directly (bypassing canMessage) but must leave data valid under canMessage. Make it idempotent by checking for existing seeded conversations (subject/participants). |\n| B19 | Shared components: FileUpload, FileList, UserAvatar, UserPicker, ConfirmDialog, Toast, EmptyState, PageHeader, DataTable (in `src/components/<Name>/`). `@mui/x-date-pickers` is installed. | src/components | FR-10/11/12/23/24: reuse FileList/FileUpload (context 'message'), UserAvatar, ConfirmDialog (delete/leave), Toast (report confirmation), DataTable (safeguarding lists). FR-12 recipient picker: UserPicker is a candidate only if it accepts a custom options source (grouped contacts). Otherwise use MUI Autocomplete with `groupBy`. FR-21 time inputs: x-date-pickers TimePicker. |\n| B20 | The mui-mcp server failed to connect in this session (CONNECT_TIMEOUT). | session | NFR-5 requires mui-mcp lookups during dev. The dev phase must retry it. This is not a blocker for architecture. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend: DM = data model/migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance job, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | Conversation, ConversationParticipant (`@@unique([conversationId,userId])`, `@@index([userId])`, per-user `lastReadAt`, `mutedAt`/`archivedAt`, `leftAt`), Message (`@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, which NFR-2 depends on; `editedAt`, `deletedAt`), MessageAttachment (messageId, fileId; cascade on message), MessageReport + `ReportStatus`, MessagingSettings (userId unique, quietStart/End `String? HH:mm`). Add `updatedAt` per convention (A2). |\n| FR-2 | DM, API, AUTH | `User.isSafeguardingLead`. It can only be edited via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (B13) and is meaningful only for ADMIN. |\n| FR-3 | DM, SVC | `MessageRevision(messageId, body, createdAt)`, `@@index([messageId])`. Written in the same tx as the edit (original body before overwrite). Cascade with Message (messages are never hard-deleted anyway, NFR-3). |\n| FR-4 | DM, JOB | `PendingMessageEmail(userId, conversationId, dueAt)`, `@@unique([userId, conversationId])` so repeated sends upsert one row (the first unread message sets dueAt = now+10 min; later sends keep the earliest dueAt). `@@index([dueAt])`. |\n| FR-5 | SVC, AUTH | `canMessage(sender, recipient)` is a pure decision over pre-loaded relationship facts. Expose a batch form `messageableIds(sender, candidateIds)` to avoid N+1 queries for groups (≤25) and contacts (FR-8). Matrix: ADMIN→any, any→ADMIN, TEACHER↔TEACHER, TEACHER→STUDENT (managed course or homeroom, B8), TEACHER→PARENT (via the linked child under the same rule), STUDENT→own teachers, PARENT→linked child's teachers, all others false. Symmetry: student→teacher uses the same relation as teacher→student. Disabled/archived recipients → false. |\n| FR-6 | SVC, AUTH | Create conversation in one tx: participants = creator ∪ recipients (dedupe, exclude self from count rules), 2..25 total. Check `canMessage(creator, each)`. If any STUDENT is present, require ≥1 TEACHER/ADMIN. Any violation → 403 with nothing created. \"Students may reply in staff groups but cannot start student-student\" follows from canMessage(student, student)=false at create, plus the send-time rule (FR-7) being evaluated per-sender against **staff** participants only (A4). |\n| FR-7 | SVC, AUTH, UI | Send-time re-check. Non-staff sender: allowed iff canMessage(sender, p) holds for at least one remaining staff participant (A4). Otherwise 403 with code/reason `RELATIONSHIP_ENDED`. Staff always pass. `GET /api/conversations/:id` returns `canSend: boolean` so the composer shows the disabled message without a failed POST. |\n| FR-8 | SVC, API | `GET /api/messaging/contacts?q=`: role-specific grouped queries (PARENT: per child, \"My child's teachers (<child>)\"; STUDENT: \"My teachers\"; TEACHER: \"Students in <course>\", \"Parents of students in <course>\", homeroom, staff; all: \"School office\" = ADMINs). Status ACTIVE only. `q` filters on name. Cap each group (e.g. 50). |\n| FR-9 | UI, API | `/messages` layout with a two-pane `useMediaQuery(theme.breakpoints.down('md'))`, single pane + back below 768 px (theme `md`=900, so use a custom `down(768)` or confirm breakpoint, A8). List from `GET /api/conversations?archived=&q=` sorted `lastMessageAt desc`, with preview and `unreadCount` per row. Route: `/messages` and `/messages/[conversationId]`. |\n| FR-10 | UI, API | `GET /api/conversations/:id/messages?before=<id>&limit=30` (keyset on `(createdAt,id)`). Deleted messages are returned with `body: null, deleted: true` and attachments stripped for normal users (NFR-3: content is never exposed to non-safeguarding users). Day grouping in the school timezone (B11). |\n| FR-11 | UI, XC | Composer validation shared by the client and `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts` (body trim 1..5000, ≤5 fileIds). Enter=send / Shift+Enter=newline. Counter shows at >4500. |\n| FR-12 | UI | New-conversation dialog: Autocomplete multi-select grouped by contacts label, subject ≤120, first message. It posts `POST /api/conversations` with `{participantIds, subject?, body, fileIds?}`, creating the conversation + first message atomically. Also opened prefilled from FR-16/FR-17. |\n| FR-13 | UI, API, XC | 5 s poll of `?after=<lastId>` on the visible thread. 30 s poll on the list + nav badge. Gate on `document.visibilityState` (B16). The `after` query must also surface **edits/deletes** of already-loaded messages, or edits only appear on reload (A9). |\n| FR-14 | API, SVC, UI | `POST /api/conversations/:id/read` (sets lastReadAt=now and marks this conversation's unread `message.received` notifications read; deletes the PendingMessageEmail row), `/mute`, `/archive` (toggle body `{archived}`), `/leave`. Leave: set `leftAt`, which blocks further reads/sends for that user. Refuse (409/403) for the creator when `involvesStudent` is true. Group-only: DMs with 2 participants cannot be left (A10). Sending auto-unarchives for other participants? (A11). |\n| FR-15 | SVC, API | `PATCH /api/messages/:id` / `DELETE` (soft: `deletedAt`). Sender only, `now - createdAt ≤ 15 min`, not already deleted. Edit writes a MessageRevision + `editedAt` in one tx. No hard-delete path exists anywhere. |\n| FR-16 | UI | Student page actions (surface per B14). TEACHER/ADMIN \"Message parents\": participants = linked parents (+ creator). Hide the action if there are none or canMessage fails. PARENT \"Message teacher\": picker of the child's teachers (subset of contacts) → dialog. |\n| FR-17 | UI | Roster selection + action (B15). TEACHER only (ADMIN may also be offered, harmless). |\n| FR-18 | CFG, API, UI | Nav entry + badge (B16). `GET /api/messaging/unread-count` = count of the user's non-left participations where `lastMessageAt > coalesce(lastReadAt, epoch)` (count conversations, not messages: cheap, index-friendly). Archived conversations excluded? (A11). |\n| FR-19 | NOTIF, SVC | After the send tx commits: for each other participant not muted and not left, delete older unread `message.received` rows with the same link (B2), then `notify()` in-app only (B3). Title \"New message from <sender>\", body = 200-char plain preview, link `/messages/<id>`. |\n| FR-20 | JOB, DM, NOTIF | Upsert a PendingMessageEmail (dueAt=now+10 min) for recipients whose email pref is on (B3). Job per B10. Quiet hours read from MessagingSettings, evaluated in the school timezone (B11). |\n| FR-21 | UI, API, DM | MessagingSettings GET (defaults: no quiet hours) / PUT, Zod `HH:mm` regex. Both-or-neither validation. start == end is rejected. Applies to all roles (A3). |\n| FR-22 | API, SVC, NOTIF | `POST /api/messages/:id/report {reason ≤1000}`. Participant only. Allowed on own/others' messages (or other people's only? A12). One OPEN report per (message, reporter) to avoid spam (unique or check). Then FR-26 notify. |\n| FR-23 | UI, API, AUTH, XC | `/admin/safeguarding` (tabs Reports / Conversations), gated by `requireSafeguardingLead` (B7). `GET /api/safeguarding/reports?status=` with OPEN first, then createdAt desc. Detail includes the message, ±5 messages (including deleted and with revisions) and participants. `PATCH /api/safeguarding/reports/:id {action: review\\|dismiss, note?}` sets status, reviewedById, reviewedAt and note, then calls `audit()` (NFR-11). The nav entry is shown only to leads (the nav filter is role-based, so either show it to ADMIN and 403 non-leads, or extend NavItem with a predicate, A13). |\n| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH | `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations?participantId=&from=&to=` with `involvesStudent: true`, paginated. `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations/:id` = read-only full thread with deleted bodies and `revisions[]`. Same lead gate. |\n| FR-25 | XC, AUTH | `audit({action:'safeguarding.conversation.view', entityType:'Conversation', entityId})` on every safeguarding conversation view **and** on report detail views, since they expose conversation context. Done in the service, so both the API and the server page paths are covered. |\n| FR-26 | NOTIF | Notify `User where role=ADMIN, isSafeguardingLead, status ACTIVE` with `message.reported` (email allowed via notify's normal path: no deferral). Link `/admin/safeguarding?report=<id>`. The body must not include the message text (keep emails minimal). |\n| FR-27 | FILE, AUTH | B6. Send validates that each fileId is owned by the sender, unattached, and context 'message', then attaches in the tx (contextId = messageId). |\n| FR-28 | API, XC | All routes under `src/app/api/{conversations,messages,messaging,safeguarding,me/messaging-settings}`. Thin handlers + Zod + services in `src/server/messaging/`. Standard ok/paginated/error shapes. |\n| FR-29 | SEED | B18. |\n| FR-30 | SVC, DM | `involvesStudent` is computed in the create tx and is immutable afterwards (no participant-add API exists, so it stays correct). |\n| FR-31 | SVC | Update `lastMessageAt` in the send tx. `@@index` on ConversationParticipant `(userId)` + Conversation `lastMessageAt` serves the list ordering. Edits/deletes do **not** bump it. |\n| FR-32 | AUTH | B8: `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`. Resolved as yes (intake default, matches the existing `teaches()`). |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH, XC | Every service entry takes the SessionUser and loads `ConversationParticipant(conversationId, userId, leftAt null)` first. Non-participant → 404. Safeguarding → `requireSafeguardingLead`. File resolver per B6. Contacts never leak non-messageable users. |\n| NFR-2 | DM, API | `after` poll = participant check (unique-index lookup) + `Message where conversationId, (createdAt,id) > cursor` on `@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, `take 100`. Return `[]` fast. The 30 s list/unread polls use the participant index. Avoid count-per-message aggregation for unread (FR-18). |\n| NFR-3 | DM, SVC, AUTH | No DELETE that removes rows. FK cascades exist only for actual tree cleanup. Deleted/edited originals are exposed only through safeguarding services. |\n| NFR-4 | API, XC | B5. Applies to `POST /api/conversations/:id/messages`. Recommend counting `POST /api/conversations` (it also sends) against the same key. |\n| NFR-5 | UI, XC | MUI only; B19/B20. Badge, Drawer/List, Autocomplete, TimePicker, Tabs, Menu, Chip, TextField. |\n| NFR-6 | XC | `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts`, `src/server/messaging/{contact-rules,conversations,messages,notifications,quiet-hours,safeguarding,maintenance}.ts`, logger, cuid, UTC storage. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | See FR-9 (breakpoint, A8). |\n| NFR-8 | XC | A 5 s poll guarantees ≤ ~5 s + request latency < 6 s. No websockets/SSE. |\n| NFR-9 | XC | There is no reactions, typing or broadcast endpoint. Do not touch announcements (PRD-12 is absent). |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | `tests/unit/messaging/contact-rules.test.ts` (matrix incl. co-teacher, homeroom, DROPPED enrollment, group student-needs-staff, 26 participants), `quiet-hours.test.ts` (wrap midnight). `tests/integration/messaging/` (notification collapse, quiet-hours deferral via maintenance job, revision capture, 15-min window, rate limit, non-participant 404, safeguarding 403 + audit). `tests/e2e/messaging.spec.ts` (two browser contexts parent→teacher < 6 s; student→student blocked in the picker and on POST 403). |\n| NFR-11 | XC | Audit report review/dismiss and `isSafeguardingLead` changes. Users' own edits/deletes of their messages are not \"someone else's\" records, so no audit is needed. |\n\n## 3. New surface summary (for traceability)\n\n- **Models:** Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageAttachment, MessageRevision, MessageReport (+ReportStatus), MessagingSettings, PendingMessageEmail. Plus User.isSafeguardingLead. (FR-1..4, FR-30, FR-31)\n- **Services (`src/server/messaging/`):** contact-rules, contacts, conversations, messages, read-state, notifications/pending-email, quiet-hours, safeguarding, maintenance (`sendDueMessageEmails`). (FR-5..8, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19..27)\n- **Routes:** conversations (list/create/get/read/mute/archive/leave), conversation messages (list before/after, send), messages/:id (patch/delete/report), messaging/unread-count, messaging/contacts, me/messaging-settings, safeguarding reports + conversations, and a hook into the internal dispatch route. (FR-28, FR-20)\n- **Pages:** `/messages`, `/messages/[conversationId]`, `/admin/safeguarding`, plus a Quiet hours section on `/account/notifications`, student layout actions and roster selection. (FR-9..18, FR-21, FR-23, FR-24)\n- **Registries:** 2 notification types, 1 file context, 1 nav item (+badge). (FR-18, FR-19, FR-26, FR-27)\n\n## 4. Open decisions for arch-design-system\n\n| # | Question | Recommendation | Drives |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A1 | Co-teachers count as \"managing\" a course? | **Yes**: matches `teaches()`/`getAccessibleStudentIds`. | FR-32, FR-5 |\n| A2 | `updatedAt` on new models (the PRD block omits it)? | Add `updatedAt @updatedAt` to Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageReport and MessagingSettings (platform convention). Leave it off append-only MessageRevision, MessageAttachment and PendingMessageEmail. Treat the PRD block as the minimum field set. | FR-1, NFR-6 |\n| A3 | Quiet hours for all roles? | **All roles** (the settings endpoint is open to any role). | FR-21, FR-20 |\n| A4 | Send-time rule in groups: what does \"relationship ended\" mean when there are many participants? | Non-staff sender may send iff canMessage(sender, s) for ≥1 staff participant still present. If no staff remain (all left), they are refused. Note that staff can never leave a student group they created (FR-14). | FR-7, FR-6 |\n| A5 | Homeroom teacher reachability: current academic year only? | Filter `section.academicYear.isCurrent = true` for messaging (otherwise last year's homeroom stays reachable). Keep student-access.ts unchanged (do not modify other PRDs' behaviour). | FR-5 |\n| A6 | Where is isSafeguardingLead edited? | API/validator only (no form exists, B13). Document that the flag is set via the seed or the API. | FR-2 |\n| A7 | Does a participant who **left** keep read access to the old thread and attachments? | No: `leftAt` set → treat as non-participant (list hides it, 404 on get). Safeguarding still sees everything. | FR-14, FR-27, NFR-1 |\n| A8 | The 768 px breakpoint does not match MUI default `md` (900). | Use `theme.breakpoints.down(768)` locally, not a theme change. | FR-9, NFR-7 |\n| A9 | How do polling clients learn about edits/deletes? | `after` responses also return `changed[]` = messages in the loaded window with `updatedAt > since` (pass `since` ISO alongside `after`). Alternatively accept staleness until reload. Recommend the former (cheap; same index plus `updatedAt`). | FR-13, FR-15 |\n| A10 | Can a participant leave a 1:1 conversation? | No: \"leave group\" only applies when there are >2 participants. Archive covers 1:1. | FR-14 |\n| A11 | Does a new message unarchive the conversation for recipients, and does the unread badge count archived conversations? | Yes, unarchive for recipients on new message (standard inbox behaviour). Unread count then needs no archive filter. | FR-9, FR-14, FR-18 |\n| A12 | Can a user report their own message, or report the same message twice? | Others' messages only. One OPEN report per (message, reporter): return 409 CONFLICT otherwise. | FR-22 |\n| A13 | Nav visibility for `/admin/safeguarding` (role-only nav filter)? | Show the item to ADMIN only via a new optional `NavItem.requires?: 'safeguardingLead'` evaluated in the shell with the flag loaded server-side. The page still enforces 403. Otherwise leave it out of nav and link from the `message.reported` notification. | FR-23 |\n| A14 | Seed Pat↔Sam link missing (B18). | The seed upserts `ParentStudentLink(Pat, Sam)` if absent before creating the Pat↔Tom thread, and skips the thread if Tom does not teach Sam. | FR-29 |\n\n## 5. Risks\n\n- **Notification collapse via `link` match** (B2) is coupled to the link format. Keep link building in a single helper used by both send and read paths.\n- **Per-process rate limiter and in-memory state** (B5) are not shared across instances. This is accepted per the existing ponytail note.\n- **Email-preference bypass**: deferring email outside `notify()` (B3) must still honour `NotificationPreference` and DISABLED/ARCHIVED filtering. Reuse `resolvePrefs`, and cover it in integration tests.\n- **mui-mcp unavailable** in this session (B20). The dev phase must retry it before writing UI.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AnCxdcDNTxEHjA3Dia73yx","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"56451f7d-c784-4a25-a233-3bc873207cca","uuid":"9134ad0c-13b0-4b69-b1df-2c2d54df2b17","timestamp":"2026-11-09T17:21:33.483Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-13\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:00:00Z), PRD-13 Direct Messaging. It has 32 FRs and 11 NFRs (43 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. The open decisions intake handed to the architect are in §4.\n\n> Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is left over from an earlier ticket (SH-12/SH-11). Its owning sub-task must overwrite it. None of those files is an SH-13 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-13 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no messaging models. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. `User` has `role`, `status` (default INVITED) and `archivedAt`, with `@@index([role, status])`. `FileObject` back-relations are explicit per attachment table. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1..4: one new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_messaging`). Add back-relations on `User` (participants, sent messages, reports filed/reviewed, settings, pending emails) and on `FileObject` (`messageAttachments`). |\n| B2 | `Notification` has **no entity/context column**: only `userId, type, title, body, link, readAt`, indexed on `(userId, readAt, createdAt)`. | schema L304-317 | FR-19 collapsing: \"replace older unread message.received rows for that conversation\" can only key on `link = /messages/<conversationId>` (plus `type` and `readAt: null`). Recommend `deleteMany({ userId in, type:'message.received', readAt:null, link })` before `notify()`. This is fine for performance because the leading `userId` index column applies. No schema change to Notification is needed. |\n| B3 | `notify()` writes the in-app rows **and enqueues email immediately** (EmailOutbox) when `input.email` is passed. It never throws and dedupes userIds. It filters DISABLED/ARCHIVED users. Preferences come from `resolvePrefs(def, pref)` in `notifications/preferences.ts`. | notify.ts L8-80 | FR-19/20 conflict: message email must be **deferred**. Call `notify()` for `message.received` **without** `email`, so only the in-app row is written. Upsert a `PendingMessageEmail` per recipient whose resolved `prefs.email` is true. The maintenance pass then re-checks `lastReadAt`/quiet hours and enqueues to EmailOutbox using the same `renderEmail('generic-notification')`. **arch-design-system** should define a small exported helper (e.g. `enqueueEmail(userIds, …)` or reuse of `resolvePrefs`) rather than duplicating notify's internals. |\n| B4 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). The `COMMUNICATION` category exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a static boolean per type and `roles` is a per-type role list. | notifications/types.ts | FR-19: `message.received` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp false, roles ALL}. FR-26: `message.reported` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true, roles ['ADMIN']}. |\n| B5 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` is a per-process sliding window that returns `{ ok, retryAfterMs }`. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-4: `rateLimit('msg:'+userId, 30, 60_000)`. On failure, throw `AppError('RATE_LIMITED')` (429) with `details.retryAfterMs`. The limiter is per-process. This is accepted (existing ponytail note). |\n| B6 | `registerFileAccess`: built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (files/contexts.ts). Unattached files (`contextId null`) are owner/ADMIN only. Resolver errors deny. Orphan files are purged after 24 h. | files/access.ts; files/contexts.ts | FR-27: add `register('message', messageResolver)` in `registerBuiltInContexts`. The resolver loads the Message by `file.contextId` (contextId = **messageId**, so a soft-deleted message can still be resolved), then allows a participant (`leftAt` irrelevant? see A7) or `isSafeguardingLead`. Attach files in the send transaction, or they are purged. Note: `FileAccessUser` is `{id, role}` only, so the resolver must query `isSafeguardingLead` itself. |\n| B7 | `SessionUser` = `{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}`. It has **no `isSafeguardingLead`**. | requireRole.ts L14-26 | NFR-1/FR-23..25: add a `requireSafeguardingLead()` helper (in `src/server/messaging/` or auth) that does `requireRole('ADMIN')` plus a DB read of the flag. Do not put the flag in the JWT: a revoked flag must take effect immediately. The page variant redirects to /forbidden (FR-23 says \"others get 403\"). |\n| B8 | Teacher→student reachability already exists: `getAccessibleStudentIds(TEACHER)` = ACTIVE enrollment in courses where `teacherId` or `coTeacherIds has` the teacher, **plus** SectionMember of sections they homeroom. The homeroom branch has **no academic-year filter**. `teaches(user, course)` is in course-access.ts. | student-access.ts L20-55; course-access.ts | FR-5/FR-32: reuse the same predicates (ideally share the Prisma `where` fragments) so contact rules and student-record access never disagree. Decide on the current-year filter for homeroom (A5). The PARENT branch is ParentStudentLink. |\n| B9 | `Enrollment @@unique([courseId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId, status])`. `ParentStudentLink @@unique([parentId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId])`. `SectionMember @@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` (no `sectionId` index). | schema | FR-5/FR-8 queries are index-backed from the student side. `coTeacherIds has` is not indexable, but a single user's course set is small. |\n| B10 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (CRON_SECRET) runs each job in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take)` → conditional `updateMany` claim → act if `count===1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts | FR-20: add `sendDueMessageEmails(now)`, isolated in its own try/catch. Process `PendingMessageEmail where dueAt <= now`. If the participant's `lastReadAt >= message time`, drop the row. If now is inside quiet hours, push `dueAt` to the end of quiet hours. Otherwise enqueue and delete the row (delete = claim; `deleteMany` count===1). |\n| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` lives in `assignments-service.ts` (precedent: other modules import it). `schoolNow(now, tz)` returns `{isoDay, hhmm}`. `formatInSchoolTz`, and `fromZonedTime` from date-fns-tz, are available. | src/lib/dates.ts; assignments-service.ts L64 | FR-20/21 quiet hours: a pure `isInQuietHours(hhmm, start, end)` with midnight wrap (`start > end`) and `quietHoursEnd(now, tz, end)` → UTC instant. Unit-test both (NFR-10). FR-10 day grouping uses `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes `RATE_LIMITED`, `FORBIDDEN`, `NOT_FOUND`, `CONFLICT`, `VALIDATION`. `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `audit()` exist. | src/server/http.ts; src/server/audit.ts | FR-28/NFR-6 handler conventions. Recommend returning 404 (not 403) for a non-participant on `GET /api/conversations/:id`, so cuids reveal nothing (NFR-1). FR-6 explicitly mandates 403 for **create** violations. |\n| B13 | **No admin user-edit UI exists.** `src/app/(app)/admin` has only attendance, courses, email-log, grading-scales, report-cards and sections. Users are edited only via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (ADMIN, `updateUserSchema`, audited). | src/app/api/users/[id]/route.ts; src/lib/validators/users.ts L103 | FR-2 resolution (intake's open question): add `isSafeguardingLead: z.boolean().optional()` to `updateUserSchema`. Reject or ignore it when the target role ≠ ADMIN. Audit the change (`user.update` metadata). **No form to extend.** Building a user-admin page is out of scope. |\n| B14 | **`/students/[id]` has no page.tsx or layout.tsx.** There are only sub-pages (attendance, assignments, courses, grades, report-cards), so there is no shared \"student page header\" today. | find src/app/(app)/students | FR-16: arch-design-system must pick the surface. Options: (a) add `students/[id]/layout.tsx` with a PageHeader + actions (affects all sub-pages, minimal per-page edits), or (b) put actions on each sub-page header. Recommend (a), keeping the `[id]` segment (no rename, per the PRD). The actions are client components that call `POST /api/conversations`. |\n| B15 | The course roster page is a **server component** rendering an MUI Table with no selection. PARENT gets notFound and STUDENT sees a name list. | courses/[courseId]/roster/page.tsx | FR-17: extract the TEACHER/ADMIN table into a client component with Checkbox selection and a toolbar button \"Message selected students\". It opens the FR-12 dialog prefilled. Rows carry `enrollmentId`, so the student id needs to be included in `RosterEntry` if it is not already there. |\n| B16 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `NotificationBell` implements a visibility-gated 30 s poll + MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L23-73 | FR-18: add `{label:'Messages', href:'/messages', roles: ALL_ROLES}` and an optional `badge?: 'messages'` key. The shell renders a polled Badge from `/api/messaging/unread-count`. Extract the bell's poll loop into a small `usePolling(fn, ms)` hook and reuse it for FR-13's 5 s/30 s polls. |\n| B17 | `/account/notifications` = page.tsx + `PreferencesTable.tsx`. `/api/me/*` routes exist (notification-preferences, profile, …). | src/app/(app)/account/notifications | FR-21: add a `QuietHoursSection` client component under that page, plus `src/app/api/me/messaging-settings/route.ts` (GET/PUT, any role). |\n| B18 | Seed users: Alice Admin, Tom Teacher, Tina Tutor, Sam Student, Sara Scholar and Pat Parent (by email). The seed creates **no ParentStudentLink** and no enrollments. Courses come from elsewhere and `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` skips when missing. | prisma/seed.ts L16-22, L304 | FR-29: set `isSafeguardingLead=true` on Alice. The Pat↔Tom thread \"about Sam's homework\" needs a Pat↔Sam link to satisfy contact rules at runtime. Recommend the seed upsert that link (or skip the thread with a log, like other seeds). The MATH-7A group uses the first 4 ACTIVE enrollments and skips if there are fewer or the course is missing. Seeds write via Prisma directly (bypassing canMessage) but must leave data valid under canMessage. Make it idempotent by checking for existing seeded conversations (subject/participants). |\n| B19 | Shared components: FileUpload, FileList, UserAvatar, UserPicker, ConfirmDialog, Toast, EmptyState, PageHeader, DataTable (in `src/components/<Name>/`). `@mui/x-date-pickers` is installed. | src/components | FR-10/11/12/23/24: reuse FileList/FileUpload (context 'message'), UserAvatar, ConfirmDialog (delete/leave), Toast (report confirmation), DataTable (safeguarding lists). FR-12 recipient picker: UserPicker is a candidate only if it accepts a custom options source (grouped contacts). Otherwise use MUI Autocomplete with `groupBy`. FR-21 time inputs: x-date-pickers TimePicker. |\n| B20 | The mui-mcp server failed to connect in this session (CONNECT_TIMEOUT). | session | NFR-5 requires mui-mcp lookups during dev. The dev phase must retry it. This is not a blocker for architecture. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend: DM = data model/migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance job, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | Conversation, ConversationParticipant (`@@unique([conversationId,userId])`, `@@index([userId])`, per-user `lastReadAt`, `mutedAt`/`archivedAt`, `leftAt`), Message (`@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, which NFR-2 depends on; `editedAt`, `deletedAt`), MessageAttachment (messageId, fileId; cascade on message), MessageReport + `ReportStatus`, MessagingSettings (userId unique, quietStart/End `String? HH:mm`). Add `updatedAt` per convention (A2). |\n| FR-2 | DM, API, AUTH | `User.isSafeguardingLead`. It can only be edited via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (B13) and is meaningful only for ADMIN. |\n| FR-3 | DM, SVC | `MessageRevision(messageId, body, createdAt)`, `@@index([messageId])`. Written in the same tx as the edit (original body before overwrite). Cascade with Message (messages are never hard-deleted anyway, NFR-3). |\n| FR-4 | DM, JOB | `PendingMessageEmail(userId, conversationId, dueAt)`, `@@unique([userId, conversationId])` so repeated sends upsert one row (the first unread message sets dueAt = now+10 min; later sends keep the earliest dueAt). `@@index([dueAt])`. |\n| FR-5 | SVC, AUTH | `canMessage(sender, recipient)` is a pure decision over pre-loaded relationship facts. Expose a batch form `messageableIds(sender, candidateIds)` to avoid N+1 queries for groups (≤25) and contacts (FR-8). Matrix: ADMIN→any, any→ADMIN, TEACHER↔TEACHER, TEACHER→STUDENT (managed course or homeroom, B8), TEACHER→PARENT (via the linked child under the same rule), STUDENT→own teachers, PARENT→linked child's teachers, all others false. Symmetry: student→teacher uses the same relation as teacher→student. Disabled/archived recipients → false. |\n| FR-6 | SVC, AUTH | Create conversation in one tx: participants = creator ∪ recipients (dedupe, exclude self from count rules), 2..25 total. Check `canMessage(creator, each)`. If any STUDENT is present, require ≥1 TEACHER/ADMIN. Any violation → 403 with nothing created. \"Students may reply in staff groups but cannot start student-student\" follows from canMessage(student, student)=false at create, plus the send-time rule (FR-7) being evaluated per-sender against **staff** participants only (A4). |\n| FR-7 | SVC, AUTH, UI | Send-time re-check. Non-staff sender: allowed iff canMessage(sender, p) holds for at least one remaining staff participant (A4). Otherwise 403 with code/reason `RELATIONSHIP_ENDED`. Staff always pass. `GET /api/conversations/:id` returns `canSend: boolean` so the composer shows the disabled message without a failed POST. |\n| FR-8 | SVC, API | `GET /api/messaging/contacts?q=`: role-specific grouped queries (PARENT: per child, \"My child's teachers (<child>)\"; STUDENT: \"My teachers\"; TEACHER: \"Students in <course>\", \"Parents of students in <course>\", homeroom, staff; all: \"School office\" = ADMINs). Status ACTIVE only. `q` filters on name. Cap each group (e.g. 50). |\n| FR-9 | UI, API | `/messages` layout with a two-pane `useMediaQuery(theme.breakpoints.down('md'))`, single pane + back below 768 px (theme `md`=900, so use a custom `down(768)` or confirm breakpoint, A8). List from `GET /api/conversations?archived=&q=` sorted `lastMessageAt desc`, with preview and `unreadCount` per row. Route: `/messages` and `/messages/[conversationId]`. |\n| FR-10 | UI, API | `GET /api/conversations/:id/messages?before=<id>&limit=30` (keyset on `(createdAt,id)`). Deleted messages are returned with `body: null, deleted: true` and attachments stripped for normal users (NFR-3: content is never exposed to non-safeguarding users). Day grouping in the school timezone (B11). |\n| FR-11 | UI, XC | Composer validation shared by the client and `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts` (body trim 1..5000, ≤5 fileIds). Enter=send / Shift+Enter=newline. Counter shows at >4500. |\n| FR-12 | UI | New-conversation dialog: Autocomplete multi-select grouped by contacts label, subject ≤120, first message. It posts `POST /api/conversations` with `{participantIds, subject?, body, fileIds?}`, creating the conversation + first message atomically. Also opened prefilled from FR-16/FR-17. |\n| FR-13 | UI, API, XC | 5 s poll of `?after=<lastId>` on the visible thread. 30 s poll on the list + nav badge. Gate on `document.visibilityState` (B16). The `after` query must also surface **edits/deletes** of already-loaded messages, or edits only appear on reload (A9). |\n| FR-14 | API, SVC, UI | `POST /api/conversations/:id/read` (sets lastReadAt=now and marks this conversation's unread `message.received` notifications read; deletes the PendingMessageEmail row), `/mute`, `/archive` (toggle body `{archived}`), `/leave`. Leave: set `leftAt`, which blocks further reads/sends for that user. Refuse (409/403) for the creator when `involvesStudent` is true. Group-only: DMs with 2 participants cannot be left (A10). Sending auto-unarchives for other participants? (A11). |\n| FR-15 | SVC, API | `PATCH /api/messages/:id` / `DELETE` (soft: `deletedAt`). Sender only, `now - createdAt ≤ 15 min`, not already deleted. Edit writes a MessageRevision + `editedAt` in one tx. No hard-delete path exists anywhere. |\n| FR-16 | UI | Student page actions (surface per B14). TEACHER/ADMIN \"Message parents\": participants = linked parents (+ creator). Hide the action if there are none or canMessage fails. PARENT \"Message teacher\": picker of the child's teachers (subset of contacts) → dialog. |\n| FR-17 | UI | Roster selection + action (B15). TEACHER only (ADMIN may also be offered, harmless). |\n| FR-18 | CFG, API, UI | Nav entry + badge (B16). `GET /api/messaging/unread-count` = count of the user's non-left participations where `lastMessageAt > coalesce(lastReadAt, epoch)` (count conversations, not messages: cheap, index-friendly). Archived conversations excluded? (A11). |\n| FR-19 | NOTIF, SVC | After the send tx commits: for each other participant not muted and not left, delete older unread `message.received` rows with the same link (B2), then `notify()` in-app only (B3). Title \"New message from <sender>\", body = 200-char plain preview, link `/messages/<id>`. |\n| FR-20 | JOB, DM, NOTIF | Upsert a PendingMessageEmail (dueAt=now+10 min) for recipients whose email pref is on (B3). Job per B10. Quiet hours read from MessagingSettings, evaluated in the school timezone (B11). |\n| FR-21 | UI, API, DM | MessagingSettings GET (defaults: no quiet hours) / PUT, Zod `HH:mm` regex. Both-or-neither validation. start == end is rejected. Applies to all roles (A3). |\n| FR-22 | API, SVC, NOTIF | `POST /api/messages/:id/report {reason ≤1000}`. Participant only. Allowed on own/others' messages (or other people's only? A12). One OPEN report per (message, reporter) to avoid spam (unique or check). Then FR-26 notify. |\n| FR-23 | UI, API, AUTH, XC | `/admin/safeguarding` (tabs Reports / Conversations), gated by `requireSafeguardingLead` (B7). `GET /api/safeguarding/reports?status=` with OPEN first, then createdAt desc. Detail includes the message, ±5 messages (including deleted and with revisions) and participants. `PATCH /api/safeguarding/reports/:id {action: review\\|dismiss, note?}` sets status, reviewedById, reviewedAt and note, then calls `audit()` (NFR-11). The nav entry is shown only to leads (the nav filter is role-based, so either show it to ADMIN and 403 non-leads, or extend NavItem with a predicate, A13). |\n| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH | `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations?participantId=&from=&to=` with `involvesStudent: true`, paginated. `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations/:id` = read-only full thread with deleted bodies and `revisions[]`. Same lead gate. |\n| FR-25 | XC, AUTH | `audit({action:'safeguarding.conversation.view', entityType:'Conversation', entityId})` on every safeguarding conversation view **and** on report detail views, since they expose conversation context. Done in the service, so both the API and the server page paths are covered. |\n| FR-26 | NOTIF | Notify `User where role=ADMIN, isSafeguardingLead, status ACTIVE` with `message.reported` (email allowed via notify's normal path: no deferral). Link `/admin/safeguarding?report=<id>`. The body must not include the message text (keep emails minimal). |\n| FR-27 | FILE, AUTH | B6. Send validates that each fileId is owned by the sender, unattached, and context 'message', then attaches in the tx (contextId = messageId). |\n| FR-28 | API, XC | All routes under `src/app/api/{conversations,messages,messaging,safeguarding,me/messaging-settings}`. Thin handlers + Zod + services in `src/server/messaging/`. Standard ok/paginated/error shapes. |\n| FR-29 | SEED | B18. |\n| FR-30 | SVC, DM | `involvesStudent` is computed in the create tx and is immutable afterwards (no participant-add API exists, so it stays correct). |\n| FR-31 | SVC | Update `lastMessageAt` in the send tx. `@@index` on ConversationParticipant `(userId)` + Conversation `lastMessageAt` serves the list ordering. Edits/deletes do **not** bump it. |\n| FR-32 | AUTH | B8: `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`. Resolved as yes (intake default, matches the existing `teaches()`). |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH, XC | Every service entry takes the SessionUser and loads `ConversationParticipant(conversationId, userId, leftAt null)` first. Non-participant → 404. Safeguarding → `requireSafeguardingLead`. File resolver per B6. Contacts never leak non-messageable users. |\n| NFR-2 | DM, API | `after` poll = participant check (unique-index lookup) + `Message where conversationId, (createdAt,id) > cursor` on `@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, `take 100`. Return `[]` fast. The 30 s list/unread polls use the participant index. Avoid count-per-message aggregation for unread (FR-18). |\n| NFR-3 | DM, SVC, AUTH | No DELETE that removes rows. FK cascades exist only for actual tree cleanup. Deleted/edited originals are exposed only through safeguarding services. |\n| NFR-4 | API, XC | B5. Applies to `POST /api/conversations/:id/messages`. Recommend counting `POST /api/conversations` (it also sends) against the same key. |\n| NFR-5 | UI, XC | MUI only; B19/B20. Badge, Drawer/List, Autocomplete, TimePicker, Tabs, Menu, Chip, TextField. |\n| NFR-6 | XC | `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts`, `src/server/messaging/{contact-rules,conversations,messages,notifications,quiet-hours,safeguarding,maintenance}.ts`, logger, cuid, UTC storage. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | See FR-9 (breakpoint, A8). |\n| NFR-8 | XC | A 5 s poll guarantees ≤ ~5 s + request latency < 6 s. No websockets/SSE. |\n| NFR-9 | XC | There is no reactions, typing or broadcast endpoint. Do not touch announcements (PRD-12 is absent). |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | `tests/unit/messaging/contact-rules.test.ts` (matrix incl. co-teacher, homeroom, DROPPED enrollment, group student-needs-staff, 26 participants), `quiet-hours.test.ts` (wrap midnight). `tests/integration/messaging/` (notification collapse, quiet-hours deferral via maintenance job, revision capture, 15-min window, rate limit, non-participant 404, safeguarding 403 + audit). `tests/e2e/messaging.spec.ts` (two browser contexts parent→teacher < 6 s; student→student blocked in the picker and on POST 403). |\n| NFR-11 | XC | Audit report review/dismiss and `isSafeguardingLead` changes. Users' own edits/deletes of their messages are not \"someone else's\" records, so no audit is needed. |\n\n## 3. New surface summary (for traceability)\n\n- **Models:** Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageAttachment, MessageRevision, MessageReport (+ReportStatus), MessagingSettings, PendingMessageEmail. Plus User.isSafeguardingLead. (FR-1..4, FR-30, FR-31)\n- **Services (`src/server/messaging/`):** contact-rules, contacts, conversations, messages, read-state, notifications/pending-email, quiet-hours, safeguarding, maintenance (`sendDueMessageEmails`). (FR-5..8, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19..27)\n- **Routes:** conversations (list/create/get/read/mute/archive/leave), conversation messages (list before/after, send), messages/:id (patch/delete/report), messaging/unread-count, messaging/contacts, me/messaging-settings, safeguarding reports + conversations, and a hook into the internal dispatch route. (FR-28, FR-20)\n- **Pages:** `/messages`, `/messages/[conversationId]`, `/admin/safeguarding`, plus a Quiet hours section on `/account/notifications`, student layout actions and roster selection. (FR-9..18, FR-21, FR-23, FR-24)\n- **Registries:** 2 notification types, 1 file context, 1 nav item (+badge). (FR-18, FR-19, FR-26, FR-27)\n\n## 4. Open decisions for arch-design-system\n\n| # | Question | Recommendation | Drives |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A1 | Co-teachers count as \"managing\" a course? | **Yes**: matches `teaches()`/`getAccessibleStudentIds`. | FR-32, FR-5 |\n| A2 | `updatedAt` on new models (the PRD block omits it)? | Add `updatedAt @updatedAt` to Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageReport and MessagingSettings (platform convention). Leave it off append-only MessageRevision, MessageAttachment and PendingMessageEmail. Treat the PRD block as the minimum field set. | FR-1, NFR-6 |\n| A3 | Quiet hours for all roles? | **All roles** (the settings endpoint is open to any role). | FR-21, FR-20 |\n| A4 | Send-time rule in groups: what does \"relationship ended\" mean when there are many participants? | Non-staff sender may send iff canMessage(sender, s) for ≥1 staff participant still present. If no staff remain (all left), they are refused. Note that staff can never leave a student group they created (FR-14). | FR-7, FR-6 |\n| A5 | Homeroom teacher reachability: current academic year only? | Filter `section.academicYear.isCurrent = true` for messaging (otherwise last year's homeroom stays reachable). Keep student-access.ts unchanged (do not modify other PRDs' behaviour). | FR-5 |\n| A6 | Where is isSafeguardingLead edited? | API/validator only (no form exists, B13). Document that the flag is set via the seed or the API. | FR-2 |\n| A7 | Does a participant who **left** keep read access to the old thread and attachments? | No: `leftAt` set → treat as non-participant (list hides it, 404 on get). Safeguarding still sees everything. | FR-14, FR-27, NFR-1 |\n| A8 | The 768 px breakpoint does not match MUI default `md` (900). | Use `theme.breakpoints.down(768)` locally, not a theme change. | FR-9, NFR-7 |\n| A9 | How do polling clients learn about edits/deletes? | `after` responses also return `changed[]` = messages in the loaded window with `updatedAt > since` (pass `since` ISO alongside `after`). Alternatively accept staleness until reload. Recommend the former (cheap; same index plus `updatedAt`). | FR-13, FR-15 |\n| A10 | Can a participant leave a 1:1 conversation? | No: \"leave group\" only applies when there are >2 participants. Archive covers 1:1. | FR-14 |\n| A11 | Does a new message unarchive the conversation for recipients, and does the unread badge count archived conversations? | Yes, unarchive for recipients on new message (standard inbox behaviour). Unread count then needs no archive filter. | FR-9, FR-14, FR-18 |\n| A12 | Can a user report their own message, or report the same message twice? | Others' messages only. One OPEN report per (message, reporter): return 409 CONFLICT otherwise. | FR-22 |\n| A13 | Nav visibility for `/admin/safeguarding` (role-only nav filter)? | Show the item to ADMIN only via a new optional `NavItem.requires?: 'safeguardingLead'` evaluated in the shell with the flag loaded server-side. The page still enforces 403. Otherwise leave it out of nav and link from the `message.reported` notification. | FR-23 |\n| A14 | Seed Pat↔Sam link missing (B18). | The seed upserts `ParentStudentLink(Pat, Sam)` if absent before creating the Pat↔Tom thread, and skips the thread if Tom does not teach Sam. | FR-29 |\n\n## 5. Risks\n\n- **Notification collapse via `link` match** (B2) is coupled to the link format. Keep link building in a single helper used by both send and read paths.\n- **Per-process rate limiter and in-memory state** (B5) are not shared across instances. This is accepted per the existing ponytail note.\n- **Email-preference bypass**: deferring email outside `notify()` (B3) must still honour `NotificationPreference` and DISABLED/ARCHIVED filtering. Reuse `resolvePrefs`, and cover it in integration tests.\n- **mui-mcp unavailable** in this session (B20). The dev phase must retry it before writing UI.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":117,"newStart":1,"newLines":116,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-12","+# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-13"," "," Written by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T18:00:00Z), PRD-12 Announcements & News. It has 36 FRs and 11 NFRs (47 requirements) at 94% confidence.","-`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:00:00Z), PRD-13 Direct Messaging. It has 32 FRs and 11 NFRs (43 requirements) at 95% confidence.","+`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. The open decisions intake handed to the architect are in §4."," ","-> All other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **SH-11 leftovers**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-12 input.","+> Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is left over from an earlier ticket (SH-12/SH-11). Its owning sub-task must overwrite it. None of those files is an SH-13 input."," "," ## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk"," ","-| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-12 |","+| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-13 |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| B1 | The schema has no Announcement* models or enums. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1: add a new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_announcements`). Add back-relations on `User` (authored, reads) and `FileObject` (attachments, and the cover image if it is an FK). |","-| B2 | `User.status` is `ACTIVE/INVITED/DISABLED/ARCHIVED` and `archivedAt` is a separate column. `notify()` filters `status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED]`, so it **includes INVITED**. | schema L17, L59; notify.ts L43 | FR-3 is stricter: audience = `status: ACTIVE, archivedAt: null`. Pass the resolved ids to `notify()`, which then filters on its own. Don't rely on notify's filter. |","-| B3 | `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId` (required). `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` has `@@index([studentId])` and a `@@unique([parentId, studentId])`. | schema L106, L144 | FR-4/5/6 parent expansion: join through the link. Parent → children is covered by the unique index's leading `parentId`. |","-| B4 | `Section(academicYearId, gradeLevelId, homeroomTeacherId?)`. `SectionMember(studentId, academicYearId)` is unique on `(studentId, academicYearId)`, and its academicYearId is denormalised. **There is no index on `sectionId`.** | schema L377-411 | FR-5: \"members\" = SectionMember rows where `academicYearId` = the section's year (that is already true per row, so filtering by `sectionId` is enough). A section belongs to one year, so the \"current year\" question reduces to \"is the section in the current year\". See §4 A1. |","-| B5 | `Course(academicYearId, sectionId?, teacherId, coTeacherIds String[], archivedAt?)`. `coTeacherIds` is queried with `has`. `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. | schema L414-447 | FR-4/5/6/10 teacher branches. `has` isn't indexable without a GIN index. The rows involved are small (only a user's own courses), so this is fine for NFR-2. Decide whether archived courses' teachers count (§4 A6). |","-| B6 | `Enrollment.status` ACTIVE/DROPPED, with `@@index([studentId, status])` and `@@unique([courseId, studentId])`. | schema L371, L450 | FR-6 student branch. Both directions are indexed. |","-| B7 | `FileObject(context, contextId)` is indexed. Uploads are created with `contextId: null`. `attachFiles(tx, context, contextId, ids)` / detach live in files-service. **`purgeOrphanFiles` deletes `contextId: null` files after 24 h.** | files-service.ts L212-244; files/purge.ts | FR-13/FR-30: attach the cover image and attachments with `context='announcement'`, `contextId=announcement.id` inside the create/update tx. A cover that is uploaded but never attached (e.g. an abandoned draft) is purged, which is correct. **A draft must still attach its files**, or they vanish after 24 h. |","-| B8 | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)`. Resolvers receive `null` for anonymous callers. Built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (contexts.ts). Resolver errors deny. `/api/files/` is already in PUBLIC_API_PATHS. | files/access.ts; contexts.ts; public-routes.ts | FR-30: add `register('announcement', announcementResolver)` to `registerBuiltInContexts` so it is guaranteed loaded, rather than as a side-effect import. Anonymous downloads already route through, so no public-route change is needed for files. |","-| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). `COMMUNICATION` exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a **static boolean per type**. | notifications/types.ts | **FR-26 conflict**: \"mandatoryInApp true when requiresAck\" can't be expressed per instance. Options: (a) two types, `announcement.published` (mandatoryInApp false) and `announcement.published_ack` (true); or (b) one type with `mandatoryInApp: true`. Recommend (a) as the smallest faithful mapping. **arch-design-system decides.** |","-| B10 | `notify({type, userIds, title, body, link, email:{template:'generic-notification', data}})` dedupes, never throws, and is called after commit. It truncates body to BODY_MAX and drops non-relative links. | notify.ts L8-60 | FR-27/28: call it after the notifiedAt claim commits. `link: /announcements/${id}`. Large audiences (a SCHOOL announcement can be thousands of users) go through one `findMany` + `createMany`. That's acceptable, but chunk the userIds if notify's `in` lists get large. |","-| B11 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` runs each pass in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take: BATCH)` → `updateMany({where:{id, claimCol: null}})` → act only if `count === 1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts L28-43 | FR-27: `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` copies this pattern exactly: `where status SCHEDULED, publishAt <= now, notifiedAt null`, claim `notifiedAt`. Publish-now uses the same claim helper, so one code path sends. |","-| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes both `RATE_LIMITED` (429) and `CONFLICT` (409). `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` exist. | src/server/http.ts | FR-34 handler conventions. FR-25: recommend **429 RATE_LIMITED** with `details.retryAfter` (ISO). It is semantically a time-based throttle, and intake suggested the same. |","-| B13 | `audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request})` never throws. The action convention is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|archive\\|delete`. | src/server/audit.ts | FR-12: `announcement.update` / `announcement.archive` when an admin acts on another author's row. Also audit the author's own archive (cheap; optional). |","-| B14 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` (formula-injection safe). | src/server/csv.ts | FR-24 `?format=csv`. |","-| B15 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from **assignments-service.ts**, not a shared module. `formatInSchoolTz` is in src/lib/dates.ts. | assignments-service.ts L64; src/lib/dates.ts L7 | NFR-7: reuse both. Importing `getSchoolTimezone` from assignments-service is the existing precedent (contexts.ts already imports from it). Don't duplicate it. |","-| B16 | `MarkdownView` = react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema) rendering to MUI components. **There is no Markdown→plain-text helper** in the codebase. | src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx | FR-18 (200-char excerpt) and FR-28 (300-char email body) need a new small pure `markdownToPlainText(md)` (e.g. in `src/lib/markdown-text.ts`). Plain text rendered by React/the email template is escaped, so NFR-4 is met as long as the excerpt is never rendered as HTML/Markdown. Prefer a regex strip over a new dependency (remark is already installed transitively if an AST approach is preferred). |","-| B17 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `navigation` is a static array. `NotificationBell` polls `/api/notifications/unread-count` every 30 s, gated by visibility, and shows an MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L42-62 | FR-32: add an optional `badge?: 'announcements-unread'` key (or a badge endpoint string) to NavItem. The sidebar renders a polled Badge for items that have one. Reuse the bell's polling hook shape. |","-| B18 | `courseTabs` is a static array with `roles`. | src/config/course-tabs.ts | FR-21: `{ key: 'announcements', label: 'Announcements', href: id => /courses/${id}/announcements, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. |","-| B19 | `assertCanViewCourse` covers ADMIN, TEACHER (teacher or co-teacher only, **not homeroom**), STUDENT (enrollment) and PARENT (child enrolled). `canSeeDrafts` checks the course-manager test. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts L25+ | FR-21 gate: `assertCanViewCourse` and then the normal audience filter. FR-10 \"courses they manage\" = the same `teacherId \\|\\| coTeacherIds.includes` test, so reuse it rather than re-deriving. |","-| B20 | Seed: Tom/Sam/Pat by email. Courses are looked up with `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` and skipped if missing. The Grade 7 GradeLevel row **is** seeded. No 7A/7B/6A sections and no `ParentStudentLink` rows are created by the seed (they come from other scripts/fixtures, if at all). | prisma/seed.ts L18-22, L109-115, L275-305 | FR-35: grade/course/section-targeted seeds skip when their target is missing, using the same `logger.info`/`console.log` style. School-wide, staff and public seeds always run. Idempotency: upsert by a stable title + author, or check for existence first. |","-| B21 | Test layout: `tests/unit`, `tests/integration/<feature>/`, `tests/e2e/*.spec.ts` + `helpers/`. | tests/ | NFR-10: `tests/unit/announcements/*`, `tests/integration/announcements/*`, `tests/e2e/announcements.spec.ts`. |","-| B22 | `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0 is installed (`@mui/x-data-grid` too). | package.json | FR-13 publishAt/expiresAt: DateTimePicker. FR-23/24 tables: the existing `DataTable` component. Look up via mui-mcp per NFR-1. |","+| B1 | The schema has no messaging models. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. `User` has `role`, `status` (default INVITED) and `archivedAt`, with `@@index([role, status])`. `FileObject` back-relations are explicit per attachment table. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1..4: one new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_messaging`). Add back-relations on `User` (participants, sent messages, reports filed/reviewed, settings, pending emails) and on `FileObject` (`messageAttachments`). |","+| B2 | `Notification` has **no entity/context column**: only `userId, type, title, body, link, readAt`, indexed on `(userId, readAt, createdAt)`. | schema L304-317 | FR-19 collapsing: \"replace older unread message.received rows for that conversation\" can only key on `link = /messages/<conversationId>` (plus `type` and `readAt: null`). Recommend `deleteMany({ userId in, type:'message.received', readAt:null, link })` before `notify()`. This is fine for performance because the leading `userId` index column applies. No schema change to Notification is needed. |","+| B3 | `notify()` writes the in-app rows **and enqueues email immediately** (EmailOutbox) when `input.email` is passed. It never throws and dedupes userIds. It filters DISABLED/ARCHIVED users. Preferences come from `resolvePrefs(def, pref)` in `notifications/preferences.ts`. | notify.ts L8-80 | FR-19/20 conflict: message email must be **deferred**. Call `notify()` for `message.received` **without** `email`, so only the in-app row is written. Upsert a `PendingMessageEmail` per recipient whose resolved `prefs.email` is true. The maintenance pass then re-checks `lastReadAt`/quiet hours and enqueues to EmailOutbox using the same `renderEmail('generic-notification')`. **arch-design-system** should define a small exported helper (e.g. `enqueueEmail(userIds, …)` or reuse of `resolvePrefs`) rather than duplicating notify's internals. |","+| B4 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). The `COMMUNICATION` category exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a static boolean per type and `roles` is a per-type role list. | notifications/types.ts | FR-19: `message.received` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp false, roles ALL}. FR-26: `message.reported` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true, roles ['ADMIN']}. |","+| B5 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` is a per-process sliding window that returns `{ ok, retryAfterMs }`. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-4: `rateLimit('msg:'+userId, 30, 60_000)`. On failure, throw `AppError('RATE_LIMITED')` (429) with `details.retryAfterMs`. The limiter is per-process. This is accepted (existing ponytail note). |","+| B6 | `registerFileAccess`: built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (files/contexts.ts). Unattached files (`contextId null`) are owner/ADMIN only. Resolver errors deny. Orphan files are purged after 24 h. | files/access.ts; files/contexts.ts | FR-27: add `register('message', messageResolver)` in `registerBuiltInContexts`. The resolver loads the Message by `file.contextId` (contextId = **messageId**, so a soft-deleted message can still be resolved), then allows a participant (`leftAt` irrelevant? see A7) or `isSafeguardingLead`. Attach files in the send transaction, or they are purged. Note: `FileAccessUser` is `{id, role}` only, so the resolver must query `isSafeguardingLead` itself. |","+| B7 | `SessionUser` = `{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}`. It has **no `isSafeguardingLead`**. | requireRole.ts L14-26 | NFR-1/FR-23..25: add a `requireSafeguardingLead()` helper (in `src/server/messaging/` or auth) that does `requireRole('ADMIN')` plus a DB read of the flag. Do not put the flag in the JWT: a revoked flag must take effect immediately. The page variant redirects to /forbidden (FR-23 says \"others get 403\"). |","+| B8 | Teacher→student reachability already exists: `getAccessibleStudentIds(TEACHER)` = ACTIVE enrollment in courses where `teacherId` or `coTeacherIds has` the teacher, **plus** SectionMember of sections they homeroom. The homeroom branch has **no academic-year filter**. `teaches(user, course)` is in course-access.ts. | student-access.ts L20-55; course-access.ts | FR-5/FR-32: reuse the same predicates (ideally share the Prisma `where` fragments) so contact rules and student-record access never disagree. Decide on the current-year filter for homeroom (A5). The PARENT branch is ParentStudentLink. |","+| B9 | `Enrollment @@unique([courseId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId, status])`. `ParentStudentLink @@unique([parentId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId])`. `SectionMember @@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` (no `sectionId` index). | schema | FR-5/FR-8 queries are index-backed from the student side. `coTeacherIds has` is not indexable, but a single user's course set is small. |","+| B10 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (CRON_SECRET) runs each job in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take)` → conditional `updateMany` claim → act if `count===1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts | FR-20: add `sendDueMessageEmails(now)`, isolated in its own try/catch. Process `PendingMessageEmail where dueAt <= now`. If the participant's `lastReadAt >= message time`, drop the row. If now is inside quiet hours, push `dueAt` to the end of quiet hours. Otherwise enqueue and delete the row (delete = claim; `deleteMany` count===1). |","+| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` lives in `assignments-service.ts` (precedent: other modules import it). `schoolNow(now, tz)` returns `{isoDay, hhmm}`. `formatInSchoolTz`, and `fromZonedTime` from date-fns-tz, are available. | src/lib/dates.ts; assignments-service.ts L64 | FR-20/21 quiet hours: a pure `isInQuietHours(hhmm, start, end)` with midnight wrap (`start > end`) and `quietHoursEnd(now, tz, end)` → UTC instant. Unit-test both (NFR-10). FR-10 day grouping uses `formatInSchoolTz`. |","+| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes `RATE_LIMITED`, `FORBIDDEN`, `NOT_FOUND`, `CONFLICT`, `VALIDATION`. `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `audit()` exist. | src/server/http.ts; src/server/audit.ts | FR-28/NFR-6 handler conventions. Recommend returning 404 (not 403) for a non-participant on `GET /api/conversations/:id`, so cuids reveal nothing (NFR-1). FR-6 explicitly mandates 403 for **create** violations. |","+| B13 | **No admin user-edit UI exists.** `src/app/(app)/admin` has only attendance, courses, email-log, grading-scales, report-cards and sections. Users are edited only via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (ADMIN, `updateUserSchema`, audited). | src/app/api/users/[id]/route.ts; src/lib/validators/users.ts L103 | FR-2 resolution (intake's open question): add `isSafeguardingLead: z.boolean().optional()` to `updateUserSchema`. Reject or ignore it when the target role ≠ ADMIN. Audit the change (`user.update` metadata). **No form to extend.** Building a user-admin page is out of scope. |","+| B14 | **`/students/[id]` has no page.tsx or layout.tsx.** There are only sub-pages (attendance, assignments, courses, grades, report-cards), so there is no shared \"student page header\" today. | find src/app/(app)/students | FR-16: arch-design-system must pick the surface. Options: (a) add `students/[id]/layout.tsx` with a PageHeader + actions (affects all sub-pages, minimal per-page edits), or (b) put actions on each sub-page header. Recommend (a), keeping the `[id]` segment (no rename, per the PRD). The actions are client components that call `POST /api/conversations`. |","+| B15 | The course roster page is a **server component** rendering an MUI Table with no selection. PARENT gets notFound and STUDENT sees a name list. | courses/[courseId]/roster/page.tsx | FR-17: extract the TEACHER/ADMIN table into a client component with Checkbox selection and a toolbar button \"Message selected students\". It opens the FR-12 dialog prefilled. Rows carry `enrollmentId`, so the student id needs to be included in `RosterEntry` if it is not already there. |","+| B16 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `NotificationBell` implements a visibility-gated 30 s poll + MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L23-73 | FR-18: add `{label:'Messages', href:'/messages', roles: ALL_ROLES}` and an optional `badge?: 'messages'` key. The shell renders a polled Badge from `/api/messaging/unread-count`. Extract the bell's poll loop into a small `usePolling(fn, ms)` hook and reuse it for FR-13's 5 s/30 s polls. |","+| B17 | `/account/notifications` = page.tsx + `PreferencesTable.tsx`. `/api/me/*` routes exist (notification-preferences, profile, …). | src/app/(app)/account/notifications | FR-21: add a `QuietHoursSection` client component under that page, plus `src/app/api/me/messaging-settings/route.ts` (GET/PUT, any role). |","+| B18 | Seed users: Alice Admin, Tom Teacher, Tina Tutor, Sam Student, Sara Scholar and Pat Parent (by email). The seed creates **no ParentStudentLink** and no enrollments. Courses come from elsewhere and `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` skips when missing. | prisma/seed.ts L16-22, L304 | FR-29: set `isSafeguardingLead=true` on Alice. The Pat↔Tom thread \"about Sam's homework\" needs a Pat↔Sam link to satisfy contact rules at runtime. Recommend the seed upsert that link (or skip the thread with a log, like other seeds). The MATH-7A group uses the first 4 ACTIVE enrollments and skips if there are fewer or the course is missing. Seeds write via Prisma directly (bypassing canMessage) but must leave data valid under canMessage. Make it idempotent by checking for existing seeded conversations (subject/participants). |","+| B19 | Shared components: FileUpload, FileList, UserAvatar, UserPicker, ConfirmDialog, Toast, EmptyState, PageHeader, DataTable (in `src/components/<Name>/`). `@mui/x-date-pickers` is installed. | src/components | FR-10/11/12/23/24: reuse FileList/FileUpload (context 'message'), UserAvatar, ConfirmDialog (delete/leave), Toast (report confirmation), DataTable (safeguarding lists). FR-12 recipient picker: UserPicker is a candidate only if it accepts a custom options source (grouped contacts). Otherwise use MUI Autocomplete with `groupBy`. FR-21 time inputs: x-date-pickers TimePicker. |","+| B20 | The mui-mcp server failed to connect in this session (CONNECT_TIMEOUT). | session | NFR-5 requires mui-mcp lookups during dev. The dev phase must retry it. This is not a blocker for architecture. |"," "," ## 2. Requirement → architectural concern"," ","-Legend for **Concern**: DM = data model / migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance/cron, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule.","+Legend: DM = data model/migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance job, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule."," "," | Req | Concern | Notes |"," |---|---|---|","-| FR-1 | DM | 2 enums, 4 models, 1 migration. AnnouncementRead has a composite PK `(announcementId, userId)`. **Needed beyond the PRD's model** (flag as deliberate additions): `Announcement.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` (FR-25), `notifiedAt DateTime?` (FR-27, likely already in the spec since FR-27 names it), and indexes `AnnouncementAudience @@index([type, refId])` and `Announcement @@index([status, publishAt])` (NFR-2). AnnouncementAudience columns implied by FR-3..FR-6: `type`, `refId?` (null for SCHOOL/STAFF), `includeStudents/Parents/Teachers` booleans. Cascade deletes from Announcement to its children. |","-| FR-2 | XC / validation | `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts`, isomorphic Zod schema, shared by the composer and the handlers. Also validate: `expiresAt > publishAt` when both are set; ROLE refId ∈ Role enum; refId required unless SCHOOL/STAFF; at least one include flag true for GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION/COURSE. |","-| FR-3 | SVC | `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`. `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` returns a set union over the rows, all filtered to `ACTIVE && archivedAt null`. SCHOOL = all, STAFF = role ∈ {ADMIN, TEACHER}, ROLE = role = refId. Do the active filter **once** at the end, including on parents. |","-| FR-4 | SVC | GRADE_LEVEL: students via `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`; parents via ParentStudentLink of **those students** (before the active filter on the students? see §4 A3); teachers = `teacherId` ∪ `coTeacherIds` of courses where `section.gradeLevelId = refId AND academicYear.isCurrent`. |","-| FR-5 | SVC | SECTION: SectionMember(sectionId) students, their parents, `homeroomTeacherId` plus the teachers/co-teachers of `Course.sectionId = refId`. \"Current year\" is implicit (§4 A1). |","-| FR-6 | SVC | COURSE: `Enrollment(courseId, status ACTIVE)` students, their parents, teacher plus coTeachers. |","-| FR-7 | SVC / perf | `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`. **Key design point**: compute a per-user *membership key set* once (≤ ~4 small queries): role; own/children's gradeLevelIds; own/children's sectionIds (current year); own/children's ACTIVE courseIds; for teachers, managed courseIds + their sectionIds/gradeLevelIds + homeroom sectionIds. Then audience matching is a pure function over `(audience, keys)`. The same key set also becomes a Prisma `where` (an OR of `{type, refId in keys[type], include<Flag>: true}`) for the feed (FR-17/NFR-2). This puts the rules in one place (intake key risk), and `resolveAudienceUserIds` is the inverse expansion. The agreement test (NFR-10) checks both. For a parent the flag is `includeParents`, and the keys come from the children. |","-| FR-8 | SVC / XC | audience.ts must not import Announcement types. Its input is `{type, refId, includeStudents, includeParents, includeTeachers}[]`, so PRD-14 can reuse it. Export the `AudienceType` enum from Prisma. |","-| FR-9 | AUTH | ADMIN: any type, `isPublic` allowed. |","-| FR-10 | AUTH | `assertCanTarget(user, audiences, isPublic)` in the service, called by **both** create and update (PATCH can change the audience). TEACHER: COURSE where they manage the course (B19); SECTION where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Everything else, and `isPublic=true`, → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')` 403. On PATCH by a teacher, also re-check when `isPublic` is omitted but already true (it can't be, since only admins set it). |","-| FR-11 | AUTH | `requireRole('ADMIN','TEACHER')` on POST, PATCH, archive, preview-audience, manage, stats and remind. |","-| FR-12 | AUTH / audit | Edit: `authorId === user.id \\|\\| ADMIN`. Archive: same. Archive sets ARCHIVED (terminal for authors, §4 A7). Admin-on-others → `audit()`. A teacher who is no longer allowed to target the existing audience (e.g. lost co-teacher status) → PATCH fails on re-validation. That's acceptable. |","-| FR-13 | UI | Pages `/announcements/new` and `/announcements/[id]/edit` (server page + client form). Reuse MarkdownEditor, FileUpload (context 'announcement'), FileList, Autocomplete pickers per audience type (grade levels, sections, courses, roles). Teachers only see their own courses/homeroom in the pickers (UX; the server still enforces). Public toggle hidden for non-admins. Show and accept dates in the school tz (NFR-7). |","-| FR-14 | API / SVC | `POST /api/announcements/preview-audience`, body = audiences[] (same Zod schema). Run `assertCanTarget` first so the preview can't enumerate other audiences' sizes. Returns `{total, byRole:{STUDENT,PARENT,TEACHER,ADMIN}}`. Debounce in the UI. Uses `resolveAudienceUserIds` + `groupBy role` (or one count query). |","-| FR-15 | SVC | On transition to PUBLISHED/SCHEDULED (create or PATCH), resolve the count and if it is 0, `VALIDATION_ERROR`. Drafts are exempt (§4 A2). Scheduled ones are validated at schedule time, not again at publishAt; an emptied audience just notifies nobody. |","-| FR-16 | SVC / XC | **Visibility predicate in one place**: `visibleWhere(now) = { OR: [{status: PUBLISHED}, {status: SCHEDULED, publishAt: {lte: now}}], AND: [{OR: [{expiresAt: null}, {expiresAt: {gt: now}}]}] }`. Use it in the feed, detail, ack, files, public news and unread-count. Precedent: `isAssignmentVisible`/`isLessonVisible`. The status column stays SCHEDULED after publishAt (unless the maintenance run also flips it to PUBLISHED; recommend it does, in the same claim, for clean manage-view status). |","-| FR-17 | API / SVC / perf | `GET /api/announcements`: `visibleWhere(now) AND audiences: { some: audienceWhereForKeys(keys) }`. Plus `?filter=unread` (`reads: {none: {userId}}` or `readAt null`) and `?filter=ack` (`requiresAck AND no acknowledgedAt`). Ordering: up to 3 pinned first (separate `take:3` query on page 1, exclude those ids from the main list), then newest by **effective publish time** (`publishAt ?? createdAt` → store a `publishedAt`, or order by `publishAt` and set it on publish-now). Overflow pins fall into the newest list (§4 A4). Include the per-user read row via a `reads: {where:{userId}}` include. |","-| FR-18 | API / UI | The card DTO = cover fileId, title, author name + role, date, audience chips (labels need names for grade/section/course refIds, so batch-load by refId), `excerpt` (B16, 200 chars, computed server-side), attachment count (`_count`). |","-| FR-19 | API / AUTH | `GET /api/announcements/:id`: access if ADMIN, the author, or (visible AND isUserInAudience). Otherwise **404** (don't leak existence, NFR-6). Upsert AnnouncementRead `{readAt: now}` only for audience members (not for admins/authors outside the audience, since that would distort stats). Client renders the body with MarkdownView. |","-| FR-20 | API / AUTH | `POST /:id/ack`: visible AND requiresAck AND audience member → upsert `{readAt ?? now, acknowledgedAt ?? now}` (idempotent; keep the first ack time). Non-member → 404. `requiresAck=false` → 409 or VALIDATION_ERROR. Display with `formatInSchoolTz`. |","-| FR-21 | API / CFG / UI | `GET /api/announcements?courseId=` → `assertCanViewCourse` then the feed query additionally filtered to `audiences some {type: COURSE, refId: courseId}`. The user must still be in the audience (a parent-only course announcement isn't shown to the course's students). Course tab page `/courses/[id]/announcements`. |","-| FR-22 | SVC / UI | Parent feed only: for each item, find matching audience rows and map them back to the children whose keys matched → `forChildren: [{id, firstName}]`. This falls out of the key-set design if keys are tracked per child (`Map<refKey, childIds>`). |","-| FR-23 | API / UI | `GET /api/announcements/manage`: no visibility filter. TEACHER `authorId = me`, ADMIN all. Reach = resolved recipient count (**expensive per row**: compute for the current page only; or snapshot `recipientCount` at publish and recompute live only on stats). Read % = `count(reads readAt not null) / reach`; ack % similar. Recommendation: resolve audiences per page row (≤ pageSize calls); keep it simple, a ponytail note for a snapshot later. |","-| FR-24 | API / UI | `GET /:id/stats`: author or ADMIN, else 404. Recipients = `resolveAudienceUserIds` (live) LEFT JOIN reads. Filters `?filter=unread\\|unacked`. `?format=csv` → `toCsv`, `Content-Disposition` attachment. Percentages over the live recipient set (AC-5: 30/50 = 60%). Readers who later left the audience are not counted. |","-| FR-25 | API / NOTIF / DM | `POST /:id/remind`: author or ADMIN. requiresAck must be true and the announcement visible. Atomic claim: `updateMany({where:{id, OR:[{lastRemindedAt:null},{lastRemindedAt:{lte: now-24h}}]}, data:{lastRemindedAt: now}})`. `count 0` → **429 RATE_LIMITED** (decision, B12). Then notify `announcement.reminder` to recipients − acknowledged. Returns `{notified: n}` (AC-5: 20). |","-| FR-26 | CFG / NOTIF | Add the types to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` (B9 conflict). roles: ALL. reminder: COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true (an ack is being chased). |","-| FR-27 | JOB / NOTIF | One `claimAndNotifyPublished(id, now)` helper: `updateMany({where:{id, notifiedAt:null, <visible>}, data:{notifiedAt: now, status: PUBLISHED}})`. If count = 1 → resolve recipients → notify. Called by publish-now (after the tx commits) and by `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` (batch 200, B11). Hook it into the dispatch route in its own try/catch. |","-| FR-28 | NOTIF | Email data: `{title, body: markdownToPlainText(body).slice(0,300), ctaLabel:'Read announcement', ctaUrl}`. Check GenericNotificationData's field names when designing. |","-| FR-29 | SVC | Follows from the notifiedAt claim: PATCH never clears notifiedAt. Also a draft → PATCH publish of an already-notified row (an archived-then-edited one) must not resend. |","-| FR-30 | FILE / AUTH | `announcementResolver(user, file)`: load the announcement by `file.contextId`. If `isPublic && visible` → true (including null user). If `!user` → false. If ADMIN or author → true. If visible && isUserInAudience → true. Else false. Register it in `registerBuiltInContexts` (B8). |","-| FR-31 | API / CFG | `getPublicNews({page})` in announcements-service: `isPublic && visibleWhere(now)`, a minimal DTO (no author email, no audience). Route `src/app/api/public/news/route.ts`. Add `'/api/public/news'` (exact match) to PUBLIC_API_PATHS. Consider `rateLimit` by IP since it is unauthenticated (cheap; the helper exists). |","-| FR-32 | CFG / UI / API | Nav entry for ALL_ROLES + the badge (B17). `GET /api/announcements/unread-count` = `count(visibleWhere ∧ audience keys ∧ no read row)`. It is polled every 30 s by every user, so it must be the same indexed query as the feed (NFR-2). |","-| FR-33 | UI | Conditional button on the feed page by role. |","-| FR-34 | API | Routes under `src/app/api/announcements/` (+`[id]/`, `[id]/archive`, `[id]/ack`, `[id]/stats`, `[id]/remind`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`, `manage`) + `src/app/api/public/news`. Note that static segments (`manage`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`) coexist with `[id]`; Next resolves static first, so that is fine. All use `withHandler` + Zod `parseBody`/`parseQuery`. |","-| FR-35 | SEED | 6 announcements, idempotent, with skip-if-missing for Grade 7 (exists), MATH-7A and the parent link (B20). The scheduled one is `publishAt = now + 2 days`, so `notifiedAt` stays null and the first real cron after that sends it. The welcome and staff-meeting seeds are already published: set `notifiedAt = now` so the seed never triggers a notification storm. The expired one has `expiresAt` in the past. |","-| FR-36 | XC | `src/server/announcements/{announcements-service.ts, audience.ts}` + (from FR-27) a `maintenance.ts` following the quiz precedent, or the function lives in the service. |","-| NFR-1 | UI / XC | MUI only. Confirm archive/remind with ConfirmDialog; toasts via useToast; pickers via Autocomplete; DateTimePicker for publishAt/expiresAt; the badge via MUI Badge; the \"Unread\" dot as a Badge/Box with visually hidden text. Every component looked up through mui-mcp (the mui-mcp server is listed in this session). `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |","-| NFR-2 | perf / DM | Feed = key-set OR join on `AnnouncementAudience(type, refId)` + `Announcement(status, publishAt)` indexes. Never `resolveAudienceUserIds` on the read path. Parent with 3 children: keys come from about 3 queries over 3 children. Verify with a seeded 2,000-row integration timing test (optional; mark as non-gating if CI is noisy). |","-| NFR-3 | AUTH | `requireUser`/`requireRole` in every handler and server page; FR-10 checks in the service (not only the route). AC-3 is an integration test. |","-| NFR-4 | XC | The body is rendered only via MarkdownView. Excerpt/email text = plain text (B16), never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Titles are plain strings. |","-| NFR-5 | UI | The unread dot has a visually-hidden \"Unread\" label (MUI `visuallyHidden` from `@mui/utils`, which ships with MUI). |","-| NFR-6 | AUTH | 404 for non-members on detail/ack/stats (not 403, to avoid existence leaks; stats → 404 for non-author non-admin). Files → the resolver denies (the files route maps that). Scheduled/expired → hidden from feeds and from non-author, non-admin detail. |","-| NFR-7 | XC | DB columns are UTC `DateTime`. The composer converts school-tz local → UTC on the server (or the client sends ISO with the tz applied). Displays use `formatInSchoolTz(getSchoolTimezone())`. |","-| NFR-8 | XC | Reuse list: notify, audit, registerFileAccess/attachFiles, toCsv, MarkdownEditor/View, FileUpload/FileList, DataTable, UserPicker (likely unused: pickers are entity pickers, not users), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, getSchoolTimezone, formatInSchoolTz, withHandler/parse*, assertCanViewCourse. |","-| NFR-9 | scope | No comments, reactions, i18n or SMS, and no public website pages. Just the service + the `/api/public/news` route. |","-| NFR-10 | TEST | Unit: audience matching per type × flag (pure key-set matcher, so no DB is needed), `assertCanTarget` rules, markdownToPlainText. Integration: an agreement property test over every seed user × every seed announcement audience; publishDueAnnouncements run twice / concurrently → one notification set; AC-3 403; AC-5 reminder 20 + 429. E2E: admin composes with ack → parent reads + acks → admin stats. The fixture creates the 6A child + Pat link (§4 A5). |","-| NFR-11 | XC | `logger` in all new server code, including the maintenance hook. |","+| FR-1 | DM | Conversation, ConversationParticipant (`@@unique([conversationId,userId])`, `@@index([userId])`, per-user `lastReadAt`, `mutedAt`/`archivedAt`, `leftAt`), Message (`@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, which NFR-2 depends on; `editedAt`, `deletedAt`), MessageAttachment (messageId, fileId; cascade on message), MessageReport + `ReportStatus`, MessagingSettings (userId unique, quietStart/End `String? HH:mm`). Add `updatedAt` per convention (A2). |","+| FR-2 | DM, API, AUTH | `User.isSafeguardingLead`. It can only be edited via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (B13) and is meaningful only for ADMIN. |","+| FR-3 | DM, SVC | `MessageRevision(messageId, body, createdAt)`, `@@index([messageId])`. Written in the same tx as the edit (original body before overwrite). Cascade with Message (messages are never hard-deleted anyway, NFR-3). |","+| FR-4 | DM, JOB | `PendingMessageEmail(userId, conversationId, dueAt)`, `@@unique([userId, conversationId])` so repeated sends upsert one row (the first unread message sets dueAt = now+10 min; later sends keep the earliest dueAt). `@@index([dueAt])`. |","+| FR-5 | SVC, AUTH | `canMessage(sender, recipient)` is a pure decision over pre-loaded relationship facts. Expose a batch form `messageableIds(sender, candidateIds)` to avoid N+1 queries for groups (≤25) and contacts (FR-8). Matrix: ADMIN→any, any→ADMIN, TEACHER↔TEACHER, TEACHER→STUDENT (managed course or homeroom, B8), TEACHER→PARENT (via the linked child under the same rule), STUDENT→own teachers, PARENT→linked child's teachers, all others false. Symmetry: student→teacher uses the same relation as teacher→student. Disabled/archived recipients → false. |","+| FR-6 | SVC, AUTH | Create conversation in one tx: participants = creator ∪ recipients (dedupe, exclude self from count rules), 2..25 total. Check `canMessage(creator, each)`. If any STUDENT is present, require ≥1 TEACHER/ADMIN. Any violation → 403 with nothing created. \"Students may reply in staff groups but cannot start student-student\" follows from canMessage(student, student)=false at create, plus the send-time rule (FR-7) being evaluated per-sender against **staff** participants only (A4). |","+| FR-7 | SVC, AUTH, UI | Send-time re-check. Non-staff sender: allowed iff canMessage(sender, p) holds for at least one remaining staff participant (A4). Otherwise 403 with code/reason `RELATIONSHIP_ENDED`. Staff always pass. `GET /api/conversations/:id` returns `canSend: boolean` so the composer shows the disabled message without a failed POST. |","+| FR-8 | SVC, API | `GET /api/messaging/contacts?q=`: role-specific grouped queries (PARENT: per child, \"My child's teachers (<child>)\"; STUDENT: \"My teachers\"; TEACHER: \"Students in <course>\", \"Parents of students in <course>\", homeroom, staff; all: \"School office\" = ADMINs). Status ACTIVE only. `q` filters on name. Cap each group (e.g. 50). |","+| FR-9 | UI, API | `/messages` layout with a two-pane `useMediaQuery(theme.breakpoints.down('md'))`, single pane + back below 768 px (theme `md`=900, so use a custom `down(768)` or confirm breakpoint, A8). List from `GET /api/conversations?archived=&q=` sorted `lastMessageAt desc`, with preview and `unreadCount` per row. Route: `/messages` and `/messages/[conversationId]`. |","+| FR-10 | UI, API | `GET /api/conversations/:id/messages?before=<id>&limit=30` (keyset on `(createdAt,id)`). Deleted messages are returned with `body: null, deleted: true` and attachments stripped for normal users (NFR-3: content is never exposed to non-safeguarding users). Day grouping in the school timezone (B11). |","+| FR-11 | UI, XC | Composer validation shared by the client and `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts` (body trim 1..5000, ≤5 fileIds). Enter=send / Shift+Enter=newline. Counter shows at >4500. |","+| FR-12 | UI | New-conversation dialog: Autocomplete multi-select grouped by contacts label, subject ≤120, first message. It posts `POST /api/conversations` with `{participantIds, subject?, body, fileIds?}`, creating the conversation + first message atomically. Also opened prefilled from FR-16/FR-17. |","+| FR-13 | UI, API, XC | 5 s poll of `?after=<lastId>` on the visible thread. 30 s poll on the list + nav badge. Gate on `document.visibilityState` (B16). The `after` query must also surface **edits/deletes** of already-loaded messages, or edits only appear on reload (A9). |","+| FR-14 | API, SVC, UI | `POST /api/conversations/:id/read` (sets lastReadAt=now and marks this conversation's unread `message.received` notifications read; deletes the PendingMessageEmail row), `/mute`, `/archive` (toggle body `{archived}`), `/leave`. Leave: set `leftAt`, which blocks further reads/sends for that user. Refuse (409/403) for the creator when `involvesStudent` is true. Group-only: DMs with 2 participants cannot be left (A10). Sending auto-unarchives for other participants? (A11). |","+| FR-15 | SVC, API | `PATCH /api/messages/:id` / `DELETE` (soft: `deletedAt`). Sender only, `now - createdAt ≤ 15 min`, not already deleted. Edit writes a MessageRevision + `editedAt` in one tx. No hard-delete path exists anywhere. |","+| FR-16 | UI | Student page actions (surface per B14). TEACHER/ADMIN \"Message parents\": participants = linked parents (+ creator). Hide the action if there are none or canMessage fails. PARENT \"Message teacher\": picker of the child's teachers (subset of contacts) → dialog. |","+| FR-17 | UI | Roster selection + action (B15). TEACHER only (ADMIN may also be offered, harmless). |","+| FR-18 | CFG, API, UI | Nav entry + badge (B16). `GET /api/messaging/unread-count` = count of the user's non-left participations where `lastMessageAt > coalesce(lastReadAt, epoch)` (count conversations, not messages: cheap, index-friendly). Archived conversations excluded? (A11). |","+| FR-19 | NOTIF, SVC | After the send tx commits: for each other participant not muted and not left, delete older unread `message.received` rows with the same link (B2), then `notify()` in-app only (B3). Title \"New message from <sender>\", body = 200-char plain preview, link `/messages/<id>`. |","+| FR-20 | JOB, DM, NOTIF | Upsert a PendingMessageEmail (dueAt=now+10 min) for recipients whose email pref is on (B3). Job per B10. Quiet hours read from MessagingSettings, evaluated in the school timezone (B11). |","+| FR-21 | UI, API, DM | MessagingSettings GET (defaults: no quiet hours) / PUT, Zod `HH:mm` regex. Both-or-neither validation. start == end is rejected. Applies to all roles (A3). |","+| FR-22 | API, SVC, NOTIF | `POST /api/messages/:id/report {reason ≤1000}`. Participant only. Allowed on own/others' messages (or other people's only? A12). One OPEN report per (message, reporter) to avoid spam (unique or check). Then FR-26 notify. |","+| FR-23 | UI, API, AUTH, XC | `/admin/safeguarding` (tabs Reports / Conversations), gated by `requireSafeguardingLead` (B7). `GET /api/safeguarding/reports?status=` with OPEN first, then createdAt desc. Detail includes the message, ±5 messages (including deleted and with revisions) and participants. `PATCH /api/safeguarding/reports/:id {action: review\\|dismiss, note?}` sets status, reviewedById, reviewedAt and note, then calls `audit()` (NFR-11). The nav entry is shown only to leads (the nav filter is role-based, so either show it to ADMIN and 403 non-leads, or extend NavItem with a predicate, A13). |","+| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH | `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations?participantId=&from=&to=` with `involvesStudent: true`, paginated. `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations/:id` = read-only full thread with deleted bodies and `revisions[]`. Same lead gate. |","+| FR-25 | XC, AUTH | `audit({action:'safeguarding.conversation.view', entityType:'Conversation', entityId})` on every safeguarding conversation view **and** on report detail views, since they expose conversation context. Done in the service, so both the API and the server page paths are covered. |","+| FR-26 | NOTIF | Notify `User where role=ADMIN, isSafeguardingLead, status ACTIVE` with `message.reported` (email allowed via notify's normal path: no deferral). Link `/admin/safeguarding?report=<id>`. The body must not include the message text (keep emails minimal). |","+| FR-27 | FILE, AUTH | B6. Send validates that each fileId is owned by the sender, unattached, and context 'message', then attaches in the tx (contextId = messageId). |","+| FR-28 | API, XC | All routes under `src/app/api/{conversations,messages,messaging,safeguarding,me/messaging-settings}`. Thin handlers + Zod + services in `src/server/messaging/`. Standard ok/paginated/error shapes. |","+| FR-29 | SEED | B18. |","+| FR-30 | SVC, DM | `involvesStudent` is computed in the create tx and is immutable afterwards (no participant-add API exists, so it stays correct). |","+| FR-31 | SVC | Update `lastMessageAt` in the send tx. `@@index` on ConversationParticipant `(userId)` + Conversation `lastMessageAt` serves the list ordering. Edits/deletes do **not** bump it. |","+| FR-32 | AUTH | B8: `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`. Resolved as yes (intake default, matches the existing `teaches()`). |","+| NFR-1 | AUTH, XC | Every service entry takes the SessionUser and loads `ConversationParticipant(conversationId, userId, leftAt null)` first. Non-participant → 404. Safeguarding → `requireSafeguardingLead`. File resolver per B6. Contacts never leak non-messageable users. |","+| NFR-2 | DM, API | `after` poll = participant check (unique-index lookup) + `Message where conversationId, (createdAt,id) > cursor` on `@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, `take 100`. Return `[]` fast. The 30 s list/unread polls use the participant index. Avoid count-per-message aggregation for unread (FR-18). |","+| NFR-3 | DM, SVC, AUTH | No DELETE that removes rows. FK cascades exist only for actual tree cleanup. Deleted/edited originals are exposed only through safeguarding services. |","+| NFR-4 | API, XC | B5. Applies to `POST /api/conversations/:id/messages`. Recommend counting `POST /api/conversations` (it also sends) against the same key. |","+| NFR-5 | UI, XC | MUI only; B19/B20. Badge, Drawer/List, Autocomplete, TimePicker, Tabs, Menu, Chip, TextField. |","+| NFR-6 | XC | `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts`, `src/server/messaging/{contact-rules,conversations,messages,notifications,quiet-hours,safeguarding,maintenance}.ts`, logger, cuid, UTC storage. |","+| NFR-7 | UI | See FR-9 (breakpoint, A8). |","+| NFR-8 | XC | A 5 s poll guarantees ≤ ~5 s + request latency < 6 s. No websockets/SSE. |","+| NFR-9 | XC | There is no reactions, typing or broadcast endpoint. Do not touch announcements (PRD-12 is absent). |","+| NFR-10 | TEST | `tests/unit/messaging/contact-rules.test.ts` (matrix incl. co-teacher, homeroom, DROPPED enrollment, group student-needs-staff, 26 participants), `quiet-hours.test.ts` (wrap midnight). `tests/integration/messaging/` (notification collapse, quiet-hours deferral via maintenance job, revision capture, 15-min window, rate limit, non-participant 404, safeguarding 403 + audit). `tests/e2e/messaging.spec.ts` (two browser contexts parent→teacher < 6 s; student→student blocked in the picker and on POST 403). |","+| NFR-11 | XC | Audit report review/dismiss and `isSafeguardingLead` changes. Users' own edits/deletes of their messages are not \"someone else's\" records, so no audit is needed. |"," ","-## 3. Risks and conflicts for arch-design-system","+## 3. New surface summary (for traceability)"," ","-| # | Risk / conflict | Recommendation |","-|---|---|---|","-| R1 | **Two audience code paths must agree** (FR-7, NFR-10). | Single source of rules: the `UserAudienceKeys` builder + a pure `matchesAudience(audience, keys)` + `audienceWhere(keys)`. `resolveAudienceUserIds` is written separately (set expansion) but tested against the matcher for every seed user. |","-| R2 | **FR-26 per-instance `mandatoryInApp`** isn't expressible in the static registry (B9). | Two type keys (`announcement.published`, `announcement.published_ack`), or accept a static `true`. Design picks one and records it as an ADR. |","-| R3 | **FR-1 \"exactly as specified\" vs. the needed additions** (`lastRemindedAt`, indexes, possibly `publishedAt`). | Add them as explicitly flagged additions; intake already pre-approved `lastRemindedAt`. |","-| R4 | **Feed ordering by \"newest\"** when publishAt is null for publish-now. | Set `publishAt = now` on publish-now so one column orders everything. |","-| R5 | **Status column vs. read-time visibility** (FR-16). | Visibility is computed from `publishAt`. The maintenance claim also flips SCHEDULED→PUBLISHED for the manage view. The UI should derive the display status with the same predicate, so it is correct between cron ticks. |","-| R6 | **Manage-view reach** (FR-23) means resolving N audiences per page. | Per-page live resolve (pageSize ≤ 50); `ponytail:` note for a `recipientCount` snapshot later. |","-| R7 | **Notification fan-out** on SCHOOL announcements (thousands of userIds in one notify). | Chunk userIds (e.g. 1,000) when calling notify. The notifiedAt claim happens before the send, so a crash mid-send loses the remainder rather than double-sending. That matches the existing quiz-release semantics; note it. |","-| R8 | **Teacher PATCH re-validation** (FR-10 on PATCH). | Run `assertCanTarget` on the *resulting* audience set whenever audiences or isPublic are present in the PATCH. |","-| R9 | **Orphan purge vs. drafts** (B7). | Attach files on every save, including drafts. |","-| R10 | **Public endpoint abuse** (FR-31). | Paginate with the max pageSize clamp from `parsePagination`, and optionally use `rateLimit` by IP. |","-| R11 | **Stats for audience changes after publish** (FR-29). | Stats use the live audience. Reads by users no longer in the audience are excluded from the percentages. Document this. |","+- **Models:** Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageAttachment, MessageRevision, MessageReport (+ReportStatus), MessagingSettings, PendingMessageEmail. Plus User.isSafeguardingLead. (FR-1..4, FR-30, FR-31)","+- **Services (`src/server/messaging/`):** contact-rules, contacts, conversations, messages, read-state, notifications/pending-email, quiet-hours, safeguarding, maintenance (`sendDueMessageEmails`). (FR-5..8, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19..27)","+- **Routes:** conversations (list/create/get/read/mute/archive/leave), conversation messages (list before/after, send), messages/:id (patch/delete/report), messaging/unread-count, messaging/contacts, me/messaging-settings, safeguarding reports + conversations, and a hook into the internal dispatch route. (FR-28, FR-20)","+- **Pages:** `/messages`, `/messages/[conversationId]`, `/admin/safeguarding`, plus a Quiet hours section on `/account/notifications`, student layout actions and roster selection. (FR-9..18, FR-21, FR-23, FR-24)","+- **Registries:** 2 notification types, 1 file context, 1 nav item (+badge). (FR-18, FR-19, FR-26, FR-27)"," ","-## 4. Assumptions carried from intake (must surface in system-design.md Overview)","+## 4. Open decisions for arch-design-system"," ","-| # | Assumption | Default |","-|---|---|---|","-| A1 | FR-5 section members = current academic-year SectionMember rows. | Members of the section row itself (a section belongs to one year). Teachers may only target current-year sections via the pickers. |","-| A2 | FR-15 drafts may have zero recipients. | Refused only on publish/schedule. |","-| A3 | Parent expansion uses linked parents of matching students; the ACTIVE filter applies to each final user. | A parent of an archived student is **not** reached through that student. Recommendation: only ACTIVE students expand to parents, and the matcher does the same. |","-| A4 | FR-17: overflow pins (>3) fall into newest-first. | Yes. |","-| A5 | AC-8: the test fixture creates Pat's 6A child + link if the seed lacks them. | Yes; the seed itself stays skip-if-missing. |","-| A6 | Archived courses (`Course.archivedAt`) in audience resolution. | Exclude archived courses from the teacher branches of GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION. Not stated in the PRD; flag it. |","-| A7 | FR-12: archive is terminal for authors; admins may still edit. | Yes. |","-| A8 | FR-25: 429 RATE_LIMITED + `lastRemindedAt` column. | Decided here (architect owns it per intake). |","+| # | Question | Recommendation | Drives |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| A1 | Co-teachers count as \"managing\" a course? | **Yes**: matches `teaches()`/`getAccessibleStudentIds`. | FR-32, FR-5 |","+| A2 | `updatedAt` on new models (the PRD block omits it)? | Add `updatedAt @updatedAt` to Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageReport and MessagingSettings (platform convention). Leave it off append-only MessageRevision, MessageAttachment and PendingMessageEmail. Treat the PRD block as the minimum field set. | FR-1, NFR-6 |","+| A3 | Quiet hours for all roles? | **All roles** (the settings endpoint is open to any role). | FR-21, FR-20 |","+| A4 | Send-time rule in groups: what does \"relationship ended\" mean when there are many participants? | Non-staff sender may send iff canMessage(sender, s) for ≥1 staff participant still present. If no staff remain (all left), they are refused. Note that staff can never leave a student group they created (FR-14). | FR-7, FR-6 |","+| A5 | Homeroom teacher reachability: current academic year only? | Filter `section.academicYear.isCurrent = true` for messaging (otherwise last year's homeroom stays reachable). Keep student-access.ts unchanged (do not modify other PRDs' behaviour). | FR-5 |","+| A6 | Where is isSafeguardingLead edited? | API/validator only (no form exists, B13). Document that the flag is set via the seed or the API. | FR-2 |","+| A7 | Does a participant who **left** keep read access to the old thread and attachments? | No: `leftAt` set → treat as non-participant (list hides it, 404 on get). Safeguarding still sees everything. | FR-14, FR-27, NFR-1 |","+| A8 | The 768 px breakpoint does not match MUI default `md` (900). | Use `theme.breakpoints.down(768)` locally, not a theme change. | FR-9, NFR-7 |","+| A9 | How do polling clients learn about edits/deletes? | `after` responses also return `changed[]` = messages in the loaded window with `updatedAt > since` (pass `since` ISO alongside `after`). Alternatively accept staleness until reload. Recommend the former (cheap; same index plus `updatedAt`). | FR-13, FR-15 |","+| A10 | Can a participant leave a 1:1 conversation? | No: \"leave group\" only applies when there are >2 participants. Archive covers 1:1. | FR-14 |","+| A11 | Does a new message unarchive the conversation for recipients, and does the unread badge count archived conversations? | Yes, unarchive for recipients on new message (standard inbox behaviour). Unread count then needs no archive filter. | FR-9, FR-14, FR-18 |","+| A12 | Can a user report their own message, or report the same message twice? | Others' messages only. One OPEN report per (message, reporter): return 409 CONFLICT otherwise. | FR-22 |","+| A13 | Nav visibility for `/admin/safeguarding` (role-only nav filter)? | Show the item to ADMIN only via a new optional `NavItem.requires?: 'safeguardingLead'` evaluated in the shell with the flag loaded server-side. The page still enforces 403. Otherwise leave it out of nav and link from the `message.reported` notification. | FR-23 |","+| A14 | Seed Pat↔Sam link missing (B18). | The seed upserts `ParentStudentLink(Pat, Sam)` if absent before creating the Pat↔Tom thread, and skips the thread if Tom does not teach Sam. | FR-29 |","+","+## 5. Risks","+","+- **Notification collapse via `link` match** (B2) is coupled to the link format. Keep link building in a single helper used by both send and read paths.","+- **Per-process rate limiter and in-memory state** (B5) are not shared across instances. This is accepted per the existing ponytail note.","+- **Email-preference bypass**: deferring email outside `notify()` (B3) must still honour `NotificationPreference` and DISABLED/ARCHIVED filtering. Reuse `resolvePrefs`, and cover it in integration tests.","+- **mui-mcp unavailable** in this session (B20). The dev phase must retry it before writing UI."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-12\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T18:00:00Z), PRD-12 Announcements & News. It has 36 FRs and 11 NFRs (47 requirements) at 94% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> All other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **SH-11 leftovers**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-12 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-12 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no Announcement* models or enums. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1: add a new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_announcements`). Add back-relations on `User` (authored, reads) and `FileObject` (attachments, and the cover image if it is an FK). |\n| B2 | `User.status` is `ACTIVE/INVITED/DISABLED/ARCHIVED` and `archivedAt` is a separate column. `notify()` filters `status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED]`, so it **includes INVITED**. | schema L17, L59; notify.ts L43 | FR-3 is stricter: audience = `status: ACTIVE, archivedAt: null`. Pass the resolved ids to `notify()`, which then filters on its own. Don't rely on notify's filter. |\n| B3 | `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId` (required). `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` has `@@index([studentId])` and a `@@unique([parentId, studentId])`. | schema L106, L144 | FR-4/5/6 parent expansion: join through the link. Parent → children is covered by the unique index's leading `parentId`. |\n| B4 | `Section(academicYearId, gradeLevelId, homeroomTeacherId?)`. `SectionMember(studentId, academicYearId)` is unique on `(studentId, academicYearId)`, and its academicYearId is denormalised. **There is no index on `sectionId`.** | schema L377-411 | FR-5: \"members\" = SectionMember rows where `academicYearId` = the section's year (that is already true per row, so filtering by `sectionId` is enough). A section belongs to one year, so the \"current year\" question reduces to \"is the section in the current year\". See §4 A1. |\n| B5 | `Course(academicYearId, sectionId?, teacherId, coTeacherIds String[], archivedAt?)`. `coTeacherIds` is queried with `has`. `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. | schema L414-447 | FR-4/5/6/10 teacher branches. `has` isn't indexable without a GIN index. The rows involved are small (only a user's own courses), so this is fine for NFR-2. Decide whether archived courses' teachers count (§4 A6). |\n| B6 | `Enrollment.status` ACTIVE/DROPPED, with `@@index([studentId, status])` and `@@unique([courseId, studentId])`. | schema L371, L450 | FR-6 student branch. Both directions are indexed. |\n| B7 | `FileObject(context, contextId)` is indexed. Uploads are created with `contextId: null`. `attachFiles(tx, context, contextId, ids)` / detach live in files-service. **`purgeOrphanFiles` deletes `contextId: null` files after 24 h.** | files-service.ts L212-244; files/purge.ts | FR-13/FR-30: attach the cover image and attachments with `context='announcement'`, `contextId=announcement.id` inside the create/update tx. A cover that is uploaded but never attached (e.g. an abandoned draft) is purged, which is correct. **A draft must still attach its files**, or they vanish after 24 h. |\n| B8 | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)`. Resolvers receive `null` for anonymous callers. Built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (contexts.ts). Resolver errors deny. `/api/files/` is already in PUBLIC_API_PATHS. | files/access.ts; contexts.ts; public-routes.ts | FR-30: add `register('announcement', announcementResolver)` to `registerBuiltInContexts` so it is guaranteed loaded, rather than as a side-effect import. Anonymous downloads already route through, so no public-route change is needed for files. |\n| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). `COMMUNICATION` exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a **static boolean per type**. | notifications/types.ts | **FR-26 conflict**: \"mandatoryInApp true when requiresAck\" can't be expressed per instance. Options: (a) two types, `announcement.published` (mandatoryInApp false) and `announcement.published_ack` (true); or (b) one type with `mandatoryInApp: true`. Recommend (a) as the smallest faithful mapping. **arch-design-system decides.** |\n| B10 | `notify({type, userIds, title, body, link, email:{template:'generic-notification', data}})` dedupes, never throws, and is called after commit. It truncates body to BODY_MAX and drops non-relative links. | notify.ts L8-60 | FR-27/28: call it after the notifiedAt claim commits. `link: /announcements/${id}`. Large audiences (a SCHOOL announcement can be thousands of users) go through one `findMany` + `createMany`. That's acceptable, but chunk the userIds if notify's `in` lists get large. |\n| B11 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` runs each pass in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take: BATCH)` → `updateMany({where:{id, claimCol: null}})` → act only if `count === 1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts L28-43 | FR-27: `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` copies this pattern exactly: `where status SCHEDULED, publishAt <= now, notifiedAt null`, claim `notifiedAt`. Publish-now uses the same claim helper, so one code path sends. |\n| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes both `RATE_LIMITED` (429) and `CONFLICT` (409). `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` exist. | src/server/http.ts | FR-34 handler conventions. FR-25: recommend **429 RATE_LIMITED** with `details.retryAfter` (ISO). It is semantically a time-based throttle, and intake suggested the same. |\n| B13 | `audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request})` never throws. The action convention is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|archive\\|delete`. | src/server/audit.ts | FR-12: `announcement.update` / `announcement.archive` when an admin acts on another author's row. Also audit the author's own archive (cheap; optional). |\n| B14 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` (formula-injection safe). | src/server/csv.ts | FR-24 `?format=csv`. |\n| B15 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from **assignments-service.ts**, not a shared module. `formatInSchoolTz` is in src/lib/dates.ts. | assignments-service.ts L64; src/lib/dates.ts L7 | NFR-7: reuse both. Importing `getSchoolTimezone` from assignments-service is the existing precedent (contexts.ts already imports from it). Don't duplicate it. |\n| B16 | `MarkdownView` = react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema) rendering to MUI components. **There is no Markdown→plain-text helper** in the codebase. | src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx | FR-18 (200-char excerpt) and FR-28 (300-char email body) need a new small pure `markdownToPlainText(md)` (e.g. in `src/lib/markdown-text.ts`). Plain text rendered by React/the email template is escaped, so NFR-4 is met as long as the excerpt is never rendered as HTML/Markdown. Prefer a regex strip over a new dependency (remark is already installed transitively if an AST approach is preferred). |\n| B17 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `navigation` is a static array. `NotificationBell` polls `/api/notifications/unread-count` every 30 s, gated by visibility, and shows an MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L42-62 | FR-32: add an optional `badge?: 'announcements-unread'` key (or a badge endpoint string) to NavItem. The sidebar renders a polled Badge for items that have one. Reuse the bell's polling hook shape. |\n| B18 | `courseTabs` is a static array with `roles`. | src/config/course-tabs.ts | FR-21: `{ key: 'announcements', label: 'Announcements', href: id => /courses/${id}/announcements, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. |\n| B19 | `assertCanViewCourse` covers ADMIN, TEACHER (teacher or co-teacher only, **not homeroom**), STUDENT (enrollment) and PARENT (child enrolled). `canSeeDrafts` checks the course-manager test. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts L25+ | FR-21 gate: `assertCanViewCourse` and then the normal audience filter. FR-10 \"courses they manage\" = the same `teacherId \\|\\| coTeacherIds.includes` test, so reuse it rather than re-deriving. |\n| B20 | Seed: Tom/Sam/Pat by email. Courses are looked up with `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` and skipped if missing. The Grade 7 GradeLevel row **is** seeded. No 7A/7B/6A sections and no `ParentStudentLink` rows are created by the seed (they come from other scripts/fixtures, if at all). | prisma/seed.ts L18-22, L109-115, L275-305 | FR-35: grade/course/section-targeted seeds skip when their target is missing, using the same `logger.info`/`console.log` style. School-wide, staff and public seeds always run. Idempotency: upsert by a stable title + author, or check for existence first. |\n| B21 | Test layout: `tests/unit`, `tests/integration/<feature>/`, `tests/e2e/*.spec.ts` + `helpers/`. | tests/ | NFR-10: `tests/unit/announcements/*`, `tests/integration/announcements/*`, `tests/e2e/announcements.spec.ts`. |\n| B22 | `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0 is installed (`@mui/x-data-grid` too). | package.json | FR-13 publishAt/expiresAt: DateTimePicker. FR-23/24 tables: the existing `DataTable` component. Look up via mui-mcp per NFR-1. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend for **Concern**: DM = data model / migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance/cron, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | 2 enums, 4 models, 1 migration. AnnouncementRead has a composite PK `(announcementId, userId)`. **Needed beyond the PRD's model** (flag as deliberate additions): `Announcement.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` (FR-25), `notifiedAt DateTime?` (FR-27, likely already in the spec since FR-27 names it), and indexes `AnnouncementAudience @@index([type, refId])` and `Announcement @@index([status, publishAt])` (NFR-2). AnnouncementAudience columns implied by FR-3..FR-6: `type`, `refId?` (null for SCHOOL/STAFF), `includeStudents/Parents/Teachers` booleans. Cascade deletes from Announcement to its children. |\n| FR-2 | XC / validation | `src/lib/validators/announcements.ts`, isomorphic Zod schema, shared by the composer and the handlers. Also validate: `expiresAt > publishAt` when both are set; ROLE refId ∈ Role enum; refId required unless SCHOOL/STAFF; at least one include flag true for GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION/COURSE. |\n| FR-3 | SVC | `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`. `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` returns a set union over the rows, all filtered to `ACTIVE && archivedAt null`. SCHOOL = all, STAFF = role ∈ {ADMIN, TEACHER}, ROLE = role = refId. Do the active filter **once** at the end, including on parents. |\n| FR-4 | SVC | GRADE_LEVEL: students via `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`; parents via ParentStudentLink of **those students** (before the active filter on the students? see §4 A3); teachers = `teacherId` ∪ `coTeacherIds` of courses where `section.gradeLevelId = refId AND academicYear.isCurrent`. |\n| FR-5 | SVC | SECTION: SectionMember(sectionId) students, their parents, `homeroomTeacherId` plus the teachers/co-teachers of `Course.sectionId = refId`. \"Current year\" is implicit (§4 A1). |\n| FR-6 | SVC | COURSE: `Enrollment(courseId, status ACTIVE)` students, their parents, teacher plus coTeachers. |\n| FR-7 | SVC / perf | `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`. **Key design point**: compute a per-user *membership key set* once (≤ ~4 small queries): role; own/children's gradeLevelIds; own/children's sectionIds (current year); own/children's ACTIVE courseIds; for teachers, managed courseIds + their sectionIds/gradeLevelIds + homeroom sectionIds. Then audience matching is a pure function over `(audience, keys)`. The same key set also becomes a Prisma `where` (an OR of `{type, refId in keys[type], include<Flag>: true}`) for the feed (FR-17/NFR-2). This puts the rules in one place (intake key risk), and `resolveAudienceUserIds` is the inverse expansion. The agreement test (NFR-10) checks both. For a parent the flag is `includeParents`, and the keys come from the children. |\n| FR-8 | SVC / XC | audience.ts must not import Announcement types. Its input is `{type, refId, includeStudents, includeParents, includeTeachers}[]`, so PRD-14 can reuse it. Export the `AudienceType` enum from Prisma. |\n| FR-9 | AUTH | ADMIN: any type, `isPublic` allowed. |\n| FR-10 | AUTH | `assertCanTarget(user, audiences, isPublic)` in the service, called by **both** create and update (PATCH can change the audience). TEACHER: COURSE where they manage the course (B19); SECTION where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Everything else, and `isPublic=true`, → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')` 403. On PATCH by a teacher, also re-check when `isPublic` is omitted but already true (it can't be, since only admins set it). |\n| FR-11 | AUTH | `requireRole('ADMIN','TEACHER')` on POST, PATCH, archive, preview-audience, manage, stats and remind. |\n| FR-12 | AUTH / audit | Edit: `authorId === user.id \\|\\| ADMIN`. Archive: same. Archive sets ARCHIVED (terminal for authors, §4 A7). Admin-on-others → `audit()`. A teacher who is no longer allowed to target the existing audience (e.g. lost co-teacher status) → PATCH fails on re-validation. That's acceptable. |\n| FR-13 | UI | Pages `/announcements/new` and `/announcements/[id]/edit` (server page + client form). Reuse MarkdownEditor, FileUpload (context 'announcement'), FileList, Autocomplete pickers per audience type (grade levels, sections, courses, roles). Teachers only see their own courses/homeroom in the pickers (UX; the server still enforces). Public toggle hidden for non-admins. Show and accept dates in the school tz (NFR-7). |\n| FR-14 | API / SVC | `POST /api/announcements/preview-audience`, body = audiences[] (same Zod schema). Run `assertCanTarget` first so the preview can't enumerate other audiences' sizes. Returns `{total, byRole:{STUDENT,PARENT,TEACHER,ADMIN}}`. Debounce in the UI. Uses `resolveAudienceUserIds` + `groupBy role` (or one count query). |\n| FR-15 | SVC | On transition to PUBLISHED/SCHEDULED (create or PATCH), resolve the count and if it is 0, `VALIDATION_ERROR`. Drafts are exempt (§4 A2). Scheduled ones are validated at schedule time, not again at publishAt; an emptied audience just notifies nobody. |\n| FR-16 | SVC / XC | **Visibility predicate in one place**: `visibleWhere(now) = { OR: [{status: PUBLISHED}, {status: SCHEDULED, publishAt: {lte: now}}], AND: [{OR: [{expiresAt: null}, {expiresAt: {gt: now}}]}] }`. Use it in the feed, detail, ack, files, public news and unread-count. Precedent: `isAssignmentVisible`/`isLessonVisible`. The status column stays SCHEDULED after publishAt (unless the maintenance run also flips it to PUBLISHED; recommend it does, in the same claim, for clean manage-view status). |\n| FR-17 | API / SVC / perf | `GET /api/announcements`: `visibleWhere(now) AND audiences: { some: audienceWhereForKeys(keys) }`. Plus `?filter=unread` (`reads: {none: {userId}}` or `readAt null`) and `?filter=ack` (`requiresAck AND no acknowledgedAt`). Ordering: up to 3 pinned first (separate `take:3` query on page 1, exclude those ids from the main list), then newest by **effective publish time** (`publishAt ?? createdAt` → store a `publishedAt`, or order by `publishAt` and set it on publish-now). Overflow pins fall into the newest list (§4 A4). Include the per-user read row via a `reads: {where:{userId}}` include. |\n| FR-18 | API / UI | The card DTO = cover fileId, title, author name + role, date, audience chips (labels need names for grade/section/course refIds, so batch-load by refId), `excerpt` (B16, 200 chars, computed server-side), attachment count (`_count`). |\n| FR-19 | API / AUTH | `GET /api/announcements/:id`: access if ADMIN, the author, or (visible AND isUserInAudience). Otherwise **404** (don't leak existence, NFR-6). Upsert AnnouncementRead `{readAt: now}` only for audience members (not for admins/authors outside the audience, since that would distort stats). Client renders the body with MarkdownView. |\n| FR-20 | API / AUTH | `POST /:id/ack`: visible AND requiresAck AND audience member → upsert `{readAt ?? now, acknowledgedAt ?? now}` (idempotent; keep the first ack time). Non-member → 404. `requiresAck=false` → 409 or VALIDATION_ERROR. Display with `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| FR-21 | API / CFG / UI | `GET /api/announcements?courseId=` → `assertCanViewCourse` then the feed query additionally filtered to `audiences some {type: COURSE, refId: courseId}`. The user must still be in the audience (a parent-only course announcement isn't shown to the course's students). Course tab page `/courses/[id]/announcements`. |\n| FR-22 | SVC / UI | Parent feed only: for each item, find matching audience rows and map them back to the children whose keys matched → `forChildren: [{id, firstName}]`. This falls out of the key-set design if keys are tracked per child (`Map<refKey, childIds>`). |\n| FR-23 | API / UI | `GET /api/announcements/manage`: no visibility filter. TEACHER `authorId = me`, ADMIN all. Reach = resolved recipient count (**expensive per row**: compute for the current page only; or snapshot `recipientCount` at publish and recompute live only on stats). Read % = `count(reads readAt not null) / reach`; ack % similar. Recommendation: resolve audiences per page row (≤ pageSize calls); keep it simple, a ponytail note for a snapshot later. |\n| FR-24 | API / UI | `GET /:id/stats`: author or ADMIN, else 404. Recipients = `resolveAudienceUserIds` (live) LEFT JOIN reads. Filters `?filter=unread\\|unacked`. `?format=csv` → `toCsv`, `Content-Disposition` attachment. Percentages over the live recipient set (AC-5: 30/50 = 60%). Readers who later left the audience are not counted. |\n| FR-25 | API / NOTIF / DM | `POST /:id/remind`: author or ADMIN. requiresAck must be true and the announcement visible. Atomic claim: `updateMany({where:{id, OR:[{lastRemindedAt:null},{lastRemindedAt:{lte: now-24h}}]}, data:{lastRemindedAt: now}})`. `count 0` → **429 RATE_LIMITED** (decision, B12). Then notify `announcement.reminder` to recipients − acknowledged. Returns `{notified: n}` (AC-5: 20). |\n| FR-26 | CFG / NOTIF | Add the types to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` (B9 conflict). roles: ALL. reminder: COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true (an ack is being chased). |\n| FR-27 | JOB / NOTIF | One `claimAndNotifyPublished(id, now)` helper: `updateMany({where:{id, notifiedAt:null, <visible>}, data:{notifiedAt: now, status: PUBLISHED}})`. If count = 1 → resolve recipients → notify. Called by publish-now (after the tx commits) and by `publishDueAnnouncements(now)` (batch 200, B11). Hook it into the dispatch route in its own try/catch. |\n| FR-28 | NOTIF | Email data: `{title, body: markdownToPlainText(body).slice(0,300), ctaLabel:'Read announcement', ctaUrl}`. Check GenericNotificationData's field names when designing. |\n| FR-29 | SVC | Follows from the notifiedAt claim: PATCH never clears notifiedAt. Also a draft → PATCH publish of an already-notified row (an archived-then-edited one) must not resend. |\n| FR-30 | FILE / AUTH | `announcementResolver(user, file)`: load the announcement by `file.contextId`. If `isPublic && visible` → true (including null user). If `!user` → false. If ADMIN or author → true. If visible && isUserInAudience → true. Else false. Register it in `registerBuiltInContexts` (B8). |\n| FR-31 | API / CFG | `getPublicNews({page})` in announcements-service: `isPublic && visibleWhere(now)`, a minimal DTO (no author email, no audience). Route `src/app/api/public/news/route.ts`. Add `'/api/public/news'` (exact match) to PUBLIC_API_PATHS. Consider `rateLimit` by IP since it is unauthenticated (cheap; the helper exists). |\n| FR-32 | CFG / UI / API | Nav entry for ALL_ROLES + the badge (B17). `GET /api/announcements/unread-count` = `count(visibleWhere ∧ audience keys ∧ no read row)`. It is polled every 30 s by every user, so it must be the same indexed query as the feed (NFR-2). |\n| FR-33 | UI | Conditional button on the feed page by role. |\n| FR-34 | API | Routes under `src/app/api/announcements/` (+`[id]/`, `[id]/archive`, `[id]/ack`, `[id]/stats`, `[id]/remind`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`, `manage`) + `src/app/api/public/news`. Note that static segments (`manage`, `unread-count`, `preview-audience`) coexist with `[id]`; Next resolves static first, so that is fine. All use `withHandler` + Zod `parseBody`/`parseQuery`. |\n| FR-35 | SEED | 6 announcements, idempotent, with skip-if-missing for Grade 7 (exists), MATH-7A and the parent link (B20). The scheduled one is `publishAt = now + 2 days`, so `notifiedAt` stays null and the first real cron after that sends it. The welcome and staff-meeting seeds are already published: set `notifiedAt = now` so the seed never triggers a notification storm. The expired one has `expiresAt` in the past. |\n| FR-36 | XC | `src/server/announcements/{announcements-service.ts, audience.ts}` + (from FR-27) a `maintenance.ts` following the quiz precedent, or the function lives in the service. |\n| NFR-1 | UI / XC | MUI only. Confirm archive/remind with ConfirmDialog; toasts via useToast; pickers via Autocomplete; DateTimePicker for publishAt/expiresAt; the badge via MUI Badge; the \"Unread\" dot as a Badge/Box with visually hidden text. Every component looked up through mui-mcp (the mui-mcp server is listed in this session). `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |\n| NFR-2 | perf / DM | Feed = key-set OR join on `AnnouncementAudience(type, refId)` + `Announcement(status, publishAt)` indexes. Never `resolveAudienceUserIds` on the read path. Parent with 3 children: keys come from about 3 queries over 3 children. Verify with a seeded 2,000-row integration timing test (optional; mark as non-gating if CI is noisy). |\n| NFR-3 | AUTH | `requireUser`/`requireRole` in every handler and server page; FR-10 checks in the service (not only the route). AC-3 is an integration test. |\n| NFR-4 | XC | The body is rendered only via MarkdownView. Excerpt/email text = plain text (B16), never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Titles are plain strings. |\n| NFR-5 | UI | The unread dot has a visually-hidden \"Unread\" label (MUI `visuallyHidden` from `@mui/utils`, which ships with MUI). |\n| NFR-6 | AUTH | 404 for non-members on detail/ack/stats (not 403, to avoid existence leaks; stats → 404 for non-author non-admin). Files → the resolver denies (the files route maps that). Scheduled/expired → hidden from feeds and from non-author, non-admin detail. |\n| NFR-7 | XC | DB columns are UTC `DateTime`. The composer converts school-tz local → UTC on the server (or the client sends ISO with the tz applied). Displays use `formatInSchoolTz(getSchoolTimezone())`. |\n| NFR-8 | XC | Reuse list: notify, audit, registerFileAccess/attachFiles, toCsv, MarkdownEditor/View, FileUpload/FileList, DataTable, UserPicker (likely unused: pickers are entity pickers, not users), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, getSchoolTimezone, formatInSchoolTz, withHandler/parse*, assertCanViewCourse. |\n| NFR-9 | scope | No comments, reactions, i18n or SMS, and no public website pages. Just the service + the `/api/public/news` route. |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | Unit: audience matching per type × flag (pure key-set matcher, so no DB is needed), `assertCanTarget` rules, markdownToPlainText. Integration: an agreement property test over every seed user × every seed announcement audience; publishDueAnnouncements run twice / concurrently → one notification set; AC-3 403; AC-5 reminder 20 + 429. E2E: admin composes with ack → parent reads + acks → admin stats. The fixture creates the 6A child + Pat link (§4 A5). |\n| NFR-11 | XC | `logger` in all new server code, including the maintenance hook. |\n\n## 3. Risks and conflicts for arch-design-system\n\n| # | Risk / conflict | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1 | **Two audience code paths must agree** (FR-7, NFR-10). | Single source of rules: the `UserAudienceKeys` builder + a pure `matchesAudience(audience, keys)` + `audienceWhere(keys)`. `resolveAudienceUserIds` is written separately (set expansion) but tested against the matcher for every seed user. |\n| R2 | **FR-26 per-instance `mandatoryInApp`** isn't expressible in the static registry (B9). | Two type keys (`announcement.published`, `announcement.published_ack`), or accept a static `true`. Design picks one and records it as an ADR. |\n| R3 | **FR-1 \"exactly as specified\" vs. the needed additions** (`lastRemindedAt`, indexes, possibly `publishedAt`). | Add them as explicitly flagged additions; intake already pre-approved `lastRemindedAt`. |\n| R4 | **Feed ordering by \"newest\"** when publishAt is null for publish-now. | Set `publishAt = now` on publish-now so one column orders everything. |\n| R5 | **Status column vs. read-time visibility** (FR-16). | Visibility is computed from `publishAt`. The maintenance claim also flips SCHEDULED→PUBLISHED for the manage view. The UI should derive the display status with the same predicate, so it is correct between cron ticks. |\n| R6 | **Manage-view reach** (FR-23) means resolving N audiences per page. | Per-page live resolve (pageSize ≤ 50); `ponytail:` note for a `recipientCount` snapshot later. |\n| R7 | **Notification fan-out** on SCHOOL announcements (thousands of userIds in one notify). | Chunk userIds (e.g. 1,000) when calling notify. The notifiedAt claim happens before the send, so a crash mid-send loses the remainder rather than double-sending. That matches the existing quiz-release semantics; note it. |\n| R8 | **Teacher PATCH re-validation** (FR-10 on PATCH). | Run `assertCanTarget` on the *resulting* audience set whenever audiences or isPublic are present in the PATCH. |\n| R9 | **Orphan purge vs. drafts** (B7). | Attach files on every save, including drafts. |\n| R10 | **Public endpoint abuse** (FR-31). | Paginate with the max pageSize clamp from `parsePagination`, and optionally use `rateLimit` by IP. |\n| R11 | **Stats for audience changes after publish** (FR-29). | Stats use the live audience. Reads by users no longer in the audience are excluded from the percentages. Document this. |\n\n## 4. Assumptions carried from intake (must surface in system-design.md Overview)\n\n| # | Assumption | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| A1 | FR-5 section members = current academic-year SectionMember rows. | Members of the section row itself (a section belongs to one year). Teachers may only target current-year sections via the pickers. |\n| A2 | FR-15 drafts may have zero recipients. | Refused only on publish/schedule. |\n| A3 | Parent expansion uses linked parents of matching students; the ACTIVE filter applies to each final user. | A parent of an archived student is **not** reached through that student. Recommendation: only ACTIVE students expand to parents, and the matcher does the same. |\n| A4 | FR-17: overflow pins (>3) fall into newest-first. | Yes. |\n| A5 | AC-8: the test fixture creates Pat's 6A child + link if the seed lacks them. | Yes; the seed itself stays skip-if-missing. |\n| A6 | Archived courses (`Course.archivedAt`) in audience resolution. | Exclude archived courses from the teacher branches of GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION. Not stated in the PRD; flag it. |\n| A7 | FR-12: archive is terminal for authors; admins may still edit. | Yes. |\n| A8 | FR-25: 429 RATE_LIMITED + `lastRemindedAt` column. | Decided here (architect owns it per intake). |\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AnCxdcDNTxEHjA3Dia73yx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
