{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsjrbD6JdiX7FYJTBx6y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've rewritten `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` for SH-13. The old file was left over from SH-12, so I replaced it. All 43 requirements (FR-1 to FR-32 and NFR-1 to NFR-11) are mapped to what they need architecturally, and every requirement id cited exists in `requirements.json`. As instructed, I only wrote this one file; the other architect sub-tasks still need to replace their old SH-11/SH-12 files.\n\n**What the codebase check found that changes the design:**\n- **Message emails can't go through the normal notification call.** `notify()` queues emails immediately, but FR-20 needs them held back (10 minutes, and outside quiet hours). The plan is to create only the in-app notification there, write a `PendingMessageEmail` row, and let the existing maintenance job send the email later.\n- **Collapsing notifications has to match on the link.** The `Notification` table has no conversation column. To replace older unread notifications for the same conversation (FR-19), the code has to match on the link `/messages/<id>`.\n- **The safeguarding-lead flag isn't on the logged-in user object.** Admin access to safeguarding needs a new helper that reads the flag from the database. The file-access check for message attachments has to do the same.\n- **There's no student page header for the FR-16 buttons.** `/students/[id]` only has sub-pages. I recommend adding a shared layout with the header and actions.\n- **The course roster can't select students yet.** It's a plain server-rendered table, so FR-17 needs a client version with checkboxes.\n- **There's no admin form for users.** The safeguarding-lead flag (FR-2) can only be set by extending the user update API and its validator.\n- **The seed has no parent–student link between Pat and Sam.** The \"Pat↔Tom about Sam's homework\" conversation wouldn't pass the contact rules without one.\n\n**Decisions left for `arch-design-system`:** The notes list 14 open questions, each with a recommendation. Among them:\n- whether co-teachers count as managing a course (recommended: yes)\n- whether to add `updatedAt` to the new models (recommended: yes, for most of them)\n- that quiet hours apply to all roles\n- how the \"relationship ended\" rule works in group chats\n- limiting homeroom contact to the current school year\n- the 768px breakpoint, which doesn't match MUI's default 900px\n- how polling picks up edits and deletes\n- rules for leaving, archiving and reporting\n\n**Problem:** the MUI documentation server didn't connect this session (connection timed out). It doesn't block the architecture work, but the rules require it for UI code, so the dev phase will need it working."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11890,"cache_read_input_tokens":57913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11890},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"56451f7d-c784-4a25-a233-3bc873207cca","uuid":"e77dd010-1fe2-4abc-849b-06b16fb4260e","timestamp":"2026-11-09T17:21:44.135Z","request_id":"req_011Cgsjramnt74Qbqrf4ZAqj"}
