{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsrVSrHPxMX9vLUfdxDL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015RVVJaA25wfcBXKnjAY1nm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-14\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:10:00Z), PRD-14 School Calendar, Events & Holidays. It has 37 FRs and 12 NFRs (49 requirements) at 96% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It has 3 warnings: PRD-12 is missing, the academic-year page is missing, and new dependencies are needed. The decisions left open are in §3.\n\n> This file replaces a leftover SH-13 version. Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is also left over from SH-13. Its owning sub-task must overwrite it, and none of those files is an SH-14 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-14 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no calendar models and no `AudienceType` enum. There is no `Announcement` model and no `audience.ts`. The latest migration is `20261112000000_add_direct_messaging`. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-2/FR-3: add one new migration, e.g. `20261113000000_add_calendar`. `AudienceType` must be defined here (see D1). Add back-relations on `User` for events created, RSVPs and the feed token. |\n| B2 | Audience targets that already exist: `GradeLevel` (Grade 6/7/8 seeded), `Section` (`homeroomTeacherId`, `gradeLevelId`, per year), `SectionMember` (`@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])`), `Course` (`teacherId`, `coTeacherIds String[]`, `sectionId?`), `Enrollment` (ACTIVE/DROPPED, `@@index([studentId,status])`) and `ParentStudentLink`. `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId` exists. | schema L115-470 | FR-3: the minimal enum is `SCHOOL`, `GRADE_LEVEL`, `SECTION` and `COURSE`, plus a role filter so the seed's \"Grade 7 parents\" works (see D1). Every type resolves to student ids through existing tables. Parents are added through `ParentStudentLink`. |\n| B3 | `getScheduleForDate` and `getSchoolScheduleForDate` both contain a placeholder comment: `// PRD-14 holidays hook in here: return [] when date is a school holiday.` Both return `ScheduleEntry[]` and have no reason field. A private `schoolTimezone()` exists at L488. | timetable-service.ts L542-583 | FR-17: put the `isSchoolDay` check at those two hooks. **The return type cannot change without touching callers** (`attendance-service.ts` L130 and L472, `getCurrentSlot`). Recommendation: keep `ScheduleEntry[]` and add a sibling, e.g. `getDayInfo(date)` → `{isSchoolDay, reason}`, which callers use to show the holiday name. The alternative is a new return shape, which needs every caller updated. |\n| B4 | Both `isSchoolDay` and `getScheduleForDate` apply the teaching-weekday rule `day?.isTeaching ?? isoDay <= 5` from the `SchoolDay` table. | timetable-service.ts L552, L572 | FR-16: reuse `listSchoolDays()` (exported L112) instead of re-implementing the fallback. Watch for import cycles: calendar-service will import from timetable-service, and timetable-service calls back into `isSchoolDay`. Put the pure date→isoDay and holiday lookup in calendar-service with **no** import from timetable-service, or pass teaching days in. |\n| B5 | Attendance teacher landing is `getToday(user, date?)` and admin overview is `getOverview(date?)`. Both are fed by the schedule functions. `RegisterForm.tsx` is the register UI. | attendance-service.ts L122-150, L463-475 | FR-18: `getToday` returns `{noSchoolReason}` alongside its existing fields. Saving a register on a no-school date requires a confirm flag in the save body (e.g. `holidayOverride: true`) and the server checks it. That makes it a server-side rule, not only a dialog. |\n| B6 | The assignment editor is `courses/[courseId]/assignments/AssignmentForm.tsx`, using `DateTimePicker` on `dueAt` with school-tz `toWall/fromWall`. Quiz settings are in `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit/QuizSettingsPanel.tsx` (`availableUntil`). | grep | FR-19: both are client components. Fetch `GET /api/school-day?date=` on date change and render a non-blocking MUI `Alert`. Saving is unchanged. |\n| B7 | Notification registry `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const and its `COMMUNICATION`/`ACADEMIC` categories exist. `notify({type,userIds,title,body,link,email})` dedupes, never throws, and is called after commit. `notifyStudentAndParents` / `expandStudentRecipients` add linked parents. | notifications/types.ts; notify.ts L30, L89-120 | FR-23/28/29: add `event.created`, `event.updated` and `event.rsvp_reminder`. **`defaultEmail` is per type, but FR-28 wants it per category** (HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK email on by default). See D5. Resolve audience → userIds once, then call `notify`. |\n| B8 | The maintenance cron `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` runs each job in its own try/catch + logger (reminders, quiz, message emails). | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-23: add `sendRsvpReminders(now)` to its own isolated block. \"Once per event\" needs a claim column: `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?`, claimed with conditional `updateMany` (quiz `resultsReleasedAt` precedent). The PRD model list doesn't include that column. Adding it is a small, justified deviation (flag it). |\n| B9 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` → `{ok, retryAfterMs}`. It is per-process and marked with a `ponytail` note. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | FR-27: `rateLimit('ical:'+tokenHash, 60, 3_600_000)` → 429 `RATE_LIMITED`. Key on the **hash**, not the raw token, so raw tokens never sit in memory maps or logs. |\n| B10 | `http.ts` provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `AppError` with codes incl. `RATE_LIMITED`, `NOT_FOUND`, `FORBIDDEN` and `VALIDATION_ERROR`. `requireRole`, `requireUser`, `requirePageRole` and `requirePageUser` exist. `audit()` exists. | http.ts; requireRole.ts; audit.ts | NFR-7/8/FR-36. The feed route is the only unauthenticated handler. It returns `text/calendar` and the 404 is a plain response, not JSON. Its token parse failure and token-not-found case return the same 404. |\n| B11 | Access helpers: `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` ('ALL' for admin, own id for students, linked children for parents, enrolled + homeroom students for teachers), `assertCanViewStudent`, `assertCanManageCourse` (course-access.ts L56) and `resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId?)` (assignments-service L262). | auth/*.ts | FR-7: teacher create checks are `assertCanManageCourse` for COURSE audiences and `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` for SECTION. FR-11/FR-32 `studentId` param: use `resolveViewedStudent`/`assertCanViewStudent` (404 for other families). |\n| B12 | Deadline data sources already exist: `/api/me/assignments`, `/api/me/timetable` and `/api/me/children` routes, `Assignment @@index([courseId, dueAt])`, `Quiz @@index([courseId,status])` with `availableUntil`, and `getPersonalTimetable`. | api/me/*; schema | FR-10/FR-32: the calendar merge should call the existing service functions behind these routes (scoped to a date range), not new queries. A range filter on `dueAt`/`availableUntil` may need adding. Only PUBLISHED assignments/quizzes should be included, matching what the user can open. |\n| B13 | School timezone is read in two places: exported `getSchoolTimezone()` in assignments-service.ts L64 and private `schoolTimezone()` in timetable-service. `getSchoolSettings` (cached) is in services/settings.ts. `src/lib/dates.ts` has `schoolNow`, `formatInSchoolTz` and `ISO_DAY_NAMES`. date-fns-tz 3.2.0 is installed. | grep | NFR-3/FR-4: use `getSchoolTimezone()` and do not add a third copy. All-day ↔ `fromZonedTime(midnight, tz)` conversions belong as pure helpers in `src/lib/dates.ts` (unit-testable, client-safe). |\n| B14 | No `/admin/academic-years` page exists. Only APIs exist: `academic-years/[id]`, `…/set-current`, `…/terms`, `…/terms/generate`, and `terms.ts` service functions. Seed terms: S1 2026-08-17→2027-01-15, S2 2027-01-18→2027-06-11. | ls src/app/(app)/admin; seed.ts L91-94 | FR-20: a host page is needed (see D2). Note that the seed's gap between S1 and S2 is a weekend (Jan 16–17), so \"Add term breaks\" on seed data produces one short break. Winter break is **inside** S1 and is seeded explicitly. |\n| B15 | `navigation.ts` has `NavItem {label, href, icon, roles, group?, badge?, requires?}` and `ALL_ROLES`. The account area has `notifications` and `security` pages only, and no account nav entries. | config/navigation.ts | FR-35: add `{label:'Calendar', href:'/calendar', roles: ALL_ROLES}`. `/account/calendar` is linked from the account area like the other `/account/*` pages; no sidebar entry is needed (D6). |\n| B16 | Shared UI exists: `components/Toast/useToast`, `ConfirmDialog`, `MarkdownView`, `MarkdownEditor`, `DataTable`, `PageHeader`, `EmptyState` and `UserPicker`. `react-markdown` 10.1.0 is installed. `components/messaging` exists, but no audience builder. | ls src/components | NFR-1/NFR-9: the drawer uses `MarkdownView` and the editor uses `MarkdownEditor`. Delete confirmation uses `ConfirmDialog`. The RSVP list uses `DataTable`. CSV export reuses `src/server/csv.ts`. A new `components/AudienceBuilder` is the only new shared component (D1). |\n| B17 | `package.json` has MUI 9.5.0 for material, icons, x-charts, x-data-grid and x-date-pickers, plus `@mui/x-internals` 9.1.0 as an override. There is no `@mui/x-scheduler`, `ics` or `node-ical`. | package.json | FR-1: pin the scheduler with an exact version from MUI MCP, and check its peer range against `@mui/material` 9.5.0 and `@mui/x-internals`. NFR-6: `node-ical` as an exact-pinned devDependency. `ics` is not needed, because a hand-written RFC 5545 builder (about 100 lines, pure) is easier to test for escaping and folding (tech-stack sub-task decides). |\n| B18 | Seed: academic year 2026-2027 is current, Grade 6/7/8 exist, and sections 7A/7B exist. **There is no \"Robotics Club\" course anywhere**, and no Announcement exists. Seeds use the `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` + skip-with-log pattern. | seed.ts; grep | FR-37: the Chess club audience needs a Robotics Club course. Either seed it (an ELECTIVE `Course`, with `CourseKind` available) or skip with a log (D7). Sports day is seeded without an announcement link. |\n| B19 | `Notification` has only `link` for context (no entity column). | schema L313-326 | FR-28/29 links: `/calendar?event=<id>` so the page can open the drawer from a query param. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern key: **DM** data model/migration, **SVC** server service, **API** route handler, **UI** page/component, **JOB** cron/maintenance, **AUTH** access boundary, **INT** change to existing module, **NOTIF** notification type, **DEP** dependency, **TEST**, **SEED**.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes for arch-design-system |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DEP | `@mui/x-scheduler` exact pin taken from the MUI MCP `useMuiDocs` + `fetchDocs`. This comes first in the dev plan. If MCP is unreachable, stop (NFR-2). Check peer deps against 9.5.0 (B17). |\n| FR-2 | DM | Enums `EventCategory`, `Recurrence` (NONE/WEEKLY/MONTHLY), `RsvpResponse` (YES/NO/MAYBE). Models `CalendarEvent`, `EventAudience` (cascade from event), `EventRsvp` (`@@id([eventId,userId])`, cascade) and `CalendarFeedToken` (`userId @unique`, `tokenHash @unique`). Add `@@index([startAt, endAt])` on events. Recurrence widens the read window, so range queries must be `startAt < to AND (endAt > from OR recurrence != NONE AND recurrenceUntil >= from)`. Index use is partial, which is fine at school scale. Possible extra columns: `rsvpReminderSentAt` (B8). |\n| FR-3 | DM, AUTH | Decision D1. The audience resolver (`resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` and `userMatchesAudience(user, audiences)`) is the hub of FR-7/10/21/23/26/28/29/31/32. Build it once, in a form PRD-12 can adopt (e.g. `src/server/audience/audience.ts`). |\n| FR-4 | SVC | Zod in `src/lib/validators/calendar.ts` (client-safe, shared with the editor dialog). Cross-field rules use `.superRefine`: endAt ≥ startAt; recurrenceUntil required when recurrence ≠ NONE and ≤ startAt + 1 year; guests 0–5. All-day normalisation (school-tz midnight, **exclusive** end) is a server-side transform, because the client sends dates and not instants. Unit-test the exclusive end (NFR-10). |\n| FR-5 | SVC | Default applied in the service when `isNoSchool` is undefined: `category in (HOLIDAY, TERM_BREAK)`. Not a DB default (it depends on another column). |\n| FR-6 | AUTH | Service-level check: a non-admin sending `isNoSchool`, `isPublic` or a HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK category gets 403. The editor UI hides these fields, but the server is authoritative. |\n| FR-7 | AUTH | A teacher's audiences must all be COURSE audiences they manage (`assertCanManageCourse`) or SECTION audiences they homeroom. SCHOOL or GRADE_LEVEL gives 403 (AC-7). This also applies on PATCH when audiences change. |\n| FR-8 | AUTH | Edit/delete when `createdById === user.id` or the user is ADMIN. Others get 403 if they can see the event, 404 otherwise. |\n| FR-9 | UI, DEP | Client page `/calendar` (server `page.tsx` does `requirePageUser`, then a client `CalendarView`). The view switches at the 768 px breakpoint via `useMediaQuery`. Agenda \"infinite scroll\" means fetching the next 30-day window on scroll. The range cap is 100 days (FR-32). Fallback components only where the Community scheduler lacks a feature. Record each fallback in system-design with its MCP doc reference. |\n| FR-10 | UI | Chips with localStorage key e.g. `calendar.sources`. Sources map 1:1 to the `sources=` query param. Timetable blocks only in Week view: don't fetch `timetable` unless the Week view is active. Holidays vs School events default: HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool` belong to \"Holidays\" only, with no duplicates (intake's default, D3). |\n| FR-11 | UI, AUTH | Parent child filter → `studentId=` (omitted = all children). Server validates via `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Deadline items carry `childName`. Event audience matching for parents uses the union of their children (and the parent's own role for role-filtered audiences). |\n| FR-12 | UI | Right `Drawer`. Data comes from the expanded item plus `GET /api/events/:id` for full detail and RSVP. \"Add to my calendar\" = `<a href=\"/api/events/:id/ics\" download>`. Edit/delete visible when `canEdit` is set; the server computes `canEdit` and returns it. |\n| FR-13 | UI | Deadline items carry an `href` set by the server (`/assignments/<id>` or the quiz route). Clicking navigates; no drawer. |\n| FR-14 | UI | `EventEditorDialog` with React Hook Form + the shared Zod schema. Uses `AudienceBuilder` (D1), the recurrence select + until date, the RSVP switch + deadline, and `MarkdownEditor`. Admin-only fields are rendered only for ADMIN (FR-6). |\n| FR-15 | SVC | Pure `expandOccurrences(event, from, to)` in calendar-service (or `src/lib/calendar/recurrence.ts`). WEEKLY = +7 days **in wall-clock school time** (DST, NFR-3), not +7×24h. MONTHLY-by-date: skip months without that day (e.g. 31st). Document this, because RRULE `BYMONTHDAY=31` also skips, so UI and feed agree. Each occurrence id = `${eventId}:${occurrenceStartISO}`. Heavily unit-tested. |\n| FR-16 | SVC | `isSchoolDay(date)` → `{isSchoolDay, reason}`. Checks the weekday against `SchoolDay` (B4), then SCHOOL-audience `isNoSchool` events covering the date, **including recurring ones** (expand within that day). Reason = `Holiday: <title>` or `Not a teaching day`. A batched variant `noSchoolDays(from, to)` for the month view/landing avoids N queries (NFR-4). |\n| FR-17 | INT | Hook at the two marked lines (B3). Today views use `GET /api/school-day` or the server-side `isSchoolDay`. Keep the `ScheduleEntry[]` signature to avoid caller churn. |\n| FR-18 | INT, AUTH | `getToday` adds the no-school reason. Register save needs the override flag, enforced server-side (B5). Banner + `ConfirmDialog` in `RegisterForm`. |\n| FR-19 | INT, UI | Non-blocking alert in two forms (B6). Only uses FR-34. |\n| FR-20 | UI, SVC | Decision D2. Service `createTermBreaks(academicYearId, actor)`: for each consecutive term pair with a gap of at least one day, create a TERM_BREAK all-day SCHOOL event over the gap (start = day after term end, exclusive end = next term start). Idempotent: skip if an identical TERM_BREAK already exists. ADMIN only + audit. |\n| FR-21 | API, AUTH | `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp`. Rules: RSVP enabled, the user is in the audience, now < `rsvpDeadline`, guests > 0 only for PARENT (D4). Deadline violations return 409 `CONFLICT` or `VALIDATION_ERROR` (pick one and document it). Upsert on the composite PK. Recurring events take a single RSVP for the series (edits apply to the whole series; no per-occurrence data). |\n| FR-22 | API, UI | `GET /api/events/:id` includes `myRsvp` + totals `{yes,no,maybe,guests}`. `GET /api/events/:id/rsvps?format=csv` is creator/ADMIN only and reuses `src/server/csv.ts`. The JSON version uses `DataTable` in the drawer or dialog. |\n| FR-23 | JOB, NOTIF, DM | `event.rsvp_reminder`. The job selects events with `rsvpEnabled`, `rsvpDeadline` within the next 48h, and `rsvpReminderSentAt` null. It claims each event, then notifies audience members with no RSVP row (B8). |\n| FR-24 | UI | `/account/calendar` (requirePageUser). Copy via `navigator.clipboard`. Instructions are static text. Reset uses `ConfirmDialog`. |\n| FR-25 | API, DM, AUTH | `GET /api/me/calendar-feed`: if no token exists, create one and return the URL once. If one exists, **the raw token cannot be shown again** because it is stored hashed. Return `{exists:true, url:null}` and require a reset to see a URL, or create on first GET only. The design must reconcile the \"copy\" UX with hashing (D8). `POST …/reset` replaces the hash. |\n| FR-26 | SVC | Pure `buildIcs(items, tz)`: VCALENDAR + VTIMEZONE (generated from the IANA tz for the covered years; transitions from date-fns-tz offsets), VEVENT with DTSTART;TZID or VALUE=DATE for all-day, RRULE `FREQ=WEEKLY|MONTHLY;UNTIL=…Z`, escaping `\\\\ ; , \\n`, and 75-octet line folding. Window is now−30d → now+365d. The items come from the same merge as FR-32 (NFR-5 parity), skipping timetable. Deadlines are 0-duration VEVENTs with a URL. |\n| FR-27 | API, AUTH | `src/app/api/calendar/feed/[token]/route.ts`. The `.ics` suffix arrives inside the param, so strip it and hash with sha256 to look up the row. Rate limit (B9). Headers: `Content-Type: text/calendar; charset=utf-8`, `Cache-Control: private, max-age=900`. Disabled or archived user → 404. |\n| FR-28 | NOTIF, SVC | `event.created` when `startAt` is within 30 days (for recurring events, the first occurrence). Email-default-by-category (D5). Recipients come from `resolveAudienceUserIds`, excluding the creator. |\n| FR-29 | NOTIF, SVC | `event.updated` only when `startAt`, `endAt`, `allDay` or `location` changes **and** the event is upcoming. One notify call per PATCH. |\n| FR-30 | SVC, API | `getPublicEvents(from,to)` → `isPublic` events expanded, public-safe fields only (no audience, no creator). The route is unauthenticated and range-capped like FR-32. PRD-18 is the consumer. Consider applying `rateLimit` per IP. |\n| FR-31 | SVC | `getUpcomingEventsForUser(user, limit)` reuses the FR-32 merge with sources=events and a 90-day window, takes `limit`. No UI (NFR-11). |\n| FR-32 | API, SVC, AUTH | `getCalendarItems(user, {from,to,sources,studentId})` is the core merge. It returns a discriminated union `{kind:'event'|'assignment'|'quiz'|'timetable', …}` with instants in UTC plus `allDay`. Validation rejects `to − from > 100 days`. Performance: one events query + one audience-match pass in memory, and one query per deadline source over all children at once (NFR-4). |\n| FR-33 | API, AUTH | `POST /api/events`, `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/events/:id`, `GET /api/events/:id/ics`. Visibility = the user matches the audience **or** is the creator or ADMIN. Not visible → 404. |\n| FR-34 | API | `src/app/api/school-day/route.ts` (singular, a new folder next to `school-days`, which stays untouched). `date` is `YYYY-MM-DD` in the school tz. Any authenticated user. |\n| FR-35 | INT | Nav entry (B15, D6). |\n| FR-36 | AUTH, SVC | In update/delete: `if (user.role==='ADMIN' && event.createdById !== user.id) audit({action:'event.update'|'event.delete', entityType:'CalendarEvent', entityId, metadata})`. |\n| FR-37 | SEED | An idempotent `seedCalendar()` in `prisma/seed.ts`, matching events by title + startAt. Parent–teacher evening date = seed run date + 14 days, so it is not stable across runs; match it by title only. Robotics Club: D7. Sports day: no announcement link. |\n| NFR-1 | UI, TEST | Lint/QA grep for banned imports. Only MUI + MUI X (incl. the scheduler). |\n| NFR-2 | process | The dev phase must call MUI MCP before using any scheduler API, and system-design should list the doc pages to fetch (Quickstart, Views, Events, Timezones, Localization). |\n| NFR-3 | SVC, TEST | One concern across expansion (wall-clock stepping), all-day storage (tz midnight), the `VALUE=DATE` / TZID feed, and the scheduler `timezone` prop (check MCP Timezones page). Test a DST week (e.g. the US 2026-11-01 or 2027-03-14 transition, depending on the seed tz). |\n| NFR-4 | SVC | <500 ms for a parent with 3 children in month view. Batch the child/course/section lookups, use one events query with an audience `OR` filter, and avoid per-day `isSchoolDay` calls. Add an index on `EventAudience(type, targetId)` beyond the PRD spec (the PRD's model has the event FK; add `@@index([type, targetId])`). |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH, SVC | `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, stored as sha256 hex. The feed reuses `getCalendarItems`, so visibility can't drift. Integration test for parity. |\n| NFR-6 | TEST, DEP | `node-ical` devDependency. Parse `buildIcs` output in a unit test and the feed route output in an integration test. |\n| NFR-7 | AUTH | Every handler uses `requireUser`/`requireRole`, except the feed (token auth) and `/api/public/events` (public by design). Per-entity checks live in calendar-service, not in the routes. |\n| NFR-8 | all | `src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts` (+ `ical.ts`, `recurrence.ts` if split). Thin routes. `{data}` responses. `logger`. cuid ids. |\n| NFR-9 | INT | Reuse list: timetable-service (B3/B4), rate-limit (B9), notify (B7), audit, DataTable, useToast, ConfirmDialog, MarkdownView/Editor, csv.ts, the dispatch cron (B8), getSchoolTimezone (B13), and the access helpers (B11). |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | Unit: expansion, isSchoolDay, ICS escaping/RRULE/folding, all-day exclusive end, term-break gaps. Integration: merge per role, token reset (old URL 404), RSVP deadline. Playwright: 3 flows. |\n| NFR-11 | scope | No per-occurrence exceptions, no room booking, no two-way sync. PRD-16/18 get only FR-30/31 hooks. |\n| NFR-12 | UI | 768 px breakpoint (FR-9). English only. Evergreen browsers. |\n\n## 3. Decisions for arch-design-system (open items from intake)\n\n- **D1 – AudienceType / audience.ts / builder (FR-3, FR-7, FR-14).** PRD-12 is absent. Recommendation: SH-14 defines `enum AudienceType { SCHOOL GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }`. `EventAudience` gets `type`, `targetId String?` (null for SCHOOL) and `roles Role[] @default([])`, where empty means all roles. `roles` covers \"Grade 7 parents\". Resolver in `src/server/audience/audience.ts`, builder in `src/components/AudienceBuilder/`. Both are named generically so PRD-12 adopts them instead of re-creating them. Membership: SCHOOL = all active users; GRADE_LEVEL = students whose current-year SectionMember section has that grade (or `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`, pick one) plus their parents plus teachers of those sections or courses; SECTION = members + homeroom teacher + parents; COURSE = ACTIVE enrollments + teacher/co-teachers + parents.\n- **D2 – FR-20 host page.** No `/admin/academic-years/[id]` UI exists. The minimal option is a small server page at that exact path that lists the year's terms (read-only) with an \"Add term breaks\" button. Full academic-year CRUD UI is out of scope. Add no nav entry; link to it from the calendar editor or admin, or reach it by URL.\n- **D3 – Holidays vs School events chips.** Use intake's default: no duplication. HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool` events appear only under \"Holidays\".\n- **D4 – RSVP guests.** Parents only. The server forces 0 for other roles.\n- **D5 – Email default per category (FR-28).** The registry's `defaultEmail` is per type. Options: (a) two types, `event.created` (defaultEmail false) and `event.holiday_created` (defaultEmail true); or (b) one type that passes `email` only for HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK, which ignores the user preference toggle semantics. Recommend (a), because it stays inside the existing preference model with no changes to notify.ts.\n- **D6 – Nav.** Add `/calendar` (all roles). `/account/calendar` gets no sidebar entry, consistent with the existing account pages. It is reached from the account menu and a \"Subscribe\" link on `/calendar`.\n- **D7 – Robotics Club course (FR-37).** Not in the seed. Recommend seeding a minimal ELECTIVE course `ROBOTICS` (teacher Tom, current year) only if absent, so the Chess club example works. The alternative is skip-with-log.\n- **D8 – Feed URL display vs hashed storage (FR-24/25, NFR-5).** The raw token is only available at creation or reset. Recommendation: `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` returns `{url}` only when it creates the first token, and `{url:null, createdAt}` otherwise. The page then says \"Reset link to get a new URL\". This needs to be explicit in the API contracts.\n- **D9 – Schema deviations from the PRD's model list** (flag them in system-design): `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt`, `EventAudience.roles`, `@@index([type,targetId])`. Each traces to FR-23, FR-3/FR-37 and NFR-4.\n\n## 4. Risks\n\n- **R1 (high):** `@mui/x-scheduler` is beta. Its API (views, timezone, all-day exclusivity, custom event rendering for chips/colours) is unverified until MCP is consulted. Budget for fallbacks (FR-9).\n- **R2:** The import cycle between timetable-service and calendar-service (B4).\n- **R3:** DST correctness spans four places (FR-15 expansion, FR-4 storage, FR-26 VTIMEZONE, UI). One shared pure helper set in `src/lib/dates.ts` keeps them consistent.\n- **R4:** Audience resolution is the performance hot path (NFR-4) and the security boundary (NFR-5/7). It needs a single implementation, tested per role.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1687,"cache_read_input_tokens":67877,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1687,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b9140b8-a7ae-4ca4-9024-504a0df7df9f","uuid":"844487f8-4d23-49b1-ab6e-871f6c98dd0b","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:50:21.131Z","request_id":"req_011CgsrVSct2i28krbxxhGbL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015RVVJaA25wfcBXKnjAY1nm":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-14\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:10:00Z), PRD-14 School Calendar, Events & Holidays. It has 37 FRs and 12 NFRs (49 requirements) at 96% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It has 3 warnings: PRD-12 is missing, the academic-year page is missing, and new dependencies are needed. The decisions left open are in §3.\n\n> This file replaces a leftover SH-13 version. Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is also left over from SH-13. Its owning sub-task must overwrite it, and none of those files is an SH-14 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-14 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no calendar models and no `AudienceType` enum. There is no `Announcement` model and no `audience.ts`. The latest migration is `20261112000000_add_direct_messaging`. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-2/FR-3: add one new migration, e.g. `20261113000000_add_calendar`. `AudienceType` must be defined here (see D1). Add back-relations on `User` for events created, RSVPs and the feed token. |\n| B2 | Audience targets that already exist: `GradeLevel` (Grade 6/7/8 seeded), `Section` (`homeroomTeacherId`, `gradeLevelId`, per year), `SectionMember` (`@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])`), `Course` (`teacherId`, `coTeacherIds String[]`, `sectionId?`), `Enrollment` (ACTIVE/DROPPED, `@@index([studentId,status])`) and `ParentStudentLink`. `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId` exists. | schema L115-470 | FR-3: the minimal enum is `SCHOOL`, `GRADE_LEVEL`, `SECTION` and `COURSE`, plus a role filter so the seed's \"Grade 7 parents\" works (see D1). Every type resolves to student ids through existing tables. Parents are added through `ParentStudentLink`. |\n| B3 | `getScheduleForDate` and `getSchoolScheduleForDate` both contain a placeholder comment: `// PRD-14 holidays hook in here: return [] when date is a school holiday.` Both return `ScheduleEntry[]` and have no reason field. A private `schoolTimezone()` exists at L488. | timetable-service.ts L542-583 | FR-17: put the `isSchoolDay` check at those two hooks. **The return type cannot change without touching callers** (`attendance-service.ts` L130 and L472, `getCurrentSlot`). Recommendation: keep `ScheduleEntry[]` and add a sibling, e.g. `getDayInfo(date)` → `{isSchoolDay, reason}`, which callers use to show the holiday name. The alternative is a new return shape, which needs every caller updated. |\n| B4 | Both `isSchoolDay` and `getScheduleForDate` apply the teaching-weekday rule `day?.isTeaching ?? isoDay <= 5` from the `SchoolDay` table. | timetable-service.ts L552, L572 | FR-16: reuse `listSchoolDays()` (exported L112) instead of re-implementing the fallback. Watch for import cycles: calendar-service will import from timetable-service, and timetable-service calls back into `isSchoolDay`. Put the pure date→isoDay and holiday lookup in calendar-service with **no** import from timetable-service, or pass teaching days in. |\n| B5 | Attendance teacher landing is `getToday(user, date?)` and admin overview is `getOverview(date?)`. Both are fed by the schedule functions. `RegisterForm.tsx` is the register UI. | attendance-service.ts L122-150, L463-475 | FR-18: `getToday` returns `{noSchoolReason}` alongside its existing fields. Saving a register on a no-school date requires a confirm flag in the save body (e.g. `holidayOverride: true`) and the server checks it. That makes it a server-side rule, not only a dialog. |\n| B6 | The assignment editor is `courses/[courseId]/assignments/AssignmentForm.tsx`, using `DateTimePicker` on `dueAt` with school-tz `toWall/fromWall`. Quiz settings are in `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit/QuizSettingsPanel.tsx` (`availableUntil`). | grep | FR-19: both are client components. Fetch `GET /api/school-day?date=` on date change and render a non-blocking MUI `Alert`. Saving is unchanged. |\n| B7 | Notification registry `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const and its `COMMUNICATION`/`ACADEMIC` categories exist. `notify({type,userIds,title,body,link,email})` dedupes, never throws, and is called after commit. `notifyStudentAndParents` / `expandStudentRecipients` add linked parents. | notifications/types.ts; notify.ts L30, L89-120 | FR-23/28/29: add `event.created`, `event.updated` and `event.rsvp_reminder`. **`defaultEmail` is per type, but FR-28 wants it per category** (HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK email on by default). See D5. Resolve audience → userIds once, then call `notify`. |\n| B8 | The maintenance cron `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` runs each job in its own try/catch + logger (reminders, quiz, message emails). | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-23: add `sendRsvpReminders(now)` to its own isolated block. \"Once per event\" needs a claim column: `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?`, claimed with conditional `updateMany` (quiz `resultsReleasedAt` precedent). The PRD model list doesn't include that column. Adding it is a small, justified deviation (flag it). |\n| B9 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` → `{ok, retryAfterMs}`. It is per-process and marked with a `ponytail` note. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | FR-27: `rateLimit('ical:'+tokenHash, 60, 3_600_000)` → 429 `RATE_LIMITED`. Key on the **hash**, not the raw token, so raw tokens never sit in memory maps or logs. |\n| B10 | `http.ts` provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `AppError` with codes incl. `RATE_LIMITED`, `NOT_FOUND`, `FORBIDDEN` and `VALIDATION_ERROR`. `requireRole`, `requireUser`, `requirePageRole` and `requirePageUser` exist. `audit()` exists. | http.ts; requireRole.ts; audit.ts | NFR-7/8/FR-36. The feed route is the only unauthenticated handler. It returns `text/calendar` and the 404 is a plain response, not JSON. Its token parse failure and token-not-found case return the same 404. |\n| B11 | Access helpers: `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` ('ALL' for admin, own id for students, linked children for parents, enrolled + homeroom students for teachers), `assertCanViewStudent`, `assertCanManageCourse` (course-access.ts L56) and `resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId?)` (assignments-service L262). | auth/*.ts | FR-7: teacher create checks are `assertCanManageCourse` for COURSE audiences and `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` for SECTION. FR-11/FR-32 `studentId` param: use `resolveViewedStudent`/`assertCanViewStudent` (404 for other families). |\n| B12 | Deadline data sources already exist: `/api/me/assignments`, `/api/me/timetable` and `/api/me/children` routes, `Assignment @@index([courseId, dueAt])`, `Quiz @@index([courseId,status])` with `availableUntil`, and `getPersonalTimetable`. | api/me/*; schema | FR-10/FR-32: the calendar merge should call the existing service functions behind these routes (scoped to a date range), not new queries. A range filter on `dueAt`/`availableUntil` may need adding. Only PUBLISHED assignments/quizzes should be included, matching what the user can open. |\n| B13 | School timezone is read in two places: exported `getSchoolTimezone()` in assignments-service.ts L64 and private `schoolTimezone()` in timetable-service. `getSchoolSettings` (cached) is in services/settings.ts. `src/lib/dates.ts` has `schoolNow`, `formatInSchoolTz` and `ISO_DAY_NAMES`. date-fns-tz 3.2.0 is installed. | grep | NFR-3/FR-4: use `getSchoolTimezone()` and do not add a third copy. All-day ↔ `fromZonedTime(midnight, tz)` conversions belong as pure helpers in `src/lib/dates.ts` (unit-testable, client-safe). |\n| B14 | No `/admin/academic-years` page exists. Only APIs exist: `academic-years/[id]`, `…/set-current`, `…/terms`, `…/terms/generate`, and `terms.ts` service functions. Seed terms: S1 2026-08-17→2027-01-15, S2 2027-01-18→2027-06-11. | ls src/app/(app)/admin; seed.ts L91-94 | FR-20: a host page is needed (see D2). Note that the seed's gap between S1 and S2 is a weekend (Jan 16–17), so \"Add term breaks\" on seed data produces one short break. Winter break is **inside** S1 and is seeded explicitly. |\n| B15 | `navigation.ts` has `NavItem {label, href, icon, roles, group?, badge?, requires?}` and `ALL_ROLES`. The account area has `notifications` and `security` pages only, and no account nav entries. | config/navigation.ts | FR-35: add `{label:'Calendar', href:'/calendar', roles: ALL_ROLES}`. `/account/calendar` is linked from the account area like the other `/account/*` pages; no sidebar entry is needed (D6). |\n| B16 | Shared UI exists: `components/Toast/useToast`, `ConfirmDialog`, `MarkdownView`, `MarkdownEditor`, `DataTable`, `PageHeader`, `EmptyState` and `UserPicker`. `react-markdown` 10.1.0 is installed. `components/messaging` exists, but no audience builder. | ls src/components | NFR-1/NFR-9: the drawer uses `MarkdownView` and the editor uses `MarkdownEditor`. Delete confirmation uses `ConfirmDialog`. The RSVP list uses `DataTable`. CSV export reuses `src/server/csv.ts`. A new `components/AudienceBuilder` is the only new shared component (D1). |\n| B17 | `package.json` has MUI 9.5.0 for material, icons, x-charts, x-data-grid and x-date-pickers, plus `@mui/x-internals` 9.1.0 as an override. There is no `@mui/x-scheduler`, `ics` or `node-ical`. | package.json | FR-1: pin the scheduler with an exact version from MUI MCP, and check its peer range against `@mui/material` 9.5.0 and `@mui/x-internals`. NFR-6: `node-ical` as an exact-pinned devDependency. `ics` is not needed, because a hand-written RFC 5545 builder (about 100 lines, pure) is easier to test for escaping and folding (tech-stack sub-task decides). |\n| B18 | Seed: academic year 2026-2027 is current, Grade 6/7/8 exist, and sections 7A/7B exist. **There is no \"Robotics Club\" course anywhere**, and no Announcement exists. Seeds use the `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` + skip-with-log pattern. | seed.ts; grep | FR-37: the Chess club audience needs a Robotics Club course. Either seed it (an ELECTIVE `Course`, with `CourseKind` available) or skip with a log (D7). Sports day is seeded without an announcement link. |\n| B19 | `Notification` has only `link` for context (no entity column). | schema L313-326 | FR-28/29 links: `/calendar?event=<id>` so the page can open the drawer from a query param. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern key: **DM** data model/migration, **SVC** server service, **API** route handler, **UI** page/component, **JOB** cron/maintenance, **AUTH** access boundary, **INT** change to existing module, **NOTIF** notification type, **DEP** dependency, **TEST**, **SEED**.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes for arch-design-system |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DEP | `@mui/x-scheduler` exact pin taken from the MUI MCP `useMuiDocs` + `fetchDocs`. This comes first in the dev plan. If MCP is unreachable, stop (NFR-2). Check peer deps against 9.5.0 (B17). |\n| FR-2 | DM | Enums `EventCategory`, `Recurrence` (NONE/WEEKLY/MONTHLY), `RsvpResponse` (YES/NO/MAYBE). Models `CalendarEvent`, `EventAudience` (cascade from event), `EventRsvp` (`@@id([eventId,userId])`, cascade) and `CalendarFeedToken` (`userId @unique`, `tokenHash @unique`). Add `@@index([startAt, endAt])` on events. Recurrence widens the read window, so range queries must be `startAt < to AND (endAt > from OR recurrence != NONE AND recurrenceUntil >= from)`. Index use is partial, which is fine at school scale. Possible extra columns: `rsvpReminderSentAt` (B8). |\n| FR-3 | DM, AUTH | Decision D1. The audience resolver (`resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` and `userMatchesAudience(user, audiences)`) is the hub of FR-7/10/21/23/26/28/29/31/32. Build it once, in a form PRD-12 can adopt (e.g. `src/server/audience/audience.ts`). |\n| FR-4 | SVC | Zod in `src/lib/validators/calendar.ts` (client-safe, shared with the editor dialog). Cross-field rules use `.superRefine`: endAt ≥ startAt; recurrenceUntil required when recurrence ≠ NONE and ≤ startAt + 1 year; guests 0–5. All-day normalisation (school-tz midnight, **exclusive** end) is a server-side transform, because the client sends dates and not instants. Unit-test the exclusive end (NFR-10). |\n| FR-5 | SVC | Default applied in the service when `isNoSchool` is undefined: `category in (HOLIDAY, TERM_BREAK)`. Not a DB default (it depends on another column). |\n| FR-6 | AUTH | Service-level check: a non-admin sending `isNoSchool`, `isPublic` or a HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK category gets 403. The editor UI hides these fields, but the server is authoritative. |\n| FR-7 | AUTH | A teacher's audiences must all be COURSE audiences they manage (`assertCanManageCourse`) or SECTION audiences they homeroom. SCHOOL or GRADE_LEVEL gives 403 (AC-7). This also applies on PATCH when audiences change. |\n| FR-8 | AUTH | Edit/delete when `createdById === user.id` or the user is ADMIN. Others get 403 if they can see the event, 404 otherwise. |\n| FR-9 | UI, DEP | Client page `/calendar` (server `page.tsx` does `requirePageUser`, then a client `CalendarView`). The view switches at the 768 px breakpoint via `useMediaQuery`. Agenda \"infinite scroll\" means fetching the next 30-day window on scroll. The range cap is 100 days (FR-32). Fallback components only where the Community scheduler lacks a feature. Record each fallback in system-design with its MCP doc reference. |\n| FR-10 | UI | Chips with localStorage key e.g. `calendar.sources`. Sources map 1:1 to the `sources=` query param. Timetable blocks only in Week view: don't fetch `timetable` unless the Week view is active. Holidays vs School events default: HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool` belong to \"Holidays\" only, with no duplicates (intake's default, D3). |\n| FR-11 | UI, AUTH | Parent child filter → `studentId=` (omitted = all children). Server validates via `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Deadline items carry `childName`. Event audience matching for parents uses the union of their children (and the parent's own role for role-filtered audiences). |\n| FR-12 | UI | Right `Drawer`. Data comes from the expanded item plus `GET /api/events/:id` for full detail and RSVP. \"Add to my calendar\" = `<a href=\"/api/events/:id/ics\" download>`. Edit/delete visible when `canEdit` is set; the server computes `canEdit` and returns it. |\n| FR-13 | UI | Deadline items carry an `href` set by the server (`/assignments/<id>` or the quiz route). Clicking navigates; no drawer. |\n| FR-14 | UI | `EventEditorDialog` with React Hook Form + the shared Zod schema. Uses `AudienceBuilder` (D1), the recurrence select + until date, the RSVP switch + deadline, and `MarkdownEditor`. Admin-only fields are rendered only for ADMIN (FR-6). |\n| FR-15 | SVC | Pure `expandOccurrences(event, from, to)` in calendar-service (or `src/lib/calendar/recurrence.ts`). WEEKLY = +7 days **in wall-clock school time** (DST, NFR-3), not +7×24h. MONTHLY-by-date: skip months without that day (e.g. 31st). Document this, because RRULE `BYMONTHDAY=31` also skips, so UI and feed agree. Each occurrence id = `${eventId}:${occurrenceStartISO}`. Heavily unit-tested. |\n| FR-16 | SVC | `isSchoolDay(date)` → `{isSchoolDay, reason}`. Checks the weekday against `SchoolDay` (B4), then SCHOOL-audience `isNoSchool` events covering the date, **including recurring ones** (expand within that day). Reason = `Holiday: <title>` or `Not a teaching day`. A batched variant `noSchoolDays(from, to)` for the month view/landing avoids N queries (NFR-4). |\n| FR-17 | INT | Hook at the two marked lines (B3). Today views use `GET /api/school-day` or the server-side `isSchoolDay`. Keep the `ScheduleEntry[]` signature to avoid caller churn. |\n| FR-18 | INT, AUTH | `getToday` adds the no-school reason. Register save needs the override flag, enforced server-side (B5). Banner + `ConfirmDialog` in `RegisterForm`. |\n| FR-19 | INT, UI | Non-blocking alert in two forms (B6). Only uses FR-34. |\n| FR-20 | UI, SVC | Decision D2. Service `createTermBreaks(academicYearId, actor)`: for each consecutive term pair with a gap of at least one day, create a TERM_BREAK all-day SCHOOL event over the gap (start = day after term end, exclusive end = next term start). Idempotent: skip if an identical TERM_BREAK already exists. ADMIN only + audit. |\n| FR-21 | API, AUTH | `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp`. Rules: RSVP enabled, the user is in the audience, now < `rsvpDeadline`, guests > 0 only for PARENT (D4). Deadline violations return 409 `CONFLICT` or `VALIDATION_ERROR` (pick one and document it). Upsert on the composite PK. Recurring events take a single RSVP for the series (edits apply to the whole series; no per-occurrence data). |\n| FR-22 | API, UI | `GET /api/events/:id` includes `myRsvp` + totals `{yes,no,maybe,guests}`. `GET /api/events/:id/rsvps?format=csv` is creator/ADMIN only and reuses `src/server/csv.ts`. The JSON version uses `DataTable` in the drawer or dialog. |\n| FR-23 | JOB, NOTIF, DM | `event.rsvp_reminder`. The job selects events with `rsvpEnabled`, `rsvpDeadline` within the next 48h, and `rsvpReminderSentAt` null. It claims each event, then notifies audience members with no RSVP row (B8). |\n| FR-24 | UI | `/account/calendar` (requirePageUser). Copy via `navigator.clipboard`. Instructions are static text. Reset uses `ConfirmDialog`. |\n| FR-25 | API, DM, AUTH | `GET /api/me/calendar-feed`: if no token exists, create one and return the URL once. If one exists, **the raw token cannot be shown again** because it is stored hashed. Return `{exists:true, url:null}` and require a reset to see a URL, or create on first GET only. The design must reconcile the \"copy\" UX with hashing (D8). `POST …/reset` replaces the hash. |\n| FR-26 | SVC | Pure `buildIcs(items, tz)`: VCALENDAR + VTIMEZONE (generated from the IANA tz for the covered years; transitions from date-fns-tz offsets), VEVENT with DTSTART;TZID or VALUE=DATE for all-day, RRULE `FREQ=WEEKLY|MONTHLY;UNTIL=…Z`, escaping `\\\\ ; , \\n`, and 75-octet line folding. Window is now−30d → now+365d. The items come from the same merge as FR-32 (NFR-5 parity), skipping timetable. Deadlines are 0-duration VEVENTs with a URL. |\n| FR-27 | API, AUTH | `src/app/api/calendar/feed/[token]/route.ts`. The `.ics` suffix arrives inside the param, so strip it and hash with sha256 to look up the row. Rate limit (B9). Headers: `Content-Type: text/calendar; charset=utf-8`, `Cache-Control: private, max-age=900`. Disabled or archived user → 404. |\n| FR-28 | NOTIF, SVC | `event.created` when `startAt` is within 30 days (for recurring events, the first occurrence). Email-default-by-category (D5). Recipients come from `resolveAudienceUserIds`, excluding the creator. |\n| FR-29 | NOTIF, SVC | `event.updated` only when `startAt`, `endAt`, `allDay` or `location` changes **and** the event is upcoming. One notify call per PATCH. |\n| FR-30 | SVC, API | `getPublicEvents(from,to)` → `isPublic` events expanded, public-safe fields only (no audience, no creator). The route is unauthenticated and range-capped like FR-32. PRD-18 is the consumer. Consider applying `rateLimit` per IP. |\n| FR-31 | SVC | `getUpcomingEventsForUser(user, limit)` reuses the FR-32 merge with sources=events and a 90-day window, takes `limit`. No UI (NFR-11). |\n| FR-32 | API, SVC, AUTH | `getCalendarItems(user, {from,to,sources,studentId})` is the core merge. It returns a discriminated union `{kind:'event'|'assignment'|'quiz'|'timetable', …}` with instants in UTC plus `allDay`. Validation rejects `to − from > 100 days`. Performance: one events query + one audience-match pass in memory, and one query per deadline source over all children at once (NFR-4). |\n| FR-33 | API, AUTH | `POST /api/events`, `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/events/:id`, `GET /api/events/:id/ics`. Visibility = the user matches the audience **or** is the creator or ADMIN. Not visible → 404. |\n| FR-34 | API | `src/app/api/school-day/route.ts` (singular, a new folder next to `school-days`, which stays untouched). `date` is `YYYY-MM-DD` in the school tz. Any authenticated user. |\n| FR-35 | INT | Nav entry (B15, D6). |\n| FR-36 | AUTH, SVC | In update/delete: `if (user.role==='ADMIN' && event.createdById !== user.id) audit({action:'event.update'|'event.delete', entityType:'CalendarEvent', entityId, metadata})`. |\n| FR-37 | SEED | An idempotent `seedCalendar()` in `prisma/seed.ts`, matching events by title + startAt. Parent–teacher evening date = seed run date + 14 days, so it is not stable across runs; match it by title only. Robotics Club: D7. Sports day: no announcement link. |\n| NFR-1 | UI, TEST | Lint/QA grep for banned imports. Only MUI + MUI X (incl. the scheduler). |\n| NFR-2 | process | The dev phase must call MUI MCP before using any scheduler API, and system-design should list the doc pages to fetch (Quickstart, Views, Events, Timezones, Localization). |\n| NFR-3 | SVC, TEST | One concern across expansion (wall-clock stepping), all-day storage (tz midnight), the `VALUE=DATE` / TZID feed, and the scheduler `timezone` prop (check MCP Timezones page). Test a DST week (e.g. the US 2026-11-01 or 2027-03-14 transition, depending on the seed tz). |\n| NFR-4 | SVC | <500 ms for a parent with 3 children in month view. Batch the child/course/section lookups, use one events query with an audience `OR` filter, and avoid per-day `isSchoolDay` calls. Add an index on `EventAudience(type, targetId)` beyond the PRD spec (the PRD's model has the event FK; add `@@index([type, targetId])`). |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH, SVC | `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, stored as sha256 hex. The feed reuses `getCalendarItems`, so visibility can't drift. Integration test for parity. |\n| NFR-6 | TEST, DEP | `node-ical` devDependency. Parse `buildIcs` output in a unit test and the feed route output in an integration test. |\n| NFR-7 | AUTH | Every handler uses `requireUser`/`requireRole`, except the feed (token auth) and `/api/public/events` (public by design). Per-entity checks live in calendar-service, not in the routes. |\n| NFR-8 | all | `src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts` (+ `ical.ts`, `recurrence.ts` if split). Thin routes. `{data}` responses. `logger`. cuid ids. |\n| NFR-9 | INT | Reuse list: timetable-service (B3/B4), rate-limit (B9), notify (B7), audit, DataTable, useToast, ConfirmDialog, MarkdownView/Editor, csv.ts, the dispatch cron (B8), getSchoolTimezone (B13), and the access helpers (B11). |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | Unit: expansion, isSchoolDay, ICS escaping/RRULE/folding, all-day exclusive end, term-break gaps. Integration: merge per role, token reset (old URL 404), RSVP deadline. Playwright: 3 flows. |\n| NFR-11 | scope | No per-occurrence exceptions, no room booking, no two-way sync. PRD-16/18 get only FR-30/31 hooks. |\n| NFR-12 | UI | 768 px breakpoint (FR-9). English only. Evergreen browsers. |\n\n## 3. Decisions for arch-design-system (open items from intake)\n\n- **D1 – AudienceType / audience.ts / builder (FR-3, FR-7, FR-14).** PRD-12 is absent. Recommendation: SH-14 defines `enum AudienceType { SCHOOL GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }`. `EventAudience` gets `type`, `targetId String?` (null for SCHOOL) and `roles Role[] @default([])`, where empty means all roles. `roles` covers \"Grade 7 parents\". Resolver in `src/server/audience/audience.ts`, builder in `src/components/AudienceBuilder/`. Both are named generically so PRD-12 adopts them instead of re-creating them. Membership: SCHOOL = all active users; GRADE_LEVEL = students whose current-year SectionMember section has that grade (or `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`, pick one) plus their parents plus teachers of those sections or courses; SECTION = members + homeroom teacher + parents; COURSE = ACTIVE enrollments + teacher/co-teachers + parents.\n- **D2 – FR-20 host page.** No `/admin/academic-years/[id]` UI exists. The minimal option is a small server page at that exact path that lists the year's terms (read-only) with an \"Add term breaks\" button. Full academic-year CRUD UI is out of scope. Add no nav entry; link to it from the calendar editor or admin, or reach it by URL.\n- **D3 – Holidays vs School events chips.** Use intake's default: no duplication. HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool` events appear only under \"Holidays\".\n- **D4 – RSVP guests.** Parents only. The server forces 0 for other roles.\n- **D5 – Email default per category (FR-28).** The registry's `defaultEmail` is per type. Options: (a) two types, `event.created` (defaultEmail false) and `event.holiday_created` (defaultEmail true); or (b) one type that passes `email` only for HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK, which ignores the user preference toggle semantics. Recommend (a), because it stays inside the existing preference model with no changes to notify.ts.\n- **D6 – Nav.** Add `/calendar` (all roles). `/account/calendar` gets no sidebar entry, consistent with the existing account pages. It is reached from the account menu and a \"Subscribe\" link on `/calendar`.\n- **D7 – Robotics Club course (FR-37).** Not in the seed. Recommend seeding a minimal ELECTIVE course `ROBOTICS` (teacher Tom, current year) only if absent, so the Chess club example works. The alternative is skip-with-log.\n- **D8 – Feed URL display vs hashed storage (FR-24/25, NFR-5).** The raw token is only available at creation or reset. Recommendation: `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` returns `{url}` only when it creates the first token, and `{url:null, createdAt}` otherwise. The page then says \"Reset link to get a new URL\". This needs to be explicit in the API contracts.\n- **D9 – Schema deviations from the PRD's model list** (flag them in system-design): `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt`, `EventAudience.roles`, `@@index([type,targetId])`. Each traces to FR-23, FR-3/FR-37 and NFR-4.\n\n## 4. Risks\n\n- **R1 (high):** `@mui/x-scheduler` is beta. Its API (views, timezone, all-day exclusivity, custom event rendering for chips/colours) is unverified until MCP is consulted. Budget for fallbacks (FR-9).\n- **R2:** The import cycle between timetable-service and calendar-service (B4).\n- **R3:** DST correctness spans four places (FR-15 expansion, FR-4 storage, FR-26 VTIMEZONE, UI). One shared pure helper set in `src/lib/dates.ts` keeps them consistent.\n- **R4:** Audience resolution is the performance hot path (NFR-4) and the security boundary (NFR-5/7). It needs a single implementation, tested per role.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015RVVJaA25wfcBXKnjAY1nm","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b9140b8-a7ae-4ca4-9024-504a0df7df9f","uuid":"868c4004-88b8-44c2-a7d8-69df0f5bcd3e","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:50:21.228Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-14\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:10:00Z), PRD-14 School Calendar, Events & Holidays. It has 37 FRs and 12 NFRs (49 requirements) at 96% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It has 3 warnings: PRD-12 is missing, the academic-year page is missing, and new dependencies are needed. The decisions left open are in §3.\n\n> This file replaces a leftover SH-13 version. Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is also left over from SH-13. Its owning sub-task must overwrite it, and none of those files is an SH-14 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-14 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no calendar models and no `AudienceType` enum. There is no `Announcement` model and no `audience.ts`. The latest migration is `20261112000000_add_direct_messaging`. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-2/FR-3: add one new migration, e.g. `20261113000000_add_calendar`. `AudienceType` must be defined here (see D1). Add back-relations on `User` for events created, RSVPs and the feed token. |\n| B2 | Audience targets that already exist: `GradeLevel` (Grade 6/7/8 seeded), `Section` (`homeroomTeacherId`, `gradeLevelId`, per year), `SectionMember` (`@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])`), `Course` (`teacherId`, `coTeacherIds String[]`, `sectionId?`), `Enrollment` (ACTIVE/DROPPED, `@@index([studentId,status])`) and `ParentStudentLink`. `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId` exists. | schema L115-470 | FR-3: the minimal enum is `SCHOOL`, `GRADE_LEVEL`, `SECTION` and `COURSE`, plus a role filter so the seed's \"Grade 7 parents\" works (see D1). Every type resolves to student ids through existing tables. Parents are added through `ParentStudentLink`. |\n| B3 | `getScheduleForDate` and `getSchoolScheduleForDate` both contain a placeholder comment: `// PRD-14 holidays hook in here: return [] when date is a school holiday.` Both return `ScheduleEntry[]` and have no reason field. A private `schoolTimezone()` exists at L488. | timetable-service.ts L542-583 | FR-17: put the `isSchoolDay` check at those two hooks. **The return type cannot change without touching callers** (`attendance-service.ts` L130 and L472, `getCurrentSlot`). Recommendation: keep `ScheduleEntry[]` and add a sibling, e.g. `getDayInfo(date)` → `{isSchoolDay, reason}`, which callers use to show the holiday name. The alternative is a new return shape, which needs every caller updated. |\n| B4 | Both `isSchoolDay` and `getScheduleForDate` apply the teaching-weekday rule `day?.isTeaching ?? isoDay <= 5` from the `SchoolDay` table. | timetable-service.ts L552, L572 | FR-16: reuse `listSchoolDays()` (exported L112) instead of re-implementing the fallback. Watch for import cycles: calendar-service will import from timetable-service, and timetable-service calls back into `isSchoolDay`. Put the pure date→isoDay and holiday lookup in calendar-service with **no** import from timetable-service, or pass teaching days in. |\n| B5 | Attendance teacher landing is `getToday(user, date?)` and admin overview is `getOverview(date?)`. Both are fed by the schedule functions. `RegisterForm.tsx` is the register UI. | attendance-service.ts L122-150, L463-475 | FR-18: `getToday` returns `{noSchoolReason}` alongside its existing fields. Saving a register on a no-school date requires a confirm flag in the save body (e.g. `holidayOverride: true`) and the server checks it. That makes it a server-side rule, not only a dialog. |\n| B6 | The assignment editor is `courses/[courseId]/assignments/AssignmentForm.tsx`, using `DateTimePicker` on `dueAt` with school-tz `toWall/fromWall`. Quiz settings are in `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit/QuizSettingsPanel.tsx` (`availableUntil`). | grep | FR-19: both are client components. Fetch `GET /api/school-day?date=` on date change and render a non-blocking MUI `Alert`. Saving is unchanged. |\n| B7 | Notification registry `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const and its `COMMUNICATION`/`ACADEMIC` categories exist. `notify({type,userIds,title,body,link,email})` dedupes, never throws, and is called after commit. `notifyStudentAndParents` / `expandStudentRecipients` add linked parents. | notifications/types.ts; notify.ts L30, L89-120 | FR-23/28/29: add `event.created`, `event.updated` and `event.rsvp_reminder`. **`defaultEmail` is per type, but FR-28 wants it per category** (HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK email on by default). See D5. Resolve audience → userIds once, then call `notify`. |\n| B8 | The maintenance cron `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` runs each job in its own try/catch + logger (reminders, quiz, message emails). | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-23: add `sendRsvpReminders(now)` to its own isolated block. \"Once per event\" needs a claim column: `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?`, claimed with conditional `updateMany` (quiz `resultsReleasedAt` precedent). The PRD model list doesn't include that column. Adding it is a small, justified deviation (flag it). |\n| B9 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` → `{ok, retryAfterMs}`. It is per-process and marked with a `ponytail` note. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | FR-27: `rateLimit('ical:'+tokenHash, 60, 3_600_000)` → 429 `RATE_LIMITED`. Key on the **hash**, not the raw token, so raw tokens never sit in memory maps or logs. |\n| B10 | `http.ts` provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `AppError` with codes incl. `RATE_LIMITED`, `NOT_FOUND`, `FORBIDDEN` and `VALIDATION_ERROR`. `requireRole`, `requireUser`, `requirePageRole` and `requirePageUser` exist. `audit()` exists. | http.ts; requireRole.ts; audit.ts | NFR-7/8/FR-36. The feed route is the only unauthenticated handler. It returns `text/calendar` and the 404 is a plain response, not JSON. Its token parse failure and token-not-found case return the same 404. |\n| B11 | Access helpers: `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` ('ALL' for admin, own id for students, linked children for parents, enrolled + homeroom students for teachers), `assertCanViewStudent`, `assertCanManageCourse` (course-access.ts L56) and `resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId?)` (assignments-service L262). | auth/*.ts | FR-7: teacher create checks are `assertCanManageCourse` for COURSE audiences and `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` for SECTION. FR-11/FR-32 `studentId` param: use `resolveViewedStudent`/`assertCanViewStudent` (404 for other families). |\n| B12 | Deadline data sources already exist: `/api/me/assignments`, `/api/me/timetable` and `/api/me/children` routes, `Assignment @@index([courseId, dueAt])`, `Quiz @@index([courseId,status])` with `availableUntil`, and `getPersonalTimetable`. | api/me/*; schema | FR-10/FR-32: the calendar merge should call the existing service functions behind these routes (scoped to a date range), not new queries. A range filter on `dueAt`/`availableUntil` may need adding. Only PUBLISHED assignments/quizzes should be included, matching what the user can open. |\n| B13 | School timezone is read in two places: exported `getSchoolTimezone()` in assignments-service.ts L64 and private `schoolTimezone()` in timetable-service. `getSchoolSettings` (cached) is in services/settings.ts. `src/lib/dates.ts` has `schoolNow`, `formatInSchoolTz` and `ISO_DAY_NAMES`. date-fns-tz 3.2.0 is installed. | grep | NFR-3/FR-4: use `getSchoolTimezone()` and do not add a third copy. All-day ↔ `fromZonedTime(midnight, tz)` conversions belong as pure helpers in `src/lib/dates.ts` (unit-testable, client-safe). |\n| B14 | No `/admin/academic-years` page exists. Only APIs exist: `academic-years/[id]`, `…/set-current`, `…/terms`, `…/terms/generate`, and `terms.ts` service functions. Seed terms: S1 2026-08-17→2027-01-15, S2 2027-01-18→2027-06-11. | ls src/app/(app)/admin; seed.ts L91-94 | FR-20: a host page is needed (see D2). Note that the seed's gap between S1 and S2 is a weekend (Jan 16–17), so \"Add term breaks\" on seed data produces one short break. Winter break is **inside** S1 and is seeded explicitly. |\n| B15 | `navigation.ts` has `NavItem {label, href, icon, roles, group?, badge?, requires?}` and `ALL_ROLES`. The account area has `notifications` and `security` pages only, and no account nav entries. | config/navigation.ts | FR-35: add `{label:'Calendar', href:'/calendar', roles: ALL_ROLES}`. `/account/calendar` is linked from the account area like the other `/account/*` pages; no sidebar entry is needed (D6). |\n| B16 | Shared UI exists: `components/Toast/useToast`, `ConfirmDialog`, `MarkdownView`, `MarkdownEditor`, `DataTable`, `PageHeader`, `EmptyState` and `UserPicker`. `react-markdown` 10.1.0 is installed. `components/messaging` exists, but no audience builder. | ls src/components | NFR-1/NFR-9: the drawer uses `MarkdownView` and the editor uses `MarkdownEditor`. Delete confirmation uses `ConfirmDialog`. The RSVP list uses `DataTable`. CSV export reuses `src/server/csv.ts`. A new `components/AudienceBuilder` is the only new shared component (D1). |\n| B17 | `package.json` has MUI 9.5.0 for material, icons, x-charts, x-data-grid and x-date-pickers, plus `@mui/x-internals` 9.1.0 as an override. There is no `@mui/x-scheduler`, `ics` or `node-ical`. | package.json | FR-1: pin the scheduler with an exact version from MUI MCP, and check its peer range against `@mui/material` 9.5.0 and `@mui/x-internals`. NFR-6: `node-ical` as an exact-pinned devDependency. `ics` is not needed, because a hand-written RFC 5545 builder (about 100 lines, pure) is easier to test for escaping and folding (tech-stack sub-task decides). |\n| B18 | Seed: academic year 2026-2027 is current, Grade 6/7/8 exist, and sections 7A/7B exist. **There is no \"Robotics Club\" course anywhere**, and no Announcement exists. Seeds use the `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` + skip-with-log pattern. | seed.ts; grep | FR-37: the Chess club audience needs a Robotics Club course. Either seed it (an ELECTIVE `Course`, with `CourseKind` available) or skip with a log (D7). Sports day is seeded without an announcement link. |\n| B19 | `Notification` has only `link` for context (no entity column). | schema L313-326 | FR-28/29 links: `/calendar?event=<id>` so the page can open the drawer from a query param. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern key: **DM** data model/migration, **SVC** server service, **API** route handler, **UI** page/component, **JOB** cron/maintenance, **AUTH** access boundary, **INT** change to existing module, **NOTIF** notification type, **DEP** dependency, **TEST**, **SEED**.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes for arch-design-system |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DEP | `@mui/x-scheduler` exact pin taken from the MUI MCP `useMuiDocs` + `fetchDocs`. This comes first in the dev plan. If MCP is unreachable, stop (NFR-2). Check peer deps against 9.5.0 (B17). |\n| FR-2 | DM | Enums `EventCategory`, `Recurrence` (NONE/WEEKLY/MONTHLY), `RsvpResponse` (YES/NO/MAYBE). Models `CalendarEvent`, `EventAudience` (cascade from event), `EventRsvp` (`@@id([eventId,userId])`, cascade) and `CalendarFeedToken` (`userId @unique`, `tokenHash @unique`). Add `@@index([startAt, endAt])` on events. Recurrence widens the read window, so range queries must be `startAt < to AND (endAt > from OR recurrence != NONE AND recurrenceUntil >= from)`. Index use is partial, which is fine at school scale. Possible extra columns: `rsvpReminderSentAt` (B8). |\n| FR-3 | DM, AUTH | Decision D1. The audience resolver (`resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` and `userMatchesAudience(user, audiences)`) is the hub of FR-7/10/21/23/26/28/29/31/32. Build it once, in a form PRD-12 can adopt (e.g. `src/server/audience/audience.ts`). |\n| FR-4 | SVC | Zod in `src/lib/validators/calendar.ts` (client-safe, shared with the editor dialog). Cross-field rules use `.superRefine`: endAt ≥ startAt; recurrenceUntil required when recurrence ≠ NONE and ≤ startAt + 1 year; guests 0–5. All-day normalisation (school-tz midnight, **exclusive** end) is a server-side transform, because the client sends dates and not instants. Unit-test the exclusive end (NFR-10). |\n| FR-5 | SVC | Default applied in the service when `isNoSchool` is undefined: `category in (HOLIDAY, TERM_BREAK)`. Not a DB default (it depends on another column). |\n| FR-6 | AUTH | Service-level check: a non-admin sending `isNoSchool`, `isPublic` or a HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK category gets 403. The editor UI hides these fields, but the server is authoritative. |\n| FR-7 | AUTH | A teacher's audiences must all be COURSE audiences they manage (`assertCanManageCourse`) or SECTION audiences they homeroom. SCHOOL or GRADE_LEVEL gives 403 (AC-7). This also applies on PATCH when audiences change. |\n| FR-8 | AUTH | Edit/delete when `createdById === user.id` or the user is ADMIN. Others get 403 if they can see the event, 404 otherwise. |\n| FR-9 | UI, DEP | Client page `/calendar` (server `page.tsx` does `requirePageUser`, then a client `CalendarView`). The view switches at the 768 px breakpoint via `useMediaQuery`. Agenda \"infinite scroll\" means fetching the next 30-day window on scroll. The range cap is 100 days (FR-32). Fallback components only where the Community scheduler lacks a feature. Record each fallback in system-design with its MCP doc reference. |\n| FR-10 | UI | Chips with localStorage key e.g. `calendar.sources`. Sources map 1:1 to the `sources=` query param. Timetable blocks only in Week view: don't fetch `timetable` unless the Week view is active. Holidays vs School events default: HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool` belong to \"Holidays\" only, with no duplicates (intake's default, D3). |\n| FR-11 | UI, AUTH | Parent child filter → `studentId=` (omitted = all children). Server validates via `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Deadline items carry `childName`. Event audience matching for parents uses the union of their children (and the parent's own role for role-filtered audiences). |\n| FR-12 | UI | Right `Drawer`. Data comes from the expanded item plus `GET /api/events/:id` for full detail and RSVP. \"Add to my calendar\" = `<a href=\"/api/events/:id/ics\" download>`. Edit/delete visible when `canEdit` is set; the server computes `canEdit` and returns it. |\n| FR-13 | UI | Deadline items carry an `href` set by the server (`/assignments/<id>` or the quiz route). Clicking navigates; no drawer. |\n| FR-14 | UI | `EventEditorDialog` with React Hook Form + the shared Zod schema. Uses `AudienceBuilder` (D1), the recurrence select + until date, the RSVP switch + deadline, and `MarkdownEditor`. Admin-only fields are rendered only for ADMIN (FR-6). |\n| FR-15 | SVC | Pure `expandOccurrences(event, from, to)` in calendar-service (or `src/lib/calendar/recurrence.ts`). WEEKLY = +7 days **in wall-clock school time** (DST, NFR-3), not +7×24h. MONTHLY-by-date: skip months without that day (e.g. 31st). Document this, because RRULE `BYMONTHDAY=31` also skips, so UI and feed agree. Each occurrence id = `${eventId}:${occurrenceStartISO}`. Heavily unit-tested. |\n| FR-16 | SVC | `isSchoolDay(date)` → `{isSchoolDay, reason}`. Checks the weekday against `SchoolDay` (B4), then SCHOOL-audience `isNoSchool` events covering the date, **including recurring ones** (expand within that day). Reason = `Holiday: <title>` or `Not a teaching day`. A batched variant `noSchoolDays(from, to)` for the month view/landing avoids N queries (NFR-4). |\n| FR-17 | INT | Hook at the two marked lines (B3). Today views use `GET /api/school-day` or the server-side `isSchoolDay`. Keep the `ScheduleEntry[]` signature to avoid caller churn. |\n| FR-18 | INT, AUTH | `getToday` adds the no-school reason. Register save needs the override flag, enforced server-side (B5). Banner + `ConfirmDialog` in `RegisterForm`. |\n| FR-19 | INT, UI | Non-blocking alert in two forms (B6). Only uses FR-34. |\n| FR-20 | UI, SVC | Decision D2. Service `createTermBreaks(academicYearId, actor)`: for each consecutive term pair with a gap of at least one day, create a TERM_BREAK all-day SCHOOL event over the gap (start = day after term end, exclusive end = next term start). Idempotent: skip if an identical TERM_BREAK already exists. ADMIN only + audit. |\n| FR-21 | API, AUTH | `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp`. Rules: RSVP enabled, the user is in the audience, now < `rsvpDeadline`, guests > 0 only for PARENT (D4). Deadline violations return 409 `CONFLICT` or `VALIDATION_ERROR` (pick one and document it). Upsert on the composite PK. Recurring events take a single RSVP for the series (edits apply to the whole series; no per-occurrence data). |\n| FR-22 | API, UI | `GET /api/events/:id` includes `myRsvp` + totals `{yes,no,maybe,guests}`. `GET /api/events/:id/rsvps?format=csv` is creator/ADMIN only and reuses `src/server/csv.ts`. The JSON version uses `DataTable` in the drawer or dialog. |\n| FR-23 | JOB, NOTIF, DM | `event.rsvp_reminder`. The job selects events with `rsvpEnabled`, `rsvpDeadline` within the next 48h, and `rsvpReminderSentAt` null. It claims each event, then notifies audience members with no RSVP row (B8). |\n| FR-24 | UI | `/account/calendar` (requirePageUser). Copy via `navigator.clipboard`. Instructions are static text. Reset uses `ConfirmDialog`. |\n| FR-25 | API, DM, AUTH | `GET /api/me/calendar-feed`: if no token exists, create one and return the URL once. If one exists, **the raw token cannot be shown again** because it is stored hashed. Return `{exists:true, url:null}` and require a reset to see a URL, or create on first GET only. The design must reconcile the \"copy\" UX with hashing (D8). `POST …/reset` replaces the hash. |\n| FR-26 | SVC | Pure `buildIcs(items, tz)`: VCALENDAR + VTIMEZONE (generated from the IANA tz for the covered years; transitions from date-fns-tz offsets), VEVENT with DTSTART;TZID or VALUE=DATE for all-day, RRULE `FREQ=WEEKLY|MONTHLY;UNTIL=…Z`, escaping `\\\\ ; , \\n`, and 75-octet line folding. Window is now−30d → now+365d. The items come from the same merge as FR-32 (NFR-5 parity), skipping timetable. Deadlines are 0-duration VEVENTs with a URL. |\n| FR-27 | API, AUTH | `src/app/api/calendar/feed/[token]/route.ts`. The `.ics` suffix arrives inside the param, so strip it and hash with sha256 to look up the row. Rate limit (B9). Headers: `Content-Type: text/calendar; charset=utf-8`, `Cache-Control: private, max-age=900`. Disabled or archived user → 404. |\n| FR-28 | NOTIF, SVC | `event.created` when `startAt` is within 30 days (for recurring events, the first occurrence). Email-default-by-category (D5). Recipients come from `resolveAudienceUserIds`, excluding the creator. |\n| FR-29 | NOTIF, SVC | `event.updated` only when `startAt`, `endAt`, `allDay` or `location` changes **and** the event is upcoming. One notify call per PATCH. |\n| FR-30 | SVC, API | `getPublicEvents(from,to)` → `isPublic` events expanded, public-safe fields only (no audience, no creator). The route is unauthenticated and range-capped like FR-32. PRD-18 is the consumer. Consider applying `rateLimit` per IP. |\n| FR-31 | SVC | `getUpcomingEventsForUser(user, limit)` reuses the FR-32 merge with sources=events and a 90-day window, takes `limit`. No UI (NFR-11). |\n| FR-32 | API, SVC, AUTH | `getCalendarItems(user, {from,to,sources,studentId})` is the core merge. It returns a discriminated union `{kind:'event'|'assignment'|'quiz'|'timetable', …}` with instants in UTC plus `allDay`. Validation rejects `to − from > 100 days`. Performance: one events query + one audience-match pass in memory, and one query per deadline source over all children at once (NFR-4). |\n| FR-33 | API, AUTH | `POST /api/events`, `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/events/:id`, `GET /api/events/:id/ics`. Visibility = the user matches the audience **or** is the creator or ADMIN. Not visible → 404. |\n| FR-34 | API | `src/app/api/school-day/route.ts` (singular, a new folder next to `school-days`, which stays untouched). `date` is `YYYY-MM-DD` in the school tz. Any authenticated user. |\n| FR-35 | INT | Nav entry (B15, D6). |\n| FR-36 | AUTH, SVC | In update/delete: `if (user.role==='ADMIN' && event.createdById !== user.id) audit({action:'event.update'|'event.delete', entityType:'CalendarEvent', entityId, metadata})`. |\n| FR-37 | SEED | An idempotent `seedCalendar()` in `prisma/seed.ts`, matching events by title + startAt. Parent–teacher evening date = seed run date + 14 days, so it is not stable across runs; match it by title only. Robotics Club: D7. Sports day: no announcement link. |\n| NFR-1 | UI, TEST | Lint/QA grep for banned imports. Only MUI + MUI X (incl. the scheduler). |\n| NFR-2 | process | The dev phase must call MUI MCP before using any scheduler API, and system-design should list the doc pages to fetch (Quickstart, Views, Events, Timezones, Localization). |\n| NFR-3 | SVC, TEST | One concern across expansion (wall-clock stepping), all-day storage (tz midnight), the `VALUE=DATE` / TZID feed, and the scheduler `timezone` prop (check MCP Timezones page). Test a DST week (e.g. the US 2026-11-01 or 2027-03-14 transition, depending on the seed tz). |\n| NFR-4 | SVC | <500 ms for a parent with 3 children in month view. Batch the child/course/section lookups, use one events query with an audience `OR` filter, and avoid per-day `isSchoolDay` calls. Add an index on `EventAudience(type, targetId)` beyond the PRD spec (the PRD's model has the event FK; add `@@index([type, targetId])`). |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH, SVC | `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, stored as sha256 hex. The feed reuses `getCalendarItems`, so visibility can't drift. Integration test for parity. |\n| NFR-6 | TEST, DEP | `node-ical` devDependency. Parse `buildIcs` output in a unit test and the feed route output in an integration test. |\n| NFR-7 | AUTH | Every handler uses `requireUser`/`requireRole`, except the feed (token auth) and `/api/public/events` (public by design). Per-entity checks live in calendar-service, not in the routes. |\n| NFR-8 | all | `src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts` (+ `ical.ts`, `recurrence.ts` if split). Thin routes. `{data}` responses. `logger`. cuid ids. |\n| NFR-9 | INT | Reuse list: timetable-service (B3/B4), rate-limit (B9), notify (B7), audit, DataTable, useToast, ConfirmDialog, MarkdownView/Editor, csv.ts, the dispatch cron (B8), getSchoolTimezone (B13), and the access helpers (B11). |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | Unit: expansion, isSchoolDay, ICS escaping/RRULE/folding, all-day exclusive end, term-break gaps. Integration: merge per role, token reset (old URL 404), RSVP deadline. Playwright: 3 flows. |\n| NFR-11 | scope | No per-occurrence exceptions, no room booking, no two-way sync. PRD-16/18 get only FR-30/31 hooks. |\n| NFR-12 | UI | 768 px breakpoint (FR-9). English only. Evergreen browsers. |\n\n## 3. Decisions for arch-design-system (open items from intake)\n\n- **D1 – AudienceType / audience.ts / builder (FR-3, FR-7, FR-14).** PRD-12 is absent. Recommendation: SH-14 defines `enum AudienceType { SCHOOL GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }`. `EventAudience` gets `type`, `targetId String?` (null for SCHOOL) and `roles Role[] @default([])`, where empty means all roles. `roles` covers \"Grade 7 parents\". Resolver in `src/server/audience/audience.ts`, builder in `src/components/AudienceBuilder/`. Both are named generically so PRD-12 adopts them instead of re-creating them. Membership: SCHOOL = all active users; GRADE_LEVEL = students whose current-year SectionMember section has that grade (or `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`, pick one) plus their parents plus teachers of those sections or courses; SECTION = members + homeroom teacher + parents; COURSE = ACTIVE enrollments + teacher/co-teachers + parents.\n- **D2 – FR-20 host page.** No `/admin/academic-years/[id]` UI exists. The minimal option is a small server page at that exact path that lists the year's terms (read-only) with an \"Add term breaks\" button. Full academic-year CRUD UI is out of scope. Add no nav entry; link to it from the calendar editor or admin, or reach it by URL.\n- **D3 – Holidays vs School events chips.** Use intake's default: no duplication. HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool` events appear only under \"Holidays\".\n- **D4 – RSVP guests.** Parents only. The server forces 0 for other roles.\n- **D5 – Email default per category (FR-28).** The registry's `defaultEmail` is per type. Options: (a) two types, `event.created` (defaultEmail false) and `event.holiday_created` (defaultEmail true); or (b) one type that passes `email` only for HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK, which ignores the user preference toggle semantics. Recommend (a), because it stays inside the existing preference model with no changes to notify.ts.\n- **D6 – Nav.** Add `/calendar` (all roles). `/account/calendar` gets no sidebar entry, consistent with the existing account pages. It is reached from the account menu and a \"Subscribe\" link on `/calendar`.\n- **D7 – Robotics Club course (FR-37).** Not in the seed. Recommend seeding a minimal ELECTIVE course `ROBOTICS` (teacher Tom, current year) only if absent, so the Chess club example works. The alternative is skip-with-log.\n- **D8 – Feed URL display vs hashed storage (FR-24/25, NFR-5).** The raw token is only available at creation or reset. Recommendation: `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` returns `{url}` only when it creates the first token, and `{url:null, createdAt}` otherwise. The page then says \"Reset link to get a new URL\". This needs to be explicit in the API contracts.\n- **D9 – Schema deviations from the PRD's model list** (flag them in system-design): `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt`, `EventAudience.roles`, `@@index([type,targetId])`. Each traces to FR-23, FR-3/FR-37 and NFR-4.\n\n## 4. Risks\n\n- **R1 (high):** `@mui/x-scheduler` is beta. Its API (views, timezone, all-day exclusivity, custom event rendering for chips/colours) is unverified until MCP is consulted. Budget for fallbacks (FR-9).\n- **R2:** The import cycle between timetable-service and calendar-service (B4).\n- **R3:** DST correctness spans four places (FR-15 expansion, FR-4 storage, FR-26 VTIMEZONE, UI). One shared pure helper set in `src/lib/dates.ts` keeps them consistent.\n- **R4:** Audience resolution is the performance hot path (NFR-4) and the security boundary (NFR-5/7). It needs a single implementation, tested per role.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":116,"newStart":1,"newLines":106,"lines":["-# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-13","+# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-14"," "," Written by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.","-Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:00:00Z), PRD-13 Direct Messaging. It has 32 FRs and 11 NFRs (43 requirements) at 95% confidence.","-`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. The open decisions intake handed to the architect are in §4.","+Source: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:10:00Z), PRD-14 School Calendar, Events & Holidays. It has 37 FRs and 12 NFRs (49 requirements) at 96% confidence.","+`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It has 3 warnings: PRD-12 is missing, the academic-year page is missing, and new dependencies are needed. The decisions left open are in §3."," ","-> Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is left over from an earlier ticket (SH-12/SH-11). Its owning sub-task must overwrite it. None of those files is an SH-13 input.","+> This file replaces a leftover SH-13 version. Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is also left over from SH-13. Its owning sub-task must overwrite it, and none of those files is an SH-14 input."," "," ## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk"," ","-| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-13 |","+| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-14 |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| B1 | The schema has no messaging models. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. `User` has `role`, `status` (default INVITED) and `archivedAt`, with `@@index([role, status])`. `FileObject` back-relations are explicit per attachment table. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1..4: one new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_messaging`). Add back-relations on `User` (participants, sent messages, reports filed/reviewed, settings, pending emails) and on `FileObject` (`messageAttachments`). |","-| B2 | `Notification` has **no entity/context column**: only `userId, type, title, body, link, readAt`, indexed on `(userId, readAt, createdAt)`. | schema L304-317 | FR-19 collapsing: \"replace older unread message.received rows for that conversation\" can only key on `link = /messages/<conversationId>` (plus `type` and `readAt: null`). Recommend `deleteMany({ userId in, type:'message.received', readAt:null, link })` before `notify()`. This is fine for performance because the leading `userId` index column applies. No schema change to Notification is needed. |","-| B3 | `notify()` writes the in-app rows **and enqueues email immediately** (EmailOutbox) when `input.email` is passed. It never throws and dedupes userIds. It filters DISABLED/ARCHIVED users. Preferences come from `resolvePrefs(def, pref)` in `notifications/preferences.ts`. | notify.ts L8-80 | FR-19/20 conflict: message email must be **deferred**. Call `notify()` for `message.received` **without** `email`, so only the in-app row is written. Upsert a `PendingMessageEmail` per recipient whose resolved `prefs.email` is true. The maintenance pass then re-checks `lastReadAt`/quiet hours and enqueues to EmailOutbox using the same `renderEmail('generic-notification')`. **arch-design-system** should define a small exported helper (e.g. `enqueueEmail(userIds, …)` or reuse of `resolvePrefs`) rather than duplicating notify's internals. |","-| B4 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). The `COMMUNICATION` category exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a static boolean per type and `roles` is a per-type role list. | notifications/types.ts | FR-19: `message.received` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp false, roles ALL}. FR-26: `message.reported` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true, roles ['ADMIN']}. |","-| B5 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` is a per-process sliding window that returns `{ ok, retryAfterMs }`. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-4: `rateLimit('msg:'+userId, 30, 60_000)`. On failure, throw `AppError('RATE_LIMITED')` (429) with `details.retryAfterMs`. The limiter is per-process. This is accepted (existing ponytail note). |","-| B6 | `registerFileAccess`: built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (files/contexts.ts). Unattached files (`contextId null`) are owner/ADMIN only. Resolver errors deny. Orphan files are purged after 24 h. | files/access.ts; files/contexts.ts | FR-27: add `register('message', messageResolver)` in `registerBuiltInContexts`. The resolver loads the Message by `file.contextId` (contextId = **messageId**, so a soft-deleted message can still be resolved), then allows a participant (`leftAt` irrelevant? see A7) or `isSafeguardingLead`. Attach files in the send transaction, or they are purged. Note: `FileAccessUser` is `{id, role}` only, so the resolver must query `isSafeguardingLead` itself. |","-| B7 | `SessionUser` = `{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}`. It has **no `isSafeguardingLead`**. | requireRole.ts L14-26 | NFR-1/FR-23..25: add a `requireSafeguardingLead()` helper (in `src/server/messaging/` or auth) that does `requireRole('ADMIN')` plus a DB read of the flag. Do not put the flag in the JWT: a revoked flag must take effect immediately. The page variant redirects to /forbidden (FR-23 says \"others get 403\"). |","-| B8 | Teacher→student reachability already exists: `getAccessibleStudentIds(TEACHER)` = ACTIVE enrollment in courses where `teacherId` or `coTeacherIds has` the teacher, **plus** SectionMember of sections they homeroom. The homeroom branch has **no academic-year filter**. `teaches(user, course)` is in course-access.ts. | student-access.ts L20-55; course-access.ts | FR-5/FR-32: reuse the same predicates (ideally share the Prisma `where` fragments) so contact rules and student-record access never disagree. Decide on the current-year filter for homeroom (A5). The PARENT branch is ParentStudentLink. |","-| B9 | `Enrollment @@unique([courseId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId, status])`. `ParentStudentLink @@unique([parentId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId])`. `SectionMember @@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` (no `sectionId` index). | schema | FR-5/FR-8 queries are index-backed from the student side. `coTeacherIds has` is not indexable, but a single user's course set is small. |","-| B10 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (CRON_SECRET) runs each job in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take)` → conditional `updateMany` claim → act if `count===1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts | FR-20: add `sendDueMessageEmails(now)`, isolated in its own try/catch. Process `PendingMessageEmail where dueAt <= now`. If the participant's `lastReadAt >= message time`, drop the row. If now is inside quiet hours, push `dueAt` to the end of quiet hours. Otherwise enqueue and delete the row (delete = claim; `deleteMany` count===1). |","-| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` lives in `assignments-service.ts` (precedent: other modules import it). `schoolNow(now, tz)` returns `{isoDay, hhmm}`. `formatInSchoolTz`, and `fromZonedTime` from date-fns-tz, are available. | src/lib/dates.ts; assignments-service.ts L64 | FR-20/21 quiet hours: a pure `isInQuietHours(hhmm, start, end)` with midnight wrap (`start > end`) and `quietHoursEnd(now, tz, end)` → UTC instant. Unit-test both (NFR-10). FR-10 day grouping uses `formatInSchoolTz`. |","-| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes `RATE_LIMITED`, `FORBIDDEN`, `NOT_FOUND`, `CONFLICT`, `VALIDATION`. `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `audit()` exist. | src/server/http.ts; src/server/audit.ts | FR-28/NFR-6 handler conventions. Recommend returning 404 (not 403) for a non-participant on `GET /api/conversations/:id`, so cuids reveal nothing (NFR-1). FR-6 explicitly mandates 403 for **create** violations. |","-| B13 | **No admin user-edit UI exists.** `src/app/(app)/admin` has only attendance, courses, email-log, grading-scales, report-cards and sections. Users are edited only via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (ADMIN, `updateUserSchema`, audited). | src/app/api/users/[id]/route.ts; src/lib/validators/users.ts L103 | FR-2 resolution (intake's open question): add `isSafeguardingLead: z.boolean().optional()` to `updateUserSchema`. Reject or ignore it when the target role ≠ ADMIN. Audit the change (`user.update` metadata). **No form to extend.** Building a user-admin page is out of scope. |","-| B14 | **`/students/[id]` has no page.tsx or layout.tsx.** There are only sub-pages (attendance, assignments, courses, grades, report-cards), so there is no shared \"student page header\" today. | find src/app/(app)/students | FR-16: arch-design-system must pick the surface. Options: (a) add `students/[id]/layout.tsx` with a PageHeader + actions (affects all sub-pages, minimal per-page edits), or (b) put actions on each sub-page header. Recommend (a), keeping the `[id]` segment (no rename, per the PRD). The actions are client components that call `POST /api/conversations`. |","-| B15 | The course roster page is a **server component** rendering an MUI Table with no selection. PARENT gets notFound and STUDENT sees a name list. | courses/[courseId]/roster/page.tsx | FR-17: extract the TEACHER/ADMIN table into a client component with Checkbox selection and a toolbar button \"Message selected students\". It opens the FR-12 dialog prefilled. Rows carry `enrollmentId`, so the student id needs to be included in `RosterEntry` if it is not already there. |","-| B16 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `NotificationBell` implements a visibility-gated 30 s poll + MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L23-73 | FR-18: add `{label:'Messages', href:'/messages', roles: ALL_ROLES}` and an optional `badge?: 'messages'` key. The shell renders a polled Badge from `/api/messaging/unread-count`. Extract the bell's poll loop into a small `usePolling(fn, ms)` hook and reuse it for FR-13's 5 s/30 s polls. |","-| B17 | `/account/notifications` = page.tsx + `PreferencesTable.tsx`. `/api/me/*` routes exist (notification-preferences, profile, …). | src/app/(app)/account/notifications | FR-21: add a `QuietHoursSection` client component under that page, plus `src/app/api/me/messaging-settings/route.ts` (GET/PUT, any role). |","-| B18 | Seed users: Alice Admin, Tom Teacher, Tina Tutor, Sam Student, Sara Scholar and Pat Parent (by email). The seed creates **no ParentStudentLink** and no enrollments. Courses come from elsewhere and `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` skips when missing. | prisma/seed.ts L16-22, L304 | FR-29: set `isSafeguardingLead=true` on Alice. The Pat↔Tom thread \"about Sam's homework\" needs a Pat↔Sam link to satisfy contact rules at runtime. Recommend the seed upsert that link (or skip the thread with a log, like other seeds). The MATH-7A group uses the first 4 ACTIVE enrollments and skips if there are fewer or the course is missing. Seeds write via Prisma directly (bypassing canMessage) but must leave data valid under canMessage. Make it idempotent by checking for existing seeded conversations (subject/participants). |","-| B19 | Shared components: FileUpload, FileList, UserAvatar, UserPicker, ConfirmDialog, Toast, EmptyState, PageHeader, DataTable (in `src/components/<Name>/`). `@mui/x-date-pickers` is installed. | src/components | FR-10/11/12/23/24: reuse FileList/FileUpload (context 'message'), UserAvatar, ConfirmDialog (delete/leave), Toast (report confirmation), DataTable (safeguarding lists). FR-12 recipient picker: UserPicker is a candidate only if it accepts a custom options source (grouped contacts). Otherwise use MUI Autocomplete with `groupBy`. FR-21 time inputs: x-date-pickers TimePicker. |","-| B20 | The mui-mcp server failed to connect in this session (CONNECT_TIMEOUT). | session | NFR-5 requires mui-mcp lookups during dev. The dev phase must retry it. This is not a blocker for architecture. |","+| B1 | The schema has no calendar models and no `AudienceType` enum. There is no `Announcement` model and no `audience.ts`. The latest migration is `20261112000000_add_direct_messaging`. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-2/FR-3: add one new migration, e.g. `20261113000000_add_calendar`. `AudienceType` must be defined here (see D1). Add back-relations on `User` for events created, RSVPs and the feed token. |","+| B2 | Audience targets that already exist: `GradeLevel` (Grade 6/7/8 seeded), `Section` (`homeroomTeacherId`, `gradeLevelId`, per year), `SectionMember` (`@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])`), `Course` (`teacherId`, `coTeacherIds String[]`, `sectionId?`), `Enrollment` (ACTIVE/DROPPED, `@@index([studentId,status])`) and `ParentStudentLink`. `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId` exists. | schema L115-470 | FR-3: the minimal enum is `SCHOOL`, `GRADE_LEVEL`, `SECTION` and `COURSE`, plus a role filter so the seed's \"Grade 7 parents\" works (see D1). Every type resolves to student ids through existing tables. Parents are added through `ParentStudentLink`. |","+| B3 | `getScheduleForDate` and `getSchoolScheduleForDate` both contain a placeholder comment: `// PRD-14 holidays hook in here: return [] when date is a school holiday.` Both return `ScheduleEntry[]` and have no reason field. A private `schoolTimezone()` exists at L488. | timetable-service.ts L542-583 | FR-17: put the `isSchoolDay` check at those two hooks. **The return type cannot change without touching callers** (`attendance-service.ts` L130 and L472, `getCurrentSlot`). Recommendation: keep `ScheduleEntry[]` and add a sibling, e.g. `getDayInfo(date)` → `{isSchoolDay, reason}`, which callers use to show the holiday name. The alternative is a new return shape, which needs every caller updated. |","+| B4 | Both `isSchoolDay` and `getScheduleForDate` apply the teaching-weekday rule `day?.isTeaching ?? isoDay <= 5` from the `SchoolDay` table. | timetable-service.ts L552, L572 | FR-16: reuse `listSchoolDays()` (exported L112) instead of re-implementing the fallback. Watch for import cycles: calendar-service will import from timetable-service, and timetable-service calls back into `isSchoolDay`. Put the pure date→isoDay and holiday lookup in calendar-service with **no** import from timetable-service, or pass teaching days in. |","+| B5 | Attendance teacher landing is `getToday(user, date?)` and admin overview is `getOverview(date?)`. Both are fed by the schedule functions. `RegisterForm.tsx` is the register UI. | attendance-service.ts L122-150, L463-475 | FR-18: `getToday` returns `{noSchoolReason}` alongside its existing fields. Saving a register on a no-school date requires a confirm flag in the save body (e.g. `holidayOverride: true`) and the server checks it. That makes it a server-side rule, not only a dialog. |","+| B6 | The assignment editor is `courses/[courseId]/assignments/AssignmentForm.tsx`, using `DateTimePicker` on `dueAt` with school-tz `toWall/fromWall`. Quiz settings are in `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit/QuizSettingsPanel.tsx` (`availableUntil`). | grep | FR-19: both are client components. Fetch `GET /api/school-day?date=` on date change and render a non-blocking MUI `Alert`. Saving is unchanged. |","+| B7 | Notification registry `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const and its `COMMUNICATION`/`ACADEMIC` categories exist. `notify({type,userIds,title,body,link,email})` dedupes, never throws, and is called after commit. `notifyStudentAndParents` / `expandStudentRecipients` add linked parents. | notifications/types.ts; notify.ts L30, L89-120 | FR-23/28/29: add `event.created`, `event.updated` and `event.rsvp_reminder`. **`defaultEmail` is per type, but FR-28 wants it per category** (HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK email on by default). See D5. Resolve audience → userIds once, then call `notify`. |","+| B8 | The maintenance cron `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` runs each job in its own try/catch + logger (reminders, quiz, message emails). | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-23: add `sendRsvpReminders(now)` to its own isolated block. \"Once per event\" needs a claim column: `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?`, claimed with conditional `updateMany` (quiz `resultsReleasedAt` precedent). The PRD model list doesn't include that column. Adding it is a small, justified deviation (flag it). |","+| B9 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` → `{ok, retryAfterMs}`. It is per-process and marked with a `ponytail` note. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | FR-27: `rateLimit('ical:'+tokenHash, 60, 3_600_000)` → 429 `RATE_LIMITED`. Key on the **hash**, not the raw token, so raw tokens never sit in memory maps or logs. |","+| B10 | `http.ts` provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `AppError` with codes incl. `RATE_LIMITED`, `NOT_FOUND`, `FORBIDDEN` and `VALIDATION_ERROR`. `requireRole`, `requireUser`, `requirePageRole` and `requirePageUser` exist. `audit()` exists. | http.ts; requireRole.ts; audit.ts | NFR-7/8/FR-36. The feed route is the only unauthenticated handler. It returns `text/calendar` and the 404 is a plain response, not JSON. Its token parse failure and token-not-found case return the same 404. |","+| B11 | Access helpers: `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` ('ALL' for admin, own id for students, linked children for parents, enrolled + homeroom students for teachers), `assertCanViewStudent`, `assertCanManageCourse` (course-access.ts L56) and `resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId?)` (assignments-service L262). | auth/*.ts | FR-7: teacher create checks are `assertCanManageCourse` for COURSE audiences and `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` for SECTION. FR-11/FR-32 `studentId` param: use `resolveViewedStudent`/`assertCanViewStudent` (404 for other families). |","+| B12 | Deadline data sources already exist: `/api/me/assignments`, `/api/me/timetable` and `/api/me/children` routes, `Assignment @@index([courseId, dueAt])`, `Quiz @@index([courseId,status])` with `availableUntil`, and `getPersonalTimetable`. | api/me/*; schema | FR-10/FR-32: the calendar merge should call the existing service functions behind these routes (scoped to a date range), not new queries. A range filter on `dueAt`/`availableUntil` may need adding. Only PUBLISHED assignments/quizzes should be included, matching what the user can open. |","+| B13 | School timezone is read in two places: exported `getSchoolTimezone()` in assignments-service.ts L64 and private `schoolTimezone()` in timetable-service. `getSchoolSettings` (cached) is in services/settings.ts. `src/lib/dates.ts` has `schoolNow`, `formatInSchoolTz` and `ISO_DAY_NAMES`. date-fns-tz 3.2.0 is installed. | grep | NFR-3/FR-4: use `getSchoolTimezone()` and do not add a third copy. All-day ↔ `fromZonedTime(midnight, tz)` conversions belong as pure helpers in `src/lib/dates.ts` (unit-testable, client-safe). |","+| B14 | No `/admin/academic-years` page exists. Only APIs exist: `academic-years/[id]`, `…/set-current`, `…/terms`, `…/terms/generate`, and `terms.ts` service functions. Seed terms: S1 2026-08-17→2027-01-15, S2 2027-01-18→2027-06-11. | ls src/app/(app)/admin; seed.ts L91-94 | FR-20: a host page is needed (see D2). Note that the seed's gap between S1 and S2 is a weekend (Jan 16–17), so \"Add term breaks\" on seed data produces one short break. Winter break is **inside** S1 and is seeded explicitly. |","+| B15 | `navigation.ts` has `NavItem {label, href, icon, roles, group?, badge?, requires?}` and `ALL_ROLES`. The account area has `notifications` and `security` pages only, and no account nav entries. | config/navigation.ts | FR-35: add `{label:'Calendar', href:'/calendar', roles: ALL_ROLES}`. `/account/calendar` is linked from the account area like the other `/account/*` pages; no sidebar entry is needed (D6). |","+| B16 | Shared UI exists: `components/Toast/useToast`, `ConfirmDialog`, `MarkdownView`, `MarkdownEditor`, `DataTable`, `PageHeader`, `EmptyState` and `UserPicker`. `react-markdown` 10.1.0 is installed. `components/messaging` exists, but no audience builder. | ls src/components | NFR-1/NFR-9: the drawer uses `MarkdownView` and the editor uses `MarkdownEditor`. Delete confirmation uses `ConfirmDialog`. The RSVP list uses `DataTable`. CSV export reuses `src/server/csv.ts`. A new `components/AudienceBuilder` is the only new shared component (D1). |","+| B17 | `package.json` has MUI 9.5.0 for material, icons, x-charts, x-data-grid and x-date-pickers, plus `@mui/x-internals` 9.1.0 as an override. There is no `@mui/x-scheduler`, `ics` or `node-ical`. | package.json | FR-1: pin the scheduler with an exact version from MUI MCP, and check its peer range against `@mui/material` 9.5.0 and `@mui/x-internals`. NFR-6: `node-ical` as an exact-pinned devDependency. `ics` is not needed, because a hand-written RFC 5545 builder (about 100 lines, pure) is easier to test for escaping and folding (tech-stack sub-task decides). |","+| B18 | Seed: academic year 2026-2027 is current, Grade 6/7/8 exist, and sections 7A/7B exist. **There is no \"Robotics Club\" course anywhere**, and no Announcement exists. Seeds use the `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` + skip-with-log pattern. | seed.ts; grep | FR-37: the Chess club audience needs a Robotics Club course. Either seed it (an ELECTIVE `Course`, with `CourseKind` available) or skip with a log (D7). Sports day is seeded without an announcement link. |","+| B19 | `Notification` has only `link` for context (no entity column). | schema L313-326 | FR-28/29 links: `/calendar?event=<id>` so the page can open the drawer from a query param. |"," "," ## 2. Requirement → architectural concern"," ","-Legend: DM = data model/migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance job, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule.","+Concern key: **DM** data model/migration, **SVC** server service, **API** route handler, **UI** page/component, **JOB** cron/maintenance, **AUTH** access boundary, **INT** change to existing module, **NOTIF** notification type, **DEP** dependency, **TEST**, **SEED**."," ","-| Req | Concern | Notes |","+| Req | Concern | Notes for arch-design-system |"," |---|---|---|","-| FR-1 | DM | Conversation, ConversationParticipant (`@@unique([conversationId,userId])`, `@@index([userId])`, per-user `lastReadAt`, `mutedAt`/`archivedAt`, `leftAt`), Message (`@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, which NFR-2 depends on; `editedAt`, `deletedAt`), MessageAttachment (messageId, fileId; cascade on message), MessageReport + `ReportStatus`, MessagingSettings (userId unique, quietStart/End `String? HH:mm`). Add `updatedAt` per convention (A2). |","-| FR-2 | DM, API, AUTH | `User.isSafeguardingLead`. It can only be edited via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (B13) and is meaningful only for ADMIN. |","-| FR-3 | DM, SVC | `MessageRevision(messageId, body, createdAt)`, `@@index([messageId])`. Written in the same tx as the edit (original body before overwrite). Cascade with Message (messages are never hard-deleted anyway, NFR-3). |","-| FR-4 | DM, JOB | `PendingMessageEmail(userId, conversationId, dueAt)`, `@@unique([userId, conversationId])` so repeated sends upsert one row (the first unread message sets dueAt = now+10 min; later sends keep the earliest dueAt). `@@index([dueAt])`. |","-| FR-5 | SVC, AUTH | `canMessage(sender, recipient)` is a pure decision over pre-loaded relationship facts. Expose a batch form `messageableIds(sender, candidateIds)` to avoid N+1 queries for groups (≤25) and contacts (FR-8). Matrix: ADMIN→any, any→ADMIN, TEACHER↔TEACHER, TEACHER→STUDENT (managed course or homeroom, B8), TEACHER→PARENT (via the linked child under the same rule), STUDENT→own teachers, PARENT→linked child's teachers, all others false. Symmetry: student→teacher uses the same relation as teacher→student. Disabled/archived recipients → false. |","-| FR-6 | SVC, AUTH | Create conversation in one tx: participants = creator ∪ recipients (dedupe, exclude self from count rules), 2..25 total. Check `canMessage(creator, each)`. If any STUDENT is present, require ≥1 TEACHER/ADMIN. Any violation → 403 with nothing created. \"Students may reply in staff groups but cannot start student-student\" follows from canMessage(student, student)=false at create, plus the send-time rule (FR-7) being evaluated per-sender against **staff** participants only (A4). |","-| FR-7 | SVC, AUTH, UI | Send-time re-check. Non-staff sender: allowed iff canMessage(sender, p) holds for at least one remaining staff participant (A4). Otherwise 403 with code/reason `RELATIONSHIP_ENDED`. Staff always pass. `GET /api/conversations/:id` returns `canSend: boolean` so the composer shows the disabled message without a failed POST. |","-| FR-8 | SVC, API | `GET /api/messaging/contacts?q=`: role-specific grouped queries (PARENT: per child, \"My child's teachers (<child>)\"; STUDENT: \"My teachers\"; TEACHER: \"Students in <course>\", \"Parents of students in <course>\", homeroom, staff; all: \"School office\" = ADMINs). Status ACTIVE only. `q` filters on name. Cap each group (e.g. 50). |","-| FR-9 | UI, API | `/messages` layout with a two-pane `useMediaQuery(theme.breakpoints.down('md'))`, single pane + back below 768 px (theme `md`=900, so use a custom `down(768)` or confirm breakpoint, A8). List from `GET /api/conversations?archived=&q=` sorted `lastMessageAt desc`, with preview and `unreadCount` per row. Route: `/messages` and `/messages/[conversationId]`. |","-| FR-10 | UI, API | `GET /api/conversations/:id/messages?before=<id>&limit=30` (keyset on `(createdAt,id)`). Deleted messages are returned with `body: null, deleted: true` and attachments stripped for normal users (NFR-3: content is never exposed to non-safeguarding users). Day grouping in the school timezone (B11). |","-| FR-11 | UI, XC | Composer validation shared by the client and `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts` (body trim 1..5000, ≤5 fileIds). Enter=send / Shift+Enter=newline. Counter shows at >4500. |","-| FR-12 | UI | New-conversation dialog: Autocomplete multi-select grouped by contacts label, subject ≤120, first message. It posts `POST /api/conversations` with `{participantIds, subject?, body, fileIds?}`, creating the conversation + first message atomically. Also opened prefilled from FR-16/FR-17. |","-| FR-13 | UI, API, XC | 5 s poll of `?after=<lastId>` on the visible thread. 30 s poll on the list + nav badge. Gate on `document.visibilityState` (B16). The `after` query must also surface **edits/deletes** of already-loaded messages, or edits only appear on reload (A9). |","-| FR-14 | API, SVC, UI | `POST /api/conversations/:id/read` (sets lastReadAt=now and marks this conversation's unread `message.received` notifications read; deletes the PendingMessageEmail row), `/mute`, `/archive` (toggle body `{archived}`), `/leave`. Leave: set `leftAt`, which blocks further reads/sends for that user. Refuse (409/403) for the creator when `involvesStudent` is true. Group-only: DMs with 2 participants cannot be left (A10). Sending auto-unarchives for other participants? (A11). |","-| FR-15 | SVC, API | `PATCH /api/messages/:id` / `DELETE` (soft: `deletedAt`). Sender only, `now - createdAt ≤ 15 min`, not already deleted. Edit writes a MessageRevision + `editedAt` in one tx. No hard-delete path exists anywhere. |","-| FR-16 | UI | Student page actions (surface per B14). TEACHER/ADMIN \"Message parents\": participants = linked parents (+ creator). Hide the action if there are none or canMessage fails. PARENT \"Message teacher\": picker of the child's teachers (subset of contacts) → dialog. |","-| FR-17 | UI | Roster selection + action (B15). TEACHER only (ADMIN may also be offered, harmless). |","-| FR-18 | CFG, API, UI | Nav entry + badge (B16). `GET /api/messaging/unread-count` = count of the user's non-left participations where `lastMessageAt > coalesce(lastReadAt, epoch)` (count conversations, not messages: cheap, index-friendly). Archived conversations excluded? (A11). |","-| FR-19 | NOTIF, SVC | After the send tx commits: for each other participant not muted and not left, delete older unread `message.received` rows with the same link (B2), then `notify()` in-app only (B3). Title \"New message from <sender>\", body = 200-char plain preview, link `/messages/<id>`. |","-| FR-20 | JOB, DM, NOTIF | Upsert a PendingMessageEmail (dueAt=now+10 min) for recipients whose email pref is on (B3). Job per B10. Quiet hours read from MessagingSettings, evaluated in the school timezone (B11). |","-| FR-21 | UI, API, DM | MessagingSettings GET (defaults: no quiet hours) / PUT, Zod `HH:mm` regex. Both-or-neither validation. start == end is rejected. Applies to all roles (A3). |","-| FR-22 | API, SVC, NOTIF | `POST /api/messages/:id/report {reason ≤1000}`. Participant only. Allowed on own/others' messages (or other people's only? A12). One OPEN report per (message, reporter) to avoid spam (unique or check). Then FR-26 notify. |","-| FR-23 | UI, API, AUTH, XC | `/admin/safeguarding` (tabs Reports / Conversations), gated by `requireSafeguardingLead` (B7). `GET /api/safeguarding/reports?status=` with OPEN first, then createdAt desc. Detail includes the message, ±5 messages (including deleted and with revisions) and participants. `PATCH /api/safeguarding/reports/:id {action: review\\|dismiss, note?}` sets status, reviewedById, reviewedAt and note, then calls `audit()` (NFR-11). The nav entry is shown only to leads (the nav filter is role-based, so either show it to ADMIN and 403 non-leads, or extend NavItem with a predicate, A13). |","-| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH | `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations?participantId=&from=&to=` with `involvesStudent: true`, paginated. `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations/:id` = read-only full thread with deleted bodies and `revisions[]`. Same lead gate. |","-| FR-25 | XC, AUTH | `audit({action:'safeguarding.conversation.view', entityType:'Conversation', entityId})` on every safeguarding conversation view **and** on report detail views, since they expose conversation context. Done in the service, so both the API and the server page paths are covered. |","-| FR-26 | NOTIF | Notify `User where role=ADMIN, isSafeguardingLead, status ACTIVE` with `message.reported` (email allowed via notify's normal path: no deferral). Link `/admin/safeguarding?report=<id>`. The body must not include the message text (keep emails minimal). |","-| FR-27 | FILE, AUTH | B6. Send validates that each fileId is owned by the sender, unattached, and context 'message', then attaches in the tx (contextId = messageId). |","-| FR-28 | API, XC | All routes under `src/app/api/{conversations,messages,messaging,safeguarding,me/messaging-settings}`. Thin handlers + Zod + services in `src/server/messaging/`. Standard ok/paginated/error shapes. |","-| FR-29 | SEED | B18. |","-| FR-30 | SVC, DM | `involvesStudent` is computed in the create tx and is immutable afterwards (no participant-add API exists, so it stays correct). |","-| FR-31 | SVC | Update `lastMessageAt` in the send tx. `@@index` on ConversationParticipant `(userId)` + Conversation `lastMessageAt` serves the list ordering. Edits/deletes do **not** bump it. |","-| FR-32 | AUTH | B8: `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`. Resolved as yes (intake default, matches the existing `teaches()`). |","-| NFR-1 | AUTH, XC | Every service entry takes the SessionUser and loads `ConversationParticipant(conversationId, userId, leftAt null)` first. Non-participant → 404. Safeguarding → `requireSafeguardingLead`. File resolver per B6. Contacts never leak non-messageable users. |","-| NFR-2 | DM, API | `after` poll = participant check (unique-index lookup) + `Message where conversationId, (createdAt,id) > cursor` on `@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, `take 100`. Return `[]` fast. The 30 s list/unread polls use the participant index. Avoid count-per-message aggregation for unread (FR-18). |","-| NFR-3 | DM, SVC, AUTH | No DELETE that removes rows. FK cascades exist only for actual tree cleanup. Deleted/edited originals are exposed only through safeguarding services. |","-| NFR-4 | API, XC | B5. Applies to `POST /api/conversations/:id/messages`. Recommend counting `POST /api/conversations` (it also sends) against the same key. |","-| NFR-5 | UI, XC | MUI only; B19/B20. Badge, Drawer/List, Autocomplete, TimePicker, Tabs, Menu, Chip, TextField. |","-| NFR-6 | XC | `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts`, `src/server/messaging/{contact-rules,conversations,messages,notifications,quiet-hours,safeguarding,maintenance}.ts`, logger, cuid, UTC storage. |","-| NFR-7 | UI | See FR-9 (breakpoint, A8). |","-| NFR-8 | XC | A 5 s poll guarantees ≤ ~5 s + request latency < 6 s. No websockets/SSE. |","-| NFR-9 | XC | There is no reactions, typing or broadcast endpoint. Do not touch announcements (PRD-12 is absent). |","-| NFR-10 | TEST | `tests/unit/messaging/contact-rules.test.ts` (matrix incl. co-teacher, homeroom, DROPPED enrollment, group student-needs-staff, 26 participants), `quiet-hours.test.ts` (wrap midnight). `tests/integration/messaging/` (notification collapse, quiet-hours deferral via maintenance job, revision capture, 15-min window, rate limit, non-participant 404, safeguarding 403 + audit). `tests/e2e/messaging.spec.ts` (two browser contexts parent→teacher < 6 s; student→student blocked in the picker and on POST 403). |","-| NFR-11 | XC | Audit report review/dismiss and `isSafeguardingLead` changes. Users' own edits/deletes of their messages are not \"someone else's\" records, so no audit is needed. |","+| FR-1 | DEP | `@mui/x-scheduler` exact pin taken from the MUI MCP `useMuiDocs` + `fetchDocs`. This comes first in the dev plan. If MCP is unreachable, stop (NFR-2). Check peer deps against 9.5.0 (B17). |","+| FR-2 | DM | Enums `EventCategory`, `Recurrence` (NONE/WEEKLY/MONTHLY), `RsvpResponse` (YES/NO/MAYBE). Models `CalendarEvent`, `EventAudience` (cascade from event), `EventRsvp` (`@@id([eventId,userId])`, cascade) and `CalendarFeedToken` (`userId @unique`, `tokenHash @unique`). Add `@@index([startAt, endAt])` on events. Recurrence widens the read window, so range queries must be `startAt < to AND (endAt > from OR recurrence != NONE AND recurrenceUntil >= from)`. Index use is partial, which is fine at school scale. Possible extra columns: `rsvpReminderSentAt` (B8). |","+| FR-3 | DM, AUTH | Decision D1. The audience resolver (`resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` and `userMatchesAudience(user, audiences)`) is the hub of FR-7/10/21/23/26/28/29/31/32. Build it once, in a form PRD-12 can adopt (e.g. `src/server/audience/audience.ts`). |","+| FR-4 | SVC | Zod in `src/lib/validators/calendar.ts` (client-safe, shared with the editor dialog). Cross-field rules use `.superRefine`: endAt ≥ startAt; recurrenceUntil required when recurrence ≠ NONE and ≤ startAt + 1 year; guests 0–5. All-day normalisation (school-tz midnight, **exclusive** end) is a server-side transform, because the client sends dates and not instants. Unit-test the exclusive end (NFR-10). |","+| FR-5 | SVC | Default applied in the service when `isNoSchool` is undefined: `category in (HOLIDAY, TERM_BREAK)`. Not a DB default (it depends on another column). |","+| FR-6 | AUTH | Service-level check: a non-admin sending `isNoSchool`, `isPublic` or a HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK category gets 403. The editor UI hides these fields, but the server is authoritative. |","+| FR-7 | AUTH | A teacher's audiences must all be COURSE audiences they manage (`assertCanManageCourse`) or SECTION audiences they homeroom. SCHOOL or GRADE_LEVEL gives 403 (AC-7). This also applies on PATCH when audiences change. |","+| FR-8 | AUTH | Edit/delete when `createdById === user.id` or the user is ADMIN. Others get 403 if they can see the event, 404 otherwise. |","+| FR-9 | UI, DEP | Client page `/calendar` (server `page.tsx` does `requirePageUser`, then a client `CalendarView`). The view switches at the 768 px breakpoint via `useMediaQuery`. Agenda \"infinite scroll\" means fetching the next 30-day window on scroll. The range cap is 100 days (FR-32). Fallback components only where the Community scheduler lacks a feature. Record each fallback in system-design with its MCP doc reference. |","+| FR-10 | UI | Chips with localStorage key e.g. `calendar.sources`. Sources map 1:1 to the `sources=` query param. Timetable blocks only in Week view: don't fetch `timetable` unless the Week view is active. Holidays vs School events default: HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool` belong to \"Holidays\" only, with no duplicates (intake's default, D3). |","+| FR-11 | UI, AUTH | Parent child filter → `studentId=` (omitted = all children). Server validates via `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Deadline items carry `childName`. Event audience matching for parents uses the union of their children (and the parent's own role for role-filtered audiences). |","+| FR-12 | UI | Right `Drawer`. Data comes from the expanded item plus `GET /api/events/:id` for full detail and RSVP. \"Add to my calendar\" = `<a href=\"/api/events/:id/ics\" download>`. Edit/delete visible when `canEdit` is set; the server computes `canEdit` and returns it. |","+| FR-13 | UI | Deadline items carry an `href` set by the server (`/assignments/<id>` or the quiz route). Clicking navigates; no drawer. |","+| FR-14 | UI | `EventEditorDialog` with React Hook Form + the shared Zod schema. Uses `AudienceBuilder` (D1), the recurrence select + until date, the RSVP switch + deadline, and `MarkdownEditor`. Admin-only fields are rendered only for ADMIN (FR-6). |","+| FR-15 | SVC | Pure `expandOccurrences(event, from, to)` in calendar-service (or `src/lib/calendar/recurrence.ts`). WEEKLY = +7 days **in wall-clock school time** (DST, NFR-3), not +7×24h. MONTHLY-by-date: skip months without that day (e.g. 31st). Document this, because RRULE `BYMONTHDAY=31` also skips, so UI and feed agree. Each occurrence id = `${eventId}:${occurrenceStartISO}`. Heavily unit-tested. |","+| FR-16 | SVC | `isSchoolDay(date)` → `{isSchoolDay, reason}`. Checks the weekday against `SchoolDay` (B4), then SCHOOL-audience `isNoSchool` events covering the date, **including recurring ones** (expand within that day). Reason = `Holiday: <title>` or `Not a teaching day`. A batched variant `noSchoolDays(from, to)` for the month view/landing avoids N queries (NFR-4). |","+| FR-17 | INT | Hook at the two marked lines (B3). Today views use `GET /api/school-day` or the server-side `isSchoolDay`. Keep the `ScheduleEntry[]` signature to avoid caller churn. |","+| FR-18 | INT, AUTH | `getToday` adds the no-school reason. Register save needs the override flag, enforced server-side (B5). Banner + `ConfirmDialog` in `RegisterForm`. |","+| FR-19 | INT, UI | Non-blocking alert in two forms (B6). Only uses FR-34. |","+| FR-20 | UI, SVC | Decision D2. Service `createTermBreaks(academicYearId, actor)`: for each consecutive term pair with a gap of at least one day, create a TERM_BREAK all-day SCHOOL event over the gap (start = day after term end, exclusive end = next term start). Idempotent: skip if an identical TERM_BREAK already exists. ADMIN only + audit. |","+| FR-21 | API, AUTH | `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp`. Rules: RSVP enabled, the user is in the audience, now < `rsvpDeadline`, guests > 0 only for PARENT (D4). Deadline violations return 409 `CONFLICT` or `VALIDATION_ERROR` (pick one and document it). Upsert on the composite PK. Recurring events take a single RSVP for the series (edits apply to the whole series; no per-occurrence data). |","+| FR-22 | API, UI | `GET /api/events/:id` includes `myRsvp` + totals `{yes,no,maybe,guests}`. `GET /api/events/:id/rsvps?format=csv` is creator/ADMIN only and reuses `src/server/csv.ts`. The JSON version uses `DataTable` in the drawer or dialog. |","+| FR-23 | JOB, NOTIF, DM | `event.rsvp_reminder`. The job selects events with `rsvpEnabled`, `rsvpDeadline` within the next 48h, and `rsvpReminderSentAt` null. It claims each event, then notifies audience members with no RSVP row (B8). |","+| FR-24 | UI | `/account/calendar` (requirePageUser). Copy via `navigator.clipboard`. Instructions are static text. Reset uses `ConfirmDialog`. |","+| FR-25 | API, DM, AUTH | `GET /api/me/calendar-feed`: if no token exists, create one and return the URL once. If one exists, **the raw token cannot be shown again** because it is stored hashed. Return `{exists:true, url:null}` and require a reset to see a URL, or create on first GET only. The design must reconcile the \"copy\" UX with hashing (D8). `POST …/reset` replaces the hash. |","+| FR-26 | SVC | Pure `buildIcs(items, tz)`: VCALENDAR + VTIMEZONE (generated from the IANA tz for the covered years; transitions from date-fns-tz offsets), VEVENT with DTSTART;TZID or VALUE=DATE for all-day, RRULE `FREQ=WEEKLY|MONTHLY;UNTIL=…Z`, escaping `\\\\ ; , \\n`, and 75-octet line folding. Window is now−30d → now+365d. The items come from the same merge as FR-32 (NFR-5 parity), skipping timetable. Deadlines are 0-duration VEVENTs with a URL. |","+| FR-27 | API, AUTH | `src/app/api/calendar/feed/[token]/route.ts`. The `.ics` suffix arrives inside the param, so strip it and hash with sha256 to look up the row. Rate limit (B9). Headers: `Content-Type: text/calendar; charset=utf-8`, `Cache-Control: private, max-age=900`. Disabled or archived user → 404. |","+| FR-28 | NOTIF, SVC | `event.created` when `startAt` is within 30 days (for recurring events, the first occurrence). Email-default-by-category (D5). Recipients come from `resolveAudienceUserIds`, excluding the creator. |","+| FR-29 | NOTIF, SVC | `event.updated` only when `startAt`, `endAt`, `allDay` or `location` changes **and** the event is upcoming. One notify call per PATCH. |","+| FR-30 | SVC, API | `getPublicEvents(from,to)` → `isPublic` events expanded, public-safe fields only (no audience, no creator). The route is unauthenticated and range-capped like FR-32. PRD-18 is the consumer. Consider applying `rateLimit` per IP. |","+| FR-31 | SVC | `getUpcomingEventsForUser(user, limit)` reuses the FR-32 merge with sources=events and a 90-day window, takes `limit`. No UI (NFR-11). |","+| FR-32 | API, SVC, AUTH | `getCalendarItems(user, {from,to,sources,studentId})` is the core merge. It returns a discriminated union `{kind:'event'|'assignment'|'quiz'|'timetable', …}` with instants in UTC plus `allDay`. Validation rejects `to − from > 100 days`. Performance: one events query + one audience-match pass in memory, and one query per deadline source over all children at once (NFR-4). |","+| FR-33 | API, AUTH | `POST /api/events`, `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/events/:id`, `GET /api/events/:id/ics`. Visibility = the user matches the audience **or** is the creator or ADMIN. Not visible → 404. |","+| FR-34 | API | `src/app/api/school-day/route.ts` (singular, a new folder next to `school-days`, which stays untouched). `date` is `YYYY-MM-DD` in the school tz. Any authenticated user. |","+| FR-35 | INT | Nav entry (B15, D6). |","+| FR-36 | AUTH, SVC | In update/delete: `if (user.role==='ADMIN' && event.createdById !== user.id) audit({action:'event.update'|'event.delete', entityType:'CalendarEvent', entityId, metadata})`. |","+| FR-37 | SEED | An idempotent `seedCalendar()` in `prisma/seed.ts`, matching events by title + startAt. Parent–teacher evening date = seed run date + 14 days, so it is not stable across runs; match it by title only. Robotics Club: D7. Sports day: no announcement link. |","+| NFR-1 | UI, TEST | Lint/QA grep for banned imports. Only MUI + MUI X (incl. the scheduler). |","+| NFR-2 | process | The dev phase must call MUI MCP before using any scheduler API, and system-design should list the doc pages to fetch (Quickstart, Views, Events, Timezones, Localization). |","+| NFR-3 | SVC, TEST | One concern across expansion (wall-clock stepping), all-day storage (tz midnight), the `VALUE=DATE` / TZID feed, and the scheduler `timezone` prop (check MCP Timezones page). Test a DST week (e.g. the US 2026-11-01 or 2027-03-14 transition, depending on the seed tz). |","+| NFR-4 | SVC | <500 ms for a parent with 3 children in month view. Batch the child/course/section lookups, use one events query with an audience `OR` filter, and avoid per-day `isSchoolDay` calls. Add an index on `EventAudience(type, targetId)` beyond the PRD spec (the PRD's model has the event FK; add `@@index([type, targetId])`). |","+| NFR-5 | AUTH, SVC | `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, stored as sha256 hex. The feed reuses `getCalendarItems`, so visibility can't drift. Integration test for parity. |","+| NFR-6 | TEST, DEP | `node-ical` devDependency. Parse `buildIcs` output in a unit test and the feed route output in an integration test. |","+| NFR-7 | AUTH | Every handler uses `requireUser`/`requireRole`, except the feed (token auth) and `/api/public/events` (public by design). Per-entity checks live in calendar-service, not in the routes. |","+| NFR-8 | all | `src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts` (+ `ical.ts`, `recurrence.ts` if split). Thin routes. `{data}` responses. `logger`. cuid ids. |","+| NFR-9 | INT | Reuse list: timetable-service (B3/B4), rate-limit (B9), notify (B7), audit, DataTable, useToast, ConfirmDialog, MarkdownView/Editor, csv.ts, the dispatch cron (B8), getSchoolTimezone (B13), and the access helpers (B11). |","+| NFR-10 | TEST | Unit: expansion, isSchoolDay, ICS escaping/RRULE/folding, all-day exclusive end, term-break gaps. Integration: merge per role, token reset (old URL 404), RSVP deadline. Playwright: 3 flows. |","+| NFR-11 | scope | No per-occurrence exceptions, no room booking, no two-way sync. PRD-16/18 get only FR-30/31 hooks. |","+| NFR-12 | UI | 768 px breakpoint (FR-9). English only. Evergreen browsers. |"," ","-## 3. New surface summary (for traceability)","+## 3. Decisions for arch-design-system (open items from intake)"," ","-- **Models:** Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageAttachment, MessageRevision, MessageReport (+ReportStatus), MessagingSettings, PendingMessageEmail. Plus User.isSafeguardingLead. (FR-1..4, FR-30, FR-31)","-- **Services (`src/server/messaging/`):** contact-rules, contacts, conversations, messages, read-state, notifications/pending-email, quiet-hours, safeguarding, maintenance (`sendDueMessageEmails`). (FR-5..8, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19..27)","-- **Routes:** conversations (list/create/get/read/mute/archive/leave), conversation messages (list before/after, send), messages/:id (patch/delete/report), messaging/unread-count, messaging/contacts, me/messaging-settings, safeguarding reports + conversations, and a hook into the internal dispatch route. (FR-28, FR-20)","-- **Pages:** `/messages`, `/messages/[conversationId]`, `/admin/safeguarding`, plus a Quiet hours section on `/account/notifications`, student layout actions and roster selection. (FR-9..18, FR-21, FR-23, FR-24)","-- **Registries:** 2 notification types, 1 file context, 1 nav item (+badge). (FR-18, FR-19, FR-26, FR-27)","+- **D1 – AudienceType / audience.ts / builder (FR-3, FR-7, FR-14).** PRD-12 is absent. Recommendation: SH-14 defines `enum AudienceType { SCHOOL GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }`. `EventAudience` gets `type`, `targetId String?` (null for SCHOOL) and `roles Role[] @default([])`, where empty means all roles. `roles` covers \"Grade 7 parents\". Resolver in `src/server/audience/audience.ts`, builder in `src/components/AudienceBuilder/`. Both are named generically so PRD-12 adopts them instead of re-creating them. Membership: SCHOOL = all active users; GRADE_LEVEL = students whose current-year SectionMember section has that grade (or `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`, pick one) plus their parents plus teachers of those sections or courses; SECTION = members + homeroom teacher + parents; COURSE = ACTIVE enrollments + teacher/co-teachers + parents.","+- **D2 – FR-20 host page.** No `/admin/academic-years/[id]` UI exists. The minimal option is a small server page at that exact path that lists the year's terms (read-only) with an \"Add term breaks\" button. Full academic-year CRUD UI is out of scope. Add no nav entry; link to it from the calendar editor or admin, or reach it by URL.","+- **D3 – Holidays vs School events chips.** Use intake's default: no duplication. HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool` events appear only under \"Holidays\".","+- **D4 – RSVP guests.** Parents only. The server forces 0 for other roles.","+- **D5 – Email default per category (FR-28).** The registry's `defaultEmail` is per type. Options: (a) two types, `event.created` (defaultEmail false) and `event.holiday_created` (defaultEmail true); or (b) one type that passes `email` only for HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK, which ignores the user preference toggle semantics. Recommend (a), because it stays inside the existing preference model with no changes to notify.ts.","+- **D6 – Nav.** Add `/calendar` (all roles). `/account/calendar` gets no sidebar entry, consistent with the existing account pages. It is reached from the account menu and a \"Subscribe\" link on `/calendar`.","+- **D7 – Robotics Club course (FR-37).** Not in the seed. Recommend seeding a minimal ELECTIVE course `ROBOTICS` (teacher Tom, current year) only if absent, so the Chess club example works. The alternative is skip-with-log.","+- **D8 – Feed URL display vs hashed storage (FR-24/25, NFR-5).** The raw token is only available at creation or reset. Recommendation: `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` returns `{url}` only when it creates the first token, and `{url:null, createdAt}` otherwise. The page then says \"Reset link to get a new URL\". This needs to be explicit in the API contracts.","+- **D9 – Schema deviations from the PRD's model list** (flag them in system-design): `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt`, `EventAudience.roles`, `@@index([type,targetId])`. Each traces to FR-23, FR-3/FR-37 and NFR-4."," ","-## 4. Open decisions for arch-design-system","+## 4. Risks"," ","-| # | Question | Recommendation | Drives |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| A1 | Co-teachers count as \"managing\" a course? | **Yes**: matches `teaches()`/`getAccessibleStudentIds`. | FR-32, FR-5 |","-| A2 | `updatedAt` on new models (the PRD block omits it)? | Add `updatedAt @updatedAt` to Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageReport and MessagingSettings (platform convention). Leave it off append-only MessageRevision, MessageAttachment and PendingMessageEmail. Treat the PRD block as the minimum field set. | FR-1, NFR-6 |","-| A3 | Quiet hours for all roles? | **All roles** (the settings endpoint is open to any role). | FR-21, FR-20 |","-| A4 | Send-time rule in groups: what does \"relationship ended\" mean when there are many participants? | Non-staff sender may send iff canMessage(sender, s) for ≥1 staff participant still present. If no staff remain (all left), they are refused. Note that staff can never leave a student group they created (FR-14). | FR-7, FR-6 |","-| A5 | Homeroom teacher reachability: current academic year only? | Filter `section.academicYear.isCurrent = true` for messaging (otherwise last year's homeroom stays reachable). Keep student-access.ts unchanged (do not modify other PRDs' behaviour). | FR-5 |","-| A6 | Where is isSafeguardingLead edited? | API/validator only (no form exists, B13). Document that the flag is set via the seed or the API. | FR-2 |","-| A7 | Does a participant who **left** keep read access to the old thread and attachments? | No: `leftAt` set → treat as non-participant (list hides it, 404 on get). Safeguarding still sees everything. | FR-14, FR-27, NFR-1 |","-| A8 | The 768 px breakpoint does not match MUI default `md` (900). | Use `theme.breakpoints.down(768)` locally, not a theme change. | FR-9, NFR-7 |","-| A9 | How do polling clients learn about edits/deletes? | `after` responses also return `changed[]` = messages in the loaded window with `updatedAt > since` (pass `since` ISO alongside `after`). Alternatively accept staleness until reload. Recommend the former (cheap; same index plus `updatedAt`). | FR-13, FR-15 |","-| A10 | Can a participant leave a 1:1 conversation? | No: \"leave group\" only applies when there are >2 participants. Archive covers 1:1. | FR-14 |","-| A11 | Does a new message unarchive the conversation for recipients, and does the unread badge count archived conversations? | Yes, unarchive for recipients on new message (standard inbox behaviour). Unread count then needs no archive filter. | FR-9, FR-14, FR-18 |","-| A12 | Can a user report their own message, or report the same message twice? | Others' messages only. One OPEN report per (message, reporter): return 409 CONFLICT otherwise. | FR-22 |","-| A13 | Nav visibility for `/admin/safeguarding` (role-only nav filter)? | Show the item to ADMIN only via a new optional `NavItem.requires?: 'safeguardingLead'` evaluated in the shell with the flag loaded server-side. The page still enforces 403. Otherwise leave it out of nav and link from the `message.reported` notification. | FR-23 |","-| A14 | Seed Pat↔Sam link missing (B18). | The seed upserts `ParentStudentLink(Pat, Sam)` if absent before creating the Pat↔Tom thread, and skips the thread if Tom does not teach Sam. | FR-29 |","-","-## 5. Risks","-","-- **Notification collapse via `link` match** (B2) is coupled to the link format. Keep link building in a single helper used by both send and read paths.","-- **Per-process rate limiter and in-memory state** (B5) are not shared across instances. This is accepted per the existing ponytail note.","-- **Email-preference bypass**: deferring email outside `notify()` (B3) must still honour `NotificationPreference` and DISABLED/ARCHIVED filtering. Reuse `resolvePrefs`, and cover it in integration tests.","-- **mui-mcp unavailable** in this session (B20). The dev phase must retry it before writing UI.","+- **R1 (high):** `@mui/x-scheduler` is beta. Its API (views, timezone, all-day exclusivity, custom event rendering for chips/colours) is unverified until MCP is consulted. Budget for fallbacks (FR-9).","+- **R2:** The import cycle between timetable-service and calendar-service (B4).","+- **R3:** DST correctness spans four places (FR-15 expansion, FR-4 storage, FR-26 VTIMEZONE, UI). One shared pure helper set in `src/lib/dates.ts` keeps them consistent.","+- **R4:** Audience resolution is the performance hot path (NFR-4) and the security boundary (NFR-5/7). It needs a single implementation, tested per role."]}],"originalFile":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-13\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:00:00Z), PRD-13 Direct Messaging. It has 32 FRs and 11 NFRs (43 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. The open decisions intake handed to the architect are in §4.\n\n> Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is left over from an earlier ticket (SH-12/SH-11). Its owning sub-task must overwrite it. None of those files is an SH-13 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-13 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no messaging models. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. `User` has `role`, `status` (default INVITED) and `archivedAt`, with `@@index([role, status])`. `FileObject` back-relations are explicit per attachment table. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1..4: one new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_messaging`). Add back-relations on `User` (participants, sent messages, reports filed/reviewed, settings, pending emails) and on `FileObject` (`messageAttachments`). |\n| B2 | `Notification` has **no entity/context column**: only `userId, type, title, body, link, readAt`, indexed on `(userId, readAt, createdAt)`. | schema L304-317 | FR-19 collapsing: \"replace older unread message.received rows for that conversation\" can only key on `link = /messages/<conversationId>` (plus `type` and `readAt: null`). Recommend `deleteMany({ userId in, type:'message.received', readAt:null, link })` before `notify()`. This is fine for performance because the leading `userId` index column applies. No schema change to Notification is needed. |\n| B3 | `notify()` writes the in-app rows **and enqueues email immediately** (EmailOutbox) when `input.email` is passed. It never throws and dedupes userIds. It filters DISABLED/ARCHIVED users. Preferences come from `resolvePrefs(def, pref)` in `notifications/preferences.ts`. | notify.ts L8-80 | FR-19/20 conflict: message email must be **deferred**. Call `notify()` for `message.received` **without** `email`, so only the in-app row is written. Upsert a `PendingMessageEmail` per recipient whose resolved `prefs.email` is true. The maintenance pass then re-checks `lastReadAt`/quiet hours and enqueues to EmailOutbox using the same `renderEmail('generic-notification')`. **arch-design-system** should define a small exported helper (e.g. `enqueueEmail(userIds, …)` or reuse of `resolvePrefs`) rather than duplicating notify's internals. |\n| B4 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). The `COMMUNICATION` category exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a static boolean per type and `roles` is a per-type role list. | notifications/types.ts | FR-19: `message.received` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp false, roles ALL}. FR-26: `message.reported` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true, roles ['ADMIN']}. |\n| B5 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` is a per-process sliding window that returns `{ ok, retryAfterMs }`. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-4: `rateLimit('msg:'+userId, 30, 60_000)`. On failure, throw `AppError('RATE_LIMITED')` (429) with `details.retryAfterMs`. The limiter is per-process. This is accepted (existing ponytail note). |\n| B6 | `registerFileAccess`: built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (files/contexts.ts). Unattached files (`contextId null`) are owner/ADMIN only. Resolver errors deny. Orphan files are purged after 24 h. | files/access.ts; files/contexts.ts | FR-27: add `register('message', messageResolver)` in `registerBuiltInContexts`. The resolver loads the Message by `file.contextId` (contextId = **messageId**, so a soft-deleted message can still be resolved), then allows a participant (`leftAt` irrelevant? see A7) or `isSafeguardingLead`. Attach files in the send transaction, or they are purged. Note: `FileAccessUser` is `{id, role}` only, so the resolver must query `isSafeguardingLead` itself. |\n| B7 | `SessionUser` = `{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}`. It has **no `isSafeguardingLead`**. | requireRole.ts L14-26 | NFR-1/FR-23..25: add a `requireSafeguardingLead()` helper (in `src/server/messaging/` or auth) that does `requireRole('ADMIN')` plus a DB read of the flag. Do not put the flag in the JWT: a revoked flag must take effect immediately. The page variant redirects to /forbidden (FR-23 says \"others get 403\"). |\n| B8 | Teacher→student reachability already exists: `getAccessibleStudentIds(TEACHER)` = ACTIVE enrollment in courses where `teacherId` or `coTeacherIds has` the teacher, **plus** SectionMember of sections they homeroom. The homeroom branch has **no academic-year filter**. `teaches(user, course)` is in course-access.ts. | student-access.ts L20-55; course-access.ts | FR-5/FR-32: reuse the same predicates (ideally share the Prisma `where` fragments) so contact rules and student-record access never disagree. Decide on the current-year filter for homeroom (A5). The PARENT branch is ParentStudentLink. |\n| B9 | `Enrollment @@unique([courseId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId, status])`. `ParentStudentLink @@unique([parentId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId])`. `SectionMember @@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` (no `sectionId` index). | schema | FR-5/FR-8 queries are index-backed from the student side. `coTeacherIds has` is not indexable, but a single user's course set is small. |\n| B10 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (CRON_SECRET) runs each job in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take)` → conditional `updateMany` claim → act if `count===1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts | FR-20: add `sendDueMessageEmails(now)`, isolated in its own try/catch. Process `PendingMessageEmail where dueAt <= now`. If the participant's `lastReadAt >= message time`, drop the row. If now is inside quiet hours, push `dueAt` to the end of quiet hours. Otherwise enqueue and delete the row (delete = claim; `deleteMany` count===1). |\n| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` lives in `assignments-service.ts` (precedent: other modules import it). `schoolNow(now, tz)` returns `{isoDay, hhmm}`. `formatInSchoolTz`, and `fromZonedTime` from date-fns-tz, are available. | src/lib/dates.ts; assignments-service.ts L64 | FR-20/21 quiet hours: a pure `isInQuietHours(hhmm, start, end)` with midnight wrap (`start > end`) and `quietHoursEnd(now, tz, end)` → UTC instant. Unit-test both (NFR-10). FR-10 day grouping uses `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes `RATE_LIMITED`, `FORBIDDEN`, `NOT_FOUND`, `CONFLICT`, `VALIDATION`. `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `audit()` exist. | src/server/http.ts; src/server/audit.ts | FR-28/NFR-6 handler conventions. Recommend returning 404 (not 403) for a non-participant on `GET /api/conversations/:id`, so cuids reveal nothing (NFR-1). FR-6 explicitly mandates 403 for **create** violations. |\n| B13 | **No admin user-edit UI exists.** `src/app/(app)/admin` has only attendance, courses, email-log, grading-scales, report-cards and sections. Users are edited only via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (ADMIN, `updateUserSchema`, audited). | src/app/api/users/[id]/route.ts; src/lib/validators/users.ts L103 | FR-2 resolution (intake's open question): add `isSafeguardingLead: z.boolean().optional()` to `updateUserSchema`. Reject or ignore it when the target role ≠ ADMIN. Audit the change (`user.update` metadata). **No form to extend.** Building a user-admin page is out of scope. |\n| B14 | **`/students/[id]` has no page.tsx or layout.tsx.** There are only sub-pages (attendance, assignments, courses, grades, report-cards), so there is no shared \"student page header\" today. | find src/app/(app)/students | FR-16: arch-design-system must pick the surface. Options: (a) add `students/[id]/layout.tsx` with a PageHeader + actions (affects all sub-pages, minimal per-page edits), or (b) put actions on each sub-page header. Recommend (a), keeping the `[id]` segment (no rename, per the PRD). The actions are client components that call `POST /api/conversations`. |\n| B15 | The course roster page is a **server component** rendering an MUI Table with no selection. PARENT gets notFound and STUDENT sees a name list. | courses/[courseId]/roster/page.tsx | FR-17: extract the TEACHER/ADMIN table into a client component with Checkbox selection and a toolbar button \"Message selected students\". It opens the FR-12 dialog prefilled. Rows carry `enrollmentId`, so the student id needs to be included in `RosterEntry` if it is not already there. |\n| B16 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `NotificationBell` implements a visibility-gated 30 s poll + MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L23-73 | FR-18: add `{label:'Messages', href:'/messages', roles: ALL_ROLES}` and an optional `badge?: 'messages'` key. The shell renders a polled Badge from `/api/messaging/unread-count`. Extract the bell's poll loop into a small `usePolling(fn, ms)` hook and reuse it for FR-13's 5 s/30 s polls. |\n| B17 | `/account/notifications` = page.tsx + `PreferencesTable.tsx`. `/api/me/*` routes exist (notification-preferences, profile, …). | src/app/(app)/account/notifications | FR-21: add a `QuietHoursSection` client component under that page, plus `src/app/api/me/messaging-settings/route.ts` (GET/PUT, any role). |\n| B18 | Seed users: Alice Admin, Tom Teacher, Tina Tutor, Sam Student, Sara Scholar and Pat Parent (by email). The seed creates **no ParentStudentLink** and no enrollments. Courses come from elsewhere and `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` skips when missing. | prisma/seed.ts L16-22, L304 | FR-29: set `isSafeguardingLead=true` on Alice. The Pat↔Tom thread \"about Sam's homework\" needs a Pat↔Sam link to satisfy contact rules at runtime. Recommend the seed upsert that link (or skip the thread with a log, like other seeds). The MATH-7A group uses the first 4 ACTIVE enrollments and skips if there are fewer or the course is missing. Seeds write via Prisma directly (bypassing canMessage) but must leave data valid under canMessage. Make it idempotent by checking for existing seeded conversations (subject/participants). |\n| B19 | Shared components: FileUpload, FileList, UserAvatar, UserPicker, ConfirmDialog, Toast, EmptyState, PageHeader, DataTable (in `src/components/<Name>/`). `@mui/x-date-pickers` is installed. | src/components | FR-10/11/12/23/24: reuse FileList/FileUpload (context 'message'), UserAvatar, ConfirmDialog (delete/leave), Toast (report confirmation), DataTable (safeguarding lists). FR-12 recipient picker: UserPicker is a candidate only if it accepts a custom options source (grouped contacts). Otherwise use MUI Autocomplete with `groupBy`. FR-21 time inputs: x-date-pickers TimePicker. |\n| B20 | The mui-mcp server failed to connect in this session (CONNECT_TIMEOUT). | session | NFR-5 requires mui-mcp lookups during dev. The dev phase must retry it. This is not a blocker for architecture. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend: DM = data model/migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance job, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | Conversation, ConversationParticipant (`@@unique([conversationId,userId])`, `@@index([userId])`, per-user `lastReadAt`, `mutedAt`/`archivedAt`, `leftAt`), Message (`@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, which NFR-2 depends on; `editedAt`, `deletedAt`), MessageAttachment (messageId, fileId; cascade on message), MessageReport + `ReportStatus`, MessagingSettings (userId unique, quietStart/End `String? HH:mm`). Add `updatedAt` per convention (A2). |\n| FR-2 | DM, API, AUTH | `User.isSafeguardingLead`. It can only be edited via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (B13) and is meaningful only for ADMIN. |\n| FR-3 | DM, SVC | `MessageRevision(messageId, body, createdAt)`, `@@index([messageId])`. Written in the same tx as the edit (original body before overwrite). Cascade with Message (messages are never hard-deleted anyway, NFR-3). |\n| FR-4 | DM, JOB | `PendingMessageEmail(userId, conversationId, dueAt)`, `@@unique([userId, conversationId])` so repeated sends upsert one row (the first unread message sets dueAt = now+10 min; later sends keep the earliest dueAt). `@@index([dueAt])`. |\n| FR-5 | SVC, AUTH | `canMessage(sender, recipient)` is a pure decision over pre-loaded relationship facts. Expose a batch form `messageableIds(sender, candidateIds)` to avoid N+1 queries for groups (≤25) and contacts (FR-8). Matrix: ADMIN→any, any→ADMIN, TEACHER↔TEACHER, TEACHER→STUDENT (managed course or homeroom, B8), TEACHER→PARENT (via the linked child under the same rule), STUDENT→own teachers, PARENT→linked child's teachers, all others false. Symmetry: student→teacher uses the same relation as teacher→student. Disabled/archived recipients → false. |\n| FR-6 | SVC, AUTH | Create conversation in one tx: participants = creator ∪ recipients (dedupe, exclude self from count rules), 2..25 total. Check `canMessage(creator, each)`. If any STUDENT is present, require ≥1 TEACHER/ADMIN. Any violation → 403 with nothing created. \"Students may reply in staff groups but cannot start student-student\" follows from canMessage(student, student)=false at create, plus the send-time rule (FR-7) being evaluated per-sender against **staff** participants only (A4). |\n| FR-7 | SVC, AUTH, UI | Send-time re-check. Non-staff sender: allowed iff canMessage(sender, p) holds for at least one remaining staff participant (A4). Otherwise 403 with code/reason `RELATIONSHIP_ENDED`. Staff always pass. `GET /api/conversations/:id` returns `canSend: boolean` so the composer shows the disabled message without a failed POST. |\n| FR-8 | SVC, API | `GET /api/messaging/contacts?q=`: role-specific grouped queries (PARENT: per child, \"My child's teachers (<child>)\"; STUDENT: \"My teachers\"; TEACHER: \"Students in <course>\", \"Parents of students in <course>\", homeroom, staff; all: \"School office\" = ADMINs). Status ACTIVE only. `q` filters on name. Cap each group (e.g. 50). |\n| FR-9 | UI, API | `/messages` layout with a two-pane `useMediaQuery(theme.breakpoints.down('md'))`, single pane + back below 768 px (theme `md`=900, so use a custom `down(768)` or confirm breakpoint, A8). List from `GET /api/conversations?archived=&q=` sorted `lastMessageAt desc`, with preview and `unreadCount` per row. Route: `/messages` and `/messages/[conversationId]`. |\n| FR-10 | UI, API | `GET /api/conversations/:id/messages?before=<id>&limit=30` (keyset on `(createdAt,id)`). Deleted messages are returned with `body: null, deleted: true` and attachments stripped for normal users (NFR-3: content is never exposed to non-safeguarding users). Day grouping in the school timezone (B11). |\n| FR-11 | UI, XC | Composer validation shared by the client and `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts` (body trim 1..5000, ≤5 fileIds). Enter=send / Shift+Enter=newline. Counter shows at >4500. |\n| FR-12 | UI | New-conversation dialog: Autocomplete multi-select grouped by contacts label, subject ≤120, first message. It posts `POST /api/conversations` with `{participantIds, subject?, body, fileIds?}`, creating the conversation + first message atomically. Also opened prefilled from FR-16/FR-17. |\n| FR-13 | UI, API, XC | 5 s poll of `?after=<lastId>` on the visible thread. 30 s poll on the list + nav badge. Gate on `document.visibilityState` (B16). The `after` query must also surface **edits/deletes** of already-loaded messages, or edits only appear on reload (A9). |\n| FR-14 | API, SVC, UI | `POST /api/conversations/:id/read` (sets lastReadAt=now and marks this conversation's unread `message.received` notifications read; deletes the PendingMessageEmail row), `/mute`, `/archive` (toggle body `{archived}`), `/leave`. Leave: set `leftAt`, which blocks further reads/sends for that user. Refuse (409/403) for the creator when `involvesStudent` is true. Group-only: DMs with 2 participants cannot be left (A10). Sending auto-unarchives for other participants? (A11). |\n| FR-15 | SVC, API | `PATCH /api/messages/:id` / `DELETE` (soft: `deletedAt`). Sender only, `now - createdAt ≤ 15 min`, not already deleted. Edit writes a MessageRevision + `editedAt` in one tx. No hard-delete path exists anywhere. |\n| FR-16 | UI | Student page actions (surface per B14). TEACHER/ADMIN \"Message parents\": participants = linked parents (+ creator). Hide the action if there are none or canMessage fails. PARENT \"Message teacher\": picker of the child's teachers (subset of contacts) → dialog. |\n| FR-17 | UI | Roster selection + action (B15). TEACHER only (ADMIN may also be offered, harmless). |\n| FR-18 | CFG, API, UI | Nav entry + badge (B16). `GET /api/messaging/unread-count` = count of the user's non-left participations where `lastMessageAt > coalesce(lastReadAt, epoch)` (count conversations, not messages: cheap, index-friendly). Archived conversations excluded? (A11). |\n| FR-19 | NOTIF, SVC | After the send tx commits: for each other participant not muted and not left, delete older unread `message.received` rows with the same link (B2), then `notify()` in-app only (B3). Title \"New message from <sender>\", body = 200-char plain preview, link `/messages/<id>`. |\n| FR-20 | JOB, DM, NOTIF | Upsert a PendingMessageEmail (dueAt=now+10 min) for recipients whose email pref is on (B3). Job per B10. Quiet hours read from MessagingSettings, evaluated in the school timezone (B11). |\n| FR-21 | UI, API, DM | MessagingSettings GET (defaults: no quiet hours) / PUT, Zod `HH:mm` regex. Both-or-neither validation. start == end is rejected. Applies to all roles (A3). |\n| FR-22 | API, SVC, NOTIF | `POST /api/messages/:id/report {reason ≤1000}`. Participant only. Allowed on own/others' messages (or other people's only? A12). One OPEN report per (message, reporter) to avoid spam (unique or check). Then FR-26 notify. |\n| FR-23 | UI, API, AUTH, XC | `/admin/safeguarding` (tabs Reports / Conversations), gated by `requireSafeguardingLead` (B7). `GET /api/safeguarding/reports?status=` with OPEN first, then createdAt desc. Detail includes the message, ±5 messages (including deleted and with revisions) and participants. `PATCH /api/safeguarding/reports/:id {action: review\\|dismiss, note?}` sets status, reviewedById, reviewedAt and note, then calls `audit()` (NFR-11). The nav entry is shown only to leads (the nav filter is role-based, so either show it to ADMIN and 403 non-leads, or extend NavItem with a predicate, A13). |\n| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH | `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations?participantId=&from=&to=` with `involvesStudent: true`, paginated. `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations/:id` = read-only full thread with deleted bodies and `revisions[]`. Same lead gate. |\n| FR-25 | XC, AUTH | `audit({action:'safeguarding.conversation.view', entityType:'Conversation', entityId})` on every safeguarding conversation view **and** on report detail views, since they expose conversation context. Done in the service, so both the API and the server page paths are covered. |\n| FR-26 | NOTIF | Notify `User where role=ADMIN, isSafeguardingLead, status ACTIVE` with `message.reported` (email allowed via notify's normal path: no deferral). Link `/admin/safeguarding?report=<id>`. The body must not include the message text (keep emails minimal). |\n| FR-27 | FILE, AUTH | B6. Send validates that each fileId is owned by the sender, unattached, and context 'message', then attaches in the tx (contextId = messageId). |\n| FR-28 | API, XC | All routes under `src/app/api/{conversations,messages,messaging,safeguarding,me/messaging-settings}`. Thin handlers + Zod + services in `src/server/messaging/`. Standard ok/paginated/error shapes. |\n| FR-29 | SEED | B18. |\n| FR-30 | SVC, DM | `involvesStudent` is computed in the create tx and is immutable afterwards (no participant-add API exists, so it stays correct). |\n| FR-31 | SVC | Update `lastMessageAt` in the send tx. `@@index` on ConversationParticipant `(userId)` + Conversation `lastMessageAt` serves the list ordering. Edits/deletes do **not** bump it. |\n| FR-32 | AUTH | B8: `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`. Resolved as yes (intake default, matches the existing `teaches()`). |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH, XC | Every service entry takes the SessionUser and loads `ConversationParticipant(conversationId, userId, leftAt null)` first. Non-participant → 404. Safeguarding → `requireSafeguardingLead`. File resolver per B6. Contacts never leak non-messageable users. |\n| NFR-2 | DM, API | `after` poll = participant check (unique-index lookup) + `Message where conversationId, (createdAt,id) > cursor` on `@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, `take 100`. Return `[]` fast. The 30 s list/unread polls use the participant index. Avoid count-per-message aggregation for unread (FR-18). |\n| NFR-3 | DM, SVC, AUTH | No DELETE that removes rows. FK cascades exist only for actual tree cleanup. Deleted/edited originals are exposed only through safeguarding services. |\n| NFR-4 | API, XC | B5. Applies to `POST /api/conversations/:id/messages`. Recommend counting `POST /api/conversations` (it also sends) against the same key. |\n| NFR-5 | UI, XC | MUI only; B19/B20. Badge, Drawer/List, Autocomplete, TimePicker, Tabs, Menu, Chip, TextField. |\n| NFR-6 | XC | `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts`, `src/server/messaging/{contact-rules,conversations,messages,notifications,quiet-hours,safeguarding,maintenance}.ts`, logger, cuid, UTC storage. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | See FR-9 (breakpoint, A8). |\n| NFR-8 | XC | A 5 s poll guarantees ≤ ~5 s + request latency < 6 s. No websockets/SSE. |\n| NFR-9 | XC | There is no reactions, typing or broadcast endpoint. Do not touch announcements (PRD-12 is absent). |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | `tests/unit/messaging/contact-rules.test.ts` (matrix incl. co-teacher, homeroom, DROPPED enrollment, group student-needs-staff, 26 participants), `quiet-hours.test.ts` (wrap midnight). `tests/integration/messaging/` (notification collapse, quiet-hours deferral via maintenance job, revision capture, 15-min window, rate limit, non-participant 404, safeguarding 403 + audit). `tests/e2e/messaging.spec.ts` (two browser contexts parent→teacher < 6 s; student→student blocked in the picker and on POST 403). |\n| NFR-11 | XC | Audit report review/dismiss and `isSafeguardingLead` changes. Users' own edits/deletes of their messages are not \"someone else's\" records, so no audit is needed. |\n\n## 3. New surface summary (for traceability)\n\n- **Models:** Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageAttachment, MessageRevision, MessageReport (+ReportStatus), MessagingSettings, PendingMessageEmail. Plus User.isSafeguardingLead. (FR-1..4, FR-30, FR-31)\n- **Services (`src/server/messaging/`):** contact-rules, contacts, conversations, messages, read-state, notifications/pending-email, quiet-hours, safeguarding, maintenance (`sendDueMessageEmails`). (FR-5..8, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19..27)\n- **Routes:** conversations (list/create/get/read/mute/archive/leave), conversation messages (list before/after, send), messages/:id (patch/delete/report), messaging/unread-count, messaging/contacts, me/messaging-settings, safeguarding reports + conversations, and a hook into the internal dispatch route. (FR-28, FR-20)\n- **Pages:** `/messages`, `/messages/[conversationId]`, `/admin/safeguarding`, plus a Quiet hours section on `/account/notifications`, student layout actions and roster selection. (FR-9..18, FR-21, FR-23, FR-24)\n- **Registries:** 2 notification types, 1 file context, 1 nav item (+badge). (FR-18, FR-19, FR-26, FR-27)\n\n## 4. Open decisions for arch-design-system\n\n| # | Question | Recommendation | Drives |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A1 | Co-teachers count as \"managing\" a course? | **Yes**: matches `teaches()`/`getAccessibleStudentIds`. | FR-32, FR-5 |\n| A2 | `updatedAt` on new models (the PRD block omits it)? | Add `updatedAt @updatedAt` to Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageReport and MessagingSettings (platform convention). Leave it off append-only MessageRevision, MessageAttachment and PendingMessageEmail. Treat the PRD block as the minimum field set. | FR-1, NFR-6 |\n| A3 | Quiet hours for all roles? | **All roles** (the settings endpoint is open to any role). | FR-21, FR-20 |\n| A4 | Send-time rule in groups: what does \"relationship ended\" mean when there are many participants? | Non-staff sender may send iff canMessage(sender, s) for ≥1 staff participant still present. If no staff remain (all left), they are refused. Note that staff can never leave a student group they created (FR-14). | FR-7, FR-6 |\n| A5 | Homeroom teacher reachability: current academic year only? | Filter `section.academicYear.isCurrent = true` for messaging (otherwise last year's homeroom stays reachable). Keep student-access.ts unchanged (do not modify other PRDs' behaviour). | FR-5 |\n| A6 | Where is isSafeguardingLead edited? | API/validator only (no form exists, B13). Document that the flag is set via the seed or the API. | FR-2 |\n| A7 | Does a participant who **left** keep read access to the old thread and attachments? | No: `leftAt` set → treat as non-participant (list hides it, 404 on get). Safeguarding still sees everything. | FR-14, FR-27, NFR-1 |\n| A8 | The 768 px breakpoint does not match MUI default `md` (900). | Use `theme.breakpoints.down(768)` locally, not a theme change. | FR-9, NFR-7 |\n| A9 | How do polling clients learn about edits/deletes? | `after` responses also return `changed[]` = messages in the loaded window with `updatedAt > since` (pass `since` ISO alongside `after`). Alternatively accept staleness until reload. Recommend the former (cheap; same index plus `updatedAt`). | FR-13, FR-15 |\n| A10 | Can a participant leave a 1:1 conversation? | No: \"leave group\" only applies when there are >2 participants. Archive covers 1:1. | FR-14 |\n| A11 | Does a new message unarchive the conversation for recipients, and does the unread badge count archived conversations? | Yes, unarchive for recipients on new message (standard inbox behaviour). Unread count then needs no archive filter. | FR-9, FR-14, FR-18 |\n| A12 | Can a user report their own message, or report the same message twice? | Others' messages only. One OPEN report per (message, reporter): return 409 CONFLICT otherwise. | FR-22 |\n| A13 | Nav visibility for `/admin/safeguarding` (role-only nav filter)? | Show the item to ADMIN only via a new optional `NavItem.requires?: 'safeguardingLead'` evaluated in the shell with the flag loaded server-side. The page still enforces 403. Otherwise leave it out of nav and link from the `message.reported` notification. | FR-23 |\n| A14 | Seed Pat↔Sam link missing (B18). | The seed upserts `ParentStudentLink(Pat, Sam)` if absent before creating the Pat↔Tom thread, and skips the thread if Tom does not teach Sam. | FR-29 |\n\n## 5. Risks\n\n- **Notification collapse via `link` match** (B2) is coupled to the link format. Keep link building in a single helper used by both send and read paths.\n- **Per-process rate limiter and in-memory state** (B5) are not shared across instances. This is accepted per the existing ponytail note.\n- **Email-preference bypass**: deferring email outside `notify()` (B3) must still honour `NotificationPreference` and DISABLED/ARCHIVED filtering. Reuse `resolvePrefs`, and cover it in integration tests.\n- **mui-mcp unavailable** in this session (B20). The dev phase must retry it before writing UI.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015RVVJaA25wfcBXKnjAY1nm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
