{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsrdHdNPBTxxY2hiNCFe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the requirements analysis notes for SH-14 to `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`, replacing a leftover copy from SH-13. All 49 requirement ids in it exist in `requirements.json`. I only wrote this one file; the other files in `artifacts/architect/` are also left over from SH-13 and need to be overwritten by the sub-tasks that own them.\n\nThe file has four parts: 19 codebase facts checked against the real code, a table mapping each requirement to what it means for the design, 9 decisions for `arch-design-system`, and 4 risks.\n\n**Things the design has to handle:**\n- **PRD-12 is missing.** There's no audience enum, no `audience.ts` and no audience builder. I recommend SH-14 adds a small `AudienceType` (SCHOOL, GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION, COURSE) plus a role filter, so \"Grade 7 parents\" in the seed works. The code would sit in shared folders (`src/server/audience/`, `src/components/AudienceBuilder/`) that PRD-12 can take over later.\n- **The holiday check has a ready slot.** `getScheduleForDate` and `getSchoolScheduleForDate` already have a comment marking where PRD-14 should plug in. I recommend keeping their return type and adding a separate `{isSchoolDay, reason}` lookup, so the attendance code that calls them doesn't have to change. There's also a risk of two modules importing each other (timetable and calendar), which the design needs to avoid.\n- **Feed links clash with hashed storage.** The token is stored hashed, so the subscribe page can only show the URL right after it's created or reset. The API contracts need to say this.\n- **Email defaults are set per notification type, not per event category.** The PRD wants holiday and term-break events emailed by default but others not. I recommend a separate `event.holiday_created` type rather than changing `notify.ts`.\n- **The schema adds things the PRD's model list doesn't include:** `rsvpReminderSentAt` (to send the RSVP reminder only once), `EventAudience.roles`, and an index on `(type, targetId)` for speed. The design should call these out.\n- **Seed and admin gaps:**\n  - There's no Robotics Club course for the Chess club event to target.\n  - There's no `/admin/academic-years/[id]` page to host \"Add term breaks\".\n  - With the seeded terms, the gap between Semester 1 and Semester 2 is only one weekend.\n\nSkipped: researching the scheduler's actual API. That waits for the dev phase, which has to look it up through the MUI MCP server first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11573,"cache_read_input_tokens":69564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11573,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b9140b8-a7ae-4ca4-9024-504a0df7df9f","uuid":"154a9544-9076-40a1-8a96-eb19da881951","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:50:30.435Z","request_id":"req_011CgsrdGzg1fM5ET1nks46m"}
